window.AURIC_DOCS=[{"t":"Auric Artisan Docs","d":"The complete user documentation for Auric Artisan — the website and its tools, the VS Code extensions, the browser extension and the services.","p":"Auric Artisan","u":"README.html","h":["Start here","Everything in these docs","How the docs are organised","About these docs"],"x":" Auric Artisan is a colour and accessibility studio. It lives in three places: the website at https://auricartisan.com, with its tools, libraries and kits; a set of extensions for Visual Studio Code; and a browser extension that brings the colour tools to any web page. A few services — a font CDN, an icon CDN and a public API — let you use the same data from your own sites and code. This documentation is written for the people who use those products: designers, developers, accessibility specialists, students and anyone curious about colour. It explains what every screen, control, command and setting does, how to complete real tasks step by step, what each tool measures and how precisely, and what to do when something does not behave as you expect. If you want to… Go to Understand what Auric Artisan is and where to begin Getting started getting started/README.md Use a tool on the website Website tools website/tools/README.md Learn the controls that appear on every page Site features website/site features/README.md Install and use a VS Code extension VS Code extensions vscode extensions/README.md Pick colours and check contrast on any web page Browser extension browser extension/READ"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan","d":"Where to begin with Auric Artisan — what it is, how its parts fit together, and the first things to set up.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/README.html","h":["In this folder","Where to go next"],"x":" This folder is the front door to the Auric Artisan documentation. It explains what Auric Artisan is, how the website, the extensions and the services fit together, and how to get from your first visit to useful work in about an hour. You do not need an account for most of it. Read the pages in order if you are new, or jump to the one that answers your question. Page What it covers What Auric Artisan is what is auric artisan.md The website tools, the VS Code extensions, the browser extension and the services, in one page How the pieces fit how the pieces fit.md What runs where, what is shared between products, and what needs an account Choose where to start choose where to start.md A goal by goal map from \"I want to…\" to the right tool or product Create an account optional create an account.md What an account adds, what works without one, and how to sign up The free tools model free tools model.md Why every tool is free, and what the paid plans add instead Privacy basics privacy basics.md What stays in your browser, what goes to a server, and how consent works Language: English and Hindi language.md Switching the website between English and हिन्दी Light and dark theme light and dar"},{"t":"Choose where to start","d":"A goal-by-goal map from what you want to do to the Auric Artisan tool or product that does it.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/choose-where-to-start.html","h":["Accessibility and readable colour","Palettes, gradients and design systems","Images and files","Colour science and research","Fonts, icons and publishing","Outside the website","Still not sure?"],"x":" Pick the row that matches what you want to do. Each row names the tool as it appears on the site, its address, and the documentation for it. Nothing in this table needs an account unless the row says so. I want to… Start with Address Docs Check whether two colours are readable together Contrast Checker https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/ Contrast Checker ../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Audit a whole web page for accessibility, contrast and colour Analyze URLs the Analyzer https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/ Analyzer ../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Crawl a whole site, several pages at once Analyzer, site scan needs an account and tokens https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/ Analyzer ../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md See a design the way people with colour vision deficiency see it Vision Simulation https://auricartisan.com/tool/vision simulation/ Vision Simulation ../website/tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Work through WCAG requirements as a checklist Accessibility Compliance https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/ Accessibilit"},{"t":"Create an account (optional)","d":"What works without an Auric Artisan account, what an account adds, and the short version of signing up.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/create-an-account.html","h":["What works without an account","What an account adds","Sign up in short","After you sign up","Related"],"x":" You do not need an account to use Auric Artisan's tools. The pricing page puts it plainly: every tool is free \"with no login required to start\". An account adds a few things that need to be tied to you rather than to one browser. Every website tool, including LUT Lab, the ICC Parser, the Color Science Lab and the clinical vision simulations. The libraries, the Learning Hub, the documentation and the blog. Saving palettes, gradients and collections to My Library in your browser. Drafting a portfolio in the Portfolio Builder. The browser extension and the VS Code extensions. With an account you can… Why it needs one Run server backed Analyzer work, such as whole site crawls It is paid for with tokens, and tokens belong to an account. The free plan includes 100 starter tokens. Buy a paid plan pass A pass belongs to your account so it follows you to other devices. An account is required before any payment. Publish your portfolio at your own address The published page is linked to your username. Create API keys for the REST API Keys and credits are counted per account API access is included from the Specialist plan . See signed in devices, turn on two step verification and export your "},{"t":"Your first hour","d":"A guided first hour on the website — finding your way, a first contrast check, a colour ramp with tokens, a page audit, vision simulation, saving work and setting preferences.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/first-hour-tour.html","h":["Stop 1 — Find your way around (5 minutes)","Stop 2 — A first contrast check (5 minutes)","Stop 3 — One brand colour to a token file (10 minutes)","Stop 4 — Audit a web page (15 minutes)","Stop 5 — See it through other eyes (10 minutes)","Stop 6 — Save and find your work (5 minutes)","Stop 7 — Make the site yours (5 minutes)","Stop 8 — Optional: create an account (5 minutes)","Where to go after the first hour"],"x":" This tour takes about an hour and needs no account. Each stop names the controls as they appear on screen, says roughly how long it takes, and ends with what you should see. Links point to the full documentation for each tool. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/. On your very first visit a short welcome animation plays; press Esc , Enter or Space , or click, to skip it. 2. When the cookie bar appears at the bottom, choose Accept All , Reject All or Customise . Every tool works whichever you pick. See Privacy basics privacy basics.md . 3. Look at the header. From left to right it gives you the home link, Search , and the Company , Tools and Learn menus, followed by icon buttons for the app, the browser extension, VS Code, search, the guide, the library, language and theme, and finally Sign in and Create account . 4. Press Ctrl + K and type \"contrast\". Open the Contrast Checker from the results, then come back. 5. Press ? while not typing in a field to open the Guide . It offers quick paths such as Run a quick audit , Build color assets , Check accessibility and Find a feature fast . Close it with Esc . Result: you can reach any tool from search, the menus or the guide. 1. On the home"},{"t":"The free-tools model","d":"Why every Auric Artisan tool is free on every plan, what the paid plans add instead, and how plan passes are sold.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/free-tools-model.html","h":["What stays free","What the paid plans add","How paid plans are sold","Tokens, in one paragraph","Related"],"x":" Every Auric Artisan tool is free, on every plan, for everyone. The pricing page https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/ opens with \"Every tool is free, forever\" and lists tools that used to sit behind a paywall — LUT Lab, the ICC Profile Parser, the Color Science Lab, the clinical vision simulations and the industrial suite — as free on every tier. Paid plans do not unlock tools. They sell conveniences and scale. Every tool, with no login required to start. Local saves in your browser. The libraries, the Learning Hub and the documentation. The browser extension and the VS Code extensions. Two step verification and account activity logging the pricing page lists \"2FA free for everyone\" . Everything that runs in your browser is free and unmetered — for example, the pricing page notes that vision simulations run in your browser and are not metered at all. The paid plans on the pricing page add, depending on the tier: ad free browsing and ad controls; watermark free Pro exports and more export formats; a monthly allowance of tokens for server backed work, such as whole site accessibility crawls of up to 24 pages a run; higher limits saved projects, URL analyses ; the REST API, with "},{"t":"How the pieces fit","d":"What runs in your browser, what runs on a server, what the account connects, and how the website, extensions and services relate.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/how-the-pieces-fit.html","h":["One engine, several places","What runs where","What the account connects","Two separate meters: tokens and API credits","Site-wide features","Related"],"x":" Auric Artisan is several products built on one colour engine and one design system. This page explains how they relate, so you know what you need to install, what needs an account, and what needs a network connection. The same colour science code powers the website tools, the Learn library's interactive figures, the REST API, the browser extension and the colour related VS Code extensions. The author page describes it this way: where an article states a formula or threshold, it is the formula the code uses. In practice this means a contrast ratio or a colour conversion should agree whether you get it from a website tool, the extension or the API. The products do not depend on each other. You can use the browser extension without ever visiting the website, or the VS Code extensions without an account. Product Where it runs Needs an account? Needs a network? Website tools most In your browser tab No Only to load the page, unless you prepared it for offline use Website Analyzer, basic analysis In your browser No Yes, to fetch the page you analyse Website Analyzer, server backed runs rendered analyses, whole site crawls On Auric Artisan's servers Yes, and uses tokens Yes Libraries and"},{"t":"Language: English and Hindi","d":"How to switch the Auric Artisan website between English and Hindi, how the choice is remembered, and what to expect in Hindi.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/language.html","h":["Switch language","How the choice is remembered","Share a page in a chosen language","Things to know about Hindi","Other products","Related"],"x":" The Auric Artisan website is available in English and Hindi हिन्दी . The interface, the tool pages and the articles are translated. English is the default. Use any of these; they all change the same setting. Header button — select the language button in the header its label is \"Switch language between English and Hindi\" . Each press switches between the two. Mobile menu — open the navigation menu and, under Preferences › Language , select English or हिन्दी . Settings — press Ctrl + , or use the floating settings button , open Appearance , and under Language select English or हिन्दी . Switching to Hindi translates the page in place, without a reload. Switching back to English reloads the page, because the original English text has to be loaded again. Dates and numbers follow the chosen language. Your language is saved in this browser and applies to every page you open afterwards, until you change it. It is not tied to your account, so a new browser or device starts in English. Add ?lang=hi to a page address to open it in Hindi, or ?lang=en for English. The person who opens the link also has that language remembered in their browser. For example: text https://auricartisan.com/compan"},{"t":"Light and dark theme","d":"How to choose Light, Dark or System theme on the Auric Artisan website, and how the choice is remembered.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/light-and-dark-theme.html","h":["Choose a theme","How the choice is remembered","Accent colour and comfort options","Related"],"x":" The website has a light theme and a dark theme. By default it follows your device: if your operating system or browser is set to dark mode, the site opens dark. Where Control Choices Header The theme button label \"Toggle dark mode\" Switches between light and dark Mobile navigation menu Preferences › Theme Auto , Light , Dark Settings Ctrl + , Appearance › Theme Light , Dark , System Keyboard Alt + T Cycles light, then dark, then system Auto and System mean the same thing: follow your device's setting, and change when it changes. A choice you make is saved in this browser and applies to every page, including after a refresh. An explicit Light or Dark choice wins over your device setting until you pick System or Auto again. The choice is per browser. Another browser or device starts by following that device's setting. The same Settings panel lets you pick an accent colour, change text size, reduce motion or transparency, boost contrast and more. See Settings panel ../website/site features/settings panel/README.md and Accessibility of the site ../help/accessibility.md . Theme ../website/site features/theme/README.md in Site features, for full details Language: English and Hindi langu"},{"t":"Offline use","d":"Install the Auric Artisan website as an app and prepare it to keep working without a network connection.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/offline-use.html","h":["Prepare the website for offline use","What works offline, and what does not","Keep it up to date","Where it runs","Related"],"x":" The Auric Artisan website can be installed as a web app a PWA — a website your browser can install and keep in its own cache and prepared to work without a connection. You do this once while you are online. The page for it is The app under Get Auric in the header, at https://auricartisan.com/download/. 1. While you are online, open https://auricartisan.com/download/. 2. Optional: if your browser offers it, select Install app to add Auric Artisan to your apps or home screen. Whether the button appears is your browser's decision. 3. Under How much to keep , leave Auto selected unless the device is short of storage. The profiles are: Profile Keeps Suits Auto Chooses for you from the device's memory, storage headroom and connection Almost everyone Lite The app shell and the core tools, and little else Phones, tight storage, metered connections Balanced Shell, core tools and the libraries you actually open A laptop you also use for other things Full The widest cache the profile allows A desktop that will be offline for a while 4. Select Prepare offline version , or Download full offline for the widest cache. The cache fills in the background and you can keep working. 5. Under Is this b"},{"t":"Privacy basics","d":"What Auric Artisan keeps in your browser, what it sends to a server, how the cookie choice works, and where to read the full policies.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/privacy-basics.html","h":["The short version","What stays in your browser","What goes to a server","Cookies and consent","Third parties","The browser extension","Your controls","Related"],"x":" This page is a short orientation. The detailed version is Privacy overview ../help/privacy.md , and the official, authoritative text is the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. Most tools run in your browser. Colour calculations, palettes, vision simulations and theme generation are done locally where possible. Your saved work and your preferences are stored in your browser on your device. An account stores the details you give it email, names, profile fields and the security records needed to keep it safe. Analytics is first party, sets no cookies, and runs only if you consent to the Analytics category. Payments go to Razorpay. Auric Artisan never sees or stores your card, UPI or bank details. The Privacy Policy states that Auric Artisan does not sell personal data or use it for behavioural advertising. Kept in your browser Examples Saved work Palettes, gradients, collections and exports in My Library Drafts Tool state and your Portfolio Builder draft Preferences Theme, language, accent colour, text size, eye rest and other settings Your cookie choice The consent record from the cookie banner T"},{"t":"What Auric Artisan is","d":"A plain overview of the Auric Artisan website, its tools and libraries, the VS Code extensions, the browser extension and the developer services.","p":"Getting started","u":"getting-started/what-is-auric-artisan.html","h":["The website","The VS Code extensions","The browser extension","Services for developers","What Auric Artisan is not","Related"],"x":" Auric Artisan is a colour science and accessibility platform built by one independent developer in India. It brings together practical colour tools, accessibility checks, colour vision simulations, learning material and developer services, and it publishes the same colour engine in several places: the website at https://auricartisan.com, a set of Visual Studio Code extensions, and a browser extension. The platform's own motto is \"Tools That Respect Intelligence\": the tools show their working, name the models they use and state their limits, so you can check a number rather than take it on trust. The website is the largest part of Auric Artisan. It has four kinds of content. Interactive tools that run in your browser. The header's Tools menu groups them as follows names as shown on the site : Group Tools Core tools Portfolio Builder, Portfolio Index, Analyze URLs, Vision Simulation, Design System Generator, Color Science Lab, Basic Tools, Personalization Generator Creative utilities Image Picker, Font Library, Icon Library, Generate ASCII Art, Generate Ishihara Plates Colour science Illuminants, Chromatic Adaptation, Gamut Mapping Gamut and rendering Gamut Explorer, HDR Gamut Plot,"},{"t":"The website","d":"A map of everything on auricartisan.com — the site-wide features, the tools, the kits, the library, the portfolio builder, search, your account and the company pages.","p":"Website","u":"website/README.html","h":["What is here","Where to start","In this folder"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com is the home of Auric Artisan. Its tools, libraries and learning material work in any modern browser, most of them without an account. You can install the site as an app and prepare it to work offline, and a set of site wide features — a settings panel, a right click menu, search, themes, English and Hindi, and comfort options such as eye rest reminders — follow you from page to page. Section What it covers Site features site features/README.md What you meet on every page: the header and navigation dock, search and spotlight, the settings panel, theme, language, the right click menu, eye rest, the screen saver, the cursor, the screen recorder, split view, shareable links, the page guide, cookie choices, notices, feedback, accessibility aids and every keyboard shortcut. Tools tools/README.md Every tool on the site, grouped by what it helps you do: accessibility and vision, the colour workspace, colorimetry and rendering, perception and spectral science, and image and file tools. Kits kits/README.md The floating panels you can open on any page: the Feature Kit calculator, graphing, unit converter, notes and developer tools , the Menu, Advanced, Status and Lib"},{"t":"Site features","d":"An overview of the controls, panels and helpers that appear on every page of auricartisan.com, with links to each feature's guide.","p":"Website › Site features","u":"website/site-features/README.html","h":["Who this section is for","The features","Quick start","In this folder"],"x":" Every page on https://auricartisan.com shares the same set of controls around its content: the header and its menus, a floating navigation dock, site search, a settings panel, a right click menu, comfort helpers such as eye rest reminders and reading mode, and a few quieter pieces such as the info bars and the cookie notice. They behave the same way on a tool, an article or a policy page, so you only learn them once. Most of these features keep their choices in your browser, not in an account. They work signed out, and many of them keep working offline once the site is installed as an app see Download and offline ../download and offline/README.md . The floating kits Feature Kit, Library Kit, UX Kit, Menu Kit, Status Kit, Update Kit and Advanced Kit also appear on every page. They have their own section: see Kits ../kits/README.md . Anyone using the site for the first time and wondering what a button or panel does. People who want the site to look or behave differently: larger text, less motion, a different accent colour, Hindi instead of English, no custom cursor. Keyboard users who want the full list of shortcuts. Folder What it covers header and navigation header and navigation/"},{"t":"Accessibility aids","d":"The site-wide aids that make Auric Artisan easier to read, see and use: reading mode, text size, contrast, motion, keyboard access and more.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan is built for accessibility work, and the site offers the same care to its own visitors. On every page you can: make text larger or smaller in four steps; switch to reading mode , a calm, narrow column of large text with the floating controls hidden; boost contrast , reduce motion , reduce transparency and underline links ; replace the custom cursor with your system pointer; choose light, dark or system theme; use the whole site from the keyboard, with shortcuts for the most common actions; switch the interface to Hindi. Many of these respond to your device settings as well: the site follows your system's light or dark preference, and it turns off the custom cursor and animated effects when your device asks for reduced motion. For the site's formal accessibility commitment, see the Accessibility statement at https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/. People with low vision, colour vision differences, reading difficulties or motion sensitivity. Keyboard and screen reader users. Anyone who reads long pages and wants fewer distractions. Settings Ctrl + , › Appearance text size, theme, language and Comfort everything else . Keyboard shortcuts anywhere: Alt + R readi"},{"t":"Accessibility aids guides","d":"Contents of the accessibility aids guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Set up text size, contrast, motion and the pointer for your needs reading mode.md reading mode.md Turn reading mode on and off, and what it changes keyboard and screen readers.md keyboard and screen readers.md Keyboard access, focus, the skip link, and screen reader support reference.md reference.md Every aid, where to find it, and its shortcut troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the accessibility aids","d":"Set up the site's text size, contrast, motion, transparency, link and pointer options for your needs.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Make text larger","Stronger contrast","Less motion","Clearer surfaces","Easier-to-spot links","Your system pointer","Fewer distractions","Language","Keep your setup"],"x":" All of these apply to every page at once and are remembered in this browser. Press Alt + + one step larger or Alt + one step smaller . Alt + 0 returns to the default. Or open Settings › Appearance › Text size and choose Small 90% , Default , Large 112% or X Large 125% . This scales the site's text. Your browser's own zoom Ctrl + + also works and scales everything, including layout. Settings › Comfort › Boost contrast draws secondary text in the stronger text colour and makes borders darker, in both themes. You can also choose the theme that suits you in Appearance › Theme . Settings › Comfort › Reduce motion or Alt + M makes animations and transitions finish instantly and turns smooth scrolling into jumps. If your device's reduced motion setting is on, the site also hides the custom cursor, stops the eye rest horizon from animating, shortens the first visit welcome, and swaps info bar messages without fading. Settings › Comfort › Reduce transparency replaces blurred, see through panels with solid ones. Settings › Comfort › Underline links always underlines links in articles and other text. Settings › Comfort › Custom cursor off restores your own pointer, including any large or hig"},{"t":"Keyboard and screen readers","d":"How the site supports keyboard-only use and screen readers, from the skip link to dialogs and announcements.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/keyboard-and-screen-readers.html","h":["Keyboard access","Screen reader support","Respecting your device settings","Reporting a barrier"],"x":" Skip link. On every page, the first Tab reveals Skip to main content . Press Enter to jump past the header. Menus. The header menus open with Enter , Space or the arrow keys and close with Esc , returning focus to their button. Panels and dialogs. Settings, Spotlight, the guide, the right click menu, the recorder and the kits all open and close from the keyboard. When a panel closes, focus returns to what you used to open it. Focus stays inside modal dialogs such as the guide, a guided tour and the Settings reset confirmation, so Tab cannot wander behind them. Shortcuts. The most common actions have shortcuts Ctrl + K search, Ctrl + , settings, ? guide, Alt + R reading mode and more . Letter shortcuts with Alt are ignored while you type in a field. See Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . Tooltips appear when a control receives keyboard focus, not only on hover. Date fields. Where the site shows its calendar for a date field, arrows move by day and week, Page Up and Page Down by month, Shift with them by year, Home and End to the start and end of the week, Enter or Space to choose, and Esc to close. Buttons that show only an icon have a spoken name, such as \"Ope"},{"t":"Reading mode","d":"Turn reading mode on and off, and understand what it changes on the page.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/reading-mode.html","h":["Turn it on or off","What changes","What does not change"],"x":" Reading mode is a distraction free layout with comfortable typography, for articles, documentation and other long pages. Press Alt + R not while typing in a field . Or Settings › Comfort › Reading mode . Or right click the page, choose View , then Reading mode Leave reading mode when it is on . Or, on card pages, right click a card and select the Reading pill. To leave it, you can also select the Reading mode ✕ chip at the bottom centre of the screen. Reading mode stays on as you move between pages until you turn it off. Area In reading mode Text column Centred and limited to a comfortable line length about 68 to 76 characters Body text Larger, with generous line spacing Headings Clear sizes and spacing, kept to a readable width Links Underlined for scanning Images and media Kept within the column Header Scrolls away with the page instead of staying pinned Floating controls Kit launchers, the library launcher and the right edge menu line are hidden Info bars and clock strip Hidden Pointer Your system pointer replaces the custom cursor Decorative animation Stopped Progress A thin bar across the top of the window fills as you scroll Exit Reading mode ✕ chip at the bottom of the scre"},{"t":"Accessibility aids reference","d":"Every accessibility aid on the site, where to find it, its shortcut and its default.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/reference.html","h":["Device settings the site follows"],"x":" Aid Where Shortcut Default Text size Small, Default, Large, X Large Settings › Appearance › Text size Alt + + / Alt + / Alt + 0 Default Theme Light, Dark, System Settings › Appearance › Theme ; header button Alt + T System Language English, Hindi Settings › Appearance › Language ; header globe — English Reading mode Settings › Comfort › Reading mode Alt + R Off Reduce motion Settings › Comfort › Reduce motion Alt + M Off Reduce transparency Settings › Comfort › Reduce transparency — Off Boost contrast Settings › Comfort › Boost contrast — Off Underline links Settings › Comfort › Underline links — Off Custom cursor Settings › Comfort › Custom cursor — On Eye rest reminders Settings › Comfort › Eye rest reminders — Off Tooltips on, detailed, advanced Settings › Tooltips Alt expands a tooltip's details On, detailed, not advanced Info bars and notices Settings › Highlights ; ✕ on each — Homepage only / on Skip link First Tab on every page — Always Device setting Site behaviour Dark or light mode Followed when the theme is System Reduced motion Custom cursor off; eye rest horizon still; shorter welcome; bars swap without fading Touch screen or no hover Custom cursor off Speech voice Us"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the accessibility aids","d":"Fixes for common problems with the accessibility aids.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The Alt shortcuts do not work","Text size did not change everywhere","Something still moves with Reduce motion on","My screen reader announces too much or too little","Reading mode did not change a page much"],"x":" Why: they are ignored while you type in a field, and when Ctrl or Cmd is also held. On some keyboards, Alt + + needs Shift as well; Alt + = also works. What to do: click an empty part of the page first, or use the Settings panel. Why: the text size setting scales the site's text. Some tools draw text inside images or canvases, which it cannot resize. What to do: use your browser's zoom Ctrl + + for those. Why: Reduce motion stops animations and transitions defined by the site's styles. A tool that animates a canvas as its purpose for example a live simulation may keep doing so. What to do: turn on your device's reduced motion setting as well, which the site also follows. What to do: report it with Report a bug see Feedback ../../feedback/README.md , naming the page, your screen reader and browser. Why: reading mode is designed for text pages. On a tool page it hides floating controls and adjusts text, but the tool's own layout stays. "},{"t":"Accessibility aids FAQ","d":"Short answers about the site's accessibility aids.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account to use these aids?","Can I carry my setup to another computer?","Is there a dyslexia-friendly font?","Where is the site's accessibility statement?","Are the colour tools themselves accessible?"],"x":" No. All of them work signed out and are kept in your browser. Yes. Use Export in the Settings panel, then Import on the other computer. The site does not offer a font switch. Reading mode, larger text and underlined links can make long text easier to read. At https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/, also reachable from the Company menu and the footer. The tools have their own documentation, which describes their keyboard and screen reader support where it differs from the site's. "},{"t":"Accessibility aids: supporting material","d":"Contents of the accessibility aids supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in these guides related.md related.md Related features and pages privacy.md privacy.md What the aids store The shortcuts for the aids are listed in Reference ../docs/reference.md and in Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Accessibility aids glossary","d":"Terms used in the accessibility aids guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Reading mode A distraction free layout with a narrow, large text column and no floating controls. Reduced motion Fewer and shorter animations; also a device setting the site follows. Transparency See through, blurred panel backgrounds; turned solid by Reduce transparency. Contrast The difference in lightness between text and its background. Skip link A link at the start of the page that jumps past the header to the main content. Focus The control that keyboard input currently goes to, shown with an outline. Screen reader Software that reads the screen aloud or in braille. Live announcement A message a screen reader reads without moving focus. Modal dialog A panel that keeps keyboard focus inside it until closed. "},{"t":"Accessibility aids privacy","d":"What the accessibility aids store.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your choices are kept in this browser as part of your settings. They are not sent to Auric Artisan or attached to an account. The site reads your device's colour scheme and reduced motion preferences only to adjust the page; it does not record them. A page link you copy can carry appearance settings that differ from the defaults, such as text size see Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . "},{"t":"Related to the accessibility aids","d":"Features and pages related to the accessibility aids.","p":"Website › Site features › Accessibility aids","u":"website/site-features/accessibility-aids/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — every setting behind the aids. Theme ../../theme/README.md , Language ../../language/README.md , Custom cursor ../../custom cursor/README.md , Eye rest ../../eye rest/README.md . Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md — the full list. Help › Accessibility ../../../../help/README.md — accessibility across all Auric Artisan products. Accessibility and vision tools ../../../tools/README.md — the Analyzer, Contrast Checker, Vision Simulation and more, for checking your own work. Accessibility statement — https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/ "},{"t":"Right-click menu","d":"What the site's own right-click menu does, how it adapts to what you clicked, and how to switch back to your browser's menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" When you right click a page on auricartisan.com, the site opens its own menu instead of your browser's. It is built around what you clicked: the top of the menu names the thing under your pointer the page, a link, an image, a selection of text or a colour and its own actions come first. Everything else is grouped into a few rows that open submenus, so the whole menu fits on one screen. A quick bar of one click buttons sits across the top. It starts with Back, Forward, Reload, Home and Copy URL, and you can pin any action to it with the star on that action's row. A filter field lets you type part of an action's name to find it anywhere in the menu, submenus included. A gear button opens the menu's own preferences: a longer \"Everything\" layout, a compact row height, or handing right click back to your browser for good. Your browser's menu is always one keystroke away: hold Shift while you right click. Anyone who wants quick actions on the thing they are looking at: copy a colour as HEX, RGB, HSL or OKLCH; copy a link as Markdown; copy an image's palette; search the web for a selection. Keyboard users: the menu can be driven entirely from the keyboard and searched by typing. People w"},{"t":"Right-click menu guides","d":"Contents of the right-click menu guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides cover the site's own right click menu: how it reads what you clicked, how to use the quick bar and the filter, how to change its layout or turn it off, and the smaller right click menus that some parts of the site have instead. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the menu, a tour of its parts, and your first actions actions for what you clicked.md actions for what you clicked.md The actions for a page, link, image, selection and colour quick bar and pinning.md quick bar and pinning.md Pin and unpin quick bar actions, and reset the quick bar filter and keyboard.md filter and keyboard.md Find actions by typing, and drive the menu with the keyboard menu preferences.md menu preferences.md Layout, row height, and making your browser's menu the default other right click menus.md other right click menus.md The clock, info bar, card, footer, Settings and Library Kit menus reference.md reference.md Every section, row, action, shortcut and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the right-click menu","d":"Open the site's right-click menu, learn its parts, and run your first actions.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the menu","The parts of the menu","Try it","Close the menu","Next steps"],"x":" Right click anywhere on a page, except inside a text field, a drop down or an editable area. Those keep your browser's menu so that spelling suggestions, paste and similar options still work. Hover the right edge. A short, thin gold line sits halfway down the right edge of the window. Rest your pointer on it for a moment and the menu opens beside it, showing the actions for the page. Move away and it closes. Keyboard. The menu key, or Shift + F10 on many keyboards, sends a right click to the page and opens the same menu. To get your browser's menu instead, hold Shift while you right click. From top to bottom: 1. Header. An icon and two lines that describe what you clicked: the kind Page , Link , Image , Selection or Colour and a detail, such as the page address, \"This site\" or \"Another site\" for a link, the pixel size and file type of an image, the word and character count of a selection, or the RGB value of a colour; a label: the page title, the link address, the image file name, the quoted selection, or the colour's hex code. For a colour, the icon is a swatch of that colour. 2. Quick bar. A row of one click buttons, each with an icon and a short label. By default: Back , Forwar"},{"t":"Actions for what you clicked","d":"How the menu decides what you clicked, and the actions it offers for a page, a link, an image, a selection and a colour.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/actions-for-what-you-clicked.html","h":["How the menu decides what you clicked","Page","Link","Image","Selection","Colour","The groups under More","Actions that depend on the page"],"x":" The menu checks, in this order, and uses the first that fits: 1. Colour — you right clicked a colour: a selected hex code such as d3af37 , or six hex characters that include at least one digit , a swatch or chip that carries a colour, or a short piece of text that is a hex code starting with . 2. Selection — you right clicked on text you have selected. A selection made earlier elsewhere on the page does not count unless your click lands on it. 3. Image — you right clicked an image. 4. Link — you right clicked a link. 5. Page — anything else. Plain words that happen to be valid hex, such as \"decade\" or \"facade\", are not treated as colours. The actions for a page appear first when you right click an empty area. For the other kinds, the same actions are in the Page row under More . Action Short label What it does Copy page URL Copy URL Copies the page's full address. Message: \"Page URL copied\". Copy page title Title Copies the page title. Message: \"Page title copied\". Copy as Markdown link Markdown Copies Page title address . Message: \"Markdown link copied\". Share page… Share Opens your device's share sheet. Without one, copies the address \"Link copied\" . Print… — Opens your browser'"},{"t":"Filter and keyboard","d":"Find any action by typing, and use the right-click menu entirely from the keyboard.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/filter-and-keyboard.html","h":["Find an action by typing","Keyboard reference","Mouse behaviour"],"x":" The filter field below the quick bar has keyboard focus as soon as the menu opens, so you can start typing straight away. 1. Right click the page. 2. Type part of an action's name, for example mark . 3. The list is replaced by matching actions from every group, submenus included, each tagged with the group it belongs to for example Page or Link . The field shows how many matched, for example \"2 of 27\". 4. The first match is highlighted. Press Enter to run it, or use the arrow keys to choose another. How matches are found: The filter matches the action's name, the name of its group, and a few extra words for some actions. For example, dark or light finds Switch theme , audit or seo finds Analyze this page , and colors finds Copy its palette . Names that start with what you typed are listed first, then names that contain it, then matches on the extra words. Up to 12 results are shown. If nothing matches, the list reads \"No actions match\" followed by your text. Typing works from anywhere in the menu: if a row has focus and you type a letter, it goes into the filter. Press Esc once to clear the filter. Keys What they do Letters and digits Type into the filter Down from the filter Move"},{"t":"Menu preferences and turning it off","d":"Change the right-click menu's layout and row height, and make your browser's own menu the default.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/menu-preferences.html","h":["Quick bar","Layout","Row height","Right-click on this site","One-off use of the browser's menu","Where preferences are kept"],"x":" The gear button at the bottom right of the menu, Customise this menu , replaces the action list with the menu's preferences. Every change is saved as soon as you make it; the footer confirms \"Saved\". Select Done , the gear again, or press Esc to return to the actions. Typing in the filter field also returns to the actions. Shows your pinned actions as chips, each with an X to unpin it, and a Reset chip that restores the default five. See Quick bar and pinning quick bar and pinning.md . Option Description on screen What it looks like Focused default What you clicked, then one row per group Your context's actions, then a More section with one row per group that opens a submenu Everything Every group open in one list Every group's actions listed in full, each under its own heading, with no submenus Choose Everything if you prefer to see all actions at once and do not mind a longer menu. Option Effect Standard default Comfortable rows, easier to hit with a pointer or a finger Compact Shorter rows, so more actions fit in the same space This choice decides which menu a plain right click opens. Option Description on screen This menu default Hold Shift for the browser’s menu The browser’s"},{"t":"Other right-click menus on the site","d":"The smaller right-click menus that some parts of the site show instead of the main menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/other-right-click-menus.html","h":["Clock strip","Info bars","Cards on browsing pages","Footer contact card","Inside the Settings panel","Inside the Library Kit","Places that keep the browser's menu"],"x":" A few parts of the site have a small right click menu of their own, with actions for that one thing. Right clicking them opens that menu instead of the main one. They share a look: a heading, labelled groups of buttons, and sometimes a Reset button and an All settings link. All of these close with Esc , a click elsewhere, a scroll or a window resize. Right click the clock strip at the top of a page when it is switched on to open Clock settings : a live preview, Format 12h , 24h , Date Long , D/M/Y , M/D/Y , ISO , Show switches Seconds , Weekday , Zone , a searchable Time zone list, Reset and All settings → . Details are in Info bars and notices › Clock strip ../../info bars and notices/docs/clock strip.md . Right click the welcome, announcement or quick links bar to open a menu headed with the bar's name \"Welcome messages\", \"Site announcements\" or \"Site tools\" . Under This bar : Button What it does Open Goes to the link you right clicked, or the bar's first link Copy link Copies that link's address Hide bar Hides this bar everywhere same as its ✕ Settings Opens the Settings panel on the Comfort section On pages with a grid of cards the homepage, Collections, Blog, Changelog, Docum"},{"t":"Quick bar and pinning","d":"Pin your most-used actions to the quick bar at the top of the right-click menu, unpin them, and reset the bar.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/quick-bar-and-pinning.html","h":["Pin an action","Unpin an action","Limits","Why a pinned action is sometimes missing","Reset the quick bar"],"x":" The quick bar is the row of one click buttons across the top of the right click menu. Each button shows an icon and a short label; hover it to see the full action name and its shortcut. By default it holds five actions: Back , Forward , Reload , Home and Copy URL . 1. Right click the page and find the action you use most, for example Split view under View , or Copy HEX on a colour. 2. Select the star at the right hand end of its row Pin to the quick bar . 3. The star fills, the footer confirms \"Pinned to the quick bar\", and the action appears at the end of the quick bar. With the keyboard: move to the action's row, press the Right arrow to move onto its star, and press Enter or Space . Select the filled star on the action's row Unpin from the quick bar . The footer confirms \"Unpinned from the quick bar\". Or open the gear Customise this menu and select the X on the action's chip under Quick bar . The quick bar holds six actions. With six pinned, selecting another star shows \"The quick bar holds 6: unpin one first\". Group rows Page, Colour tools, View, Site , greyed out actions and Browser’s own menu have no star and cannot be pinned. The quick bar shows only pinned actions that mak"},{"t":"Right-click menu reference","d":"Every part, action, shortcut, preference and message of the site's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/reference.html","h":["Ways to open","Header","Sections of the list","All actions","Preferences (gear)","Footer hints","Messages"],"x":" Method Opens Right click not in a text field The menu for what is under the pointer Shift + right click The browser's menu or the site menu, if you made the browser's menu the default Rest the pointer on the gold line at the right edge The menu for the page, beside the line Menu key or Shift + F10 The same as a right click What you clicked Kind and detail line Label Page Page · page address Page title Link Link · This site or Another site Link address Image Image · width × height · file type File name Selection Selection · word count · character count The quoted text, shortened to about 70 characters Colour Colour · rgb r g b with a colour swatch icon Hex code Section Shown when Contents Context actions Always This page, Link, Image, Selection or Colour actions More Focused layout One row per group: Page not for a page , Colour tools, View, Site Group headings Everything layout Every group listed in full under its heading Browser Always Browser’s own menu Website update banner An update is available, running or failed Update available , Updating website or Retry update Action Group Short label Shortcut shown Back Navigation Back Alt + ← Forward Navigation Forward Alt + → Reload pa"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the right-click menu","d":"Fixes for common problems with the site's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["I get my browser's menu instead of the site menu","I cannot get my browser's menu","A copy action says \"Could not copy\"","Copy image copies the address instead of the picture","Copy its palette is missing","The Colour tools group is missing","Right-clicking a word gave me a colour","A pinned action does not show in the quick bar","The menu closed while I was using it","Read aloud does nothing"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: You right clicked inside a text field, drop down or editable area. These always keep the browser's menu. Right click outside the field. You held Shift . Right click again without it. You chose Browser’s own menu on your previous right click. That lasts for one right click only; try again. You set Right click on this site to The browser’s menu . Hold Shift and right click to reach the site menu, then change it back under the gear. The page has only just loaded. The menu arrives a moment after the page; wait and try again. You right clicked something with its own menu, such as the clock strip or a card. See Other right click menus other right click menus.md . Hold Shift while you right click. If you often need it, make it the default under the gear Right click on this site › The browser’s menu . Why: the browser blocked access to the clipboard. This can happen in some embedded views, when the page is not in focus, or when a browser setting blocks clipboard access. What to do: click the page once so it has focus and try again, or select the text and use Ctrl + C . Why: some browsers do not let web pages put images on the clipboard, and images from other web"},{"t":"Right-click menu FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the site's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/docs/faq.html","h":["Can I turn the site menu off?","Does the menu work on phones and tablets?","Where do Search the web and Translate send my text?","Is my quick bar the same in every browser?","Why does the same menu look shorter on some pages?","Is the browser extension's menu the same thing?","Can I see the colour formats before copying?"],"x":" Yes. Right click, select the gear, and under Right click on this site choose The browser’s menu . The site menu is then available only with Shift + right click or from the line at the right edge of the window. A long press on a touch screen is handled by the browser and usually opens the browser's own menu or text selection. The site menu is designed for a mouse, trackpad or keyboard. Only where you ask. Search the web opens the search engine you pick in a new tab with the selected text in the address. Translate opens Google Translate in a new tab. Nothing is sent until you choose one of them. No. Pins and preferences are kept in the browser you set them in. Some rows depend on what the page loads. Published portfolio pages, for example, have no colour tools and remove some site actions, so their menu is shorter. No. The Auric Artisan browser extension has its own right click menu for other websites. On auricartisan.com the extension steps aside and the site's own menu is the one you see. See Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md . Yes. Each colour copy row shows the exact value it will copy. "},{"t":"Right-click menu: supporting material","d":"Contents of the right-click menu's supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Background material for the right click menu: terms, shortcuts, related features, what it stores and when it changed. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used by the menu and its guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts for opening and using the menu related.md related.md Related features, tools and pages privacy.md privacy.md What the menu stores and what uses the network release notes.md release notes.md User facing history "},{"t":"Right-click menu shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts for opening the right-click menu, moving around it, and running its site-wide actions.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Opening and switching menus","Inside the menu","Site-wide shortcuts the menu offers"],"x":" Keys Action Right click Open the site menu or the browser's, if you made it the default Shift + right click Open the other menu: the browser's by default Menu key or Shift + F10 Same as a right click Keys Action Type any letter Filter the actions Up / Down Move between rows Right Open a group's submenu, or move to a row's pin star Left Leave a pin star, or close a submenu Enter / Space Run the focused action Esc Close a submenu, clear the filter, or close the menu, in that order These work anywhere on the site, with or without the menu open. Keys Action Ctrl + Shift + C Open the colour tools menu. If you have selected a hex code, it is loaded. Ctrl + Shift + U Check for and apply a website update Ctrl + Shift + D Open or close split view Ctrl + K Open Spotlight search Alt + R Reading mode on or off The full list for the site is in Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Right-click menu glossary","d":"Terms used by the right-click menu and its guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Context The thing you right clicked: a page, link, image, selection or colour. Context menu A menu that opens on right click and offers actions for what is under the pointer. Quick bar The row of one click buttons at the top of the menu. Holds up to six pinned actions. Pin To add an action to the quick bar with the star on its row. Group A set of related actions Page, Colour tools, View, Site shown as one row that opens a submenu. Submenu The small panel that opens beside a group row, listing that group's actions. Filter The field that narrows the menu to actions whose names match what you type. Focused layout The default layout: your context's actions, then one row per group. Everything layout A layout that lists every group's actions in full, with no submenus. Markdown link Text written as label address , which many editors turn into a link. HEX, RGB, HSL Common ways of writing a colour: a hex code, red green blue values, or hue saturation lightness. OKLCH A way of writing colour as lightness, chroma and hue that follows human perception closely. Alt text The text alternative of an image, read by screen readers and shown when the image cannot load. Share sheet Your "},{"t":"Right-click menu privacy","d":"What the right-click menu stores and which of its actions use the network.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/privacy.html","h":["Stored in your browser","Actions that leave the site","Actions that stay on your device","Actions that use the site"],"x":" Your quick bar pins, layout, row height and right click choice, in local storage for auricartisan.com. Nothing about what you right click or copy is stored or sent. These open another website in a new tab and pass it the text you chose: Search the web › Google , Bing , DuckDuckGo , Wikipedia or YouTube — sends the selected text as the search query. Translate — sends the selected text to Google Translate. Open in new tab , Open in new window and Open image in new tab — open the address you right clicked. The copy actions put text or an image on your clipboard. Read aloud uses your device's own speech voice. Share… hands the link to your device's share sheet; what happens next depends on the app you pick. Copy its palette reads the image's colours inside your browser. Search this site opens the site's search page. Analyze this page opens the URL Analyzer with the address of the page you are on, ready to audit it. Update website checks the site for a newer version. "},{"t":"Right-click menu release notes","d":"User-facing history of the site's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" When Change September 2026 The menu was rebuilt around what you clicked: a header naming the page, link, image, selection or colour; a quick bar of pinnable actions up to six ; groups that open submenus; a filter that searches every action; and preferences for layout, row height and whether a right click opens this menu or the browser's. Earlier site releases are listed in the public changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The v0.9.10 entry 27 July 2026 refers to a custom right click menu in the browser extension, which is a separate product. "},{"t":"Related to the right-click menu","d":"Features, tools and pages related to the site's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Right-click menu","u":"website/site-features/context-menu/others/related.html","h":["Features the menu opens","Other right-click menus","Tools the Colour actions open","The browser extension"],"x":" Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md — Search the site . Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — Settings and Keyboard shortcuts . Split view ../../split view/README.md — Split view . Theme ../../theme/README.md — Switch theme . Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — Reading mode . Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the Update Kit behind Update website , and the Library Kit's own menu. Info bars and notices ../../info bars and notices/README.md — the clock strip and info bar menus. Collections › Card menu ../../../library/collections/docs/card menu.md — the card menu on browsing pages. Basic colour tools ../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — the floating colour tools and the Basic Tools page. Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — what Analyze this page starts. Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md — has its own right click menu for other websites. "},{"t":"Cookie consent and privacy choices","d":"The cookie notice, the four cookie categories, and how to accept, reject, customise or withdraw your choice.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" On your first visit, after the short welcome animation, a bar appears at the bottom of the page: We value your privacy . It explains that Auric Artisan uses cookies and local storage to keep the site secure, remember your preferences and understand basic, anonymous usage, and it offers three choices: Accept All , Reject All and Customise . The page stays readable and usable while the bar is showing. Your choice covers four categories: Essential always on , Functional , Analytics and Marketing . You can change it at any time on the Cookie Policy page, which lists every cookie in each category with its purpose and how long it lasts, and where you can also clear the site's non essential cookies or withdraw your consent. Every visitor. The choice decides whether the site may measure how pages are used, and which optional cookies it may set. The consent bar on your first visit. The Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/, section Manage Cookie Preferences . The Cookies link in the footer. 1. On your first visit, read the bar at the bottom of the page. 2. Select Customise . The Cookie Policy page opens at Manage Cookie Preferences . 3. Switch Analytics Cookies on or off"},{"t":"Cookie consent guides","d":"Contents of the cookie consent guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The consent bar and its three buttons manage cookie preferences.md manage cookie preferences.md Change, clear or withdraw your choice on the Cookie Policy page reference.md reference.md The categories, the listed cookies, the buttons and the messages troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with cookie consent","d":"What the cookie consent bar says, and what each of its buttons does.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/getting-started.html","h":["When the bar appears","What it says","The three buttons","What your choice affects"],"x":" The consent bar appears at the bottom of the page on your first visit, once the short welcome animation has finished. It stays until you choose. It does not dim or block the page, so you can read the page before deciding. It does not appear on the sign in and verification pages, and it does not appear again once you have made a choice in this browser. We value your privacy The bar explains that Auric Artisan uses cookies and local storage to keep the platform secure, remember your preferences theme, accent colour, language and tool settings and understand basic, anonymous usage. Essential cookies are always on; analytics and other optional cookies run only with your consent, and your data is never sold. It links to the full Cookie Policy . Button What it does Accept All Turns on every category: Essential, Functional, Analytics and Marketing Reject All Keeps only Essential, turns the others off, and deletes the site's non essential cookies Customise Opens the Cookie Policy page at Manage Cookie Preferences , where you choose each category After Accept All or Reject All , the bar slides away and your choice is recorded with the date and time. Note: The bar says you can change your c"},{"t":"Manage your cookie preferences","d":"Change, save, clear or withdraw your cookie choices on the Cookie Policy page.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/manage-cookie-preferences.html","h":["Open the preferences","Choose by category","Clear all non-essential cookies","Withdraw consent","Where your choice applies"],"x":" All cookie controls are in the Manage Cookie Preferences section of the Cookie Policy page. Select Customise on the consent bar; or open https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ cookies preferences; or select Cookies in the footer, then Manage Cookie Preferences in the page's section rail. The section opens and scrolls into view. Each category is a card with a title, a count of listed cookies, a description and a switch: Essential Cookies — marked Always Active ; the switch cannot be turned off. Functional Cookies Analytics Cookies Marketing Cookies Select Show cookies under a card to see a table of that category's cookies Cookie, Purpose, Duration, Type , and Hide cookies to fold it away. To save a choice: 1. Turn the switches on or off. 2. Select Save Preferences . Result: \"Cookie preferences saved successfully.\" Cookies from any category you switched off are deleted, and the Consent recorded line shows the new date and time. Important: Accept All and Reject All on this page only set the switches. Select Save Preferences afterwards to apply them. If you have never made a choice, the switches start with Functional on and Analytics and Marketing off. Select Clear All Cookies . The "},{"t":"Cookie consent reference","d":"The cookie categories, every listed cookie, the consent controls and their messages.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/reference.html","h":["Categories","Listed cookies","Consent bar","Preferences section (Cookie Policy page)","Messages","Defaults before any choice"],"x":" Category Can be turned off Description on the Cookie Policy page summary Essential No Always Active Core functions: authentication, security, session management and access control Functional Yes Remembers settings such as theme, language, layout choices and form data Analytics Yes How visitors use the platform; aggregate or pseudonymous, never used for advertising profiles Marketing Yes Reserved for campaign attribution if enabled later; no marketing pixels or cross site profiles now Cookie Category Purpose Duration Type aa sid Essential Signed in session management and authentication Up to 30 days First party aa csrf Essential Cross site request forgery protection Up to 30 days First party aa cookie consent Essential Stores your cookie preferences 1 year First party aa theme Functional Stores light/dark mode preference 1 year First party aa lang Functional Language and locale preference 1 year First party aa eye rest Functional Eye rest feature interval and duration settings 1 year First party aa layout Functional Grid/list view and sidebar preferences 6 months First party aa recent Functional Recently viewed items for quick access 30 days First party aa analytics id Analytics An"},{"t":"Troubleshooting cookie consent","d":"Fixes for common problems with the cookie notice and preferences.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The consent bar keeps coming back","I cannot find the cookie settings in the Settings panel","I pressed Accept All or Reject All on the Cookie Policy page and nothing changed","My settings survived Reject All","The bar does not appear on the sign-in page"],"x":" Why: your choice is kept in this browser's storage. It is lost if the browser clears site data on exit, if you use a private window, or if storage is blocked for the site. What to do: allow auricartisan.com to keep site data, or accept that a private window asks each time. Why: the consent bar mentions Settings, but the controls are on the Cookie Policy page. What to do: open https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ cookies preferences. Why: on that page, those buttons only set the switches. What to do: select Save Preferences . Why: your preferences theme, accent, language and the Settings panel's choices are kept in your browser's local storage so that the features you use keep working. Rejecting optional cookies does not reset them. What to do: use Reset all in the Settings panel, or clear the site's data in your browser, to remove them. Why: the notice is not shown over sign in and verification pages. It appears on the next ordinary page. "},{"t":"Cookie consent FAQ","d":"Short answers about cookies and privacy choices on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/docs/faq.html","h":["Does the site sell my data?","Are the cookies third-party?","What happens if I ignore the bar?","Does rejecting cookies stop the tools from working?","Does my browser's Do Not Track setting count?","Where are the full policies?"],"x":" The consent notice states that your data is never sold. The full terms are in the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/. All cookies listed on the Cookie Policy page are first party set by auricartisan.com . Nothing optional is enabled. No analytics events are recorded until you accept Analytics. The bar stays until you choose. No. Essential functions and every tool keep working. Rejecting only turns off the optional categories. Yes. With Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control turned on in your browser, the site's analytics stays off even if you accepted Analytics. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Cookie Policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ Privacy Policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ They are also summarised in Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Cookie consent: supporting material","d":"Contents of the cookie consent supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the cookie guides related.md related.md Policies and related features privacy.md privacy.md What the site measures with and without your consent "},{"t":"Cookie consent glossary","d":"Terms used in the cookie consent guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Cookie A small piece of data a website stores in your browser and receives back on later visits. Local storage Browser storage that a website's pages can read, but which is not sent to the website automatically. First party Set by the website you are visiting here, auricartisan.com , not by another company. Consent Your recorded choice about which optional categories the site may use. Essential Needed for the site to work securely; cannot be turned off. Functional Remembers your preferences. Analytics Measures how the site is used, in aggregate or pseudonymously. Marketing Campaign attribution and advertising measurement; not currently used. Do Not Track, Global Privacy Control Browser settings that ask websites not to track you. Pseudonymous Linked to a random identifier rather than to your name or account. "},{"t":"What the site measures","d":"What the site measures with and without your consent, and how browser privacy signals are respected.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/others/privacy.html","h":["With Analytics consent","Without Analytics consent","Browser privacy signals","Your preferences"],"x":" The site's own, first party analytics may record usage events: the name of an event such as a feature being used , the page's path, and a few small details. It does not record what you type into fields, email addresses, or the query part of addresses. No third party analytics scripts are used for this. With the same consent, the site also measures whether a visit behaves like a person rather than an automated script, from how pointer and keyboard input vary during the visit. It does not record what you clicked, what you typed, where you came from or who you are. No usage events are recorded. The site still counts that a page was viewed: the page's path and the site's host name, with nothing about how you used the page and no identifier stored on your device. If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control , the site's analytics stays off and page views are not counted at all, whatever your cookie choice. Settings you choose theme, language, accent colour, comfort options and similar are kept in your browser's local storage so that the features work. They are not sent to Auric Artisan. The full, binding descriptions are in the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com"},{"t":"Related to cookie consent","d":"Policies and features related to cookie consent.","p":"Website › Site features › Cookie consent and privacy","u":"website/site-features/cookie-consent-and-privacy/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Cookie Policy — https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ Privacy Policy — https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md — summaries of the policies. Help › Privacy ../../../../help/README.md — privacy questions across all Auric Artisan products. Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — your preferences, which are kept in your browser. Info bars and notices ../../info bars and notices/README.md — the first visit welcome animation that plays before the consent bar. "},{"t":"Custom cursor","d":"The ring-and-dot pointer that follows your mouse on Auric Artisan, the shapes it takes, and how to turn it off.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" On a computer with a mouse or trackpad, Auric Artisan replaces your system pointer with its own: a thin ring that follows your pointer smoothly, and a small dot at the exact point you are aiming. The ring changes shape to tell you what the thing under it does: it grows over links and buttons, becomes an I beam over text, a double arrow over a resize handle, a crosshair over precise controls, and so on. The ring also picks its colour from what is under it. It keeps the hue of the surface but pushes its lightness away from it, so the ring stays visible on a dark photo, a light page or a colourful canvas. Over grey or neutral surfaces it uses your accent colour. The custom cursor is on by default and can be turned off at any time in Settings. It is never shown on touch screens, on devices without a hovering pointer, or when your device asks for reduced motion. Mouse and trackpad users. If you prefer your system pointer, for example because you use a large or high contrast system cursor, turn the custom cursor off. Settings Ctrl + , › Comfort › Custom cursor . 1. Move your mouse over a page. The ring and dot follow it. 2. Point at a link. The ring grows slightly. 3. Point at a paragra"},{"t":"Custom cursor guides","d":"Contents of the custom cursor guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md How the cursor behaves, when it is hidden, and how to turn it off reference.md reference.md Every cursor shape and effect troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the custom cursor","d":"How the custom cursor behaves, when it is hidden, and how to turn it off.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/docs/getting-started.html","h":["The two parts","How it reacts","When the custom cursor is not shown","Turn it off or on"],"x":" The dot is where you are pointing. Clicks happen at the dot. The ring trails slightly behind and changes shape to show what the element under it does. Hover: over links, buttons and other clickable things, the ring grows and softly glows the \"magnetic\" look . Over text it becomes an I beam. Click: the ring shrinks briefly. Fast movement: the ring stretches in the direction you move. Rest: when you stop moving for a moment, or the pointer leaves the window, the ring fades to half strength. Loading: while a page or tool is busy, the ring turns dashed and spins. Colour: the ring's colour follows the surface under it, and the dot switches between dark and light so it is always visible. The full list of shapes is in the Reference reference.md . Your system pointer is used instead when: you switched off Custom cursor in Settings › Comfort; your device uses touch, or has no pointer that can hover such as most phones and tablets ; your device's reduced motion setting is on; reading mode is on. When the custom cursor is off, the site still shows the right system pointer: a hand over links and buttons, an I beam over text fields, and a left right arrow over sliders. 1. Press Ctrl + , and se"},{"t":"Custom cursor reference","d":"Every shape and effect of the custom cursor, and where each appears.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/docs/reference.html","h":["Shapes","Effects","Setting"],"x":" Shape Looks like Appears over Default Round ring with a dot Ordinary page areas Pointer Larger ring with a soft glow Links, buttons and other clickable items Text Tall, narrow I beam Text and text fields Grab Rounded square Things you can drag Grabbing Smaller rounded square While dragging Precision Small ring Sliders and vector graphics such as charts and diagrams Canvas Small dashed, spinning ring Drawing and graphics areas in tools Resize Double headed arrow, turned to the direction Resize handles and split view dividers left right, up down or diagonal Move Four way arrow Things you can move in any direction Zoom in / Zoom out Plus or minus in the ring Images and areas you can zoom Help Question mark in the ring Abbreviations and help items Copy Small plus at the ring's corner Items that copy when clicked Crosshair Hairline cross in a tight ring Pickers and crosshair areas Not allowed Red ring with a slash Actions that are not allowed Disabled Faint, grey ring Disabled controls Loading Dashed, spinning ring While the page or a tool is busy Effect When Magnetic glow Over clickable items and draggable items Shrink On click Stretch During fast movement Fade to half When idle, or w"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the custom cursor","d":"Fixes for common custom cursor problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The cursor feels slow or lags behind","I cannot see the cursor","My large or high-contrast system pointer is replaced","The custom cursor does not appear at all","Screen recordings show a ring and dot"],"x":" Why: the ring follows the pointer smoothly on purpose, and on a busy page or a slower computer it can fall further behind. What to do: aim with the dot, which is exact. If the lag bothers you, switch off Custom cursor in Settings › Comfort. Possible causes and fixes: The ring fades when you stop moving. Move the mouse. The page is still loading. Wait a moment. Switch off Custom cursor in Settings to use your system pointer. Why: the custom cursor hides the system pointer. What to do: switch off Custom cursor in Settings › Comfort. Your system pointer, with its size and colour, returns everywhere on the site. Why: it is off in Settings, your device has no hovering pointer, your device asks for reduced motion, or reading mode is on. This is intended. Why: the custom cursor is part of the page, so recordings of the page include it. What to do: switch it off before recording, or use the recorder's Highlight the cursor option with the custom cursor off. "},{"t":"Custom cursor FAQ","d":"Short answers about the custom cursor.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/docs/faq.html","h":["Does the custom cursor change where I click?","Does Reduce motion in Settings turn it off?","Why does the ring change colour?","Is it shown on my phone?","Does it work in the installed app?"],"x":" No. Clicks happen at the dot, exactly where your system pointer would be. No. The custom cursor follows your device's reduced motion setting, not the site's Reduce motion switch. Use the Custom cursor switch to turn it off. It reads the colour of the surface under it and picks a version of that colour that stands out, so it stays visible on any background. No. Touch screens use the device's normal behaviour. Yes, on computers with a mouse or trackpad, the same as in the browser. "},{"t":"Custom cursor: supporting material","d":"Contents of the custom cursor supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the cursor guides related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What the cursor reads and stores The cursor has no keyboard shortcut. Turn it on or off in Settings › Comfort Ctrl + , . "},{"t":"Custom cursor glossary","d":"Terms used in the custom cursor guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning System pointer The mouse pointer drawn by your operating system. Ring The outer part of the custom cursor that changes shape. Dot The small inner point of the custom cursor, where clicks land. Hover Resting the pointer over something without clicking. Reduced motion A device setting that asks apps and websites to limit animation. Adaptive colour The ring's colour, chosen from the surface under it so it stays visible. "},{"t":"Custom cursor privacy","d":"What the custom cursor reads and stores.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The cursor reads the colour of the page under the pointer, inside your browser, to choose its own colour. It does not record where you point or send pointer movements anywhere. Your on or off choice is kept in this browser as part of your settings. "},{"t":"Related to the custom cursor","d":"Features related to the custom cursor.","p":"Website › Site features › Custom cursor","u":"website/site-features/custom-cursor/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel › Comfort options ../../settings panel/docs/comfort options.md — the Custom cursor switch. Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — reading mode and other comfort settings. Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md — its Highlight the cursor option. Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — the accent colour the cursor uses on neutral surfaces. "},{"t":"Eye rest","d":"Optional reminders that invite you to look away from the screen for a few seconds, on a schedule you choose.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Eye rest is an optional reminder to look away from the screen. When it is on, a small card appears after a set time on a page, \"Time to look away\", and invites you to rest your eyes for a few seconds. Select Rest now and the screen dims to a quiet horizon with one instruction: look at something about twenty feet away. A line on the horizon shrinks as the seconds pass, and when the rest is over the whole screen brightens, so you can tell it has finished without looking back at it. Reminders are off by default . You choose how often they come every 20, 35, 45 or 60 minutes and how long each rest lasts 5 to 30 seconds . Every reminder can be put off with Later , silenced for the session, or turned off for good. People who spend long stretches looking at colours, contrast checks or code on the site and want a gentle prompt to look away now and then. Settings Ctrl + , › Comfort › Eye rest reminders . 1. Press Ctrl + , and select Comfort . 2. Switch on Eye rest reminders . 3. Under Reminder interval , select 20m . 4. Keep working on a page. After 20 minutes the card \"Time to look away\" appears. 5. Select Rest now . The screen dims; look at something far away until it brightens. 6. The p"},{"t":"Eye rest guides","d":"Contents of the eye rest guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Turn reminders on and choose how often they come the reminder and the rest.md the reminder and the rest.md The reminder card, its options, and the rest screen reference.md reference.md Every control, value, default and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with eye rest","d":"Turn eye-rest reminders on, choose the interval, and turn them off again.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Turn reminders on","How the countdown works","Turn reminders off","Next step"],"x":" 1. Press Ctrl + , to open Settings, then select Comfort . 2. Switch on Eye rest reminders \"Gentle reminders to rest your eyes on a schedule.\" . 3. Under Reminder interval minutes between reminders , select 20m , 35m , 45m or 60m . The countdown starts at once. Changing the interval later restarts it. The countdown runs while a page is open. It starts again whenever you load a page, including moving to another page or reloading. It keeps running while the tab is in the background, so a reminder can be waiting when you come back. After a reminder, the next countdown starts when you finish, end or put off the rest. Any of these: Settings › Comfort › switch off Eye rest reminders . This is the most reliable way. On a reminder card, select Turn these off . For this session only, select Not this session on a reminder card. Note: Turn these off on the card stops the reminders but does not move the switch in Settings. If you later change any setting while that switch still shows on, the reminders come back. Switch it off in Settings as well to keep them off. The reminder and the rest the reminder and the rest.md explains the card and the rest screen. "},{"t":"The reminder and the rest","d":"What the eye-rest reminder card offers, how to change its timings, and what happens during and after a rest.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/the-reminder-and-the-rest.html","h":["The reminder card","Change how often and how long","During the rest","When the rest ends"],"x":" When the countdown ends, a card appears: Time to look away \"You have been at this for 20 minutes. 30 seconds looking into the distance is enough.\" with your own interval and rest length Rest now and Later a quieter row: Change , Not this session , Turn these off a thin bar that empties over 60 seconds If you do nothing, the card leaves by itself after 60 seconds when the bar is empty , and the next countdown starts. Button What it does Rest now Starts the rest straight away Later Closes the card; the next reminder comes after a full interval Change Shows the timing options below Not this session No more reminders until you close this browser tab Turn these off Stops reminders see the note in Getting started getting started.md turn reminders off Select Change . The card becomes How often, and how long : 1. Remind me every : 20m , 35m , 45m or 60m . This changes the same setting as Reminder interval in Settings, and the card's sentence updates. 2. Rest for : 5s , 10s , 15s , 20s , 25s or 30s . 3. Select Rest now to start a rest with these timings, or Later or Turn these off below. This view also leaves by itself after 60 seconds. Note: The rest length you pick here applies until you"},{"t":"Eye rest reference","d":"Every eye-rest control, value, default and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/reference.html","h":["Settings panel (Comfort)","Reminder card","Timing view (after Change)","Rest screen","End screen","What each way of stopping does"],"x":" Control Values Default Eye rest reminders On, off Off Reminder interval 20m , 35m , 45m , 60m 20m Element Text or values Title Time to look away Sentence \"You have been at this for N minutes. S seconds looking into the distance is enough.\" Main actions Rest now , Later Quiet actions Change , Not this session , Turn these off Auto dismiss 60 seconds, shown by an emptying bar Element Values Default Title How often, and how long — Remind me every 20m , 35m , 45m , 60m Your Reminder interval Rest for 5s , 10s , 15s , 20s , 25s , 30s 30s resets on each page load Actions Rest now ; quiet Later , Turn these off — Auto dismiss 60 seconds — Element Text Heading Look past the screen Instruction \"Something about twenty feet away — a doorway, a window, the far wall. The screen will brighten when the rest is over.\" Countdown Seconds remaining Progress Horizon line shrinking to the centre still with reduced motion Button End early Element Text Kicker Rest complete Heading Welcome back Line \"Next reminder in N minutes.\" Duration About 2.6 seconds, then the page returns Action Effect Lasts Later Closes the card; next reminder after a full interval Until the next reminder End early Stops the rest;"},{"t":"Troubleshooting eye rest","d":"Fixes for common eye-rest problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["I switched reminders on but none appear","Reminders came back after I turned them off","The rest always lasts 30 seconds","The horizon line does not move","The screen went white at the end of a rest"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: The countdown restarts on every page load. If you move between pages often, a 20 minute reminder may never be reached. Stay on one page, or choose a shorter interval. You selected Not this session earlier in this tab. Open the site in a new tab. You selected Turn these off earlier. Switch Eye rest reminders off and on again in Settings › Comfort. A few pages do not include the eye rest reminder. Try another page. Why: Turn these off on the card does not change the switch in Settings. Changing any setting while that switch shows on brings the reminders back. What to do: switch off Eye rest reminders in Settings › Comfort. Why: the Rest for choice lasts only until you move to another page or reload. What to do: choose it again under Change on the card. Why: your device's reduced motion setting is on, so the line stays still. The countdown number still shows the time left, and the screen still brightens at the end. That is the end signal. It lasts about 2.6 seconds, then the page returns. "},{"t":"Eye rest FAQ","d":"Short answers about eye-rest reminders.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/docs/faq.html","h":["Why are reminders off by default?","Why twenty feet?","Does eye rest work when the tab is in the background?","Is eye rest the same as the screen saver?","Can I trigger a rest without waiting?"],"x":" They interrupt what you are doing, so the site leaves the choice to you. Looking into the distance gives your eyes a break from focusing close up. The reminder's wording follows the common \"20 20 20\" habit: every 20 minutes, look at something about 20 feet 6 metres away for about 20 seconds. The site's default interval is 20 minutes and its default rest is 30 seconds. The countdown keeps running, so the reminder can be waiting when you return. It is shown on the page, not as a system notification. No. Eye rest reminds you on a schedule while you work. The screen saver appears after you stop using the page for a while. See Screen saver ../../screen saver/README.md . Not directly. Choose the shortest interval, 20m , or wait for the next reminder. "},{"t":"Eye rest: supporting material","d":"Contents of the eye rest supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the eye rest guides limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What eye rest is and is not related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What eye rest stores Eye rest has no keyboard shortcut. Use Tab , Enter and Space on the card's buttons. "},{"t":"Eye rest glossary","d":"Terms used in the eye rest guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Reminder interval How long a page is open before a reminder appears: 20, 35, 45 or 60 minutes. Rest The few seconds 5 to 30 during which the screen dims and invites you to look away. Reminder card The small card that appears when the interval ends: \"Time to look away\". Horizon The line across the rest screen that shrinks to show how much of the rest is left. Dawn The brightening of the whole screen that marks the end of a rest. Session The life of a browser tab; Not this session lasts until the tab is closed. 20 20 20 A common screen habit: every 20 minutes, look about 20 feet away for about 20 seconds. "},{"t":"Eye rest limits and accuracy","d":"What eye rest does, what it does not do, and how precise its timings are.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" Not medical advice. Eye rest is a comfort reminder. It does not diagnose, treat or prevent any eye condition. If your eyes are uncomfortable, talk to an eye care professional. Per page. The countdown runs per page and restarts whenever a page loads. It does not track your total screen time, or time spent in other apps or other websites. Timings. Reminders appear after the chosen interval measured from the page load or the previous reminder. Browsers may delay timers in background tabs, so a reminder in a background tab can arrive a little late. Where it appears. Only on auricartisan.com, and only in the tab where the countdown ran. It is not a system notification. Rest length. The Rest for choice is not saved and returns to 30 seconds on the next page load. "},{"t":"Eye rest privacy","d":"What eye rest stores and sends.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your on or off choice and your interval are kept in this browser, as part of your settings. Turn these off is remembered in this browser too, and Not this session in this tab only. Eye rest does not record when you rest, how often you skip, or anything about your activity, and it sends nothing over the network. The cookie policy lists the eye rest preference under Functional storage. "},{"t":"Related to eye rest","d":"Features related to eye rest.","p":"Website › Site features › Eye rest","u":"website/site-features/eye-rest/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel › Comfort options ../../settings panel/docs/comfort options.md — the switch and the interval. Screen saver ../../screen saver/README.md — the idle screen shown when you stop using the page. Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — reading mode, reduced motion and other comfort settings. Theme ../../theme/README.md — a dark theme can be easier on the eyes in low light. "},{"t":"Feedback","d":"The occasional feedback prompt, the quick star rating, the six-question survey and bug reports, and how often the site asks.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan asks for feedback rarely and quietly. After you have spent twenty minutes of active time on a page, a small Feedback panel may appear: \"You have been here a little while — how is it going?\" You can give a star rating and a comment, open a six question survey, or report a bug with details of what happened. You can also put it off with Maybe later , or tell the site never to ask again with Don't ask again . Contact details are always optional. You can send any feedback anonymously, and adding your name or email is a separate, equal choice. The site does not ask on pages where a prompt would get in the way: signing in, checking out, paying, or reading legal pages. After any prompt, it waits at least a week before asking again on this device. To give feedback whenever you like, use the Feedback panel in the Feature Kit see Kits ../../kits/README.md . Anyone with something to say: praise, a complaint, a missing feature, or a bug. The automatic prompt, occasionally, after twenty minutes of active use. The Feature Kit's Feedback panel, at any time. 1. When the Feedback panel appears, select a number of stars or press 1 to 5 . 2. The question below changes to suit your ratin"},{"t":"Feedback guides","d":"Contents of the feedback guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md When the prompt appears, and how to answer, postpone or stop it rate survey and report.md rate survey and report.md The quick rating, the contact step, the survey and bug reports reference.md reference.md Every question, button, timing and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with feedback","d":"When the feedback prompt appears, and how to answer it, postpone it or stop it.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/getting-started.html","h":["When the prompt appears","Answer it","Put it off or stop it","Give feedback at any time"],"x":" The automatic prompt can appear when all of these are true: you have spent 20 minutes with the page visible in front of you time in a background tab does not count ; you are not on a sign in, checkout, payment or legal page; you have not been asked, and have not answered, in the last week or more on this device see the quiet periods below ; you have not chosen Don't ask again . The prompt is a small panel titled Feedback . It does not block the page. Select a star rating, optionally type a comment, and select Continue . Then choose Send anonymously or Add contact details . The full flow is in Rate, survey and report a bug rate survey and report.md . Choice What happens Maybe later Closes the panel; no automatic prompt for at least 7 days Close × or Esc Counts as dismissed; no automatic prompt for 14 days Don't ask again No automatic prompt ever again on this device Sending feedback No automatic prompt for 90 days Even if you close the page while the prompt is open, the site waits at least 7 days before asking again. The automatic prompt is not the only way. Open the Feature Kit Ctrl + Shift + K , or Feature in the page utilities bar and choose Feedback . See Kits ../../../kits/REA"},{"t":"Rate, survey and report a bug","d":"Give a quick rating, choose whether to be contacted, answer the survey, or report a bug.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/rate-survey-and-report.html","h":["Quick rating","Choose whether to be contacted","The survey","Report a bug","When you are offline"],"x":" The panel asks \"You have been here a little while — how is it going?\" or \"How is Auric Artisan working for you?\" . 1. Select one to five stars, or press 1 to 5 when you are not typing in the comment box . 2. The comment question changes with your rating: Stars Question Hint 1 What went wrong? We would like to fix it. The more specific, the better 2 What let you down? What would have made this work for you? 3 What would move this from fine to good? Optional 4 Anything that would have made it a five? Optional 5 What worked well? It helps us keep it that way. Optional Before you rate, it reads \"Anything you would like to add?\". 3. With one or two stars, the Report a bug button is highlighted and reads Something broke? , in case a bug report fits better. 4. Select Continue . It becomes available once you have chosen a rating or typed a comment. The next screen asks \"Would you like us to contact you about this feedback?\" and notes that contact information is completely optional. Send anonymously sends your rating and comment straight away, without asking again. Add contact details shows two optional fields: Name — optional \"How should we address you?\", up to 120 characters ; Email — op"},{"t":"Feedback reference","d":"Every feedback screen, button, timing and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/reference.html","h":["When the automatic prompt may appear","Quiet periods","Quick rating screen","Contact step","Survey","Bug report","Messages"],"x":" Condition Value Active time needed 20 minutes with the page visible Pages where it never appears Sign in, checkout, payment and legal pages Minimum gap between prompts 7 days on this device Outcome No automatic prompt for Prompt shown whatever happens next 7 days Maybe later 7 days Dismissed × or Esc 14 days Feedback, survey or report sent 90 days Don't ask again Ever, on this device Control Notes Stars 1 to 5 Also keys 1 to 5 Comment box Question and hint change with the rating Maybe later Postpone Don't ask again Stop automatic prompts Report a bug / Something broke? Opens the bug form Full survey Opens the survey Continue Goes to the contact step Control Notes Add contact details Shows Name and Email Send anonymously Sends without contact details Name — optional Up to 120 characters Email — optional Up to 254 characters; checked for a valid form Back / Send feedback Return, or send with details Six optional questions; Not now and Send answers ; counter \"N of 6 answered\". Field Required Notes What happened? Yes Enables Send report What did you expect instead? No — How can we reproduce it? No — How badly does it affect you? No Minor, Normal default , Blocking Attached automatical"},{"t":"Troubleshooting feedback","d":"Fixes for common feedback problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The prompt never appears","I chose Don't ask again by mistake","Continue is greyed out","Send report is greyed out","Pressing a number changed my rating","I was offline when I sent feedback"],"x":" Why: it needs 20 minutes of active time on one page, it does not appear on sign in, checkout, payment or legal pages, it waits at least a week between prompts, and it stops for good after Don't ask again . What to do: use the Feature Kit's Feedback panel whenever you want to give feedback. Why: the choice is kept in this browser. What to do: use the Feature Kit's Feedback panel, which is always available. Clearing the site's data in your browser also resets the choice. Why: it needs a star rating or a comment. Why: What happened? is required. Why: the keys 1 to 5 set the rating when the comment box does not have focus. What to do: click in the comment box before typing numbers. It is kept on your device and sent automatically when you are back online. "},{"t":"Feedback FAQ","d":"Short answers about giving feedback on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I have to give my name or email?","Will I get a reply?","Can I attach a screenshot or recording?","Why does the site wait so long before asking?","Does the prompt appear on every device?"],"x":" No. Send anonymously is always available and sends your feedback without contact details. Only if you add contact details and the team decides to follow up. A bug report is not a promise of a fix, but reports are reviewed. Not in the feedback panel. You can describe the problem, or contact the team through https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/. So that it asks people who have actually used the site, and does not interrupt short visits. The timing and your choices are kept per browser, so each browser counts separately. "},{"t":"Feedback: supporting material","d":"Contents of the feedback supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the feedback guides related.md related.md Related features and pages privacy.md privacy.md What feedback sends and stores Keys inside the panel: 1 to 5 set the star rating, and Esc closes the panel. "},{"t":"Feedback glossary","d":"Terms used in the feedback guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Automatic prompt The feedback panel the site shows by itself after 20 minutes of active use. Active time Time with the page visible on screen; time in a background tab does not count. Quiet period The time after a prompt during which the site does not ask again. Anonymous feedback Feedback sent without a name or email. Bug report A description of something that went wrong, sent with details of the page. Severity How badly a bug affects you: Minor, Normal or Blocking. Draft Text you have typed but not sent, kept on your device. "},{"t":"Feedback privacy","d":"What feedback sends to Auric Artisan and what it keeps on your device.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/others/privacy.html","h":["Sent when you submit","Kept on this device"],"x":" Rating and comment: your stars and what you typed, and the page you were on. Survey: your answers. Bug report: what you typed, the severity, and page details: the page address, window and screen size, browser and platform, language, theme, and recent page errors where available. Contact details: only if you choose Add contact details and fill them in. Nothing is sent until you select a send button. When you were last asked and how you answered to respect the quiet periods and Don't ask again . Unsent bug report drafts. Feedback waiting to be sent while you are offline. To remove these, clear the site's data in your browser. "},{"t":"Related to feedback","d":"Features and pages related to feedback.","p":"Website › Site features › Feedback","u":"website/site-features/feedback/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the Feature Kit's Feedback panel, available at any time. Contact page — https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ Help ../../../../help/README.md — support and contact across all products. Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md — record what happened before you describe it. "},{"t":"Guide and page outline","d":"The page guide opened with ?, its guided tours, and the section rail on long company, legal and trust pages.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The guide is a help panel for the page you are on. Press ? or select the question mark Guide button in the header and it opens by saying what the page is and what it is for. It offers a guided tour of the page, which highlights each important area in turn with a short explanation; a map of the tour's stops; quick links to other parts of the site; and recommended paths for common jobs, such as running an audit or finding a tool. The guide remembers how far you got in each page's tour, so you can pick up where you left off. Long company, pricing, legal and trust pages also have a section rail : a row of section links pinned under the header, labelled \"On this page\", which highlights the section you are reading and jumps to any other. A third outline, the Page outline button in the navigation dock, lists any page's headings; it is described in Navigation dock › Page outline ../navigation dock/docs/page outline.md . First time visitors who want to know what a page does. Anyone who prefers a short walkthrough to exploring alone. Readers of long policy and company pages who want to jump between sections. Press ? on any page when you are not typing in a field . Select Guide the question "},{"t":"Guide and page outline guides","d":"Contents of the guide and page outline documentation.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the guide, a tour of the panel, filtering and tabs guided tours.md guided tours.md Take, leave, resume, replay and skip through a tour section rail.md section rail.md The \"On this page\" rail on company, legal and trust pages reference.md reference.md Every section, control, key and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the guide","d":"Open the page guide, learn its sections, and filter it.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open and close the guide","The panel","Find something in the guide","What the tabs contain"],"x":" Open: press ? , select Guide in the header, tap Guide in the mobile drawer, or choose Open the page guide in Spotlight's commands. Close: press Esc , select the X Close guide or the ESC button beside the filter box, or click outside the panel. The guide opens only when you ask for it. It never opens by itself when you visit a page. While the guide is open, Tab stays inside it. From top to bottom: 1. What this page is. A kicker naming the kind of guide for example Home guide , Analyzer guide , Collections guide , Search guide , Workspace guide , Library guide , Tool guide , Company guide , Policy guide or Site guide , the page's title, and a one sentence summary. 2. Filter box. Type to narrow everything below. The placeholder reads \"Filter this guide…\". 3. Tabs. All , Tour , Tools , Pages , Learn and Help . Each shows only that kind of item. With a tab focused, Left and Right move between tabs. 4. Tour card. Starts, resumes or replays the guided tour of this page, with a progress bar see Guided tours guided tours.md . 5. On this page. The tour's stops for this page, numbered. A tick marks stops you have already seen. Select a stop to start the tour there. 6. Getting around. The sto"},{"t":"Guided tours","d":"Take a guided tour of any page, move through its stops, leave, resume, replay and skip.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/guided-tours.html","h":["Start a tour","The tour card","Move through a tour","The stops every page shares","When an eye rest appears"],"x":" A guided tour walks through the important areas of the page you are on. Each stop highlights one area and explains it in a small card beside it. 1. Press ? to open the guide. 2. The tour card at the top reads Take the guided tour , with the number of stops, for example \"11 stops · leave at any point\". 3. Select it its action reads Start the tour . To start at a particular stop, select that stop under On this page or Getting around . What it shows When Take the guided tour — \"N stops · leave at any point\" You have not taken this page's tour Pick up where you left off — \"You stopped at X of N · leave at any point\", action Resume at stop X You left this page's tour part way Replay the tour — \"N stops on this page · you have finished this one\" You finished this page's tour Start over from stop 1 below the card You left part way and want the whole tour again A progress bar on the card shows how much of the tour you have seen. Progress is kept for each page separately. If a page has nothing to tour, the guide says \"This page has no tourable sections yet, but the paths below will still help you move around.\" The highlighted area is outlined on the page, which scrolls to bring it into vie"},{"t":"The section rail","d":"Use the \"On this page\" section rail on long company, pricing, legal and trust pages.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/section-rail.html","h":["Where it appears","How it behaves","Other outlines"],"x":" Long pages about the company, pricing, policies and security have a section rail : a row of links to the page's sections, labelled \"On this page\", near the top of the page. Company pages: About, Pricing, Accessibility and FAQ. Every legal page, such as Privacy, Terms, Cookies, Refund Policy, Licenses, Security, Transparency, Acceptable Use Policy, Content & Intellectual Property, Data Retention & Deletion, Subscription & Billing and the Extension privacy policy. The Trust Center at https://auricartisan.com/security/. Pinned. As you scroll down, the rail sticks just below the site header, so it is always in reach. It gains a shadow once it is pinned. Shows where you are. The link for the section you are reading is highlighted. A section counts as \"current\" once its heading has passed a line a little below the rail. Jumps. Select a link to scroll to that section. On legal pages, whose sections can be folded, jumping to a folded section opens it. Narrow screens. The rail scrolls sideways, and keeps the current section's link in view. At the very end of the page, the last section is highlighted. The links are ordinary page links, so they also work with the keyboard Tab and Enter , and"},{"t":"Guide and page outline reference","d":"Every part, control, key and message of the guide, the tours and the section rail.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/reference.html","h":["Ways to open the guide","Guide panel","Guide kinds","Elsewhere links","Recommended paths","Keys in the guide panel","Tour card and controls","Section rail","Stored"],"x":" Method Notes ? Not while typing in a field, and not with Ctrl , Alt or Cmd held Header Guide button Tooltip: \"Search pages, tools, and quick paths, or start a guided tour. Shortcut: ?\" Drawer Guide tile \"Tours and shortcuts\" Spotlight Open the page guide \"What this page is, and its tour\" Part Content Head Kicker, page title, summary Filter box \"Filter this guide…\" Tabs All, Tour, Tools, Pages, Learn, Help Tour card Take the guided tour / Pick up where you left off / Replay the tour Start over Start over from stop 1 after leaving part way On this page Numbered stops for this page; tick when seen Getting around The site wide stops, with \"x/y seen\" Elsewhere Full Search, Analyze a website, Find the right tool, Open saved work, Read documentation, Learn color concepts, Install the PWA, Install the extension Recommended paths Run a quick audit, Build color assets, Check accessibility, Find a feature fast Close X Close guide , ESC button, click outside Home, Analyzer, Collections, Search, Workspace, Library, Tool, Company, Policy and Site guides, chosen from the page you are on. Link Goes to Full Search /search/ Analyze a website /tool/analyzer/ Find the right tool /collections/ Open sa"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the guide and section rail","d":"Fixes for common problems with the guide, tours and section rail.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Pressing ? does nothing","The tour highlights nothing, or the wrong place","The tour card says I finished, but I want to see it again","The tour starts in the middle","The section rail covers part of a heading after jumping","A legal section stayed folded"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: The cursor is in a text field. Click an empty part of the page first. A modifier key is held, or your keyboard layout needs Shift for ? that is fine but also another key such as Alt Gr which is not . Use the header's Guide button instead. The page is still loading. Wait a moment. A tour or the guide is already open. Why: a stop points at an area the page has not shown yet, for example one that loads late, is hidden on small screens or is folded away. What to do: select Next to move on, or widen the window and try again. Select Replay the tour . Why: you left part way through last time. The card offers Pick up where you left off . What to do: select Start over from stop 1 . Why: on some pages the header scrolls away during the jump, leaving the heading slightly lower than expected. What to do: scroll a little; the correct section stays highlighted. What to do: select its heading to open it. Jumping from the rail or a direct link normally opens it for you. "},{"t":"Guide and page outline FAQ","d":"Short answers about the guide, tours and section rail.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/docs/faq.html","h":["Will the guide pop up by itself?","Is the tour the same on every page?","Does finishing one page's tour mark others as finished?","What is the difference between the three outlines?","Is the guide available in Hindi?"],"x":" No. It opens only when you press ? or select a Guide button. No. Each kind of page home, analyzer, collections, search, workspace, library, tools, company and policy pages has its own stops, plus a few site wide stops shared by all. No. Progress is kept separately for each page. The guide explains the page and tours it. The section rail is the pinned row of section links on long company, legal and trust pages. The navigation dock's Page outline lists the headings of any page. Yes. When the site is in Hindi, the guide and its tours are shown in Hindi. "},{"t":"Guide and page outline: supporting material","d":"Contents of the guide and page outline supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in these guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keys for the guide and tours related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What the guide remembers "},{"t":"Guide and tour shortcuts","d":"Keys for the guide and guided tours.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Action ? Open the guide Esc Close the guide, or leave a tour Down / Up Move through the guide's items Home / End First or last item Enter Open the focused item, or the top filter match Left / Right on a tab Change tab Right during a tour Next stop Left during a tour Previous stop See Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md for the whole site. "},{"t":"Guide and page outline glossary","d":"Terms used in the guide and page outline guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Guide The help panel for the current page, opened with ? . Guided tour A step by step walk through a page's important areas. Stop One step of a tour, highlighting one area of the page. Site wide stops Tour stops about the header, search, library, theme and footer, the same on every page. Recommended path A short recipe in the guide for a common job. Section rail The pinned \"On this page\" row of section links on long company, legal and trust pages. Folded section A section of a legal page that shows only its heading until opened. "},{"t":"Guide privacy","d":"What the guide remembers.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The guide keeps, in this browser, whether you have opened it and how far you got in each page's tour. This is what lets it offer Pick up where you left off . Nothing about your use of the guide or tours is sent to Auric Artisan. The section rail stores nothing. "},{"t":"Related to the guide and outlines","d":"Features related to the guide and outlines.","p":"Website › Site features › Guide and page outline","u":"website/site-features/guide-and-page-outline/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md — the Page outline button. Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md — find any page; Open the page guide command. Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/README.md — the Guide button and drawer tile. Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md — the pages with the section rail. Getting started with Auric Artisan ../../../../getting started/README.md — a first tour of the whole site. "},{"t":"Header and navigation","d":"The site header, its menus and quick tools, the mobile drawer, the page utilities bar and the footer.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Every page on auricartisan.com opens with the same header. On a computer it shows the Auric Artisan name, three menus Company , Tools and Learn , a row of quick tools the app, the browser extension, the VS Code extensions, search, the guide, your library, language and theme and a Sign in button. On a phone or a narrow window, the menus and tools fold into a drawer that opens from the menu button, with every item labelled. Two more pieces of navigation float over every page. The page utilities bar sits at the bottom left: one button that opens a row of launchers for the kits, the navigation dock and Settings. The navigation dock is a slim rail on the left or right edge with Back, Forward, Reload and scrolling controls; it has its own guide in Navigation dock ../navigation dock/README.md . At the bottom of every page, the footer gathers product links, policies, trust pages, contact details and social links. Everyone who visits the site. The header is the quickest way to find a tool, the documentation or your saved work, and to switch theme or language. The header is at the top of every page. It stays pinned to the top as you scroll except in reading mode . The page utilities bar but"},{"t":"Header and navigation guides","d":"Contents of the header and navigation guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain the header on large and small screens, the page utilities bar, and the footer. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Find your way around the header and footer on any page desktop header.md desktop header.md The Company, Tools and Learn menus and the quick tools row mobile drawer.md mobile drawer.md The drawer on phones and narrow windows, with tool chips and preferences page utilities bar.md page utilities bar.md The launcher bar at the bottom left for kits, navigation and Settings footer.md footer.md Every section and link of the footer reference.md reference.md Every menu item, button and link, with its destination troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the header and navigation","d":"Find your way around the header, the page utilities bar and the footer on any page.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/getting-started.html","h":["A tour of the page frame","Open a tool from the header","Open a tool on a phone","Get back to where you were","Find something without the menus"],"x":" Every page has the same frame around its content: 1. Header top . The Auric Artisan name on the left returns you to the homepage. The rest depends on the width of your window: 960 pixels wide or more: the Company , Tools and Learn menus, the quick tools icons and Sign in . Narrower than 960 pixels: a Search button and the three line menu button, which opens the drawer. 2. Info bars below the header, homepage by default . Optional strips such as the announcements bar and the clock strip. See Info bars and notices ../../info bars and notices/README.md . 3. Page content. 4. Floating controls. The page utilities button at the bottom left, and the navigation dock on the left or right edge. 5. Footer bottom . 1. Select Tools in the header. 2. The menu lists All Tools under Overview , then the tools under group headings: Core tools , Creative utilities , Colour science , Gamut & rendering , Perception , Spectral and Utilities . 3. Scroll the menu if needed. While there is more below, a SCROLL DOWN hint shows at its foot. 4. Select a tool. Result: the tool page opens. The menu closes by itself. 1. Tap the three line button at the top right. The drawer opens. 2. Under Browse , tap Tools . "},{"t":"The desktop header","d":"Use the Company, Tools and Learn menus and the quick-tools icons in the header on wide screens.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/desktop-header.html","h":["The brand","The three menus","The quick-tools row","Sign in","When the header scrolls"],"x":" On windows 960 pixels wide or more, the header shows everything in one row: the brand, three menus, the quick tools icons and Sign in . Auric Artisan with the tagline Colour intelligence studio . Select it to return to the homepage. Select Company , Tools or Learn to open a menu below it. Each entry has a picture or icon, a name and a one line description. Only one menu is open at a time. Menu Groups Entries Company Company About, Timeline, Pricing, Accessibility, FAQ, Contact Tools Overview All Tools Core tools Portfolio Builder, Portfolio Index, Analyze URLs, Vision Simulation, Design System Generator, Color Science Lab, Basic Tools, Personalization Generator Creative utilities Image Picker, Font Library, Icon Library, Generate ASCII Art, Generate Ishihara Plates Colour science Illuminants, Chromatic Adaptation, Gamut Mapping Gamut & rendering Gamut Explorer, HDR Gamut Plot, Tonal Steps, Tints & Shades, Tone Mapping Perception Perception & Vision, Neuroscience, Psychophysics Engine Spectral Material Lighting, Industrial Dye Chemistry Utilities LUT Lab, ICC Parser, Collage Maker, M Gradient Palette, SVG Recolor Learn Learn Learning Hub, Accessibility Compliance, Blog, Documentati"},{"t":"The footer","d":"Every section and link of the footer at the bottom of each page.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/footer.html","h":["Introduction","Directory","Bottom row","Closing note","Where the links go"],"x":" The footer closes every page. It has four parts. The Auric Artisan logo links to the homepage and the statement \"Color intelligence. Crafted for everyone.\" The Start a conversation card: \"Questions, collaborations, or support?\" with an Email our studio link to hello@auricartisan.com , and Explore our portfolio, LEACB , which opens the studio's portfolio site in a new tab. Right click the Start a conversation card for a small menu: Email us , Copy email , Copy link and LEACB . See Other right click menus ../../context menu/docs/other right click menus.md footer contact card . Under the heading \"Tools, policies, and useful links\", four numbered columns: Column Links 01 Product Tools, Learn, Blog, Portfolios, API, Search Console, Download 02 Explore Privacy, Terms, Cookies, Refund Policy, License 03 Policies Acceptable Use Policy, Content & Intellectual Property, Data Retention & Deletion, Transparency, Subscription & Billing 04 Trust Trust Center, Security, Accessibility, Contact The copyright line and \"Design and development by Auric Artisan\", with the company's registered address. Social links, each opening in a new tab: Product Hunt, LinkedIn, GitHub and X. Made with care · Built"},{"t":"The mobile drawer","d":"Use the navigation drawer on phones, tablets and narrow windows, including tool chips, theme and language switches.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/mobile-drawer.html","h":["The bar","Open and close the drawer","What is in the drawer","With the keyboard"],"x":" When the window is narrower than 960 pixels, for example on a phone, a tablet in portrait, or a narrow desktop window, the header menus and quick tools move into a drawer . The drawer is the same content as the desktop header, with every item labelled in words. The header bar on a narrow screen holds: the Auric Artisan name to the homepage ; a Search button. On screens 600 pixels wide or more it also shows the word \"Search\" and a Ctrl K hint; on phones it is an icon; your account button, once you are signed in; the menu button three lines . Its label is Open navigation , and Close navigation while the drawer is open, when it shows an X. 1. Tap the menu button. The drawer opens: on phones, as a full width sheet from under the bar to the bottom of the screen; on screens from 600 to 959 pixels wide, as a sheet 400 pixels wide on the right. 2. While it is open, the page behind it does not scroll, and the floating buttons are hidden. 3. To close it, tap the menu button again, tap the dimmed page outside the drawer, press Esc , or open any link in it. It also closes if you widen the window past 960 pixels or go back or forward in your history. From top to bottom: Search tools, colours a"},{"t":"The page utilities bar","d":"Open the launcher bar at the bottom-left of every page to reach the kits, the navigation dock and Settings.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/page-utilities-bar.html","h":["Open and close the bar","On a phone","Things to know"],"x":" The page utilities bar is a single round button at the bottom left corner of every page. Select it to open a bar of labelled launchers: Launcher Opens Feature The Feature Kit Menu The Menu Kit Advanced The Advanced Kit Status The Status Kit Library The Library Kit Navigate The navigation dock Back, Forward, Reload, outline, split view and more Settings The Settings panel The kits are documented in Kits ../../../kits/README.md , which also covers this bar in more depth. The dock is documented in Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md , and the panel in Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md . 1. Select the button at the bottom left. Its tooltip reads Page utilities : \"Show navigation, settings, and the Feature, Menu, Advanced, Status and Library kits.\" 2. The bar opens along the bottom of the window. The first button now reads Close Hide page utilities . 3. Select a launcher. The bar closes and that kit or panel opens. To close the bar without choosing, select Close , press Esc , or click anywhere else on the page. Closing the bar does not close a kit you already opened; an open kit's launcher stays visible so you can close the kit from it. On screens up to about 58"},{"t":"Header and navigation reference","d":"Every header menu entry, quick tool, drawer control and utilities-bar launcher, with its destination.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/reference.html","h":["Header menus","Quick tools (wide screens)","Mobile drawer (narrow screens)","Page utilities bar"],"x":" Addresses are relative to https://auricartisan.com. Menu Group Entry Description shown Address Company Company About Our Story & Mission /company/about/ Company Company Timeline Milestones & evolution /company/timeline/ Company Company Pricing Plans for every workflow /company/pricing/ Company Company Accessibility Inclusive by design /company/accessibility/ Company Company FAQ Frequently Asked Questions /company/faq/ Company Company Contact Support & partnerships /company/contact/ Tools Overview All Tools Explore every color utility /collections/ Tools Core tools Portfolio Builder Publish your work /portfolio/ Tools Core tools Portfolio Index Find people by craft and colour /portfolios/ Tools Core tools Analyze URLs Accessibility /tool/analyzer/ Tools Core tools Vision Simulation Accessibility /tool/vision simulation/ Tools Core tools Design System Generator Design Systems /tool/design engine/ Tools Core tools Color Science Lab Color Science /tool/color science lab/ Tools Core tools Basic Tools Generators /tool/basic tools/ Tools Core tools Personalization Generator Generators /tool/personalization gen/ Tools Creative utilities Image Picker Utilities /tool/general/tools/image pic"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the header and navigation","d":"Fixes for common problems with the header, the drawer, the page utilities bar and the footer.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The header shows a menu button instead of Company, Tools and Learn","A header menu closed before I could click an entry","I cannot see the bottom of a long menu","The page does not scroll while the drawer is open","The floating buttons disappeared","The theme buttons in the drawer do not match what I see","The Library button does nothing"],"x":" Why: your window is narrower than 960 pixels, or your browser is zoomed in far enough to make the page that narrow. What to do: use the drawer, or widen the window or zoom out Ctrl + to see the full header. Why: menus close when keyboard focus or a click moves outside them. What to do: open the menu again and select the entry directly. On a touch screen, use the drawer, whose sections stay open until you close them. Why: tall menus scroll inside themselves. What to do: scroll inside the menu. The SCROLL DOWN hint shows while more entries are below. Why: this is intended, so that swiping inside the drawer does not move the page behind it. What to do: close the drawer with the menu button, Esc , or a tap on the dimmed area. Why: the page utilities button and other floating buttons are hidden while the mobile drawer, the screen saver or an eye rest is showing. What to do: close the drawer, move the mouse or press a key to leave the screen saver, or finish or end the eye rest. Why: the drawer shows the stored choice: Auto follows your device, so a dark page can show Auto selected. What to do: select Light or Dark to fix the theme regardless of your device. Why: the library panel loads"},{"t":"Header and navigation FAQ","d":"Short answers about the header, drawer, page utilities bar and footer.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/docs/faq.html","h":["Is there a page that lists every tool?","Do the menus open when I hover over them?","Can I hide the page utilities bar?","Where is the navigation dock on my phone?","What does the flag in the footer do?","How do I contact Auric Artisan?"],"x":" Yes. All Tools at the top of the Tools menu opens https://auricartisan.com/collections/, which shows every tool with filters. No. They open when you click or tap their button, or press Enter , Space or Down on it, and they stay open until you choose an entry or move away. The bar collapses to a single button when you close it, and that button cannot be removed. Reading mode hides the kit launchers. On phones the dock has no button of its own. Open the page utilities bar and select Navigate . Double click it to play a short celebration animation. It does nothing else. Use Email our studio in the footer hello@auricartisan.com , or the Contact page in the Company menu. "},{"t":"Header and navigation: supporting material","d":"Contents of the header and navigation supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Terms, shortcuts, related features and privacy notes for the header, drawer, page utilities bar and footer. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in these guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts for the header and its tools related.md related.md Related features and sections privacy.md privacy.md What the header and drawer remember "},{"t":"Header and navigation shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts for the header menus, the drawer and the tools the header opens.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Menus and drawer","Tools the header opens"],"x":" Keys Action Enter / Space on a menu button Open or close the menu Down / Up on a menu button Open the menu at its first or last entry Down / Up in a menu Next or previous entry Home / End in a menu First or last entry Esc Close the open menu, or else the drawer Keys Opens Ctrl + K Cmd + K on a Mac Spotlight search ? The page guide Ctrl + Shift + L The Library Kit Alt + T Switch theme Light, Dark, System Ctrl + , The Settings panel Esc Close the page utilities bar See Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md for the full list. "},{"t":"Header and navigation glossary","d":"Terms used in the header and navigation guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Header The strip at the top of every page with the brand, menus, quick tools and sign in. Menu header The Company, Tools or Learn list that opens below its button. Quick tools The row of icon buttons in the header: app, extension, VS Code, search, guide, library, language, theme. Drawer The sliding sheet that holds the header's contents on narrow screens. Breakpoint A window width at which the layout changes. The header's is 960 pixels. Group chip A button in the drawer's Tools section that shows one group of tools at a time. Page utilities bar The launcher bar at the bottom left for the kits, the navigation dock and Settings. Kit A floating panel of extra tools, such as the Feature Kit or Library Kit. Navigation dock The slim floating rail with Back, Forward, Reload, outline and scroll controls. Footer The section at the end of every page with directory links, contact details and social links. PWA Progressive web app: a website you can install and run like an app, with offline support. "},{"t":"Header and navigation privacy","d":"What the header, drawer and page utilities bar remember, and what they send.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The header's menus and the drawer do not store anything themselves. The Theme and Language switches in the header and drawer store your choice in this browser, the same way the Settings panel does. The header checks whether you are signed in, so it can show your account menu instead of Sign in . For visitors who are not signed in, no account request is made. The page utilities bar does not store whether it was open. The footer's social links open other websites Product Hunt, LinkedIn, GitHub, X in a new tab only when you select them. Explore our portfolio, LEACB opens the studio's own portfolio site. "},{"t":"Related to the header and navigation","d":"Features and sections related to the header and navigation.","p":"Website › Site features › Header and navigation","u":"website/site-features/header-and-navigation/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md — the floating Back, Forward and scroll controls. Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md — what the Search button opens. Guide and page outline ../../guide and page outline/README.md — what the Guide button opens. Theme ../../theme/README.md and Language ../../language/README.md — the two switches in the header and drawer. Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — opened from the page utilities bar. Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the kits launched from the page utilities bar, including the Library Kit. Download and offline ../../../download and offline/README.md — where Browser PWA and The app lead. Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md — where Browser Extension leads. VS Code extensions ../../../../vscode extensions/README.md — where VS Code Extensions leads. Account and billing ../../../account and billing/README.md — signing in and the account menu. Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md — the Company menu and the footer's policy links. "},{"t":"Info bars and notices","d":"The welcome, announcement and quick-links bars, the clock strip, hero notice, demo chips, the first-visit welcome and the site's status messages.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Around the content of a page, the site can show a few slim strips and small notices: the welcome bar , which cycles through short introductions to the platform; the announcement bar , with the latest news, such as roadmap updates and offline support; the quick links bar , a scrolling row of cards for Documentation, Changelog, Timeline, Blog and Learn; the clock strip , a live clock with the date and your time zone; the hero notice on the homepage, and demo chips that mark live or demo sections. By default the three bars appear on the homepage only, and the clock strip is off, so ordinary pages start with their own content. Every bar and notice has a ✕ to hide it, and the Settings panel's Highlights section switches each one on or off, for the homepage or for every page. The site also shows short status messages : a brief welcome animation on your first visit, \"Offline mode\" and \"Back online\" when your connection changes, and prompts when the installed app has an update. Everyone. Keep the bars if you like to see news and shortcuts; hide them for a quieter page. The bars and the clock strip appear under the header. Their switches are in Settings Ctrl + , › Highlights . Right click "},{"t":"Info bars and notices guides","d":"Contents of the info bars and notices guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md What appears where, and how to show or hide it info bars.md info bars.md The welcome, announcement and quick links bars and their menu clock strip.md clock strip.md The live clock strip and its Clock settings menu notices and messages.md notices and messages.md Hero notice, demo chips, first visit welcome, loading screen and status messages reference.md reference.md Every bar, switch, default and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with info bars and notices","d":"What bars and notices appear where, and how to show or hide each one.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/getting-started.html","h":["What appears by default","Hide something","Show something again, or everywhere","Changes apply everywhere at once","In reading mode and the screen saver"],"x":" Item Default Welcome bar Homepage only Announcement bar Homepage only Quick links bar Homepage only also at the foot of the Collections page Clock strip Off Hero notice On homepage Demo chips On where a page has them On every page, the announcement bar sits directly under the header, followed by the clock strip, then the page content. Select the ✕ at the end of a bar, on the hero notice, or on a demo chip. It disappears at once, and the matching switch in Settings › Highlights turns off. A demo chip's ✕ hides every demo chip on the site. 1. Press Ctrl + , and select Highlights . 2. Switch on the item you want. For the three bars, switching on shows the bar on every page. To return to the homepage only default, select Restore section defaults . Details are in Settings panel › Highlights and clock ../../settings panel/docs/highlights and clock.md . A change made with a ✕ or in Settings applies straight away to every page, including pages already open in other tabs. The bars and the clock strip are hidden in reading mode and while the screen saver is showing. "},{"t":"The clock strip","d":"Show a live clock under the header and set its format, date, weekday, zone label and time zone from its own menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/clock-strip.html","h":["Turn it on","What it shows","The Clock settings menu","How it relates to Settings › Clock","Turn it off"],"x":" The clock strip is a live clock under the header. It is off by default . 1. Press Ctrl + , and select Highlights . 2. Switch on Clock strip \"Off by default. Turn this on for a live clock, date and timezone above every page.\" . It appears under the header and under the announcement bar, if shown on every page. The flag of your time zone's country, or a globe for other zones. The zone's name, for example \"India Standard Time\" it reads Local time for a moment while the clock starts . \" default \" is added when the site could not match your zone and used a close one. The time, ticking every second, for example 10:42:07 AM . The date, the weekday, and the zone's abbreviation with its offset from UTC, for example \"EDT · UTC 4\" for New York in summer. Where the browser has no abbreviation for a zone, the offset is shown in both places. Screen readers can read the time on demand; it is not announced every second. Right click anywhere on the clock strip to open Clock settings : Part Options Preview The clock and date as they will look Format 12h , 24h Date Long , D/M/Y , M/D/Y , ISO Show Seconds , Weekday , Zone each on or off Time zone A search box \"Search time zone…\" and a list: Auto dete"},{"t":"The info bars","d":"Use the welcome, announcement and quick-links bars, pause them, open their links and hide them.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/info-bars.html","h":["The welcome bar","The announcement bar","The quick-links bar","Pausing and motion","Hide a bar","The bar's right-click menu"],"x":" A single line bar that shows one message at a time and cross fades to the next every six seconds. Its seven messages introduce the platform: colour science, colour space tooling, accessibility, vision simulation, palettes, research tools such as Ishihara plates, and what comes next. Each message links to the welcome article on the blog. Hover a message for a short tooltip. Also one message at a time, every six seconds. It carries the latest platform news, for example: \"New library updates and workflow improvements are in progress — read the roadmap.\" to the roadmap article \"Every tool works offline — install Auric Artisan as an app from the Download page.\" to the Download page \"Early access: accounts, pricing, and sync are rolling out in stages.\" to the roadmap article Highlighted messages are featured news. A row of cards that scrolls continuously across the page: Card Subtitle Goes to Documentation Guides & API reference /library/documentation/ Changelog What's new lately /library/changelog/ Timeline Milestones & history /company/timeline/ Blog Posts & site news /library/blog/ Learn Tutorials & resources /library/learn/ Point at the welcome or announcement bar to pause it on the"},{"t":"Notices and status messages","d":"The hero notice, demo chips, first-visit welcome, loading screen, and the short status messages the site shows.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/notices-and-messages.html","h":["Hero notice","Demo chips","First-visit welcome","Loading screen","Connection messages","App messages","Confirmation messages","Notifications"],"x":" A highlighted notice banner in the homepage's opening section. Select its ✕ Dismiss re enable in Settings → Comfort to hide it. Switch it back on with Hero notice in Settings › Highlights . Small labels with an information mark that sit above sections showing a live demo, marking them as \"live\" or \"demo\" content. Select the ✕ on any chip Hide demo chips re enable in Settings → Highlights to hide every demo chip on the site. Switch them back on with Live demo chips in Settings › Highlights. The first time you open the site in a browser, a short animated welcome plays over the page for about a second shorter if your device asks for reduced motion . Click it, or press Esc , Enter or Space , to skip it. It plays only once per browser. The cookie consent bar appears after it. While a page is loading, a brief screen with the Auric Artisan logo and the line \"Preparing local color tools.\" may show, with a progress bar. It disappears when the page is ready. A small message appears at the edge of the screen when your connection changes: Message Meaning Offline mode Your device has lost its connection. The message stays while you are offline. Saved pages and tools keep working. Back online T"},{"t":"Info bars and notices reference","d":"Every bar, notice, switch, default, timing and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/reference.html","h":["Items and switches","Bar behaviour","Bar menu (right-click)","Clock settings menu (right-click the clock strip)","First-visit welcome","Status messages"],"x":" Item Settings › Highlights switch Default Hide from the page Welcome bar Welcome bar Homepage only ✕ or right click › Hide bar Announcement bar Announcement bar Homepage only ✕ or right click › Hide bar Quick links bar Quick links bar Homepage only; also Collections ✕ or right click › Hide bar Clock strip Clock strip Off Switch off in Settings Hero notice Hero notice On ✕ Demo chips Live demo chips On ✕ on any chip hides all Behaviour Value Message rotation welcome, announcement Every 6 seconds, cross fade Pause While the pointer is over the bar, and while the tab is hidden Reduced motion Messages swap without fading Quick links bar Continuous scrolling row of cards Order under the header Announcement bar, then clock strip, then page content Heading Buttons Welcome messages / Site announcements / Site tools Open , Copy link , Hide bar , Settings Control Options Default Format 12h, 24h 12h Date Long, D/M/Y, M/D/Y, ISO Long Show › Seconds On, off On Show › Weekday On, off On Show › Zone On, off On Time zone Auto detect, or any zone Auto detect Reset Restores all of the above — All settings → Opens Settings › Clock — Item Value Shown Once per browser Length About 1.1 seconds; about 0"},{"t":"Troubleshooting info bars and notices","d":"Fixes for common problems with the info bars, clock strip and notices.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["A bar I hid is back","A bar now shows on every page, not just the homepage","The ✕ tooltip says Comfort, but I cannot find the switch there","The clock shows the wrong time zone","The clock strip is missing","\"Offline mode\" will not go away"],"x":" Why: someone switched it on in Settings › Highlights, or you restored the section's defaults, which brings the bars back on the homepage. What to do: select its ✕ again. Why: switching a bar on in Settings shows it everywhere. What to do: select Restore section defaults in Settings › Highlights to go back to homepage only. Why: the switches are in the Highlights section of Settings, not Comfort. Why: a fixed zone was chosen in the clock menu or in Settings › Clock, or your device reports a zone the site could not match exactly the label then shows \" default \" . What to do: right click the strip and choose Auto detect , or pick your zone from the list. Why: it is off by default, and it is hidden in reading mode. What to do: switch on Clock strip in Settings › Highlights. Why: your device reports that it has no connection. The message stays until the connection returns. What to do: check your connection. Saved pages keep working meanwhile. "},{"t":"Info bars and notices FAQ","d":"Short answers about the info bars, clock strip and notices.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/docs/faq.html","h":["Why are the bars only on the homepage?","Can I see the first-visit welcome again?","Does the site send notifications?","Can I show a world clock for another city?","Does the clock strip use my Settings clock choices?"],"x":" They are an introduction. On other pages they would push the content down, so by default they stay on the homepage. You can show them everywhere from Settings › Highlights. It plays once per browser. It plays again only if you clear the site's data in your browser. No. All messages appear on the page itself. Yes. Right click the clock strip and choose that city's time zone. The strip shows one zone at a time. Yes. The strip and Settings › Clock share 24 hour time, seconds, date format and time zone. "},{"t":"Info bars and notices: supporting material","d":"Contents of the info bars and notices supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in these guides related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What is stored There are no keyboard shortcuts for the bars. The clock strip's menu opens with a right click; the Settings panel opens with Ctrl + , . "},{"t":"Info bars and notices glossary","d":"Terms used in the info bars and notices guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Info bar A slim strip under the header: welcome, announcement or quick links. Clock strip A live clock under the header with the date and time zone. Hero notice A highlighted banner in the homepage's opening section. Demo chip A small label marking a live or demo section. Time zone A region's standard time, such as Asia/Kolkata or Europe/London. UTC offset How far a time zone is ahead of or behind Coordinated Universal Time. ISO date A date written year month day, for example 2026 09 24. Status message A short message at the edge of the screen about the connection or the app. "},{"t":"Info bars and notices privacy","d":"What the info bars, clock strip and notices store.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Which bars and notices you show or hide, and your clock choices, are kept in this browser as part of your settings. The first visit welcome remembers that it has played, in this browser. The clock uses your device's time and time zone. Nothing about them is sent to Auric Artisan. Nothing is recorded when you open, copy or hide a bar. "},{"t":"Related to info bars and notices","d":"Features related to the info bars and notices.","p":"Website › Site features › Info bars and notices","u":"website/site-features/info-bars-and-notices/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel › Highlights and clock ../../settings panel/docs/highlights and clock.md — every switch and clock setting. Cookie consent and privacy ../../cookie consent and privacy/README.md — the consent bar shown after the first visit welcome. Download and offline ../../../download and offline/README.md — the app and offline messages. Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the Update Kit's update notices. Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — reading mode, which hides the bars. "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","d":"The master list of keyboard shortcuts for the whole Auric Artisan website.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","The ten most useful","In this folder"],"x":" Almost everything on auricartisan.com can be reached from the keyboard. This section gathers every site wide shortcut in one place: search, settings, the guide, reading mode, theme, text size, split view, the recorder, the kits and the right click menu, followed by the keys that work inside each panel. On a Mac, use Cmd where this list says Ctrl for the shortcuts marked \"Ctrl or Cmd\". Shortcuts that use Alt use the Option key on a Mac. Letter shortcuts are ignored while you are typing in a text field, so they never interfere with what you type. Keyboard users, power users, and anyone who wants to move faster around the site. The full list: docs/reference.md docs/reference.md . Inside the site: Settings Ctrl + , › Shortcuts lists the Settings panel's own shortcuts, and right click › Site › Keyboard shortcuts opens it. 1. Press Ctrl + K and search for anything. 2. Press Ctrl + , to open Settings. 3. Press ? for the page guide. 4. Press Alt + R for reading mode, and again to leave it. 5. Press Ctrl + Shift + D for split view, and Esc to close it. Keys Action Ctrl + K Search the site Spotlight Ctrl + , Settings ? Page guide and tour Alt + R Reading mode Alt + T Switch theme Alt + + / "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts documentation","d":"Contents of the keyboard shortcuts documentation.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers reference.md reference.md The master list: site wide shortcuts, kit shortcuts, and keys inside each panel troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Why a shortcut might not work, and what to do "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcut reference","d":"Every keyboard shortcut on the Auric Artisan website, grouped by where it works.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/docs/reference.html","h":["Anywhere on the site","Kits","Header menus and drawer","Spotlight","Settings panel","Right-click menu","Guide and tours","Split view","Screen recorder","Other places"],"x":" \"Ctrl or Cmd\" means Ctrl on Windows, Linux and ChromeOS, and Cmd on a Mac. On a Mac, Alt is the Option key. Keys Action Notes Ctrl + K Ctrl or Cmd Open or close Spotlight search Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md Ctrl + , Ctrl or Cmd Open or close Settings Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md ? Open the page guide Guide and page outline ../../guide and page outline/README.md Alt + R Reading mode on or off Not while typing Alt + T Theme: Light, Dark, System Not while typing Alt + + or Alt + = Text one size larger Not while typing Alt + Text one size smaller Not while typing Alt + 0 Default text size Not while typing Alt + M Reduced motion on or off Not while typing Ctrl + Shift + D Open or close split view Split view ../../split view/README.md Alt + click a site link Open split view with that page — Alt + Shift + R Open the recorder; while recording, stop and save Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md Alt + Shift + P Pause or resume a recording — Ctrl + Shift + U Check for and apply a website update Kits ../../../kits/README.md Update Kit Ctrl + Shift + C Open the colour tools menu with a selected hex code, if any Uses Shift , so it is not "},{"t":"Troubleshooting keyboard shortcuts","d":"Why a site shortcut might not work, and what to do.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["A shortcut does nothing","The browser did something else instead","? does not open the guide","Alt shortcuts open the browser's menu bar","Alt + + does not enlarge text"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: You are typing in a field. Alt letter shortcuts and ? are ignored in text fields. Click an empty part of the page, or press Esc to leave the field, then try again. The page is still loading. Most panels load a moment after the page. Wait, then try again. The feature is not on this page. A few simple pages for example sign in pages do not load every panel. Another panel has focus. Some panels use keys for themselves while open; close the panel first. Why: browsers and operating systems reserve some combinations. For example, Ctrl + Shift + D can bookmark all tabs, Ctrl + Shift + A can search tabs, and Cmd + M minimises a window on a Mac. The site claims its shortcuts where the browser allows it, but some browsers keep certain combinations for themselves. What to do: use the on screen control instead the navigation dock for split view, the page utilities bar for kits and Settings . Why: on some keyboard layouts, ? needs a modifier the site does not accept, such as Alt Gr . What to do: use the Guide button in the header. Why: in some browsers on Windows, pressing and releasing Alt alone moves focus to the menu bar. What to do: hold Alt while pressing the se"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts: supporting material","d":"Contents of the keyboard shortcuts supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers related.md related.md Where each group of shortcuts is explained in detail Shortcuts need no settings and store nothing, so there is no separate privacy page. "},{"t":"Related to keyboard shortcuts","d":"Where each group of keyboard shortcuts is explained in detail.","p":"Website › Site features › Keyboard shortcuts","u":"website/site-features/keyboard-shortcuts/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel › Shortcuts ../../settings panel/others/shortcuts.md Context menu › Shortcuts ../../context menu/others/shortcuts.md Search and Spotlight › Shortcuts ../../search and spotlight/others/shortcuts.md Split view › Shortcuts ../../split view/others/shortcuts.md Screen recorder › Shortcuts ../../screen recorder/others/shortcuts.md Guide and page outline › Shortcuts ../../guide and page outline/others/shortcuts.md Header and navigation › Shortcuts ../../header and navigation/others/shortcuts.md Theme › Shortcuts ../../theme/others/shortcuts.md Accessibility aids › Keyboard and screen readers ../../accessibility aids/docs/keyboard and screen readers.md Kits ../../../kits/README.md — each kit's own keys. "},{"t":"Language","d":"Switch Auric Artisan between English and Hindi, and learn what is and is not translated.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan is available in English and Hindi हिन्दी . English is the default. When you switch to Hindi, the page you are on is translated in place, without a reload, and every page you open afterwards appears in Hindi too, until you switch back. The translation covers the site's interface and its pages: menus, buttons, labels, tooltips, messages, settings, kits and the text of articles and tool pages. The site's own brand and product names are written in Devanagari for example ऑरिक आर्टिज़न for Auric Artisan , while names of other companies and products, code, hex values and keyboard keys stay as they are. Hindi text uses Devanagari fonts chosen for each platform, with slightly taller line spacing for comfortable reading. Switching back to English reloads the page in English. Hindi readers, and anyone who prefers to use the site in Hindi. The language choice also sets how dates and times are written Indian Hindi conventions . The globe button in the header tooltip Language / भाषा . It switches between the two languages. Settings › Appearance › Language : English or हिन्दी . The mobile drawer › Preferences › Language . Spotlight: press Ctrl + K , type , and choose Switch languag"},{"t":"Language guides","d":"Contents of the language guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Switch between English and Hindi, and share a Hindi link what is translated.md what is translated.md What changes in Hindi and what stays in English reference.md reference.md Every language control and its behaviour troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with languages","d":"Switch the site between English and Hindi, and share a link that opens in Hindi.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Switch to Hindi","Switch back to English","Share a link that opens in Hindi","Language buttons are always readable"],"x":" Use any one of these: Header: select the globe button. Its tooltip reads Language / भाषा with the description in both languages. Settings: press Ctrl + , , and under Appearance › Language भाषा — interface and articles select हिन्दी . Drawer narrow screens : open the menu, and under Preferences › Language tap हिन्दी . Spotlight: press Ctrl + K , type , and choose Switch language English ⇄ हिन्दी . What happens: 1. The site downloads the Hindi text for the page you are on. On a first switch this can take a moment on a slow connection. 2. The page is translated where it stands. You stay at the same place on the page and nothing you typed is lost. 3. Text that appears later, such as a kit you open or a tool's results, is translated as it appears. 4. Every page you open afterwards loads in Hindi. Use the same controls: the globe, English in Settings or the drawer, or Switch language in Spotlight. The page reloads in English. Translation changes the page's text in place, so a reload is how the site returns to the original English. If you were typing into a form, finish or copy your text first. Add ?lang=hi to the end of any page address, for example: text https://auricartisan.com/tool/v"},{"t":"What is translated","d":"What changes when the site is in Hindi, and what deliberately stays in English or Latin script.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/what-is-translated.html","h":["Translated into Hindi","Written in Devanagari rather than translated","Kept as they are","Not covered by this switch"],"x":" Site chrome: the header, drawer, footer, info bars, cookie notice, navigation dock and page utilities bar. Panels: the Settings panel, the kits, Spotlight, the guide and tours, the right click menu and the eye rest reminder. Page content: the text of company and legal pages, tool pages, Learn articles, documentation, blog posts and library pages. Hidden text: tooltips, placeholders in empty fields, image descriptions and the labels read out by screen readers. Messages built from live values, such as labels that include a colour code or a count, for the common kinds of message. The logo: the Auric Artisan wordmark is shown in Devanagari. Promotional images with text in them are swapped for Hindi versions where one exists. Dates and times are written the Hindi India way, for example on the clock strip. Pages that open without the rest of the site around them, such as sign in, checkout, the offline page and the \"page not found\" page, are translated too. The site's own brand and product names are transliterated, not translated: Auric Artisan becomes ऑरिक आर्टिज़न, and names such as Auric Icons and the kit names फ़ीचर किट, मेन्यू किट and so on are written the same way. Code, keyboard k"},{"t":"Language reference","d":"Every language control, what it does, and how the language choice is kept.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/reference.html","h":["Controls","Behaviour","Opting parts of a page out"],"x":" Control Where What it does Globe button Language / भाषा Header, wide screens Switches English ⇄ Hindi English / हिन्दी Settings › Appearance › Language Picks a language English / हिन्दी Drawer › Preferences › Language Picks a language Switch language Spotlight, command mode Switches English ⇄ Hindi; shows the current language ?lang=hi / ?lang=en Any page address Opens the page in that language and remembers it Item Behaviour Languages English en , Hindi hi Default English Switching to Hindi Translates the page in place, then every page after Switching to English Reloads the page Remembered In this browser, for every page, until you switch Page language Marked as Hindi while in Hindi, so screen readers and translation tools know Date and time format Hindi India while in Hindi; English United States style in English, except where your Clock settings choose a format Fonts Devanagari system fonts such as Nirmala UI, Noto Sans Devanagari, Mukta, Hind or Kohinoor Devanagari, depending on your device In the settings export file No Offline Hindi text is included in the offline download when you prepare it while the site is in Hindi Some elements are deliberately never translated: the lang"},{"t":"Troubleshooting languages","d":"Fixes for common problems when using the site in Hindi.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The page stays in English after I choose Hindi","Some words are still in English","Switching to English reloaded the page and I lost what I typed","Devanagari text looks like boxes or a plain font","The site opened in Hindi although I never chose it","Search does not find anything when I type in Hindi"],"x":" Why: the Hindi text is downloaded when you switch. On a slow or broken connection it may not arrive. What to do: check your connection and reload the page; the site remembers Hindi and translates again on load. In the installed app offline, Hindi is available only if you prepared the offline version while the site was in Hindi. Why: some names and terms are kept in English on purpose see What is translated what is translated.md , and a few messages made up of several live values are not yet translated. Why: returning to English needs a reload. What to do: before switching back, finish or copy your text. Many tool pages keep their inputs in the page address, so a reload restores them see Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . Why: your device has no Devanagari font, or not one of those the site asks for. What to do: install a Devanagari font such as Noto Sans Devanagari, or add the Hindi language pack in your operating system's language settings. Why: you followed a link that ended in ?lang=hi , which switches the site to Hindi and remembers it. What to do: select the globe button, or choose English in Settings. Why: page search matches the English text of pages. What to"},{"t":"Language FAQ","d":"Short answers about English and Hindi on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/docs/faq.html","h":["Which languages are available?","Is the Hindi version a separate website?","Does switching language change my other settings?","Does my account remember the language?","Why are some brand names written in Devanagari?","Can I read an article in Hindi and a tool in English?"],"x":" English and Hindi. No. Every page has one address, and the same page is shown in the language you chose. No. Theme, accent, text size and your other settings stay as they are. The language is kept in your browser, not in your account. Choose it once on each browser you use, or open a link with ?lang=hi . The site writes its own brand and product names in Devanagari so that Hindi pages read in one script. Names of other companies and tools that you would type into a search engine stay in Latin letters. Not at the same time. The language applies to the whole site in this browser. "},{"t":"Language: supporting material","d":"Contents of the language supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the language guides limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md How complete and how exact the Hindi translation is related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and downloaded There are no keyboard shortcuts for switching language. Use the globe button or Spotlight's Switch language command. "},{"t":"Language glossary","d":"Terms used in the language guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Devanagari The script used to write Hindi हिन्दी . Transliteration Writing a name in another script by its sound, not its meaning, such as ऑरिक आर्टिज़न for Auric Artisan. Translation in place Replacing the text of a page that is already open, without loading it again. Locale The language and region conventions used to write dates, times and numbers, such as Hindi India . Query parameter A part of a web address after ? , such as ?lang=hi , that passes a setting to the page. "},{"t":"Language limits and accuracy","d":"How complete the Hindi translation is and what to expect from it.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" Coverage. The site's interface and page text are translated across the site. A small number of strings stay in English: terms that are international such as CIELAB or OKLCH style colour notations , third party names, code, and some messages built from several live values. Emphasis. Where an English heading has part of it styled differently for example in italics , the Hindi heading may show it as plain text. Layout. Hindi text can be longer or shorter than English. Lines use slightly taller spacing to keep Devanagari marks clear. Search. Page search matches English text. Technical terms. Names used internationally, such as CIELAB, xyY or Bradford, are kept in Latin letters so they match the literature and other tools. "},{"t":"Language privacy","d":"What is stored about your language choice and what switching downloads.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your language choice is kept in this browser's local storage for auricartisan.com. The cookie policy lists it under Functional storage as the language and locale preference. Switching to Hindi downloads the Hindi text for the pages you open, from auricartisan.com. No text from the page, and nothing you type, is sent anywhere to be translated: translation happens in your browser from those downloaded files. Nothing about your language is sent to an account. "},{"t":"Related to languages","d":"Features related to the site's language setting.","p":"Website › Site features › Language","u":"website/site-features/language/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — the Language control in Appearance. Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/README.md — the globe button and the drawer's Language switch. Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md — the Switch language command. Download and offline ../../../download and offline/README.md — keeping Hindi available offline. Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md — a separate product with its own language support. "},{"t":"Navigation dock","d":"The floating navigation rail with Back, Forward, Reload, page outline, split view, recorder, copy, share and scroll controls.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The navigation dock is a slim floating rail on the edge of every page. It gathers the controls you reach for while reading or working: Back , Forward and Reload ; a Page outline that lists the page's headings and jumps to them; Open split view ; Record screen ; Copy link and Share ; and Scroll to top with a ring that fills as you read and Scroll to bottom . The dock is independent of the header, so it stays with you as you scroll. When you are not using it, it tucks away to a thin gold line at the edge of the window and slides out when you point at it. You can drag it up or down, and move it to the other side of the screen; it remembers where you put it. On phones it becomes a horizontal bar at the bottom of the screen, opened from the page utilities bar. Readers of long pages who want to jump between sections or back to the top. Anyone using the site as an installed app, where the browser's own Back and Reload buttons may be hidden. People who share pages often. Desktop and tablets: a thin gold line halfway down the left edge of the window or the right edge, if you moved it . Point at it to open the dock. Phones: open the page utilities bar at the bottom left and select Navigate "},{"t":"Navigation dock guides","d":"Contents of the navigation dock guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the dock and a tour of its buttons move and collapse.md move and collapse.md Drag, flip, collapse and reopen the dock, on desktop and phone page outline.md page outline.md Use the outline to see and jump to the page's sections reference.md reference.md Every button, its label and what it does troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the navigation dock","d":"Open the navigation dock and learn what each of its buttons does.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the dock","The buttons","Try it"],"x":" When a page loads on a computer, the dock shows fully for a moment and then tucks itself away into a thin gold line at the edge of the window. To bring it back: point at the line; or click it; or move keyboard focus into it with Tab . It tucks away again about half a second after your pointer leaves, unless the page outline is open or a button in the dock has keyboard focus. On a phone, open the page utilities bar at the bottom left and select Navigate . From top to bottom left to right on a phone : Button What it does Grip six dots Drag to move the dock. Tooltip: \"Drag to move\". Not shown on phones. Back Goes back one page. Greyed out when there is nothing to go back to. Forward Goes forward one page. Greyed out when there is nothing ahead. Reload Reloads the page. Page outline Opens the On this page list of headings. Open split view Opens split view with this page see Split view ../../split view/README.md . Record screen Alt+Shift+R Opens the screen recorder see Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md . Copy link Copies the page's address. The icon briefly becomes a tick. Share Opens your device's share sheet; without one, copies the link and shows a tick. Scroll to top "},{"t":"Move and collapse the dock","d":"Drag the navigation dock, flip it to the other side, and understand how it collapses on desktop and on phones.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/move-and-collapse.html","h":["Move the dock up or down","Move the dock to the other side","How the dock collapses","On a phone","When the dock is hidden"],"x":" 1. Point at the dock so it opens. 2. Press and hold the grip six dots at its top. 3. Drag up or down. The dock can sit anywhere between 10% and 90% of the window's height. 4. Let go. Result: the dock stays at that height on every page, in this browser. Either: drag the grip across the middle of the window, then let go; or select Flip dock side the arrow at the bottom of the dock . Result: the dock moves to the other edge and stays there on every page. The outline panel opens on the side facing the page. On screens wider than 700 pixels: after a page loads, the dock stays open for about 1.6 seconds so you can see it, then collapses; collapsed, it is a thin gold line, 64 pixels tall, flush with the edge. It is faint until you point at it; it opens when you point at it, click it or tab into it, and collapses about half a second after you move away; it stays open while the page outline is open, while you are dragging it, and while a button in it has keyboard focus. On screens 700 pixels wide or narrower: the dock is a horizontal bar centred at the bottom of the screen. If its buttons do not fit, swipe it sideways; the grip and Flip dock side are not shown, and the dock cannot be dragg"},{"t":"Jump around with the page outline","d":"Use the dock's page outline to see the page's sections, find where you are, and jump to any heading.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/page-outline.html","h":["Open the outline and jump to a section","Close the outline","What the outline lists","Other outlines on the site"],"x":" The Page outline button opens a panel titled On this page beside the dock. It lists the headings of the page you are on and highlights the one you are reading. 1. Point at the dock and select Page outline the list icon . 2. The On this page panel opens. Main headings are listed normally; sub headings are indented and slightly smaller. 3. The heading of the section you are reading is highlighted in the accent colour. As you scroll, the highlight moves with you. 4. Select a heading. Result: the page scrolls smoothly to that heading, leaving room for the site header above it, and the panel closes. Select Page outline again, press Esc , or click anywhere outside the panel and the dock. The main headings and their sub headings heading levels 1, 2 and 3 in the page's main content. Headings in the header, footer and navigation areas are left out, as are hidden headings and headings longer than 90 characters. The list is rebuilt every time you open it, so headings that appear later for example in a tool's results are included. On a page without headings, the panel reads \"No sections on this page\". Long company, pricing, legal and security pages also have a section rail pinned under the he"},{"t":"Navigation dock reference","d":"Every control of the navigation dock with its label, action and availability.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/reference.html","h":["Controls","States and sizes","Remembered settings","Timings"],"x":" Control Label tooltip Action Phone Grip Drag to move Drag vertically; drag across the middle to change side Hidden Back Back Browser history back Shown Forward Forward Browser history forward Shown Reload Reload Reloads the page Shown Outline Page outline Opens or closes On this page Shown Split view Open split view Opens split view Shown Record Record screen Alt+Shift+R Opens the recorder setup Shown Copy Copy link Copies the current address; shows a tick Shown Share Share Share sheet, or copies the address and shows a tick Shown Top Scroll to top Smooth scroll to the top; ring shows progress Shown Bottom Scroll to bottom Smooth scroll to the end Shown Flip Flip dock side Moves the dock to the other edge Hidden Collapsed line or button Show navigation Navigation Opens the dock Button on some phones Back and Forward are greyed out when there is no page in that direction, in browsers that report this such as Chrome and Edge . In other browsers they are always available. State Appearance Open desktop Vertical pill of buttons, 12 pixels from the edge Collapsed desktop Thin gold line, 3 by 64 pixels, 4 pixels from the edge Open 700 px and narrower Horizontal bar centred at the bottom,"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the navigation dock","d":"Fixes for common problems with the navigation dock.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["I cannot find the dock","The dock closes before I can use it","Back and Forward are greyed out","Share only copied the link","The copied link is very long","The outline says \"No sections on this page\"","The dock covers part of the page"],"x":" Why: it collapses to a thin, faint line at the edge of the window a moment after the page loads. On phones it has no visible button on the narrowest screens. What to do: look halfway down the left edge or the right edge, if you moved it and point at the line. On a phone, open the page utilities bar and select Navigate . Why: it collapses half a second after the pointer leaves it. What to do: keep the pointer over the dock, or tab into it with the keyboard; it stays open while a button in it has focus. The outline keeps it open too. Why: there is no page in that direction in this tab's history. If you opened the page in a new tab, there is nothing to go back to. Why: your browser or device has no share sheet available to web pages, so the dock copies the link instead and shows a tick. What to do: paste the link into the app you want to share it with. Why: the address includes the page's remembered state after p= , such as your scroll position and values you entered. See Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . What to do: to share a clean link, scroll to the top of the page and clear any values you typed before copying, or delete the part from p= onwards after pasting. Why"},{"t":"Navigation dock FAQ","d":"Short answers about the navigation dock.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/docs/faq.html","h":["Can I turn the dock off?","Can I keep the dock open all the time?","Does the dock work in the installed app?","Is the dock the same as the header menus?","Why is there no dock inside split view?"],"x":" There is no switch to remove it. It collapses to a thin line when you are not using it, and you can move it wherever it is least in the way. No. On desktop it opens when you point at it or tab into it, and collapses when you move away. Yes. It is especially useful there, where the browser's own Back, Forward and Reload buttons may not be visible. No. The header takes you to other pages; the dock moves you around the page you are on and through your history. Each pane of split view has its own Back, Forward and Reload buttons, so the dock stays out of the panes. "},{"t":"Navigation dock: supporting material","d":"Contents of the navigation dock's supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the dock guides related.md related.md Features the dock opens and similar features privacy.md privacy.md What the dock remembers and shares The dock has no keyboard shortcuts of its own. The shortcuts for the features it opens split view, the recorder are in Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Navigation dock glossary","d":"Terms used in the navigation dock guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Dock The floating rail of navigation buttons on the edge of the window. Collapsed The dock's resting state: a thin line at the edge desktop or a small round button phone . Grip The six dot handle at the top of the dock, used to drag it. Page outline The On this page panel listing the page's headings. Progress ring The ring around Scroll to top that fills as you scroll down the page. Share sheet Your device's own panel for sending a link to another app or person. Page state Details the site keeps in the address after p= , such as your scroll position. "},{"t":"Navigation dock privacy","d":"What the navigation dock stores and what its buttons share.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The dock remembers only which side of the window it is on and how high it sits, in this browser. Copy link puts the page address on your clipboard. Share hands it to your device's share sheet. Neither sends anything to Auric Artisan. The address can include the page's remembered state after p= , such as values you typed into a tool. Check the link before you share it if that matters. See Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . "},{"t":"Related to the navigation dock","d":"Features related to the navigation dock.","p":"Website › Site features › Navigation dock","u":"website/site-features/navigation-dock/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Split view ../../split view/README.md — opened by Open split view . Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md — opened by Record screen . Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md — what Copy link and Share include. Guide and page outline ../../guide and page outline/README.md — the page guide and the section rail on long pages. Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/README.md — the page utilities bar, whose Navigate button opens the dock. Context menu ../../context menu/README.md — also offers Back, Forward, Reload, scroll and copy link actions. "},{"t":"Screen recorder","d":"Record your screen, a window, this tab, a region of the page or a tool's canvas, and export video, animated GIF or PNG images.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Every page on auricartisan.com has a built in recorder. Press Alt + Shift + R , choose what to record, and start. You can capture: Screen or window — any screen, window or tab you pick in your browser's sharing dialog; This tab — the page you are on; Region of this page — a rectangle you draw, or a part of the page you click; Tool canvas — a tool's drawing surface, captured pixel for pixel. While you record, a small bar shows the time and file size, with pause, stop and discard buttons. When you stop, the recording is kept on your device under My recordings , where you can play it, rename it, trim it, and export it as a video file, an animated GIF, a ZIP of PNG frames or a single PNG still. Recordings are made and stored entirely in your browser. Nothing is uploaded. Designers and developers showing a tool, a palette or a bug to someone else. Teachers and writers making short clips or GIFs of colour tools. Anyone filing a bug report who wants to show what happened. Press Alt + Shift + R on any page. Select Record screen in the navigation dock. The recorder works in desktop browsers that let web pages capture the screen, such as Chrome, Edge and Firefox. Mobile browsers generally c"},{"t":"Screen recorder guides","d":"Contents of the screen recorder guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the recorder, a tour of the dialog, and your first recording record a take.md record a take.md Sources, capture settings, audio, the countdown, the recording bar and the region picker my recordings and export.md my recordings and export.md Play, rename, trim, export and delete recordings reference.md reference.md Every option, default, format and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the screen recorder","d":"Open the recorder, learn the setup dialog, and make your first recording.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the recorder","A tour of the dialog","Your first recording","Move or reset the dialog","Close the dialog"],"x":" Press Alt + Shift + R on any page. Or point at the navigation dock and select Record screen Alt+Shift+R . The first time, the recorder takes a moment to load. The Your Recorder dialog opens. It floats over the page without blocking it. 1. Header. A grip to move the dialog, the title Your Recorder , Reset dialog position and Close . 2. Recording source choose what enters the frame : Screen or window , This tab , Region of this page , Tool canvas . Each has a one line description. A source the page or browser cannot use is greyed out with the reason. 3. Capture settings video output : Frame rate , Quality , Resolution cap and Countdown . 4. Audio & pointer optional capture layers : Microphone , Tab audio and Highlight the cursor . 5. A note saying which video format this browser records: \"Recording to MP4 — plays anywhere.\" or \"Recording to WebM. Export to GIF or frames from My recordings.\" 6. Footer. My recordings , Reset setup , the Alt Shift R reminder, and Start recording . Your choices are remembered for next time. 1. Open the recorder. 2. Choose Screen or window . 3. Select Start recording . Your browser's sharing dialog opens. 4. Pick the window or screen to record and confir"},{"t":"My recordings and export","d":"Play, rename, trim, export and delete your recordings.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/my-recordings-and-export.html","h":["The list","Play a recording","Download the video","Export an animated GIF","Export frames","Save a still","Trim a recording","Delete a recording","File names","If an export fails"],"x":" My recordings lists every recording kept in this browser. It opens after each recording, or from My recordings in the recorder dialog. The panel header has a grip to move it, the title My recordings , New recording opens the setup dialog and Close . Esc closes it. Each recording shows: a thumbnail; select it to play the recording; its title, which you can edit in place an empty title becomes \"Untitled recording\" ; details: length, file size, pixel size, and \"with audio\" when it has sound; actions: Download video , GIF , Frames , Still , Trim and Delete . The foot of the panel shows the total, for example \"4 recordings · 38.2 MB used · 1.1 GB free\". With no recordings, the panel reads \"No recordings yet.\" with a Record something button. Select the thumbnail. A player opens with the recording's title and standard video controls. Esc or Close closes it. Select Download video . The file downloads as MP4 or WebM, whichever format this browser recorded. 1. Select GIF Export as an animated GIF . 2. A progress bar shows \"Encoding GIF…\". 3. The GIF downloads, and the message gives its size, for example \"GIF exported — 2.4 MB.\" GIFs are made at 10 frames per second, at most 640 pixels wide,"},{"t":"Record a take","d":"Choose a source and capture settings, add audio, draw a region, and control the recording with the recording bar.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/record-a-take.html","h":["Choose a source","Choose capture settings","Add audio and a pointer highlight","Record a region","Record a tool canvas","The countdown","The recording bar","When a recording stops by itself","After you stop","Reset your setup"],"x":" Source Description on screen Good for Screen or window Pick any screen, window, or tab. Controls stay out of the video unless you share this tab. Showing several apps or windows This tab Records this page. The recording bar is part of the page, so collapse it to keep it small. Walking through a page or tool Region of this page Drag a rectangle or click an element. Everything outside it is cropped away. A tidy clip of one panel or control Tool canvas Records a tool's drawing surface directly — pixel exact, and nothing on screen can spoil the take. Animated or drawn output from a tool When a source is not possible, it is greyed out with the reason: \"No recordable canvas on this page.\" — the page has no canvas large enough to record; \"This browser cannot capture the screen.\" — the browser does not let pages capture the screen the Tool canvas source may still work . Note: When you record this tab, anything shown on the page is in the video, including the recording bar. Collapse the bar to a dot, or record a region or a canvas, to keep it out. Setting Options Default Frame rate 15 fps — smallest, 24 fps — cinematic, 30 fps — standard, 60 fps — smoothest 30 fps Quality Low — smallest fi"},{"t":"Screen recorder reference","d":"Every recorder option, default, output format, limit and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/reference.html","h":["Setup dialog (Your Recorder)","Recording bar","Recordings list","Formats","Limits","Keyboard","Messages"],"x":" Control Options Default Recording source Screen or window, This tab, Region of this page, Tool canvas Screen or window Frame rate 15, 24, 30, 60 fps 30 fps Quality Low — smallest file, Balanced, High — sharpest text Balanced Resolution cap Native, 1080p, 720p, 480p Native Countdown None, 3 seconds, 5 seconds 3 seconds Microphone On, off Off Tab audio On, off On Highlight the cursor On, off Off My recordings Opens the recordings list — Reset setup / Confirm reset Two step reset of all the above — Start recording Starts with the chosen source — Reset dialog position Centres the dialog — Close Closes the dialog — All choices are remembered in this browser, as is whether the recording bar is collapsed. Control Action Grip Move the bar Timer and size Elapsed time and file size Pause recording / Resume recording Pause or resume Stop and save Stop and keep Discard recording Stop and throw away Collapse to a dot / Expand controls Shrink or restore the bar Action Output Thumbnail Play Opens the player Title Editable name Download video MP4 or WebM file GIF Animated GIF: 10 fps, up to 640 px wide, up to 300 frames, loops Frames ZIP of PNGs: 5 per second, up to 1,280 px wide, up to 120 frame"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the screen recorder","d":"Fixes for common screen recorder problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The screen sources are greyed out","Tool canvas is greyed out","Nothing happened after Start recording","The recording bar is in my video","There is no sound","The recording stopped by itself","The recording was downloaded instead of saved","Exporting a GIF is slow or the GIF is large","Trimming takes a long time","My recordings disappeared"],"x":" Why: \"This browser cannot capture the screen.\" Most mobile browsers, and some older desktop browsers, do not let web pages capture the screen. What to do: use a current desktop browser such as Chrome, Edge or Firefox, or use Tool canvas on a tool page. Why: \"No recordable canvas on this page.\" The page has no visible canvas larger than 80 by 80 pixels. What to do: open a tool that draws on a canvas, or choose another source. Why: you cancelled or closed your browser's sharing dialog, or denied permission. What to do: select Start recording again and allow sharing. If you denied it permanently, allow screen sharing for auricartisan.com in your browser's site settings. Why: with This tab , the bar is part of the page, so it is recorded. What to do: collapse it to a dot, record a Region of this page that leaves it out, or use Screen or window and pick another window. Possible causes: Tab audio was off, or the page made no sound. In your browser's sharing dialog, the option to share audio was not ticked some browsers only offer audio for tabs . The microphone was refused \"Microphone unavailable — recording without it.\" . Why: it reached 30 minutes, you pressed your browser's Stop shar"},{"t":"Screen recorder FAQ","d":"Short answers about the screen recorder.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/docs/faq.html","h":["Are my recordings uploaded?","Are recordings saved in my Library?","Can I record other websites or apps?","Why MP4 in one browser and WebM in another?","Can I keep recording while I move to another page on the site?","Does the custom cursor appear in recordings?"],"x":" No. They are recorded and stored in your browser on this device. They leave it only when you download them. No. Recordings have their own list, My recordings , separate from the library of palettes and assets. Yes, with Screen or window : your browser lets you pick any screen, window or tab to share. The recorder uses MP4 where the browser can record it, because it plays almost everywhere. Otherwise it records WebM. The dialog tells you which. No. Leaving or reloading the page ends the recording; the browser asks you to confirm first. Record with Screen or window if you need to move between pages, and pick the browser window. Yes, when you record the page itself. Switch it off in Settings › Comfort for a clean system pointer, and use Highlight the cursor if you want the pointer emphasised. "},{"t":"Screen recorder: supporting material","d":"Contents of the screen recorder supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the recorder guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Recorder keyboard shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Limits on length, size, formats and quality related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What is captured, stored and shared release notes.md release notes.md User facing history "},{"t":"Screen recorder shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts for the screen recorder.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Action Alt + Shift + R Open the recorder; while recording, stop and save Alt + Shift + P Pause or resume a recording Esc Close the dialog, recordings list or player; cancel the region picker Arrow keys on the dialog grip Move the dialog; hold Shift for finer steps Alt + Shift was chosen to avoid browser shortcuts: Ctrl + Shift + R is your browser's hard reload. The full list is in Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Screen recorder glossary","d":"Terms used in the screen recorder guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Source What the recorder captures: a screen or window, this tab, a region, or a tool canvas. Take One recording, from start to stop. Frame rate fps How many images per second a video holds. Higher is smoother and larger. Resolution cap The largest width a recording is allowed; bigger sources are scaled down. Canvas A drawing surface that tools use for graphics and animation. Region A rectangle of the page, or one element, that a recording is cropped to. MP4, WebM Video file formats. MP4 plays almost everywhere; WebM is widely supported by browsers. GIF An animated image format that plays in most apps and web pages without a player. Re encode To play a video and record it again, which is how trimming makes a new file. Sharing dialog The browser's own window asking which screen, window or tab to share. "},{"t":"Screen recorder limits and accuracy","d":"Limits on recording length, storage, formats and quality.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" Length. A recording stops at 30 minutes. Storage. Recordings use your browser's storage for this site, which the browser limits. A minute of high resolution video can take several megabytes to tens of megabytes. The list shows how much is used and free. Video length metadata. Browsers do not always write a length into recorded files. Some players may show an unknown length or seek slowly in a downloaded WebM file; the recorder's own player and exports account for this. GIF. Up to 300 frames at 10 per second and 640 pixels wide, with at most 255 colours. Long recordings are sampled, not played frame by frame, and subtle gradients can band. Frames. Up to 120 PNG images, five per second, up to 1,280 pixels wide. It is a sampling of the recording, not every frame. Trim. Runs in real time and makes a new file; the quality matches the original recording's format. Region crop. Where the browser can crop the shared tab itself, it does so; otherwise the recorder crops each frame, which uses more processing power. Browser support. Screen capture depends on the browser. Most mobile browsers cannot capture the screen. "},{"t":"Screen recorder privacy","d":"What the recorder captures, where recordings are kept, and what is shared.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Permission first. Nothing is captured until you start a recording and, for screen, window, tab and region sources, allow sharing in your browser's dialog. The microphone is used only if you switch it on and allow it. What is captured. Exactly what you shared: a screen or window can include other apps, notifications and personal information. Check what is visible before you record. Where recordings live. In your browser's storage for auricartisan.com, on this device only. They are not uploaded, not added to your account and not placed in your Library. Sharing. A recording leaves your device only when you download it and send the file yourself. Preferences. Your recorder settings and the dialog position are kept in this browser. Deleting. Delete in My recordings removes a recording. Clearing site data for auricartisan.com removes them all. "},{"t":"Screen recorder release notes","d":"User-facing history of the screen recorder, from the public changelog.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" Date Release Change 2026 08 12 v0.9.11 Added a site wide screen, tab, region and canvas recorder with video, animated GIF, PNG frame, poster and trim export. The full entry is in the changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. "},{"t":"Related to the screen recorder","d":"Features related to the screen recorder.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen recorder","u":"website/site-features/screen-recorder/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md — the Record screen button. Custom cursor ../../custom cursor/README.md — how the pointer appears in recordings. Feedback ../../feedback/README.md — report a bug from the site; a recording you make can help you describe what happened. Split view ../../split view/README.md — record two pages side by side with This tab . "},{"t":"Screen saver","d":"The optional idle screen that fills the window with a colour from the site's colour atlas after a period of inactivity.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The screen saver is an optional idle screen. When you have not touched the page for a while, it fills the window with a single colour from the site's colour atlas, laid out as seven bands from its darkest shade to its lightest, with the colour itself sitting on its own step. A readout names the colour and gives its hex code, its OKLCH value, the mood it reads as, the art movement associated with it, and its contrast against black. A new colour arrives every twelve seconds, and a small clock shows the time. Move the mouse, press a key, scroll or touch the screen, and the page comes back exactly as you left it. The screen saver is off by default . You choose whether it runs and how long the page must be idle first 1, 5, 10, 20 or 30 minutes . People who leave the site open on a second screen or in a studio, and anyone who enjoys a slow tour of the site's colour atlas. Settings Ctrl + , › Comfort › Screen saver . 1. Press Ctrl + , and select Comfort . 2. Switch on Screen saver . 3. Under Start after , select 1m to try it. 4. Leave the page alone for a minute or so. 5. The screen fills with a colour and its readout. Wait twelve seconds to see the next one. 6. Move the mouse. The page "},{"t":"Screen saver guides","d":"Contents of the screen saver guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Turn the screen saver on, set the delay, and leave it reading the screen.md reading the screen.md What each part of the screen saver shows reference.md reference.md Settings, timings and what counts as activity troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the screen saver","d":"Turn the screen saver on, choose when it starts, and return to the page.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Turn it on","When it starts","Return to the page","Turn it off"],"x":" 1. Press Ctrl + , to open Settings, then select Comfort . 2. Switch on Screen saver \"Ambient animation after long periods of inactivity.\" . 3. Under Start after minutes of inactivity , select 1m , 5m , 10m , 20m or 30m . The default is 10m . The screen saver starts when the page has had no mouse movement, click, key press, scroll, touch or wheel movement for the time you chose. The site checks every ten seconds, so it can start up to about ten seconds after the time is reached. It counts activity on this page only. Time spent in other tabs or apps counts as idle time for this page, so the screen saver may already be showing when you come back to the tab. Do any of these: move the mouse, click, press a key, scroll, use the wheel, or touch the screen. The page comes back as you left it. A hint, Move to return , shows at the bottom of the screen saver for its first minute, then fades. Switch off Screen saver in Settings › Comfort. If it is showing at that moment for example in another window you can see , it closes at once. "},{"t":"Reading the screen","d":"What each part of the screen saver shows, from the colour bands to the readout and clock.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/reading-the-screen.html","h":["The colour bands","The readout","The rotation","The foot of the screen","What is hidden"],"x":" The whole screen is seven bands of one colour, from its darkest shade to its lightest. On a wide screen the bands run side by side; on a narrow or portrait screen they run top to bottom. The bands are steps of lightness in OKLCH: 0.22, 0.35, 0.48, 0.61, 0.74, 0.85 and 0.94. Each band shows its step number. The fourth band 0.61 is the colour's own step, marked as the sample. The darkest step is pure black for every colour. Colourfulness tapers towards both ends, because very dark and very light shades cannot hold a strong colour. Each step number sits on a small chip that keeps it readable on its band. OKLCH describes a colour by its lightness L , chroma or colourfulness C and hue H , in a way that follows how people see colour. Stepping lightness in OKLCH gives even looking shades. Line What it shows Colour atlas and a number The colour's number in the site's atlas of 8,192 colours, for example \"6,400 / 8,192\" Name The colour's name, for example Crocus Yellow Hex Its hex code oklch Its lightness, chroma and hue reads as The mood the atlas associates with it, for example calm or playful movement The art movement the atlas associates with it, for example Bauhaus or Art Deco on black"},{"t":"Screen saver reference","d":"Screen saver settings, timings, and what counts as activity.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/reference.html","h":["Settings (Settings › Comfort)","What counts as activity","Timings","Readout fields","Bands","Related settings"],"x":" Control Values Default Screen saver On, off Off Start after 1m , 5m , 10m , 20m , 30m 10m The Start after buttons are dimmed while Screen saver is off. Mouse movement, mouse button press, key press, scrolling, touch, and mouse wheel. Any of them resets the idle time and closes the screen saver. Item Value Idle check Every 10 seconds Time per colour 12 seconds Move to return hint First 60 seconds Clock refresh Every 30 seconds Label Content Colour atlas Atlas number of the colour, out of 8,192 Name Colour name Hex Hex code oklch Lightness, chroma, hue reads as Associated mood movement Associated art movement on black WCAG contrast ratio against black Seven OKLCH lightness steps: 0.22, 0.35, 0.48, 0.61 the colour's own step , 0.74, 0.85, 0.94. Side by side on wide screens; stacked on narrow or portrait screens. Setting Effect on the screen saver Settings › Clock › 24 hour time The screen saver clock uses 24 hour time Language The clock uses the page's language for dates "},{"t":"Troubleshooting the screen saver","d":"Fixes for common screen saver problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The screen saver never starts","It starts too soon or too late","My computer's own screen saver or sleep takes over first","The colour readout is missing and only a plain colour shows"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: It is off. Switch on Screen saver in Settings › Comfort. Something keeps registering as activity, for example a mouse that drifts slightly or a page that scrolls itself. Keep the mouse still. A few pages do not include the screen saver. Try another page. The idle check runs every ten seconds, so allow a few seconds beyond your chosen time. What to do: change Start after in Settings › Comfort. The new time applies at the next check. Why: your operating system's power settings are separate from the site. If the system dims or sleeps sooner than the site's delay, you will not see the site's screen saver. What to do: choose a shorter Start after , or a longer delay in your system settings. Why: the colour list is downloaded the first time the screen saver starts. If that fails, the screen saver uses a small built in set of colours instead. What to do: nothing is needed; it still works. Check your connection if you want the full atlas. "},{"t":"Screen saver FAQ","d":"Short answers about the screen saver.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/docs/faq.html","h":["Does the screen saver stop my computer from sleeping?","Can I choose which colours it shows?","Where do the colours come from?","Does it use much power?","Is the screen saver the same as eye rest?"],"x":" No. It is part of the web page. Your computer's own power and sleep settings still apply. No. It picks a random starting colour from the atlas and moves on every twelve seconds. From the site's colour atlas of 8,192 named colours, each with a mood and an art movement associated with it. It is drawn with plain page elements rather than animation heavy graphics, and it pauses while its tab is hidden. No. Eye rest reminds you to look away while you are working; the screen saver appears when you have stopped. See Eye rest ../../eye rest/README.md . "},{"t":"Screen saver: supporting material","d":"Contents of the screen saver supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the screen saver guides limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the readout's values mean and how precise they are related.md related.md Related features and libraries privacy.md privacy.md What the screen saver stores and downloads The screen saver has no keyboard shortcut: any key press closes it. "},{"t":"Screen saver glossary","d":"Terms used in the screen saver guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Idle No mouse, keyboard, scroll, wheel or touch activity on the page. Colour atlas The site's collection of 8,192 named colours with mood and movement notes. OKLCH A way of writing colour as lightness L , chroma C and hue H that follows human perception. Lightness step One of the seven bands, each a fixed OKLCH lightness from 0.22 to 0.94. Chroma How colourful a colour is, from grey 0 upwards. Contrast on black The WCAG contrast ratio between the colour and pure black. "},{"t":"Screen saver limits and accuracy","d":"What the screen saver's values mean and how precise they are.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" Values. The OKLCH values are shown to two decimal places for lightness and chroma and to whole degrees for hue. The contrast against black uses the WCAG 2 formula, to two decimal places. Shades. The seven bands are drawn in OKLCH where your browser supports it; very colourful shades may be outside what your screen can show and are drawn as close as the screen allows. Mood and movement. \"reads as\" and \"movement\" are descriptive notes from the colour atlas, not measurements. Timing. The idle check runs every ten seconds, so the screen saver can start up to about ten seconds after your chosen delay. Scope. It runs only in the page's own tab and does not replace your operating system's screen saver or power settings. "},{"t":"Screen saver privacy","d":"What the screen saver stores and downloads.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your on or off choice and delay are kept in this browser, as part of your settings. The screen saver watches for activity only to know when you are idle. It does not record or send what you do. The first time it starts, it downloads a small list of atlas colours from auricartisan.com. Nothing is sent in return. "},{"t":"Related to the screen saver","d":"Features and libraries related to the screen saver.","p":"Website › Site features › Screen saver","u":"website/site-features/screen-saver/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel › Comfort options ../../settings panel/docs/comfort options.md — the switch and the delay. Settings panel › Highlights and clock ../../settings panel/docs/highlights and clock.md — the 24 hour setting used by its clock. Eye rest ../../eye rest/README.md — reminders to look away while you work. Colour libraries ../../../library/colour libraries/README.md — the site's colour collections, including the Color Library. "},{"t":"Search and Spotlight","d":"Spotlight, the site-wide search palette opened with Ctrl + K, with scopes, colour answers, filters and commands.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Spotlight is the search box that floats over any page when you press Ctrl + K Cmd + K on a Mac or select Search in the header. Type a few letters and it lists matching pages, tools, documentation and Learn articles from across the site, with a preview of the highlighted result and the reasons it ranked there. Tabs narrow the search to Pages , Tools , Docs or Learn , and a Web tab searches trusted sources beyond the site. Spotlight also answers some questions directly. Type a hex colour such as 2f5eaa and it shows that colour's values and its contrast on black and white. Type two hex colours and it judges them as a text and background pair against WCAG. Type and it becomes a command palette that can switch the theme, open the guide, the library or Settings, switch language, and more. For a larger results page with filters, Spotlight hands your query to the full search page at https://auricartisan.com/search/, which is documented in Search ../../search/README.md . Anyone looking for a tool, article or page without browsing the menus. Keyboard users who want to reach site actions without the mouse. Designers who want a quick reading of a colour or a colour pair. Press Ctrl + K Cmd + "},{"t":"Search and Spotlight guides","d":"Contents of the Spotlight search guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open Spotlight, a tour of its parts, and your first search scopes and results.md scopes and results.md Scope tabs, results, the preview pane, recent searches and web search colour answers and filters.md colour answers and filters.md Colour and colour pair answers, field filters, phrases and exclusions commands.md commands.md The command palette reference.md reference.md Every control, launcher, command and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with Spotlight","d":"Open Spotlight, learn its parts, and run your first search.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open and close Spotlight","The parts of Spotlight","Your first search","Go further"],"x":" Open: press Ctrl + K Cmd + K on a Mac , or select Search in the header. Close: press Esc the first press clears what you typed, the second closes , press Ctrl + K again, or click the dimmed page around Spotlight. While Spotlight is open, the page behind it does not scroll. 1. Search box. A magnifier, an optional mode chip for example Colour or Command , the text box, an ESC hint and an X to clear the box. The box's placeholder names the current scope, for example \"Search Auric Artisan…\". 2. Scope tabs. All , Pages , Tools , Docs , Learn and Web . 3. Results list on the left. 4. Preview pane on the right. It shows details of the highlighted result, or the answer when you type a colour. 5. Footer. Key hints ↑ ↓ navigate, ↵ open, TAB filter, ESC close and, on the right, a count such as \"12 results · 3ms\". 1. Open Spotlight. Before you type, it shows: Recent : up to six of your recent searches, with a Clear button; Quick Actions : shortcuts to Full Search, Collections, URL Analyzer, Color Science Lab, Documentation, Learn Color, Vision Simulations, Install the PWA and Install Extension. 2. Type at least two characters, for example contrast . 3. Results appear under Results . Each show"},{"t":"Colour answers and filters","d":"Get instant colour and contrast answers in Spotlight, and use field filters, quoted phrases and exclusions.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/colour-answers-and-filters.html","h":["Read a colour","Check a colour pair","Field filters","Phrases and exclusions"],"x":" Spotlight reads what you type and, for some kinds of query, answers directly. A small mode chip at the start of the search box says how it read your query. You type Chip What Spotlight does Ordinary words none Searches the site One hex colour, such as 2f5eaa Colour Shows the colour's values in the preview Two hex colours, such as ffffff 2f5eaa Contrast pair Judges the pair against WCAG in the preview followed by anything Command Lists commands see Commands commands.md A field filter such as title:gamut title:gamut Searches only that field 1. Open Spotlight and type a colour as and six hex digits, for example 2f5eaa , with nothing else. 2. The chip reads Colour . The preview pane shows: a swatch of the colour with its OKLCH value; Hex , RGB , On black and On white the WCAG contrast ratio of the colour against black and against white ; a link, Check it against a background , which opens the Contrast Checker with this colour. 3. The list shows Pages that mention it up to three pages whose text contains that hex code , or the note \"Nothing in the index mentions this colour by name — the answer is on the right.\" 1. Type two hex colours, for example ffffff 2f5eaa . The first is treated "},{"t":"Scopes and results","d":"Narrow Spotlight to pages, tools, documentation, Learn or the web, read the results and preview, and reuse recent searches.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/scopes-and-results.html","h":["Scope tabs","Reading the results","The preview pane","When nothing is found","Searching the web","Recent searches","How results are ranked"],"x":" The tabs under the search box decide where Spotlight looks. The box's placeholder changes to match. Tab Searches Placeholder All Everything on the site Search Auric Artisan… Pages Site pages such as home, collections, company and security not tools, documentation or Learn Search pages… Tools Every tool page Search tools… Docs Documentation and developer references Search documentation… Learn Learn colour science guides Search learn guides… Web Trusted sources on the wider web Search the web… Switch scope by selecting a tab, or press Tab next and Shift + Tab previous while the search box has focus. Your query re runs in the new scope at once. Spotlight remembers the scope you chose until you reload the page. With an empty box, each scope shows its own launch points: Scope Heading Launchers All Quick Actions Full Search, Collections, URL Analyzer, Color Science Lab, Documentation, Learn Color, Vision Simulations, Install the PWA, Install Extension Pages Jump to Pages Home, Collections, About, Pricing, FAQ, Contact, Security Tools Jump to Tools URL Analyzer, Color Science Lab, Vision Simulations, ASCII, Ishihara Plates, General Tools Docs Jump to Docs Documentation Home, Changelog Le"},{"t":"Spotlight reference","d":"Every Spotlight control, key, launcher, command, query mode and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/reference.html","h":["Ways to open","Controls","Keys","Query modes","Colour answer fields","Contrast pair fields","Commands","Launchers (empty box)","Messages"],"x":" Method Result Ctrl + K / Cmd + K Opens Spotlight, or closes it if open Header Search button Opens Spotlight Drawer Search tools, colours and pages Opens Spotlight Right click › Site › Search the site Opens Spotlight Control What it does Search box Type a query; results update as you type Mode chip Shows Colour , Contrast pair , Command or the field filter in use ESC hint Reminder that Esc clears, then closes Clear search X Empties the box and shows the launchers Scope tabs All , Pages , Tools , Docs , Learn , Web Results list Up to 8 results, commands, launchers or recent searches Preview pane Details of the highlighted result, or the colour answer Recent › Clear Deletes your recent searches Footer count Results and time, command count, or \"colour\" / \"contrast pair\" Dimmed page Click to close Keys What they do Up / Down Move through the list Enter Open or run the highlighted row Ctrl + Enter / Cmd + Enter Open the highlighted result in a new tab Tab / Shift + Tab Next or previous scope tab Esc Clear the box; if already empty, close Query Mode Minimum Words Search 2 characters rrggbb alone Colour — rrggbb rrggbb Contrast pair first = text, second = background — … Command — title: ,"},{"t":"Commands","d":"Use Spotlight as a command palette by typing > to switch theme, open the guide, library or settings, change language and more.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/commands.html","h":["Run a command","The site's commands","Commands a page adds","Commands in Hindi"],"x":" Type at the start of the Spotlight box to switch to command mode . The chip reads Command , and the list shows actions you can run on this page instead of pages you can open. 1. Press Ctrl + K and type . 2. The list shows every command available on this page, under the heading Commands . The footer counts them, for example \"7 commands\". 3. Keep typing to narrow the list, for example theme . 4. Select a command, or highlight it and press Enter . If nothing matches, the list reads \"No command matches that on this page.\" Command Description Shows Toggle light and dark The header's theme button The current theme, and ⌥T Open the page guide What this page is, and its tour — Open the library Saved palettes, gradients and reports — Open settings Theme, motion, density, language ⌘, Switch language English ⇄ हिन्दी The current language Open the full search page The whole index, with filters and instant answers — Install the app Offline cache and an app window — A command appears only when the page has the control it drives. For example, Open the library is missing on a page without the library button. The key hints are shown in Mac notation: ⌥T is Alt + T , and ⌘, is Ctrl + , on Windows an"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Spotlight","d":"Fixes for common problems with Spotlight search.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Ctrl + K opens my browser's address bar or search","The list says \"Search engine is loading…\"","A page I know exists does not appear","Web search says \"Global search is unavailable right now\"","Typing a colour does not show a colour answer","A command is missing","Recent searches are gone"],"x":" Why: Spotlight loads a moment after the page. A shortcut pressed before that goes to the browser. What to do: wait for the page to finish loading, or select Search in the header. Why: the first time you open Spotlight on a page, it builds its search index in the background. What to do: wait a moment and keep typing; results appear once the index is ready. On a slow connection this takes longer. Possible causes and fixes: A scope tab is hiding it. Select All , or Show all N results under Try instead . You typed only one character. Type at least two. Only 8 results are listed. Select View all results for \"…\" for the full list. A word in your query excluded it, or a quoted phrase is too strict. Remove it. Why: the Web tab needs a network connection and the site's web search service. What to do: check your connection and try again later, or search the site with All . Why: only six digit hex codes with a , and nothing else in the box, are read as a colour. fff , rebeccapurple or rgb ... are searched as text. What to do: type the full six digit form, for example ffffff . For other formats, use the Contrast Checker or the colour tools. Why: commands appear only when the page has the cont"},{"t":"Spotlight FAQ","d":"Short answers about Spotlight search.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/docs/faq.html","h":["What is the difference between Spotlight and the search page?","Does Spotlight work offline?","Can I search in Hindi?","Why does a result I open often move up?","Does Spotlight show ads?","What does Ctrl + Shift + K do?"],"x":" Spotlight is the quick box that floats over any page and shows up to 8 results. The search page at https://auricartisan.com/search/ shows every result with filters, previews and answers. View all results for \"…\" moves your query from one to the other. The search page is documented in Search ../../../search/README.md . Searching the site can work offline once you have prepared the offline version on the Download page, because the site's search index is part of it see Download and offline ../../../download and offline/README.md . Opening a result offline works only for pages that were saved. The Web tab always needs a connection. Commands can be found by their Hindi or English names. Page search matches the English text of pages, so English words give the best results. Spotlight gives a small boost to pages you have opened from search before, in this browser. It can show a compact sponsored strip while ads are running on the site. The Ads in panels & search setting controls it on plans that include ad preferences see Settings panel › Tooltips and ads ../../settings panel/docs/tooltips and ads.md . It opens the Feature Kit calculator, converter and other small tools , which is separa"},{"t":"Search and Spotlight: supporting material","d":"Contents of the Spotlight search supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Spotlight guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keys for opening and using Spotlight limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What Spotlight searches, how colour answers are computed, and limits related.md related.md The search page, tools and features Spotlight links to privacy.md privacy.md What Spotlight stores and what uses the network "},{"t":"Spotlight shortcuts","d":"Keys for opening and using Spotlight.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Action Ctrl + K Cmd + K on a Mac Open or close Spotlight Up / Down Move through results Enter Open the highlighted result or run the command Ctrl + Enter Cmd + Enter Open the highlighted result in a new tab Tab Next scope tab Shift + Tab Previous scope tab Esc Clear the box, then close Spotlight as the first character Command mode In some kits, Ctrl + K moves to the kit's own search field while that kit is open. See Kits ../../../kits/README.md and Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Spotlight glossary","d":"Terms used in the Spotlight search guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Spotlight The floating search box opened with Ctrl + K . Scope The part of the site a search covers: All, Pages, Tools, Docs, Learn or Web. Launcher A shortcut row shown when the search box is empty. Index The list of the site's pages and their words that Spotlight searches. Preview pane The panel beside the results showing details of the highlighted result or a colour answer. Field filter A prefix such as title: that limits a search to one part of each page. Exclusion A word with a minus sign in front, such as gradient , which removes matching pages. Command mode The mode entered by typing , which lists actions instead of pages. Contrast ratio The WCAG measure of lightness difference between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1. AA, AAA WCAG contrast levels: AA body text needs 4.5:1, AAA needs 7:1, AA large text needs 3:1. OKLCH A way of writing a colour as lightness, chroma and hue that follows human perception closely. "},{"t":"Spotlight limits and accuracy","d":"What Spotlight searches, how its colour answers are computed, and its limits.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is searched","Result limits","Colour answers","Language"],"x":" Spotlight searches the site's own search index: the titles, descriptions, tags, categories, addresses and text of the site's pages. It does not search inside your saved library items or inside tool results. The Web tab searches a curated set of trusted outside sources through the site's web search service, not the whole web. Scopes are decided by page address: Tools is every page under /tool/ , Docs is under /library/documentation/ , Learn is under /library/learn/ , and Pages is everything else. Searches start at two characters. Spotlight lists up to 8 results; the full search page lists all of them. Up to six recent searches are kept. Web results are limited to 8. Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2 relative luminance formula and are shown to two decimal places. Only plus six hex digits is recognised as a colour. Colours are treated as sRGB. The pass and fail verdicts use the WCAG 2 thresholds: 4.5:1 for AA body text, 7:1 for AAA body text and 3:1 for AA large text. The answer is a quick reading, not an audit. For a page wide check, use the Analyzer. The index holds the English text of pages. Searching in Hindi finds commands, but page results depend on English words. "},{"t":"Spotlight privacy","d":"What Spotlight stores and what it sends over the network.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/privacy.html","h":["Stored in your browser","Uses the network"],"x":" Your last six searches the Recent list . Select Clear to delete them. A small record of which results you have opened from search, used only to rank those pages a little higher for you next time. Both stay in this browser and are not sent to Auric Artisan. Site searches run inside your browser against the site's search index, which is downloaded from auricartisan.com. Your query is not sent anywhere. Web searches send your query to the site's web search service to find matches in trusted outside sources. Opening a web result opens that outside website in a new tab. "},{"t":"Related to Spotlight","d":"The search page, tools and features related to Spotlight.","p":"Website › Site features › Search and Spotlight","u":"website/site-features/search-and-spotlight/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Search ../../../search/README.md — the full search page at https://auricartisan.com/search/. Contrast Checker ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — where colour answers lead. Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — a full accessibility audit of a page. Guide and page outline ../../guide and page outline/README.md — the guide has its own filter box for the current page. Context menu ../../context menu/README.md — Search the site and, for a selection, Search this site and Search the web . Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the Menu Kit and Status Kit have their own search fields. "},{"t":"Settings panel","d":"What the Settings panel is, how to open it, and what you can change with it on every page of Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Settings panel, titled Your Settings , is a floating panel that changes how the whole site looks and behaves for you. It holds your accent colour, theme, language and text size; comfort options such as reading mode, reduced motion and eye rest reminders; which info bars appear; how clocks show the time; how tooltips behave; ad preferences; and a list of keyboard shortcuts. Every change applies at once, on the page you are on and on every page you open afterwards. The panel keeps your choices in this browser, so they work without an account. If you have the site open in several tabs, a change in one tab is picked up by the others. You can also save all your settings to a file and load them again on another browser or device. The panel is modeless: it floats over the page without dimming it, so you can keep reading and clicking the page while it is open. You can drag it, widen it, collapse it to its title bar and close it. Everyone who uses the site: the defaults suit most people, and every choice can be undone. People who need larger text, stronger contrast, underlined links or less motion. People who prefer the site in Hindi, a 24 hour clock or a particular time zone. Anyone w"},{"t":"Settings panel guides","d":"Contents of the Settings panel guides, from opening the panel to backing up and resetting every setting.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Settings panel: how to open it and find your way around, how to change each group of settings, and how to back up, restore and reset them. The reference lists every control with its values and default. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the panel, a tour of its parts, and your first change change the appearance.md change the appearance.md Accent colour, saved colours, custom colours, theme, language and text size comfort options.md comfort options.md Reading mode, motion, transparency, contrast, links, cursor, eye rest and screen saver highlights and clock.md highlights and clock.md Which bars and notices appear, and how clocks show the time tooltips and ads.md tooltips and ads.md Tooltip detail levels and ad preferences back up restore and reset.md back up restore and reset.md Export and import a settings file, restore a section, reset everything, the panel's right click menu reference.md reference.md Every control, its values and its default troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Get started with the Settings panel","d":"Open the Settings panel, learn its parts, and make your first change.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the panel","A tour of the panel","Make your first change","Close the panel","Next steps"],"x":" Use whichever way is closest: Where you are What to do Anywhere, with a keyboard Press Ctrl + , Cmd + , on a Mac . Press it again to close the panel. Anywhere, with a mouse or touch Select the page utilities button at the bottom left of the screen, then Settings . Right clicking the page Choose Site , then Settings . Choose Keyboard shortcuts to open the Shortcuts section directly. In Spotlight search Press Ctrl + K , type , and choose Open settings . On the clock strip Right click the strip and select All settings . The panel opens on the Clock section. On an info bar Right click the bar and select Settings . The panel opens on the Comfort section. The page utilities bar is the launcher row that also holds the kits. It is described in Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/docs/page utilities bar.md and, in more depth, in Kits ../../../kits/README.md . The panel has four parts. 1. The title bar. It reads Your Settings . Drag it to move the panel; the position is remembered. On the right are four buttons: Focus mode — the pin style button shared with the kits. Its tooltip reads \"Keep Settings open through navigation and while opening other kits.\" Resize — switches betwe"},{"t":"Back up, restore and reset","d":"Export your settings to a file, import them on another browser, restore one section, reset everything, and use the panel's right-click menu.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/back-up-restore-and-reset.html","h":["Export your settings","Import settings from a file","Restore one section","Reset everything","Use the panel's right-click menu"],"x":" Your settings live in this browser only. Clearing the browser's site data, using a private window or switching to another browser starts you from the defaults. A settings file lets you carry them across. 1. Open the panel Ctrl + , . 2. Select Export in the footer. 3. Your browser downloads a file named auric settings.json . A message confirms \"Settings exported\". The file contains every setting in the panel, including your saved colours. It is plain JSON see Reference reference.md the settings file for its fields . It contains no account details. 1. Open the panel on the browser you want to set up. 2. Select Import in the footer. 3. Choose an auric settings.json file any .json file is accepted for selection . 4. The settings apply at once, including the theme. A message confirms \"Settings imported\". What happens to the file's contents: Only settings the panel knows are read. Anything else in the file is ignored. A setting missing from the file is set to its default. A value that is not allowed for example a text size that does not exist is replaced by that setting's default. If the file is not valid JSON, nothing changes and the message reads \"That file isn't valid settings\". If t"},{"t":"Change the appearance","d":"Recolour the site with an accent, keep saved colours, and choose the theme, language and text size.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/change-the-appearance.html","h":["Read the preview and the contrast readout","Choose a preset accent","Use any colour you like","Keep colours in Saved colors","Choose a theme","Choose a language","Change the text size","Restore the section"],"x":" The Appearance section controls the site's accent colour, theme, language and text size. It opens first whenever you open the panel. The accent is the site's highlight colour: the gold of links, active tabs, buttons, focus rings, kit launchers and tooltip borders. Changing it recolours all of those at once. At the top of the section are two live readouts. Preview live appearance shows a heading, an Accent chip, A link , a sample sentence and a Primary button drawn in your current accent, theme and text size. Accent accessibility live WCAG contrast shows two rows: Accent on background — the contrast between your accent and the page background of the current theme. Text on accent — the contrast between the accent and the text colour the site places on it. The site picks a dark or a light text colour automatically, whichever reads better. Each row shows a ratio such as 4.87:1 and a badge. Contrast ratio is the WCAG measure of how far apart two colours are in lightness, from 1:1 identical to 21:1 black on white . Badge Ratio Meaning AAA 7:1 or more Meets the strictest WCAG level for body text AA 4.5:1 or more Meets the standard WCAG level for body text AA Large 3:1 or more Meets WCAG "},{"t":"Comfort options","d":"Turn on reading mode, reduce motion and transparency, boost contrast, underline links, turn off the custom cursor, and schedule eye rest and the screen saver.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/comfort-options.html","h":["Reading mode","Reduce motion","Reduce transparency","Boost contrast","Underline links","Custom cursor","Eye-rest reminders","Screen saver","Restore the section"],"x":" The Comfort section holds switches that make the site easier to read and calmer to use. Each switch takes effect at once and applies to every page. Open it with Ctrl + , , then select Comfort . Reading mode gives a distraction free layout with comfortable typography. While it is on: floating chrome is hidden: the kit launchers, the right edge menu strip, the info bars and the clock strip; the custom cursor is replaced by your system cursor; the main text sits in a narrower, centred column with larger type and more generous line spacing; the header no longer sticks to the top of the screen; a thin bar across the very top of the window fills as you scroll down the page; a Reading mode ✕ chip appears near the bottom of the screen. Select it to leave reading mode. Ways to switch it on or off: the Reading mode switch in Comfort; Alt + R anywhere on the site not while typing in a field ; right click the page, choose View , then Reading mode or Leave reading mode ; on card pages home, collections, blog, changelog, documentation, learn , right click a card and select the Reading pill. A short message \"Reading mode on\" or \"Reading mode off\" confirms a change made from the right click menu."},{"t":"Highlights and clock","d":"Choose which info bars, notices and demo chips appear, and set how the site's clocks show the time and date.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/highlights-and-clock.html","h":["Highlights: bars, notices and chips","Clock: time and date display"],"x":" The Highlights section decides which extra strips and labels appear around page content. The bars themselves are described in Info bars and notices ../../info bars and notices/README.md . Switch What it shows Default Live demo chips The highlighted \"live / demo\" chips above demo sections On Welcome bar The rotating welcome bar above the page Homepage only Announcement bar The site announcements bar Homepage only Quick links bar The quick links bar documentation, changelog, timeline, blog, learn Homepage only Clock strip A live clock, date and time zone above every page Off Hero notice The highlighted notice banner on the homepage hero On The Welcome, Announcement and Quick links bars start in a third state: shown on the homepage only. In that state the switch appears on. Switch it off to hide that bar everywhere, including the homepage. Switch it on again to show that bar above every page, not only the homepage. To get back to \"homepage only\", select Restore section defaults . The Quick links bar also shows by default at the foot of the Collections page, where it is part of the layout. Each bar, the hero notice and each demo chip has its own ✕ button. Selecting it has the same eff"},{"t":"Tooltips and ads","d":"Turn the site's tooltips off or change how much they show, and adjust ad preferences on paid plans.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/tooltips-and-ads.html","h":["Tooltips","Ads"],"x":" Most buttons, links and cards on the site show a tooltip when you hover over them or move keyboard focus to them: a small card with a title, a description and sometimes a picture, tags, a keyboard shortcut and extra details. The Tooltips section starts with a Live preview how tooltips will look . It shows a sample tooltip for the Design System Generator with a picture, three tags, a description, the Ctrl + K shortcut and a details table, and it changes as you flip the switches below it. Switch What it does Default Show tooltips Shows the rich hover and focus tooltips across the site. Off hides them; the preview reads \"Tooltips are turned off\". On Detailed tooltips Expands the collapsible details: preview image, metadata and tags. Off keeps tooltips compact: title, description and shortcut. On Advanced tooltips Always expands the data section category, route, read time . Off keeps it collapsed. Off With Advanced tooltips off, a tooltip that has extra data shows an Alt — More details hint at its foot. While the tooltip is open, press Alt to expand the data section for that tooltip only. The next tooltip starts collapsed again. Restore section defaults returns the three switches to t"},{"t":"Settings panel reference","d":"Every control in the Settings panel, with what it does, its values and its default, plus the settings file format and messages.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/reference.html","h":["Panel frame","Appearance","Comfort","Highlights","Clock","Tooltips","Ads","Shortcuts","The settings file","Messages"],"x":" All settings apply immediately, are kept in this browser, and are shared by every tab of the site you have open. Control What it does Title Your Settings Drag to move the panel. The position is remembered. Focus mode Kit style focus button. Tooltip: \"Keep Settings open through navigation and while opening other kits.\" Resize Switches between normal width and a wider panel up to 980 px . The choice is remembered. Minimize / Restore Collapses the panel to its title bar. Select the bar or the button to restore. Close settings X Closes the panel. Focus returns to the control that opened it. Section list Appearance, Comfort, Highlights, Clock, Tooltips, Ads, Shortcuts, each with a control count Export Downloads auric settings.json Import Loads a settings file Reset all Resets every setting after a confirmation saved colours are kept Ctrl , hint Reminder of the open and close shortcut Control What it does Values Default Preview Live sample of heading, accent chip, link, text and button Read only — Accent on background WCAG contrast of the accent against the page background Ratio and badge — Text on accent WCAG contrast of the automatic text colour on the accent Ratio and badge — Shade s"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Settings panel","d":"Fixes for common problems with the Settings panel and the settings it controls.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["My settings are gone","Ctrl + , does nothing","The Alt shortcuts do nothing","A change in one tab did not reach another tab","My theme, accent or text size changed after I opened a link","The Ads controls are greyed out","I cannot find the Ads section","The Eyedropper button is missing","The + button next to my custom colour is disabled","The Settings panel does not stay open when I move to another page","Import says \"That file isn't valid settings\"","After Reset all my saved colours are still there","A bar I switched on shows on every page, not just the homepage"],"x":" Why: settings are kept in this browser's local storage. They are lost when you clear site data or cookies for auricartisan.com, when you use a private or incognito window which forgets everything when it closes , or when you open the site in a different browser or on another device. What to do: set them again, or import a settings file you exported earlier Import in the panel footer . Export a file now so you have a copy next time. Why: the panel loads a moment after the page. A shortcut pressed while the page is still loading can be missed. Some browser extensions also claim Ctrl + , . What to do: wait until the page has finished loading and try again, or open the panel from the page utilities bar at the bottom left Settings . Why: Alt + R , Alt + T , Alt + M , Alt + + , Alt + and Alt + 0 are ignored while your cursor is in a text field, so they cannot interfere with typing. They are also ignored when Ctrl or Cmd is held. What to do: click an empty part of the page first, then press the shortcut. Why: other open tabs pick up a change when the browser tells them about it. This works in normal windows but not between a normal window and a private window, which keep separate storage"},{"t":"Settings panel FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Settings panel.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account to use Settings?","Do my settings follow me to another device?","Does the accent colour change the colours inside the tools?","Why is the default gold darker in the light theme?","What is the difference between Restore section defaults and Reset all?","Is language included in an exported settings file?","Can I open the panel on a specific section?","Does Reduce motion affect the custom cursor?","Why does the panel look different on my phone?"],"x":" No. Every setting works signed out and is kept in this browser. The only exception is the Ads section, whose controls need a paid plan. Not automatically. Export them with Export and load the file on the other device with Import . No. The accent recolours the site's interface: links, buttons, focus rings, tabs, kit launchers and tooltip borders. Colours you are working with in a tool, and colours shown in libraries, are not changed. Plain gold on a near white page has too little contrast to read comfortably, so the light theme uses a darker gold for the default accent. Colours you pick yourself are used as chosen. The Accent accessibility readout shows how your accent performs. Restore section defaults resets only the section you are in. Reset all resets every section after asking you to confirm. Neither removes your saved colours. No. The language is kept separately. Choose it again on the new browser, or open any page with ?lang=hi added to its address see Language ../../language/README.md . Yes, from a few places: the right click menu's Keyboard shortcuts opens Shortcuts, the clock strip's All settings opens Clock, and an info bar's Settings opens Comfort. No. The custom cursor"},{"t":"Settings panel: supporting material","d":"Contents of the Settings panel's supporting files: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the background material for the Settings panel: the terms it uses, its keyboard shortcuts, what its contrast readout measures, where to go next, what it stores, and when it changed. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the panel and its guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts that open the panel or change settings limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the accent contrast readout measures, and other limits related.md related.md Related site features, kits and pages privacy.md privacy.md What the panel stores and where release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the settings controls "},{"t":"Settings panel shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts that open the Settings panel, move around it, and change settings from anywhere on the site.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Anywhere on the site","Inside the panel"],"x":" Keys Action Ctrl + , Cmd + , on a Mac Open or close the Settings panel Alt + R Turn reading mode on or off Alt + T Switch theme: Light, then Dark, then System Alt + + Make text one step larger Alt + Make text one step smaller Alt + 0 Return text to the default size Alt + M Turn reduced motion on or off The Alt shortcuts are ignored while you type in a text field. Keys Action Left / Right arrow on the section list Move to the previous or next section Tab / Shift + Tab Move between controls Space or Enter on a switch or button Change it Esc Close an open drop down list first, then the panel Esc in the Reset all confirmation Cancel the reset Tab in the Reset all confirmation Stays inside the confirmation until you choose For every shortcut on the site, see Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Settings panel glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Settings panel.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Accent The site's highlight colour for links, buttons, active tabs, focus rings, kit launchers and tooltip borders. Gold by default. Contrast ratio The WCAG measure of how different two colours are in lightness, from 1:1 none to 21:1 black on white . WCAG The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, the international standard for accessible web content. AA, AAA WCAG contrast levels for body text: AA needs 4.5:1, the stricter AAA needs 7:1. AA Large A contrast of at least 3:1, accepted by WCAG for large text and interface parts but not body text. Eyedropper A browser tool that lets you click any pixel on your screen to read its colour. Hex colour A colour written as and six hexadecimal digits for red, green and blue, for example D3AF37 . Local storage A small store inside your browser where a website keeps data on your device. Modeless A panel that does not block the page behind it. You can keep using the page while it is open. Reading mode A distraction free layout with a narrow text column, larger type and no floating controls. Saved colors Your own palette of up to 18 accent colours, added only when you select the + button. Section One of the groups in the panel's list"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the accent contrast readout measures, how precise it is, and other limits of the Settings panel.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The accent contrast readout","The shade strip","Storage and scope"],"x":" Formula. Both rows use the WCAG 2 relative luminance contrast formula, and the badges use the WCAG 2 thresholds 7:1, 4.5:1, 3:1 . Accent on background compares your accent with the background colour of the page you are on, read from the page itself. On a page with a coloured or image background under a particular block, the real contrast in that block can differ. Text on accent compares your accent with the text colour the site places on it. The site chooses between a very dark and a very light text colour, whichever gives more contrast. Precision. Ratios are shown to two decimal places. Colours are treated as sRGB with no transparency. The readout is a guide for choosing an accent, not a certified accessibility audit. For a full check of a page, use the Analyzer or the Contrast Checker tools. The seven shades are three darker steps, your accent itself in the middle, and three lighter steps, made by mixing the accent towards black or towards white in sRGB. They are not a perceptual OKLCH ramp; use the site's shade and design tools for that. Settings are kept per browser and per device. They are not synced to your account. A private window starts from the defaults and forgets its c"},{"t":"Settings panel privacy","d":"What the Settings panel stores, where, and what it sends over the network.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays on your device","What uses the network","Links can carry settings","Removing your settings"],"x":" Every setting in the panel, including your saved colours, is kept in your browser's local storage for auricartisan.com. The panel's position and size are kept the same way. Nothing is sent to Auric Artisan when you change a setting. The settings work signed out and are not attached to an account. Export creates a file on your own device. It contains only your settings. Opening the Ads section checks your plan in the background, to decide whether the ad controls are unlocked. If you are signed in, this uses your existing session. Choosing हिन्दी downloads the Hindi dictionaries for the pages you visit see Language ../../language/README.md . If you copy a page link from the site, it can include your appearance settings that differ from the defaults for example your accent and text size , so the person you send it to sees the page as you do. See Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md for what a link contains and how to share a clean one. Reset all in the panel returns everything to the defaults saved colours are kept until you remove them . Clearing site data for auricartisan.com in your browser removes all stored settings. The site's full policies are on https://auricartisa"},{"t":"Settings panel release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Settings panel, taken from the public changelog.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" The site's changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ records releases. Entries that concern the settings controls: Date Release Change 2026 06 05 v0.9.9 Added user settings controls, alongside guide content, PWA app support and the UX Kit. 2026 05 02 v0.9.8 Added complexity management, which lets you control how many advanced tools the site shows through the Advanced Kit . The panel as documented here seven sections, saved colours, the accent contrast readout, the Custom cursor switch, the Highlights section and the panel's right click menu reflects the site as of September 2026. Later changes appear in the changelog. "},{"t":"Related to the Settings panel","d":"Site features, kits and tools that work with the Settings panel.","p":"Website › Site features › Settings panel","u":"website/site-features/settings-panel/others/related.html","h":["Features the panel controls","Other ways in","Tools for checking colour properly"],"x":" Theme ../../theme/README.md — light, dark and system themes and every other way to switch them. Language ../../language/README.md — English and Hindi. Eye rest ../../eye rest/README.md — the reminders scheduled in Comfort. Screen saver ../../screen saver/README.md — the idle screen scheduled in Comfort. Custom cursor ../../custom cursor/README.md — the pointer switched in Comfort. Info bars and notices ../../info bars and notices/README.md — the bars, notices, chips and clock strip switched in Highlights. Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — reading mode and the other comfort settings, alongside the site's other aids. Context menu ../../context menu/README.md — Site › Settings and Keyboard shortcuts . Search and Spotlight ../../search and spotlight/README.md — the command Open settings . Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/README.md — the page utilities bar and the mobile drawer's theme and language switches. Kits ../../../kits/README.md — the floating kits share the panel's title bar controls and follow your accent colour. Contrast Checker ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — check any two colours. Analyzer ../../.."},{"t":"Shareable links","d":"What the address bar remembers about the page you are on, how to share an exact view, and the other link options the site understands.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" As you use a page on auricartisan.com, the site quietly keeps the page's state in the address bar, after p= : how far you have scrolled, what you have typed or chosen in the page's fields, which tabs and toggles are selected, which panels are open, and your appearance settings where they differ from the defaults. Reload the page and it comes back as you left it. Copy the address and send it, and the other person sees the same view. The site also understands a few other additions to an address: ?lang=hi opens a page in Hindi, ?color= opens a colour inspector over any page, and split= restores a split view. Anyone who wants a reload to keep their place and their inputs. People sharing a specific tool setup, a scroll position in a long article or a filled in form. Teachers and support staff pointing someone to an exact view. It works on its own on every page. To copy the current address, use your browser's address bar, Copy link in the navigation dock, or Copy URL in the right click menu. 1. Open a tool, for example https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/, and change a few inputs. 2. Scroll down a little. After a moment the address gains a p= part. 3. Reload the page. Your inputs "},{"t":"Shareable links guides","d":"Contents of the shareable links guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md What the page remembers in its address, how it restores, and how to share or clear it other link options.md other link options.md ?lang= , ?color= and split= reference.md reference.md Exactly what is and is not saved in a link troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with shareable links","d":"How the page keeps its state in the address, how that state is restored, and how to share or clear it.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/getting-started.html","h":["What happens as you work","What comes back when you open the address","Share an exact view","Share a clean link","Pages that use their own #"],"x":" On every page, about a third of a second after you scroll, type or change a control, the site updates the address in your browser's address bar. It adds p= followed by a short code that describes the page's state. For example: text https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/ p=eyJ2IjoxLCJ5IjoxNjkwLCJ4IjowfQ The code is not secret or encrypted: it is the page's state written compactly. The update replaces the current address rather than adding a new entry, so it does not fill your Back button with steps. When you are at the top of the page and have changed nothing, the address stays clean, with no p= . When you reload the page or open the address later, the site restores the state in this order: 1. Panels that were open the Settings panel and the Feature, Menu, Advanced and Status Kits open again. 2. Tool specific state is applied, on tools that save their own. 3. Field values are put back, and the page recalculates as if you had typed them. 4. Selected tabs and toggles are selected again. 5. The page scrolls back to where you were. Some parts of a page load late, such as kits and tool panels; the site keeps trying for a few seconds until they are ready. 1. Set up the page the way y"},{"t":"Other link options","d":"Add ?lang=, ?color= or #split= to an address to open a page in a language, inspect a colour, or restore a split view.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/other-link-options.html","h":["Open a page in Hindi or English: ?lang=","Inspect a colour over any page: ?color=","Restore a split view: #split=","Search: /search/?q="],"x":" Add ?lang=hi to any page address to open it in Hindi, or ?lang=en for English. The browser that opens the link remembers the choice for later visits. text https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/?lang=hi If the address already contains ? , use &lang=hi . See Language ../../language/README.md . Add ?color= and a colour to any page address, and a floating colour inspector opens over that page with a full reading of the colour. text https://auricartisan.com/?color=CEA1B5 https://auricartisan.com/library/palette/?colour=%23d3af37&on=ffffff Parameter names: color , colour or hex for the colour; on , bg , against or vs for a background to compare it with. Colour formats: hex with or without 3, 4, 6 or 8 digits; must be written %23 in an address , a CSS colour name such as rebeccapurple , or a CSS colour function such as oklch … , lab … or rgb … . Short or partial hex still works: ?color=CEA is read as a colour. Several colours: separate them with or ; or , when no colour function is used . The inspector reports contrast against the page it opens on unless you give a background with on= . The inspector itself is part of the colour tools; see Basic colour tools ../../../tools/colour worksp"},{"t":"Shareable links reference","d":"Exactly what is and is not saved in a page's address, and how it is restored.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/reference.html","h":["Saved after #p=","Not saved","Timing and size","When it does not write","Other parameters"],"x":" Item Detail Scroll position Vertical and horizontal; not saved when within 4 pixels of the top left Text, number and other input fields Their values, in the page's main content and in the Settings panel Drop down lists and text areas Their values Checkboxes and radio buttons On or off Tabs, toggles and pressed buttons Which are selected Editable text areas Their text Open panels Settings panel, Feature Kit, Menu Kit, Advanced Kit, Status Kit Appearance settings Only those that differ from their defaults: accent, theme mode, text size, comfort switches, eye rest, screen saver, clock format, seconds, date and date format Tool state On tools that save their own extra state Only controls that have an identity on the page an id or a name can be saved. Item Why Passwords Never recorded File choosers Files cannot be put in a link Search boxes Excluded Hidden fields and buttons Not user input Disabled controls Not in use Areas a page marks as private Excluded by the page Controls outside the main content other than Settings Out of scope Language Use ?lang= instead Behaviour Value Update delay About 0.34 seconds after a change History Replaces the current entry; adds no Back steps Maximum "},{"t":"Troubleshooting shareable links","d":"Fixes for common problems with page links and their saved state.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The link opened but my inputs were not restored","Opening a link changed my theme, accent or text size","A panel opened by itself when I loaded a page","The address changes as I scroll","I want a link without the extra part","?color= did not open the inspector"],"x":" Possible causes and fixes: The field has no identity on the page, so it cannot be saved. Nothing can be done from your side. It was a password, file or search field, which are never saved. The state was too long over about 3,600 characters , so only the scroll position and open panels were kept. The page uses its own part, so no p= was added. Use the tool's own sharing option if it has one. The page had not finished loading when the link was copied. Wait a moment after your last change before copying. Why: the link carried the sender's appearance settings that differ from the defaults. What to do: change them back in Settings, or use Restore section defaults in Appearance. Why: the address had a p= part recorded while that panel was open. What to do: close the panel. The address updates and it will not reopen. That is the page saving your position. It does not add steps to your Back button. Scroll to the top and undo your changes before copying, or delete everything from p= onwards. Why: the value is not a colour the site can read, or the was not written as %23 . What to do: write the hex without ?color=d3af37 or as %23d3af37 . "},{"t":"Shareable links FAQ","d":"Short answers about page links and their saved state.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the #p= part sent to Auric Artisan?","Is it encrypted?","Can I turn it off?","Does it work offline?","Does it include what I saved in my library?"],"x":" No. Browsers do not send the part of an address after to the website. It is read by the page in the browser that opens it. No. It is the page's state written compactly. Anyone who has the link can read what it contains. There is no switch for it. It only affects the address; it does not store anything elsewhere. Share a clean link if you prefer. Yes, for pages that are saved on your device: reloading restores the state without a connection. No. It includes what is on the page, not your saved library items. "},{"t":"Shareable links: supporting material","d":"Contents of the shareable links supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the shareable links guides related.md related.md Features that copy or use links privacy.md privacy.md What a link can reveal and how to share safely "},{"t":"Shareable links glossary","d":"Terms used in the shareable links guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Address URL The web address shown in the browser's address bar. Fragment The part of an address after . Browsers keep it on your device and do not send it to the site. Query parameter A part of an address after ? , such as ?lang=hi , which the page reads. Page state The scroll position, inputs, selections and open panels of a page. p= The fragment in which the site keeps a page's state. Restore Putting a page back into the state its address describes. Clean link An address without the p= part. "},{"t":"Shareable links privacy","d":"What a copied page link can reveal, and how to share one safely.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Stays in the address. The page state is kept only in the address bar of your browser tab. It is not stored elsewhere and, because it follows , it is not sent to Auric Artisan when the page loads. Travels with the link. When you copy and share the address, the state goes with it: what you typed into the page's fields except passwords and search boxes , your selections, open panels, your scroll position, and your appearance settings that differ from the defaults. Readable by anyone with the link. The state is written compactly, not encrypted. Browser history. The latest state of each page can appear in your browser history and bookmarks, like any address. To share safely, share a clean link: scroll to the top and undo changes, or delete everything from p= onwards. "},{"t":"Related to shareable links","d":"Features that copy, share or read page links.","p":"Website › Site features › Shareable links","u":"website/site-features/shareable-links/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md — Copy link and Share . Context menu ../../context menu/README.md — Copy page URL , Copy as Markdown link and Share page… . Split view ../../split view/README.md — split= addresses. Language ../../language/README.md — ?lang= . Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — the appearance settings a link can carry. Basic colour tools ../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — the colour inspector opened by ?color= . "},{"t":"Split view","d":"Show two pages of Auric Artisan side by side, each fully working and responsive, with per-pane theme, viewport and zoom.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Split view shows two pages side by side or one above the other in the same browser tab. The left pane, the live pane, is a working copy of the page you were on, scrolled to where you were. The right pane, the companion , can show any other page: a tool next to its documentation, two palettes, or the same page in light and dark. Both panes are complete, working pages, and each one behaves like a real window: make a pane narrow and the page inside it switches to its phone layout. Each pane has its own Back, Forward, Reload and address bar, and its own theme, device width and zoom. A toolbar across the top lets you change the layout, swap the panes, overlay them in Compare mode to see differences, sync their scrolling, send links from one pane to the other, and watch live performance numbers. The address of the page changes as you work, so you can copy it and share the exact split. Your original page keeps running untouched behind split view. When you close it, you are back where you were, or on the page the live pane moved to. Designers checking a page or palette in light and dark, or at desktop and phone width, at the same time. Developers comparing two versions of a page. Learners"},{"t":"Split view guides","d":"Contents of the split view guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open split view, a tour of the toolbar, and closing panes and controls.md panes and controls.md Pane tabs, history buttons, address bars, and each pane's More menu layout compare and sync.md layout compare and sync.md Layout, swap, divider, compare, mirror, route links, scroll sync and performance share a split.md share a split.md Copy and restore a split from its address reference.md reference.md Every control, value and shortcut troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with split view","d":"Open split view, learn its toolbar, and close it again.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open split view","The screen","Close split view","Next steps"],"x":" How What opens Ctrl + Shift + D Live pane: this page. Companion: your last companion page, or the homepage Navigation dock › Open split view The same Right click › View › Split view The same Alt + click a link to another site page Live pane: this page. Companion: the page the link points to The first time, split view takes a moment to load. The live pane opens scrolled to where you were on the page. Split view covers the whole window: Toolbar across the top, in three groups: the live pane's controls its tab, Back , Forward , Reload , address bar and More menu ; the companion pane's controls the same set ; the global controls: the performance chip, Toggle layout , Swap panes , Compare , Mirror , Route links , Scroll sync , Equal split and Close . Two panes below it, with a divider between them that you can drag. On windows narrower than about 900 pixels, the toolbar wraps: each pane's controls take a full row. Your original page stays behind split view and keeps running; nothing on it is changed. Press Esc if a pane's More menu is open, the first Esc closes the menu; if you are editing an address bar, the first Esc puts back the address . Or select Close at the right end of the too"},{"t":"Layout, compare and sync","d":"Change the split layout, resize and swap panes, compare pages visually, sync scrolling, route links and watch performance.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/layout-compare-and-sync.html","h":["Side by side or stacked","Resize the panes","Swap the panes","Maximise one pane","Compare two pages","Mirror","Route links","Scroll sync","Performance chip"],"x":" These are the global controls at the right of the split view toolbar. Select Toggle layout or press Alt + V to switch between panes side by side and panes one above the other. Drag the divider between the panes. A badge follows the pointer showing the split as two percentages, for example \"62 38\". The divider snaps when you pass near 25%, 33%, 50%, 66% or 75%. A pane cannot be made smaller than 80 pixels. Double click the divider, select Equal split , or press Alt + E to return to 50 50. The sizes you choose are remembered separately for side by side and stacked layouts. Select Swap panes or press Alt + S . The panes trade places; both pages keep running, with nothing reloaded. Use Maximize in a pane's More menu to give it the whole area, and select it again to restore. Compare overlays the two panes and highlights what differs: 1. Load the two pages you want to compare, for example the same page with one pane in light theme and the other in dark, or two palettes. 2. Select Compare . 3. A note appears: \"Compare mode — matching areas go dark, differences light up. Scroll is synced.\" Areas where the two pages are identical turn black; anything different shows in colour. Scroll sync "},{"t":"Panes and their controls","d":"Use each pane's tab, history buttons, address bar and More menu for theme, viewport, zoom, focus and more.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/panes-and-controls.html","h":["The pane tab","Back, Forward and Reload","The address bar","The More menu","Keyboard inside a pane"],"x":" Each pane has the same row of controls in the toolbar. The tab at the start of each row names the pane: by default the page's own title for example \"Basic Tools\" . A dot shows its state: amber and pulsing while the page loads, green when it is ready. Rename a pane: double click its tab, type a name and press Enter or click elsewhere . Press Esc to cancel. An empty name returns to the page title. Your name stays on the pane while you browse in it, until you close split view. Each pane has its own history. Back and Forward move through the pages that pane has shown; Reload reloads just that pane. Each pane has an address bar showing its page's address on the site, for example /library/palette/ . To load another page: 1. Select the address bar. A list of destinations opens, grouped under Home , Tools , Libraries , Account , Company , Legal and your Recent pages. 2. Type to narrow the list: page names, addresses and keywords all match for example oklch finds the Colour Science Lab . 3. Use Up and Down to choose and Enter to load, or click an entry. You can also type an address that is not in the list: a site path such as /tool/icon/ the list offers Go to that path or a full https:// a"},{"t":"Share a split","d":"Copy the address of a split view and reopen it, with both pages, the layout and each pane's settings.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/share-a-split.html","h":["Share or bookmark a split","Things to know"],"x":" While split view is open, the browser's address bar keeps a description of the split after split= . It records: the live pane's page and the companion pane's page, including where each is scrolled and what you entered on them; side by side or stacked layout; the divider position; each pane's theme, viewport and zoom; whether the panes are swapped. 1. Set up split view the way you want it. 2. Copy the address from your browser's address bar or bookmark it . 3. Open the address later, or send it to someone. Result: the page opens straight into split view, with both panes, the layout and the pane settings restored. The address updates as you work, including as you scroll either pane. Pane names you typed are not part of the address. Closing split view removes the split details from the address. Copy URL in a pane's More menu copies only that pane's page, without the split. A shared split contains the addresses of both pages and the values entered on them. Check it before sending it to someone. "},{"t":"Split view reference","d":"Every split view control, value, default, shortcut and message.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/reference.html","h":["Pane controls (one set per pane)","More menu","Global controls","Divider","Keyboard","Performance panel","Recent destinations"],"x":" Control Label Action Tab Live view / Companion Page title and load state; double click to rename Back Back History back in this pane Forward Forward History forward in this pane Reload Reload Reloads this pane Address bar Live pane URL / Companion URL Type or choose a destination; Enter loads, Ctrl + Enter opens a new tab More three dots More pane controls Opens the menu below Control Values Default Theme Auto, Light, Dark Auto Viewport Desktop, Tablet 820 px , Phone 400 px Desktop Zoom 100%, 125%, 150%, 75% cycles in that order 100% Focus this pane On, off Off Maximize On, off Off Open in new tab — — Copy URL — — Control Label tooltip Action Key Performance chip Performance metrics Shows FPS; hover for details; click to pin — Layout Toggle layout Side by side or stacked Alt + V Swap Swap panes Trade sides Alt + S Compare Compare Overlay and highlight differences — Mirror Mirror Load the live page into the companion — Route links Route links Live pane links open in the companion — Scroll sync Scroll sync Mirror scrolling between panes — Equal split Equal split Reset to 50 / 50 Alt + E Close Close Exit split view Esc Behaviour Value Snap points 25%, 33%, 50%, 66%, 75% Minimum pane "},{"t":"Troubleshooting split view","d":"Fixes for common split view problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Ctrl + Shift + D does nothing, or bookmarks the page","An outside website shows as a blank pane","A pane is slow or the page stutters","Closing split view took me to a different page","The Theme control shows Auto but the pane is not following my theme","Compare shows everything in colour","A shared split opened as a normal page"],"x":" Why: in some browsers Ctrl + Shift + D also means \"bookmark all tabs\". Split view claims the shortcut once the page has loaded; pressed too early, the browser may act on it instead. What to do: wait for the page to finish loading, or use Open split view in the navigation dock. Why: many websites do not allow themselves to be shown inside another page. External pages that do load are not controlled by split view, so the pane's theme, zoom and history buttons may not affect them. What to do: use Open in new tab from the pane's More menu. Why: two full pages are running at once. What to do: let eco mode switch on, close heavy tools in one pane, or use a smaller viewport. The performance chip shows what is happening. Why: you loaded another page in the live pane. Closing follows the live pane. What to do: use your browser's Back button to return. Why: switching a pane back to Auto reloads it. If the reload has not finished, wait a moment. Why: the two pages differ everywhere, for example because they are scrolled to different places or use different themes on purpose. What to do: load the same page in both panes Mirror , then change one thing, such as the theme, to see just that diffe"},{"t":"Split view FAQ","d":"Short answers about split view.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the live pane a screenshot?","Does split view change my page?","Can I see a page at phone width?","Can I compare light and dark?","Can I have more than two panes?","Does split view work on a phone?"],"x":" No. It is the real page, fully working, in its own window area. You can click, type and scroll in it. No. Your original page keeps running untouched behind split view. Yes. Set the pane's Viewport to phone 400 pixels in its More menu. The page reflows as it would on a phone. Yes. Use Mirror so both panes show the same page, then set one pane's Theme to Light and the other to Dark. Compare then highlights every difference. No. Split view shows two panes. It opens, but two pages on a small screen are cramped. It is designed for larger windows. "},{"t":"Split view: supporting material","d":"Contents of the split view supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the split view guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Split view keyboard shortcuts related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What split view stores and puts in the address release notes.md release notes.md User facing history "},{"t":"Split view shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts for split view.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Action Ctrl + Shift + D Open or close split view Esc Close an open More menu; otherwise close split view Alt + 1 Focus the live pane Alt + 2 Focus the companion pane Alt + V Side by side or stacked Alt + S Swap panes Alt + E Equal split Alt + click on a link Open the link in the other pane; with split view closed, open split view with it Enter in an address bar Load the address or highlighted destination Ctrl + Enter in an address bar Open the typed address in a new browser tab Esc in an address bar Close the destination list, then restore the address See Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md for the whole site. "},{"t":"Split view glossary","d":"Terms used in the split view guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Live pane The pane that starts with the page you were on. Closing split view follows it. Companion pane The second pane, for any other page. Divider The bar between the panes that you drag to resize them. Viewport The width a pane's page is laid out for: desktop, tablet 820 px or phone 400 px . Responsive A page that rearranges itself to fit the width it is given. Compare mode An overlay of both panes in which identical areas turn black and differences show. Route links A mode in which links clicked in the live pane open in the companion. Scroll sync Scrolling one pane scrolls the other to the same relative position. Eco mode Automatic low performance mode that turns off decorative effects when the panes run slowly. FPS Frames per second: how smoothly the screen is updating. "},{"t":"Split view privacy","d":"What split view stores and what it writes into the page address.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Stored in your browser: your recent pane destinations up to 10 site pages and the divider sizes. In the address bar: while open, the address describes both panes, including each page's remembered state scroll position and values entered . Anyone you send the address to sees those pages and values. Not sent anywhere: split view runs entirely in your browser. Opening an external address in a pane loads that website directly, as a normal visit would. Performance readings are measured in your browser and shown only to you. "},{"t":"Split view release notes","d":"User-facing history of split view, from the public changelog.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" Date Release Change 2026 04 19 v0.9.75 Fixed split screen issues with the address, refresh, resizing, embedded content and window close. Split view as documented here, with a live mirror pane and a companion pane, named pane tabs, the More menu, Compare mode, performance readings and shareable split addresses, reflects the site as of September 2026. See https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ for later changes. "},{"t":"Related to split view","d":"Features related to split view.","p":"Website › Site features › Split view","u":"website/site-features/split-view/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../navigation dock/README.md — Open split view . Context menu ../../context menu/README.md — View › Split view . Theme ../../theme/README.md — the site theme, and per pane themes. Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md — the page state each pane keeps in its address. Screen recorder ../../screen recorder/README.md — record both panes with This tab . "},{"t":"Theme","d":"The site's light, dark and system themes, and every place you can switch between them.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan has a light theme and a dark theme. A third choice, System called Auto in the mobile drawer , follows your device: when your operating system switches between light and dark, the site switches with it, even on a page that is already open. System is the default. You can change the theme from several places: the sun and moon button in the header, the Settings panel, the mobile drawer, a keyboard shortcut, the right click menu, Spotlight's commands and the card menu. They all change the same setting, which applies to every page in this browser and to every open tab. The site also applies your theme before the page is drawn, so a page does not flash the wrong theme as it loads. Some panels can override the theme for themselves: each kit has its own light and dark button, and each pane of split view can be forced light or dark. These do not change the site's theme. Everyone. Dark suits low light and long sessions; light suits bright rooms, printing and checking colours against white. When you compare colours or contrast, it can help to check them in both. The sun or moon button at the right of the header. Settings › Appearance › Theme Ctrl + , . The mobile drawer › Prefer"},{"t":"Theme guides","d":"Contents of the theme guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The three theme modes and how System works every way to switch.md every way to switch.md The header, Settings, drawer, keyboard, right click menu, Spotlight, card menu, kits and split view reference.md reference.md Every theme control and how they interact troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with themes","d":"Understand the light, dark and system theme modes and choose one.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/getting-started.html","h":["The three modes","Choose a mode","How System mode follows your device","What the header button does to System mode","What changes with the theme"],"x":" Mode What you see Light Light pages with dark text, always Dark Dark pages with light text, always System Auto in the drawer Light or dark to match your device's setting, changing when it changes System is the default for a new visitor. 1. Press Ctrl + , to open Settings. Appearance is selected. 2. Under Theme , select Light , Dark or System . The page changes at once, and every other page and open tab follows. With System selected, the site asks your browser whether your device is set to dark mode, and uses dark if it is. When the device switches for example on a schedule at sunset , the site switches too, without a reload. Where to change your device's setting: Windows: Settings › Personalisation › Colours › Choose your mode. macOS: System Settings › Appearance. Android: Settings › Display › Dark theme. iOS and iPadOS: Settings › Display & Brightness. The header's sun and moon button always switches to the opposite of what you see now, and makes that choice fixed. If you were on System and the page was dark, selecting the sun sets the theme to Light , and the Settings panel moves from System to Light . To follow your device again, choose System in Settings or Auto in the drawer."},{"t":"Every way to switch the theme","d":"All the places you can change the theme, and how each one behaves.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/every-way-to-switch.html","h":["Header button","Settings panel","Mobile drawer","Keyboard","Right-click menu","Spotlight command","Card menu","A kit's own theme button","A split-view pane"],"x":" All of these change the same site wide setting, except the last two, which affect only one panel. The sun or moon at the right of the header tooltip Theme : \"Switch between light and dark mode\" . It shows a moon while the page is light select it to go dark and a sun while the page is dark. It always switches to the opposite of what you see, and fixes that choice it leaves System mode . Settings Ctrl + , › Appearance › Theme : Light , Dark , System . This is the only place, with the drawer, that can set System . On narrow screens, open the drawer and use Preferences › Theme : Auto , Light , Dark . Auto is the same as System . The highlighted button shows your current choice. Alt + T anywhere on the site not while typing in a field moves one step through Light , Dark and System , in that order, and shows a message such as \"Theme: Dark\". Right click the page, open View , and choose Switch theme . The row shows the current theme Light or Dark . It works like the header button. You can pin it to the quick bar with its star, and filter for it by typing dark or light . Press Ctrl + K , type , and choose Toggle light and dark . The row shows the current theme. It works like the header but"},{"t":"Theme reference","d":"Every theme control, the values it sets, and how the controls interact.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/reference.html","h":["Controls","Defaults and storage","How the stored choice is read","Messages"],"x":" Control Values Sets System? Scope Header sun/moon button Toggles light and dark No fixes the opposite of what you see Whole site Settings › Appearance › Theme Light , Dark , System Yes Whole site Drawer › Preferences › Theme Auto , Light , Dark Yes Auto Whole site Alt + T Light → Dark → System → Light Yes Whole site Right click › View › Switch theme Toggles light and dark No Whole site Spotlight › Toggle light and dark Toggles light and dark No Whole site Card menu › System › Theme Toggles light and dark No Whole site Kit title bar theme button Light, dark — That kit only Split view pane › Theme Auto, Light, Dark — That pane only Item Value Default mode System Where it is kept This browser Shared across tabs Yes, open tabs update when you change it Applied before the page is drawn Yes In the settings export file Yes, as themeMode When a page loads, the site uses, in order: the mode chosen in Settings or the drawer, or Alt + T ; otherwise the last choice made with a light/dark toggle; otherwise your device's setting. Message When Theme: Light / Theme: Dark / Theme: System After Alt + T "},{"t":"Troubleshooting themes","d":"Fixes for common theme problems.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The site does not follow my device any more","The site is dark but my device is light (or the other way round)","One panel is in a different theme from the page","My theme changed after I opened a link someone sent me","The theme resets every time I close the browser"],"x":" Why: a light/dark toggle the header button, the right click menu, Spotlight or the card menu fixes the theme and leaves System mode. What to do: choose System in Settings › Appearance, or Auto in the mobile drawer. Possible causes: You chose Light or Dark at some point, so System mode is off. Open Settings and check Theme . Your browser has its own theme setting that overrides the device. In some browsers you can set the website appearance separately from the operating system. Why: kits remember their own theme once you use their theme button, and split view panes can be forced light or dark. What to do: use the kit's own theme button to match the page. For split view, set the pane's theme back to Auto . Why: page links copied from the site can carry the sender's appearance settings, including the theme mode. See Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . What to do: set your theme again in Settings. Why: you are using a private window, or your browser clears site data on exit. What to do: use a normal window, or allow auricartisan.com to keep site data. "},{"t":"Theme FAQ","d":"Short answers about the site's themes.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/docs/faq.html","h":["Is there a high-contrast theme?","Does the theme change colours in the tools?","Does my account remember my theme?","Can I set a different theme for one kit?","Why does the page not flash when it loads?"],"x":" There is no separate theme, but Settings › Comfort › Boost contrast strengthens text and borders in both themes. See Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md . No. The theme changes the site's interface. Colours you are working with, swatches and images are shown as they are. The site theme is kept in your browser, not in your account. Your account dashboard has its own theme preference; see Account and billing ../../../account and billing/README.md . Yes. Use the sun or moon button in that kit's title bar. It affects only that kit. The site reads your saved theme before it draws the page, so it starts in the right theme. "},{"t":"Theme: supporting material","d":"Contents of the theme supporting files.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the theme guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts that change the theme related.md related.md Related features privacy.md privacy.md What is stored about your theme "},{"t":"Theme shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts that change the theme.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Action Alt + T Cycle Light, Dark, System Ctrl + , Open Settings, where Theme is in Appearance Ctrl + K , then Spotlight commands, including Toggle light and dark Alt + T does nothing while you are typing in a field. The full list is in Keyboard shortcuts ../../keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Theme glossary","d":"Terms used in the theme guides.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Theme The overall colour scheme of the site's interface: light or dark. Light theme Light backgrounds with dark text. Dark theme Dark backgrounds with light text. System mode A setting that follows your device's light or dark preference. Called Auto in the drawer. Toggle A control that switches between two states, here light and dark. Override A theme set for one panel a kit or a split view pane that differs from the site's theme. "},{"t":"Theme privacy","d":"What is stored about your theme choice.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your theme mode is kept in this browser's local storage for auricartisan.com, along with the last light or dark choice made with a toggle. The cookie policy lists this under Functional storage. Each kit's own theme choice is kept the same way. Nothing about your theme is sent to Auric Artisan when you change it. A page link copied from the site can include your theme mode see Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md . "},{"t":"Related to themes","d":"Features related to the site's themes.","p":"Website › Site features › Theme","u":"website/site-features/theme/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Settings panel ../../settings panel/README.md — the Theme control and the accent colour. Accessibility aids ../../accessibility aids/README.md — Boost contrast, Reduce transparency and reading mode. Header and navigation ../../header and navigation/README.md — the header button and the drawer's Theme switch. Split view ../../split view/README.md — compare light and dark side by side. Kits ../../../kits/README.md — each kit's own theme button. Shareable links ../../shareable links/README.md — how links can carry a theme. "},{"t":"Website tools","d":"Every tool on auricartisan.com, grouped by what it helps you do, with its address and a link to its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools","u":"website/tools/README.html","h":["Accessibility and vision","Colour workspace","Colorimetry and rendering","Perception and spectral","Image and file tools","Which tool for which job","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan's tools run in your browser at https://auricartisan.com. Most need no account: what you make is kept in your browser, and you can export it as files. Each tool below has its own folder of documentation with a quick start, task guides, a complete reference, troubleshooting and a glossary. The tools fall into five groups. If you are not sure which one you need, start with Which tool for which job which tool for which job . Check colour contrast, audit whole websites, work through WCAG, and see colour the way people with different vision do. Group overview: Accessibility and vision accessibility and vision/README.md . Tool Address What it does Analyzer accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md /tool/analyzer/ Audits a website's colours, contrast and accessibility, and keeps the reports. Contrast Checker accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md /tool/contrast checker/ Grades a text and background pair with WCAG 2.x ratios and APCA. Accessibility Checklist accessibility and vision/accessibility checklist/README.md /resources/accessibility checklist/ 50 WCAG 2.2 checks with the law by jurisdiction and an inspector. Accessibility Compliance accessibility and vi"},{"t":"Accessibility and vision tools","d":"What the accessibility and vision tools on auricartisan.com are for, and which one to open for each job.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/README.html","h":["The tools","Which tool should I open?","In this folder"],"x":" This group covers the tools on auricartisan.com that help you make a design or a website usable by more people. Some of them measure a live page against the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines WCAG , the W3C standard that most accessibility laws point at. Others show you how colour looks to people with colour vision deficiencies or low vision, so you can catch problems that a number alone does not reveal. The tools range from a one question checker to a full audit console. Use the small tools when you already know what you are asking, and the Analyzer when you want to find the problems you do not know about yet. Every tool here is free to use. A few actions that run on Auric Artisan's servers, such as rendering someone else's website or crawling a whole site, need an account and are metered in tokens. Each tool's own docs say exactly which actions those are. Tool Address Use it to Analyzer analyzer/README.md https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/ Audit a whole web page: accessibility 126 rules , contrast, performance, SEO, security and more Contrast Checker contrast checker/README.md https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/ Grade one text colour against one background wit"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist","d":"What the Accessibility Checklist is, who it is for, and how to start working through its 50 WCAG 2.2 checks.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Accessibility Checklist is a free working checklist of 50 accessibility checks, grouped into nine areas, from semantics and keyboard focus to forms, media, colour, motion, ARIA, zoom and testing. Each check is explained in full: what it means, who it affects, how to test it, what the fix looks like in code, and what usually breaks it. You work through it in the Inspector : a list of every check beside the selected check in full. Mark each one Pass , Fail or N/A , attach annotated screenshots as evidence, and watch a meter count what is left. When you are done, print the findings or copy them as Markdown into your issue tracker. Everything stays in your browser; there is no account and nothing is uploaded. The page also carries a Reference of what the WCAG levels mean and what the law asks for in 15 jurisdictions, India first, with links to the primary sources. Front end developers, designers and accessibility testers preparing or running a manual review. Teams who want evidence of a process to go with an automated audit. Anyone who needs to know which accessibility law applies where, and to which WCAG version. Address: https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist documentation","d":"The list of Accessibility Checklist guides with one line on each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to use the checklist at https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/. Start with Getting started; the reference lists every control. Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md The masthead, the tab rail and meter, the Inspector, and your first check Work through the checklist work through the checklist.md Selecting checks, marking them, filters, folding areas, the meter, and the phone layout Attach evidence attach evidence.md Adding screenshots to a check and annotating them Export your results export your results.md The Export tab: printing, copying Markdown, and clearing your work The 50 checks the 50 checks.md Every check, area by area, with its criterion and how much the Analyzer can decide Laws by jurisdiction laws by jurisdiction.md The Reference tab: WCAG levels and the law in 15 jurisdictions Reference reference.md Every control, label, message and stored item Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Common problems and what to do FAQ faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Accessibility Checklist","d":"Open the Accessibility Checklist, learn the screen, and mark your first check.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open it","The screen, top to bottom","Mark your first check","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Accessibility Compliance . No account is needed. The kicker \"Auric Artisan · Accessibility\", the title The accessibility checklist , and a line: \"Fifty checks across the whole of WCAG 2.2, each one explained: what it means, who it affects, how to test it, and what the fix looks like in code.\" A note under it says: \"The analyzer decides 11 of these outright and narrows 23 more. The rest needs a person, which is what the explanations are for.\" Two links follow: Run the automated pass first → opens the Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md . Wire it into CI → opens the public API documentation. Three tabs: Checklist , Export and Reference . With a tab focused, Left and Right move between tabs wrapping round , and Home and End jump to the first or last. Beside the tabs is the meter : \"0 passed · 0 flagged · 50 left\", a two colour bar passed and flagged , and \"of 50\". The meter always counts all 50 checks, whatever filter is on. When a filter is on, a small chip beside it names the filter and how many rows it shows, for example \"REQUIRED · 35\". On wide screens the tab rai"},{"t":"Attach evidence","d":"Add screenshots to a check and annotate them with the pen, highlighter, arrows, boxes, redaction and numbered callouts.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/attach-evidence.html","h":["Add a screenshot","Annotate it","Manage screenshots","In the pane","What the marks do to the image","Limits"],"x":" A finding is easier to fix, and harder to dispute, when it carries a screenshot. Every check can hold any number of screenshots, each with its own annotations. 1. Select the check in the index. 2. Select Attach screenshot in the pane. On narrow phones this is an icon only button with the same name. The Screenshot evidence dialog opens. 3. Add one or more images in any of three ways: drag and drop image files anywhere on the dialog; paste an image with Ctrl + V ; select Choose a file and pick one or more images. 4. The dialog announces how many screenshots were attached. Only image files are accepted; other files are ignored. Screenshots are saved in your browser as soon as they are added. The toolbar on the left of the dialog \"Annotation tools\" holds six tools. Each has a key while the dialog is open. Tool Key What it draws Pen P A freehand line Highlighter H A wide, translucent freehand stroke Arrow A A straight arrow. This is the default tool. Box B A rectangle outline Redact R A solid filled rectangle in the chosen colour Callout C A numbered circle 1, 2, 3 and so on with one click Colours: Red default , Blue, Green and Black. Line widths: Fine, Medium default and Broad. Drag a"},{"t":"Export your results","d":"Use the Export tab to print your findings, copy them as Markdown for an issue tracker, or clear your work.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/export-your-results.html","h":["What the tab shows","Copy as Markdown","Export the report (print)","Reset","What is not available","The \"What a claim actually needs\" link"],"x":" Open the Export tab. Its heading is \"Turn the flags into a report\". What the report will contain — four tiles with your current counts: Flagged , Passed , Not applicable and Untouched which starts at 50 . Decided, by level — a bar for each of A out of 22 , AA out of 13 , AAA out of 2 and Practice out of 13 . Here \"decided\" means Passed or Flagged; N/A does not count. Evidence — \"No screenshots attached\", or how many screenshots are attached across how many checks. Preview — the first lines, as they will read — the first lines of the Markdown export, exactly as it will be copied. Three ways out — the three buttons below. A privacy note: \"Your work stays on this device.\" Before you send it — how many checks are untouched, and a reminder that \"A worked checklist is evidence of a process, not a conformance claim.\" \"Straight into the tracker.\" Best for Jira, Linear, GitHub and similar tools. 1. Select Copy as Markdown . 2. The page says \"The findings are on your clipboard, as Markdown.\" 3. Paste into your tracker. The Markdown always covers all 50 checks, whatever filter is on. It has this shape: text Worked 24 September 2026 · WCAG 2.2 · 15 of 50 checks decided Flagged: 3 Passed: 10 N"},{"t":"Laws by jurisdiction","d":"The Reference tab of the Accessibility Checklist: what the WCAG levels mean and what the law asks for in 15 jurisdictions.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/laws-by-jurisdiction.html","h":["The four levels on this page","Finding your way","India","United States","European Union","United Kingdom","Canada","Australia","Japan","Elsewhere: eight more worth knowing","What this is not"],"x":" The Reference tab is headed \"What the levels mean, and what the law asks for\". It explains the four levels used on the page and summarises the accessibility law in 15 jurisdictions, with links to the primary sources. Important: The page states this is \"Orientation, not legal advice.\" Dates move: the page notes that two of its dates moved in the eighteen months before its last review. It was last reviewed on 11 September 2026 , covering 29 instruments in 15 jurisdictions. Check the primary source before you rely on any date. The summaries below repeat the page's content as of that review. Level Checks What the page says A 22 The floor. Nearly every instrument below names it, or something built on it. AA 13 What the statutes and procurement documents actually cite. A + AA is the legal line. AAA 2 Stricter than any law here requires. Worth doing; never demanded wholesale. Practice 13 No criterion covers it, and every audit finds it anyway. The page's summary: WCAG 2.1 Level AA is the common denominator almost everywhere. The UK and Australia have already moved to WCAG 2.2 AA, and EN 301 549 V4 takes the European standard there too. Build to WCAG 2.2 AA and you are above every line on"},{"t":"The 50 checks","d":"Every check in the Accessibility Checklist, area by area, with its WCAG criterion, level and how much the Analyzer can decide.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/the-50-checks.html","h":["How to read the tables","01 Semantics & structure","02 Keyboard & focus","03 Forms & errors","04 Images & media","05 Colour & contrast","06 Motion & preferences","07 ARIA & custom widgets","08 Zoom, reflow & spacing","09 Testing & proof","Links inside the checks"],"x":" The checklist has 50 checks in nine areas. This page lists them all, with the one line summary the page shows for each a few are slightly shortened to fit the table . Open a check on the page for its full explanation, test and fix. ID is the check's identifier. Open it directly with check plus the ID, for example https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/ check k2 . Tag is the level and WCAG success criterion, as the page shows it. Practice means good practice with no criterion of its own. Checks at Level A or AA are Required ; AAA and Practice checks are optional. Decided by says how much the Analyzer can do: AUTO — \"The analyzer decides this one on its own\" PARTLY — \"The analyzer narrows this down; a person confirms it\" BY HAND — \"Only a person can decide this one\" The checklist itself does not import Analyzer results. Run the Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md and mark the checks yourself. Totals Count Level A 22 Level AA 13 Level AAA 2 Practice 13 Required A and AA 35 AUTO / PARTLY / BY HAND 11 / 23 / 16 \"What a screen reader builds its map from. Nothing below works if this is wrong.\" ID Check Tag Decided by Summary d1 Landmarks wrap every region of the page A "},{"t":"Work through the checklist","d":"Select checks, mark them Pass, Fail or N/A, filter the list, fold areas, read the meter, and use the one-check view on a phone.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/work-through-the-checklist.html","h":["Select a check","Mark a check","Where the keys work","Filter the list","Fold an area","Read the meter","On a phone: the one-check view","Suggested order of work"],"x":" With a mouse or touch: select a row in the index. With the keyboard: focus a row, then press Down or Up to move to the next or previous visible check, and Home or End for the first or last. Only one row is in the Tab order at a time, so Tab moves out of the list rather than through every row. From the pane: select Previous check or Next check , or press K or J . From the address: open check plus the check's ID, for example check f2 . The pane's bar shows where the check sits in the full list of 50, for example \"12 of 50\", whatever filter is on. Previous check and Next check are disabled at either end of the visible list. Button Key Meaning State word Pass Space The page meets this check Passed Fail F The page does not meet it: it is flagged Failed N/A N The check does not apply to this page Not applicable Selecting the active verdict again clears it back to Not checked yet . Space marks Pass only when focus is on a row, on the pane, or on the check title. Elsewhere Space presses the focused button as usual. A screen reader hears the new state word after every mark. Each row shows its state as a shape as well as a colour: State Symbol Not checked yet An empty ring Passed A gold dis"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist reference","d":"Every control, label, message and stored item of the Accessibility Checklist.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","Tabs and meter","Index","Pane","Screenshot evidence dialog","Export tab","Messages","Stored in this browser","Layout"],"x":" Item Detail Address https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/ Old addresses /accessibility compliance/ and /compliance forward here Menu entry Learn › Accessibility Compliance \"WCAG checks & guidance\" Deep link to a check check plus the ID, for example check k2 Masthead links Run the automated pass first → Analyzer , Wire it into CI → API documentation Control What it does Checklist The Inspector: index and pane Export Counts, a preview of the Markdown, and the three export actions Reference WCAG levels and the law in 15 jurisdictions Meter \"N passed · N flagged · N left … of 50\", with a two part bar. Always counts all 50. Scope chip Shown when a filter is on: the filter's name and how many rows are visible Control What it does All 50 Show every check default Required Show Level A and AA checks 35 AAA Show Level AAA checks 2 Practice Show good practice checks 13 Open only Hide checks marked Passed; combines with the filters above Area header Fold or unfold the area; shows decided out of total Row Select the check; shows state, title and tag Control What it does All checks Back to the list phone layout only Position \"N of 50\", the check's place in the full list Pr"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Accessibility Checklist","d":"Common problems with the Accessibility Checklist, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Why: marks and screenshots live only in this browser on this device. They are lost if you cleared this site's data, used a private window, switched browser, profile or device, or selected Reset which does not ask first . What to do: there is no server copy to restore from. In future, copy the Markdown or print before clearing anything. Why: in the current version, Reset clears all marks and screenshots immediately, even though its description says it asks first. What to do: nothing can be recovered. Export before you reset. Why: screenshots need your browser's database storage, which some private windows block. Only image files are accepted. What to do: use a normal window, and attach PNG, JPEG or other image files. Why: they only work while focus is in the index or the pane, not with Ctrl , Alt or Cmd held, and not while the screenshot dialog is open. Space marks Pass only from a row, the pane or the check title. During the site's first visit guide tour, the tour may take the arrow keys. What to do: select a row first, then press the key. Why: a filter is on, Open only is hiding passed checks, or the area is folded. What to do: look at the chip beside the meter; select All 50 , s"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Accessibility Checklist.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/docs/faq.html","h":["Is it free? Do I need an account?","Is a finished checklist a WCAG certification?","Does it cover all of WCAG 2.2?","What do AUTO, PARTLY and BY HAND mean?","Which checks are required?","How do I undo a mark?","Where is my work saved?","Can I move my progress to another computer, or share it with a colleague?","Can I add notes to a check?","Are screenshots included in the export?","Is the legal information up to date?","Why is the menu entry called Accessibility Compliance?"],"x":" It is free, and there is no account. Nothing to install either: it works in any modern browser. No. The page says it plainly: \"A worked checklist is evidence of a process, not a conformance claim.\" A claim needs a full evaluation against the whole standard, and the involvement of people who use assistive technology every day. It covers the ground most audits hit, in 50 checks tied to 33 WCAG criteria, plus 13 good practice checks. It does not have a check of its own for every criterion; for example, the WCAG 2.2 additions Dragging Movements 2.5.7 , Consistent Help 3.2.6 , Redundant Entry 3.3.7 and Accessible Authentication 3.3.8 have no dedicated check. The Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md has automated rules for three of those four. How much the Analyzer can decide: AUTO checks it decides on its own, PARTLY checks it narrows down for a person to confirm, and BY HAND checks only a person can judge. The checklist does not read Analyzer results; you mark every check yourself. Level A and AA checks, 35 in all, marked Required . They are what laws and procurement documents cite. AAA and Practice checks are optional. Select the same verdict again. The check goes back to Not checked ye"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist: supporting material","d":"The checklist's glossary, keyboard shortcuts, limits, related tools and privacy notes.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the checklist guides with the terms they use, the full list of keys, an honest account of what the checklist covers, related tools, and where your work is kept. The public changelog has no entries for the checklist, so there is no release notes page. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms used on the page and in these docs Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Every key the checklist responds to Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the checklist covers, known differences between its wording and its behaviour, and what it is not Related tools and reading related.md Tools and articles that pair with the checklist Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist keyboard shortcuts","d":"Every key the Accessibility Checklist responds to, and where each one works.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Moving between checks","Marking","Tabs","In the screenshot evidence dialog","Printing"],"x":" The single letter keys work only while focus is inside the index including its filter buttons and area headers or the pane. They are ignored in text fields, when Ctrl , Alt or Cmd is held, and while the screenshot dialog is open. Keys Where Action Down / Up On a row Next or previous visible check; focus moves with it Home / End On a row First or last visible check J / K Index or pane Next or previous check. From the pane, focus stays and the new title is announced. E Index or pane Open the check: the one check view on a phone, the pane title on a wide screen Esc Pane On a phone, back to the list; on a wide screen, back to the check's row Key Action Space Pass only on a row, the pane or the check title F Fail N N/A Pressing the key for the current verdict again clears it. Keys Action Left / Right Previous or next tab, wrapping round Home / End First or last tab Keys Action P Pen H Highlighter A Arrow B Box R Redact C Callout Ctrl + V Paste a screenshot Esc Close the dialog, like Done Ctrl + P prints the same report as Export the report . For shortcuts that work across the whole site, see Keyboard shortcuts ../../../../site features/keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used by the Accessibility Checklist.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" APG — The W3C ARIA Authoring Practices Guide, which sets out the expected keyboard behaviour for widgets such as tabs and menus. Area — One of the nine numbered groups of checks, 01 to 09. AUTO, PARTLY, BY HAND — How much the Analyzer can decide a check: on its own, by narrowing it down for a person, or not at all. Check — One of the 50 items on the checklist. Decided — Marked. On the Export tab's level bars this means Passed or Flagged; in the Markdown export it also includes N/A. Evidence — Screenshots attached to a check, with their annotations. Flagged — A check marked Fail . The button says Fail, the state word says Failed, and the meter and exports say flagged. Inspector — The two column working view: the index of checks beside the selected check in full. Index — The list of checks on the left of the Inspector. Level A, AA, AAA — WCAG conformance levels. A and AA are what laws cite; AAA is stricter and optional. Meter — The counter beside the tabs: passed, flagged and left, out of 50. One check view — The phone layout that shows one check at a time. Pane — The selected check in full, on the right of the Inspector. Pen — The screenshot evidence dialog and its annotation tools"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Accessibility Checklist covers, where its wording and behaviour differ, and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it covers","AUTO, PARTLY and BY HAND","Where the wording and the behaviour differ","Legal information","What it is not"],"x":" 50 checks: 37 tied to 33 distinct WCAG success criteria at Levels A, AA and AAA, and 13 good practice checks. The masthead describes the checks as spanning \"the whole of WCAG 2.2\". In practice some criteria have no check of their own, including four added in WCAG 2.2: Dragging Movements 2.5.7 , Consistent Help 3.2.6 , Redundant Entry 3.3.7 and Accessible Authentication Minimum 3.3.8 . The Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md checks 2.5.7, 3.2.6 and 3.3.8 automatically. Two level tags differ from WCAG: check m2 text in images, 1.4.5 and check f6 legal and financial submissions, 3.3.4 are tagged Level A, but WCAG places both criteria at Level AA. Both are still counted as Required , so your work is unaffected; only the A and AA counts shift by two. Check d3 also asks for lang on foreign language passages, which WCAG covers under 3.1.2 Language of Parts AA , although the check cites only 3.1.1. These labels describe what the Analyzer can decide. The checklist does not import Analyzer results. Two AUTO labels are really judgement calls: x1 an automated pass in continuous integration is a process check, and c6 simulating colour vision deficiencies needs a person to look at the result. The"},{"t":"Accessibility Checklist privacy","d":"Where the Accessibility Checklist keeps your marks and screenshots, and how to delete them.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/privacy.html","h":["What is kept, and where","What leaves your device","Redaction","Working in two tabs","Delete your data"],"x":" The page puts it simply: \"Your work stays on this device.\" Item Where Your marks on each check Your browser's local storage Screenshots, the original image and its marks, and a marked up copy Your browser's database storage There is no account, no sync and no server copy. The checklist sends none of your marks or screenshots anywhere. Your work is per browser, per profile and per device. In a private window, or when storage is blocked, the page still works but forgets when you close it. Without database storage, screenshots cannot be attached, but marks still work. Only what you choose to take out: Copy as Markdown puts the findings on your clipboard. Screenshots are never included. Export the report prints the page, including small marked up screenshot thumbnails. The Redact tool covers an area only in the marked up copy used for thumbnails and printing. The original screenshot stays stored in your browser, unredacted. Crop or blur sensitive details before you attach a screenshot. Each open tab keeps its own copy of your marks and saves it as a whole. Working in two tabs at once may overwrite marks made in the other. Use one tab at a time. Export › Reset removes every mark and ev"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and articles that pair well with the Accessibility Checklist.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-checklist/others/related.html","h":["External"],"x":" Where Why Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md Run the automated pass first; it decides many AUTO checks and narrows the PARTLY ones Contrast Checker ../../contrast checker/README.md Settle a single colour pair for checks c1, c2 and c4 Vision Lab ../../vision simulation/README.md Simulate colour vision deficiencies for checks c3 and c6 Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md Automate an audit in continuous integration, as check x1 suggests Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md The science behind each rule, in plain language Accessibility Compliance ../../accessibility compliance/README.md The old address for this page WCAG 2.2 quick reference at the W3C: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/ W3C Understanding documents, linked from every check: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/ W3C guidance on evaluating accessibility, linked from area 09: https://www.w3.org/WAI/test evaluate/ "},{"t":"Accessibility Compliance","d":"What the Accessibility Compliance address offers a visitor today, and where it takes you.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-compliance/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com/accessibility compliance/ is the address of Auric Artisan's accessibility compliance resource. It no longer has a page of its own: opening it forwards you straight to the Accessibility Checklist ../accessibility checklist/README.md at https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/, which is where the compliance material now lives. What a visitor gets, therefore, is the checklist: 50 WCAG 2.2 checks explained and ready to mark, the tools to record evidence and export findings, and a Reference tab on what the law asks for in 15 jurisdictions. The site header still calls this destination Accessibility Compliance in its Learn menu. Anyone following an old link, a bookmark, or the Accessibility Compliance menu entry, who wants to know what WCAG and the law require and how to check a site against them. Address What happens https://auricartisan.com/accessibility compliance/ Forwards immediately to the Accessibility Checklist https://auricartisan.com/compliance/ Redirects permanently to /accessibility compliance/ , which then forwards to the checklist https://auricartisan.com/compliance Shows the /accessibility compliance/ page, which forwards to the "},{"t":"Accessibility Compliance documentation","d":"The guides for the Accessibility Compliance address.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-compliance/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" The Accessibility Compliance address forwards to the Accessibility Checklist, so these guides are short. For everything the checklist does, see the Accessibility Checklist docs ../../accessibility checklist/docs/README.md . Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md What happens when you open the address, and what to do next FAQ faq.md Why the address forwards, and what happened to the old page "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"What happens when you open the Accessibility Compliance address, and how to use the checklist it takes you to.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-compliance/docs/getting-started.html","h":["What happens when you open the address","What to do next","Update your links"],"x":" 1. You open https://auricartisan.com/accessibility compliance/ or /compliance/ . 2. A very short page titled \"Redirecting to Accessibility Checklist\" loads, with the text \"Redirecting to Accessibility Checklist...\" and a link. 3. Your browser moves on at once to https://auricartisan.com/resources/accessibility checklist/. The forward replaces the old address in your history, so your browser's Back button skips it. If your browser blocks the automatic forward, select the Accessibility Checklist link on that page. The result: you are on the Accessibility Checklist, with its Checklist , Export and Reference tabs. If you want to Go to Know which law applies to you, and which WCAG level it cites The Reference tab. See Laws by jurisdiction ../../accessibility checklist/docs/laws by jurisdiction.md . Check your site against WCAG 2.2 by hand The Checklist tab. See Work through the checklist ../../accessibility checklist/docs/work through the checklist.md . Find the problems a tool can find automatically Run the automated pass first → , which opens the Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md Hand findings to your team The Export tab. See Export your results ../../accessibility checklist/docs/exp"},{"t":"Accessibility Compliance FAQ","d":"Short answers about the Accessibility Compliance address and where its content went.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-compliance/docs/faq.html","h":["Why does /accessibility-compliance/ open the checklist?","Is there still a separate compliance page?","Does the forward keep anything I had on the old page?","Does the checklist make my site compliant?","Where is the menu entry?"],"x":" The compliance resource was folded into the Accessibility Checklist, which now carries both the checks and the legal reference. The old address forwards there so existing links keep working. No. Everything a visitor needs is on the checklist page: the 50 checks, evidence and export, and the Reference tab on the law in 15 jurisdictions. The address has no content of its own to keep. Work you do on the checklist is saved in your browser, as described in the checklist's Privacy ../../accessibility checklist/others/privacy.md page. No. It is a structured way to check and record your work. The page says a worked checklist is evidence of a process, not a conformance claim, and its legal summaries are orientation, not legal advice. In the site header, Learn › Accessibility Compliance \"WCAG checks & guidance\" . It opens the checklist. "},{"t":"Accessibility Compliance: supporting material","d":"Where to find the glossary, limits, privacy notes and related material for the compliance resource.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/accessibility-compliance/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" The Accessibility Compliance address has no page or behaviour of its own beyond forwarding to the Accessibility Checklist, so its supporting material is the checklist's. There is nothing stored at this address, no shortcuts, and no separate release history. Topic Where Terms such as Required, Practice and WCAG levels Checklist glossary ../../accessibility checklist/others/glossary.md Keyboard shortcuts Checklist shortcuts ../../accessibility checklist/others/shortcuts.md What the checklist covers and what it is not Checklist limits and accuracy ../../accessibility checklist/others/limits and accuracy.md Where your work is kept Checklist privacy ../../accessibility checklist/others/privacy.md Related tools Checklist related tools ../../accessibility checklist/others/related.md The automated audit Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md "},{"t":"Analyzer","d":"What the Auric Artisan Analyzer audits, who it is for, and how to run your first audit.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Analyzer audits a web page from its URL. It reads the page, measures what it can in a real browser, and reports back across accessibility, colour contrast, palette, performance, SEO and metadata, media, responsive behaviour, security and reliability. The page it lives on introduces it as \"One URL, audited seven ways.\" Every finding names the element that caused it, explains why it matters, and, where it can, gives you the code to fix it. At its centre is an accessibility engine of 126 rules mapped to WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2 success criteria, Section 508 and EN 301 549. Around it sit a contrast audit with suggested replacement colours, a colour vision simulation of the page's own palette, Core Web Vitals, a raw versus rendered HTML comparison, a site map built from robots.txt and the sitemap, a security header check, and exports in JSON, HTML, PDF, CSS, CSV and Markdown. The Analyzer has two modes. Simple shows the sections most people need and runs a fixed set of checks. Advanced opens all 22 sections as a workspace of panels you can arrange, lets you choose which checks run, and adds whole site scanning, live editing and custom rules. Every run is filed in your browser so you c"},{"t":"Analyzer documentation","d":"The list of Analyzer guides, from a first audit to exports, with one line on each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to use the Analyzer at https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/. Start with Getting started, then open the guide for the job in front of you. The reference page lists every control and output in one place. Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md Open the Analyzer, learn the screen, and run your first audit Run an analysis run an analysis.md What happens after you select Analyze, how a page is reached, and the progress card Choose what to scan choose what to scan.md The 13 checks, the What to scan picker in Advanced, and how a run is priced Scan a whole site scan a whole site.md Site scan settings, the live progress console and paged per page results Arrange the workspace arrange the workspace.md Panels, the Sections picker, width, Focus, Collapse, and saved Layouts Read the Overview and scores read the overview and scores.md The overall score, grade bands, category weights and issue cards The accessibility engine accessibility engine.md Every view of the A11y+ panel: findings, fixes, widgets, tree, screen reader, conformance, export Accessibility rules accessibility rules.md All 126 accessibility rules, grouped by category, with impact and W"},{"t":"Getting started with the Analyzer","d":"Open the Analyzer, learn what each part of the screen does, and run your first audit.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the Analyzer","The screen, top to bottom","Simple or Advanced?","Run your first audit","Where to go next"],"x":" This guide takes you from opening the Analyzer to reading your first result. It takes about five minutes. Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/, or open the Tools menu in the site header and select Analyze URLs . You do not need an account to audit a page on auricartisan.com. To audit another website you need to be signed in, because that page is rendered on Auric Artisan's servers. See Run an analysis run an analysis.md for the details. The top of the page names the tool: the kicker \"Auric Artisan · Analyzer\", the headline \"One URL, audited seven ways.\", and a line explaining that accessibility, metadata, palette, contrast, performance, reliability and security are all checked against the page's own markup. Under it, a thin rail lists WCAG 2.1 / 2.2 and LCP · CLS · INP , with a link, Read the API reference , to the public API documentation. A one line note may appear under the masthead: \"Automate this — 12 API credits per call to POST /v1/analyzer/inspect .\" It tells developers that the same kind of audit is available from the REST API, and that API credits are a separate balance from your tool tokens. Select API docs to open that endpoint's documentation, or the × button"},{"t":"The accessibility engine (A11y+)","d":"Read and act on every view of the A11y+ panel, from the grade and findings to the accessibility tree, screen-reader transcript, conformance table and exports.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/accessibility-engine.html","h":["How the panel is organised","Key terms","Overview view","Findings: Issues view","Findings: Fixes view","Inspect: Widgets view","Inspect: Annotations view","Inspect: A11y tree view","Inspect: Screen reader view","Inspect: Vision view","Inspect: Focus & targets view","Report: Conformance view","Report: Export view","Below the engine: Advanced Accessibility","A practical order of work"],"x":" The A11y+ panel holds the Analyzer's accessibility engine: 126 rules checked against the page as your browser actually renders it, plus widget pattern checks, an accessibility tree, a screen reader transcript, a colour vision table, a focus and target map, a WCAG 2.2 conformance table and five exports. It is available in Advanced mode, and runs when the Accessibility check is on. In Simple mode the same engine still runs and feeds the Accessibility category of the overall score; you just do not see its panel. A row of four groups sits at the top of the panel. Selecting a group opens its first view; groups with more than one view show a second row of view buttons. Group Views Overview Overview Findings with the issue count Issues , Fixes Inspect Widgets , Annotations , A11y tree , Screen reader , Vision , Focus & targets Report Conformance , Export Most blocks inside a view are folding cards: select the card's title to open or close it. Rule — one automated check, such as \"Buttons must have discernible text\". Each rule applies to some elements and passes, fails, or needs review on each. Impact — how badly a failure affects someone using the page. The engine uses four levels, each w"},{"t":"Accessibility rules","d":"Every one of the 126 accessibility rules the Analyzer checks, grouped by category, with its impact, WCAG mapping and what it looks for.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/accessibility-rules.html","h":["How to read the tables","Text alternatives (12 rules)","Audio & video (4 rules)","Structure & semantics (12 rules)","Tables (9 rules)","Forms & labels (15 rules)","Zoom, reflow & motion (6 rules)","Colour & contrast (4 rules)","Keyboard & focus (12 rules)","Timing & animation (3 rules)","Navigation (9 rules)","Safe linking (1 rule)","Pointer & touch (4 rules)","Language & readability (5 rules)","ARIA correctness (24 rules)","Landmarks & regions (6 rules)","ARIA widget patterns","WCAG criteria the engine knows"],"x":" The accessibility engine in the A11y+ panel checks 126 rules. This page lists every one, grouped into the 15 categories the panel uses for its Area filter and its Where the problems are bars. For how to read the results, see The accessibility engine accessibility engine.md . Rule is the title the Issues view shows. ID is the rule's identifier, shown in each rule's details and used in the exports. Impact is how badly a failure affects people: critical, serious, moderate or minor. WCAG lists the success criteria the rule maps to. \"Best practice\" means the rule maps to no criterion: it is good advice, but not part of conformance. The Level filter in the Issues view uses the lowest level among a rule's criteria. A rule mapped to a Level A criterion is filtered as WCAG A . Rules that map to WCAG 2.0 Level A or AA criteria also carry a Section 508 badge, and rules that map to WCAG 2.0 or 2.1 Level A or AA criteria carry an EN 301 549 badge. Across the catalogue, 18 rules are critical, 61 serious, 30 moderate and 17 minor. By level, 81 are filtered as Level A, 20 as Level AA, 5 as Level AAA and 20 as best practice. Rules only judge what is actually exposed. Elements hidden from assistive"},{"t":"Arrange the workspace","d":"Open, move, resize, focus and close report panels, find sections with the Sections picker, and save layouts.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/arrange-the-workspace.html","h":["What opens by itself","The panel title bar","Open sections with the Sections picker","Open a section from the progress rail","Layouts (Advanced)","What is remembered"],"x":" The Analyzer shows its report as a workspace: each section is a panel in a grid, and you choose which panels are on screen and where. This lets you read a finding and the thing it is about side by side, for example the accessibility findings next to the contrast pairs and the fixes. Both modes use the workspace. Simple mode offers 8 sections and no Layouts menu; Advanced offers all 22 sections and saved layouts. Before your first run , the workspace holds only the Overview panel, across the full width. After a run , the section of every check that ran is opened, if your mode can show it. The Devices section is never opened automatically. The first time you use Advanced , the default arrangement is Overview and Contrast side by side, with Fixes across the full width below. It replaces the single Overview panel when your first run finishes, but only if you have not already changed the arrangement. Sections you closed during a run are not reopened for you. Every panel has a title bar with a grip and four buttons: Control What it does Grip the section icon and name Drag to move the panel. With the keyboard, focus it and press Left or Right to move it one place. Width Cycles the panel "},{"t":"Choose what to scan","d":"Pick which of the 13 checks run in Advanced mode, understand which sections each check fills, and read what a run costs in tokens.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/choose-what-to-scan.html","h":["The checks","What Simple mode runs","Use the picker (Advanced)","Sections whose check did not run","What a run costs"],"x":" A full audit runs every check the Analyzer has. You rarely need all of them. In Advanced mode you can switch checks off, which makes a run faster and can make it cheaper. In Simple mode the set of checks is fixed. One check, Page structure , always runs: it reads the page and its resources, and everything else is built on it. The other 13 can be switched on and off. Check What it does Fills the section Notes Project model One deduplicated model of the page: resources, colours, media, schema, dependencies Project from Page structure Colour contrast Every text pair measured against WCAG, with a passing colour to replace it Contrast Before / After The page as it is beside the page with the contrast fixes applied Before / After from Colour contrast Accessibility The full rule engine: WCAG 2.1 and 2.2, the a11y tree, keyboard and screen reader order A11y+ slow Palette Dominant colours and generated accessible palettes Palette Vision simulation The palette through colour vision and low vision filters Simulation from Palette SEO and metadata Title, description, headings, schema, robots, canonical, keyword density SEO Media Every image, video and audio file: size, dimensions, alt text, ca"},{"t":"Colour, contrast and vision","d":"Read the Contrast, Palette, Simulation and Before / After panels, and understand the WCAG contrast ratio and the APCA Lc value.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/colour-contrast-and-vision.html","h":["Two ways to measure contrast","The Contrast section","The Palette section","The Simulation section","The Before / After section","A practical workflow for colour"],"x":" Four sections deal with colour: Contrast measures every text colour pair on the page, Palette extracts the page's colours, Simulation shows the page through colour vision filters, and Before / After previews the contrast fixes. The Vision view of the A11y+ panel adds a table of every pair under four colour vision deficiencies see The accessibility engine accessibility engine.md . WCAG 2.x measures contrast as a ratio between two colours' relative luminance , which is how much light a colour gives off on a scale from 0 black to 1 white . Green counts most towards it and blue least, as in human vision. The ratio is the lighter luminance plus 0.05, divided by the darker plus 0.05. It runs from 1:1 the same colour twice to 21:1 black on white , and it does not matter which colour is the text. What Needs at least Level Normal text 4.5:1 AA Large text 3:1 AA The visible edge of a control, focus indicators, meaningful graphics 3:1 AA Normal text, enhanced 7:1 AAA Large text, enhanced 4.5:1 AAA Large text means at least 24 CSS pixels, or at least 18.66 CSS pixels in bold. It is a size threshold, not a heading rule. APCA, the Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, is a newer contrast mo"},{"t":"Export and share","d":"Every way to take a result out of the Analyzer — reports, data files, stylesheets and share links — with formats and file names.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/export-and-share.html","h":["The Report section","Exports in other sections","Share a result","Which format should I use?"],"x":" This guide lists every export the Analyzer offers, what each file contains, and the ways to share a result. Most exports are in the Report section; others live in the section they come from. Report opens with Full Analysis Report , the date it was generated and the audited address, the score and the issue count. Then comes the Export row. Button What you get File Export JSON The full report data, for automation, regression checks and comparing fields over time analysis.json Export HTML A self contained HTML report that opens in any browser and can be printed auric analyzer report.html Export PDF A PDF of the report paid plans; see below auric report <number .pdf , or your browser's print dialog Export Fix CSS One clean stylesheet of the generated fixes auric analyzer fixes.css Developer Report A Markdown report written for developers auric developer report.md Client Report A Markdown report written for clients and stakeholders auric client report.md Copy Report The developer report, copied to the clipboard as Markdown — Share Link A link to re run this audit see below — PDF is a Pro export format, included with paid plans. On the free plan, selecting it opens an upgrade prompt tha"},{"t":"Fix and preview","d":"Turn findings into code with the Fixes panel, try changes live in the Playground, add your own checks in Rules, and let your site be previewed with CSP Setup.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/fix-and-preview.html","h":["Fixes","Playground","Rules","CSP Setup"],"x":" Four sections help you act on what the audit found. Fixes gives you the code. Playground lets you try colour changes on the page and watch the score move. Rules adds your own checks to every audit. CSP Setup explains how to let the Analyzer preview a site you own. Fixes is available in both modes; the other three are Advanced only. For the accessibility engine's own patches the ready to paste CSS and per element suggestions , see the Fixes view in The accessibility engine accessibility engine.md . The developer hand off: every actionable fix for the page, grouped by type. Part What it does How to use this Explains that colour fixes give exact CSS values and structural fixes describe the HTML to change Total The number of actionable fixes Fix This First The top fixes, numbered, each with its reason and an impact label such as \"Low impact\" Fix Mode Safe fixes or Aggressive fixes below Heuristic Auto Fix Four buttons that apply or export the generated fix stylesheet below Fix Details Color Fixes High Priority with a Copy fix button on each, and Structural & Semantic Fixes Safe fixes favours brand safe contrast changes and structural recommendations. This is the default. Aggressive fi"},{"t":"Performance, SEO and page health","d":"What the Performance, SEO, Media, Deep, Devices, Security, Project, Site Map and Insights sections measure, and how to read them.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/performance-seo-and-page-health.html","h":["Performance","SEO","Media","Deep","Devices","Security","Project","Site Map","Insights"],"x":" Beyond accessibility and colour, the Analyzer checks how fast the page is, how search engines see it, what JavaScript changes, how it copes with small screens, which security headers it sends, and how it fits into the rest of the site. This guide covers each of those sections. Most are available in Advanced mode only; Project , Site Map and Insights are also in Simple mode. Every scored section has a Why this score? box, built like the one in the Overview, that explains its formula, what moved the score and the top recommendations. See Read the Overview and scores read the overview and scores.md . A Lighthouse style audit built from the page's HTML, CSS, JavaScript, assets, DOM size and layout stability, and from real browser timing when it is available. Block What it shows Score and one line verdict For example \"Fast, stable, and well within most budgets.\" Data Source Whether scores use real browser timing or estimates Performance Context Critical performance issues, acceptable architecture patterns, and the real world load time Quick Wins The first changes to make Sub scores Loading , Interactivity , Visual Stability , Asset Weight , Maintainability Browser Timing DOM content lo"},{"t":"Read the Overview and scores","d":"Understand the overall score, the grade bands, how categories are weighted, and how to work through the issue cards.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/read-the-overview-and-scores.html","h":["The score","How the overall score is made","The rest of the Overview","Work through the issue cards","Use the score well"],"x":" The Overview panel is the summary of a run: one score, the categories behind it, and the issues ranked by how much fixing them is worth. This guide explains each part and how the numbers are made. The large number at the top is the Overall Audit Score , from 0 to 100, with a letter grade beside it. Under it, a line names the categories it was weighted from. If some checks were switched off, the line says so, for example \"Scored on 4 of 10 categories — performance, reliability, security, media, colour and palette, rendered DOM were not scanned for this run and were excluded rather than counted as zero.\" A page that could not be measured a bot challenge page or an almost empty page gets no score at all, rather than a misleading one. See Run an analysis run an analysis.md . The overall score and each section's own score use the same bands: Grade Tier Range Meaning shown A+ Excellent 90–100 Production ready; meets or exceeds best practices. A Strong 80–89 Solid foundations with only minor refinements left. B Good 70–79 Generally healthy, with a few clear gaps to close. C Fair 55–69 Usable, but several material issues should be addressed. D Weak 40–54 Significant issues are affecting r"},{"t":"Run an analysis","d":"What happens when you select Analyze, which addresses are accepted, how the page is reached, and what the progress card tells you.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/run-an-analysis.html","h":["Start a run","Which addresses are accepted","How the page is reached","The progress card","When the run finishes","Pages that cannot be scored","Rate limits on the target site","Re-running"],"x":" This guide explains a single page audit from the moment you select Analyze to the moment results appear. For a whole site crawl, see Scan a whole site scan a whole site.md . 1. Type or paste an address into the URL field. 2. Select Analyze , or press Enter in the field. 3. To stop a run part way, select Cancel . The Overview panel then says \"Analysis cancelled\". There are three other ways to start a run: Open a link of the form https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/?url=<address . The Analyzer fills the field and starts at once. Open a link someone made with Share . It re runs the audit on the same address. Select Re analyze next to a past run in the Workspace panel, or Recheck on an issue card. You type What the Analyzer uses https://example.com/page Exactly that address example.com or example.com/page The same with https:// added in front /tool/contrast checker/ That path on auricartisan.com Nothing at all The Analyzer's own page ftp: , mailto: , tel: , javascript: or a malformed address Refused with \"That URL doesn't look valid\" and a hint to try a full address such as https://example.com When the Analyzer tidies what you typed, it writes the tidied address back into the field"},{"t":"Save, reopen and compare","d":"How finished runs are kept in your browser, how to reopen them, how to compare two versions of a site, and how to keep a copy in your account.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/save-reopen-and-compare.html","h":["How runs are kept","Reopen a past run","The Workspace section (Advanced)","Compare two versions","Keep a copy in your account","Good habits"],"x":" You do not have to save a run by hand. Every finished audit is filed in your browser as a version of the site it audited, so you can reopen it later without running it again, and compare it with the next run to see what your changes did. One project per site. A single page audit is filed as a project named \"Audit · \" followed by the host and path. A whole site scan is its own project, named \"Audit · \" followed by the host. Every run is a version. Running the same address again adds a new version to the same project instead of creating a new entry. Versions are never deleted to make room; after the 25 newest, older versions keep their scores and dates in the list and their full reports stay stored. One collection per host. Projects for the same host are grouped in a library collection named \"URL Analyzer \" plus the host and \" \", together with the site's palette. The palette is filed too. The colours the page is built from are saved as a palette named \"Palette · \" plus the host, so colour tools in your library can open it. The full report is stored. Every section of the report is stored in your browser, so reopening a version redraws every panel exactly as it was. The site map, whic"},{"t":"Scan a whole site","d":"Audit several pages of one site in a single run, follow the live progress, and page through the per-page results.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/scan-a-whole-site.html","h":["Before you start","The site scan settings","Run a site scan","The live console","Read the results","How the combined score is worked out","Pages the scanner cannot audit","After the scan"],"x":" A site scan finds the pages of a site from its links and sitemap, audits each one in a real browser on Auric Artisan's servers, and combines the results into one report with a page by page breakdown. Use it to find the shared components that fail on every page, or to check a set of pages before a release. You need to be signed in . Without an account the scan stops with \"Sign in to scan a site. Analyzing this page still works without an account.\" Whole site scanning is part of the Artisan plan and above . On other plans the scanner answers \"Whole site crawling is part of the Artisan plan and above.\" A site scan costs tokens. The pricing page describes it as one token per page analysed, so a 24 page crawl costs 24. The token sheet shows the exact quote, with a line for finding the pages and a line for the pages themselves. Tokens are held when the scan starts; you are charged for the pages that come back and refunded the rest. One run audits up to 24 pages . Switch to Advanced and open Site scan settings under the strip. Setting What it does Values Default Scan Site Starts the site scan for the address in the URL field Button — Robots Follow robots.txt rules while scanning On or of"},{"t":"Analyzer reference","d":"Every control, option, section, input and output of the Analyzer in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/reference.html","h":["Page elements","The strip","What to scan (Advanced)","Site scan settings (Advanced)","The run line","Search results","Workspace controls","Sections","A11y+ views","Issue card statuses","Scores and thresholds","Limits","Links you can build","Remembered in this browser"],"x":" A complete list of the Analyzer's controls and outputs. Each entry links to the guide that explains it in more depth. Element What it does Masthead The headline \"One URL, audited seven ways.\", a lede, and a rail with Read the API reference API hint The REST API equivalent and its price in API credits; dismissing it hides it on every tool page Save this run The site wide library button, fixed at the bottom right Control What it does Values Default URL field The address to audit Any http or https address, a bare host name, or a path on auricartisan.com Empty Analyze Starts a single page audit. Enter in the URL field does the same. Button — Cancel Stops the running audit or site scan Shown only while running — Share Opens the share dialog with a link that re runs the audit Button — Sections Opens the Sections picker. Shows Ctrl + P . Advanced only — Layouts Opens the layout menu Advanced only — Simple / Advanced Switches mode; remembered in this browser Simple, Advanced Simple URL field placeholder: \"Enter a URL to analyze…\" Simple or \"Enter a URL for deep DOM, SEO, contrast & accessibility audit…\" Advanced . See Run an analysis run an analysis.md . The row's heading reads \"What to s"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Analyzer","d":"What each Analyzer error or odd result means, why it happens, and what to do about it.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Starting a run","Reaching the page","Results","Previews","Exports, saving and sharing"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom as you see it, the cause, and what to do. Why: the address could not be turned into a web address, or it uses a scheme the Analyzer cannot fetch, such as mailto: , tel: , ftp: or javascript: . What to do: type a full address including https:// , for example https://example.com . Why: auditing a website other than auricartisan.com runs on Auric Artisan's servers, which needs an account. Nothing has failed. What to do: select Sign in , then run the audit again. Pages on auricartisan.com can be audited without an account. Note: The tips under this and other error panels may mention a \"This Page\" button. That button has been removed from the strip. To audit a page on auricartisan.com, type or paste its address into the URL field. Why: your account's plan does not include URL analysis, or the server refused the run for a plan reason. The message under the heading gives the exact reason. If it says \"This run costs N tokens and your balance is M\", your token balance is too low. What to do: select See plans . On a paid plan the monthly token allowance renews; the free plan's starter balance does not. Why: you have used your monthly allowance of server side URL"},{"t":"Analyzer FAQ","d":"Short answers to the questions people most often ask about the Analyzer.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the Analyzer free?","Do I need an account?","Can I audit a page on my computer, or on a company intranet?","What is the difference between Simple and Advanced?","How many accessibility rules does it check?","Does a good score mean my site is accessible, or legally compliant?","Why does another tool score my page 100 when the Analyzer does not?","Why are there two different grade scales?","What does \"needs review\" mean?","What is APCA Lc, and does it affect my score?","Can I scan my whole site?","Where are my results stored?","Can I compare before and after a fix?","Can I share a report with someone who has no account?","Why does Ctrl + P not print?","Can I automate audits?","Why do some sections say the page could not be embedded?"],"x":" Yes. The tool, every section and most exports are free. Work that runs on Auric Artisan's servers is metered: auditing another website rendered on a server , whole site scans, and server screenshots. Signed in accounts can claim 100 free tokens, and the free plan includes 20 server side URL analyses a month. PDF export is a paid Pro export, and the VPAT shaped conformance CSV is a Specialist plan perk. See Choose what to scan choose what to scan.md . Not to audit pages on auricartisan.com. To audit another website you need to be signed in, because your browser is not allowed to read another site's pages directly; the page is rendered on Auric Artisan's servers instead. Generally no. The server scanner refuses private and local addresses such as localhost and 192.168.x.x , and your browser cannot read another origin's pages unless that server explicitly allows it. Put a copy of the page somewhere publicly reachable, such as a staging site. Simple shows 8 sections and runs a fixed set of checks. Advanced shows all 22 sections, lets you choose which of 13 checks run, and adds site scanning, the Playground, custom rules, saved layouts and CSP Setup. The audit itself is the same qualit"},{"t":"Analyzer: supporting material","d":"The Analyzer's glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy notes.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds material that supports the Analyzer guides: the terms they use, the keyboard shortcuts, an honest account of what the Analyzer measures and where it stops, related tools and reading, the history of changes, and what happens to your data. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Every technical term used in the Analyzer docs, in one sentence each Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys for the URL field, the Sections picker, panels and the token meter Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the Analyzer measures, how precisely, and what it is not Related tools and reading related.md Other Auric Artisan tools, extensions and articles that pair with the Analyzer Release notes release notes.md User facing history of the Analyzer Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser, what goes to a server, and what you can delete "},{"t":"Analyzer keyboard shortcuts","d":"The keys the Analyzer responds to, in the URL field, the Sections picker, the workspace panels and the token meter.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Anywhere on the Analyzer page","In the URL field","In the Sections picker","On a panel","On the token meter","Disclosures and cards"],"x":" The Analyzer can be used entirely from the keyboard. Tab and Shift + Tab move between controls as usual; the keys below are the Analyzer's own. Keys What they do Ctrl + P Open the Sections picker, in Simple or Advanced; replaces the print shortcut on this page Keys What they do Enter Start the audit, the same as Analyze Keys What they do Type any text Filter the sections by name Up / Down Move to the row above or below, as the rows are laid out Left / Right Move across columns, when the filter field is empty Enter Open the highlighted section or scroll to it and close the picker Space Open or close the highlighted section and keep the picker open Esc Close the picker Keys What they do Left / Right on the panel grip Move the panel one place earlier or later in the workspace Enter or Space on Width , Focus , Collapse , Close Use that button Keys What they do Enter or Space Open the token sheet Folding cards and disclosures, such as Why this score? , Cause chain and the A11y+ cards, open and close with Enter or Space . For shortcuts that work across the whole site, see Keyboard shortcuts ../../../../site features/keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Analyzer glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Analyzer and its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Accessible name — The name assistive technology announces for an element, worked out from its visible text, its label, alt , aria label or aria labelledby . Accessibility tree — The simplified version of a page that browsers give to screen readers and other assistive technology. APCA — The Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a newer model of perceived contrast being developed for a future version of WCAG. Advisory only in the Analyzer. API credits — The balance that pays for calls to Auric Artisan's REST API. Separate from tool tokens; neither pays for the other. ARIA — Accessible Rich Internet Applications: attributes such as role , aria label and aria expanded that add meaning for assistive technology. ARIA widget pattern — A standard way to build a composite control, such as tabs or a menu, described in the W3C ARIA Authoring Practices. Axe format — The JSON shape used by a widely used open source accessibility testing library, which many continuous integration tools can read. The A11y+ Results JSON export uses it. Before / After — The section that shows the page as it is beside the page with the contrast fixes applied. Bot challenge — A page a site shows automated visito"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Analyzer measures, how precisely, which pages it can reach, and what its results are not.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it measures","Which pages it can reach","Accessibility","Colour and contrast","Scores","Performance","Site scans","What the Analyzer is not"],"x":" The Analyzer gives you a short, specific, evidence backed list of things that are wrong with a page. It does not certify a page, predict every visitor's experience, or replace a manual review. This page is honest about where the line is. One page per run , or up to 24 pages in a whole site scan. The page as it was at one moment. Content that loads later, changes with an A/B test, or appears only after a user action may not be seen. A page part way through an animation measures differently from a page at rest. Lab results, not visitor data. Performance figures come from one load in one browser, not from real visitors on real devices and networks. Page Can it be audited? Any page on auricartisan.com Yes, in your browser, with or without an account A public page on another website Yes, when you are signed in: it is rendered in a real browser on Auric Artisan's servers Another website, signed out Only if that site allows cross origin requests, or with Public proxy turned on, and then only from its HTML A page behind a login, a bot challenge or a strict firewall No. The scanner is refused, or receives a challenge page and declines to score it. localhost , private network and link local"},{"t":"Analyzer privacy","d":"What the Analyzer keeps in your browser, what it sends to Auric Artisan's servers or third parties, and how to delete it.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/privacy.html","h":["What happens in your browser","What goes to Auric Artisan's servers","What goes to third parties","What is kept in your browser","What share links contain","Delete your data"],"x":" This page explains where your data goes when you use the Analyzer. For the site's full privacy policy, see the company and legal docs in Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . When you audit a page on auricartisan.com and you are not signed in, the whole audit runs in your browser. The page is loaded into a hidden frame on your device, measured there, and nothing about the audit is sent anywhere. Contrast, palette, media and SEO analysis run on your own device, whichever way the page was reached. When a page is rendered on Auric Artisan's servers, the accessibility rules run there, in the server's browser, because they need the page as it was laid out. When What is sent Why You are signed in and audit another website The address you entered The page is rendered on the server and the results come back to you You run Scan Site The address and the number of pages The site is crawled and each page audited on the server You use Capture all devices or the Device Lab captures screenshots The address Screenshots are rendered on the server A run, scan or capture is metered Your account and the token amount Tokens and the monthly allowance are recorded against your acco"},{"t":"Analyzer release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Analyzer, from the public changelog and the current page.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/release-notes.html","h":["Since v0.9.11 (current page, September 2026)","v0.9.11 — 12 August 2026","v0.9.10 — 27 July 2026","v0.9.8 — 2 May 2026"],"x":" The Analyzer changes with the website. Dated entries below come from the public changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The first section describes how the current page differs from the last changelog entry that mentions the Analyzer. These changes are visible on the page today: 126 accessibility rules , up from the 112 announced in v0.9.10. The engine also checks eight ARIA widget patterns, and proposes concrete fixes with a confidence level in a new Fixes view. A workspace instead of a tab row. Sections open as panels you can move, resize, focus, collapse and close, in both modes. Advanced adds a Sections picker Ctrl + P and a Layouts menu with ready made and saved layouts. What to scan. In Advanced mode you choose which of 13 checks run. The token meter prices the checks you chose, at four checks to a token. Simple mode now shows 8 sections, including Project , Site Map and Compare . Runs are kept. Every run is filed in your browser as a version of its site, with the full report, and can be reopened without running again. Compare sets two versions of a site side by side and lists what was fixed, what appeared and what stayed. A version can be kept in your acco"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools, extensions and articles that work well with the Analyzer.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/analyzer/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other parts of Auric Artisan","Articles on auricartisan.com","Standards"],"x":" Tool Use it with the Analyzer to Contrast Checker ../../contrast checker/README.md Settle one colour pair by hand after the Analyzer finds it failing Accessibility Checklist ../../accessibility checklist/README.md Cover the WCAG criteria that automated testing cannot check, and read the law by country Vision Lab ../../vision simulation/README.md Simulate many more vision conditions, at chosen severities, on colours and images Ishihara Plate Generator ../../ishihara plate generator/README.md Show colleagues how colour vision deficiencies change what people see Where Why Basic colour tools ../../../colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Build a palette or a family of tints after the Analyzer has told you a colour must move Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md Find, organise and reopen saved Analyzer projects and palettes Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md How the site wide share dialog behind the Share button works Account and billing ../../../../account and billing/README.md Tokens, plans, the monthly allowance and keeping reports in your account Browser extension ../../../../../browser extension/README.md Inspect colour and acc"},{"t":"Contrast Checker","d":"What the Contrast Checker does, who it is for, and how to grade a colour pair in under a minute.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Contrast Checker answers one question quickly: does this text colour work on this background? You give it two hex colours. It gives back the exact WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio to two decimal places, a Pass or Fail badge against five thresholds, and a preview panel painted in the pair you are testing. Two buttons do the rest. Make it pass AA appears when body text fails and moves the text colour to the nearest value that reaches 4.5:1. Copy link copies the page address, which always carries both colours, so a pair can be pasted into a ticket or a review and reopened exactly as you left it. The tool is deliberately small. All the maths runs in your browser: nothing is uploaded, nothing is stored, and no account is needed. It tests one pair at a time. To find every failing pair on a whole page, use the Analyzer ../analyzer/README.md . Designers choosing text and background colours for a component. Developers and reviewers who need a number, not an opinion, in a code or design review. Accessibility specialists checking a single pair reported by another tool. Anyone learning what the WCAG contrast levels mean. Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/ With a pair already "},{"t":"Contrast Checker documentation","d":"The list of Contrast Checker guides with one line on each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to use the Contrast Checker at https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/. Start with Getting started; the reference lists every control and threshold. Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md The screen, part by part, and your first check Check a colour pair check a colour pair.md What the colour fields accept, how the ratio is worked out, and which grade applies to you Make a pair pass make a pair pass.md What Make it pass AA does, what it does not do, and how to keep your brand colour Share a pair share a pair.md How the address carries the pair, Copy link, and the ways into the tool Reference reference.md Every control, threshold, output and keyboard behaviour Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Odd results and what causes them FAQ faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Contrast Checker","d":"Open the Contrast Checker, learn each part of the screen, and grade your first colour pair.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open it","The screen, part by part","Check your first pair","Try the other controls","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/. The page loads with a default pair, text 1A1400 on background F7F3E6 , and grades it straight away, so there is no empty state to get past. On a wide screen the tool is two columns over a full width strip: controls on the left, the result on the right, and the preview underneath. Below 720 pixels wide it becomes one column in the order controls, result, preview, and the swap button turns so its arrows point up and down. Nothing is hidden on a narrow screen. Area What it holds Breadcrumb Home , Tools links to the tools collection and Contrast Checker Heading The kicker \"WCAG 2.1 · Contrast\", the title Color Contrast Checker , and a line saying nothing is uploaded API hint \"Automate this — 1 API credit per call to POST /v1/accessibility/check \", with API docs and a dismiss button Controls Text colour and Background colour , each a colour swatch beside a hex field, with the swap button between them Result The ratio Contrast ratio , five grade rows, Make it pass AA , Copy link and a status line Preview A panel painted in your pair, with a line of large text, a paragraph of body text and an \"Interface element\" chip Below What the n"},{"t":"Check a colour pair","d":"Enter a text and background colour, read the WCAG 2.1 ratio, and work out which of the five grades applies to what you are colouring.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/check-a-colour-pair.html","h":["Enter the colours","Read the ratio","Read the five grades","Use the preview","A check in five steps"],"x":" Each colour has two controls that stay in step: a colour swatch and a hex field. Use the swatch to explore and the field to paste a value from a stylesheet or a design file. Control What it does Starts at Text colour swatch Opens your system's colour picker. Moving it writes the hex into the field and re grades as you go. 1a1400 Text colour hex field Accepts a typed or pasted hex value and re grades on every keystroke 1A1400 Swap button Exchanges the two colours and re grades — Background colour swatch The same picker for the background f7f3e6 Background colour hex field The same typed entry for the background F7F3E6 Hex only, in three or six digits, with or without a leading . These are all the same colour to the checker: 1A1400 , 1A1400 . Three digits are expanded, so f00 and f00 both mean FF0000 . When you leave a field, a value it understood is rewritten in full: uppercase, six digits, with a . Anything else is not accepted: rgb , hsl , colour names such as rebeccapurple , and eight digit hex with an alpha channel. Important: While a field holds something it cannot read, such as a half typed 1A , the checker grades pure black in its place for the text or pure white for the bac"},{"t":"Make a pair pass","d":"Use Make it pass AA to find a passing text colour, understand how it chooses, and keep your brand hue.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/make-a-pair-pass.html","h":["Use it","How it chooses","What it will not do","The mid-grey surprise","Keep your brand colour"],"x":" Make it pass AA is the main button in the result area. It only appears while the pair fails body text AA under 4.5:1 , so seeing it is itself a signal that body text is failing. 1. Enter a failing pair, for example text D3AF37 on background F7F3E6 1.90:1 . 2. Select Make it pass AA . 3. Read the status line. For this pair it says \"Adjusted text to 836C22 4.58:1 .\" The result: the new colour is in the Text colour field and swatch, the pair is re graded, the button disappears, and the address updates a moment later with the new pair. 1. It looks at the background. If the background's relative luminance is above 0.5 it moves the text towards black; otherwise towards white. 2. It walks the text colour along a straight line towards that end, in about fifty small steps, checking the ratio at each step. 3. It stops at the first step that reaches 4.5:1. If none does, it uses pure black or pure white. It only aims at 4.5:1. There is no option for 3:1 or 7:1. For AAA, use the button first, then keep darkening or lightening by hand while you watch the ratio. It never changes the background. Only the text colour moves. If the background is the colour you are allowed to change, select the swap"},{"t":"Share a pair","d":"Share or bookmark a colour pair as a link, and the ways other parts of the site open the checker.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/share-a-pair.html","h":["The address is the state","Copy link","Partial links","Two things the address does not do","Ways into the checker","What is kept"],"x":" The Contrast Checker keeps no history. The page address is the only place a pair is kept, and it is always up to date. Each time the checker re grades, it rewrites the address with the current pair, without the : text https://auricartisan.com/tool/contrast checker/?fg=1A1400&bg=F7F3E6 fg is the text colour and bg the background. Open that address and the checker restores both colours and grades them at once. Bookmark it, or paste it into a pull request, a bug report or a design review. 1. Set up the pair you want to share. 2. Select Copy link . 3. The status line says \"Share link copied.\" Paste the link where you need it. If your browser does not allow clipboard access for example on an insecure connection, or after you declined the permission , the full address is printed in the status line instead, so you can select and copy it by hand. Only values that are valid hex are used. A link with ?fg=D3AF37 and nothing else sets the text colour and leaves the background at the default. Site search uses exactly this when its answer is about a single colour, and sends both values when its answer is about a pair. It does not add history entries. The address is replaced, not added to, so yo"},{"t":"Contrast Checker reference","d":"Every control, input, threshold, output, message and keyboard behaviour of the Contrast Checker.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/reference.html","h":["Controls","Outputs","Thresholds","Status messages","Address parameters","Keyboard and screen readers","Layout","Content below the tool"],"x":" Control What it does Values Default Text colour swatch Opens the system colour picker; writes uppercase hex into the field Any colour 1a1400 Text colour hex field Typed or pasted text colour 3 or 6 digit hex, with or without 1A1400 Swap button Exchanges text and background — — Background colour swatch Opens the system colour picker Any colour f7f3e6 Background colour hex field Typed or pasted background colour 3 or 6 digit hex, with or without F7F3E6 Make it pass AA Moves the text colour to the nearest value that reaches 4.5:1 Shown only when body text fails AA — Copy link Copies the address, which carries both colours — — The swatches are your browser's own colour input, not the site's custom colour picker, so the swatch always shows the value that is being graded. Output What it shows Contrast ratio The WCAG 2.1 ratio to two decimals, from 1.00:1 to 21.00:1. Shows a dash until the first grading. Grade badges Pass or Fail for each of the five thresholds below Status line The result of Make it pass AA or Copy link Preview Your pair as large text, a body text paragraph and an \"Interface element\" chip Row Threshold Body text · AA 4.5:1 Body text · AAA 7:1 Large text · AA 3:1 Large t"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Contrast Checker","d":"Odd results in the Contrast Checker, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Why: a half typed value such as 1A cannot be read, so the checker grades pure black for the text or pure white for the background in its place. What to do: finish typing all three or six digits, or press Tab to leave the field. The field rewrites a valid value in full, and the ratio is then yours. Why: the fields take hex only. rgb , hsl , colour names and eight digit hex with transparency are not accepted. What to do: convert the colour to six digit hex first. For a semi transparent colour, work out the colour it actually shows over its background, and test that. Why: the display is rounded to two decimals; the badge uses the exact value, which is just under 4.5. What to do: treat it as failing and move the colour a little further. Why: the ratio does not depend on which colour is the text. Only the preview, and which colour Make it pass AA moves, change. What to do: nothing; this is correct. Why: it moves the text colour in a straight line towards black or white and stops at the first passing step, which removes saturation. What to do: use its result as a target and adjust your original colour towards it by hand. See Make a pair pass make a pair pass.md . Why: the direction foll"},{"t":"Contrast Checker FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Contrast Checker and colour contrast.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/docs/faq.html","h":["What contrast ratio do I actually need?","What counts as large text?","Does passing the ratio mean the text is readable?","Do disabled controls and logos have to pass?","Does the checker show APCA?","Can I check a colour with transparency?","Can I check many pairs at once?","Is anything uploaded or saved?","Do I need an account?","Can I use it with a keyboard and a screen reader?"],"x":" 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for large text is WCAG 2.1 Level AA, the level most laws and contracts reference. AAA asks for 7:1 and 4.5:1. Interface components and meaningful graphics need 3:1 against what sits next to them. At least 18.66 pixels in bold, or 24 pixels otherwise. A large heading in a light weight can still fall under the body text requirement. No. The WCAG 2.1 formula ignores font weight, size beyond the large text threshold, and the way light text on dark backgrounds appears to spread. A pass is a floor, not a verdict. Check the preview as well as the number. No. WCAG 2.1 exempts inactive controls, pure decoration, text that is part of a logo, and text in a picture of something else. Everything a person has to read or operate is in scope. No. The page's title mentions APCA, but the tool itself calculates only the WCAG 2.1 ratio. For APCA Lc values beside the ratio, audit a page with the Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md ; its A11y+ panel shows them. The REST API endpoint named in the page's API hint also covers APCA. Not directly. Work out the solid colour it shows over its background and test that. Not here. It checks one pair at a time. The Analyzer ../../analyze"},{"t":"Contrast Checker: supporting material","d":"The Contrast Checker's glossary, limits, related tools and privacy notes.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the material that supports the Contrast Checker guides. The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own keyboard use is covered in the Reference ../docs/reference.md , and the public changelog has no entries for it, so there are no shortcut or release note pages. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md The terms used in the Contrast Checker docs Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the ratio measures, how precisely, and what it is not Related tools and reading related.md Tools and articles that pair with the checker Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Contrast Checker glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used by the Contrast Checker.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" AA and AAA — WCAG conformance levels. AA is what most laws and contracts require; AAA is stricter and not required everywhere. APCA — The Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a newer contrast model being developed for a future version of WCAG. The Contrast Checker does not calculate it. Contrast ratio — The WCAG measure of how different two colours are in lightness, from 1:1 identical to 21:1 black on white . Hex colour — A colour written as a and six hexadecimal digits for red, green and blue, such as 1A1400 , or three digits as shorthand, such as F00 . Large text — Text of at least 18.66 pixels in bold or 24 pixels otherwise. It needs less contrast than body text. Relative luminance — How much light a colour gives off, from 0 for black to 1 for white, weighted towards green as in human vision. sRGB — The standard colour space of the web, which the ratio formula assumes. UI & graphics — Interface components, focus indicators and meaningful graphics, which need 3:1 against the colour next to them. WCAG — The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines published by the W3C. The checker uses the WCAG 2.1 contrast formula and thresholds. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Contrast Checker measures, how precisely, and where it stops.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it measures","What it does not measure","Make it pass AA","One pair at a time","Not a certification"],"x":" The WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio between two solid sRGB colours, using the relative luminance formula from the WCAG specification. The number is exact for the two colours you enter; it is displayed to two decimal places, and the pass or fail decisions use the unrounded value. APCA, WCAG 3 drafts or colour difference. Despite the page title, there is no APCA or Lc score, no colour difference metric and no colour vision simulation in this tool. Transparency or layering. Hex values only, with no alpha. Text at partial opacity, or over an image or a gradient, has to be reduced to its effective solid colour first. Font weight and spread. The formula ignores weight, ignores size beyond the large text threshold, and does not model how light text on a dark background appears to spread. A pass is a floor, not a verdict; use the preview. Context. The UI & graphics row compares the two colours you typed. In a real design, a component's edge is judged against whatever is next to it. Scope decisions. Disabled controls, decoration, logos and text in pictures are exempt from WCAG, but the checker grades any pair you give it. Deciding what is in scope is up to you. Aims at 4.5:1 only. Changes only the"},{"t":"Contrast Checker privacy","d":"What the Contrast Checker does with the colours you enter.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Everything runs in your browser. The ratio, the grades and the fix are calculated on your device. The colours you enter are not sent anywhere. Nothing is stored. There is no history, no saved pairs and no account state. The only record of a pair is the page address, which your browser keeps in its own history like any other address. Shared links contain the colours. A copied link carries both colours in plain text in the address. Anyone with the link can see them. The API hint. If you dismiss the \"Automate this\" note, that choice is remembered in this browser so the note stays hidden on every tool page. The site wide privacy policy is covered in Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and articles that pair well with the Contrast Checker.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/contrast-checker/others/related.html","h":["Articles on auricartisan.com","Standard"],"x":" Where Why Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md Find every failing pair on a live page, with the elements named and a replacement that keeps your hue Vision Lab ../../vision simulation/README.md See how your colours look with colour vision deficiencies Accessibility Checklist ../../accessibility checklist/README.md Work through the rest of WCAG, including the contrast checks, by hand Basic colour tools ../../../colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Build ramps, tints and shades, or pull colours from an image, once you know a colour must move Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md Plain language articles on contrast, colour vision and readable type Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md Check pairs from code with POST /v1/accessibility/check 1 API credit per call Color Contrast Checker User Guide — the site's own long form guide to this tool: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 09 03 contrast checker user guide Understanding Your Accessibility Report — how contrast results fit into a full accessibility audit: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 08 20 understanding your accessibility report WCAG 2.1 Understand"},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator","d":"What the Ishihara Plate Generator makes, who it is for, and how to generate, check and export your first plates.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Ishihara Plate Generator makes dot plates in the style of the Ishihara colour vision test: a circle of coloured dots in which a figure a number, a letter, a symbol, a shape or a path to trace stands out to typical colour vision and blends into the background for a particular colour vision deficiency. The page describes them as \"Dot plates that carry a figure to normal colour vision and hide it from a specific deficiency — generated, measured and scored on this device.\" Every plate is scored as it is drawn. The generator measures how far apart the figure and background colours are for typical vision, then recomputes that distance through simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, and combines four measurements into a quality score. You can preview plates under each deficiency, build a standard set of 38 plates, and export plates as PNG or SVG with a seed that rebuilds any plate exactly. Everything runs in your browser. There is no account, and nothing is uploaded. Important: The page states: \"Not a colour vision test. These plates are illustrative. A screen is not colour calibrated and a real Ishihara examination is printed, lit and administered under controlled conditi"},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator documentation","d":"The list of Ishihara Plate Generator guides with one line on each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to use the generator at https://auricartisan.com/tool/ishihara plate generation/. Start with Getting started; the reference lists every control. Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md The masthead, the four tabs, and your first plates Generate plates generate plates.md Plate types, palettes, difficulty, batches, custom plates, fine tuning, cards and the full size view Read the diagnostics read the diagnostics.md The quality score, its four components, and the ΔE through each deficiency Build the standard 38 build the standard 38.md The fixed 38 plate set and what it contains Export plates export plates.md PNG, SVG, ZIP and seed files, and reproducing a plate Reference reference.md Every control, option, default and output Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Common problems and what to do FAQ faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Ishihara Plate Generator","d":"Open the Ishihara Plate Generator, learn the screen, and generate and inspect your first plates.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open it","The screen, top to bottom","Your first plates","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/ishihara plate generation/. No account is needed. When the page loads, it generates six starter plates and says \"Welcome! 6 starter plates generated.\" The kicker \"Auric Artisan · Vision\", the title Ishihara Plate Generation , and a one line description. The description depends on the site wide Simple or Advanced preference; in Simple mode it reads \"Dot plates that carry a figure to normal colour vision and hide it from a specific deficiency — generated, measured and scored on this device.\" A row of facts follows: 7 plate types, 9 colour palettes, 4 difficulty tiers, 3 CVD simulations, OKLab colour science, ΔE validation, PNG / SVG export, On device, and a Developer reference → link. \"Automate this — 3 API credits per call to POST /v1/ishihara/plate .\" It tells developers that plates can also be generated from the REST API, and that API credits are a separate balance from tool tokens. API docs opens the endpoint's documentation; × hides the hint on every tool page. \"Not a colour vision test. These plates are illustrative. A screen is not colour calibrated and a real Ishihara examination is printed, lit and administered under controlled conditions"},{"t":"Build the standard 38","d":"Generate the fixed 38-plate set, the composition a printed plate book uses, from a single seed.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/build-the-standard-38.html","h":["Build it","What the set contains","Use the set"],"x":" The Set 38 tab builds \"The standard thirty eight\": \"Twenty four numbers, six letters, four symbols, two shapes and two traceable paths — the composition a printed book uses, built from a single seed so it is the same every time.\" 1. Open the Set 38 tab. 2. Select Generate the set . The button reads \"Building…\" while it works. 3. When it finishes, the tab shows every plate in a grid, and a summary with Plates 38 , Seed 42 and Built how long it took, a few seconds . The Lab is left alone: \"The set is built and shown here; nothing on the bench is cleared or replaced. Thirty eight plates take a moment and a quarter of a million dots.\" You can also start the set from the empty Lab with Or build the standard 38 . Kind Count Plates content and difficulty Number 24 0 to 23; each block of eight runs easy, easy, medium, medium, medium, hard, hard, extreme Letter 6 A and B easy , C, D and E medium , F hard Symbol 4 star hard , arrow extreme , triangle easy , heart easy Shape 2 circle and square medium Path 2 two paths, medium and hard Because the set is built from one seed 42 in a fixed composition, \"the same call gives the same book every time\". Show it to a class to explain how plates grad"},{"t":"Export plates","d":"Download plates as PNG or SVG, export every plate as a ZIP, save a seeds file, and rebuild a plate from its seed.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/export-plates.html","h":["One plate, from its card","Every plate, from the Export tab","Reproduce a plate","Over the REST API","Messages"],"x":" Every file is built in your browser and handed straight to the download. Nothing leaves your device. Button What you get File name Download PNG A raster image, 4,096 pixels square, on the chosen card material ishihara plate <number <content .png Download SVG A vector image with one circle per dot, which scales to any print size ishihara plate <number <content .svg Copy seed The plate's seed, on your clipboard — The page says \"Rendering high res PNG…\" while it builds the PNG. For example, plate 1 showing 93 downloads as ishihara plate 1 93.png . The Export tab has four actions. They cover every plate currently in the Lab. Action What you get Everything at once › Export every plate One ZIP, ishihara plates.zip , with a PNG 2,048 pixels , an SVG and a JSON description for each plate PNG Raster › Download every .png The same ZIP of every plate SVG Vector › Download every .svg One SVG file per plate, downloaded one after another Seeds Reproducible › Download the seeds A text file, ishihara seeds.txt , with the seed, palette and settings of every plate ↓ Export All in the Lab does the same as Export every plate . Inside the ZIP, files are named by plate number, type and content, for exa"},{"t":"Generate plates","d":"Use the Lab to choose a plate type, palette and difficulty, generate single plates or batches, make custom plates, fine-tune the dots, and read the plate cards.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/generate-plates.html","h":["Choose what to generate","Generate","Create a custom plate","Plate size","Fine tuning","This batch","The plate card","Open a plate full size","Remember"],"x":" Everything in this guide happens on the Lab tab. Type What the figure is Number A number to read Letter A letter to read Symbol A symbol, such as a star or an arrow Number Gradient A number drawn with a colour gradient Shape A shape, such as a ring Multi layer Shape+Number A shape and a number together Hidden Path A winding path to trace The colour families the figure and background are drawn from. The names say which colours are set against each other. Auto Random , a palette chosen at random for each plate default Red vs Green Green vs Brown Blue vs Purple Orange vs Green Teal vs Magenta Yellow vs Blue Sepia Mono Mixed Pastel Easy , Medium default , Hard or Extreme . Difficulty \"Controls colour similarity between figure and background\": the harder the plate, the closer the figure's colours are to the background's. Button What it does + Generate Draws one plate with the current settings and adds it to the bench ×1 , ×3 , ×6 Generates 1, 3 or 6 plates in a row Custom Opens Create Custom Plate below Clear All Removes every plate from the bench \"All plates cleared\" ↓ Export All Downloads every plate as a ZIP see Export plates export plates.md Each new plate is announced, for example"},{"t":"Read the diagnostics","d":"Understand each plate's quality score, its four weighted components, and how well it hides from each colour-vision deficiency.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/read-the-diagnostics.html","h":["How colour distance is measured","The summary","Each plate's card","When a plate passes","Using the diagnostics"],"x":" A good plate does two things at once: its figure is easy to see with typical colour vision, and it disappears for the deficiency it is meant to catch. The Diagnostics tab shows how well each plate does both. \"One number hides four measurements, so the score is shown taken apart. A plate fails when it is either invisible to normal vision or still legible to the deficiency it is meant to catch.\" The generator works in OKLab , a colour space designed so that equal distances look roughly equally different. ΔE here is the straight line distance between two colours in OKLab. On this scale, 0 means identical and a few hundredths is already a visible difference; figures such as 0.150 are clearly different colours. Separation is the ΔE between the average figure colour and the average background colour: how far apart they are for someone with typical colour vision. Concealment is that same distance recomputed after simulating protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. The smaller it gets, the better the plate hides. At the top, This batch gives Plates , Passing for example \"9 of 10\" , Mean score and Weakest the lowest scoring plate and its score . The plate's content, its type, palette and d"},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator reference","d":"Every control, option, default and output of the Ishihara Plate Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","Lab: main controls","Create Custom Plate","Fine tuning","Plate card","Full-size view","This batch (Lab)","Diagnostics","Set 38","Export","Remembered in this browser"],"x":" Item Detail Address https://auricartisan.com/tool/ishihara plate generation/ Tabs Lab , Diagnostics , Set 38 , Export API hint 3 API credits per call to POST /v1/ishihara/plate On load Six starter plates are generated Notice \"Not a colour vision test. These plates are illustrative…\" Control Options Default Plate Type Number, Letter, Symbol, Number Gradient , Shape, Multi layer Shape+Number , Hidden Path Number Color Palette Auto Random or one of eight named palettes see Generate plates generate plates.md Auto Random Difficulty Easy, Medium, Hard, Extreme Medium + Generate One plate — ×1 , ×3 , ×6 Several plates — Custom Opens Create Custom Plate — Clear All Removes every plate — ↓ Export All ZIP of every plate — Plate Size S 210 px , M 290 px , L 440 px , XL 900 px M Field Values Plate Type As above Content A number, a letter, or a symbol or shape name Color Palette As above Difficulty As above Seed optional Any whole number; the same seed and settings give an identical plate Cancel / Generate — Symbol names: star, arrow, triangle, heart, diamond, circle, square, moon, sun, check, x, target, squareDot, dot, leaf, wave, shield. Shape names: pentagon, octagon, rounded square, annulu"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Ishihara Plate Generator","d":"Common problems with the Ishihara Plate Generator, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Why: plates are kept only while the page is open. Reloading or leaving the page loses them. What to do: export plates you want to keep, or download the seeds file so you can rebuild them. Why: the plate's colours still differ for that deficiency. Palettes and difficulty decide how well a figure hides. What to do: check Concealment in Diagnostics , choose a palette that targets that deficiency, raise the difficulty, or regenerate. Why: at Hard and Extreme the figure's colours are very close to the background's, and your screen, brightness and room light all affect what you see. What to do: lower the difficulty, raise Color separation in Fine tuning , or check the plate's Separation in Diagnostics . Why: its quality score is under 45, or its density, figure share or separation is out of range. What to do: see Read the diagnostics read the diagnostics.md and regenerate with adjusted settings. Why: the bench is empty. What to do: generate plates first. Set 38 plates are shown in their own tab and are not on the bench. Why: the ZIP builder could not load, often because of a network problem or a content blocker. What to do: reload and try again, or download plates one at a time from the"},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Ishihara Plate Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/docs/faq.html","h":["Can I use these plates to test someone's colour vision?","Is it free? Do I need an account?","What does the quality score mean?","Which colour-vision deficiencies are simulated?","Why can I not keep my plates after closing the page?","Can I make a plate with my own number or word?","What is a seed?","Which format should I export?","What is the standard 38?"],"x":" No. The page says: \"Not a colour vision test. These plates are illustrative. A screen is not colour calibrated and a real Ishihara examination is printed, lit and administered under controlled conditions. For diagnosis, see an eye care professional.\" It is free and needs no account. Plates are generated in your browser. Generating plates from code through the REST API costs 3 API credits per call. It combines four measurements: dot density, figure ratio, separation for typical vision, and concealment through the simulated deficiencies. A plate passes when it is visible to typical vision and hidden from the deficiency it targets. See Read the diagnostics read the diagnostics.md . Protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, using the Brettel, Viénot and Mollon 1997 model. Plates are not stored between visits. Export them, or keep their seeds. Use Custom and type a number, a letter, or one of the listed symbol or shape names. See Generate plates generate plates.md . A number that fixes every random choice in a plate. The same seed with the same settings produces the same plate, dot for dot, on any machine. PNG for slides and documents; SVG for printing at any size, since every dot is a "},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator: supporting material","d":"The Ishihara Plate Generator's glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy notes.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the generator's guides with the terms they use, the keys it responds to, an honest account of what the plates are and are not, related tools, its history, and what happens to your data. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms used in the generator's docs Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys for plates and the full size view Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the scores measure, and why this is not a vision test Related tools and reading related.md Tools and articles that pair with the generator Release notes release notes.md User facing history Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator keyboard shortcuts","d":"The keys the Ishihara Plate Generator responds to.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys Where Action Enter or Space A focused plate Open it full size Double click A plate Open it full size Right Full size view Next plate Left Full size view Previous plate Esc Full size view Close it All other controls are standard buttons and menus: move between them with Tab and Shift + Tab , and use them with Enter or Space . For shortcuts that work across the whole site, see Keyboard shortcuts ../../../../site features/keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used by the Ishihara Plate Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Concealment — How well a figure hides under a simulated deficiency: its distance from the background there, compared with its distance for typical vision. Lower distance means better concealment. CVD colour vision deficiency — Reduced ability to tell some colours apart, often called colour blindness. Deuteranopia, protanopia, tritanopia — Colour vision deficiencies in which the green , red or blue sensitive cones do not work. The generator simulates all three. Dot density — The share of the plate's area covered by dots. ΔE delta E — A measure of colour difference. The generator measures it in OKLab, where 0 is identical and a few hundredths is a visible difference. Difficulty — How similar the figure's colours are to the background's: Easy, Medium, Hard or Extreme. Figure — What the plate shows: a number, letter, symbol, shape or path. Figure ratio — The share of dots that belong to the figure. Ishihara plate — A circle of coloured dots containing a figure, used in colour vision screening. The originals were published by Shinobu Ishihara. OKLab — A colour space designed so that equal distances look roughly equally different. P3 HDR / sRGB — Colour spaces. sRGB is the standard web "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Ishihara Plate Generator's scores measure, how far to trust them, and why the plates are not a colour-vision test.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Not a colour-vision test","What the scores measure","Previews","Reproducibility","Nothing is kept"],"x":" The page is explicit: \"Not a colour vision test. These plates are illustrative. A screen is not colour calibrated and a real Ishihara examination is printed, lit and administered under controlled conditions. For diagnosis, see an eye care professional.\" In particular: Screens differ. Colour, brightness, gamut and night modes change what a plate looks like. The same file looks different on two screens. Printing differs. Paper, ink and light change colours again. A printed plate from this tool is not a calibrated plate. Examinations are controlled. A real test controls lighting, viewing distance and timing, and uses validated plates. These plates are not validated against people with colour vision deficiencies. Colour distances are calculated in OKLab between the average figure colour and the average background colour. Deficiencies are simulated with the Brettel, Viénot and Mollon 1997 model for protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. A simulation models a typical, complete dichromatic deficiency; milder forms and individual differences are not modelled. The quality score weighs four components density .24, figure ratio .20, separation .32, concealment .24 . It describes how well a"},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator privacy","d":"What the Ishihara Plate Generator does with your plates and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Everything happens in your browser. Plates are generated, scored and exported on your device. The Export tab says: \"Nothing leaves the browser — each file is built here and handed straight to the download.\" Nothing about your plates is stored. Plates exist only while the page is open. The one thing remembered in this browser is your Plate Size choice. Custom content stays local. A number or word you type into Custom is used only to draw the plate. The ZIP builder. The first time you export a ZIP, the page loads its ZIP library from auricartisan.com. No plate data is sent. The API hint. If you dismiss the \"Automate this\" note, that choice is remembered in this browser so the note stays hidden on every tool page. The site wide privacy policy is covered in Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Ishihara Plate Generator release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Ishihara Plate Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current page (September 2026)","v0.9.75 — 19 April 2026"],"x":" Dated entries come from the public changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The first section describes the page as it is now. Four tabs: Lab , Diagnostics , Set 38 and Export . Diagnostics shows each plate's quality score taken apart into its four components, with the ΔE through each simulated deficiency. Set 38 builds the standard 38 plate set from seed 42 without touching the plates in the Lab. Export offers a ZIP of every plate, individual SVGs, and a seeds file. ×1 , ×3 and ×6 generate several plates at once; Plate Size offers S, M, L and XL. Each card has a per plate Normal , Protan , Deutan and Tritan preview, and double clicking opens a plate full size. The Ishihara plate generator was added to the tools collection. "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and articles that pair well with the Ishihara Plate Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/ishihara-plate-generator/others/related.html","h":["Articles on auricartisan.com"],"x":" Where Why Vision Lab ../../vision simulation/README.md See colours, palettes and images through 78 vision conditions, with measurements Contrast Checker ../../contrast checker/README.md Check that text colours are readable, a different question from colour confusion Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md See a web page's colours under colour vision filters Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md Plain language articles on colour vision Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md Generate plates from code with POST /v1/ishihara/plate 3 API credits per call Ishihara Plate Generation — an earlier article about the generator. The page has been redesigned since, so some names and layouts differ; this documentation describes the current page: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 04 18 ishihara plate generation "},{"t":"Vision Lab","d":"What the Vision Lab simulates, who it is for, and how to see a colour, a palette or an image through 78 vision conditions.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Vision Lab page title: Vision Deficiency Lab shows how colours, palettes and images look to people with 78 different vision conditions, from the common colour vision deficiencies such as deuteranopia to cataract, glaucoma, macular degeneration and dozens of rarer retinal, optic nerve and corneal conditions. Its masthead reads \"Seventy eight ways of seeing, simulated.\" Seventeen of the conditions are per colour transforms : every colour has an exact answer, computed in linear light with the published colour vision models of Brettel 1997 , Viénot 1999 and Machado 2009 . The other sixty one are field effects : they change where and how clearly you see blur, lost regions, glare, distortion rather than changing each colour. Every condition runs the same ten reference swatches, so two conditions can be compared fairly. The lab has five views. The Workbench takes one condition apart on a colour, a palette or your own image. The Catalogue is every condition as a card that opens a detailed floating panel. Compare lays one source out under many conditions side by side. Palette audit checks every pair in your palette under all 17 colour conditions and suggests fixes. Analytics maps the w"},{"t":"Vision Lab documentation","d":"The list of Vision Lab guides with one line on each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to use the Vision Lab at https://auricartisan.com/tool/vision simulation/. Start with Getting started; the reference lists every control. Guide What it covers Getting started getting started.md The masthead, the five views, the notice, and a first simulation Use the Workbench use the workbench.md Specimens, base colour, severity, model, stage, what collapses, and the measurements Browse the Catalogue and panels browse the catalogue and panels.md Cards, search, filters, favourites, floating panels, Vision Control and the source image Compare conditions compare conditions.md The contact sheet: tiles, order, columns and severity Audit a palette audit a palette.md Which of your colour pairs merge under 17 conditions, and how to fix them Explore Analytics explore analytics.md The severity matrix, the map, statistics and exports The 78 conditions the 78 conditions.md Every condition with its category, kind, severity score and prevalence Links, saving and exports links saving and exports.md Sharing views, what is remembered, and every export Reference reference.md Every control, option and output Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Common problems and what to do F"},{"t":"Getting started with the Vision Lab","d":"Open the Vision Lab, learn the five views, and run your first simulation.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open it","The screen, top to bottom","Two kinds of condition","Your first simulation","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/vision simulation/. No account is needed to use it. The kicker \"Auric Artisan · Vision\", the headline \"Seventy eight ways of seeing, simulated.\", and a line explaining that every condition runs the same ten reference swatches through the published models, in linear light, so two cards differ because the conditions differ. A rail of facts follows: Conditions 78 , Categories 11 , Brettel 1997 · Viénot 1999 · Machado 2009 , and Read the API reference → . \"Automate this — 5 API credits per call to POST /v1/vision/audit .\" It tells developers that the palette audit is also available from the REST API, and that API credits are a separate balance from tool tokens. Select API docs to read about the endpoint, or × to dismiss the hint on every tool page. Five buttons switch between the lab's views. The lab remembers which one you last used. View What it is for Workbench One condition taken apart: a specimen, a severity dial, the model, and measurements Catalogue Every condition as a card; a card opens a detailed floating panel Compare One source shown under many conditions at once, as a contact sheet Palette audit Every pair in your palette checked under "},{"t":"Audit a palette","d":"Check every pair of colours in your palette under all 17 colour conditions, see which pairs merge, and get a lightness fix for each.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/audit-a-palette.html","h":["Enter your palette","Set the threshold","Read the result","Choose the condition","Fix a merged pair","Take it further"],"x":" Simulating one colour tells you what it becomes. It does not tell you that two of your colours became the same thing, which is what breaks a chart legend, a status badge or a map. Palette audit checks every pair in your palette, under all 17 colour conditions, on the same engine the panels use. 1. Select Palette audit in the view bar. It opens with a five colour sample palette. 2. For each colour, use its swatch \"Change colour N\" or type into its hex field. 3. Select Add colour to add another, up to 24 colours. 4. Select Remove beside a colour to take it out. Each colour shows how many collapses it is involved in, for example \"15 collapses\". Select a swatch to see only where that colour collapses. The palette is remembered in this browser. Merge below , measured in CIEDE2000, is how close two simulated colours must be to count as merged. Setting Range Default ΔE threshold 1 \"identical\" to 15 \"loose\" , in steps of 0.5 5 A lower threshold only flags pairs that become almost identical; a higher one also flags pairs that become merely similar. The middle column shows one condition at a time: a verdict, for example \"4 of 10 pairs merge under Achromatopsia\"; Your palette above the same "},{"t":"Browse the Catalogue and panels","d":"Find conditions in the Catalogue, open them as floating panels, arrange panels with Vision Control, and feed them an image.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/browse-the-catalogue-and-panels.html","h":["The Catalogue bar","The cards","Daily limit on the free plan","Floating panels","Vision Control","The source image"],"x":" The Catalogue shows every condition as a card. Each card runs the same ten reference swatches, so the differences between two cards are real differences between two conditions. Selecting a card opens that condition as a floating panel, where you can run your own image through it and use every advanced control. Control What it does Search simulations… Filters cards by name. / jumps to it; Esc clears it. Clear empties it. Scope button Shows the current category and its count, for example \"All conditions 17\"; opens a menu of categories Filter Opens the Kind and Level filters, with Done ; a badge counts active filters Count How many conditions are showing, for example \"17 of 78\" About this catalogue Explains how the cards are built Copy link Copies a link to the whole current workspace see Links, saving and exports links saving and exports.md Daily tally On the free plan, how many simulations you have opened today out of 25 Kind offers All , Per colour and Field ; Level offers All , Basic and Advanced . The Level filter follows the site wide Simple and Advanced preference. Basic shows the 17 per colour conditions, Advanced shows the 61 field conditions, and All shows all 78. On a firs"},{"t":"Compare conditions","d":"Lay one source out under many vision conditions at once on the Compare contact sheet, and find the condition that costs the most.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/compare-conditions.html","h":["Open the sheet","The tiles","The controls","Reorder with the keyboard","A way to use it"],"x":" Compare is a contact sheet: the same source shown under several conditions side by side, each tile measured the same way. Use it to answer \"which of these conditions hurts my design most?\" Select Compare in the view bar. From the Workbench, select Compare this to add the current condition. Press C outside text fields to jump to Compare. The first tile is Normal vision , marked \"control\", so you always have the original to compare against. Every other tile shows: the source under that condition; \"N pairs lost of 45\", the number of reference colour pairs that stop being distinguishable; \"CTA\" and a contrast ratio: the contrast of the mock up's call to action button label on its fill, under the condition; the condition's severity score and name; a grip to reorder it \"Reorder … — drag, or use the arrow keys\" and × to remove it. Select Add a condition it says how many are available to choose from to add another tile. Control What it does Options or range Default Severity for every tile One severity for all tiles 0–100% 100% Order How tiles are sorted By impact , By severity , As arranged — Columns Tiles per row 3 , 4 , 5 — Copy link to this sheet Copies a link that reopens this sheet —"},{"t":"Explore Analytics","d":"See the whole collection of vision conditions by category and severity, and export the catalogue as JSON or CSV.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/explore-analytics.html","h":["Views","The matrix","The collection","Actions"],"x":" Analytics maps the collection of conditions: which categories they fall into, how severe they are estimated to be, and which are the most severe. It reflects the conditions currently showing, so it follows the Catalogue's Level and Kind filters. Choose a view under View : View What it shows Matrix A grid of categories against severity. Each cell counts how many conditions land there. Map A map of how the conditions relate to each other Statistics Figures for the collection Rows are categories and columns are severity scores, running left to right. Each row ends with its count and mean severity, and the last row totals the columns. Colour shows how many conditions are in a cell, not how bad they are: the column already says that. A key shows the range of counts. Select a cell to list the conditions in it. A note explains: \"Severity is an estimated visual impact score, not a clinical grade. It orders the collection; it does not rank anyone's sight.\" A summary of what is showing: how many conditions, how many categories, the mean severity, and how many are per colour transforms and field effects. It notes that the 17 per colour conditions are exactly the 17 the Catalogue calls basic."},{"t":"Links, saving and exports","d":"Share a Vision Lab view as a link, see what the lab remembers in your browser, and export results.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/links-saving-and-exports.html","h":["Share a view as a link","What the lab remembers in your browser","Exports","Save to your library"],"x":" From Button What the link restores Workbench Copy link to this view The Workbench, on the same condition, severity and model Catalogue bar Copy link The level, category, open panels linked or pinned and source image settings Compare Copy link to this sheet The Compare sheet The Catalogue link restores the whole workspace: the level filter, the active category, the open panels and which are linked or pinned , and the source image settings. The Analytics CSV has the columns slug, name, category, complexity, severity score, description and prevalence. Export all CVD records the base colour at several severities for each colour vision type. A Workbench link has the form: text https://auricartisan.com/tool/vision simulation/?vw=deuteranopia:60:vienot The value is the condition's short name, then optionally the severity from 0 to 100, then optionally the model brettel , vienot or machado . Opening such a link always opens the Workbench, whatever view you used last. The Catalogue's link adds v= and an encoded value to the address. The lab keeps that part of the address up to date as you work, without adding history entries, so the address bar always holds a link to your current workspace"},{"t":"The 78 conditions","d":"Every condition the Vision Lab simulates, by category, with its kind, severity score, summary and prevalence as the cards show them.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/the-78-conditions.html","h":["How to read the tables","Color Vision (9)","Cone Isolation (4)","Ocular Conditions (5)","Retinal Dystrophies (20)","Optic Nerve Disorders (9)","Corneal & Anterior Segment (10)","Perceptual Effects (6)","Vascular & Retinal (4)","Vitreous & Structural (4)","Developmental & Congenital (5)","Functional Aging (2)","The 17 colour conditions used by Palette audit"],"x":" The Vision Lab simulates 78 conditions in 11 categories. This page lists them as the cards show them. Severity is an estimated visual impact score from 1 to 10. It orders the collection; it is not a clinical grade and does not rank anyone's sight. Kind is Per colour a colour in, colour out transform: every colour has an exact answer or Field an effect on the visual field, such as blur, lost regions or glare . The 17 per colour conditions are the Catalogue's Basic level; the 61 field conditions are Advanced . Summary and Prevalence are the short texts on each card, with abbreviations such as \"/yr\" and \"HTN\" spelled out here. Prevalence figures are approximate, and some cards say \"Educational\" or \"N/A\" for conditions that are teaching aids rather than diagnoses. Condition Severity Kind Summary Prevalence Protanopia 6 Per colour Red cone absent ~1% males Protanomaly 4 Per colour Red cone weakened ~1% males Deuteranopia 6 Per colour Green cone absent ~1% males Deuteranomaly 3 Per colour Green cone weakened ~5% males Tritanopia 5 Per colour Blue cone absent under 0.01% Tritanomaly 3 Per colour Blue cone weakened under 0.01% Achromatopsia 9 Per colour Total color absence ~1 in 33,000 Co"},{"t":"Use the Workbench","d":"Take one condition apart in the Workbench: choose a specimen, set the base colour, severity and model, and read what collapses.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/use-the-workbench.html","h":["The source column","The stage","The conditions column","The action rail","What is remembered"],"x":" The Workbench shows one condition at a time, in three columns: the source on the left, the stage in the middle, and the list of conditions on the right. It opens with Deuteranopia selected, or with the condition named in the page address. What the stage shows: Specimen What you see Interface A small interface mock up: a header with a Get started button, and a \"Palette health\" card Palette The ten reference swatches as a strip Image Your own image: drop it on the stage, or select Choose an image With the Image specimen, the stage says \"Drop an image on the stage\" and \"Whatever you drop stays on your machine — the pipeline runs in this tab and nothing is uploaded.\" To open a condition's floating panel, see Browse the Catalogue and panels browse the catalogue and panels.md . Type a hex colour into the field up to seven characters, such as E53E3E . Next to it, \"under condition →\" shows the colour it becomes. Under the field, ten swatches the reference strip each have a Use button that makes that swatch the base colour. A slider from 0 to 100%, with marks for Normal , the condition's clinical default for example Clinical default 100% and Full . The figure above it says how strongly the"},{"t":"Vision Lab reference","d":"Every control, option and output of the Vision Lab in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","Workbench","Catalogue","Floating panel","Vision Control","Universal Source Image","Compare","Palette audit","Analytics","Numbers used throughout"],"x":" Item Detail Address https://auricartisan.com/tool/vision simulation/ Masthead facts Conditions 78, Categories 11, Brettel 1997 · Viénot 1999 · Machado 2009 API hint 5 API credits per call to POST /v1/vision/audit Views Workbench , Catalogue , Compare , Palette audit , Analytics Notice Educational visualisation only; not a medical simulation or diagnostic tool; screens are not calibrated Control What it does Values Default Specimen What the stage shows Interface , Palette , Image Interface Base colour The colour to simulate Hex, up to 7 characters E53E3E Reference strip Ten swatches, each with a Use button — — Severity Strength of the condition 0–100% The condition's clinical default Model Colour vision model Brettel , Viénot , Machado Brettel Stage Layout of the stage Split , Simulated only Split Search 78 conditions Filters the condition list Text — List filters Narrow the list All 78 , Colour , Field , Basic only All 78 Open the full panel Opens the condition as a floating panel — — Compare this Adds the condition to Compare — — Copy link to this view Copies a ?vw= link — — Readouts: What collapses reference pairs that fall under ΔE2000 8 from 12 or more and Measured · base colo"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Vision Lab","d":"Common problems in the Vision Lab, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Why: the Level filter is set to Basic , which shows only the per colour conditions. It follows the site wide Simple/Advanced preference. What to do: select Filter , then Level › All . Why: the search and filters together exclude every condition. What to do: select Clear the filters , or clear the search. Why: on the free plan you can open 25 simulations a day from the Catalogue, and today's are used. What to do: use the Workbench , which is not counted, or come back tomorrow. Paid plans have no daily cap. Why: up to five panels can be open; a sixth replaces the oldest panel that is not pinned. What to do: select Pin panel on panels you want to keep, or close panels you no longer need. Why: five panels are open and all five are pinned, or today's free simulations are used. What to do: unpin or close a panel, or check the daily tally. Why: Auto apply to new panels may be off or paused, or the image was loaded before the panels opened. What to do: open Source image and select Apply to all panels . Why: Quality is set to Balanced or Full, which processes more pixels. What to do: choose Fast · 1024px while exploring. Why: the model applies to the colour vision conditions. Field conditi"},{"t":"Vision Lab FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Vision Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/docs/faq.html","h":["Is it free?","Is it a medical tool?","Which models does it use?","What is the difference between per-colour and field conditions?","What does the severity score mean?","What does the severity slider do?","How do I check a whole palette?","Are my images uploaded?","Can I share what I am looking at?","How is this different from the Analyzer's Simulation section?","Can I automate it?"],"x":" Yes. Every simulation is free on every plan. The free plan counts up to 25 simulations a day opened from the Catalogue; paid plans lift that cap. The Workbench, Compare, Palette audit and Analytics are free to use. No. The page says: \"Educational visualisation only. Not a medical simulation, a diagnostic tool, or a substitute for professional eye care — and screen colours are not calibrated.\" It cannot diagnose or test anyone's vision. For the colour vision conditions, the published models of Brettel 1997 , Viénot 1999 and Machado 2009 , calculated in linear light. You can switch between them in the Workbench and in each panel. A per colour condition changes each colour in a predictable way, so every colour has an exact answer. A field condition changes how and where you see, such as blur, dark patches or a lost half of the visual field; colour may survive while the field does not. It is an estimated visual impact score from 1 to 10. It orders the collection; it is not a clinical grade and does not rank anyone's sight. It sets how strongly the model is applied, from 0 normal vision to 100% full expression . As the page puts it, severity is a dial on the model, not a milder diagnos"},{"t":"Vision Lab: supporting material","d":"The Vision Lab's glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy notes.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the Vision Lab guides with the terms they use, the keyboard shortcuts, an honest account of what the simulations are and are not, related tools, the history of changes, and what happens to your images. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms used in the Vision Lab docs Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Every key the lab responds to Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md The models, what they approximate, and what the lab is not Related tools and reading related.md Tools and articles that pair with the lab Release notes release notes.md User facing history from the public changelog Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Vision Lab keyboard shortcuts","d":"Every key the Vision Lab responds to.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Navigation","Panels","Cards and tiles"],"x":" The lab's single key shortcuts work anywhere on the page except while you are typing in a field, and not with Ctrl , Alt or Cmd held. Press ? to see them on screen. Key Action / Focus the search field Esc Clear the search while it has focus ? Show or hide the keyboard shortcuts overlay F Favourites A Analytics C Compare Keys Action R Open a random simulation T Tile all panels 1 to 5 Bring panel 1 to 5 forward Shift + click, or Ctrl + click, on a card Duplicate a panel that is already open Keys Where Action Enter or Space A focused Catalogue card Open its panel Left / Up A Compare tile's grip Move the tile one place earlier Right / Down A Compare tile's grip Move the tile one place later Home / End A Compare tile's grip Move the tile to the start or end For shortcuts that work across the whole site, see Keyboard shortcuts ../../../../site features/keyboard shortcuts/README.md . "},{"t":"Vision Lab glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used by the Vision Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Achromatopsia — Seeing no colour at all, only light and dark. CAM colour appearance model — A model of how a colour looks in context: under a given light, surround and brightness. The panels offer CAT16, CAM16 UCS, CIECAM02 and Hunt Stevens options. CIE xy — A two number description of a colour's hue and saturation chromaticity , plotted on the CIE 1931 diagram. CIEDE2000 ΔE2000 — A formula for colour difference that follows human perception closely. Around 1 is barely noticeable. Clinical default — The severity at which a condition is shown by default. Collapse — Two colours that were clearly different becoming indistinguishable under a condition. The Workbench counts a reference pair as collapsed when it was 12 or more apart and falls within 8 CIEDE2000 . Cone — A light sensitive cell in the eye. L, M and S cones respond to long red , medium green and short blue wavelengths. Correlated colour temperature CCT — The colour of a white light, in kelvin: lower is warmer, higher is cooler. CVD colour vision deficiency — Reduced ability to tell some colours apart, often called colour blindness. Deuteranopia, protanopia, tritanopia — Colour vision deficiencies in which the green , red o"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"How the Vision Lab's simulations are made, how far to trust them, and what the lab is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the simulations are","What changes the result you see","Measurements","Images","What the lab is not"],"x":" Educational visualisations. The page states they are \"not a medical simulation, a diagnostic tool, or a substitute for professional eye care\". They show how a typical case of a condition might affect what you see, to help design and teaching. Per colour conditions use published colour vision models, calculated in linear light colours are converted from screen values to values proportional to light before any maths : Brettel 1997 projects colours onto the plane a dichromat can see, in LMS cone space. Viénot 1999 is a simplified, single plane version of the same idea. Machado 2009 models reduced cone sensitivity, which suits the milder \" anomaly\" forms and partial severities. The floating panels label their version \"Machado like\". The models agree on the broad picture and differ in detail. Try more than one. Field conditions are illustrative effects blur, dimming, lost regions, glare, distortion drawn over the image. They show the kind of loss, not a measured map of any real patient's field. Severity is a dial on the model, not a milder diagnosis. The severity score 1 to 10 is an estimated visual impact score that orders the collection; it is not a clinical grade. Your screen. Scree"},{"t":"Vision Lab privacy","d":"What the Vision Lab does with your colours and images, and what it keeps in your browser.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/privacy.html","h":["Your images stay on your device","What is kept in your browser","The daily count","Links"],"x":" The page says it plainly: \"Whatever you drop stays on your machine — the pipeline runs in this tab and nothing is uploaded.\" Every simulation, measurement and audit runs in your browser. the view you last used, and the Workbench's condition, severity, model, specimen and base colour; the Catalogue category, your favourites, the Compare sheet and the Palette audit palette; the panels you had open, their snapshots, and the position of the Vision Control dock. Clearing this site's data in your browser removes all of it. On the free plan, the lab counts how many simulations you open from the Catalogue each day, and the count is also checked by Auric Artisan. Only the count is involved; your colours and images are not sent. A workspace link v= and a Workbench link ?vw= carry your settings in the address, readable by anyone who has the link. They never contain your own images. The site wide privacy policy is covered in Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Vision Lab release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Vision Lab, from the public changelog and the current page.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current page (September 2026)","v0.9.8 — 2 May 2026","v0.9.6 — 13 April 2026"],"x":" Dated entries come from the public changelog at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The first section describes the page as it is now. The lab opens on a Workbench that takes one condition apart, with Interface , Palette and Image specimens, a severity dial, a choice of Brettel, Viénot or Machado, and measurements of what collapses. Five views sit behind one bar: Workbench , Catalogue , Compare , Palette audit and Analytics . Compare is a contact sheet with a normal vision control tile, ordering by impact or severity, and a choice of 3, 4 or 5 columns. Palette audit checks every pair of up to 24 colours under 17 colour conditions and suggests lightness fixes. Analytics shows the collection as a matrix of categories against severity, with JSON and CSV exports. Floating panels are arranged from a compact Vision Control dock. The medical notice appears once, at the foot of the lab. Vision Simulation moved into the Unified Simulation system as a panel based workflow. Improved protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia simulation models, with revised coefficients validated against published datasets. A multi model comparison view for side by side analysis. Expanded exports for re"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and articles that pair well with the Vision Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Accessibility and vision","u":"website/tools/accessibility-and-vision/vision-simulation/others/related.html","h":["Articles on auricartisan.com"],"x":" Where Why Analyzer ../../analyzer/README.md Preview a whole web page under colour vision filters, and see every text pair under four deficiencies in its A11y+ panel Contrast Checker ../../contrast checker/README.md Check the contrast of a pair once you have chosen new colours Ishihara Plate Generator ../../ishihara plate generator/README.md Generate dot plates that show how colour vision tests work Accessibility Checklist ../../accessibility checklist/README.md Checks c3 and c6 ask for exactly what the Vision Lab shows Perception and vision tools ../../../perception and spectral/README.md Other perception tools on the site Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md Plain language articles on colour vision Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md Run the palette audit from code with POST /v1/vision/audit Vision Simulation User Guide — an earlier guide to the lab. The page has been redesigned since, so some names and layouts differ; this documentation describes the current page: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 24 vision simulation user guide "},{"t":"Colour workspace","d":"The Auric Artisan tools for building palettes and design systems, converting and studying colours, and choosing fonts and icons.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/README.html","h":["Tools in this group","Which tool should I use?","Related"],"x":" The colour workspace is the group of Auric Artisan website tools you use to make things with colour: palettes, gradients, harmonies and whole design systems, plus the fonts and icons that go with them. It also includes the site wide Colour Tools, fourteen floating colour tools you can open over any page. Every tool runs in your browser. Most work without an account; saving to your Library and some account features need you to sign in. Each tool has its own folder with an overview, task guides, a full reference, troubleshooting, a glossary and notes on accuracy and privacy. Tool Address What it is for Docs Basic Color Tools https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/ A panel workspace with seven everyday tools Palette Studio, Palette Remix, Gradient Maker, Color Picker, Color Battle, Collage Maker, Quick Converter and the home of the fourteen site wide Colour Tools. basic colour tools/ basic colour tools/README.md Color Science Lab https://auricartisan.com/tool/color science lab/ Colour science models and analyses in floating panels: colour spaces, conversions, colour difference and more. colour science lab/ colour science lab/README.md Personalization Generator https://auricartisan"},{"t":"ASCII Art Generator","d":"What the ASCII Art Generator is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to turn a picture or a word into character art and take it away as text, image or code.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The ASCII Art Generator turns a picture into character art: rows of letters, symbols, blocks or Braille dots whose density follows the light and dark of the image. You drop in a photo, a screenshot or a logo, or type a word, and the art appears straight away and updates as you change anything. Five ready made looks cover most needs. Behind Fine tuning sit the controls that decide how the picture is read: seven character sets or your own ramp, the cell shape, brightness model, gamma and contrast, three sampling methods, Floyd–Steinberg and Bayer dithering, edge aware glyph choice, the output font, filters such as flip, rotate and frame, and a seed. The art can be shown as plain text, colour HTML, a canvas image or SVG. Everything happens in your browser. Pictures are read and converted on your device and are not uploaded. You can copy the art, or download it as TXT, PNG, SVG, HTML, JSON, CSV or a colour ANSI file for terminals. An Analysis tab and a Compare tab measure the character sets and the render for anyone who wants to know why the art looks the way it does. Developers who want a banner for a README, a terminal or a commit message. Designers and artists making text based art"},{"t":"ASCII Art Generator documentation","d":"The list of guides for the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the page, learn the layout, make your first piece. sources.md sources.md Image, Text and Webcam sources; dropping, pasting and the example. looks colour and detail.md looks colour and detail.md The five looks, mono or colour, ink and paper, detail and invert. fine tuning.md fine tuning.md Character set, shape, tone, sampling, edges, type, filters and advanced settings. render modes.md render modes.md Text, HTML, Canvas and SVG renders; the readouts; full screen. charts and compare.md charts and compare.md The Analysis tab's charts and benchmark, and the Compare tab's character set table. export.md export.md Copy, every download format, Export all, and batch rendering. reference.md reference.md Every control, range, default and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. ASCII Art Generator overview ../README.md Supporting material ../others/README.md "},{"t":"Getting started with the ASCII Art Generator","d":"Open the ASCII Art Generator, learn its layout, and make and copy your first piece of character art.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","The layout","The empty stage","Your first piece","Next steps","Related"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/ascii/. The masthead reads ASCII Art Generator , Drop in a picture and get character art back. Nothing is uploaded — every pixel is read and converted in this browser. , with a row of labels and Developer reference → . A short strip under it reads Drop a picture , Pick a look , Take it away and It converts as you go. Its × hides it for good on this browser. Four tabs: Lab , Analysis , Compare and Export . You do almost everything in Lab . Lab has two parts: The control rail on the left: Source : Image , Text or Webcam , and the controls for the one you pick; Look : five named looks, a strip showing the characters in use from Light to Dark , and their count, such as 10 glyphs ; Colour : Mono or From image , and in Mono the Ink and Paper colours; Detail : how many characters wide the art is, and Invert for dark paper ; Fine tuning : a button that opens every other setting, in folded groups. The stage on the right: Render chips Text , HTML , Canvas , SVG and the render time, the art itself, and a footer with Grid , Chars , Render , Copy and Full screen . Select any group heading in the rail to fold it away or open it again. On screens narrower than"},{"t":"Charts, benchmark and Compare","d":"The measurements, charts and benchmark in the Analysis tab, and the character set comparison in the Compare tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/charts-and-compare.html","h":["The Analysis tab","The Compare tab","Related"],"x":" The Analysis and Compare tabs explain why the art looks the way it does. You do not need them to make art; they help when a result bands, looks flat or converts slowly. The left column repeats the facts of the last conversion: Grid , Characters and Render time in milliseconds ; Character set , and Ramp the number of glyphs, for example 10 glyphs ; Sampler and Dithering . Run benchmark converts the current source ten times with the current settings and reports the average, for example Avg: 18.4 ms 10 runs , and the Min , Max and Spread . Use it to see which setting makes conversion slow. With the Image source and no picture loaded, it reads Load an image first . Six charts. Each has a ⛶ button, and you can also double click a chart, to open it full screen. Close the full screen chart with × , Esc , or by selecting the dark background. Chart What it shows What to look for Glyph density calibration The ink of each character in the current set, measured by drawing it at 32 × 32 pixels, sorted light to dark. A smooth rise. Big jumps or flat runs mean some tones have no matching character. Character frequency How often each character appears in the latest output. A spike at one end mean"},{"t":"Copy, export and batch","d":"Copy the art, download it as TXT, PNG, SVG, HTML, JSON, CSV or ANSI, export several files at once, and render a list of words in one go.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/export.html","h":["Copy","Download one format","Export several files at once","Batch: render a list of words","Save to your Library","Related"],"x":" Every file is built in your browser and handed straight to your downloads. Nothing is uploaded. Copy under the art copies the plain characters. The message reads Copied! Copy for terminal in the ANSI card copies the art with colour codes, for pasting into a terminal. The message reads Copied with colour — paste into a terminal , or just Copied if colour is off. Paste plain text into a place that uses a monospaced font a code block, a terminal, a text editor , or the columns will not line up. Open the Export tab. Each card has a download button. Card Button File What it contains TXT Download .txt ascii art.txt The characters, one line per row, with filters applied. PNG Download .png ascii art.png A picture of the art. SVG Download .svg ascii art.svg Vector art with selectable characters. HTML Download .html ascii art.html A standalone web page. The only download that keeps colour as coloured text. JSON Download .json ascii research.json The characters and every setting that produced them. CSV Download .csv ascii analysis.csv How often each character appears. ANSI Download .ans ascii art.ans The characters with 24 bit colour codes for terminals. A message confirms each download, for"},{"t":"Fine tuning","d":"Every setting behind the Fine tuning button — character set and custom ramp, shape, tone, sampling and dithering, edges, type, filters and advanced options.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/fine-tuning.html","h":["Character set","Shape","Tone","Sampling","Edges","Type","Filters","Advanced","Related"],"x":" Select Fine tuning at the bottom of the rail to open eight more groups. Each starts folded; select a group's heading to open it. Every change re converts the art a moment later. Changing anything here clears the highlight on the Look buttons, since the art no longer matches a named look. A menu of seven sets, each listed light to dark: Set Characters Count Standard space .: =+ %@ 10 Detailed space and 69 punctuation marks, letters and digits 70 Blocks space ░▒▓█ 5 Minimal space .: @ 5 Symbols space ·•●◉⬤ 6 Lines space and box drawing characters ─│┌┐└┘ and more 23 Braille space and all 255 Braille patterns 256 Custom ramp lets you type your own characters, lightest first and darkest last, up to 200. It needs at least two characters; with fewer, the set chosen in the menu is used. Start with a space so the lightest areas stay empty, for example .oO@ . The Look strip in the rail always shows the set actually in use, custom ramp included. Character cells are taller than they are wide, so without correction the art comes out stretched. Control Range Default What it does Match the output font on or off on Measures the output font and sets Cell aspect to match it. Cell aspect 0.2 to 1.2 "},{"t":"Looks, colour and detail","d":"The five named looks, mono or colour art, ink and paper, the Detail slider and Invert for dark paper.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/looks-colour-and-detail.html","h":["Look","Colour","Detail","Related"],"x":" The three groups under Source are the ones most people need: Look , Colour and Detail . Five buttons. Each sets a character set and a few tone and edge settings at once, then re converts the art. Look Character set What it sets Classic Standard Gamma 1, contrast 0.15, edge aware on, edge weight 0.65 Blocks Blocks Gamma 1, contrast 0.2, edge aware off Fine Detailed Gamma 1, contrast 0.1, edge aware on, edge weight 0.5 Bold Minimal Gamma 0.9, contrast 0.45, edge aware off Line art Standard Gamma 1.4, contrast 0.6, edge aware on, edge weight 1 Classic is highlighted when the page opens, but its contrast is not applied until you select it. If you change anything in Fine tuning , the highlight clears, because the art no longer matches a named look. Under the buttons, a strip shows the characters in use from Light to Dark , and the heading counts them, for example 10 glyphs . Sets longer than 24 characters are shown as an even sample of 24. Classic suits most photos. Blocks gives solid, graphic shading and works well at small sizes. Fine uses a long ramp of 70 characters and keeps the most tonal detail at large widths. Bold uses only four marks and a space, for strong, poster like art. "},{"t":"Render modes and full screen","d":"The Text, HTML, Canvas and SVG renders, the readouts under the art, and the full-screen view.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/render-modes.html","h":["The four renders","The readouts","Copy","Full screen","Related"],"x":" The Render chips above the art choose how it is shown. The characters are the same in every mode; what changes is how they are drawn and what they can carry. Chip Shows the art as Colour Filters Best for Text Plain characters in the page's text colour No Yes Copying and pasting HTML Characters in coloured runs on your paper colour Yes No Colour art on screen and the HTML download Canvas A picture drawn at the output font and size Yes Yes A pixel exact PNG SVG Vector text, one line per row Yes Yes Scalable art and the SVG download Colour means the render can show From image colour. See Looks, colour and detail looks colour and detail.md . Filters means the render shows the filters from Fine tuning . The HTML render always shows the art before filters. Choosing From image switches to HTML , and choosing Mono switches back to Text . You can pick another chip afterwards. The Text and HTML renders are scaled to fit the stage. The Canvas and SVG renders are drawn at the Size set under Type in Fine tuning , and shrink to fit the stage width if they are wider. The footer under the art shows: Grid : columns × rows, for example 100 × 42 ; Chars : the number of characters; Render : how long "},{"t":"Choose a source","d":"Convert an image, a line of text or a webcam frame, and every way to get a picture into the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/sources.html","h":["Image","Text","Webcam","Related"],"x":" The Source group at the top of the rail has three buttons: Image , Text and Webcam . Switching source converts the new source at once if it has something to show, or returns to the empty stage if it has not. Use a photo, screenshot, logo or drawing. Ways to load one: select the drop area Drop an image, or click to browse or Choose a file on the empty stage, and pick a file; drag a file anywhere onto the tool; the stage highlights while you drag; copy an image and press Ctrl + V Cmd + V on a Mac anywhere on the page, as long as you are not typing in a field; select Try an example to load a built in picture of a lit sphere on a dark gradient. Accepted types are PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, SVG and TIFF, up to 20 MB. Whether TIFF opens depends on your browser. After loading, the rail shows the picture's size, such as 1200 × 800 px . Pictures larger than 4,000 pixels on a side, or larger than 12 megapixels, are scaled down first, and a note says so, for example Downscaled from 6000×4000 to 4000×2667 . The art never needs that much detail, so you will not normally see a difference. Clear removes the picture and returns the stage to its empty state. An animated GIF is converted as a singl"},{"t":"ASCII Art Generator reference","d":"Every control, range, default, file and message in the ASCII Art Generator in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/reference.html","h":["Address","Tabs","Source","Look, colour and detail","Fine tuning","Character sets","Stage","Files","Messages","Related"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com/tool/ascii/ https://auricartisan.com/ascii opens the same page. Tab Purpose Lab Source, look, colour, detail, fine tuning, and the art. Analysis Readouts, benchmark and six charts. Compare Ink measurements for all seven character sets. Export Seven download formats, Export all, and batch rendering. Control Values Default Source Image , Text , Webcam Image Image file PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, SVG, TIFF; up to 20 MB none Large images Scaled to at most 4,000 px a side and 12 megapixels always Text any text ASCII Text font monospace, Courier New, Consolas, Monaco, Fira Code, Source Code Pro monospace Text size 8 to 128 px 48 Text weight Normal, Bold, Black Bold White on black on or off off Keep converting every frame on or off off Smooth between frames on or off off Control Values Default Look Classic , Blocks , Fine , Bold , Line art Classic highlighted Colour Mono , From image Mono Ink any colour f0f0f0 Paper any colour 0f0e0c Detail 20 to 300 columns 100 Invert for dark paper on or off follows the paper Group Control Values Default Character set Set Standard, Detailed, Blocks, Minimal, Symbols, Lines, Braille Standard Character set Custom ramp 2 to 200 cha"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for common problems in the ASCII Art Generator, from files that will not load to downloads that do not match the art.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Nothing happens when I open the page","My file will not load","Pasting a picture does nothing","The webcam will not start","The art looks stretched or squashed","The art looks like a negative","The art is too dark, too light or flat","Smooth areas show bands","Colour does not show","Filters do nothing","The PNG, SVG or HTML download does not match the art","The ANSI download says to turn colour on","Export all gave me five files, not six","Full screen shows no colour","The Analysis charts are empty","Conversion is slow or lags behind the sliders","Related"],"x":" That is expected: the stage waits for a source. Choose a file, drop or paste a picture, select Try an example , or switch to Text . There is no Render button; conversion starts by itself. Unsupported file type : use PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, SVG or TIFF. Convert other formats, such as HEIC, first. File too large : the limit is 20 MB. Save a smaller copy or a JPEG. Failed to load image : the file may be damaged, or your browser cannot read that format. TIFF in particular opens only in some browsers. Click on an empty part of the page first, so you are not typing in a field, then press Ctrl + V Cmd + V on a Mac . The clipboard must hold an image, not a link to one. At the time of writing, auricartisan.com tells browsers not to allow camera access on any of its pages. Start then shows a message that camera permission was denied. Changing permissions in your browser does not help. Take a photo with your camera app and load it with Image instead. Leave Match the output font on in Fine tuning › Shape , so the cell shape matches the font. If you pasted the art somewhere else, use a monospaced font there too; a proportional font breaks the columns. If Lock row count is on, the row count "},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/docs/faq.html","h":["Are my pictures uploaded?","Do I need an account?","Is it really ASCII?","Which settings give the best result?","How wide should the art be?","Can I keep the colours?","Can I make animated ASCII art?","Can I convert text into big letters?","Why does my text look wrong when I paste it?","Can I load a JSON file back in?","Does it work on a phone?","Related"],"x":" No. Pictures are read and converted in your browser and never leave your device. Downloads are built on your device too. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . No. The generator works without signing in. Only the Standard , Detailed and Minimal sets use plain ASCII characters. Blocks , Symbols , Lines and Braille use Unicode characters, which need a font that has them and may not display in every terminal or app. Start with a look: Classic for photos, Line art for logos and drawings, Blocks for small, bold art, Fine for large, detailed art. Then adjust Detail for the space you have. Pictures with a clear subject and strong contrast convert best. It depends on where it goes. A README or chat message fits 60 to 100 columns; a terminal is often 80 to 120 columns wide; a poster or a PNG can go up to 300. Yes, with From image . Colour survives in the HTML, PNG from the Canvas render , SVG and ANSI downloads. Plain text and Copy carry no colour; Copy for terminal does. Not on this page. An animated GIF is converted as one still frame, and the webcam source cannot currently be used on the site. Yes. Choose Text as the source, type a word, and pick a font, size and weight. The word is drawn a"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"The glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used by the generator. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Known limits and what the measurements mean. related.md related.md Tools and reading that go with the generator. privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what is remembered. ASCII Art Generator overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + V Cmd + V on a Mac Anywhere on the page, when not typing in a field Loads an image from the clipboard. Drag a file onto the tool Lab Loads the image. Enter or Space On a group heading in the rail Folds or opens the group. Double click a chart Analysis Opens the chart full screen. Esc Full screen chart Closes it. The full screen view of the art closes with × only. Getting started ../docs/getting started.md Supporting material README.md "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Terms used in the ASCII Art Generator and its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning ANSI colour codes Escape sequences that terminals read as colour instructions. The ANSI download uses 24 bit true colour codes. Area average A sampling method that averages every pixel under a character cell. The page labels it SAT, after the summed area table that makes it fast. Bayer matrix A fixed grid of thresholds used for ordered dithering, here 4 × 4 or 8 × 8. Bilinear sampling Reads a cell's value by blending the four nearest pixels. Braille pattern One of the 256 characters made of up to eight raised dots, used here as fine texture. Cell aspect A character cell's width divided by its height. Used to keep the art in proportion. Character set, ramp The characters the art is drawn with, ordered from least ink to most. Density How much of a character's cell is covered by ink, from 0 to 1. Dithering Spreading the rounding error between cells so that smooth tones appear as texture rather than bands. Edge aware selection Swapping in a thin line character where the picture has a strong edge. Floyd–Steinberg An error diffusion dithering method that passes each cell's error to its neighbours. Gamma A curve applied to brightness before conversion. Here, above 1 lightens"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"Known limits of the ASCII Art Generator and what its measurements can and cannot tell you.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Size limits","Sources","Fonts decide how the art looks","Colour","Filters","Edge-aware selection","Downloads","The benchmark","Related"],"x":" Limit Value Image file 20 MB Image size used Up to 4,000 pixels a side and 12 megapixels; larger pictures are scaled down Width of the art 20 to 300 characters Locked row count 10 to 300 rows Custom ramp 2 to 200 characters Render timeline The last 100 conversions The webcam source cannot currently be used on auricartisan.com, because the site does not allow camera access on its pages. An animated GIF is converted as a single still frame. TIFF opens only in browsers that can display TIFF images. The Text source draws with fonts installed on your device; a missing font is replaced by another. Character art depends on a monospaced font. The same characters look different in different fonts, and wrong in a proportional one. Match the output font measures the chosen output font to keep proportions right, but the place you paste the art into uses its own font. The glyph density measurements in Analysis and Compare are made by drawing characters with the fonts on your device, so they can differ slightly from one computer to another. Text and Copy carry no colour. Colour needs the HTML, Canvas or SVG render, or the ANSI file. The HTML render shows the art before filters and Thin out . Wi"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the ASCII Art Generator keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" Pictures you load, paste or drop are read and converted on your device. They are not uploaded. Text you type is drawn and converted the same way. Every download is built in your browser. In your browser's local storage: whether you dismissed the Drop a picture · Pick a look · Take it away strip. In the page address: like other pages on the site, the generator keeps the values of its controls in the address after p= , so a reload restores them. Your picture is not part of the address. If you share the address, the other person gets your settings, not your picture. See Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md . Loading the page and its scripts. The Library's Save to Library , if you use it, stores the art and settings in your Auric Artisan Library. See the Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Site wide analytics and advertising follow your cookie choices. See the Help centre ../../../../../help/README.md . Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md Copy, export and batch ../docs/export.md "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and reading that go with the ASCII Art Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/ascii-art-generator/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Site features","Reading","Related"],"x":" Image and file tools ../../../image and file tools/README.md : prepare, crop or recolour a picture before converting it. Basic Color Tools ../../basic colour tools/README.md : pick ink and paper colours, or build a palette from a picture. Font Library ../../font library/README.md : find a monospaced font for your art. Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md : how the page address keeps your settings, so a reload or a shared link restores them. Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md : find art you saved to your Library. ASCII Art Generator developer reference https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 24 ascii art generator developer reference : the technical write up linked from the page's masthead. Supporting material README.md "},{"t":"Basic Color Tools","d":"What Basic Color Tools is, who it is for, where to find it and how to start using its panel workspace and the site-wide Colour Tools.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Basic Color Tools is a workspace for everyday colour work on the Auric Artisan website. It brings seven small tools together on one page: Palette Studio , Palette Remix , Gradient Maker , Color Picker , Color Battle , Collage Maker and Quick Converter . Each tool opens as a floating panel with a controls sidebar on the left and a work area on the right. You can keep up to five panels open at once, move and resize them, dock them, and switch between them without leaving the page. The same folder also documents the Colour Tools workbench: fourteen further floating tools such as Color Inspector , Contrast System and CMYK Soft Proof that you can open on any page of the site from the right click menu, with Ctrl + Shift + C , or by adding ?color= to a page address. When a page cannot open those tools, the site sends you to Basic Color Tools instead, so the two belong together. Everything runs in your browser. Palettes, gradients, colours and collages are computed on your device, images you add are read locally, and your preferences favourites, level, last view are remembered in your browser's local storage. You can save results to your Auric Artisan Library and reopen them in the right "},{"t":"Basic Color Tools documentation","d":"The list of every guide for Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools workbench.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/README.html","h":["Guides in this folder","Subfolders","Related"],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Basic Color Tools page and everything on it: the three views, the panel windows, the seven workspace tools, and the fourteen site wide Colour Tools. Start with the getting started guide, then open the guide for the tool you need. The reference lists every control in one place. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the page, tour the screen, make and export a first palette. workspace and panels.md workspace and panels.md Workspace, Catalogue and Panels views; search, level and favourites; moving, docking and closing panels. import export and library.md import export and library.md Every copy and download format, the palette share link, Save to Library and reopening saved items. reference.md reference.md Every control, option, range, default and output format of the workspace and its seven tools. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, why they happen and what to do. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. Folder What it covers panel tools/ panel tools/README.md One guide per workspace tool: Palette Studio, Palette Remix, Gradient Maker, Color Picker, Color Battle, Collage Maker, Quick Converter. colour to"},{"t":"Getting started with Basic Color Tools","d":"Open Basic Color Tools, learn the parts of the screen, and make, check and export your first palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first palette","Work with two tools at once","Next steps","Related"],"x":" This guide takes you from opening the page to exporting a checked palette. It takes about five minutes. 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/ in a current desktop or mobile browser. JavaScript must be enabled. 2. Wait for the page to load. You see the title Basic Color Tools , a short description, and a row of labels: 4 Categories , 7 Tools , Palette Remix · Color Battle , Sidebar + Panel Layout and In page Floating Panels . 3. Below the title is a row of three view buttons: Workspace , Catalogue and Panels . The page opens on Workspace the first time, and on the view you used last after that. View What it shows Workspace A launcher list on the left and a stage on the right. Tools you open appear as panels on the stage. This is where you work. Catalogue A searchable grid of tool cards with a category filter, a level switch, favourites and a copy link button. Use it to browse and filter. Panels A list of the panels that are open, each with its state, and a reminder of what the panel title bar buttons do. Open a tool left column lists every tool the catalogue currently shows, grouped by category: Generate , Pick , Compose and Convert . Each row has a small colour band,"},{"t":"Import, export and the Library","d":"Every way to bring colours and images into Basic Color Tools, every copy and download format, the palette share link, and saving to and reopening from your Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/import-export-and-library.html","h":["Bringing colours and images in","Copy and download formats","The palette share link","Save to Library","Reopening saved items","Related"],"x":" Open panels in Basic Color Tools are not kept when you reload or leave the page. To keep your work, copy it, download it, or save it to your Auric Artisan Library. This guide lists every way in and out. Into How Accepts Palette Studio From Image Any image file your browser can open. Colours are extracted on your device. Palette Studio Select a HEX label on a strip Any colour, through the site colour picker. Palette Remix Seed colors box HEX, rgb , rgba , hsl , hsla , hsv , oklch , separated by lines, spaces, commas, semicolons or vertical bars. Color Battle Team A and Team B boxes Same as Palette Remix, up to nine colours per team. Gradient Maker Stop HEX boxes and colour wells Three or six digit HEX, or the browser's picker. Color Picker HEX box, colour well, Pick eyedropper HEX; any pixel on screen where the eyedropper is supported. Quick Converter Input box, colour well HEX, rgb , rgba , hsl , hsla , hsv , oklch . Collage Maker + Add Images , or select a cell Image files from your device. Any tool Your Library Saved palettes, gradients and colours reopen in the matching tool. See below. Colours you type in any of the text boxes are converted to sRGB HEX codes. Values outside th"},{"t":"Workspace and panels","d":"How the Workspace, Catalogue and Panels views work, how to find tools, and how to move, resize, dock, duplicate and close panels.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/workspace-and-panels.html","h":["The three views","The Workspace view","The Catalogue view","The Panels view","Working with panels","Related"],"x":" Basic Color Tools is a panel workspace. You open tools as floating windows called panels, keep several on screen, and arrange them as you like. This guide explains the three views of the page, the catalogue's filters, and every way to handle a panel. A panel is a movable, resizable window inside the page. It holds one tool. Panels are not browser windows or tabs, so they disappear when you reload or leave the page. The row of buttons under the page title switches between three views. The page remembers the view you used last, in your browser's local storage, and opens on it next time. The first visit opens on Workspace . View Use it to Workspace Open tools from a short list and work with them on a stage. Catalogue Browse tool cards, search, filter by category and level, and mark favourites. Panels See which panels are open and in what state, and read what each title bar button does. Open panels are never closed by switching views. In the Workspace view they sit inside the stage. In the Catalogue and Panels views they float over the whole page. When you return to Workspace they move back into the stage. The Open a tool list on the left shows the tools, grouped under their category "},{"t":"Basic Color Tools reference","d":"Every control, option, range, default and output of the Basic Color Tools page, its views and its seven panel tools, with pointers to the Colour Tools references.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","View buttons","Workspace view","Catalogue view","Panels view","Panel window","Palette Studio","Palette Remix","Gradient Maker","Color Picker","Color Battle","Collage Maker","Quick Converter","Save to Library","Colour Tools","Related"],"x":" This page lists every control on the Basic Color Tools page. Defaults are given only where the page sets one. For the fourteen Colour Tools, each tool's guide ends with its own full controls table; see Colour Tools colour tools at the end. Item Value Address https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/ also https://auricartisan.com/basic tools Tools 7, in 4 categories Maximum open panels 5 Sign in Not needed to use the tools Works offline The tools compute everything in the browser once the page has loaded Control What it does Values Default Workspace Launcher, capacity meter and stage — Shown on first visit Catalogue Card grid with filters — — Panels List of open panels and a title bar legend — — Last view Reopens on the view you used last Stored in your browser — Control What it does Open a tool rows Open a tool, or bring its open panel forward restoring it if docked . Rows show Advanced and open labels. Panels meter Shows N of 5 open , a bar, and Room for N more. or the ceiling message. Panels entries One per panel with Floating , Docked or Maximised . Select to bring it forward. Stage Holds the panels in this view. Shows Nothing open yet. when empty. Control What it does Values "},{"t":"Troubleshooting Basic Color Tools","d":"Symptoms you may meet in Basic Color Tools, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Panels","Copying, downloading and sharing","Colours and images","Saving to the Library","Related"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom, the reason, and what to do. For problems with the site wide Colour Tools, see also Open the Colour Tools and manage their panels colour tools/launcher and panels.md . Why: five panels is the limit. Opening a sixth closes the panel that was opened earliest. What to do: before opening a sixth tool, save or export what you need from the oldest panel, or close a panel you no longer need. The Workspace Panels meter shows how many slots are left. Why: Escape inside a panel closes it or, if it is maximised, restores its size first . What to do: select outside the panel before pressing Escape for other purposes. Closed panels cannot be reopened with their work; save to your Library as you go. Why: a minimised panel is hidden completely and kept in a dock. What to do: in the Workspace view, select it in the Panels list, or select the tool again in Open a tool . In the Catalogue, choose Open Panels in the category list and select its card. Why: open panels and their contents live only in the page. They are not saved when you reload or leave. What to do: copy, download or Save to Library before leaving. See Import, export and the Library import export and librar"},{"t":"Basic Color Tools FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools workbench.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account?","Does it cost anything or use tokens?","Are my images uploaded?","How many panels can I have open?","Why are some tools missing from the list?","Will my work still be there tomorrow?","Can I open the same tool twice?","What is the difference between Color Picker and Quick Converter?","What is the difference between Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools?","Which contrast standard do the tools use?","Is the ASE export an Adobe swatch file?","Where are the palette, shade and gradient collections?","Related"],"x":" No. All seven tools and the Colour Tools work without signing in. Saving to your Library uses the site's Library; see the Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md and Account and billing ../../../../account and billing/README.md . The seven tools compute everything in your browser and do not call the server for their results, so they do not spend tool tokens. See Account and billing ../../../../account and billing/README.md for plans. No. Images you add to Palette Studio From Image or Collage Maker are read by your browser on your device. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Five. Opening a sixth closes the oldest one. See Workspace and panels workspace and panels.md . The Catalogue's Level switch or search is filtering them, and the Workspace list follows the Catalogue. Set Level to Both , clear the search and choose All Tools . Open panels are not saved. Your favourites, level, category and last view are remembered in your browser. To keep results, export them or use Save to Library . Yes. Select Open another instance on the panel's title bar, or hold Shift , Ctrl or Cmd while selecting the tool's card in the Catalogue. Each copy has its own state. Color Picker is built "},{"t":"Colour Tools workbench","d":"The fourteen floating Colour Tools you can open on any page of Auric Artisan, how to open them, and a guide for each.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/README.html","h":["Opening and managing the tools","Essentials","Explore","Design","Deep dive","Related"],"x":" The Colour Tools are fourteen floating colour tools that open over whatever page you are on: right click and use the Colour tools group, press Ctrl + Shift + C , right click a colour value, or add ?color= to a page address. They share one launcher, one kind of panel window and a control bar for arranging panels. Basic Color Tools is their home page, and this folder documents them. Start with launcher and panels.md launcher and panels.md , then open the guide for the tool you need. File What it covers launcher and panels.md launcher and panels.md Every way to open the tools, the ?color= address parameters, the launcher, the panel window, linking and pinning, the control bar, and what all fourteen tools share. File Tool In one line colour inspector.md colour inspector.md Color Inspector Everything about one colour: formats, contrast, vision, harmony, names, psychology, scales, science and code export. accessibility lab.md accessibility lab.md Accessibility Lab Two to six colours under WCAG 2.1, 2.2, APCA or ISO 9241 3, with a vision filter grid. contrast system.md contrast system.md Contrast System Up to five foregrounds on one background: three measures, fixes, APCA size table, con"},{"t":"Accessibility Lab","d":"Compare two to six colours under WCAG 2.1, WCAG 2.2, APCA or ISO 9241-3, preview text in them, and see every colour through seven vision filters.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/accessibility-lab.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Tasks","Standards and levels","Vision filters","Presets","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Accessibility Lab checks a small set of colours, from two to six, as a group. The first colour is the background; the others are foreground colours such as text, buttons and icons. The lab shows a contrast matrix for every pair under the standard you choose, a live text sample in your first two colours, and a grid showing each colour through seven vision filters with its contrast against the background. It supports four ways of measuring contrast: WCAG 2.1 and WCAG 2.2 : the luminance contrast ratio, from 1:1 to 21:1. Both versions use the same formula. WCAG 3 APCA : the Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, reported as Lc lightness contrast . It takes into account which colour is the text and which is the background. ISO 9241 3 : luminance modulation, a measure from an older ergonomics standard for display text. Accessibility Lab is in the launcher's Essentials group. Open the launcher and select Accessibility Lab , or pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group. See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with a dark navy background 0F172A and one foreground: the colour you opened it with, or gold D3AF37 . Standard : WCAG 2.1, WCAG 2.2, WCAG 3 APC"},{"t":"Animation Contrast","d":"Sample an animated background, from CSS keyframe colours or a video file, at 48 points, check text contrast at each one, find the worst frame and get a text colour that passes throughout.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/animation-contrast.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Thresholds","Tasks","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Most contrast checks assume the background stays still. Hero sections with animated gradients, background videos and colour transitions do not: text that is readable at the start of a loop can become unreadable for part of it. Animation Contrast checks the whole timeline. You give it a text colour and an animated background, either a list of keyframe colours or a video file. It takes 48 evenly spaced samples along the timeline, checks the text against each one with the standard you choose, shows a pass or fail strip, picks out the worst moment, and suggests a single text colour that would pass at every sample. Animation Contrast is in the launcher's Essentials group. Open the launcher and select Animation Contrast . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . The text colour starts as the colour you opened the tool with, or white FFFFFF . 1. Setup Text + animated background : Text color : a colour field. Threshold : the standard to test against. Source : CSS keyframes or Video frames . 2. The background section: For CSS keyframes : Keyframe stops , with a note such as 4 colors · interpolated in OKLab , one numbered colour row per stop, and + Add stop , − Remove last and Res"},{"t":"CMYK Soft-Proof","d":"Simulate a screen colour or an image on five press and paper conditions, see the CMYK separation after dot gain and ink limits, spot colours that will shift, and copy CMYK values.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/cmyk-soft-proof.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Press conditions","How the simulation works","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Screens mix light; printing presses lay down ink on paper. Many bright screen colours cannot be printed, paper is never pure white, printed black is never pure black, and ink spreads as it soaks in. CMYK Soft Proof gives you a quick feel for these effects. It takes a colour, or an image you drop in, and shows how it may look on one of five print conditions, the CMYK ink amounts involved, and which parts of an image will change most. Soft proofing means previewing on screen how something will print. CMYK is the four ink process cyan, magenta, yellow and black . Dot gain is the darkening of mid tones as ink spreads on paper. TAC total area coverage is the maximum combined ink a press allows, in percent C + M + Y + K, up to 400 % . This tool is an intuition builder, not a colour managed proof. It does not use ICC profiles. CMYK Soft Proof is in the launcher's Design group. Open the launcher and select CMYK Soft Proof . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with the colour you opened with, or a process blue 0085CA . 1. Source Soft proof preview : a colour field, the Press condition list, and a note describing the condition its TAC limit, paper colour, black poin"},{"t":"Color Formulation","d":"Read one colour as channels, follow it through the conversion pipeline, see a reflectance sketch, and get a two-pigment paint mix that comes close to it.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-formulation.html","h":["How to open it","Screen tour","Walkthroughs","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Formulation takes one colour apart. It shows the numbers a screen stores for the colour, how those numbers are converted into the perceptual spaces designers use, a sketch of how a painted surface of that colour might reflect light, and which two artist pigments, mixed in which ratio, come closest to it. Use it when you want to understand a colour rather than only copy its code: to teach or learn how sRGB, linear light and OKLab relate, to judge whether a colour is a light tint or a deep shade, or to get a starting point for mixing a physical paint that matches a screen colour. Everything is calculated in your browser from the colour you enter. The paint recipe and the reflectance chart are simplified models, not measurements; see Accuracy and limits accuracy and limits . Open Color Formulation from the Deep dive group of the Colour Tools launcher tag FORM or from the Color Inspector's Open in list, which passes the inspected colour in; see Open the Colour Tools and manage their panels launcher and panels.md . If you open it with a colour, it starts with that colour. Otherwise it starts with D3AF37 . The panel has a sidebar on the left and a tabbed main area on the right. Wh"},{"t":"Color Inspector","d":"Use the Color Inspector to read one colour in every format, check it for contrast and colour-vision safety, find its name, build scales and harmonies, and export it as code.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-inspector.html","h":["How to open it","Screen tour","Walkthroughs","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" The Color Inspector takes one colour and shows you everything the site can work out about it. A plain language summary tells you how light, saturated, warm and readable the colour is. Around it sit ten tabs of detail: more than forty notations, contrast against real surfaces, how the colour looks with colour vision deficiencies, harmonies, the nearest named colours and industry swatches, colour psychology, tint and shade scales, spectral science, and ready to paste code. Use it when you meet a colour and want to know whether you can use it, and how. It is also the tool behind the site's ?color= links: add ?color= and a hex code to any page address and the Inspector opens over that page. The Inspector is one of the six Essentials in the Colour Tools. It opens in a floating panel; for moving, resizing and closing panels, see Open the Colour Tools and manage their panels launcher and panels.md . Launcher: right click the page, choose Colour tools › All colour tools… or press Ctrl + Shift + C , then select Color Inspector in the Essentials group. Right click a colour: when you right click a hex code or a colour swatch on the site, choose Inspect in Colour Tools . The Inspector opens w"},{"t":"Color Library","d":"Search and filter 1,058 named colours by family, open any colour's detail view with sixteen formats, a triadic harmony and similar colours, and download a swatch as SVG or PNG.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-library.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Families","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Library is a browsable catalogue of 1,058 named colours, such as Crimson , Dusty Rose or Gunmetal , grouped into 13 families. You can search by name or HEX code, filter by family, page through the results, and open any colour for a detail view with every common format, its temperature, contrast against white and black, a triadic harmony and the twelve most similar named colours. This in panel library is different from the site's large colour collections palettes, shades, gradients and the colour atlas in the library area; for those, see Colour libraries ../../../../../library/colour libraries/README.md . Color Library is in the launcher's Explore group. Open the launcher and select Color Library , or pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group. See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . If you open it with a colour for example from another tool , it starts on that colour's detail view; otherwise it starts on the list. A search box Search by name or hex… . A Category list: All and the 13 families. A count of matching colours, for example 146 colors . A grid of up to 60 colour cells per page, each with a swatch, name and HEX code. A pager: ‹ Prev , Page N of"},{"t":"Color Name Finder","d":"Enter a colour and find the closest of more than a thousand named colours, with seventeen similar colours and ten copyable formats.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-name-finder.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Tasks","How matching works","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Name Finder answers \"what is this colour called?\". You give it one colour and it finds the nearest match in a built in list of 1,058 named colours, shows seventeen more close matches, and lists the colour in ten copyable formats. It is the quickest tool in the workbench: one input, three result sections. The names come from a general purpose colour name list grouped into 13 families: red, pink, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple, brown, gray, white, black, metallic and neon. For matches against formal systems such as Pantone, RAL or NCS, use Pantone & Named Lookup pantone and named lookup.md . Color Name Finder is in the launcher's Essentials group. Open the launcher and select Color Name Finder , pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group, or right click a colour value and select Find its name . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with the colour you opened it with, or gold D3AF37 . 1. Source : the colour field a colour well, a HEX box and a dice button for a random colour . 2. Nearest match with the note ΔE2000 : two large chips side by side: your colour with its HEX code and hue family, and the nearest named colour with its name, HEX "},{"t":"Color Psychology","d":"Enter one to six colours and read their combined warmth and energy, emotion words, personality traits, brand-fit notes and cultural meanings by region.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-psychology.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Hue families","How the mood is worked out","Cultural meanings","Tasks","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Psychology gives a quick reading of what colours tend to suggest. For up to six colours it shows a combined palette mood how warm and how energetic the set feels, with emotion words and personality traits , and for each colour its emotional associations, personality, the kinds of brand it tends to suit, and what it can mean in different cultures and traditions. The readings are organised by hue family. The tool decides each colour's family for example Red, Teal or Gray from its hue, saturation and lightness, looks up that family's associations, and adjusts them for very light or very dark colours. Color Psychology is in the launcher's Explore group. Open the launcher and select Color Psychology . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with one colour: the colour you opened with, or gold D3AF37 . 1. A toolbar with + Color , − Color , Random and a count such as 2 colors . 2. Colors 1–6 : one colour field per colour, labelled Color 1 , Color 2 and so on. 3. Palette mood : a strip of your colours; a Warmth meter from Cool to Warm and an Energy meter from Calm to Stimulating ; a sentence such as The palette feels warm and inviting, with high energy. ; up to "},{"t":"Color Space Converter","d":"Convert one colour into 34 notations across eight groups, from HEX and HSL to Lab, OKLCH, Display P3, Rec.2020, ACEScg, JzAzBz and YCbCr, with gamut badges, two diagrams, channel bars and a JSON export.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/colour-space-converter.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","The notations","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Space Converter writes one colour in every colour space you are likely to meet, from web notations to scientific and broadcast ones: 34 notations in eight groups. Each row has a copy button, wide gamut rows show whether the colour fits the space, and two diagrams place the colour on the CIE 1931 chromaticity chart and on an OKLab slice. A third tab shows the main channels as bars. A colour space is a system of numbers that describes colours. Different spaces suit different jobs: HEX and RGB for screens and code, CMYK for print, Lab and OKLab for measuring how different colours look, P3 and Rec.2020 for wide gamut screens, YCbCr for video. A gamut is the range of colours a space or device can represent. Color Space Converter is in the launcher's Deep dive group. Open the launcher and select Color Space Converter , or pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group. See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with the colour you opened with, or gold D3AF37 . Color : a colour field. A large chip showing the colour and its HEX code. Key figures: Luminance WCAG relative luminance , OKLCh L , Chroma , Hue° , Saturation HSL and CCT estimated colour temperatu"},{"t":"Contrast System","d":"Check up to five foreground colours on one background under WCAG 2.x, APCA and ISO 9241-3, read an APCA font-size table, sweep lightness on a contrast curve, fix colours to AA or AAA, and preview them in a realistic interface.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/contrast-system.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","The Analysis tab","Tasks","Quick presets","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Contrast System is the workbench's in depth contrast tool. You set one background and up to five foreground colours. For each pair it reports three measures side by side, suggests the nearest colour that passes, shows which font sizes and weights the pair can carry under APCA, and draws the pair in a realistic interface sample. The three measures: WCAG 2.x contrast ratio : the luminance ratio used by WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2, from 1:1 to 21:1. 4.5:1 is AA for normal text, 7:1 is AAA, 3:1 is AA for large text. APCA Lc shown as WCAG 3 APCA : the Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, proposed for WCAG 3. Lc lightness contrast runs from about −108 to +106. A negative value means light text on a dark background, a positive value dark text on a light background. Readability depends on its size and on the font's size and weight. ISO 9241 3 modulation M : Lmax − Lmin / Lmax + Lmin , from 0 to 1, from the ergonomics standard for display text. Contrast System is in the launcher's Essentials group. Open the launcher and select Contrast System , pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group, or right click a colour value and select Check its contrast . See Open the Colour Tools laun"},{"t":"Gradient Library","d":"Browse and filter 512 curated linear gradients by colour scheme and number of stops, open any gradient's details, and copy it as CSS, a CSS variable, a Tailwind class, SVG or JSON, or download it as SVG or PNG.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/gradient-library.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","The collection","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Gradient Library is a collection of 512 ready made linear gradients. Each has a name, an angle, two to four colour stops and a colour scheme it was built from. You can filter by scheme and number of stops, search by name, and open any gradient to see its stops in detail and copy it in five code formats or download it as an image. When you want to build your own gradient instead, use Gradient Maker ../panel tools/gradient maker.md in the Basic Color Tools workspace. For the site's full gradient collection, see Colour libraries ../../../../../library/colour libraries/README.md . Gradient Library is in the launcher's Design group. Open the launcher and select Gradient Library , or pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group. See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It shows Loading gradients… while it downloads the collection from the site the first time you open it. A search box Search gradients… . A Scheme list. A Stops list: Any stops , 2 stops , 3 stops or 4 stops . A count of matching gradients, for example 72 gradients . A grid of up to 24 gradient cards per page. Each shows the gradient, its name, and its number of stops and scheme. A pager with ‹ Prev , P"},{"t":"Harmony Studio","d":"Generate eight kinds of colour harmony from one base colour, optionally adjust every swatch to meet a contrast target on your background, preview them and export HEX, CSS, JSON or PNG.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/harmony-studio.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Schemes","Modes","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Harmony Studio builds a palette from one base colour using a classic colour harmony pattern, such as complementary, triadic or square, and shows it on a colour wheel. It can then adjust each colour so that it reaches a contrast target against a background you choose, which turns a pretty palette into one you can use for text and interface elements. A colour harmony is a set of hues chosen by their position on the colour wheel: opposite each other complementary , evenly spaced triadic, square , or close together analogous . Harmony Studio rotates hue in OKLCH, a perceptual colour space, so the colours keep the base colour's lightness and chroma. Harmony Studio is in the launcher's Design group. Open the launcher and select Harmony Studio , pick it from the right click menu's Colour tools group, or right click a colour value and select Build harmonies . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . The base colour starts as the colour you opened with, or gold D3AF37 ; the background starts as dark navy 0F172A . Base color and Background : colour fields. Scheme : the harmony pattern. Mode : how the colours are adjusted for contrast. Mono count : a slider for the number of colour"},{"t":"Open the Colour Tools and manage their panels","d":"Every way to open the 14 floating Colour Tools, how the launcher works, and how to move, arrange, pin and close the panels they open in.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/launcher-and-panels.html","h":["Where the Colour Tools are available","Ways to open a tool","The launcher","The panel window","The control bar","What all 14 tools share","Related"],"x":" The Colour Tools are 14 small colour tools that open in floating panels over the page you are on. You do not have to leave an article, a tool page or the home page to check a contrast ratio or look up a colour's name. The panel opens on top, you work in it, and you close it when you are done. This page covers everything the 14 tools share: the ways to open them, the Color Tools launcher, the floating panel window and the control bar that appears while panels are open. Each tool has its own page in this folder. The Colour Tools load on almost every page of the site, a moment after the page finishes loading. The Basic Color Tools page https://auricartisan.com/tool/basic tools/ is their home page. A few pages do not load them, for example the Analyzer. On those pages the right click menu has no Colour tools group, and Ctrl + Shift + C takes you to the Basic Color Tools page instead of opening the launcher. Right click anywhere on a page outside a text field to open the site's menu. The Colour tools row opens a submenu: Item What it opens All colour tools… The launcher, at the place you right clicked. The row shows the shortcut Ctrl + Shift + C . Contrast System Contrast System Access"},{"t":"Pantone & Named Lookup","d":"Enter a colour and find its nearest matches in HTML/CSS named colours, a Pantone Solid Coated subset, RAL Classic, NCS and Crayola, ranked by ΔE2000 with a plain-language closeness label.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/pantone-and-named-lookup.html","h":["Open it","The systems","Screen tour","Closeness labels","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Pantone & Named Lookup finds the closest matches for a colour in five named colour systems at once. It shows the single closest match across all systems, the top matches in each system, and a small list of values to copy. Each match carries its ΔE2000 distance and a label that says in plain words how close it is. Designers use named systems to talk to printers, paint suppliers and manufacturers. This tool helps you find a starting reference, for example \"which Pantone is nearest to our brand blue?\", before you check a physical swatch book. Pantone & Named Lookup is in the launcher's Explore group. Open the launcher and select Pantone & Named Lookup . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . It starts with the colour you opened with, or 0F4C81 a classic blue . System Entries Example name HTML/CSS 141 aliceblue Pantone Solid C 105 PANTONE Yellow C RAL Classic 148 RAL 1000 Green beige NCS 56 NCS S 0500 N Crayola 111 Crayola Red The HTML/CSS list holds the named colours of CSS. The Pantone, RAL, NCS and Crayola lists are curated subsets, not complete systems, with widely published approximate screen sRGB renderings of each colour. 1. Source color ΔE2000 nearest match : a col"},{"t":"Type Readability Sim","d":"Combine text and background colours with font style, size, weight, letter-spacing and a viewing condition to get an APCA reading, a comfort score, size and weight sweeps, and recommendations.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/colour-tools/type-readability-sim.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Options","How the numbers work","Tasks","Controls","Outputs and exports","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" A contrast ratio on its own does not tell you whether text will be comfortable to read. The same colour pair can be easy at 24 pixels and bold, and hard at 12 pixels and light. Viewing conditions matter too: blur from low vision or glare on a screen eats into the margin. Type Readability Sim puts these together. You choose a text colour, a background, a font style, size, weight and letter spacing, and a viewing condition. It reports the APCA contrast and the minimum the APCA guidance asks for at that size and weight, a comfort score from 0 to 100, the WCAG ratio, a live preview, two sweeps across sizes and weights, and practical recommendations. Type Readability Sim is in the launcher's Essentials group. Open the launcher and select Type Readability Sim . See Open the Colour Tools launcher and panels.md . The text starts white FFFFFF . The background starts as the colour you opened the tool with, or a deep navy 1A1A2E . Text and Background : colour fields. Font : one of five font styles. Size shows the current value, for example Size · 16px , Weight and Letter spacing sliders. Viewing condition . Sample content . 1. Reading comfort Composite estimate : three meters. Comfort : a sc"},{"t":"Panel tools","d":"The seven tools that open as panels in the Basic Color Tools workspace, with a guide for each.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" These are the seven tools you open from the Basic Color Tools workspace. Each opens as a floating panel with a controls sidebar and a main area. The level column shows whether the tool appears under Basic or Advanced in the Catalogue's level switch. Guide Category Level In one line palette studio.md palette studio.md Generate Basic Live palette generator with harmony, WCAG and accessibility modes, locking, OKLCH editing, image extraction and eight exports. palette remix.md palette remix.md Generate Advanced Turns seed colours into four styled variant palettes; copy CSS, JSON or all HEX codes. gradient maker.md gradient maker.md Generate Basic Linear, radial and conic gradients with any number of stops, perceptual interpolation, easing and CSS, SVG, PNG, JSON and Tailwind export. colour picker.md colour picker.md Pick Basic One colour in eight formats, with harmonies, colour vision previews, chromaticity and contrast notes. colour battle.md colour battle.md Pick Advanced Scores two palettes against each other for contrast, separation and colour vision resilience. collage maker.md collage maker.md Compose Advanced Arranges your images in one of 29 layouts and exports a 4K PNG. quick"},{"t":"Collage Maker (panel)","d":"Put your own images into one of 29 collage layouts, style the grid, apply filters, add a title and export a 4K PNG, all inside a Basic Color Tools panel.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/collage-maker.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Layouts","Tasks","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" The Collage Maker panel arranges images from your device into a layout: a plain grid, an editorial magazine page, a filmstrip, a pinboard and 25 more. You can set spacing, corner radius, background, borders and a drop shadow, apply a colour filter to all images or to single cells, add a title, and export the result as a large PNG. It is useful for mood boards, palette boards and quick visual references. This is the compact collage tool inside Basic Color Tools. The site also has a separate, fuller Collage Maker page; see Image and file tools ../../../../image and file tools/README.md . The panel's Collage Maker is in the Compose category at the Advanced level. In the Workspace view, select Collage Maker in Open a tool . It opens with an empty three by two grid. Layout : 29 layouts. Cols , Rows , Gap and Radius number boxes. Background colour. Border width / color : a number and a colour. Drop shadow check box. Global filter . Title overlay : text and colour. + Add Images , a shuffle button and a clear bin button. Export PNG 4K . A 4:3 preview of the collage. Empty cells read + Add . Under it: Click any cell to assign an image. Drag from desktop to drop multiple at once. Right clic"},{"t":"Color Battle","d":"Enter two palettes, score each for contrast, perceptual separation and colour-vision resilience, compare them in a cross-palette matrix, and copy the winner or a report.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/colour-battle.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","What you can type","How the score works","Tasks","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Battle compares two palettes, Team A and Team B , and gives each a score out of 100. The score rewards palettes whose colours contrast well with each other, look clearly different, and stay different for people with colour vision deficiencies. It also shows a matrix of contrast between every colour in Team A and every colour in Team B, which helps when one palette will be used for text and the other for backgrounds. Use it to choose between two candidate palettes, to test a palette against a competitor's, or to see how much a change improves things. Color Battle is in the Pick category at the Advanced level. In the Workspace view, select Color Battle in Open a tool . It opens with two five colour teams already scored. Team A , with the hint HEX/RGB/HSL/OKLCH, one per line. , a dice button that fills the team with random colours, and a text box. Team B , with the hint Competing palette. , its own dice button and text box. Battle and Swap . Copy winner and Copy report . Result : Team A wins , Team B wins or Draw . Two score cards side by side stacked on narrow panels , one per team. A Cross palette contrast matrix card below them. Each team box accepts the same colour forms as"},{"t":"Color Picker","d":"Pick a colour with a saturation-value plane, hue slider, eyedropper or HEX code, then copy it in eight formats and see harmonies, colour-vision previews, chromaticity and contrast.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/colour-picker.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Ways to set the colour","Tasks","The Info tab","The Chromaticity tab","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Color Picker is for one colour at a time. You choose the colour with a saturation value plane and a hue slider, the browser's colour well, a HEX code, a random button or the system eyedropper. The main area then shows the colour in eight notations, eight harmony sets built from it, how it looks under colour vision deficiencies, where it sits on the CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram, and how well it contrasts with common backgrounds. The picker works in HSV hue, saturation, value : the hue slider picks the hue, and the square plane picks saturation left to right and value, or brightness bottom to top . Color Picker is in the Pick category at the Basic level. In the Workspace view, select Color Picker in Open a tool . A colour well and a HEX text box, side by side. Pick tooltip Use OS eyedropper and Random . The saturation value plane, with a round marker. The hue slider, with a bar shaped marker. Tab What it shows Formats The colour in HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV, OKLCH, Lab, XYZ and CMYK, each with a copy button. Harmonies Eight rows of colours derived from the current hue. CVD The colour under normal vision and four colour vision deficiencies, with the difference from the original. Chromatici"},{"t":"Gradient Maker","d":"Build linear, radial and conic gradients with any number of stops, choose the colour space they blend in, add easing, and export CSS, SVG, PNG, JSON or Tailwind.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/gradient-maker.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Tasks","Other buttons","Curves","Export","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Gradient Maker builds CSS gradients. You set a type linear, radial or conic , add colour stops along a track, and choose how the colours blend between stops. It shows a large live preview, charts of how lightness, chroma and hue change along the gradient, nine presets, and export options for code and images. A colour stop is a colour pinned at a position along the gradient, from 0 % the start to 100 % the end . Interpolation is the colour space the gradient blends in between stops: blending in sRGB what CSS does by default can pass through dull or dark middles, while blending in OKLCH keeps lightness and saturation more even. Easing changes the pace of the blend along the gradient. Gradient Maker is in the Generate category at the Basic level. In the Workspace view, select Gradient Maker in Open a tool . It opens with a two stop linear gradient from gold D3AF37 to deep blue 1D2A3E at 90 degrees. Type : Linear , Radial or Conic . Angle : the direction in degrees. Hidden for radial gradients. Interpolation : sRGB native CSS , OKLCh perceptual , HSL or CIE Lab . Easing : Linear , Ease in , Ease out , Ease in out or Sine . Reverse , + Stop , Even and Random . Export : Copy CSS , SVG ,"},{"t":"Palette Remix","d":"Paste seed colours, choose a remix style, and get four controlled variant palettes you can copy as CSS, JSON or HEX.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/palette-remix.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Seed colours you can paste","Remix styles","Tasks","Export","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Palette Remix takes colours you already have, such as a brand palette, and makes four variations of them in one step. Each variation follows a recipe: it shifts hue, lightness and chroma by set amounts, spreads the colours a little across the palette, and adds as much random variation as you ask for. Use it when you need alternatives that still feel related to the original: an editorial set, a darker mood, a set of UI neutrals or a complementary accent family. Palette Remix is in the Generate category at the Advanced level. With the Catalogue's level set to Basic it is hidden. In the Workspace view, select Palette Remix in Open a tool . It opens with five seed colours already filled in and four remix sets shown. Seed colors : a text box, one colour per line to start with. Remix style : the recipe family. Colors per palette : how many colours each output palette has. Remix energy : a slider for how much random variation to add. Remix and New seed buttons. Export : CSS , JSON and All HEX . Output Palettes , with a summary such as 5 seed colors → 4 remix sets . Four cards, numbered 1 to 4. Each shows the recipe name, a short note, a row of swatches with HEX labels, and two buttons: C"},{"t":"Palette Studio","d":"Generate palettes from harmony, WCAG and accessibility modes, lock and edit colours, extract colours from an image, check contrast and colour-vision behaviour, and export.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/palette-studio.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Generation modes","Tasks","Analysis tabs in detail","CVD Preview","Export","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Palette Studio is a live palette generator. It shows your palette as tall colour strips that you can regenerate, lock, reorder, edit and remove. Around the strips are analysis tabs for contrast, lightness and chroma curves, colour vision previews and colour details, and a set of export buttons. It has thirteen generation modes. Ten are colour harmony shapes. Three build role palettes designed for accessible interfaces: each colour has a job page canvas, body ink, primary surface, text on the primary surface, focus ring and so on and the tool picks lightness so the pairs meet a contrast target. Palette Studio is in the Generate category at the Basic level. In the Workspace view, select Palette Studio in Open a tool . In the Catalogue, select its card. It opens with five colours generated in Random mode. Harmony : the generation mode. Changing it regenerates the palette straight away. Generate , + Add and From Image . Accessibility Generate : three shortcut buttons, WCAG AA , WCAG AAA and Accessibility , that switch the mode and generate in one step. CVD Preview : shows the strips as they may appear with a colour vision deficiency. Export : Share , CSS , SCSS , TW , JSON , SVG , PNG"},{"t":"Quick Converter","d":"Enter a colour in any common notation and copy it in fourteen formats; compare two colours by ΔE and contrast; check wide-gamut values; see the colour on charts.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/docs/panel-tools/quick-converter.html","h":["Open it","Screen tour","Entering a colour","The fourteen formats","Tasks","Quick Info","Save to and restore from the Library","Controls","Accuracy and limits","Related"],"x":" Quick Converter is the fastest way to restate one colour in many notations. Paste a HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV or OKLCH value and it shows fourteen conversions, each with a copy button, plus the colour's luminance and nearest name. Three more tabs compare the colour with a second colour, show its coordinates in wide gamut display spaces, and plot it on charts. Quick Converter is in the Convert category at the Basic level. In the Workspace view, select Quick Converter in Open a tool . It opens showing gold D3AF37 . A large swatch showing the colour and its HEX code. An input box placeholder D3AF37, rgb … , hsl … , oklch … , a colour well and a dice button for a random colour. Quick Info : Luminance and Nearest name . Tab What it shows Convert Fourteen notations, each with a copy button. Compare ΔE Two colours side by side with difference and contrast figures and a chart. Wide Gamut Linear coordinates in sRGB, Display P3, Rec.2020 and Adobe RGB, with in gamut status. Visualize CIE 1931 position, hue wheel, a lightness ramp and a hue ramp. The input box understands: HEX with three or six digits, with or without . rgb 211, 175, 55 and rgba … the alpha value is ignored . hsl 46, 64%, 52% and h"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"The glossary, shortcuts, limits, related links and privacy notes for Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools workbench.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" This folder holds the reference material that supports the Basic Color Tools guides: the terms they use, every shortcut, what the numbers mean and do not mean, where to go next, and what happens to your data. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Colour, contrast and workspace terms used in these docs. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keys and mouse gestures for the workspace, the panel tools and the Colour Tools. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md How precise the conversions, contrast checks and simulations are, and what they are not. related.md related.md Related tools, colour libraries, kits and Learn articles. privacy.md privacy.md What stays on your device, what is stored in your browser, and what uses the network. Basic Color Tools overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut and mouse gesture in Basic Color Tools, its panel tools and the Colour Tools workbench.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Basic Color Tools page","Colour Tools workbench","Site-wide shortcuts","Related"],"x":" Cmd applies on a Mac where the table lists it. Shortcuts that act on \"the panel\" act on the focused panel, the one you selected last. Keys or gesture Where What it does Space Palette Studio, panel focused, not typing Generates a new palette locked colours stay . Escape Focus inside a panel Restores a maximised panel; otherwise closes the panel. Double click the title bar Any panel Maximises or restores. Drag the title bar Any panel not maximised Moves the panel. Drag the bottom right corner Any panel not maximised Resizes the panel. Shift , Ctrl or Cmd + select a tool card Catalogue Opens another instance of the tool. Drag a colour strip Palette Studio Reorders the palette. Shift + right click a filled cell Collage Maker Cycles that cell's filter. Enter or leave the box Color Picker HEX box; Quick Converter Compare HEX boxes Applies the typed HEX code. Ctrl + Enter Cmd + Enter Save to Library window Saves. Keys or gesture Where What it does Ctrl + Shift + C Any page that loads the Colour Tools Opens the Colour Tools launcher. If the selected text is a HEX code, the tool you pick opens with that colour. Right click Any page Opens the site menu with the Colour tools group. Shift + r"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the colour, contrast, print and workspace terms used in the Basic Color Tools and Colour Tools documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Terms are in alphabetical order. Term Meaning Achromatopsia Complete absence of colour vision; everything appears in shades of grey. ACEScg A linear, wide gamut RGB space used in film and visual effects rendering. Adobe RGB 1998 A wider gamut RGB space used in photography and print workflows, especially for greens and cyans. APCA Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a contrast method proposed for WCAG 3 that accounts for which colour is text and which is background. APCA Lc APCA's lightness contrast value, from about −108 to +106; its size, together with font size and weight, predicts readability. Analogous A harmony of hues next to each other on the colour wheel, typically about 30° apart. Black point The darkest colour a printing process can actually produce, which is never a pure black. CCT Correlated colour temperature, in kelvin; an estimate of how warm or cool a light like colour appears. Chroma How colourful a colour is compared with a grey of the same lightness. Chromaticity The colour quality of a light apart from its brightness, usually given as CIE x and y. CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram A horseshoe shaped chart of all colours people can see, used to compare gamuts."},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"How the colour conversions, contrast checks, colour-vision simulations and scores in Basic Color Tools are calculated, how precise they are, and what they are not.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Colour values","Contrast","Colour-vision simulation","Colour difference","Generators and scores","Images","What these tools are not","Related"],"x":" Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools calculate everything with published formulas in your browser. The results are good for design decisions and checks. They are not certified measurements, and a few of them are deliberate simplifications. This page says which. Starting point. Every panel tool works from 8 bit sRGB colours the HEX codes you see . Values you type in other notations are converted to sRGB first. Out of range colours are clipped. OKLCH, OKLab and Lab can describe colours that sRGB cannot show. When a slider, ramp or harmony asks for one, the tools clip each channel to the displayable range. The HEX code shows the colour you actually get, which can be less saturated than the numbers suggest. Rounding. Readouts are rounded for display for example, OKLCH chroma to three or four decimals . Copy buttons copy the rounded text. White point. Lab, XYZ and xyY use a D65 white point without adapting to D50. Tools that report Lab relative to D50 can show slightly different numbers. CMYK. The CMYK figures in Color Picker and Quick Converter come from a simple formula with no ink, paper or press profile. Use CMYK Soft Proof ../docs/colour tools/cmyk soft proof.md for a press awar"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools keep on your device, what they store in your browser, and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays on your device","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools do their work in your browser. This page lists what stays on your device, what is remembered, and what reaches the network. Colours you enter or generate. Palettes, gradients, conversions and scores are calculated in the page. Images. Images you choose for Palette Studio's From Image or for Collage Maker are read by your browser from your device. They are not uploaded. Images and videos in the Colour Tools for example CMYK Soft Proof or Animation Contrast are also processed in the browser. The eyedropper. Color Picker's Pick button uses your browser's eyedropper. It samples a single pixel only when you choose one, and the page receives only that colour. Clipboard. The tools write to your clipboard only when you select a copy button. They do not read your clipboard. Downloads. PNG and SVG files are created in the browser and saved by your browser's download feature. These preferences are stored in your browser's local storage on this device. They are not sent anywhere by the tools, and clearing the site's data in your browser removes them. What Where it is used The view you used last Workspace, Catalogue or Panels Basic Color Tools Level Basic"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools, colour libraries, kits and Learn articles that go well with Basic Color Tools and the Colour Tools.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/basic-colour-tools/others/related.html","h":["In the colour workspace","Other tool groups","Colour libraries","Kits and site features","Learn articles","Related"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it next Color Science Lab ../../colour science lab/README.md Deeper colour space, conversion and colour difference work. Personalization Generator ../../personalisation generator/README.md Turn colours into a personalised design system, palettes and gradients. Design Engine ../../design engine/README.md Generate a full design system colour, type, spacing, tokens and open its colours in the Colour Tools. Font Library ../../font library/README.md Choose type to go with your palette. Icon Library ../../icon library/README.md Find icons and colour them with your palette. ASCII Art Generator ../../ascii art generator/README.md Turn images and text into ASCII art. Accessibility and vision ../../../accessibility and vision/README.md : the Contrast Checker, Vision Simulation, the URL Analyzer and more, for full accessibility checks beyond colour pairs. Image and file tools ../../../image and file tools/README.md : the full Collage Maker page, Image Picker palettes from images , SVG Recolour, LUT Lab and more. Colorimetry and rendering ../../../colorimetry and rendering/README.md : gamut, illuminant and tone mapping tools. Perception and spectral ../../../perception "},{"t":"Color Science Lab","d":"What the Color Science Lab is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to start with its Workbench, Compare, Gamut audit and Illuminants views and its 45 panel tools.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Color Science Lab is a research workspace for colour science on the Auric Artisan website. It has five views. Four of them work on colours you enter and compute their results with published formulas: the Workbench resolves one colour into CIE XYZ, xyY, Lab, LCh, Oklab, Oklch and more under the illuminant and standard observer you choose; Compare measures the difference between two colours with ΔE 2000, ΔE 1994, ΔE 1976 and Oklab distance; Gamut audit checks a palette against sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB and Rec. 2020; and Illuminants shows how one colour shifts under seven standard lights. The fifth view, the Catalogue , opens 45 tools in eight domains colorimetry, chromatic adaptation, spectral analysis, appearance models, perceptual spaces, colour spaces, theory and history, and gamut and rendering as floating panels. Each panel has the same controls sample and compare colours, model, colour space, theory, white points, strength and colour temperature and six tabs, and it reads out coordinates in any of 63 colour spaces. Up to five panels can be open, linked so that shared controls move together, arranged with a floating control centre, and exported as one image. Everything i"},{"t":"Color Science Lab documentation","d":"The list of guides for the Color Science Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" These guides cover the lab's five views, the 45 panel tools, and how to arrange, link, save and export panels. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the lab, tour the views, make a first measurement. workbench.md workbench.md Resolve one colour under any illuminant, observer and adaptation transform. compare two colours.md compare two colours.md ΔE 2000, 1994, 1976 and Oklab distance, and where the difference lies. gamut audit.md gamut audit.md A palette checked against four RGB working spaces. illuminants.md illuminants.md One colour adapted to seven standard illuminants. catalogue and panels.md catalogue and panels.md Finding tools, and every control and tab in a tool panel. tool list.md tool list.md All 45 tools by domain, with their level and default model. catalogue compare and analytics.md catalogue compare and analytics.md Tool comparison on a test palette; heat map, mind map, stats and catalogue exports. arrange link save export.md arrange link save export.md Panel windows, linking, the Color Control centre, the dock, image export and the Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, option, default and output. troubleshooting.md troubleshootin"},{"t":"Getting started with the Color Science Lab","d":"Open the Color Science Lab, learn its five views, and make your first measurements.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","The five views","First measurement: one colour, two lights","First panel","Next steps","Related"],"x":" 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/color science lab/ in a current desktop browser. 2. Under the title Color Science Lab you see a short description and labels: 8 Domains , 45 Tools , 60+ Color Spaces , Von Kries · Newton · Fairchild and In page Floating Panels , then a note about the matching API call, which you can dismiss with × . 3. A row of five view buttons follows: Workbench , Catalogue , Compare , Gamut audit and Illuminants . The lab opens on Workbench the first time and on the view you used last after that. View Use it to Workbench See one colour in every CIE and perceptual notation, under the illuminant, observer and adaptation you choose. Catalogue Browse 45 tools and open them as floating panels. Compare Measure the difference between a reference and a candidate colour. Gamut audit Check how much room a palette has in sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB and Rec. 2020. Illuminants See one colour adapted to seven standard lights. The Workbench and Illuminants views share one colour, the specimen ; Compare's Reference starts from it. The lab remembers the specimen in your browser. 1. On Workbench , type D3AF37 in the specimen HEX box include the . 2. Read Resolved coordinate"},{"t":"Arrange, link, save and export panels","d":"Move, resize, pin, dock and link Color Science Lab panels, arrange them with the Color Control centre, export a combined image, and save panels to your Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/arrange-link-save-export.html","h":["Panel windows","Linking panels","The Open Panels list","The Color Control centre","Export a combined image","Save to and restore from the Library","Related"],"x":" Lab panels float over the whole page, whichever view you are on. Each opens at 1120 by 720 pixels or smaller to fit your window , offset slightly from the last one. Button Tooltip What it does Link Link shared controls Links this panel. Linked panels copy each other's control changes see below . Duplicate Open another instance Opens another copy of the tool with its own settings. Pin Keep panel open Protects the panel from being closed automatically or by Close unpinned and Close all . − Minimize Hides the panel and adds it to the dock. □ Maximize or restore Fills the window; select again to restore. × Close Closes the panel. Drag the title bar to move; double click it to maximise or restore. Drag the bottom right corner to resize. The minimum is 520 by 420 pixels, or the window size if smaller. Select a panel to bring it to the front. With the keyboard focus inside a panel, Escape restores a maximised panel, or closes the panel otherwise. Selecting a tool that is already open brings its panel forward instead of opening a second one. Up to five panels can be open. Opening a sixth closes the oldest panel that is not pinned. If all five are pinned, the new tool does not open until y"},{"t":"The Catalogue and its panels","d":"Find tools in the Catalogue, and use every control and tab of a Color Science Lab tool panel.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/catalogue-and-panels.html","h":["The filter bar","Tool cards","The panel","Tasks","Related"],"x":" The Catalogue view lists the lab's 45 tools as cards. Selecting a card opens that tool as a floating panel over the page. All 45 panels share one layout, so once you know one, you know them all; the tool you choose sets the defaults model, colour space and theory and what the canvas draws. Control What it does Color Lab Reloads the page. Search box Search tools, models, spaces, illuminants... . Matches tool names, summaries, tags, domains, default models and spaces, and, for colour space and theory tools, the names and details of every space and theory. Results update a moment after you stop typing. Clear Empties the search. Domain list All , the eight domains, Favorites , Compare , Analytics and Open Panels . Level Basic 20 Foundation tools , Advanced 25 Research tools or Both all 45, the default . Count Cards shown out of the total, for example 20 of 45 . Copy link Copies the page address. Quick start button Shows or hides the quick start note. The Level setting is shared with the site wide complexity mode the Advanced Kit , so changing it in one place changes it in the other. The domains are Colorimetry , Chromatic Adaptation , Spectral Analysis , Appearance Models , Perceptual"},{"t":"Catalogue Compare and Analytics","d":"Preview up to eight tools on a six-colour test palette, and explore the lab's heat map, mind map, statistics and catalogue, with JSON and CSV export.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/catalogue-compare-and-analytics.html","h":["Compare (in the Catalogue)","Analytics","Related"],"x":" Two entries in the Catalogue's domain list are not domains. Compare previews several tools side by side before you open any, and Analytics maps the whole lab. This Compare is different from the top level Compare view, which measures two colours. Choose Compare in the domain list, or press C when the cursor is not in a text box. The left column, Select tools , lists the tools that match the current level and search, each marked F Basic / Foundation or R Advanced / Research . Tick the ones to compare. Buttons: Basic select all Foundation tools , Advanced all Research tools , Filtered everything listed and Clear . The first four tools selected at the start are CIE XYZ and Lab Workbench, Bradford Adaptation, Blackbody Radiation and 40+ Color Space Atlas. The matrix shows up to eight selected tools as columns and six test colours as rows: Auric gold D3AF37 , Signal red D84444 , Cyan blue 2FA7D8 , Forest green 3C8D5A , Violet 7C5CE2 and Skin tone C98E69 . The Reference column shows the original colour. Each tool cell shows that tool's preview of the colour, its HEX code and its ΔE 76 from the reference. Each column header has Open to open that tool as a panel. With nothing selected, it "},{"t":"Compare two colours","d":"Measure the difference between a reference and a candidate colour with ΔE 2000, ΔE 1994, ΔE 1976 and Oklab distance, and see whether the gap is lightness, chroma or hue.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/compare-two-colours.html","h":["Layout","Tasks","Controls","Related"],"x":" The Compare view measures how different two colours are. It is useful for checking a match a print against a screen colour, a paint against a brand colour, a new token against an old one and for understanding why two colours look different. ΔE delta E is a number for colour difference. Several formulas exist; newer ones follow human perception more closely. Two cards side by side: Reference A and Candidate B , each with a large swatch, a HEX box, a colour well, and a table of CIE XYZ , CIE Lab , CIE LCh and Oklab coordinates. The Reference starts as the Workbench specimen; the Candidate starts as 5A86D8. Below them, four verdicts: Verdict Meaning ΔE 2000 The current CIE standard CIEDE2000 . Its note says whether the difference is below the just noticeable threshold under 1 , noticeable only side by side 1 to 2 , perceptible at a glance but acceptable side by side 2 to 5 , or two different colours 5 and above . ΔE 1976 The original straight line Lab distance. It overstates differences in blues, which is why it was replaced. ΔE 1994 The step between the two: it weights chroma by its own size. Oklab distance Plain distance in Oklab, a space designed to make that distance meaningful. "},{"t":"Gamut audit","d":"Check a palette against sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB and Rec. 2020, see how much headroom its tightest colour has, and what clipping would cost.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/gamut-audit.html","h":["Layout","Tasks","Controls","Related"],"x":" The Gamut audit view checks a palette against four RGB working spaces. A gamut is the range of colours a space can hold. A palette written in HEX is sRGB by definition, so it always fits sRGB; the useful number is headroom margin : how far the palette's tightest colour is from the edge of each space. At 0 % a colour already sits on a primary, and any adjustment clips it. The palette N colours · target sRGB : each colour with its HEX code and a line saying its sRGB margin for example 12% margin or, for a colour from a wider space, clips ΔE N . Each has a × to remove it. Below: a colour well and Add to palette . The starting palette has eight colours: 4F7FE0, D3AF37, 00C264, C4562C, 2F6D3A, 00E07A, 8F3B22 and 2B6F8F. A palette holds from 1 to 16 colours. A table with one row per space sRGB , Display P3 , Adobe RGB , Rec. 2020 : Tightest headroom : a bar for the smallest margin in the palette. In gamut : how many colours fit, for example 8 / 8 . Margin : the tightest margin as a percentage. Red if any colour falls outside, amber if the margin is under 2 %, green otherwise. A large figure such as 8/8 with Every colour survives sRGB unchanged. , or how many clip and whether they fit Di"},{"t":"Illuminants","d":"See one colour adapted to seven CIE illuminants with the Bradford transform, and how far it shifts under each.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/illuminants.html","h":["Layout","The illuminants","Tasks","Notes","Related"],"x":" The Illuminants view shows the Workbench specimen as it would appear to an observer adapted to each of seven standard lights, and measures how far it moves from its D65 appearance. The same colour, adapted Bradford · from D65 : one patch per illuminant with its name, colour temperature and ΔE00 from D65. The explanation under it: each patch is the specimen re rendered for an observer adapted to that illuminant, using the Bradford transform. The verdict: the largest shift and the illuminant that causes it, with A match made under D65 will not hold there. when the shift is above 5, or The colour holds reasonably across the set. Shift by illuminant ΔE00 from D65 : each illuminant other than D65 with its description and shift, coloured green below 3, amber 3 to 8 and red above 8. Illuminant Description Temperature D65 Daylight · reference 6504 K D50 Print viewing 5003 K D55 Mid daylight 5503 K C Average daylight obsolete 6774 K A Incandescent 2856 K F2 Cool white fluorescent 4230 K F11 Narrow tri band fluorescent 4000 K 1. Set the specimen on the Workbench or keep the current one . 2. Open Illuminants and read the verdict and Shift by illuminant . Result: the light under which the col"},{"t":"The 45 tools","d":"Every Color Science Lab panel tool by domain, with its level, what it is for and its default model.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/tool-list.html","h":["Colorimetry (5)","Chromatic Adaptation (6)","Spectral Analysis (6)","Appearance Models (6)","Perceptual Spaces (6)","Color Spaces (7)","Theory and History (4)","Gamut and Rendering (5)","The colour-space registry","Related"],"x":" Level F means Basic / Foundation shown when the level is Basic or Both ; R means Advanced / Research shown when the level is Advanced or Both . Every tool opens the same panel described in The Catalogue and its panels catalogue and panels.md ; the default model, space and theory differ. Tool Level What it is for CIE XYZ and Lab Workbench F Convert samples between sRGB, CIE XYZ, xyY and CIE Lab with live white point context. Chromaticity Diagram F Plot samples, white points and approximate sRGB gamut positions on the CIE xy diagram. Delta E Comparator F Compare two colours by Lab distance, luma drift, chroma drift and hue direction. Standard Observer Lab R Compare 2° and 10° observers, xy chromaticity and u'v' uniform chromaticity. Default model: CIE 1931 observer. Color Difference Suite R Audit Delta E 76 distance, chroma drift, luma drift and perceptual proxy spaces side by side. Default space: DIN99. Tool Level What it is for Bradford Adaptation F Move a colour from one reference white to another with a Bradford transform. CAT02 and CAT16 Bench R Compare modern adaptation transforms with source and target whites. Illuminant Match Bench R Study a colour under A, D50, D65, D75 and"},{"t":"The Workbench","d":"Resolve one colour into CIE XYZ, xyY, Lab, LCh, Oklab, Oklch, sRGB, HSL and CMYK under a chosen illuminant, standard observer and adaptation transform, and see its gamut and how it shifts under other lights.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/workbench.html","h":["Layout","How the numbers are computed","Tasks","Controls","Related"],"x":" The Workbench takes one colour, the specimen , and computes it in nine notations at once, all from the same linear light values. You can change the viewing conditions the illuminant, the standard observer and the chromatic adaptation transform and every row moves together. The page's own note under the board says: Computed, not looked up. A few terms: Illuminant : a standard light defined by its white point, such as D65 average daylight or A incandescent . Standard observer : the CIE's model of human colour matching over a 2° field 1931 or a 10° field 1964 . Lab values depend on which one you use. Chromatic adaptation transform : a formula that predicts how a colour appears after the eye adapts to a different white. Bradford, CAT02 and CAT16 are three versions of the von Kries method. Specimen sRGB in : a large swatch, a HEX box, a colour well and eight preset swatches 4F7FE0, D3AF37, 2F6D3A, C4562C, 8F3B22, 2B6F8F, B0169A, F0E6D2 . Observer CIE standard : 2° 1931 or 10° 1964 . Illuminant white point : D65 , D50 , D55 , C , A , F2 and F11 . Adaptation von Kries family : Bradford , CAT02 or CAT16 . While the illuminant is D65, a note says no adaptation is applied: the transform onl"},{"t":"Color Science Lab reference","d":"Every view, control, option, default, output and file of the Color Science Lab in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","Workbench","Compare (view)","Gamut audit","Illuminants","Catalogue filter bar","Panel controls","Panel windows","Open Panels toolbar and Color Control","Catalogue Compare and Analytics","Files","Remembered in your browser","Related"],"x":" Item Value Address https://auricartisan.com/tool/color science lab/ also /model Views Workbench, Catalogue, Compare, Gamut audit, Illuminants Tools 45 in 8 domains 20 Foundation, 25 Research Colour spaces 63 Theories and models 24 White points panels 13 Maximum open panels 5 API equivalent POST /v1/science/dossier, 5 API credits per call Control Values Default Specimen HEX / colour well RRGGBB 4F7FE0 then remembered Presets 4F7FE0, D3AF37, 2F6D3A, C4562C, 8F3B22, 2B6F8F, B0169A, F0E6D2 — Observer 2° 1931, 10° 1964 2° 1931 Illuminant D65, D50, D55, C, A, F2, F11 D65 Adaptation Bradford, CAT02, CAT16 Bradford Outputs: CIE XYZ, CIE xyY, CIE L a b , CIE LCh, Oklab, Oklch, sRGB, HSL, CMYK; xy plot with L, C and hue angle; gamut in sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB, Rec. 2020; ΔE 2000 under each other illuminant. Control Default Reference A The specimen Candidate B 5A86D8 Outputs: coordinates in CIE XYZ, Lab, LCh and Oklab for each; ΔE 2000, ΔE 1976, ΔE 1994, Oklab distance; Δ lightness, Δ chroma, Δ hue angle with a verdict sentence. Control Values Default Remove × — At least 1 colour Add to palette Up to 16 colours 8 starting colours Outputs: per colour sRGB margin or clip ΔE; per space tigh"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Color Science Lab","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the Color Science Lab, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Why: the Workbench, Compare and the gamut tools accept a full RRGGBB code, with the . What to do: type all six digits with the , or use the colour well or a preset. Why: five panels are open and all are pinned. What to do: unpin or close one, then open the tool again. Why: at five panels, opening another closes the oldest unpinned panel. What to do: pin panels you want to keep. Why: Escape inside a panel closes it or restores it first if it is maximised . What to do: select outside the panel before pressing Escape for other reasons. Why: single letter shortcuts / , ? , F , A , C , R , T , 1 to 5 work anywhere on the page when the cursor is not in a text box. What to do: click into a text box before typing, or see Shortcuts ../others/shortcuts.md . Why: only panels whose link button is on share changes. What to do: turn on linking in each panel, or use Sync all . Why: the search waits a moment after you stop typing. What to do: pause briefly after typing. Why: the Workbench uses the illuminant and observer you selected with a chosen adaptation; a panel reports Lab against its source or target white. What to do: set the same white on both for example D65 on the Workbench and D65 as "},{"t":"Color Science Lab FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Color Science Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/docs/faq.html","h":["Are the numbers accurate enough for research?","Can I enter spectral data or measured values?","Why does a HEX colour always show \"inside\" sRGB?","What is the difference between the Catalogue's Compare and the Compare view?","Do I need an account?","Does the level switch affect other pages?","Related"],"x":" The Workbench, Compare, Gamut audit and Illuminants views and the panels' coordinate readouts use published formulas sRGB, CIE XYZ and Lab, Bradford, CAT02, CAT16, CIEDE2000, Oklab . They are exact within 8 bit sRGB input and floating point rounding. Some panel Result previews are illustrations, not full model outputs. Read Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md before citing a figure. No. Every input is an sRGB colour. The lab does not accept spectral reflectance or measured XYZ. A HEX code is an sRGB colour by definition. The useful figure is the headroom, which the Gamut audit reports. The Compare view measures two colours. The Catalogue's Compare entry previews several tools on a test palette. No. Saving panels uses your Auric Artisan Library. Yes. Basic , Advanced and Both follow the site wide complexity mode, so changing it here changes it on other pages that use it. Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Getting started getting started.md "},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the Color Science Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Reference material that supports the Color Science Lab guides. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Colour science terms used in these docs. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and mouse gestures. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What is computed exactly, what is illustrative, and what the lab does not do. related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles. privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what is stored. Color Science Lab overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts and mouse gestures in the Color Science Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Related"],"x":" The single key shortcuts work anywhere on the page when the cursor is not in a text box, list or text area, and when Ctrl , Cmd and Alt are not held. The letter shortcuts act on the Catalogue, even if another view is showing. Keys What it does / Focus the Catalogue search. Esc In the search box: clear the search. Also closes the shortcuts overlay. ? Show or hide the keyboard shortcuts overlay. F Show Favorites in the Catalogue. A Show Analytics in the Catalogue. C Show Compare in the Catalogue. R Open a random tool from those visible. T Tile all panels. 1 to 5 Bring panel 1 to 5 in opening order to the front. Shift or Ctrl + select a card Open another copy of a tool. Esc inside a panel Restore a maximised panel; otherwise close the panel. Double click a title bar Maximise or restore. Enter in a panel HEX box Apply the typed colour. Arrow Down , Enter or Space on a panel list Open the list; Esc closes it. Supporting material README.md Arrange, link, save and export ../docs/arrange link save export.md "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the colour-science terms used in the Color Science Lab documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning ACES Academy Color Encoding System, a family of colour spaces for film and visual effects AP0, AP1, ACEScg . Appearance model A model that predicts how a colour looks under given viewing conditions, such as CIECAM02 or CAM16. Bradford transform A widely used chromatic adaptation transform from the von Kries family. CAT02, CAT16 Chromatic adaptation transforms from the CIECAM02 and CAM16 appearance models. CCT Correlated colour temperature, in kelvin. Chromatic adaptation The eye's adjustment to the colour of the light, and the formulas that predict it. Chromaticity x, y The colour of a stimulus apart from its brightness, plotted on the CIE 1931 diagram. CIEDE2000 ΔE 2000 The CIE's current formula for perceived colour difference. CIE XYZ The tristimulus values that other colour spaces are defined from. CIELAB / LCh A perceptual space lightness, a, b and its polar form lightness, chroma, hue . Dossier The panel's detailed description of a colour space for the current sample. Gamut The range of colours a space or device can hold. Headroom margin How far a colour sits from the edge of a gamut. Illuminant A standard light defined by its spectrum or white point, such as D65"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Color Science Lab computes with published formulas, which previews are illustrative, and what it cannot do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Computed with published formulas","Illustrative, not full models","Inputs and precision","What the lab is not","Related"],"x":" Workbench : sRGB decoding, CIE XYZ D65, 2° , adaptation with the published Bradford, CAT02 and CAT16 matrices, Lab and LCh against the chosen white with separate white points for the 2° and 10° observers , Oklab and Oklch, and gamut checks with the published matrices for sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB and Rec. 2020. Compare : CIEDE2000 written out in full, CIE94, CIE76 and Oklab distance. Gamut audit and Illuminants : the same matrices and CIEDE2000. Panels : the Sample coordinates , Result coordinates and the colour space dossier come from a colour space engine that implements each of the 63 spaces' conversions. The Chromatic Adaptation tools' Result colour uses real adaptation matrices, scaled by Experiment strength . In the panels of the Spectral, Appearance, Perceptual, Color Spaces, Theory and Rendering domains, the Result swatch and the metrics derived from it, such as dE76 after model is an illustration of the direction and size of the named model's effect, controlled by Experiment strength . It is not the output of a full implementation of CIECAM16, ICtCp, ACES or the other models named. The same applies to the Catalogue Compare matrix and the Heat Map's analysis depth score,"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Color Science Lab keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" All calculations run in the page. Colours you enter are not sent anywhere to be computed. Exports PNG, JSON, CSV are created in your browser. In your browser's local storage on this device: the last view, the Workbench specimen colour, the Catalogue domain, favourites, the last ten tools opened, whether you dismissed the quick start note, and the level, which is shared with the site wide complexity setting. Open panels are not stored. Loading the page and its scripts. Save to Library stores presets in your Auric Artisan Library; see the Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Site wide analytics and advertising follow your cookie choices; see the Help centre ../../../../../help/README.md . Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go with the Color Science Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/colour-science-lab/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Services","Learn articles","Related"],"x":" Colorimetry and rendering tools ../../../colorimetry and rendering/README.md : chromatic adaptation, gamut maps, illuminants, HDR plots, tonal steps and tone mapping as full pages. Perception and spectral tools ../../../perception and spectral/README.md : spectral, perception and material tools. Basic Color Tools ../../basic colour tools/README.md and its Color Space Converter ../../basic colour tools/docs/colour tools/colour space converter.md for quick conversions. Design System Generator ../../design engine/README.md , which can open the lab with your palette. Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md : the colour dossier as a REST call. CIELAB and LCh Explained https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cielab and lch explained Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces Gamut Mapping https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 17 gamut mapping clipping and rendering intents Gamut Volume: How Much Color a Wide Gamut Actually Adds https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 26 gamut volume how much color HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HL"},{"t":"Design System Generator","d":"What the Design System Generator (Design Engine) is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to generate, check and export your first design system.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Design System Generator, also called the Design Engine, turns three choices into a complete design system. You pick an industry , a style and a contrast target , and the tool composes colour ramps in OKLCH, light and dark colour roles that meet your contrast target, semantic colours, a font pairing with a modular type scale, an icon family, and spacing, radius, shadow, motion, z index and breakpoint scales. That is 177 design tokens in the default light and dark mode. There is no Generate button. Every change regenerates the whole system at once, and a contrast audit on the right of the screen re runs with it, showing a score out of 100, the twelve pairings it checks and whether each passes. When you are happy, you export the tokens to any of twelve targets, from CSS and Tailwind to Figma, SwiftUI and Jetpack Compose, or share a link that rebuilds the exact same system. Everything is calculated in your browser, and the same inputs always give the same system. The tool does not know your brand, your competitors or your product: the page itself says the result is generated, not designed . Treat it as a well built, well checked starting point. Product designers who want a coheren"},{"t":"Design System Generator documentation","d":"The list of guides for the Design System Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" These guides explain how to use the Design System Generator: setting the brief, reading each tab, using the component playground and the contrast audit, comparing systems, exporting tokens, and saving and sharing. The reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the tool, tour the screen, generate and export a first system. set the brief.md set the brief.md Industry, style, contrast target, density, seed, harmony, colour mode, corners, type ratio, ramp shape and token naming. read the system.md read the system.md The Overview, Colour, Type, Icons and Scales tabs. component playground.md component playground.md The live component gallery and its preview controls. contrast audit.md contrast audit.md The audit rail, the score, the full audit view and suggested fixes. compare.md compare.md Running the same brief through every style or every industry. export tokens.md export tokens.md The Tokens tab, the twelve export formats and what each contains. share save and connect.md share save and connect.md Share links, saving to the Library, the Workspace view and sending the palette to other tools. reference.md reference.md Every control, opt"},{"t":"Getting started with the Design System Generator","d":"Open the Design System Generator, learn the layout, and generate, check and export your first design system.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","A tour of the screen","Your first system","Next steps","Related"],"x":" This guide takes about ten minutes. By the end you will have a design system that meets a contrast target, and its tokens in a file. 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/design engine/ in a current desktop browser. The tool works on smaller screens, but the three column layout is easiest on a wide one. 2. A system appears straight away. Which one depends on how you arrived: from a shared link, the link's settings are applied first; otherwise, on a return visit, the settings you used last in this browser; otherwise the defaults: Auto industry, Modern style, AAA contrast. The top of the page reads Three choices, one whole system. with a short description, the number of tokens, Targets 12 and OKLCH · WCAG 2.1 · APCA . On the right are five buttons and a link: Control What it does Surprise Picks a random industry, style and contrast target, resets the seed to auto, and sets harmony to auto or a random harmony. Share Copies a link that rebuilds this system. Save Saves the system to your Library. Help Opens How this works : what the defaults assume and how the score is worked out. Workspace Opens your saved systems and the options for sending the palette to other tools. Read the API r"},{"t":"Compare styles and industries","d":"Run your brief through every style or every industry at once, sort the results, and adopt the one you prefer.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/compare.html","h":["Open Compare","The controls","Each card","Adopt a result","Things to know","Related"],"x":" Because a system is generated almost instantly, the tool can build many at once. The Compare view keeps your brief and varies one thing, the style or the industry, so you can see every option side by side. Select Compare every style → at the bottom of The brief . ← Back to the system returns to the tab you were on. The heading says what is being compared, for example Healthcare at AAA, through all ten styles. , and the range of scores. Control Options What it does Vary Style , Industry Varies the style ten cards or the industry one card per industry setting, including Auto . Order by Score , Chroma , Listed Sorts by score, by how colourful the primary is, or in the list order. Compare uses your contrast target, density and other overrides, but ignores your seed colour so that each style or industry shows its own hue. The name, on screen if it matches your current system, and the score colour coded . The primary ramp, and chips for primary, accent, success, warning and danger. The heading font drawn in its weight, with the body font, type ratio and icon family. A sample Continue button and a tile showing the corner and shadow. A footer with the corner style and harmony, audit clean"},{"t":"Use the component playground","d":"Try your generated tokens on a live, clickable component gallery, and change the preview's theme, density, corners, elevation, button shape and viewport.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/component-playground.html","h":["What is in the gallery","The preview controls","Tasks","Things to know","Related"],"x":" The Components tab draws a complete interface gallery with your generated tokens, and it works: tabs switch, menus open, switches toggle, modals and drawers open and close, toasts appear, steppers count and ratings set. It is the fastest way to notice that muted text is too light, that the primary is too close to the info colour, or that the corners feel wrong. Choose a category with the chips above the stage. ✦ All shows every category in this order: Category What it contains Navigation A navigation bar, Tabs , Breadcrumbs , Pagination , Steps / wizard Buttons Variants , Sizes & icon buttons , Loading, block & FAB Forms Text & select , Choice & toggles , Slider, stepper & rating , Tags, upload & OTP Feedback Alerts , Toast, banner & tooltip , Progress & loading , Validation & empty Data Stat tiles , Data table , List & avatars , Timeline Overlays Modal & drawer , Dropdown menu , Command palette , Consent & popover Commerce Product card , Pricing , Cart & checkout Marketing A hero, Feature grid , Testimonial , Newsletter & FAQ and a closing section Industry An Industry showcase : a small branded app screen written for one industry The showcase is a short app screen app name, navig"},{"t":"Check contrast with the audit","d":"Read the always-visible audit rail, understand the score, open the full audit for both themes, and use the suggested fixes.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/contrast-audit.html","h":["The audit rail","The twelve pairings","The score","The full audit","Tasks","What the audit does not cover","Related"],"x":" The audit is the evidence that a generated system meets its contrast target. It re runs on every change, it covers both the light and the dark roles, and it reports two measures: the WCAG 2.1 contrast ratio , from 1:1 to 21:1, the measure most accessibility requirements use; the APCA Lc value, the Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm proposed for WCAG 3, which handles light on dark and mid tone pairs better. The tool shows its size without a sign as context, not as a pass or fail gate. The right hand column, The audit live , has four sections. 1. The score : a large number out of 100, out of 100 , a line saying how the last change moved it first run , no change or, for example, +3 on that change , and a pill: all 12 pass or N failing . Select the score to open the full audit. A line underneath says how many tokens changed on the last change, for example 14 of 177 tokens moved on that change. 2. Where the points went : the four parts of the score as bars, and a sentence naming the weakest part. 3. Light wcag · apca : the twelve pairings for the light roles. Each row shows a sample, the pairing, the kind of content and its requirement normal text · needs 7 , the ratio green for "},{"t":"Export tokens","d":"Browse and search every token, then copy or download the system in any of twelve formats, and know what each format contains.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/export-tokens.html","h":["The token list","Export","What each format covers","Example","Related"],"x":" A design token is a named design decision stored as data, such as color primary 500: 1f6feb or space 4: 16px . Tokens let designers and developers share one source of truth. The Tokens tab lists every token the system generates and exports them in twelve formats. Find token filters the list by name or value as you type, for example primary , radius or 1f . Clear shows everything again. Design tokens shows the total and the tokens in groups, each with a count: Color · Primary, Color · Secondary, Color · Accent, Color · Neutral, Color · Semantic, Color · Roles light , Color · Roles dark , Color · Gradients, Typography, Typography · Size, Typography · Leading, Typography · Tracking, Spacing, Radius, Shadow, Motion, Z index and Breakpoints. Colour tokens have a chip. Select any token to copy its value. The default light and dark system has 177 tokens; with Colour mode set to Light , the fourteen dark role tokens are left out 163 . The names follow Token naming in the brief; see Set the brief set the brief.md . Scroll to Export tokens . Select a format pill; the code below it changes, and its bar shows the file name and language. Three buttons: Copy copies the code shown. Download save"},{"t":"Read the system","d":"What the Overview, Colour, Type, Icons and Scales tabs show, and how to copy any value from them.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/read-the-system.html","h":["Overview","Colour","Type","Icons","Scales","Copying values","Related"],"x":" The first five tabs show the generated system from different angles. Every tab is made of cards; select a card's heading to fold or unfold it. Some cards start folded. Almost every colour, gradient and token can be selected to copy its value, and a short message confirms the copy. Four cards: System summary : a score ring green at 85 and above, amber from 65, red below , the industry and style, the mood and target, the harmony, and badges for the seed, All pairings pass or N to review , the font pairing and the icon family. Under it, eight headline swatches: primary, secondary, accent, success, warning, danger, info and text. The primary swatch also shows its contrast against white. At a glance : Color ramps 4 × 11 , Type sizes , Base size , Scale ratio , Spacing unit , Radius , Shadows 6 levels and Total tokens . Generation recipe : every input written out, including the resolved primary hue and the secondary and accent hue angles, the colour mode, the font pairing and the icon family with its stroke width. Use it to explain how a system was made. Jump to : shortcuts to Color , Type , Components and Export . Color ramps : primary, secondary and accent at eleven steps 50, 100, 200"},{"t":"Set the brief","d":"What every input in the brief rail does: industry, style, contrast target, density, seed, harmony, colour mode, corner style, type ratio, ramp shape and token naming.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/set-the-brief.html","h":["Industry","Style","Contrast target","Density","Seed","Harmony","Colour mode","Corner style","Type ratio","Ramp shape","Token naming","Compare every style","Tasks","Related"],"x":" The brief is the left hand column. It holds every input the system is built from. Each section shows a short note on the right that says what the choice resolved to, for example auto → analogous or 4.5:1 body text . Any change regenerates the whole system immediately, and the audit shows what the change did. The first three inputs industry, style and contrast target decide most of the system. The rest are overrides. Industry sets the brand hue and how much colour chroma the system uses, plus a mood and a set of tags used to pick the font pairing and icon family. A coloured dot beside the list shows the industry's hue. Industry Hue Mood Auto default 250° No vertical assumed; your seed decides. Fintech 258° trustworthy, precise, secure Healthcare 192° calm, clean, reassuring SaaS / B2B 264° efficient, modern, focused E commerce 22° energetic, inviting, urgent Education 234° approachable, clear, friendly Creative / Agency 320° expressive, bold, original Gaming 282° high energy, immersive, sharp Luxury 44° refined, exclusive, timeless Food & Drink 18° warm, appetizing, organic Travel 200° open, adventurous, fresh Real Estate 168° stable, premium, grounded Non profit 148° hopeful, huma"},{"t":"Share, save and connect","d":"Share a link that rebuilds a system, save systems to your Library and restore them, and send the palette, fonts and icons to other Auric Artisan tools.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/share-save-and-connect.html","h":["Share a link","Your last settings","Save to your Library","The Workspace view","Related"],"x":" The generator is deterministic: the same inputs always produce the same system. That makes a system easy to share and keep, because only its inputs need to travel. 1. Select Share in the masthead. 2. The link is copied, Shareable link copied ✓ appears, and the address bar updates to the same link. The link lists your inputs as address parameters. Settings left on Auto are left out. For example: text https://auricartisan.com/tool/design engine/?industry=wellness&rampSpan=default&rampPeak=default&tokenPrefix=&tokenCase=kebab&style=elegant&a11y=AA&mode=both&density=spacious When someone opens the link, the page applies these parameters before generating, so they see the same system. You can also write a link by hand with only the parameters you need, for example ?industry=wellness&style=elegant&a11y=AA . Parameter Values industry fintech , healthcare , saas , ecommerce , education , creative , gaming , luxury , food , travel , realestate , nonprofit , crypto , wellness style modern , minimal , classic , bold , playful , elegant , corporate , brutalist , organic , futuristic a11y AA large , AA , AAA mode light , dark , both density compact , comfortable , spacious harmony complementar"},{"t":"Design System Generator reference","d":"Every control, option, default, view and output of the Design System Generator in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/reference.html","h":["Page","Masthead","The brief","Generated system","Tabs","Component playground controls","Audit","Compare","Export formats","Share link parameters","Messages","Related"],"x":" Item Value Address https://auricartisan.com/tool/design engine/ Tabs Overview, Colour, Type, Icons, Scales, Components, Tokens Views Compare, Workspace, Audit, Help Tokens 177 light + dark , 163 light only Export targets 12 Contrast measures WCAG 2.1 ratio, APCA Lc API equivalent POST /v1/tokens/generate, 4 API credits per call Control What it does Surprise Random industry, style and target; seed reset to auto; harmony auto or random. Keeps other overrides. Share Copies a link with the current inputs and updates the address bar. Save Saves the system to your Library. Help Opens the How this works view. Workspace Opens saved systems and the Connect cards. Read the API reference → Opens the API documentation. API note × Hides the \"Automate this\" note; remembered in your browser. Expand / Collapse Hides or shows both side rails; remembered in your browser. Control What it does Values Default Industry Brand hue, chroma, mood and font/icon tags Auto, Fintech, Healthcare, SaaS / B2B, E commerce, Education, Creative / Agency, Gaming, Luxury, Food & Drink, Travel, Real Estate, Non profit, Crypto / Web3, Wellness Auto Style Saturation, corners, shadows, weights, ratio, motion Modern, Minim"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Design System Generator","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the Design System Generator, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Generation and inputs","Audit","Fonts and icons","Share, save and export","Related"],"x":" Why: every change regenerates the whole system and rebuilds every tab. What to do: settle the brief first, then explore the tabs and the playground. Why: the seed's chroma is kept within a workable range, and ramp steps outside sRGB have their chroma reduced until they fit. What to do: this is expected. For more colour, try a more saturated style Bold, Playful, Futuristic or a Vivid ramp peak. Why: the primary fill is the ramp step that is visible on the background 3:1 and takes a readable label at your target. Your exact seed may not meet that. What to do: keep the generated fill for accessibility, or lower the Contrast target if your requirements allow. Why: when a seed is set, the seed decides hue and chroma; the industry then only affects fonts and icons. What to do: select Auto beside the seed to go back to the industry's hue. Why: an unexpected error while generating. What to do: reload the page. If a shared link caused it, check its parameter values against Share, save and connect share save and connect.md . Why: a role colour does not meet its requirement. What to do: open the full audit and read What would fix it . Try the next contrast target, a less saturated style, or "},{"t":"Design System Generator FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Design System Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/docs/faq.html","h":["Is it the same as \"Design Engine\"?","Do I need an account?","Is anything generated on a server?","Will the same inputs always give the same system?","Where is the Generate button?","Why is there no dark-theme score?","Which export should I use?","Can I use my own font or icon set?","Are the fonts free to use?","Does passing the audit make my product accessible?","Related"],"x":" Yes. The page's title is the Design System Generator; its address and some labels use Design Engine. No, to generate, share and export. Saving systems uses your Auric Artisan Library; see the Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . No. The system is calculated in your browser. The page downloads fonts and icons for the previews; see Privacy ../others/privacy.md . The same job is also available through the public REST API, which is billed in API credits. Yes. That is why a share link reproduces a system. The only exceptions are the ramp shape and token naming, which links and saved systems do not carry; see Share, save and connect share save and connect.md . There is none. Every change regenerates the system at once. The score is calculated from the light roles. The dark roles are fully audited in the audit view under Dark . CSS or JSON if you want everything. Tailwind v4 for Tailwind projects with roles. Figma / W3C to import into Figma Variables or Tokens Studio colours, type, spacing, radius and shadow only . The native formats for Android, iOS, Flutter or Compose colours and dimensions . See Export tokens export tokens.md . The tool recommends from its own list. Af"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Glossary, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the Design System Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Reference material that supports the Design System Generator guides. The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond the standard ones, so there is no shortcuts page. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Design system, colour and contrast terms used in these docs. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the generator and audit calculate, and what they do not. related.md related.md Related tools, services and Learn articles. privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network. Design System Generator overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Design System Generator documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning APCA / Lc Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a contrast method proposed for WCAG 3; Lc is its lightness contrast value, shown here without its sign. Brief The set of inputs industry, style, target and overrides a system is generated from. Chroma How colourful a colour is; in OKLCH, the C value. Colour mode Whether the system builds light roles, dark roles or both. Contrast target The minimum WCAG contrast body text must reach: 3:1, 4.5:1 or 7:1. Density How compact the type and spacing are. Design system A shared set of design decisions colours, type, spacing and more and the components built from them. Design token One named design decision stored as data, such as space 4: 16px . Deterministic Always producing the same output from the same inputs. Gamut mapping Reducing a colour's chroma until it can be shown in sRGB. Harmony The positions of the secondary and accent hues relative to the primary. Headroom How far body text's contrast clears the target. Hierarchy Body, muted and subtle text reading as three distinct levels. Modular scale Font sizes that grow by a fixed ratio, such as 1.25. Neutral ramp A ramp of greys, here tinted slightly towards the brand hue"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Design System Generator calculates, how reliable the audit and score are, and where the output stops.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is calculated","What the audit covers","What the score means","What the generator does not do","Previews depend on the network","Related"],"x":" Colours are built in OKLCH and converted to sRGB HEX codes. Steps outside sRGB have their chroma reduced by search until they fit, so no channel is clipped. Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2.x relative luminance formula. Translucent tokens are blended over the surface beneath them before measuring. APCA values come from a compact implementation of the APCA formula. APCA is still a draft for WCAG 3, and its values are shown as context, not as a gate. Colour vision previews use simple matrix simulations of deuteranopia, protanopia and tritanopia. Twelve pairings per theme: eight role pairings and the four semantic solids with their labels, each against the requirement for its content. A matrix of every foreground role against every surface role. It does not cover your layout, font sizes and weights in use, text over images, focus rings on coloured backgrounds, hover and disabled states, or any accessibility requirement beyond colour contrast. The score 40 to 100 blends accessibility 55 , vibrancy 18 , headroom 15 and hierarchy 12 , from the light roles only. It is a heuristic for comparing systems, not a quality grade or a compliance result. It does not know your brand, your audience o"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Design System Generator keeps in your browser, what it saves, and which services it contacts.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" The whole system is generated in the page. Your inputs are not sent to a server to generate it. Copies go to your clipboard only when you select a copy control. Downloads are created in the browser. Stored in your browser's local storage on this device: your last set of inputs, used to restore the system on your next visit; whether the side rails are expanded; whether you dismissed the API note. What Where Why Fonts for the type previews fonts.auricartisan.com Auric font CDN and fonts.googleapis.com fallback To draw the specimens in the recommended families. The requests name the font families. Icons for the previews icons.auricartisan.com Auric icon CDN To show the recommended icon family. Saving Your Auric Artisan Library When you select Save or the save button. Share links Your clipboard and address bar The link contains your inputs; anyone you send it to can see them. Opening another tool from Connect passes your seed colour and palette to that tool in the address, and keeps a copy for that tool in your browser's session storage. For the CDNs as services, see the Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md and Icon CDN ../../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md . Site "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools, services and Learn articles that go with the Design System Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/design-engine/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Services","Library and kits","Learn articles","Related"],"x":" Tool Why Personalization Generator ../../personalisation generator/README.md Another way to generate a personalised palette and tokens from a brief. Basic Color Tools ../../basic colour tools/README.md Palettes, gradients and conversions, and the Colour Tools the Connect view opens. Font Library ../../font library/README.md Inspect, compare and embed the recommended font families, and check their licences. Icon Library ../../icon library/README.md Browse and export the recommended icon family. Color Science Lab ../../colour science lab/README.md Deeper colour analysis of your palette. Accessibility and vision tools ../../../accessibility and vision/README.md Contrast Checker, Vision Simulation and the URL Analyzer for checks beyond tokens. Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md : the service that serves the fonts. Icon CDN ../../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md : the service that serves the icons. Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md : generate design tokens from your own code. Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md : where saved systems live. Colour libraries ../../../../library/colour libraries/README.md : palette, shade, gradient "},{"t":"Font Library","d":"What the Font Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to find, test, compare and take away open-licence fonts from the Auric Artisan catalogue.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Font Library is the browsing and testing page for the Auric Artisan font catalogue: 2,213 families and 4,883 font files, 550 of them variable fonts, covering 60 scripts and Unicode blocks. Every card is set in its own typeface, so you judge fonts by looking at them. Type your own words and every card shows them. Open a family and a panel docks beside the grid with eleven tabs: a specimen you can type into and style, variable axis sliders and OpenType switches, computed suitability scores, suggested pairings, the full glyph set, every style and file, the licence and its permissions, the character coverage, developer exports font stacks, Tailwind, SCSS, tokens and a modular type scale and ready to paste embed code. Star the families you like and they gather in Your kit , kept in your browser. From there you can compare up to four side by side, copy one combined embed snippet, or download a self hosting kit: a ZIP with the font files, a stylesheet, a demo page and the licence. A Recommend panel suggests families for an industry, a brand style or even a colour palette. The fonts are served by the Auric Artisan Font CDN, so previews and embeds make no request to any third party. Th"},{"t":"Font Library documentation","d":"The list of guides for the Font Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the page, learn the layout, find and keep a first family. browse and filter.md browse and filter.md Preview text and size, search, sort, categories, facets, applied filters, grid and list. collections and recommender.md collections and recommender.md The six collections, the recommender and recently viewed families. specimen panel.md specimen panel.md The docked panel, and the Specimen tab's editor, axes and OpenType switches. family details.md family details.md Suitability, Pairings, Glyphs, Features, Styles, About, License and Charset tabs. develop and embed.md develop and embed.md Font stacks, code exports, the type scale, and embed code. kit compare and download.md kit compare and download.md Selecting families, Your kit, the Selected view, Compare, combined embed and download kits. reference.md reference.md Every control, option and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. Font Library overview ../README.md Supporting material ../others/README.md Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md "},{"t":"Getting started with the Font Library","d":"Open the Font Library, learn its layout, and find, test and keep your first family.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","The layout","A card","Your first family","Next steps","Related"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/. The masthead reads Two thousand faces, set in their own. Its labels give the live counts of families, font files, variable fonts and scripts. The catalogue loads from the Font CDN. If it cannot be reached, a notice explains that the library is temporarily unavailable; see Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Three views sit in a row at the top: Specimens with the number of families shown , Collections 6 and Selected the number you have starred . The Specimens view has two columns: The rail on the left, which stays in view as you scroll: Find : the search box, the sort menu, Filters , Recommend , and the number of matching families; Applied : what is switched on, when anything is; Category : All , Serif , Sans Serif , Handwriting , Monospace and Display , with counts; Narrow it : six groups of filter chips; at the foot, Reset all filters and, once you have starred something, Download selected . The stage on the right: the preview text box with Shuffle , Grid and List , the Size slider, and the grid of cards, which loads more as you scroll. Once you have opened a family, a Recently viewed strip appears under the three views. On screens narr"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Preview your own text, set the specimen size, search, sort, pick a category, narrow with filter chips, and switch between grid and list.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/browse-and-filter.html","h":["Preview your own text","Specimen size","Grid or list","Search","Sort","Category","Narrow it: the filter chips","See and clear what is applied","Related"],"x":" Everything here happens on the Specimens view. The grid shows 48 families at first and loads more as you scroll. Type in Type to preview every family… above the grid. Every card shows your text in its own face. Clear the box to go back to each family's name. Your text also starts the specimen in the family panel and appears in the Styles tab and in Compare . The Size row sets how large the card specimens are. Drag the slider, use − and + 2 pixels a step , or select Reset to 40 . The slider snaps near 16, 24, 48, 72 and 96. Cards keep their specimens between 22 and 48 pixels, so settings below 22 or above 48 make no further difference to the grid. For a bigger view, open the family: the specimen editor goes up to 400 pixels. Grid shows cards in columns; List shows one family per row, which suits long preview text. Type in Family, designer or foundry . Results update as you type. The search looks for what you type anywhere in the family name, the designer's name or the category for example mono or serif , ignoring capitals. Foundry names are not searched, despite the placeholder. Option Order Alphabetical A to Z default Accessibility score Intended to put the highest accessibility s"},{"t":"Collections and the recommender","d":"The six curated collections, the Find your font recommender, and the Recently viewed strip.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/collections-and-recommender.html","h":["Collections","Find your font: the recommender","Recently viewed","Related"],"x":" Three shortcuts past the alphabet: curated collections, a recommender that ranks families for a brief, and a strip of families you opened recently. Open the Collections view. Under Featured collections curated starting points, ranked by our computed scores there are six rows of up to 14 families each: Collection Description on the page Popular Fonts Widely used, battle tested families New Fonts Most recently published in the collection Best UI Fonts Interface & product type — clean, high legibility sans Best Accessibility Fonts Highest legibility & character distinction Best Developer Fonts Monospaced, distinct, code ready Best Editorial Fonts For headlines & long form reading Each mini card shows the family in its own face with its accessibility score. Select one to open the family. The collections are hidden while a search, a filter or the recommender is active on the Specimens view. If the Collections view looks empty, clear those first; see Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Select Recommend in the rail or choose Find your font from the command palette to open ✨ Find your font above the grid: Describe the brand or drop a colour palette — we rank the catalogue by computed fit"},{"t":"Develop and embed","d":"Copy a font stack, CSS variables, Tailwind, SCSS, design tokens or a modular type scale from the Develop tab, and embed code from the Use & Embed tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/develop-and-embed.html","h":["Develop","Use & Embed","Embed several families at once","Related"],"x":" Two tabs in the family panel give you code. Develop is for your stylesheets and design system; Use & Embed is for loading the font on a page. For how the Font CDN serves these files, and for self hosting, see the Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md documentation. A font family line with the family first and safe fallbacks for its category, for example for a serif: css font family: 'Lora', ui serif, Georgia, Cambria, 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; Copy copies it; the message reads Copied stack . Five formats, each with Copy : Format What you get CSS variables A :root variable such as font serif and a body rule using it Tailwind A tailwind.config.js fragment that adds the stack to fontFamily SCSS A $font … variable and a body rule Design tokens A JSON token such as font.family.serif with type fontFamily CSS @import An @import of the family's CDN stylesheet and the variable The variable and token names use mono for monospace families, serif for serif families and sans for everything else. A scale of nine sizes, xs , sm , base , md , lg , xl , 2xl , 3xl and 4xl , each shown in the family with its size in pixels and rem. Control Options Default Base 10 to 24 px 16 Rat"},{"t":"Family details","d":"The Suitability, Pairings, Glyphs, Features, Styles, About, License and Charset tabs of the family panel.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/family-details.html","h":["Suitability","Pairings","Glyphs","Features","Styles","About","License","Charset","Related"],"x":" These eight tabs in the family panel tell you what a family is good for, what goes with it, what it contains and what you may do with it. The page explains: Scores are computed from this font's own outlines and metrics — x height, character distinction, proportions, weight range and screen rendering — not editorial opinion. Five scores from 0 to 100, sorted best first: Score Meaning on the page Accessibility Legibility & character distinction for the widest audience Readability Comfort for long form body text UI / Product Clarity at small sizes in interfaces Developer / Code Monospacing & glyph disambiguation for code Editorial Headlines & long form print character Why these scores shows the measurements behind them, each 0 to 100: x height , with the measured value in em; Character distinction I l 1 · 0 O , noting distinct zero where the zero differs from the letter O; Proportion / width ; Weight flexibility , with the number of weights; Screen rendering ; Low stroke contrast . Best for lists uses the family qualifies for: UI & product UI 78 or more , Body text readability 78 or more , Code developer 75 or more , Headlines editorial 78 or more and Accessibility critical accessibi"},{"t":"Your kit, compare and download","d":"Select families into Your kit, see them in the Selected view, compare up to four side by side, copy combined embed code, and download self-hosting kits.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/kit-compare-and-download.html","h":["Select families","The Your kit tray","The Selected view","Compare","Combined embed code","Download a self-hosting kit","Related"],"x":" Families you select gather in Your kit . The kit is kept in your browser on this device, so it is still there next time, and a second tab of the page sees the same kit. Any of these adds a family to your kit: the star ☆ on a card, which turns to ★ ; ＋ Select in the family panel, which turns to ✓ Selected ; ＋ Select both on the Pairings tab, which adds the open family and its partner. Select the star or the button again to remove the family. Once something is selected, a Your kit button with a count appears in the bottom right corner. Select it to open the tray: Your kit with the count and Kept in this browser , a list of families each with ✕ to remove it , and four buttons: Button What it does Needs Embed Shows combined embed code for the whole kit 1 family Download Downloads one ZIP of self hosting kits 1 family Compare Opens a side by side comparison 2 families Clear Empties the kit always available Hide closes the tray. Download selected at the foot of the rail does the same as Download , and shows the count, for example Download selected 3 . The Selected view at the top lists your kit as cards with each family's name and category. With nothing selected it reads Nothing selecte"},{"t":"The specimen panel","d":"How the family panel docks, resizes and closes, and how to use the Specimen tab's editor, variable axes, named instances, OpenType switches and presets.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/specimen-panel.html","h":["Where the panel sits","The panel header","The Specimen tab","Related"],"x":" Selecting a card opens that family in a panel. It is where you test a family and find everything about it. On a wide screen wider than about 1,180 pixels , the panel docks to the right edge as a column of the page. The page moves aside, nothing is covered, and you can keep selecting cards: the panel simply shows the next family. Drag the grip on the panel's left edge to make it wider or narrower 380 to 720 pixels; 460 at first . Double click the grip to go back to 460. With the grip focused, ← and → resize it by 16 pixels, or 48 with Shift . The width you choose is remembered. On a narrower screen , the panel is a sheet from the bottom, covering about 62% of the screen so the card you tapped stays visible. Drag the grip up to open it to 94%, or down to close it. With the grip focused, ↑ and ↓ move it in steps. Tapping the dimmed page above closes it. Close the panel with ✕ or Esc . Focus returns to the card you opened it from. The family name, and a line with its category, by designer, number of styles, ⚡ number of variable axes for variable fonts and number of glyphs. ＋ Select adds the family to Your kit ; it then reads ✓ Selected , and selecting it again removes the family. Down"},{"t":"Font Library reference","d":"Every view, control, option, file and message in the Font Library in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Address","Catalogue","Views","Rail","Stage","Family panel","Specimen tab","Scores","Develop tab","Use & Embed tab","Recommender","Files","Messages","Related"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/ Figure Value Families 2,213 Font files 4,883 Variable families 550 Families with italics 401 Served Library 2,023 Listed only System, marked Installed 190 Scripts and Unicode blocks 60 Licences Open Font License 1,929; Unspecified 191; Apache 2.0 45; Creative Commons 40; MIT 7; Custom 1 View Contents Specimens Rail and grid; the count of matching families Collections Six curated rows Selected Your kit as cards; the count Control Values Default Search Family name, designer or category empty Sort Alphabetical, Accessibility score, UI score, Readability score, Most weights, Most glyphs, Variable first, Surprise me Alphabetical Filters Shows or hides the chip groups shown Recommend Opens Find your font closed Category All, Serif, Sans Serif, Handwriting, Monospace, Display All Filter these options Text empty Properties ⚡ Variable, 𝘐 Italic, ⌗ Monospace off Weights available 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800, 900 off Features Ligatures, Small Caps, Oldstyle Figures, Tabular Figures, Fractions, Slashed Zero, Stylistic Sets, Swashes off Scripts The 18 most common off Licence Six licence types off Source Library, System off Reset all filters Clear"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Font Library, from an empty page to downloads and shortcuts that do not behave.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The page stays empty, or says the library is unavailable","Some cards show a plain font instead of the family","Sorting by Accessibility score or Readability score shows A to Z","The Collections view is empty","The Size slider stops changing the cards","Searching for a foundry finds nothing","I cannot filter for my language","The F and R keys do nothing","The Selected view shows names in a plain font","The weight chips in Use & Embed do not change the code","Download kit is disabled or says Installed only","The ZIP is missing a file","My kit disappeared","The panel covers the page on my tablet","Related"],"x":" The catalogue and the fonts load from the Font CDN. If it cannot be reached, after a few seconds the grid shows Font library is temporarily unavailable or The live font engine didn’t load , with the likely causes. Check that you are online. Turn off extensions that block scripts or requests for this site, and allow requests to fonts.auricartisan.com. Select Retry , or reload the page, once the connection is back. The specimen appears once the family's font file has loaded; slow connections show a stand in first. Cards marked Installed only appear in their own face if that font is installed on your device; see Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . At the time of writing these two sort options do not take effect, and the grid stays in alphabetical order. UI score works. For accessible families, open Collections and use Best Accessibility Fonts , or open Recommend with Accessibility priority set to Essential . Each card's badge also shows its accessibility score. The collections are hidden while a search, a filter chip, a category or the recommender is active on Specimens . Select Clear all under Applied or Reset all filters and close the recommender, then open Colle"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Font Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account?","Are the fonts free to use?","What does Installed mean?","Does embedding a font send my visitors' data to a third party?","How are the suitability scores worked out?","Why does the recommender keep suggesting well-known fonts?","Can I test variable fonts?","Can I see a font in my own layout?","Can I upload my own fonts?","Is my kit shared between devices?","Related"],"x":" No. Browsing, testing, embed code and downloads all work without signing in. Your kit is kept in your browser. Most families are under the SIL Open Font License, and others under Apache 2.0, MIT, Creative Commons or other terms; 191 families have no licence the catalogue could identify. Check each family's License tab and its full licence text before you use it, especially commercially. The Font CDN licences ../../../../../services/font cdn/others/licences.md page explains the licence types. The family is listed for reference but not served: it came from fonts installed on a computer, whose licences do not allow redistribution. The page can show it only if the same font is installed on your device, and it cannot be downloaded or embedded from the CDN. The embed code points at the Auric Artisan Font CDN, not at a third party font service. To avoid any external request, download the kit and self host the files. They are computed from each font's own outlines and metrics, such as x height, how distinct look alike characters are I, l, 1; 0, O , proportions, weight range and how well it renders on screens. They are not editorial ratings. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and acc"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"The glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the Font Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Type and font terms used on the page. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and the command palette. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the catalogue, scores and previews can and cannot tell you. related.md related.md Tools, services and reading that go with the library. privacy.md privacy.md What is kept in your browser and what uses the network. Font Library overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts and the command palette in the Font Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["The command palette","In the family panel","Related"],"x":" Shortcuts work when you are not typing in a field. They do not use Ctrl , Cmd or Alt : Ctrl + K belongs to the site wide search. Key What it does ? Opens the library command palette / Focuses the search box S Shuffles the results into a random order G Grid view L List view T Opens the Your kit tray close it with Hide Makes card specimens smaller Makes card specimens larger C Compares your kit two or more families Esc Closes the command palette or the family panel F Meant to show or hide filters; see below R Meant to open the recommender; see below At the time of writing, F and R switch their panel twice, so nothing appears to change. Use the Filters and Recommend buttons, or the command palette. Press ? to open a search box of commands. Type to narrow the list for example shuffle , filters or size , move with ↑ and ↓ , run a command with Enter , and close with Esc . Commands include Focus search , Shuffle results , Grid view , List view , Toggle filters , Find your font , Open selected tray , Download selected , Increase preview size , Decrease preview size , Scroll to top , Toggle light / dark theme and Focus preview text , plus a Category · command for each category. Each shows "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Type and font terms used in the Font Library and its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning Axis One dimension a variable font can change along, such as weight wght or width wdth . Character variant An OpenType feature cv01 to cv99 that swaps the design of one particular character. Code point The number Unicode gives a character, written like U+0041. Family All the styles of one typeface, such as Regular, Bold and Italic. Fallback stack The fonts listed after the one you want, used if it is missing. @font face The CSS rule that tells a browser where a font file is and which style it provides. Foundry The company or person that publishes a typeface. Glyph A single drawn shape in a font, usually a character. Heading and body The two roles in a type pairing: a display face for titles and a text face for reading. Installed A family listed from system fonts, shown only if you have it installed, and not served. Instance A named point on a variable font's axes, such as Light or Condensed Bold. Ligature Two or more characters drawn as one glyph, such as fi, or = in coding fonts. Modular type scale A set of sizes where each step is the previous one times a fixed ratio. OpenType feature A switchable behaviour inside a font, named by a four letter tag such as liga or t"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Font Library's catalogue, categories, scores, recommendations and previews can and cannot tell you.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The catalogue is read from the font files","Categories are detected automatically","Scores are computed, not judged","Recommendations and pairings use a shortlist","Installed families","Previews are your browser's rendering","Page limits","Known issues","Related"],"x":" Names, designers, foundries, versions, dates, weights, scripts and licences come from the data inside each font file. Where a file leaves something out, the page leaves it out too, or shows it as unknown. 191 families have no licence the catalogue could identify; they appear under Unspecified . Each family's category serif, sans serif, display, handwriting or monospace and its serif or sans serif classification are worked out from the font's data and letter shapes, not assigned by hand. Some families are misclassified; rounded sans serifs in particular can be listed as serif. If the category filter hides a family you expect, search for it by name. The suitability scores and style fingerprints are calculated from measurements of each font: x height, how distinct look alike characters are, proportions, weight range, stroke contrast and how it renders on screen. They are useful for sorting and comparing, but: they do not know how a font was designed to be used, so a display face can score well in a category it was not made for; a high accessibility score is a good sign, not a guarantee. Test your text at real sizes with real readers, and check colour contrast separately. This is why "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Font Library keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" Your preview text, specimen edits, recommender choices and palettes are used only in the page. They are not sent anywhere. Download kits are assembled in your browser. In your browser's local storage on this device: Your kit : the families you selected; which filter groups you folded; the width of the family panel; the last twelve families you opened Recently viewed . Like other pages on the site, the page also keeps the values of some fields, such as your preview text, in the page address after p= , so a reload restores them. If you share the address, the other person sees those values. See Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md . Loading the page and its scripts. The catalogue, the specimens and every font file load from the Auric Artisan Font CDN at fonts.auricartisan.com. No third party font service is involved. Downloads fetch the font files from the same CDN. Site wide analytics and advertising follow your cookie choices. See the Help centre ../../../../../help/README.md . For what the CDN itself records, see Font CDN privacy ../../../../../services/font cdn/others/privacy.md . Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md Your kit, compare and down"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools, services and reading that go with the Font Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/font-library/others/related.html","h":["Services","Tools","Learn articles","Related"],"x":" Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md : the service that serves these fonts, with its loader, self hosting guide and licences. Icon CDN ../../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md : the matching service for icons. Icon Library ../../icon library/README.md : the same kind of browser for 12,896 icons. Design System Generator ../../design engine/README.md : build a colour and type system from a brief. Personalization Generator ../../personalisation generator/README.md : palettes, type pairings and a brand Studio from your colours. Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md : check the colour contrast of your text. Color in Typography and Text https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 13 color in typography and text Building a Color System https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 16 building a color system scales tokens themes Supporting material README.md "},{"t":"Icon Library","d":"What the Icon Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to find, restyle and take away icons from seven open-licence sets.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Icon Library puts seven open licence icon sets under one search: Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. That is 12,896 icons in 32,803 variants across 21 styles, such as outline, fill, duotone or 16 pixel solid. Resize, recolour and change the stroke of every icon at once, then open one to see it large, switch its style, and copy it as SVG, a React JSX component, an image data URI or a one line CDN tag. Select the icons you need into Your kit and take them away as a ZIP of SVG files or a single SVG sprite. The icons are served by the Auric Artisan Icon CDN, so nothing loads from a third party. The CDN itself the loader script, embedding, self hosting and licences is documented under Icon CDN ../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md . Developers who need an icon as SVG, JSX or an embed tag. Designers comparing how an idea is drawn across several sets. Anyone building a small, consistent icon kit for a project. Page: https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/ No sign in is needed. Your kit and view settings are kept in your browser. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/. 2. Type what you need in Name, tag or set , for example arrow . 3. Pick a set on the"},{"t":"Icon Library documentation","d":"The list of guides for the Icon Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the page, learn the layout, copy a first icon. browse and filter.md browse and filter.md Search, sort, sets and styles, category and licence filters, size, stroke and colour. sets and finder.md sets and finder.md The Sets view, featured collections, Find your icon and Recently viewed. icon panel.md icon panel.md The docked panel: preview controls, copy and download, code blocks, details, Material icons. kit and export.md kit and export.md Selecting icons, Your kit, the ZIP and the SVG sprite. reference.md reference.md Every control, set, style and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. Icon Library overview ../README.md Supporting material ../others/README.md Icon CDN ../../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md "},{"t":"Getting started with the Icon Library","d":"Open the Icon Library, learn its layout, and find, restyle and copy your first icon.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","The layout","Your first icon","Next steps","Related"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/. The masthead reads Twelve thousand icons, one line to serve them and its labels give the live counts of icons, variants, sets and styles. The catalogue loads from the Icon CDN. If it cannot be reached, a notice explains that the library is temporarily unavailable; see Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Two views sit in a row at the top: Icons with the number of icons shown and Sets 7 . The Icons view has two columns: The rail on the left, which stays in view as you scroll: Find : the search box, the sort menu, Recommend , Shuffle , Filters and the number of matching icons; Applied : what is switched on, when anything is; Set : All and the seven sets with their counts, and a style switch when the chosen set has more than one style; Narrow it : the Category and License chips; at the foot, Reset filters and Download selected . The stage on the right: Size , Stroke and Colour controls, then the grid of icons with their names, which loads more as you scroll. Once you have opened an icon, a Recently viewed strip appears under the two views. On screens narrower than about 1,180 pixels the rail sits above the grid and its filter groups start fo"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Search, sort, choose a set and style, filter by category and licence, and preview every icon at your size, stroke and colour.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/browse-and-filter.html","h":["Search","Sort","Sets and styles","Narrow it: category and licence","See and clear what is applied","Size, stroke and colour","Related"],"x":" Everything here happens on the Icons view. The grid shows 120 icons at first and loads more as you scroll. Each tile shows the icon and its name; hover it to see the name in full. Select a tile to open the icon. Type in Name, tag or set . Results update as you type. The search looks for your text in the icon's name, in its identifier which begins with the set's name, so lucide finds every Lucide icon , and in its keywords. Only Tabler and Remix icons carry keywords, so a word such as notification finds more in those two sets. Option Order Alphabetical A to Z by name default Group by set Set by set, A to Z within each Surprise me Random order Shuffle switches the sort to Surprise me and deals a new random order. The Set chips pick one set at a time: All 12,896 , Phosphor 1,512 , Tabler 5,093 , Lucide 1,714 , Remix 1,690 , Heroicons 324 , Feather 287 or Material 2,276 . When the chosen set has more than one style, a style switch appears under the set chips: Set Styles, in the order shown default in bold Phosphor Thin, Light, Regular , Bold, Fill, Duotone Tabler Outline , Filled Lucide Regular only Remix Line , Fill Heroicons 24 · Outline , 24 · Solid, 20 · Solid, 16 · Solid Feather "},{"t":"The icon panel","d":"Preview an icon large, switch its style, size, colour and stroke, copy it as SVG, JSX, a data URI or a CDN tag, download it, and read its details.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/icon-panel.html","h":["Where the panel sits","The header","Preview controls","Copy and download","The code blocks","Details","Material icons","Related"],"x":" Selecting an icon opens it in a panel. On a wide screen wider than about 1,180 pixels , the panel docks to the right edge as a column of the page. Nothing is covered, and selecting another icon shows that one instead. Drag the grip on the panel's left edge to resize it 380 to 720 pixels; 460 at first . Double click the grip to go back to 460. With the grip focused, ← and → resize it, faster with Shift . The width is remembered. On a narrower screen , the panel is a sheet from the bottom at about 62% of the screen. Drag the grip up to open it to 94%, or down to close it. Tapping the dimmed page closes it. Close the panel with ✕ or Esc . The icon's name, and a line with its set, licence, category Tabler and Remix only and number of styles. ＋ Select adds the icon to Your kit ; it then reads ✓ Selected . See Your kit and export kit and export.md . Download .svg downloads the icon in the style the grid is showing, as it comes from the set, without your panel colour or stroke. Use Download .svg among the copy buttons for a restyled file. A large preview sits beside the controls. Changing these affects the preview; colour and stroke also change the code below. Control Range Notes Style T"},{"t":"Your kit and export","d":"Select icons into Your kit, and take them away as a ZIP of SVG files or a single SVG sprite.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/kit-and-export.html","h":["Select icons","The Your kit tray","The ZIP","The SVG sprite","Related"],"x":" Icons you select gather in Your kit . The kit is kept in your browser on this device, so it is still there next time. Open an icon and select ＋ Select in its panel; it turns to ✓ Selected , and the icon's tile in the grid is marked as selected. Select the button again to remove it. Each icon is kept in the style the grid was showing when you selected it. To keep a different style, switch the style in the rail first. Once something is selected, a Your kit button with a count appears. Select it to open or close the tray: Your kit with the count and Kept in this browser , a list of your icons with a small preview, name and set each with ✕ to remove it , and three buttons: Button What it does Message Download ZIP Downloads all your icons as SVG files Downloaded n icons Copy sprite Copies one SVG sprite containing all your icons SVG sprite copied Clear Empties the kit none Hide closes the tray. Download selected at the foot of the rail does the same as Download ZIP and shows the count, for example Download selected 5 ; it is disabled while the kit is empty. With an empty kit, the messages read Select some icons first . The file is auric icons.zip . Inside: a folder per set, holding one"},{"t":"Sets, collections and Find your icon","d":"The Sets view, the featured collections, the Find your icon panel and the Recently viewed strip.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/sets-and-finder.html","h":["The Sets view","Find your icon","Recently viewed","Related"],"x":" Open Sets at the top. Seven sets, each a shortcut past the alphabet. A card for each set shows its name, Open set and its number of icons. Select a card to choose that set and go back to the Icons view. Set Icons Styles Licence Author Phosphor 1,512 6 MIT Phosphor Icons Tabler 5,093 2 MIT Paweł Kuna Lucide 1,714 1 ISC Lucide Contributors Remix 1,690 2 Remix v1.0 Remix Design Heroicons 324 4 MIT Tailwind Labs Feather 287 1 MIT Cole Bemis Material 2,276 5 Apache 2.0 Google Material icons are a webfont rather than SVG files, which changes what you can copy; see The icon panel icon panel.md . Under the set cards, Featured collections Fast starts, just like the font library. has two rows: Icon sets Browse complete families : a card per set with its count and licence. Selecting one chooses the set, clears the search and category, and scrolls to the icons. Popular categories Jump straight into a use case : the ten largest categories, such as System , Design , Arrows , Brand and Devices , with their counts. Selecting one switches to All sets, filters to that category, and scrolls to the icons. Featured collections are hidden while a search, a set other than All , a filter or Find your ico"},{"t":"Icon Library reference","d":"Every view, control, set, style, file and message in the Icon Library in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Address","Catalogue","Sets","Views","Rail","Grid controls","Icon panel","Find your icon","Files","Messages","Related"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/ Figure Value Icons 12,896 Variants icon and style combinations 32,803 Sets 7 Styles 21 Icons with categories and keywords Tabler and Remix only 51 categories Set Icons Styles Default style Licence Kind Phosphor 1,512 Thin, Light, Regular, Bold, Fill, Duotone Regular MIT SVG, filled shapes Tabler 5,093 Outline, Filled Outline MIT SVG, stroked Lucide 1,714 Regular Regular ISC SVG, stroked Remix 1,690 Line, Fill Line Remix v1.0 SVG, filled shapes Heroicons 324 24 · Outline, 24 · Solid, 20 · Solid, 16 · Solid 24 · Outline MIT SVG, mixed Feather 287 Regular Regular MIT SVG, stroked Material 2,276 Outlined, Round, Sharp, Regular, Twotone Outlined Apache 2.0 Webfont View Contents Icons Rail, controls and grid; the count of matching icons Sets Seven set cards and Featured collections Control Values Default Search Name, identifier or keyword empty Sort Alphabetical, Group by set, Surprise me Alphabetical Recommend Opens Find your icon closed Shuffle Random order button Filters Shows or hides the chip groups shown Set All and seven sets All Style The chosen set's styles The set's default Category Up to 40 for the current set off License MIT, ISC, Remix v1"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Icon Library, from an empty page to filters and exports that do not behave as expected.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The page stays empty, or says the library is unavailable","Some tiles show a plain rounded square","The Category filter says No categories for this set","A keyword search finds only Tabler and Remix icons","Moving Stroke changes nothing","The Featured collections are missing from the Sets view","Removing a licence filter with × turns on a different licence","Find your icon shows high match numbers for poor matches","The ZIP icons are not the size or colour I previewed","The header Download .svg ignores my colour","A Material icon will not download as SVG","My kit disappeared","Related"],"x":" The catalogue and the icons load from the Icon CDN. If it cannot be reached, after a few seconds the grid shows Icon library is temporarily unavailable or The live icon engine didn’t load , with the likely causes. Check that you are online. Turn off extensions that block scripts or requests for this site, and allow requests to icons.auricartisan.com. Select Retry , or reload the page, once the connection is back. That square stands in for an icon whose drawing could not be loaded. Scroll away and back, or reload the page. If it persists for a particular set and style, try another style. Only Tabler and Remix icons have categories. Choose All , Tabler or Remix , or search by name instead. Only those two sets carry keywords. For the other sets, search by the words in the icon's name, such as bell , arrow or user . Stroke affects outline icons only: Tabler Outline , Lucide, Feather and outline Heroicons. Filled sets such as Phosphor, Remix and Material have no stroke to change. They are hidden while a search, a set other than All , a filter or Find your icon is active. Select Clear all under Applied , close Find your icon , and open Sets again. The seven set cards are always shown. A"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Icon Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account?","Can I use these icons in commercial projects?","Why do icons change colour with my text?","Which format should I copy?","Can I mix icons from different sets?","Can I upload my own icons?","Is my kit shared between devices?","Related"],"x":" No. Browsing, copying and downloading all work without signing in. Each set keeps its own open licence: MIT Phosphor, Tabler, Heroicons, Feather , ISC Lucide , the Remix Icon licence Remix and Apache 2.0 Material . The panel shows each icon's licence and author, and links to the set's website where the full terms are. See also Icon CDN licences ../../../../../services/icon cdn/others/licences.md . The icons are drawn in currentColor , which means \"the colour of the surrounding text\". Pick a colour in the panel before copying to fix it, or set color in your CSS. SVG to paste into HTML or a design tool. JSX for a React component. data URI for an <img tag or a CSS background without a separate file. CDN tag to let the Icon CDN script insert the icon for you. Yes, but sets differ in line weight, corner style and grid size. For a consistent look, keep to one set, or compare the same idea across sets by searching its name with All chosen. No. The library shows the seven bundled sets only. No. It is kept in the browser on the device where you made it. Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Getting started getting started.md Icon CDN FAQ ../../../../../services/icon cdn/docs/faq.md "},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"The glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the Icon Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Icon and SVG terms used on the page. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and the command palette. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the catalogue, search and exports can and cannot do. related.md related.md Tools and services that go with the library. privacy.md privacy.md What is kept in your browser and what uses the network. Icon Library overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts and the command palette in the Icon Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["The command palette","In the icon panel","Related"],"x":" Shortcuts work when you are not typing in a field. They do not use Ctrl , Cmd or Alt : Ctrl + K belongs to the site wide search. Key What it does ? Opens the library command palette / Focuses the search box S Shuffles the icons into a random order F Shows or hides the filter chips R Opens or closes Find your icon T Opens or closes the Your kit tray Makes the icons smaller Makes the icons larger Esc Closes the command palette or the icon panel Press ? to open a search box of commands. Type to narrow the list, move with ↑ and ↓ , run a command with Enter , and close with Esc . Commands include Focus search , Shuffle results , Toggle filters , Find your icon , Open selected tray , Download selected , Increase preview size , Decrease preview size , Scroll to top , Toggle light / dark theme , Pick icon color , Thicker stroke and Thinner stroke , plus a Category · command for each set. Each shows its key, if it has one. Key Where What it does ← , → The panel grip, wide screens Makes the panel wider or narrower; add Shift for bigger steps ↑ , ↓ The panel grip, narrow screens Raises or lowers the sheet Getting started ../docs/getting started.md Supporting material README.md "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Icon and SVG terms used in the Icon Library and its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning currentColor A CSS keyword meaning the current text colour. Icons drawn with it take the colour of the text around them. Data URI A way to put a whole file inside a link or src attribute, so no separate file is needed. Duotone A style with two tones: a solid shape and a lighter fill behind it. Filled and outline Two ways of drawing icons: solid shapes, or lines of a set width. Identifier An icon's unique name, beginning with its set, such as lucide bell. JSX The HTML like syntax used to write React components. Set A family of icons drawn to one design, such as Lucide or Material. Sprite One SVG file holding many icons as symbols, each shown with a <use reference. Stroke width The thickness of the lines in an outline icon. Style One drawing of a set, such as Outline, Fill or 16 · Solid. SVG Scalable Vector Graphics: an image format made of shapes, sharp at any size. Symbol A reusable piece of an SVG sprite, identified by an id . Variant One icon in one style. 12,896 icons come in 32,803 variants. Webfont A font whose characters are icons, used for the Material set. Reference ../docs/reference.md Icon CDN glossary ../../../../../services/icon cdn/others/glossary.md "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Icon Library's catalogue, search, recommendations and exports can and cannot do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Categories and keywords cover two sets","Find your icon filters, it does not rank","Names are the sets' own","Previews and exports","Page limits","Known issues","Related"],"x":" Only Tabler and Remix icons 6,783 of 12,896 have categories and keywords. For Phosphor, Lucide, Heroicons, Feather and Material, the category filter, the popular categories and keyword search find nothing, and you search by the words in the icon's name. Find your icon lists the first twelve icons that match your set, category and brief, in catalogue order. Its match figures follow the list order and do not measure fit. Icon names come from each set, so the same idea can have different names in different sets for example trash , delete or bin . Try more than one word. The grid and panel controls change the preview. Only the panel's colour and stroke carry into the copied code and the restyled Download .svg . The Download .svg button in the panel header, the ZIP and the sprite hold icons as they come from their sets, in the style the grid showed when you selected them. The data URI is sized to the grid's Size , not the panel's preview size. Stroke only affects outline icons. Material icons are a webfont: they cannot be downloaded as SVG, are left out of the sprite, and appear in the ZIP as text notes. Limit Value Icons shown before scrolling loads more 120 Category chips per set 40 "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Icon Library keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" Your searches, colour and stroke choices and copied code are used only in the page. ZIP files and sprites are assembled in your browser. In your browser's local storage on this device: Your kit : the icons you selected; the chosen set, style, sort, size, stroke and colour; which filter groups you folded; the width of the icon panel; the last twelve icons you opened Recently viewed . Like other pages on the site, the page address may also record how far you have scrolled, after p= , so a reload returns you there. See Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md . Loading the page and its scripts. The catalogue and the icon drawings load from the Auric Artisan Icon CDN at icons.auricartisan.com. No third party icon service is involved. Site wide analytics and advertising follow your cookie choices. See the Help centre ../../../../../help/README.md . For what the CDN itself records, see Icon CDN privacy ../../../../../services/icon cdn/others/privacy.md . Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md Your kit and export ../docs/kit and export.md "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools and services that go with the Icon Library.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/icon-library/others/related.html","h":["Services","Tools","Related"],"x":" Icon CDN ../../../../../services/icon cdn/README.md : the service that serves these icons, with its loader, embedding, export and licences. Font CDN ../../../../../services/font cdn/README.md : the matching service for fonts. Font Library ../../font library/README.md : the same kind of browser for 2,213 font families. Basic Color Tools ../../basic colour tools/README.md : pick and test colours for your icons. Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md : check that an icon colour stands out from its background. Design System Generator ../../design engine/README.md : build the colours and type your icons sit among. Supporting material README.md "},{"t":"Personalization Generator","d":"What the Personalization Generator is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to turn a colour pool and a short brief into palettes, gradients, type, UI pairs, posters, design tokens and a live brand Studio.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Personalization Generator turns the colours you like and a short brief into a whole visual system. You give it a pool of colours your brand colours, colours you admire, a preset , pick a few style words and a use case, and describe what you want, such as calm premium dashboard for creators . It then runs a sweep : it samples hundreds or thousands of candidate palettes, scores each one for closeness to your pool, colour harmony, fit with your styles, variety, contrast and colour vision safety, and keeps the best. From the kept palettes it derives gradients in twelve styles, typography pairings, UI colour pairs, posters in twelve layouts, a full design token system semantic roles, tonal ramps, light, dark and high contrast themes, a WCAG and APCA contrast audit and data visualisation scales and a Brand Studio that paints any palette across sixteen live mockups, from a dashboard to an email. Everything can be copied as CSS, downloaded as JSON or saved to your Library. The sweep runs in your browser in small chunks, so the page stays responsive, and you can stop it at any time without losing what it has found. Brand and product designers exploring colour directions from a starting"},{"t":"Personalization Generator documentation","d":"The list of guides for the Personalization Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" These guides follow the generator's own order: pool, tune, generate, Studio, export. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the page, tour the layout, run a first sweep. build the pool.md build the pool.md Adding, building, randomising, jittering and removing pool colours; pool statistics. tune the sweep.md tune the sweep.md Style chips, intent, preference note, engine settings, scoring weights and filters; Simple and Advanced modes. run a sweep.md run a sweep.md Generate, Stop, Endless, progress, the run panel and the Overview tab. result tabs.md result tabs.md Palettes, Gradients, Typography, UI Pairs and Posters, and their actions. design tokens.md design tokens.md Semantic roles, ramps, themes, contrast audit and data visualisation scales. brand studio.md brand studio.md The sixteen mockups and their controls. presets.md presets.md The seventeen presets. export and save.md export and save.md CSS, JSON, copying and saving to the Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, option, range and default. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. Personalization Generator overview .."},{"t":"Getting started with the Personalization Generator","d":"Open the Personalization Generator, learn its layout, and run your first sweep.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","The layout","Your first sweep","Next steps","Related"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/personalization gen/. The masthead reads Describe it once, keep what survives. , with a short description, a row of labels and Read the API reference → . Each time the page opens, a quick sweep of up to 120 candidates runs by itself, so there are results on screen straight away. Results are not kept between visits; your pool and settings are. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . On a wide screen the tool has a row of tabs and three columns under it. Tabs : Overview , Pool , Tune , Palettes , Gradients , Typography , UI Pairs , Posters , Tokens , Studio , Presets and Export . Pool and the five result tabs show a count. The brief left column : a text box, Describe the system you want… e.g. calm premium dashboard for creators , with Generate , Stop and Endless under it; Search : the Simple and Advanced switch. In Advanced mode it also shows the Depth , Pool , Size and Keep boxes, the CVD safe , Contrast and Unique check boxes, and an Advanced Kit note; This run : what the next sweep will do depth, pool target, palette size, top kept, and which of the three filters are on . It shows in both modes. The stage centre : the Search results box with Clear ,"},{"t":"Brand Studio","d":"Paint any generated palette across sixteen live mockups, switch theme and density, inspect tokens, swap colours live and save the brand system.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/brand-studio.html","h":["How the palette is turned into a brand system","Choose the palette","The toolbar","The mockups","Test: swap colours live","Save the brand system","Tips","Related"],"x":" The Studio tab applies one palette to sixteen live mockups at once, so you can judge it on real layouts rather than as swatches. It opens on the leader of the last sweep; Open in Studio on any palette card, or a row in Recent palettes on Overview , opens that palette instead. From the palette the Studio picks: a background and text pair: the most readable pair in the palette; an accent : the most colourful remaining colour, and an accent 2 , the next most colourful; a surface : the background mixed a little towards the accent; quieter tones mixed between background and text for secondary surfaces, muted text and borders; success , warning , danger and info colours: a palette colour in the green, amber, red or blue range where there is one, otherwise the accent or accent 2; a type system chosen from your use case and style chips. Available Palettes lists up to 24 of the kept palettes with their names and scores. Select one to apply it to every mockup. Shuffle in the toolbar picks another at random from the same 24. Choosing a palette clears any colours you swapped in with Test . Control What it does Auto , Light , Dark Auto uses the palette's readable pair as it is. Light swaps bac"},{"t":"Build your colour pool","d":"Add, generate, randomise, nudge and remove the colours the Personalization Generator builds palettes around, and read the pool statistics.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/build-the-pool.html","h":["Add one colour","Remove a colour","Grow the pool automatically","Quick seeds","Other ways to fill the pool","Read the pool statistics","Tips","Related"],"x":" The pool is the set of colours the generator treats as yours . Every palette it keeps is scored partly on how close its colours sit to the nearest pool colour, so the pool is the strongest steer you have. It holds up to 240 colours. Open the Pool tab. The heading reads Personal Color Pool , with the count, for example Pool: 8/240 . 1. Pick a colour with the colour well, or type a HEX value such as 3C6E71 in the box next to it. Three digit values such as 3a7 also work. 2. Select Add . The colour goes to the front of the pool. If it is already in the pool, nothing changes. An invalid value shows the message Use a valid HEX color . Select any swatch in the grid. Each swatch shows an × and removes itself when selected. Clear empties the whole pool; there is no undo. If you generate with an empty pool, the generator puts the eight starting colours back first. Button What it does Build 64 Fills the pool up to your Pool target 64 by default; the label shows the current target . New colours are variations of your pool and of built in reference palettes that match your styles, use case and brief. If the pool is already larger than the target, it is cut down to the target. +24 random Adds 2"},{"t":"Design tokens","d":"The token system the Personalization Generator builds from the top palette — semantic roles, tonal ramps, light, dark and high-contrast themes, a WCAG and APCA audit, and data-visualisation scales — and how to copy it.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/design-tokens.html","h":["Semantic roles","Theme preview","Tonal ramps","Contrast audit","Data-visualisation scales","Copying the tokens","Related"],"x":" The Tokens tab turns the leader the top palette of the last sweep into a complete set of design tokens. It always uses the leader, whichever palette is open in the Studio, and it changes whenever a new sweep produces a new leader. The heading reads, for example, Semantic roles, 88 tonal stops, light/dark/high contrast themes, APCA + WCAG audit, and chart scales — from your top palette. Four figures sit beside it: Roles , Tones , WCAG floor and APCA floor . The two floors are the weakest of the first four contrast checks in the light theme body text, muted text, text on surface and the primary button . Eight role chips. Select one to copy its HEX. Role How it is chosen primary The most chromatic palette colour with a usable mid lightness. secondary The most chromatic remaining colour. accent A strongly coloured palette colour whose hue is furthest from the primary. neutral The least chromatic palette colour. success A green, pulled a little towards the nearest palette hue. warning An amber, pulled the same way. danger A red, pulled the same way. info A blue, pulled the same way. If the palette is missing something for example, it has only one strongly coloured colour , the generato"},{"t":"Export, save and share","d":"Copy CSS, download the JSON snapshot, save results to your Library, bring Library colours in, and automate the generator through the Public API.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/export-and-save.html","h":["The Export tab","Copy single results","Save to your Library","Bring colours in from your Library","Automate it","Related"],"x":" Results live only in the open page; a reload starts a fresh sweep. Copy, download or save anything you want to keep. The Export tab has two buttons at the top and two cards. Control What it does Copy CSS top Copies the CSS shown in the CSS tokens card. Download JSON Downloads the full snapshot as auric personalization generator.json . Copy CSS tokens card The same as Copy CSS . Copy JSON JSON snapshot card Copies the full snapshot as text. The JSON snapshot card previews only the start of a long snapshot and marks it truncated, full file in download . The copy and the download are always complete. A :root block with: aa personal 1 , aa personal 2 and so on: the leader's colours, in order if there are no results yet, the first six pool colours ; aa personal gradient : the first gradient; aa font display , aa font body and aa font mono : the first typography card's three font stacks; followed by the design tokens for the light, dark and high contrast themes, as described in Design tokens design tokens.md . preferences : your pool, styles, use case, brief, and the search settings palette size, depth, keep, the three weights and the three filters ; results : every palette with its rel"},{"t":"Presets","d":"The seventeen starting points in the Personalization Generator and what loading one changes.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/presets.html","h":["Load a preset","The presets","Related"],"x":" The Presets tab holds seventeen starting points. Each has a name, five colours, two style chips and a use case. 1. Open Presets . 2. Select a preset card. A message confirms it, for example Creator SaaS loaded . 3. Select Generate . Loading a preset: replaces your pool with the preset's five colours, then builds the pool up to your Pool target with variations of them; replaces your style chips with the preset's two; sets Use case to the preset's use case. It does not change your brief, the engine settings, the weights or the filters, and it does not start a sweep. Loading a preset discards your current pool. If you want to keep your own colours, note them first, or add them back with Add afterwards. Preset Styles Use case Creator SaaS Tech, Minimal Ui Premium Studio Luxe, Editorial Brand Festival Poster Neon, Playful Poster Earth Brand Earthy, Heritage Brand Calm Editorial Calm, Editorial Editorial Data Console Tech, Calm Dashboard Pastel Atlas Pastel, Calm Brand Cyber Console Cyber, Tech Ui Vintage Press Heritage, Editorial Editorial Monochrome Lab Monochrome, Minimal Ui Botanical Brand Botanical, Earthy Brand Nordic Calm Nordic, Minimal Ui Sunset Studio Sunset, Playful Poster Mi"},{"t":"Palettes, gradients, typography, UI pairs and posters","d":"What each result tab of the Personalization Generator shows, how the cards are scored, and what every card button copies or saves.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/result-tabs.html","h":["Palettes","Gradients","Typography","UI Pairs","Posters","Related"],"x":" Five tabs hold the results of the last sweep. Palettes come straight from the sweep; the other four are built from the kept palettes, in rank order. Tab Built from Most cards Palettes the sweep up to 96 Gradients the top 28 palettes 28 Typography the top 24 palettes 24 UI Pairs the top 28 palettes 28 Posters the top 28 palettes 28 Every card has Save , which saves it to your Library, and Add to pool , which puts its colours at the front of your pool. See Export, save and share export and save.md . The heading summarises the set, for example 24 kept · best 81 Balanced Analogous · avg 74 · most common Analogous , with Top , Average , Kept and Sweeps figures. Each card shows: the palette name, such as Balanced Analogous : a mood word Vivid , Deep , Soft or Balanced , from the average saturation and lightness and the colour relationship; a line such as Analogous · from Soft Product . The first part is the colour relationship the palette was built on 19 relationships, from Analogous to Brand trio ; see the Reference reference.md . The second is the built in reference palette it drew on; the score, from 0 to 100 highlighted from 60 and again from 80 ; the swatches with their HEX values."},{"t":"Run a sweep and read the results","d":"Start, stop and repeat sweeps, follow their progress, and read The run panel and the Overview tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/run-a-sweep.html","h":["Start a sweep","Stop a sweep","Endless mode","When it finishes","The run panel","The Overview tab","Filter the results","Related"],"x":" A sweep samples a set number of candidate palettes the Search depth , scores every one, and keeps the best Keep top . From the kept palettes the generator then builds the gradients, typography, UI pairs, posters, tokens and Studio. Do any one of these: select Generate under the brief; press Enter in the brief box; select Run sweep in Tune . While it runs, Generate reads Generating… , the status line reads, for example, Generating 320 … , and the progress bar appears at the top of The run with a label such as Sweep 3 — 320 candidates , then Sampling… 45% and a line like 144/320 · 139 kept · ETA 0.4s . The count of kept candidates there is everything that has survived so far, before the final cut. The sweep works in small batches and lets the page redraw between them, so you can scroll, switch tabs and read results while it runs. A new sweep replaces the previous results. To add to them instead, use Endless . Select Stop under the brief, or Cancel beside the progress bar. The sweep stops at the end of the current batch and keeps the best of what it had already found. The status reads, for example, Cancelled after 192/320 140ms . Select Endless to keep sweeping. The button reads Endl"},{"t":"Tune the sweep","d":"Style chips, use case, the brief, engine settings, scoring weights and filters, and what each one changes in the Personalization Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/tune-the-sweep.html","h":["Style chips","Use case","The brief and the preference note","Engine settings","Scoring weights","Filters","Simple and Advanced","Current configuration","Related"],"x":" Open the Tune tab to shape the next sweep. It has four cards Style chips , Intent & note , Engine and Scoring weights and a Current configuration summary. Changes apply to the next sweep; they do not change results you already have. Eighteen chips: Calm , Luxe , Playful , Tech , Earthy , Editorial , Neon , Minimal , Heritage , Pastel , Cyber , Sun , Monochrome , Botanical , Nordic , Sunset , Midnight and Coastal . Calm and Editorial are on at first. Select a chip to turn it on or off. You can combine several; at least one is always on, and turning the last one off switches Calm back on. Each style describes a range of saturation, lightness and chroma, a warmth and a contrast level. With several chips on, the generator averages them. Styles affect the sweep in three ways: new colours are drawn towards the style's ranges; each palette gets a style score for how well its colours fall inside those ranges; built in reference palettes that share your styles are drawn on more often. Use case has five options: Ui the default , Brand , Poster , Editorial and Dashboard . It favours the colour relationships and reference palettes suited to that use, and, together with your styles, chooses th"},{"t":"Personalization Generator reference","d":"Every control, setting, range, default and list in the Personalization Generator in one place.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/reference.html","h":["Address","The brief column","Tabs","Pool","Tune settings","Style chips","Colour relationships","Palette names","Score parts","Gradient styles","Type systems","Poster layouts","Studio","Tokens","Result limits","Messages","Related"],"x":" https://auricartisan.com/tool/personalization gen/ https://auricartisan.com/personalization opens the same page. Control Type Notes Brief box text Same setting as Preference note in Tune. Enter starts a sweep. Generate button Starts a sweep. Reads Generating… while one runs. Stop button Stops the running sweep and keeps what it found. Also ends Endless . Endless toggle Keeps sweeping and merging results until stopped. Reads Endless ✓ when on. Simple , Advanced switch Advanced shows the search settings below. Default Simple . Depth number, 40 to 4,000 Advanced only. Same as Search depth . Pool number, 5 to 240 Advanced only. Same as Pool target . Size number, 5 to 12 Advanced only. Same as Palette size . Keep number, 6 to 120 Advanced only. Values above 96 act as 96. CVD safe , Contrast , Unique check boxes Advanced only. All on by default. This run summary Depth, pool target, palette size, top kept and the filters. Tab Purpose Overview Summary tiles, the leader with its score breakdown, sweep diagnostics, recent palettes. Pool Add, remove, build, randomise and nudge pool colours; pool statistics; quick seeds. Tune Style chips, use case, preference note, engine settings, weights, f"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Personalization Generator, from lost results to unreadable palettes.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["My results disappeared after a reload","The brief box is empty after a reload, but the results still follow my old brief","Changing the brief does not change much","Every palette looks like my pool","The palettes have no readable text pair","Generate does nothing","A big sweep is slow","Endless mode shows the same kind of palette over and over","The Studio shows colours that are not in the palette","The check boxes in the left column disagree with Tune","This run shows old numbers","The fonts in Typography or the Studio look wrong","Save says Already saved","Save says Save failed","Loading a preset lost my colours","Related"],"x":" Results are kept only while the page is open. On every visit a quick new sweep runs, using your saved pool and settings. Before you leave, copy what you need, select Download JSON in Export , or Save the results you want to your Library. See Export, save and share export and save.md . The brief is remembered, but the box in the left column starts empty. The remembered text is still used, and it shows in Tune under Preference note . Edit or clear it there, or type a new brief. The brief is matched word by word against the names of built in reference palettes; it is not read as a sentence. Words that appear in no name have no effect. Use a few distinctive words, and steer with the pool, style chips and Use case for bigger changes. See Tune the sweep tune the sweep.md . Preference, closeness to your pool, carries the largest share of the score. Select Jitter once or twice in Pool . Raise Diversity in Tune . Remove near duplicates from the pool. Use +24 random or Build to widen the pool. Make sure Contrast UI contrast bonus 4.5:1 is on. Raise Accessibility in Tune . Add a very dark and a very light colour, or select + Grayscale in Quick seeds . Contrast is a weight, not a filter, so a"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Personalization Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need an account?","Is the brief read by an AI?","Where do the generated colours come from?","Will I get the same results if I run the same settings again?","Are my results saved?","Can I load a JSON snapshot back in?","What does the score mean?","Is a high-scoring palette guaranteed to pass WCAG?","Are the design tokens ready to use in code?","Can I use my own fonts in the Typography tab or the Studio?","Can I export the posters or mockups as images?","Can I automate the generator?","Does it work on a phone?","Related"],"x":" No. The generator runs in your browser without signing in. Saving to your Library uses your Auric Artisan Library. No. The brief is split into words, and each word is compared with the names of built in reference palettes. A match makes that reference palette more likely to be drawn on. Your pool, style chips and use case steer the sweep far more. See Tune the sweep tune the sweep.md . From your pool, from built in reference palettes that match your styles, use case and brief, and from small variations of both, arranged on a colour relationship such as Analogous or Triadic. Every candidate is then scored and only the best are kept. Usually not. Each sweep starts from a different random seed, so results vary from run to run. Save or download the results you like. Your pool and settings are remembered in your browser. The results are not: each visit starts with a fresh quick sweep. See Export, save and share export and save.md . No. The JSON is a record of your settings and results for your own use. To carry a palette back in, save it to your Library and open it in the generator, or add its HEX values to the pool. It is how well a palette fits your settings: closeness to your pool, "},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"The glossary, limits, related tools and privacy notes for the Personalization Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/others/README.html","h":["Related"],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used by the generator. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the scores, checks and previews can and cannot tell you. related.md related.md Tools, services and reading that go with the generator. privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what is saved. The only keyboard shortcut specific to the generator is Enter in the brief box, which starts a sweep. Personalization Generator overview ../README.md Documentation contents ../docs/README.md "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Terms used in the Personalization Generator and its documentation.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/others/glossary.html","h":["Related"],"x":" Term Meaning Accent The most colourful colour in a palette once the background and text are chosen. Accent 2 is the next most colourful. APCA Lc A contrast value from the Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm. Higher means easier to read. The generator shows its size without the sign. Brief The text box at the top of the left column; the same setting as Preference note in Tune. Its words are matched against reference palette names. Candidate One palette generated during a sweep, before it is scored. CIEDE2000 A formula for the perceived difference between two colours. CVD Colour vision deficiency. The generator simulates protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. Endless A mode that runs sweep after sweep and merges the results until stopped. Leader The highest scoring palette of the last sweep. It feeds the Tokens tab and opens first in the Studio. OKLCH A colour model of lightness, chroma and hue in which equal steps look roughly equal. Pool Your own set of colours, up to 240. Palettes are scored on how close they stay to it. Pool target The size Build fills the pool to. Preset A starting point of five colours, two style chips and a use case. Reference palette One of about 80 b"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Personalization Generator's scores, contrast checks, colour-vision checks and previews can and cannot tell you.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The score is a ranking, not a verdict","The brief is keyword matching","Contrast and colour-vision are weights, not guarantees","WCAG and APCA","Tokens are generated, not designed","Fonts are not downloaded","Results are not reproducible","Size and speed limits","Mockups and posters are illustrations","Related"],"x":" A palette's score says how well it fits your settings: your pool, style chips, use case and weights. It is useful for sorting one sweep's candidates. It does not measure whether a palette is good in general, and scores from sweeps with different settings are not comparable. The brief is not understood as language. Its words are compared with the names of about 80 built in reference palettes, and even short words such as a can match part of a name. The pool, style chips and use case have a much larger effect. A palette with weak contrast or poor colour vision separation is ranked lower, not removed. It can still be kept. The three contrast bars on a palette card all show the single best pair in the palette. A palette can have one strong pair and many weak ones. The colour vision check simulates protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. It does not model partial forms such as deuteranomaly or achromatopsia, and simulations only approximate what any one person sees. With CVD safe off, every palette gets the same fixed colour vision score. Always check your final text and background pairs in context, with the WCAG and APCA figures in UI Pairs and Tokens , and with tools built for acces"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Personalization Generator keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/others/privacy.html","h":["Stays in your browser","Remembered in your browser","Uses the network","Related"],"x":" Every sweep, score, token system and mockup is computed in the page. Your colours and your brief are not sent anywhere to generate results. The JSON download is created in your browser. In your browser's local storage on this device: your pool, style chips, use case, brief, engine settings, weights and filters, the open tab, Simple or Advanced mode, and the Studio's palette choice, theme, density, Test and Inspect settings and overrides. Results are not stored. Clearing your browser's site data resets the generator to its starting pool and defaults. Like other pages on the site, the page may also keep the values of some on page controls in the page address after p= , so a reload or a shared link restores them. See Shareable links ../../../../site features/shareable links/README.md . Loading the page and its scripts. Save and Save brand system store items in your Auric Artisan Library. See the Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . The Public API, if you choose to use it, runs on Auric Artisan's servers. See the Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md . Site wide analytics and advertising follow your cookie choices. See the Help centre ../../../../../h"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Tools, services and Learn articles that go with the Personalization Generator.","p":"Website › Tools › Colour workspace","u":"website/tools/colour-workspace/personalisation-generator/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Library","Services","Learn articles","Related"],"x":" Design System Generator ../../design engine/README.md : build a full design system from a brief, with more control over ramps and token export. Basic Color Tools ../../basic colour tools/README.md : palettes, gradients, a colour picker and the Colour Tools workbench. Color Science Lab ../../colour science lab/README.md : look closely at any colour the generator produces. Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md : test a final text and background pair. Vision Lab ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md : see a palette through colour vision and other vision conditions. Colour libraries ../../../../library/colour libraries/README.md : browse palettes, gradients and shades, save them, and open them here to seed your pool. Library Kit ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md : find and manage the items you saved from the generator. Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md : the same generation as a REST call. Color Theory and Harmony https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony Building a Color System https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 16 building a color "},{"t":"Colorimetry and rendering tools","d":"What the colorimetry, gamut and rendering tools on auricartisan.com are for, where to find them, and which one to open for your question.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/README.html","h":["Where to find them","The tools","Which tool do I need?","Concepts in one page","In this folder"],"x":" This area documents seven colour science tools on auricartisan.com. They answer questions that sit underneath everyday colour work: what \"white\" means under a given light, how a colour changes when the light changes, which colours a screen or file format can hold, what happens to a colour that does not fit, and how a high dynamic range signal becomes light on a display. The tools are split into two groups on the site: Colorimetry — measuring and converting colour with the standard CIE methods: light sources illuminants , white points, chromatic adaptation and gamut mapping. Gamut and rendering — the limits of colour spaces and displays, HDR transfer curves, tone mapping, and ramps of tints and shades. Every tool runs entirely in your browser. Each one has a Data tab that lists the published tables and formulas it uses, with a status for each verbatim, computed, stand in or absent , so you can see which figures are standard values and which are illustrations. None of them is a certified measurement instrument. The tools are listed in the Colorimetry and Gamut & Rendering categories of the site's tool collection at https://auricartisan.com/collections/. The three hub addresses below"},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation","d":"What the Chromatic Adaptation lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to adapt your first image.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" When you walk from daylight into a room lit by a tungsten lamp, white paper looks orange for a moment and then white again. Your eyes have rebalanced to the new light. This is chromatic adaptation , and colour science models it with chromatic adaptation transforms CATs that convert a colour seen under one white point into the colour that would look the same under another. The Chromatic Adaptation lab applies eight published transforms Bradford, Von Kries, CAT02, CAT16, Sharp, CMCCAT2000, HPE and plain XYZ scaling to a photograph of your own or to a built in test sweep, between any two of 12 standard illuminants. It also models the time the eye takes to adapt, using the two phase time course measured by Fairchild and Reniff 1995 : about half the adaptation happens within a second and the rest over tens of seconds. You can scrub or animate that timeline, and set how complete the adaptation becomes. Supporting views show the matrices behind each transform with copy ready code , compare all eight on your illuminant pair, list every dataset the lab uses and its status, and export the result as an image, JSON or a shareable link. Everything runs on your device; images are never uploaded"},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Chromatic Adaptation lab: a screen tour, task guides for images, the time course, matrices and colour lists, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the lab, the six tabs and your first adapted image adapt an image.md adapt an image.md Adapting a photo between two illuminants and exporting it explore the time course.md explore the time course.md The Dynamics tab and how adaptation unfolds over time compare transforms and copy matrices.md compare transforms and copy matrices.md The Matrix tab, the eight transform comparison and copying code adapt a colour list.md adapt a colour list.md Batch Colour Analysis for HEX lists reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with Chromatic Adaptation","d":"Open the Chromatic Adaptation lab, learn its tabs and controls, and adapt your first image.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Adapt your first image","Why the image is not fully adapted after five seconds","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/chromatic adaptation dynamic/. The page heading is Chromatic Adaptation . You do not need an account. Images you load are processed in your browser and are never uploaded. A white point is the colour of the light a scene is viewed under, such as D65 average daylight or A tungsten . A chromatic adaptation transform CAT predicts what a colour seen under the source white point would have to become to look the same under the destination white point. It works by converting XYZ into a cone like space L, M, S , scaling each channel by the ratio of the two whites, and converting back. The transforms differ in the cone like matrix they use. The degree of adaptation D says how complete the adaptation is: 0 means none, 1 means the source white maps exactly onto the destination white. Adaptation takes time . In this lab, the adaptation at a moment t is the starting state moved towards D along a measured two phase curve fast phase with a 1 s time constant carrying half the change, slow phase with a 30 s half life carrying the rest . A note at the top says every figure names its source: which table a white point came from, which paper a ma"},{"t":"Adapt a list of colours","d":"Paste up to 50 HEX colours and get their adapted values, colour shift and L*C*h° at the current adaptation state.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/adapt-a-colour-list.html","h":["Steps","Tips","Result"],"x":" Batch Colour Analysis on the Export tab applies the current adaptation to a list of colours — useful for checking how a brand palette shifts between D65 and D50, or under tungsten light. 1. On the Lab tab, set the source and destination illuminants, the CAT method, the degree of adaptation D and the time. The batch uses the adaptation applied at the current moment of the timeline, exactly as the image does. 2. Open the Export tab and find Batch Colour Analysis . 3. Paste HEX colours into the box, one per line. Each must have six digits; the is optional. Up to 50 lines are used; any more are ignored. 4. Select Run Batch . A message confirms how many colours were analysed. 5. Read the table: Column Meaning Color Your input colour and its swatch Adapted The adapted colour as an sRGB HEX, clipped to the displayable range ΔE₀₀ The CIEDE2000 difference between the colour's CIELAB value under the source white and the adapted colour's CIELAB value under the destination white. Green below 1, amber below 3, red from 3 up L\\ Lightness of the adapted colour C\\ Chroma of the adapted colour h° Hue angle of the adapted colour L , C and h° are computed against the destination white point. Lines t"},{"t":"Adapt an image to a new light","d":"Load a photo, adapt it between two illuminants with a chosen transform and degree of adaptation, and export the frame.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/adapt-an-image.html","h":["Steps","What each result shows","Choosing D and time","Tips","Result"],"x":" Use this to see how the colours of a picture shift when it is re expressed for a different light: for example a D65 photo prepared for a D50 print booth, or a daylight scene shown as it would appear once the eye has adapted to tungsten. 1. Open the Lab tab. 2. Under Image Source , select Choose image and pick a PNG, JPEG or other image file your browser can open. The file name appears beside the button. Large images are scaled down to fit 480 × 320 pixels for processing; small images are not enlarged. The status chip shows the size used, for example \"Image loaded 480×320 \". 3. Under Illuminants , set Source illuminant to the light the picture was taken or balanced for. Most camera and web images are D65. 4. Set Destination illuminant to the light you want to adapt to. Use Swap to exchange the two. 5. Choose a CAT Method . Bradford is the common choice in colour management; CAT16 is the most recent model. 6. Set Degree of adaptation D . 1.00 means complete adaptation; lower values leave part of the source cast in place, as happens when the eye does not fully adapt. 7. Set the moment in time with Time scrubber 0 to 5 s , or select Animate to play it. 8. If bright colours clip harshl"},{"t":"Compare transforms and copy a matrix","d":"Read the adaptation matrix, check its round trip, copy it as code, and compare all eight transforms on your illuminant pair.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/compare-transforms-and-copy-matrices.html","h":["The maths in one line","The eight transforms","Read and copy the matrix","Compare all eight on your pair","The Compare All Methods panel","Result"],"x":" Every transform in the lab has the same shape: text X′ = M⁻¹ · diag d · M · X d = 1 + D × ρ destination ÷ ρ source − 1 for each of L, M, S M converts XYZ into a cone like space. diag d scales each cone channel by the ratio of the destination white to the source white, softened by the degree of adaptation D. M⁻¹ converts back. The transforms differ only in M. Transform Source of the matrix Notes Bradford Lam 1985 The usual choice in ICC colour management; the reference the comparison is measured against Von Kries Hunt–Pointer–Estévez Estévez 1979 , normalised to D65 Reads the same as HPE, because normalising rows cancels out in the formula CAT02 CIE 159:2004 CIECAM02 — CAT16 Li et al. 2017 CAM16 — Sharp Finlayson and Süsstrunk 2000 A spectrally sharpened matrix CMCCAT2000 Li, Luo, Rigg and Hunt 2002 — HPE Hunt–Pointer–Estévez — XYZ scaling Identity matrix The null case: scales X, Y and Z directly 1. Choose the illuminants and transform on the Lab tab, and set Degree of adaptation D . 2. Open the Matrix tab. The title names the transform, the pair and the D, for example \"Bradford, D65 → D50 at D = 1.00\". 3. Read the three blocks: M — XYZ to cone like : the transform's own matrix; di"},{"t":"Explore the adaptation time course","d":"Use the Dynamics tab to see how quickly the eye adapts to a new light, with the two-phase model and its single-exponential predecessor side by side.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/explore-the-time-course.html","h":["The model","Steps","Reading the chart","How this relates to the Lab tab","Result"],"x":" Adaptation is not instant. Fairchild and Reniff 1995 measured it for colour appearance judgements and found two components: a fast phase , completing about half the adaptation within roughly a second, and a slow phase with a half life near 30 seconds. The Dynamics tab plots that model over two minutes. The fraction of adaptation completed t seconds after the light changes is: text fraction t = w1 × 1 − e^ −t / τ1 + 1 − w1 × 1 − e^ −t / τ2 τ2 = t½ ÷ ln 2 τ1 is the fast time constant default 1.0 s . w1 is the share of adaptation in the fast phase default 0.50 . t½ is the half life of the slow phase default 30 s, which is τ2 ≈ 43 s . The defaults come from the paper. For comparison the chart also draws the single exponential the page used before time constant 0.6 s after a 0.4 s delay , which reaches 90% within two seconds. 1. Choose your illuminants and transform on the Lab tab. The Dynamics heading shows the pair, for example \"D65 → A\". 2. Open the Dynamics tab. 3. Under Model , keep Two components selected. Single exponential hides the fast and slow controls and reads the playhead value from the older curve; the half adapted and 90% figures still describe the two component model. "},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/reference.html","h":["Lab tab","Dynamics tab","Matrix tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/chromatic adaptation dynamic/ Control What it does Values Default Choose image Opens a file picker for an image Any image type the browser can decode — File name Shows the chosen file — \"No file chosen\" Sample Generates a synthetic HSL sweep a test target, not a photograph 360 × 240 pixels — Generate the sample sweep , Choose an image The same two actions, offered in the empty state before any image is loaded — — Loaded images are scaled to fit within 480 × 320 pixels never enlarged . Control What it does Values Default Source illuminant The original viewing white point 12 illuminants, below CIE D65 6504 K — sRGB daylight Swap Exchanges source and destination Button — Destination illuminant The target white point 12 illuminants CIE D50 5003 K — ICC PCS / printing CAT Method The chromatic adaptation transform Bradford Lam 1985 ; Von Kries Hunt–Pointer–Estévez ; CAT02 CIE 159:2004 ; CAT16 Li et al. 2017 ; Sharp Finlayson & Süsstrunk 2000 ; CMCCAT2000 Li et al. 2002 ; HPE Hunt–Pointer–Estévez ; XYZ scaling null case Bradford The 12 illuminants and their white points CIE xy : Choice x y Spectrum drawn? CIE D65 6504 K — sRGB da"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Chromatic Adaptation","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The image area is dark and says \"No image yet\" No image has been loaded Select Generate the sample sweep or Choose an image Nothing changes when I move a slider Live is off, or no image is loaded Tick Live , or select Run after changes The image hardly changes at 0 s Adaptation starts at 0.1 and grows with time Move Time scrubber towards 5 s The image is only partly adapted even at 5 s and D = 1 The measured slow phase has a 30 s half life, so at 5 s about 55% of the change has happened Expected. The Matrix tab shows the matrix at the D you set; the Dynamics tab shows when 90% is reached Display Gamma, the per pixel scales, Local radius, Local strength, Mix, Tile factor or Target FPS change nothing These controls are not applied in the current version; they are only recorded in the JSON export See Reference reference.md controls with no visible effect in the current version The GPU box or G changes nothing Processing always runs on the CPU Expected The state map is a flat grey The per pixel model has no effect in the current version, so every pixel has the same adaptation Expected. Its brightness equals the adaptation in use The SPD overlay says \""},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/docs/faq.html","h":["Which transform should I use?","Why do Von Kries and HPE give the same result?","What is XYZ scaling for?","What does \"degree of adaptation\" mean?","How long does adaptation really take?","Why does the time-course prose in Reference quote different time constants?","Is my image uploaded?","Can I adapt a video?","Can I get the full adaptation matrix as numbers?","Does the lab model colour appearance (CIECAM02 or CAM16)?"],"x":" For ICC colour management and D65 ↔ D50 conversions, Bradford is the common convention. CAT16 is the transform of the most recent CIE lineage appearance model CAM16 . The lab does not rank them for accuracy, because that needs corresponding colour data sets it does not hold; it shows what each one does on your pair. The lab's Von Kries matrix is the Hunt–Pointer–Estévez matrix normalised to D65. Normalising scales each row, and that scaling cancels out in M⁻¹ · diag d · M, so the two produce identical adaptations. It is the simplest possible adaptation, scaling X, Y and Z directly. It is not a model of the eye and is kept as a baseline to compare the others against. How complete the adaptation is. At D = 1 the source white maps exactly onto the destination white. Real viewers often adapt incompletely, especially in dim or complex scenes, so values below 1 are realistic in some situations. The lab uses Fairchild and Reniff's 1995 measurements: about half the adaptation within a second or so, and the rest with a half life of about 30 seconds. With the default settings, 90% adaptation takes about 70 seconds. The Dynamics tab computes the exact times. Some background text in the Refer"},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md : the terms used, the keyboard shortcuts, how far the results can be trusted, related tools, what has changed and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the lab shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the results are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" These keys work when the focus is not in a text box, slider or list. Click an empty part of the page first if a key does nothing. Key What it does Space Plays or pauses the 0–5 s animation R Resets the time to 0 s C Runs Compare All Methods results on the Export tab G Toggles the GPU checkbox which has no effect on processing Esc Clears the Reference filter; closes a full screen chart Mouse What it does Double click a chart or image Opens it full screen "},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Adaptation time course — how the degree of adaptation grows after the light changes. The lab uses a fast and a slow exponential phase. Bradford transform — a CAT whose cone like matrix comes from Lam 1985 . The usual choice in ICC colour management. CAT02 — the CAT inside the CIECAM02 colour appearance model CIE 159:2004 . CAT16 — the CAT inside the CAM16 colour appearance model Li et al., 2017 . Chromatic adaptation — the visual system's adjustment to the colour of the light, keeping surface colours roughly stable. Chromatic adaptation transform CAT — a formula that converts a colour under one white point into the corresponding colour under another: X′ = M⁻¹ · diag d · M · X. CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ — the CIE colour difference formula CIE 142:2001 . Around 1 is a just noticeable difference for many viewers. CIELAB L\\ a\\ b\\ and L\\ C\\ h° — a colour space with lightness L , and either a , b or chroma C and hue angle h°. Values depend on the reference white. CMCCAT2000 — a CAT published by Li, Luo, Rigg and Hunt 2002 . Condition number, cond M — how much a matrix can stretch a small difference. The lab shows it as a description, not a quality score. Cone like space LMS — the space a CAT matri"},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation limits and accuracy","d":"What the Chromatic Adaptation lab computes exactly, what it approximates, and what it does not do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is exact","What is modelled or simplified","What is not done","Precision"],"x":" The lab is an educational and research simulator that runs in your browser. It is not a substitute for measured device profiles, calibrated displays, spectrophotometer data or a validated ICC workflow. White points of all 12 illuminants are tabulated CIE xy values, held verbatim. Adaptation needs only these, so it is correct even where a spectrum is not held. Transform matrices are the published values; each inverse is recomputed, and the Matrix tab shows the round trip error. sRGB conversion uses the IEC 61966 2 1 primaries and transfer function. Adaptation happens in linear light; the transfer function is applied only at the ends. ΔE₀₀ is the CIEDE2000 formula CIE 142:2001 . Time course. The two phase model uses constants from Fairchild and Reniff 1995 . It describes average behaviour in their experiments, not any particular viewer or scene. Degree of adaptation is yours to set. CIECAM02 would compute it from the adapting luminance and the surround; the lab does not. Clipping. Adapted colours outside sRGB are clipped per channel or compressed first with HDR Tonemap . This is not perceptual gamut mapping. For that, see Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md . Spectra. The daylig"},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation privacy","d":"What the Chromatic Adaptation lab does with your images and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your image never leaves your device. When you choose an image, the browser reads it locally, draws it onto the page and adapts it there. Nothing is uploaded. Exports are created locally. The PNG frame and JSON file are generated in the browser and saved through your normal download. Share links carry settings only — illuminants, transform, D, initial adaptation and time. They never include your image. Clipboard. Copy Link, Generate, Copy and the Copy as buttons write to your clipboard only when you use them; your browser may ask for permission. Batch colours you paste stay in the page and are gone when you close it. Save to Library stores a preset of your settings in your Auric Artisan Library; it does not store the image. The page loads the site's shared features in the same way as every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"Chromatic Adaptation release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — the workbench rebuild","May 2026"],"x":" The tabs are now Lab , Dynamics , Matrix , Data , Export and Reference . Standards, Formulas, References and Research became one Reference view with a search filter. The adaptation timeline now follows the two phase time course measured by Fairchild and Reniff 1995 . The former single exponential 0.6 s with a 0.4 s delay is drawn on the new Dynamics tab for comparison. The delay and τ sliders were removed from the Lab. The Lab gained a Degree of adaptation D control, and every figure states the D it used. Illuminant spectra now come from the same checked tables as the Illuminants lab. Where a spectrum is not held B, C, F2, F7, F11 , the plot says so instead of drawing a daylight curve under that name. The new Matrix tab shows M, diag d and the full matrix, with a round trip check, copy as code buttons and a comparison of all eight transforms against Bradford. The new Data tab lists the 11 datasets and their status. Three citations were corrected Sharp, CAM16 and CMCCAT2000 ; corrected entries are marked in the Reference view. The Chromatic Adaptation Dynamic User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to Chromatic Adaptation","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the Chromatic Adaptation lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/chromatic-adaptation/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Illuminants ../../illuminants/README.md Spectra, white points and CCT of the illuminants, plus a 24 patch adaptation preview with six transforms Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md Includes an \"adapt white, then clip\" mapping between spaces with different white points Gamut Lab ../../gamut lab/README.md White points and primaries of 13 RGB spaces Colour Science Lab ../../../colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md Adaptation and appearance models in a wider laboratory White Points and Chromatic Adaptation: von Kries, Bradford, and CAT02 — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 11 white points chromatic adaptation transforms Color Constancy, Adaptation, and Why Colors Change with Context — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 color constancy adaptation Color Appearance Models — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 21 color appearance models ciecam ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 26 delta e metrics cie76 ciede2000 itp CIELAB and LCH Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cielab and lch explained The site's "},{"t":"Gamut Lab","d":"What the Gamut Lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to compare your first colour spaces.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Gamut Lab shows where an RGB colour space ends. Every RGB space is defined by three primaries the reddest red, greenest green and bluest blue it can make , a white point , and a transfer function that turns stored values into light. Plot the primaries on a chromaticity diagram and they form a triangle: the space's gamut . The lab draws those triangles for 13 standard spaces — from sRGB and Display P3 to Rec. 2020, the HDR Rec. 2100 encodings, Adobe RGB, ProPhoto RGB, the ACES spaces and legacy television standards — plus any space you define yourself. Beyond the diagram, it derives the RGB to XYZ matrices from the primaries, draws each space's transfer curve and tells you whether that curve is exactly the one its standard defines , slices gamuts at constant lightness in CIELAB, and measures gamut volume in CIELAB and overlap in u′v′ with quasi random sampling. You can keep your own spaces in a library in your browser, import and export them as JSON, and export the diagram as SVG or PNG. The Gamut Lab defines and measures spaces. It does not map colours from one space into another; that is the job of Gamut Mapping ../gamut map/README.md . Designers and developers choosing a wor"},{"t":"Gamut Lab documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Gamut Lab: a screen tour, task guides for comparing spaces, defining your own and reading transfer curves, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the lab, the six tabs and the chromaticity diagram compare colour spaces.md compare colour spaces.md Diagram, slices, volume, overlap and the Compare tab define a custom space.md define a custom space.md Entering primaries, solving matrices, importing, exporting and the library inspect transfer functions.md inspect transfer functions.md The Lab's transfer curve panel and the Transfer tab reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with the Gamut Lab","d":"Open the Gamut Lab, learn its tabs and panels, and read the chromaticity diagram.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Read the diagram","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/gamut/. The heading is Gamut Lab . All calculations run in your browser. The chromaticity diagram maps colour without brightness. Its curved edge, the spectral locus , is made of single wavelengths of light; the straight line closing it at the bottom joins deep violet and deep red the purples . Every colour a person can see lies inside. An RGB space's gamut on the diagram is the triangle between its three primaries. A larger triangle holds more saturated colours. The CIE 1931 xy diagram is the classic one, but equal distances on it are not equal visual differences it stretches greens . The CIE 1976 u′v′ diagram is more even, so the lab quotes shares of the locus in u′v′. A triangle shows chromaticity only. Gamut volume in CIELAB also accounts for lightness, which is why the lab measures it separately. Tab What it is for Lab The diagram, the working space's primaries and matrices, a transfer curve, volume and slice panels Transfer Every distinct transfer curve, plotted, with its fidelity to its standard Compare Every space measured the same way: volume, ratio to sRGB and share of the locus Data The eight datasets the l"},{"t":"Compare colour spaces","d":"Compare RGB spaces by triangle, slice, CIELAB volume, u′v′ overlap and share of the spectral locus.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/compare-colour-spaces.html","h":["Compare two spaces in the Lab","Slice at constant lightness","Measure every space at once","Why \"> 100%\" appears","Why the figures differ from published percentages","Result"],"x":" The Gamut Lab gives four ways to compare spaces. Each answers a different question. Measure Question it answers Where Triangle area and share of the locus How much of the range of visible chromaticities does the space cover? Lab panel, Compare tab Constant lightness slice At a given lightness, which hues can each space make vivid? Lab › Gamut slice CIELAB volume How many distinguishable colours, including lightness, does the space hold? Lab › Volume comparison, Compare tab Overlap in u′v′ How much of one space's triangle lies inside another's? Lab › Volume comparison 1. On the Lab tab, find Volume comparison . 2. In the first list, choose the reference: sRGB default , Display P3 , Rec. 2020 or ACEScg . 3. In the second list, choose Active space the working space selected at the top or one of the same four spaces. 4. Select Compute volume . The panel shows \"Computing…\" and then: each space's CIELAB volume in Lab³, with a ± spread against a run at half the samples and the half width of the sampling box; Overlap in u′v′ — the share of space A inside B \"of A\" and of B inside A \"of B\" ; Jaccard — the area both share divided by the area either covers. These figures use 10,000 quasi rand"},{"t":"Define a custom colour space","d":"Enter your own primaries and white point, derive the RGB ↔ XYZ matrices, and keep, import or export the space.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/define-a-custom-space.html","h":["How the matrices are derived","Enter and solve","Keep it in the library","Export a space","Result"],"x":" Use this to check a display's measured primaries, a camera's native gamut, or a proposed working space. Given the xy chromaticities of the red, green and blue primaries and of the white point, the lab: 1. turns each primary into XYZ with Y = 1; 2. builds a matrix with those three columns; 3. solves for the scale of each column that makes RGB 1, 1, 1 equal the white point; 4. applies the scales to get the RGB → XYZ matrix; 5. inverts it to get the XYZ → RGB matrix. This is the standard construction as described by Bruce Lindbloom , so a custom space gets exactly the same treatment as a published one. 1. On the Lab tab, set Working color space to Custom . 2. Under Primaries xy , type the R , G and B x and y values, and the W white point x and y. The fields accept four decimal places. 3. Select Solve from primaries . 4. Read RGB ↔ XYZ matrices : the RGB → XYZ and XYZ → RGB matrices, then the triangle's Area xy and Area % sRGB . 5. White point XYZ shows the white as X, Y, Z with Y = 1, for reference. 6. Your triangle is drawn on the diagram as Custom . A custom space made this way uses the sRGB transfer curve. It lasts until you reload the page. To keep it, export it with This space b"},{"t":"Inspect transfer functions","d":"Read each space's transfer curve, understand EOTF and OETF, and check which curves are exact to their standard.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/inspect-transfer-functions.html","h":["Key ideas","The ten distinct curves","The Transfer tab","The Lab tab's transfer panel","Result"],"x":" A transfer function links stored values to light. The OETF opto electronic encodes light into a signal; the EOTF electro optical turns a signal back into light on a display. Most spaces use a relative curve: signal 0 to 1 becomes light 0 to 1 of the display's peak. PQ SMPTE ST 2084 is absolute : a signal value means a specific luminance in cd/m² nits , up to 10,000. HLG hybrid log gamma is a relative HDR curve. Its full EOTF needs a display peak luminance and a surround; this lab draws the inverse OETF only, and marks it Partial . Curve Used by Fidelity IEC 61966 2 1 sRGB piecewise sRGB, Display P3, Custom Exact ITU R BT.2020 2 Rec. 2020 Exact corrected ROMM / ISO 22028 2, γ 1.8 plus toe ProPhoto RGB Exact corrected Adobe RGB 1998 , γ 563/256 Adobe RGB Exact corrected SMPTE ST 2084 PQ Rec. 2100 PQ Exact ARIB STD B67 — inverse OETF Rec. 2100 HLG Partial Linear ACES 2065 1 AP0 , ACEScg AP1 Exact Gamma 2.6 DCI P3 Exact Gamma 2.2 Adobe Wide Gamut, NTSC 1953 Exact Gamma 2.8 PAL/SECAM Exact \"Corrected\" marks a curve that an earlier version of the page did not run as its standard defines. 1. Open the Transfer tab. The note gives the number of distinct curves across the spaces. 2. Under P"},{"t":"Gamut Lab reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/reference.html","h":["The 13 standard spaces","Lab tab","Transfer tab","Compare tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/gamut/ Space Red x, y Green x, y Blue x, y White x, y Transfer sRGB / BT.709 0.64, 0.33 0.30, 0.60 0.15, 0.06 0.3127, 0.329 sRGB Display P3 0.68, 0.32 0.265, 0.69 0.15, 0.06 0.3127, 0.329 sRGB DCI P3 0.68, 0.32 0.265, 0.69 0.15, 0.06 0.314, 0.351 Gamma 2.6 Rec. 2020 0.708, 0.292 0.17, 0.797 0.131, 0.046 0.3127, 0.329 BT.2020 Rec. 2100 PQ as Rec. 2020 as Rec. 2020 as Rec. 2020 0.3127, 0.329 PQ Rec. 2100 HLG as Rec. 2020 as Rec. 2020 as Rec. 2020 0.3127, 0.329 HLG inverse OETF Adobe RGB 0.64, 0.33 0.21, 0.71 0.15, 0.06 0.3127, 0.329 γ 563/256 ProPhoto RGB 0.7347, 0.2653 0.1596, 0.8404 0.0366, 0.0001 0.3457, 0.3585 ROMM Adobe Wide Gamut 0.7347, 0.2653 0.1152, 0.8264 0.1566, 0.0177 0.3457, 0.3585 Gamma 2.2 ACES 2065 1 AP0 0.7347, 0.2653 0.0, 1.0 0.0001, −0.077 0.32168, 0.33767 Linear ACEScg AP1 0.713, 0.293 0.165, 0.83 0.128, 0.044 0.32168, 0.33767 Linear NTSC 1953 0.67, 0.33 0.21, 0.71 0.14, 0.08 0.31, 0.316 Gamma 2.2 PAL/SECAM 0.64, 0.33 0.29, 0.60 0.15, 0.06 0.3127, 0.329 Gamma 2.8 Custom is a 14th option whose primaries you enter. Control What it does Values Default Working color space Chooses the space shown in th"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Gamut Lab","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do A space I picked earlier disappeared from the diagram The diagram draws up to five spaces; adding a sixth drops the oldest Tick Show all library spaces , or pick the space again Choosing Custom shows nothing The custom space does not exist until you solve it Enter primaries and white, then select Solve from primaries My custom space vanished after reloading A solved Custom space is not saved Export it This space , JSON and import it with Add to the library Import says \"Invalid JSON\" The pasted object has no name or no primaries Use the format in Define a custom colour space define a custom space.md Import says \"Parse error: …\" The text is not valid JSON Check quotes, commas and brackets Choosing the 10° observer changes nothing Only the CIE 1931 2° observer is used Expected The OKLab slice does not move with Level In the current version the OKLab slice is fixed at L = 0.5; only the label changes Use Constant L\\ CIELAB to move through lightness In the u′v′ diagram, the vertex readout colour and membership look wrong The readout treats the clicked coordinates as CIE 1931 x, y Switch Diagram mode to CIE 1931 xy before probing The vertex readout alway"},{"t":"Gamut Lab FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/docs/faq.html","h":["What is the difference between Display P3 and DCI-P3?","Why do Rec. 2020 and Rec. 2100 have the same triangle?","Why does the ACES AP0 blue primary sit outside the diagram?","Why is the u′v′ share quoted rather than xy?","Is a bigger triangle always a bigger gamut?","Why does the spectral locus stop at 715 nm?","Are the MacAdam ellipses real data?","Can the lab convert or map colours between spaces?","Where are my imported spaces stored?"],"x":" They share primaries. Display P3 uses the D65 white and the sRGB transfer curve; DCI P3 the cinema reference projector uses a greener white at x 0.314, y 0.351 and a pure 2.6 gamma. Rec. 2100 HDR television uses the Rec. 2020 primaries and white. It differs in the transfer curve: PQ or HLG instead of the BT.2020 curve. AP0 uses an imaginary blue primary so its triangle contains every visible colour. That makes it suitable for archiving, and it is why its share of the locus reads \" 100%\". Equal distances on the xy diagram are not equal visual differences; it exaggerates greens. u′v′ is more uniform, so areas there compare more fairly. Not exactly. The triangle ignores lightness. CIELAB volume counts how much colour a space holds at every lightness, which is why the lab measures it separately. The lab builds the locus from the published colour matching functions at four decimals. Beyond about 715 nm the values are too small to give a reliable chromaticity, so those points are left out rather than distorting the areas. No. The overlay is an illustrative approximation of MacAdam's 1942 figure, useful for showing that ellipses vary in size and orientation. It is not a basis for reading"},{"t":"Gamut Lab: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the lab shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the figures are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and where "},{"t":"Gamut Lab shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The Gamut Lab has no single key shortcuts of its own. Shortcut Where What it does Click or drag Chromaticity diagram Moves the probe and updates the vertex readout Double click A chart Opens it full screen Esc Full screen view Closes it Esc Reference › Filter Clears the filter "},{"t":"Gamut Lab glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" ACES AP0, AP1 — the Academy Color Encoding System. AP0 ACES 2065 1 is an archival space with imaginary primaries; AP1 ACEScg is a working space with primaries inside the locus. Both are linear. Chromaticity diagram — a map of colour without brightness. CIE 1931 xy is the classic form; CIE 1976 u′v′ is more uniform. CIELAB — a colour space with lightness L and axes a green–red and b blue–yellow , used here to measure gamut volume and slices. EOTF — electro optical transfer function: turns a signal into light on a display. Gamma — shorthand for a power law transfer curve, such as 2.2 or 2.6. Gamut — the colours a space can represent. On a chromaticity diagram, an RGB gamut is a triangle. Gamut volume — the size of a gamut in CIELAB, in Lab³ units cubed . Halton sampling — quasi random sampling that covers space evenly; its error shrinks faster than random sampling. HLG hybrid log gamma — a relative HDR transfer curve ARIB STD B67, ITU R BT.2100 . Imaginary primary — a primary outside the spectral locus: a mathematical colour no light can produce. Jaccard index — the overlap of two areas divided by their combined area. Line of purples — the straight edge of the chromaticity diagram b"},{"t":"Gamut Lab limits and accuracy","d":"How far the Gamut Lab's diagrams, curves, areas and volumes can be trusted.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Exact","Computed with stated limits","Stand-ins","Not done","Current-version caveats"],"x":" Primaries and white points of the 13 spaces are the published chromaticities. Matrices are derived from the primaries and white by the standard construction. Transfer curves run as their standards define them, except HLG see below . The BT.2020, ROMM and Adobe RGB curves were corrected in the current version and are marked so on the Transfer tab. Areas are computed by the shoelace formula in the named plane. Spectral locus — built from the CIE 1931 2° colour matching functions at 5 nm and four decimals, from 380 to 715 nm. Beyond 715 nm the published values are too small to give a reliable chromaticity. Share of the locus — divided by the lab's own locus area in the same plane. Published shares divided by other locus areas differ for Rec. 2020: 63.4% of the xy locus here against the often quoted 75.8% . Volume — Halton quasi random sampling in a box fitted to each space. The ± is the spread against a half size run, not a confidence interval. Overlap — sampled in u′v′ with point in triangle tests. HLG — the lab draws the inverse OETF only. The full HLG EOTF needs a display peak luminance and a surround the lab does not ask for. MacAdam ellipses — 24 hand rounded ellipses approximat"},{"t":"Gamut Lab privacy","d":"What the Gamut Lab stores, where, and what leaves your device.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" All calculations run in your browser. Diagrams, matrices, volumes and overlaps are computed on your device. Imported colour spaces are stored in this browser. They are kept in the site's local storage on your device, not on a server, and are removed with Del or by clearing site data. They do not follow you to another browser or device. Exports are created locally and saved through your browser's download, or copied to your clipboard when you choose. The link encodes your view settings drawn spaces, diagram mode, overlays and similar . Anyone with the link sees them. If you defined a custom space, its primaries may be part of the encoded settings. Save to Library stores a snapshot in your Auric Artisan Library. The page loads the site's shared features like every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"Gamut Lab release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version (2026 workbench rebuild)","May 2026"],"x":" Tabs are now Lab , Transfer , Compare , Data , Export and Reference . Three transfer curves now match their standards: Rec. 2020 runs the BT.2020 curve it previously ran the sRGB curve , ProPhoto runs ROMM with its linear toe, and Adobe RGB uses 563/256 rather than 2.2. HLG is labelled as the inverse OETF. The new Transfer tab plots every distinct curve, with PQ on its own absolute axis, and tags each as Exact, Partial or Corrected. Volume is measured with Halton sampling in a box fitted to each space, and quoted with a spread against a half size run. Overlap is measured in u′v′. Shares of the spectral locus are quoted in u′v′, with xy kept as a legacy option, and \" 100%\" is shown for spaces with imaginary primaries. The spectral locus is computed from the observer data and stops at 715 nm. The MacAdam ellipse overlay is labelled as a stand in. Export now previews the exact payload and names the file before you download it; the library, import and export sit together on the Export tab. Citations were checked and several corrected; corrected entries are marked in Reference. The Gamut Lab User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to the Gamut Lab","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the Gamut Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-lab/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md Map colours from one space into another HDR Gamut Plot ../../hdr gamut plot/README.md Rec.709, P3 and Rec.2020 with PQ, HLG, ICtCp and Jzazbz Illuminants ../../illuminants/README.md The white points behind each space, and the Planckian and daylight loci ICC Profile Parser ../../../image and file tools/icc profile parser/README.md Read the primaries and curves stored in an ICC profile LUT Lab ../../../image and file tools/lut lab/README.md Build lookup tables that move colour between spaces Chromaticity Diagrams Without the Intimidation — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 chromaticity diagrams Gamut Volume: How Much Color a Wide Gamut Actually Adds — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 26 gamut volume how much color HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HLG, and Modern Displays — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 hdr wide gamut pq hlg modern displays Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces CIE XYZ Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cie xyz exp"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping","d":"What the Gamut Mapping lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to map your first colour.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" A gamut is the set of colours a colour space or device can hold. When a colour moves from a wide space such as Display P3 or ProPhoto RGB into a narrower one such as sRGB , some colours will not fit. Gamut mapping decides what they become. The Gamut Mapping lab shows this as a horizontal slice through CIELAB at a lightness you choose: the source gamut on one side, the colours mapped into the target on the other, with each space's boundary outlined. It supports five RGB spaces sRGB, Display P3, Rec. 2020, Adobe RGB and ProPhoto RGB , each decoded with its own transfer curve and white point, and four mapping methods named for what they do: chroma compression, clipping in the target RGB, uniform RGB scaling, and adapting the white point before clipping. Around the slice you can probe any point, map a base colour or a list of colours, measure every space's volume in CIELAB with a stated standard error, compare the four methods on a fixed set of probe colours, and compare colour differences with three ΔE formulas. The lab is explicit that none of its methods is an ICC rendering intent: ICC perceptual and saturation intents are lookup tables built into profiles, not algorithms. Designer"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Gamut Mapping lab: a screen tour, task guides for mapping a colour, comparing spaces and methods and mapping a list, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the lab, the six tabs, and reading a slice map a colour.md map a colour.md Mapping one colour and choosing a method and strength compare spaces and methods.md compare spaces and methods.md The Boundary and Methods tabs, volumes and the ΔE playground map a colour list.md map a colour list.md Mapping up to 50 colours and exporting reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with Gamut Mapping","d":"Open the Gamut Mapping lab, learn its tabs, and read a CIELAB gamut slice.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Read your first slice","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/gamut map/. The heading is Gamut Mapping . Everything is computed in your browser. CIELAB describes a colour by lightness L\\ 0 black to 100 white and two opponent axes, a\\ green to red and b\\ blue to yellow . Chroma C\\ is the distance from the grey axis and hue h° the angle around it. A gamut slice is a cut through CIELAB at one L . Seen from above, each RGB space's gamut at that lightness is an irregular shape around the grey centre. Colours outside the shape cannot be represented in that space. A colour is out of gamut OOG for a space when converting it to that space's linear RGB gives a channel below 0 or above 1. Each space has its own transfer function the curve between stored values and light and white point . The lab decodes a HEX value with the source space's own curve, and draws the slice on the source space's white. Tab What it is for Lab Choose the colour, spaces, method and slice, and see the mapping Boundary Boundaries of up to five spaces at five lightness levels, and volumes in CIELAB Methods The four mapping methods explained, with figures on the base colour or 12 probe colours Data The nine datasets the lab u"},{"t":"Compare spaces and methods","d":"Use the Boundary and Methods tabs and the ΔE Playground to compare colour spaces, gamut volumes, mapping methods and colour differences.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/compare-spaces-and-methods.html","h":["Compare boundaries up the lightness axis","Measure gamut volumes","Compare the four methods","Compare two colours with the ΔE Playground","Result"],"x":" 1. Open the Boundary tab. 2. Under Spaces on the plot , select the spaces to draw. Each chip toggles one space; sRGB and Display P3 are on at first. 3. Read The boundary up the lightness axis : five tiles at L 20, 40, 65, 80 and 90. All tiles share one scale shown in the note, for example \"one scale, ±150\" , so sizes can be compared directly. The source space from the Lab tab is drawn with a thicker line. What to look for: at low and high lightness all gamuts shrink towards the grey axis; the biggest differences are in the middle; yellows keep chroma at high lightness and blues at low lightness. 1. On the Boundary tab, set Volume samples n from 5,000 to 200,000 in steps of 5,000. The default is 20k. 2. Select Measure the five . The button reads \"Measuring…\" while it works. 3. Read The five spaces, measured , sorted from smallest to largest: Column Meaning Space The space and its colour swatch White The white point the space is defined against D65, or D50 for ProPhoto Lab volume ± 1 SE The volume in CIELAB units cubed, and its standard error vs sRGB The volume as a multiple of sRGB's Sample box The a , b half width of the sampling box, fitted to each space The volume is estimated b"},{"t":"Map a list of colours","d":"Map up to 50 HEX colours at once and export images, settings and a link.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/map-a-colour-list.html","h":["Map the list","Export","Result"],"x":" 1. On the Lab tab, set the Source and Target spaces, the Method and, for chroma compression, the Compression Strength . The list goes through the same settings. 2. Open the Export tab and find Map a list of colours at once . 3. Enter HEX values, one per line commas also separate them . Three digit F0A and six digit FF00AA forms are accepted, with or without . Up to 50 are used. 4. Select Run the list . 5. Read the table: Column Meaning Input Your colour and its swatch Output The mapped colour, converted to sRGB HEX for display on screen OOG Yes if the input was outside the target gamut, otherwise No ΔE₀₀ The colour change caused by mapping Lab The input's L , a , b A summary line gives the number processed, how many were out of gamut and the average ΔE₀₀. If no valid HEX is found, the panel says \"No valid hex values found.\" The Output HEX is an sRGB value for your screen. When the target is wider than sRGB for example Rec. 2020 , it is not the target space code value. Button What you get Source slice, PNG gamut map gm canvas src.png : the source slice at its drawn size, on the dark background, with outlines Mapped slice, PNG gamut map gm canvas dst.png : the mapped slice Everythin"},{"t":"Map a colour into a smaller gamut","d":"Check whether a colour fits a target space, choose a mapping method and strength, and read the result.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/map-a-colour.html","h":["The four methods","Steps","About the Mapped to Target slice","Reading ΔE₀₀","Result"],"x":" All four are this tool's own methods. None is an ICC rendering intent. Method What it does Keeps Gives up Chroma compression Holds L and hue, and reduces chroma until the colour fits found by bisection . Compression Strength sets how far: 1 lands exactly on the boundary, 0 keeps the original chroma and leaves the final clip to deal with it Lightness and hue Vividness Clip in target RGB Converts to the target's linear RGB and clamps each channel to 0–1 Everything already inside the gamut Detail and hue near the boundary; different out of gamut colours can collapse onto one Uniform RGB scale Divides all three channels by the largest, so the brightest channel becomes 1; if a channel is negative it falls back to clipping The ratio between channels Lightness: everything darkens together Adapt white, then clip Adapts from the source white to the target white with the Bradford transform, then clips. This is the shape of ICC relative colorimetric The relationship to each space's white Accuracy of out of gamut colours, which are clipped The last method only differs from Clip in target RGB when the two spaces have different white points. Of the five spaces, ProPhoto RGB uses D50; the others"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/reference.html","h":["The five colour spaces","Lab tab","Boundary tab","Methods tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/gamut map/ Space White Transfer curve used to decode HEX sRGB / Rec.709 D65 sRGB piecewise curve IEC 61966 2 1 Display P3 D65 sRGB piecewise curve Rec. 2020 D65 BT.2020 curve Adobe RGB D65 Power law 563/256 about 2.2 ProPhoto RGB D50 ROMM: power 1.8 with a linear toe The slice is drawn on the source space's white. A space with a different white is adapted onto it with the Bradford transform before its boundary is tested. Control What it does Values or range Default Base colour picker and HEX field The colour to analyse, interpreted in the source space Any six digit HEX 247DEB Random Picks a random base colour Button — Lightness Slice L\\ The lightness of the a b slice 5 to 95, step 1 65 Source The space colours come from The five spaces sRGB / Rec.709 Target The space colours go to The five spaces Display P3 Swap Source & Target Exchanges the two Button — Method The mapping method Chroma compression, Clip in target RGB, Uniform RGB scale, Adapt white, then clip Chroma compression Compression Strength How far chroma compression goes used by chroma compression only 0 to 1, step 0.01 0.90 Resolution Sample grid for the slices "},{"t":"Troubleshooting Gamut Mapping","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The Mapped to Target slice does not change when I change method or strength In the current version that slice is always drawn with chroma compression to the boundary Judge methods with Before / After , the Methods tab or the batch list, which use your method and strength Changing Compression Strength has no effect Strength only applies to Chroma compression , and never changes a colour that is already in gamut Choose Chroma compression and use an out of gamut colour Adapt white, then clip gives the same result as Clip in target RGB Both spaces share the D65 white, so there is nothing to adapt Use ProPhoto RGB D50 as one of the spaces to see a difference The slice looks dull or clipped at the edges Slices are painted in sRGB so your screen can show them; wider colours are displayed clipped Expected. Use the probe and figures, not the painted colour, for wide gamut values The slice looks grainy or speckled A low Resolution , or the Stratified sampler, which places points at random Raise Resolution, or choose Uniform grid or Halton The page is slow after raising Resolution 512 × 512 samples per slice is a lot of work Lower Resolution My base colour's"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/docs/faq.html","h":["Are these the ICC rendering intents?","Which method should I use?","Why is the slice painted in sRGB?","Why does ProPhoto RGB look lopsided?","Why do the areas in the statistics line differ from percentages I see elsewhere?","Is a ΔE₀₀ of 2 acceptable?","Can I load an ICC profile?","Is anything uploaded?"],"x":" No. ICC perceptual and saturation intents are lookup tables that a profile author builds for a particular device, so no general algorithm can reproduce them. The lab's four methods are named for what they do. Adapt white, then clip has the shape of ICC relative colorimetric; Clip in target RGB no white adaptation resembles absolute colorimetric clipping. For photographs, chroma compression usually looks most natural because it keeps lightness and hue. For logos and spot colours that must match exactly where they can, clipping keeps in gamut colours untouched. The lab does not rank methods, because there is no agreed reference set of correct mappings; it reports what each does. Most screens and browsers show sRGB reliably. The geometry which colours are in each gamut is computed exactly; only the painting is limited to what your screen can show. ProPhoto RGB is defined against D50 and includes colours outside human vision. The lab adapts it onto the Lab plane's white with Bradford before testing its boundary, and its chroma can run past the ±128 range the slice draws. They are areas of the a b slice at one lightness, not the \"percentage of the spectral locus\" often quoted from the "},{"t":"Gamut Mapping: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the lab shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the figures are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Gamut Mapping shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The lab has no single key shortcuts of its own. Shortcut Where What it does Click Source Slice or Mapped to Target Probes that a b point at the current L Double click A slice or the Before / After strip Opens it full screen Esc Full screen view Closes it Esc Reference › Filter Clears the filter Enter A ΔE Playground HEX field Applies the typed colour "},{"t":"Gamut Mapping glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" a\\ , b\\ — the two opponent axes of CIELAB: a runs green to red, b blue to yellow. Adobe RGB 1998 — a D65 space with a greener green primary than sRGB, encoded with a power of 563/256. Bisection — finding a boundary by repeatedly halving an interval. The lab finds each gamut boundary this way along 360 hue directions. Bradford transform — a chromatic adaptation transform used to move colours between white points. C\\ chroma — distance from the grey axis in CIELAB: how vivid a colour is. CIELAB — a colour space with lightness L and axes a and b , designed so equal distances are roughly equal perceived differences. Clipping — forcing each out of range RGB channel to 0 or 1. Display P3 — a D65 space with the DCI P3 primaries and the sRGB curve, used on many modern devices and in CSS Color 4. ΔE delta E — a colour difference. ΔE 76 is plain distance in CIELAB; ΔE 94 and ΔE₀₀ CIEDE2000 weight lightness, chroma and hue to match perception better. Gamut — the set of colours a space or device can represent. Gamut boundary — the edge of a gamut. On a slice it is a closed outline around the grey centre. Gamut mapping — choosing what an out of gamut colour becomes in the target space. Gamut vo"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping limits and accuracy","d":"What the Gamut Mapping lab computes exactly, what it approximates and what it does not do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Exact","Estimated","Not done","Current-version caveats"],"x":" The lab is a visual and numerical explorer that runs in your browser. It is not an ICC colour management engine and does not reproduce any vendor's conversion. Primaries and white points of the five spaces are published values, held verbatim. Transfer curves are each space's own: the sRGB curve sRGB and Display P3 , the BT.2020 curve, Adobe RGB's 563/256 power law and ProPhoto's ROMM curve with its linear toe. Boundaries are traced by 24 bisection steps along 360 hue directions, accurate to about 0.00001 in chroma — far below what the plot can show. ΔE formulas follow CIE definitions; ΔE₀₀ follows the Sharma, Wu and Dalal implementation notes. Gamut volume is a Monte Carlo estimate with a standard error. It changes slightly each run and narrows as you raise the sample count. Out of gamut tests allow a tiny tolerance so that colours on the boundary count as inside. ICC perceptual and saturation intents — these are profile lookup tables, not algorithms, and no profile is loaded. Ranking methods — there is no published reference set of correct mappings, so the lab reports what each method does. Loading profiles or tables — the Data tab's install area is not active. Showing wide gamut"},{"t":"Gamut Mapping privacy","d":"What the Gamut Mapping lab does with your colours and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" All mapping runs in your browser. Colours, slices, volumes and batch lists are computed on your device and not sent anywhere. Exports are created locally and saved through your browser's download. The share link contains the spaces, method, L , resolution, sampler, strength and base colour. Anyone with the link sees those settings. Clipboard. Copy writes the link to your clipboard only when you select it. Save to Library stores a snapshot in your Auric Artisan Library. The page loads the site's shared features like every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"Gamut Mapping release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version (2026 workbench rebuild)","May 2026"],"x":" Tabs are now Lab , Boundary , Methods , Data , Export and Reference . The four methods are renamed for what they do: Chroma compression , Clip in target RGB , Uniform RGB scale and Adapt white, then clip . They were previously labelled with ICC intent names, two of which were on the wrong method. Every space now decodes HEX values with its own transfer curve, and ProPhoto RGB uses its own D50 white, adapted onto the Lab plane. Compression Strength now affects the result of chroma compression. Gamut volume moved to the new Boundary tab, measured in a box fitted to each space and reported with a standard error. The xy area percentage was removed. The new Methods tab compares the four methods on the base colour or 12 fixed probe colours. The new Data tab lists the nine datasets and their status. The Export tab offers PNG slices, a settings JSON, a link to the exact state and a 50 colour batch. The Gamut Map User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to Gamut Mapping","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the Gamut Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/gamut-map/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Gamut Lab ../../gamut lab/README.md 13 RGB spaces on the chromaticity diagram, their transfer curves and volumes HDR Gamut Plot ../../hdr gamut plot/README.md Rec.709, P3 and Rec.2020 with HDR transfer curves and perceptual planes Chromatic Adaptation ../../chromatic adaptation/README.md Moving colours between white points with eight transforms ICC Profile Parser ../../../image and file tools/icc profile parser/README.md Inspect the ICC profiles whose lookup tables implement rendering intents Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Check that a mapped colour still has enough contrast Gamut Mapping — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 17 gamut mapping clipping and rendering intents Gamut Volume: How Much Color a Wide Gamut Actually Adds — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 26 gamut volume how much color CIELAB and LCH Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cielab and lch explained ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 26 delta e metrics cie76 ciede2000 itp HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HLG, and Modern Displa"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot","d":"What the HDR Gamut Plot does, who it is for, where to find it and how to take your first reading.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" High dynamic range HDR video changes two things at once: it widens the gamut more saturated colours, typically Rec. 2020 primaries and extends the luminance range from about 100 nits for standard video to as much as 10,000 nits . The HDR Gamut Plot puts both on screen. It draws the three broadcast gamuts — Rec. 709/sRGB, Display P3 and Rec. 2020 — on a CIE 1931 xy or CIE 1976 u′v′ chromaticity diagram, and measures each as a share of the spectral locus. It plots the HDR transfer curves PQ from SMPTE ST 2084 and HLG from BT.2100, with its system gamma against standard gamma 2.2 and 2.4, on an axis in real cd/m². It draws the gamuts in two HDR perceptual spaces, ICtCp and Jzazbz, at a luminance you choose, and stacks their boundaries at eight luminance levels from 0.1 to 10,000 nits. You can also drop in an image to measure how much of each gamut its colours occupy. The page is careful about what a nit is. A PNG or JPEG does not record absolute luminance, so the lab does not claim one from an image; where a luminance comes from the peak brightness control rather than from a signal, it says so. Video, streaming and games developers working with HDR10, HLG or wide gamut content. Desig"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the HDR Gamut Plot: a screen tour, task guides for gamuts, transfer curves and perceptual planes, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs and the chromaticity diagram compare broadcast gamuts.md compare broadcast gamuts.md The three gamuts, locus shares and plotting an image read hdr curves.md read hdr curves.md PQ, HLG and gamma curves, peak brightness and surround explore perceptual planes.md explore perceptual planes.md ICtCp and Jzazbz planes, boundary rings and HEX conversion reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with the HDR Gamut Plot","d":"Open the HDR Gamut Plot, learn its tabs, and read the chromaticity diagram.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Read the diagram","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/hdr gamut plot/. The heading is HDR Gamut Plot . Everything runs in your browser. Gamut — the range of chromaticities a space can make, drawn as a triangle on a chromaticity diagram. HDR video usually uses the wide Rec. 2020 gamut. Luminance — how much light, in candelas per square metre cd/m², also called nits . Standard video is mastered around 100 nits; HDR can reach 1,000 to 10,000. Transfer function — the curve from signal 0 to 1 to light. PQ gives an absolute luminance for every signal value. HLG and the gamma curves are display referred: their output depends on the display's peak. ICtCp and Jzazbz — colour spaces designed for HDR, in which equal steps are closer to equal visible differences across a wide luminance range. A note at the top reminds you that a nit is a measurement, not a setting. Tab What it is for Lab The chromaticity diagram, overlays, gamut metrics and plotting an image Curves Tone curves from signal to cd/m², peak brightness, HLG surround and signal level Planes The gamuts in ICtCp or Jzazbz, and boundary rings at eight luminances Data The ten datasets the tool uses and their status Export Mea"},{"t":"Compare broadcast gamuts","d":"Compare Rec.709/sRGB, Display P3 and Rec.2020 by area and share of the spectral locus, and measure how much of each an image occupies.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/compare-broadcast-gamuts.html","h":["The three spaces","Read the share of the locus","Measure an image's colours","Compare side by side","Result"],"x":" Space Red x, y Green x, y Blue x, y White Rec.709 / sRGB 0.640, 0.330 0.300, 0.600 0.150, 0.060 D65 Display P3 0.680, 0.320 0.265, 0.690 0.150, 0.060 D65 Rec.2020 0.708, 0.292 0.170, 0.797 0.131, 0.046 D65 All three share the D65 white. The P3 here is Display P3, not the DCI cinema version with its greener white. 1. On the Lab tab, read Gamut metrics . 2. Share of locus is each triangle's area divided by the area of the spectral locus in the same plane. In CIE 1931 xy the tool measures 33.6% for Rec.709, 45.6% for Display P3 and 63.6% for Rec.2020. 3. Press A or change Chromaticity axes to CIE 1976 u′v′ . The shares change because u′v′ spaces colours more evenly; the u′v′ figures are the fairer comparison. The often quoted 35.9%, 53.6% and 75.8% are against a smaller locus area than the one the tool draws. Neither set is wrong; the tool divides by the locus it shows. Its locus is the CIE 1931 2° observer's, tabulated at 65 points from 380 to 700 nm. 1. Under Plot an image on it , select Drop a PNG or JPEG and choose an image. Images larger than 1,024 pixels on a side are reduced for analysis. 2. Read the results under the button: Pixels on the diagram — the analysed size, how many"},{"t":"Explore ICtCp and Jzazbz planes","d":"View the three gamuts in the ICtCp or Jzazbz perceptual planes, read the boundary rings from 0.1 to 10,000 nits, and convert HEX colours.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/explore-perceptual-planes.html","h":["Key ideas","View the plane","Convert a list of colours","Export the plane","Result"],"x":" ICtCp ITU R BT.2100, from Dolby splits colour into I intensity , Ct tritan, blue–yellow and Cp protan, red–green . It converts linear Rec. 2020 RGB to cone responses, encodes each with the PQ curve, then rotates to I, Ct, Cp. It is the basis of the ΔE ITP colour difference. Jzazbz Safdar et al., 2017 gives lightness Jz and opponent axes az and bz . It starts from absolute XYZ and uses its own PQ like quantiser with the exponent raised by a factor of 1.7 p = 134.034375 . Both are built to keep equal steps roughly equal from very dark to very bright, which CIELAB does not. 1. Set the luminance first: on the Curves tab, choose a tone curve, peak brightness and Signal level . Together they define the absolute luminance the plane is drawn at. 2. Open the Planes tab. 3. Under Perceptual plane , choose ICtCp Ct–Cp default or JzAzBz Az–Bz . The title and note change to name the space and its quantiser. 4. Read the plane: each gamut switched on in the Lab's Overlay gamuts is outlined, showing how far its chroma extends at that luminance. 5. Read Boundary rings by luminance : the same boundaries at eight luminances — 0.1, 1, 10, 100, 500, 1,000, 4,000 and 10,000 nits — listed under Boundary"},{"t":"Read HDR transfer curves","d":"Compare PQ, HLG and gamma curves in cd/m², set peak brightness and HLG surround, and read what a signal value means in nits.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/read-hdr-curves.html","h":["The four curves","HLG system gamma","Steps","The EOTF comparison chart","Export the curve","Result"],"x":" Curve Defined by Kind What the output means PQ ST.2084 SMPTE ST 2084 Absolute Signal 0 to 1 maps to 0 to 10,000 cd/m² on any display that can reach it. Signal 0.5 is about 92 cd/m² HLG BT.2100 ARIB STD B67, with the BT.2100 OOTF Display referred Scene light is shaped by a system gamma that depends on the display's peak, then scaled to that peak Gamma 2.4 BT.1886, zero black ITU R BT.1886 Display referred signal^2.4 × peak Gamma 2.2 SDR Pure power law Display referred signal^2.2 × peak Absolute means the curve states a luminance outright. Display referred means it reaches a luminance only by way of the display's peak, which the Peak brightness control supplies. HLG applies an opto optical transfer function OOTF with a system gamma that depends on the display peak L W: text γ = 1.2 + 0.42 × log10 L W ÷ 1000 At 1,000 nits γ is 1.2. The tool also offers two surround adjustments: Dim surround multiplies γ by 0.95 and Bright surround by 0.90. These two factors are this tool's own; they are not in BT.2100 or BT.2390. Choosing one marks the HLG reading Adjusted . Reference dark uses BT.2100's value unchanged. The system gamma is never set below 1.0. 1. Open the Curves tab. 2. Set Peak bri"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/reference.html","h":["Lab tab","Curves tab","Planes tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/hdr gamut plot/ Control What it does Values Default Working colour space Shown on the page, but in the current version it does not change the diagram or figures sRGB / Rec.709 BT.709 ; Display P3 D65 ; Rec.2020 BT.2020 Rec.2020 Overlay gamuts Shows or hides each triangle also used by the Planes tab Rec.709 / sRGB, Display P3, Rec.2020 All on Spectral locus Draws the locus On or off On Line of purples Draws the straight edge of the locus On or off On ICtCp marker Shown, but draws nothing in the current version On or off Off Chromaticity axes The diagram's plane CIE 1931 xy; CIE 1976 u′v′ CIE 1931 xy Standard observer Shown, but the locus is always the CIE 1931 2° observer's CIE 1931 2° Standard ; CIE 2015 10° Revised CIE 1931 2° Drop a PNG or JPEG Opens a file picker and measures the image's gamut occupancy Image files; reduced to at most 1,024 pixels a side — Readout What it shows Gamut chromaticity diagram The triangles, locus, purples line and D65 marker; the axis name is shown over it Hover line Coordinates, XYZ at Y = 0.35, L , and I, Ct, Cp at the PQ luminance of the Signal level Gamut metrics Space, Primaries"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the HDR Gamut Plot","d":"Fixes for common problems in the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do Changing Working colour space changes nothing The control is not applied in the current version Use Overlay gamuts to choose which spaces are drawn Choosing the 2015 10° observer changes nothing The locus is always the CIE 1931 2° observer's Expected ICtCp marker draws nothing Not applied in the current version No workaround The Tone mapping operator menu changes nothing Not applied in the current version Use the Tone Mapping ../../tone mapping/README.md lab PQ does not change when I move Peak brightness PQ is absolute; the peak does not scale it Expected. Choose HLG or a gamma curve to see the peak's effect The HLG reading is marked Adjusted Dim or bright surround applies this tool's own factor Choose Reference dark for BT.2100's value The EOTF comparison chart does not follow my settings It is drawn once when the page loads Use Tone curve output for your settings My image does not appear on the diagram The current version reports the image's occupancy as text under the drop area; it does not scatter the pixels on the diagram Read the results under Plot an image on it The image readout shows no nits A PNG or JPEG does not record absolute luminanc"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/docs/faq.html","h":["What is the difference between PQ and HLG?","What does a PQ signal of 0.5 mean?","Why is HLG's system gamma 1.2?","Are the dim and bright surround settings standard?","Why can't the tool tell me the peak brightness of my image?","Why do ICtCp and Jzazbz use different quantisers?","Is the \"ACES Filmic\" operator the Academy's transform?","Why 33.6%, 45.6% and 63.6% rather than the usual figures?","Does it work with HDR displays?"],"x":" PQ SMPTE ST 2084 is absolute: each signal value means a specific luminance, up to 10,000 nits, and displays that cannot reach it must tone map. HLG ARIB STD B67 / BT.2100 is relative: the display applies a system gamma based on its own peak, which makes HLG backward compatible with standard displays. About 92 cd/m², on any display that can show it. That is its value for a 1,000 nit display under BT.2100: γ = 1.2 + 0.42 × log10 L W ÷ 1000 . It rises for brighter displays and falls for dimmer ones. No. The multipliers 0.95 and 0.90 are this tool's own. Readings made with them are marked Adjusted. An ordinary 8 bit PNG or JPEG stores code values with no record of the light they stood for. Absolute luminance needs an HDR format with PQ or HLG and mastering metadata, or a format such as OpenEXR, which the tool does not read. ICtCp uses ST 2084 as written. Jzazbz's authors raised the curve's exponent by a factor of 1.7 p = 134.034375 . The tool runs each with its own. No. It is Krzysztof Narkowicz's 2016 curve fit that approximates the look of the ACES output transforms. The Reference section says so. They are shares of the spectral locus the tool draws the CIE 1931 2° locus, 65 points "},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md HDR and colour terms used in the tool shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the figures are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" These keys work when the focus is not in a text box, slider or list. The Lab tab's rail lists them as \"1 4 cycle curves\" and \"A toggle axes\". Key What it does 1 Tone curve: Gamma 2.2 SDR 2 Tone curve: Gamma 2.4 BT.1886, zero black 3 Tone curve: PQ ST.2084 4 Tone curve: HLG BT.2100 A Switches the chromaticity axes between CIE 1931 xy and CIE 1976 u′v′ Esc Closes a full screen chart; clears the Reference filter Mouse What it does Move over the diagram Updates the hover readout Double click a chart Opens it full screen "},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the HDR and colour terms used in the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Absolute curve — a transfer curve whose output is a stated luminance, independent of the display. PQ is absolute. BT.1886 — the ITU R reference EOTF for standard dynamic range flat panel displays; with zero black level it is a 2.4 power law. BT.2020 Rec. 2020 — the ultra high definition television standard, whose wide primaries HDR video usually uses. BT.2100 — the ITU R standard for HDR television. It defines PQ and HLG, the HLG system gamma and the ICtCp colour space. cd/m² nit — the unit of luminance. Display referred curve — a curve whose output depends on the display's peak luminance. HLG and gamma curves are display referred. EOTF — electro optical transfer function: signal to light. HDR high dynamic range — images and displays with a much wider luminance range than standard video. HLG hybrid log gamma — a relative HDR transfer function ARIB STD B67 , combining a square root segment for darks with a logarithmic segment for highlights. ICtCp — an HDR colour space from BT.2100: I intensity , Ct blue–yellow and Cp red–green , built on PQ encoded cone responses. Jzazbz — a perceptually uniform colour space for HDR and wide gamut Safdar et al., 2017 , with its own PQ like quantis"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot limits and accuracy","d":"How far the HDR Gamut Plot's curves, planes, shares and image readings can be trusted.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Exact to the standard","Computed","This tool's own","Not available","Current-version caveats"],"x":" Primaries and white of Rec.709/sRGB, Display P3 and Rec.2020. PQ with the ST 2084 constants written as the standard's exact fractions. ICtCp matrices, matching BT.2100. HLG with the BT.2100 system gamma reference surround . Jzazbz from Safdar et al. 2017 , with its own quantiser. Areas and locus shares by the shoelace formula, divided by the tabulated CIE 1931 2° locus 65 points, 380–700 nm; area 0.33323 in xy against a published 0.334 . Tone mapping operators with published constants. \"ACES Filmic\" is Narkowicz's approximation, not the Academy's transform. Image occupancy , binned at 0.002 in xy. The dim and bright surround multipliers for HLG 0.95 and 0.90 . They are not in BT.2100 or BT.2390, and readings made with them are marked Adjusted. Image luminance. 8 bit PNG and JPEG files carry no absolute luminance. HDR formats OpenEXR, or PNG with PQ or HLG and mastering metadata are not read. The 10° observer. The option has no effect. Working colour space , ICtCp marker and Tone mapping operator do not change the output. The image's pixels are measured but not drawn on the diagram. The EOTF comparison chart is drawn at page load and does not follow the controls. The Convert a list"},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot privacy","d":"What the HDR Gamut Plot does with your images, colours and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Images stay on your device. An image you drop in is read and analysed by your browser; it is not uploaded, and the tool keeps only the resulting figures on the page. All curves, planes and measurements are computed in your browser. Exports are created locally and saved through your browser's download, or copied to your clipboard when you choose. The link carries the axes, peak brightness, tone curve and perceptual plane. Anyone with the link sees those settings. Save to Library stores a snapshot in your Auric Artisan Library. The page loads the site's shared features like every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"HDR Gamut Plot release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version (2026 workbench rebuild)","May 2026"],"x":" Tabs are now Lab , Curves , Planes , Data , Export and Reference . Gamut shares are quoted against the spectral locus in the plane on screen 33.6%, 45.6% and 63.6% in xy . They were previously divided by Rec.2020's area, so Rec.2020 always read 100%. The image readout no longer prints a \"peak luminance\" or 100% coverage for every image. It measures the image's occupancy of each gamut instead. The tone curve axis now covers whatever is drawn, so PQ is shown in full to 10,000 cd/m². Peak brightness is documented as not scaling PQ. Jzazbz now runs its own quantiser p = 134.034375 instead of ICtCp's. HLG surround adjustments are marked as this tool's own, and readings using them are labelled Adjusted. The boundary rings are now drawn automatically with a key to their eight luminance levels. Export previews the exact payload and names the file; the CSV column formerly headed \"Coverage%\" is now \"Locus share %\". The \"ACES\" operator is identified as Narkowicz's 2016 approximation. The HDR Gamut Plot User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to the HDR Gamut Plot","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the HDR Gamut Plot.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/hdr-gamut-plot/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Tone Mapping ../../tone mapping/README.md Apply and compare tone mapping operators Gamut Lab ../../gamut lab/README.md 13 RGB spaces, including Rec. 2100 PQ and HLG, with transfer curves and volumes Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md What happens to colours outside a smaller gamut LUT Lab ../../../image and file tools/lut lab/README.md Build and preview lookup tables for grading HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HLG, and Modern Displays — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 hdr wide gamut pq hlg modern displays ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 26 delta e metrics cie76 ciede2000 itp Chromaticity Diagrams Without the Intimidation — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 chromaticity diagrams Gamut Volume: How Much Color a Wide Gamut Actually Adds — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 26 gamut volume how much color Color in Real Time 3D: Albedo, PBR, and Tone Mapping — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 02 color in real time 3d albedo pbr tone mapping The site's Documentation library https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/ "},{"t":"Illuminants","d":"What the Standard Illuminants lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to take your first reading.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Standard Illuminants lab shows you what a light source is made of and what that does to colour. You pick one of 18 CIE standard illuminants A, D50, D55, D65, D75, equal energy E and the fluorescent series F1 to F12 or a blackbody radiator at any colour temperature from 1,500 K to 25,000 K. The lab draws its spectral power distribution, integrates it against the CIE 1931 2° standard observer, and reports its white point, correlated colour temperature CCT , Duv, colour rendering, how surfaces look under it, and how a set of colours adapts from one white point to another. Around that core it adds views for the chromaticity diagram in three planes , a Monte Carlo estimate of how measurement error propagates into x, y, CCT and Duv, a comparison of calculation methods, a small query console for comparing many illuminants at once, and a data register that says where every table comes from. Every reading carries a line naming the dataset, observer and interval behind it. The lab is honest about its limits. The CIE fluorescent tables and the CIE 13.3 test colour samples are not held, so fluorescent spectra and colour rendering figures are built from stand ins and labelled as such. IES "},{"t":"Illuminants documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the working guides for the Standard Illuminants lab: a screen tour, step by step tasks, a full reference to every control and output, and help for when a reading looks wrong. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the lab, the eight tabs, and your first reading compare light sources.md compare light sources.md Comparing two illuminants: spectra, CRI, metamerism and surface shifts adapt between white points.md adapt between white points.md Adapting a colour chart from one white point to another, and reading the matrix estimate uncertainty.md estimate uncertainty.md Running the Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation query console.md query console.md Using the query console, its grammar and its exports reference.md reference.md Every control, readout, option and export, tab by tab troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with Illuminants","d":"Open the Standard Illuminants lab, learn its eight tabs and take your first reading of a light source.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","Key ideas before you start","A tour of the screen","Take your first reading","Where the numbers come from","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/illuminants/. The page title is Standard Illuminants . Nothing needs installing and you do not need to sign in. All calculations run in your browser. An illuminant is a light source described by its spectral power distribution SPD : the relative power it emits at each wavelength from 380 nm violet to 780 nm deep red . The lab turns an SPD into colour by weighting it with the CIE 1931 2° standard observer — three curves that describe how an average observer matches colours in a small 2° field of view. The result is the tristimulus values X, Y, Z , and from them the chromaticity x, y — the illuminant's white point . Correlated colour temperature CCT is the temperature, in kelvin, of the blackbody Planckian radiator whose colour is closest to the light. Low CCT is warm candle, tungsten ; high CCT is cool north sky . Duv is how far the light's chromaticity sits from the blackbody curve, in the CIE 1960 uv plane. Positive Duv is greenish; negative is pinkish. CCT only means something when Duv is small. A note at the top of the tool explains that every figure is traceable: the line under each result names the dataset, observer and "},{"t":"Adapt colours between white points","d":"Use the chromatic adaptation panel to move a 24-colour chart from one white point to another and read the transform matrix.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/adapt-between-white-points.html","h":["How a CAT works, briefly","Steps","Reading the result","Tips","Result"],"x":" Colour managed work often needs a colour expressed under one white point to be re expressed under another. The classic case is ICC colour management, whose profile connection space uses D50, while sRGB and most screens use D65. A chromatic adaptation transform CAT does this by imitating how the eye rebalances its cone sensitivities to a new light. 1. Convert the colour's XYZ values into a cone like space L, M, S with a 3 × 3 matrix M. 2. Scale each of L, M and S by the ratio of the destination white to the source white. This is the von Kries idea: each cone type adjusts its gain independently. 3. Convert back to XYZ with the inverse of M. The transforms differ only in the matrix M. The lab offers: Choice What it is Bradford The matrix from Lam 1985 , the usual choice in ICC workflows. Default. CAT16 The matrix from the CAM16 colour appearance model Li et al., 2017 . CAT02 The matrix from CIECAM02 CIE 159:2004 . Von Kries The Hunt–Pointer–Estévez cone matrix, normalised to D65. Sharp A spectrally sharpened matrix Finlayson and Süsstrunk, 2000 . XYZ scaling Scales X, Y and Z directly. Kept as the simplest case to compare against; it is not a model of the eye. None No adaptation. The"},{"t":"Compare two light sources","d":"Overlay two illuminants, read their CCT, CRI and white points side by side, and judge metamerism risk with the surface samples.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/compare-light-sources.html","h":["Before you start","Steps","Reading the result","Tips","Result"],"x":" Use this when you need to explain why a product, print or swatch looks different in two places — for example daylight at a window against tungsten at home, or a D50 viewing booth against a D65 screen. Metamerism is when two surfaces match under one light and differ under another. The lab estimates the risk between two lights with a metamerism index : the average CIEDE2000 colour difference of 14 test samples rendered under each light. Bigger means more risk. CRI colour rendering index scores how faithfully a light renders test colours compared with a reference light of the same CCT a blackbody below 5,000 K, CIE daylight at or above . Ra is the mean of the first eight scores; R9 is saturated red. In this lab the test samples are approximations of the CIE 13.3 set, not the published reflectances. CRI and the metamerism index are therefore indicative. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . 1. Open the Lab tab. 2. Under Illuminant , choose the first light, for example CIE D65 6504 K — Daylight, sRGB . 3. Under Comparison illuminant , tick Enable comparison . 4. Open the comparison list and choose the second light. The choices are CIE A, D50, D55, D65, D75, equal e"},{"t":"Estimate measurement uncertainty","d":"Propagate a spectroradiometer uncertainty budget into x, y, CCT and Duv with the Monte Carlo view.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/estimate-uncertainty.html","h":["The input budget","Steps","Reading the result","Tips","Result"],"x":" A measured spectrum is never exact. The wavelength scale may be slightly off, the instrument's slit blurs sharp peaks, and the detector adds noise. The Uncertainty tab asks how much those errors move the numbers you would report: x, y, CCT and Duv. It uses the Monte Carlo method described in JCGM 101:2008 Supplement 1 to the Guide to the Expression of Uncertainty in Measurement : it perturbs the spectrum thousands of times at random, according to the error sizes you give, and measures the spread of the results. The budget is preset for a typical array spectroradiometer. It is a starting point, not your instrument: every value is editable. Hover over a label to see what the term models and whether it is treated as a normal or a rectangular distribution. Term Unit Preset Distribution What it models Wavelength scale nm 0.20 Normal A shift of the whole wavelength axis. Dominates on a spiky source. Bandwidth FWHM nm 5.0 Rectangular The finite slit width, modelled as a triangular blur. Stray light relative 0.0001 Rectangular A flat pedestal added across the range. Non linearity % 0.10 Rectangular A gain error that depends on signal level. Detector noise % 0.05 Normal Independent noise a"},{"t":"Query many illuminants at once","d":"Use the Console tab's query language to tabulate, sort, plot and export readings for many illuminants.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/query-console.html","h":["Steps","The grammar","The recipes","Stand-in rows","The export files","Result"],"x":" The Console tab answers questions such as \"which of these lights is furthest from the Planckian locus?\" in one table. You type a short query; the lab computes every requested column with the same engine the other tabs use, so a console row and a Lab reading cannot disagree. The query is parsed, never run as code. 1. Open the Console tab. The Query box already holds an example. 2. Edit the query, or select one of the Recipes to load a ready made one. 3. Select Run , or press Ctrl + Enter in the query box. 4. Read the Results table. Its heading shows the number of rows. The status line beside the buttons shows rows, time taken and the interval and interpolation used. 5. Under Any two columns, plotted , choose a Horizontal axis and a Vertical axis . The scatter plot labels each point with the illuminant name. 6. Select CSV or JSON to download the results. A query is a few lines, each starting with a keyword. Anything after // on a line is a comment. Line What it does Example select The illuminants to include, separated by commas or spaces. Names are case insensitive. A range such as F1..F12 expands to every name in between. select A, D50, D65, F1..F12 with Pipeline settings as name=v"},{"t":"Illuminants reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the Standard Illuminants lab, tab by tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/reference.html","h":["Lab tab","Chromaticity tab","Uncertainty tab","Methods tab","Console tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/colorimetry/illuminants/ Control What it does Values or range Default Source mode Chooses between a tabulated standard illuminant and a Planckian blackbody spectrum Standard , Blackbody Standard Illuminant The standard illuminant to analyse 18 choices, listed below CIE D65 6504 K — Daylight, sRGB CCT slider and number box Colour temperature of the blackbody source. Moving either switches to Blackbody mode 1,500 to 25,000 K in 50 K steps 6500 Link to select When ticked, choosing a standard illuminant also sets the CCT field to that illuminant's nominal CCT On or off On Reset to D65 Returns to Standard mode, D65 and 6500 K Button — Enable comparison Overlays a second illuminant on the SPD chart and fills the comparison table On or off Off Comparison illuminant list The second illuminant CIE A, D50, D55, D65, D75, Equal energy E, F2, F7, F11 CIE A 2856 K Surface reflectance samples Which surfaces appear under Surface appearance White, Gray, Red, Green, Blue, Skin, Yellow, Cyan White, Gray, Red, Green, Skin on Adapt from Source white point for the adaptation preview D65, D50, D55, D75, A, E D65 Swap Exchanges Adapt from and Adapt to Butto"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Illuminants","d":"What to do when a reading, chart, export or shortcut in the Standard Illuminants lab does not behave as expected.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do Moving the CCT slider changed my illuminant to a blackbody The CCT controls drive Blackbody mode, so touching them switches the source Choose Standard under Source mode and pick the illuminant again, or select Reset to D65 The CCT box jumps back when I pick a standard illuminant Link to select copies the illuminant's nominal CCT into the box Untick Link to select to keep your own CCT value The Illuminant comparison panel is empty Comparison is off Tick Enable comparison CCT shows \"n/a\" or a validity warning The light is too far from the blackbody curve Duv beyond ±0.05 or outside 1,000–100,000 K, where CCT is not defined Read Duv and x, y instead. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md The dominant wavelength shows a dash The light is almost the same colour as the D65 reference white, so there is no direction to measure Expected. Purity will read close to 0% The CRI of a fluorescent light looks wrong compared with a datasheet The lab's test colour samples and fluorescent spectra are stand ins, not the CIE tables Treat CRI as indicative. Use a published or measured value for specifications I want TM 30 Rf and Rg The 99 colour eval"},{"t":"Illuminants FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/docs/faq.html","h":["Why does CIE A show 2856 K when the standard defines it at 2848 K?","Are the D65 and D50 spectra the published CIE tables?","Why are the fluorescent illuminants marked as stand-ins?","Is the CRI value a real CIE 13.3 result?","Why is there no TM-30 figure?","What is the difference between the Ohno and McCamy CCT?","What does a negative Duv mean?","Can I use the 10° observer?","Can I load my own measured spectrum?","Does it work offline?","Can I save my settings?"],"x":" Illuminant A is defined as a Planckian radiator at 2848 K using the 1931 value of the second radiation constant. Measured on a modern ITS 90 Planckian locus, its CCT is 2856 K. The lab computes A the way it is defined and reports the CCT you would measure, which is why the list says 2856 K. The Data tab explains this under Illuminant A. They are reconstructed from the published CIE daylight basis functions S0, S1, S2 , which the lab holds verbatim. The reconstructions land on their published chromaticities to better than 0.0003, which is why they are marked \"computed\" rather than \"verbatim\". The lab does not hold the CIE 15 table of fluorescent spectra. F1 to F12 are built from smooth peaks as illustrations, so their chromaticity, CCT and rendering figures describe the stand in, not the real CIE illuminant. They are flagged wherever they appear. No. The 14 test colour samples are approximations, so Ra and R1–R14 are indicative only. The Methods tab shows the CIE 13.3 card as switched off for that reason. TM 30 is defined on 99 colour evaluation samples that the lab does not hold. Rather than invent a figure, the lab leaves TM 30 switched off. The Reference tab still explains what "},{"t":"Illuminants: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . They define the terms the lab uses, say how far its numbers can be trusted, and point to related tools and articles. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the lab, from SPD to Duv shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What is standard, what is a stand in, and what is not computed related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Illuminants shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/shortcuts.html","h":["About the S, R, C and E hint"],"x":" Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + Enter Console, in the Query box Runs the query Esc Reference, in the Filter box Clears the filter Esc A full screen chart Closes the full screen view Double click SPD or CRI chart Opens the chart full screen Click SPD chart Probes the nearest wavelength and shows its relative power On macOS, Cmd + Enter also runs a console query. The Lab rail shows a Keyboard shortcuts hint: S swap adaptation, R reset D65, C toggle compare, E export CSV. These single key shortcuts are not active in the current version of the page. Use the buttons instead: Hint Button to use S Swap under Chromatic adaptation R Reset to D65 C Enable comparison E Export SPD CSV on the Export tab The site's own shortcuts such as the search palette also work on this page; see the site features documentation. "},{"t":"Illuminants glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the colour-science terms used in the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Blackbody Planckian radiator — an idealised object whose emitted light depends only on its temperature, described by Planck's law. Tungsten lamps are close to one. Chromatic adaptation — the eye's adjustment to the colour of the prevailing light, so that a white sheet still looks white under warm or cool light. Chromatic adaptation transform CAT — a calculation that predicts chromatic adaptation. It maps XYZ into a cone like space, scales each channel by the ratio of two white points, and maps back. Bradford, CAT02, CAT16, Von Kries HPE and Sharp differ in the cone like matrix. Chromaticity — the colour of a light or surface without its brightness, written as two coordinates. Chromaticity diagram — a plot of chromaticity. The lab offers CIE 1931 xy, CIE 1960 uv where Duv is defined and CIE 1976 u′v′ more evenly spaced . CIE — the International Commission on Illumination, which publishes the standard observers, illuminants and formulas used here. Colour matching functions CMFs — three curves describing how a standard observer matches colours. Weighting a spectrum by them gives X, Y and Z. Colour rendering index CRI — a score of how faithfully a light renders test colours compared w"},{"t":"Illuminants limits and accuracy","d":"Which Illuminants readings are standard values, which rest on stand-ins, and what the lab does not compute.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Standard values you can rely on","Readings that rest on stand-ins","Not computed at all","Precision notes"],"x":" The lab is a reference calculator that runs in your browser. It is not calibrated measurement software and not a substitute for official CIE or IES tools. This page says what each kind of reading rests on. Reading Rests on Notes x, y, XYZ of A, D50, D55, D65, D75, E and blackbody sources CIE 1931 2° colour matching functions verbatim, 5 nm, 380–780 nm The D series is reconstructed from the verbatim daylight basis and lands on the published chromaticities to better than 0.0003 CCT and Duv Ohno's method over a Planckian locus computed through the same observer Reported as valid only for 1,000–100,000 K and Duv within ±0.05 Chromaticity in xy, u′v′ and uv Exact conversions — Chromatic adaptation matrices Published Bradford, CAT02, CAT16, HPE and Sharp matrices XYZ scaling is included as the simplest case, not as a model of vision Dominant wavelength and purity The spectral locus of the 2° observer, from the D65 white Undefined shown as a dash when the light is almost white Monte Carlo uncertainty JCGM 101:2008 method Only as good as the budget you enter; inputs are treated as uncorrelated Reading Why it is not a standard value Anything for F1 to F12 spectrum, x, y, CCT, CRI The CIE f"},{"t":"Illuminants privacy","d":"What the Standard Illuminants lab keeps on your device and what, if anything, leaves it.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" All calculations run in your browser. Spectra, readings, uncertainty runs and console queries are computed on your device. The lab does not send them anywhere. Nothing you type is uploaded. Budget values and console queries stay in the page and are gone when you close it. Downloads are made on your device. CSV, JSON and PNG exports are generated in the browser and saved through your browser's normal download. Clipboard. Copy white HEX and the share Copy button write to your clipboard only when you select them. Your browser may ask for permission. Share links contain only the settings listed in the reference ../docs/reference.md export tab mode, illuminant or CCT, and adaptation settings . Anyone you send the link to sees those settings. Save to Library stores a preset in your Auric Artisan Library. See the Library documentation for where that is kept. The page itself loads the site's shared features in the same way as every other page on auricartisan.com. See the site's privacy policy for those. "},{"t":"Illuminants release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — the workbench rebuild","May 2026"],"x":" The lab was rebuilt around a new colorimetric core and a new layout. New tabs: Chromaticity , Uncertainty , Methods , Console and Data join Lab, Export and Reference. CCT and Duv are now computed with Ohno's method, with a signed Duv and a validity check. The older McCamy figure is shown only on the Methods tab for comparison. The daylight illuminants are rebuilt from the published daylight basis at its tabulated interval, and Illuminant A is computed as defined 2848 K with the 1931 constant, measuring 2856 K . Chromatic adaptation now offers Bradford, CAT16, CAT02, Von Kries, Sharp, XYZ scaling and None, with the matrix shown. A provenance line under results names the dataset, observer and interval. A data register marks each dataset verbatim, computed, stand in or absent. Fluorescent spectra and CRI test samples are labelled as stand ins; TM 30 is shown as not computed rather than estimated. The Standards, Formulas, References and Research tabs became one Reference view with a search filter and status chips; the citation list grew to 22 entries, each marked Runs here, Data missing or Context only. The Illuminants User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, desc"},{"t":"Related to Illuminants","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the Standard Illuminants lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/illuminants/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Chromatic Adaptation ../../chromatic adaptation/README.md Applies eight adaptation transforms to a real image, with a time course of adaptation Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md What happens to a colour moved between RGB spaces with different white points Gamut Lab ../../gamut lab/README.md RGB primaries and white points on the chromaticity diagram Material Lighting ../../../perception and spectral/material lighting/README.md Surface reflectance rendered under different illuminants Colour Science Lab ../../../colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md A broader laboratory for adaptation, appearance models and spectra Spectral Power Distributions and Why RGB Is Not Enough — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 spectral power distributions CIE XYZ Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cie xyz explained Chromaticity Diagrams Without the Intimidation — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 chromaticity diagrams Metamerism Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 metamerism White Points and Chromatic Adaptation: von Kries, Bradford, and CAT02 — https://auricartisa"},{"t":"Tonal Steps","d":"What the Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades tool does, who it is for, where to find it and how to build your first ramp.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Tonal Steps builds a lightness ramp from one colour: a sequence of steps running from white, through versions of your colour, to black. Alongside it the tool builds tints your colour mixed towards white , shades towards black , tones towards grey , a neutral ladder of greys, and a 50–950 or 50–900 key set of the kind design systems use. Two ramp engines are offered. HSL lightness spaces the steps evenly in HSL lightness. Equal luminance spaces them evenly in relative luminance, the quantity WCAG contrast is built on, with an easing exponent to bunch steps where you want them. Tints, shades, tones and key sets are mixed in the space you choose: CIELAB, OKLab, HSL or linear sRGB. Every step is measured: OKLab lightness, WCAG 2.2 contrast ratio and APCA W3 0.1.9 Lc against white, black or your base colour. A Ramps view compares the engines and reports how even each ramp is in three measures. Exports give CSS custom properties, an SCSS map, JSON or CSV, each with a header recording how the ramp was made. Designers building colour scales for a design system or brand. Front end developers who need ramp tokens with known contrast against white and black. Accessibility specialists checkin"},{"t":"Tonal Steps documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use Tonal Steps: a screen tour, task guides for ramps, tints and shades, contrast and exports, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs and your first ramp build a ramp.md build a ramp.md Choosing an engine, steps and easing, and reading evenness tints shades tones.md tints shades tones.md Tints, shades, tones, the neutral ladder, mixing spaces and key sets check contrast.md check contrast.md WCAG 2.2 and APCA against white, black or the base export tokens.md export tokens.md CSS, SCSS, JSON, CSV, links and list analysis reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with Tonal Steps","d":"Open Tonal Steps, learn its tabs, and build and read your first ramp.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Build your first ramp","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/tonal steps tints shades/. The heading is Tonal Steps . Everything runs in your browser. A ramp is a sequence of colours from light to dark built from one base colour. A tint is a colour mixed with white, a shade mixed with black, and a tone mixed with grey. Relative luminance Y is the physical brightness of a colour on a 0 black to 1 white scale. WCAG contrast ratios are calculated from it. OKLab L is a perceptual lightness from 0 to 1 Ottosson, 2020 : equal steps in it look roughly equally spaced. The tool uses it to show where your steps fall. WCAG 2.2 contrast is a ratio from 1:1 to 21:1 with thresholds of 3, 4.5 and 7. APCA Lc is a signed contrast value from the APCA W3 0.1.9 algorithm; its sign shows which colour is lighter. A note at the top explains a correction the tool made: OKLab needs linear sRGB as input, and the page now provides it. Tab What it is for Lab Build the ramp and see its steps, lightness chart, base colour details and optional sets Ramps Compare engines, measure evenness, see the ramp in chroma, and build key sets Contrast Every step's WCAG and APCA contrast against a colour you choose Data T"},{"t":"Build a ramp","d":"Choose a ramp engine, step count and easing, and judge how even the ramp is.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/build-a-ramp.html","h":["The engines","Steps","Compare the engines","Tips","Result"],"x":" Engine How it builds the steps Holds even Easing γ HSL lightness Keeps your colour's HSL hue and saturation and steps HSL lightness evenly from 100 white to 0 black HSL L, a coordinate rather than a perceptual quantity Not used Equal luminance For each step, finds the HSL lightness at your colour's hue and saturation that gives a target relative luminance Y = 1 − t ^γ, from 1 white to 0 black Relative luminance Y, the quantity WCAG contrast is built on at γ = 1 Bends the targets A third engine, Equal contrast equal steps in WCAG ratio against black , is not offered on the Lab tab because it produces the same ramp as Equal luminance: equal steps in WCAG ratio are equal steps in luminance. The Ramps tab shows it with a \"same ramp as equal luminance\" badge, and it can still be reached with the 3 key or a saved link. Both engines start at white and end at black. The Mix in setting does not affect the main ramp; it affects tints, shades, tones and key sets. 1. On the Lab tab, enter the Base colour as a six digit HEX or use the picker, or Random base . 2. Choose HSL lightness or Equal luminance under Ramp engine . 3. Set Steps from 3 to 21 default 11 . 4. For Equal luminance, set Easing"},{"t":"Check contrast","d":"Read every ramp step's WCAG 2.2 ratio and rating and its APCA-W3 Lc against white, black or the base colour.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/check-contrast.html","h":["Two measures","Steps","Reading the result","Tips","Result"],"x":" WCAG 2.2 contrast ratio — L1 + 0.05 ÷ L2 + 0.05 , lighter over darker, where L is relative luminance. Thresholds: 3:1 for large text AA large , 4.5:1 for normal text AA , 7:1 for enhanced AAA . APCA Lc APCA W3 0.1.9 — a perceptual contrast value that treats dark on light and light on dark differently. It is signed: the sign tells you which way round the pair is. APCA is a working draft of what WCAG 3 may adopt, not a ratified requirement. 1. Build your ramp on the Lab tab. 2. Open the Contrast tab. 3. Under Against , choose White default , Black or The base your base colour . The caption changes to \"Every step against white\", and so on. 4. Read the table: Column Meaning Step The step's swatch and HEX WCAG The ratio, for example 4.63:1 Rating AAA 7 and above , AA 4.5 and above , AA large 3 and above or Fail APCA Lc The signed Lc, to one decimal 5. Under Superseded APCA , choose Show the difference to add two columns: Superseded the approximate figure an earlier version of the page computed and Difference . Differences of 1 Lc or more are highlighted. Choose Hide to remove them the default . 6. Look at The ladder for a chart of the steps' contrast. The Metric choice WCAG 2.2 or APCA"},{"t":"Export tokens","d":"Export the ramp, key set or contrast table as CSS, SCSS, JSON or CSV, share a link, and analyse a list of colours.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/export-tokens.html","h":["Steps","File names","What each format contains","The link","Analyse a list of colours","Result"],"x":" 1. Build the ramp you want on the Lab tab. 2. Open the Export tab. 3. Under What to take , choose: The ramp — every step of the Lab's ramp; The key set — the 50–950 or 50–900 ladder chosen on the Ramps tab; The contrast table — the ramp with its contrast figures; A link to this view . 4. Under As , choose a format. Only formats that fit are offered: CSS, SCSS, JSON or CSV for the ramp and key set; CSV or JSON for the contrast table; URL for the link. 5. Check Exactly what you will get : the preview and its size in bytes. 6. Select the download button, which names the file for example Download tonal 2563eb.css , or Copy to clipboard . For a link the button reads Copy the link . Choice File The ramp tonal <hex .<ext The key set tonal <hex 50 950.<ext or tonal <hex 50 900.<ext The contrast table tonal <hex contrast.<ext <hex is your base colour without , in lower case. Every file records how the ramp was made: the base, engine, mixing space, step count and gamma, and a footer stating that OKLab was fed linear sRGB, WCAG 2.2, APCA W3 0.1.9 and the D65 white. CSS — custom properties in :root , one per step, with a comment giving OKLab L, WCAG ratio against white and APCA Lc against whi"},{"t":"Make tints, shades, tones and key sets","d":"Build tints, shades, tones, a neutral ladder and 50–950 or 50–900 key sets, and choose the space they are mixed in.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/tints-shades-tones.html","h":["The sets","Mixing spaces","Steps","Result"],"x":" Set How it is made Number of swatches Tints — toward white Your colour mixed with white in equal steps, from 0% your colour to 100% white Steps + 1 Shades — toward black Your colour mixed with black, from your colour to black Steps + 1 Tones — toward grey Your colour mixed with mid grey 808080 , from your colour to that grey Steps + 1 Neutral ladder Greys from black to white; each value is i ÷ steps − 1 ^γ Steps Key set 50–950 Keys 50, 100 … 900, 950. Below 500 your colour is mixed towards white by 1 − key ÷ 500 ; 500 is your colour; above 500 it is mixed towards black by key − 500 ÷ 500 11 Key set 50–900 The same ladder with keys 50 to 900 10 The key sets borrow the Tailwind and Material key names only. They are not the Tailwind or Material palettes: Tailwind's colours are hand tuned per hue, and Material's tonal palettes are specified in HCT at fixed tones. The Mix in setting chooses the space in which tints, shades, tones and key sets are interpolated. It changes the middle of a mix, not its ends. Choice Effect OKLab default Perceptually even mixes; hues stay steady CIELAB Mixes in CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ against D65 HSL Mixes in hue, saturation and lightness sRGB linear In the current ve"},{"t":"Tonal Steps reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/reference.html","h":["Lab tab","Ramps tab","Contrast tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/tonal steps tints shades/ Control What it does Values or range Default Base colour field and picker The colour every step is built from Six digit HEX 2563EB Random base Picks a random base colour Button — Ramp engine How the main ramp is built HSL lightness; Equal luminance HSL lightness Mix in Space for tints, shades, tones and key sets sRGB linear; CIELAB; OKLab; HSL OKLab Steps Number of ramp steps 3 to 21 11 Easing γ Bends the Equal luminance targets and the neutral ladder 0.4 to 2.6, step 0.05 1.0 Full ramp Adds the ramp to The other sets On or off On Tints — toward white Shows tints On or off Off Shades — toward black Shows shades On or off Off Tones — toward grey Shows tones On or off Off Neutral ladder Shows greys On or off Off In the current version, sRGB linear mixes the same way as OKLab. Readout What it shows Caption Steps, engine and mixing space Base note The base HEX, whether it is one of the steps \"step n\" or \"not a step\" and γ Strip and step rows Each step's swatch, HEX, OKLab L and contrast against white Base OKLab L , Largest step , Smallest step , Evenness Lightness and step size statistics in O"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Tonal Steps","d":"Fixes for common problems in Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do My base colour is not in the ramp The engines step lightness or luminance evenly from white to black; the base rarely lands exactly on a step. The base note says \"not a step\" Expected. Use the key sets, where 500 is always your colour, or tints and shades, which start from it Changing Mix in does not change the ramp The mixing space applies to tints, shades, tones and key sets, not to the main ramp Tick a set under Also show to see the effect sRGB linear gives the same result as OKLab In the current version the sRGB linear option mixes in OKLab Use CIELAB or HSL for a visibly different mix Easing γ does nothing Easing applies only to Equal luminance and the neutral ladder Switch the engine to Equal luminance The Equal contrast engine is missing It produces the same ramp as Equal luminance, so it is not offered on the Lab tab Use Equal luminance; the Ramps tab shows both Pressing 3 shows a ramp that looks like Equal luminance 3 selects the Equal contrast engine, which gives the same colours Expected The base colour field ignores my value It needs a six digit HEX with Type a value such as D3AF37 The Metric choice on Contrast changes nothing Both WCA"},{"t":"Tonal Steps FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/docs/faq.html","h":["Which engine should I use?","Why are there two engines, not three?","Why is OKLab used to measure the steps?","What is the difference between tints, shades and tones?","Are the 50–950 keys the Tailwind colours?","Is APCA a requirement?","Why does the APCA sign change?","Can I use more than 21 steps?","Does anything leave my browser?"],"x":" Use HSL lightness for a quick, familiar ramp. Use Equal luminance when you want steps tied to WCAG contrast, and adjust easing so the steps look even. The Ramps tab measures how even each one is. Equal steps in WCAG contrast ratio are, mathematically, equal steps in relative luminance. The third engine produced the same colours as Equal luminance, so it is not offered as a separate choice. OKLab lightness tracks perceived lightness well, so gaps in OKLab L show whether a ramp looks evenly spaced. You can switch to CIELAB L or relative Y on the Ramps tab. A tint adds white, a shade adds black, and a tone adds grey. All three start from your base colour. No. They are this tool's ladder with Tailwind's key names: mixed towards white below 500 and towards black above. Tailwind's own colours are tuned by hand per hue. No. APCA is a working draft of what WCAG 3 may adopt. WCAG 2.2 ratios remain the published requirement. The tool shows both. APCA Lc is signed. Positive and negative values mark which colour is lighter, because APCA treats dark text on light backgrounds differently from light text on dark. No. The range is 3 to 21. No. Ramps, contrast and exports are computed and created "},{"t":"Tonal Steps: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for Tonal Steps.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the tool shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the figures are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Tonal Steps shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts in Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" These keys work when the focus is not in a text box, slider or list. Key What it does 1 Ramp engine: HSL lightness 2 Ramp engine: Equal luminance 3 Ramp engine: Equal contrast gives the same colours as Equal luminance R Random base colour Esc Closes a full screen chart Mouse What it does Double click a chart Opens it full screen Hover a swatch in The other sets Shows its HEX, luminance Y and contrast against black "},{"t":"Tonal Steps glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" AA, AAA, AA large — WCAG 2.2 contrast ratings: AAA at 7:1 or more, AA at 4.5:1 or more, AA large at 3:1 or more for large text . Below 3:1 the tool shows Fail . APCA Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm — a contrast method by Myndex; the tool runs version APCA W3 0.1.9. Its result, Lc , is signed. CIELAB L\\ a\\ b\\ — a CIE colour space with lightness L and opponent axes a and b , computed here against the D65 white. Easing γ — an exponent that bends where steps fall in the Equal luminance engine and the neutral ladder. Evenness — how much the gaps between neighbouring steps stray from their average, as ±%. Smaller is more even. HSL — hue, saturation and lightness: a simple rearrangement of RGB. HSL lightness is a coordinate, not a measure of perceived lightness. Key set — a ladder of colours named by keys such as 50, 100 … 900, as used in design system palettes. LCh — CIELAB expressed as lightness, chroma and hue angle. Linear sRGB — sRGB values with the transfer curve removed, proportional to light. OKLab and luminance need it as input. Mixing space — the colour space in which two colours are interpolated. It changes the middle of a mix. Neutral ladder — a scale of greys from b"},{"t":"Tonal Steps limits and accuracy","d":"What the Tonal Steps figures rest on, how precise they are, and what the tool does not claim.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Standard values","This tool's own","Precision","Current-version caveats","Not a substitute for"],"x":" WCAG 2.2 ratios and ratings use relative luminance from linear sRGB with the BT.709 weights, exactly as WCAG defines. APCA Lc runs APCA W3 0.1.9 as published: a plain 2.4 power, separate exponent pairs for each polarity, the soft clamp below Y 0.022 and the ±0.027 low clip offset. APCA itself is a working draft, not a ratified requirement. OKLab uses Ottosson's matrices on linear sRGB. CIELAB follows CIE 015:2018 against D65. The ramp engines are the tool's own constructions. Equal luminance searches HSL lightness at the base's hue and saturation for each target luminance; the first and last steps are exactly white and black. The key sets borrow Tailwind and Material key names only. Nothing here is a Tailwind or Material colour. Evenness is the tool's own measure: the largest deviation of a step size from the mean step size, as a percentage. All colours are 8 bit sRGB; HEX values are rounded to the nearest code value, so luminance and contrast figures reflect the rounded colour. OKLab L is shown to three or four decimals, WCAG ratios to two, APCA Lc to one. sRGB linear mixing produces the same result as OKLab. The Metric choice on the Contrast tab does not change the table. The co"},{"t":"Tonal Steps privacy","d":"What Tonal Steps does with your colours and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Everything runs in your browser. Ramps, sets, contrast figures and list analyses are computed on your device. Exports are created locally and saved through your browser's download, or copied to your clipboard when you choose. The link carries the base colour, engine, step count, gamma and mixing space. Anyone with the link sees them. Colours you paste into Analyse a list stay in the page. Save to Library stores a palette in your Auric Artisan Library. The page loads the site's shared features like every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"Tonal Steps release notes","d":"User-facing changes to Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version (2026 workbench rebuild)","May 2026"],"x":" Tabs are now Lab , Ramps , Contrast , Data , Export and Reference . OKLab now receives linear sRGB, as its definition requires. OKLab lightness values, the lightness chart and the OKLab mixing mode changed for every tone except black, white and the primaries. The Lab offers two ramp engines instead of three: the equal contrast engine produced the same colours as equal luminance and ran in reverse . The Ramps tab shows all three side by side. The equal luminance engine's end steps are exactly white and black. The APCA column now runs APCA W3 0.1.9 as published. The Contrast tab can show the former approximate figure and the difference. The \"Tailwind 50–950\" and \"Material 50–900\" scales are now presented as key sets that borrow the names only. New evenness measures in OKLab L, CIELAB L and relative luminance. Exports now carry a header recording the base, engine, mixing space, steps and gamma, and a footer recording the OKLab input, WCAG and APCA versions. The share link control works and the link field always shows the current link. The Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to Tonal Steps","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tonal-steps/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Check one text and background pair in depth M Gradient Palette ../../../image and file tools/m gradient palette/README.md Multi stop gradients and ramps across colour spaces Design Engine ../../../colour workspace/design engine/README.md Generate a whole design system with accessible OKLCH ramps Basic Colour Tools ../../../colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Quick palettes, gradients and conversions Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md See whether ramp colours fit a target space The Vocabulary of Color: Hue, Saturation, Value, Tint, Tone, and Shade — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 29 vocabulary of color hue saturation value Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contrast — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 wcag contrast accessible color CIELAB and LCH Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cielab and lch explained Black, White, and Gray: The Achromatic Colors — http"},{"t":"Tone Mapping","d":"What the Tone Mapping lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to map your first frame.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" A real scene can hold far more light than any display can show: a sunlit window may be thousands of times brighter than the shadows in the room. Tone mapping is the curve that squeezes that range into the display's range while deciding what to keep — shadow detail, mid tones, or colour in the highlights. The Tone Mapping lab runs a frame through an eleven step pipeline you control: decode the source, convert it to a working space with white point adaptation, set exposure, apply an optional low level operator, apply the tone curve, grade it, convert to the target display space with gamut mapping, and encode it for output. It offers seven working tone curves — clipping, Reinhard, Uchimura Gran Turismo , Hable filmic, the Narkowicz fit of the ACES look, a soft log curve and your own three point curve — and shows two retired operators on the Operators tab for comparison. You can work on built in test scenes or your own image, read the result on a histogram, waveform, vectorscope and false colour map, compare two versions side by side, and export the tone curve as a 1D .cube or CSV, or the whole pipeline as a 3D .cube LUT. Game, 3D and VFX artists choosing a tone curve for renders. Col"},{"t":"Tone Mapping documentation","d":"The guides, reference and help pages for the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder explains how to use the Tone Mapping lab: a screen tour, task guides for mapping, comparing, measuring and exporting, a complete reference and help pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the lab, the six tabs and the pipeline map a frame.md map a frame.md Source, exposure, curve, grade and output for one frame compare operators.md compare operators.md The Operators tab and what each curve does read the scopes.md read the scopes.md Histogram, waveform, vectorscope, false colour and A/B export a lut.md export a lut.md 1D and 3D .cube , CSV, links and colour lists reference.md reference.md Every control, readout and export troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started with Tone Mapping","d":"Open the Tone Mapping lab, learn its tabs and the eleven-step pipeline, and read your first mapped frame.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the lab","Key ideas","A tour of the screen","Read your first frame","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/tone mapping/. The heading is Tone Mapping . All processing happens in your browser. Scene referred values describe light in the scene. They start at 0 and can go far above 1; 0.18 is the conventional mid grey , and 1.0 is often treated as diffuse white. Display referred values run from 0 to 1, where 1 is the brightest the display shows. A tone curve tone mapping operator maps scene values to display values. A good curve keeps mid grey where you expect it and rolls highlights off gently instead of clipping them. Exposure is measured in stops EV . One stop doubles or halves the light, and it is applied before the curve, so it changes which part of the curve the scene lands on. A note at the top warns that two of the nine operators the page once offered were one line stand ins; see the Data tab. Tab What it is for Lab The pipeline controls, the mapped frame and the curve Operators All nine operators on one table and one chart Scopes Histogram, waveform, vectorscope, false colour, A/B split and timing Data The eight datasets and transforms the lab rests on, with their status Export Curve and pipeline LUTs, CSV, a link, a"},{"t":"Compare operators","d":"Compare all nine operators by what they return for chosen inputs, where they reach white, and how their curves look.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/compare-operators.html","h":["The nine operators","Steps","Reading the result","Result"],"x":" Operator Source Formula or shape Offered in the Lab None clip — Clamps to 0–1 Yes Reinhard Reinhard et al. 2002 L ÷ 1 + L ; approaches 1 but never reaches it Yes Uchimura / Gran Turismo Uchimura 2017 A toe, a linear section and a shoulder blended together Yes Hable filmic Hable 2010 Uncharted 2 A filmic curve with six constants, exposure bias 2.0, white point 11.2 Yes Narkowicz fit Narkowicz 2016 x 2.51x + 0.03 ÷ x 2.43x + 0.59 + 0.14 , clamped. Approximates the look of ACES; it is not the Academy's transform Yes Log soft This tool log2 1 + v ÷ log2 11 Yes Custom 1D curve This tool Knee, mid and shoulder Yes Gamma domain scale This tool; formerly labelled \"BT.2446 Method A\" Y × k^2.4, a constant multiplication about 0.004 at the default peaks that turns mid grey nearly black No Scaled Reinhard This tool; formerly labelled \"BT.2446 Method C\" reinhard Y × r ÷ r, which can never exceed 1 ÷ r 0.1 at the default ratio of 10 No The last two are not tone curves and do not implement ITU R BT.2446. They are shown so that old links still open and so you can see what they did. 1. Set the Display peak and Source peak on the Lab tab. They only affect the two retired operators. 2. Open the Oper"},{"t":"Export a LUT","d":"Export the tone curve as a 1D .cube or CSV, the whole pipeline as a 3D .cube, a link to the view, and map a list of colours.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/export-a-lut.html","h":["Steps","The files","The link","Map a list of colours","Result"],"x":" A LUT lookup table stores a colour transform as a table so another program — a grading application, a game engine, a video tool — can apply it. A 1D LUT maps each channel on its own; a 3D LUT maps every RGB combination and can carry cross channel steps such as saturation, hue and gamut conversion. The .cube format is the Adobe Cube LUT specification. 1. Set up the frame on the Lab tab. 2. Open Export . 3. Under What to take , choose: The tone curve — step 5 of the pipeline only; The whole pipeline — all eleven steps; A link to this view . 4. Under As , choose a format: .cube or CSV for the curve; .cube for the pipeline; URL for the link. 5. For the tone curve, choose the Input domain : 0 – 1 default or 0 – 12 . It is written into the file as DOMAIN MIN and DOMAIN MAX or, in the CSV, as the input range . 6. Check Exactly what you will get : a preview long files show the start and end , the size in bytes and the number of lines. 7. Read What this file carries, of the eleven steps the viewport ran : a tick or cross for each step. A curve export carries only step 5. 8. Select the download button it names the file or Copy to clipboard . For a link, the button reads Copy the link . Choi"},{"t":"Map a frame","d":"Choose a source, set exposure and a tone curve, grade the result and set the output for your display.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/map-a-frame.html","h":["1. Choose the source","2. Set exposure","3. Choose a tone curve","4. Optional low-level operator","5. Grade","6. Output","Presets","Result"],"x":" 1. Under Source , choose HDR test scene , Exposure gradient , ColorChecker patches or Uploaded image . 2. For Uploaded image , select Choose a file and pick an image. The file name replaces \"no file\" and a message confirms the load. 3. Tell the lab how the source was written: encoding: Linear scene , sRGB , PQ ST 2084 , HLG inverse OETF , Gamma 2.2 or Gamma 2.4 ; primaries: Rec.709 , Display P3 , Rec.2020 or ACEScg AP1 ; white point: D65 , D60 or D50 . An ordinary PNG or JPEG is 8 bit sRGB: choose sRGB encoding and Rec.709 primaries for it. Its values stop at 1.0, so there are no true highlights above white for the curve to shape; use Exposure to push it into the curve's shoulder. The built in scenes are generated with values above 1. The chip over the frame says Scene referred when the encoding is linear and Display referred otherwise. Move Exposure from −6 to +6 EV steps of 0.1 . Each stop doubles or halves the values before the curve. Watch the histogram behind the curve slide along it. Select one of the seven curves under Tone curve : None clip , Reinhard , Uchimura / Gran Turismo , Hable filmic default , Narkowicz fit , Log soft or Custom 1D curve . See Compare operators comp"},{"t":"Read the scopes","d":"Use the histogram, waveform, vectorscope, false-colour map and A/B split to judge a mapped frame.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/read-the-scopes.html","h":["The three scopes","The false-colour exposure map","Compare two versions (A / B)","Timing","Controls that were removed","Result"],"x":" The Scopes tab measures the mapped output — the end the question is about. The note at the top names the working and target spaces and the operator. Scope What it shows How to read it Histogram — output, 256 bins How many pixels sit at each output level A pile up at the right edge means clipped highlights; at the left, crushed shadows Waveform — output luma by column Brightness of each column of the image, left to right The dashed line is display white. A trace pressed flat against it is clipping Vectorscope — output chroma Colour direction and strength, after gamut mapping Distance from the centre is saturation; angle is hue. It shows only what the target can carry 1. Tick Show the exposure map under False colour . The frame on the Lab tab is replaced by bands of colour. 2. Read the key under False colour, and the peak it is counted against . Pixels are coloured by estimated luminance: Up to nits Colour 0.01 Black 0.1 Deep violet 1 Blue 10 Teal 100 Green 203 Yellow 203 nits is the HDR diffuse white of ITU R BT.2408 1,000 Orange 4,000 Red 10,000 Magenta Above White 3. The note reports the source's brightest pixel, using the Source peak , and greys out bands the source cannot reach"},{"t":"Tone Mapping reference","d":"Every control, readout, option and export in the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/reference.html","h":["Lab tab","Operators tab","Scopes tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Save to Library"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/gamut and rendering/tone mapping/ Control What it does Values Default Source The frame to map HDR test scene; Exposure gradient; ColorChecker patches; Uploaded image HDR test scene Choose a file Picks an image shown for Uploaded image Image files \"no file\" Source encoding How the source values are decoded step 1 Linear scene ; sRGB; PQ ST 2084 ; HLG inverse OETF ; Gamma 2.2; Gamma 2.4 Linear scene Source primaries The source's RGB space Rec.709; Display P3; Rec.2020; ACEScg AP1 Rec.709 Source white The source's white point D65; D60; D50 D65 Control What it does Values Default Exposure Multiplies by 2^EV before the curve step 3 −6 to +6 EV, step 0.1 0.0 EV Tone curve The operator step 5 None clip ; Reinhard; Uchimura / Gran Turismo; Hable filmic; Narkowicz fit; Log soft ; Custom 1D curve Hable filmic Use the custom curve instead Uses the knee / mid / shoulder curve whatever is selected On or off Off Custom curve knee, mid, shoulder The three points of the custom curve 0 to 1 each 0.15, 0.5, 0.85 Low level operator A per channel function before the curve step 4 None; Add; Multiply; Soft clip; Power; Sigmoid; Exp; Log; Tanh None Paramete"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Tone Mapping","d":"Fixes for common problems in the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do My photo looks flat or unchanged by the curve An 8 bit PNG or JPEG stops at 1.0, so there are no highlights above white for the curve to compress Raise Exposure , or use the built in HDR test scene to compare curves My photo looks too dark or washed out The source encoding does not match the file For ordinary images choose sRGB encoding and Rec.709 primaries Changing Display peak or Source peak changes nothing The seven working curves do not use the peaks Expected. The peaks affect the retired operators and the false colour map Soft compress looks exactly like Clip In the current version the two give the same result Use Preserve hue to keep channel ratios in out of gamut colours The HDR 1000 preset looks pale and washed out on my screen PQ output is an HDR encoding a display value of 1.0 is encoded as 10,000 nits , and an ordinary screen shows PQ code values as if they were sRGB Use sRGB output for viewing on a standard display; use PQ only when exporting for HDR Linear axis , Log axis or Film stops does not change the chart They set the custom curve's knee, mid and shoulder Tick Use the custom curve instead to see their effect The custom curve fi"},{"t":"Tone Mapping FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/docs/faq.html","h":["Which curve should I use?","Is \"Narkowicz fit\" the ACES tone mapper?","What happened to the BT.2446 operators?","What is the difference between scene-referred and display-referred?","Why ACEScg as the default working space?","Which export reproduces the preview?","Can I load an EXR or HDR file?","Can I save and reload my settings as a file?","Is my image uploaded?"],"x":" For a photographic look with gentle highlight roll off, Hable filmic or the Narkowicz fit are common choices. Reinhard is simple and never clips, but never reaches pure white. Compare them on the Operators tab at mid grey and scene white before deciding. No. It is Krzysztof Narkowicz's 2016 curve fit that approximates the look of the ACES output transforms. The Academy's own transforms are not implemented. The two operators once labelled BT.2446 Method A and Method C did not implement ITU R BT.2446. One multiplied by a small constant and turned the frame nearly black; the other could never exceed a 10% linear grey. They are renamed Gamma domain scale and Scaled Reinhard, shown on the Operators tab, and no longer offered in the Lab. Scene referred values describe light in the scene and can exceed 1. Display referred values are 0 to 1 of what the display can show. The lab treats a linear source as scene referred and anything encoded sRGB, PQ, HLG, gamma as display referred. ACEScg is a wide, linear working space designed for rendering and compositing. Grading in it and converting to the display at the end is common practice. You can choose Rec.709, Display P3 or Rec.2020 instead. Th"},{"t":"Tone Mapping: supporting pages","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy for the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the guides in docs/ ../docs/README.md . File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the lab shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the results are and are not related.md related.md Related tools and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md What has changed for users privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Tone Mapping shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse shortcuts in the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The lab has no single key shortcuts of its own. Shortcut Where What it does Double click A chart or scope Opens it full screen Esc Full screen view Closes it "},{"t":"Tone Mapping glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" ACEScg AP1 — a linear, wide gamut working space from the Academy Color Encoding System, with a D60 white. Bradford transform — a chromatic adaptation method used to move colours between white points. .cube — the Adobe Cube LUT file format, used by many grading and video applications. Display referred — values relative to what a display can show, from 0 black to 1 peak white . Dither — tiny random noise added before quantising to 8 bits, to hide banding. EV exposure value, stop — a factor of two in light. False colour — an overlay that paints each pixel by its brightness band instead of its colour. Gamut mapping — handling colours outside the target space: clipping, compressing or scaling them. Grade — creative adjustments after the curve: contrast, saturation, lift, gamma, gain, temperature, tint, hue and vibrance. Hable filmic — a filmic tone curve published by John Hable 2010 . HLG — hybrid log gamma, an HDR transfer function ARIB STD B67 . Histogram — a count of pixels at each level. Lift, gamma, gain — adjustments that mainly move the shadows, the mid tones and the highlights. LUT lookup table — a table that stores a colour transform. A 1D LUT maps each channel alone; a 3D LUT"},{"t":"Tone Mapping limits and accuracy","d":"What the Tone Mapping lab implements exactly, what is its own, and what it does not do.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Exact to the source","This tool's own","Not implemented","Current-version caveats","Precision"],"x":" Transfer functions : the sRGB curve, PQ SMPTE ST 2084, constants as the standard gives them and HLG the OETF and its inverse; the OOTF is not applied . Primaries and white points of Rec.709, Display P3, Rec.2020 and ACEScg. Bradford adaptation between white points. Operators with their published constants: Reinhard 2002 , Hable 2010 , Narkowicz 2016 and Uchimura 2017 . Log soft and the custom curve . The grade controls, the low level operators and the gamut mapping options. Working luminance is read from each working space's own matrix, so saturation and vibrance mix towards the right grey. ITU R BT.2446 Methods A and C. The two operators once named after them are kept as \"Gamma domain scale\" and \"Scaled Reinhard\" and are not tone curves. The Academy's ACES transforms RRT and ODT . The Narkowicz fit approximates their look. HDR image files such as OpenEXR. Uploaded images are 8 bit and carry no absolute luminance. The operators work per channel, not on luminance, so strongly saturated highlights can shift hue. Soft compress gives the same result as Clip . Display peak and Source peak affect only the two retired operators and the false colour display; they do not scale the working "},{"t":"Tone Mapping privacy","d":"What the Tone Mapping lab does with your images and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Your image stays on your device. An uploaded image is decoded and processed in your browser, and is never sent to a server. Exports are created locally and saved through your browser's download, or copied to your clipboard when you choose. The page address is updated as you work to record the operator, exposure, source encoding, display peak, output encoding and target primaries. Copying or sharing the address shares those settings, never your image. Stored A and B frames exist only in the open page. Save to Library stores an image of the mapped frame in your Auric Artisan Library. The page loads the site's shared features like every other page on auricartisan.com; see the site's privacy policy. "},{"t":"Tone Mapping release notes","d":"User-facing changes to the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version (2026 workbench rebuild)","May 2026"],"x":" Tabs are now Lab , Operators , Scopes , Data , Export and Reference . The Lab offers seven tone curves instead of nine. The two labelled BT.2446 Method A and C were renamed Gamma domain scale and Scaled Reinhard and moved to the Operators tab, because neither implements BT.2446. The \"ACES\" operator is named Narkowicz fit. Display peak and source peak are now two separate controls. The grade mixes towards the working space's own luminance, and the hue control rotates hue. Mark out of gamut pixels now paints an overlay. The false colour scale was rebuilt with a key, including the 203 nit HDR diffuse white. Scene reference white, Highlight stress and the zebra thresholds were removed; the Scopes tab lists them as controls that did nothing. Export now offers a 1D curve .cube or CSV with a stated domain, and a 3D .cube that runs the whole pipeline, with a preview and a list of the steps each file carries. The Tone Mapping User Guide was published in the site's Documentation library, describing the earlier version. "},{"t":"Related to Tone Mapping","d":"Tools and Learn articles that go well with the Tone Mapping lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Colorimetry and rendering","u":"website/tools/colorimetry-and-rendering/tone-mapping/others/related.html","h":["Tools","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Tool Why HDR Gamut Plot ../../hdr gamut plot/README.md PQ and HLG curves in cd/m², and gamuts in ICtCp and Jzazbz LUT Lab ../../../image and file tools/lut lab/README.md Build, read and preview .cube LUTs Gamut Mapping ../../gamut map/README.md Compare gamut mapping methods between RGB spaces Gamut Lab ../../gamut lab/README.md The working and target spaces, their primaries and curves Color in Real Time 3D: Albedo, PBR, and Tone Mapping — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 02 color in real time 3d albedo pbr tone mapping HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HLG, and Modern Displays — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 hdr wide gamut pq hlg modern displays Spectral Rendering: Why Three Numbers Aren't Enough — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 22 spectral rendering beyond rgb The site's Documentation library https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/ has an earlier Tone Mapping User Guide . This documentation follows the current page. "},{"t":"Perception and spectral tools","d":"What the three perception and neuroscience tools and the two spectral tools on auricartisan.com are for, where to find them, and which one to open for each job.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/README.html","h":["Where to find them","The tools","Which tool for which job","What the five share","In this folder"],"x":" This group holds five workbenches for questions that sit behind a colour value rather than in it. Three of them are about the observer: how a colour travels through the early visual system, how a scene looks to a different visual system, and how to measure the faintest contrast a person can see. Two of them are about light and matter: what colour a dye bath makes under a named light, and how a material looks under a light source at a given angle. All five are teaching and exploration tools that show their working. Each page says, in a strip at the top that cannot be closed, what its pictures and numbers rest on. Each has a Data tab that lists every table, formula and model the tool uses and marks it Verbatim taken unchanged from a publication or standard , Computed derived from verbatim data by stated arithmetic , Stand in this tool's own values, chosen to be plausible or Absent not held, with a note on what it would take . A figure that rests on a stand in or an absent entry is never presented as a published value. None of the five is a clinical, physiological or laboratory instrument. Everything runs in your browser. Nothing you load, type or measure is uploaded, and nothing lea"},{"t":"Industrial Dye Chemistry (Dye in Solution)","d":"What the Dye in Solution tool does, who it is for, where to find it and how to watch a first pH indicator change colour.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Industrial Dye Chemistry tool, whose page is titled Dye in solution , models a dye bath one wavelength at a time. You choose up to four dyes, their concentrations and the bath's pH and path length. The tool works out how much light the bath absorbs at each of 81 wavelengths from 380 to 780 nm, what colour that makes under a light source you name, and how far that colour moves under the other lights it holds. Each dye is modelled as two forms, an acid form and a base form, each with its own absorption band. The pH sets how much of the dye is in each form, so a pH indicator changes colour as the two bands trade places, and the curves for every pH cross at one wavelength, the isosbestic point. Absorbance follows the Beer–Lambert law, and the page flags when the bath is too strongly coloured for that law to hold. Colour is computed against the CIE 1931 standard observer under daylight D65 or D50, tungsten illuminant A, or equal energy light E, and colour differences use CIEDE2000. The model is real; the dyes are not. The six preset dyes stand for classes of dye for example \"the methyl orange family\" with constants chosen by the tool, and their bands are drawn as Gaussians. You can"},{"t":"Using Dye in Solution","d":"Contents of the how-to documentation for the Dye in Solution tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to build and analyse a dye bath, from the first titration to exporting the spectrum. Start with getting started; the task guides can be read in any order; the reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs, the Lab screen tour and a first bath build a bath.md build a bath.md The six dyes, adding, muting and removing components, concentration, path length and Beer–Lambert run a titration.md run a titration.md pH, pKa, the base fraction, the two forms, the titration animation and the isosbestic point compare lights.md compare lights.md The four illuminants, the colour readouts, colour inconstancy against metamerism, dominant wavelength and purity run a tolerance sweep.md run a tolerance sweep.md The Method tab's sweep over concentration, path length and molar absorptivity use a measured spectrum.md use a measured spectrum.md Loading a UV–Vis spectrum into a dye's acid or base form export and share.md export and share.md The spectrum CSV, the bath JSON and links reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, readout, message and file format, with ranges and defaults troubleshooting.md trou"},{"t":"Getting started with Dye in Solution","d":"Open Dye in Solution, learn the layout of the Lab tab and read the default bath.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The six tabs","A tour of the Lab tab","Read the default bath","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/spectral tools/industrial dye chemistry/. The page opens on the Lab tab with a default bath: one Weak acid indicator standing for the methyl orange family at 34.0 µM, pKa 3.5, at pH 3.50, in a 1.0 cm path, lit by D65 daylight. A note strip above the tabs, which cannot be closed, says what an earlier version of the page got wrong and links to the Method and Safety tabs. Tab What it is for Lab Build the bath, see the spectrum, read the colour and compare the lights Method How the titration, Beer–Lambert law and light are modelled; the tolerance sweep Safety What the page does and does not know about hazards Data The register of 18 tables and formulas, with a status for each; load a measured spectrum here Export The spectrum CSV, the bath JSON and a link Reference Thirteen sources, filterable by whether they run The rail left , top to bottom: The bath — pH , Path length and Run the titration . The light — the illuminant menu. The components — the list of dyes in the bath, a menu of dyes to add, and Add , Mute and Remove . The selected dye — its name, what it stands for, and its pKa and Concentration sliders. Reset the bath . The stage right"},{"t":"Build a bath","d":"Add, select, mute and remove dyes, set concentration and path length, and understand absorbance and the Beer–Lambert law.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/build-a-bath.html","h":["Absorbance in brief","The six preset dyes","Add, select, mute and remove components","Set concentration and path length","Read the absorbance readouts","Try it"],"x":" A dye solution looks coloured because it absorbs some wavelengths of light more than others. Transmittance T is the fraction of light at a wavelength that gets through. Absorbance A is its negative base 10 logarithm, A = −log₁₀ T: an absorbance of 1 lets 10% through, 2 lets 1% through. The Beer–Lambert law says absorbance is proportional to how much dye the light meets: A = ε × c × l ε epsilon , the molar absorptivity , is the dye's own strength at that wavelength, in litres per mole per centimetre M⁻¹ cm⁻¹ . c is the concentration in moles per litre. The page shows it in micromolar µM, millionths of a mole per litre . l is the path length , the distance the light travels through the solution, in centimetres. Absorbances of several dyes, and of the two forms of one dye, simply add. So doubling the concentration or the path length doubles the absorbance at every wavelength. The law holds well only up to about A = 1. Above that, real solutions fall below the straight line, because dye molecules clump together and spectrophotometers have finite bandwidth. The page flags a bath whose absorbance exceeds 1 anywhere. Every preset stands for a class of dye and says which; none is a named "},{"t":"Compare lights","d":"Choose the illuminant, read the colour readouts, compare the bath under every light, and understand colour inconstancy, metamerism, dominant wavelength and purity.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/compare-lights.html","h":["Why the light matters","Choose the illuminant","Read the colour readouts","Compare the bath under every light","Colour inconstancy is not metamerism","Dominant wavelength and excitation purity","Try it"],"x":" A dye does not have a colour on its own. The colour you see is the light that the bath lets through, and that depends on what light went in. The page computes it wavelength by wavelength: the illuminant's power × the bath's transmittance × the CIE 1931 2° standard observer's colour matching functions, summed over 81 samples from 380 to 780 nm at 5 nm. The observer is used at the 5 nm spacing it is published at, so no sample is interpolated. Under The light : Option What it is D65 — daylight, 6504 K default CIE standard average daylight, reconstructed from the published CIE daylight basis D50 — daylight, 5003 K Warmer daylight, the usual reference in graphic arts A — a blackbody at 2856 K Incandescent tungsten light, from Planck's law E — equal energy Equal power at every wavelength; a theoretical reference F11 is not offered. Fluorescent lamps such as F11, the light most often used in shops and the one a dyer most wants, have narrow mercury emission lines. The CIE publishes them as measured tables that cannot be computed from a formula, and the page does not hold them. It shows F11 as a card marked not held rather than offering a smooth imitation under that name. Readout Meaning s"},{"t":"Export and share","d":"Download the 81-row spectrum CSV and the whole-bath JSON, and copy a link that rebuilds the bath.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/export-and-share.html","h":["The spectrum CSV","The bath JSON","Links"],"x":" Open the Export tab. What to take switches the preview between The spectrum the first lines of the CSV , The whole bath the first part of the JSON and A link to this ; the note above it gives the row count. Nothing leaves the page until you press a button. Exports are never gated on a tick box. Button Result Download the spectrum Saves dye in solution spectrum.csv Download the bath Saves dye in solution bath.json Copy a link to this bath Copies a link; the message Link copied confirms it, or the link is shown if the clipboard is unavailable The file starts with header lines that state everything a reader needs to compare it with another spectrum: the time; the sampling 380–780 nm at 5 nm, 81 samples ; the observer CIE 1931 2°, not interpolated ; the illuminant; the bath's pH and path length; for each component: name and \" disabled \" if muted , concentration, pKa, both forms' λmax and ε, whether the band shape is MEASURED or SYNTHESISED, the base fraction at this pH and the isosbestic point; the peak absorbance and whether it is inside the Beer–Lambert linear range; which white point the swatch and the L\\ a\\ b\\ use; the colour inconstancy ΔE₀₀ to each other illuminant; statements t"},{"t":"Run a titration","d":"Change the pH, understand pKa, the base fraction and the two forms of a dye, animate a titration and find the isosbestic point.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/run-a-titration.html","h":["How pH changes a dye's colour","Change the pH","Animate a titration","Find the isosbestic point","Compare with the old model on the Method tab","Try it"],"x":" Many dyes, and all pH indicators, exist in two chemical forms: an acid form , written HA, which holds an extra hydrogen ion, and a base form , written A⁻, which has given it up. Each form has its own absorption band, so each has its own colour. The pKa is the pH at which half the dye is in each form. The Henderson–Hasselbalch relation gives the share in the base form, the base fraction f: f = 1 ÷ 1 + 10^ pKa − pH Two pH units below the pKa, about 1% of the dye is in the base form; at the pKa, 50%; two units above, about 99%. What a spectrophotometer measures is the weighted sum of the two bands: A λ = c × l × 1 − f × ε HA λ + f × ε A λ Because the total amount of dye does not change, there is one wavelength where the two forms absorb equally. At that wavelength the absorbance is the same at every pH, so every curve of a titration passes through one point: the isosbestic point . It is the signature of a clean two form equilibrium. 1. Select the dye you want to study in The components list. 2. Drag pH 0–14, step 0.05, default 3.50 . 3. Watch Base fraction for the selected dye, three decimals and the plot. As the pH rises past the pKa, the filled curve moves from the acid band to the"},{"t":"Run a tolerance sweep","d":"Estimate how far a bath's colour moves when concentration, path length and molar absorptivity vary within stated tolerances.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/run-a-tolerance-sweep.html","h":["Run it","Read the result","How the draws are made","What this is not"],"x":" A real bath never matches its recipe exactly. The balance and flask set the concentration to within a tolerance, the cell's specification sets the path length, and a published molar absorptivity comes with its own uncertainty. The sweep on the Method tab asks: if each of those varies within its tolerance, how far does the colour move, in ΔE₀₀? 1. Set up the bath on the Lab tab. 2. Open the Method tab. The sweep controls are under The sweep on the rail: Control Range and step Default Concentration ±0–20%, step 0.5 ±2.0% Path length ±0–2 mm, step 0.01 ±0.10 mm Molar absorptivity ±0–30%, step 0.5 ±5.0% Draws 100–2000, step 100 500 3. Replace the defaults with your own tolerances if you know them. The defaults are the tool's guess at a hand weighed bath in a 10 mm cell, not a measurement of your laboratory. 4. Select Run the sweep . A message reports how many draws took how long. Under How far the colour moves when the tolerances do , three figures appear, each a ΔE₀₀ from the unperturbed bath under the current light: Figure Meaning Median Half the draws moved less than this 95th percentile 95% of draws moved less than this Worst draw The largest movement seen The note beside the head"},{"t":"Use a measured spectrum","d":"Replace a drawn dye band with a measured UV–Vis molar absorptivity spectrum, and go back to the drawn bands.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/use-a-measured-spectrum.html","h":["Prepare the file","Load it","What changes","Go back"],"x":" The preset dyes' bands are drawn as Gaussian curves around a stated λmax. Real absorption bands are asymmetric, with a longer tail towards the blue, and the tails matter most where dyes overlap in a mixture. If you have a UV–Vis scan of a real dye, you can load it into one form of a dye in the bath. A plain text file: .csv , .tsv or .txt . Two columns per line: wavelength in nm and molar absorptivity ε, in M⁻¹ cm⁻¹ . Columns may be separated by commas, semicolons, tabs or spaces. At least eight numeric rows, covering at least 420 to 680 nm . Lines that are not two numbers headers, comments are skipped. Negative values are read as 0. If your instrument exported absorbance rather than molar absorptivity, divide each absorbance by the concentration in mol/L and path length in cm of the measured sample first. 1. On the Lab tab, select the dye whose band you want to replace in The components list. 2. Open the Data tab. Under Measure your own dye , choose Into the acid form or Into the base form . 3. Drop the file on Drop a spectrum , or select the area or press Enter or Space on it to choose the file. You can also drop the file directly on the spectrum plot on the Lab tab, or click the"},{"t":"Dye in Solution reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, message and file format in Dye in Solution, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — The bath","Lab tab — The light","Lab tab — The components and the selected dye","Lab tab — Spectrum plot","Lab tab — Readouts","Lab tab — The same bath under every light","Method tab","Safety tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages","File formats","Link parameters"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/spectral tools/industrial dye chemistry/ Tab Contents Lab Bath, light and component controls; the spectrum plot; colour, absorbance and wavelength readouts; the lights row Method Four explanation views and the tolerance sweep Safety The withdrawn hazard gate and what stays Data The register of 18 tables and formulas, filterable by status; the tab label shows the count; measured spectrum loader Export Spectrum CSV, bath JSON and link Reference Thirteen sources, filterable Links in the page text for example Method or Safety in the note strip switch to that tab. Control Range and step Default pH 0–14, step 0.05 3.50 Path length 0.1–10 cm, step 0.1 1.0 cm Run the titration Steps pH from 0 to 14 by 0.2 every 90 ms; reads Stop while running — Control Values Default Illuminant D65 — daylight, 6504 K , D50 — daylight, 5003 K , A — a blackbody at 2856 K , E — equal energy D65 Control What it does Values or range Default Component buttons Select a dye; show its swatch, pKa, concentration, band peaks and Stand in or Measured 1 to 4 dyes Weak acid indicator Dye menu The dye Add will add Six presets Weak acid indicator Add Adds the dye in the menu"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Dye in Solution","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for Dye in Solution: flags, refused spectra, component limits, the plot and links.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Beer–Lambert holds\" reads \"no\"","Moving pH changes almost nothing","\"Isosbestic point\" is highlighted or reads \"(weak)\" or \"none in range\"","The plot does not change when I change concentration or path length","The plot shows a different dye from the one I am editing","A file chooser opens when I click the spectrum","My spectrum file is refused","I cannot add a fifth dye or remove the last one","\"Inside sRGB\" reads \"no\"","Dominant wavelength starts with \"c\" and purity reads \"—\"","The sweep result looks out of date","A link did not restore a muted dye or my measured spectrum","I need F11, a fastness result or hazard information"],"x":" Why: the bath's absorbance is above 1 at some wavelength. Past that point real solutions depart from the law and spectrophotometers become unreliable, so the computed colour is less trustworthy. What to do: lower Concentration or Path length . For the default dye at pH 3.5, the limit is reached at about 54 µM in a 1 cm path. Why: the selected dye is one of the pH stable presets azo red, anthraquinone blue, yellow , whose two forms have nearly the same band, or the pH is far from the dye's pKa, where almost all of it is already in one form. What to do: use an indicator preset, or move the pH to within about two units of the pKa watch Base fraction . Why: weak means the two forms cross so deep in their tails below 5% of the peak that the point cannot be seen on the plot. none in range means they do not cross between 380 and 780 nm. What to do: nothing is wrong; it describes the dye. The mid range and high range indicators have weak crossings. Why: the plot shows the selected dye's molar absorptivity a property of the dye , not the bath's absorbance. What to do: read Peak absorbance and λmax for the bath, or export the spectrum CSV, whose absorbance column is the whole bath. Why: the"},{"t":"Dye in Solution FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Dye in Solution.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/docs/faq.html","h":["Are the preset dyes real products?","Can I use it to formulate a real recipe?","Does it model dye on fabric?","Why is there no F11 or other fluorescent light?","Is the \"ΔE₀₀\" in the lights row a metamerism index?","Which colour difference formula does it use?","Why do the swatch and the L*a*b* disagree when I change the light?","Can the tool tell me if a dye is hazardous?","Does it do lightfastness or wash-fastness tests?","Is my data uploaded?"],"x":" No. Each stands for a class of dye, such as \"the methyl orange family\", with constants chosen by the tool to be plausible. None is a named commercial substance, and every preset is marked Stand in . Not as it stands. The model two forms, Beer–Lambert, a stated light and observer is sound, but the dye data are the tool's own and the bands are Gaussian. With measured spectra for both forms of your dyes it becomes much closer, but it still models dye in solution, not on cloth. No. There is no substrate or reflectance mode in the current interface. The Data register describes a Kubelka–Munk model for opaque substrates as a stand in, and the Reference tab explains why it is not offered. Fluorescent illuminants are measured spectra with narrow emission lines, published as tables, and the page does not hold them. It will not substitute a smooth imitation under that name. No. It is colour inconstancy: one bath under two lights. Metamerism concerns two baths that match under one light and not under another. See Compare lights compare lights.md . CIEDE2000 CIE 142 2001 , the full formula including its rotation term, checked against published test pairs. On purpose. The swatch shows the ligh"},{"t":"Dye in Solution background","d":"Contents of the background material for the Dye in Solution tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the how to pages with the chemistry and colour terms the tool uses, its keyboard and pointer actions, a statement of what is published, what is the tool's own and what is not held including safety , related tools and articles, its history and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Chemistry and colour terms used in Dye in Solution shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Drop zones, Enter and Space , and tab links limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The data register entry by entry, precision, what is not held, and safety related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Dye in Solution shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Dye in Solution tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond these. Site wide shortcuts are described in Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . Action Where Result Drop a file The spectrum plot on the Lab tab, or Drop a spectrum on the Data tab Loads a measured spectrum into the form chosen on the Data tab Click The spectrum plot or Drop a spectrum Opens a file chooser Enter or Space Focused Drop a spectrum area Opens a file chooser Enter or Space A focused row on the Data tab Expands or collapses the row Click a tab name in the page text Note strip and hints Switches to that tab Tab Anywhere Moves between controls; sliders then respond to the arrow keys "},{"t":"Dye in Solution glossary","d":"Chemistry and colour terms used in the Dye in Solution tool, each explained briefly.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Absorbance A −log₁₀ of the fraction of light transmitted; A = 1 lets 10% through Acid form HA The protonated form of a dye, holding an extra hydrogen ion Base form A⁻ The deprotonated form of a dye Base fraction f The share of a dye in its base form at a given pH, from Henderson–Hasselbalch Beer–Lambert law A = ε × c × l: absorbance is proportional to molar absorptivity, concentration and path length CIE 1931 2° observer The standard set of colour matching functions describing average human colour vision for small fields CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ A colour space with lightness L\\ and opponent axes a\\ red–green and b\\ yellow–blue CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ The CIE's recommended formula for how different two colours look Colour inconstancy How far one sample's colour changes between two lights Complementary wavelength For purples, the wavelength on the opposite side of the white point, given instead of a dominant wavelength Concentration c Amount of dye per volume; shown in micromoles per litre µM Dominant wavelength The spectral colour that, mixed with the light's white, matches the sample Excitation purity How far a colour lies from the white point towards the spectral edge, as a percentage Ga"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Dye in Solution takes from published sources, what is its own, how precise it is, what it does not hold, and what it cannot tell you about safety.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the tool is","The data register, in plain terms","Precision","What the tool does not do","Safety"],"x":" A spectral model of a dye bath for learning and exploration. The physics and colorimetry follow published standards; the dyes are the tool's own inventions unless you load measured spectra. It is not a formulation system, a spectrophotometer, a fastness tester or a safety tool. Entry Status What it means for you CIE 1931 2° standard observer Verbatim Colours use the published 5 nm observer table, with no interpolated samples CIE D series eigenvector basis Verbatim D65 and D50 are reconstructed from the published daylight basis and land within 0.0003 of their published chromaticities sRGB primaries and transfer curve Verbatim The swatch and gamut flag use the published sRGB definition CIEDE2000 colour difference Verbatim Every ΔE₀₀ uses the full CIE 142 2001 formula The Beer–Lambert law Verbatim Absorbance is ε × c × l, additive over dyes and forms, flagged above A = 1 Henderson–Hasselbalch Verbatim The base fraction follows the standard relation The two species absorbance Computed Each dye is two forms weighted by pH, which is what produces an isosbestic point The isosbestic point Computed Located precisely between samples, with a strength Dominant wavelength and excitation purity"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Dye in Solution keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What leaves the page, and only when you ask","The rest of the page"],"x":" Every calculation: spectra, colours, the lights row and the tolerance sweep are computed in the page. Spectrum files you load are read from your disk by the page. They are not uploaded and are forgotten when you reload. Download the spectrum and Download the bath create files through your browser's normal download. The bath file includes the name of any spectrum file you loaded. Copy a link to this bath writes a link to your clipboard. It contains the pH, path length, light and each dye's preset, pKa and concentration, never your spectrum files. The tool page loads the site's usual pages, styles and scripts, and, depending on your cookie choices, advertising and consent based analytics, like the rest of auricartisan.com. See the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Dye in Solution tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — rebuilt as Dye in Solution","Earlier"],"x":" The site wide history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The entries below cover what changed for users of this tool. The page was rebuilt with six tabs Lab , Method , Safety , Data , Export , Reference . Changed: Each dye is now two forms acid and base weighted by pH, so the pH control changes every dye's colour through its pKa, and a titration shows an isosbestic point. Earlier, most presets did not respond to pH at all. The colour is computed under a named light source, and L\\ a\\ b\\ is taken against that light's own white. Earlier there was no light source. The spectrum is sampled at 5 nm from 380 to 780 nm, the grid the CIE observer is published on. The preset list is now six dye classes with the tool's own constants, instead of named commercial dyes with unsourced values. Dominant λ is now a true dominant wavelength with excitation purity, rather than the wavelength of peak transmittance. Added: the illuminant menu D65, D50, A, E and the lights row with colour inconstancy; the Beer–Lambert holds check; Base fraction and Isosbestic point ; the tolerance sweep; loading measured spectra; the Data register; header lines stating the method in every export. Removed:"},{"t":"Related tools and articles","d":"Tools and Learn articles related to Dye in Solution.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Industrial Dye Chemistry","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/industrial-dye-chemistry/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other tools on the site","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Material Lighting ../../material lighting/README.md — the same spectral approach for opaque materials: reflectance, illuminant and surface model. Perception and Vision ../../perception and vision/README.md — check how a dyed colour looks to viewers with colour vision deficiency. Illuminants ../../../colorimetry and rendering/illuminants/README.md — the standard light sources in detail. Chromatic adaptation ../../../colorimetry and rendering/chromatic adaptation/README.md — how colours are predicted to shift when the light changes. The Learn section is described in Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md . Color on Textiles: Dyeing, Printing, and Why Fabric Color Is Hard — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 10 color on textiles dyeing and printing Metamerism Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 metamerism Spectral Power Distributions and Why RGB Is Not Enough — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 spectral power distributions ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 26 delta e metrics cie76 ciede2000 itp Dye in Solution Developer Reference — h"},{"t":"Material Lighting (Material Under Light)","d":"What the Material Under Light tool does, who it is for, where to find it and how to render a first material under a chosen light.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Material Lighting tool, whose page is titled Material under light , computes the colour of a surface the way light actually produces it: one wavelength at a time. It multiplies three things at each of 81 wavelengths from 380 to 780 nm: the power of a light source the illuminant , the share of that light the material reflects its reflectance spectrum , and how much of the reflected light travels towards your eye at the angles you set the reflectance lobe . It then turns the result into a colour with the CIE 1931 standard observer and shows it as a shaded sphere, a swatch and a set of numbers. Because the calculation is spectral, the tool can show things a three channel RGB renderer cannot: why the same material looks different under daylight and tungsten, and why two materials that match under one light can part under another metamerism . It also compares your material under your chosen light with the same material under the reference light the CIE rule names for that light's colour temperature, and reports the difference as a CIEDE2000 colour difference. The twenty material presets are the tool's own curves, built from a flat level plus bell shaped bumps; none is a measurement"},{"t":"Using Material Under Light","d":"Contents of the how-to documentation for the Material Under Light tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to set up a scene, compare it with its reference light, test its sensitivity, load your own data and export. Start with getting started; the reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs, the Lab screen tour and a first scene set up a scene.md set up a scene.md Illuminants and colour temperature, the twenty materials, dielectric and conductor, roughness, the five lobes, the three angles compare with the reference.md compare with the reference.md Measured colour temperature, the reference rule, the rendering shift, the two white points, metamerism run a sensitivity sweep.md run a sensitivity sweep.md The Metrics tab: the sweep, and why CRI and TM 30 are withdrawn use a measured reflectance.md use a measured reflectance.md Loading a reflectance file and going back to the presets export and share.md export and share.md The spectrum CSV, the scene JSON and links reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, readout, message and file format, with ranges and defaults troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Black spheres, disabled sliders, clipping flags, refused files, links faq.md faq.md Sho"},{"t":"Getting started with Material Under Light","d":"Open Material Under Light, learn the layout of the Lab tab and read the default gold-under-daylight scene.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The six tabs","A tour of the Lab tab","Read the default scene","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/spectral tools/material lighting/. The page opens on the Lab tab with a default scene: Gold , as a dielectric with refractive index 1.50, under D65 — daylight, 6504 K , with the GGX lobe at roughness 0.40, the light 30° and the eye 20° from the surface normal, and 0° between them. A note strip above the tabs, which cannot be closed, says that two rendering figures from an earlier version were withdrawn and links to the Metrics and Method tabs. Tab What it is for Lab Set up the scene, see the spectrum and the sample, read the colour, compare with the reference light Method How a spectrum becomes a colour, how the reference is chosen, the five lobes, the two white points Metrics The sensitivity sweep, and the two withdrawn rendering indices Data The register of 17 tables and formulas, with a status for each; load a measured reflectance here Export The spectrum CSV, the scene JSON and a link Reference Fourteen sources, filterable The rail left , top to bottom: The light — the illuminant menu and Temperature used only by the last two options . The material — the material menu, Dielectric / Conductor , and Refractive index . The surface — Rou"},{"t":"Compare with the reference light","d":"Read the measured colour temperature and its error band, understand how the reference light is chosen, and interpret the colour difference between a material under its source and under that reference.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/compare-with-the-reference.html","h":["Colour temperature","The reference rule","The colour difference","Two white points","Metamerism","The Method tab's reference view"],"x":" The correlated colour temperature CCT of a light is the temperature of the blackbody whose colour is closest to it, in kelvin. Low values 2700 K are warm and orange; high values 6500 K and above are cool and bluish. Measured temperature gives the CCT the page computes back from the illuminant spectrum you chose, using McCamy's formula, rounded to 10 K, with its error band. The error bands were measured against blackbodies of known temperature: Temperature Worst measured error 1800–2500 K ±18 K 2500–4000 K ±13 K 4000–7000 K ±11 K 7000–10000 K ±139 K 10000–15000 K ±1069 K Above 7000 K the readout is highlighted and adds McCamy's fit is out of its range up here . The reference chosen is a daylight either way. To judge how a light renders colours, the CIE compares it with a reference light of the same CCT CIE 13.3, section 5.1 : below 5000 K, a blackbody at that temperature; at or above 5000 K, a CIE daylight at that temperature. Reference for it shows the choice for example daylight 6500 K or blackbody 2860 K , and the note above the swatches gives the reason, for example below 5000 K the reference is a Planckian radiator . A light that is its own reference, such as D65 or a blackbod"},{"t":"Export and share","d":"Download the 81-row spectrum CSV and the whole-scene JSON, and copy a link that rebuilds the scene.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/export-and-share.html","h":["The spectrum CSV","The scene JSON","Links"],"x":" Nothing leaves the page until you press a button. Save the spectrum on the Lab tab and Download the spectrum on the Export tab save the same file. On the Export tab, What to take switches the preview between The spectrum the first lines of the CSV , The whole scene the first part of the JSON and A link to this ; the note above it gives the row count. Button Result Download the spectrum Saves material under light spectrum.csv Download the scene Saves material under light scene.json Copy a link to this scene Copies a link; Link copied confirms it, or the link is shown if the clipboard is unavailable The file starts with header lines: Line Contents sampling 380–780 nm at 5 nm, 81 samples observer CIE 1931 2°, published at 10 nm, interpolated to 5 illuminant The light and its definition measured cct The measured colour temperature and its error band reference The reference light's kind, temperature and the reason material , reflectance The material, and whether its curve is MEASURED with the file name or SYNTHESISED surface Conductor, or dielectric with its refractive index; the lobe; the roughness geometry Light, view and azimuth angles exposure The scale that makes a white diffuser "},{"t":"Run a sensitivity sweep","d":"Use the Metrics tab to see how far the colour moves when the reflectance curve is perturbed, and read why the CRI and TM-30 figures were withdrawn.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/run-a-sensitivity-sweep.html","h":["Run it","Read the result","Why the perturbation is correlated","What used to print here"],"x":" A reflectance curve is never known exactly: a spectrophotometer's reading carries error, and the presets are inventions. The sweep asks how much that matters for the colour. 1. Set up the scene on the Lab tab. 2. Open the Metrics tab. Under Sensitivity sweep : Control Range and step Default Meaning Perturbation ±0.005–0.1, step 0.005 ±0.02 The size of the random change to the reflectance, in reflectance units Correlation length 0–120 nm, step 5 40 nm How far along the spectrum neighbouring changes move together; 0 shows independent Draws 100–2000, step 100 500 How many perturbed curves to try 3. Select Run the sweep . A message reports how many draws took how long. Under How far the colour moves when the curve does appear Median , 95th percentile and Worst draw , each a ΔE₀₀ between the unperturbed colour and a perturbed one. The note gives the number of draws and the time, and the line under the figures restates the perturbation and correlation, adding, for a synthesised material, that this is the sensitivity of the model, not of any pigment. For gold under D65 with the defaults, the median is typically about 0.5 and the 95th percentile about 1.2. The draws are random, so each ru"},{"t":"Set up a scene","d":"Choose the light, the material, the surface model and the viewing geometry, and understand what each does to the spectrum and the colour.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/set-up-a-scene.html","h":["How the colour is made","1. Choose the light","2. Choose the material","3. Set the surface","4. Choose a lobe","5. Set the geometry","6. Read the sample"],"x":" At each of 81 wavelengths, 380 to 780 nm in 5 nm steps, the tool multiplies: 1. The illuminant's spectral power — how much light the source emits at that wavelength its spectral power distribution , SPD . 2. The material's reflectance — the fraction of that light the material sends back, from 0 to 1. 3. The lobe's weight — how much of the reflected light travels towards your eye at the angles you set. The products are summed against the CIE 1931 2° observer's colour matching functions to give CIE XYZ, and converted to sRGB for the screen. The Method tab's From spectrum to colour view shows these steps. The published observer table is at 10 nm; the tool interpolates it to 5 nm, and says so in its exports. Option What it is D65 — daylight, 6504 K default CIE average daylight D50 — daylight, 5003 K Warmer daylight, the graphic arts reference D55 — daylight, 5503 K Mid morning or mid afternoon daylight D75 — daylight, 7504 K Cool north sky daylight A — a blackbody at 2856 K Incandescent tungsten light E — equal energy Equal power at every wavelength Blackbody at a temperature you choose Planck's law at Temperature Daylight at a temperature you choose The CIE daylight model at Temperat"},{"t":"Use a measured reflectance","d":"Load a spectrophotometer reflectance file in place of the synthesised presets, and go back to the presets.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/use-a-measured-reflectance.html","h":["Prepare the file","Load it","What changes","Go back"],"x":" The twenty presets are invented curves. If you have a measured reflectance spectrum, from a spectrophotometer or a published dataset, you can render it instead. A plain text file: .csv , .tsv or .txt . Two columns per line: wavelength in nm and reflectance . Columns may be separated by commas, semicolons, tabs or spaces. Lines that are not two numbers are skipped. Reflectance from 0 to 1. A file in percent is detected automatically: if any value is above 1, every value is divided by 100. Values outside 0–1 after that are clipped. At least eight rows, covering at least 420 to 680 nm . 1. Drop the file on the spectrum plot on the Lab tab, or on Drop a reflectance file under Measure the material on the Data tab. You can also click either area or press Enter or Space on the Data tab's area to choose the file. 2. Read the message: for example 41 rows accepted, read as percent — the register now says verbatim , or Not installed: with a reason. The file is resampled onto the 5 nm grid from 380 to 780 nm by straight line interpolation between your rows; beyond the ends of your file, the first and last values are held flat. The material menu now holds a single entry, named after your file "},{"t":"Material Under Light reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, message and file format in Material Under Light, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — The light","Lab tab — The material and surface","Lab tab — The geometry","Lab tab — Buttons","Lab tab — Lobe cards","Lab tab — Spectrum and sample","Lab tab — Readouts","Lab tab — Against the reference the standard names","Method tab","Metrics tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages","File formats","Link parameters"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/spectral tools/material lighting/ Tab Contents Lab Light, material, surface and geometry controls; the spectrum plot; the sample sphere and lobe cards; readouts; the reference comparison Method Four explanation views Metrics The sensitivity sweep and the two withdrawn rendering indices Data The register of 17 tables and formulas, filterable by status; the tab label shows the count; reflectance loader Export Spectrum CSV, scene JSON and link Reference Fourteen sources, filterable Links in the page text for example Metrics or Data switch to that tab. Control Values or range Default Illuminant D65 — daylight, 6504 K , D50 — daylight, 5003 K , D55 — daylight, 5503 K , D75 — daylight, 7504 K , A — a blackbody at 2856 K , E — equal energy , Blackbody at a temperature you choose , Daylight at a temperature you choose D65 Temperature 1800–10000 K, step 50; enabled only for the last two options; daylight is raised to at least 4000 K 2700 K Control Values or range Default Material White , Gray , Black , Red , Green , Blue , Yellow , Cyan , Magenta , Skin , Leaf , Ocean , Concrete , Wood , Sky , Gold , Copper , Silver , Ceramic , Rubber ; or one"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Material Under Light","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for Material Under Light: black samples, disabled controls, clipping, refused files and links.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The sphere and swatch are black","The Temperature slider does nothing or is greyed out","I set a daylight below 4000 K but the readout says 4000 K","\"Measured temperature\" is highlighted and mentions McCamy","\"clipped to sRGB\" appears, or \"Inside sRGB\" reads \"no\" or \"the highlight is not\"","Moving \"Seen from\" or \"Between them\" does not change the sphere","The Refractive index slider is greyed out","Every material looks similar under E or a high-temperature light","My reflectance file is refused","The material menu shows only my file","A file chooser opens when I click the spectrum","The sweep result is out of date","A link did not restore my measured material"],"x":" Why: you chose Conductor with the Oren Nayar lobe. A conductor has no diffuse term, and Oren Nayar has no specular term, so nothing is reflected. What to do: choose Dielectric , or a specular lobe such as GGX , Beckmann , Ward or Ashikhmin Shirley . Why: it is used only by Blackbody at a temperature you choose and Daylight at a temperature you choose . Every other light has its own fixed definition. What to do: choose one of those two options. Why: the CIE daylight model is defined from 4000 K upwards, so lower values are raised to 4000 K. The exports record this. What to do: use Blackbody at a temperature you choose for warmer sources. Why: above 7000 K the colour temperature formula is outside its accurate range; the error band grows to ±139 K and beyond. What to do: nothing; the reference chosen above 5000 K is a daylight either way. Treat the temperature as approximate. Why: the material's colour, or its highlight, is outside what sRGB can show; the swatch and sphere show the nearest displayable colour. Saturated materials such as the default gold, and bright highlights on shiny surfaces, often do this. What to do: nothing is wrong; the L\\ a\\ b\\ values are computed before clip"},{"t":"Material Under Light FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Material Under Light.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/docs/faq.html","h":["Are the materials measured?","Why is there no CRI or TM-30 score?","So what does the ΔE₀₀ under the swatches mean?","Why does the swatch look warm under tungsten when L*a*b* barely changes?","Is the rendering physically accurate?","Can it show metamerism?","What does Jz add?","Why does a metal go black with Oren-Nayar?","How accurate is the measured colour temperature?","Is my reflectance file uploaded?"],"x":" No. All twenty presets are invented curves a flat level plus bell shaped bumps and are marked synthesised everywhere. Load a measured file on the Data tab to use real data. Both need specified sets of measured test colours and specific colour spaces that the tool does not hold. The figures an earlier version printed were wrong in ways the Metrics tab demonstrates, so they are withdrawn. How far this one material's colour moves between your light and the CIE reference light for its colour temperature, each taken against its own light's white. It describes the material in that light, not the light in general. The swatch is un adapted: it shows the light that actually leaves the surface, as a camera would record it. L\\ a\\ b\\ is taken against the light's own white, so it measures the material relative to the light. The spectral pipeline, observer, daylights, colour difference and the five lobes follow their published forms. The materials are invented, the scene is a single light and a single surface with no inter reflection, and the sphere is a simple shaded preview. It is a teaching and exploration tool, not a renderer for production images. It shows one material at a time. Because i"},{"t":"Material Under Light background","d":"Contents of the background material for the Material Under Light tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the how to pages with the colour and rendering terms the tool uses, its keyboard and pointer actions, a statement of what is published, what is the tool's own and what is not held, related tools and articles, its history and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Colour, light and reflectance terms used in Material Under Light shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Lobe cards, drop zones, Enter and Space , and tab links limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The data register entry by entry, precision, and what the tool is not related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Material Under Light shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Material Under Light tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond these. Site wide shortcuts are described in Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . Action Where Result Select a card The five lobe cards under the sample Chooses that lobe Drop a file The spectrum plot on the Lab tab, or Drop a reflectance file on the Data tab Loads a measured reflectance Click The spectrum plot or Drop a reflectance file Opens a file chooser Enter or Space Focused Drop a reflectance file area Opens a file chooser Enter or Space A focused row on the Data tab Expands or collapses the row Click a tab name in the page text Note strip and hints Switches to that tab Tab Anywhere Moves between controls; sliders then respond to the arrow keys "},{"t":"Material Under Light glossary","d":"Colour, light and reflectance terms used in the Material Under Light tool, each explained briefly.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Azimuth The angle between the light and the eye measured around the surface normal Between them Blackbody Planckian radiator An ideal hot object whose light depends only on its temperature, given by Planck's law BRDF lobe A model of how a surface spreads reflected light over directions CIE 1931 2° observer The standard colour matching functions describing average human colour vision CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ A colour space with lightness L\\ and opponent axes a\\ red–green and b\\ yellow–blue CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ The CIE's recommended formula for how different two colours look Conductor A metal; its colour comes entirely from specular reflection tinted by its reflectance Correlated colour temperature CCT The temperature of the blackbody whose colour is closest to a light's, in kelvin CRI colour rendering index A CIE score of how faithfully a light renders a set of test colours; withdrawn from this tool D series daylight D50, D55, D65, D75 CIE standard daylights reconstructed from a published basis, named for their temperature Dielectric A non metal; a faint colourless highlight plus coloured diffuse reflection Diffuse reflection Light that enters a material, scatters and leaves in many dir"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Material Under Light takes from published sources, what is its own, how precise it is, and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the tool is","The data register, in plain terms","Precision","Model limits","What the tool does not do"],"x":" A spectral appearance bench for learning and exploration: one light, one flat material, one geometry, computed wavelength by wavelength. It is not a production renderer, a lighting design certification tool or a colour rendering meter. Entry Status What it means for you CIE 1931 2° standard observer Verbatim The published 10 nm table, unaltered; every other 5 nm sample is interpolated CIE D series eigenvector basis Verbatim D50, D55, D65, D75 and chosen daylights land within 0.0003 of their published chromaticities sRGB primaries and transfer curve Verbatim The swatch uses the published sRGB definition, un adapted CIEDE2000 colour difference Verbatim Every ΔE₀₀ uses the full formula, against the light's own white JzAzBz Verbatim The published constants Planck's radiation law Verbatim Every blackbody is computed at the 81 samples GGX microfacet distribution Verbatim The published form, including Smith masking The other four reflectance lobes Verbatim Beckmann, Ward, Ashikhmin Shirley and Oren Nayar in their published forms Correlated colour temperature Computed McCamy's formula, with error bands measured for the whole chain ±11 to ±18 K below 7000 K The reference illuminant for a s"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Material Under Light keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What leaves the page, and only when you ask","The rest of the page"],"x":" Every calculation: spectra, the sphere, the readouts, the reference comparison and the sweep are computed in the page. Reflectance files you load are read from your disk by the page. They are not uploaded and are forgotten when you reload. Save the spectrum , Download the spectrum and Download the scene create files through your browser's normal download. They include the name of any reflectance file you loaded. Copy a link to this scene writes a link to your clipboard. It contains your scene settings, never your files. The tool page loads the site's usual pages, styles and scripts, and, depending on your cookie choices, advertising and consent based analytics, like the rest of auricartisan.com. See the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Material Under Light tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — rebuilt as Material Under Light","Earlier"],"x":" The site wide history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The entries below cover what changed for users of this tool. The page was rebuilt with six tabs Lab , Method , Metrics , Data , Export , Reference . Changed: The D series daylights D50, D55, D65, D75 and chosen daylights are now true CIE daylights. Earlier they were blackbodies at the same temperature, which shifted colours slightly for example about 1.2 ΔE₀₀ for skin under D65 . The twenty material curves are unchanged in shape but now labelled synthesised everywhere, including exports. The earlier \"bootstrap\" is now a sensitivity sweep with a stated, correlated perturbation you control. Added: Measured temperature with its error band, Reference for it , and the comparison of the material under its source and under the CIE reference light. The two white point treatment: an un adapted swatch, and L\\ a\\ b\\ against the light's own white. Loading a measured reflectance file. The Data register and header lines stating the method in every export. Removed: The CIE colour rendering index and the TM 30 Rf and Rg figures. The Metrics tab shows why and what they would need. What stayed the same: the spectral pipeline, "},{"t":"Related tools and articles","d":"Tools and Learn articles related to Material Under Light.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Material Lighting","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/material-lighting/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other tools on the site","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Industrial Dye Chemistry ../../industrial dye chemistry/README.md — the same spectral approach for transparent dye baths, with colour inconstancy between lights. Perception and Vision ../../perception and vision/README.md — how the viewer's visual system changes what a colour looks like. Illuminants ../../../colorimetry and rendering/illuminants/README.md — the standard light sources and their spectra in detail. Chromatic adaptation ../../../colorimetry and rendering/chromatic adaptation/README.md — predicting how colours appear when the eye adapts to a new light. Colour Science Lab ../../../colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md — colour spaces and conversions. The Learn section is described in Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md . Spectral Power Distributions and Why RGB Is Not Enough — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 spectral power distributions Spectral Rendering: Why Three Numbers Aren't Enough — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 22 spectral rendering beyond rgb Color Rendering: Why Two \"White\" Lights Reveal Colors Differently — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 07 color rendering and cri Meta"},{"t":"Neuroscience (Visual Pathway)","d":"What the Visual Pathway tool does, who it is for, where to find it and how to follow a first grating from the cones to V4.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Neuroscience tool, whose page is titled Visual Pathway , follows one stimulus through five stages of the early visual system, one stage at a time. It starts with a colour on your screen, turns it into the signals of the three cone types, combines those into opponent channels, and then shows what a retinal centre surround cell, a bank of V1 orientation filters, a V2 boundary signal and a V4 colour cell would each respond to. Every stage produces a map you can view beside the stimulus, with a scale bar that says what a bright pixel means. The stimulus is a grating, a pattern of stripes whose spatial frequency you set in cycles per degree of visual angle. Because cycles per degree depends on how far you sit from the screen and how large its pixels are, the page asks for both and derives every frequency from them. It also warns you when the frequency you ask for is finer than your pixel grid can draw. The tool is an educational approximation, not a physiological measurement. The page says so, and its Data tab lists which of its numbers come from published sources and which are its own. In particular, the cone curves drawn in the figure are the tool's own and put the L and M cones "},{"t":"Using the Visual Pathway","d":"Contents of the how-to documentation for the Visual Pathway tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to use the Visual Pathway, from the first grating to exporting cone signals for your own colours. Start with getting started, then read the task guides in any order. The reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs, the Lab screen tour and a first walk through the stages explore the stages.md explore the stages.md Stimulus and geometry, each of the five stages, the nine maps, the scale bar and the Cells tab cones and opponent channels.md cones and opponent channels.md Cone signals, opponent axes, the Pipeline tab, the cone figure, colour vision simulation and installing a cone table export and share.md export and share.md The colour list, the CSV and clipboard formats, saving the map, the settings JSON and view links reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, readout, message and file format, with ranges and defaults troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Flat maps, alias and contrast warnings, refused cone tables, links and copying faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Visual Pathway","d":"Open the Visual Pathway, learn the layout of the Lab tab and follow a first grating through all five stages.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The six tabs","A tour of the Lab tab","Your first walk through the stages","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/neuroscience/. The page opens on the Lab tab with a default stimulus already drawn: a chromatic grating based on the colour 3A8CFF , at 4.0 cycles per degree and 25% contrast, viewed from 57 cm on a screen with 0.248 mm pixels. A note strip above the tabs says what the pictures rest on: the L and M cones peak 25 nm apart in the published data, but the cone table this page draws peaks them at the same wavelength. The strip cannot be closed. Its Data link opens the Data tab, where the reason is explained. Tab What it is for Lab The workbench: controls on the left, the stimulus and the chosen stage map on the right, the cone figure and the readouts below Pipeline Where a colour goes before any cortex sees it, step by step, with the opponent values of seven test colours Cells All the stages side by side over the same small stimulus Data The register of every dataset and transform the tool rests on, with a status for each; you can install a cone table here Export A list of colours through the front end, and the download, copy and link buttons Reference Standards, formulas, citations and research notes, with a searc"},{"t":"Cones, opponent channels and the cone table","d":"How the Visual Pathway turns a screen colour into cone signals and opponent channels, how to read the Pipeline tab and the cone figure, and how to install your own cone table.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/cones-and-opponent-channels.html","h":["The idea in brief","How the tool gets from a hex colour to opponent values","Use the Pipeline tab","Read the cone figure","Install your own cone table","Simulate a colour vision deficiency","Take the numbers away"],"x":" Your retina has three kinds of cone. The L long wavelength cones respond most to yellowish red light, the M medium cones to green light and the S short cones to violet blue light. Their sensitivities overlap heavily: in the published CIE 2006 fundamentals the L and M cones peak at 566.8 nm and 541.2 nm, only about 25 nm apart, and the S cones at 441.8 nm. A colour you see is summarised by three numbers, the cone signals , one per type. Early in the visual pathway these three signals are recombined into opponent channels : one that compares L with M red against green , one that compares S with the sum of L and M blue against yellow , and one that adds L and M roughly, lightness . A neutral grey drives neither chromatic channel, which is why you never see a \"reddish green\" or a \"bluish yellow\". The Pipeline tab draws the chain as a row of steps: Step What happens sRGB The 8 bit, gamma encoded screen value linear Decoded through the sRGB transfer curve IEC 61966 2 1 XYZ Converted to CIE XYZ with the sRGB primaries at D65 LMS Converted to cone signals with the Hunt Pointer Estévez matrix cone contrast Marked not held : the tool has no adapting white to express cone contrast against op"},{"t":"Explore the five stages","d":"Set up the stimulus and viewing geometry, then read what the retina, LGN, V1, V2 and V4 stages do to it, map by map.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/explore-the-stages.html","h":["1. Choose a stimulus","2. State the viewing geometry","3. Switch stages on and off","4. What each stage computes","5. Choose and read a map","6. Read the readouts","7. See every stage at once on the Cells tab"],"x":" This guide covers the stimulus, the viewing geometry, each stage of the pathway, the nine maps and the Cells tab. All controls named here are on the Lab tab unless stated. Under Stimulus , choose one of two sources. Grating — stripes whose brightness or colour varies as a sine wave across the frame. It is the only source with a defined spatial frequency, so it is the one the stages can be read against. Its controls are a colour picker Base colour , default 3A8CFF and a Carrier menu: Chromatic — the stripes swing between the base colour's hue and its opposite, around a grey with the same L + M cone signal. Both phases have the same L + M, so the pattern changes colour with little change in lightness. Luminance — grey stripes that swing lighter and darker around a grey with the base colour's relative luminance. The pattern changes lightness only. Test card — six colour bars E03131 , 2F9E44 , 1971C2 , F59F00 , C2255C , 0CA678 across the top half, a nine step grey ramp below them, and a red to green gradient along the bottom. The base colour, carrier, frequency and contrast do not apply to it, and the grating controls are hidden. Contrast 0 to 100%, default 25% sets how far the gratin"},{"t":"Export and share","d":"Run a list of colours through the Visual Pathway's front end, download it as CSV or copy it, save the active map as PNG, download the settings and copy a link to the view.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/export-and-share.html","h":["Run a list of colours","Download or copy the table","Save the active map","Download the settings","Copy a link to the view","The What to take buttons"],"x":" Nothing leaves the page until you press one of the buttons described here. Downloads are saved by your browser; copies go to your clipboard. 1. Open the Export tab. 2. In Colours , enter hex colours, one per line. Commas and semicolons also separate entries. Three digit F80 and six digit FF8800 forms work, with or without . Anything else is ignored. 3. The table updates as you type; Run them redraws it. The default list is E03131 , 2F9E44 , 1971C2 , F59F00 and 808080 . The table has one row per colour: Input a swatch and the hex , L , M , S , L − M , S − L+M /2 and L + M , each to four decimals. The header note gives the number of rows. The current Colour vision setting on the Lab tab is applied first, at full strength, so you can see what a dichromat's cone signals would be. Read the grey row first. Because the cone matrix gives equal L, M and S for the D65 white, a neutral has both chromatic values at zero, and the page highlights them. If a grey row shows non zero chromatic values, a colour vision simulation is on. Download the CSV saves cones opponent.csv . It starts with comment lines, then one row per colour: text visual pathway — cone signals and opponent channels chain: sR"},{"t":"Visual Pathway reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, message and file format in the Visual Pathway, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — Stimulus","Lab tab — Geometry, frequency and contrast","Lab tab — Stages","Lab tab — Show","Lab tab — Stage settings","Lab tab — Colour vision","Lab tab — Canvases, scale bar and figure","Lab tab — Readouts","Lab tab — Notes and buttons","Pipeline tab","Cells tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages","File formats","Link parameters"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/neuroscience/ Tab Contents Lab Stimulus, geometry and stage controls; stimulus and map canvases; scale bar; cone figure; readouts; save and link buttons Pipeline The colour chain, the opponent axis table of seven colours and the sensitivity table, with an earlier version comparison Cells Previews of every stage over one stimulus, and the list of controls from an earlier version Data The register of nine datasets and transforms, filterable by status; the tab label shows the count 9 ; cone table installer Export Colour list, CSV, clipboard, settings JSON and link Reference Standards, formulas, citations and research notes, with a search box Links in the page text for example Data or Cells in a hint switch to that tab. Control What it does Values or range Default Stimulus Chooses the source Grating , Test card Grating Base colour The colour the grating is built from grating only Any colour from the picker 3A8CFF Carrier What the grating modulates grating only Chromatic , Luminance Chromatic Control What it does Range and step Default Viewing distance Eye to screen distance used for every frequency 20–200 cm, s"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Visual Pathway","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for flat maps, warnings, refused cone tables, links and copying in the Visual Pathway.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["A map is completely black and its name ends in \"— stage off\"","The scale bar says \"flat — this stage found no variation in this stimulus\"","A warning says \"Above the pixel grid's Nyquist limit\"","A warning says \"The contrast you asked for does not fit in sRGB\"","Moving the Pupil slider changes nothing","L − M peak gap reads 0 nm and is highlighted","My cone table is refused","My installed cone table disappeared","The Cells previews do not match my new settings","Nothing is copied, or the page says \"Copy blocked\"","A link I opened does not restore the stage checkboxes or pupil","Sliders feel slow on an older device"],"x":" Why: the stage that produces that map is switched off under Stages , or it is V2 and V1 is off. What to do: tick the stage's checkbox. For V2, boundary signal , tick both V1 — Gabor bank and V2 — boundary signal . Why: the stage gave the same response everywhere. This is a real result. Common cases: the off centre retinal map with a chromatic grating the retinal stage reads luminance, and a surround weight below 1 adds a positive constant , the chromatic LGN maps with a luminance grating a grey pattern has no colour to oppose , or any map at Contrast 0%. What to do: change the Carrier , raise Contrast , or set Surround weight closer to 1 for the off centre map. Why: at your viewing distance and pixel pitch, the screen cannot draw the spatial frequency you asked for. The pattern you see is an alias, a coarser false pattern. What to do: lower Spatial frequency below the Nyquist limit of the grid readout. Also check that Viewing distance and Pixel pitch match your real setup. The limit rises when you sit further away and when the pixels are smaller; the warning's own text suggests moving closer, but moving closer lowers the limit. Why: the colour opposite your base colour, at the swi"},{"t":"Visual Pathway FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Visual Pathway.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/docs/faq.html","h":["Is this a model of real neurons?","Why are the tool's L and M cone curves on top of each other?","Are the opponent channels the DKL space?","Why does a grey not read exactly zero on the chromatic channels?","What does \"Sensitivity at this frequency\" mean? Is it the chance I can see the grating?","Why do I need to enter a viewing distance and pixel pitch?","Can I load my own image?","Can I simulate a milder colour vision deficiency?","Does the pupil control do anything?","Is there a spike raster or firing rate?","Does anything I enter leave my computer?"],"x":" No. Each stage uses a standard form from the literature a difference of Gaussians, a Gabor energy model, divisive normalisation, a projection in an opponent plane , but every constant is the tool's own and sizes are in pixels rather than degrees of retina. The maps show the shape of what each area does. The page marks itself \"Educational, not physiological\". The built in spectral table is the tool's own and puts both peaks at 590 nm. It only draws the figure. The cone signals the stages use come from a published matrix Hunt Pointer Estévez applied to CIE XYZ. You can install a published table on the Data tab to fix the figure. No. They are differences of absolute cone signals L − M, S − L+M /2 and a luminance channel of L + M. DKL uses cone contrast against a stated white and scaled isoluminant axes. See Cones, opponent channels and the cone table cones and opponent channels.md . It reads about 0.0002 at worst, because the published cone matrix is given to four decimals. That is the Neutral off axis readout. It is a weighting curve that peaks at 1.0 at 4 c/deg and falls off either side. It is not a probability of detection; the page deliberately gives no detection figure. To measu"},{"t":"Visual Pathway background","d":"Contents of the background material for the Visual Pathway tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds material that supports the how to pages: the terms the tool uses, its keyboard and pointer actions, an honest statement of what is published and what is the tool's own, related tools and articles, its history and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Visual Pathway, each in a sentence or two shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Double click to enlarge, Esc , and keyboard use of the register limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The data register entry by entry, precision, and what the tool is not related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network "},{"t":"Visual Pathway shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Visual Pathway tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond these. Site wide shortcuts, such as the search palette, are described in Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . Action Where Result Double click Stimulus or map canvas on the Lab tab Opens the canvas enlarged, filling the window Esc Enlarged view Closes it Select the × button or the dark area around the image Enlarged view Closes it Enter or Space A focused row on the Data tab Expands or collapses the row Tab Anywhere Moves between controls; sliders then respond to the arrow keys Drag a file Drop a CSV or JSON on the Data tab Installs a cone table "},{"t":"Visual Pathway glossary","d":"Terms used in the Visual Pathway tool, each explained briefly.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Alias A false, coarser pattern that appears when a screen is asked to draw stripes finer than its pixels can carry Carrier What a grating varies: colour at constant L + M Chromatic or lightness in grey Luminance Centre surround A receptive field that compares a small central region with a larger surrounding one Colourmap The ramp of colours used to draw a map's values, here Viridis, Inferno or Grayscale Complex cell energy The combined response of two filters a quarter cycle apart; it responds to stripes regardless of their exact position Cone signals L, M, S The responses of the long , medium and short wavelength sensitive cones to a colour Cone table A table of cone spectral sensitivities by wavelength; the page's built in one is its own, and you can install another Cycles per degree c/deg How many light dark cycles of a pattern fall within one degree of visual angle Degrees per pixel The angle one screen pixel covers at your viewing distance: atan pixel pitch ÷ distance Deuteranopia Colour vision without M cones Dichromacy Colour vision with only two of the three cone types working Difference of Gaussians DoG A centre blur minus a weighted surround blur, the standa"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Visual Pathway takes from published sources, what is its own, how precise its numbers are and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the tool is","The data register, in plain terms","Precision","What it does not do"],"x":" An educational simulation of how early vision transforms a stimulus. It is not a physiological model fitted to measurements, not a diagnostic tool and not a vision test. Nothing it shows is a measurement of any real visual system. The Data tab lists nine entries. This is what each means for the numbers you see. Entry Status What it means for you sRGB transfer and primaries Verbatim Screen colours are decoded and converted with the published IEC 61966 2 1 curve and matrices Dichromacy projection Verbatim The three colour vision simulations use the published Viénot, Brettel and Mollon 1999 matrices, applied in cone space Cone transform Computed Cone signals come from the published Hunt Pointer Estévez matrix applied to XYZ; greys sit within about 2.2 × 10⁻⁴ of zero on the chromatic axes Spectral sensitivity table Stand in The cone curves in the figure are the tool's own, with L and M both peaking at 590 nm; they draw the figure and nothing else Opponent axes Stand in L − M, S − L+M /2 and L + M are useful axes but are not DKL; nothing is in cone contrast units Spatial sensitivity Stand in The weighting curve is the tool's own log Gaussian peaking at 4 c/deg; it has no threshold crit"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Visual Pathway keeps in your browser and what, if anything, uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What leaves the page, and only when you ask","The rest of the page"],"x":" Every calculation: the stimulus, the five stages, the readouts and the colour list are computed in the page. A cone table you install is read from your disk by the page. It is not uploaded and is forgotten when you reload. The colours you type in the Export tab stay in the page. Download the CSV , Save the map and Download the settings create files through your browser's normal download. Copy to clipboard and Copy a link to this view write to your clipboard. A copied link contains your settings in its address for example the base colour and viewing distance . Anyone you send it to can read them. The tool page loads the site's usual pages, styles and scripts, and, depending on your cookie choices, advertising and consent based analytics, like the rest of auricartisan.com. See the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Visual Pathway tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — rebuilt as the Visual Pathway","May 2026"],"x":" The site wide history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The entries below cover what changed for users of this tool. The page was rebuilt with six tabs Lab , Pipeline , Cells , Data , Export , Reference . The Pipeline and Cells tabs can show values from the earlier version beside the current ones. Added: Viewing distance and Pixel pitch controls; every frequency is now in cycles per degree, including the V1 Gabor frequency previously cycles per image . The Nyquist limit of the grid readout and a warning when the grating is finer than the screen can draw. Contrast achieved and a note when the requested contrast does not fit in sRGB. A working scale bar under every map, including a hue wheel for the orientation map and a \"flat\" label for maps with no variation. The Test card as a stimulus source. The cone figure with the published peak wavelengths marked, the L − M peak gap , Published gap and Neutral off axis readouts, and a cone table installer on the Data tab. The Data register with a status for every dataset and model. Changed: Cone signals are now computed from CIE XYZ, so greys sit at zero on both chromatic channels. This changes all LGN and V4 values and the "},{"t":"Related tools and articles","d":"Tools and Learn articles related to the Visual Pathway.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Neuroscience","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/neuroscience/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other tools on the site","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Perception and Vision ../../perception and vision/README.md — the same dichromacy simulation, plus night vision, lens ageing, cataract, central loss and acuity, over your own images and with a severity control. Psychophysical Experiment Engine ../../psychophysical experiment engine/README.md — measure a real contrast threshold for a Gabor patch, using the same viewing geometry idea. Material Lighting ../../material lighting/README.md and Industrial Dye Chemistry ../../industrial dye chemistry/README.md — where the colour a cone receives comes from: light and matter, wavelength by wavelength. Vision simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — the Vision Lab for checking designs under different visual conditions. Colour Science Lab ../../../colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md — colour spaces and conversions in a workspace. The Learn section is described in Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md . Human Color Vision: Cones, Opponent Signals, and the Brain — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 human color vision cones opponent Afterimages and the Opponent Process: Why Colors Leave Ghosts — https://auricartisan.com/libr"},{"t":"Perception and Vision","d":"What the Perception Vision tool does, who it is for, where to find it and how to run a first colour vision simulation over your own image.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Perception and Vision the page is titled Perception Vision runs eight simulations of how a scene reaches a different visual system: colour vision deficiency protan, deutan and tritan , rod only night vision, twilight vision, a yellowing lens, cataract, loss of central vision, light adaptation and reduced acuity. You run them over a built in test card, a grey ramp, a Snellen chart or an image of your own, and compare the result with the original in a split view. The colour vision simulation follows the published method of Viénot, Brettel and Mollon 1999 : each colour goes from sRGB through CIE XYZ into cone signals, the missing cone type is projected away, and the result comes back to sRGB. The page checks itself as it goes. A grey ramp shows whether the simulation tints neutrals a correct dichromacy simulation never does , a counter reports how many of the frame's colours merged into one, and the graphics card and processor renderers are compared on 216 colours after every change. The tool is an educational and design review aid. Only the colour vision projection comes from a publication; the other seven simulations use the tool's own constants and show that an effect exists rathe"},{"t":"Using Perception and Vision","d":"Contents of the how-to documentation for the Perception Vision tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to run the simulations over your own material, how to read the page's built in checks and how to take results away. Start with getting started; the reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the six tabs, the Lab screen tour and a first simulation simulate a design.md simulate a design.md Sources, the eight simulations and their settings, daltonising, the illuminant, adjustments, presets and comparison views read the checks.md read the checks.md The grey ramp, every readout, renderer agreement, and the Simulation and Modes tabs check a palette and export.md check a palette and export.md Running hex colours through the simulation, CSV and clipboard formats, the frame PNG, settings JSON and links reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, readout, message and file format, with ranges and defaults troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Camera, WebGL2, uploads, readouts that say n/a, links and copying faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with Perception and Vision","d":"Open Perception Vision, learn the layout of the Lab tab and run a first colour vision simulation over the test card and your own image.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The six tabs","A tour of the Lab tab","Your first simulation","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/perception vision/. The page opens on the Lab tab in its default state: the built in test card, the Colour vision simulation at Protan , Severity 1.00, a Split comparison with the divider in the middle, illuminant D65 the scene as authored and the GPU renderer. A note strip above the tabs, which cannot be closed, states the check this page is built around: a colour blind viewer sees white as white. Its Data link opens the register that explains the method. Tab What it is for Lab The workbench: controls on the left, the simulated frame on the right, the grey ramp check and the readouts below Simulation One colour's route through the colour vision simulation, the matrices, and a table of test colours Modes Every simulation side by side over the same source Data The register of every dataset and transform the tool rests on, with a status for each Export A list of colours through the simulation, and the download, copy, load and link buttons Reference Standards, formulas, citations and research notes, with a search box The rail left , from top to bottom: Source — test card, grey ramp, Snellen chart, your image, or "},{"t":"Check a palette and export","d":"Run a list of hex colours through the active simulation, find colours that become indistinguishable, and export CSV, clipboard text, the frame, the settings and links.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/check-a-palette-and-export.html","h":["Check a palette","Download or copy the table","Save the frame","Download and load settings","Copy a link to the view","The What to take buttons"],"x":" Nothing leaves the page until you press one of the buttons described here. 1. On the Lab tab, set up the simulation you want to test, for example Colour vision , Deutan , Severity 1.00. 2. Open the Export tab. 3. In Colours , enter your hex colours, one per line. Commas and semicolons also separate entries; three and six digit forms work, with or without ; anything else is ignored. Include a grey. 4. The table updates as you type; Run them redraws it. The default list is E03131 , 2F9E44 , 1971C2 , F59F00 and 808080 . The caption names the simulation, for example The colours, through colour vision protan at severity 1.00 . Column Meaning Input Your colour, as a swatch and hex Simulated The colour after the simulation, as a swatch and hex L , M , S The cone signals of the input colour, four decimals ΔE00 The CIEDE2000 colour difference between input and simulated colour, one decimal In sRGB yes , or clamped when the simulated colour fell outside sRGB and was clipped How to read it: Two rows with the same or nearly the same Simulated hex are two colours the simulated viewer cannot tell apart. Change one of them. The grey row should read ΔE00 0.0 and an identical simulated hex under C"},{"t":"Read the checks","d":"Understand the grey-ramp test, every readout under the frame, the renderer agreement check, and the Simulation and Modes tabs.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/read-the-checks.html","h":["The grey ramp: the test that needs no reference","The readouts","Renderer agreement","The Simulation tab","The Modes tab","The Data and Reference tabs"],"x":" The page does not ask you to trust its simulation. It shows checks you can read yourself. This guide explains each one. Under the frame, The grey ramp, which is the test that needs no reference shows nine grey steps from black to white, and under each step a number: how far apart the red, green and blue channels of that grey end up after the simulation, in 8 bit code values 0 to 255 . For Colour vision the numbers must all be 0 . A dichromacy projection removes one colour axis and leaves the grey axis alone, so a person with a colour vision deficiency sees a grey as grey and white as white. A non zero step is a defect and is shown in red. The note under the strip also shows what an earlier version of the page produced. For Scotopic , Mesopic , Lens yellowing , Cataract and Light adaptation , non zero numbers are the effect itself: these simulations are meant to tint or shift neutrals. The note says so. For Central loss and Acuity , which depend on position rather than colour, the ramp measures only their colour part, which is none. For None , every number is zero. The ramp leaves out the illuminant, because relighting a scene with illuminant A tints greys on purpose; including it "},{"t":"Simulate a design or image","d":"Choose a source, run any of the eight simulations with its settings, relight the scene, apply adjustments and presets, and compare the result.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/simulate-a-design.html","h":["1. Choose a source","2. Pick a simulation","3. Relight the scene (Before the eye)","4. Apply adjustments","5. Use a preset","6. Compare","7. Save the result"],"x":" All controls in this guide are on the Lab tab. Source What it is Test card default Eight colour patches, a nine step grey ramp and red, green and blue ramps, 800 × 600 Grey ramp only The nine grey steps across the whole frame, for reading neutral drift at a glance Snellen chart Letter rows labelled 20/200, 20/100, 20/70, 20/50, 20/40, 20/30 and 20/20, so the Acuity simulation has something to be judged on Uploaded image A picture from your device Camera Live frames from a camera; see the note below Uploaded image. Choose it, then select Choose a file and pick any image your browser can open PNG, JPEG, WebP and so on . The file name appears beside the button. Large images are scaled down to fit within 1200 × 900 pixels; small ones are not enlarged. The image is read by the page and never uploaded. Camera. Choose it, then Start or stop switches the camera on and off; the status reads off , active or unavailable . The camera needs your browser's permission, and auricartisan.com currently does not allow its pages to use the camera, so in most browsers the page shows a message beginning Camera: , sets the status to unavailable and returns to the test card. Use a screenshot or photo wit"},{"t":"Perception and Vision reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, message and file format in Perception Vision, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — Source","Lab tab — Simulation","Lab tab — Compare and renderer","Lab tab — Before the eye","Lab tab — Adjustments","Lab tab — Presets","Lab tab — Stage elements","Lab tab — Readouts","Simulation tab","Modes tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages","File formats","Link parameters"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/perception vision/ Tab Contents Lab Source, simulation, comparison, renderer, illuminant, adjustments and presets; the frame, grey ramp check and readouts Simulation The colour vision chain, its matrices and a seven colour table, with an earlier version comparison Modes Previews of every simulation over one source, and the list of controls from an earlier version Data The register of nine datasets and transforms, filterable by status; the tab label shows the count 9 Export Colour list, CSV, clipboard, settings download and load, link Reference Standards, formulas, citations and research notes, with a search box Control Values Default Source Test card , Grey ramp only , Snellen chart , Uploaded image , Camera Test card Choose a file Opens a file chooser for images shown for Uploaded image ; images are fitted within 1200 × 900 — Start or stop Switches the camera shown for Camera ; status off , active or unavailable off Control Values or range Default Shown for Simulation Colour vision , Scotopic , Mesopic , Lens yellowing , Cataract , Central loss , Light adaptation , Acuity , None Colour vision Always Type P"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Perception and Vision","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for the camera, WebGL2, uploads, readouts that say n/a, links and copying in Perception Vision.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The camera does not start","The page says \"No WebGL2 here.\"","My uploaded image looks smaller than the original","The grey ramp shows non-zero numbers","Readouts show \"n/a\", \"spatial mode\" or \"n/a — spatial\"","\"GPU and CPU agree\" shows a number followed by \"off\"","The divider moves when I click the frame","The Install a table area on the Data tab does nothing","A preset did not reset my adjustments","A link or loaded settings file did not bring back my image","Nothing is copied, or the page says \"Copy blocked\"","Sliders are slow with a large image"],"x":" Symptom: after choosing Camera or selecting Start or stop , a message beginning Camera: appears, the status reads unavailable and the source goes back to Test card . Why: the camera needs permission, and auricartisan.com currently does not allow its pages to use the camera. Browsers also block cameras on pages that are not secure, and a camera already in use by another application may refuse. What to do: take a screenshot or photo and load it with Uploaded image . Why: your browser or device does not provide WebGL2, or it is switched off. What to do: nothing is required: every simulation runs on the processor CPU and gives the same colours, more slowly. The GPU button is disabled and GPU and CPU agree reads not run . To use the GPU, update the browser or enable hardware acceleration in its settings. Why: images larger than 1200 × 900 pixels are scaled down to fit. Smaller images are shown at their own size. What to do: nothing; to inspect detail, crop the image before loading it. Double click the frame to enlarge the view. Why: under Scotopic , Mesopic , Lens yellowing , Cataract and Light adaptation , shifting greys is the effect being simulated. Under Colour vision the numbers s"},{"t":"Perception and Vision FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Perception Vision.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/docs/faq.html","h":["Can I use this to diagnose colour blindness?","Which colour vision simulation does it use?","Does a severity of 0.5 simulate anomalous trichromacy?","Why does white stay white under protanopia?","What is daltonising?","How accurate are the night-vision, lens, cataract and acuity simulations?","Why is there no contrast sensitivity mode?","Can I check a whole palette at once?","Does my image get uploaded?","Why does the camera option not work?","GPU or CPU: which should I use?"],"x":" No. It simulates how an image might appear to someone with a condition; it does not test anyone's vision. The settings file and CSV carry clinical: false and \"not a clinical measurement\". The Viénot, Brettel and Mollon 1999 projection, applied in cone space: sRGB is decoded, converted to CIE XYZ and then to cone signals with the Hunt Pointer Estévez matrix, projected, and converted back. The Simulation tab shows every matrix. Not as a physiological model. Between 0 and 1 the page blends linearly between normal vision and full dichromacy. The Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes 2009 model would be needed for anomalous trichromacy, and the page does not implement it. The Mild deuteranomaly preset uses this blend at 0.40. Because it should: people with a colour vision deficiency see neutrals as neutral. The grey ramp under the frame checks this for every change. A recolouring that moves information from a colour axis a dichromat cannot see into one they can. Tick Daltonise instead of simulate to preview it. It changes colours for everyone, so it is a preview of a correction filter, not a design fix. They show that an effect exists and its direction, not its size for any person. Their con"},{"t":"Perception and Vision background","d":"Contents of the background material for the Perception Vision tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the how to pages with the terms the tool uses, its keyboard and pointer actions, a statement of what is published and what is the tool's own, related tools and articles, its history and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in Perception Vision shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Dragging the divider, enlarging the frame, Esc and keyboard use of the register limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The data register entry by entry, precision, and what the tool is not related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser, the camera, and what uses the network "},{"t":"Perception and Vision shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Perception Vision tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond these. Site wide shortcuts are described in Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . Action Where Result Press or drag The frame, with Compare set to Split Moves the divider to the pointer Double click The frame Opens the frame enlarged, filling the window Esc Enlarged view Closes it Select the × button or the dark area around the image Enlarged view Closes it Enter or Space A focused row on the Data tab Expands or collapses the row Tab Anywhere Moves between controls; sliders then respond to the arrow keys "},{"t":"Perception and Vision glossary","d":"Terms used in the Perception Vision tool, each explained briefly.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Acuity Snellen Sharpness of vision written as a fraction such as 20/40: the viewer sees at 20 feet what a typical eye sees at 40 Anomalous trichromacy Colour vision with all three cone types but one of them shifted, giving weaker colour discrimination than normal Bradford transform A published method for predicting how colours shift when the light source changes, used here to relight the scene Cataract Clouding of the eye's lens, which scatters light and lowers contrast CIEDE2000 ΔE00 The CIE's current formula for how different two colours look; larger is more different Clamped A colour pushed back inside the sRGB range because the simulation produced a value a screen cannot show Cone signals L, M, S The responses of the long , medium and short wavelength sensitive cones Daltonising Recolouring an image to move information into colour differences a dichromat can see Deutan Relating to the M medium wavelength cones; deuteranopia is the absence of M cones Dichromacy Colour vision with only two working cone types Illuminant D65, D50, A A standard light source: D65 and D50 are daylights, A is tungsten incandescent light Mesopic vision Vision in twilight, when both rods an"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Perception Vision takes from published sources, what is its own, how precise it is and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the tool is","The data register, in plain terms","What is and is not modelled","Precision","What the tool does not do"],"x":" An educational and design review simulator. It shows how an image may reach a viewer with a different visual system. It is not a clinical or diagnostic instrument and nothing it prints is a measurement of anyone's vision. Entry Status What it means for you sRGB transfer and primaries Verbatim Colours are decoded and re encoded with the published IEC 61966 2 1 curve and matrices Hunt Pointer Estévez cone fundamentals Verbatim Cone signals come from the published matrix, applied to CIE XYZ as it is defined Bradford chromatic adaptation Verbatim The D50 and A options relight the scene with the published Bradford transform and CIE chromaticities Dichromacy projection Computed Protan, deutan and tritan use the published Viénot, Brettel and Mollon 1999 matrices; the severity blend is the tool's convention One implementation, two renderers Computed GPU and CPU use one combined matrix and are checked against each other on 216 colours The shader's matrix literals Computed The GPU receives its matrices in the correct orientation; the grey ramp confirms it Rod spectral weighting Stand in Scotopic and Mesopic use the tool's own rod weights 0.10, 0.59, 0.31 , not the CIE scotopic curve; no sco"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Perception Vision keeps in your browser, how it treats images and the camera, and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","The camera","What leaves the page, and only when you ask","The rest of the page"],"x":" Images you load are read by the page, drawn on a canvas and processed on your own graphics card or processor. They are not uploaded, and they are forgotten when you leave or reload the page. Every simulation, readout and the colour list are computed in the page. Settings files you load are read locally. The page has a Camera source. It would process frames locally in the same way as images, but auricartisan.com currently does not allow its pages to use the camera, so the page reports it as unavailable. No camera frames are captured or sent anywhere. Save the frame , Download the CSV and Download the settings create files through your browser's normal download. A saved frame contains your image as simulated. Copy to clipboard and Copy a link to this view write to your clipboard. A link contains your settings in its address, but never your image. The tool page loads the site's usual pages, styles and scripts, and, depending on your cookie choices, advertising and consent based analytics, like the rest of auricartisan.com. See the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Perception Vision tool.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — rebuilt","May 2026"],"x":" The site wide history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The entries below cover what changed for users of this tool. The page was rebuilt with six tabs Lab , Simulation , Modes , Data , Export , Reference . The Simulation tab can show the results an earlier version produced on screen and in its export beside the current ones. Changed: The colour vision simulation now converts through CIE XYZ into cone signals before projecting, as the published method defines, and the screen and the export use the same calculation. Colours in earlier exports and screenshots can differ widely from current results; white now stays white under every type. Uploaded images are no longer drawn upside down. The readouts refresh after every change. The hero now counts eight simulations; None is listed but not counted. Added: A CPU renderer, used automatically when WebGL2 is not available, and a check that the GPU and CPU agree. The grey ramp strip, Neutral drift , Colours merged , Distinct colours left , Out of sRGB and Largest channel shift . The Grey ramp only and Snellen chart sources. Load settings , and the chain, matrix, illuminant and renderer check in the settings file and CSV hea"},{"t":"Related tools and articles","d":"Tools and Learn articles related to Perception Vision.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Perception and Vision","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/perception-and-vision/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other tools on the site","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Neuroscience ../../neuroscience/README.md — the same cone and dichromacy maths, followed through the retina, LGN, V1, V2 and V4. Psychophysical Experiment Engine ../../psychophysical experiment engine/README.md — measure a contrast threshold, the quantity a contrast sensitivity simulation would need. Material Lighting ../../material lighting/README.md — how an illuminant changes a material's colour, spectrally rather than by adaptation. Vision simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — the Vision Lab, for checking designs under many visual conditions. Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — check the contrast of a colour pair against accessibility guidelines. Ishihara plate generator ../../../accessibility and vision/ishihara plate generator/README.md — generate pseudo isochromatic plates. The Learn section is described in Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md . Color Blindness and Color Vision Deficiency — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 color blindness cvd Human Color Vision: Cones, Opponent Signals, and the Brain — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 hum"},{"t":"Psychophysical Experiment Engine","d":"What the Psychophysics Bench does, who it is for, where to find it and how to measure a first contrast threshold.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Psychophysical Experiment Engine, whose page is titled Psychophysics bench , measures a contrast detection threshold: the faintest pattern you can reliably see. It shows a Gabor patch a soft edged patch of stripes or a grating in a circular aperture, asks you to say where or whether you saw it, and uses an adaptive staircase to move the contrast up after errors and down after correct answers, so that most trials fall near your threshold. At the end it reports the threshold as a Michelson contrast, together with the percentage correct that the threshold belongs to. The bench states its units. Contrast is Michelson contrast in relative luminance, about a background grey you choose, passed through the sRGB transfer curve; spatial frequency is in cycles per degree of visual angle, worked out from a viewing distance and pixel pitch you enter. When your screen cannot show the contrast or the frequency you asked for, the page says so instead of silently drawing something else. It is an educational instrument that runs in your browser, not a calibrated laboratory display. It assumes your screen follows the sRGB standard rather than measuring it. Two of the five staircase procedures ar"},{"t":"Using the Psychophysics Bench","d":"Contents of the how-to documentation for the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages cover designing an experiment, running it, reading the results and taking the data away. Start with getting started; the reference lists every control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, the tabs, the Lab screen tour and a first threshold design an experiment.md design an experiment.md The two tasks, the stimulus, viewing geometry, the five procedures and their parameters, timing run a session.md run a session.md Practice and measured runs, the trial sequence, responding, stopping rules and good practice read the results.md read the results.md Threshold, target percentage, reversals, delivered contrast, the trace, and the Method, Paradigms, Data and Reference tabs export your data.md export your data.md The trials CSV, the session JSON and setup links, and what to do while the Export tab does not open reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, readout, message, file format and link parameter troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Tabs that do not open, warnings, stuck staircases, keys that do nothing faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Psychophysics Bench","d":"Open the Psychophysics Bench, learn the Lab tab and measure a first contrast threshold with the default two-interval task.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The six tabs","A tour of the Lab tab","Measure your first threshold","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/psychophysical experiment engine/ on a computer with a keyboard. The page opens on the Lab tab. A note strip above the tabs, which cannot be closed, says what the numbers are of: contrast in light, not in screen code values, and frequency in cycles per degree. Tab What it is for Lab Design and run an experiment and read the results Method What a contrast is on this page, how the frequency axis is built, and what each staircase estimates Paradigms The two tasks that can be scored and three that were withdrawn Data The register of every method and constant a threshold rests on 13 entries Export Downloads of the trials and the session, and a link to the setup Reference Eleven sources and what each is used for Note: At the time of writing, only the Lab tab opens. See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . The rail left , from top to bottom: Task — Two interval forced choice or Yes / no detection . Stimulus — Gabor or Grating in an aperture , then Spatial frequency , Orientation , Envelope σ and Background . Geometry — Viewing distance and Pixel pitch . Staircase — the procedure, then Step , Starting contrast , Stop "},{"t":"Design an experiment","d":"Choose a task, build the stimulus, state the viewing geometry, pick a staircase procedure and set its parameters and the timing.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/design-an-experiment.html","h":["What a threshold is","1. Choose the task","2. Build the stimulus","3. State the viewing geometry","4. Choose the procedure","5. Set the timing","6. Save your design"],"x":" Every setting in this guide is on the Lab rail. Settings take effect at the next Run or Practice ; the stage preview updates as you change them. Psychophysics measures the relationship between a physical stimulus and what a person reports. A detection threshold is the stimulus strength at which an observer reports the stimulus a stated proportion of the time. The proportion matters: \"your threshold is 0.01\" means nothing until it says \"at 70.7% correct\" or \"at 79.4% correct\", because the chance of a correct answer rises smoothly with contrast. That rising curve is the psychometric function . This bench always reports a threshold together with the percentage it belongs to, and says when a procedure has no stated percentage. Task What happens on a trial Chance level Two interval forced choice default Two intervals are shown one after the other, marked Interval 1 and Interval 2 . The patch is in exactly one, chosen at random. You say which. 50% Yes / no detection One interval. The patch is present on a random half of trials and absent on the rest. You say whether you saw it. No guess rate of this kind; your answers depend on how willing you are to say yes Forced choice is the usual m"},{"t":"Export your data","d":"The trials CSV, the session JSON and setup links on the Export tab, their exact contents, and what to do while the Export tab does not open.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/export-your-data.html","h":["The Export tab","The trials CSV","The session JSON","Setup links","While the Export tab does not open"],"x":" Important: At the time of writing, the Export tab does not open, so the three buttons below cannot be reached. The last section of this page describes what you can do meanwhile. What to take switches the preview on the right between Every trial the CSV , The session the JSON, first part and A link to this . The note above the preview gives the number of rows. Nothing leaves the page until you press a button: Button Result Download the trials Saves psychophysics trials.csv Download the session Saves psychophysics session.json Copy a link to this setup Copies a link with every rail setting; shows Link copied , or the link itself if the clipboard is unavailable With no trials yet, the download buttons show No trials yet — run the experiment first . The file starts with header lines that record what the numbers mean, then one row per trial: text trial,contrast,delivered,response,correct,rt ms,interval,present,cpd Column Meaning trial Trial number contrast The Michelson contrast the procedure asked for delivered The contrast the screen could show; lower than contrast when capped response 0 first interval or 1 second in two interval; yes or no in yes/no correct 1 or 0 rt ms Response tim"},{"t":"Read the results","d":"Understand the threshold readouts, the staircase trace and the explanation tabs of the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/read-the-results.html","h":["The readouts","The staircase trace","Warnings under the readouts","What the page does not show","The explanation tabs"],"x":" Readout What it tells you Threshold, Michelson Your threshold contrast, four decimals; highlighted when there is not yet an estimate At what percentage The proportion correct the threshold belongs to Reversals used How many reversals went into the estimate, out of how many occurred Delivered / asked The contrast the screen could show divided by the contrast the staircase asked for; 1.00 means nothing was capped Trials run Trials completed and scored Proportion correct Correct trials divided by trials run, three decimals Degrees per pixel The angle one pixel covers at your geometry Nyquist limit of the grid The finest frequency your screen can show at your geometry; highlighted when the stimulus is above it 1 up / 2 down, 3 down / 1 up and Accelerated. The first two reversals are a warm up and are discarded. Of the rest, an even number is used if an odd number remain, the earliest is dropped too , because up runs and down runs of a transformed staircase are not symmetric around the threshold. The threshold is the geometric mean of those reversal contrasts, because the staircase steps by ratios. Reversals used reads, for example, 10 of 12 ; before there are two usable reversals it r"},{"t":"Run a session","d":"Practise, run a measured session, respond with keys or buttons, and understand when and how a run stops.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/run-a-session.html","h":["Before you start","Practise","Run","When a run stops","Good practice"],"x":" Sit at the Viewing distance you entered and keep your head still. Dim the room and turn off automatic brightness, night light or colour shifting modes on your screen. Keep brightness fixed for the whole session. Look at the centre of the stage throughout. Close other busy windows; a slow computer can delay intervals. Select Practice . A practice run shows up to 12 trials fewer if Trial ceiling is lower and does not stop on reversals. Its answers appear in the readouts while you practise, and are cleared when you start a measured run. A message confirms Practice — arrow keys respond, Esc stops , and the run state reads practice . Select Run . The message Running — arrow keys respond, Esc stops appears, the run state reads running , Run and Practice are disabled, and Stop appears. Two interval forced choice 1. A fixation cross on the background grey, for 240 ms. 2. Interval 1 lights and the stage shows either the patch or a blank patch of the background, for the Stimulus duration. 3. A 300 ms blank. 4. Interval 2 lights and shows the other one. 5. The stage returns to the background and waits for your answer. Yes / no detection 1. A fixation cross for 240 ms. 2. One interval: the pa"},{"t":"Psychophysics Bench reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, message, file format and link parameter in the Psychophysics Bench, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — Task","Lab tab — Stimulus","Lab tab — Geometry","Lab tab — Staircase","Lab tab — Timing","Lab tab — Buttons","Lab tab — Stage and trace","Lab tab — Readouts","Lab tab — Warnings","Method tab","Data tab","Export tab","Messages","File formats","Link parameters"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/perception and neuroscience/psychophysical experiment engine/ Tab Contents Opens at the time of writing Lab All experiment controls, the trial stage, response buttons, the staircase trace, readouts and warnings Yes Method The contrast chain, the frequency axis, what each ladder estimates No Paradigms Two scoring tasks and three withdrawn ones No Data The register of 13 methods and constants; the tab label shows the count No Export Trials CSV, session JSON, setup link No Reference Eleven sources and their use No Control Values Default Task Two interval forced choice , Yes / no detection Two interval forced choice Control Range and step Default Stimulus type Gabor , Grating in an aperture Gabor Spatial frequency 0.25–20 c/deg, step 0.25 4.0 c/deg Orientation 0–179°, step 1 45° Envelope σ 0.10–2.00°, step 0.05 Gabor only 0.50° Background Code 40–220, step 1 Code 128 Control Range and step Default Viewing distance 20–200 cm, step 1 57 cm Pixel pitch 0.05–0.6 mm, step 0.001 0.248 mm Control Values or range Default Procedure 1 up / 2 down — 70.7% , 3 down / 1 up — 79.4% , Bayesian tracker — this tool's own , Accelerated — this tool's own , "},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Psychophysics Bench","d":"Symptoms, causes, fixes and workarounds for the Psychophysics Bench, including tabs that do not open.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Only the Lab tab opens; Method, Paradigms, Data, Export and Reference do nothing","The arrow keys do nothing","Stop does not end the run immediately","The staircase climbs to the top and stays there","\"The contrast asked for does not fit about this background\" appears","\"Above the pixel grid's Nyquist limit\" appears","The threshold reads \"—\"","\"At what percentage\" says \"not defined for this ladder\"","The trace stays empty during a run","Practice results disappeared","Intervals look uneven or flicker"],"x":" Why: at the time of writing checked on the live site in September 2026 , the page's tab buttons do not switch the view. Links in the page text that point to another tab for example Data in the note strip, or Paradigms under Task do nothing for the same reason. What this affects: everything on the Lab tab works: designing, running and reading results. The explanation tabs and the Export tab's downloads and link button cannot be reached. What to do: Read the content of those tabs in these docs: Read the results read the results.md summarises Method, Paradigms, Data and Reference, and Export your data export your data.md describes the files. Record results from the Lab readouts, or take a screenshot, before starting another run. Share a setup by building a link by hand, as shown in Export your data export your data.md . Why: answers are accepted only after the intervals of the current trial have finished and the page is waiting; between runs they do nothing. The keys also do nothing when focus is in another window or the browser's address bar. What to do: click an empty part of the page, then use the keys, or use the on screen response buttons. Why: Stop takes effect at the end of th"},{"t":"Psychophysics Bench FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/docs/faq.html","h":["Is this a vision test?","Which staircase should I use?","Why does the threshold come with a percentage?","Is the Bayesian tracker QUEST?","Is the accelerated staircase PEST?","Does it fit a psychometric function, compute d′ or give a confidence interval?","Why is my threshold different every run?","Can I use a different number of alternatives, same/different or odd-one-out?","Why does the page ask for my viewing distance and pixel pitch?","Does it measure my screen's gamma?","Why can I not download my results?","Is anything I do sent anywhere?"],"x":" No. It measures a contrast threshold on your screen under your conditions, as a teaching and exploration instrument. It is not calibrated, not clinical and not a diagnosis. 1 up / 2 down — 70.7% for most purposes: it is the standard transformed up down rule and converges at a stated percentage. 3 down / 1 up — 79.4% converges higher and takes longer. The other three are the tool's own or not adaptive. Because the probability of a correct answer rises gradually with contrast. A threshold is the contrast at a chosen point on that curve, so it means nothing without the point. No. It works on a log scale with a stated prior, like QUEST, but its slope, lapse rate and prior width are the tool's choices rather than estimated or taken from previous measurements, so it carries its own name. No. PEST is a sequential procedure driven by a statistical test; the accelerated staircase simply halves its step at reversals and doubles it after three moves in one direction. Not on screen in the current version. The Data register describes a logistic fit with guess and lapse rates, d′ and criterion for yes/no sessions, and a trial bootstrap, but no readout shows them. Export the session when the Exp"},{"t":"Psychophysics Bench background","d":"Contents of the background material for the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the how to pages with the psychophysics terms the bench uses, its response keys, a statement of what is published and what is the tool's own, related tools and articles, its history and what stays on your device. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Psychophysics and display terms used in the bench shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Response keys, Esc , enlarging the stage and the trace limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The data register entry by entry, display limits and what is not shown related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the bench privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"Psychophysics Bench shortcuts","d":"Response keys and other keyboard and pointer actions in the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys work while the page is waiting for an answer. Site wide shortcuts are described in Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . Key or action Two interval forced choice Yes / no detection ← First interval Yes, I saw it → Second interval No, I did not Esc Stops the run Stops the run Action Where Result Double click The stimulus stage or the staircase trace Opens it enlarged, filling the window Esc Enlarged view Closes it Select the × button or the dark area around the image Enlarged view Closes it Tab Anywhere Moves between controls; sliders then respond to the arrow keys Between runs the arrow keys are not used by the bench, so a focused slider responds to them instead. Click an empty part of the page before a run so the response keys are not also moving a slider. "},{"t":"Psychophysics Bench glossary","d":"Psychophysics and display terms used in the Psychophysics Bench, each explained briefly.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning 2AFC two interval forced choice A task with two intervals, one holding the stimulus; the observer must pick one, so chance is 50% Adaptive staircase A procedure that sets each trial's stimulus from the previous answers so trials cluster near threshold Alias A false pattern that appears when a screen is asked to draw a frequency above its Nyquist limit Background mean luminance The grey the contrast swings around; given as an 8 bit code and converted to relative luminance Bayesian tracker A procedure that keeps a probability distribution over the threshold and updates it after each answer Bootstrap Estimating the uncertainty of a result by refitting many resampled copies of the data Constant stimuli A method that tests at fixed contrasts rather than adapting; here, at the starting contrast only Criterion c and β Signal detection measures of an observer's willingness to say \"yes\" d′ d prime A signal detection measure of sensitivity that separates seeing from willingness to say \"yes\"; needs stimulus absent trials Decibel step A step size given as a ratio: 20 × log₁₀ ratio ; 2 dB multiplies or divides contrast by about 1.26 Degrees per pixel The visual angle one pixel cov"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Psychophysics Bench takes from published sources, what is its own, the limits of an uncalibrated screen, and what it does not show.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the bench is","The data register, in plain terms","Limits of a screen","What the bench does not show","What it does not do"],"x":" An educational instrument for measuring a contrast detection threshold in a browser. It is not a calibrated laboratory system and not a clinical test. Results depend on your screen, your room and your attention as much as on your vision. Entry Status What it means for you sRGB transfer and primaries Verbatim Contrast is converted to screen values with the standard sRGB curve, which is a standard, not a measurement of your screen Transformed up down rules Verbatim 1 up / 2 down and 3 down / 1 up follow Levitt 1971 , including averaging an even number of reversals Extreme proportion correction Verbatim The 1/2N rule of Macmillan and Kaplan 1985 for hit rates of 1 or false alarm rates of 0 Michelson contrast in luminance Computed Every contrast is placed symmetrically around the background's luminance, so the contrast asked for is the contrast drawn, unless capped Viewing geometry Computed Degrees per pixel and the Nyquist limit follow exactly from the distance and pitch you enter Signal detection formulae Computed d′, criterion and β as in Macmillan and Creelman 2005 , for yes/no only Inverse normal CDF Computed An approximation accurate to 4.5 × 10⁻⁴; it caps any d′ at about 6.18 N"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Psychophysics Bench keeps in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What leaves the page, and only when you ask","The rest of the page"],"x":" Your trials, answers and response times are held by the page only for the current run. They are cleared when you start another run or leave the page. All stimulus drawing and every calculation happen in the page. Download the trials and Download the session create files through your browser's normal download. They contain your answers and response times, so treat them as personal data if you collect them from other people. Copy a link to this setup writes a link to your clipboard. It contains settings only, never results. The tool page loads the site's usual pages, styles and scripts, and, depending on your cookie choices, advertising and consent based analytics, like the rest of auricartisan.com. See the Privacy Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ and the Cookie Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/release-notes.html","h":["September 2026 — known issue","September 2026 — rebuilt as the Psychophysics Bench","May 2026"],"x":" The site wide history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The entries below cover what changed for users of this tool. Only the Lab tab opens; the other five tabs, including Export , do not respond. See Troubleshooting ../docs/troubleshooting.md . Changed: Contrast is now Michelson contrast in relative luminance about a stated background, through the sRGB curve. Earlier versions built the grating in screen code values, so a requested 0.02 was drawn at about 0.051. Sessions recorded before this change cannot be converted to the new axis, because their exports did not record the background. Spatial frequency is now in cycles per degree, from a viewing distance and pixel pitch you enter. Earlier versions used cycles across the patch. Staircase steps are ratios in decibels instead of a fixed 0.05, and reversals are averaged geometrically in an even number. The Bayesian and accelerated procedures are named as the tool's own rather than QUEST and PEST. The stage shows the stimulus at the starting contrast between runs. Added: Background , Viewing distance , Pixel pitch , Envelope σ in degrees, Delivered / asked , At what percentage , the Nyquist and contrast cap warnings,"},{"t":"Related tools and articles","d":"Tools and Learn articles related to the Psychophysics Bench.","p":"Website › Tools › Perception and spectral › Psychophysical Experiment Engine","u":"website/tools/perception-and-spectral/psychophysical-experiment-engine/others/related.html","h":["Tools in this group","Other tools on the site","Learn articles","Documentation on the site"],"x":" Neuroscience ../../neuroscience/README.md — the same viewing geometry controls, and a V1 Gabor bank that models the cells a Gabor patch is designed to drive. Perception and Vision ../../perception and vision/README.md — simulate acuity loss, cataract and low light, which all raise contrast thresholds. Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — contrast between two colours for text accessibility, a different measure from the Michelson contrast of a grating. The Learn section is described in Learn ../../../../library/learn/README.md . Contrast Sensitivity: The Spatial Frequencies You Can and Can't See — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 08 24 contrast sensitivity spatial frequency Human Color Vision: Cones, Opponent Signals, and the Brain — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 human color vision cones opponent Color Illusions and the Limits of Perception — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 10 color illusions and perception Psychophysical Experiment Engine User Guide — https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 25 psychophysical experiment engine user guide "},{"t":"Image and file tools","d":"What the six image and file tools on auricartisan.com are for, where to find them, and which one to open for each job.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/README.html","h":["Where to find them","The tools","Which tool for which job","In this folder"],"x":" These six tools work on files you already have: photographs, SVG artwork, colour profiles and colour lookup tables. Each one reads your file in the browser, shows you what is in it, lets you change or measure it, and gives you a file or a report to take away. Nothing you load is uploaded; the reading and the arithmetic happen on the page. The tools share a layout. A row of tabs runs across the top of each tool. The first tab is the working area, and later tabs explain the method, list where every number comes from the Data tab , offer the exports the Export or Actions tab and cite the published sources the Reference tab . The Image Picker is the exception: it has three tabs, Workbench , Analysis and Actions . The group's own address is https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/. Opening it takes you to the Collections page at https://auricartisan.com/collections/, which lists every tool on the site under All tools . Use the category filter or the Sort menu there, or open a tool directly from the table below. The Collections page is described in Collections ../../library/collections/README.md . Tool Address Use it to Collage Maker collage maker/README.md https://auricartisan.com/"},{"t":"Collage Maker","d":"What the Collage Maker does, who it is for, where to find it and how to make a first collage.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Collage Maker the page is titled Collage Studio puts your pictures on a canvas so you can move, scale, rotate, flip and stack them, then export the result as a PNG or JPEG. You choose the shape of the canvas from six presets, round its corners, and decide whether the background is transparent or white. A grid arranger lays the pictures out for you and compares every possible grid before you commit to one. Beside the canvas, the tool measures what you have made. It reports how much of the canvas the pictures cover, how much of it is painted twice where pictures overlap, and how much picture area hangs off the edge and will not be exported. Coverage and overlap are read from the pixels of the same image the export produces, so the figures describe the file you download. Undo reaches back to where you started, including pictures you removed and a canvas you cleared. Pictures are read in the page and drawn straight to the canvas; nothing is uploaded. Designers and social media editors assembling a set of photographs into one image. Anyone who needs a transparent PNG composite with rounded corners. People who want to know, in numbers, how much of the frame their pictures fill befor"},{"t":"Collage Maker documentation","d":"The list of how-to guides, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the Collage Maker, the full reference of its controls and outputs, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started if you have not used the tool before; go to the Reference when you need the exact range or default of a control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the six tabs, and a first collage from start to export build a collage.md build a collage.md Adding pictures, the canvas settings, selecting and editing pictures, the layers list, undo and redo arrange in a grid.md arrange in a grid.md The Layout tab: fit or fill, enlarging small pictures, the arrangement table and applying a grid read the measurements.md read the measurements.md The five readout cards, what each figure measures, and the Measure and Data tabs export and sessions.md export and sessions.md Saving PNG and JPEG, export scale and quality, the clipboard, session files and the reading reference.md reference.md Every tab, control, button, message and file format, with ranges and defaults troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when pictures will not load, exports look wrong, or undo behaves unexpecte"},{"t":"Getting started with the Collage Maker","d":"Open the Collage Maker, find your way around its six tabs, and make and export a first collage.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The screen at a glance","Make a first collage","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/collage maker/. The page opens on the Studio tab with an empty 1200 × 900 canvas. You do not need an account, and nothing needs installing. A note under the page heading explains what the numbers on the page are measurements of. It has no close button on purpose. The tool has six tabs. Tab What it is for Studio The working area: pictures, canvas settings, history, the canvas, layers and readout cards Layout Every grid arrangement for your pictures, laid out and measured, with a button to apply each one Measure How the coverage, overlap and off canvas figures are measured, with worked examples Data A list of every figure on the page and where it comes from; the tab shows the number of entries 12 Export Export scale and JPEG quality, the save, copy and session buttons, file sizes and the reading Reference The published sources the tool relies on, and the arithmetic it runs The Studio tab has two parts. The left hand panel holds, from top to bottom: Pictures the drop box , The canvas shape, padding, gap, corner radius and three switches , History undo and redo , The selected picture sliders and buttons for the picture you have selecte"},{"t":"Arrange pictures in a grid","d":"Use the Layout tab to compare every grid arrangement for your pictures and apply the one you want.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/arrange-in-a-grid.html","h":["How a grid is built","Choose how a picture fits its cell","Read the arrangement table","Apply an arrangement","Tips","What you should see"],"x":" The Layout tab answers one question: which grid gives these pictures the most canvas? Every arrangement is laid out on the real canvas and measured, rather than estimated from the size of the cells, because a cell is only filled by a picture that shares its shape. A grid is a set of equal cells, filled row by row in the order the pictures are painted the bottom of the stack goes in the first cell . Two settings from the Studio tab decide the size of the cells: Padding is the margin between the canvas edge and the block of cells. Gap is the space between neighbouring cells. Both come out of the same canvas. The cell width is the canvas width, minus padding on both sides, minus one gap between each pair of columns, divided by the number of columns; the height works the same way. With a large gap on a small canvas this can come out as zero or less. The tool then refuses that arrangement and says why, rather than drawing it inside out. Only visible pictures are arranged. Hidden pictures keep their place and are not counted. The Fitting group on the left of the Layout tab has two buttons and a switch. Control What it does Fit inside the cell default Scales each picture so all of it sit"},{"t":"Build and edit a collage","d":"Add pictures, set up the canvas, select and edit pictures, use the layers list, and undo or redo any step.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/build-a-collage.html","h":["Add pictures","Set up the canvas","Select a picture","Move, resize and nudge","Change the selected picture","The layers list","Arrange in a grid, or start again","Undo and redo","What you should see"],"x":" Everything in this guide happens on the Studio tab. 1. Drop one or more image files onto the Drop pictures box in the left hand panel. You can also drop them straight onto the canvas, or select the box or press Enter or Space while it has focus to open a file chooser that accepts several files at once. 2. Wait for the message at the bottom of the screen. It reads Added followed by the file name, or Added 4 pictures for a batch. What happens to each picture: It is centred on the canvas. It keeps its own pixels. If it is larger than 42% of the canvas width or height, it is scaled down to fit inside that box; a smaller picture stays at 100%. It is added on top of the others and becomes the selected picture. It appears at the top of the Layers · top first list, with a thumbnail, its file name, its size in pixels and its current scale. Any image type your browser can open is accepted; the box names JPG, PNG, WebP and GIF. Files that are not images are ignored. If a file cannot be decoded, a message reads Could not read followed by its name, and the other files in the batch are still added. Adding a batch is one history step. The controls under The canvas apply to the whole collage. Con"},{"t":"Export, copy and save sessions","d":"Save your collage as PNG or JPEG at the size you need, copy it to the clipboard, and save or reload the layout as a session file.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/export-and-sessions.html","h":["What an export contains","Set the size and quality","Save an image","Copy to the clipboard","Save and load a session","Save the reading","What you should see"],"x":" All exports are on the Export tab. The exported image is the canvas drawn again at the scale you choose. It contains: every visible picture, at its position, scale, rotation, opacity and flip; the background: transparent, or white when Transparent background is cleared; the rounded corners set by Corner radius , scaled with the export. It does not contain: the guides, the selection outline, the corner handles or the chequerboard, which are only on screen; hidden pictures; any part of a picture outside the canvas. The outside the canvas card on the Studio tab tells you how much that is. Under What to take : Control What it does Range Default Scale Multiplies the canvas size for the export 0.25× to 4×, in steps of 0.25 1.00× JPEG quality Compression quality for JPEG only 0.10 to 1.00 0.92 The size line shows the export size in pixels, for example 2400 × 1800 at 2×, and background shows transparent or the colour in use. Pictures are drawn from their own pixels, so exporting larger than 1× is sharp for pictures that were scaled down, and soft for any picture scaled above its own size. 1. Set Scale and, for JPEG, JPEG quality . 2. Select Save the PNG or Save a JPEG . 3. Your browser do"},{"t":"Read the measurements","d":"What the canvas covered, overlapping, outside the canvas and history cards measure, and how to use the Measure and Data tabs.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/read-the-measurements.html","h":["The five cards","Measurement resolution","The Measure tab","The Data tab","The Reference tab"],"x":" Under the canvas on the Studio tab, a row of cards headed What is on the canvas describes the collage. The figures update after every change. Card What it reports How it is found canvas covered The share of the canvas that pictures paint Measured from the pixels overlapping The share of the canvas painted by two or more pictures Measured from the pixels outside the canvas The share of total picture area that lies beyond the edges and will not be exported Computed exactly from positions history How many steps you can undo, back to the start Counted the old readout said The sum of every picture's area divided by the canvas area Computed, for comparison only The outside the canvas card changes colour as a warning when more than 0.1% of picture area is off the canvas. The tool draws the canvas twice, once without the pictures and once with them, exactly as the export would. Every pixel that differs between the two drawings is a pixel a picture has put something on. The figure is that count divided by the number of pixels on the canvas. Because it reads pixels, this figure notices transparency. A PNG cut out with a transparent background covers only its visible part. A picture at 0% op"},{"t":"Collage Maker reference","d":"Every tab, control, button, readout, message and file format in the Collage Maker, with ranges and defaults.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Studio tab — Pictures","Studio tab — The canvas","Studio tab — History","Studio tab — The selected picture","Studio tab — Other buttons","Studio tab — Canvas and layers","Studio tab — Readout cards","Layout tab","Measure tab","Data tab","Export tab","File formats","Messages"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/collage maker/ Tab Contents Studio Pictures, canvas settings, history, selected picture controls, the canvas, the layers list, the readout cards Layout Fitting options, apply buttons, the arrangement table and drawings of the three best arrangements Measure Worked examples of how coverage, overlap and off canvas area are measured Data The list of every figure and its source, filterable by status; the tab label shows the count 12 Export Export scale, JPEG quality, save, copy and session buttons, file sizes, the reading Reference Sources, each marked Runs or Withdrawn , and the arithmetic table Links in the page text for example Measure or Data in a note switch to that tab. Control What it does Accepts Drop pictures box Adds pictures by drag and drop, or opens a file chooser when selected or when Enter or Space is pressed Any image type the browser opens; JPG, PNG, WebP, GIF named The canvas Also accepts dropped image files As above Several files can be added at once. New pictures are centred, scaled down to fit within 42% of the canvas width and height never enlarged , placed on top and selected. Control Values or range Default S"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Collage Maker","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the Collage Maker, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Pictures will not load","A picture is in the wrong place or missing","Grid arrangements","Undo and redo","Exports","Sessions","Still stuck"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do Nothing happens after dropping a file The file is not an image type, so it is ignored Convert it to JPG, PNG, WebP or GIF and try again Could not read followed by a file name Your browser could not decode that file Save it again as JPG or PNG in another program; HEIC and camera RAW files are not opened by every browser The page slows down with many pictures Every change is measured from pixels, once per picture for the overlap figure Use fewer or smaller pictures, or resize very large photographs before adding them Symptom Why What to do A picture cannot be clicked It is hidden, or another picture is on top of it Select it in the Layers · top first list; use Show or Bring to front A picture moved partly off the canvas after changing Shape Changing the shape does not move pictures Use Arrange in a grid , Centre , or drag it back; watch the outside the canvas card Dragging jumps in steps Snap to a 10 px grid is on Clear the switch, or use the arrow keys for 1 px nudges Arrow keys scroll the page instead of nudging The canvas does not have keyboard focus Click the canvas once, then use the arrow keys Symptom Why What to do No arrangement fits at this padding an"},{"t":"Collage Maker FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/docs/faq.html","h":["Are my pictures uploaded?","What file types can I add?","How many pictures can I add?","Can I change the canvas size to something other than the presets?","Can I choose a background colour other than white?","Why do the rounded corners appear in my export?","Why does the export not show the gold outline and the guides?","Does \"Fill the cell, crop\" actually crop my pictures?","Why is \"canvas covered\" lower than I expected for a PNG?","What is \"the old readout said\"?","Does a session file contain my pictures?","Can I undo after clearing the canvas or removing a picture?","Does the tool know how big my collage will print?"],"x":" No. Pictures are read in the page and drawn straight to a canvas in your browser. Nothing is sent to a server. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Any image your browser can open. The drop box names JPG, PNG, WebP and GIF. The export is a still image, so an animated GIF contributes a single frame. The tool sets no fixed limit. Each picture is measured separately for the overlap figure, so very many large pictures make the page slower. No. There are six shapes, all 1200 pixels wide. To get a larger file, use Scale on the Export tab: 4× gives a canvas 4800 pixels wide. The switch offers transparent or white. A session file that carries another background colour will apply it when loaded, but the page has no colour control of its own. Corner radius clips the canvas itself, and the default is 18 px. Set it to 0 px for square corners. They are drawing aids shown only on screen. The export contains the pictures and the background, nothing else. No. It scales each picture to cover its cell, but the part beyond the cell is not cut away; it overlaps the neighbouring pictures or hangs off the canvas. The Overlap and Off canvas columns on the Layout tab show how much. The figure reads pixels."},{"t":"Collage Maker background material","d":"The contents of the Collage Maker's others folder: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the how to guides: the terms the tool uses, its keyboard and pointer actions, what it measures and what it does not, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your files. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in the Collage Maker shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and pointer actions limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What each figure measures, how precisely, and what the tool does not hold related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network "},{"t":"Collage Maker shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts and pointer actions in the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard","Pointer"],"x":" Keys Action Works when Ctrl + Z Undo Focus is not in a slider, menu or text box Ctrl + Shift + Z Redo As above Ctrl + Y Redo As above Arrow keys Nudge the selected picture 1 px The canvas has focus click it first Shift + arrow keys Nudge the selected picture 10 px The canvas has focus Delete or Backspace Remove the selected picture The canvas has focus Enter or Space Open the file chooser The Drop pictures box has focus On a Mac, Cmd works in place of Ctrl . With the canvas focused, one press of the undo or redo shortcut can move two steps; use the Undo and Redo buttons when you want exactly one. Every control on the page can be reached with Tab . Each tab button, slider, switch and button responds to the keyboard in the usual way. Action Result Click a picture Select it the top one where pictures overlap Click empty canvas Clear the selection Drag a picture Move it; snapped to 10 px when snapping is on Drag a corner handle Resize the selected picture around its centre, from 2% to 800% Click a row in Layers · top first Select that picture, including a hidden one Drop image files on the canvas or the drop box Add them as pictures "},{"t":"Collage Maker glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Arrangement A grid of equal cells, given as columns × rows, into which the visible pictures are placed in stacking order Canvas The rectangle the collage is drawn on; always 1200 pixels wide, with a height set by the shape Canvas covered The share of canvas pixels that pictures paint, found by drawing with and without them and counting differences Cell One rectangle of a grid arrangement, sized from the canvas, padding, gap and grid Chequerboard The on screen pattern behind the canvas that shows transparency; never exported Corner radius How far the canvas corners are rounded, in pixels; exports are clipped to the rounded shape Export scale The factor, 0.25× to 4×, by which the canvas size is multiplied when an image is saved or copied Fill Scaling a picture so it covers its whole cell; in this tool the excess is not trimmed away Fit Scaling a picture so all of it lies inside its cell, leaving part of the cell empty if the shapes differ Gap The space between neighbouring cells of a grid arrangement Guides The thirds lines across the canvas and the dashed lines through the selected picture's centre; screen only History step One recorded change that Undo can reverse; th"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Collage Maker measures, how precisely, and what it does not know.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is measured, and how","Choices the tool makes for you","Limits","What the tool is not"],"x":" Figure Method Precision canvas covered The canvas drawn with and without the pictures; differing pixels counted Exact at full size; see resolution below overlapping Each picture drawn alone; pixels painted by two or more counted As above outside the canvas Each picture's corners after scale and rotation, clipped to the canvas Exact geometry, no pixels involved Covered on the Layout tab Placed area minus pairwise overlap Exact unless three pictures meet at one point, when it shows a dash Export file sizes The encoded file, measured before it is offered Exact for your browser Coverage and overlap are read from the same drawing the export uses, so they describe the file you download at 1× scale. Canvases up to 1,440,000 pixels are measured at full size. Larger canvases the 9 : 16 and 2 : 3 shapes are measured on a proportionally smaller copy; the label above the canvas then reads measured at followed by the size used. The resulting percentages agree with a full size measurement to well under a tenth of a percentage point. A pixel counts as covered when any picture changes it. Fully transparent pixels in a picture and pictures at 0% opacity change nothing and are not counted. A pictur"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Collage Maker does with your pictures, and what stays in your browser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/privacy.html","h":["Your pictures stay in your browser","Nothing is kept after you leave","What a session file contains","The page itself"],"x":" Pictures are read by the page itself and drawn straight to a canvas in your browser. The tool does not upload them or send them anywhere. The measurements, the arrangement comparison and the exports are all worked out on your device. Exported files PNG, JPEG, session and reading are created in the browser and saved by your browser's normal download. The clipboard is used only when you select Copy to the clipboard , and only to place the PNG there. The tool does not store your pictures, your layout or your history. Reloading or leaving the page clears them. To keep a layout, save a session file; to keep the picture, save a PNG or JPEG. A session file contains the canvas settings and, for each picture, its file name, position, size, scale, rotation, opacity, flips and visibility. It contains no image data. If you share a session file, the recipient sees your picture file names. The Collage Maker is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wide features such as sign in, preferences and any consent based services follow the site's own privacy policy and your cookie choices; they are covered in the site's help pages at Help ../../../../../help/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version — the measured studio","25 May 2026 — earlier version"],"x":" The tool was rebuilt as the Collage Studio workbench, with six tabs: Studio , Layout , Measure , Data , Export and Reference . The developer reference that describes this version in the site's documentation library is dated 5 June 2026. What changed for you: Undo reaches the start. Every step records the state before the change, so undoing takes you all the way back. A removed picture, or a cleared canvas, comes back with the step that removed it. Exports contain only the collage. Guides, the selection outline, corner handles and the transparency chequerboard are drawn only on screen. A PNG saved with Transparent background ticked is transparent. Coverage is measured. The single coverage figure, which added up picture areas, is replaced by canvas covered and overlapping read from pixels, and outside the canvas computed from positions. The old figure stays on screen as the old readout said for comparison. The Layout tab lays out and measures every grid arrangement before you apply one, and marks a winner only when one truly covers more. Two features were withdrawn: a \"95% confidence interval\" for coverage and a batch table of hypothetical layouts. Neither measured the collage on th"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools and Learn articles that work well with the Collage Maker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Collage Maker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/collage-maker/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with the Collage Maker Image Picker ../../image picker/README.md Take a palette from a finished collage exported as PNG or JPEG SVG Recolour ../../svg recolour/README.md Recolour vector artwork before exporting it as a picture for a collage LUT Lab ../../lut lab/README.md Check what a colour grade does to your photographs Basic Tools ../../../colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md The Basic Tools workspace includes its own quick collage panel Vision Simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md See how the finished collage looks with different kinds of colour vision Color Theory and Harmony — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony RGB, sRGB, Adobe RGB, ProPhoto, Display P3, and Rec.2020 — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 rgb working spaces compared Skin Tones and Inclusive Color — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 18 skin tones and inclusive color The group overview: Image and file tools ../../README.md . The site's documentation library carries a developer reference for the collage measurements, \"Collage Measurement Developer Ref"},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser","d":"What the ICC Profile Parser does, who it is for, where to find it and how to read a first profile.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The ICC Profile Parser the page is titled ICC Profile Reading opens a colour profile file, .icc or .icm , and tells you what it says. An ICC profile is a small file, defined by the International Color Consortium, that describes how a device or colour space reproduces colour, so that software can convert colours between devices. The tool reads the profile's header at the byte positions the ICC specification ICC.1:2010, also published as ISO 15076 1:2010 sets out, lists every tag in the file, and runs a conformance check in which every finding names the clause of the specification it enforces. For RGB display style profiles, it recovers the primaries behind the stored colorants, draws them on a CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram, plots the tone curves, and identifies which of six well known colour spaces the profile matches most closely: sRGB, Rec. 709, Display P3, Adobe RGB 1998 , Rec. 2020 or ProPhoto RGB. It reports gamut area and coverage against the space you choose, using the more even CIE 1976 u′v′ diagram. For press and other profiles with no colorants, it walks the profile's lookup table to draw the gamut in CIELAB instead. The file is read in the page and never sent anywhere. Y"},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser documentation","d":"The list of guides, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the ICC Profile Parser, a concept page on how ICC profiles are organised, the full reference of every field and rule the tool shows, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. If ICC profiles are new to you, read Understand ICC profiles before the other guides. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the six tabs, and reading a first profile understand icc profiles.md understand icc profiles.md What a profile is: classes, colour spaces, the connection space, tags, versions, intents, curves and tables identify and gamut.md identify and gamut.md The verdict, the ranking table, the chromaticity diagram, gamut area and coverage, and the tone curves check conformance.md check conformance.md Reading findings, what error, warning and note mean, and the Conformance tab export a reading.md export a reading.md Saving and copying the JSON reading and the tag table CSV reference.md reference.md Every header field, value table, tag type, rule, readout and export format troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when a file will not read or a panel stays empty faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the ICC Profile Parser","d":"Open the ICC Profile Parser, find your way around its tabs, and read a first profile.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","Find a profile to read","The screen at a glance","Read a first profile","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/icc profile parser/. The page opens on the Lab tab. Until you load a file, the main panel reads Nothing loaded yet and explains what the tool will and will not tell you. A note under the heading explains what the numbers on the page are measurements of. It has no close button on purpose. An ICC profile is a file ending in .icc or .icm that describes how a device or colour space reproduces colour. Your computer already has some: Windows: C:\\Windows\\System32\\spool\\drivers\\color\\ macOS: /Library/ColorSync/Profiles/ , ~/Library/ColorSync/Profiles/ and /System/Library/ColorSync/Profiles/ Monitor calibration software, printer drivers and paper manufacturers also supply profiles. The tool reads standalone profile files. A profile embedded inside a JPEG, PNG, TIFF or PDF must first be saved out as its own file by another application. Tab What it is for Lab Load a profile; read the header, verdict, diagrams, figures, findings and tag table Method How each figure is derived, in five sections Conformance The rules the check runs, filtered by severity, with the clause each one enforces Data Every figure and what it rests on; the tab shows the "},{"t":"Check conformance","d":"Read the conformance verdict and findings, understand error, warning and note, and use the Conformance tab to see every rule and the clause it enforces.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/check-conformance.html","h":["Read the result","Read a finding","The rules","The Conformance tab","What a pass means"],"x":" Every profile you load is checked against 23 rules. Each rule either holds or raises a finding. Every rule cites the clause of ICC.1:2010 it enforces, except two that are marked as house preferences because the specification does not require them. 1. Load a profile on the Lab tab. 2. Look at the conformance card under the diagrams: clean — no rule raised anything; no errors — only warnings or notes were raised; the profile is still conformant; 1 error , 2 errors and so on — the profile breaks that many rules graded as errors. The card turns red. 3. Read the last sentence of the verdict. It says either \"It is conformant: N of 23 rules pass\", adding how many findings are below the level of an error, or how many rules the profile should satisfy do not hold. 4. Scroll to Findings . When every rule holds you see a single Pass line, All 23 rules hold . Otherwise there is one row per finding. A profile is conformant when no rule graded as an error is broken. There is no score out of 100: a profile is conformant or it is not, and where it is not the clause says why. Each finding row shows: Part Example Meaning Severity warning error , warning or note Title The profile ID matches the bytes"},{"t":"Export a reading","d":"Save or copy the full JSON reading of a profile, save its tag table as CSV, and see what each export contains.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/export-a-reading.html","h":["Save the reading","Copy the reading","Save the tag table as CSV","Clear","Preview the reading on the Export tab","What the reading contains"],"x":" A reading is the tool's full account of a profile as a JSON file: the header with the clause behind each field, the tag table, the identification, the gamut figures and every conformance finding. Every derived figure carries the clause or the method it came from, so someone else can check it without opening this page. 1. Load a profile on the Lab tab. 2. Under Take it away , select Save the reading . 3. Your browser downloads a file named after the profile, for example srgb color space profile reading.json for sRGB Color Space Profile.icm . The name is the file name in lower case, with the .icc or .icm ending removed and anything other than letters and digits turned into hyphens. If no profile is loaded, the message reads Load a profile first and nothing is saved. Select Copy it to place the same JSON on the clipboard, ready to paste into a ticket or a message. The message reads Copied the reading , or The clipboard refused if your browser blocks clipboard access. Select Tag table, CSV to download a spreadsheet ready list of every tag, named like the reading but ending tags.csv . text signature,type,offset,size,aligned,in bounds,shares with desc,desc,240,108,yes,yes, A2B0,mft2,576"},{"t":"Identify a profile and read its gamut","d":"Read the verdict and ranking, choose a reference space, and interpret the chromaticity diagram, gamut area, coverage and tone curves.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/identify-and-gamut.html","h":["The verdict","The ranking table","Choose the space to compare against","The chromaticity diagram","The tone-response plot","Profiles with no colorants","The figure cards","The Method tab"],"x":" After you load a profile on the Lab tab, the right hand panel opens with What this profile is . This guide explains each part of it. The verdict is a heading and a few sentences. Profile Heading reads, for example Has RGB colorants \"An sRGB profile, matrix/TRC, ICC v2.1.0\" No colorants, but a readable A2B table \"A CMYK output profile, ICC v2.0.0\" Anything else \"An ICC v4.3.0 display profile\" The sentences under the heading say: how far the colorants sit from the closest space's primaries, in CIE 1976 u′v′, and which of two adaptation methods, Bradford or XYZ scaling, fits the profile better; how closely the tone curve fits that space's published transfer function, as a peak difference; for a profile with no colorants, which table its gamut was read from, how many grid points it has and the range of CIELAB lightness L it covers; whether it is conformant: \"It is conformant: 21 of 23 rules pass, with 2 below the level of an error\", or how many rules it should satisfy do not hold. Two extra lines can appear: \"This profile cannot be told apart from Rec. 709 here\" appears when two reference spaces share the same primaries and white, and the profile has no tone curve to separate them. sR"},{"t":"Understand ICC profiles","d":"The concepts you need to read an ICC profile: classes, colour spaces, the connection space, tags, versions, intents, colorants, curves and tables.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/understand-icc-profiles.html","h":["What a profile is for","The profile connection space","Device classes","Data colour space and channels","Versions","Rendering intents","Tags","Two ways to describe a device","Colorants are not primaries","Tone response curves","The profile ID","What a profile cannot tell you"],"x":" This page explains the parts of an ICC profile that the ICC Profile Parser shows you. It is a short primer, not a replacement for the specification, ICC.1:2010 also published as ISO 15076 1:2010 . A colour management system converts colours from one device to another, for example from a camera to a monitor, or from a monitor to a printing press. It does this in two halves. Each device has a profile that converts between the device's own colour values and a shared, device independent space called the profile connection space PCS . Converting from device A to device B means going from A into the PCS with A's profile, then out of the PCS with B's profile. An ICC profile is the file that holds one of those halves. It has three parts: 1. a 128 byte header that says what kind of profile it is; 2. a tag table that lists the pieces of data inside; 3. the tag data itself: curves, matrices, tables and text. The PCS is either CIE XYZ or CIELAB, always relative to the D50 illuminant, a standard daylight white at about 5000 K. The header's PCS field says which. D50 is fixed by the specification, which is why the tool checks that the header's PCS illuminant is D50 and that a display profile's m"},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser reference","d":"Every tab, control, header field, value table, tag type, readout, rule and export format in the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — controls","Lab tab — What the header says","Value tables","Tag types the tool reads","Lab tab — the reading","Reference spaces","Conformance rules","Method tab","Conformance tab","Data tab","Reference tab","Export formats","Messages"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/icc profile parser/ Tab Contents Lab The drop box, header fields, Compare against , export buttons, and the full reading of the loaded profile Method Five sections explaining how each figure is derived Conformance All 23 rules, filterable by severity, with clauses and the two withdrawn checks Data The 20 entries that every figure rests on, filterable by status Export The contents, size and file name of the reading, and a preview Reference The nine published sources, filterable by whether they run in the tool Control What it does Values Drop a profile Loads a profile by drag and drop, or opens a chooser when selected or when Enter or Space is pressed .icc , .icm or application/vnd.iccprofile in the chooser Compare against Chooses the reference space for the diagram, the tone curve plot and the area cards sRGB, Rec. 709, Display P3, Adobe RGB 1998 , Rec. 2020, ProPhoto RGB Save the reading Downloads the reading as JSON — Copy it Copies the reading to the clipboard — Tag table, CSV Downloads the tag table as CSV — Clear Removes the loaded profile — Only one profile is loaded at a time. Loading another replaces it. Field Shows Examp"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the ICC Profile Parser","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the ICC Profile Parser, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The file will not read","A panel is empty or missing","The figures look wrong","Findings","Clipboard and downloads"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do A profile is at least 132 bytes; this file is N. The file is too short to hold a header and tag count Check you chose the right file; it may be empty or cut short by a failed download Bytes 36 39 are … not 'acsp' — this is not an ICC profile. The file does not carry the ICC signature You may have dropped an image, a PDF or another format. Save the embedded profile out as a standalone .icc file first My .icc file is greyed out in the file chooser The chooser filters for .icc and .icm Drag the file onto the Drop a profile box instead, or rename it with the right ending The reader could not get through this file: … Reading stopped part way, usually because the file is damaged Try the original source of the profile. The reason after the colon says where it failed That file could not be read The browser could not open the file Check the file is not locked or still downloading, then try again Symptom Why What to do No ranking table, diagram or tone curves The profile has no RGB colorants for example a CMYK, greyscale or LUT only RGB profile This is expected. A CMYK profile with an A2B table shows a CIELAB hull instead No gamut hull for a CMYK profile Its A2B table"},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/docs/faq.html","h":["Is my profile uploaded?","Which files can I open?","Can I compare two profiles side by side?","Why does my monitor profile say \"sRGB\" when I calibrated a wide-gamut screen?","What does \"matrix/TRC\" mean?","Why are the stored colorants and the primaries different triangles?","Is \"136% sRGB\" coverage?","Does a clean result mean my colours are right?","Why is there no score out of 100?","Can the tool fix or edit a profile?","Can it convert colours using the profile?","Why is a named-colour profile nearly empty?"],"x":" No. The file is read in the page and never sent anywhere. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Standalone ICC profiles, usually ending .icc or .icm , of version 2 or version 4. A profile embedded in an image or PDF must be saved out as its own file first. A version other than 2 or 4 is still read, with a warning. Not on one page. The tool holds one profile at a time. To compare, save a reading of each and compare the JSON files, or open the tool in two browser tabs. The verdict names the closest of six reference spaces. Check the Primaries Δu′v′ column: if the first row's distance is large, the match is loose. Also check whether the menu under Compare against shows the space you expect. The profile describes an RGB device with three colorants a matrix and three tone response curves TRCs . See Understand ICC profiles understand icc profiles.md . Colorants are stored after adaptation to D50, the connection space white. The primaries of the space the profile describes are recovered by reversing that adaptation. The diagram shows both so you can see the difference. No. That kind of figure is an area ratio. The tool gives both: area, u′v′ is the area ratio, and covers of it is the true s"},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser background material","d":"The contents of the ICC Profile Parser's others folder: glossary, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the guides: the terms the tool uses, what it can and cannot read and how precisely, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your files. The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond standard keyboard access, so there is no shortcuts page. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in the ICC Profile Parser limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the tool reads, how precisely, and what it does not hold related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"ICC Profile Parser glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning A2B / B2A table Tables converting device values to the PCS A2B or back B2A ; 0, 1, 2 are perceptual, colorimetric, saturation Area ratio The area of one gamut triangle divided by another's; can exceed 100% Bradford transform The standard chromatic adaptation method, from Lam 1985 , carried by the chad tag chad tag A 3×3 matrix recording how the colorants were adapted to D50 Chromatic adaptation Converting colour values from one white point to another Chromaticity diagram A plot of colour without brightness; the tool uses CIE 1931 xy for drawing CIE 1976 u′v′ A chromaticity diagram in which equal distances look more nearly equal than in xy CIELAB A colour space with lightness L and two colour axes, a green to red and b blue to yellow Clause A numbered section of ICC.1:2010 that a conformance rule enforces CLUT Colour lookup table: a grid of output values sampled at points across the input CMM Colour management module, the software that performs conversions; named in the header Colorant The stored XYZ value of a primary, already adapted to D50 Conformant Breaking no rule graded as an error Coverage The share of a reference gamut that lies inside the profile's gamut; at "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the ICC Profile Parser can and cannot read, how precise its figures are, and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it reads","What it cannot read","How the figures are found, and how precise they are","Choices the tool makes","What it is not"],"x":" Standalone profile files of ICC version 2 and version 4, at the byte positions ICC.1:2010 ISO 15076 1:2010 gives. The whole header, the full tag table, and the tag types listed in the Reference ../docs/reference.md : text, descriptions, multi language text, XYZ values, tone curves in every form, the chad matrix, signatures, and lut8 and lut16 tables. A tag that cannot be decoded is reported as a finding, and the rest of the profile is still read. Item What happens Profiles embedded in images or PDFs Not read. Save the profile out as its own file first Version 4 mAB , mBA tables Listed in the tag table but not decoded; no gamut hull is drawn from them mpet multi process elements Its structure is read; the pipeline is not run, so its behaviour is not measured ncl2 named colours Not resolved to colours and not listed on the page Private tags such as vcgt Listed with their type, not decoded Description and copyright text Read, but not printed on the page or in the reading Figure Method Notes Header fields Read directly at the published offsets Exact Profile ID match MD5 recomputed with the flags, intent and ID fields zeroed Exact Primaries Colorants un adapted with the profile's chad "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the ICC Profile Parser does with your profile files.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/privacy.html","h":["Your profile stays in your browser","Nothing is kept after you leave","What a reading contains","The page itself"],"x":" The profile file is read by the page itself in your browser. The tool does not upload it or send it anywhere. Every figure, diagram and finding is worked out on your device. Save the reading and Tag table, CSV create their files in the browser and save them through your browser's normal download. Copy it writes the reading to your clipboard only when you select it. The tool does not store the profile or the reading. Clear , reloading, or leaving the page removes them. A reading contains the profile's file name and size, its header values, its tag table, the tool's identification, gamut figures and findings. It does not contain the profile file itself. The file name appears in the reading, so check that it says nothing you would rather not share. The ICC Profile Parser is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wide features such as sign in, preferences and any consent based services follow the site's own privacy policy and your cookie choices; see Help ../../../../../help/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/release-notes.html","h":["4 June 2026 — ICC Profile Reading","25 May 2026 — earlier version"],"x":" The earlier engine was replaced by the current workbench, titled ICC Profile Reading , with six tabs: Lab , Method , Conformance , Data , Export and Reference . The site's earlier user guide carries a notice that it describes the engine replaced on this date. What changed for you: The version is read correctly. The version now comes from the whole of byte 8 and the two halves of byte 9, as the specification says. Profiles are no longer reported as version 0.2 or 0.4, and no longer flagged for an \"unusual\" version. Shared tag data is allowed. Two tags pointing at one data block, which the specification permits, are shown as sharing rather than reported as corrupt. A partial overlap is still an error. Identification works on conformant profiles. Reference spaces are adapted into the connection space before comparing, so a correct D50 white no longer counts against a profile. The ranking shows primaries distance, curve fit and white separately instead of one blended score. Colorants and primaries are drawn separately. The diagram shows the stored colorants, the primaries recovered from them, and the reference space. Area in u′v′, and coverage. Gamut area is given in CIE 1976 u′v′ wit"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools and Learn articles that go with the ICC Profile Parser.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › ICC Profile Parser","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/icc-profile-parser/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with the ICC Profile Parser Gamut Explorer ../../../colorimetry and rendering/gamut lab/README.md Inspect device and working space gamuts in chromaticity and 3D views Gamut Mapping ../../../colorimetry and rendering/gamut map/README.md Explore how colours are mapped between gamuts, and rendering intents Chromatic Adaptation ../../../colorimetry and rendering/chromatic adaptation/README.md Work with Bradford and other adaptation transforms directly Illuminants ../../../colorimetry and rendering/illuminants/README.md Look up D50, D65 and other standard illuminants LUT Lab ../../lut lab/README.md Read and write .cube lookup tables, a different kind of colour transform file ICC Profiles and How Color Management Actually Works — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 icc profiles color management How to Calibrate and Profile a Display — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 how to calibrate and profile a display RGB, sRGB, Adobe RGB, ProPhoto, Display P3, and Rec.2020 — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 rgb working spaces compared Gamma, Linear Light, and Transfer Functions — https://auricartisa"},{"t":"Image Picker","d":"What the Image Picker does, who it is for, where to find it and how to take a first palette from a picture.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Image Picker the page is titled Image Color Picker & Palette Tool turns a picture into a palette. Drop a photograph, a screenshot or a scan and the tool samples its pixels, groups them into clusters with the k means++ method, and shows the resulting colours with the share of the picture each one takes up. For flat artwork such as logos and icons, where the picture has no more distinct colours than you asked for, it keeps the exact colours instead of averages. Alongside the palette it sorts the colours into shadows, midtones and highlights, lists the pairs with the most contrast for text by the WCAG 2 ratio, and spots harmony relationships between the colours. A live eyedropper reads any pixel under the pointer, and a click pins it, so you can keep exact colours the clustering merged away. The Analysis tab charts the same palette four ways. You can copy the palette as hex values, CSS custom properties or JSON, download it as SVG, JSON or CSV, and analyse a list of hex colours without any picture at all. Pictures are read in the page; nothing is uploaded. Designers building a palette from a photograph, moodboard or product shot. Brand and editorial teams auditing the colours in "},{"t":"Image Picker documentation","d":"The list of guides, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the Image Picker, the full reference of its controls and outputs, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started, then go to the guide for the job you have. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the three tabs, and a first palette extract a palette.md extract a palette.md Loading a picture from a file or a web address, and every extraction setting pick exact colours.md pick exact colours.md The live eyedropper, pinning pixels, and managing pins read contrast and harmony.md read contrast and harmony.md Swatches, tone bands, contrast pairs and harmony relationships chart the palette.md chart the palette.md The four charts on the Analysis tab and the full screen view export and share.md export and share.md Copying hex, CSS and JSON; downloading SVG, JSON and CSV; the page link batch analysis.md batch analysis.md Analysing a typed list of hex colours on the Actions tab reference.md reference.md Every control, value, readout, file format and keyboard key troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when a picture will not load or a control seems to do nothing faq.md faq.md Short"},{"t":"Getting started with the Image Picker","d":"Open the Image Picker, find your way around its three tabs, and take a first palette from a picture.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The screen at a glance","Take a first palette","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/image picker/. The page opens on the Workbench tab with a large empty panel that reads Drop an image anywhere in here . Under the page heading there may be a short line that begins Automate this . It says the same job is available through the site's REST API, what one call costs in API credits, and links to the API documentation. You can close it with × ; it stays closed in that browser. You do not need the API to use the tool. Tab What it is for Workbench Load a picture, set the extraction, see the preview, the palette, the tone bands and the readouts Analysis Four charts of the current palette; the tab label shows 4 Actions Download JSON or CSV, copy the page link, and analyse a list of hex colours The Workbench has three columns. Left: The image file name, size, and the Replace and Load URL buttons with a web address field , Extraction the Clusters , Quality and Merge threshold sliders and the Ignore dark and Ignore light switches , Run Re extract and Reset , and History how many extractions you have run . Middle: before a picture is loaded, the drop area. After, the Preview with the eyedropper readout and Pin button, the Extrac"},{"t":"Analyse a list of hex colours","d":"Use batch colour analysis on the Actions tab to get RGB, HSL, CIELAB, LCH, luminance and tone band for a list of hex colours.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/batch-analysis.html","h":["Run a batch","The results table","Input rules","Messages","Uses"],"x":" Batch colour analysis gives the same figures the palette uses for any list of colours you type or paste. No picture is needed. 1. Open the Actions tab. 2. In the box under Batch colour analysis , type or paste hex colours. Separate them with new lines, commas, semicolons or spaces. The is optional. text 3. Select Run batch . 4. A table appears under the box, one row per colour. Column Meaning Example Position in your list 1 Swatch The colour — Hex The colour as six digit hex, in capitals D3AF37 RGB Red, green, blue, 0 to 255 211,175,55 HSL Hue, saturation, lightness 46° 64% 52% Lab CIELAB lightness, a , b , for a D65 white 72.8,0.9,62.8 LCH CIELAB lightness, chroma, hue angle 72.8,62.8,89° Lum WCAG relative luminance, 0 to 1 0.4478 Tone Shadow, Midtone or Highlight Midtone The example column shows the row for D3AF37 . The tone bands use the same limits as the Workbench : below 0.18 is a Shadow, below 0.65 a Midtone, and 0.65 or above a Highlight. Three digit hex values such as abc are expanded to six digits AABBCC . Entries that are not hex values are skipped. Use three or six digit hex. The box accepts four and eight digit values with an alpha part , but they are not read as the "},{"t":"Chart the palette","d":"Read the four charts on the Analysis tab and open any of them full screen.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/chart-the-palette.html","h":["Open the charts","The four charts","Full screen","When the charts update"],"x":" The Analysis tab draws the current palette four ways. Every chart is drawn in the palette's own colours, so a bar and a swatch of the same colour are the same cluster. 1. Extract a palette on the Workbench tab. 2. Select the Analysis tab. 3. The left hand panel, Charting , names the picture and its working size and pixel count, for example 667 × 500 · 333,500 px . Until a picture is loaded, the tab reads Nothing charted yet . Chart Subtitle What it shows Cluster population share of the samples One bar per cluster, largest first, with the share of the largest and smallest at the top Colour distribution every cluster A ring divided by share, with the leading share, its hex value and the cluster count in the middle Hue vs saturation HSL scatter Each cluster placed by hue 0° to 360° across and saturation 0% to 100% up ; larger dots are larger shares Relative luminance WCAG, 0 → 1 One bar per cluster, sorted from darkest to lightest, height set by relative luminance Details: Cluster population labels each bar with its share when there is room; with many clusters the labels are left off, and the share is still on the swatch. Colour distribution labels slices larger than 8% with their sh"},{"t":"Export and share","d":"Copy the palette as hex, CSS custom properties or JSON, download it as SVG, JSON or CSV, and copy the page link.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/export-and-share.html","h":["What each export contains","Hex","CSS","JSON","SVG","CSV","Copy the page link","Automate it"],"x":" There are two places to take a palette away: Take it with you on the right of the Workbench tab, and Download on the Actions tab. The page shows no confirmation after copying or downloading. Paste the text, or check your downloads, to confirm. Export Where Contains Pins included Hex Workbench Palette hex values, comma separated No CSS Workbench Palette as CSS custom properties No JSON copy Workbench Full analysis Yes SVG Workbench A strip of palette swatches with labels, downloaded No JSON download Actions Full analysis, as palette analysis.json Yes CSV Actions One row per palette colour, as palette.csv No The heading Take it with you says palette + pins , but only the JSON carries the pins. Selecting Hex , or pressing H , copies the palette in order of share: text Selecting CSS copies a block of numbered custom properties: css :root { palette 01: 2E4A5C; palette 02: D9C7A8; palette 03: 8A6A4F; palette 04: C0392B; } Selecting JSON on the Workbench , or pressing J , copies the full analysis. JSON on the Actions tab downloads the same content as palette analysis.json . json { \"image\": { \"width\": 4032, \"height\": 3024, \"canvasWidth\": 667, \"canvasHeight\": 500, \"label\": \"harbour.jpg\" },"},{"t":"Extract a palette","d":"Load a picture from a file or a web address, and use every extraction setting to get the palette you want.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/extract-a-palette.html","h":["Load a picture","How the palette is made","The extraction settings","Re-extract, reset and history","What you should see"],"x":" 1. On the Workbench tab, drop an image onto the middle panel, or select the panel to open a file chooser. 2. To load a different picture later, select Replace under The image and choose a file. The drop area is only there until a picture is loaded. After that, use Replace , or select Reset or press R to bring the drop area back. Accepted: any image your browser can open. The drop area names PNG, JPEG, WEBP, GIF and BMP. A file that is not an image is ignored. 1. Type or paste the image's address into the field under The image , for example https://example.com/image.jpg . 2. Select Load URL , or press Enter in the field. This only works when the server hosting the image allows other websites to read its pixels known as cross origin access, or CORS . Many sites do not. If nothing appears, download the image and load it as a file instead. The picture is shrunk, if necessary, to fit a working area of 800 × 500 pixels, keeping its proportions. It is never enlarged. The line under the file name shows the original size, the working size and the name, for example 4032 × 3024 → 667 × 500 harbour.jpg . The palette is extracted straight away with the current settings. 1. Sampling. The tool r"},{"t":"Pick exact colours","d":"Use the live eyedropper to read any pixel, pin exact colours, and copy them.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/pick-exact-colours.html","h":["Read a pixel","Pin a colour","Use your pins","Copy a palette colour"],"x":" The palette is made of averages. When you need the exact colour of one spot, such as a logo's red or a product's trim, use the eyedropper and pins. 1. Load a picture on the Workbench tab. 2. Hover the Preview . The readout beside the swatch under it shows the colour under the pointer: text RGB 192,57,43 · HSL 6°,63%,46% · L=0.1431 · px 212,88 Part Meaning C0392B The hex value RGB … Red, green and blue, 0 to 255 HSL … Hue in degrees, saturation and lightness in percent L= Relative luminance, 0 black to 1 white , as used by WCAG px … The pixel's position in the working copy of the picture, not in the original When the pointer leaves the preview, the readout returns to Hover the image to preview . The eyedropper reads the working copy, which is shrunk to fit 800 × 500. On a large photograph each working pixel stands for several original pixels. 1. Hover the spot you want. 2. Click. The exact colour is added to Pinned on the right. Rule Detail Limit Up to 24 pins. Adding a 25th removes the oldest Duplicates A colour already pinned is not added again Transparent pixels Nearly transparent pixels cannot be pinned Counter The heading reads Pinned with the count, for example 3 of 24 Clicki"},{"t":"Read contrast pairs, tone bands and harmony","d":"What the swatches, tone bands, contrast pairs and harmony readouts tell you about a palette taken from a picture.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/read-contrast-and-harmony.html","h":["The swatches","Tone bands","Pairs that carry text","Harmony","What you should see"],"x":" Once a palette is extracted, the Workbench tab describes it in four ways. All four use the extracted palette only; pinned colours are not included. Each swatch under Extracted palette shows: Line Example Meaning Inside the swatch 24% Share of the sampled pixels in this cluster First line 2E4A5C Hex value Second line 203° 33% 27% HSL: hue, saturation, lightness Third line L=0.063 Relative luminance, 0 black to 1 white The heading reads, for example, 6 clusters · 41750 samples : how many colours the palette has and how many pixels were sampled. Tone bands sorts the palette by relative luminance, the brightness measure used by WCAG: Band Relative luminance Shadows Below 0.18 Midtones 0.18 to below 0.65 Highlights 0.65 and above A band with no colours reads None . The bands show where the weight of the palette sits: a moody photograph piles up in Shadows , a high key one in Highlights . Pairs that carry text , marked WCAG 2.1 , lists the eight pairs of palette colours with the highest contrast ratio. The contrast ratio is the WCAG measure of how different two colours are in brightness, from 1:1 identical to 21:1 black on white . Each row shows the two swatches, the ratio, a rating, an"},{"t":"Image Picker reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, export format and keyboard key in the Image Picker, with ranges and starting values.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/reference.html","h":["Above the tabs","Tabs","Workbench — The image","Workbench — Extraction","Workbench — Run and history","Workbench — Preview and palette","Workbench — Readouts","Analysis tab","Actions tab","Export formats","Batch results","Keyboard"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/image picker/ Element What it does Read the API reference → Opens the site's API documentation Automate this line The REST endpoint and its cost in API credits; API docs opens its documentation; × hides the line Tab Contents Workbench Loading, extraction settings, preview and eyedropper, palette, tone bands, contrast pairs, harmony, pins, quick exports Analysis Four charts of the current palette; the label shows 4 Actions JSON and CSV downloads, Copy page link , batch colour analysis Control What it does Accepts Drop area middle panel, before loading Loads a dropped image, or opens a file chooser when selected Any image type; PNG, JPEG, WEBP, GIF, BMP named Replace Opens a file chooser to load a different picture As above Address field The web address of an image https://… Load URL Loads the address in the field; Enter in the field does the same Images whose server allows cross origin reading File name and size line The name, and original size → working size — Pictures are scaled down to fit 800 × 500 pixels, never up. Control Values Starting value Clusters 2 to 12 on the slider 16 when the page opens Quality Fast every 10th pix"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the Image Picker","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the Image Picker, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Loading pictures","The palette","Eyedropper and pins","Copying and exports","Batch analysis","Charts"],"x":" The Image Picker does not show pop up messages, so when something fails, the usual sign is that nothing changes. This page lists the common causes. Symptom Why What to do Nothing happens after dropping or choosing a file The file is not an image, or your browser cannot decode it Save it as PNG or JPEG and try again. Some formats, such as HEIC or camera RAW, are not opened by every browser Dropping a second picture on the preview opens it in the browser instead The drop area is only active before a picture is loaded Use Replace , or select Reset first to bring the drop area back Load URL does nothing The address is not an image, cannot be reached, or the server does not allow other sites to read its pixels Download the image and load it with Replace After Load URL the middle panel goes blank The picture loaded, but its server does not allow its pixels to be read cross origin protection Download the image and load it as a file The size line shows a much smaller working size Pictures are shrunk to fit 800 × 500 for analysis This is expected; the palette still covers the whole picture Symptom Why What to do The Clusters label says 16 but the slider will not go past 12 The page starts "},{"t":"Image Picker FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/docs/faq.html","h":["Is my picture uploaded?","Why do I get different colours each time I extract?","Why is a colour I can see not in the palette?","Are the swatches real pixel colours?","How many colours can I extract?","Does the contrast check mean the pairs are accessible?","What colour space are the Lab and LCH values in?","Can I compare palettes from two pictures?","Can I share my palette with a link?","Is there an API for this?"],"x":" No. A picture you load from a file is read in the page and never leaves the tab. When you use Load URL , your browser fetches the image from that address, as it would for any web page. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . The k means++ method starts from randomly chosen colours, so two runs on the same picture can settle on slightly different averages. Flat artwork with few colours is not affected, because its exact colours are used. The palette holds the colours that cover the most of the picture. A small detail may not make up enough pixels to become a cluster. Raise Clusters or Quality , or pin the colour with the eyedropper. For flat artwork with no more distinct colours than the cluster count, yes. For photographs, each swatch is the average of a cluster of similar pixels, and may not match any single pixel exactly. Pins are always exact pixels of the working copy. The slider goes from 2 to 12. When the page first opens it uses 16 until you move the slider. It gives the WCAG 2 contrast ratio and rating for the strongest eight pairs, as a first pass. Test the exact text and background pair you plan to use, at its real size, in a dedicated contrast tool. CIELAB and its LCH form, "},{"t":"Image Picker background material","d":"The contents of the Image Picker's others folder: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the guides: the terms the tool uses, its keyboard keys, how the palette is made and what it is not, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your pictures. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in the Image Picker shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and pointer actions limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md How the palette is made, how precise it is, and what it is not related.md related.md Related tools, the API and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network "},{"t":"Image Picker shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts and pointer actions in the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard","Pointer"],"x":" Key Action E Re extract the palette with the current settings H Copy the palette's hex values J Copy the full analysis as JSON R Reset: clear the picture, palette and pins Enter in the address field Load the image at that address Escape Close a full screen chart The letter keys work anywhere on the page when focus is not in a text field, slider, switch or menu. Because a single R resets the workbench, click into a field before typing if you do not want to reset. Action Result Hover the preview Read the pixel under the pointer Click the preview Pin that pixel's colour Click a palette swatch Copy its hex value Click a pin Copy its hex value Double click a chart Open it full screen Click outside a full screen chart Close it "},{"t":"Image Picker glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning CIELAB A colour space with lightness L and two colour axes, a and b , designed so distances track perceived difference Cluster A group of similar sampled pixels, represented in the palette by their average colour Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of brightness difference between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1 CORS Cross origin resource sharing: a server's permission for other sites to read its images' pixels D65 A standard daylight white at about 6500 K, used here as the white for CIELAB Eyedropper The live readout of the pixel under the pointer on the preview Harmony A pair of colours whose hues sit at a classic colour wheel angle Hex A colour written as RRGGBB , two hexadecimal digits each for red, green and blue HSL Hue 0° to 360° , saturation and lightness 0% to 100% : a cylindrical form of RGB k means++ A clustering method that picks well spread starting colours, then moves each cluster to the average of its nearest pixels LCH CIELAB written as lightness, chroma colourfulness and hue angle Merge threshold The RGB distance below which two clusters are combined Palette The extracted colours, sorted by their share of the picture Pin An exact pixel colour kept by clic"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"How the Image Picker makes a palette, how precise its figures are, and what it is not.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["How the palette is made","Precision","Limits","What it is not"],"x":" Step Detail Working copy The picture is shrunk to fit 800 × 500 pixels; it is never enlarged Sampling A regular grid set by Quality , widened so that no more than about 50,000 pixels are sampled Skipped pixels Nearly transparent pixels; with the switches on, relative luminance below 0.03 or above 0.97 Exact colours Used when the samples hold no more distinct colours than the cluster count Clustering k means++ in RGB, up to 20 refinement rounds, stopping early once fewer than 1 in 2,000 samples change cluster Merging Clusters closer than the merge threshold in RGB are combined, weighted by size Shares Each cluster's sample count divided by all samples Swatch colours are averages of their clusters, rounded to whole RGB values. The same picture can give slightly different averages on different runs, because k means++ starts from random colours. Shares are shares of the sampled pixels, not of every pixel in the original picture. With widely spaced sampling, very small areas may not be sampled at all. The eyedropper and pins read the working copy. On a large photograph each working pixel stands for a block of original pixels, so a pin is exact to the working copy, not to a single origi"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Image Picker does with your pictures, and when it uses the network.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/privacy.html","h":["Pictures from your device stay in your browser","Pictures from a web address","Nothing is kept after you leave","What an export contains","The page itself"],"x":" A picture you drop or choose is read by the page itself and drawn to a canvas in your browser. The tool does not upload it or send it anywhere. The extraction, the readouts, the charts and the batch analysis are all worked out on your device. Downloads are created in the browser and saved by your browser's normal download. The clipboard is written only when you select a copy button or press H or J , or when you click a swatch or pin. When you use Load URL , your browser requests the image from the address you typed, exactly as it would when you open that address. The site that hosts the image sees that request. The Image Picker does not send the image anywhere afterwards. The picture, the palette and the pins are not stored. Reset , reloading or leaving the page clears them. The only thing remembered is whether you closed the Automate this line, which is kept in your browser. The JSON export contains the picture's file name or the last part of its address , its sizes, your settings, the palette and your pins. It does not contain the picture itself. The Image Picker is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wide features such as sign in, preferences and any consent based services "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version","25 May 2026 — user guide published"],"x":" No dated changelog entry for the Image Picker has been published on the site. This page records what can be confirmed. Three tabs: Workbench , Analysis and Actions . The whole middle panel is the drop target before a picture is loaded. The four charts live on their own Analysis tab, with full screen viewing. The keyboard keys are listed on the Workbench before a picture is loaded. A line under the heading points to the equivalent REST endpoint and its cost in API credits. The Image Picker User Guide was published in the site's documentation library. It describes a layout with two tabs, Lab and Actions , with the charts on the Lab tab. The extraction method, eyedropper, pins, exports and batch analysis it describes are the same as today. "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools, the public API and Learn articles that go with the Image Picker.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › Image Picker","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/image-picker/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","The public API","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with the Image Picker Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Test the exact text and background pair you chose from the palette Vision Simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md See how the picture and palette look with different kinds of colour vision M Gradient Palette ../../m gradient palette/README.md Build an evenly stepped ramp between two colours taken from the picture SVG Recolour ../../svg recolour/README.md Apply colours from the palette to SVG artwork Collage Maker ../../collage maker/README.md Combine several pictures into one before extracting a palette from all of them Basic Tools ../../../colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Quick palette, gradient and conversion utilities The same job is available as a REST call, POST /v1/palette/from image , documented at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/ ep post palette from image. See Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md for keys, credits and limits. Color Theory and Harmony — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony Accessible Color Design and WCA"},{"t":"LUT Lab","d":"What LUT Lab does, who it is for, where to find it and how to try a first look and write a .cube file.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" LUT Lab reads, applies and writes colour lookup tables. A lookup table, or LUT, is a file that says what colour each input colour should become; colourists use LUTs to carry a grade or a conversion from one program to another. LUT Lab works with the .cube format, in its one dimensional 1D and three dimensional 3D forms. The Lab tab shows a scene before and after a transform, side by side. The transform is either one of six built in looks, such as Teal and orange or a Reinhard tone map , or a .cube file you load. Under the pair, the tool measures what the transform moved: the average and largest colour difference in CIEDE2000, the share of pixels it clipped to pure white or black, and, on a ring of test colours, how far it turned hue and changed lightness and chroma. You can test on four drawn scenes or on your own picture. The Export tab writes the transform in force as a .cube , at any size from 2 to 65, as a 3D cube or a 1D curve. The file's header states plainly that the tool works in 8 bits and that the sample order is red fastest, as the format requires. Everything runs in your browser; nothing is uploaded. Colourists and editors checking what a .cube does before using it in "},{"t":"LUT Lab documentation","d":"The list of guides, the concept page, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for LUT Lab, a concept page on how lookup tables work, the full reference of controls and formats, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. If LUTs are new to you, read LUT concepts first. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the six tabs, and a first look lut concepts.md lut concepts.md 1D and 3D LUTs, grid size, domain, sample order, interpolation, clipping and 8 bit precision apply a look.md apply a look.md Choosing a scene or your own picture, the six looks, strength, exposure and the Looks tab load a cube file.md load a cube file.md Loading a .cube, the file card, warnings and errors, and switching back to the looks read what it moved.md read what it moved.md The clip overlay, the difference cards and the hue circle write a cube file.md write a cube file.md Exporting a .cube, resampling, the header, round trip accuracy, CSV, JSON and the share link reference.md reference.md Every control, readout, keyword, file format and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when a file will not load or a result looks wrong faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with LUT Lab","d":"Open LUT Lab, find your way around its six tabs, and try a first look.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The screen at a glance","Try a first look","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/lut lab/. The page opens on the Lab tab, showing the Neutral wedge scene before and after the Teal and orange look. A note under the heading explains what the numbers on the page are measurements of. It has no close button on purpose. Tab What it is for Lab The scene, the transform, the before and after pair, and what the transform moved Method Five short explanations: sample order, interpolation, clipping, round trip and linear light Looks A card for each built in look, with what it is and what it does to a test strip Data Every figure and what it rests on; the tab shows the number of entries 17 Export Kind and size of the table, the file preview, and the save and copy buttons Reference The published sources, marked by whether they run in the tool The left hand panel holds The scene four scene buttons and a Drop an image box , The look a menu, Strength and Tone map exposure , A .cube file a Drop a .cube box and Clear the file , and Show the What the transform crushed switch and Copy a link to this setting . The right hand panel holds Before and after , a key to the clip overlay, the cards under What it moved , and the hue circle u"},{"t":"Apply a look","d":"Choose a test scene or your own picture, apply one of the six built-in looks, and set its strength and exposure.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/apply-a-look.html","h":["Choose what to test on","Choose a look","Set the strength","Set the tone-map exposure","Compare looks on the Looks tab","Show what the transform crushed","What you should see"],"x":" Under The scene on the Lab tab, select one of four drawn scenes. Each is 320 × 180 pixels. Scene What it contains Good for spotting Neutral wedge A 16 step grey ramp above 16 step red, green and blue ramps Banding, contrast changes and colour casts in greys Colour patches 24 flat patches: six hues at four lightness levels Hue and saturation shifts across the colour wheel Skin tones Six skin like tones from dark to light on a mid grey surround What a look does to faces Saturation field Hue across, from grey at the bottom to strong colour at the top Hue twists and clipping in saturated colours The scenes are drawings, not photographs. They show the shape of a transform evenly, but they have no grain, lens flare or real camera colour. 1. Drop an image on Drop an image , or select the box to choose one. 2. The picture is scaled to fit 480 × 270, keeping its proportions it is never enlarged , and becomes the scene. A message confirms the size, for example Loaded beach.jpg at 480×270 . 3. A fifth button with your file name appears among the scenes, selected. 4. To go back, select Back to the drawn scenes , or any of the four scene buttons. Every figure on the page is then computed from "},{"t":"Load a .cube file","d":"Load a 1D or 3D .cube file, read what the tool reports about it, and switch between the file and the built-in looks.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/load-a-cube-file.html","h":["Load the file","The file card","What the reader accepts","Notes the tool may add","Files that cannot be read","How the file is applied","Switch between the file and the looks","Resample or convert the file"],"x":" 1. On the Lab tab, drop a .cube file on Drop a .cube , or select the box to choose one. The chooser offers .cube and plain text files. 2. A message confirms Loaded followed by the file name, and says how many notes there are if the tool found any. 3. The before and after pair now shows your file applied to the current scene. The label above the pair shows the file's title, or its name if it has none. While a file is shown, the look menu and Strength are greyed out and the note under them reads The pair is showing the loaded file. The looks are paused. A loaded file is always applied at full strength. A card under the drop box describes the file. Line Meaning Example Heading The TITLE in the file, or the file name Warm Film kind 1D or 3D 3D size For 3D, N³ and the number of rows; for 1D, the number of rows 33³ 35937 rows domain The declared input range for red, green and blue 0.000, 0.000, 0.000 – 1.000, 1.000, 1.000 reachable The share of the table that an 8 bit sRGB input can reach 100.0% Under these lines is a list of notes. When there is nothing to report it reads no discrepancies between the header and the body . LUT Lab reads the .cube format as defined in the Adobe / IRIDAS "},{"t":"LUT concepts","d":"What a lookup table is, 1D and 3D LUTs, grid sizes, domains, sample order, interpolation, clipping and 8-bit precision.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/lut-concepts.html","h":["What a LUT is","1D and 3D LUTs","The domain","Sample order","Interpolation","Clipping","8-bit precision","Stylisations and transforms","Measuring colour difference"],"x":" This page explains the ideas behind LUT Lab's controls and figures. A lookup table LUT is a list that says, for a set of input colours, what each should become. Software applies it to every pixel of an image or video. Because it is just a table of numbers, a LUT carries a look or a conversion from one program to another without carrying the program's settings. A LUT does not know what the colours mean. It works on whatever numbers it is given, so a LUT made for one kind of footage gives the wrong result on another. LUT Lab applies LUTs to ordinary 8 bit sRGB values, the kind of colour a web page or a JPEG holds. 1D LUT 3D LUT What it maps Each channel on its own: red in to red out, green to green, blue to blue Every combination of red, green and blue to a new colour Can express Brightness, contrast, gamma, per channel curves, colour casts that depend only on each channel Anything a 1D can, plus hue shifts, saturation changes and effects that mix channels Size N rows, each holding a red, green and blue output N × N × N rows Keyword in .cube LUT 1D SIZE LUT 3D SIZE A 3D LUT of size N is a cube of N points along each axis. The number of rows grows quickly: Size Rows in a 3D LUT 17 4,"},{"t":"Read what a transform moved","d":"Interpret the clip overlay, the colour difference cards and the hue circle on the Lab tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/read-what-it-moved.html","h":["The pair","What it moved","Where it moved things to","Reading the numbers together","The Method tab"],"x":" Everything below the before and after pair on the Lab tab describes the difference between the two images, for the transform currently shown: a look at its strength, or a loaded file. Before is the scene, with its pixel count beside the label, for example 57600 for a 320 × 180 scene. After is the scene through the transform, with the clipped share beside the label, for example 0.83% clipped . With What the transform crushed switched on, the After image is hatched with diagonal stripes where the transform clipped a pixel: Stripes Meaning Pink A channel was driven to white 255 that was not at 255 before Blue A channel was driven to black 0 that was not at 0 before Pixels that were already at 0 or 255 and stayed there are not marked. Switch the overlay off to see the clean result; the figures do not change. Card Meaning mean ΔE₀₀ The average CIEDE2000 colour difference between each pixel before and after 95th percentile The difference that 95% of pixels are at or below; shows how big the typical large change is largest The single largest difference on any pixel clipped The share of pixels with at least one channel driven to 0 or 255 by the transform; the card turns red above 1% the o"},{"t":"Write a .cube file","d":"Export the transform in force as a 3D or 1D .cube at any size, understand the header and round-trip accuracy, and save the hue sweep, report and share link.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/write-a-cube-file.html","h":["Save a .cube","3D cube or 1D curve","Choosing a size","The file preview","Round trips: what survives","Other exports","Share your settings"],"x":" The Export tab writes the transform currently shown on the Lab tab: a look at its strength and exposure, or a loaded .cube file. 1. On the Lab tab, set up the transform you want: choose a look and its Strength , or load a .cube . 2. Open the Export tab. 3. Choose Kind : 3D cube default or 1D curve . 4. Set Size from 2 to 65 default 33 . The label shows, for example, 33³ for a 3D cube. 5. Check the lines under the slider: rows , file size and file name , and the note on whether the grid lands on 8 bit values. 6. Select Save the .cube . Your browser downloads the file, for example auric teal and orange 33.cube , and a message confirms it. To paste the table somewhere instead, select Copy it . The message reads Copied the .cube , or The clipboard refused if clipboard access is blocked. The file name is auric , the transform's name in lower case with spaces and symbols turned into hyphens, the size, and 1d for a 1D curve. Kind What it captures Rows 3D cube The full transform: every mix of red, green and blue Size³ 1D curve Only what the transform does to neutral greys, written as a curve per channel Size A 1D curve is made by sending greys through the transform and recording each outp"},{"t":"LUT Lab reference","d":"Every tab, control, readout, .cube keyword, export format, link parameter and message in LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Lab tab — The scene","Lab tab — The look","Lab tab — A .cube file","Lab tab — Show","Lab tab — Readouts","Looks tab","Method tab","Data tab","Export tab",".cube keywords","Share link parameters","Reference tab","Messages"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/lut lab/ Tab Contents Lab Scene, look, .cube file, overlay switch, share link; the before and after pair and what the transform moved Method Five explanations: Sample order , Interpolation , Clipping , Round trip , Linear light Looks A card per look with a test strip and figures; the two withdrawn features Data The 17 entries every figure rests on, filterable by status Export Kind, size, file details, save and copy buttons, the file preview Reference The ten sources, filterable by whether they run Control What it does Default Neutral wedge 16 step grey ramp over red, green and blue ramps, 320 × 180 Selected Colour patches 24 flat patches, six hues at four lightness levels — Skin tones Six skin like tones on a mid grey surround — Saturation field Hue across, chroma from none at the bottom to strong at the top — Drop an image Loads your picture, scaled to fit 480 × 270, as the scene — Back to the drawn scenes Removes your picture and returns to the drawn scenes Shown with your picture Control Values Default Look menu None, Teal and orange, Bleach bypass, Film soft, Mono contrast, Log ish lift, Reinhard tone map Teal and orange Str"},{"t":"Troubleshooting LUT Lab","d":"Symptoms you may meet in LUT Lab, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Loading a .cube","Looks and controls","Your picture","Exports","Share links"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do LUT 3D SIZE N needs M rows; the file has K The file is shorter than its header says, often from a failed download Download the file again no LUT 1D SIZE or LUT 3D SIZE keyword and no usable sample rows The file is not a .cube , or is empty of data Check the file; convert other LUT formats to .cube first empty file The file has no content Choose the right file My .3dl or other LUT file is greyed out or will not load Only .cube is supported Convert it to .cube in another program A note says rows beyond the declared number were ignored The file has extra data rows Check the file at its source; the declared table is used A note says the file was read as a 1D or 3D table because no size keyword was found The size keyword is missing The guess is stated; fix the file at its source if it is wrong reachable is below 100% The file's domain is wider than 0 to 1, for example for HDR or log footage Only part of the table affects 8 bit sRGB pictures; the file was made for different input The result looks badly wrong, with red and blue swapped The file was written by a program that orders rows blue fastest Re export it from its source with the standard order; LUT Lab reads"},{"t":"LUT Lab FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/docs/faq.html","h":["Are my files uploaded?","Which LUT formats can I use?","Will a .cube from LUT Lab work in my editing program?","What size should I choose?","Why does the file say it is 8-bit when it has six decimals?","Can I make a LUT with more precision than 8 bits?","Why is there no ACEScct or log conversion?","Is \"Bleach bypass\" a real film process simulation?","What does \"clipped\" count?","Can I adjust the strength of a loaded .cube?","Can I use LUT Lab to convert a 3D LUT to a different size?","Does the tool show the LUT as a 3D cube?"],"x":" No. Your .cube and your picture are read in the page and never sent anywhere. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Only .cube , 1D or 3D, as defined in the Adobe / IRIDAS Cube LUT Specification 1.0. Convert other formats first. It is written to the .cube specification: TITLE , LUT 3D SIZE or LUT 1D SIZE , DOMAIN MIN and DOMAIN MAX , and rows with red changing fastest. Programs that read standard .cube files should read it. The looks are designed for ordinary sRGB images, not log camera footage. 33 is a common default. 17 is smaller and coarser, 65 larger and more faithful to curved looks. Sizes 2, 4, 6, 16, 18 and 52 put every grid point exactly on an 8 bit value. The tool reads and writes pixels at 8 bits, so every value it can produce is one of 256 levels. Six decimals is simply how the format writes numbers. The header says this because the format has no other way to record precision. Not in LUT Lab. A 32 bit float export was withdrawn because the tool has no floating point path to fill it. Such conversions need values far above the 0 to 1 range an 8 bit canvas holds. The ACEScct look was withdrawn for that reason; the Looks tab shows why. No. It is a stylisation named after the "},{"t":"LUT Lab background material","d":"The contents of LUT Lab's others folder: glossary, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the guides: the terms the tool uses, the limits of its 8 bit path and what it does not hold, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your files. LUT Lab has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond standard keyboard access, so there is no shortcuts page. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in LUT Lab limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md The 8 bit path, how figures are measured, and what the tool does not hold related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"LUT Lab glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning 1D LUT A table mapping each channel on its own, one row per input level 3D LUT A cube of grid points mapping every combination of red, green and blue to a new colour 8 bit 256 levels per channel, 0 to 255; the precision LUT Lab works in ACEScct / ACEScg Encodings from the Academy Color Encoding System for film work; not offered, because they need values above 1 .cube A plain text LUT format defined by the Adobe / IRIDAS Cube LUT Specification 1.0 CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ The CIE's standard formula for the size of a colour difference CIELAB A colour space of lightness L and colour axes a and b , used here with a D65 white Chroma C How colourful a colour is in CIELAB, its distance from grey Clipped A pixel with a channel driven by the transform to 0 or 255 that was not there before Domain The input range a .cube table covers, set by DOMAIN MIN and DOMAIN MAX ; 0 to 1 by default Exposure In the tone map, the factor the linear scene light is multiplied by before compression Grid point One of the sampled inputs of a LUT, at which the output is stored Hue sweep The ring of 72 test colours at L 60, C 40 used to measure hue, lightness and chroma shifts Identity A LUT that changes nothi"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"LUT Lab's 8-bit path, how its figures are measured, and what it does not hold.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The 8-bit path","What is measured, and how","Choices the tool makes","What the tool does not hold","Limits","What it is not"],"x":" Every value in LUT Lab travels as an 8 bit integer, because it comes from and returns to a canvas. This is a real limit: A loaded LUT's output is rounded to 8 bits when applied. An exported .cube holds only the 256 values k ÷ 255 per channel, written to six decimals. The header says so. A 1D export longer than 256 entries would only repeat values; the tool writes at most 65. At sizes where N − 1 does not divide 255 including 17, 33 and 65 , grid points in an exported file sit up to half an 8 bit step from the exact grid. An 8 bit image is unaffected; a program reading at higher precision is not. Figure Method mean ΔE₀₀ , 95th percentile , largest CIEDE2000 between each pixel before and after, in CIELAB with a D65 white clipped Pixels with a channel moved to 0 or 255 from somewhere else the old test said Pixels with any output channel at 0 or 255; kept for comparison only Hue circle 72 colours at L 60, C 40 in CIELAB, every 5°; 13 are pulled inside sRGB first Hue shift Change of CIELAB hue angle, not HSL hue Round trip Values written and read back agree to the six decimals of the format The CIEDE2000 formula is checked against a second transcription of the standard and against publ"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What LUT Lab does with your .cube files and pictures.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/privacy.html","h":["Your files stay in your browser","Nothing is kept after you leave","What leaves in an export or link","The page itself"],"x":" A .cube file you load is read as text by the page itself, in your browser. It is not uploaded. A picture you load is read in the page and scaled to fit 480 × 270 for the analysis. It is not uploaded. The looks, the measurements and the exports are all worked out on your device. Exported files are created in the browser and saved by your browser's normal download. The clipboard is written only when you select Copy it or Copy a link to this setting . LUT Lab does not store your .cube , your picture or your settings. Reloading or leaving the page clears them. An exported .cube contains the transform's name; for a loaded file, that is the file's title or name. The JSON report contains your picture's file name, if you used one, and the figures. A share link contains only the scene, look, strength, exposure, size and kind. It does not contain your file or picture. LUT Lab is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wide features such as sign in, preferences and any consent based services follow the site's own privacy policy and your cookie choices; see Help ../../../../../help/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/release-notes.html","h":["3 June 2026 — the measured workbench","25 May 2026 — earlier version"],"x":" The earlier engine was replaced by the current workbench, with six tabs: Lab , Method , Looks , Data , Export and Reference . The site's earlier user guide carries a notice that it describes the engine replaced on this date. What changed for you: Exported .cube files use the standard sample order. Files written by the earlier version had their red and blue axes swapped, so they looked right when read back by the same tool and wrong everywhere else. Re export any .cube you made with the earlier version. The overlay shows what the transform crushed. The earlier out of gamut overlay flagged pure colours, black and white even when nothing had changed them. The new overlay marks only pixels the transform drove to white or black, in two colours. \"Cine Log to Rec.709\" is now \"Log ish lift\". The arithmetic is unchanged; the old name claimed a log encoding and a conversion that were never applied. The Reinhard tone map runs in linear light, with an exposure control. Mid grey now comes out where the operator puts it. Two features were withdrawn: the ACEScct to ACEScg look, which turned 114 of 256 input codes pure white, and a 32 bit float export that could not produce anything but 8 bit val"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools and Learn articles that go with LUT Lab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › LUT Lab","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/lut-lab/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with LUT Lab Tone Mapping ../../../colorimetry and rendering/tone mapping/README.md Experiment with tone mapping operators for HDR to standard range ICC Profile Parser ../../icc profile parser/README.md Read ICC profiles, the other common kind of colour transform file Image Picker ../../image picker/README.md Take a palette from a picture before and after a look Collage Maker ../../collage maker/README.md Combine test pictures into one scene to load into LUT Lab Vision Simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Check a graded picture for different kinds of colour vision Color Grading and LUTs — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 19 color grading and luts Gamma, Linear Light, and Transfer Functions — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 gamma linear light transfer functions ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 26 delta e metrics cie76 ciede2000 itp HDR, Wide Gamut, PQ, HLG, and Modern Displays — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 hdr wide gamut pq hlg modern displays Color in Real Time 3D: Albedo"},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette","d":"What the M-Gradient Palette does, who it is for, where to find it and how to build a first ramp.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The M Gradient Palette the page is titled Gradient Ramp builds a colour ramp: a row of evenly spaced steps between two colours, of the kind used for data visualisation scales, tint and shade series, and design tokens. You choose the two ends, the number of steps, and the space the colours are blended in: OKLCH, sRGB, linear RGB or HSL, with a short or long way round the hue circle for the two polar spaces. The tool then measures the ramp. It gives the CIEDE2000 colour difference between every pair of neighbouring steps, their average, and how even they are, and counts the steps whose colourfulness had to be reduced to fit sRGB. A second tab builds all thirty combinations of route and easing between your two colours and marks the evenest. A third checks every step as a background for a text colour you choose, with both the WCAG 2.2 ratio and the APCA lightness contrast, and the whole ramp can be viewed as people with protanopia, deuteranopia or tritanopia see it. You can copy the ramp as a CSS gradient, as CSS custom properties, as a list of hex values or as SVG, and save a JSON reading of what was measured. Everything runs in your browser. Designers building tint and shade scales,"},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette documentation","d":"The list of guides, the concept page, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the M Gradient Palette, a concept page on colour spaces, interpolation and gamut mapping, the full reference, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Read Interpolation and gamut if you want to know why the same two colours give different ramps. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the six tabs, and a first ramp interpolation and gamut.md interpolation and gamut.md The four spaces, short and long hue routes, easing, CIEDE2000, evenness and gamut mapping build a ramp.md build a ramp.md Setting the ends, presets, routes, steps and easing, and reading the Ramp tab compare routes.md compare routes.md The Spaces tab: 30 combinations measured, and the desaturated middle check contrast and colour vision.md check contrast and colour vision.md WCAG 2.2 and APCA against a text colour, and the colour vision views export a ramp.md export a ramp.md CSS gradient, custom properties, hex list, SVG and the JSON reading reference.md reference.md Every control, preset, readout, format and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when a ramp or an export does not look right faq.md faq.md Short answer"},{"t":"Getting started with the M-Gradient Palette","d":"Open the M-Gradient Palette, find your way around its six tabs, and build a first ramp.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The screen at a glance","Build a first ramp","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/m gradient palette/. The page, titled Gradient Ramp , opens on the Ramp tab with a 12 step ramp from a deep blue, 0B3D5C , to a gold, F2B134 . A note under the heading explains what the numbers on the page are measurements of. It has no close button on purpose. Tab What it is for Ramp The controls, the ramp, the step by step differences, the figures and the hue circle Spaces All six routes by five easings, built and measured, and three ramps drawn side by side Contrast A text colour, and every step checked as a background with WCAG 2.2 and APCA Data Every figure and what it rests on; the tab shows the number of entries 15 Export Copy and save buttons, previews and the JSON reading Reference The published sources and the arithmetic The left hand panel holds The two ends a swatch and a hex box for each, Swap the ends , and A starting point , Interpolate in six route buttons , Shape Steps and the Easing buttons , and Show it as seen by four vision buttons . The right hand panel holds The ramp one button per step , the bars of ΔE₀₀ between adjacent steps , the cards under What the ramp measures , and the circle under Where the ramp goe"},{"t":"Build a ramp","d":"Set the two ends, use a preset, choose a route, steps and easing, and read everything on the Ramp tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/build-a-ramp.html","h":["Set the two ends","Start from a preset","Choose a route","Set the shape","Read the ramp","Read the differences between steps","Read the figures","Read the hue circle","View it with a colour-vision deficiency","What you should see"],"x":" Everything in this guide happens on the Ramp tab. The ramp and its figures update as soon as you change a control. Under The two ends , the first row is the start colour and the second the end colour. 1. Select a swatch to open the colour picker and choose a colour, or 2. type a hex value in the box beside it and press Enter or move focus away. Three or six digit hex is accepted, with or without , for example F2B134 or abc . If the box holds something that is not a colour, it returns to the previous value and a message reads That is not a colour. Swap the ends exchanges the start and end colours. A starting point offers 25 named pairs. Choosing one sets both ends; the steps, route and easing stay as they are. The pairs are a starting point only and make no claim to be good ramps. The full list is in the Reference reference.md . Under Interpolate in , select one of six routes: Route Space Hue direction OKLCH, short hue default OKLCH The shorter way round OKLCH, long hue OKLCH The longer way round sRGB sRGB — Linear RGB Linear RGB — HSL, short hue HSL The shorter way round HSL, long hue HSL The longer way round See Interpolation and gamut interpolation and gamut.md for how the space"},{"t":"Check contrast and colour vision","d":"Check every step of a ramp as a background for a text colour with WCAG 2.2 and APCA, and view the ramp as seen with three colour-vision deficiencies.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/check-contrast-and-colour-vision.html","h":["Check text on every step","What the evidence table shows","View the ramp with a colour-vision deficiency"],"x":" 1. Build your ramp on the Ramp tab. 2. Open the Contrast tab. 3. Under Text colour , select the swatch and choose the colour your text will be. The default is white, FFFFFF . 4. Read Your ramp, checked both ways . The note beside the heading names the text colour, for example against FFFFFF . Every step is treated as a background for text in the chosen colour, and measured by two methods at once. Column Meaning Step The step's swatch and hex value WCAG 2 The WCAG 2.2 contrast ratio, for example 7.90:1 Rating AAA , AA , AA large or fail APCA Lc The APCA lightness contrast, signed Good for What APCA considers the pair suitable for The old figure The Lc an earlier version of this tool printed, struck through; highlighted where it differs by more than 20 The WCAG 2.2 contrast ratio compares the relative luminance of the two colours, from 1:1 identical to 21:1 black on white . Rating Ratio Meaning AAA 7:1 or more Body text at the enhanced level AA 4.5:1 or more Body text at the minimum level AA large 3:1 or more Large text only fail Below 3:1 Not enough for text APCA, the Advanced Perceptual Contrast Algorithm version APCA W3 0.1.9 here , measures lightness contrast in units called Lc."},{"t":"Compare routes and easings","d":"Use the Spaces tab to build all thirty route and easing combinations for your two colours and find the evenest.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/compare-routes.html","h":["Read the table","What to look for","The desaturated middle, drawn","Use the result"],"x":" The Spaces tab answers: which route and easing give the evenest ramp between these two colours? Every row is built at your two ends and your step count and then measured; nothing is predicted from a model of the space. 1. Set the ends and Steps on the Ramp tab. 2. Open the Spaces tab. The note beside the heading repeats your ends and step count, for example 0B3D5C → F2B134 · 12 steps . The table has thirty rows: six routes by five easings. Column Meaning Route One of the six routes Easing One of the five easings Mean ΔE₀₀ Average difference between neighbouring steps Min Smallest difference between neighbouring steps Max Largest difference between neighbouring steps Evenness Standard deviation of the differences; lower is more even What happens the evenest of the thirty , or how many steps were moved to fit sRGB The evenest row is highlighted and marked the evenest of the thirty . It is marked only when one row is strictly evenest; if two or more tie, none is marked, and the note under the table says so. For the default ends at 12 steps, the evenest row is OKLCH, short hue with linear easing, at an evenness of 0.69. The note under the table points out two patterns you will usually"},{"t":"Export a ramp","d":"Copy the ramp as a CSS gradient, custom properties, a hex list or SVG, save an SVG, and save the JSON reading.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/export-a-ramp.html","h":["The CSS gradient","The custom properties","The hex list","The SVG","The reading","Which to use"],"x":" All exports are on the Export tab, under Take it away . They always use the true colours, whatever Show it as seen by is set to. Button What you get Copy the CSS gradient A CSS linear gradient from the two ends, in the space of your route Copy the custom properties One CSS custom property per measured step Copy the hex list The steps' hex values, one per line Copy the SVG An SVG gradient built from the measured steps Save the SVG The same SVG, downloaded as ramp.svg Save the reading A JSON record of the ramp and its measurements, downloaded as ramp reading.json A message confirms each copy, for example Custom properties copied or 12 colours copied . If the browser blocks the clipboard, it reads The browser refused the clipboard. The table under What leaves this page gives the size of each form for your ramp and what each is good for. The CSS gradient asks the browser to do the blending, from your two ends: Route Copied text OKLCH, short hue background: linear gradient in oklch shorter hue, 0B3D5C 0%, F2B134 100% ; OKLCH, long hue background: linear gradient in oklch longer hue, 0B3D5C 0%, F2B134 100% ; HSL, short or long hue As above, with in hsl Linear RGB background: linear grad"},{"t":"Interpolation and gamut","d":"How the four colour spaces blend two colours differently, what short and long hue routes and easing do, how evenness is measured, and how out-of-gamut steps are brought back.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/interpolation-and-gamut.html","h":["The four spaces","Short and long hue routes","Easing","Measuring a ramp","Gamut and gamut mapping","The desaturated middle"],"x":" A ramp is made by interpolation : choosing colours part of the way between the two ends. What \"part of the way\" means depends on the colour space the blending happens in, so the same two colours give different ramps in different spaces. Space What is blended Character of the ramp sRGB The red, green and blue values as stored in a web colour The browser's default. Middles between very different colours can turn dull or dark Linear RGB Red, green and blue as amounts of light, before the sRGB curve is applied Physically like mixing light. Middles tend to look too light, and the dark end changes quickly HSL Hue, saturation and lightness, a cylinder built from sRGB Keeps colours saturated, but HSL lightness is not perceived lightness, so brightness can bulge in the middle OKLCH Lightness, chroma and hue in OKLab Designed so equal steps look equal. Keeps colourfulness through the middle. The default OKLab is a perceptual colour space published by Björn Ottosson in 2020. It has a lightness axis, L, and two colour axes, a and b, arranged so that equal distances look roughly equally different. OKLCH is the same space in polar form: L for lightness, C for chroma how colourful, the distance "},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette reference","d":"Every tab, control, preset, readout, export format and message in the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Ramp tab — controls","Presets","Easing curves","Ramp tab — readouts","Spaces tab","Contrast tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/m gradient palette/ Tab Contents Ramp Ends, presets, routes, steps, easing, colour vision view; the ramp, the step differences, figures and hue circle Spaces Thirty route and easing combinations measured; three ramps drawn with their least chromatic step Contrast Text colour; evidence table; every step checked by WCAG 2.2 and APCA; samples Data The 15 entries every figure rests on, filterable by status; the corrections list Export Six copy and save buttons, previews, the size table and the reading Reference Eight sources and the arithmetic table Control What it does Values Default Start swatch and hex box The first colour Any colour; hex as 3 or 6 digits, optional 0B3D5C End swatch and hex box The last colour As above F2B134 Swap the ends Exchanges start and end — — A starting point Sets both ends to a preset pair 25 presets, listed below Choose a pair… Interpolate in The route OKLCH, short hue; OKLCH, long hue; sRGB; Linear RGB; HSL, short hue; HSL, long hue OKLCH, short hue Steps Number of colours, ends included 2 to 32 12 Easing Where the steps land linear, ease in, ease out, ease in out, step linear Show it as seen by Colour"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the M-Gradient Palette","d":"Symptoms you may meet in the M-Gradient Palette, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Building the ramp","The Spaces tab","Contrast","Exports"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do That is not a colour. and the hex box reverts The value is not three or six hex digits Type a value such as F2B134 or abc ; eight digit hex with alpha is not accepted Some steps have a gold underline Their chroma was reduced to fit sRGB Expected with saturated ends in OKLCH. Choose less saturated ends, or accept the boundary colours Neighbouring steps are identical The step easing has only five positions Choose another easing, or five steps The middle of the ramp is grey or muddy sRGB and linear RGB pass near grey between very different hues Use OKLCH, short hue ; see the Spaces tab The ramp passes through unexpected hues A long hue route, or HSL, goes round the colour wheel Use a short hue route One bar is much taller than the rest A visible jump at that step Try another route or easing; check largest jump A preset gave a poor ramp Presets make no claim to be good ramps Adjust the ends, route or easing Symptom Why What to do No row is marked the evenest Two or more rows tie Choose any of the tied rows Choosing a row does nothing The table is a comparison, not a control Select that route and easing on the Ramp tab Symptom Why What to do APCA Lc is negative T"},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/docs/faq.html","h":["Which route should I use?","Why are there four spaces but six routes?","What does \"evenness\" mean?","Why did some steps get a gold underline?","Can I have more than two colours in a ramp?","Can I have more than 32 steps?","Is the CSS gradient the same as the steps?","Why does the tool show two contrast figures?","Why is the APCA figure negative?","Does the colour-vision view change the exports?","Does it simulate mild colour blindness?","Is anything saved between visits?"],"x":" For even looking steps, start with OKLCH, short hue , and confirm on the Spaces tab, which measures all six routes and five easings for your two colours. OKLCH and HSL have a hue angle, and each can go the short or the long way round the colour wheel. That is two routes in the same space, not two spaces. The standard deviation of the colour differences between neighbouring steps. Lower means the steps look more equally spaced. It is a ranking, not a pass mark: the tool marks the evenest of the thirty combinations but sets no threshold for \"even enough\". Blending in OKLCH asked for a colour more colourful than sRGB can show. The tool reduced its chroma, keeping its lightness and hue, until it fitted. No. A ramp runs between two ends. For a multi stop scale, build one ramp per section, or join exported steps yourself. No. The Steps slider runs from 2 to 32. No. The CSS gradient asks the browser to blend smoothly between the two ends in the chosen space. The custom properties and the hex list are the exact steps the tool measured. WCAG 2.2 and APCA measure contrast differently and often disagree. Both are shown so you can see the disagreement. APCA is signed. Negative means light tex"},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette background material","d":"The contents of the M-Gradient Palette's others folder: glossary, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the guides: the terms the tool uses, what it measures and does not hold, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your data. The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond standard keyboard access, so there is no shortcuts page. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in the M Gradient Palette limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What is measured, how precisely, choices the tool makes and what it does not hold related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser "},{"t":"M-Gradient Palette glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning APCA Advanced Perceptual Contrast Algorithm; a lightness contrast measure in Lc units, signed by polarity Chroma How colourful a colour is, its distance from grey; in OKLCH, the C value CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ The CIE's standard formula for how different two colours look CIELAB A colour space of lightness and two colour axes; used here only to compute ΔE₀₀ Clipping Forcing each channel into 0 to 255 separately, which also shifts hue; not used by this tool Colour vision deficiency Reduced ability to tell some colours apart; simulated here as full protanopia, deuteranopia or tritanopia Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of luminance difference, from 1:1 to 21:1 Custom property A CSS variable such as ramp 01 , holding one step's colour Deutan Deuteranopia: no working medium wavelength green cones Easing A curve that decides where along the route the steps land Evenness The standard deviation of the differences between neighbouring steps; lower is more even Gamut The range of colours a space or device can show Gamut mapping Bringing an out of range colour back inside, here by reducing chroma at fixed lightness and hue HSL Hue, saturation and lightness: a cylinder built from sRGB Hu"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the M-Gradient Palette measures, how precisely, the choices it makes, and what it does not hold.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is measured, and how precisely","Choices the tool makes","What the tool does not hold","Limits","What it is not"],"x":" Figure Method Accuracy ΔE₀₀ per step CIEDE2000 ISO/CIE 11664 6:2014 between neighbouring steps, via CIELAB with a D65 white Agrees with the 34 published test pairs of Sharma, Wu and Dalal 2005 to within 0.000042 Evenness Standard deviation of the step differences Exact from the above OKLab and OKLCH Ottosson's published matrices Checked against the article's own reference values sRGB conversions The piecewise sRGB transfer function, both directions Exact WCAG 2 ratio L₁ + 0.05 ÷ L₂ + 0.05 from relative luminance Exact: 21.00, 4.54 for 767676 , 7.00 for 595959 on white APCA Lc APCA W3 0.1.9 with all its constants Black on white 106.04 Colour vision view Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes 2009 , severity 1.0, in linear light Full dichromacy only Gamut mapping Chroma halved towards the boundary 20 times, lightness and hue held Far finer than one 8 bit step Every step is rounded to an 8 bit hex colour before it is measured, so the figures describe the colours you export. These are listed as This tool's choice on the Data tab. How out of gamut steps are brought back: by reducing chroma, not by clipping channels. A different method gives a visibly different ramp. The five easings are CSS a"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the M-Gradient Palette does with your colours and settings.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/privacy.html","h":["Everything runs in your browser","Nothing is kept after you leave","The page itself"],"x":" The ramp, the measurements, the route comparison, the contrast checks and the colour vision views are all worked out on your device. The tool sends nothing to a server. Save the SVG and Save the reading create their files in the browser and save them through your browser's normal download. The clipboard is written only when you select a copy button or a step of the ramp. Your colours and settings are not stored. Reloading or leaving the page returns to the default ramp. To keep a ramp, copy the custom properties or save the reading. The M Gradient Palette is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wide features such as sign in, preferences and any consent based services follow the site's own privacy policy and your cookie choices; see Help ../../../../../help/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/release-notes.html","h":["Current version — Gradient Ramp","25 May 2026 — earlier version"],"x":" The tool was rebuilt as the Gradient Ramp workbench, with six tabs: Ramp , Spaces , Contrast , Data , Export and Reference . The developer reference that describes this version in the site's documentation library is dated 6 June 2026. What changed for you: APCA figures are now correct. The earlier contrast readout used the wrong scale and left out two parts of the APCA algorithm, so it reported contrast about 1.4 times too high: 161.80 for black on white, where APCA gives 106.04. Across 2,704 grey on grey pairs, 520 cleared its Lc 60 line that real APCA fails. If you chose text colours with the earlier version, check them again. Both contrast figures side by side. Each step shows the WCAG 2.2 ratio and the APCA Lc together, and the old figure for comparison. The colour vision simulation is correctly attributed to Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes 2009 ; the simulation itself is unchanged. \"Six spaces\" is now four spaces and six routes. Short and long hue are routes in the same space. The hue plot is a circle. A ramp crossing 0° no longer draws a line across the whole plot. The route table marks the measured evenest row, and none when rows tie, instead of starring every row under a f"},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools and Learn articles that go with the M-Gradient Palette.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › M-Gradient Palette","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/m-gradient-palette/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with the M Gradient Palette Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Test a single text and background pair in more depth Vision Simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Simulate more kinds of colour vision on a finished design Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades ../../../colorimetry and rendering/tonal steps/README.md Generate tonal step charts from one colour Gamut Mapping ../../../colorimetry and rendering/gamut map/README.md Explore how out of gamut colours are brought back Design Engine ../../../colour workspace/design engine/README.md Generate a whole design system of OKLCH colour ramps Image Picker ../../image picker/README.md Take the two end colours from a picture SVG Recolour ../../svg recolour/README.md Apply ramp colours to SVG artwork Color Gradients and Interpolation — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 07 color gradients and interpolation Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces ΔE Metrics from CIE76 to CIEDE2000 and ΔEITP — https://auricartisan.com/librar"},{"t":"SVG Recolour","d":"What SVG Recolour does, who it is for, where to find it and how to recolour a first SVG.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" SVG Recolour listed as SVG Recolor in Collections changes the colours of an SVG file. It finds every colour in the file, wherever and however it is written, lists each distinct colour once with the number of places it is used, and lets you choose what each should become. The new file is written from your original in one pass, so two colours can trade places, a colour written as a name such as red is changed like any other, and the count beside each colour is the number of places actually rewritten. Before and after previews sit side by side on a chequerboard. You can recolour by hand, one colour at a time, or from a harmony built on the file's main colour: complementary, analogous, triadic, tetradic or split complementary. The Check tab measures every colour as a background for a text colour of your choice, with both WCAG 2.2 and APCA, and finds the two colours in the file that are hardest to tell apart, with normal vision and with each of three colour vision deficiencies. You can save the recoloured SVG, copy its markup, copy the new palette as CSS custom properties, and save a JSON report of every change. The file is parsed in the page and never uploaded, and scripts and other a"},{"t":"SVG Recolour documentation","d":"The list of guides, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for SVG Recolour, the full reference of its controls and formats, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started, then go to the guide for the job you have. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the tool, a tour of the six tabs, and a first recolour recolour an svg.md recolour an svg.md Loading an SVG, what the tool finds, mapping and swapping colours, write styles, the Mapping tab use a harmony.md use a harmony.md Recolouring the whole file from a harmony, and putting colours back check contrast and colour vision.md check contrast and colour vision.md Contrast against a text colour, the closest pair, and the colour vision previews export the result.md export the result.md Saving and copying the SVG, custom properties and the JSON report reference.md reference.md Every control, property, colour form, readout, format and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when a file will not parse or a colour does not change faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with SVG Recolour","d":"Open SVG Recolour, find your way around its six tabs, and recolour a first SVG.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the tool","The screen at a glance","Recolour a first SVG","Next steps"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/svg recolor/. The page, titled SVG Recolour , opens on the Recolour tab with a small sample SVG already loaded, so you can try every control straight away. A note under the heading explains what the numbers on the page are measurements of. It has no close button on purpose. Tab What it is for Recolour Load the file, choose how colours are written, preview before and after, and remap each colour Mapping Every colour, where it is used, what it becomes, and how many places were written Check Contrast of every colour against a text colour, and the colours hardest to tell apart Data Every figure and what it rests on; the tab shows the number of entries 15 Export Save and copy buttons, the custom properties and the report Reference The published sources, and how the tool works step by step The left hand panel holds The file the Drop an SVG box, Load the sample , a box to paste markup, and Read the markup , Write colours as , Show it as seen by , and Recolour from a harmony with Put every colour back . The right hand panel holds Before, and after two previews on a chequerboard , Every colour in the file one row per colour , and the cards "},{"t":"Check contrast and colour vision","d":"Measure every colour in the SVG as a background for text with WCAG 2.2 and APCA, find the colours hardest to tell apart, and preview the artwork as seen with colour-vision deficiencies.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/check-contrast-and-colour-vision.html","h":["Contrast against a text colour","The colours hardest to tell apart","The artwork under three dichromacies","Preview with a colour-vision deficiency on the Recolour tab","Using the results"],"x":" The Check tab measures the colours the file will have after your changes: the targets, not the originals. 1. Open the Check tab. 2. Under Text laid over the artwork , select the swatch and choose the colour of any text that will sit on the artwork. The default is white, FFFFFF . 3. Read What can be read on it . The note beside the heading gives the number of colours checked. Each colour is treated as a background for text in the chosen colour: Column Meaning Colour The colour's swatch and hex value WCAG The WCAG 2.2 contrast ratio, for example 4.54:1 Rating AAA 7:1 and above , AA 4.5:1 , AA large 3:1 or fail APCA Lc The APCA W3 0.1.9 lightness contrast; negative when the text is lighter than the colour Good for APCA's guidance by size of Lc, from any text to not for text see the table below It used to say The Lc an earlier version of this tool printed, struck through The two methods measure different things, so a row can pass one and fail the other. Neither is a verdict on the artwork; both describe text laid on that colour. Absolute Lc Good for 90 or more any text 75 or more body text 60 or more large text 45 or more headlines only 30 or more non text only Below 30 not for text U"},{"t":"Export the result","d":"Save or copy the recoloured SVG, copy the new palette as CSS custom properties, and save a JSON report of every change.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/export-the-result.html","h":["The recoloured SVG","The custom properties","The report"],"x":" All exports are on the Export tab, under Take it away . They always use the true colours, whatever Show it as seen by is set to. Button What you get Save the recoloured SVG Your file with the colour values replaced, downloaded as recoloured.svg Copy the markup The same SVG markup, copied to the clipboard Copy the custom properties The file's colours as CSS custom properties Save the report A JSON record of every mapping, downloaded as recolour report.json The table under What leaves this page gives the size of each for your file and what it is good for. The exported file is your file with the colour values replaced, and nothing else changed on purpose: Structure, ids, gradients, filters, titles, comments and any markup the tool does not understand are carried across. Only occurrences you changed are rewritten, in the style chosen under Write colours as . In style sheets, only the changed declarations are rewritten. The message confirms, for example Saved · 3 occurrences written . If nothing is loaded, it reads Nothing loaded. Things to know about the file: It is rewritten from your original, not from the preview, so any scripts, event handlers or javascript: links in the original "},{"t":"Recolour an SVG","d":"Load an SVG, understand what colours the tool finds and where, remap and swap colours, choose how they are written, and read the Mapping tab.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/recolour-an-svg.html","h":["Load a file","What the tool finds","The colour list","Remap a colour","Choose how colours are written","What the file holds","The Mapping tab","What you should see"],"x":" On the Recolour tab, under The file , use any of these: Method How Drop Drop an .svg file on Drop an SVG Choose Select Drop an SVG or press Enter or Space while it has focus and choose an .svg file Paste Paste SVG markup into the box under Or paste the markup , then select Read the markup Sample Select Load the sample ; its markup also appears in the paste box A message confirms, for example Loaded logo.svg or Loaded the pasted markup. Loading a new file replaces the previous one and resets every mapping. The file must be well formed XML. If it is not, nothing is changed, the message reads That file will not parse as SVG, so nothing was changed. , and a warning under the paste box gives the parser's own complaint. A file is never half recoloured. An SVG can carry scripts, event handlers and javascript: links. Before drawing the previews, the tool removes script , foreignObject and handler elements, every attribute starting with on , and any href or xlink:href that starts with javascript: . If anything was removed, a notice above the previews lists it, for example 1 <script , 2 onclick handlers . This applies to the previews only. The exported file is rewritten from your original f"},{"t":"Recolour from a harmony","d":"Recolour every colour in an SVG at once from a colour harmony built on the file's main colour, and put the colours back.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/use-a-harmony.html","h":["Apply a harmony","How the harmony is built","After applying","Things to know"],"x":" A harmony is a set of colours at fixed angles round the colour wheel, such as opposite complementary or evenly spaced in threes triadic . Recolour from a harmony builds one from your file's main colour and assigns it to every colour in the file in one step. 1. Load an SVG on the Recolour tab. 2. Under Recolour from a harmony , select one of the five buttons: complementary , analogous , triadic , tetradic or split complementary . 3. Every colour in the file gets a new target, the After preview updates, and a message names the harmony and the base colour, for example A triadic palette from E5484D. If no file is loaded, the message reads Load an SVG first. The base colour is the first row of Every colour in the file : the colour used in the most places. It keeps its own colour. The angles are applied to the base colour's hue in OKLCH, a perceptual colour space, keeping its lightness and chroma. Rotating hue in OKLCH keeps colours looking equally light and colourful, which rotating in HSL does not. Assignment goes down the colour list in order: the second row gets the second angle, and so on. Harmony Hue angles from the base complementary 0°, 180° analogous 0°, −30°, +30° triadic 0°, "},{"t":"SVG Recolour reference","d":"Every tab, control, paint property, colour form, readout, export format and message in SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/reference.html","h":["Tabs","Recolour tab — The file","Recolour tab — Options","Paint properties searched","Colour forms","Active content removed from the previews","Recolour tab — Readouts","Harmonies","Mapping tab","Check tab","Data tab","Export tab","Reference tab","Messages"],"x":" Address: https://auricartisan.com/tool/general/tools/svg recolor/ Tab Contents Recolour Loading, write style, vision preview, harmonies; before and after previews, the colour list and figures Mapping Every colour's use, target and written count; worked examples of swaps and counts Check Text colour; WCAG 2.2 and APCA per colour; closest pairs; the artwork under three dichromacies Data The 15 entries every figure rests on, filterable by status; six corrections Export Four save and copy buttons, the size table, custom properties and the report Reference Nine sources and a six step description of how the tool works Control What it does Accepts Drop an SVG Loads a dropped file, or opens a chooser when selected or when Enter or Space is pressed .svg , image/svg+xml Load the sample Loads a built in sample and puts its markup in the paste box — Paste box SVG markup Text Read the markup Loads the markup in the paste box Well formed SVG The sample loads automatically when the page opens. Control Values Default Write colours as Write hex , Keep the source form Write hex Show it as seen by Normal vision , Protan , Deutan , Tritan Normal vision Recolour from a harmony complementary, analogous"},{"t":"Troubleshooting SVG Recolour","d":"Symptoms you may meet in SVG Recolour, why they happen, and what to do.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Loading","Colours not found or not changed","Previews and checks","Exports"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do That file will not parse as SVG, so nothing was changed. The markup is not well formed XML Read the parser's message under the paste box; fix the markup often an unclosed tag or a stray & and try again Paste some SVG markup first. The paste box is empty Paste the markup, then select Read the markup My file is greyed out in the file chooser The chooser offers .svg files Drag the file onto Drop an SVG , or rename it with the .svg ending A notice says active content was removed The file contains scripts, event handlers or javascript: links The previews are safe; remember the exported file still contains them My mappings disappeared Loading a file, markup or the sample resets every mapping Set the targets again, or apply a harmony Symptom Why What to do A colour I can see is not in the list It is written in a form the tool does not read, such as oklch or var brand Rewrite it as hex, rgb , hsl or a CSS name before loading A colour inside a picture did not change It is part of an embedded raster image, not markup Recolour the raster image in an image editor A row reads left alone The value is currentColor , none , transparent , a keyword such as inherit , or a url"},{"t":"SVG Recolour FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/docs/faq.html","h":["Is my SVG uploaded?","Can I swap two colours?","Does it change colours written as names, like red?","Why is currentColor left alone?","Does it recolour gradients?","Does it recolour embedded images?","Can I recolour several files at once?","Are near-identical colours merged into one row?","Will the exported file look exactly like the After preview?","What does \"near royalblue\" mean?","Is the harmony a guarantee of good colours?","Does the colour-vision preview change the exported file?"],"x":" No. The file is parsed in the page and never sent anywhere. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Yes. Set each colour's target to the other. Every change is planned from the original file before anything is written, so the swap works cleanly. Yes. Names, hex, rgb and hsl forms are all found and rewritten. The same colour written different ways appears as one row. It takes its value from the color of the page the SVG is placed in, so the file does not contain the colour. The tool counts it and leaves it as it is, which keeps icons that rely on it working. Yes, through the stop color of each gradient stop, which appear as their own rows. The shape that uses the gradient refers to it with url , which is left alone. No. Pictures embedded in an SVG are pixels, not markup, and are not found or changed. No. The tool works on one file at a time. No. Only exactly identical colours share a row, however they are written. Yes, in colour: the preview is drawn from the same rewrite. The preview has active content removed, but the file keeps it. It is the nearest CSS colour name, found by colour difference, to make hex values easier to read. An exact CSS name is shown without \"near\". Nothing depen"},{"t":"SVG Recolour background material","d":"The contents of SVG Recolour's others folder: glossary, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference material that supports the guides: the terms the tool uses, what it finds and does not, related tools and reading, its history, and what happens to your files, including active content. The tool has no keyboard shortcuts of its own beyond standard keyboard access, so there is no shortcuts page. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Definitions of the terms used in SVG Recolour limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the tool finds and writes, how precisely, and what it does not hold related.md related.md Related tools on the site and Learn articles release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the tool privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser, and how active content is handled "},{"t":"SVG Recolour glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Active content Parts of an SVG that run code: scripts, event handlers and javascript: links APCA Advanced Perceptual Contrast Algorithm; lightness contrast in Lc units, signed by polarity CIEDE2000 ΔE₀₀ The CIE's standard formula for how different two colours look Closest pair The two colours in the file with the smallest CIEDE2000 difference Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of luminance difference, from 1:1 to 21:1 CSS colour name One of the 148 named colours of CSS, such as red or rebeccapurple currentColor A value that takes the colour from the page the SVG is placed in Custom property A CSS variable, such as colour 01 , holding a colour Dichromacy Colour vision with one of the three cone types missing Harmony A set of colours at fixed angles round the colour wheel Left alone A value with no colour the tool can change, listed but not written OKLCH A perceptual colour space of lightness, chroma and hue, used for the harmonies Occurrence One place in the file where a colour value is written Paint property A property that sets colour, such as fill or stroke Presentation attribute An SVG attribute that sets a style directly, such as fill=\" E5484D\" Protanopia, deuteran"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What SVG Recolour finds and writes, how precise its figures are, and what it does not hold.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is found and written","What is not found or not changed","Precision and choices","Limits","What it is not"],"x":" Eight paint properties: fill , stroke , stop color , flood color , lighting color , color , solid color and text decoration color . In presentation attributes, style attributes and <style elements. Colours written as hex with or without alpha , shorthand hex, rgb , rgba , hsl , hsla and all 148 CSS names. The count beside each colour is the number of occurrences, and the written count is the number actually rewritten. The colour list, the Mapping tab, the report and the exported file all use the same list, so they always agree. Every change is planned from the original file before anything is written, so no change can be caught by another. Item What happens currentColor and other inherited keywords Counted and left alone; the colour comes from outside the file none , transparent , url references Counted and left alone Colours in other CSS functions or variables oklch , lab , var Not recognised, not counted, not changed Embedded raster images Not read; their pixels are not changed Colours set by CSS outside the file Not visible to the tool Item Detail Colour values Parsed to 8 bit sRGB; an unrecognised value is never guessed as black Alpha Kept for rgba and hsla with Keep the sourc"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What SVG Recolour does with your SVG files, and how it handles active content.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/privacy.html","h":["Your file stays in your browser","Active content","Nothing is kept after you leave","What the report contains","The page itself"],"x":" An SVG you drop, choose or paste is read and parsed by the page itself, in your browser. It is not uploaded. Finding colours, rewriting them, the checks and the previews all happen on your device. Exported files are created in the browser and saved by your browser's normal download. The clipboard is written only when you select a copy button. An SVG is a document, not just a picture, and can contain scripts, event handlers and javascript: links. Because this tool is often used on files other people send, the previews on the page are drawn from a copy with that content removed, and a notice lists what was removed. The file's scripts are not run by the page. The exported file is rewritten from your original, so it still contains any active content the original had. If you do not trust the file, remove that content in an editor before using the export elsewhere. The tool does not store your file, your mappings or your settings. Loading another file, reloading or leaving the page clears them. The report contains counts of elements and colours, every colour mapping and the values left alone. It does not contain the SVG markup. SVG Recolour is a normal page on auricartisan.com. Site wid"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/release-notes.html","h":["7 June 2026 — rewrites planned from the original","25 May 2026 — earlier version"],"x":" The earlier engine was replaced by the current workbench, titled SVG Recolour , with six tabs: Recolour , Mapping , Check , Data , Export and Reference . The site's earlier user guide carries a notice that it describes the engine replaced on this date. What changed for you: Two colours can trade places. The earlier version replaced colours one after another as text, so swapping red and blue left both red. Every change is now planned from the original file and written once. Colours written as names are changed. A fill=\"red\" was listed and offered for remapping but never rewritten. It is now rewritten like any other form. Three digit colours stay the colour you chose. The earlier version could write a new colour as a three digit shorthand that browsers read as a different colour. New colours are written as six digits. The count is the number of places. The earlier count doubled or quadrupled depending on how the file was written. The count is now the number of occurrences, and the written count is what was actually changed. The APCA column works. It printed zero for every pair; it now gives real APCA W3 0.1.9 figures beside the WCAG 2.2 ratio. Grouping uses a real colour difference "},{"t":"Related tools and reading","d":"Other Auric Artisan tools and Learn articles that go with SVG Recolour.","p":"Website › Tools › Image and file tools › SVG Recolour","u":"website/tools/image-and-file-tools/svg-recolour/others/related.html","h":["Tools on the site","Learn articles","Other documentation"],"x":" Tool Why you might use it with SVG Recolour Icon Library ../../../colour workspace/icon library/README.md Find open source SVG icons to recolour M Gradient Palette ../../m gradient palette/README.md Build an evenly stepped palette to apply to artwork Image Picker ../../image picker/README.md Take target colours from a photograph Contrast Checker ../../../accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Test one text and background pair in more depth Vision Simulation ../../../accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Simulate more kinds of colour vision on a finished design Collage Maker ../../collage maker/README.md Place exported artwork, as PNG, into a collage Color Theory and Harmony — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony Color Blindness and Color Vision Deficiency — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 color blindness cvd Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contrast — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 wcag contrast accessible color Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color space"},{"t":"Kits","d":"What the Auric Artisan kits are, how to open them from the page utilities bar, and the controls every kit panel shares.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","The kits","Controls every kit shares","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Kits are small floating panels that you can open on any page of auricartisan.com without leaving the page you are on. Each kit does one job: the Feature Kit holds a calculator, a unit converter, notes, date tools and developer utilities; the Menu Kit is a start menu for the whole site; the Advanced Kit decides which tools the site shows you; the Status Kit shows the status of pages and your device; the Library Kit holds everything you have saved from the tools. Kits are modeless. A kit floats above the page, and the page underneath stays usable: you can scroll, click and type in a tool while a kit is open. You can drag a kit anywhere in the window, make it larger, shrink it to its title bar, give it its own light or dark theme, and keep it open while you move from page to page. All kits open from one place: the page utilities bar in the bottom left corner of the window. A few kits also have keyboard shortcuts, and the Library Kit has a button in the site header. Anyone using the site's tools who wants a quick calculation, conversion or note without opening another tab. Designers and developers who save palettes, gradients, reports and presets and want to find, compare and reuse th"},{"t":"Guides for all kits","d":"Contents of the shared kit guides, which cover the launcher bar and the panel controls every kit uses.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder covers what the kits have in common: how to open them, the page utilities bar that launches them, and the title bar controls that move, resize, minimise, theme and close every panel. Guides for a single kit live in that kit's own folder. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open your first kit, learn the parts of a kit panel, and close it again the kit dock.md the kit dock.md The page utilities bar: its launchers, its phone layout and how it behaves panel controls.md panel controls.md Every title bar control, what each kit remembers, and how the kits differ troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems that affect all kits, with causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions about kits Kit specific guides: Feature Kit guides ../feature kit/docs/README.md Menu Kit guides ../menu kit/docs/README.md Advanced Kit guides ../advanced kit/docs/README.md Status Kit guides ../status kit/docs/README.md Library Kit guides ../library kit/docs/README.md Update Kit guides ../update kit/docs/README.md "},{"t":"Getting started with kits","d":"Open your first kit from the page utilities bar, learn the parts of a kit panel, and close it again.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","Open your first kit","The parts of a kit panel","Keep working while a kit is open","Open more than one kit","Close a kit","Next steps"],"x":" A kit is a floating panel that opens over the page you are on. This guide opens one, walks through the parts every kit shares, and closes it again. Kits work on desktop and on phones. On a narrow screen the launcher bar wraps into two rows. Kits need JavaScript. Each kit loads the first time you open it, so the first open can take a moment on a slow connection. While it loads, its launcher looks dimmed and shows a busy pointer. Nothing needs an account. Kits keep their preferences in your browser. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . 1. Go to any page, for example https://auricartisan.com. 2. Find the round button in the bottom left corner of the window. Its tooltip reads Page utilities . 3. Select it. A bar slides open with labelled launchers: Close , Feature , Menu , Advanced , Status , Library , Navigate and Settings . 4. Select Feature . The bar folds away and the Feature Kit opens in the bottom left corner of the window, showing six cards. 5. Select Scientific Calculator , type 2+3 with your keyboard and press Enter . You see 5 in the calculator's display. You have opened a kit, switched to one of its tools and used it. Every kit panel has the same frame. Title bar. The kit's n"},{"t":"Panel controls","d":"Every title-bar control shared by the kit panels, what each one remembers, and where the kits differ.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/panel-controls.html","h":["Sizes and starting position","Move a panel","Focus mode","Theme","Resize","Minimize","Close","What the title bar holds in each kit","What the kits remember","Other things you may see in a kit","Related"],"x":" Every kit panel has a title bar with the same set of controls: move, Focus mode , Theme , Resize , Minimize and Close . This page explains each control, what the kits remember between visits, and the places where a kit does something different. A kit opens in the bottom left corner of the window, just above the page utilities bar, until you move it. It opens at its normal size unless you left it expanded. Kit Normal width Expanded width Feature Kit 560 px 640 px Menu Kit 680 px 820 px Advanced Kit 480 px 720 px Status Kit 560 px 760 px Library Kit 680 px 940 px An expanded kit is never wider than the window, less a small margin. An expanded Menu, Advanced, Status or Library Kit grows to at most 900 px tall, and always leaves room for its title bar at the top of the window. An expanded Feature Kit grows to at most 900 px or 90% of the window height, whichever is smaller. On a phone 580 px wide or narrower every kit spans the width of the screen, less a small margin. With a pointer or touch: 1. Press on the kit's title bar, away from the buttons. 2. Drag the panel to where you want it. 3. Release. The panel stays inside the window: you cannot drag it past an edge. The kit remembers "},{"t":"The page utilities bar","d":"How the launcher bar in the bottom-left corner opens every kit, how it looks on a phone, and how it closes.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/the-kit-dock.html","h":["Closed and open","Open the bar and a kit","Close the bar","Launchers of open kits","Loading","On a phone","Keyboard use","Accessibility","Related"],"x":" The page utilities bar is the one place every kit opens from. It sits in the bottom left corner of every page. Closed, it is a single round button; open, it is a row of labelled launchers. Closed , the bar is one round button with a gold outline. Its tooltip reads Page utilities : \"Show navigation, settings, and the Feature, Menu, Advanced, Status and Library kits.\" Open , the bar becomes a single card with one cell per launcher. Each cell shows an icon with a one word name under it: Cell What it opens Tooltip Close Folds the bar away. This is the same round button, relabelled while the bar is open. Hide page utilities Feature Feature Kit ../feature kit/README.md Calculator, converter, graph tools, and feedback. Menu Menu Kit ../menu kit/README.md Open site navigation, grouped pages, and quick search. Advanced Advanced Kit ../advanced kit/README.md Choose Basic, Advanced, or Everything tool visibility. Status Status Kit ../status kit/README.md View the current page status and scan page status entries. Library Library Kit ../library kit/README.md Browse, search and restore everything you have saved across the tools. Navigate The page navigation dock Back, forward, reload, outline, "},{"t":"Troubleshooting kits","d":"Fixes for problems that affect every kit, such as a missing launcher, a kit that keeps reopening, or a panel stuck in the wrong place.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The Page utilities button is missing","A launcher is dimmed and does nothing","A kit opens by itself on every page","Opening one kit closes another","The page goes dark behind the Feature Kit","A kit is off to one side, or I cannot find it","A kit is light on a dark page, or dark on a light page","A keyboard shortcut does nothing","Ctrl + K opens the site search instead of the kit's search","Esc closed more than one kit","My kit settings are not remembered","The launcher bar covers the bottom of the page on a phone","Still stuck"],"x":" This page covers problems that affect all kits. Each kit also has its own troubleshooting page for problems inside that kit. Why: The bar is added by the site's scripts after the page has loaded. It does not appear if JavaScript is blocked, if a content blocker removes the site's scripts, or while the page is still loading on a slow connection. What to do: 1. Wait a few seconds after the page appears. The button is added once the page is ready. 2. Check that JavaScript is allowed for auricartisan.com. 3. Pause content blocking extensions for the site and reload. Why: The kit is still loading. A launcher is dimmed, with a busy pointer, from the moment you select it until the kit has loaded. It ignores further clicks during that time. What to do: Wait for the kit to open. If the launcher stays dimmed for a long time, or returns to normal without opening anything, the kit could not load, usually because the connection dropped. Reload the page and try again. Why: Its Focus mode is on. The Menu, Advanced, Status and Library Kits keep Focus mode on after you close them, and open again on the next page you load. What to do: Open the kit, select Focus mode the target icon so it is no long"},{"t":"Kits FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the floating kits on auricartisan.com.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/docs/faq.html","h":["What is a kit?","Do I need an account to use the kits?","Are the kits free?","Where do I find the kits?","Can I have two kits open at once?","Will a kit stay open when I go to another page?","Does a kit block the page?","Why does a kit look different from the rest of the page?","Can I move a kit back to the corner?","Do kits work on a phone?","Can I use kits with the keyboard only?","What is the \"UX Kit\" in the changelog?","Is the Update Kit a panel?","What do the kits store about me?"],"x":" A floating panel that opens over any page of the site and does one job: calculations and utilities Feature Kit , site navigation Menu Kit , tool visibility Advanced Kit , page and device status Status Kit , or your saved work Library Kit . No. Every kit works without signing in. The Library Kit keeps your saved items in your browser, not in an account. Yes. Every kit is available on every plan. Your plan only sets how many active items the Library Kit can keep; see the Library Kit FAQ ../library kit/docs/faq.md . Select the round Page utilities button in the bottom left corner of any page. See The page utilities bar the kit dock.md . Yes. Turn on Focus mode in the first kit before opening the second. Without Focus mode, opening a kit closes the one already open. The Status Kit always closes when another kit opens. Only with Focus mode on. Each page load starts fresh, and kits with Focus mode on open again automatically. No, with one exception. Kits float above the page and you can keep using the page. The Feature Kit dims the page while its Focus mode is off; turn Focus mode on to keep the page usable. Each kit can have its own light or dark theme, set with its Theme button. Once "},{"t":"Advanced Kit","d":"Choose which of the site's tools you see, site-wide: Basic, Advanced, Everything, or a Custom set you tick yourself.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan has tools for everyday colour work and tools for colour science, vision research and diagnostics. The Advanced Kit decides which of them the site puts in front of you. You choose one of four modes: Basic , Advanced , Everything or Custom . The choice applies across the whole site and is remembered in your browser. It changes which tools appear in the Menu Kit and in the tool collections, which keypads the Feature Kit calculator offers, and some of the wording on the home page and on several tool pages. In Custom mode you tick individual tools on or off from a searchable checklist. No tool is ever locked or removed: every tool page still opens from its address, and Everything mode shows all of them. New visitors who want a short, friendly list of tools Basic , the default . Scientists, researchers and specialists who want the diagnostic and scientific tools up front Advanced . People who want to see the full range Everything . Regular users who want exactly their own set of tools Custom . On any page of https://auricartisan.com, select Page utilities in the bottom left corner, then Advanced . Or press Ctrl + Shift + A . 1. Press Ctrl + Shift + A . The Advanced Kit ope"},{"t":"Advanced Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Advanced Kit guides: getting started, the four modes, custom tool sets and what each mode changes.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain the Advanced Kit's four tool visibility modes, how to build your own set of tools, and exactly what changes on the site when you switch mode. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the Advanced Kit and learn its screen choose a mode.md choose a mode.md Basic, Advanced, Everything and Custom, and how to switch build a custom tool set.md build a custom tool set.md Tick tools on and off in Custom mode what each mode changes.md what each mode changes.md Every part of the site that follows the mode reference.md reference.md Every control and message in the kit troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems and how to fix them faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions Shared controls such as moving, Focus mode and theme are explained in Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with the Advanced Kit","d":"Open the Advanced Kit, learn the parts of its screen, and change the site's tool visibility mode.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the kit","The screen, top to bottom","Change the mode","If you have never chosen a mode","Close the kit","Next steps"],"x":" Use either: Page utilities bottom left corner Advanced , or Ctrl + Shift + A . The launcher's tooltip reads \"Choose Basic, Advanced, or Everything tool visibility.\" The kit opens with keyboard focus on the card for your current mode. 1. Title bar. Advanced Kit and the buttons Focus mode , Theme , Resize , Minimize and Close . 2. Heading. Tool visibility , with the line \"Choose which tools stay visible by default.\" 3. Current mode. A badge showing Basic , Advanced , Everything or Custom . 4. Mode summary. An illustration of the current mode, a one line title, a short description and one or two buttons to switch mode. 5. Default visibility. Four illustrated cards, one per mode. The Basic card carries a Recommended tag. The selected card shows a tick. 6. Choose your tools. The Custom checklist. It appears only in Custom mode. 7. Quick cards. Links to example tools that fit the current mode. 1. Select a card under Default visibility , for example Advanced . 2. The tick moves to that card, Current mode updates, and the summary changes to \"Advanced tools are on\". The change applies at once to the whole site, on this page and every page you open next. You do not need to save. New visitor"},{"t":"Build a custom tool set","d":"Use Custom mode in the Advanced Kit to tick exactly the tools you want the site to list.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/build-a-custom-tool-set.html","h":["Open the checklist","The checklist","Turn tools on or off","Find a tool in the list","Change many tools at once","Where your custom set applies","Your ticks are kept when you switch mode","Example: a palette-only set","Related"],"x":" In Custom mode you decide tool by tool what the site lists. Unticked tools disappear from the Menu Kit and from the tool collections, on every page of the site. 1. Open the Advanced Kit. 2. Select the Custom card under Default visibility . A section called Choose your tools appears below the cards. The first time, it shows Loading tools… while it gathers the list. Every tool starts ticked. Tools are grouped by category, for example Accessibility , Colorimetry , Generators , Perception , Spectral and Utilities , with categories in alphabetical order and tools in alphabetical order within each. The list covers the site's tool pages only. Account, library, company and legal pages are not in it and always stay visible. Some names differ slightly from the Menu Kit, because the checklist uses the collections' names where it can. For example the URL Analyzer appears as Analyze URLs and the Ishihara plate tool as Generate Ishihara Plates . 1. Untick a tool to hide it. The change applies at once, across the site. 2. Tick it again to show it. There is no save button. Type part of a name in Filter tools… . Rows that do not match hide, and categories with no matching rows hide too. Clear the "},{"t":"Choose a mode","d":"What the Basic, Advanced, Everything and Custom tool visibility modes mean, and how to switch between them.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/choose-a-mode.html","h":["The four modes","How tools are sorted into Basic and Advanced","Switch mode","Which mode to pick","Where the mode is stored","Other places that change the same setting","Related"],"x":" The tool visibility mode is one site wide setting with four values. It decides which tools the site lists for you. Every tool can still be opened from its own address in any mode. Mode Card description Summary shown when active Basic Recommended Beginner friendly tools stay visible while deeper scientific tools are hidden. Advanced tools are hidden — \"Science, research, and precision tools stay tucked away until you need them.\" Advanced Scientific, diagnostic, and power user tools stay visible while simple tools are hidden. Advanced tools are on — \"Keep the scientific set visible, or open the full platform when you want more.\" Everything Every tool stays available, including removed or not yet used cards. Everything is available — \"Removed and not yet used tools come back while Everything is active.\" Custom Turn individual tools on or off — your picks apply across the whole site. Your custom tool set is active — \"Tick the tools you want — your picks apply across the menu and every tool grid, site wide.\" Each tool is treated as basic , advanced or both : Both tools show in every mode. They include the URL Analyzer, the Vision Deficiency Simulator, the Design System Generator, and a"},{"t":"What each mode changes","d":"Every part of auricartisan.com that follows the tool visibility mode, from the Menu Kit and collections to page wording and the Feature Kit calculator.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/what-each-mode-changes.html","h":["Summary","Menu Kit","Tool collections","Feature Kit calculator","Page wording","What the mode never changes","Related"],"x":" The mode you pick in the Advanced Kit is read by several parts of the site. This page lists each one and what it does in each mode. Part of the site Basic Advanced Everything Custom Menu Kit tiles and search Basic and both tools Advanced and both tools All All except unticked tools Tool collections Basic and both tools Advanced and both tools All, including cards hidden earlier All except unticked tools Feature Kit calculator keypads Basic only Scientific , Programmer All three All three Page wording see below Basic wording Advanced wording Everything wording Basic wording The Menu Kit shows only the tools the mode allows, in its tiles and in its search results. A tab with nothing to show is hidden: Basic: the Design tab disappears. Advanced: the Design tab appears, and the General Color Tools section of the Tools tab is hidden. Everything: every tab and page. Custom: every page except unticked tools. See Find a page ../../menu kit/docs/find a page.md . Tool collection grids, such as the one at https://auricartisan.com/collections/, show only the tools the mode allows. In Everything mode they also bring back cards that were hidden, whether you hid them or the grid hid them because"},{"t":"Advanced Kit reference","d":"Every control, card, button and message in the Advanced Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Launcher","Title bar","Body","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Control What it does Default Advanced launcher slider icon Opens or closes the kit. Announces itself as Open Advanced Kit or Close Advanced Kit Closed Ctrl + Shift + A Same as the launcher — Tooltip \"Choose Basic, Advanced, or Everything tool visibility.\" — Control What it does Values Default Advanced Kit title Drag the title bar to move the kit — Bottom left corner Focus mode Keeps the kit open across pages and when other kits open On or off; remembered Off Theme Switches the kit between light and dark Light or dark; remembered Follows the site Resize Normal 480 px wide or expanded up to 720 px wide Remembered Normal Minimize Collapses the kit to its title bar — — Close Closes the kit \"Close the Advanced Kit panel.\" — — Element What it shows or does Tool visibility Heading, with \"Choose which tools stay visible by default.\" Current mode badge Basic , Advanced , Everything or Custom Mode summary Illustration, title and description for the current mode, and switch buttons Default visibility cards Four selectable cards; a tick marks the current one. The Basic card is tagged Recommended . Each card's tooltip repeats its description Choose your tools The Custom checklist; shown only i"},{"t":"Advanced Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for Advanced Kit problems, such as a mode that changes by itself or a tool that will not reappear.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["My mode changed by itself","A tool I unticked still appears","A tool I want is missing from the menu","The Custom checklist says \"No tools found.\"","The checklist names do not match the Menu Kit","Ctrl + Shift + A does nothing","The mode is different on my other computer","Page wording did not change"],"x":" For problems shared by every kit, see Troubleshooting kits ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: Some tools have their own mode switch that sets the same site wide mode. Opening the URL Analyzer sets the site to Basic or Advanced to match the Analyzer's Simple or Advanced mode. The Vision Simulation lab and the Colour Science Lab can also change it, and resetting the Vision Simulation filters sets Everything . What to do: Open the Advanced Kit and choose your mode again. If you were in Custom mode, your ticks are still there; select Custom to use them again. Why: Your ticks only apply while the current mode is Custom . Another mode may be active, or a tool may have changed the mode see above . What to do: Check Current mode in the Advanced Kit and select Custom . Why: The current mode hides it, or you unticked it in Custom mode. What to do: Select Everything , or tick the tool in Custom mode. Every tool also opens from its own address. Why: The tool list could not be downloaded. What to do: Check your connection, reload the page, and open the Advanced Kit again. Why: The checklist uses the names from the tool collections where it can, such as Analyze URLs for the URL Analyzer and B"},{"t":"Advanced Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Advanced Kit and the tool visibility modes.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["Does Basic mode lock the advanced tools?","Is the Advanced Kit a paid feature?","Which mode do new visitors get?","Is my mode saved to my account?","Do my Custom ticks survive if I switch to another mode?","What does Everything bring back that Basic and Advanced do not?","Why does the calculator lose its Scientific keypad in Basic mode?","What is the \"UX Kit\"?","Does the mode affect the site-wide search?"],"x":" No. It only hides them from the menus and collections. Every tool page opens from its address in every mode. No. All modes are available to everyone, signed in or not. Basic , which the kit marks as Recommended . No. It is stored in your browser. Each browser and device keeps its own mode. Yes. They apply again whenever you select Custom . Reset is the only thing that clears them. Every tool, plus collection cards that were hidden earlier, whether you hid them or the collection hid them because you had not used them yet. The Feature Kit calculator follows the mode: Basic shows only the Basic keypad. Choose Everything to see all three. The expression bar still accepts every function in any mode. The name the changelog uses for the part of the site that changes page wording when you switch mode. It has no panel; you control it from the Advanced Kit. See What each mode changes what each mode changes.md . No. The site wide search shows results for every tool whatever the mode. "},{"t":"Advanced Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Advanced Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Advanced Kit: the terms it uses, its shortcuts, what the modes do and do not affect, related pages, its public history and what it keeps in your browser. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Advanced Kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Advanced Kit keyboard shortcuts limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the modes affect, and how tools are classified related.md related.md Related kits, tools and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the Advanced Kit privacy.md privacy.md What the Advanced Kit keeps in your browser "},{"t":"Advanced Kit shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts for the Advanced Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + Shift + A Anywhere Opens or closes the Advanced Kit Esc Kit open Closes the kit Tab , Shift + Tab Kit open Move between the mode cards, buttons, filter box and checkboxes Enter or Space A mode card Selects that mode Space A tool checkbox Ticks or unticks the tool When the kit opens, keyboard focus goes to the card of the current mode. See Kit keyboard shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md for the other kits. "},{"t":"Advanced Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Advanced Kit guides.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Tool visibility mode — The site wide setting that decides which tools are listed: Basic, Advanced, Everything or Custom. Sometimes called complexity mode. Basic mode — Shows everyday, beginner friendly tools and hides the scientific ones. The default. Advanced mode — Shows scientific, diagnostic and power user tools and hides the simplest ones. Everything mode — Shows every tool, including collection cards that were hidden earlier. Custom mode — Shows every tool except the ones you untick in the checklist. Basic, advanced and both tools — The level each tool is given. Both tools show in every mode. Custom checklist — The Choose your tools list of tick boxes shown in Custom mode. Quick cards — The three example tool links at the bottom of the kit. Mode summary — The illustrated panel under Current mode that describes the active mode and offers switch buttons. UX Kit — The changelog's name for the part of the site that changes page wording when the mode changes. It has no panel of its own. Colorimetry — The measurement of colour as numbers, such as chromaticity and colour spaces. Gamut — The range of colours a device or colour space can show. Spectral — To do with light broken into "},{"t":"Advanced Kit limits","d":"What the tool visibility modes affect, what they do not, and how tools are classified.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the modes affect","What they do not affect","How tools are classified","Custom mode","Storage"],"x":" The Menu Kit's tiles and search results. Tool collection grids, such as https://auricartisan.com/collections/. The Feature Kit calculator's keypad tabs. Some wording on the home page and on the URL Analyzer, Vision Simulation, Colour Science Lab, Basic Colour Tools and Ishihara Plate Generation pages. Whether a tool page opens: nothing is locked. Browser tab titles and search engine descriptions. The site wide search. Your saved library items, settings and account. Tools listed in the Menu Kit carry a level of basic, advanced or both, set by the site. Where no level is set, the site decides from the tool's section: tools in the Tools tab count as basic, tools in the Design tab as advanced, and account, library, company and legal pages as both. The classification is the site's, not yours. To show or hide a particular tool regardless of its level, use Custom mode. The checklist covers tool pages only addresses starting with /tool/ , not other pages. Custom choices are stored as a list of tools you have turned off. New tools added to the site later start switched on. Page wording follows the Basic set while Custom is active. The mode and your custom choices are stored in this browser"},{"t":"Advanced Kit privacy","d":"What the Advanced Kit keeps in your browser and what it downloads.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Kept in your browser","Downloaded","Related"],"x":" What Why Your tool visibility mode So every page shows the tools you chose The tools you unticked in Custom mode So your custom set applies site wide Position, expanded size, Focus mode and theme Shared kit preferences Nothing is linked to your account or sent anywhere. Clearing this site's data in your browser resets the mode to Basic and clears your custom choices. When you first open the Custom checklist on a page, the kit downloads the site's tool lists from auricartisan.com to build it. Privacy for all kits ../../others/privacy.md The site's privacy policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ "},{"t":"Advanced Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about the Advanced Kit and the tool visibility modes.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Advanced Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.8 2 May 2026 \"Added and improved the Advanced Kit\", with complexity management added v0.9.9 5 June 2026 UX Kit features and stronger complexity handling, alongside site wide interface work Four illustrated mode cards: Basic Recommended , Advanced , Everything and Custom . A Current mode badge and an illustrated mode summary with switch buttons. A Custom checklist of the site's tools, grouped by category, with Filter tools… , Enable all , Disable all and Reset . Quick cards for Analyze URLs , Image Color Picker and Generate Ishihara Plates . Shared kit controls: Focus mode, per kit theme, Resize, Minimize, Close, and a labelled Advanced launcher in the page utilities bar. Changes not recorded in the public history are not listed here. "},{"t":"Related to the Advanced Kit","d":"Kits, tools and pages related to the Advanced Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Advanced Kit","u":"website/kits/advanced-kit/others/related.html","h":["Kits that follow the mode","Tools with their own mode switch","Tools behind the quick cards","Pages"],"x":" Menu Kit ../../menu kit/README.md — tiles and search follow the mode. Feature Kit ../../feature kit/README.md — the calculator's keypad tabs follow the mode. All kits ../../README.md and Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — Simple and Advanced modes. Vision Simulation ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — mode buttons and filters. Colour Science Lab ../../../tools/colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md — mode buttons. URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Analyze URLs Image Picker ../../../tools/image and file tools/image picker/README.md Image Color Picker Ishihara Plate Generator ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/ishihara plate generator/README.md Generate Ishihara Plates Collections ../../../library/collections/README.md — tool collections that follow the mode. "},{"t":"Feature Kit","d":"A floating toolbox with a scientific calculator, graphing, a unit converter, notes, date and time tools, developer utilities and a feedback form.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Feature Kit is a floating toolbox that opens on any page of auricartisan.com. It holds six tools behind one menu: a Scientific Calculator with graphing and history, a Unit Converter with 1,344 units in 70 categories, a Feedback form, a Markdown Notes scratchpad, a Date & Time workbench and a set of Developer Tools . The calculator is more than a keypad. Its expression bar understands variables, functions you define yourself such as f x = x^2 + 1 , statistics, number theory, physical constants and numerical calculus: derivatives, integrals, equation solving, sums and products. Results show as exact fractions when a tidy one exists, and any function can be plotted on a graph you can pan and zoom. Everything except sending feedback and loading the unit list runs in your browser. Calculator history and notes are kept in your browser between visits. Designers and developers who need a quick calculation, conversion, timestamp or hash while working in a tool. Students checking maths, including derivatives, integrals and statistics. Anyone who wants a scratchpad or a date calculator that stays one click away on every page. Visitors who want to tell the Auric Artisan team what works an"},{"t":"Feature Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Feature Kit guides, one per tool, plus the full reference, troubleshooting and FAQ.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides cover each of the Feature Kit's six tools, the calculator's complete function list, and every control in the kit. Start with Getting started if you have not opened the kit before. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the kit, tour the menu and the title bar, and run a first calculation calculator.md calculator.md Keypad modes, the expression bar, results, RAD and DEG, memory and history calculator functions.md calculator functions.md Every operator, function and constant, variables, your own functions, calculus, statistics and programmer features graphing.md graphing.md Plot a function, pan, zoom and reset the graph unit converter.md unit converter.md Convert values between units and search the unit list notes.md notes.md Write, preview, copy, export and delete Markdown notes date and time.md date and time.md Calendar readouts, date differences, adding and subtracting, and world clocks developer tools.md developer tools.md JSON, Base64, URL, Hash, UUID, JWT, Epoch, Regex, Cron, Text and HTML tools feedback.md feedback.md Send quick or detailed feedback, and what happens if sending fails reference.md reference.md Every button, tab, field and m"},{"t":"Getting started with the Feature Kit","d":"Open the Feature Kit, tour its menu and title bar, and run your first calculation.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the kit","The menu","The title bar","Dimmed page and Focus mode","Your first calculation","Leave the kit","Next steps"],"x":" The Feature Kit opens on a menu of six tools. This guide opens the kit, explains what you see, and runs a first calculation. Use either: Page utilities bottom left corner Feature , or Ctrl + Shift + K Cmd + Shift + K on a Mac from anywhere on the page. The first time you open it on a page, the launcher dims for a moment while the kit loads. The kit opens on its menu: six cards, each with an illustration, a title, a one line description and a number key. Key Card Description on the card 1 Scientific Calculator Advanced math, graphing, history 2 Unit Converter 1000+ conversions across 50+ categories 3 Feedback Quiet, optional feedback in Feature Kit 4 Notes Markdown scratchpad with autosave 5 Date & Time Date math, durations, time zones 6 Developer Tools JSON, JWT, regex, cron, hash, UUID, text tools Below the cards, a hint line reads 1 – 6 Open · Ctrl ⇧ K Toggle with ⌘ on a Mac . To open a tool, select its card, press its number key, or use the arrow keys to reach the card and press Enter . Button When you see it What it does Back left arrow Inside any tool Returns to the menu Title Always Reads Feature Kit on the menu and the tool's name inside a tool. Drag it to move the kit. Gra"},{"t":"Calculator functions","d":"The complete expression language of the Feature Kit calculator: operators, numbers, functions, constants, variables, your own functions, calculus, statistics and programmer features.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/calculator-functions.html","h":["How expressions are read","Functions","Constants","Variables","Your own functions","Calculus and series","How results are shown"],"x":" This page lists everything you can type into the calculator's expression bar. The keypad uses the same rules; it simply types the symbols for you. Spaces are ignored. 2 + 3 and 2+3 are the same. This also means sin 30 is read as the unknown name sin30 ; always use brackets: sin 30 . Multiplication must be written. Type 2 pi , not 2pi . A missing operator gives Unexpected token after expression . Names are case sensitive. sin works, SIN does not; NA is Avogadro's number, na is not defined. Brackets must balance. A missing gives Expected . From the loosest to the tightest binding: 1. bitwise OR 2. xor bitwise exclusive OR, written after a value: 5 xor 3 3. & bitwise AND 4. << and bit shifts 5. + and the keypad's − is the same as 6. or × , / or ÷ , and % 7. A leading or + sign 8. ^ power, which groups from the right 9. ! factorial Things that follow from this order: 2^2 is 4 , because the power is worked out before the sign. 2^3^2 is 2^9 , which is 512 . 2^ 1 is 0.5 . % is the remainder , not a percentage: 10 % 3 is 1 . To take 15% of 80, type 80 15/100 . Dividing by zero gives the error Division by zero . A remainder by zero gives NaN . You type Meaning Example result 42 , 3.14 , .5"},{"t":"Use the calculator","d":"Use the Feature Kit's Scientific Calculator: keypads, the expression bar, angle mode, memory, copying results and history.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/calculator.html","h":["The screen, top to bottom","Calculate with the keypad","The three keypads","Calculate with the expression bar","The function reference (ƒx)","The variables strip","Angle mode: RAD and DEG","Memory keys","Copy a result","Use the history","Related"],"x":" The Scientific Calculator gives you two ways to calculate: a keypad which you can also drive from your keyboard and an expression bar for full expressions with variables, your own functions and calculus. Both share one result display, one ans value and one history. Open it from the Feature Kit menu with the Scientific Calculator card or the 1 key. 1. Display. A small expression line, a large result line, and the angle buttons RAD and DEG . 2. Expression bar. A long text box with a calculator icon and an ƒx button at its right end. Its placeholder reads f x = x^2 · integral sin x , 0, pi · solve x^2−2, 1 . 3. Function reference. Hidden until you select ƒx . 4. Variables strip. Appears once you have defined a variable or a function. 5. Graph and History areas. Hidden until you select Graph or History in the title bar. 6. Keypad tabs: Basic , Scientific , Programmer . 7. Memory row: MC , MR , M+ , M− . 8. Keypad for the selected tab. 1. Select keys, or type on your keyboard while the cursor is not in a text box. 2. Watch the result line: it previews the answer as you type. 3. Select = or press Enter to finish. The result becomes ans , and the calculation goes into the history. After "},{"t":"Work with dates and times","d":"Use the Feature Kit's Date & Time tool to read a date in many formats, count days between dates, add or subtract time, and watch world clocks.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/date-and-time.html","h":["The calendar picker","Calendar tab: read a date in every format","Difference tab: count the time between two dates","Add / Subtract tab: shift a date","Timezones tab: world clocks","Related"],"x":" Date & Time is a small date workbench with four tabs: Calendar , Difference , Add / Subtract and Timezones . Dates are written in the format of the site's language, or of your browser if the site has no preference. Open it with the Date & Time card on the Feature Kit menu, or press 5 on the menu. All four tabs use the same calendar: The month and year sit at the top, with ‹ previous month on the left and « previous year , » next year and › next month on the right. The week starts on Sunday: Su Mo Tu We Th Fr Sa . Today is marked. The selected day is highlighted. Weekends and days from the neighbouring months look different. Clear removes the selection. Today selects today and jumps to its month. 1. Select the Calendar tab it opens first . 2. Pick a day. Today is selected when you arrive. 3. Set the time of day in the Time box if it matters. Under the calendar you see the date in ISO form with a relative description Today , Tomorrow , Yesterday , in 12 days , 3 days ago , then one row per format, each with a Copy button: Row Example Full culture The full date and short time in your locale, for example Thursday 24 September 2026 at 14:05 Long date 24 September 2026 ISO 8601 2026 09 "},{"t":"Use the developer tools","d":"Use the eleven developer utilities in the Feature Kit: JSON, Base64, URL, Hash, UUID, JWT, Epoch, Regex, Cron, Text and HTML.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/developer-tools.html","h":["JSON","Base64","URL","Hash","UUID","JWT","Epoch","Regex","Cron","Text","HTML","Related"],"x":" Developer Tools gathers eleven small utilities behind one row of tabs. Everything runs in your browser: nothing you paste is sent anywhere or kept after you leave the page. Open it with the Developer Tools card on the Feature Kit menu, or press 6 on the menu. It opens on JSON . Select a tab to switch tool. Most tools share one layout: an input box, a row of buttons, and an output box. Copy copies the output box. It briefly reads Copied , or Copy failed if your browser blocked the clipboard. Errors show in the output box in a warning colour. Paste JSON into the box the placeholder shows { \"hello\": \"world\", \"n\": 1 } , then choose: Button Output Format The JSON indented with two spaces Minify The JSON on one line with no spaces Sort keys Indented, with every object's keys sorted alphabetically, at every depth → TypeScript A TypeScript interface Root or type Root for arrays and plain values describing the data Stats Size in bytes, number of keys, objects, arrays, and the deepest nesting level Escape Your input as a quoted JSON string, ready to embed Copy Copies the output If the input is not valid JSON, the output reads Invalid JSON: with the browser's message and, where the browser g"},{"t":"Send feedback","d":"Send quick or detailed feedback about Auric Artisan from the Feature Kit, and what happens when sending fails.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/feedback.html","h":["Open the feedback form","Send quick feedback","Send detailed feedback","Not now","If sending fails","When the kit asks for feedback","What is sent"],"x":" The Feedback tool in the Feature Kit lets you tell the Auric Artisan team how the site is working for you. A quick rating takes one click; a detailed form takes about a minute. Both are optional. Select the Feedback card on the Feature Kit menu, or press 3 on the menu. You may also see a small prompt inside the Feature Kit that reads Feedback when you're ready with the line \"The full form lives in Feature Kit and stays out of the way.\" Select Open form to go to the form, or Later to dismiss it. The prompt hides by itself after 10 seconds. 1. Read the question at the top. It depends on what you did last in the kit, for example How's your experience so far? , How was the calculator? or How was the unit converter? 2. Choose one of five faces: Terrible , Bad , Okay , Good or Amazing . 3. A comment box appears: Tell us more optional ... . Type a comment if you like. 4. Select Submit . It reads Sending... while it sends. A thank you message appears, matched to your rating: Thank you! , We hear you. or Thanks for sharing! . Select Done , or wait 5 seconds, to return to the Feature Kit menu. Submit stays disabled until you choose a face. 1. On the quick feedback screen, optionally choose "},{"t":"Plot a function","d":"Plot a function in the Feature Kit calculator, then pan, zoom and reset the view.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/graphing.html","h":["Show the graph","Plot your own expression","Move around the graph","Make the graph bigger","Hide the graph","Related"],"x":" The calculator can draw the graph of any expression in x . The graph redraws as you type, uses the same functions and constants as the calculator, and can use the variables and functions you have defined. 1. Open Scientific Calculator in the Feature Kit. 2. Select Graph the wave icon in the title bar. The button turns gold and a graph area opens under the expression bar. 3. The y = box already holds sin x , and its curve is drawn. The graph shows a grid with numbered axes, the curve in gold, and a label in its top left corner such as y = sin x . 1. Select the y = box. 2. Replace the text with your expression, for example x^3 3 x . 3. The graph redraws as you type. Rules: Use x as the variable. Inside the graph, x always means the horizontal position, even if you have a variable called x . Write every multiplication: 3 x , not 3x . You can use your own functions and variables: after f x = x^2 2 in the expression bar, type f x in the y = box. Trigonometric functions follow the RAD or DEG setting. Where the expression is undefined or infinite for example 1/x at x = 0 , or sqrt x for negative x , the curve simply has a gap. Very steep jumps, such as those of tan x , are drawn as separ"},{"t":"Keep notes","d":"Keep Markdown notes in the Feature Kit that save as you type, preview them, copy them and export them as .md files.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/notes.html","h":["Open Notes","The screen","Write a note","Add a note","Switch between notes","Preview the formatting","Copy a note","Export a note","Delete a note","Where notes are kept","Related"],"x":" Notes is a scratchpad inside the Feature Kit. You can keep several notes, write them in Markdown, preview the formatting, and copy or export any note. Notes save automatically in your browser, so they are there the next time you open the kit on any page. Select the Notes card on the Feature Kit menu, or press 4 on the menu. The first time, you see one note called Scratchpad containing a short example. Note tabs along the top, one per note, named after the note's first line. A + button at the end adds a note. A toolbar with Edit and Preview on the left and Copy , Export and Delete on the right. The editor, or the preview when Preview is selected. A status line at the bottom: Saving… while you type, then Saved · and the time. 1. Select the editor. 2. Type. The placeholder reminds you of the syntax: Title , bold , italic , code , lists , tasks . 3. Stop typing for a moment. The status changes from Saving… to Saved · and the time. The note's tab takes its name from the first non empty line, without any leading , cut to 24 characters. An empty note is called Untitled . Select + New note . An empty note opens at the front of the tabs, in edit mode, with the cursor in the editor. Select "},{"t":"Convert units","d":"Convert values between 1,344 units in 70 categories with the Feature Kit's Unit Converter.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/unit-converter.html","h":["Open the converter","Convert a value","Swap the units","Copy the result","Find a unit","The categories","How results are shown","Things to know","If the units do not load","Related"],"x":" The Unit Converter converts a value from one unit to another within a category, such as metres to feet or Celsius to Fahrenheit. It has 70 categories and 1,344 units, including every metric prefix from yocto to yotta for the units that take them. Select the Unit Converter card on the Feature Kit menu, or press 2 on the menu. The first time you open it on a page, the kit downloads the unit list. A loading message reads Loading units — Preparing the converter. It takes a moment on a slow connection. 1. Select a category pill, for example Temperature . The converter starts on Length . 2. Type a number in the From box placeholder Enter value . 3. Choose the unit you have in the From unit list, for example celsius °C . 4. Choose the unit you want in the To unit list, for example fahrenheit °F . The result appears in the To row as you type, for example 98.6 , with a sentence under it: 37 celsius = 98.6 fahrenheit . When you pick a category, the converter preselects its first two units. Select the swap button two opposing arrows between From and To . The two units change places and the result updates. Select the result value. A Copied! message confirms it is on your clipboard. 1. Type pa"},{"t":"Feature Kit reference","d":"Every control, tab, field, option and message in the Feature Kit, with what it does and its default.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Launcher","Title bar","Menu","Calculator","Unit Converter","Feedback","Notes","Date & Time","Developer Tools","Messages"],"x":" Every control in the Feature Kit, grouped by where it appears. Defaults are given where the kit sets one. Control What it does Default Feature launcher nine dot icon Opens the kit on its menu; closes it when open without Focus mode Closed Ctrl + Shift + K Same as the launcher, from anywhere on the page — Launcher tooltip \"Calculator, converter, graph tools, and feedback.\" — Control What it does Values or range Default Back Returns to the menu from a tool Shown only inside a tool — Title Shows Feature Kit or the open tool's name; drag it to move the kit — Bottom left corner Graph Shows or hides the graph area Calculator only; gold when on Off History Shows or hides past calculations Calculator only; gold when on Off Focus mode Keeps the kit open across pages and other kits, and stops dimming the page On or off; remembered Off Theme Switches the kit between light and dark Light or dark; remembered Follows the site Resize Normal 560 px wide or full size up to 640 px wide, 900 px tall Remembered Normal Minimize Shrinks the kit to a small round icon; select the icon to reopen at the menu — — Close Closes the kit, hides the graph and history, and turns Focus mode off — — Card Key Opens "},{"t":"Feature Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for Feature Kit problems, and what every calculator error message means.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The page goes dark and I cannot click it","The Feature launcher does not close the kit","Typing numbers does nothing on the calculator","The Scientific or Programmer tab is missing","My variables and functions disappeared","The result of 2+3×2 is 8, not 10","% does not give a percentage","A derivative shows 12.0000000001 instead of 12","Calculator error messages","The graph is empty","The Unit Converter says \"Units could not be loaded\"","A conversion shows a strange number","I cannot find a unit in the search results","A note disappeared","Copy does not work","A tool card shows \"failed to load\"","The feedback form keeps saying \"Could not send yet\""],"x":" For problems shared by every kit, such as a missing launcher or a panel in the wrong place, see Troubleshooting kits ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: With Focus mode off, the Feature Kit dims the page and keeps keyboard focus inside the kit. What to do: Click the dimmed page to close the kit, or select Focus mode in the kit's title bar to keep it open without dimming. Why: With Focus mode on, the launcher and Ctrl + Shift + K move focus into the kit instead of closing it. What to do: Select Close in the title bar, or press Esc twice once to leave a tool, once to close . Why: Keyboard typing reaches the keypad only while the Scientific Calculator is open and the cursor is not in a text box. If the cursor is in the expression bar, the y = box or a page field, your keys go there instead. What to do: Click an empty part of the calculator, or the display, then type. Or type into the expression bar and press Enter . Why: The site's tool visibility mode is Basic , which shows only the Basic keypad. In Advanced mode, the Basic keypad is hidden instead. What to do: Open the Advanced Kit ../../advanced kit/README.md and choose Everything to see all three tabs. Why: Variables, your own f"},{"t":"Feature Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Feature Kit's calculator, converter, notes, date tools, developer tools and feedback.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["Does the Feature Kit work offline?","Is my calculator history saved?","Can I plot more than one function at once?","Does the calculator handle complex numbers?","Is % a percentage?","Can I solve an equation such as x² = 5?","Does the calculator give exact answers?","Why can I not see the Scientific keypad?","Are my notes private?","Can I move notes to another computer?","Is it safe to paste a token or secret into Developer Tools?","Does the JWT tool check signatures?","Why does the Business days figure differ from my calendar?","Who reads my feedback?","How do I stop feedback prompts?"],"x":" Mostly. Once the kit and its tools have loaded on a page, the calculator, graph, notes, date tools and developer tools work without a connection. The Unit Converter needs a connection the first time you open it on a page, to download its unit list. Feedback waits on your device until you are back online. Yes. Your last 100 calculations are kept in your browser and appear in History on any page. Variables, functions you define and the memory value are not saved. No. The graph shows one expression at a time. Define functions in the expression bar and switch between them in the y = box. No. Results are real numbers. Expressions with no real answer, such as sqrt 1 , show NaN . No. It is the remainder after division: 10 % 3 is 1 . Yes. Move everything to one side and use solve : solve x^2 5, 2 returns 2.2360679775 . It gives decimal answers rounded to 14 significant digits, shown to 12. In the expression bar it also shows an exact fraction when one with a denominator up to 10,000 matches, such as 0.875 = 7/8 . Calculus results are numerical estimates. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . The site is in Basic mode. Choose Everything in the Advanced Kit ../../advanc"},{"t":"Feature Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Feature Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the supporting pages for the Feature Kit: definitions of the terms the guides use, every keyboard shortcut, the numeric limits and approximations of each tool, related pages, the kit's public history and what it keeps or sends. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Feature Kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every key the Feature Kit responds to limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Precision, ranges and approximations related.md related.md Related tools, kits and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the Feature Kit privacy.md privacy.md What stays in your browser and what is sent "},{"t":"Feature Kit shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut the Feature Kit responds to, from opening the kit to typing on the calculator keypad.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Open, close and move around","Calculator keypad","Calculator text boxes","Unit Converter","Developer Tools"],"x":" The kit's menu shows ⌘ instead of Ctrl on a Mac. Where a shortcut below uses Ctrl , use Cmd on a Mac. Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + Shift + K Anywhere Opens or closes the kit. With Focus mode on, moves focus into the open kit instead of closing it Esc Kit open In a tool, returns to the menu. On the menu, closes the kit 1 to 6 Menu Opens Scientific Calculator, Unit Converter, Feedback, Notes, Date & Time, Developer Tools Ctrl + 1 to Ctrl + 6 Focus inside the kit Switches straight to that tool, even from inside another tool or a text box Arrow keys, Home , End Menu Move between the six cards Enter or Space A focused card Opens that tool Left arrow , Right arrow , Home , End A focused title bar button Move between the title bar buttons Tab , Shift + Tab Kit open, Focus mode off Move between the kit's controls; focus stays inside the kit Enter or Space Minimised kit icon Reopens the kit Browsers commonly use Ctrl + a number to switch browser tabs and may act on it before the Feature Kit does. If that happens, use the plain number keys on the menu instead. These work while the Scientific Calculator is open and the cursor is not in a text box. Key Action 0 to 9 Digit + Add Subtract"},{"t":"Feature Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Feature Kit guides, from ans and derivative to UUID and cron.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" ans — The result of your last calculation. Type ans or select Ans to reuse it. Expression — A calculation written as text, such as 2 3+4 . Expression bar — The calculator's text box for full expressions, variables, functions and calculus. Variable — A name that holds a value, set with name = value , such as r = 4 . User defined function — A function you create with name x = expression , such as f x = x^2 + 1 . Constant — A fixed named value, such as pi , e or the speed of light c . Radians RAD and degrees DEG — Two units for angles. A full turn is 2π radians or 360 degrees. Remainder modulo — What is left after whole division. 10 % 3 is 1 . Factorial — The product of all whole numbers from 1 to n, written n! . 5! is 120 . Gamma function — An extension of the factorial to non whole numbers. gamma n equals n 1 ! for whole numbers. Derivative — The rate of change, or slope, of an expression at a point. diff estimates it. Second derivative — The rate of change of the slope. diff2 estimates it. Integral — The signed area under a curve between two points. integral estimates it. Root — A value where an expression equals zero. solve finds one. Numerical method — A way of computing an answ"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"How precise the Feature Kit's calculator, graph, converter and date tools are, the ranges they handle, and where they approximate.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Calculator precision","Exact fractions","Calculus","Other calculator ranges","Graph","Unit Converter","Date & Time","Developer Tools"],"x":" The Feature Kit is a quick use toolbox. Its results are good for everyday design, development and study work. They are not certified for engineering, medical, legal or financial use. The calculator uses the browser's standard double precision numbers, which hold about 15 to 17 significant digits. Every result is rounded to 14 significant digits to hide floating point artefacts, so 0.1+0.2 shows 0.3 . Results are displayed with up to 12 significant digits. Whole numbers under 10^15 are shown in full. Results smaller than 10^ 10 or larger than 10^15 are shown in scientific notation. Numbers beyond about 1.8 × 10^308 become ∞ . There are no complex numbers; operations with no real answer give NaN . The fraction hint in the expression bar such as 0.875 = 7/8 is found by searching for a fraction with a denominator up to 10,000 that matches the result to within about one part in 10^11. A shown fraction is exact for that decimal; no fraction is shown when none fits. The hint does not appear for keypad results. All calculus functions are numerical estimates, not symbolic algebra. Function Method What to expect diff Five point difference with a step scaled to the point Very close, but the "},{"t":"Feature Kit privacy","d":"What the Feature Kit keeps in your browser, what it sends, and how to remove it.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Kept in your browser","Not kept","Sent over the network","Feedback delivery","Related"],"x":" The Feature Kit runs in your browser. Apart from feedback you choose to send and the unit list it downloads, nothing leaves your device. What Details How to remove it Calculator history Your last 100 calculations: the expression, the result and the time History bin icon in the heading Notes Every note's text, title and last saved time Delete on each note Recent dates The last 8 dates you picked in the Calendar tab Clear the site's data in your browser Kit preferences Position, expanded size, Focus mode, the tool that was open while Focus mode was on, and the kit theme Clear the site's data Feedback Each submission, kept so it can be retried until delivered, along with when you were last prompted and how often you dismissed prompts Clear the site's data Calculator variables, functions you define and the memory value cleared when you leave or reload the page . The angle setting RAD or DEG and the graph's y = expression. Anything you type into the Unit Converter or the Developer Tools. Text in the feedback form until you send it. When What is sent or fetched You open the Unit Converter for the first time on a page The kit downloads the unit list from auricartisan.com. Nothing about y"},{"t":"Feature Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about the Feature Kit, and what the kit contains as of September 2026.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Feature Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. It records site releases as a whole and does not list the Feature Kit by name. This page lists the entries that concern the kits, and describes the Feature Kit as it is today. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.75 19 April 2026 A broad stability pass that included fixes to converter flows and to the kit interfaces v0.9.9 5 June 2026 Interface and consistency improvements across the site, including shortcut updates Six tools behind one menu: Scientific Calculator, Unit Converter, Feedback, Notes, Date & Time and Developer Tools. A calculator with Basic, Scientific and Programmer keypads, an expression bar with variables, user defined functions, statistics, number theory, physical constants and numerical calculus diff , diff2 , integral , solve , sum , product , exact fraction hints, a function reference panel, a graph and a 100 entry history. A Unit Converter with 70 categories and 1,344 units. Notes with several Markdown notes, preview, copy and .md export. Date & Time with Calendar, Difference, Add / Subtract and Timezones tabs. Develo"},{"t":"Related to the Feature Kit","d":"Kits, tools and pages related to the Feature Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Feature Kit","u":"website/kits/feature-kit/others/related.html","h":["Other kits","Tools with related features","Site features","Help"],"x":" Advanced Kit ../../advanced kit/README.md — its mode decides which calculator keypads you see. Library Kit ../../library kit/README.md — for palettes, gradients and reports you save from the site's tools. Feature Kit notes and calculations are not saved there. Menu Kit ../../menu kit/README.md — jump to any tool on the site. All kits ../../README.md and Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . Basic Colour Tools ../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — colour format conversion, which the Unit Converter does not cover. Colour Science Lab ../../../tools/colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md — colour maths such as colour space conversion and colour difference. Design Engine ../../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md — spacing, type and colour tokens, if you are converting units for a design system. The site wide search Ctrl + K , settings Ctrl + , and the site wide feedback prompt: Site features ../../../site features/README.md . Help ../../../../help/README.md — contact and support. "},{"t":"Library Kit","d":"The Universal Library as a floating panel: browse, search, restore, organise, compare, share, export and sync everything you save from the site's tools.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Library Kit is where everything you save from Auric Artisan's tools lives. When you select Save to Library in a tool, the palette, gradient, type scale, preset, plate, report or image lands in your library, and the Library Kit shows it as a tile you can find, reopen and reuse from any page. The kit is a floating panel, so you can open it without leaving what you are doing. Select a tile to restore that item into the tool that made it, or open it in another tool that can use it. Organise items with favourites, collections and the archive; compare two versions side by side with colour difference figures; share an item as a link; export it, or the whole library, as files; and generate reports in seven formats. Your library is stored in your browser on this device. It is not uploaded to your account. You can export it as a single file, import it elsewhere, and optionally push it to web addresses you control. Anyone who saves work from the site's tools and wants to find it again. Designers who iterate on palettes and gradients and want to compare versions. Teams that want to share a palette or gradient as a link, or back up and move a library between browsers. Developers who want t"},{"t":"Library Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Library Kit guides, from browsing and organising to comparing, sharing, syncing and reports.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides cover everything you can do with your saved work in the Library Kit. Start with Getting started, then pick the task you need. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Save your first item, open the kit and learn its screen browse and find.md browse and find.md Tabs, search, sort, grouping, grid and list views, filters organise your library.md organise your library.md Favourites, renaming, collections, projects, archive, delete and multi select restore and reuse.md restore and reuse.md Restore items into tools, open them in other tools, the details dialog and downloads compare items.md compare items.md Compare palettes, images, settings and audits share export and import.md share export and import.md Share links, per item files, library backups and imports settings sync and reports.md settings sync and reports.md Preferences, reporting, sync destinations, reports and storage commands and right click menus.md commands and right click menus.md The command palette and the right click menus reference.md reference.md Every control and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems and how to fix them faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions S"},{"t":"Getting started with the Library Kit","d":"Save your first item from a tool, open the Library Kit, and learn the parts of its screen.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Save something first","Open the kit","The screen, top to bottom","A tile","Your first actions","Panel options","Close the kit","Next steps"],"x":" Items reach your library from the tools: 1. Open a tool, make something a palette, a gradient, a plate, a report and select Save to Library . 2. In the dialog, type a name the box says Name your save , and optionally a description, a collection or ＋ New collection… and tags separated by commas. 3. Select Save to Library , or press Ctrl + Enter Cmd + Enter on a Mac . The item is saved in your browser and appears in the Library Kit straight away, even if the kit is already open. Use any of: Page utilities Library ; the Library button in the site header \"Open your saved palettes, gradients, presets and exports.\" ; Ctrl + Shift + L ; a page address ending in library ; https://auricartisan.com/library/workspace/. That page shows Opening your library… and opens the panel. If it cannot, it shows an Open library panel button and the hint \"Or press Ctrl Shift L anywhere on the site.\" The kit opens with the cursor in the search box. When you close it, keyboard focus returns to where it was before. 1. Title bar. A six dot grip drag it, or use the arrow keys, to move the panel , the title Your Library , an item count such as 12 items , the Panel options button and Close . 2. Tabs. All , Recen"},{"t":"Browse and find items","d":"Find saved items in the Library Kit with tabs, search, sorting, grouping, grid or list view, density and filters.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/browse-and-find.html","h":["Tabs","Search","Sort","Group","Grid or list","Density","Filter by collection, tool or tag","Move with the keyboard","The item count","Related"],"x":" Tab Shows Count All Every item that is not archived Yes Recent Items changed in the last 7 days Yes Favorites Items you starred Yes Projects Items of the Project type Yes Collections Your collections, as folders Number of collections Archive Items you archived Yes Compare The comparison workspace; see Compare items compare items.md No Settings Library settings; see Settings, sync and reports settings sync and reports.md No One tab per type Items of that type, such as Palette , Gradient , Plate , Analysis Yes Type tabs appear only for types you have saved. Possible types include Color, Palette, Shade, Gradient, Typography, Component, Template, Preset, Effect, Image, LUT, Plate, ASCII, Simulation, Spectral, Export and Analysis; tools can add their own, such as design systems. The kit remembers the last tab you used. Type in Search your library… . After a short pause the view shows only items whose name, description, tool name, type or tags contain your text. Search works within the current tab. Select the cross in the box, or press Esc , to clear the search. A second Esc closes the kit. Press Down arrow in the box to jump to the first tile. Start with to search commands instead of i"},{"t":"Commands and right-click menus","d":"Run any Library Kit action from the > command palette or from the right-click menus for items and for the panel.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/commands-and-right-click-menus.html","h":["The command palette","Right-click an item","Right-click the panel","How the menus behave","Keyboard shortcuts sheet","Related"],"x":" Two shortcuts put every Library Kit action within reach: a command palette in the search box, and right click menus. 1. Select the search box. 2. Type . The tiles are replaced by a list of commands, each with a short hint. 3. Type more to narrow the list, for example export . Commands match on their name or hint. 4. Press Up arrow or Down arrow to move the highlight, and Enter to run the command, or select it with the pointer. The search box clears when a command runs. If nothing matches you see No matching command — \"Type part of a command name, or clear the to search items instead.\" Command Hint shown New project Bundle several saved items into one project New collection Group saved items into a folder Import library file Merge a previously exported .json Export library snapshot Download everything as a single .json Sync now Push to every configured destination Library settings Storage, sync, defaults and data controls Compare items Open two saved items side by side Switch to list view or Switch to grid view Change how items are laid out Group by type or Stop grouping by type Collapsible sections per asset type Compact density or Comfortable density Fit more items on screen Mult"},{"t":"Compare two items","d":"Compare two saved items in the Library Kit: palettes by colour difference and contrast, images side by side or as a heatmap, settings field by field, and audits by score.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/compare-items.html","h":["Open a comparison","Choose the two items","Palettes","Images and plates","Presets and configurations","URL Analyzer audits","Different kinds of item","Related"],"x":" The Compare tab puts two saved items side by side and shows exactly what changed between them. What you see depends on the kind of items you compare. Any of these opens the Compare tab: Select the Compare tab. Right click a tile and choose Compare with… . That item becomes Before . In multi select, select two items, then type and choose Compare items . The first becomes Before and the second After . Right click empty space in the panel and choose Compare items… . The workspace is headed Comparison workspace — Compare saved assets , with the line \"Choose a before and after asset to inspect exactly what changed.\" 1. In Before , choose an item from the list — Choose an asset — means none . Each entry shows a short type label in brackets and the name, newest first. Archived items are included. 2. In After , choose the second item. 3. Select Swap sides to exchange them. Under the pickers, each side shows its type, tool, name, description and Updated date. Until both are chosen, the comparison area reads Pick assets on both sides to see the diff. When both items are palettes, or both carry colours, you see: Summary figures Figure Meaning Swatches Number of colours before → after, and th"},{"t":"Organise your library","d":"Favourite, rename, describe, tag, duplicate, collect, archive and delete saved items, one at a time or in bulk.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/organise-your-library.html","h":["Favourite an item","Rename an item","Add a description and tags","Duplicate an item","Collections","Projects","Archive an item","Delete an item","Work with several items at once","Related"],"x":" Hover over the tile and select the star Favourite , or right click the tile and choose Favourite . A star appears on the tile and the item joins the Favorites tab. Do the same again Remove favourite to unstar it. 1. Right click the tile and choose Rename… . 2. In Rename item , change the Name and select Rename . A message confirms Renamed . You can also rename an item in its details; see Restore and reuse restore and reuse.md . 1. Hover over the tile and select the pencil Open details . 2. Type a Description , and Tags comma separated , for example brand, spring, web . 3. Select Save changes . Search matches descriptions and tags, and the command palette offers filters for your most used tags. Right click the tile and choose Duplicate in list view, the copy icon on the row does the same . The copy is named after the original with \" copy\" added, and starts neither favourited nor archived. A collection is a folder of saved items. Each item can be in one collection at a time. Grouping by project uses collections as its headings. On the Collections tab, select the New collection tile \"Group saved items\" , or type and choose New collection , or right click empty space in the panel and "},{"t":"Restore and reuse items","d":"Reopen saved items in the tool that made them, open them in other tools, edit their details and download them in many formats.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/restore-and-reuse.html","h":["Restore an item into its tool","Open an item in a different tool","Open an item's details","Copy colours and names","Related"],"x":" Select a tile or focus it and press Enter , or right click it and choose Restore into its tool . If you are already on that tool's page, the item loads into the tool straight away and the Library Kit closes. If you are on another page, the site opens the tool's page and loads the item there. If the item cannot be restored into a tool, its details open instead. Many items can be used by more than one tool. For example, a palette saved in one tool can be opened in another tool that accepts palettes. Right click the tile. Under Open , up to three entries read Open in followed by a tool's name. Or open the item's details: a Use in row lists every tool that accepts the item. Selecting one opens that tool, on this page or another, with the item loaded. Hover over the tile and select the pencil Open details , or right click and choose Open details . A details dialog opens over the page. The item's type above its name. A large preview: the image, the SVG, colour swatches with their values, the gradient or the colour. If there is nothing to preview you see No image stored with a hint. Editable fields: Name , Description , Collection with Unfiled for none and Tags comma separated . The tool"},{"t":"Settings, sync and reports","d":"Every option on the Library Kit's Settings tab: preferences, reporting, sync destinations, report generation and storage.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/settings-sync-and-reports.html","h":["Preferences","Reporting","Sync & auto-update","Generate reports","Storage","Related"],"x":" Open the Settings tab or select Settings in the footer, or type and choose Library settings . It has five sections, chosen from a row of tabs: Preferences , Reporting , Sync & auto update , Generate reports and Storage . Changes save as soon as you make them. Setting What it does Values Default Autosave drafts as you work Lets tools keep drafts of unsaved work in the library On or off On Show archived items in default views Includes archived items in library views outside the Archive tab. In the Library Kit itself, archived items stay on the Archive tab On or off Off Auto update: keep all integrations in sync as items change Allows sync destinations to be updated when items change On or off On Autosave interval How often drafts are saved 4, 8, 15 or 30 seconds 8 seconds Keep drafts for How long unsaved drafts are kept before they expire 3, 7, 14, 30 or 90 days 14 days \"Controls how much each tool reports back into the library when it saves an asset.\" Setting What it does Default Capture full output payload from every tool Saves the tool's complete output with each item On Capture the tool's settings/state alongside the asset Saves the tool's settings, so restoring brings them back"},{"t":"Share, export and import","d":"Share a saved item as a link, download items as files, back up the whole library and import it again.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/share-export-and-import.html","h":["Share an item as a link","Download one item","Download several items","Back up the whole library","Import a library file","Reports","Move a library to another browser or device","Related"],"x":" 1. Hover over the tile and select Share , or right click it and choose Share a link… . 2. The Share link dialog opens with the item's name as its title and the note \"Anyone with this link can open a copy. State is encoded in the URL — no account needed.\" 3. Select Copy it briefly reads Copied! , or Share via… to use your device's share sheet where available, or Open in new tab to try the link yourself. 4. Select Close when you are done. The item itself is packed into the link, so the recipient does not need an account and nothing is uploaded. The link opens the tool that can show the item. Under the address, the dialog shows the link's length in characters and the size limit, with the note \"safe to paste into chat, docs, or email.\" Links are limited to 6 KB of packed data. Palettes, gradients and small presets fit easily; large items such as audits and images often do not. When an item is too large, the dialog is titled Too large to share and reads \"Encoded payload is\" followed by its size and \"over the 6 KB share limit\", with a bar showing how far over it is. Export the item as a file instead. In list view, select the download icon on the row Export JSON , or right click the tile"},{"t":"Library Kit reference","d":"Every control, tab, option, dialog and message in the Library Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Ways to open the kit","Title bar","Tabs","Search and toolbar","Tiles","Collections tab","Bulk bar (multi-select)","Footer","Dialogs","Compare tab","Settings tab","Messages"],"x":" Entry point What it does Library launcher Opens or closes the kit. Shows a badge with the item count up to 99+ once the kit has loaded Library button in the site header Opens the kit Ctrl + Shift + L Cmd + Shift + L on a Mac Opens or closes the kit library at the end of a page address Opens the kit on that page library=all , recent , favorites or favourites , projects , collections , archive , compare , settings Opens the kit on that tab https://auricartisan.com/library/workspace/ Opens the kit; links to this page elsewhere on the site open the kit in place Control What it does Default Six dot grip Drag, or focus it and use arrow keys 12 px; Shift for 1 px , to move the panel \"Move library panel\" Bottom left corner Your Library Title; the title bar is also a drag handle — Item count N items not counting archived items . Hidden on narrow phone screens — Panel options Opens Keep open , Theme , Panel size , Minimize , Reset position — Close Closes the kit \"Close Library Kit.\" — Panel size: normal 680 px wide, expanded up to 940 px wide. All , Recent last 7 days , Favorites , Projects , Collections , Archive , Compare , Settings , and one tab per saved item type. Counts show on all bu"},{"t":"Library Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for Library Kit problems, from missing items and full storage to share links that are too large and sync failures.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["My saved items are missing","An item is not on the All tab","Saving is refused because of my plan","\"This browser has run out of room for saved projects\"","\"Library storage is full. Some image data couldn't be saved.\"","Selecting a tile opens the details instead of the tool","\"Too large to share\"","Only one file downloaded when I exported several items","\"That file could not be imported.\"","Sync reports \"Push failed\"","\"Sync is switched off\"","Show archived items does nothing in the kit","A comparison shows \"Couldn't load the image\"","Ctrl + Shift + L does nothing"],"x":" For problems shared by every kit, see Troubleshooting kits ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: The library lives in your browser on this device. It is not in your account, so items saved in another browser, on another device, or in a private window are not here. Clearing this site's data in your browser also deletes the library. What to do: Open the library in the browser where you saved the items. To move items, export them there Export in the footer and import the file here. There is no way to recover a library that was cleared without an export. Why: It is archived, a filter is active, or you are searching. What to do: Check the Archive tab, select Clear all under the toolbar, and clear the search box. Why: Each plan allows a number of active saved items archived items do not count : 20 on Apprentice, 500 on Artisan, 2,500 on Specialist and 10,000 on Industrial Pro. The message reads \"Your plan keeps N saved projects, and you have M. Archive or delete one to make room, or upgrade for more.\" What to do: Archive or delete items you no longer need, or change plan. See Account and billing ../../../account and billing/README.md . Why: Browsers limit how much each site can store, wh"},{"t":"Library Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Library Kit and your saved work.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["Is my library saved to my account?","How many items can I keep?","Are the tools still free if I reach the limit?","What happened to the Library Workspace page?","Can other people see my library?","What does a share link contain?","What is the difference between archive and delete?","What is the difference between a collection and a project?","Can I undo a delete?","Does the library work offline?","Which tools can save to the library?"],"x":" No. It is stored in your browser on this device. Export it Export in the footer to keep a backup or move it to another browser. Your plan sets the number of active saved items: 20 on Apprentice, 500 on Artisan, 2,500 on Specialist and 10,000 on Industrial Pro. Archived items do not count. Your browser's storage limit applies on top of that, especially for images. Yes. The limit only affects saving new items. See Account and billing ../../../account and billing/README.md . The library now opens as a floating panel on any page. https://auricartisan.com/library/workspace/ still works and opens the panel. No. Only items you share as links, export as files or push to your own sync destinations leave your browser. The item's data, packed into the address. Anyone with the link can open a copy. Nothing is stored on a server. Archiving hides an item and keeps it on the Archive tab, where you can restore it. Deleting removes it for good. A collection is a folder that groups items; each item can be in one. A project is a type of saved item; the Library Kit can create empty ones, and some tools save their own. Use collections to group your items. No. Deletes, Empty the archive and Reset libra"},{"t":"Library Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Library Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Library Kit: its terms, its keys, the storage, sharing and comparison limits, related pages, its history and where your library is kept. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Library Kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every key the Library Kit responds to limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Storage, plan, sharing, sync and comparison limits related.md related.md Related tools, kits and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the library and the Library Kit privacy.md privacy.md Where your library is kept and what can leave your device "},{"t":"Library Kit shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut the Library Kit responds to.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Open and close","Search box","Tiles","Moving the panel","Menus and dialogs"],"x":" The kit's own shortcut sheet Keys in the footer shows ⌘ for Mac. Where a shortcut below uses Ctrl , use Cmd on a Mac. Shortcut What it does Ctrl + Shift + L Opens or closes the Library Kit, from anywhere on the site Esc Closes, in this order: an open menu or dialog, the Panel options menu, multi select, the search text, then the panel Shortcut What it does at the start Switches to the command palette Up arrow , Down arrow Move through commands command palette Enter Runs the highlighted command command palette Down arrow Moves to the first tile normal search Esc Clears the search Shortcut What it does Left arrow , Right arrow Previous or next tile Up arrow , Down arrow Tile above or below; up from the first row returns to the search box Home , End First or last tile Enter or Space Restores the item selects it in multi select Delete Asks to delete the item Ctrl + A Selects all items, while multi select is on Shortcut Where What it does Arrow keys The six dot grip has focus Move the panel 12 pixels Shift + arrow keys The six dot grip has focus Move the panel 1 pixel Shortcut Where What it does Up arrow , Down arrow , Home , End Panel options menu Move between options Enter Name dialo"},{"t":"Library Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Library Kit guides.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Universal Library — Everything you have saved from the site's tools, kept in your browser. Item asset — One saved thing, such as a palette, gradient, image, preset or audit. The kit's dialogs sometimes say \"asset\". Type — What kind of item it is, such as Palette, Gradient, Plate or Analysis. Each type you have saved gets a tab. Restore — Reopen an item in the tool that made it, with its data and settings. Open in — Load an item into a different tool that accepts its type. Collection — A folder of items. An item belongs to at most one collection. Unfiled — Not in any collection. Project — A type of saved item. The kit can create empty projects; some tools save their own. Favourite — An item marked with a star; listed on the Favorites tab. Archive — A holding area for items you want out of the way without deleting them. Draft — Unsaved work a tool keeps in the library while autosave is on. Drafts expire after the Keep drafts for period. Snapshot backup — A single JSON file containing your whole library, made with Export . Share link — A web address that carries a copy of an item inside it, so anyone with the link can open it. Sync destination — A web address you configure to receive"},{"t":"Library Kit limits","d":"Storage, plan, sharing, sync, report and comparison limits of the Library Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Storage","Plan allowance","Share links","Sync","Reports","Comparisons","Details and downloads"],"x":" The library is kept in your browser's storage for auricartisan.com. Browsers typically allow a site only a few megabytes of this kind of storage, whatever your plan, and images use it fastest. Images saved from some tools are reduced before storing, so what you download from the library can be smaller than what the tool produced. Export from the tool itself for full size output. The storage figure in the footer and in Settings Storage is an estimate of the library's own use. Plan Active saved items Apprentice 20 Artisan 500 Specialist 2,500 Industrial Pro 10,000 Archived items do not count. Editing an existing item is always allowed, even at the limit. The figures are from https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/, which is authoritative if they differ. Limited to 6 KB of packed data per link. The link contains a copy of the item at the moment you shared it; later changes are not reflected. Runs only in an open page of the site; nothing is sent while the site is closed. Automatic pushes run no more often than every 15 seconds, whatever interval you choose. The receiving server must accept cross origin requests from auricartisan.com. The console and local transports are for testing"},{"t":"Library Kit privacy","d":"Where the Library Kit keeps your saved work, and the only ways it can leave your device.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Where your library is kept","The only ways your items leave the device","Sensitive settings","Removing your data","Related"],"x":" Every saved item, collection, draft and library setting is stored in your browser's storage for auricartisan.com, on this device. It is not uploaded to Auric Artisan and not linked to your account. Anyone who uses the same browser profile can see it. The Library Kit's own view preferences tab, grouping, density, collapsed groups, panel position, size, theme and Keep open are stored the same way. Action What leaves, and where it goes Share a link… A copy of the item, packed into the link. It goes wherever you send the link. Anyone with the link can open the copy Export , Export JSON , downloads, reports Files saved to your device by your browser Sync Your library with or without full data, drafts and previews, as you choose sent from your browser to the URLs you configure, with your bearer token if you set one Nothing is sent to Auric Artisan's servers by the Library Kit. Sync destinations, including any Auth bearer token , are stored in your browser as part of the library settings. They are included in a full library backup auric library backup.json and in full reports. Treat those files as private if you use tokens, or remove destinations before exporting. Delete items individual"},{"t":"Library Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about the library, and what the Library Kit contains as of September 2026.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Library Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. It does not list the Library Kit by name. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.9 5 June 2026 Improved consistency across \"reusable library surfaces\" and fixed library behaviour bugs, alongside new public library areas The library opens as a floating kit panel on every page, from the Library launcher, the header Library button, Ctrl + Shift + L , library links, or https://auricartisan.com/library/workspace/, which now opens the panel rather than a separate workspace page. Tabs for All, Recent, Favorites, Projects, Collections, Archive, Compare, Settings and each saved type. Search, a command palette, sorting, grouping by project or type, grid and list views, density and filters. Right click menus for items and for the panel, multi select with bulk actions, and drag and drop import. Compare and Settings work inside the panel rather than in separate windows. Share links, per item downloads in nine formats, library backups, reports in seven formats and optional sync to your own endpoints. Shared kit controls in a Panel options menu, with Rese"},{"t":"Related to the Library Kit","d":"Tools, kits and pages related to the Library Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Library Kit","u":"website/kits/library-kit/others/related.html","h":["Tools that save to the library","Other kits","Pages"],"x":" Any tool with a Save to Library button, for example: Basic Colour Tools ../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Personalisation Generator ../../../tools/colour workspace/personalisation generator/README.md Design Engine ../../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Ishihara Plate Generator ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/ishihara plate generator/README.md M Gradient Palette ../../../tools/image and file tools/m gradient palette/README.md Image Picker ../../../tools/image and file tools/image picker/README.md Status Kit ../../status kit/README.md — shows how much browser storage the site uses. Menu Kit ../../menu kit/README.md — its Workspace tile opens the Library Kit. All kits ../../README.md and Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . The site's colour, palette, gradient, harmony, shade and accessibility libraries, which are public reference collections rather than your saved work: Colour libraries ../../../library/colour libraries/README.md . Portfolio ../../../portfolio/README.md — build a public page from your saved work. Plans and the saved item allowance: htt"},{"t":"Menu Kit","d":"A floating start menu for auricartisan.com with tabbed page groups, recommended and most-used tools, fuzzy search and quick actions.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Menu Kit is a start menu for the whole of auricartisan.com. It opens over any page and lists the site's tools and pages as illustrated tiles, grouped into seven tabs: Tools , Design , Analyze , Account , Library , Company and Trust . Selecting a tile takes you to that page. Type in its search box and the tiles give way to a ranked list of matching pages and quick actions, such as Copy current URL or Open a random tool . The search forgives typos in the middle of words: typing clrlib finds Color Library . Pages you open often rise in the results and fill the Most Used section. The Menu Kit follows the site's tool visibility mode, set in the Advanced Kit ../advanced kit/README.md : in Basic mode it shows beginner friendly tools, in Advanced mode the scientific ones, and in Everything mode the lot. New visitors who want an overview of everything the site offers. Regular users who want to jump to a tool in a couple of keystrokes from any page. Anyone looking for account, library, company or legal pages. On any page of https://auricartisan.com, select Page utilities in the bottom left corner, then Menu . Or press Ctrl + M . 1. Press Ctrl + M . The Menu Kit opens with the cursor in "},{"t":"Menu Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Menu Kit guides: getting started, browsing, searching, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain how to open the Menu Kit, browse its tabs, search the site and run quick actions, followed by a full reference. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the Menu Kit and learn its screen find a page.md find a page.md Browse tabs, sections, Recommended and Most Used search and quick actions.md search and quick actions.md Search pages and run quick actions from the keyboard reference.md reference.md Every tab, section, control and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems and how to fix them faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions Shared controls such as moving, Focus mode and theme are explained in Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with the Menu Kit","d":"Open the Menu Kit, learn the parts of its screen, and open your first page from it.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the kit","The screen, top to bottom","Tiles","Open your first page","The status chip","Close the kit","Next steps"],"x":" Use either: Page utilities bottom left corner Menu , or Ctrl + M from anywhere on the page. The launcher's tooltip reads \"Open site navigation, grouped pages, and quick search.\" The first time you open the kit on a page it shows Loading menu with the line \"Reframing tools by intent.\" while it fetches the list of pages. 1. Title bar. Menu Kit , a status chip showing the site's release status for example Beta , and the buttons Focus mode , Theme , Resize , Minimize and Close . 2. Search bar. A magnifier, the box Search Auric Artisan… , and an ESC hint to its right. Once you type, a clear button a cross replaces the hint. 3. Tabs. Tools , Design , Analyze , Account , Library , Company , Trust . The row scrolls sideways if it does not fit. 4. Body. Section headings and tiles for the selected tab. 5. Footer. Key hints Ctrl K Search · Esc Close, with ⌘ on a Mac and a home icon that goes to the Auric Artisan home page. Each tile shows an illustration or an icon and the page's name. Hover over a tile to see its description in a tooltip. The tile for the page you are on has a small dot; its tooltip reads You are here . Select a tile to go to that page. The kit remembers how often you open "},{"t":"Find a page by browsing","d":"Browse the Menu Kit's tabs and sections, use Recommended and Most Used, and collapse sections you do not need.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/find-a-page.html","h":["Switch tabs","What each tab holds","Recommended","Most Used","Collapse and expand sections","Move with the keyboard","How the tool visibility mode changes the menu","Related"],"x":" The Menu Kit groups every page it knows into seven tabs, and each tab into sections. This guide shows how to move around them. Select a tab, or with a tab focused press Left arrow , Right arrow , Home or End . Each tab's tooltip reads \"Show tab pages.\" The kit remembers the last tab you used and opens on it next time. Tab Sections number of pages Examples Tools Recommended up to 8 , Most Used up to 8 , Start Here 9 , Search 2 , General Color Tools 7 All Tools, URL Analyzer, Icon Library, Design System Generator, Portfolio Builder, Color Foundations, Tonal Steps, Tints and Shades Design Color Science Lab 3 , Colorimetry 3 , Gamut and Rendering 3 , Perception and Neuroscience 3 , Spectral and Material Tools 2 , Utility Labs 6 Personalization Generator, Ishihara Plate Generation, Gamut Mapping, Tone Mapping, LUT Lab, SVG Recolor Analyze Vision Simulation 1 Vision Deficiency Simulator Account Account and Sign In 14 Sign In, Create Account, Dashboard, API Keys, Billing, Sessions Library Library 11 Documentation, Changelog, Blog, Learn, Workspace, Color Library, Palette Library Company Company 7 About, Pricing, Contact, FAQ, Timeline, Accessibility, Projects Trust Legal and Security 12 "},{"t":"Search and quick actions","d":"Search every page in the Menu Kit with forgiving matching, and run quick actions such as copying the page URL.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/search-and-quick-actions.html","h":["Search for a page","How matching works","Quick actions","Clear the search","Search the whole site instead","Related"],"x":" Typing in the Menu Kit's search box turns the menu into a ranked list of results, like a command palette. Results include pages from every tab and a set of quick actions. 1. Open the Menu Kit. The cursor is already in Search Auric Artisan… . If it is not, press / or select the box. 2. Type a few letters, for example gamut . 3. The tiles are replaced by a list of up to 16 results, and a count such as 4 results appears. 4. Press Up arrow or Down arrow to highlight a result, or move the pointer over it. 5. Press Enter , or select the result, to open it. The kit closes and the page opens. If you pick the page you are already on, the kit just closes. Each result shows the page's illustration or icon, its name, the section it belongs to, and Open ↵ on the right. Letters in order. A result matches if the letters you type appear in its name in the same order, with anything in between. clrlib matches Color Library , and tmap matches Tone Mapping . Section names count. If the name alone does not match, the section and name together are tried, so legal priv finds Privacy in Legal and Security . Descriptions count. If neither matches, a page whose description contains your exact text still ap"},{"t":"Menu Kit reference","d":"Every control, tab, section, state and message in the Menu Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Launcher","Title bar","Search bar","Tabs","Sections","Tiles","Results list (while searching)","Footer","States and messages"],"x":" Control What it does Default Menu launcher four square icon Opens or closes the kit. Announces itself as Open start menu or Close start menu Closed Ctrl + M Same as the launcher — Tooltip \"Open site navigation, grouped pages, and quick search.\" — Control What it does Values Default Menu Kit title Drag the title bar to move the kit — Bottom left corner Status chip The site's release status; tooltip \"Auric Artisan is status .\" For example Beta Beta at the time of writing Focus mode Keeps the kit open across pages and when other kits open On or off; remembered Off Theme Switches the menu between light and dark \"Switch this menu between light and dark mode.\" Light or dark; remembered Follows the site Resize Normal 680 px wide or expanded up to 820 px wide Remembered Normal Minimize Collapses the kit to its title bar; select the bar to restore — — Close Closes the kit \"Close Menu Kit.\" — — Control What it does Search Auric Artisan… Type to switch to the results list; has focus when the kit opens ESC hint Shown while the box is empty Clear button cross Shown while the box has text; clears it \"Clear search\" Result count N results while searching Tab Tooltip Tools Show Tools pages. Design"},{"t":"Menu Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for Menu Kit problems, such as a missing tab, a tool that does not appear, or a shortcut that does nothing.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The Design tab is missing","A tool I expect is not in the menu or the search results","Ctrl + M does nothing","Ctrl + K opens a different search","The menu says \"Menu unavailable\"","Most Used shows pages I have never opened","A section is empty or missing","Selecting a result does nothing","The kit opens on every page","The status chip says Beta"],"x":" For problems shared by every kit, see Troubleshooting kits ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: The site's tool visibility mode is Basic , which is the default. Basic mode hides the scientific tools, and the Design tab has nothing else to show. What to do: Open the Advanced Kit ../../advanced kit/README.md and choose Advanced or Everything . Why: The tool visibility mode hides it, or you unticked it in Custom mode. What to do: Choose Everything in the Advanced Kit, or tick the tool in Custom mode. If the tool still does not appear, it may not be in the Menu Kit's list; try All Tools in the Tools tab or the site wide search Ctrl + K . Why: Your browser or operating system uses that key combination first. On a Mac, Cmd + M minimises the window. What to do: Open the Menu Kit from Page utilities Menu . Why: Ctrl + K opens the site wide search, even while the Menu Kit is open. What to do: Press / to put the cursor in the Menu Kit's own search box. Why: The list of pages could not be downloaded, usually because the connection dropped. What to do: Check your connection and reload the page, then open the Menu Kit again. Why: Until you have opened pages from the Menu Kit, Most Used has no "},{"t":"Menu Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Menu Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["How is the Menu Kit different from the site header menu?","How is it different from the site-wide search?","Does the Menu Kit list every page on the site?","Why do I see fewer tools than a friend?","Can I reorder or pin tiles?","Can I reset Most Used?","Does search understand typos?","Is anything I type sent anywhere?"],"x":" The Menu Kit opens on any page, including tool pages where the header is scrolled away, and holds the whole site in one searchable panel with tabs, recommended pages and your most used pages. The Menu Kit searches its own list of pages by name, section and description, and also offers quick actions. The site wide search Ctrl + K , or https://auricartisan.com/search/ searches the content of pages and can search the web. See Search ../../../search/README.md . No. It lists the main tools and pages. Individual articles, library entries and some tool sub pages are not in it; use the site wide search for those. The Menu Kit follows the tool visibility mode chosen in the Advanced Kit ../../advanced kit/README.md , which is stored in each browser. New visitors start in Basic mode. No. The order is fixed, apart from Most Used , which follows how often you open pages from the Menu Kit. There is no reset button. Clearing this site's data in your browser resets it, along with your other kit preferences. Partly. It matches letters in order with gaps, so clrlib finds Color Library . It does not correct swapped or wrong letters. No. Searching and quick actions run in your browser. See Privacy .."},{"t":"Menu Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Menu Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Menu Kit: the terms it uses, its keyboard shortcuts, what it covers and how search ranks, related pages, its public history and what it keeps in your browser. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Menu Kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every key the Menu Kit responds to limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the menu includes, and how search matches and ranks related.md related.md Related kits, site features and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the Menu Kit privacy.md privacy.md What the Menu Kit keeps in your browser "},{"t":"Menu Kit shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut the Menu Kit responds to.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + M Anywhere Opens or closes the Menu Kit / Kit open, cursor not in a text box Puts the cursor in the search box Esc Search box with text Clears the search Esc Kit open Closes the kit Down arrow Search box not searching or tab row Moves into the tiles Left arrow , Right arrow Tab row Previous or next tab Home , End Tab row First or last tab Arrow keys Tiles and section headings Move to the previous or next item Home , End Tiles and section headings First or last item Enter or Space Section heading Collapses or expands the section Enter Tile Opens the page Up arrow , Down arrow Search box while searching Moves the highlight through the results Enter Search box while searching Opens the highlighted page or runs the highlighted action Ctrl + K , shown in the footer, opens the site wide search rather than the Menu Kit's search box. See Site features ../../../site features/README.md . See Kit keyboard shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md for the other kits. "},{"t":"Menu Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Menu Kit guides.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Start menu — The Menu Kit's role: one panel that lists the site's pages, like the start menu of a desktop computer. Tab — One of the seven top level groups: Tools, Design, Analyze, Account, Library, Company, Trust. Section — A collapsible group of tiles inside a tab, such as Start Here or Utility Labs . Tile — One page in the menu, shown as an illustration and a name. Recommended — Eight entry points picked for first time visitors, at the top of the Tools tab. Most Used — Up to eight Tools tab pages you open most often from the Menu Kit. Results list — The ranked list that replaces the tiles while you search. It works like a command palette. Fuzzy matching — Search that matches the letters you type in order, allowing other letters in between. Quick action — A command in the results list that does something on the current page, such as Copy current URL . Status chip — The label next to the kit's title showing the site's release status, such as Beta . Tool visibility mode — The site wide choice of Basic, Advanced, Everything or Custom tools, set in the Advanced Kit. The Menu Kit shows only tools the mode allows. "},{"t":"Menu Kit limits","d":"What the Menu Kit includes, how its search matches and ranks, and what it does not do.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the menu covers","Search","Most Used","Status chip"],"x":" The Menu Kit lists 83 pages in 14 sections across seven tabs, plus the Recommended and Most Used sections built from the Tools tab. It does not list individual Learn articles, blog posts, documentation articles, changelog entries or library items. Use the site wide search for those. The Projects tile links to an external site. The results list shows at most 16 results. Matching is by letters in order, then by section and name together, then by an exact phrase in the description. It does not correct wrong or swapped letters, and it does not search the text of pages. Results respect the tool visibility mode, so hidden tools cannot be found through the Menu Kit. Ranking gives a modest boost to pages you open often, capped so a single much used page does not always come first. Counts only visits started from the Menu Kit, in this browser. Covers pages in the Tools tab only. Is not shared between browsers or devices and cannot be reset from the kit. The chip shows one status for the whole site, not the status of the page you are on. For per page status, use the Status Kit ../../status kit/README.md . "},{"t":"Menu Kit privacy","d":"What the Menu Kit keeps in your browser and what it downloads.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Kept in your browser","Downloaded","Related"],"x":" What Why The last tab you used To open on it next time Which sections you collapsed To keep them collapsed How many times you opened each page from the Menu Kit To fill Most Used and rank search results Position, expanded size, Focus mode and theme Shared kit preferences None of this is sent anywhere. It is removed when you clear this site's data in your browser. The first time you open the Menu Kit on a page, it downloads the list of pages and the site status from auricartisan.com. Your searches are not sent: matching happens in your browser. The Copy current URL quick action writes the page address to your clipboard, which your browser may ask permission for. Privacy for all kits ../../others/privacy.md The site's privacy policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ "},{"t":"Menu Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about the Menu Kit, and what the kit contains as of September 2026.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Menu Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.75 19 April 2026 Interface fixes to the Menu Kit and the Status Kit, as part of a broad stability release v0.9.8 2 May 2026 Complexity management added the tool visibility modes that the Menu Kit follows , with Advanced Kit upgrades v0.9.9 5 June 2026 Interface consistency improvements and shortcut updates across the site Seven tabs Tools, Design, Analyze, Account, Library, Company, Trust with collapsible, remembered sections. Recommended and Most Used sections at the top of the Tools tab. A search that turns into a ranked results list with quick actions and keyboard navigation. A You are here marker on the current page's tile. The site status chip in the title bar. Shared kit controls: Focus mode, per kit theme, Resize, Minimize, Close, and a labelled Menu launcher in the page utilities bar. Changes not recorded in the public history are not listed here. "},{"t":"Related to the Menu Kit","d":"Kits, site features and pages related to the Menu Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Menu Kit","u":"website/kits/menu-kit/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Advanced Kit ../../advanced kit/README.md — choose which tools the Menu Kit shows. Status Kit ../../status kit/README.md — the status of each page, and scans of whole sections. Library Kit ../../library kit/README.md — opened by the Workspace tile in the Library tab. All kits ../../README.md and Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . Site features ../../../site features/README.md — the site header, the page navigation dock Navigate , the site wide search and the right click menu. Search ../../../search/README.md — the full search page at https://auricartisan.com/search/. Collections ../../../library/collections/README.md — the tool collections at https://auricartisan.com/collections/, another way to browse tools by workflow. "},{"t":"Status Kit","d":"See how finished the page you are on is, scan a whole section of the site for page statuses, and watch live device, network and performance readings.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Status Kit answers two questions: how finished is this part of Auric Artisan, and how is my device coping? Its This page card shows the status of the page you are on, such as Beta , Stable or Experimental . Its scanner lists every page under a path, such as /tool/ or /library/ , with each page's status, a summary and filters. Above the scanner, a collapsible System status panel shows live readings from your browser across five tabs: Network , Hardware , Memory , Display and Runtime , including your connection type, battery level, storage use, screen resolution, colour gamut and a live frame rate graph. All readings are taken in your browser and shown only to you. Scans read pages of auricartisan.com. Visitors who want to know whether a tool is stable or still experimental before relying on it. Anyone reporting a problem who needs to describe their device, browser and connection. Designers checking what their display supports, such as the P3 wide gamut. On any page of https://auricartisan.com, select Page utilities in the bottom left corner, then Status . The Status Kit has no keyboard shortcut. 1. Select Page utilities Status . The Status Kit opens with the cursor in the path "},{"t":"Status Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Status Kit guides: page status, section scans, system status, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain the Status Kit's three parts: the This page card, the System status panel and the page scanner. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Open the Status Kit and learn its screen check page status.md check page status.md Read the current page's status and what each status means scan a section.md scan a section.md Scan a path, read the summary, filter, search and reuse scans system status.md system status.md Every reading in the Network, Hardware, Memory, Display and Runtime tabs reference.md reference.md Every control and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems and how to fix them faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions Shared controls such as moving, Focus mode and theme are explained in Panel controls ../../docs/panel controls.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with the Status Kit","d":"Open the Status Kit and learn its three parts: the This page card, System status and the page scanner.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the kit","The screen, top to bottom","Try it","Opening another kit closes the Status Kit","Close the kit","Next steps"],"x":" Select Page utilities bottom left corner Status . The launcher's tooltip reads \"View the current page status and scan page status entries.\" There is no keyboard shortcut to open it. The kit opens with the cursor in the path box, ready for a scan. 1. Title bar. Status Kit and the buttons Focus mode , Theme , Resize , Minimize and Close . 2. This page. The status badge of the page you are on and a link with the page's title. See Check a page's status check page status.md . 3. System status. A collapsible panel with an Online or Offline pill and five tabs: Network , Hardware , Memory , Display , Runtime . See System status system status.md . 4. Path box and Scan button. The box shows https://auricartisan.com as a placeholder. See Scan a section scan a section.md . 5. Results search. Appears after a scan: Search pages... . 6. Recent scans. Your last scans, once you have run one. 7. Summary cards and filter chips. Appear after a scan. 8. Results. Before your first scan this area shows \"Scan a path for page statuses\" with the hint \"Enter a URL or path for example /tool/ and press Scan to list every page and its status.\" 1. Open the Status Kit on the home page. 2. The This page card show"},{"t":"Check a page's status","d":"Read the status of the page you are on in the Status Kit, and what each status label means.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/check-page-status.html","h":["Read the This page card","What each status means","How a page gets its status","The site status versus a page status","Related"],"x":" Every page on Auric Artisan has a status that says how finished it is. The Status Kit's This page card shows it for the page you are on. 1. Open the Status Kit Page utilities Status . 2. Look at the This page card at the top. The card shows: the label This page ; a coloured status badge, for example Beta . Its tooltip reads \"Current page status: Beta.\"; the page's title as a link. Selecting it opens the same page in a new tab. Until the status has been worked out, the badge reads Unknown for a moment. The kit can show the labels below. The site does not publish formal definitions for them; they carry their usual software meanings. Status Meaning Stable Finished and expected to keep working as it does now Beta Complete and usable, still being refined. Most of the site is Beta, matching the site's overall status Alpha Early; expect gaps and changes Experimental A trial feature that may change a lot or be withdrawn In development Being built Under testing Being tested before a wider release Maintenance Temporarily limited while it is being worked on Research A research tool; results are exploratory Archived Kept for reference, no longer developed Deprecated Being retired; use its rep"},{"t":"Scan a section of the site","d":"List every page under a path with its status, then summarise, filter, search and repeat the scan.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/scan-a-section.html","h":["Run a scan","Read the results","Filter and search the results","Collapse groups","Recent scans","Which pages are included","Empty and error states","Related"],"x":" The scanner lists every page of auricartisan.com whose address starts with a path you give, and shows each page's status. 1. Open the Status Kit. The cursor is in the path box. 2. Type a path such as /tool/ , /library/ or /company/ . You can also paste a full address such as https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/ ; only its path is used. 3. Press Enter or select Scan . While the scan runs, the results area shows Scanning pages with a running count such as 12 / 48 . The kit reads the site map to find the pages, then fetches each page to read its title, so a large section takes a little while. When the scan finishes you see, from top to bottom: 1. Summary cards. Card Counts Pages Every page found Tools Pages in the tool categories Tools, Color Lab and Vision Stable Pages with the Stable status Beta Pages with the Beta status Issues Pages that are Alpha, Deprecated or Archived 2. Filter chips. All , one chip per status found, and Issues if any, each with a count. They appear only when the results contain more than one status or any issues. 3. Result count , for example 48 pages , or Showing 12 of 48 pages when a filter or search is active. 4. Target page. If a page's address matches "},{"t":"System status","d":"Every live reading in the Status Kit's System status panel, what it means and when it shows a dash.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/system-status.html","h":["Open, collapse and switch pages","Network","Hardware","Memory","Display","Runtime","Using the readings for a bug report","Related"],"x":" The System status panel shows live information about your device, connection and the page, read from your browser. It refreshes every two seconds while the Status Kit is open, and at once when your connection goes on or off line. The panel is expanded when the kit opens. Select its heading System status or the chevron to collapse or expand it. With the keyboard, focus the heading and press Enter or Space . The pill next to the heading shows Online or Offline . Select a tab to switch between Network , Hardware , Memory , Display and Runtime . A reading shows — when your browser does not provide it. Some readings exist only in certain browsers, noted below. Reading What it shows Connection Your connection's effective speed class, such as 4G or 3G , or Online or Offline if the browser does not report a class Speed Estimated download speed in Mbps, with a bar full at 20 Mbps and the connection type, such as wifi, when known Latency Estimated round trip time in milliseconds Data Saver On if your browser's data saving mode is on, otherwise Off Speed, latency and data saver come from the browser's network information, which Chromium based browsers provide and others often do not. They ar"},{"t":"Status Kit reference","d":"Every control, reading, filter and message in the Status Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Launcher","Title bar","This page card","System status panel","Scanner","Statuses","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Control What it does Default Status launcher tick in circle icon Opens or closes the kit. Announces itself as Open status kit or Close status kit Closed Tooltip \"View the current page status and scan page status entries.\" — There is no keyboard shortcut to open the Status Kit. Control What it does Values Default Status Kit title Drag the title bar to move the kit — Bottom left corner Focus mode Opens the kit again on the next page you load. Does not keep it open when another kit opens On or off; remembered Off Theme Switches the kit between light and dark Light or dark; remembered Follows the site Resize Normal 560 px wide or expanded up to 760 px wide Remembered Normal Minimize Collapses the kit to its title bar — — Close Closes the kit \"Close Status Kit.\" — — Element What it shows This page Label Status badge The current page's status; tooltip \"Current page status: status .\" Shows Unknown until worked out Title link The page's title; opens the page in a new tab Control What it does Default System status heading and chevron Collapse or expand the panel Expanded Online / Offline pill Your connection state — Network , Hardware , Memory , Display , Runtime tabs Switch page Network R"},{"t":"Status Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for Status Kit problems, such as empty readings, slow scans or a kit that closes on its own.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Many readings show a dash (—)","The Status Kit closes when I open another kit","A scan takes a long time","\"No pages found\"","\"Couldn’t complete the scan\"","A page shows Beta although it looks finished","Ctrl + K opens a different search","The frame rate looks low","Storage is nearly full"],"x":" For problems shared by every kit, see Troubleshooting kits ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: Your browser does not provide that information. Network speed, latency and data saver, battery, JS heap and device memory are available only in some browsers, mostly Chromium based ones. What to do: Nothing is wrong. Try another browser if you need those readings. Why: The Status Kit always closes when another kit opens, even with Focus mode on. What to do: Reopen it after using the other kit. Focus mode still reopens it on each new page. Why: The kit fetches every page in the section to read its title. A broad path such as /tool/ or /library/ means many pages. What to do: Scan a narrower path, such as /library/blog/ . The running count shows how far the scan has got. Why: No page's address starts with what you typed. Paths are matched from the start, and must be paths on auricartisan.com. What to do: Start with a slash and a top level folder, such as /tool/ , /library/ , /company/ or /legal/ . Why: The site map could not be read, usually because the connection dropped. What to do: Check your connection and select Scan again. Why: Pages take the site's overall Beta status unless the sit"},{"t":"Status Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Status Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["Can I scan another website?","Does the Status Kit send my device details anywhere?","Is the Speed reading a speed test?","Why is there no keyboard shortcut?","Does P3 gamut mean my screen is colour-accurate?","Can I export a scan?","What counts as an issue?"],"x":" No. The scanner lists pages of auricartisan.com only. If you paste another site's address, only its path is used, and it is looked up on auricartisan.com. To check other websites, use the URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md . No. The readings are taken in your browser and shown only to you. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . No. It is your browser's rough estimate of your connection, not a measurement. The Status Kit has none. Open it from Page utilities Status . No. It means your browser reports that the display can show roughly the P3 range of colours. It says nothing about calibration. No. Scan results stay in the panel. Your last eight scan paths are remembered under Recent scans . Pages whose status is Alpha , Deprecated or Archived . "},{"t":"Status Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Status Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Status Kit: the terms it uses, its keys, what its readings can and cannot tell you, related pages, its public history and what it reads or keeps. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Status Kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keys the Status Kit responds to limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the statuses and readings mean, and their limits related.md related.md Related kits, tools and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the Status Kit privacy.md privacy.md What the Status Kit reads, keeps and fetches "},{"t":"Status Kit shortcuts","d":"Keys the Status Kit responds to.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" The Status Kit has no shortcut to open it. Open it from Page utilities Status . While it is open: Key Where What it does / Cursor not in a text box Puts the cursor in the path box, or in Search pages... after a scan Enter Path box Runs the scan Down arrow Path box or Search pages... Moves into the results Up arrow , Down arrow Results Previous or next item Home , End Results First or last item Enter A result row Opens the page in a new tab Enter or Space System status heading Collapses or expands the panel Esc Anywhere Closes the kit Ctrl + K opens the site wide search, not the Status Kit's boxes. See Kit keyboard shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md for the other kits. "},{"t":"Status Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Status Kit guides.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Page status — A label that says how finished a page is, such as Beta or Stable . Site status — The status of the site as a whole, shown in the Menu Kit. Pages without their own status share it. Scan — A listing of every page whose address starts with a given path, with each page's status. Path — The part of an address after the domain, such as /library/blog/ . Site map — The site's published list of its pages, which the scanner reads. Issues — Pages with the Alpha, Deprecated or Archived status. Target page — In a scan, the page whose address matches your path exactly. Effective connection type — The browser's classification of your connection speed, such as 4G. Round trip time latency — How long a message takes to reach a server and come back, in milliseconds. JS heap — Memory used by the page's scripts. Device pixel ratio — How many physical screen pixels make up one CSS pixel. 2× is typical of high density screens. CSS pixel — The unit web pages are laid out in. It may be several physical pixels. Colour gamut — The range of colours a display can show. sRGB is the standard range; P3 is wider. Colour depth — The number of bits used per pixel to store colour, such as 24 bit. Frame"},{"t":"Status Kit limits","d":"What the Status Kit's page statuses and system readings can and cannot tell you.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Page statuses","Scans","System readings"],"x":" Statuses are the site's own labels, set centrally. They are not measured from the page. A page without its own entry takes the status of its folder, or of the whole site Beta . The kit does not explain why a page has a given status. Scans cover pages of auricartisan.com only, taken from the site map. The home page and individual colour pages under /color/ are never listed. Titles come from fetching each page, so a scan of a large section makes many requests and takes longer. Categories come from the Menu Kit where a page is listed there, and are otherwise guessed from words in the address, so a page can land in Other or in a category that does not quite fit. Results are not saved; only your last eight scan paths are remembered. Readings are what your browser chooses to report. Browsers round, cap or withhold some values to protect privacy, so the same device can show different figures in different browsers. Speed and Latency are browser estimates, not a speed test. Device memory is approximate and capped by the browser. Storage shows the space the site uses against the space your browser allows it, which is not your disk's free space. Color reports whether the display can show rou"},{"t":"Status Kit privacy","d":"What the Status Kit reads from your browser, what it keeps, and what it fetches.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Read from your browser, shown only to you","Kept in your browser","Fetched from auricartisan.com","Related"],"x":" The System status panel reads your connection estimate, battery, device memory, processor threads, memory use, storage use, cache count, screen and window size, pixel ratio, colour depth and gamut, frame rate, page load time, service worker state, app mode, language, time zone and cookie setting. These readings are displayed in the panel and not stored or sent anywhere. They stop updating when you close the kit. What Why Your last 8 scans: the path, target page title and status, page count and time For Recent scans Which result categories you collapsed To keep them collapsed Position, expanded size, Focus mode and theme Shared kit preferences When the kit first opens on a page: the central list of page statuses, the site map, and the current page to read its title . During a scan: the Menu Kit's page list and each page in the scanned section. These are ordinary page requests to auricartisan.com, like visiting the pages. Privacy for all kits ../../others/privacy.md The site's privacy policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ "},{"t":"Status Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about the Status Kit, and what the kit contains as of September 2026.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Status Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.75 19 April 2026 Interface fixes to the Menu Kit and the Status Kit, as part of a broad stability release v0.9.9 5 June 2026 The site's release language moved to Beta, the status most pages now show A This page card with the current page's status and title. A collapsible System status panel with Network, Hardware, Memory, Display and Runtime tabs, refreshing every two seconds, including a live frame rate sparkline. A page scanner with summary cards, status filters, results search, category groups and the last eight scans. Shared kit controls: Focus mode, per kit theme, Resize, Minimize, Close, and a labelled Status launcher in the page utilities bar. The page status is shown only inside the kit, not as a floating badge on the page. Changes not recorded in the public history are not listed here. "},{"t":"Related to the Status Kit","d":"Kits, tools and pages related to the Status Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Status Kit","u":"website/kits/status-kit/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Menu Kit ../../menu kit/README.md — shows the site's overall status chip, and supplies page names and categories for scans. Library Kit ../../library kit/README.md — manage the saved items that use your browser storage. Update Kit ../../update kit/README.md — update the site's cached files when a new release is out. URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — audit any website, not just this one. Download and offline use ../../../download and offline/README.md — installing the site as an app and using it offline, which the App mode and Service worker readings reflect. Release history: https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ see Changelog ../../../library/changelog/README.md . Help ../../../../help/README.md — contact support, using the System status readings in your report. "},{"t":"Update Kit","d":"How auricartisan.com tells you a new release is out, and how the Update website command refreshes the site's files in your browser.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Update Kit keeps the copy of Auric Artisan in your browser up to date. Browsers and the site's offline support keep copies of the site's files so pages load quickly and work offline. After a new release, those copies can be out of date. The Update Kit notices when a newer release is out and lets you refresh everything in one step. It has no panel. You meet it in two places: an Update available notice that appears at the top of the page when a new release is detected, and the Update website command in the site's right click menu, also available as Ctrl + Shift + U . Updating clears the site's cached files, re downloads the files the current page uses, and reloads the page. Your saved library items, notes, settings and account are not touched. Anyone who sees the Update available notice. Anyone whose page looks broken or out of date after a release. People who use the site offline or as an installed app, whose cached copy is used most. The notice appears by itself at the top of any page of https://auricartisan.com when an update is available. Right click anywhere on a page outside text boxes and choose Update website . Press Ctrl + Shift + U on any page. 1. When Update available"},{"t":"Update Kit guides","d":"Contents of the Update Kit guides: the update notice, the Update website command, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides explain the Update available notice and the Update website command, and what happens when you update. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The notice and the command at a glance update the website.md update the website.md Each step of an update and what it changes reference.md reference.md Every control, state and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Problems and how to fix them faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions "},{"t":"Getting started with the Update Kit","d":"Recognise the Update available notice and the Update website command, and update the site for the first time.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/getting-started.html","h":["When the site checks","The notice","The command","Your first update","Next steps"],"x":" Each time a page loads, the site waits until the page is ready and then checks which release is the newest. This takes a moment and does not slow the page. On your first visit, the site simply notes the current release. You see nothing. On later visits, if a newer release has come out since you last updated, the Update available notice appears. If the check cannot reach the release information, for example offline, nothing is shown. The notice appears centred at the top of the page across the top on a phone . It shows: Update available and the version, for example Update available v0.9.11 ; a line such as New update found: 0.9.11 ; an Update now button; a small x button labelled Hide update notice . Select Update now to update. Select x to put the notice away; it comes back on your next page load until you update. You can update at any time, even when no notice is showing: Right click anywhere on the page not in a text box and choose Update website . The menu shows the shortcut next to it, Ctrl+⇧+U . Or press Ctrl + Shift + U . When an update is available, the right click menu shows the same entry as Update available with the version and Ready , also at the top of the menu under W"},{"t":"Update the website","d":"What happens, step by step, when you select Update now or run Update website, and what is and is not affected.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/update-the-website.html","h":["Start an update","What happens","What is not affected","What to expect afterwards","Put the notice away without updating","Related"],"x":" Use any of: Update now on the Update available notice; Update website or Update available in the right click menu; Ctrl + Shift + U . The command always refreshes, even if you are already on the newest release. In that case the notice may show briefly with the line Refreshing website cache... . 1. Check. The site reads its newest release number. When run from the right click menu or the keyboard, the message Checking for updates… appears. 2. Clear cached files. The site deletes the copies of its files that your browser keeps for this site the caches used for speed and offline use . The message Updating website... appears. 3. Refresh the offline helper. The site asks its service worker, the background part that makes offline use possible, to check for a new version of itself. 4. Re download current files. The files the current page uses its scripts, styles, images and data, up to 180 files are downloaded again, bypassing the browser's cache. 5. Record the version. The site notes that you are now on the newest release. 6. Reload. The message Update ready. Reloading... appears and the page reloads. For a moment the address carries ?auric update= and the version; it is removed once th"},{"t":"Update Kit reference","d":"Every control, state and message of the Update Kit's notice and command.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/reference.html","h":["Update notice","Right-click menu entry","Keyboard","Messages","When the site checks","What an update clears and keeps"],"x":" Element What it shows or does Title Update available followed by the version, such as Update available v0.9.11 Message For example New update found: 0.9.11 , or Refreshing website cache... during a forced refresh Update now Starts the update x Hide update notice Hides the notice until the next page load Position: centred at the top of the page; across the top on screens 520 px wide or narrower. The notice follows the site's light or dark theme and is announced politely to screen readers. State Label Hint on the right Up to date or unknown Update website Ctrl+⇧+U Update available Update available and the version Ready Updating Updating website … Failed Retry update Error When an update is available or running, the entry also appears as a banner at the top of the right click menu, in a group named Website update . The entry is not offered on shared public portfolio pages. Shortcut What it does Ctrl + Shift + U Runs Update website on any page Message When Checking for updates… You started an update from the right click menu or keyboard Updating website... Caches are being cleared and files re downloaded Update ready. Reloading... The update finished; the page reloads Update failed. T"},{"t":"Update Kit troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for update problems, such as a notice that keeps returning, an update that fails, or a page that still looks old.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The notice keeps coming back","\"Update failed. Try again.\"","The page still looks old after updating","No notice appears, but I know there is a new release","Ctrl + Shift + U does nothing, or types a character","The right-click menu does not show Update website","I lost work when the page reloaded"],"x":" Why: x only hides the notice for the current page. It returns on every page load until you update. What to do: Select Update now . Why: The update could not finish, usually because the connection dropped while files were re downloading, or the browser refused access to its storage. What to do: Check your connection and run Update website again. If it keeps failing, allow site storage for auricartisan.com in your browser settings. Why: Some pages you have not visited since the update still use older cached files until you open them, and some browsers keep their own short term copies. What to do: Open the page and run Update website there, or reload it with your browser's hard reload shortcut. Why: The notice appears only when the release number has changed since you last updated in this browser. On your first visit the site records the current release silently. If the release information cannot be reached, nothing is shown. What to do: Run Update website from the right click menu or with Ctrl + Shift + U ; it refreshes regardless. Why: Some systems use Ctrl + Shift + U to enter special characters, and take the key press first. What to do: Use the right click menu's Update website i"},{"t":"Update Kit FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about updating auricartisan.com in your browser.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/docs/faq.html","h":["Why does a website need updating?","Will updating delete my saved work?","Is the Update Kit a panel I can open?","How do I know which release I am on?","Does updating need a connection?","Should I update the installed app the same way?","Does the Update Kit update my browser extension or VS Code extensions?"],"x":" Your browser, and the site's offline support, keep copies of the site's files so pages load fast and work offline. After a release, those copies can be older than the site. Updating replaces them. No. Library items, notes, calculator history, settings and your sign in are kept. Only unsaved work in the page you are on is lost when it reloads. No. It is the notice and the Update website command. There is no launcher for it in the page utilities bar. The notice names the new version. The site's release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. Yes. Files are re downloaded from auricartisan.com. Yes. The installed app is the same site, so the notice and the command work there too. See Download and offline use ../../../download and offline/README.md . No. It only refreshes the website in your browser. Extensions update through their own stores. "},{"t":"Update Kit reference material","d":"Contents of the Update Kit reference pages: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, release notes and privacy.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Update Kit: the terms used, its shortcut, what an update does and does not refresh, related pages, its public history and what it stores. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Update Kit pages shortcuts.md shortcuts.md The update shortcut limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What an update refreshes, and when the notice appears related.md related.md Related features and pages release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of the Update Kit privacy.md privacy.md What the Update Kit stores and fetches "},{"t":"Update Kit shortcuts","d":"The keyboard shortcut for updating the website.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Shortcut Where What it does Ctrl + Shift + U Any page Runs Update website : clears the site's cached files, re downloads the page's files and reloads Tab , Enter Update notice Reach and select Update now or x The right click menu shows this shortcut as Ctrl+⇧+U next to Update website . See Kit keyboard shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md for the other kits. "},{"t":"Update Kit glossary","d":"Terms used in the Update Kit pages.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Release — A published version of the website, such as v0.9.11, listed in the changelog. Update notice — The Update available message at the top of the page. Cache — Copies of the site's files kept by your browser so pages load faster and work offline. Service worker — A background script from the site that manages its offline copies. Hard reload — A browser reload that ignores cached copies of the page's files. Installed app — The site installed from your browser and opened in its own window. Site storage — Data the site keeps in your browser, such as library items and settings. An update does not clear it. "},{"t":"Update Kit limits","d":"What an update refreshes, what it leaves alone, and when the notice appears.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["When the notice appears","What an update refreshes","What it does not do"],"x":" The site compares the newest release it can find with the release recorded the last time you updated in this browser. The notice appears only when they differ. On a first visit the current release is recorded silently, so you will not see a notice until the following release. If the release information cannot be reached, for example offline, no notice is shown. The check runs once per page load. All of the site's caches in your browser are deleted. The service worker is asked to update itself; it is not removed. Up to 180 files used by the current page are downloaded again. Files used only by other pages refresh when you visit those pages. The page reloads. It does not clear site storage: library items, notes, calculator history, settings and your sign in are kept. It does not update browser extensions, VS Code extensions or the browser itself. It does not change anything on the server; it only refreshes your browser's copy of the site. It cannot bypass a network or company proxy that serves old copies. "},{"t":"Update Kit privacy","d":"What the Update Kit stores in your browser and what it fetches.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/privacy.html","h":["Stored in your browser","Fetched from auricartisan.com","What an update deletes","Related"],"x":" The release number you last updated to, so the site can tell when a newer one is out. Nothing else. On each page load: the site's release information, to find the newest release number. When you update: the files the current page uses, downloaded again. These are ordinary requests to auricartisan.com. No information about you or your device is sent by the Update Kit. The site's cached files in your browser. Your saved library, notes, settings and sign in are not deleted. Privacy for all kits ../../others/privacy.md The site's privacy policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ "},{"t":"Update Kit release notes","d":"What the public changelog records about website updates, and how the Update Kit works as of September 2026.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/release-notes.html","h":["Recorded releases","The Update Kit as of 24 September 2026"],"x":" The website's public release history is at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ and https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/. It does not list the Update Kit by name. Release Date What the public history says v0.9.9 5 June 2026 PWA installable app support was added, the offline caching that the Update Kit refreshes v0.9.11 12 August 2026 The newest release in the public changelog at the time of writing Checks for a newer release on each page load and shows an Update available notice with Update now and x . Update website in the right click menu, with states for available, updating and failed, and a banner at the top of the menu when an update is ready. Ctrl + Shift + U from any page. Updates clear the site's caches, refresh the service worker and the current page's files, and keep your saved data. Changes not recorded in the public history are not listed here. "},{"t":"Related to the Update Kit","d":"Features and pages related to the Update Kit.","p":"Website › Kits › Update Kit","u":"website/kits/update-kit/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Site features ../../../site features/README.md — the right click menu, which holds Update website . Download and offline use ../../../download and offline/README.md — installing the site as an app and using it offline, which relies on the cached files an update refreshes. Status Kit ../../status kit/README.md — its Runtime tab shows whether the service worker is active and whether you are in the installed app. Changelog ../../../library/changelog/README.md — what each release changed, at https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. All kits ../../README.md . "},{"t":"Reference material for all kits","d":"Contents of the shared reference pages for all kits: glossary, shortcuts, privacy and related pages.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds reference pages that apply to every kit: the terms the kit guides use, all kit keyboard shortcuts in one place, what the kits keep in your browser, and related parts of the site. Each kit's own others/ folder has the same pages for that kit alone. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used across the kit guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every keyboard shortcut for opening and using the kits privacy.md privacy.md What each kit stores in your browser and what uses the network related.md related.md Site features, tools and pages that work with the kits "},{"t":"Kit keyboard shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut for opening, closing and using the kits, in one table.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Open and close kits","Inside the Feature Kit","Inside the Menu Kit","Inside the Status Kit","Inside the Library Kit","Site-wide shortcuts that interact with kits"],"x":" Shortcuts that open a kit work on any page. Shortcuts that act inside a kit work only while that kit is open. Each kit's own shortcuts page has the full detail. Shortcut What it does Ctrl + Shift + K Cmd + Shift + K on a Mac Open or close the Feature Kit Ctrl + M Open or close the Menu Kit Ctrl + Shift + A Open or close the Advanced Kit Ctrl + Shift + L Cmd + Shift + L on a Mac Open or close the Library Kit Ctrl + Shift + U Update the website Update Kit Esc Close the page utilities bar, or close the open kit The Status Kit has no shortcut to open it. Use the Status launcher. Shortcut What it does 1 to 6 On the Feature Kit menu, open Scientific Calculator, Unit Converter, Feedback, Notes, Date & Time or Developer Tools Ctrl + 1 to Ctrl + 6 Switch straight to one of the six tools while the kit has focus Esc In a tool, go back to the menu. On the menu, close the kit Digits, + , , , / , . , , , ^ , % , ! Type on the calculator keypad when the cursor is not in a text box Enter or = Work out the calculator expression Backspace Delete the last character on the keypad Delete Clear the keypad / In the Unit Converter, jump to the unit search box See Feature Kit shortcuts ../feature kit/othe"},{"t":"Kits glossary","d":"Terms used across the kit guides, from launcher and Focus mode to tool visibility mode.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Kit — A floating panel that opens over any page of the site and does one job, such as calculating or finding a page. Page utilities bar — The launcher bar in the bottom left corner of every page. Closed, it is a single round button labelled Page utilities ; open, it shows one labelled launcher per kit. Launcher — The labelled button in the page utilities bar that opens and closes one kit, for example Feature or Library . Hub — The round button that opens and closes the page utilities bar. While the bar is open it reads Close . Panel — The floating window a kit opens in. Title bar — The strip across the top of a kit panel, holding the kit's name and its controls. You drag it to move the panel. Modeless — Describes a panel that does not block the page behind it. You can keep using the page while a modeless kit is open. Focus mode — A title bar setting that keeps a kit open when you open another kit and opens it again on the next page you load. In the Library Kit it is called Keep open . Expanded — The larger size a kit takes after you select Resize . Minimised — A kit shrunk to its title bar or, for the Feature Kit, to a small round icon . Kit theme — A light or dark setting that be"},{"t":"Kits and your privacy","d":"What each kit keeps in your browser, what it sends over the network, and how to clear it.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/others/privacy.html","h":["What every kit keeps in your browser","What each kit keeps, and what it sends","Things that are never stored","Private windows and blocked storage","Clear what the kits have stored"],"x":" The kits run in your browser. Almost everything they remember stays in your browser's storage for auricartisan.com and is never sent anywhere. This page lists what each kit keeps and the few cases where a kit uses the network. For each kit separately: the panel position after you drag it; whether it is expanded; whether Focus mode is on; its own light or dark theme, once you have used its Theme button. Kit Kept in your browser Uses the network for Feature Kit Calculator history up to 100 entries , notes, recently picked dates up to 8 , the tool you had open while Focus mode was on, feedback waiting to be sent Loading the unit list the first time you open the Unit Converter; sending feedback you submit Menu Kit Last tab, collapsed sections, how often you open each page for Most Used Loading the list of pages and the site status Advanced Kit Your tool visibility mode and your Custom tool ticks Loading the list of tools for the Custom checklist Status Kit Your last 8 scans, collapsed result groups Reading the site map and the pages you scan, all from auricartisan.com Library Kit Every saved item, collection and library setting, including any sync destinations you add Only the sync de"},{"t":"Related to the kits","d":"Site features, tools and pages that work alongside the kits.","p":"Website › Kits","u":"website/kits/others/related.html","h":["Site features next to the kits","Tools that work with the kits","Pages"],"x":" The page utilities bar also launches two site features that are not kits: Navigate opens the page navigation dock back, forward, reload, outline, split view, jump to top or bottom . Settings opens the site settings panel theme, accent colour, text size, motion, ads and more . Both, along with the site wide search Ctrl + K , the right click menu and the eye rest reminder, are documented in Site features ../../site features/README.md . Every tool with a Save to Library button saves into the Library Kit ../library kit/README.md . The URL Analyzer ../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md , the Vision Simulation ../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md lab and the Colour Science Lab ../../tools/colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md have mode switches that change the same site wide setting as the Advanced Kit ../advanced kit/README.md . The Basic Colour Tools ../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md workspace uses floating panels of its own, separate from the kits. The site's release history: https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ see Changelog ../../library/changelog/README.md Collections of tools, which follow the Ad"},{"t":"Library","d":"An overview of the Auric Artisan library and a map of its documentation.","p":"Website › Library","u":"website/library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan library is the reading and reference side of the site. It brings together six searchable colour libraries, the catalogue of every tool, a course of articles on colour science and accessibility, a user guide for each tool, the blog and the changelog. The colour libraries are large, browsable collections of generated colour data: 8,192 measured colours, five million palettes, 8,192 gradients, 8,192 colour harmonies, 8,192 shade scales and five million foreground and background pairs scored for contrast. Each one lets you search, filter, inspect and copy or export values for use in your own work. The rest of the library is for learning and finding your way: Collections lists every tool, Learn teaches the ideas behind them with interactive labs, Documentation explains each tool step by step, and the blog and changelog record what has been built and when. Designers and front end developers who need ready made, measured colour values. Accessibility specialists who need contrast checked colour pairs. Students and colour enthusiasts learning colour science. Anyone who wants to find the right Auric Artisan tool, or learn how to use it. Part Address Collections all tools h"},{"t":"Blog","d":"What the Auric Artisan blog contains, where to find it, and how to read and follow it.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan blog is where the site's author writes, in the page's words, \"occasional posts about what is being built and why — roadmaps, product notes, and the odd essay on colour\". It is small by design: there are three posts so far. Release by release detail lives in the changelog, and long form colour science in Learn; the blog is for the reasoning and the plans in between. The blog page shows the newest post large, with its opening paragraph and a Read the post link, and lists the earlier posts underneath with their dates, categories and one line summaries. Anyone who wants to know where Auric Artisan is heading and why. Existing users who want a readable summary of what has changed, beyond the changelog's lists. The blog: https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/ From the site header: Learn menu › Blog \"Articles, ideas & studio news\" . RSS feed: https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/rss.xml 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/. 2. Read the opening of the newest post and select Read the post . 3. On the post, use the Table of Contents or open and close sections as you read. 4. Select ← Back to Blog to return, or Print to print the post. 5. Add the RSS feed to your"},{"t":"Blog: docs","d":"Guides to the Auric Artisan blog and a summary of every post.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The blog page, reading a post, printing and RSS. posts.md posts.md Every post with its date, category and a summary. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Blog overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Read the Auric Artisan blog page and its posts, print a post, and follow new posts by RSS.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/docs/getting-started.html","h":["The blog page","Reading a post","Follow new posts","Result"],"x":" Open https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/. The heading Blog and the line \"Occasional posts about what is being built and why — roadmaps, product notes, and the odd essay on colour\", followed by a count such as Three so far. The newest post , shown large: its date for example 27 July 2026 , its category, its title, its opening paragraph, an illustration and Read the post . Earlier — the other posts, newest first, each with date, category, title and a one line summary. A footer that points to the changelog ../../changelog/README.md for release detail and Learn ../../learn/README.md for longer colour science writing, and an RSS link. If the list of posts cannot be loaded, the page shows The blog could not be loaded. and a plain list of All posts still links to every post. Each post has: Part What it does Date , Author , Category When it was written, by whom, and what kind of post it is. Print Prints the post. ← Back to Blog Returns to the blog page. Overview A short summary of the post. Table of Contents Links to each section. Sections The post itself. Each section heading can be selected to fold the section away or open it again. Some older posts open with a dated update note, for"},{"t":"All posts","d":"A summary of every post on the Auric Artisan blog.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/docs/posts.html","h":["What Shipped Since April","Auric Artisan Roadmap — Next Few Months","Welcome to the Auric Artisan Blog"],"x":" Newest first. Each entry gives the date, the category shown on the post, the link and a summary of what the post says. Date: 27 July 2026 Category: Product Link: https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/articles/2026 07 27 what shipped since april An honest account of what came out of the April roadmap by late July 2026, with the reasoning, and a list of what was not yet done: One browser extension instead of four. The colour, accessibility, developer tools and suite extensions were merged into one product, which gained a side panel, pickers that work on any page, a custom right click menu and a searchable settings view. Its accessibility checks grew from 20 to 97. The Analyzer's accessibility checks were rebuilt on a 112 rule engine covering ARIA 1.2, accessible names and APCA contrast, reporting an accessibility tree, a screen reader transcript, colour vision simulation and a VPAT export. The rules load only when you open the tab. Payments went live for one time purchases, with prices and what you receive both decided by the site rather than the browser. First party, consent based analytics arrived at the same time. The VS Code extension reached 0.13.2 , joining the plugins for Fig"},{"t":"Blog FAQ","d":"Short answers about the Auric Artisan blog.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/docs/faq.html","h":["How often are posts published?","What is the difference between the blog, the changelog and Learn?","Can I comment?","Is there a feed?"],"x":" Occasionally. The page describes them as \"occasional posts\". There were three at the time of writing. The blog explains plans and reasoning. The changelog ../../changelog/README.md records what changed in each release. Learn ../../learn/README.md holds the long form colour science course. Posts do not have comments. The welcome post invites questions and topic ideas by email or social media; see Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md for contact details. Yes: https://auricartisan.com/library/blog/rss.xml. "},{"t":"Blog: other material","d":"Supporting material for the blog.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Related related.md Where to find release detail, the Learn course and tool guides, and what the blog pages store. Back to the Blog overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Related","d":"Pages related to the blog, and a note on privacy.","p":"Website › Library › Blog","u":"website/library/blog/others/related.html","h":["Privacy"],"x":" Changelog ../../changelog/README.md — the versioned record of each release. Learn ../../learn/README.md — the long form colour science course. Documentation ../../documentation/README.md — user guides for every tool. Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md and VS Code extensions ../../../../vscode extensions/README.md — products the posts discuss. The blog page downloads the list of posts, and the newest post's opening paragraph, from auricartisan.com. It stores nothing about what you read. Analytics on the site follow your consent choices; see Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Changelog","d":"What the Auric Artisan changelog contains, how to search it, and where to find a summary of each release.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The changelog is the versioned record of Auric Artisan's releases: \"Every release, what was in it, and what it touched.\" It lists eleven entries, from v0.9.0 on 31 December 2025 to v0.9.11 on 12 August 2026, as a timeline, newest first. Each entry opens in place to show what changed and which parts of the platform it touched, with a link to the full release note. Its search reads the changes themselves, not just the headings, so you can ask it questions such as \"when did overage arrive?\" and it will find the release and highlight the words where they appear. Users who want to know what is new, or when something changed. Teams who need to check when a feature, plan change or fix arrived. The changelog: https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ From the site header: Learn menu › Changelog \"Releases & improvements\" . RSS feed: https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/rss.xml A single release: add its version after , for example https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ 0.9.10 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The newest release is already open. 2. Type a word into the search box, for example recorder . Matching releases stay, with the matches marked. 3. Selec"},{"t":"Changelog: docs","d":"Guides to the changelog page and a summary of every release.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The changelog page: search, type filters, Touched tags, expanding releases, links and RSS. releases.md releases.md A user facing summary of each of the eleven releases, newest first. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Changelog overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Use the changelog page to find a release, search every change, filter by type and by what was touched, and link to a release.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/docs/getting-started.html","h":["The page","A release entry","Search","Filter by type","Filter by what was touched","Open everything","Link to a release","Follow releases"],"x":" Open https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. Changelog , with the line \"Every release, what was in it, and what it touched. The search reads the changes themselves, not just the headings — so 'when did overage arrive?' is a question this page can answer.\" A facts line: 11 releases · v0.9.0 → v0.9.11 · 12 August 2026 — the latest . A search box, Search every change — overage, recorder, dark mode… , with a clear button. Type buttons: All , Releases , Patches . A count, for example 11 of 11 releases , and Expand all . The timeline: one entry per release, newest first. The newest is open when the page loads. The header shows the version for example v0.9.10 , a type badge release , patch , or another label such as Changelog and the date. Under it, a summary sentence — shortened while the entry is closed, in full when it is open. Select the header to open or close the entry. Open, it shows: Part What it contains What changed The list of changes. Notes Extra notes, where the release has them. Touched Tags for the parts of the platform the release touched, such as analyzer or pricing . Read the full release note A link to the release's own page. 1. Type a word or phrase. The timeline"},{"t":"Release summaries","d":"A user-facing summary of every release in the Auric Artisan changelog, newest first.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/docs/releases.html","h":["v0.9.11 — 12 August 2026 (release)","v0.9.10 — 27 July 2026 (release)","v0.9.9 — 5 June 2026 (release)","v0.9.8 — 2 May 2026 (patch)","v0.9.75 — 19 April 2026 (changelog entry)","v0.9.7 — 15 April 2026 (release)","v0.9.6 — 13 April 2026 (release)","v0.9.6 — 8 April 2026 (release)","v0.9.5 — 24 March 2026 (release)","v0.9.4 — 20 February 2026 (patch)","v0.9.0 — 31 December 2025 (release)"],"x":" A plain language summary of each release listed in the changelog, newest first. Each heading gives the version and date as published. For the full notes, open the release on https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/. The REST API became a metered product, and the site gained a recorder. API credits. API calls are now measured in credits: one credit is one standard request, and heavier endpoints cost more. Specialist includes 1,000,000 credits a month and Industrial Pro 10,000,000, refreshing each billing month. Subscriptions to Industrial Pro started before 12 August 2026 keep their previous allowance. Overage, only if you want it. Extra usage is opt in and prepaid at $1.00 ₹85 per 100,000 credits, so you are never invoiced after the fact. You can set a monthly spend cap, and a hard ceiling of ten times your included allowance always applies. Top ups. You can buy credit packs from Dashboard → API keys → Add credits . Purchased credits do not expire at the end of the period. API console on the dashboard's API Keys tab: burn down, projection, usage chart, spend by endpoint, credit balance, spend cap, overage switch and a live call feed. New API areas: colour science 63 colour spac"},{"t":"Changelog FAQ","d":"Short answers about the Auric Artisan changelog.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/docs/faq.html","h":["Why are there two v0.9.6 entries?","What is the difference between a release and a patch?","Where do I report a problem with a release?","Is every change listed?","Can I follow it?"],"x":" Two entries share version 0.9.6: \"System Integration & Validation\" 8 April 2026 and \"Vision Simulation & Color Model Lab Advancement\" 13 April 2026 . A link to 0.9.6 opens the newer one. Releases add features; patches fix and tidy. One entry, v0.9.75, is labelled Changelog rather than either. Release notes ask for steps to reproduce, your browser and operating system, the page or tool affected, and screenshots — and, for API problems, the x request id header from the response. See Help ../../../../help/README.md for how to get in touch. The changelog lists the notable changes in each release. Smaller changes between releases, and improvements to individual tools, may appear only on the tool's own pages and guides. Yes: https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/rss.xml. "},{"t":"Changelog: other material","d":"Supporting material for the changelog.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Related related.md The blog, account and API documentation, and a note on privacy. Back to the Changelog overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Related","d":"Pages related to the changelog, and a note on privacy.","p":"Website › Library › Changelog","u":"website/library/changelog/others/related.html","h":["Privacy"],"x":" Blog ../../blog/README.md — the reasoning behind releases, such as \"What Shipped Since April\". Account and billing ../../../account and billing/README.md — plans, tokens and API credits described in v0.9.11. Public API ../../../../services/public api/README.md — the REST API. Browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md — Auric Studio, consolidated in v0.9.10. Documentation ../../documentation/README.md — guides for each tool. The changelog page downloads the list of releases from auricartisan.com and filters it in your browser. It stores nothing about what you search. Analytics follow your consent choices; see Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Collections","d":"What the Collections page is, who it is for, and how to find, pin and open any Auric Artisan tool from it.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Collections is the catalogue of Auric Artisan's tools. It lists every tool, engine and generator on the site — from the URL Analyzer and Vision Simulation to the Font Library, LUT Lab and the Portfolio Builder — as a grid of cards you can search, filter, sort and pin. Each card says what the tool does in one sentence and opens the tool with one click. The page learns a little from how you use it. Tools you pin stay easy to reach, tools you open often can rise to the top of the Most used order, and the Recommended order leans on both. All of this is remembered only in the browser you are using; nothing about your pins or opens is sent to an account. Every tool in the collection is free to use on every plan. The lower part of the page shows the plans, which add conveniences such as cloud sync and watermark free exports rather than unlocking tools. Anyone new to Auric Artisan who wants to see everything the site offers. Regular users who want a fast way back to the tools they use most. Designers, developers, accessibility specialists and colour science students who want to browse by category Accessibility, Colorimetry, Gamut & Rendering, Perception, Spectral and more or by topic. Add"},{"t":"Collections docs","d":"The task guides and reference pages for the Collections tool catalogue.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the working guides for the Collections page at https://auricartisan.com/collections/. Start with the getting started tour, then use the task guides for specific jobs. The reference lists every control and every tool in the catalogue. File What it covers Getting started getting started.md A tour of the page from top to bottom and a first search. Browse, search and filter browse search and filter.md Searching, category and topic filters, sorting, grid or list, loading more. Pin tools and use recommendations pin and recommendations.md Pinning, the Pinned category, Most used, Recommended, and resetting them. Use the card menu card menu.md The right click menu on a card: card actions, view, density, columns, sort, system toggles. Show basic or advanced tools show basic or advanced tools.md Why the catalogue may show fewer than 30 tools, and how to change that. Reference reference.md Every control, sort order, filter and the full list of 30 tools. Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Missing tools, lost pins, the menu not opening and other problems. FAQ faq.md Short answers to common questions. Back to the Collections overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with Collections","d":"Tour the Collections page and find your first tool.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","The screen, top to bottom","Your first search","Next steps"],"x":" Collections is the page that lists every Auric Artisan tool. This guide walks through the page from top to bottom and ends with you opening a tool you found by search. Go to https://auricartisan.com/collections/, or open the Tools menu in the site header and choose All Tools . You do not need to sign in. The page opens with the heading \"All Auric Artisan tools, engines & generators in one place.\" Under it, three counters show: Tools — how many tools the catalogue is currently showing. Categories — how many different categories those tools belong to. Topics — how many different topic tags those tools carry. The counters follow your tool visibility setting see Show basic or advanced tools show basic or advanced tools.md , so they can be lower than the full catalogue of 30 tools. Beside the heading, three quick links lead to Tools this page , Learn the Learn library and Pricing the plans page . Start here is a shortlist of three featured tools shown as large cards in a slider. Each card shows the tool's name, a one line description and its category. The slider moves on by itself, one card at a time. A thin bar along the bottom fills up to show when the next card is due. It pauses whi"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Narrow the tool catalogue with search, category and topic filters, sort orders and layout options.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["Search","Filter by category","Filter by topic","How the filters combine","Sort the grid","Grid or list","Loading more tools","Search and sort while scrolled down","Result"],"x":" The All tools section of https://auricartisan.com/collections/ gives you four ways to narrow the catalogue: a search box, category filters, topic filters and a sort order. They work together, and the grid updates as soon as you change any of them. The search box sits above the grid and reads Search tools... . 1. Select the box and start typing. 2. The grid updates on every keystroke; you do not need to press Enter . 3. To clear the search, delete the text. How matching works: Matching ignores upper and lower case. Each word you type must appear somewhere in the tool's details. colour vision finds tools that mention both \"colour\" and \"vision\", in any order. A word can match part of a longer word. grad finds \"gradient\" and \"gradients\". The details searched are the tool's name, its one line description, its category, its address on the site, and its topic tags. Tip: The catalogue uses both spellings in places — some descriptions say \"colour\" and some tags say \"color\". If a search finds less than you expect, try the other spelling. Search does not treat them as the same word. Open Category in the Filter and sort panel. Each category is a tick box with the number of tools in it. The ca"},{"t":"Use the card menu","d":"Right-click any tool card to pin, open or copy it, and to change the grid's view, density, columns and sort order.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/card-menu.html","h":["Open the menu","Close the menu","Card","View","Density","Columns","Sort","System","Footer","Result"],"x":" Every card in the All tools grid has its own menu. It gathers the actions for that one tool together with the settings for the whole grid, so you can change the layout without scrolling back to the controls. 1. Scroll to All tools on https://auricartisan.com/collections/. 2. Right click any card. On a keyboard, move focus to a card and press the context menu key or Shift + F10 . 3. The menu opens at the pointer. If there is not enough room, it moves so it stays on screen. The menu replaces the site's usual right click menu while you are over a card. Right click anywhere else on the page to get the site's usual menu see Site features ../../../site features/README.md . The top line of the menu shows the card's title. A small pin mark appears before the title when that tool is pinned. Any of these closes it: select anywhere outside the menu; press Escape ; scroll the page; resize the window; choose Open , New tab or Copy link . The layout settings View , Density , Columns , Sort keep the menu open so you can try several in a row. Four buttons act on the card you right clicked: Button What it does Pin / Unpin Pins or unpins the tool, exactly like the pin button on the card. The button"},{"t":"Pin tools and use recommendations","d":"Pin the tools you rely on, see your most used tools first, understand the Recommended order, and reset all of it.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/pin-and-recommendations.html","h":["Pin a tool","Most used","Recommended","Reset your pins and usage","Result"],"x":" Collections can put the tools that matter to you first. It uses two signals, both kept only in the browser you are using: Pins — tools you have marked yourself. Opens — how often, and how recently, you have opened each tool from the Collections page. From these the page builds three groupings: Pinned , Most used and Recommended . 1. Find the tool's card in All tools . 2. Select the pin button in the card's corner. Its label reads \"Pin\" followed by the tool's name. 3. The button fills in to show the tool is pinned, and the card is marked as pinned. You can also right click the card and choose Pin in the card menu see Use the card menu card menu.md . To unpin, select the same button again its label now reads \"Unpin\" and the tool's name , or choose Unpin in the card menu. The Pinned category. A Pinned tick box appears at the top of Category in the Filter and sort panel, with a count. Tick it to see only your pinned tools. When you unpin your last tool, the box disappears and the filter switches itself off. Pinned first. Choose Pinned first in the sort list to bring pinned tools to the top while keeping everything else below them. Start here. The three card Start here shortlist shows "},{"t":"Show basic or advanced tools","d":"Understand why Collections may show fewer than 30 tools, and switch between Basic, Advanced, Everything and a custom set.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/show-basic-or-advanced-tools.html","h":["Why you might see fewer than 30 tools","Tools shown in each setting","Change the setting","Result"],"x":" Auric Artisan has 30 tools. Some are everyday tools, such as the Image Picker and the Font Library; others are scientific tools, such as Illuminants, Tone Mapping and the Psychophysics Engine. The site lets you choose which of these you see, and Collections follows that choice. Every tool in the catalogue is labelled with a mode: Basic — beginner friendly, everyday tools. Advanced — scientific, diagnostic and power user tools. Both — tools that belong to every set. The URL Analyzer and the Portfolio Builder are the two tools marked this way. The site wide tool visibility setting decides which modes are shown. Until you choose otherwise, the site uses Basic , so a first visit to Collections shows the basic tools and the two tools marked Both . The hero counters, the category counts and the result count all reflect the tools in view, not the full catalogue. You can see any card's mode in its tooltip: hover over the card and read the Mode line. Setting What Collections shows Number of tools Basic the default Basic tools plus the two tools marked Both. 14 Advanced Advanced tools plus the two tools marked Both. 18 Everything Every tool. 30 Custom Only the tools you have switched on, on"},{"t":"Collections reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order and menu item on the Collections page, and the full catalogue of 30 tools.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/reference.html","h":["Page sections","Hero counters","Start here slider","Filter and sort panel","Results bar","Cards","Loading","Floating search button","Card menu (right-click)","Plans section","What is remembered","Tool catalogue"],"x":" This page lists every control on https://auricartisan.com/collections/ and every tool in the catalogue. For step by step help, see the task guides in this folder. Section What it contains Hero The page heading, three counters Tools , Categories , Topics and three quick links Tools , Learn , Pricing . Start here A slider of three featured tools, with previous and next buttons, dots and a slide counter. All tools The full catalogue with the Filter and sort panel, search box, view switch and cards. Featured Highlights Two short notes: Accessibility & Analysis and Creative Generation . Plans \"Every tool here is free. Upgrade for superpowers.\" The four plans with billing and currency switches. Explore All Collections Closing banner with Browse All Collections and See full pricing & FAQ . Counter What it counts Tools Tools the catalogue is showing under your tool visibility setting. Categories Different categories among those tools. Topics Different topic tags among those tools. Control What it does Values or range Default Previous button Shows the previous featured tool. — — Next button Shows the next featured tool. — — Dots Jump to a featured tool. Each dot's label is \"Show\" and the t"},{"t":"Troubleshooting Collections","d":"Fix common problems on the Collections page, from missing tools to lost pins.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["A tool I know exists is not in the grid","The grid is empty and says \"No matching tools\"","The grid is not in alphabetical order, although Sort shows \"Title A to Z\"","\"Newest first\" and \"Oldest first\" do not change anything","My pins or usage history have gone","\"Most used\" does not show a tool I use every day","Right-clicking a card shows the site's normal menu, not the card menu","The Columns setting makes cards tiny, or seems to do nothing","The featured slider keeps moving while I read it","The page says \"Unable to load tools.\"","Prices show in the wrong currency"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom, the reason, and what to do. Why: The site's tool visibility setting hides tools that do not match it. The default setting, Basic , shows 14 of the 30 tools; advanced tools such as Illuminants or LUT Lab are hidden. A Custom setting hides every tool you switched off. What to do: Open the Advanced Kit and choose Everything , or switch the tool back on in Custom . The grid updates at once. See Show basic or advanced tools show basic or advanced tools.md . Why: Your search words, ticked categories and ticked topics together match nothing. Every search word must appear in a tool's details, and a tool must pass the category and topic filters as well. What to do: 1. Shorten the search, or try the other spelling color or colour . 2. Untick all Topics . 3. Untick all Category boxes, including Pinned . Why: When the page first opens, the grid is in the catalogue's own order. The Sort list shows its first option, Title A to Z , but that order has not been applied yet. What to do: Choose a different order and then Title A to Z again, or right click a card and select Title under Sort . The card menu's Reset button also applies Title A to Z . Why: Tools have no pub"},{"t":"Collections FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Collections tool catalogue.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/docs/faq.html","h":["How many tools are there?","Are the tools free?","Do I need an account to pin tools?","Will my pins appear on my phone too?","What is the difference between Pinned, Most used and Recommended?","Does Auric Artisan see which tools I pin or open here?","How do I reset the page to how it was?","Can I share a link to a tool?","Why does the right-click menu look different on cards?","Why are some categories spelled \"Color\"?","Where do I find guides for each tool?"],"x":" Thirty. With the default Basic tool visibility setting, Collections shows 14 of them; choose Everything in the Advanced Kit to see all 30. See Show basic or advanced tools show basic or advanced tools.md . Yes. Every card says Free to use , and the plans section states \"Every tool free on every plan\". Paid plans add conveniences such as cloud sync, version history, batch power, API access and watermark free exports. No. Pins work without signing in. They are stored in the browser you are using. No. Pins and usage history stay in the browser where you made them. Signing in does not copy them to other devices. Pinned is the tools you chose yourself. Most used is the tools you open most often and most recently from this page. Recommended combines your pins and opens with how central a tool is to the site's main subjects and how fully it is described. See Pin tools and use recommendations pin and recommendations.md . The Collections page keeps pins and opens in your browser and does not send them to Auric Artisan. The site's own analytics, which run only with your consent, are covered by the privacy policy. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Right click a card and select Reset to rest"},{"t":"Collections: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Collections page: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages and privacy.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the supporting pages for Collections: the terms it uses, its keyboard and mouse actions, what its orders and counts can and cannot tell you, related pages, and what it stores. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms such as pin, topic, mode, frecency and density. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and mouse actions on the page. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the counts, sort orders and recommendations mean, and their limits. Related related.md Related pages, kits and libraries. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network. Back to the Collections overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Collections shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and mouse actions on the Collections page.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Mouse","Keyboard"],"x":" Action Result Select a card Opens the tool and counts one open towards Most used . Select a card's pin button Pins or unpins the tool. Right click a card Opens the card menu. Right click elsewhere Opens the site's usual right click menu. Hover a card Shows a tooltip with category, mode, address and tags. Hover the Start here slider Pauses autoplay. Keys Where Result Tab Anywhere Moves between links, buttons and filter boxes. Left / Right Start here slider, when focused Previous or next featured tool. Context menu key, or Shift + F10 A focused card Opens the card menu. Escape Card menu Closes the menu. Escape Floating search panel Closes the panel and returns focus to its button. Space A focused tick box Ticks or unticks a category or topic. The site wide shortcuts, such as Alt + R for reading mode and Alt + T to switch theme, also work here. See Site features ../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Collections glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used on the Collections page.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Card One tool's tile in the grid: artwork, category, name, description and a pin button. Catalogue order The fixed order in which tools are listed in the catalogue. The Reference lists all 30 tools in this order. Category The broad group a tool belongs to, such as Colorimetry or Utilities. Each tool has exactly one. Card menu The menu that opens when you right click a card, with card actions and grid settings. Columns How many cards sit side by side in grid view. Auto fits the screen; 2 , 3 or 4 force a number. Density The spacing between cards. Cozy is normal; Compact is tighter. Everything The tool visibility setting that shows all 30 tools. Frecency A mix of frequency and recency: how often you opened a tool, weighted towards recent opens. The Most used order is based on it. Mode A tool's level: Basic everyday , Advanced scientific or power user or Both shown in every setting . Open Selecting a card to go to the tool. Each open is counted towards Most used . Pin A mark you put on a tool so it is grouped under Pinned and comes first in Start here and Pinned first . Reading mode A site setting that makes pages calmer and easier to read. The card menu's Reading switch"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Collections counts, sort orders and recommendations tell you, and what they do not.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Counts","Search","Sort orders","What Collections is not"],"x":" Collections is a catalogue, not a measurement tool. Its numbers and orders are simple, local and predictable. This page says what they mean. The hero counters and category counts cover only the tools your tool visibility setting shows. With the default Basic setting, Tools reads 14, not 30. Topics counts different tags among the tools in view. The Topics filter lists only the 14 most common of them, so a rarer tag cannot be chosen as a filter; type it into the search box instead. Search is a plain text match. It does not correct typing mistakes and does not know that \"color\" and \"colour\" mean the same thing. Every word you type must match. Adding a word can only narrow the results. Newest first and Oldest first have no effect, because tools carry no dates. Most used counts only opens from the Collections page itself, in this browser. It knows nothing about how you use the tools elsewhere, or on other devices. Recommended is a fixed recipe, not a learning system. It adds points for your pins and opens, for mentions of core subjects such as accessibility, WCAG, contrast, gamut, HDR and ICC and for how fully a tool is described. It is a starting point, not advice about which tool is "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Collections page stores in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" The Collections page remembers a few things in your browser's local storage. None of it is sent to Auric Artisan or saved to your account. What Why How to remove it Pinned tools To show Pinned , Pinned first and your Start here picks. Unpin each tool, or clear this site's data. Tool opens count and last time To build Most used and part of Recommended . Clear this site's data. Grid or list view To keep your chosen layout. Choose the other view, or clear this site's data. Density and columns To keep your card menu layout choices. Select Reset in the card menu. Tool visibility setting To show the tool set you chose in the Advanced Kit. Change it in the Advanced Kit. Because these are stored per browser, a private window starts with none of them and forgets them when it closes. The page downloads the tool catalogue and card artwork from auricartisan.com when it loads. Copy link writes to your device's clipboard only; nothing is sent. The page can show advertising. Advertising and analytics on the site follow your cookie and consent choices. For the site's full privacy policy, consent choices and cookie settings, see Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Related pages","d":"Pages, kits and libraries that work alongside the Collections catalogue.","p":"Website › Library › Collections","u":"website/library/collections/others/related.html","h":["Settings that change Collections","Other libraries","Tools in the catalogue","Plans"],"x":" Advanced Kit ../../../kits/advanced kit/README.md — chooses Basic , Advanced , Everything or a Custom tool set, which decides which tools Collections shows. Site features ../../../site features/README.md — the site theme, reading mode, the settings panel and the site's usual right click menu. Library overview ../../README.md — every part of the Auric Artisan library. Colour libraries ../../colour libraries/README.md — searchable libraries of colours, palettes, gradients, harmonies, shades and accessible colour pairs. Learn ../../learn/README.md — articles on colour science and accessibility, many with interactive labs. Documentation ../../documentation/README.md — user guides and references for the tools. Documentation for some of the tools in the catalogue: URL Analyzer ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md the Analyze URLs card and Vision Simulation ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md . Basic Tools ../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md and the Design System Generator ../../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md . Font Library ../../../tools/colour workspace/font library/README.md and Icon Libr"},{"t":"Colour libraries","d":"An overview of the six Auric Artisan colour libraries and a map of their documentation.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/README.html","h":["The six libraries","Which library do I need?","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan has six colour libraries. Each is a large, searchable collection of generated colour data that you can browse, filter, inspect and copy or export. They share one idea: every item carries its measurements with it, so you can choose colours by what they do — how they contrast, how they step, how they read to people with colour vision deficiencies — and not only by how they look in a thumbnail. The libraries are free to use and need no account. They open in any modern browser. Library What it holds Address Color Library color library/README.md 8,192 measured colours, each in seven colour spaces with contrast and colour blindness data. https://auricartisan.com/library/color/ Palette Library palette library/README.md 5,000,000 generated palettes, filterable by hue, lightness, chroma, harmony method and WCAG. https://auricartisan.com/library/palette/ Gradient Library gradient library/README.md 8,192 gradients with OKLCH metadata, 2 to 46 stops, and a measured verdict on banding. https://auricartisan.com/library/gradient/ Harmony Library harmony library/README.md 8,192 colour harmonies across 23 colour theory schemes, plus a tool that names the scheme your own colours form."},{"t":"Accessibility Library","d":"What the Accessibility Color Pair Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to find text colours that pass on any background.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Accessibility Library — the Accessibility Color Pair Library — answers one question: \"What may I write on this? \" You choose a background colour the page calls it the ground and a contrast target, and the page draws a map of every foreground colour, with a line showing exactly where text starts to pass. Contrast depends on both colours continuously, so the answer is a territory, not a list, and the boundary moves with hue: at the same lightness, yellow gives far more contrast than blue, so \"just make it darker\" means different things for different hues. Around the map, the page gives you a concrete answer — up to twelve foreground colours, one per 30° of hue, that clear your target on your ground, ready to copy as CSS — and an audit for colours you already have: paste your palette and each colour is placed on the map, with how much lighter or darker it would need to be to pass. Behind all of this is an index of 5,000,000 scored foreground and background pairs. Like the other libraries, it is defined by a seed rather than stored, so any record — for example acc 91 — can be cited in an audit and recomputed by whoever reads it. Every figure is computed in your browser. Designers "},{"t":"Accessibility Library documentation","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Accessibility Color Pair Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour, and a first set of passing text colours. read the contrast map.md read the contrast map.md Grounds, targets, the map, its lines, the readout, swap and keyboard control. use the picks.md use the picks.md The twelve suggested foregrounds and Copy as CSS . check your own colours.md check your own colours.md Or bring your own : pasting a palette and reading what each colour needs. look up and browse the index.md look up and browse the index.md The five million pair index: record lookup and browsing. reference.md reference.md Every control, output and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Accessibility Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Accessibility Library, learn the screen, and find passing text colours for a background.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: text colours for a dark green banner"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/accessibility/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Accessibility Library under Libraries . The map draws straight away; it needs nothing from the network. Kicker Auric Artisan · Accessibility ; headline What may I write on this? ; and a line with Corpus 5,000,000 , Seed 9001 , Every figure computed in your browser , and Read the API guide → . A note starting Automate this may appear: the same job is available through the site's REST API — 8 API credits per call to POST /v1/accessibility/map — with API docs . Select × to dismiss it. Ground — four preset swatches 0D0D0D , 1D2A3E , FFFCF7 , 1B4D3E , a colour picker for any other ground, and Swap . Target — 3:1 , 4.5:1 or 7:1 . Territory — the share of the map that passes, as a percentage. On the left, the contrast map: hue from left 0°, red to right 360° , lightness from bottom 0 to top 1.0 . Three lines mark where contrast reaches 3:1, 4.5:1 and 7:1, and the part of the map that fails your target is dimmed. A small caret marks your current foreground. On the right, the readout: a text specimen in your foreground on the ground, the contrast ratio with a verdict, a table of figu"},{"t":"Check your own colours","d":"Paste your palette into \"Or bring your own\" to place each colour on the map and see how much lightness each failing colour needs.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/check-your-own-colours.html","h":["Steps","The table","Rules for pasting","Example"],"x":" Or bring your own audits a palette you already have against the current ground and target. 1. Choose the ground your palette will sit on, and a target. 2. Click in the box under Or bring your own and paste your colours as hex codes, for example D3AF37 8A6D16 6B7280 136B39 B91C1C . Separators do not matter: spaces, commas or new lines all work. 3. Wait a moment. Each colour is placed on the map as a pin at its real hue and lightness, and appears in the table. 4. Read the table below . Failing colours also get a line on the map drawn up or down to the target line, showing the move they need. 5. Change the ground or target to re check the whole palette at once. Result: every colour in your palette placed on the map, with a pass or fail and the lightness change each failure needs. Column Meaning Colour The swatch and hex code. Here Its contrast ratio against the current ground; failing ratios are marked. Lightness Its OKLCH lightness as a percentage. Needs nothing if it passes; otherwise +N% lightness , the change needed at its hue to reach the line; or unreachable if no lightness at its hue can pass on this ground. The \"+N%\" is the size of the change. On a dark ground it means lighte"},{"t":"Look up and browse the index","d":"Look up any of five million scored colour pairs by record id, read its WCAG, APCA and Auric SD scores, and browse pairs that pass.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/look-up-and-browse-the-index.html","h":["Look up a record","Browse the index","API"],"x":" The index is a set of five million foreground and background pairs, each scored. As the page explains, it is \"defined by a seed rather than stored\": any record is a function of the seed 9001 and its number, so a record cited in an audit can be recomputed by anyone who reads it. 1. Scroll to The index . 2. Type a record id such as acc 91 , or a plain number such as 325 , into the box A record id like acc 91, or an index like 325 . 3. Select Look up , or press Enter . Record ids are acc followed by the record's number in base 36; acc 91 is record 325. The result shows a specimen of the pair and: Fact Meaning Pair Foreground on background, for example 4E1229 on D86062 . Contrast The WCAG 2 contrast ratio, for example 4.00:1 . APCA The APCA Lc value, rounded, for example 35 . Auric SD Auric Artisan's combined score from 0 to 100 and its grade, for example 43.6 · F . Recommended for The strongest use the pair supports, for example large text . The examples are the real values of acc 91 . A note underneath gives the seed, the index and the batch it belongs to — \"Anyone with the same three numbers recomputes the same pair, which is what makes this citable.\" Messages: Not a record id. The"},{"t":"Read the contrast map","d":"Choose a ground and a target, explore the contrast map by pointer or keyboard, and read the ratio, APCA value, vision margin and distance to the line.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/read-the-contrast-map.html","h":["What the map shows","Choose a ground","Choose a target","Explore","The readout","Swap foreground and ground","Result"],"x":" Across: hue, from 0° red through 60° yellow , 120° green , 180° cyan , 240° blue and 300° magenta to 360°. Up: OKLCH lightness, from 0 black at the bottom to 1.0 white at the top. Each point: the most colourful colour your screen's sRGB range can show at that hue and lightness. Three lines: where contrast against the ground reaches 3:1 dashed amber , 4.5:1 body solid green and 7:1 AAA dashed pale blue . Dimmed area: the part of the map that fails your chosen target. On a dark ground the passing region is above the line lighter colours ; on a light ground it is below darker colours . Notice that the line is not flat: yellows and greens pass at lower lightness than blues and purples, because they carry more luminance. A ground is the background your text will sit on. 1. Select one of the preset swatches: 0D0D0D near black , 1D2A3E dark navy, the default , FFFCF7 warm off white or 1B4D3E dark green . 2. Or use the colour picker beside them to choose any ground. The lines, the dimmed area, Territory and the picks all update for the new ground. Target Meaning 3:1 Large text and user interface components such as icons and borders WCAG AA . 4.5:1 Body text WCAG AA . The default. 7:1 Body"},{"t":"Use the picks","d":"Take up to twelve passing foreground colours for your ground, preview them, and copy them as CSS custom properties.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/use-the-picks.html","h":["How the picks are chosen","Steps"],"x":" The section headed N that work on this ground for example 12 that work on this ground is the page's concrete answer: foreground colours that clear your target on your ground. One pick per 30° of hue, starting at 15°, so up to twelve picks cover the whole colour wheel. Each is placed a little inside its hue's line — 10% of lightness into the passing region — so you have room to adjust it later without it dropping out. Every pick clears the target. If a hue cannot reach the target on this ground, or a pick would land just under it, that hue is left out, so you may see fewer than twelve. The text under the heading repeats the target and ground, for example \"everything here clears 4.5:1 on 1D2A3E \". 1. Choose your ground and target in the control bar see Read the contrast map read the contrast map.md . 2. Scroll to the picks. Each card shows Readable and a sample sentence in the pick on your ground, with its ratio and hex code. Hover a card to see its ratio and hue. 3. Select a card to move the map's caret onto that colour and read its full figures. 4. Select Copy as CSS to copy the whole set. The button reads Copied or Copy failed if your browser blocked the clipboard . Result: CSS l"},{"t":"Accessibility Library reference","d":"Every control, output and message in the Accessibility Color Pair Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","Control bar","The map","Readout","Picks","Or bring your own","All of this from your own code","The index","Messages"],"x":" Everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/accessibility/. Item Content Kicker Auric Artisan · Accessibility Headline What may I write on this? Facts Corpus 5,000,000 , Seed 9001 , Every figure computed in your browser Read the API guide → The accessibility corpus API guide. Automate this note 8 API credits per call to POST /v1/accessibility/map ; API docs ; × dismisses. Control What it does Values Default Ground swatches Set the background. 0D0D0D , 1D2A3E , FFFCF7 , 1B4D3E 1D2A3E Colour picker Any other ground. Any colour — Swap Puts the current foreground on the ground and moves the caret to the old ground. — — Target The contrast threshold. 3:1 , 4.5:1 , 7:1 4.5:1 Territory Share of the map that clears the target. 0% to 100% — Element Meaning Horizontal axis Hue: 0° red , 60° yellow , 120° green , 180° cyan , 240° blue , 300° magenta , 360° . Vertical axis OKLCH lightness, 0 to 1.0 . Colour at each point The most colourful sRGB colour at that hue and lightness. Lines 3:1 dashed amber , 4.5:1 body solid green , 7:1 AAA dashed pale blue . Dimmed area Fails the current target. Caret The current foreground. Starts at hue 190°, lightness 0.78. Pins Your pasted colours; failures"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Fewer than twelve picks appear","\"unreachable at this hue\"","Territory is very small","Pasted colours do not appear","A colour passes here but fails in an audit tool","\"Copy failed\"","The browse grid shows few cards","The index lookup says \"Not a record id\""],"x":" Why: Some hues cannot reach the target on this ground at any lightness, or their pick would land just under the target. Those hues are left out rather than showing a failing colour. What to do: Lower the target, or choose a ground further from mid grey very dark or very light . Why: On a mid tone ground, some hues never reach the target however light or dark they are. What to do: Move to a different hue, change the ground, or use Swap to explore from the other side. Why: Mid tone grounds leave little room: text must be much lighter or much darker, and at some hues neither is possible. What to do: Use a darker or lighter ground if the design allows. Territory tells you how much room each ground leaves. Why: Only hex codes that start with are read, with 3 to 6 digits. Names, rgb and hex codes without are ignored. Only the first 24 colours are placed. What to do: Paste hex codes with , for example 6B7280 . Why: This page measures against the ground you chose, with the WCAG 2 formula. An audit tool may use the actual background behind the text including images or transparency , text size, or a different method such as APCA. What to do: Check that the ground matches the real background"},{"t":"Accessibility Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/docs/faq.html","h":["What contrast do I need?","What is APCA?","Why does the line curve?","What is the Vision margin?","What is the index for?","Is anything sent to a server?","Can I automate this?","Do I need an account?"],"x":" Under WCAG 2: 4.5:1 for normal body text AA , 3:1 for large text at least 18 point, or 14 point bold and for user interface components and graphics, and 7:1 for body text at AAA. The Advanced Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a newer contrast measure developed for the draft WCAG 3. It gives a lightness contrast value, Lc, from about −108 to 106; the sign shows polarity negative for light text on dark . Higher absolute values mean more readable text. The page shows it alongside the WCAG 2 ratio. Because contrast depends on luminance, and luminance depends on hue as well as lightness: yellows and greens are much brighter than blues and purples at the same OKLCH lightness. How far apart the two colours stay when viewed as someone with each of eight colour vision deficiencies, cataracts or low vision would see them, taking the worst case, on a 0 to 1 scale. A low margin means the pair can merge for some people even if its contrast ratio passes. It is a reproducible set of five million scored pairs. Any record id, such as acc 91 , always gives the same pair, so you can cite it in an audit. No. Every figure on the page is computed in your browser. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Yes, th"},{"t":"Accessibility Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Accessibility Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Ground, target, territory, APCA, Auric SD and other terms. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard control of the map and other keys. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the figures measure, and what they do not. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What is computed locally and what uses the network. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Accessibility Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Accessibility Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard control of the contrast map and other keys in the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["The map (focus it first)","Elsewhere"],"x":" Keys Effect Left / Right Hue −5° / +5°. Shift + Left / Right Hue −25° / +25°. Up / Down Lightness +0.02 / −0.02. Shift + Up / Down Lightness +0.10 / −0.10. Home Lightness 1 top . End Lightness 0 bottom . Keys or action Effect Enter in the index box Looks up the record. Select a pick Moves the caret to it. Select an index card Loads its pair into the map. The site wide shortcuts also work here. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Accessibility Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning AA, AAA WCAG conformance levels. For normal text, AA needs 4.5:1 and AAA needs 7:1. APCA Lc Advanced Perceptual Contrast Algorithm; its lightness contrast value Lc runs from about −108 to 106. Larger absolute values are more readable. Auric SD Auric Artisan's combined 0–100 score for a pair WCAG, APCA, vision separation, lightness gap, hue gap , graded S, A, B, C, D or F. Caret The marker on the map showing the current foreground. Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of the luminance difference between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1. Corpus The five million scored pairs behind the index. Foreground The text or icon colour. Gamut The range of colours a colour space or screen can show. The map shows the sRGB gamut. Ground The background colour you are testing against. Large text At least 18 point 24 CSS pixels , or 14 point about 18.7 CSS pixels bold. OKLCH A perceptual colour space: lightness 0 to 1 , chroma and hue. Pick One of up to twelve suggested passing foregrounds. Record id acc followed by a record's number in base 36. Seed The fixed number 9001 from which every record is derived. Target The contrast threshold you are testing: 3:1, 4.5:1 or 7:1. Territory The share"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Accessibility Library measures, how precisely, and what it is not.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The map","The figures","The index","What it is not"],"x":" The map is drawn at 72 hue columns one every 5° , and the lines are found for each column. Between columns the line is drawn straight, so a pick or pin near a sharp bend can sit very slightly on the other side. The ratio in the readout is always exact for the colour under the caret. Each point shows the most colourful colour sRGB allows at that hue and lightness. Less colourful versions of the same hue and lightness have slightly different luminance, so their contrast can differ a little from the map's. Territory is the share of this drawn slice that passes; it is a comparison between grounds, not a count of all possible colours. Contrast ratio uses the WCAG 2 formula exactly. APCA is computed by the page's own implementation of the APCA method. APCA is part of draft work towards WCAG 3 and is not yet a formal requirement; use it as a second opinion. Vision margin is based on standard simulation matrices for eight colour vision deficiencies plus simple models of cataracts and low vision. Simulations are a design aid, not a diagnosis, and real people vary. The Auric SD score and the Recommended for labels are Auric Artisan's own combinations of these measures. They are guidance, no"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Accessibility Library computes locally and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/privacy.html","h":["Computed in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" Everything the page shows — the map, the lines, the picks, your pasted colours, the index records and the browse grid — is computed in your browser. The colours you paste and the grounds you try are not sent anywhere and are not remembered after you leave. This page has no saved list. The only thing it remembers is whether you dismissed the Automate this note, so it stays hidden. The page itself and a small description of the corpus are downloaded from auricartisan.com. If the description does not arrive, the page uses the same built in values and carries on. Copy as CSS writes only to your clipboard. The API section links to other pages; an API key is only needed if you call the API yourself. Advertising and analytics follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Accessibility Library was added in release 0.9.9 as part of the library expansion. See the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The page has since been rebuilt around the question \"What may I write on this?\": a contrast map for any ground, twelve passing picks, a palette audit, and the five million pair index for lookup and browsing. The earlier version was a catalogue of pair cards with tabs for inspecting, auditing and exporting; the existing Accessibility Library user guide in the documentation library still describes that version. These changes are not listed as a separate changelog release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Accessibility Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Accessibility Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/accessibility-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","Guides and API"],"x":" Color Library ../../color library/README.md — 8,192 colours with contrast on white and black. Shade Library ../../shade library/README.md — scales with a per token contrast ladder. Palette Library ../../palette library/README.md , Harmony Library ../../harmony library/README.md and Gradient Library ../../gradient library/README.md . Contrast Checker ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — check one pair in detail. URL Analyzer ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — audit a whole page. Vision Simulation ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — see images through different kinds of colour vision. Accessibility Checklist ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/accessibility checklist/README.md . Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contrast — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 wcag contrast accessible color Color Blindness and Color Vision Deficiency — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 color blindness cvd Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces T"},{"t":"Color Library","d":"What the Color Library is, who it is for, where to find it and how to look up your first colour.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Color Library is a searchable atlas of 8,192 colours. Every colour in it carries the same set of precomputed data: its values in seven colour notations HEX, RGB, HSL, CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ , OKLab, OKLCH and CMYK , perceptual measures such as chroma and relative luminance, its contrast ratio against white and against black, how it looks to people with three kinds of colour blindness, and five descriptive labels emotion, art movement, mood, design usage and design tag . The page headline sums it up: \"Eight thousand colours, measured. \" You can use the atlas in three ways. You can paste a colour you already have, in almost any CSS format, and see the five catalogued colours nearest to it and what each of them can do. You can ask for what a colour has to do, such as \"readable on white\" or \"for typography\", and see how many colours are left after each requirement. Or you can browse the whole atlas with a search box, eight filters and six sort orders, then open any colour to read everything the atlas knows about it. Everything you browse is worked out in your browser from data the page downloads. You can copy a colour in six formats, download it as JSON, SVG or PNG, download the whole filte"},{"t":"Color Library documentation","d":"The list of task guides, the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the Color Library, the full reference of its controls and outputs, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started if you have not used the page before. Go to the Reference when you need the exact threshold behind a filter or the exact text a copy button produces. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour of its sections and tabs, and a first lookup find nearest colours.md find nearest colours.md Pasting a colour in any CSS format and reading its five nearest atlas colours choose by requirement.md choose by requirement.md The seven requirement chips, what each one tests and how the counts work browse search and filter.md browse search and filter.md Search, filter inside results, the eight filters, sort, shuffle, random and reset read a colour.md read a colour.md The The colour tab: contrast verdict, colour blindness values, every notation, neighbours read the statistics.md read the statistics.md The four histograms on the Stats tab copy and export.md copy and export.md Copy formats, single colour downloads and bulk downloads, with examples save colours.md save colours.md Saving with th"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Color Library, learn what each section and tab does, and look up your first colour.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: find out what your brand colour is good for","Next steps"],"x":" This page takes you through opening the Color Library, what you see on screen, and a first task from start to finish. 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/color/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Color Library under Libraries . 2. Wait for the atlas to load. While it loads, the grid area shows Loading color atlas… . When it is ready, the grid fills with colour tiles and the counter under it reads, for example, 1–48 of 8,192 colours . The page needs a network connection to load the atlas. If loading fails you see Could not load color atlas with the reason; see Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . The page runs top to bottom in this order. The kicker reads Auric Artisan · Colour and the headline Eight thousand colours, measured. A line under it shows Atlas 8,192 , Spaces 7 and Every figure precomputed , and a link, Read the API reference → , to the site's public REST API documentation. Under the heading you may see a note that starts Automate this . It names the REST API call that does the same job and how many API credits it costs, links to API docs , and has a dismiss button × . Once you dismiss it, it stays hidden in this browser. API credits are separate"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Narrow the 8,192-colour atlas with the two search boxes, eight filters and six sort orders, and move around the grid.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["Search","Filter inside results","The eight filters","Sort","Shuffle, random and reset","Moving around the grid","Result"],"x":" The Browse the atlas section and the Library tab hold everything you need to narrow the atlas and scan it. This page covers each control in the order you meet it. The first search box reads Search by hex a6e223 or id… . 1. Select the box, or press / anywhere on the page outside a text field to jump to it. 2. Type part of a hex code, an atlas id, or a label. The grid updates a moment after you stop typing. A colour matches when every word you type appears in at least one of these: its hex code, its atlas id, its emotion, its art movement, its mood or its design usage. Matching ignores case and accepts part words, so a6e matches A6E223 , and rom matches both romantic and Romanticism . Note: Ids match as text, so typing 12 also finds ids such as 120 , 1203 and 4812 . The second row, Filter inside results , has its own box hex, emotion, mood, usage… and a Clear button. It works exactly like the first search box; the words in both boxes are combined, and every word must match. Use it to add a narrowing word without editing the first search. Clear empties only this second box. The filters sit at the top of the Library tab. Each is a drop down list; choose a value to keep only matching c"},{"t":"Choose colours by requirement","d":"Use the seven requirement chips to narrow the atlas by what a colour has to do, and read what each requirement costs.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/choose-by-requirement.html","h":["The seven requirements","Steps","How the chips combine","Where the labels come from"],"x":" The Or from what it has to do section lets you ask for a job rather than for coordinates. Instead of \"hue 199, chroma 0.10\", you ask for \"readable on white\" or \"for typography\". Each requirement is a chip, and each chip shows how many colours would be left if you selected it, so you can see the cost of one more requirement before you add it. Chip A colour passes when Colours that pass on their own Readable on white Its contrast on white is 4.5:1 or more WCAG AA for body text . 2,998 Readable on black Its contrast on black is 4.5:1 or more. 5,344 Vivid Its OKLCH chroma is 0.18 or more. 2,707 Muted Its OKLCH chroma is below 0.06. 695 Calm Its emotion label is calm . 843 For typography Its design usage label is typography . 819 As an accent Its design tag label is accent . 822 The last column is the number each chip shows when no other chip is selected, out of 8,192. 1. Scroll to Or from what it has to do . 2. Read the numbers on the chips. Each is the count you would get by selecting that chip now. 3. Select a chip, for example Readable on white . It is highlighted, and the grid in Browse the atlas now shows only colours that pass. 4. Read the line under the chips. It now says, for "},{"t":"Copy and export","d":"Copy one colour in six formats, download it as JSON, SVG or PNG, and download every matching colour in seven formats.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/copy-and-export.html","h":["Copy or download one colour","Download every matching colour","Result"],"x":" The Export tab has two parts: Selection , for the one colour you have open, and Visible set , for every colour that currently matches your chips, searches and filters. You can reach the tab directly, or select Export visible on the Library tab. 1. Open a colour select its tile . See Read a colour read a colour.md . 2. Select the Export tab. The first card is headed Selection · and the colour's hex code. 3. Under Copy formats , select a format. The text goes to your clipboard and a short message confirms it, such as HEX copied . 4. Under Download , select a file type. Your browser saves the file. If no colour is open, the card reads No color selected. Click any tile in the Library tab to enable selection exports. Examples are for the atlas colour 76CDF6 . Button What is copied Example HEX The hex code in capitals. 76CDF6 RGB A CSS rgb value with commas. rgb 118, 205, 246 HSL A CSS hsl value, whole numbers. hsl 199 88% 71% Lab A CSS lab value, two decimals. lab 78.56% 15.21 28.22 OKLCH A CSS oklch value. oklch 80.89% 0.102 230.17 CSS variables A :root block with four custom properties. See below The CSS variables button copies: css :root { color hex: 76cdf6; color rgb: 118, 205, 246"},{"t":"Find a colour's nearest neighbours","d":"Paste a colour in any CSS format and read the five catalogued colours closest to it, with their distance and contrast.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/find-nearest-colours.html","h":["Steps","Reading the results","If the field does not accept your colour"],"x":" The Start from a colour you already have section answers the question most people arrive with: \"I have this colour — what is it, and what can it do?\" It finds the five atlas colours closest to yours and shows what each of them carries. 1. Select the field under Start from a colour you already have . It starts with D3AF37 . 2. Replace the value with your colour. You can type or paste it in any of these forms: hex, with or without , in 3, 4, 6 or 8 digits: 76cdf6 , 76cdf6 , abc ; rgb or rgba : rgb 118 205 246 , rgb 118, 205, 246 ; hsl or hsla : hsl 199 88% 71% ; hwb : hwb 199 46% 4% ; lab and lch : lab 78.6 15.2 28.2 , lch 78.6 32 241 ; oklab and oklch : oklab 0.81 0.07 0.08 , oklch 0.81 0.1 230 ; color in the srgb , srgb linear or display p3 space: color display p3 0.5 0.8 0.95 ; any of the 148 CSS colour names, such as rebeccapurple ; three bare numbers read as RGB: 118 205 246 . 3. Select Find its neighbours , or stop typing for a moment. The swatch beside the field changes to your colour and the results update. 4. Read the results described below . 5. To learn more about one of the matches, select its cell. The The colour tab opens with that colour's full record. Result: six cel"},{"t":"Read a colour","d":"Everything on The colour tab: the contrast verdict, the colour-blindness values, every notation and metric, and the nearest neighbours.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/read-a-colour.html","h":["Open a colour","The identity block","What it can carry","Under other eyes","Every space, and the metrics","Nearest in the atlas","Result"],"x":" The colour tab shows the full record of one colour. It puts the verdict first — what the colour can carry as text — then the evidence, then the raw numbers. Any of these opens a colour on The colour tab: select a tile in the grid, or focus it and press Enter or Space ; select one of the five neighbour cells under Start from a colour you already have ; select Open a random colour ; select a tile on the Saved tab. The tab switches straight away; the full record loads a moment later. If you open the tab before choosing a colour, it says No colour open with the hint Pick one from the atlas, or paste a hex above to find its neighbours. At the top left: a large swatch of the colour; its hex code in capitals, for example 76CDF6 ; a line with Atlas id and the id number, followed by the colour's labels emotion, art movement, mood, design usage and design tag , separated by dots. The block also shows Copy and Save buttons. To copy values or save the colour, use the Export tab or the star on the colour's tile; see Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md if these two buttons do not respond. Two specimens show the sentence \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\" written in the colour: on a w"},{"t":"Read the statistics","d":"Use the four histograms on the Stats tab to see how hue, lightness, chroma and contrast are spread across the colours you have filtered.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/read-the-statistics.html","h":["Steps","The four histograms","Keeping it up to date","Example"],"x":" The Stats tab draws four histograms of the colours that currently match your chips, searches and filters. A histogram splits a range of values into equal bands and counts how many colours fall in each band, so you can see at a glance where a set is crowded and where it is thin. 1. Narrow the grid on the Library tab, or leave it unfiltered to see the whole atlas. 2. Select the Stats tab. 3. Read the four cards. Each card's heading carries a badge with the number of colours it describes. 4. Select a card's heading to fold it away, and again to unfold it. Result: four bar charts that describe the set you filtered. Card Range Bands What it tells you Hue HSL 0° to 360° 12 bands of 30° Which hue families the set contains. Lightness Lab L\\ 0 to 100 10 bands of 10 How dark or light the set is. Chroma 0 to 0.40 10 bands of 0.04 How muted or colourful the set is. Contrast on white 1:1 to 21:1 10 bands of 2 How much of the set can be used as text on white. Each row shows the band's range, a bar scaled to the fullest band, and the count. Values beyond the last band are counted in it. The histograms are drawn when you open the tab. If you change a search or a chip while the tab is open, select"},{"t":"Save colours","d":"Save colours with the star, find them on the Saved tab, and reach them again from your Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/save-colours.html","h":["Save a colour","See your saved colours","Remove a colour","Your saved colours in your Library","Where saves are kept","Result"],"x":" You can keep a shortlist of atlas colours. Saved colours are listed on the Saved tab and are also copied into your Library, the site wide collection of things you save from any tool. 1. Find the colour's tile in the grid. 2. Select the empty star ☆ in the tile's footer. It becomes a filled star ★ , and the Saved tab's badge goes up by one. Selecting the star does not open the colour, so you can save several colours in a row while you scan the grid. 1. Select the Saved tab. 2. Your saved colours appear as tiles, in the atlas's own order. 3. Select a tile to open it on The colour tab, or select its star to unsave it. A note above the tiles says they are Also saved to your Library workspace with image previews , with a link. When you have saved nothing, the tab says No saved colors yet and explains how to save one. Select the filled star ★ on the colour's tile, in the grid or on the Saved tab. The star empties, the tile leaves the Saved tab, and the copy in your Library is removed too. Each saved colour is also added to your Library as a colour item named by its hex code, with its emotion and art movement as the description and a picture of the colour as the preview. In the Library y"},{"t":"Color Library reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order, tab, output, file name and message in the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","Start from a colour you already have","Or from what it has to do","Browse the atlas","Tabs","Filters (Library tab)","Sort by","Library tab buttons and grid","The colour tab","Stats tab","Export tab","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" This page lists everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/color/. For step by step help, see the task guides in this folder. Item What it shows or does Kicker Auric Artisan · Colour Headline Eight thousand colours, measured. Atlas The number of colours: 8,192. Spaces 7 HEX, RGB, HSL, CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ , OKLab, OKLCH, CMYK . Every figure precomputed The figures come stored with each colour. Read the API reference → Opens the site's API documentation at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/. Automate this note Names the API call for the same job and its credit cost; links to API docs ; can be dismissed. Control What it does Values Default Colour field Takes a colour in any CSS format; results update as you type. Hex 3, 4, 6, 8 digits , rgb , hsl , hwb , lab , lch , oklab , oklch , color srgb , srgb linear , display p3 , 148 CSS names, three bare numbers D3AF37 Swatch Shows the colour the field was read as. — — Find its neighbours Runs the match now. — — Result cells Your colour, then the five nearest atlas colours with ΔE and contrast. Select a neighbour to open it. — — Neighbourhood sentence One of three verdicts on whether nearby colours carry text. — — ΔE CIE76 Word"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Could not load color atlas\"","\"Not a colour this reads.\"","My colour shows \"outside sRGB\"","\"No colors match these filters\"","The WCAG filter \"AA on white\" shows no colours","CSV (flat) does not download","The Copy and Save buttons on The colour tab do nothing","The nearest colours on The colour tab cannot be opened","The Stats tab does not reflect my latest filter","Searching for an id finds many colours","My saved colours have disappeared","Copy does not reach the clipboard"],"x":" Why: The page downloads the atlas when it opens. The download failed — usually because the network connection dropped, a content blocker stopped it, or the site was opened from an old offline copy. What to do: Check your connection, allow auricartisan.com in any content blocker, and reload the page. Why: The text in Start from a colour you already have is not a colour format the page understands. What to do: Check brackets and separators: rgb 118 205 246 or rgb 118, 205, 246 . Use one of the supported color spaces: srgb , srgb linear or display p3 . Replace a CSS variable such as var brand with its actual value. Remove anything after the colour, such as a trailing semicolon or comment. Why: The colour you entered, for example a strong oklch or display p3 value, cannot be shown on a standard sRGB screen. The page brings it to the nearest displayable colour before matching. What to do: Nothing is wrong. The matches are for the nearest displayable version of your colour. If you need a colour inside sRGB, use one of the neighbours. Why: Your requirement chips, search words and filters together exclude every colour. For example, Vivid and Muted together always leave nothing, and Neutra"},{"t":"Color Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/docs/faq.html","h":["How many colours are in the atlas?","Does it cover every colour?","Which contrast formula does it use?","What is ΔE?","Can I test a colour against a background other than white or black?","Are the emotion, mood and art-movement labels scientific?","Do I need an account?","Can I use the colours commercially?","Is there an API?","Does it work offline?"],"x":" 8,192. The number never changes as you filter; the counters show how many of the 8,192 match. No. The atlas is a fixed, generated set of 8,192 colours spread across the sRGB range. Your exact colour may not be in it, which is why Start from a colour you already have finds the nearest ones. The WCAG 2 contrast ratio, from 1:1 to 21:1, measured against pure white FFFFFF and pure black 000000 . 4.5:1 is the AA threshold for normal body text and 7:1 is AAA. A number for how different two colours look. The Color Library uses CIE76, the straight line distance between two colours in CIE Lab. Under about 2.3, most people cannot see a difference. Not in the Color Library. Use the Contrast Checker or the Accessibility Library for any pair of colours. See Related ../others/related.md . No. They are descriptive labels assigned when the atlas was generated, useful for browsing by feel. The contrast, luminance and chroma figures are measurements. No. Everything works signed out. Saved colours stay in your browser. Colour values themselves are not ownable. For the terms that apply to the site and its content, see Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . Yes. The heading links "},{"t":"Color Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Color Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the background material for the Color Library: the terms it uses, its keyboard actions, what its figures mean and do not mean, where to go next, what it stores, and its history. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Colour terms used on the page, from chroma to ΔE. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and pointer actions. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the atlas measures, how, and what it is not. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network. Release notes release notes.md User facing history of the Color Library. Back to the Color Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Color Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard","Pointer"],"x":" Keys Where Result / Anywhere, when you are not typing in a field Moves the cursor to Search by hex a6e223 or id… . Enter or Space A focused tile in the grid Opens the colour on The colour tab. Tab Anywhere Moves between controls, chips and tiles. Action Result Select a tile Opens the colour. Select a tile's star Saves or unsaves the colour without opening it. Select a neighbour under Start from a colour you already have Opens that colour. Select a card heading on Stats Folds or unfolds the card. Pause typing in the colour field Updates the nearest matches without pressing Find its neighbours . The site wide shortcuts also work on this page. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Color Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the colour terms used in the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning AA, AAA WCAG contrast levels. For normal size text, AA needs a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 and AAA at least 7:1. Atlas The fixed set of 8,192 colours the Color Library holds. Atlas id A colour's number in the atlas, from 0 to 8,191. Chroma How colourful a colour is, compared with a grey of the same lightness. The page uses OKLCH chroma, which runs from 0 grey to about 0.4 for the most vivid screen colours. CIE L\\ a\\ b\\ Lab A colour space designed so that equal distances look roughly like equal differences. L is lightness 0 to 100 ; a runs from green to red; b from blue to yellow. CIE76 The simplest ΔE formula: the straight line distance between two colours in Lab. CMYK Cyan, magenta, yellow and black: the four inks of process printing. The values are a simple conversion, not a print profile. Colour vision deficiency CVD Reduced ability to tell some colours apart, often called colour blindness. Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of how much two colours differ in brightness, from 1:1 none to 21:1 black on white . Deuteranopia A form of colour blindness with no working green sensitive cones \"green blind\" . ΔE delta E A number for how different two colours look. Under"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Color Library's figures measure, how precisely, and what they are not.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is measured","How distance is measured","What the labels are","The atlas is a sample","Your screen","What the Color Library is not"],"x":" Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2 formula against pure white and pure black. They are exact for those two backgrounds, rounded to two decimals. They say nothing about any other background. Relative luminance, Lab, OKLab, OKLCH and HSL are standard conversions from each colour's sRGB value, assuming a D65 white point. CMYK is a simple arithmetic conversion. It is not a print separation and does not account for paper, ink or a print profile. Use a proper colour managed workflow for print. Colour blindness values are simulations of complete protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. People with milder colour vision deficiencies see something between the original and the simulation. Simulations are a design aid, not a diagnosis. ΔE in the Color Library is CIE76: the straight line distance in Lab. It is fast enough to recompute as you type, and the page names it so it is not mistaken for a newer formula. CIE76 over states differences between very saturated colours compared with CIEDE2000, so treat the words a close match and visibly different as guides. The 2.3 threshold for indistinguishable is a commonly quoted just noticeable difference for CIE76, not a guarantee for every viewer or scre"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Color Library keeps in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What Why How to remove it Saved colours To fill the Saved tab and mark stars on tiles. Unsave each colour, or clear this site's data. A copy of each saved colour in your Library So saved colours appear alongside your other saved items. Unsave the colour, or remove it in the Library. Whether you dismissed the Automate this note So it stays hidden. Clear this site's data. The colours you type into Start from a colour you already have , your searches, filters and chip choices are worked out in your browser and are not sent anywhere. They are not remembered after you leave the page. When the page opens, it downloads the atlas from auricartisan.com. When you open a colour, it may download that colour's full record from auricartisan.com. Downloads you make JSON, SVG, PNG, CSS and so on are created in your browser and saved straight to your device. Copying writes to your device's clipboard only. The page can show advertising, and the site's analytics run only with your consent. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md for the privacy policy and your consent choices. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Color Library was added to the site as part of the library expansion in release 0.9.9, alongside the Palette, Gradient, Harmony, Shade and Accessibility libraries and the Font and Icon libraries. See the release entry on the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The page as documented here opens with three routes into the atlas — Start from a colour you already have , Or from what it has to do and Browse the atlas — and gathers everything about one colour on a single tab, The colour . The changelog does not list these changes as a separate release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Color Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Color Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/color-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","API"],"x":" Palette Library ../../palette library/README.md — sets of colours that work together. Shade Library ../../shade library/README.md — one colour taken through lightness, for design system scales. Accessibility Library ../../accessibility library/README.md — foreground and background pairs scored for contrast against any ground, not only white and black. Harmony Library ../../harmony library/README.md and Gradient Library ../../gradient library/README.md . Contrast Checker ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — test any two colours against each other. Vision Simulation ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — see whole images as people with colour vision deficiencies do. Basic Tools ../../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — pickers, converters and palette tools. Your Library ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md — where saved colours also appear. CIELAB and LCH Explained — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 24 cielab and lch explained Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spac"},{"t":"Gradient Library","d":"What the Gradient Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to check your own gradient and export one from the collection.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Gradient Library is a collection of 8,192 generated colour gradients, each with its colour stops, the colour space it was blended in, its easing, a quality score and — the thing a thumbnail cannot show — a measured verdict on whether it bands. The page headline puts it plainly: \"Eight thousand ramps, and which of them band. \" About 77% of the collection is measured as smooth. Banding is when a gradient that should flow shows visible steps or a hard edge. It often happens at the dark end of a ramp, or where two stops are far apart in lightness. The library measures every gradient for it, lets you filter by the verdict, and — through Will your gradient band? at the top of the page — applies the same measurement to any stops you type in. That makes the collection useful not only to shop from, but to check your own work against. For any gradient in the collection you can read its stops and metrics, preview it under four kinds of colour vision deficiency and low vision, test text colours on top of it, and take it away as CSS, a CSS class, JSON, SVG, PNG, a Tailwind token or design tokens for eight platforms, or as a share link. Designers and front end developers choosing a gradient"},{"t":"Gradient Library documentation","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the Gradient Library, the full reference of its controls and outputs, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour of the screen, and a first gradient from check to export. check your gradient.md check your gradient.md Will your gradient band? : entering stops, reading the verdict and fixing a step. browse search and filter.md browse search and filter.md Searching, the eight filters, sorting, cards and the grid. inspect a gradient.md inspect a gradient.md The Inspect tab: preview, quick facts, CSS, stops and generator metrics. test vision contrast and text.md test vision contrast and text.md The Vision , Accessibility and Pair tabs. tags and statistics.md tags and statistics.md The Tags and Stats tabs. copy export and share.md copy export and share.md Every copy, download, design token and share option, one gradient or many. save gradients.md save gradients.md Saving, the Saved tab and your Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, option, output, file name and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answe"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Gradient Library, learn what each part of the screen does, and check, pick and export a first gradient.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: choose a smooth gradient for a hero banner with white text"],"x":" 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/gradient/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Gradient Library under Libraries . 2. While the collection loads, the grid area shows Loading gradient library... . 3. When it is ready, the grid fills with gradient cards and the counter under the grid reads, for example, 1–24 of 8,192 . If loading fails you see Could not load gradient library and the reason. See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . The kicker reads Auric Artisan · Gradient and the headline Eight thousand ramps, and which of them band. The line under it shows Collection 8,192 , Smooth 77% and Measured in OKLab , and a link, Read the API guide → , to the Gradient Library's API guide. A note starting Automate this may appear. It says browsing the collection is also available through the site's REST API — 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/gradient/library — and links to API docs . Select × to dismiss it. A row of colour stops, each with a colour swatch you can click to pick a colour and a text field you can type into, plus Add a stop and Measure it . Under them, the verdict for the ramp: a preview strip with a marker at the worst step, a word Smooth , Some compr"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Narrow 8,192 gradients by search, method, scheme, complexity, stops, interpolation, easing, score and banding, and sort the results.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["Search","Filters","Sort by","Buttons","The grid and cards","Result"],"x":" The box Search by name, hex or scheme… filters as you type. Every word must appear in at least one of these: the gradient's name, its type, its angle, any stop's hex code, its scheme, method, complexity, interpolation space, easing or banding label. Examples: aurora — gradients of the Aurora scheme. 7b36 — gradients with a stop whose hex starts 7B36 . oklch smooth — gradients blended in an OKLCH space and measured as smooth. The Filter inside results row has its own box name, hex, scheme… and a Clear button. Its words are combined with the first box's. Press / anywhere outside a text field to jump to the search box. All filters sit on the Library tab and combine with each other and with the search. Filter Options Meaning Method All methods and twelve methods: Analogous, Aurora, Chaotic, Complementary, Duotone, Golden, Monochrome, Nebula, Prismatic, Spectral, Terrain, Thermal How the gradient's colours were chosen. Scheme All schemes and the same twelve names The scheme family, which also forms the first word of each gradient's name. Complexity Any complexity , Simple , Detailed , Extreme How elaborate the gradient is. Stops Any stops , 2 to 4 stops , 5 to 8 stops , 9 to 16 stops ,"},{"t":"Check your own gradient","d":"Enter your gradient's stops in \"Will your gradient band?\", read the verdict, find the worst step and fix it.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/check-your-gradient.html","h":["What banding is","How the check measures","Steps","Reading the result","While you are typing","Fixing a gradient that steps"],"x":" Will your gradient band? applies the collection's own banding measurement to stops you give it. A gradient bands when part of it changes colour much faster than the rest, so the eye sees a step or an edge instead of a smooth flow. It is common at the dark end of a ramp: standard sRGB spends few of its values on the darkest shades, so a black to colour blend often lurches just after black. 1. The page paints your stops the way a browser paints a plain CSS linear gradient : evenly spaced, blended straight between neighbouring stops in sRGB. 2. It takes 96 samples along the ramp. 3. It measures the colour difference between each pair of neighbouring samples in OKLab, a colour space where equal distances look like roughly equal differences. 4. It divides the largest step by the average step. This step ratio is the verdict's basis. A perfectly even ramp has a ratio of 1. Step ratio Verdict Meaning Below 3.2 Smooth No transition is large enough to read as a step. 3.2 to below 5.5 Some compression One part of the ramp is noticeably faster than the rest. 5.5 or more It will step Expect a visible step. The page explains the thresholds: across 3,000 gradients the collection had already labe"},{"t":"Copy, export and share","d":"Copy a gradient's CSS, download it as a CSS class, JSON, SVG, PNG or Tailwind token, export design tokens, share a link, and export whole filtered sets.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/copy-export-and-share.html","h":["One gradient","Design tokens","Share a link","Many gradients","Result"],"x":" You can export the open gradient from three places: the Inspect tab, its Quick Export card, and the Active Gradient card on the Export tab. If no gradient is open, the Export tab says Select a gradient to enable active exports. and its buttons reply Select a gradient first . The examples use the first gradient in the collection, Aurora Simple 00001 . File names are made from the gradient's name in lower case with dashes, for example aurora simple 00001 . Button Where Output Copy CSS / Copy CSS gradient Inspect, CSS card, Export Copies the CSS value CSS copied . Download CSS / Download CSS class CSS card, Export aurora simple 00001.css , a ready made class. Download JSON Quick Export, Export aurora simple 00001.json : angle, type, stops position, hex, OKLCH , name and all metadata. Download SVG CSS card, Export aurora simple 00001.svg , a 1440 × 900 image using an SVG linear gradient at the same angle. Download Tailwind / Download Tailwind token Quick Export, Export aurora simple 00001.tailwind.txt , one \"name\": \"css\" line for a Tailwind configuration for example under backgroundImage . Download PNG / Download PNG preview Quick Export, Export aurora simple 00001.png , 1600 × 1000 p"},{"t":"Inspect a gradient","d":"Read the Inspect tab: the preview, twelve quick facts, the CSS, the colour stops, the generator metrics and quick exports.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/inspect-a-gradient.html","h":["Open a gradient","Preview and quick facts","CSS","Color Stops","Generator Metrics","Quick Export","Result"],"x":" Select a card, or focus it and press Enter or Space . Select Open a random gradient . Select a card on the Saved tab. Open a share link see Copy, export and share copy export and share.md . Before you open one, the tab says No gradient selected and describes what you will see. At the top, a large preview of the gradient with its name and a line \"scheme / interpolation space / easing\", and a Copy CSS button. Beside it, twelve quick facts: Fact Meaning Type Linear . Every gradient in the collection is linear. Angle The direction in degrees, as in CSS 0deg points up, 90deg to the right . Stops Number of colour stops. Method How the colours were chosen. Complexity Simple , Detailed or Extreme . Score Quality score from 0 to 1, three decimals. Space The interpolation space used when the gradient was generated. Easing The easing curve used between stops. Banding Smooth , Subtle Compression or Visible Step Risk . White min The lowest contrast ratio between white and any of 24 samples along the gradient. Black min The same against black. Hue The dominant hue in degrees. The CSS card shows the gradient as a CSS value, for example: css linear gradient 0deg, 723c2d 0%, 7b3600 100% Buttons: C"},{"t":"Save gradients","d":"Save gradients, find them on the Saved tab, and reach them from your Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/save-gradients.html","h":["Save a gradient","See saved gradients","Remove a gradient","In your Library","Limits"],"x":" Select Save on a card it changes to Saved , or open the gradient on Inspect and select Save gradient under Quick Export it changes to Remove saved . The page confirms Gradient saved , and the Saved tab's badge goes up by one. Select the Saved tab. Your gradients appear as cards, most recently saved first. They work like cards in the grid: select one to inspect it, CSS to copy its CSS, Saved to unsave it. A note says they are Also saved to your Library workspace with image previews . With nothing saved, the tab says No saved gradients . Select Saved on its card, or Remove saved on Inspect . The page confirms Gradient removed , and the gradient also leaves your Library. Each saved gradient is also added to your Library under its name for example Aurora Simple 00001 , described by its scheme, number of stops and interpolation space, with a preview image. Open your Library from any page with Ctrl + Shift + L . See the Library Kit docs ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . The Saved tab keeps up to 240 gradients; saving more drops the oldest. Saves are kept in this browser, not in your account. Clearing this site's data removes them. "},{"t":"Tags and statistics","d":"Browse the collection by tag on the Tags tab, and read distributions for your filtered set on the Stats tab.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/tags-and-statistics.html","h":["Tags tab","Stats tab","Example"],"x":" The Tags tab lists every value in six groups, each with the number of gradients in the whole collection, most common first: Group Values Methods Analogous, Aurora, Chaotic, Complementary, Duotone, Golden, Monochrome, Nebula, Prismatic, Spectral, Terrain, Thermal Schemes The same twelve scheme names Complexity Detailed, Simple, Extreme Interpolation Lch Short, Linear Rgb, Oklab, Oklch Long, Oklch Short Easing Cubic In Out, Linear, Quart In Out, Sine In Out, Smootherstep Banding Smooth, Visible Step Risk, Subtle Compression Select a value in Methods , Schemes , Complexity , Interpolation or Easing to set that filter and return to the Library tab with the grid narrowed. The Banding values are shown for information; filter by banding with the Banding filter on the Library tab. The counts on this tab always describe the whole collection, whatever filters are set. The Stats tab describes the gradients that currently match your search and filters or the whole collection when nothing matches . Seven cards, each a bar chart with counts: Card Groups Banding Smooth, Compresses, Steps Methods One bar per method Complexity Simple, Detailed, Extreme Stop Counts 2–4, 5–8, 9–16, 17–32, 33+ Interp"},{"t":"Test vision, contrast and text","d":"Use the Vision, Accessibility and Pair tabs to see a gradient under colour vision deficiencies, measure its contrast along the ramp, and test a text colour on it.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/test-vision-contrast-and-text.html","h":["Vision tab","Accessibility tab","Pair tab"],"x":" These three tabs work on the gradient you have open. If none is open, each says Select a gradient and asks you to pick one first. The Color Vision Preview card shows the gradient six times: Preview What it simulates Normal The original. Deuteranopia No working green sensitive cones. Protanopia No working red sensitive cones. Tritanopia No working blue sensitive cones. Achromatopsia No colour vision: greys only. Low Vision Blurred, with reduced saturation. Use it to check that a gradient carrying meaning — for example a heat map scale from cool to hot — still reads in order for colour blind viewers. The previews are approximate screen filters; see Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . A gradient can pass contrast in one region and fail in another, so this tab samples the whole ramp. Row Meaning White text min Lowest contrast of white text anywhere on the 17 samples. Black text min Lowest contrast of black text. Auto text min Lowest contrast if each region used whichever of near white or near black reads better there. Best sampled max The highest contrast of white or black text anywhere. Adjacent stop min The lowest contrast between two neighbouring stops. AA safe s"},{"t":"Gradient Library reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order, tab, output, file name and message in the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","Will your gradient band?","Browse controls","Tabs","Filters","Sort by","Library tab buttons","Card","Inspect tab","Vision, Accessibility, Pair","Tags and Stats","Export tab","Files","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/gradient/. Item Content Kicker Auric Artisan · Gradient Headline Eight thousand ramps, and which of them band. Facts Collection 8,192 , Smooth 77% , Measured in OKLab Read the API guide → Opens the Gradient Library API guide. Automate this note 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/gradient/library ; API docs ; × dismisses. Control What it does Values Default Stop swatch Opens a colour picker for the stop. Any colour — Stop text field Takes any CSS colour. Hex, rgb , hsl , hwb , lab , lch , oklab , oklch , color , names 000000 , 0B3D91 , FFFFFF × Removes the stop. Hidden when two stops remain. — — Add a stop Adds a stop at the end, halfway between the last two. Up to 12 stops — Measure it Measures again. — — Output Meaning Preview strip and marker The ramp, evenly spaced, with the worst step marked. Verdict Smooth ratio below 3.2 , Some compression 3.2 to below 5.5 , It will step 5.5 or more . step ratio Largest step divided by the mean step. Mean step , Largest step OKLab distances between neighbouring samples, five decimals. Worst transition at Percentage along the ramp. Sampled 96 steps, sRGB . Control What it does Search by name, hex "},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Could not load gradient library\"","\"No gradients match\"","My gradient says \"It will step\" but looks fine to me","The checker gives a different verdict from the same gradient in the collection","\"Stop N is not a colour yet\"","Selecting a Banding value on the Tags tab does nothing","Vision, Accessibility or Pair say \"Select a gradient\"","The Stats tab has not changed after I filtered","A share link opens the page but not the gradient","Saved gradients have gone","Downloads do not start"],"x":" Why: The collection could not be downloaded — usually a dropped connection or a content blocker. What to do: Check your connection, allow auricartisan.com in any blocker, and reload. Why: The search and filters together exclude everything. Some combinations are rare, for example Extreme complexity with 2 to 4 stops . What to do: Select Reset , then add filters back one at a time. Why: The check measures the ratio between the largest and the average step. On a small preview, a step can be hard to see; on a large hero area, on a different screen, or after image compression, it often shows. What to do: Look at the ramp full width on the screens you care about. If the worst step is at the dark end, lift the black slightly; otherwise add a stop near Worst transition at . Why: The checker always paints evenly spaced stops blended in plain sRGB, the way a basic CSS gradient is drawn. The collection's gradients were generated with their own stop positions, interpolation space and easing, and their verdict describes that. What to do: Treat the checker as \"how will this look as a basic CSS gradient\". To keep a collection gradient's smoothness, use its CSS exactly as exported. Why: The text "},{"t":"Gradient Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/docs/faq.html","h":["How many gradients are there?","How smooth is the collection?","Can I check a gradient I made elsewhere?","What does interpolation space mean?","What is easing?","What does the score mean?","Can I put text on a gradient?","Do I need an account?","Is there an API?"],"x":" 8,192, with between 2 and 46 stops each. All of them are linear gradients. 6,342 gradients about 77% are measured as smooth, 330 show subtle compression, and 1,520 carry a visible step risk. Yes. Type its stops into Will your gradient band? in any CSS colour format. See Check your own gradient check your gradient.md . The colour space in which the colours between two stops are worked out. Blending in sRGB the CSS default can produce muddy middles and uneven steps; blending in OKLab or OKLCH usually gives more even, brighter transitions. A curve that controls how fast a blend moves between two stops — steadily Linear , or slowly at the ends and faster in the middle Sine In Out , Cubic In Out , Quart In Out , Smootherstep . A quality score from 0 to 1 recorded for each gradient. The Score filter groups it into Top quality 0.70 or more , Balanced+ 0.55 or more and Wild / experimental below 0.55 . It is a ranking aid, not a guarantee. Yes, if it stays readable across the whole ramp. Use the Pair tab to test your text colour; see Test vision, contrast and text test vision contrast and text.md . No. Saved gradients stay in your browser and your Library. Yes. The heading links to the Gra"},{"t":"Gradient Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Gradient Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Background material for the Gradient Library. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Banding, step ratio, interpolation, easing and other terms. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and pointer actions. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the banding check and contrast figures measure, and their limits. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Gradient Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Gradient Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard","Pointer"],"x":" Keys Where Result / Anywhere, when not typing Focuses Search by name, hex or scheme… . Tab Grid Moves between cards and their buttons. Enter or Space A focused card Opens it on Inspect . Escape Share link or design tokens dialog Closes it. Action Result Select a card Opens it on Inspect . Select CSS on a card Copies its CSS. Select a stop's hex on Inspect Copies the hex. Select a value on Tags Filters the Library by it except Banding . Select a card heading on Vision , Accessibility , Pair , Tags , Stats or Export Folds or unfolds the card. The site wide shortcuts also work here. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Gradient Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Achromatopsia Complete colour blindness: only shades of grey are seen. Angle The direction of a linear gradient, in degrees, as in CSS: 0deg runs bottom to top, 90deg left to right. Banding Visible steps or edges in a gradient that should look smooth. Complexity Simple , Detailed or Extreme : how elaborate a gradient is, backed by a complexity score. Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of the lightness difference between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1. Design tokens Named values in a format a design system or platform reads. Easing The curve controlling how fast a blend moves between two stops. Interpolation space The colour space in which in between colours are calculated: for example sRGB, linear RGB, LCH, OKLab or OKLCH. \"Short\" and \"long\" say which way round the hue circle the blend travels. OKLab, OKLCH A modern perceptual colour space, and its lightness–chroma–hue form. Equal distances in it look roughly equally different, which is why the banding check measures in OKLab. Scheme The colour family a gradient belongs to, such as Aurora, Thermal or Terrain. Score A quality score from 0 to 1 recorded for each gradient. sRGB The standard colour space of the web. Plain C"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Gradient Library's banding verdicts, contrast figures and previews measure, and what they do not.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The banding verdict","Contrast","Vision previews","Scores and labels","Exports","What it is not"],"x":" The checker samples 96 points along the ramp and compares neighbouring samples in OKLab. The verdict depends on the ratio of the largest step to the average step, so it does not change with the number of samples. The thresholds 3.2 and 5.5 were set from the collection's own labelled gradients, as the page explains. They are a good guide, not a guarantee: whether a step is visible also depends on the screen, its bit depth, the size of the gradient, image compression and the viewer. The checker models a plain CSS gradient: evenly spaced stops blended in sRGB. It ignores stop positions, colour hints, easing and in oklch style interpolation you may use in your own CSS. The collection's verdicts were recorded when each gradient was generated, using its own positions, space and easing. Contrast uses the WCAG 2 formula on sampled colours: 24 samples for White min and Black min , 17 on the Accessibility tab, and 33 on the Pair tab. A very narrow dark or light band between samples could be missed. Passing contrast is one part of readable text; font size, weight and any texture behind the text also matter. The Vision tab uses approximate screen filters for complete deuteranopia, protanopia,"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Gradient Library keeps in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What Why How to remove it Saved gradients up to 240 To fill the Saved tab. Unsave each one, or clear this site's data. A copy of each saved gradient in your Library So it appears with your other saved items. Unsave it, or remove it in the Library. Whether you dismissed the Automate this note So it stays hidden. Clear this site's data. The stops you type into Will your gradient band? are measured in your browser and are never sent anywhere. Searches and filters are not remembered after you leave. On opening, the page downloads the collection's index from auricartisan.com. Opening a gradient downloads its detailed metrics from auricartisan.com. Downloads are created in your browser. Download all in the design tokens dialog may fetch a small helper from auricartisan.com to build the ZIP. Share links carry the gradient in the link itself; nothing is uploaded. Advertising and analytics follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Gradient Library was added in release 0.9.9 as part of the library expansion. See the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The page now opens with Will your gradient band? , which measures any stops you give it, shows a banding chip on every card, and puts every tab on screen at once. These changes are not listed as a separate changelog release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Gradient Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Gradient Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/gradient-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","Guides and API"],"x":" Shade Library ../../shade library/README.md — one colour taken from light to dark, measured for even steps. Palette Library ../../palette library/README.md , Harmony Library ../../harmony library/README.md , Color Library ../../color library/README.md and Accessibility Library ../../accessibility library/README.md . Basic Tools ../../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — includes a gradient maker. M Gradient Palette ../../../../tools/image and file tools/m gradient palette/README.md — multigradient palettes. Tonal Steps, Tints & Shades ../../../../tools/colorimetry and rendering/tonal steps/README.md — step charts. Vision Simulation ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md — full simulations of colour vision deficiencies. Your Library ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md — where saved gradients also appear. Color Gradients and Interpolation — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 07 color gradients and interpolation Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces Color in CSS: Modern Color in the Browser — https://"},{"t":"Harmony Library","d":"What the Harmony Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to identify your own colours' harmony and export a scheme.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Harmony Library is a collection of 8,192 colour harmonies built on 23 colour theory schemes — complementary, split complementary, triadic, tetradic, square, analogous, monochromatic, hexadic, pentadic, golden ratio and more — grouped into five families. The headline says \"Eight thousand schemes, and none of them stored \": every harmony is worked out from a fixed seed when you need it, so an id such as har 5k always means the same colours, anywhere. It is, in the page's words, \"a claim anyone can recompute\". A colour harmony is a set of colours whose hues sit in a deliberate pattern around the colour wheel — opposite each other, evenly spaced, or close neighbours. The library shows each harmony's colours with their roles in the scheme base, complement, triad, accent and so on , how closely they keep to the scheme's ideal angles, and — the part a row of swatches cannot show — which of its colours can carry text on each other. Only about a quarter of the collection contains two colours you could set text with. The library also works the other way round. In What harmony is this? , you type in colours you already use and it tells you which of the 23 schemes they form, how closely, "},{"t":"Harmony Library documentation","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" Task guides, the full reference, and troubleshooting and FAQ for the Harmony Library. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour of the screen, and a first harmony from identification to export. identify your colours.md identify your colours.md What harmony is this? : entering colours, reading the fit, ties and runners up. browse search and filter.md browse search and filter.md Ids, search, filters, sorting and the grid. inspect a harmony.md inspect a harmony.md The Inspect tab: roles, summary, scheme, pair contrast and per colour values. analyse the collection.md analyse the collection.md The Theory , Accessibility and Stats tabs. copy export and share.md copy export and share.md Copy formats, downloads, Coolors, design tokens, share links and bulk export. save harmonies.md save harmonies.md Saving, the Saved tab and your Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, option, output and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Harmony Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Harmony Library, learn the screen, and identify, inspect and export a first harmony.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: name your brand palette's harmony, then find a text-safe alternative"],"x":" 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/harmony/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Harmony Library under Libraries . 2. While the page works out the collection, the grid shows Loading harmony database… . This takes a moment: all 8,192 harmonies are calculated in your browser so the filters can look at every one. 3. The grid fills and the counter reads, for example, 1–48 of 8,192 harmonies . If loading fails you see Could not load harmony database . See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Kicker Auric Artisan · Harmony ; headline Eight thousand schemes, and none of them stored. ; facts Collection 8,192 , 23 methods and Derived, not stored ; and Read the API guide → to the Harmony Library's API guide. A note starting Automate this may appear: browsing the collection is also available through the site's REST API — 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/harmony/library — with a link to API docs . Select × to dismiss it. A row of colours, each with a swatch to click and pick, and a text field that takes any CSS colour. Add a colour and Identify it sit below, then the answer: the scheme your colours form, a fit score, and what else was considered. See Identify your col"},{"t":"Analyse the collection","d":"Use the Theory, Accessibility and Stats tabs to see how schemes, families, adherence and contrast are distributed across the harmonies you have filtered.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/analyse-the-collection.html","h":["Theory tab","Accessibility tab","Stats tab"],"x":" The Theory , Accessibility and Stats tabs describe every harmony that matches your current search and filters — the whole collection when nothing is set. Because all 8,192 harmonies are calculated when the page opens, these are complete counts, not samples. Each tab is drawn when you open it and redrawn after the filters change. If a tab looks out of date, select it again. With nothing matching, each tab shows No harmonies . Card What it counts Color theory scheme Harmonies per method. Family Harmonies per family. Dominant hue bucket Harmonies per overall hue: red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, purple, pink. Color count Harmonies with 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 or 7 colours. Adherence to canonical scheme High ≥ 0.85 , Medium 0.60 0.85 and Low < 0.60 . Lightness & chroma profile Dark L < 0.4 , Mid 0.4 0.7 , Light 0.7 ; Muted < 0.07 , Balanced , Vivid 0.15 . In the full collection there are 1,070 complementary family, 2,138 polyadic, 1,424 analogous, 2,136 monochromatic and 1,424 compound harmonies, and adherence is high for 6,521, medium for 1,608 and low for 63. Row Meaning Has any AA pair 4.5+ Harmonies with at least one pair at 4.5:1 or more. Has any AAA pair 7+ Harmonies with at least "},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Jump to a harmony by id, search, filter by hue, chroma, lightness and family, and sort the collection.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["Ids","Jump to a harmony","Search","Filters","Sort by","Buttons","The grid"],"x":" Every harmony has a number from 0 to 8,191 and an id: har followed by that number in base 36. har 0 is the first; har 5k is number 200. The id always gives the same colours. The schemes take turns: harmony 0 is complementary, 1 is split complementary, 2 is triadic, and so on through all 23 before starting again. The collection therefore holds 356 or 357 harmonies of each scheme. Type an id har 5k or a number 200 into Search by id, hex or method… . The grid shows that harmony alone. Filters are ignored while an id is in the box. Type anything else. Every word must appear in the harmony's id, its method for example split complementary , its family, or the hex code of one of its colours. The Filter inside results box id, hex, method… adds more words; Clear empties it. Tip: Method names use underscores, as in analogous 5 or golden ratio . Searching analogous finds all three analogous schemes and the accented analogous one. Press / outside a text field to jump to the search box. Filter Options Meaning Base hue All hues , Red , Orange , Yellow , Green , Cyan , Blue , Purple , Pink The harmony's overall hue: the average of its colours' OKLCH hues, weighted towards the more colourful ones"},{"t":"Copy, export and share","d":"Copy a harmony as hex, CSS, SCSS or Tailwind with role-named variables, download JSON, ASE, SVG or PNG, export design tokens, share a link, and export many harmonies.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/copy-export-and-share.html","h":["Quick copies from the grid","One harmony","Design tokens","Share a link","Many harmonies","Result"],"x":" Select a swatch to copy its hex code. Select Copy on a card to copy all its hex codes, separated by commas. Open the harmony on Inspect . Use its Quick export row, or the Selection card on the Export tab headed Selection · with the id and scheme . With nothing open, the Export tab says No harmony selected. Click Inspect on any card in the Library tab to enable selection exports. Variables are named after the harmony's id and each colour's role, which makes them easy to read. The examples use har 0 , a complementary harmony. Quick export Export tab What is copied Copy HEX HEX list Hex codes, one per line. Copy CSS vars CSS variables A :root block. Copy SCSS SCSS variables Sass variables. Copy Tailwind Tailwind config A colour object keyed by role. css :root { har 0 base: D17671; har 0 complement: 71CCD1; } text $har 0 base: D17671; $har 0 complement: 71CCD1; json { \"har 0\": { \"base\": \" D17671\", \"complement\": \" 71CCD1\" } } Quick export Export tab File Contents Download JSON JSON har 0.json Id, method, family, base hue, saturation, lightness, hex , every colour role, hex, RGB, HSL, OKLCH, Lab and metadata including canonical angles, description, adherence and the contrast table. Down"},{"t":"Identify your colours' harmony","d":"Use \"What harmony is this?\" to find which of the 23 schemes your colours form, how closely, and which schemes it cannot tell apart.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/identify-your-colours.html","h":["How the match works","Steps","Reading the answer","Special cases","Example"],"x":" What harmony is this? compares the hue pattern of colours you give it against all 23 schemes in the collection. A harmony is a shape on the colour wheel, and a shape has no first colour. So the page tries each of your colours as the base in turn and keeps the best fit. The order you enter colours in does not change the answer. Only schemes with the same number of colours as yours are compared. Three colours are compared with the 3 colour schemes, five with the 5 colour schemes, and so on. For each scheme it measures how far, on average, your hues are from the scheme's ideal angles, in degrees. The fit runs from 1 exact down to 0 60° or more off on average — a whole scheme's worth of wrong . Only hue is compared. Lightness and saturation are ignored. 1. Scroll to What harmony is this? . It starts with three colours: E4572E , 2EE457 and 572EE4 . 2. For each colour, click the swatch to pick one, or type into the field. Any CSS colour works: hex, rgb , hsl , lab , oklch , color or a name. 3. Select Add a colour to add one up to 12 . The new colour is the opposite of the first colour. Select × to remove one; at least two always remain. 4. The answer updates as you type. Identify it run"},{"t":"Inspect a harmony","d":"Read the Inspect tab: colour roles and names, the harmony summary, the colour-theory scheme, pair contrast and each colour's values.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/inspect-a-harmony.html","h":["The colour strip","Harmony summary","Color-theory scheme","Pair-by-pair WCAG contrast","Quick export","One card per colour","Why adherence is not always 100%"],"x":" Open a harmony by selecting Inspect or the card, pressing Enter or Space on a focused swatch, selecting Open a random harmony , or opening a share link. Until then the tab shows No harmony selected . One column per colour, each with: its role in the scheme — for example Base , Complement , Split Low , Split High , Triad ② , Triad ③ , Ally , Comp Ally , Right 90° , Left 90° , Accent , Warm Shift , Cool Shift , Ally Comp , Temperature Mate , or a numbered role such as Analogous 1 , Shade 1 , Tint 3 , Neutral 2 , Hex 2 , Pent 4 or Phi 2 ; a three word descriptive name, such as soft saturated teal tone, colourfulness and hue from OKLCH ; its hex code. Select a column to copy its hex code. The card's badge shows the family. Row Meaning Harmony ID For example har 5k . Global index The harmony's number. Scheme The method, for example triadic . Family complementary, polyadic, analogous, monochromatic or compound. Colors 2 to 7. Base hue The base colour's hue in degrees. Avg L\\ OKLCH Average OKLCH lightness, 0 to 1. Avg chroma Average OKLCH chroma. Hue span Widest angle between two of its hues, 0° to 180°. DeltaE avg Average colour difference between pairs CIE76 . Adherence How closely the"},{"t":"Save harmonies","d":"Save harmonies, find them on the Saved tab, and reach them from your Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/save-harmonies.html","h":["Save","Find your saved harmonies","Unsave","In your Library","Limits"],"x":" Select Save on a card it becomes Saved , or Save to library under Quick export on Inspect the page confirms Saved . The Saved tab's badge goes up. Open the Saved tab. Harmonies appear as cards, most recently saved first, with a note that they are Also saved to your Library workspace with image previews . With nothing saved, the tab says No saved harmonies yet . Select Saved on the card, or Unsave on Inspect Removed . The harmony also leaves your Library. Each saved harmony is added to your Library as a palette named, for example, Harmony har 5k , described by its method, family and number of colours. Open your Library from any page with Ctrl + Shift + L . See the Library Kit docs ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Up to 500 harmonies are kept; saving more drops the oldest. Saves are kept in this browser only. Clearing site data removes them. Noting a harmony's id is a permanent way to find it again. "},{"t":"Harmony Library reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order, tab, output and message in the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","What harmony is this?","Browse controls","Tabs","Filters","Sort by","Library tab buttons","Card","Inspect tab","Analysis tabs","Export tab","Files","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/harmony/. Item Content Kicker Auric Artisan · Harmony Headline Eight thousand schemes, and none of them stored. Facts Collection 8,192 , 23 methods , Derived, not stored Read the API guide → The Harmony Library API guide. Automate this note 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/harmony/library ; API docs ; × dismisses. Control What it does Default Colour swatch Opens a colour picker. — Colour field Any CSS colour. E4572E , 2EE457 , 572EE4 × Removes a colour; hidden at two. — Add a colour Adds the opposite of the first colour; up to 12. — Identify it Runs the match again. — Output Meaning Verdict Scheme name fit ≥ 0.85 , Close to … 0.65 to 0.85 , Not one of the 23 below 0.65 . fit 0 to 1, three decimals. Note Angle error, or schemes indistinguishable by hue. Family , Base colour , Worst pair , Best pair Family, best base, lowest and highest pair contrast AA at 4.5:1 . Also considered Up to four runners up with fit. Control What it does Search by id, hex or method… An id har … or number shows that harmony; other words must match id, method, family or a hex. Shuffle Sort Random . Open a random harmony Opens any harmony on Inspect . Filter in"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Could not load harmony database\"","The page is slow to open","Choosing a Method does not change the grid","\"No scheme uses N colours\"","The identifier names several schemes","My palette is \"Not one of the 23\"","Few harmonies have text-safe pairs","A share link does not open the harmony","Saved harmonies have gone"],"x":" Why: The small description of the collection could not be downloaded. What to do: Check your connection and any content blocker, and reload. Why: All 8,192 harmonies are calculated in your browser when the page opens, so that every filter looks at the whole collection. On an older device this can take a moment. What to do: Wait for the grid to appear. After that, filtering is immediate. Why: On the current page, the Method filter does not narrow the results. What to do: Type the method's name into the search box, for example triadic or golden ratio . Use Family for broader groups. Why: The schemes have between two and seven colours. With eight or more colours there is nothing to compare. What to do: Remove colours until you have seven or fewer. Why: Some schemes differ only in lightness or saturation, which hue matching cannot see: shades, tints and neutral share a shape with monochromatic 5; warm cool with complementary; triad shifted with triadic. What to do: Choose between them by looking at your colours' lightness and saturation. See the scheme descriptions in the Glossary ../others/glossary.md . Why: Its hues do not sit near any scheme's pattern. As the page says, most palett"},{"t":"Harmony Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/docs/faq.html","h":["What is a colour harmony?","How many schemes are there?","Why \"none of them stored\"?","Can it tell me my palette's harmony?","Does the colour order matter?","Why does it ignore lightness?","What does adherence mean?","Do I need an account?","Is there an API?"],"x":" A set of colours whose hues sit in a deliberate pattern on the colour wheel: opposite complementary , evenly spaced triadic, square, pentadic, hexadic , neighbouring analogous or one hue at different lightness monochromatic . 23, in five families. See the list in the Glossary ../others/glossary.md . Each harmony is calculated from a fixed seed when needed, so the same id always gives the same colours, and anyone can recalculate it. Yes: What harmony is this? matches 2 to 12 colours against every scheme with the same number of colours. See Identify your colours' harmony identify your colours.md . No. Each colour is tried as the base. Harmony schemes are defined by hue angles. Lightness and saturation are what make a scheme usable for text, which is why the page reports pair contrast separately. How closely a harmony's actual hues keep to its scheme's ideal angles, from 0% to 100%. No. Yes. The heading links to the Harmony Library API guide, and the Automate this note names GET /v1/harmony/library . See Public API ../../../../../services/public api/README.md . "},{"t":"Harmony Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Harmony Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Background material for the Harmony Library. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms, and all 23 schemes with family, colours, angles and description. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and pointer actions. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the identifier and the figures can and cannot tell you. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Harmony Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Harmony Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys or action Where Result / Anywhere, when not typing Focuses Search by id, hex or method… . Enter or Space A focused swatch in the grid Opens its harmony on Inspect . Escape Share link or design tokens dialog Closes it. Select a swatch Grid Copies its hex. Select a column Inspect strip Copies its hex. Select a card heading Inspect Folds or unfolds the card. The site wide shortcuts also work here. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Harmony Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms and all 23 colour-theory schemes used in the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/glossary.html","h":["Terms","The 23 schemes"],"x":" Term Meaning Adherence How closely a harmony's actual hues keep to its scheme's canonical angles, from 0% to 100%. Base The colour a scheme is built around. Other colours are placed at angles from its hue. Canonical angles A scheme's ideal hue offsets from the base, such as 120° and 240° for triadic. Colour wheel Hues arranged in a circle from 0° to 360° red, yellow, green, cyan, blue, magenta and back to red . Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 lightness difference measure between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1. 4.5:1 is AA for body text. Family A group of related schemes: complementary, polyadic, analogous, monochromatic or compound. Fit In What harmony is this? : 1 minus the average angle error divided by 60°, never below 0. Harmony id har followed by the harmony's number in base 36. Hue span The widest angle between two of a harmony's hues. Role What a colour does in its scheme: base, complement, ally, accent and so on. Scheme method One of the 23 rules for placing hues. Scheme Family Colours Canonical angles Description as the page gives it complementary complementary 2 180° Base hue and its 180° opposite — the strongest possible contrast pair. split complementary complementary 3 150°,"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Harmony Library's identifier, adherence and contrast figures measure, and what they do not.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The identifier","The collection","Contrast","Your screen"],"x":" It compares hue only, measured as the HSL hue of each colour. Two palettes with the same hues but very different lightness get the same answer. Five schemes cannot be separated by hue shades, tints and neutral from monochromatic 5; warm cool from complementary; triad shifted from triadic . The page names all of them rather than guessing. Very grey colours have an unstable hue: a tiny change in value can swing the hue angle a long way. Identifying a palette of near greys gives an unreliable answer. It only compares schemes with the same number of colours as you entered. The fit bands 0.85 and 0.65 are guides for how deliberate a pattern looks, not rules of colour theory. Colours are generated in HSL from each scheme's rule and a base colour whose saturation is between 45% and 95% and lightness between 35% and 80%. HSL hue steps are not perfectly even to the eye, which is one reason adherence varies. The Base hue filter uses the harmony's overall hue a weighted average of its colours' OKLCH hues , which can differ from the base colour's own hue. Scheme descriptions are the page's short summaries of common colour theory practice, not formal definitions. Pair contrast uses the WCAG 2 "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Harmony Library keeps in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What How to remove it Saved harmony ids up to 500 Unsave each one, or clear this site's data. A copy of each saved harmony in your Library Unsave it, or remove it in the Library. Whether you dismissed the Automate this note Clear this site's data. The colours you type into What harmony is this? are matched in your browser and never sent anywhere. On opening, the page downloads a 5 KB description of the collection from auricartisan.com; the harmonies are calculated in your browser. Open in Coolors sends the harmony's hex codes to coolors.co in the address of a new tab. Download all in the design tokens dialog may fetch a small helper from auricartisan.com. Share links carry the harmony in the link; nothing is uploaded. Advertising and analytics follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Harmony Library was added in release 0.9.9 as part of the library expansion. See the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The page now calculates all 8,192 harmonies when it opens, so filters and the analysis tabs cover the whole collection rather than one page of it, and What harmony is this? identifies the scheme behind your own colours. Every tab is shown at once an earlier Simple/Advanced switch has gone . These changes are not listed as a separate changelog release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Harmony Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Harmony Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/harmony-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","Guides and API"],"x":" Palette Library ../../palette library/README.md — five million five colour palettes. Accessibility Library ../../accessibility library/README.md — text and background pairs scored for contrast. Color Library ../../color library/README.md , Gradient Library ../../gradient library/README.md and Shade Library ../../shade library/README.md . Basic Tools ../../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — build and remix palettes. Personalisation Generator ../../../../tools/colour workspace/personalisation generator/README.md — palettes conditioned on your preferences. Contrast Checker ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md . Your Library ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Color Theory and Harmony — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contrast — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 wcag contrast accessible color Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces The Harmony Library user guide in the Documentation library ../../../documentatio"},{"t":"Palette Library","d":"What the Palette Library is, who it is for, where to find it and how to find and export your first palette.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Palette Library is a browsable collection of 5,000,000 five colour palettes. The page headline is \"Five million palettes, and a 660 byte file. \": the collection is not stored as a list, because written out in full it would take 3.9 GB. Instead, every palette is worked out from a fixed starting number a seed the moment you scroll to it. The same palette id always gives the same five colours, on any computer, so an id such as pal abc is a stable reference you can write down or share. That design has one consequence the page is open about. Nothing can look at five million palettes at once, so a filter does not narrow a list — it starts a scan through the collection, and the counter under the grid tells you how many palettes were worked out to find the ones you are looking at. The analysis tabs Harmony, Accessibility, Stats likewise measure a sample and say how big it was. For each palette you can read every colour in HEX, RGB, OKLCH and CIE Lab, check the contrast between every pair of its colours and against white and black, copy it as CSS, SCSS or Tailwind, download it as JSON, Adobe ASE, SVG or PNG, export it as design tokens for eight platforms, share a link to it, or save it"},{"t":"Palette Library documentation","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides for the Palette Library, the full reference of its controls and outputs, and the troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started if you are new to the page. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour of the screen and a first palette from search to export. browse search and filter.md browse search and filter.md Scrolling five million palettes, jumping to an id, searching, filtering, sorting and reading the counter. inspect a palette.md inspect a palette.md The Inspect tab: colour names, summary metrics, pair contrast, per colour values. analyse the collection.md analyse the collection.md The Harmony , Accessibility and Stats tabs and the samples they measure. copy export and share.md copy export and share.md Copy formats, downloads, Coolors, design tokens, share links and bulk export. save palettes.md save palettes.md Saving, the Saved tab and your Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, filter, sort, output, file name and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md What to do when something does not behave as expected. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. Back to the Palet"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Palette Library, learn what each part of the screen does, and find, inspect and export a first palette.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: find a calm, dark palette and use it in CSS","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/palette/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Palette Library under Libraries . 2. While the page prepares, the grid area shows Loading palette database… . This takes a moment only: the page downloads a tiny description of the collection, not the palettes themselves. 3. When it is ready, the grid fills with palettes and the counter under the grid reads, for example, 1–48 of 5,000,000 palettes . If loading fails you see Could not load palette database with the reason. See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . The kicker reads Auric Artisan · Palette and the headline Five million palettes, and a 660 byte file. A short paragraph explains that the collection is worked out as you scroll rather than stored. The line under it shows Collection 5,000,000 , Five colours each and Derived, not stored , with a link, Read the API guide → , to the Palette Library's API guide. A note starting Automate this may appear under the heading. It says the same job can be done through the site's REST API — 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/palette/library — and links to API docs . It also points out that API credits are a separate balance from your"},{"t":"Analyse the collection","d":"Use the Harmony, Accessibility and Stats tabs to see how methods, hues, contrast and lightness are distributed across a sample of palettes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/analyse-the-collection.html","h":["The sample","Harmony tab","Accessibility tab","Stats tab","Keeping the tabs current","Result"],"x":" The Harmony , Accessibility and Stats tabs describe many palettes at once. A browser cannot count five million palettes, so each tab measures a sample and says how big it was. Every tab opens with a line such as: Measured on 2,000 palettes from the start of the collection. Five million cannot be counted in a browser, so these are a sample — the API samples the same way. No filter or search: the sample is the first 2,000 palettes of the collection. A filter or search is on: the page looks through up to 40,000 palettes from the start of the collection and keeps up to 2,000 that match. The line then says, for example, Measured on 812 palettes matching this filter, out of 40,000 derived . An id is in the search box: the sample is that one palette. The sample is rebuilt every time you change a filter or search, so the tabs always describe the filter the grid is showing. If nothing in the looked at stretch matches, the tabs show No palettes and suggest widening the filter. Four cards, each a bar chart with counts: Card What it counts Generation method How many sampled palettes carry each method label. Dominant hue bucket How many have each dominant hue: red, orange, yellow, green, cyan,"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Scroll five million palettes, jump to a palette by id, search, filter and sort, and read the counter that says how far a scan went.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["How the collection works","Scroll the whole collection","Jump to a palette by id","Search by hex or method","Filters","Read the counter while filtering","Sort","Shuffle, random, reset","Cards","Result"],"x":" Each palette has a number from 0 to 4,999,999, and an id made from that number: pal followed by the number written in base 36 digits 0–9 then letters a–z . Palette 0 is pal 0 , palette 10 is pal a , palette 13,368 is pal abc . The five colours of a palette are worked out from its number every time you need them, so they never change. Because every palette can be reached by its number, the unfiltered grid can show any part of the collection instantly. A filtered grid cannot: the only way to find the hundredth blue palette is to look through every palette before it. So the page scans forward in chunks as you scroll, and the counter under the grid tells you how far it has looked. With no search or filter: The grid starts at pal 0 and scrolls continuously. The counter reads, for example, 1–48 of 5,000,000 palettes . A browser cannot make a page tall enough to scroll through five million palettes, so the scrollbar stops before the end. When it does, the counter adds scroll reaches N; search an id for the rest . Every palette beyond that point can still be opened by searching for its id. Back to top returns to pal 0 . 1. Type an id into Search by id or hex… , for example pal abc , or ty"},{"t":"Copy, export and share","d":"Copy a palette as hex, CSS, SCSS or Tailwind, download it as JSON, ASE, SVG or PNG, export design tokens, share a link, and download many palettes at once.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/copy-export-and-share.html","h":["Quick copies from the grid","Export one palette","Export design tokens","Share a link","Export many palettes","Result"],"x":" Select one swatch to copy that colour's hex code. Select Copy on a card to copy all five hex codes separated by commas, for example 28ACE4, 715ED2, F84461, 6F30E7, BBC8BA . Open the palette on the Inspect tab see Inspect a palette inspect a palette.md . You can then use either the Quick export row on Inspect , or the Selection card on the Export tab. They produce the same results. If no palette is open, the Export tab says No palette selected. Click Inspect on any card in the Library tab to enable selection exports. The examples use palette pal 0 . Variable names are built from the palette id and the colour's position, 1 to 5. Quick export Export tab What is copied Copy HEX HEX list The five hex codes, one per line. Copy CSS vars CSS variables A :root block with one custom property per colour. Copy SCSS SCSS variables Five Sass variables. Copy Tailwind Tailwind config A colour object you can paste into theme.extend.colors . css :root { pal 0 1: 28ACE4; pal 0 2: 715ED2; pal 0 3: F84461; pal 0 4: 6F30E7; pal 0 5: BBC8BA; } text $pal 0 1: 28ACE4; $pal 0 2: 715ED2; $pal 0 3: F84461; $pal 0 4: 6F30E7; $pal 0 5: BBC8BA; json { \"pal 0\": { \"c1\": \" 28ACE4\", \"c2\": \" 715ED2\", \"c3\": \" F84461\""},{"t":"Inspect a palette","d":"Read everything on the Inspect tab: the colour strip, the palette summary, pair-by-pair contrast and each colour's values.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/inspect-a-palette.html","h":["Open a palette","The colour strip","Palette summary","Pair-by-pair WCAG contrast","Quick export","One card per colour","Result"],"x":" The Inspect tab turns one palette into a full report. Select Inspect on a card, or select the card outside its swatches and buttons. Focus a swatch and press Enter or Space . Select Open a random palette . Open a share link someone sent you see Copy, export and share copy export and share.md . Before any palette is open, the tab shows No palette selected and explains what you will see. Five tall columns, one per colour. Each shows: a descriptive name made of three words — a tone, a colourfulness and a hue — for example soft muted blue ; the hex code. Select a column to copy its hex code. Word Meaning from OKLCH Tone: deep , rich , soft , pale Lightness below 0.35, below 0.55, below 0.75, and 0.75 or more. Colourfulness: neutral , muted , saturated , vivid Chroma below 0.04, below 0.10, below 0.18, and 0.18 or more. Hue: red , orange , yellow , green , teal , blue , purple , pink The colour's OKLCH hue angle. The Palette summary card carries a badge that classifies the palette from its real colours: Badge When Neutral Average chroma below 0.05. Triadic The widest gap between any two hues is more than 90°. Analogous The widest gap is more than 30°. Monochrome The widest gap is 30° o"},{"t":"Save palettes","d":"Save palettes, find them on the Saved tab, and reach them from your Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/save-palettes.html","h":["Save a palette","See your saved palettes","Remove a palette","In your Library","Limits","Result"],"x":" Either: select Save on the palette's card in the grid it changes to Saved ; or open the palette on Inspect and select Save to library under Quick export the page confirms Saved . The Saved tab's badge goes up by one. Select the Saved tab. Your palettes appear as cards, the most recently saved first. The cards work like cards in the grid: select a swatch to copy it, Copy to copy all five, Inspect to open the palette, or Saved to unsave it. A note above the cards says your palettes are Also saved to your Library workspace with image previews , with a link. With nothing saved, the tab shows No saved palettes yet and explains how to save one. Select Saved on its card, or Unsave under Quick export on Inspect the page confirms Removed . The palette leaves the Saved tab and your Library. Each saved palette is also added to your Library as a palette named, for example, Palette pal abc , described by its method and colour count, with a picture of its five colours. Open your Library from any page with Ctrl + Shift + L . See the Library Kit docs ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . The Saved tab keeps up to 500 palettes. Saving more drops the oldest from the list. Saved palettes are kept"},{"t":"Palette Library reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order, tab, output, file name and message in the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","Browse controls","Tabs","Filters","Sort by","Library tab buttons","Card","Counter under the grid","Inspect tab","Analysis tabs","Export tab","Files","Design tokens dialog","Share link dialog","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/palette/. Item Content Kicker Auric Artisan · Palette Headline Five million palettes, and a 660 byte file. Collection 5,000,000 Facts Five colours each , Derived, not stored Read the API guide → Opens the Palette Library API guide in the documentation library. Automate this note 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/palette/library ; links to API docs ; × dismisses it. Control What it does Default Search by id or hex… An id pal … or a number shows that one palette. Other words must each match the id, the method or a colour's hex. Empty Shuffle Sets Sort by to Random . — Open a random palette Opens any of the 5,000,000 palettes on Inspect . — Filter inside results box id, hex, method… A second search, combined with the first. Empty Clear Empties the second box. — Tab Badge Contents Library 5M Filters, sort, grid, counter. Inspect — The open palette. Harmony — Method, hue, harmony and lightness/chroma distributions of the sample. Accessibility — Pair contrast summaries of the sample. Stats — Four histograms of the sample. Export — Selection and sample exports. Saved Number saved Saved palettes. Filter Options Test Dominant hue All hues , Re"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Could not load palette database\"","A filter shows \"Nothing matched yet\"","Filtering feels slow","The scrollbar stops before the end of the collection","A sort does not seem to cover the whole collection","Filters seem to be ignored","The palette's method does not match its colours","\"Export visible\" exported more palettes than I can see","A share link opens the page but not the palette","The ASE file will not open","Saved palettes have gone"],"x":" Why: The page could not download the short description of the collection it needs to work out palettes, usually because of a dropped connection or a content blocker. What to do: Check your connection, allow auricartisan.com in any content blocker, and reload. Why: A filter starts a scan from the beginning of the collection. A rare combination, such as Dark lightness with Vivid chroma and one method, may need to look through many palettes before the first match. What to do: Scroll down to let the scan continue, or widen the filter. Watch the counter: N matches from M derived shows how far it has looked. Why: Every palette the scan looks at is worked out on the spot. The page does this in small steps so it stays responsive, but a rare filter can mean a lot of work. What to do: Remove a filter you do not need, or use the search box to jump straight to a known id. Why: No browser can make a page tall enough for five million palettes. The counter says scroll reaches N; search an id for the rest . What to do: Type the id or number of the palette you want into Search by id or hex… . Every palette can be reached this way. Why: Sorting needs the whole set in hand, and five million palettes"},{"t":"Palette Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/docs/faq.html","h":["Are there really five million palettes?","Why not store them?","How do I get back to a palette I found?","Why does a filter say \"derived\"?","Can every colour in a palette be used as text on every other?","What do the method names mean?","Which export should I use?","Do I need an account?","Is there an API?"],"x":" Yes. Each of the 5,000,000 palettes is defined by its number and worked out when you view it. The same id always gives the same five colours. Written out in full, the collection was 3.9 GB. Working palettes out as you scroll keeps the page fast and the download tiny. Note its id for example pal abc and type it into the search box, save it, or copy a share link. Because the page has to work out palettes to test them. 96 matches from 1,500 derived means it has looked at 1,500 palettes and 96 passed. No — not in this library or any other. There is only room for three lightness levels that are all 4.5:1 apart, so at most three colours can all be legible on each other, and in practice palettes here offer two. Use Pair by pair WCAG contrast on Inspect to find the pairs that work. See Analyse the collection analyse the collection.md . They are the palette's generation method labels: complementary , triadic , analogous , tetradic , golden ratio , random and monochromatic . The badge on Inspect measures the hue relationship the colours actually have. Pasting into CSS: Copy CSS vars . A Tailwind project: Copy Tailwind , or Design tokens… › Tailwind Config . Adobe apps: Download ASE . A desi"},{"t":"Palette Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Palette Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Background material for the Palette Library: its terms, keyboard actions, what its figures mean and do not mean, related pages, what it stores, and its history. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms such as seed, derived, dominant hue, hue span and mutually legible. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and pointer actions. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md Samples, scans, method labels and contrast. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser and what uses the network. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Palette Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Palette Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard","Pointer"],"x":" Keys Where Result / Anywhere, when not typing in a field Focuses Search by id or hex… . Tab Grid Moves between swatches and buttons. Enter or Space A focused swatch Opens its palette on Inspect . Escape Share link or design tokens dialog Closes the dialog. Action Result Select a swatch in the grid Copies its hex code. Select a column on Inspect Copies its hex code. Select a card outside its buttons Opens the palette on Inspect . Select a card heading on Inspect Folds or unfolds the card. Select outside a dialog Closes it. The site wide shortcuts also work here. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Palette Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning ASE Adobe Swatch Exchange, a swatch file format read by Adobe apps and other design tools. Base 36 Writing numbers with the digits 0–9 and the letters a–z. Palette ids use it: pal a is palette 10. Chroma How colourful a colour is compared with a grey of the same lightness. The page uses OKLCH chroma. Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 measure of the lightness difference between two colours, from 1:1 to 21:1. 4.5:1 is the AA level for body text; 7:1 is AAA. Derived Worked out on the spot from the palette's number rather than read from storage. Design tokens Named colour values in a format a design system or platform reads, such as CSS variables, a Tailwind config or an Android colors.xml . Dominant hue A palette's overall hue: the average of its five hues, weighted towards the more colourful colours. Entropy On Inspect : how many 36° hue bands the five colours fall in, divided by 5. 1.00 means five different hue families. Hue span The widest angle between any two of a palette's five hues, from 0° to 180°. Method The generation method label a palette carries, such as triadic . Mutually legible A set of colours that all reach a contrast threshold against each other, so any one ca"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Palette Library's scans, samples and figures can tell you, and what they cannot.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Scans and samples","Method labels and measured harmony","Contrast","Colour values","Your screen","What it is not"],"x":" A filtered browse is a scan from the start of the collection. It shows the matches found so far, not all matches in five million. The counter always states how many palettes were looked at. Sorting orders a first stretch of 1,500 palettes or the matches among them , not the whole collection. The Harmony , Accessibility and Stats tabs, and the Visible page export, use a sample of up to 2,000 palettes: the first 2,000, or the first matches found in up to 40,000. Percentages describe that sample. Because the sample always starts at the beginning of the collection, it is consistent from visit to visit but is not a random draw from all five million. Each palette carries a method label such as triadic . The colours are worked out from the palette's number, and the label does not guarantee a particular hue relationship. The Palette summary badge and Hue span on Inspect are measured from the actual colours; rely on those when the relationship matters. Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2 formula. They are exact for the colours as sRGB values. WCAG 2 contrast is one requirement for readable text. Font size, weight, and the surrounding design also matter. Newer measures such as APCA can rate some"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Palette Library keeps in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What Why How to remove it Saved palette ids up to 500 To fill the Saved tab. Unsave each palette, or clear this site's data. A copy of each saved palette in your Library So it appears with your other saved items. Unsave it, or remove it in the Library. Whether you dismissed the Automate this note So it stays hidden. Clear this site's data. Your searches, filters and sort choices are handled in your browser and are not remembered after you leave. When the page opens, it downloads a short description of the collection from auricartisan.com. Palettes themselves are worked out in your browser. Open in Coolors opens coolors.co in a new tab and passes it the palette's five hex codes in the address. Coolors is a separate service with its own privacy policy. Download all in the design tokens dialog may download a small helper from auricartisan.com to build the ZIP file. Share links contain the palette's id and colours in the link itself; nothing is uploaded when you create one. Advertising and analytics on the site follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Palette Library was added in release 0.9.9 as part of the library expansion, together with the Color, Gradient, Harmony, Shade and Accessibility libraries. See the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The current page streams the whole five million collection as you scroll, reports how far every filtered scan has looked, measures the analysis tabs on a stated sample, and shows every tab at once earlier versions hid the analysis tabs behind a Simple/Advanced switch, and paged the grid in fixed page sizes . These changes are not listed as a separate changelog release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Palette Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Palette Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/palette-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","Guides and API"],"x":" Harmony Library ../../harmony library/README.md — palettes built on named colour theory schemes. Accessibility Library ../../accessibility library/README.md — text and background pairs scored for contrast. Color Library ../../color library/README.md , Gradient Library ../../gradient library/README.md and Shade Library ../../shade library/README.md . Basic Tools ../../../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md — generate and remix your own palettes. Image Picker ../../../../tools/image and file tools/image picker/README.md — extract a palette from a picture. Contrast Checker ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — test any two colours. Design System Generator ../../../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md — build a full design system from colours. Your Library ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md — where saved palettes also appear. Color Theory and Harmony — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 04 color theory and harmony Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contra"},{"t":"Shade Library","d":"What the Shade Library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to find and export a first shade scale.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Shade Library is a collection of 8,192 shade scales also called shade systems or colour ramps . A shade scale is one colour taken from very light to very dark in named steps — the familiar 50 , 100 , 200 … 900 , 950 of design systems such as Tailwind CSS or Material Design. The page puts the difference from a palette clearly: \"A shade scale is not a palette. It is one colour taken through lightness so that some steps are surfaces and others are text on them.\" The headline, \"Eight thousand ramps, and 8% of them even \", sums up what the page measures. All 8,192 scales run in one direction and all can carry text, but only 8.2% have genuinely even steps. The scales come from ten generation methods — from Material like and Tailwind like ramps to accessible UI, neutral, ink and paper, duotone and temperature shift systems — with 5 to 21 tokens each. For each scale you can read every token's value in HEX, RGB, OKLCH and CIE Lab, see which tokens can carry body text with black or white text on them, and export the whole scale as CSS custom properties, SCSS, a Tailwind colour group, JSON, SVG, PNG or design tokens for eight platforms. Designers and developers building a design system w"},{"t":"Shade Library documentation","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Opening the page, a tour of the screen, and a first scale from filter to CSS. browse search and filter.md browse search and filter.md Search, filters, sorting and cards. inspect a scale.md inspect a scale.md The Inspect tab: tokens, summary, contrast ladder and per token values. analyse the collection.md analyse the collection.md The Harmony , Accessibility and Stats tabs. copy export and share.md copy export and share.md Copy formats, downloads, design tokens, share links and bulk export. save scales.md save scales.md Saving, the Saved tab and your Library. reference.md reference.md Every control, output and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Shade Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the Shade Library, learn the screen, and find, check and export a first shade scale.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the page","A tour of the screen","Your first task: a blue scale for a design system"],"x":" 1. Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/shades/, or open the Learn menu in the site header and select Shade Library under Libraries . 2. While the collection loads, the grid shows Loading shade library... . 3. The grid fills and the counter reads, for example, 1–24 of 8,192 scales . If loading fails you see Could not load shade library . See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Kicker Auric Artisan · Shades ; headline Eight thousand ramps, and 8% of them even. ; facts Collection 8,192 , 10 methods and Measured in OKLab ; and Read the API guide → to the Shade Library's API guide. A note starting Automate this may appear: browsing is also available through the site's REST API — 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/shade/library — with API docs . Select × to dismiss it. A search box Search by id, hex, token or method… , Shuffle , Open a random scale , and Filter inside results with its own box and Clear . Tab What it shows Library Filters, sort and the grid. The badge shows how many scales match. Inspect The scale you last opened. Harmony Distributions of methods, hues, profiles and token counts. Accessibility Which scales' tokens can carry text. Stats Five histograms. Export Exports "},{"t":"Analyse the collection","d":"Use the Harmony, Accessibility and Stats tabs to see how methods, profiles, text safety and token counts are distributed across your filtered scales.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/analyse-the-collection.html","h":["Harmony tab","Accessibility tab","Stats tab"],"x":" These tabs describe every scale that matches your current search and filters — all 8,192 when nothing is set. Each is drawn when opened and redrawn after a filter change; select the tab again if it looks out of date. With nothing matching, each shows No shade systems . Card What it counts Generation method Scales per method. Dominant hue bucket Scales per base hue. Shade profile Neutral, Hue Shift, Light, Deep and Balanced see Inspect a scale inspect a scale.md . Token count Scales with 5, 7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 16 or 21 tokens. Lightness & chroma profile Dark, Mid and Light; Muted, Balanced and Vivid. Row Meaning All tokens auto AA Scales in which every token reaches 4.5:1 with automatic text. 75%+ tokens auto AA Scales in which at least three quarters of tokens do. White text coverage Scales in which at least 35% of tokens reach 4.5:1 with white text. Black text coverage The same with black text. In the full collection, 403 scales have every token at AA with automatic text. The token contrast ladder for the open scale, or Select a shade system to see per token contrast. Up to 24 matching scales where every token passes. Cards work as in the grid. If there are none: No full auto AA sh"},{"t":"Browse, search and filter","d":"Search and filter 8,192 shade scales by base hue, chroma, lightness and method, and sort the results.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/browse-search-and-filter.html","h":["Search","Filters","Sort by","Buttons","The grid","A note on evenness"],"x":" Search by id, hex, token or method… filters as you type. Every word must appear in the scale's id, its name, its base colour, its method, its base hue name red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, purple, pink , its token names, or any of its hex codes. The Filter inside results box adds more words; Clear empties it. Press / outside a text field to jump to the search box. Examples: ff724c — scales based on, or containing, that colour. tailwind blue — Tailwind like scales with a blue base. 950 — scales that have a 950 token. Filter Options Meaning Base hue All hues , Red , Orange , Yellow , Green , Cyan , Blue , Purple , Pink The OKLCH hue of the scale's base colour. Chroma Any chroma , Muted < 0.07 , Balanced 0.07 to 0.15 , Vivid 0.15 Average OKLCH chroma of the tokens. Lightness Any lightness , Dark below 0.40 , Mid 0.40 to 0.70 , Light above 0.70 Average OKLCH lightness of the tokens. Method All methods , Accessible Ui , Brand System , Duotone Shift , Ink Paper , Material Like , Neutral System , Oklch Ramp , Tailwind Like , Temperature Shift , Vivid Product How the scale was generated. All filters and searches combine. Method Scales Brand System 1,418 Accessible Ui 1,287 Tailwind"},{"t":"Copy, export and share","d":"Copy a shade scale as hex, token-named CSS, SCSS or Tailwind, download JSON, SVG or PNG, export design tokens, share a link, and export many scales.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/copy-export-and-share.html","h":["One scale","Design tokens","Share a link","Many scales"],"x":" Open the scale on Inspect . Use Quick export , or the Selection card on the Export tab headed Selection and the id . With nothing open, the Export tab says No shade system selected. Click Inspect on any card in the Library tab to enable selection exports. Names in the output come from the scale's name with the hex codes removed, in lower case with dashes: Material Like FF724C 00001 becomes material like 00001 . Each variable ends in the token name. Quick export Export tab What is copied Message Copy HEX HEX list All hex codes, comma separated. HEX list copied Copy CSS vars CSS variables A CSS class holding one custom property per token. CSS variables copied Copy SCSS SCSS variables One Sass variable per token. SCSS copied Copy Tailwind Tailwind config A colour group keyed by token. Tailwind copied For the first scale in the collection: css .aa shade material like 00001 { material like 00001 50: fff0ec; material like 00001 100: ffdfd7; material like 00001 300: ff886b; material like 00001 500: ff724c; material like 00001 700: cd5531; material like 00001 900: 4b1200; material like 00001 950: 1e0400; } text $material like 00001 50: fff0ec; $material like 00001 100: ffdfd7; ... $materi"},{"t":"Inspect a scale","d":"Read the Inspect tab: token strip, shade summary, token contrast ladder and each token's values.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/inspect-a-scale.html","h":["The token strip","Shade summary","Token contrast ladder","Quick export","One card per token","Example"],"x":" Open a scale with Inspect , by selecting the card, with Enter or Space on a focused swatch, with Open a random scale , or from a share link. Until then the tab shows No shade system selected . One column per token, labelled with the token name and a descriptive colour name — for example 500 soft vivid orange — and the hex code. Select a column to copy its hex. The badge gives the scale's profile: Badge When Neutral Average chroma below 0.035. Hue Shift Its hues span more than 35°. Light Average lightness above 0.72. Deep Average lightness below 0.38. Balanced Anything else. The badges are checked in that order, so a scale is Neutral before it can be Hue Shift , and so on. Row Meaning Shade ID For example shade 000000 . Global index The scale's number. Method For example Material Like . Base The base colour the scale is built around. Tokens Number of steps. Avg L OKLCH Average lightness, 0 to 1. Avg chroma Average OKLCH chroma. Hue span Widest hue difference between two tokens. Score The quality score recorded for the scale. Auto AA tokens How many tokens reach 4.5:1 with automatic text near black on light tokens, white on dark ones , for example 4 / 7 . All tokens is good; 70% or "},{"t":"Save scales","d":"Save shade scales, find them on the Saved tab, and reach them from your Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/save-scales.html","h":["Save","Find saved scales","Unsave","In your Library","Limits"],"x":" Select Save on a card, or Save to library under Quick export on Inspect . The page confirms Shade saved , and the Saved tab's badge goes up. Open the Saved tab. Scales appear as cards, most recently saved first, with a note that they are Also saved to your Library workspace with image previews . With nothing saved: No saved shade systems yet . Select Saved on the card, or Unsave on Inspect . The page confirms Shade removed , and the scale leaves your Library too. Each saved scale is added to your Library under its name for example Material Like FF724C 00001 , described by method, base colour and token count. Open your Library with Ctrl + Shift + L . See the Library Kit docs ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Up to 500 scales are kept; saving more drops the oldest. Saves are kept in this browser only. "},{"t":"Shade Library reference","d":"Every control, filter, sort order, tab, output and message in the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/reference.html","h":["Heading","Browse controls","Tabs","Filters","Sort by","Library tab buttons","Card","Inspect tab","Analysis tabs","Export tab","Files","Messages","Keyboard"],"x":" Everything on https://auricartisan.com/library/shades/. Item Content Kicker Auric Artisan · Shades Headline Eight thousand ramps, and 8% of them even. Facts Collection 8,192 , 10 methods , Measured in OKLab Read the API guide → The Shade Library API guide. Automate this note 3 API credits per call to GET /v1/shade/library ; API docs ; × dismisses. Control What it does Search by id, hex, token or method… Every word must match id, name, base, method, base hue name, a token name or a hex. Shuffle Sort Random . Open a random scale Opens any scale on Inspect . Filter inside results id, hex, method… Second search, combined. Clear Empties the second search. Library badge: matches , Inspect , Harmony , Accessibility , Stats , Export , Saved badge: saved . Filter Options Base hue All hues , Red 340° to under 20° , Orange 20–50° , Yellow 50–80° , Green 80–160° , Cyan 160–200° , Blue 200–260° , Purple 260–300° , Pink 300–340° Chroma Any chroma , Muted < 0.07 , Balanced 0.07–0.15 , Vivid 0.15 Lightness Any lightness , Dark < 0.40 , Mid 0.40–0.70 , Light 0.70 Method All methods , Accessible Ui , Brand System , Duotone Shift , Ink Paper , Material Like , Neutral System , Oklch Ramp , Tailwind L"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems in the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["\"Could not load shade library\"","I cannot find an evenness filter","\"No shade systems match\"","Pasted CSS variables do nothing","The middle steps fail contrast","Bulk export buttons do nothing","A share link does not open the scale","Saved scales have gone"],"x":" Why: The collection about 2 MB could not be downloaded. What to do: Check your connection and any content blocker, and reload. Why: The page's introduction recommends filtering by evenness, but the current filter row has only Base hue , Chroma , Lightness and Method . What to do: Narrow the list with the other filters, then compare Min adjacent contrast and the Token contrast ladder on Inspect : uneven scales show one or two big jumps between neighbouring steps. Why: The filters together exclude everything, for example Light lightness with Ink Paper . What to do: Select Reset and add filters back one at a time. Why: Copy CSS vars declares the variables on a class such as .aa shade material like 00001 , not on :root . What to do: Change the selector to :root , or add the class to the element where you use the variables. Why: In almost every scale, the middle steps around 300 – 700 are too close in lightness to both black and white to carry body text. That is expected: they are fills, borders and accents. What to do: Use light steps for surfaces with dark text, dark steps for text or dark surfaces with light text, and check the Token contrast ladder . Why: No scales match the curren"},{"t":"Shade Library FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/docs/faq.html","h":["What is a shade scale?","What are tokens?","What do the methods mean?","What does \"8% even\" mean?","Can every step carry text?","Can I use a scale in Tailwind?","Do I need an account?","Is there an API?"],"x":" One colour taken through lightness in named steps, from a near white tint to a near black shade. Light steps become surfaces, dark steps become text, and middle steps become fills and accents. The named steps of a scale, such as 50 , 100 … 900 , 950 . The collection uses several naming patterns and has between 5 and 21 tokens per scale. They are the ten generation styles: Material Like , Tailwind Like , Brand System , Accessible Ui , Oklch Ramp , Neutral System , Ink Paper , Vivid Product , Duotone Shift and Temperature Shift . Tailwind Like and Material Like follow the step naming of those design systems. The page reports that only 8.2% of the scales have genuinely even steps — no step much larger than the average. Even steps make a scale predictable to use. In 403 of the 8,192 scales, every token reaches 4.5:1 with automatic black or white text. In most scales the middle steps do not. See Analyse the collection analyse the collection.md . Yes: Copy Tailwind gives a colour group keyed by token, and Design tokens… › Tailwind Config gives a full configuration file. No. Yes. The heading links to the Shade Library API guide, and the Automate this note names GET /v1/shade/library . Se"},{"t":"Shade Library: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Shade Library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Scale, token, tint, shade, auto text and other terms. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard and pointer actions. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the figures measure, and what they do not. Related related.md Related libraries, tools and Learn articles. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Shade Library overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Shade Library shortcuts","d":"Keyboard and pointer actions in the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys or action Where Result / Anywhere, when not typing Focuses the search box. Enter or Space A focused swatch Opens its scale on Inspect . Escape Share link or design tokens dialog Closes it. Select a swatch Grid Copies its hex. Select a column Inspect strip Copies its hex. The site wide shortcuts also work here. See Site features ../../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Shade Library glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Auto text The better of near black 111111 or white text for a token: near black on tokens with luminance above 0.5, white otherwise. Base The colour a scale is built around, usually near its middle. Contrast ratio The WCAG 2 lightness difference measure, 1:1 to 21:1. 4.5:1 is AA for body text; 3:1 for large text. Even steps A scale in which no step between neighbouring tokens is much larger than the average step. Min adjacent contrast The contrast between the two most similar neighbouring tokens. OKLCH A perceptual colour space: lightness 0 to 1 , chroma colourfulness and hue angle. Profile The Shade summary badge: Neutral, Hue Shift, Light, Deep or Balanced. Scale shade system, ramp One colour taken through lightness in named steps. Shade A darker version of a colour, towards black. Tint A lighter version of a colour, towards white. Token A named step in a scale, such as 500 . "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Shade Library's figures measure, and what they do not.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" Contrast uses the WCAG 2 formula. \"Auto AA\" tests each token against near black or white, whichever the page picks from the token's luminance the split is at 0.5 . The other text colour can sometimes do slightly better; check WCAG vs white and WCAG vs black on the token cards. Averages lightness and chroma are across all tokens, so a scale with a very light start and a very dark end can average Mid . Base hue is the hue of the base colour only. Scales from the Temperature Shift and Duotone Shift methods deliberately change hue along the ramp; their Hue span shows how much. Score is recorded with each scale when it was generated. It is a ranking aid, not a judgement of fitness for your project. Evenness : the 8.2% figure is reported by the page; there is no per scale evenness figure or filter in the current page. The three word colour names on Inspect come from fixed OKLCH bands and are descriptions, not standard names. Swatches look different on different screens; the values do not. The library is not an accessibility audit of your design. Where a token sits text, border, background and at what size still decides whether it passes. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Shade Library keeps in your browser and what it fetches over the network.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What How to remove it Saved scale ids up to 500 Unsave each one, or clear this site's data. A copy of each saved scale in your Library Unsave it, or remove it in the Library. Whether you dismissed the Automate this note Clear this site's data. Searches and filters are handled in your browser and are not remembered after you leave. On opening, the page downloads the collection from auricartisan.com. Downloads are created in your browser. Download all in the design tokens dialog may fetch a small helper from auricartisan.com. Share links carry the scale in the link; nothing is uploaded. Advertising and analytics follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.9.9 — 5 June 2026","The current page"],"x":" The Shade Library was added in release 0.9.9 as part of the library expansion. See the Changelog ../../../changelog/README.md . The page now filters and scrolls all 8,192 scales at once and shows every tab an earlier Simple/Advanced switch has gone . These changes are not listed as a separate changelog release. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and Learn articles that work alongside the Shade Library.","p":"Website › Library › Colour libraries › Shade Library","u":"website/library/colour-libraries/shade-library/others/related.html","h":["Other colour libraries","Tools","Learn articles","Guides and API"],"x":" Accessibility Library ../../accessibility library/README.md — see what text colours a background allows. Gradient Library ../../gradient library/README.md — measured ramps for smooth blends. Color Library ../../color library/README.md , Palette Library ../../palette library/README.md and Harmony Library ../../harmony library/README.md . Design System Generator ../../../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md — builds accessible OKLCH ramps and a whole design system. Tonal Steps, Tints & Shades ../../../../tools/colorimetry and rendering/tonal steps/README.md — tonal step charts. Contrast Checker ../../../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md . Your Library ../../../../kits/library kit/README.md . Oklab and Oklch: Modern Perceptual Color Spaces — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 06 02 oklab oklch perceptual color spaces Accessible Color Design and WCAG Contrast — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 25 wcag contrast accessible color Color in CSS: Modern Color in the Browser — https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 07 16 color in css modern color in the browser The Shade Library user guide in the D"},{"t":"Documentation","d":"What the documentation library contains, who it is for, and how to find a tool's guide.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The documentation library is where Auric Artisan publishes the written guide for each tool. Its heading, \"Every tool, twice\", describes the idea: most subjects have two documents — a user guide , which explains how to use the tool, and a developer reference , which explains how it works and what it computes. You pick the subject, then pick which of the two you want. The index lists 54 subjects and 89 documents. 35 subjects have both a guide and a reference; the others have one. Subjects cover the site's tools such as the URL Analyzer, Vision Simulation and the Font Library , the colour libraries, the browser extension and design tool plugins, the generators behind the libraries, and the public REST API, including guides to using the Palette, Gradient, Harmony, Shade and accessibility collections from your own code. Anyone who wants step by step help with a tool: read its user guide. Developers and technical users who want to know exactly what a tool measures and how: read its developer reference. Developers automating the site's tools: read the API guides and the endpoint reference. The index: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/ From the site header: Learn menu › Docum"},{"t":"Documentation: docs","d":"Guides for using the documentation library, the list of all subjects, and the reference.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The index page: search, the Both / Guides / References filter and the subject rows. read a guide.md read a guide.md A documentation article: the side list, breadcrumb, pair switch, contents, code blocks and pager. all subjects.md all subjects.md All 54 subjects with links to their user guides and developer references. reference.md reference.md Every control and label on the index and article pages. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Documentation overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Use the documentation index to find a tool's user guide or developer reference.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the index","The page","Find a guide","Show only guides or only references","Which should I read?","Result"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/, or open the site header's Learn menu and choose Documentation . The kicker Documentation and the heading Every tool, twice , with the line \"35 of 54 subjects carry both a user guide and a developer reference. Pick the subject, then pick which of the two you are.\" A search box, Search 54 subjects… . An audience switch: Both , Guides , References . A count, for example 54 subjects · 89 documents . The list of subjects, alphabetical. Each row has the subject's name a link to its first document , a one line description, and one or two buttons: Guide and Reference . 1. Type part of the tool's name or a word from its description into the search box, for example gamut . 2. The list narrows as you type, and the count updates, for example 3 subjects · 6 documents . 3. Select Guide for the user guide, or Reference for the developer reference. If nothing matches, the page says No subject matches that. Try a tool name. Select Guides to hide every Reference button, or References to hide every Guide button. Subjects that have only the other kind disappear, and the count changes to match. Select Both to show everything again. You can link st"},{"t":"All documentation subjects","d":"Every subject in the documentation library, with links to its user guide and developer reference.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/all-subjects.html","h":[],"x":" The documentation library at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/ lists 54 subjects and 89 documents. 35 subjects have both a user guide and a developer reference; the rest have one of the two. This page lists them all, in the order the index shows them, with the index's own one line description. Note: Some guides describe an earlier version of their tool. Where a guide and the tool disagree, the tool is right. The guides for the Accessibility Library and the Palette Library, for example, describe earlier layouts. Accessibility Gen — User guide https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 25 accessibility gen user guide · Developer reference https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 25 accessibility gen developer reference . Check foreground and background color pairs against WCAG 2.1, WCAG 2.2, WCAG 3.0 APCA, Auric SD Flexible and Strict. Accessibility Library — User guide https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 26 accessibility library user guide · Developer reference https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/articles/2026 05 26 accessibility library developer reference . Browse 5,000,000 determinis"},{"t":"Read a guide","d":"Find your way around a documentation article: the subject list, breadcrumb, pair switch, contents, code blocks and pager.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/read-a-guide.html","h":["The parts of the page","Tips","Result"],"x":" Documentation articles share a three column layout on wide screens: every subject on the left, the article in the middle, and its contents on the right. On narrow screens the columns stack. Part What it does Subject list left Headed Documentation . Every subject, alphabetically; the current one is highlighted and scrolled into view. Select a subject to open its first document. Breadcrumb Documentation › the subject's name. Select Documentation to return to the index. Pair switch User guide and Developer reference . The current document is highlighted; select the other to switch. If a subject has only one document, the missing half is shown greyed out, with the tooltip \"No user guide for this subject yet\" or \"No developer reference for this subject yet\". Title and introduction The subject's name and a short introduction. Author and dates Who wrote the document and when it was published or updated, where the article states them. On this page right The article's numbered sections. Select one to jump to it. On narrow screens it is a collapsible list. Sections The article itself. Code blocks Each has a Copy button. After copying it reads Copied ; if your browser blocks the clipboard it"},{"t":"Documentation reference","d":"Every control and label on the documentation index and on documentation articles.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/reference.html","h":["Index page (https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/)","Article pages","Other addresses"],"x":" Control What it does Values Default Search 54 subjects… Shows subjects whose name or description contains the text. Any text Empty Audience switch Shows both kinds of document, or only one. Both , Guides , References Both Count Subjects and documents currently shown. For example 54 subjects · 89 documents — Subject row Name link , description, Guide and/or Reference buttons. — — No subject matches that. Try a tool name. Shown when nothing matches. — — Address Effect ?audience=guide Opens the index showing guides only. ?audience=reference Opens the index showing references only. Element What it does Documentation side list All subjects; current one highlighted. Breadcrumb Documentation › subject. User guide / Developer reference Switch between the pair; a missing half is greyed out. On this page Section links. Copy on code blocks Copies the code; shows Copied or Press Ctrl C . The pair Link to the other document for the subject. Next subject Link to the next subject alphabetically. Page Address API endpoint reference https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/ URL Analyzer API guide https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/analyzer/ RSS feed https://auricartisan.c"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes when using the documentation library.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["A subject disappeared when I chose Guides or References","\"No subject matches that. Try a tool name.\"","The guide does not match what I see in the tool","The side list or the pair switch is missing","\"Press Ctrl C\" appears instead of \"Copied\""],"x":" Why: The subject has only the other kind of document. Hiding it avoids showing a row with nothing to open. What to do: Select Both . Why: No subject name or description contains your text. What to do: Use a shorter word, or the tool's name as it appears in the site's menus. Descriptions use US spelling \"color\" . Why: Guides are dated. Some tools have been redesigned since their guide was written — for example the Accessibility Library and the Palette Library. What to do: Trust the tool. Check the date on the guide, and see this documentation set for current behaviour. Why: The article could not load the list of subjects, for example because the connection dropped. The article itself is still complete. What to do: Reload the page. Use the breadcrumb or your browser's back button to reach the index. Why: Your browser blocked clipboard access. What to do: The code is selected for you; press Ctrl + C on a Mac, the equivalent copy command . "},{"t":"Documentation FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the documentation library.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/docs/faq.html","h":["What is the difference between a user guide and a developer reference?","Why do some subjects have only one document?","Where is the API documentation?","Can I follow new documents?","Does the documentation library work without JavaScript?"],"x":" A user guide shows how to use a tool. A developer reference explains how it works — the methods, formulas and data behind the results. Some tools have only a guide so far, and some subjects such as a measurement method behind a tool have only a reference. The pair switch on each article shows which half exists. The API guides are listed as subjects ending in \"API\", and the full endpoint reference is at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/. See also Public API ../../../../services/public api/README.md . Yes, with the RSS feed at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/rss.xml. Yes. The index is a plain list of links; search, the audience filter and the article side list are added on top. "},{"t":"Documentation: other material","d":"Supporting material for the documentation library.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Subject, user guide, developer reference and other terms. Related related.md Where else to find help. Privacy privacy.md What the documentation pages store and send. Back to the Documentation overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Documentation glossary","d":"Terms used in the documentation library.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Subject A tool or topic in the documentation index, such as \"Gamut Map\". User guide A document that explains how to use a tool. Developer reference A document that explains how a tool works and what it computes. Pair A subject's user guide and developer reference together. Audience Which kind of document the index shows: Both , Guides or References . API guide A guide to getting a tool's results from your own code through the site's REST API. Endpoint reference The list of the REST API's endpoints and their parameters. RSS A feed format for following new documents in a news reader. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the documentation pages store and send.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The documentation index and articles do not ask for any information and do not keep a history of what you read. Search and the audience filter run in your browser. The audience you choose can be part of the page address ?audience=… , so it appears in your browser history like any other address. Articles download a list of subjects from auricartisan.com to build the side list and the pair switch. Analytics on the site follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Related","d":"Other places to find help with Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Library › Documentation","u":"website/library/documentation/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Collections ../../collections/README.md — every tool, to open alongside its guide. Learn ../../learn/README.md — the colour science behind the tools. Changelog ../../changelog/README.md — what changed in each release. Public API ../../../../services/public api/README.md — the REST API. Help ../../../../help/README.md — the FAQ, glossary and contact options for the whole site. "},{"t":"Learn","d":"What the Learn library is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to start reading.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Learn is Auric Artisan's library of long form articles about colour: 113 articles that run, in the page's words, \"from what light is to how a press holds a colour\". The Learn page presents them as a course, in the order they were written to be read, numbered 1 to 113, with about 64 hours of reading in total. You can start at article 1 and work through, or filter by one of seven categories — Foundations, Physics, Vision, Colorimetry, Digital, Design and Print — and take the part you need. Most articles are interactive. They include live demos the site calls them labs that you can open in a panel, adjust and explore — spectra you can reshape, contrast you can test, gamuts you can rotate — and end with a short quiz and a \"Continue your journey\" section that suggests what to read next based on the article, the course order and what you have already read. The Learn page remembers how far you have got, in your browser. It shows a tick next to articles you have read, a progress bar, and a link to pick up where you left off. Students and self learners who want a structured course in colour science. Designers and developers who want the reasoning behind contrast, colour spaces, gradients a"},{"t":"Learn documentation","d":"The guides, catalogue, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Learn library.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md The Learn page: the course list, categories, search, progress and resuming. read an article.md read an article.md An article page: header actions, contents, badges, live demos, the quiz, print and download. continue your journey.md continue your journey.md How the end of article recommendations are chosen, pinning and More like this . article catalog.md article catalog.md Every article, grouped by category, with number, reading time and summary. reference.md reference.md Every control and label on the Learn page and article pages. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Learn overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Use the Learn page to browse the course, filter by category, search, and pick up where you left off.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the Learn page","The page, top to bottom","How \"read\" is decided","Your first task: start the course"],"x":" Go to https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/, or choose Learning Hub from the Learn menu in the site header. Learn , with a line such as: \"Every article on this site about colour, in the order it was written to be read — 113 of them, about 64 hours end to end, from what light is to how a press holds a colour. Start at one, or take the part you need.\" Once you have opened at least one article, a panel appears under the heading: Pick up where you left off — the article you opened most recently and did not finish; or Next in the course — the first article, in course order, that you have not read. It shows the article's number, title, category and reading time, and a progress bar with a line such as 12 of 113 read · about 58 hours to go . Search titles and topics — type one or more words. An article is shown when every word appears in its number, title, summary or category. The list updates as you type. Category chips — All and the seven categories, in the order the course introduces them: Foundations , Physics , Vision , Colorimetry , Digital , Design , Print . Each chip shows how many articles it holds. Select a chip to show only that category; select it again or All to show everyt"},{"t":"Learn article catalogue","d":"Every published Learn article, grouped by topic, with its number in the course, reading time, link and a one-line summary.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/article-catalog.html","h":["Categories","Foundations","Physics","Vision","Colorimetry","Digital","Design","Print","Notes"],"x":" This catalogue lists all 113 articles in the Learn library, grouped by the seven categories the Learn page uses as filters. Within each group, articles are in course order: the number before each title is its place in the course, which is meant to be read from 1 to 113. Together they take about 64 hours to read. Each entry gives the article number, the title linked to the article , the reading time stated on the article, and a one line summary taken from the article's own description. Titles keep the site's published spelling. Category Articles Reading time Foundations 15 about 8 hours Physics 17 about 9 hours Vision 16 about 8 hours Colorimetry 17 about 11 hours Digital 18 about 11 hours Design 15 about 8 hours Print 15 about 8 hours What colour is, how it has been understood, and the ideas everything else builds on. 1. What Color Is and How Humans See It https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/articles/2026 05 04 what color is and how humans see it — 45 min. An interactive, comprehensive guide to color: the physics of light, the biology of vision, photoreceptor science, trichromatic and opponent theories. 2. The History of Color Science from Newton to Hering https://auricartisan."},{"t":"Continue your journey","d":"How the recommendations at the end of each Learn article are chosen, and how to pin articles and see more suggestions.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/continue-your-journey.html","h":["What you see","How suggestions are chosen","Pin an article","See more","If the suggestions do not change","Result"],"x":" Every Learn article ends with Continue your journey . Instead of a fixed list, the page suggests seven articles chosen for the one you are reading and for what you have already read in this browser. A line above the cards: Tailored to the article's category, followed by You've read N of 113 in the library . A More like this button, when there are more suggestions to show. One featured card, full width — usually the natural next article. Six more cards. Each card has an illustration coloured by category, a small badge giving the reason it was chosen, the title, the category, a tick if you have read it, and a pin button. Badge Meaning Pinned You pinned this article. Up next in a category The next unread article in the same category, in course order. Shares a topic It shares one or more topic tags with the current article. More in a category It is in the same category. Related idea Its title or summary shares key words with the current article. Recommended A good general match. The page scores every other article against the one you are reading: same category: a strong boost; each shared topic tag: a boost; shared key words in title and summary: a small boost; close to it in course o"},{"t":"Read an article","d":"Find your way around a Learn article: header actions, facts, table of contents, live demos, the quiz, printing and downloading.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/read-an-article.html","h":["The header","The table of contents","Sections","Live demos","Test your understanding","Continue your journey","The foot of the article","Keeping your place","Result"],"x":" Every Learn article follows the same layout. This page walks through it from top to bottom. A small line reading Auric Artisan · Learn above the title. The title and an introductory paragraph. A row of facts, each with a bold label: the article's category and its number in the course for example \"Physics · 112\" , how many live demos it has, the reading time for example \"~30 min\" , and its subject. Three actions: Action What it does Download Opens a small menu: Markdown \".md — Formatted, portable text\" or Plain text \".txt — Just the words\" . The file is made in your browser from the article's text; interactive demos, figures and the quiz are left out. Print Opens your browser's print dialog. ← All Articles Returns to the Learn page. Downloaded files are named after the article, without the date, for example the color of heat.md . Each starts with the title, the introduction and a \"Source:\" line with the article's address. Press Escape to close the Download menu. A Table of Contents lists the article's numbered sections. Select an entry to jump to it. A reading progress bar at the top of the window fills as you scroll. Articles are divided into numbered sections, typically: an intro"},{"t":"Learn reference","d":"Every control and label on the Learn page and on Learn article pages.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/reference.html","h":["The Learn page (https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/)","An article page","Keys","Addresses"],"x":" Element What it does or shows Heading line Number of articles and total reading time. Pick up where you left off / Next in the course Your most recent unfinished article, or the first unread one; with number, title, category, minutes. Shown only after you have opened an article. Progress bar N of 113 read · time left. Search titles and topics Filters as you type; every word must match the number, title, summary or category. Category chips All , Foundations , Physics , Vision , Colorimetry , Digital , Design , Print , each with a count. Select again to clear. Count line N of 113 · time, shown only when filtered. Course row Number, title link , category, minutes, tick when read, summary. Nothing in the course matches that. No results; Show all articles clears the search and category. Foot Links to the blog and changelog. If the course list cannot be built for example, offline , the page shows a plain list of All articles instead. Category Articles Includes Foundations 15 — Physics 17 — Vision 16 — Colorimetry 17 Articles tagged Computational Digital 18 Articles tagged Measurement and Workflows Design 15 — Print 15 — Shown in minutes per article; totals under 90 minutes are given in "},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems on the Learn page and in Learn articles.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The Learn page shows a plain list, with no search or categories","My progress and ticks have gone","An article I finished is not ticked","\"Continue your journey\" is the same on every visit","A live demo will not open, or looks empty","The downloaded file has no demos or pictures","Search finds nothing"],"x":" Why: The page could not load the Learn catalogue, so it shows the built in list of all articles instead. What to do: Check your connection and reload. Every link in the plain list still works. Why: Progress is kept in this browser only. It does not follow you to another browser or device, and clearing this site's data, or using a private window, removes it. What to do: Nothing can restore it. Reading past 55% of an article marks it as read again. Why: An article counts as read when you have scrolled at least 55% of the way through it. Jumping straight to the end with the table of contents still counts; reading only the top half does not. What to do: Scroll through the article. Why: If the Learn catalogue cannot load, or the article is not in it, the author's original suggestions stay. What to do: Reload with a working connection. Also note that pinned articles always come first. Why: Demos need JavaScript and a modern browser. Some content blockers or very old browsers stop them. What to do: Allow scripts for auricartisan.com and use a current browser. Try Full screen if the demo is cramped. Why: Download saves the article's text only. Demos, figures and the quiz are left out by d"},{"t":"Learn FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Learn library.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/docs/faq.html","h":["How many articles are there?","Do I have to read them in order?","Do I need an account?","Does my progress sync between devices?","Can I keep a copy of an article?","Are the demos accurate?","Is there a feed?","Why do titles say \"color\"?"],"x":" 113, numbered in course order, taking about 64 hours in total. See the Article catalogue article catalog.md . No. The order is a suggested path from basics to specialist topics. Filter by category or search for what you need. No. Everything is free and open, and your progress is kept in your browser. No. Progress, ticks and pins stay in the browser where you read. Yes. Use Download for Markdown or plain text, or Print . They are teaching models built for the article, computed in your browser. They illustrate the ideas faithfully but are not measurement instruments. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . Yes: https://auricartisan.com/library/learn/rss.xml. Article titles keep the spelling they were published with. The site's own interface text uses British spelling. "},{"t":"Learn: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Learn library: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related pages, privacy and release notes.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms used on the Learn page and in article chrome. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys on the Learn page and in articles. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the articles, demos and progress tracking are and are not. Related related.md Libraries and tools that put the articles into practice. Privacy privacy.md What Learn remembers in your browser. Release notes release notes.md User facing history. Back to the Learn overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Learn shortcuts","d":"Keys and pointer actions on the Learn page and in Learn articles.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/shortcuts.html","h":[],"x":" Keys or action Where Effect Type in Search titles and topics Learn page Filters the course as you type. Select a category chip again Learn page Clears the category. Escape Demo panel Closes the panel. Escape Download menu Closes the menu. Select Dock panel / Full screen Demo panel Docks or enlarges the demo. Select More like this End of article Shows the next seven suggestions. Your browser's own print shortcut works on articles as well as Print . The site wide shortcuts also work. See Site features ../../../site features/README.md . "},{"t":"Learn glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used on the Learn page and in Learn articles' page furniture.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Each article also ends with its own glossary, The terms, defined , for the colour science terms it teaches. This page covers the terms of the Learn library itself. Term Meaning Article number An article's place in the course, from 1 to 113. Category One of seven groups used to filter the course: Foundations, Physics, Vision, Colorimetry, Digital, Design, Print. Course order The order the articles were written to be read in, from what light is to printing. Continue your journey The personalised suggestions at the end of each article. Docked A demo panel placed beside the article so both can be seen. Lab, live demo An interactive demonstration inside an article, opened with Live demo . Pin A mark that keeps an article at the front of Continue your journey . Quick check The short quiz at the end of an article. Read An article you have scrolled at least 55% of the way through, in this browser. RSS A feed format that lets a news reader show new articles automatically. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Learn articles, demos and progress tracking are, and what they are not.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The articles","The demos","Reading times and categories","Progress tracking"],"x":" The articles are educational explanations of colour science, perception and practice. They are not standards documents; where an article describes a standard such as WCAG or a CIE formula , the standard itself is the authority. Articles on vision and light — for example colour vision deficiency or light and the body clock — are written to educate, not to diagnose or advise on health. Consult a professional for medical questions. Demos are teaching models computed in your browser. They follow the published formulas their articles describe, but: colours on screen depend on your display, its settings and the light around you; simulations of colour vision deficiency show typical cases, not any particular person's sight; numbers are rounded for display. Use the site's tools for measurement work see Related related.md . Reading times are the authors' estimates. Three small categories Computational, Measurement, Workflows are folded into Colorimetry and Digital on the Learn page. \"Read\" means scrolled past 55% of the page in this browser. It does not know whether you actually read the text, and it is lost if the browser's site data is cleared. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Learn library remembers in your browser and what uses the network.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays in your browser","What uses the network"],"x":" What Why How to remove it How far you scrolled in each article, and when To tick read articles, show your progress and offer Pick up where you left off . Clear this site's data. Articles you pinned in Continue your journey To keep them at the front of the suggestions. Unpin them, or clear this site's data. None of this is sent to Auric Artisan or linked to an account. Pages, images and the Learn catalogue are downloaded from auricartisan.com. Demos run in your browser. Download builds the file in your browser. Advertising and analytics follow your consent choices. See Company and legal ../../../company and legal/README.md . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of the Learn library.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" 4 May 2026 — Article 1, \"What Color Is and How Humans See It\", the course's cornerstone explainer. 0.9.9, 5 June 2026 — the release added Learn content alongside documentation and blog content see the Changelog ../../changelog/README.md . May to August 2026 — articles were published in course order, one a day for much of the period, reaching 113 articles; the most recent is dated 31 August 2026. The current Learn page presents the articles as a course in reading order, with categories, search, reading times, progress ticks and a resume link, and each article ends with personalised Continue your journey suggestions. "},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries and tools that put the Learn articles into practice.","p":"Website › Library › Learn","u":"website/library/learn/others/related.html","h":["Put the ideas to work","Keep up"],"x":" Colour libraries ../../colour libraries/README.md — measured colours, palettes, gradients, harmonies, shade scales and contrast pairs. Collections ../../collections/README.md — every Auric Artisan tool. Documentation ../../documentation/README.md — how to use each tool. Accessibility and vision tools ../../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md , starting with the URL Analyzer. Colour Science Lab ../../../tools/colour workspace/colour science lab/README.md . Blog ../../blog/README.md — shorter notes on what is being built. Changelog ../../changelog/README.md — what changed in each release. "},{"t":"Portfolio Builder and Portfolio Index","d":"What the Portfolio Builder and the Portfolio Index are, who they are for, and how to publish your first portfolio.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Portfolio Builder at https://auricartisan.com/portfolio/ turns the work you make on Auric Artisan into a public page. You stack sections — headings, Markdown text, images, galleries, a timeline, stats, testimonials, your saved palettes and more, 25 kinds in all — and type straight into a live preview of the page as it builds beside you. You choose a typeface, a paper and a rhythm, and an accent colour taken from your own saved palettes and graded for contrast. A Check pane audits the rendered page for accessibility problems before anyone else sees it. When it is ready, you publish it at your own address, auricartisan.com/p/your name , or share it privately as a self contained link. You can also download it as an HTML file or PDF, or export the document as JSON to keep or move. Publishing again updates the same address, and you can take it down at any time. The Portfolio Index at https://auricartisan.com/portfolios/ lists portfolios in one place — those made with the builder and those people keep on their own sites — searchable by name, craft, place and colour. A builder portfolio joins it when you publish unless you switch that off ; a portfolio on your own site can be added t"},{"t":"Portfolio documentation","d":"Task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Portfolio Builder and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/README.html","h":["The builder","The Portfolio Index","Reference and help"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Signing in, a tour of the builder and a first portfolio. templates.md templates.md The eight templates and what each contains. manage sections.md manage sections.md Adding, ordering, hiding, duplicating and deleting sections; bulk actions. section types.md section types.md All 25 section types and every field they have. edit in the preview.md edit in the preview.md Typing into the live preview, the section rail and the row controls. markdown and raw html.md markdown and raw html.md What Markdown the builder understands, and what Raw HTML allows and removes. header and avatar.md header and avatar.md The Header panel, following your profile, and choosing an avatar. style and theme.md style and theme.md Typeface, paper, rhythm and accent. preview and check.md preview and check.md Preview widths, full screen, full preview, and the Check pane. save undo and sync.md save undo and sync.md Autosave, draft sync to your account, undo and redo. export and import.md export and import.md HTML, PDF, JSON, import, snapshot links and the credit line. publish and share.md publish and share.md The publish dialog, your address, sharing, updat"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Sign in, learn the builder's screen, and build and publish a first portfolio.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Sign in","A tour of the screen","Your first portfolio"],"x":" Open https://auricartisan.com/portfolio/. If you are not signed in, the page shows Sign in to build your portfolio — \"Sign in to add sections, write in Markdown or HTML, showcase your work, and publish or export your portfolio.\" — with a Sign In button. Sign in, and the builder opens. For accounts and signing in, see Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md . Part What it does Your portfolio and an address Your published address, for example auricartisan.com/p/your name , and Not published until it is live. Command field — \"Add a section, change the look, publish…\" Ctrl K Opens a searchable list of everything the builder can do. Type a few letters and press Enter . Section count and Saved How many sections the page has, and whether your latest change is saved. Undo and Redo Step back and forward through changes. Templates Start from a ready made layout. Preview Open the finished page in a new tab. Export Download HTML or PDF, export or import JSON, copy a snapshot link, and the credit line switch. Publish Open the publish dialog. On narrower screens, Templates , Preview and Export may be tucked away; the command field still reaches them. Content — the Header panel a"},{"t":"Edit in the preview","d":"Type directly into the live preview, use the section rail and row controls, and add sections in place.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/edit-in-the-preview.html","h":["Type into the page","The section rail","Row controls","Add a section at the end","Result"],"x":" The live preview is not only a picture of your page: you can write in it. Click a heading and type; the change is saved and appears everywhere the portfolio goes. 1. Hover over text in the preview. Editable text shows a faint outline. 2. Click it. A coloured outline shows you are editing. 3. Type. Empty fields show grey example text until you fill them. 4. Finish: Enter finishes a one line field a heading, a name, a button label . In longer fields quotes, descriptions, code, Markdown , Enter starts a new line; click elsewhere to finish. Escape finishes too. Pasting into a plain field pastes text only, without formatting. Section Editable in the page Heading The heading text Text / Markdown The whole text kept as Markdown Two columns Each column kept as Markdown Quote The quote and the attribution Testimonial The quote, name and role Callout The text kept as Markdown Button The label Call to action The heading, text and button label Image The caption Code The code Skills / Tags The title Timeline The title, and each entry's date, title, subtitle and description Stats The title, and each metric's value and label Feature list The title, and each feature's title and description Steps "},{"t":"Export and import","d":"Download your portfolio as HTML or PDF, export and import the JSON document, copy a snapshot link, and control the credit line.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/export-and-import.html","h":["The credit line","Printing and PDF","Snapshot links","Result"],"x":" Select Export in the top bar to open the menu. Each item is also a command in the command field. Menu item What you get Message Download HTML A single, self contained .html file of the finished page, including its styles and the live palette swatches. Open it in any browser or host it anywhere. HTML downloaded. Download PDF Opens the page in a new tab and your browser's print dialog; choose Save as PDF or your browser's equivalent there. — Export JSON The portfolio document as a .json file: header, sections and style. Use it as a backup or to move the portfolio. Portfolio JSON exported. Import JSON… Pick a .json file exported from the builder. It replaces your current portfolio undoable . Portfolio imported. or That file is not a valid portfolio export. Copy snapshot link A link that contains the whole portfolio. Public link copied File names are based on your name. At the foot of the menu, the switch \"Made with Auric Artisan\" credit — \"On every exported HTML and PDF. Paid plans can drop it.\" — adds a small \"Made with Auric Artisan\" line at the end of exported files. On a paid plan that includes watermark free exports, you can switch it off. On a free plan, switching it off explai"},{"t":"Header and avatar","d":"Fill in the portfolio header, follow your profile or override it, choose what to show, and set an avatar.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/header-and-avatar.html","h":["The fields","Choose an avatar","Result"],"x":" The Header panel at the top of the Content column controls the top of your portfolio: \"The top of your portfolio. Leave a field blank to follow your profile.\" Field Limit Show switch Notes Name 80 characters Always shown Blank follows your profile's display name. Headline / tagline 120 characters Always shown Also used on your share card. Email 120 characters Show — off by default The address you publish can differ from the one you sign in with. Location 80 characters Show — on by default Placeholder \"City, Country\". Website 200 characters Show — on by default — Avatar image address 500 characters Show — on by default Or pick a picture below . Accent A colour picker — The page's accent colour, also set from Style . A blank field is not \"no value\" — it means \"use my profile\". The profile's value appears as grey placeholder text in the empty field, so you can see what the page will say. Type into the field to use a different value just for your portfolio; clear it to go back to following your profile. Changes to your profile then reach the portfolio automatically. A Show switch that is off keeps that detail off the page, off exports and out of anything you publish or share, even if "},{"t":"List your portfolio","d":"Put a builder portfolio or a portfolio on your own site into the Portfolio Index, check its status, change it or take it out.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/list-your-portfolio.html","h":["A portfolio made with the builder","A portfolio on your own site","Check your entries","Change or remove an external entry","Result"],"x":" There are two ways into the Portfolio Index portfolio index.md : publish with the Portfolio Builder, or add a portfolio you keep on your own site through the Search Console. 1. Publish your portfolio at an address see Publish and share publish and share.md . 2. In the publish dialog's settings, keep Let search engines list it and List it in the Portfolio Index switched on both are on by default . 3. Wait a little: builder portfolios are copied into the index within fifteen minutes of publishing. It joins as Made here , with its palette, crafts and headline. Changes you publish later are copied in the same way. To leave the index, switch off List it in the Portfolio Index or Let search engines list it and select Publish these changes . Unpublishing also removes it. You add these in the Search Console's Portfolios tab at https://auricartisan.com/search/console/ portfolios the Add one you host button on the index goes there . You need to be signed in. 1. Open the Portfolios tab. It lists Made with the Portfolio Builder and Kept on your own sites . 2. Under Add a portfolio you keep elsewhere , fill in: Field Required Notes Address Yes For example https://yourname.com/work/ . Name Yes "},{"t":"Manage sections","d":"Add, open, reorder, hide, duplicate and delete sections, and use the bulk actions.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/manage-sections.html","h":["Add a section","The section card","Bulk actions","Tips","Result"],"x":" A portfolio is a stack of sections , shown top to bottom in the order you set. Each section has a card in the Content column. Any of these adds one: Add a section at the foot of the Content column: type in Search sections… to narrow the 25 types, then select a tile. Each tile shows the type's name and a short hint; hover for the hint. If nothing matches, it says No sections match that search. The builder confirms, for example, Added a Timeline section. In the preview, the add control at the end of the page, or Add a section below on a section's rail see Edit in the preview edit in the preview.md . The command field: type \"add\" and choose, for example, Add a Gallery section . New sections start empty; grey example text placeholders shows what goes where, and disappears as you type. With no sections yet, the column says No sections yet — add one below to start building. Control What it does Drag handle ⠿ Drag to reorder \"Drag to reorder\" . Chevron ▾ Expand or collapse the card's fields. Type icon and name Which kind of section it is. Hidden badge Shown when the section is hidden from the portfolio. Eye button Hide from portfolio / Show in portfolio . Hidden sections stay in your dra"},{"t":"Markdown and Raw HTML","d":"The Markdown the Portfolio Builder understands, and what a Raw HTML section keeps and removes.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/markdown-and-raw-html.html","h":["Markdown","Raw HTML"],"x":" Markdown is a simple way to format text with ordinary characters: bold , Heading , item . The Text / Markdown , Two columns , Callout and FAQ answer fields accept it. You type You get Heading to Heading Headings, levels 1 to 6 bold , italic Bold, italic label https://example.com A link label https://example.com \"Title\" A link with a title <https://example.com or a bare https://example.com A link ! alt text https://example.com/pic.png An image code Inline code A line of three or more , or A horizontal rule quoted A block quote quotes can contain other Markdown item or 1. item , indented for sub items Lists, including nested lists task , x done Task lists, shown as ticked or unticked boxes that visitors cannot change A pipe table with a row, and : : for alignment A table; wide tables scroll sideways Three backticks, optionally followed by a language A code block Tips: Links and images need full https:// addresses. An address with spaces can be wrapped in angle brackets: <https://example.com/my file.png . Images from other websites load on your published page as long as they are served over https:// . A line break inside a paragraph is kept as a line break. The Raw HTML section lets "},{"t":"The Portfolio Index","d":"Browse, search and filter the Portfolio Index by name, craft, place and colour, and share a search.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/portfolio-index.html","h":["The page","Search","Filter","Sort and view","The cards","Messages","Share a search","How a portfolio gets in"],"x":" The Portfolio Index at https://auricartisan.com/portfolios/ is \"Every portfolio, in one place\": portfolios made with the Portfolio Builder and portfolios people keep on their own sites, \"searched together by name, craft, place and colour\". Anyone can browse it; no account is needed. The heading, with Publish yours opens the Portfolio Builder and Add one you host opens the Search Console's Portfolios tab . Four counts: In the index , Made here , From elsewhere , Verified . The search box. Source buttons, Filters , the results, and How a portfolio gets in . Type into Search by name, craft, place or a colour like d3af37 , or press / anywhere on the page to jump to it. Results update as you type; Escape clears the box. Words are matched against names, headlines, crafts, places and descriptions, with allowance for typing mistakes and word beginnings. You can also use: You type It means \"exact words\" Those words together, in that order. word Leave out results with that word. A hex colour such as d3af37 Portfolios whose colours are nearest to it come first colours are compared perceptually, in OKLab . tag:branding or tag:\"brand identity\" A craft. in:lisbon A place. made:here / made:elsew"},{"t":"Preview and check","d":"Preview your portfolio at different widths and full screen, and use the Check pane to fix accessibility problems before publishing.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/preview-and-check.html","h":["Preview widths","Full preview in a new tab","The Check pane","Result"],"x":" The Live preview bar has four width buttons: Button Width Use Fit default The width of the preview column, at full size Writing and editing. Desktop 1160 px Checking the desktop layout. Tablet 800 px Checking a tablet layout. Mobile 390 px Checking a phone layout. The bar shows the current width for example Desktop · 1160px and the number of sections. Desktop, Tablet and Mobile may be scaled down to fit the column; Fit is the width to write at. The builder remembers your choice in this browser. Fullscreen preview the button at the right of the bar enlarges the preview to fill the screen; select it again, or press Escape , to leave. Select Preview in the top bar or the command Open a full preview . The finished page opens in a new tab, exactly as an exported HTML file would look. If nothing opens, the builder says Allow pop ups to preview. — allow pop ups for auricartisan.com. Open Check . It audits the page as it is actually rendered — the colours, sizes and text a visitor will get — against WCAG 2.2 AA. Finding Severity What it means The fix it suggests Text below AA Blocking when well below; otherwise a warning Normal text is under 4.5:1 against its background. \"Take a darker st"},{"t":"Publish and share","d":"Publish your portfolio at your own address or as a private link, update it, control search, the index, PDF and views, and unpublish.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/publish-and-share.html","h":["Choose who can see it","Publish at an address","When it is live","Settings","Take it down","Share a private link","Close","Result"],"x":" Select Publish in the top bar. The dialog, headed Portfolio and Put this online , shows Not published until your page is live. If Publish is greyed out, the Check pane has blocking findings to fix first; see Preview and check preview and check.md . Choice What it means Public at an address \"Anyone with the link can open it, and it stays current — publish again and the same address shows the new version.\" Only people I send the link to \"No address on the site, and search engines never see it.\" The builder gives you a snapshot link instead: \"The link is the portfolio\" — it needs no account, works offline, never updates, and can be too long to paste in some places if the page has several images. 1. Choose Public at an address . 2. In Your address , after auricartisan.com/p/ , type the name you want. Lower case letters, numbers and hyphens, 2 to 31 characters. While you type, the field says Checking… , then whether the address is available; a tick shows when it is yours to take. Under the field, Or take offers suggestions based on your name. 3. Look at the side panel: What a shared link shows — the card people see when your address is shared in a chat or social app: your name, headlin"},{"t":"Save, undo and sync","d":"How the Portfolio Builder saves your draft, keeps it on your account, and lets you undo and redo.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/save-undo-and-sync.html","h":["Autosave","Draft sync","Undo and redo","Keep a copy yourself","Result"],"x":" There is no Save button. Every change is saved automatically. The top bar shows the state: Label Meaning Saved Kept in this browser. Tooltip: \"Kept in this browser. Sign in and it follows you.\" Saved to your account Kept in this browser and on your account. Tooltip: \"Kept in this browser and on your account\". Saving your draft never changes what visitors see. Only Publish does that. When you are signed in, your draft is also kept on your account, so it follows you to another browser or device. Open the builder on another device and it loads the newer copy: Loaded your portfolio from your account. when this browser had nothing or Loaded the newer draft from your account. A brand new, untouched starter page never overwrites real work on your account. The builder does not replace a draft you are in the middle of editing. If the account copy cannot be reached, the builder keeps working in this browser and tries again later. Select Undo or Redo in the top bar \"Undo Ctrl+Z \", \"Redo Ctrl+Shift+Z \" , or use the commands Undo and Redo in the command field. Undo covers adding, editing, moving, hiding, duplicating and deleting sections, bulk actions, templates and imports. The buttons are gr"},{"t":"Section types","d":"All 25 section types in the Portfolio Builder and every field and option each one has.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/section-types.html","h":["Text and structure","Images and media","Actions and links","Your work","Lists","Quotes and notes","Data and code","Spacing","Empty sections"],"x":" The Add a section panel offers 25 types, in this order. Each entry lists the tile's hint and every field on the section's card. Fields marked \"Markdown\" accept the Markdown described in Markdown and Raw HTML markdown and raw html.md . Field Values Default Text Any text Empty Size H1 , H2 , H3 H2 Align Left , Center , Right Left Field Values Markdown Markdown text. \"Supports headings, bold/italic, links, images, lists, quotes, code.\" Field Values HTML Your HTML, including <style . \"Styles, SVG and page structure all work. Scripts, iframes and forms are removed — your page is opened by strangers. A <style block only reaches this section.\" Field Values Left column Markdown Markdown Right column Markdown Markdown Field Values Default Image URL An https:// address Empty Or upload Choose image An image file from your device — Alt text A description for screen readers Empty Caption Text under the image Empty Width Full , Half , Small Full Links to An optional address the image opens Empty Uploaded images are stored inside the portfolio itself, which makes it larger see Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md . Field Values Default Columns 2 , 3 , 4 3 Image list One address p"},{"t":"Style and theme","d":"Choose a typeface, paper, rhythm and accent for your portfolio, with the accent graded for contrast.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/style-and-theme.html","h":["Typeface","Paper","Rhythm","Accent","Reset","From the command field","Result"],"x":" Open the Style tab. A portfolio's look is four choices, each from a named, checked set rather than free colour pickers, so the page stays readable. Choice Headings Body text Fraunces default Fraunces serif Manrope sans serif Newsreader Newsreader Newsreader Space Grotesk Space Grotesk Space Grotesk Manrope Manrope Manrope The page's background and text colour. Choice Background Notes Cream default FBFAF7 Dark text. White FFFFFF Dark text. Sand F2EDE3 Dark text. Ink 14151A A dark page with light text. No background None — \"Nothing behind the page\" No fill, padding or rounded corner. Text follows the viewer's own light or dark theme. For pages that draw their own background, such as a Raw HTML hero. All the greys the page uses for secondary text are chosen to clear AA contrast on each of the four papers. The spacing and roundness of the page. Choice Feel Tight Close spacing, square corners. Even default Moderate spacing, softly rounded. Airy Generous spacing, well rounded. The accent colours links, headings and buttons. Under Accent, from your library , the Style tab lists the palettes and scales you have saved in your Library, newest first, as swatches. Each swatch is graded agains"},{"t":"Templates","d":"Start a portfolio from one of eight templates, and what each template contains.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/templates.html","h":["Use a template","The eight templates","Result"],"x":" A template replaces your sections with a ready made set of example sections for a kind of portfolio. It does not change your header or your style. 1. Select Templates in the top bar, or type \"template\" in the command field and choose Start from a template . 2. The Start from a template dialog shows eight tiles. Select one; a tick marks it. 3. Select Use this template , or Cancel or Escape , or click outside the dialog to leave without changing anything. The builder confirms, for example, Designer template applied. Your previous sections are replaced, but you can bring them back with Undo. Template Description as shown Main sections Designer Work first — selected projects, an about section, skills and links. Selected Work heading, your library work up to 9 , About heading and text, skills, Elsewhere links Dribbble, Instagram . Developer Intro, tech stack, a projects grid and a code snippet. Intro text, Stack skills, Projects heading and your library work, a code snippet, links GitHub, Email . Photographer Visual first — a portfolio grid, stats and a booking call to action. Intro text, Portfolio work grid up to 12 , stats shoots, countries, clients , a Book a session call to action."},{"t":"The published page","d":"What visitors see at a published portfolio address and at a snapshot link.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/the-published-page.html","h":["At your address","At a snapshot link","Result"],"x":" A published portfolio lives at https://auricartisan.com/p/ followed by your address. It opens quickly: the portfolio appears first, and the site's header, footer, cursor and right click menu arrive a moment later. Visitors see: your header and sections, in your chosen typeface, paper, rhythm and accent; your saved palettes in the Work / Projects section as swatches they can select, and copy as CSS or JSON ; Copy link and, if you allowed it, PDF ; the view count, if you chose to show it. On a portfolio page, the site's right click menu offers actions for readers: Action What it does Copy link to this portfolio Copies the address. Save this portfolio as PDF Opens the print dialog. Email and the owner's first name Starts an email, when the portfolio shows an email address. Reading mode Alt + R Switches the site's reading mode. Make your own portfolio Opens the Portfolio Builder. A snapshot link opens https://auricartisan.com/portfolio/public/ with the portfolio carried in the address. The page shows Opening portfolio… , then the portfolio with Copy link and PDF , and a footer: \"Built with Auric Artisan — Colour intelligence, accessibility tools, and a portfolio builder.\" with Make yo"},{"t":"Portfolio reference","d":"Every control, option, command, message and limit in the Portfolio Builder, the published page and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/reference.html","h":["Top bar (https://auricartisan.com/portfolio/)","Mode tabs","Header panel","Section card controls","Section types (25)","Style options","Preview","Check findings","Publish dialog","Commands (command field)","Limits","Messages","Portfolio Index (https://auricartisan.com/portfolios/)"],"x":" Control What it does Your portfolio , address, Not published Shows your published address and state. Command field Ctrl K \"Add a section, change the look, publish…\" — opens the list of builder commands. Section count, Saved / Saved to your account Document size and save state. Undo / Redo Step back / forward. Disabled when there is nothing to undo or redo. Templates Opens Start from a template . Preview Opens the finished page in a new tab. Export Download HTML , Download PDF , Export JSON , Import JSON… , Copy snapshot link , \"Made with Auric Artisan\" credit switch. Publish Opens the publish dialog; disabled while Check has blocking findings. Tab Contents Content Header panel, section cards, Add a section . Style Typeface , Paper , Rhythm , Accent, from your library , Reset to defaults . Check Accessibility findings; a dot marks findings while you are elsewhere. Control Limit Default Use the built in header On / off On Name 80 characters Follows profile Headline / tagline 120 characters Empty Email + Show 120 characters Follows profile; Show off Location + Show 80 characters Follows profile; Show on Website + Show 200 characters Follows profile; Show on Avatar image address + Sho"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems with the Portfolio Builder, publishing and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["The builder shows \"Sign in to build your portfolio\"","Publish is greyed out","In the publish dialog, Publish stays disabled","\"That portfolio is larger than half a megabyte.\"","Images do not show on the page","My Raw HTML looks different, or parts are missing","An embed says \"Paste a YouTube, Vimeo, CodePen, Figma or Spotify link.\"","The Work / Projects section is empty","Undo with Ctrl+Z does nothing","\"Allow pop-ups to preview.\" or \"Allow pop-ups to print.\"","The exported PDF has no background colours","I cannot switch off the credit line","A snapshot link does not open","My portfolio is not in the Portfolio Index","\"The portfolio index could not be reached\"","My draft is different on another device"],"x":" Why: Building needs an account. What to do: Select Sign In , then return to https://auricartisan.com/portfolio/. Why: The Check pane has one or more blocking findings. The button's tooltip says how many. What to do: Open Check , select each Blocking finding and fix it. See Preview and check preview and check.md . Why: The address is not valid or not available yet. What to do: Use 2 to 31 lower case letters, numbers and hyphens, wait for the availability check, or pick one of the Or take suggestions. If it says Could not check that just now. , try again in a moment. Why: Uploaded images in Image and Gallery sections, or a large avatar are stored inside the portfolio and make it too big to publish. What to do: Host the images elsewhere and paste their https:// addresses instead of uploading them. Why: The address is not https:// , points to a page rather than an image, or the image host does not allow other sites to show it. What to do: Use a direct https:// link to the image file, or upload it keeping the size limit in mind . Add alt text so the Check pane does not flag it. Why: The builder removes scripts, iframes, forms, event attributes, javascript: addresses and fixed or sticky"},{"t":"Portfolio FAQ","d":"Short answers about the Portfolio Builder, publishing and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the Portfolio Builder free?","Do I need an account?","Can I change my address later?","Does publishing again change the address?","Can I keep my portfolio private?","Who can see my email address?","Is the view count tracking visitors?","Can I host the portfolio myself?","What does \"Verified\" mean in the Portfolio Index?","Can I import a portfolio from another tool?"],"x":" Yes. Building, publishing and exporting are free on every plan. Paid plans can remove the \"Made with Auric Artisan\" credit from exported files. To build and publish, yes. To view portfolios and the Portfolio Index, no. Unpublish and publish again at a new address. Taking a page down frees its address for others, so your old link stops working. No. Publish these changes updates the same address. Choose Only people I send the link to to share a snapshot link that is not stored on the site and never seen by search engines. Or publish with Let search engines list it and List it in the Portfolio Index switched off. Only if you switch on Show next to Email . It is off by default. No. It is \"Counted as a number and nothing else — no visitor records, no addresses.\" Yes. Download HTML gives you a single file to put on any web host. You can then add that address to the Portfolio Index through the Search Console. The owner proved, in the Search Console, that the site hosting the portfolio is theirs. Other external portfolios are reviewed by a person before they appear, and are marked Reviewed . Only files exported from this builder with Export JSON . "},{"t":"Portfolio: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Portfolio Builder and Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Section, snapshot link, handle, paper, rhythm and other terms. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys and pointer actions in the builder and the index. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md Sizes, what the checks cover, and what they do not. Related related.md Libraries, tools and pages that work with portfolios. Privacy privacy.md What is stored where, what becomes public, and how to remove it. Back to the Portfolio overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Portfolio shortcuts","d":"Keys and pointer actions in the Portfolio Builder, on published portfolios and in the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Builder","Published portfolio","Portfolio Index"],"x":" Keys or action Effect Ctrl + K or the command field Opens the list of builder commands; type, then Enter . Enter Finishes a one line field you are typing in the preview. Escape Finishes editing in the preview; closes the templates dialog, the section picker, full screen preview and the publish dialog. Enter in the section picker's search Adds the first matching section type. Double click the avatar Choose a picture. Drag a card's handle ⠿ Reorder sections. The Undo and Redo buttons show Ctrl + Z and Ctrl + Shift + Z in their tooltips; if the keys do not respond, use the buttons or the Undo and Redo commands. Keys or action Effect Right click Copy link to this portfolio , Save this portfolio as PDF , Email the owner, Reading mode , Make your own portfolio . Alt + R Reading mode. Keys Effect / Focus the search box. Escape Clear the search box, or close an open filter menu. See also Site features ../../site features/README.md for site wide shortcuts. "},{"t":"Portfolio glossary","d":"Terms used in the Portfolio Builder and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Accent The colour used for links, headings and buttons, picked from your saved palettes. Address handle The name after auricartisan.com/p/ in your published address. Alt text A written description of an image for people using screen readers. Blocking finding A Check result that must be fixed before you can publish. Credit line The small \"Made with Auric Artisan\" line on exported HTML and PDF files. Draft Your portfolio as it is in the builder, saved automatically; not what visitors see until you publish. External portfolio A portfolio on your own website, added to the Portfolio Index through the Search Console. Markdown A plain text way of writing formatted text, such as bold and Heading . Paper The page's background and text colour: Cream, White, Sand, Ink or No background. Placeholder Grey example text in an empty field; it is not published. Portfolio Index The directory of portfolios at https://auricartisan.com/portfolios/. Publish Put the current draft online at your address. Raw HTML A section that accepts your own HTML and CSS, cleaned for safety. Rhythm The page's spacing and corner roundness: Tight, Even or Airy. Reviewed An external portfolio a person has che"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"Size limits, what the Check pane can and cannot tell you, and other limits of the Portfolio Builder and the Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Size","The Check pane","Style","Drafts and sync","The Portfolio Index","Published pages"],"x":" A published portfolio can be up to half a megabyte. Uploaded images and pictures are stored inside it and use that space quickly; linking to images hosted elsewhere does not. Snapshot links carry the whole portfolio in the address. With several embedded images they become very long, and some apps and sites will not accept them. Large avatars are left out of snapshot links. It checks the rendered page for text contrast WCAG 2.2 AA , link text, image alt text, heading order and target size. It is a strong pre flight, not a full accessibility audit: it cannot judge whether your alt text is accurate, whether your content is clear, or how the page behaves with every assistive technology. Text in colour formats it cannot measure is reported as unknown rather than passed. Contrast is measured against the page's own paper. Text over images is not measured. Accents offered in Style come from palettes saved in your Library in this browser. The No background paper takes its text colour from the visitor's light or dark theme, so the page can look different for different visitors. Drafts sync to your account when you are signed in. If both devices change the draft, the newer copy wins; the bui"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Portfolio Builder stores, what becomes public when you publish or list a portfolio, and how to remove it.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/privacy.html","h":["While you build","When you publish","Snapshot links","The Portfolio Index","Remove it"],"x":" What Where Notes Your draft This browser, and your account when signed in Syncing to your account lets it follow you between devices. Your preview width This browser A convenience setting. Your draft is not public. Nothing a visitor sees changes until you publish. What becomes public at your address: everything in your visible sections hidden sections are left out ; the header details you chose to show — your name and headline always; email, location, website and avatar only if their Show switches are on; a copy of the Library items in your Work / Projects section, taken at the moment you publish. Your sign in email is not published unless you type it into the header and switch on Show . Settings under your control: Let search engines list it — off keeps the page out of search engines. List it in the Portfolio Index — off keeps it out of the directory. Allow a PDF download and Show the view count . The view count is \"Counted as a number and nothing else — no visitor records, no addresses.\" Uploaded avatars are re encoded, which removes hidden photo information such as camera and location details. A snapshot link contains the portfolio itself. Nothing is stored on the site, but any"},{"t":"Related","d":"Libraries, tools and pages that work with the Portfolio Builder and Portfolio Index.","p":"Website › Portfolio","u":"website/portfolio/others/related.html","h":["Make work to show","Publish and be found","Account"],"x":" Colour libraries ../../library/colour libraries/README.md — save palettes, gradients and scales to show in your portfolio. Basic Tools ../../tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md and the Design System Generator ../../tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md . Library Kit ../../kits/library kit/README.md — your saved items, which the Work / Projects section and the Style accents draw on. Search ../../search/README.md — the Search Console, where you verify a site and add an external portfolio. Collections ../../library/collections/README.md — the Portfolio Builder's place among all tools. Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md — signing in, your profile which the header follows and paid plans which remove the export credit line . "},{"t":"Search and the Search Console","d":"What the Auric Artisan search page and the Search Console are, who they are for, and how to run your first search.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The search page at https://auricartisan.com/search/ finds tools, Learn articles, documentation, blog posts, changelog entries, portfolios and every other page on Auric Artisan. The search runs in your browser: the page downloads a small index of the site once, and everything you type is matched on your device. Results appear as you type, sorted by relevance, and you can narrow them to one section, sort them, and use a few simple operators such as \"a phrase\" , word and type:learn . Because this is a colour site, the search also answers colour questions directly. Type a hex code such as d3af37 and an answer card shows the colour with its contrast against black and white. Type two hex codes and it judges them as a text and background pair against WCAG 2.1. Type the name of a common tool, such as contrast , and a card takes you straight to it. The globe button switches to a second index: Auric Artisan's own crawl of the web, an independent index much smaller than the big search engines. Site owners can put their own site into that index, and see how it is found, with the free Search Console at https://auricartisan.com/search/console/. Anyone looking for a tool, article or guide on Aur"},{"t":"Search documentation","d":"Task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the search page and the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/README.html","h":["Searching","The Search Console","Reference and help"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md A tour of the search page and a first search. search this site.md search this site.md Typing, suggestions, results, section tabs, sorting, paging and recent searches. query syntax.md query syntax.md Phrases, exclusions and field filters, for the site and for the web. instant answers.md instant answers.md The colour, contrast pair and tool cards. understand the ranking.md understand the ranking.md Why a result ranks where it does, and the score display. search the web.md search the web.md The globe: searching Auric Artisan's own web index. File What it covers search console.md search console.md Signing in, adding a site and proving you own it. console reports.md console reports.md Overview, Performance, Coverage, Pages, inspection and Links. request a crawl.md request a crawl.md Submitting pages and sitemaps, the crawl queue, and what the crawler obeys. manage your sites.md manage your sites.md The list of sites on your account, and removing one. File What it covers reference.md reference.md Every control, operator, status line and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short"},{"t":"Getting started with search","d":"A tour of the Auric Artisan search page and a first search, step by step.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","A tour of the page","Your first search","Try a colour","Next steps"],"x":" You need nothing but a browser. Searching the site needs no account and no sign in. The first time you open the page it prepares its index; the status line then reads Index ready with the number of items indexed. Before you type, the page shows a start screen: The search field at the top, with the placeholder Search Auric Artisan . A clear button appears once you type, and the globe button beside it switches to web search. A privacy line : Indexed on this device — nothing you type leaves the browser . Your recent searches sit on the same line, with Clear . Three example cards that run real queries when you select them: Paste a hex — a colour with its contrast against black and white. Give it two — a pair of colours judged for contrast. Narrow by section — the query type:learn contrast , with how many pages it matches. A ribbon of sections with how many pages each holds for example Learn, Documentation, Tools , and the total number of pages in the index . Each section links to its own page. More ways to ask — buttons for the operators type:learn , \"a phrase\" , word and tag:oklch . Select one to put it in the field. A line about the globe : it searches a second index, Auric Artisan'"},{"t":"Read the console reports","d":"What the Overview, Performance, Coverage, Pages and Links sections of the Auric Artisan Search Console show, and how to inspect a single address.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/console-reports.html","h":["What counts as an impression and a click","Overview","Performance","Coverage","Pages","Links"],"x":" These sections show data for the site chosen in the console header, once it is verified. Dated figures follow the period chosen at the top: 7d , 28d or 90d . Each figure is compared with the same length of time just before it. An impression is counted when a page from your site appears in a result on Auric Artisan's web search. A click is counted when a searcher opens that result. Position is where the result appeared in the list; lower is better. Figures start counting the first time your site appears in a result. The console opens on the Overview. It leads with what you can fix. Four cards : Indexed pages , with the share of known addresses; Impressions \"times you appeared\" ; Clicks \"times someone came\" ; Average position \"lower is better\" . Each has a small trend line and the change against the previous period. In your first period the card says first period instead. In the index and Not in the index : the two counts, a bar that splits them, and how many of the addresses outside the index are yours to fix. The line below gives the total number of addresses the crawler has met on the site. Why pages are not indexed : every reason the crawler recorded, most common first. Reasons "},{"t":"Instant answers","d":"The colour, contrast-pair and tool cards that lead the Auric Artisan search results, what each value means and how to use them.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/instant-answers.html","h":["The colour card","The contrast-pair card","The tool card","Accuracy"],"x":" For some queries the search page answers the question itself, in a card above the results. There are three kinds. Answer cards appear in site search only, not in web search. Type one hex code, for example d3af37 . Hex codes work with or without , in three digit or six digit form. The card is headed Colour and read from your query · sRGB . It shows: A large swatch of the colour, labelled with its OKLCH value. On black — the colour as text on black, with the contrast ratio and a grade. On white — the same on white. Hex , RGB and OKLCH values. Two buttons follow: Check it against a background opens the Contrast Checker with this colour as the text colour. Palettes with it opens the Palette Library. The library opens at its usual view; to find palettes that contain the colour, type the hex code into the library's search field. d3af37 gives: Value Result Hex D3AF37 RGB rgb 211 175 55 OKLCH oklch 76.6% 0.138 91.6 On black 9.96:1, AAA On white 2.11:1, FAILS The grade is for body text at that ratio, following WCAG 2.1: Grade Ratio AAA 7:1 or more AA 4.5:1 or more AA LARGE 3:1 or more; enough for large text only FAILS Below 3:1 Type two hex codes separated by a space, text colour first, th"},{"t":"Manage your sites","d":"How to see every site on your Search Console account, switch between them, read how the crawler treats a site, and remove one.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/manage-your-sites.html","h":["The list","How the crawler treats the open site","Remove a site","Keep pages out of the index"],"x":" Your sites in the Search Console's side rail lists every site on your account. It stays available even while a site is waiting to be verified, because it is where you add, prove and remove sites. The heading says how many sites the account has, for example 2 sites on this account. Removing one takes it off this console, not out of the index. Each row shows: The site's name and its status, such as verified or pending. The site the console is showing is marked open . For a verified site: how many pages are indexed, how many are excluded, and when it was last crawled, for example 120 indexed · 8 excluded · crawled 3 hours ago . For an unverified site: not proved yet — nothing is crawled until it is . Open , to make it the site the console shows. Remove , to take it off your console. You can also switch sites from the switcher in the console header, which appears when the account has more than one site. Below the list, a card named after the open site shows: The ownership line, for example Ownership proven by file on the site, 2026 09 20. Last crawl — when, and the HTTP status the site answered with. Pace — how long the crawler waits between requests to the site. robots.txt — Found , "},{"t":"Query syntax","d":"The operators the Auric Artisan search page understands — phrases, exclusions and field filters — for site search and for web search.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/query-syntax.html","h":["Site search operators","Web search operators","Tips"],"x":" Plain words are enough for most searches. The operators below narrow a search when you need to. The line under the search field shows how your query was read, with a chip for each filter, phrase, word and exclusion, so you can check that an operator was understood. Operator Example What it does Words oklch gradient Finds pages that contain the words; pages with more of them, and with the words close together, rank higher. \"…\" \"colour blindness\" Only pages where the words appear together, in that order. word palette tailwind Leaves out pages that contain the word. The word must be at least two characters. type: type:learn contrast Only one kind of page. See the list below. tag: tag:oklch Only pages with a tag containing the value. title: title:gamut Only pages whose title contains the value. desc: or description: desc:printing Only pages whose description or text contains the value. path: path:/library/learn/ Only pages whose address contains the value. category: category:legal Only pages whose category contains the value. Categories mostly match the type: values below. A hex code d3af37 Shows the colour answer card. See Instant answers instant answers.md . Two hex codes d3af37 0d0"},{"t":"Request a crawl","d":"How to submit pages and sitemaps in the Auric Artisan Search Console, read the crawl queue, and control what the crawler fetches with robots.txt.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/request-a-crawl.html","h":["Submit a page or a sitemap","The queue","Your sitemaps","What the crawler obeys","Crawled is not yet searchable","When the crawler is turned away"],"x":" The crawler finds pages by following links and by reading sitemaps. You can speed this up by submitting a page or a whole sitemap in the Submit section of the Search Console. Your site must be verified first; see Set up the Search Console search console.md . 1. Open Submit in the console's side rail. The section is headed Crawling . 2. In Add a page or a sitemap , paste an address, for example https://example.com/sitemap.xml . 3. As you type, a hint says what it will do: Looks like a sitemap — every URL inside it will join the queue. or Queued as one page. The hint is a guess; the console decides when it reads the address. 4. Select Submit or press Enter . The result: Message Meaning Read as a sitemap — 120 URLs queued. The address was a sitemap, and its addresses were queued. Read as a sitemap, but every URL in it was outside this property. The sitemap lists addresses on a different site. Submit it under the site it belongs to. Queued. It will be crawled at this host's own pace. The address was queued as one page. To queue a single address from a report, use Ask for a crawl in the inspection panel instead. See Read the console reports console reports.md . The first card shows how"},{"t":"Set up the Search Console","d":"How to sign in to the Auric Artisan Search Console, add your site and prove you own it with a file, a meta tag or a DNS record.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/search-console.html","h":["Before you start","Sign in","Add your site","Prove you own it","After verification","The console at a glance","Next steps"],"x":" The Search Console at https://auricartisan.com/search/console/ shows what Auric Artisan's crawler found on a site you own, which searches put it in front of people, and, for every page that is not indexed, the reason why. It is free, for any site you own. The console covers Auric Artisan's own web index only. What you do here changes what this index knows about your site. It has no effect on how you appear in Google, Bing or anywhere else. You need an Auric Artisan account. The account is needed only so that a site stays yours. You need to be able to change one of these for your site: a file on the web server, the home page's HTML, or the domain's DNS records. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/search/console/. 2. If you are signed out, the page explains the console under Your site, in the index . Select Sign in to start , sign in, and come back. 1. Open Your sites in the console's side rail. With no sites yet, the page says No properties yet. Add one below, then prove you own it. 2. Under Add another site , type your domain in Domain or URL prefix , for example example.com . 3. Select Add or press Enter . The page says Added. Prove you own it and the crawler will start. A domain co"},{"t":"Search the web","d":"How to use the globe on the Auric Artisan search page to search Auric Artisan's own index of the web, with suggestions, spelling correction and paging.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/search-the-web.html","h":["Switch the globe on","Search","Read the results","More results","Operators","When the index has nothing","What web mode does not do","Your privacy in web mode"],"x":" The globe button beside the search field switches from the site to the web. Web search uses Auric Artisan's own crawl of the web: an independent index, very much smaller than Google's or Bing's. Pages get into it when the crawler finds them by following links, and when site owners submit them through the Search Console search console.md . 1. Select the globe button beside the search field. Its tooltip reads Web search . The mode label beside the status line changes from LOCAL to GLOBAL . 2. If there is already a query in the field, it runs on the web straight away. 3. To go back to site search, select the globe again. You can also switch from the no results screen: Search the web instead turns the globe on and runs the same query. 1. Type your query. In web mode, results do not update as you type. Instead, a list suggests up to eight words from the web index's own vocabulary, most common first, marked web . 2. Press Enter , or choose a suggestion, to search. 3. The status line reads Searching the web for your query while it works. Each result shows: The site's icon, or the first letter of its name on a coloured tile when it has no icon. The page title, with your words highlighted."},{"t":"Search this site","d":"How site search works on the Auric Artisan search page — typing, suggestions, results, section tabs, sorting, paging, corrections and recent searches.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/search-this-site.html","h":["Type a query","Suggestions","Read the results","Narrow by section","Sort","Paging","When a word is misspelt","When nothing matches","Recent searches","Share or bookmark a search","Results you open rise over time","Related"],"x":" Site search is the default mode of the search page. The mode label beside the status line reads LOCAL . Type at least two characters. Results update as you type, after a short pause. Words shorter than two letters and very common words such as \"the\", \"and\" or \"with\" are ignored. A word does not have to be complete: grad finds pages about gradients. Small typing mistakes are tolerated. A word of three to five letters may be one letter out; a longer word may be two out. This applies only when the word as typed matches nothing. Related words also count, at reduced weight, when your query has four words or fewer. For example, palette also finds pages that say \"swatch\" or \"scheme\", and colour also finds \"color\". These related words appear dashed in the line under the field. While you type, a list opens under the field with up to eight suggestions: Pages whose title or address contains what you typed. Choose one to open that page. Tags , shown with a , for example oklch . Choose one to search for pages with that tag. Close the list with Escape , or by clicking elsewhere on the page. The status line above the list says how many results there are and how long the search took, for example "},{"t":"Understand the ranking","d":"How site search orders results, the \"Why it ranks here\" panel, the field weights and the option to show a score on every result.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/understand-the-ranking.html","h":["How results are scored","Why it ranks here","Show the score on every result","Why a result you expected is missing"],"x":" Site search orders results by relevance, and it shows its working. You can see why any result sits where it does, and switch on a score for every row. The page uses a ranking method called BM25F. Each page is split into six fields, and a match in a heavier field counts for more: Field Weight Title ×6 Tags ×4 Description ×3 Category ×2 URL ×1.5 Content ×1 On top of that: Rare words count for more than common ones. Pages that contain more of your words, and have them close together, rank higher. Partial words such as grad for \"gradient\" and corrected typos count, but less than exact words. Related words, shown dashed under the field, count at half weight. Pages you have opened from search before are nudged up, in this browser only. The same table is printed on the page: open Tools at the end of the tab row and look under Ranking . It also shows the two tuning values, k1 / b , as 1.2 / 0.4 . Hover a result, or highlight it with the arrow keys, and a panel opens above the list. It shows: The kind of page and its title, address and description. Why it ranks here — the BM25F score , then each field that matched, with its weight and how many times your words appear in it. Matched on — th"},{"t":"Search reference","d":"Every control, operator, status line, message and limit on the Auric Artisan search page and in the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/reference.html","h":["Search page controls","Section tabs","Field weights","Operators","Start screen","Answer cards","Status lines","Page address parameters","Limits","Search Console: layout","Search Console: verification","Search Console: Performance","Search Console: Coverage totals","Coverage reasons","Search Console: Pages","Search Console: inspection","Search Console: Submit","Search Console: messages"],"x":" Control What it does Values or range Default Search field Takes your query. Results start at two characters. Any text Empty Clear button Empties the field and returns to the start screen. Appears once you type. — Hidden Globe button Web search Switches between site search and web search. On, off Off Mode label Shows which index you are searching. LOCAL , GLOBAL LOCAL Suggestions list Pages and tags that match what you typed site search , or words from the web index web search . Up to 8 — Section tabs Filter site search results by kind of page, with a count on each. All , Tools , Learn , Docs , Blog , Portfolios , Pages All Tools menu Opens sorting and ranking options. — Closed Sort by Orders site search results. Shown with two or more results. Relevance , Newest , A–Z Relevance Ranking Shows the field weights and tuning values. — — Show the score on every result Adds a score bar, number and matched fields to each result. Remembered in this browser. On, off Off Query chips Show how the query was read: filters, colours, phrases, words, exclusions and related words dashed . — — did you mean Runs the corrected query. — — More results Loads the next 20 web results, with how many are le"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems with the Auric Artisan search page, web search and the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Search page","Web search","Search Console"],"x":" Why: Search starts at two characters, and the page may still be loading its index. While it loads, the page shows Building search index… . What to do: Type at least two characters and wait for Index ready . If the status line says Search index is empty. Try refreshing the page. , reload the page. Why: The page may use different words, an operator may be ruling it out, or the page may be newer than the index your browser has. What to do: Try a shorter or different word. The Worth trying list on the no results screen suggests changes based on your query. Remove filters, exclusions and quotes one at a time. Check the section tab: select All . Reload the page to fetch the latest index. Why: That section has no results for the current query. What to do: Select All , or change the query. Why: Newest uses the date in a page's address. Pages without a date, which are most pages, go to the end in no particular date order. What to do: Use Newest for dated pages such as blog posts and changelog entries, together with the Blog or Docs tab. Why: A word of three or six letters made only from a to f, such as bad , add or facade , is read as a hex code. What to do: Put the word in quotes: \"facade"},{"t":"Search FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Auric Artisan search page, web search and the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/docs/faq.html","h":["Does the site search send what I type anywhere?","Does web search send my query?","Is web search the same as Google?","Do I need an account to search?","Can I link to a search?","Why does a hex code show a card instead of results?","Which colour comes first in a pair?","Why does #777777 on white fail AA?","Why did a page about swatches appear when I searched for palettes?","Is the Search Console free?","Does the Search Console affect my Google ranking?","How long until a submitted page is searchable?","How do I stop the crawler?","If I remove my site from the console, does it leave the index?","How many sites can I add?","Can I list my portfolio from the console?"],"x":" No. Site search runs in your browser against an index the page downloads once. The start screen says so: Indexed on this device — nothing you type leaves the browser . Web search is different; see below. Yes. With the globe on, your query goes to Auric Artisan's search service. When you open a web result, the query, the result and its position are reported too. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . No. It is Auric Artisan's own independent crawl of the web, much smaller than Google's or Bing's. No. Only the Search Console needs an account. Yes. Copy the page address after searching. It includes ?q= and, for a section tab, &scope= . A colour is usually the answer to a colour query. The card shows the colour and its contrast. The results for the hex code, if any, follow below it. The text colour first, then the background: d3af37 0d0d0d is gold text on near black. The ratio is the same either way; the sample text changes. Swap them reverses the pair. Its ratio is 4.48:1, just under the 4.5:1 that AA needs for body text. The card uses the exact ratio, not a rounded one. Related words count at reduced weight. The line under the field shows them dashed. See Understand the ranking understa"},{"t":"Search: other material","d":"Supporting material for the Auric Artisan search page and the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Index, impression, property, canonical and other terms. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys on the search page and in the Search Console. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What each index covers, how exact the numbers are, and the limits. Related related.md Spotlight, tools and pages that work with search. Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser, what is sent, and how to clear it. Back to the Search overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Search shortcuts","d":"Keyboard shortcuts on the Auric Artisan search page and in the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Getting to search","In the search field","Outside the search field","Search Console"],"x":" Keys or action What it does Ctrl + K Opens Spotlight from any page. Choose View all results for your query to open the search page. Right click selected text, Search this site Searches the site for the selected text in a new tab. Keys What it does ↓ / ↑ Moves through the suggestions, or through the results when no suggestions are open. Wraps round at the ends. Home / End Jumps to the first or last suggestion or result, once one is highlighted. Otherwise they move the text cursor. Enter Opens the highlighted suggestion or result. With nothing highlighted, runs the search and saves it as recent. Escape Closes the suggestions. Pressed again, clears the query. Keys What it does ↓ / ↑ Selects the next or previous result and shows why it ranks there. Enter Opens the selected result. End Goes to the bottom of the page once every result is shown. These keys do nothing while you are typing in another field, or when Ctrl , Alt or a command key is held. Keys What it does ↓ / → and ↑ / ← Move between sections in the side rail when it has focus. Home / End The first or last section in the side rail. Enter Adds the site in Domain or URL prefix , or submits the address in Add a page or a sitemap"},{"t":"Search glossary","d":"Terms used on the Auric Artisan search page and in the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning AuricBot The name Auric Artisan's crawler uses when it fetches pages. BM25F The ranking method site search uses: it scores word matches, weighting each field of a page differently. Canonical address The address a page names as its preferred version, with a rel=canonical link. Click In the Search Console, a searcher opening your page from a web search result. Click through CTR Clicks divided by impressions. Coverage Which of a site's addresses are in the index, and why the others are not. Crawl Fetching a page so it can be indexed. Crawled index Auric Artisan's own index of the web, searched with the globe. Crawl delay A robots.txt line asking crawlers to wait between requests. Exclusion A word in a query, which leaves out pages containing the word. Field filter An operator such as type: or tag: that narrows results by one field. Impression In the Search Console, one appearance of your page in a web search result. Index The collection of pages a search looks through. Index build The step that makes crawled pages searchable. Inspection The Search Console panel that explains one address. LOCAL, GLOBAL The mode label: site search or web search. noindex A robots meta tag o"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What each Auric Artisan search index covers, how exact the answers and console figures are, and the limits that apply.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Site search","Answer cards","Web search","Search Console","Sponsored units"],"x":" What is covered. The public pages of Auric Artisan: tools, Learn articles, documentation, blog, changelog, company, legal and similar pages, plus portfolios listed in the Portfolio Index. The start screen shows the current total as pages in the index . What is not covered. The contents of the libraries themselves. Individual colours, palettes, gradients and scales are not pages in the index; search inside each library for those. Freshness. Your browser downloads the index when you open the page. A page published after that appears when you reload. Result cap. Up to 100 results are listed for a query. Words. Words under two letters and very common words are ignored. Typo tolerance applies only to words of three letters or more that match nothing as typed. Newest. Sorting by date uses a date in the page's address; most pages have none. Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2.1 relative luminance formula on sRGB colours. They match the standard reference values: 21:1 for white on black, and 4.54:1 for 767676 on white. Grades are decided on the exact ratio. The ratio shown is rounded to two decimals, so a pair shown as 4.50:1 can still be just under the threshold. OKLCH values are converted fr"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Auric Artisan search page and Search Console keep in your browser, what they send, and how to clear it.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/privacy.html","h":["Site search","Web search","The Search Console","Sponsored units","More"],"x":" Site search runs on your device. The page downloads the site's index and the list of portfolios once, and matches your queries in the browser. What you type in site search is not sent anywhere. These are saved in this browser only: What Why How to clear Your six most recent searches To offer them on the start screen and in Spotlight. Select Clear next to Recent . Which results you have opened To nudge those pages up in your future results. Clear this site's data in your browser. The Show the score on every result setting To remember your choice. Untick the setting, or clear site data. A private window starts with none of these and forgets them when you close it. With the globe on, the page sends to Auric Artisan's search service: Your query, and the words you type, for suggestions. When you open a web result: the query, which result you chose and its position in the list. Clicks are used to improve ranking and to give site owners their click counts in the Search Console. Site icons in the results are fetched through Auric Artisan, so other services are not told which sites appear in your results. Web results open other websites in a new tab; those sites have their own privacy term"},{"t":"Related","d":"Site features, tools and pages that work with the Auric Artisan search page and the Search Console.","p":"Website › Search","u":"website/search/others/related.html","h":["Other ways to find things","Where the answer cards lead","Portfolios","Account"],"x":" Site features ../../site features/README.md — Spotlight Ctrl + K , the site menu and the right click menu, which all lead into search. Library ../../library/README.md — the Learn articles, documentation, blog and changelog that site search covers. Collections ../../library/collections/README.md — every tool, browsable and filterable. Contrast Checker ../../tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md — Check it against a background and Open the checker . Palette Library ../../library/colour libraries/palette library/README.md — Palettes with it . URL Analyzer ../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — a full contrast and accessibility check of a web page. Portfolio Builder and Portfolio Index ../../portfolio/README.md — portfolios appear in site search under Portfolios , and the Search Console's Portfolios section lists yours. Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md — the account the Search Console needs. "},{"t":"Account and billing","d":"Everything about your Auric Artisan account — signing up and in, the dashboard, security, plans, tokens, payments, invoices, refunds, API keys and deleting your account.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" An Auric Artisan account is optional. Every tool on the website is free to use without one. The account exists for the things that have to belong to a person rather than to one browser: a paid plan pass, a token balance for server backed tool work, API keys, a published portfolio, and the security controls that protect them. The account lives at https://auricartisan.com/auth/. Signing in opens the account dashboard, which has four sections: Overview , Profile , Plan & Usage , and Security & Privacy . From there you manage your profile and username, see your plan and usage, buy and review plan passes, view invoices, create API keys, see every device that is signed in, turn on two step verification, export your data and, if you choose, delete the account. Billing is deliberately simple. A paid plan is a one time pass for one month or twelve months, paid through Razorpay. Nothing renews automatically, no card is stored, and there is no subscription to cancel; when a pass ends the account returns to the free Apprentice plan. Plan purchases have a 7 day money back window. Anyone who wants to run server backed tool work, such as whole site accessibility crawls in the Analyzer. People wh"},{"t":"Account and billing docs","d":"The task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for the Auric Artisan account, dashboard and billing.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/README.html","h":["Getting in","The dashboard","Plans, tokens and payments","Developers","Your data","Reference and help"],"x":" This folder holds the working guides for the Auric Artisan account: one page per task, a guide to each dashboard section, the plan and payment pages, and the reference, troubleshooting and FAQ pages. Start with Getting started with the dashboard getting started.md if you are new. Page What it covers Getting started with the dashboard getting started.md Opening the dashboard, a tour of the screen, and the first five tasks Sign up sign up.md Creating an account with email and password, or with Google or GitHub Sign in and sign out sign in.md Signing in with email or username, Remember me, the human check, sessions, signing out Verify your email verify email.md The verification link, the 24 hour window, resending, and what stays locked until you verify Passwords passwords.md Forgotten passwords, the reset page, changing your password, accounts without a password Two step verification two step verification.md Turning on authenticator codes, backup codes, signing in with them, turning them off Device sign in device sign in.md Approving the Auric command line tool with a device code Page What it covers Overview section dashboard overview.md The statement, your work, next steps, Start so"},{"t":"Getting started with the dashboard","d":"Open the Auric Artisan account dashboard, learn its layout, and complete the first five tasks for a new account.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Open the dashboard","The screen, top to bottom","Your first five tasks","Related"],"x":" The account dashboard is one page with four sections. It shows what the account holds — your work, the public page that shows it, what you are paying for, and who is signed in — and it is where you change all of it. 1. Sign in at https://auricartisan.com/auth/ see Sign in and sign out sign in.md . 2. Open https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/, or select your account chip in the header and choose Dashboard . If you are not signed in, the dashboard sends you to the sign in page and brings you back afterwards. Tip: After you sign in, the site takes you to the dashboard automatically if your account has no username yet, so you can claim one. Otherwise it returns you to the page you came from, or to the home page. Part What it shows Auric Artisan · Account The page kicker @yourhandle Your username. It reads @unclaimed until you choose one, with a Claim your handle link beneath. Profile photo Your photo, or your initial, or an empty outline. Double click it to open the photo viewer. Plan Your plan name, for example Apprentice . A status is added when it is not simply active, for example \"Artisan · Past due\". Email address The address you sign in with Join date \"Joined today\", or \"Mem"},{"t":"API credits and spend controls","d":"How Auric Artisan API credits are counted, what is included, buying prepaid credits, paid overage, the monthly spend cap, the hard ceiling, and the usage panels in the dashboard.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/api-credits-and-spend.html","h":["How credits are counted","What is included","When the allowance runs out","Credits & spend panel","Usage and cost","Where the credits went","Live usage","Related"],"x":" The REST API is metered in API credits. This page explains the rules and the dashboard panels that show and control them: Usage & cost , Credits & spend , Where the credits went and Live usage , all under Plan & Usage on plans with API access. The API itself is documented in Public API ../../../services/public api/README.md . API credits are not tokens. Tokens pay for server work you start in a website tool; API credits pay for calls your own code makes. Neither pays for the other. One credit is one standard request. Heavier endpoints cost more, \"so a caller doing simple color maths is not subsidising one rendering images\", as the pricing page puts it. Credits are counted per account, not per key. Every key you create draws on the same allowance and the same prepaid balance. Request type pricing page Credits Examples Standard 1 Colour conversion, contrast check, vision simulation Generators 2–4 Palette, harmony, gradient, shade scale, design tokens Colour dossier 5 All 63 colour spaces plus a locus search, in one call Rendered PNG 10–12 Palette, gradient and Ishihara images; image analysis Async job 25 Batch work queued and run on Auric Artisan's clock The API documentation lists "},{"t":"API keys","d":"Create, view, copy and revoke Auric Artisan API keys in the dashboard, and understand key limits, plans and what happens after a downgrade.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/api-keys.html","h":["Before you start","Create a key","The key list","Revoke a key","After a downgrade","Keys and the live usage panel","Messages","Related"],"x":" An API key lets your own code call the Auric Artisan REST API as your account. Keys are created and revoked in the dashboard, under Plan & Usage › Your API Keys . How to use a key in a request, and every endpoint, is documented in Public API ../../../services/public api/README.md and on https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/. Plan. API access is included from the Specialist plan upward. On Apprentice and Artisan the create button is withdrawn, because a key there would authenticate but be refused on every metered call. Specialist is marked Coming soon on the pricing page today. Verified email. API keys are locked until your email address is verified. Limit. An account can hold up to 10 active keys. One meter per account. Every key on the account draws on the same monthly credit allowance and the same prepaid balance. Credits are counted per account, not per key. 1. Open the dashboard and select Plan & Usage . 2. In Your API Keys , select Create your first key or Create key if you already have some . 3. Type a name that says where the key is used, for example \"CI pipeline\". Names can be up to 64 characters. 4. Select Create . Select Cancel to stop. 5. A panel appears: "},{"t":"Buy a plan","d":"Buy an Auric Artisan plan pass from the pricing page through Razorpay checkout, pay in dollars or rupees, and read the confirmation page.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/buy-a-plan.html","h":["Before you start","Buy a plan pass","The amount you pay","Paying from outside India","The confirmation page","If something goes wrong during checkout","Stay safe","Buying API credits","Related"],"x":" A paid plan is a one time purchase of a pass for one month or twelve months, paid through Razorpay's checkout on https://auricartisan.com. This page walks through the purchase and every screen you can see afterwards. Today the plan on sale is Artisan ; Specialist and Industrial Pro are marked Coming soon . Sign in. An account is required before any payment, so the pass belongs to you rather than to one browser. Verify your email. Billing is locked until your email address is verified. See Verify your email verify email.md . Know what you are buying. Read Plans and pricing plans and pricing.md . Every tool is already free; a plan adds conveniences. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/. 2. Choose Monthly or Annual with the switch above the plan cards. Annual costs ten times the monthly price for twelve months. 3. Choose USD $ or INR ₹ . You are charged in the currency shown. 4. On the Artisan card, select Get Artisan . 5. If you are not signed in, a note appears under the button instead of a checkout: \"Sign in first — a plan is attached to your account, not to this browser.\" Select Sign in or create a free account . You come straight back to the pricing page afterwards,"},{"t":"Overview section","d":"Every part of the Overview section of the Auric Artisan dashboard — the statement, your saved work, next steps, quick links and the side column.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/dashboard-overview.html","h":["The statement","Your work","Next","Start something","The side column","Related"],"x":" The Overview is the first section of the dashboard https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/ overview . It answers \"is my account in order?\" first, then shows your work, then suggests what to do next. Everything it shows is read from your account and from this browser; a part with nothing true to say is left out rather than filled with zeros. On a wide screen the Overview has a main column and a side column. On a screen narrower than about 1,024 pixels, the side column moves to the top because it holds the things you most need to act on. The statement opens the main column. Statement — the heading is the current month and year. A one line summary appears when there is something to say, for example \"One key is doing the work.\" or \"3 keys are in use.\" Below it is a ledger. A row appears only when it has a real value: Row Shows Plan Your plan name Credits used API credits used this billing period, with the period as a note plans with API access, once usage has loaded Credits left Included API credits left, with \"N days left in the period\" Your work The number of items you have saved, with a note such as \"12 palettes · 3 collections · 40 KB\"; or Nothing yet Two factor authentication On"},{"t":"Delete your account","d":"Unlock the Auric Artisan danger zone, erase this browser's workspace, or permanently delete your account, and what deletion does and does not remove.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/delete-your-account.html","h":["Before you delete","Unlock the danger zone","Erase this browser's workspace","Delete this account","What deletion does","What is kept, and why","What deletion does not touch","Ask for deletion instead","Messages","Related"],"x":" The Danger zone , at the bottom of Security & Privacy , holds the two actions that cannot be undone: Erase this browser's workspace — clears the library, collections, drafts and preferences stored in this browser. Anything saved to the account stays. Delete this account — permanently deletes your profile, portfolio, keys, sessions and billing history. There is no undo and no recovery. The zone is locked until you prove it is you, and each action asks for its own confirmation word on top of that. Export anything you want to keep. See Export your data export your data.md . Download invoices you need from Plan & Usage . Revoke or note your API keys. They stop working when the account is deleted. Consider a refund first if you bought a plan in the last 7 days. See Refunds refunds.md . Accounts created with Google or GitHub need a password to unlock the danger zone. If you never set one, the zone says \"Set an account password before using these actions.\" Set one with Forgot password? first — see Passwords passwords.md add a password to a google or github account . 1. Open the dashboard and select Security & Privacy . Scroll to Danger zone . Its state reads Locked . 2. The list Behind t"},{"t":"Device sign-in","d":"Approve the Auric command-line tool from your browser with a device code, so it can act as your account.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/device-sign-in.html","h":["Before you start","Approve a device","Messages","Only approve codes you started","Related"],"x":" The Auric command line tool auric , listed as @auric artisan/cli on the API documentation page signs in without asking for your password in the terminal. Instead it shows a short code, and you approve that code in a browser where you are already signed in. This is called a device sign in. The approval page is https://auricartisan.com/auth/device/. Its heading is Authorize Auric CLI . You need an Auric Artisan account, signed in in your browser. Your email address must be verified. Device approval is one of the features locked until you verify see Verify your email verify email.md . Install the command line tool as described on the API documentation page: Public API ../../../services/public api/README.md . 1. In your terminal, run: bash auric login 2. The tool prints a short code and an approval address. 3. Open the address in your browser. If you are not signed in, the page sends you to sign in and brings you back. 4. The page shows Signed in as and your email or name, so you can check it is the right account. 5. If the address included the code, it is already in Device code . Otherwise type it; it has the form ABCD EFGH letters and numbers; the dash is added for you . 6. Select A"},{"t":"Emails and messages","d":"The emails your Auric Artisan account sends, where replies to your messages arrive, and why there is no in-account inbox.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/emails-and-messages.html","h":["Emails the account sends","Where replies come from","Beware of look-alikes","Change the email address on the account","Related"],"x":" Your Auric Artisan account has no message inbox of its own. Everything the site needs to tell you arrives by email, at the address on your account, and replies to anything you send through the contact form arrive by email too. Email When it arrives What to do with it Verification link After you sign up with email and password, or when you ask for a fresh link Open it within 24 hours and select Confirm email ownership . See Verify your email verify email.md . Welcome Once your account is usable — straight away for Google or GitHub sign ups, after verification for email sign ups Nothing; it lists places to start: the tools, the Learn library and your dashboard. Replying reaches a person. Password reset link When you use Forgot password? Open it within one hour. See Passwords passwords.md . Receipt After a purchase Keep it; it carries your order reference, which starts with order . Contact form confirmation When you send a message through the contact page Nothing; it confirms the message arrived. Reply to your message When Auric Artisan answers Reply in the same thread. Email is delivered through Resend, named on the Security page as a third party provider. The contact page routes ea"},{"t":"Export your data","d":"Download your Auric Artisan account details, preferences, portfolio draft and saved library as one JSON file from the dashboard.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/export-your-data.html","h":["Download the export","What the file contains","What it does not contain","A complete copy of what Auric Artisan holds","Keep the file safe","Related"],"x":" The dashboard can put your account details and the work saved in this browser into one JSON file a plain text data format that most tools can read . Nothing secret is included. 1. Open the dashboard and select Security & Privacy . 2. Find the row Export everything . 3. Select Export . Result: \"Export downloaded.\" and a file named like auric artisan export 2026 09 25.json the date of the export is saved by your browser. Section Contents exported at When you made the export profile Your account details as the site holds them: display name, username, email address, bio, website, location, photo and related account fields preferences Your dashboard preferences portfolio Your Portfolio Builder draft as saved in this browser portfolio stats The view, download and share counters kept in this browser library Everything in My Library in this browser — palettes, gradients, collections and other saved items Secrets. Passwords, two step verification material and API keys are never included. Work saved in other browsers. The library and portfolio sections come from the browser you are using. Export from each browser you use. Receipts. The on screen description mentions receipts, but your invoi"},{"t":"Invoices and receipts","d":"Find your Auric Artisan payment history, open an invoice, print it or save it as PDF, and understand what the receipt is for tax purposes.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/invoices-and-receipts.html","h":["Find your payment history","Open an invoice","Print or save as PDF","Share or keep the link","Receipts and GST","Your receipt email and order reference","Messages on the invoice page","Related"],"x":" Every payment, refund and chargeback on your account is listed in the dashboard, and each one has its own printable invoice page. 1. Open the dashboard and select Plan & Usage or choose Billing & plan in the header account menu . 2. Scroll to Invoices & Payment History . The table lists Date , Description Payment, Refund or Chargeback, with the plan and term , Amount , Status Paid, Failed or Refunded and a View link. It shows 25 rows at a time; use < Newer and Older to page through more. With no purchases yet it reads \"No payments yet. Receipts appear here after your first purchase.\" 1. Select View on a row. 2. The invoice page opens at https://auricartisan.com/auth/billing/invoice/ with that invoice's reference in the address. The invoice shows: Part Contents Header Auric Artisan — \"Color science platform & creative tools\", the website and the support email address Invoice , Date , Status The invoice reference, the date and Paid, Failed or Refunded From Auric Artisan, \"Internet · Worldwide\", support@auricartisan.com Billed to Your name and email address Line items What was bought the plan and its term and the amount, then the Total Payment note \"Payment processed via\" the provide"},{"t":"Passwords","d":"Reset a forgotten Auric Artisan password, change your password from the dashboard, and add a password to a Google or GitHub account.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/passwords.html","h":["Password rules","Reset a forgotten password","Change your password","Add a password to a Google or GitHub account","Related"],"x":" This page covers three tasks: resetting a password you have forgotten, changing a password you know, and adding a password to an account that was created with Google or GitHub. Every Auric Artisan password must have: 12 to 128 characters, both upper case and lower case letters, at least one number, at least one symbol, no single character repeated four or more times in a row, not be a common password such as \"password123\". Passwords are stored only as a one way hash the Security page names PBKDF2 SHA256 at 600,000 iterations , so nobody at Auric Artisan can read or recover your password. A reset replaces it rather than revealing it. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/auth/ and select Forgot password? under the password field. 2. The Recover access. panel opens. If you had typed an email address in the sign in form, it is copied into Email . 3. Type the email address on the account not your username and select Send Reset Link . 4. The page always answers \"If that address belongs to an account, a one hour reset link is on its way.\" It says the same whether or not the address has an account, so nobody can use the form to find out who is registered. 5. Open the email and select the rese"},{"t":"Plan & Usage section","d":"Your Auric Artisan plan, usage meters, the Change plan cards, invoices and payment history, and the API console for plans with API access.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/plan-and-usage.html","h":["Current Plan","Change plan","Invoices & Payment History","The API console (Specialist and above)","Related"],"x":" The Plan & Usage section https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/ plan shows what you pay for and what you use: your plan, your usage meters, your invoices, and — on plans that include the REST API — your API keys, credits and spend controls. The header menu items Billing & plan and API keys both open this section, as do the older addresses billing and api keys . What you see depends on your plan: On Apprentice and Artisan , the section shows your plan and receipts, and one card explaining that the API is not part of your plan. On Specialist and Industrial Pro , it also shows the full API console. If your account holds API keys from an earlier plan, the API console stays visible whatever you pay now, so you can still see and revoke those keys. The Current Plan panel names your plan and its state in one line: Line When \"You're on the free Apprentice plan.\" Free plan \"Artisan — active until 12 Oct 2026. Does not renew automatically.\" plan and date vary A paid pass, which ends on that date \"Your Artisan subscription has ended.\" A plan that has ended \"Payment for your Artisan plan failed — please update your payment method.\" A failed payment \"Artisan — no active subscription on this a"},{"t":"Plan terms, renewal and cancelling","d":"Why Auric Artisan plan passes never renew, what happens when a pass ends, how to stop early, and what happens to tokens and credits.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/plan-terms-and-cancelling.html","h":["Nothing renews","When a pass ends","Buying another term","Stopping early","Tokens and API credits when a plan ends","If recurring billing is ever introduced","Related"],"x":" Every paid plan sold on Auric Artisan is a one time purchase of a fixed period — one month or twelve. This page explains what that means in practice. No recurring subscription is created when you buy a plan. No payment mandate, standing instruction or saved card is kept for a future charge. No second charge is ever scheduled. So there is no renewal to be surprised by, and nothing to cancel. The dashboard's plan line says so: for example \"Artisan — active until 12 Oct 2026. Does not renew automatically.\" Note: Some policy pages use the word \"subscription\". The Terms of Service explain that, on Auric Artisan, it means the plan record and its billing period — not a recurring charge. The pass ends on its own at the end of the term you bought. You do not need to do anything. The account returns to the free Apprentice plan. Every tool keeps working. Your saved work is not touched. It lives in your browser, so it stays exactly where it is whatever your plan does. The paid conveniences stop: ad free browsing, watermark free exports, the monthly token allowance and any higher limits. The plan's included API credit allowance ends with it. Purchased API credits stay on the account see below "},{"t":"Plans and pricing","d":"Every Auric Artisan plan with its prices in US dollars and rupees, monthly and annual terms, token and API allowances, the full comparison table, add-ons, and what is not built yet.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/plans-and-pricing.html","h":["The model in one paragraph","The four plans","Prices","What each plan includes","Compare all features","Tokens and API credits","Optional add-ons","Token estimator","Trials, discounts and custom deals","Related"],"x":" This page restates the pricing page at https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/ as of the date above. The pricing page is authoritative: if a figure here and there ever differ, the pricing page and the checkout are what you are charged by. Every tool is free on every plan. Paid plans add conveniences and scale — ad free browsing, watermark free exports, a monthly token allowance for server backed work, higher limits and, from Specialist, the REST API. A paid plan is a one time pass for one month or twelve months: it does not auto renew, and there is nothing to cancel. Plan purchases carry a 7 day money back window, and an account is required before any payment. Plan Who it is for pricing page Availability Apprentice \"Every tool, free forever. No account needed to start creating.\" Free, always Artisan \"For creators who want ad free browsing, watermark free exports, and higher limits.\" Available now Specialist \"For power users — automate with the API and ship branded WCAG reports.\" Coming soon — not on sale Industrial Pro \"For labs, agencies, and organizations that need scale, security, and white label.\" Coming soon — not on sale The buttons on the plan cards read Get Started Free "},{"t":"Profile section","d":"Edit your Auric Artisan display name, username, bio, website, location and profile photo, choose an avatar from the gallery, and reach your public portfolio.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/profile.html","h":["The fields","Edit your profile","Change your username","Change your photo","The Auric avatar gallery","Public portfolio card","Related"],"x":" The Profile section https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/ identity holds who you are on the site: the name that signs anything you publish, and the username your public page lives at. The panel is headed Who you are . Field What it is Rules Profile photo Your photo, shown in the header, the dashboard and your portfolio PNG, JPG or GIF, up to 2 MB. It is cropped to a square. Display name The name shown on your profile and anything you publish Up to 64 characters Username Your handle, typed after the @ . Your public page lives at this address, and you can sign in with it. 3–30 characters: letters, numbers and underscores. It can be changed once every 30 days. Bio \"A line or two about what you make.\" Up to 500 characters Email address The address you sign in with Read only. Hover over it: \"Email changes are not supported yet — contact support.\" Website A link to your own site Up to 200 characters, a full http:// or https:// address Location City and country, or anything you like Up to 120 characters 1. Open the dashboard and select Profile . 2. Change any of the fields. 3. Watch the How you appear card on the right: it previews the header of your public page as you type — photo, n"},{"t":"Refunds","d":"The 7-day money-back window on Auric Artisan purchases, how to ask for a refund, how long it takes, and what a refund removes.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/refunds.html","h":["What you can get back","Ask for a refund","How long it takes","What a refund removes","Charges you do not recognise","Related"],"x":" This page summarises the Refund Policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/refund/. The policy page is authoritative; this page explains how to use it. Purchase Refund terms Plan pass one month or twelve Within 7 days of purchase, refunded for any reason. After 7 days, considered case by case. Prepaid API credits Within 7 days of that purchase, to the extent they are unused. Credits already spent on API requests are not refundable; a partly used balance may be refunded pro rata at Auric Artisan's discretion. Token packs Within 7 days if unused; partly used packs may be refunded pro rata at Auric Artisan's discretion. Token packs are not on sale today. Included allowances Not refundable separately. The tokens and API credits that come with a plan are part of the plan price, and refunding the plan refunds them with it. Advertising bookings In full at any time before the campaign starts; after that, case by case. After the 7 day window, the policy says refunds are considered against the purchase terms shown at checkout, payment provider records, account status, usage and applicable law. 1. Open the dashboard and select Plan & Usage . 2. In Current Plan , select Request a refund . This "},{"t":"Security & Privacy section","d":"Check your password and two-step status, manage signed-in devices, review sign-ins, export your data and reach the danger zone in the Auric Artisan dashboard.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/security-and-privacy.html","h":["The readout strip","Signed-in devices","Export everything","Danger zone","Related"],"x":" The Security & Privacy section https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/ security answers two questions: who can get into the account, and what leaves it. Its heading counts what is signed in right now, for example \"2 devices are holding this account open.\" The line beneath reads: \"End anything you do not recognise — a device you revoke here is signed out immediately.\" The older addresses settings and sessions open this section too. Four cells state the account's condition. The cell that needs attention is highlighted. Cell What it says Control Password When the password was last set: \"Set when you signed up\", \"Unchanged since you signed up\", \"Changed today\", \"Changed yesterday\" or \"Changed N days ago\" Change — see Passwords passwords.md change your password Two factor \"Off — nothing but your password\" highlighted , or \"On — N backup codes left\" Enable 2FA or Disable 2FA — see Two step verification two step verification.md Usage data \"On — anonymous usage only\" or \"Off — nothing is collected\" A switch that records your choice on your account Cookies Your cookie choice: \"Not answered yet\", \"Necessary only\", or \"Necessary +\" the optional categories you accepted Change opens the Cooki"},{"t":"Sign in and sign out","d":"Sign in to Auric Artisan with your email or username, with Google or GitHub, or with a second factor, and understand how long a sign-in lasts.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/sign-in.html","h":["Sign in with your email or username","Sign in with Google or GitHub","Sign in with a second factor","How long a sign-in lasts","If you are already signed in","The account menu","Sign out","Related"],"x":" The sign in page is https://auricartisan.com/auth/. Select Sign in in the site header to open it; it returns you to the page you were on once you are in. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/auth/. The Sign In tab is selected and the panel reads Welcome back. 2. In Email or username , type either the email address on the account or your username without the @ . 3. Type your Password . Select the eye button to show it. 4. Optional: tick Remember me to stay signed in on this browser see How long a sign in lasts how long a sign in lasts . 5. Select Sign In . 6. The first time you submit, the Auric human check appears: repeat the three mark sequence and select Verify sequence , then select Sign In again. How the check works is described in Sign up sign up.md the auric human check . 7. If the account has two step verification, the Second factor. panel appears; see Sign in with a second factor sign in with a second factor . Result: the message \"Identity confirmed. Opening your workspace…\" appears and the site opens: the page you were trying to reach, if you came from a link that needed sign in; otherwise the dashboard, if your account has no username yet; otherwise the home page. Message Wh"},{"t":"Sign up","d":"Create an Auric Artisan account with an email address and password, or with Google or GitHub, including every field rule and the human check.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/sign-up.html","h":["Sign up with email and password","The Auric human check","Sign up with Google or GitHub","After you sign up","Related"],"x":" You can create an account in two ways: with an email address and a password, or with an existing Google or GitHub account. Both are free and neither asks for a card. The sign up form is at https://auricartisan.com/auth/ register. You can also open https://auricartisan.com/auth/ and select the Create Account tab, or select Create account in the site header. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/auth/ and select Create Account . The panel is headed Create your identity. 2. Fill in the fields: Field What to enter Rules Display Name The name shown on anything you publish Required, 2–64 characters Username Your public handle, typed after the @ Required, 3–30 characters: letters, numbers and underscores only. You can sign in with it instead of your email. Email Your email address Required, a valid address Password Your password 12–128 characters, upper and lower case letters, at least one number and one symbol, no character repeated four or more times in a row, not a common password Confirm Password The same password again Must match 3. As you type the username, a tick means it is available and a cross means it is not. Hover over the mark, or read the message under the field, for the reason."},{"t":"Tokens","d":"What Auric Artisan tokens pay for, how much each plan includes, when included tokens expire, how to claim and check them, and how they differ from API credits.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/tokens.html","h":["How many tokens each plan includes","What a run costs","Claim your tokens","Check your balance","Expiry","When you run out","Tokens are not API credits","Refunds and tokens","Related"],"x":" Tokens meter the work that runs on Auric Artisan's servers when you start it from a website tool — for example rendered page analyses, snapshots and whole site accessibility crawls in the Analyzer. Everything that runs in your browser is free and unmetered. Tokens belong to your account, so you need to be signed in to have or spend them. Plan Included tokens Renews? Apprentice free 100, once No — a one time starter grant Artisan 250 a month Yes, each billing month Specialist coming soon 1,000 a month Yes, each billing month Industrial Pro coming soon 2,500 a month Yes, each billing month One token is sized at a reference rate of about $0.10 of metered work. The pricing page describes the Artisan allowance as \"250 pages a month however you spend them — a 24 page crawl costs 24\". The Analyzer shows the token cost of a run beside the button that starts it — \"This run\", the cost, and your balance — before you spend anything. After a site scan it shows a receipt: what was authorised, what was scanned, what was charged, and anything returned pages that failed are free, and tokens held for pages a site did not have are given back . The Analyzer's own guide explains the costs of each kind"},{"t":"Two-step verification","d":"Protect your Auric Artisan account with authenticator-app codes and single-use backup codes, sign in with them, and turn them off.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/two-step-verification.html","h":["Turn it on","Sign in with two-step verification","Turn it off","Get new backup codes","Setup messages","How it is protected","Reminders on the dashboard","If you lose your authenticator","Related"],"x":" Two step verification the dashboard calls it Two factor or 2FA adds a second check after your password: a six digit code from an authenticator app on your phone or computer. The codes use the standard TOTP method time based one time passwords, which change every 30 seconds , so any common authenticator app works. Two step verification is free on every plan. 1. Install an authenticator app if you do not have one. 2. Open the dashboard and select Security & Privacy . 3. The Two factor cell in the readout strip reads \"Off — nothing but your password\" and is highlighted while it is off. Select Enable 2FA . 4. The form below the strip says \"Setting up… fetching your secret.\" and then \"Scan this with your authenticator app, then enter the 6 digit code it shows.\" 5. Scan the QR code with the app. If you cannot scan, use the text under \"Can't scan? Enter this secret manually:\", or select Open in authenticator on a device that has the app. 6. Type the 6 digit code the app shows into the box placeholder 123456 . 7. Select Verify & enable . Result: \"Two factor authentication is ON. Store these one time backup codes somewhere safe:\" followed by ten backup codes. 8. Select Download backup code"},{"t":"Verify your email","d":"Confirm the email address on your Auric Artisan account, resend the link, and understand what stays locked until you do.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/verify-email.html","h":["What stays locked until you verify","Verify from the email","Time limits","Get a new link","Messages on the verification page","Related"],"x":" When you sign up with an email address and password, Auric Artisan sends a one time link to prove the address is yours. Accounts created with Google or GitHub are already verified and skip this page. You can sign in and use the dashboard straight away — the sign up screen calls this the \"limited workspace\". The sign in page lists what stays locked until the address is verified: billing buying a plan , promotions, API keys, device approval signing in the command line tool . 1. Open the verification email from Auric Artisan and select its link. 2. The page https://auricartisan.com/auth/verify email/ opens with the heading One click confirms it is really you. It removes the link's code from your address bar straight away. 3. Check that you asked for this account. The panel reads Ready to verify. \"Confirm this address only if you requested the account.\" 4. Select Confirm email ownership . Result: the heading changes to Email verified. with \"Ownership is confirmed and protected account features are now unlocked.\" and the message \"Verification complete. This link cannot be used again.\" Select Open workspace to go to the dashboard. A welcome email follows. Note: The page asks you to pres"},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every screen, control, field, rule and status in the Auric Artisan account area, from the sign-in page to the dashboard, pricing, checkout and invoices.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/reference.html","h":["Sign-in page","Other account pages","Header account menu","Dashboard masthead","Section rail","Overview section","Profile section","Plan and Usage section","Security and Privacy section","Finish setting up panel","Pricing page controls","Upgrade dialog","Related"],"x":" This page lists every control in the account area, screen by screen. Labels are as they appear on screen. For step by step instructions, follow the links to the task guides. Address: https://auricartisan.com/auth/ add register to open Create Account , forgot to open password recovery . Control What it does Sign In tab Shows the sign in form \"Welcome back.\" Create Account tab Shows the sign up form \"Create your identity.\" Exit Returns to the home page Arrow keys, Home , End Move between the two tabs Control What it does Values or rules Email or username Who you are An email address checked as an address if it contains @ or a username of 3–30 letters, numbers and underscores Password Your password Required Eye button \"Show password\" Shows or hides the password Toggle Remember me Keeps you signed in on this browser Up to 30 days; ends after seven days unused. Off: ends when the browser closes, 24 hours at most. Forgot password? Opens Recover access. Copies an email address you typed Sign In Submits; shows the human check on first use — Google , GitHub Sign in with that provider — Control Rules Display Name Required, 2–64 characters Username Required, 3–30 characters, letters, numbers"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for problems with signing in, verification emails, passwords, two-step codes, payments, invoices, API keys and the Auric Artisan dashboard.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["I cannot sign in","Google or GitHub sign-in errors","The verification email did not arrive","The reset email did not arrive","My authenticator code is refused","The dashboard","The danger zone will not unlock","Payments and checkout","Invoices","API keys and credits","Related"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom, the likely cause and what to do. For problems with the website in general — browser support, cookies, offline use — see Help: troubleshooting ../../../help/troubleshooting.md . Symptom Why What to do \"Enter a valid email address.\" although you typed a username The field contains an @ , so it is checked as an email address Type the username without @ , or your full email address The sign in is refused with a credentials message Wrong email, username or password Check for typing errors, then use Forgot password? Refused after several attempts Sign in attempts are rate limited; repeated failures can lock sign in for a while Wait, then try again, or reset your password \"Complete the Auric human check before continuing.\" A human check is on screen and not finished Repeat the three marks and select Verify sequence , then Sign In The human check keeps expiring Each check lasts a few minutes and is used once Select New sequence , answer, and sign in straight away \"Enter your email or username before verifying the sequence.\" The check is tied to the identifier in the form Fill in Email or username first You signed up with Google or GitHub and have no password "},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan accounts, plans, payments, tokens, API keys and deleting an account.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/docs/faq.html","h":["Accounts","Plans and payments","Tokens and credits","Security and data","Related"],"x":" No. Every tool is free with no login required. An account is needed for server backed tool work tokens , buying a plan, API keys, publishing a portfolio, and account security. See Create an account optional ../../../getting started/create an account.md . Yes. The first field on the sign in page accepts your email address or your username. Not from the dashboard yet. The field is read only: \"Email changes are not supported yet — contact support.\" Once every 30 days. A username that someone gives up is held for 30 days before anyone else can claim it. Changing a password signs out every device, including the one you are using, so that anyone holding an old session loses it. Sign in with the new password. The FAQ page says multiple accounts are technically permitted, but using them to get around usage limits may lead to all of them being suspended. No. Everything arrives by email. See Emails and messages emails and messages.md . Yes, every tool on every plan. Paid plans add conveniences such as ad free browsing, watermark free exports, a monthly token allowance and higher limits. See Plans and pricing plans and pricing.md . Artisan, today. Specialist and Industrial Pro are marked Com"},{"t":"Account and billing: supporting pages","d":"Supporting material for the Auric Artisan account area — glossary, keyboard shortcuts, limits, privacy and related pages.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the reference material that supports the task guides in docs ../docs/README.md : the terms used in the account area, its keyboard shortcuts, every numeric limit in one place, what the account stores and where, and links to related documentation. Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md Account, billing and security terms, defined in plain language Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Keys that work on the sign in page, the dashboard and the related dialogs Limits limits and accuracy.md Every rule, limit, time window and count in the account area, and what the figures mean Privacy privacy.md What the account stores on Auric Artisan's servers, what stays in your browser, and what never leaves Related related.md Other documentation, policies and pages connected to the account "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","d":"Keyboard keys that work on the Auric Artisan sign-in page, the account dashboard and the related dialogs.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Sign-in page","Dashboard","Dialogs","Site-wide keys you may use here"],"x":" The account pages can be used entirely from the keyboard. These are the keys with special behaviour; everything else follows normal browser conventions Tab to move, Enter or Space to press . Keys Where What it does Left / Right or Up / Down Sign In and Create Account tabs Switch tab Home / End The tabs First or last tab Enter Any form field Submits the form Keys Where What it does Left / Right Section rail Move to the previous or next section Home / End Section rail Jump to Overview or Security & Privacy Enter or Space Profile photo strip in Profile Choose a photo file Esc Photo viewer Closes it Esc Your account is nearly there panel Dismisses it for a week Keys Where What it does Esc Upgrade dialog Closes it Tab / Shift + Tab Upgrade dialog Cycle through its buttons without leaving it Keys What it does Ctrl + K Opens search ? Opens the guide when you are not typing in a field Ctrl + , Opens or closes Settings The full list is in Keyboard shortcuts ../../site features/keyboard shortcuts/README.md in Site features. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the account, billing, security and API terms used in the Auric Artisan account area.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Account chip — The photo, first name and plan shown in the site header when you are signed in. Selecting it opens the account menu. Allowance included — The tokens or API credits that come with a plan for each billing month. Included allowances do not roll over. Annual term — A plan pass bought for twelve months, costing ten times the monthly price. API credit — The unit that meters REST API calls. One credit is one standard request; heavier endpoints cost more. Separate from tokens. API key — A secret string that lets your code call the REST API as your account. Shown once when created; begins with aa live . Apprentice — The free plan. Every tool, 100 one time starter tokens, no API access. Artisan — The paid plan on sale today: ad free browsing, watermark free Pro exports, 250 tokens a month and higher limits. Auric human check — A short test on the sign in page repeat a sequence of three marks that proves a person is signing in. Each proof works once. Backup code — One of ten single use codes, in the form XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX , that replaces an authenticator code at sign in. Billing period — The month or the twelve months a plan pass covers. Monthly allowances refresh at the sta"},{"t":"Limits","d":"Every rule, size limit, time window and count in the Auric Artisan account area, and what the dashboard's figures do and do not measure.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Identity","Passwords and sign-in","Two-step verification","Dashboard","API","What the figures mean"],"x":" All the numbers in the account area in one place. Plan prices and allowances are on Plans and pricing ../docs/plans and pricing.md ; the pricing page at https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/ is authoritative for them. Item Limit Display name 2–64 characters at sign up; up to 64 in the profile Username 3–30 characters; letters, numbers and underscores; reserved words and near duplicates refused Username changes Once every 30 days Released usernames Held for 30 days before anyone else can claim them Bio Up to 500 characters Website Up to 200 characters; an http:// or https:// address Location Up to 120 characters Profile photo PNG, JPG or GIF, up to 2 MB before upload; cropped to a square and made smaller before it is saved Email address Cannot be changed from the dashboard Item Limit Password length 12–128 characters Password content Upper and lower case, a number, a symbol; no character four times in a row; not a common password Session with Remember me Up to 30 days; ends after seven days without use Session without Remember me Until the browser closes; 24 hours at most Second factor step 10 minutes to enter the code Human check proof Single use, tied to the email or username"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Auric Artisan account stores on its servers, what stays in your browser, what never reaches Auric Artisan, and how to export or delete it.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/privacy.html","h":["Stored with your account","Kept in your browser, not the account","Never reaches Auric Artisan","Cookies the account uses","Exporting and deleting","Related"],"x":" This page describes what the account area stores and where. The authoritative documents are the Privacy Policy https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ , the Cookie Policy https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ and the Data Retention and Deletion Policy https://auricartisan.com/legal/data retention and deletion policy/ . Data Why Email address, display name, username To identify you and sign you in Bio, website, location, profile photo What you chose to put on your profile Password as a one way hash only To check your password; it cannot be read back Two step secret encrypted and backup codes To check your codes Sessions and sign in records To list your devices and protect the account Dashboard preferences, including the Usage data choice So they follow you between browsers Plan, orders and payments To give you what you paid for and keep receipts Token and API credit balances and their history To meter and show your usage API keys as a hash and a short prefix only To recognise your keys; the full key is shown once Published portfolio To serve your public page My Library — palettes, gradients, collections and exports. Portfolio draft and its counters views, downloads, shares . Site"},{"t":"Related","d":"Documentation, policies and site pages connected to the Auric Artisan account, plans and billing.","p":"Website › Account and billing","u":"website/account-and-billing/others/related.html","h":["In these docs","Policy summaries","Site pages"],"x":" Page Why it is related Getting started ../../../getting started/README.md What an account adds, and the free tools model Public API ../../../services/public api/README.md Using the API keys and credits managed here Portfolio ../../portfolio/README.md Building and publishing the page your username points to Library ../../library/README.md Where your saved work lives Analyzer ../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Where tokens are claimed and spent Cookie consent and privacy ../../site features/cookie consent and privacy/README.md The cookie choice shown in Security & Privacy Help ../../../help/README.md General FAQ, troubleshooting and contact Summary Official page Subscription and Billing Policy ../../company and legal/docs/subscription and billing policy.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/subscription billing/ Refund Policy ../../company and legal/docs/refund policy.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/refund/ Privacy Policy ../../company and legal/docs/privacy policy.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ Cookie Policy ../../company and legal/docs/cookie policy.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ Data Retention and Deletion Policy ../../company and legal/"},{"t":"Download and offline","d":"Install Auric Artisan as an app, prepare it to work offline, keep it up to date, manage its storage, and remove it.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan is a progressive web app PWA : a website that your browser can install like an app and keep working without an internet connection. There is nothing to download from an app store. You install it from the browser you already use, and it opens in its own window with its own icon. The Download page at https://auricartisan.com/download/ \"Install it. Then lose the connection\" is where you install the app and, more importantly, prepare the offline version . Preparing it copies the site's pages, tools, libraries, palettes and data into your browser's storage while you are online, so that the workspace keeps working when you are not. You choose how much to keep with an offline profile : Auto , Lite , Balanced or Full . The page then shows exactly what is on your device: readiness checks, storage used, cached files and missing files, with buttons to audit, repair or reset the offline copy. Nothing large is downloaded unless you ask. On a first visit, the browser keeps only a small core of the site the app shell so that an offline visit can still show something useful. People who work on trains, planes or unreliable connections. Anyone who wants Auric Artisan in its own window"},{"t":"Download and offline guides","d":"Contents of the download and offline guides.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md A tour of the Download page and the three step offline workflow install the app.md install the app.md Installing on Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, iOS and iPadOS prepare offline.md prepare offline.md Offline profiles, preparing and downloading, persistent storage what works offline.md what works offline.md What works without a connection, what needs one, and the offline page updates.md updates.md How updates arrive and how to apply them storage and cache.md storage and cache.md Readiness checks, live metrics, audit, repair and reset installed app features.md installed app features.md App shortcuts, opening files, sharing to the app, links uninstall.md uninstall.md Removing the app and its offline data reference.md reference.md Every control, check, metric, profile and message troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes faq.md faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Get started with the app and offline use","d":"A tour of the Download page and the three steps to a working offline copy.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Two separate things","A tour of the Download page","The three steps","Next steps"],"x":" Installing puts Auric Artisan in its own window with an icon. Whether a browser offers this is the browser's decision. Preparing the offline version stores the site in your browser so it works without a connection. This works in any modern browser with a secure connection, installed or not. You can do either, or both. For reliable offline use, prepare the offline version even if you install. Open https://auricartisan.com/download/. From top to bottom: 1. The head. \"Auric Artisan · Browser PWA\", the title Install it. Then lose the connection , one paragraph, and the actions: Install app only when your browser offers installation ; Update app only when an update is waiting ; Prepare offline version ; Download full offline ; Open in browser to the homepage . Below them, a status line says what is happening, with a progress bar. 2. Readiness — Is this browser ready. A badge Checking , Preparing , Shell ready or Offline ready and six checks: Shell , Full cache , Persistent storage , Local capabilities , Install and Update . Buttons: Check readiness , Audit cache , Repair cache , Reset cache . 3. Live metrics — What is actually on this device. Cache entries, storage used, CPU threads, g"},{"t":"Install the app","d":"Install Auric Artisan as an app on each platform the Download page covers, and what installing changes.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/install-the-app.html","h":["Using the Install app button","Windows","macOS","Linux","ChromeOS","Android","iOS and iPadOS","Other devices","What installing changes"],"x":" The same app runs on Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, iOS and iPadOS. What differs is how you install it: whether a browser offers an install button is the browser's decision. The Download page marks your current platform with \"current\". In browsers that offer installation to web pages such as Chrome and Edge on desktop and Android , the Download page shows an Install app button. 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/download/. 2. Select Install app . The status reads \"Opening the browser install prompt...\". 3. Confirm in your browser's dialog. Result Status line Installed \"App install accepted. Finishing setup...\" and a message \"Auric Artisan installed\" You cancelled \"Install dismissed. You can still cache offline tools.\" Browser cannot install \"Install prompt is not available in this browser.\" Once installed, the button reads App installed and is hidden, and the Install check reads \"App is installed and running standalone.\" when you open the page in the app. If there is no Install app button, use your browser's own install option below. Install from Microsoft Edge or Google Chrome : Edge: select the app icon in the address bar, or Settings and more … › Apps › Install this si"},{"t":"Installed app features","d":"App shortcuts, opening files with the app, sharing to it, and how links behave once Auric Artisan is installed.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/installed-app-features.html","h":["App shortcuts","Open files with the app","Share to the app","Links","Standalone window"],"x":" These work once Auric Artisan is installed, in systems and browsers that support them mostly Chromium based browsers such as Chrome and Edge, and Android . Right click the app's icon on the taskbar or dock, or long press it on Android, for shortcuts: Shortcut Opens Palette Library Saved and generated palettes Gradient Library Gradient collections Basic Tools The core colour tool workspace Workspace Saved local palettes, gradients, assets and exports Analyzer The website analyzer Browser PWA The Download page's offline controls The installed app can be chosen to open these file types, for example from your file manager's Open with menu: Type Extensions JSON .json CSS .css CSV .csv Text and Markdown .txt , .md Images .png , .jpg , .jpeg , .svg The files open in your Workspace. A message reads \"1 file ready\" or the number of files . Text files up to 500 KB and images up to 2 MB are read straight away; larger files are passed on to open later. If a file cannot be read, the message is \"Could not open file\". On systems with a share menu such as Android , you can share a link or text to Auric Artisan . It opens in your Workspace with what you shared. Links to auricartisan.com can open in"},{"t":"Prepare the offline version","d":"Choose an offline profile and download the site into your browser so it works without a connection.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/prepare-offline.html","h":["What is stored automatically","Choose a profile","Download","Hindi offline","Persistent storage","If the connection drops","Data use"],"x":" On your first visit, your browser keeps a small core of the site, called the app shell : the main pages such as the homepage, Download, the tools index, Basic Tools, the Colour Science Lab, the Personalization Generator, the colour libraries, Search and Security , the site's styles and scripts, and the offline page. That is enough for an offline visit to show something useful, but not the whole site. Everything beyond the shell is downloaded only when you ask for it. On the Download page, under Profile — How much to keep : Profile Description on screen What it keeps Suits Auto default Device aware cache choice Chooses Lite, Balanced or Full from what the device reports Almost everyone Lite Smallest offline footprint The app shell and the core tools, and little else Phones, tight storage, metered connections Balanced Core tools plus active libraries Shell, core tools and the colour libraries and their data A laptop you also use for other things Full Download the widest local cache Every file the site lists for offline use A desktop that will be offline for a while Selecting Lite , Balanced or Auto only sets the profile \"Updated offline hardware profile.\" . Selecting Full sets it an"},{"t":"Storage and cache","d":"Read the readiness checks and live metrics, and audit, repair or reset the offline copy.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/storage-and-cache.html","h":["Readiness checks","Live metrics","Audit the offline copy","Repair it","Reset it","How much space it takes"],"x":" The Download page reads its figures from your browser itself: the offline store, the storage estimate and the browser's capabilities. Open it on the device you care about. Select Check readiness to refresh them. Check Possible states Shell \"Service worker shell is preparing.\" / \"Service worker shell is ready for cached navigation.\" Full cache \"Full offline cache is not warmed yet.\" / \"Run prepare offline version to warm every core route.\" / \"Offline cache has warmed this device profile.\" Persistent storage \"Persistent storage is active for this browser.\" / \"Storage is best effort until the browser grants persistence.\" Local capabilities The number of CPU threads available for local work Install Checking / available / not offered by this browser yet / installed and running standalone / accepted / dismissed / could not be opened Update See Updates updates.md The badge sums it up: Checking , Preparing , Shell ready the core is stored or Offline ready your profile is complete . Metric What it shows Cache entries How many files are stored Storage used Space used by the site, and the browser's quota for it persistent or best effort Local CPU Processor threads, and approximate device mem"},{"t":"Uninstall and remove data","d":"Remove the installed app, and clear the offline copy and other data the site keeps in your browser.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/uninstall.html","h":["Remove the installed app","Remove the offline copy","Remove everything"],"x":" Uninstalling is done by your browser or system. The usual ways: Chrome or Edge Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS : open the app, open its menu ⋮ or … in the title bar, and choose Uninstall Auric Artisan . On Windows you can also use Settings › Apps . Safari on macOS: remove the app from the Dock and delete it from your Applications folder. Android: long press the icon and choose Uninstall or Remove , or use App info . iOS and iPadOS: long press the icon, choose Remove App , then Delete from Home Screen wording varies by version . The exact wording depends on your browser and system version. Uninstalling the app may leave the offline copy and your other site data in the browser. To remove the offline copy: 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/download/. 2. Select Reset cache . The offline store is deleted and only the small app shell is rebuilt. To remove all data the site keeps in this browser the offline copy, your settings, your library, recordings, and preferences , clear the site data for auricartisan.com in your browser's settings, usually under Privacy or Site settings . Important: Clearing site data deletes your local library items and recordings. Export or download anything you "},{"t":"Updates","d":"How new versions of the site reach your browser and installed app, and how to apply them.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/updates.html","h":["How you find out","Apply an update","Check for an update","Your offline copy after an update"],"x":" Auric Artisan updates itself from the website: there is no app store update. Each release has a version name, shown on the Download page as PWA version for example 2026 09 24 pwa 303 . When your browser has downloaded a newer version in the background, it waits for you. You may see: a prompt, Update ready — \"Refresh to use the newest offline cache.\" — with Refresh and Later ; on the Download page, an Update app button in the head, the Update check reading \"Update is ready.\", and the summary's Update action saying the same; in the right click menu, a highlighted Update available row see Context menu ../../site features/context menu/README.md . Select Refresh on the prompt, or Update app on the Download page \"Applying update...\" . The page reloads on the new version. Or press Ctrl + Shift + U , or choose Update website in the right click menu, which checks for an update and applies it. Later closes the prompt; the update is applied the next time all the site's tabs and app windows are closed and reopened, or when you choose to apply it. Open the Download page: it checks when it loads, and the Update check shows one of: State Meaning Checking for updates. A check is running Offline a"},{"t":"What works offline","d":"What keeps working without a connection, what needs one, and what the offline page shows.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/what-works-offline.html","h":["Works offline, once stored","Needs a connection","How pages are served","The offline page"],"x":" After you prepare the offline version, these work without a connection, as far as your profile includes them: the pages and colour tools stored on the device; the colour libraries and their data Balanced and Full ; your library of saved palettes, gradients and exports, which lives on your device; site features such as the Settings panel, theme, the right click menu, split view between stored pages, the recorder, eye rest and the screen saver; searching the site with Spotlight the search index is part of the Balanced and Full profiles ; Hindi, if it was included see Prepare the offline version prepare offline.md hindi offline . When you go offline, a message reads Offline mode and stays until the connection returns; then Back online appears. Anything that has to reach a server: signing in, your account, billing and anything synced to your account; the Analyzer's audits of live websites; the Web tab in Spotlight and web results on the search page; sending feedback it is kept and sent when you are back online ; installing or updating the app; pages and files you have not stored. Pages are fetched fresh from the network when you are online, and stored as you visit them. Offline, the s"},{"t":"Download and offline reference","d":"Every control, check, metric, profile, app property and message of the Download page and offline system.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/reference.html","h":["Head actions","Readiness section","Metrics section","Profile section","The installed app","Messages"],"x":" Page: https://auricartisan.com/download/ Control Shown Action Install app When the browser offers installation Opens the browser's install dialog Update app When an update is waiting Applies the update and reloads Prepare offline version Always Downloads the profile in effect Download full offline Always Downloads the Full profile Open in browser Always Opens the homepage Status line and progress bar Always What is happening now Control Action Badge Checking, Preparing, Shell ready, Offline ready Checks Shell, Full cache, Persistent storage, Local capabilities, Install, Update Check readiness Refreshes the checks Audit cache Compares the store with the profile Repair cache Fetches missing files of the profile Reset cache Deletes the offline store and rebuilds the shell Cache entries, Storage used, Local CPU, Graphics, Offline profile, Cache target, Missing assets, PWA version; Browser capabilities Ready or Limited : Service worker, Cache API, Persistent storage, IndexedDB, File access, Clipboard, Share, Camera input, EyeDropper, Workers, Graphics, Offline privacy; Check local hardware . Control Values Default Profile Auto , Lite , Balanced , Full Auto Limit background cache work o"},{"t":"Troubleshooting the app and offline use","d":"Fixes for common problems installing Auric Artisan, preparing it offline and keeping it up to date.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["There is no Install app button","\"Install prompt is not available in this browser.\"","\"PWA runtime is still loading.\"","\"Offline download could not start yet.\"","The download finished with failed files","Persistent storage stays \"best-effort\"","A page says \"You are offline\"","The site seems out of date","Storage is nearly full","iPhone or iPad cleared the offline copy"],"x":" Why: the button appears only in browsers that let pages offer installation, such as Chrome and Edge. Safari and Firefox do not; the site is already installed; or the browser has decided not to offer it yet. What to do: use your browser's own install option see Install the app install the app.md . On iPhone and iPad, use Safari's Share › Add to Home Screen . You can still prepare the offline version without installing. Why: the browser did not offer installation to the page, or you dismissed it recently. What to do: use the browser menu to install, or try later. Why: the offline system starts after the page finishes loading. What to do: wait a few seconds; if it does not clear, reload the page. Why: the browser has not finished setting up the site's offline system, or service workers are blocked for example in some private windows or by an extension . What to do: reload the page and try again. Use a normal window, and make sure the site is not blocked from storing data. Why: some files could not be fetched, usually because of a brief network problem. What to do: select Repair cache while online. Why: the browser decides whether to grant it. Some grant it only to installed apps or s"},{"t":"Download and offline FAQ","d":"Short answers about installing Auric Artisan and using it offline.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/docs/faq.html","h":["Is there a desktop app to download?","Is the app free?","Does the installed app need an account?","Do my saved palettes work offline?","Does the app update itself?","Can I install it on more than one device?","How much space does it need?","Which browsers work best?"],"x":" The app is installed from your browser, not downloaded as a separate program. It then runs in its own window. The browser extension and the VS Code extensions are separate products. Yes. Installing and using it offline costs nothing. Every tool is free on every plan. No. An account is needed only for account features, which also need a connection. Yes. Your library is kept on your device and works offline. Yes, from the website. When a new version is ready you are asked to refresh; see Updates updates.md . Yes. Install and prepare it on each device. Your library and settings stay on each device separately, unless you use account features that sync them. It depends on the profile. Lite is small; Full can take more than 100 MB. The Storage used figure on the Download page shows your actual use. For installing: Chrome and Edge on desktop and Android, and Safari on iPhone and iPad Add to Home Screen and on macOS Add to Dock . For offline use: any current browser with service workers on a secure connection. "},{"t":"Download and offline: supporting material","d":"Contents of the download and offline supporting files.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the download and offline guides limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Platform limits, storage, and what the page's figures mean related.md related.md Related features and products privacy.md privacy.md What is stored on your device and what the page reads release notes.md release notes.md User facing history There are no shortcuts specific to the Download page. Ctrl + Shift + U applies a waiting website update from any page. "},{"t":"Download and offline glossary","d":"Terms used in the download and offline guides.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning PWA Progressive web app: a website a browser can install like an app and run offline. Install Adding the site to your device as an app with its own window and icon. Standalone Running in its own window without the browser's toolbar. Service worker A part of the site that runs in your browser and serves stored files when you are offline. Cache The browser's store of site files kept for offline use. App shell The small core of pages, styles and scripts stored automatically on your first visit. Offline profile How much of the site to store: Auto, Lite, Balanced or Full. Persistent storage Browser storage that is not cleared automatically when space runs low. Best effort storage Browser storage that the browser may clear when space runs low. Quota The amount of storage the browser allows the site to use. Audit A check of which files of your profile are stored and which are missing. Background sync A browser feature that finishes a task, such as a download, when you are next online. Share target An app that appears in your device's share menu. "},{"t":"Download and offline limits and accuracy","d":"Platform limits, storage limits, and what the Download page's figures do and do not tell you.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Platform limits","Storage","What the figures mean","What offline cannot do"],"x":" Installing depends on the browser. Chrome and Edge offer it on desktop and Android; Safari offers Add to Home Screen on iPhone and iPad and Add to Dock on macOS; Firefox on desktop does not install web apps. Offline use needs a browser with service workers and a secure https connection. It does not work in browsers or modes that block service workers or site storage. Mobile Safari limits how much a website may store and may clear it if the site is not used for a while. App shortcuts, file opening, sharing to the app and link types work only where the system and browser support them, mostly Chromium based browsers and Android. Background sync , which finishes interrupted downloads, is available only in some browsers. The browser sets the site's quota. The Storage used figure shows use and quota as the browser reports them. Without persistent storage, the browser may clear the offline copy when the device is short of space. Reset cache clears only the offline copy. Your library, settings and recordings are separate. Cache entries counts stored files; it includes pages you visited as well as prepared files. Cache target is the number of files in the profile for the current release; i"},{"t":"Download and offline privacy","d":"What the installed app and offline copy store on your device, and what the Download page reads.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/privacy.html","h":["Stored on your device","What the Download page reads","What uses the network","Removing it"],"x":" The offline copy of the site's files, in your browser's storage for auricartisan.com. Your profile choice, the low power switch, and whether you have asked for an offline copy so an interrupted or out of date copy can be completed later . Files you open with the installed app, or text and links you share to it, are held on your device for the Workspace to pick up. The page reads your device's processor thread count, approximate memory, graphics processor name, connection type and storage estimate, as your browser reports them. It uses them to show the metrics and to choose the Auto profile. It does not send them to Auric Artisan. Downloading the offline copy and updates, from auricartisan.com. Checking for updates. Select Reset cache on the Download page, uninstall the app, or clear the site's data in your browser see Uninstall and remove data ../docs/uninstall.md . "},{"t":"Download and offline release notes","d":"User-facing history of the installable app and offline support, from the public changelog.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/release-notes.html","h":[],"x":" Date Release Change 2026 06 05 v0.9.9 Added PWA app support, alongside user settings controls, guide content and the UX Kit. The Download page as documented here readiness checks, live metrics, the Auto, Lite, Balanced and Full profiles, and audit, repair and reset reflects the site as of September 2026, app version 2026 09 24 pwa 303 . The PWA version figure on the Download page shows the version in your browser. See https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ for later releases. "},{"t":"Related to download and offline","d":"Features and products related to installing and offline use.","p":"Website › Download and offline","u":"website/download-and-offline/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Navigation dock ../../site features/navigation dock/README.md — Back, Forward and Reload in the installed app's window. Info bars and notices ../../site features/info bars and notices/docs/notices and messages.md — the offline, update and install messages. Language ../../site features/language/README.md — keeping Hindi available offline. Kits ../../kits/README.md — the Update Kit. Browser extension ../../../browser extension/README.md — Auric Artisan's tools in your browser on other websites. VS Code extensions ../../../vscode extensions/README.md — Auric Artisan in your code editor. Header and navigation ../../site features/header and navigation/README.md — the Browser PWA icon and the drawer's The app link. "},{"t":"Advertise on Auric Artisan","d":"What advertising on Auric Artisan offers, who it is for, and how to request your first campaign with the AdsSense campaign builder.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" AdsSense is Auric Artisan's own advertising system. It puts your product in front of the designers, developers and colour scientists who use the site, next to the tools and articles they came for. The page at https://auricartisan.com/advertise/ has everything in one place: the formats and their prices, a live example of each placement, and a six step campaign builder that shows the full price before you send anything. Every ad is clearly labelled Sponsored . Ads are placed by page context, not by following people across sites: you choose where your campaign runs, and the audience groups you pick guide the creative review only. Every creative that runs is listed publicly in the Ad Library at https://auricartisan.com/advertise/library/. Campaigns are booked by request. When you send a campaign from the builder, nothing is booked and nothing is charged. Auric Artisan confirms the campaign and then sends you a Razorpay link to pay the price you were shown. Your campaign runs after payment and creative approval. Companies and makers of design, development and colour products. Studios, educators and communities that want to reach people who work with colour. Anyone launching a product t"},{"t":"Advertise documentation","d":"Task guides, reference, troubleshooting and FAQ for advertising on Auric Artisan and the Ad Library.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/README.html","h":["Plan and build a campaign","Transparency","Reference and help"],"x":" File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md A tour of the advertise page and your first campaign request. formats and placements.md formats and placements.md The four formats, the five zones, benchmarks and where ads appear. create a campaign.md create a campaign.md The six step campaign builder, step by step. destination and tracking.md destination and tracking.md The destination address, UTM auto tagging, custom parameters and macros. design your creative.md design your creative.md The creative studio, uploading artwork, specifications and the creative policy. pricing and booking.md pricing and booking.md The live quote, discounts, promo codes, currency, payment, refunds and the flight report. File What it covers ad library.md ad library.md Browsing the Ad Library and reporting an ad. File What it covers reference.md reference.md Every control, option, price, limit and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers. Back to the Advertise overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with advertising","d":"A tour of the Auric Artisan advertise page and how to send your first campaign request.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","A tour of the page","Send your first request","Next steps"],"x":" Have these ready: The address you want clicks to go to. Your brand or company name. An email address for receipts and campaign updates. Finished artwork, if you have it. If not, you can design the ad on the page. You do not need an Auric Artisan account. https://auricartisan.com/advertise/ is one long page. A row of links near the top jumps to each part: Campaign builder , Live placements , Formats , Ad Library and Policy & measurement . The introduction — Put your work in front of people who build with color. , with Create a campaign and View live ads . Figures beside it describe the audience, such as the estimated daily ad views and the number of Learn guides. Engine telemetry — this page, right now — four live counts for the ads on the page you are reading: units mounted , impressions , MRC viewable and clicks . They are measured in your browser, not modelled. See a live placement — real ad units, served the same way your campaign would be. A unit with no ad to show disappears. Formats & benchmarks — a table of the four formats with size, position, typical click through rate, what each is best for and the starting price. Create your campaign — the six step builder, with the liv"},{"t":"The Ad Library","d":"How to browse the Auric Artisan Ad Library, read an ad's details, and report an ad that breaks the creative policy.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/ad-library.html","h":["Browse the library","Read an ad","Report an ad","Who may sell these ads","Advertise yourself"],"x":" The Ad Library at https://auricartisan.com/advertise/library/ lists every ad that runs on Auric Artisan: Every ad, in the open . Each entry shows the creative, the advertiser, the format, where it runs, its flight dates and its landing address. There are no hidden ads and no ads shown only to some people. An ad is listed for its full run and for at least 90 days after it ends. Anyone can open the library; no account is needed. At the top of the page: Search advertiser or text… — filters the ads by advertiser, ad text or landing address as you type. Format chips — All formats , Leaderboard , Rectangle , In feed and Strip . Status chips — All , Active and Ended . The count beside the filters says how many ads match, for example 12 ads . If none match, the page says No ads match those filters. Each card shows: Item Meaning Creative The ad exactly as it is served. Advertiser Who runs the ad. Auric Artisan's own promotions are marked house . Status badge Active or Ended . Format For example Leaderboard · 728×90 . Runs on The zones where it appears, such as Homepage or Learn library 113 articles . Flight since and the start date, or the start and end dates. Landing Where a click goes. A"},{"t":"Create a campaign","d":"A step-by-step guide to the six-step AdsSense campaign builder on the Auric Artisan advertise page.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/create-a-campaign.html","h":["Moving between steps","Step 1: Basics","Step 2: Format","Step 3: Creative","Step 4: Audience","Step 5: Budget","Step 6: Review","Send the request"],"x":" The campaign builder is under Create your campaign on https://auricartisan.com/advertise/. It has six steps: Basics , Format , Creative , Audience , Budget and Review . The quote panel beside it shows the step you are on, for example Step 2/6 , and updates the price with every choice. Continue → checks the current step and moves on. If something is missing, a message under the buttons says what, for example Add a campaign name to continue. On the fifth step the button reads Review campaign → . ← Back returns to the previous step. The numbered step chips at the top open any step you have already reached. Your draft is saved in this browser automatically, with the note Draft saved locally . If you come back later, the builder picks up where you left off. A start date that has passed is moved to tomorrow. Start with the campaign basics. Field What to enter Limit Campaign name A name for your own reference. Only you see it. 2 to 80 characters Brand / company Who is running the campaign. 2 to 80 characters Destination URL Where every click lands. A bare domain is completed with https:// when you leave the field. Up to 500 characters in the field Below these, Destination & tracking buil"},{"t":"Design your creative","d":"How to design an ad in the AdsSense creative studio or upload finished artwork, the specifications for each format, and the creative policy.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/design-your-creative.html","h":["Design it in the studio","Upload finished artwork","Specifications for each format","The creative policy","Accessibility tips"],"x":" The third step of the campaign builder, Creative , is where you make the ad itself. Under Creative source , choose Design it here to use the built in creative studio, or Choose a file to upload finished artwork. The Live preview always shows your creative at the exact ratio of the format you chose, for example 728×90 · Leaderboard , with the Sponsored label. The studio renders your text and colours as a crisp vector image at the exact size of your format. Field What it is Limit If left empty Headline The main line. 40 characters Your brand name Supporting line One clear reason to click. 60 characters \"Reach people who work in color\" Call to action The button text. 20 characters \"LEARN MORE\" Creative description A description of the visual for screen readers. 120 characters A description made from your brand name Background The background colour. Colour picker FFF8EC Accent The colour of the border, the side bar or mark, and the button. Colour picker D3AF37 Text The colour of the headline and supporting line. Colour picker 1F2937 The button text is set in dark or white automatically, to stand out on the accent colour. Under the colours, a line checks the headline against the backgr"},{"t":"Destination and tracking","d":"How to set the destination address of an Auric Artisan ad campaign, with UTM auto-tagging, custom URL parameters and tracking macros.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/destination-and-tracking.html","h":["The destination address","Auto-tagging","Custom URL parameters","Tracking macros","The final URL"],"x":" The Destination URL in the first step is where every click on your ad lands. Below it, Destination & tracking builds the full address that clicks will actually use, called the Final URL . Type the address of your landing page. If you type a bare domain such as your product.com , it becomes https://your product.com when you leave the field. Display link shows the short form of the address that goes with the ad: the site and the start of the path. Test link ↗ opens the final address with sample values in place of the macros, so you can check it loads. It appears once the address is valid. Message Meaning Enter a destination URL. The field is empty. That doesn't parse as a complete URL — include https://. The address is incomplete. Only http s destinations can be served. The address uses another scheme. Credentials inside the URL are not allowed. The address contains a user name or password. That hostname doesn't look reachable. The site name is not a full domain. These stop you continuing. Two warnings let you continue: Not secure http — browsers may warn your visitors. Prefer https. Link shorteners hide the real destination from the Ad Library — use the final URL. This appears for "},{"t":"Formats and placements","d":"The four ad formats on Auric Artisan, the five zones a campaign can run in, their sizes, benchmarks and starting prices.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/formats-and-placements.html","h":["The four formats","The five zones","Goals and recommendations","How ads are shown"],"x":" A campaign has one format and runs in one zone. The format is the shape of the ad; the zone is the part of the site it appears on. Format Size Position Typical CTR Best for From Leaderboard 728×90 In content, all page types ~0.4% Awareness at scale ₹399/day Medium Rectangle 300×250 Inline with articles ~0.7% Consideration ₹499/day Native In Feed Card Card Inside tool and article grids ~1.2% Traffic and launches ₹649/day Panels & Search Strip 320×100 Kits, Spotlight, search ~0.5% Power user reach ₹299/day In US dollars the starting prices are $5, $6, $8 and $4 a day. Select USD $ in the builder to see every price in dollars. The click through rates are house averages measured by the ad system. Your flight report shows your own numbers. A wide banner in the content of articles, tools and hub pages. The page calls it the workhorse unit. A 300×250 unit inline with content, and the page's highest engagement display unit. A sponsored card that sits inside the tool and article grids, with a native look. Card artwork is 720×600. A compact 320×100 strip inside the site's kits, in Spotlight Ctrl + K and in search results. Choose the zone in the Audience step, under Where it runs . Each show"},{"t":"Pricing and booking","d":"How the AdsSense live quote is worked out, the discounts and promo codes, currencies, what happens after you send a request, payment, refunds and the flight report.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/pricing-and-booking.html","h":["The live quote","What changes the price","Example quotes","Send the request","What happens next","Refunds","Talk to a person"],"x":" Beside the campaign builder, the Live estimate panel prices your campaign as you build it. Every choice updates it at once, and the price shown is the price you are asked to pay. Your campaign shows: Line Meaning Summary Format, zone, days and share, for example Leaderboard · Run of site everywhere · 30 days @ 50% . Base run The price before discounts. Flight discount The saving for a longer flight. Shown only when there is one. Promo The promo code saving, with the code. Shown only when there is one. Tax Shown only when tax applies. Total What you pay. Estimated delivery shows: Figure Meaning impressions How many times the ad is expected to be shown: the zone's daily views, times the days, times your share of voice. est. uniques Roughly how many different people see it. est. clicks Impressions times the format's typical click through rate. eff. CPM The effective price per thousand impressions, before tax. These are estimates. Your flight report shows what was actually delivered. Format : each has a daily rate, from ₹299 $4 to ₹649 $8 a day. See Formats and placements formats and placements.md . Zone : busier zones cost more a day. Run of site everywhere costs the most and reaches"},{"t":"Advertise reference","d":"Every control, option, price, limit and message in the AdsSense campaign builder and the Ad Library.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/reference.html","h":["Formats","Zones","Step 1: Basics","Step 2: Format","Step 3: Creative","Step 4: Audience","Step 5: Budget","Step 6: Review","Quote panel","Messages","Ad Library controls"],"x":" Format Size INR a day USD a day Typical CTR Leaderboard 728×90 ₹399 $5 ~0.4% Medium Rectangle 300×250 ₹499 $6 ~0.7% Native In Feed Card Card, artwork 720×600 ₹649 $8 ~1.2% Panels & Search Strip 320×100 ₹299 $4 ~0.5% The daily prices are the \"from\" prices; the zone, flight and share change the total. Zone Estimated views a day Homepage ~1,400 Learn library 113 articles ~2,600 Tools & workspaces ~1,900 Collections · Blog · Docs ~1,100 Run of site everywhere ~7,000 Control What it does Values or range Default Campaign name Your own name for the campaign. 2 to 80 characters Empty Brand / company Who runs the campaign; also the studio's fallback headline. 2 to 80 characters Empty Destination URL Where clicks land. http or https; the field takes up to 500 characters Empty Display link Short form of the destination. — — Test link ↗ Opens the final address with sample macro values. — — Auto tagging Adds UTM parameters. On, off On utm source … utm term UTM values. Up to 60 characters each See below + Add parameter Adds a custom parameter. Up to 5; name up to 32, value up to 200 characters None Macro chips Insert a macro in the last used tracking field. {placement} , {zone} , {campaign} , {"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems with the AdsSense campaign builder, booking requests and the Ad Library.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Continue does nothing","I cannot open a later step from the step chips","The destination address is rejected","My uploaded file is rejected","The preview crops my artwork","The studio says \"below WCAG AA\"","The start date will not go earlier","My promo code shows \"unknown code\"","The request button stays on \"Complete campaign to request booking\"","\"Could not send the request\"","The confirmation says \"Payment verified\", but I have not paid","I have not received the payment link","My draft has gone","My campaign is not in the Ad Library"],"x":" Why: Something in the current step is missing or not valid. The message under the buttons says what. What to do: Read the message and fix that field. In the first step, fields with a problem are also marked. See the messages in the Reference reference.md . Why: The chips open only steps you have already reached with Continue . What to do: Work through the steps in order once. After that you can jump between them. Why: It is incomplete, uses a scheme other than http or https, contains a user name or password, or its site name is not a full domain. What to do: Paste the full address from your browser's address bar, starting https:// . Use the final address, not a link shortener. Why: The file is not PNG, JPG, WebP or SVG, is over 300 KB, or cannot be read as an image. What to do: Export the artwork again in one of the four types and compress it under 300 KB. The Creative specs section suggests under 150 KB for the Leaderboard and Medium Rectangle. Why: The artwork's shape does not match the format. What to do: Upload artwork at the recommended size for your format, shown under the upload area: 728×90, 300×250, 320×100, or 720×600 for the in feed card. Why: The headline colour and ba"},{"t":"Advertise FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about advertising on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I pay when I send the campaign?","How soon can my campaign start?","Do I need an account?","Which currencies can I pay in?","Is tax included?","Can I target individual people?","Do my ads track visitors?","How is my campaign measured?","Who sees my ad?","What is share of voice?","Can I change the format after designing the creative?","Can Auric Artisan make the creative for me?","Can I get a refund?","Is my ad listed publicly?","What gets an ad rejected?"],"x":" No. Sending books nothing and charges nothing. Auric Artisan confirms the campaign and sends a Razorpay link for the price you were shown. The earliest start date is tomorrow. A campaign starts at 00:00 IST on its start date, after payment and creative approval. The confirmation and payment link arrive within one business day of your request. No. You need a billing email for receipts and campaign updates. Indian rupees or US dollars. Choose in the Budget step. The quote shows a Tax line when tax applies. The Total is the price you are asked to pay. No. Campaigns are placed by page context: you choose the zone. The audience groups you choose guide the creative review only; they do not identify or follow visitors. No. Ads never track visitors across sites. Third party ad technology runs only for visitors who accept the marketing cookie category. Impressions, MRC viewable impressions at least half the ad visible for one second , clicks and effective CPM. You receive them in a flight report at the end of the campaign. Visitors to the zone you chose, up to your frequency cap per session. Paid Auric Artisan subscribers browse without ads. The fraction of eligible ad renders in your zone"},{"t":"Advertise: other material","d":"Supporting material for advertising on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Share of voice, flight, CPM, viewability and other advertising terms. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the estimates are based on, and the limits of the builder. Related related.md Pages and policies that work with advertising. Privacy privacy.md What advertisers share, what is kept in the browser, and what ads do not track. Back to the Advertise overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Advertise glossary","d":"Advertising terms used on the Auric Artisan advertise page and in the Ad Library.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Ad Library The public list of every ad that runs on Auric Artisan. ads.txt A public file that declares who may sell a site's ad space. AdsSense Auric Artisan's own advertising system. Auto tagging Adding UTM parameters to the click address automatically. Booking request A campaign sent from the builder. It books and charges nothing until confirmed and paid. Call to action The button text on an ad, such as \"LEARN MORE\". Campaign One ad in one format and zone, for one flight. Creative The ad itself: the artwork people see. CTR click through rate Clicks divided by impressions. Destination URL The page a click on the ad opens. Display link The short form of the destination shown with the ad. eff. CPM Effective cost per thousand impressions: the price divided by estimated impressions, times 1,000. Final URL The destination with tracking parameters added. Flight The period a campaign runs, from its start date. Flight report The report of delivered impressions, viewable impressions, clicks and effective CPM at the end of a campaign. Format The shape of an ad: Leaderboard, Medium Rectangle, Native In Feed Card, or Panels & Search Strip. Frequency cap The most times one visito"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the AdsSense price and delivery estimates are based on, how accurate they are, and the limits of the campaign builder.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["The price","The delivery estimate","What reduces delivery","Builder limits","Drafts"],"x":" The quote in the builder is the price you are asked to pay. It is worked out from the format's daily rate, the zone, the flight length, the share of voice and any promo code, in the currency you chose. The payment link is for the price shown. Impressions are estimated from each zone's typical daily views, shown on the zone buttons, multiplied by the days in the flight and your share of voice. Real traffic varies from day to day. Unique viewers are a rough estimate from impressions. Clicks use each format's typical click through rate: house averages measured by the ad system, not a promise for your ad. eff. CPM divides the price before tax by the estimated impressions. The figures on the page, such as estimated daily ad views, are the page's own estimates. Your flight report gives the delivered figures, measured by the ad system rather than estimated. Paid Auric Artisan subscribers browse without ads. Your frequency cap limits how often one visitor sees the ad. Ad units render only as they come near the part of the page on screen, so a unit far down a page a visitor never scrolls to is not shown. Item Limit Formats per campaign 1 Zones per campaign 1 Audience groups Up to 3 Custom "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What you share when you request an Auric Artisan ad campaign, what stays in your browser, and what ads do and do not track about visitors.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/others/privacy.html","h":["For advertisers","For visitors who see ads"],"x":" When you select Request campaign , Auric Artisan receives: Your brand or company name and your billing email. The campaign details: campaign name, goal, format, zone, flight, start date, share of voice, frequency cap, audience groups, final destination address, quoted total and estimated impressions. Your billing email is used for receipts and campaign updates. Your draft, including any uploaded artwork, is saved in this browser while you build, so you can return to it. It is cleared when you send the request. To discard a draft without sending, clear this site's data in your browser. Payment is made through a Razorpay link that Auric Artisan sends after confirming your campaign. Card and bank details are handled by Razorpay. While your campaign runs, the Ad Library ../docs/ad library.md lists your creative, your brand as the advertiser, the format, the zones, the flight dates and the landing address, for the full run and at least 90 days after. Your campaign name, billing email and price are not listed. Every ad is labelled Sponsored . Campaigns are placed by page context. The audience groups advertisers choose guide the creative review and do not identify or follow individual vi"},{"t":"Related","d":"Pages, policies and product areas that work with advertising on Auric Artisan.","p":"Website › Advertise","u":"website/advertise/others/related.html","h":["Where your ad can appear","Policies","Accounts and plans"],"x":" Library ../../library/README.md — the Learn articles, blog and documentation in the Learn library and Collections · Blog · Docs zones. Collections ../../library/collections/README.md — the tool grids that can hold a Native In Feed Card. Search ../../search/README.md — the search page, one home of the Panels & Search Strip. Site features ../../site features/README.md — Spotlight Ctrl + K and the site's panels, where the strip also appears. Company and legal ../../company and legal/README.md — the terms, the acceptable use policy, the refund policy and the cookie settings. Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md — paid plans, whose members browse without ads. "},{"t":"Company and legal","d":"Plain-language summaries of Auric Artisan's company pages and legal policies, each linked to the official page that governs.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find the official pages","Quick start","What you can do with this folder","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan publishes a set of company pages — About, Contact, FAQ, Timeline, Accessibility, the author page, Pricing and a Security page — and twelve legal documents, from the Terms of Service to the Transparency and Ethics Policy. This folder summarises each of them in plain language so you can find what matters to you quickly. The official pages are authoritative. These summaries are written to help you understand the documents, not to replace them. They add no obligations and remove none. Where a summary and the official page differ, the official page wins; each summary links to its source, and names the version and date it was written from. Some pages on the site describe the same thing slightly differently, because they were updated at different times. Where that matters to you — for example, which address to send a security report to — the summary points it out and names the more specific or more recent page. Anyone deciding whether to use Auric Artisan, create an account or buy a plan. People who want to know what happens to their data. Researchers reporting a security issue. Anyone who needs to cite or check a policy. Group Address All legal documents https://auricartis"},{"t":"Company and legal docs","d":"The list of plain-language summaries of Auric Artisan's company pages and legal policies.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/README.html","h":["Start here","Company pages","Legal documents"],"x":" One page per official document. Each summary names the official address, the version and date it was written from, and restates the document's key points and sections in plain language. The official page is always authoritative. Page What it covers How to read the policies getting started.md Finding a policy, reading its dates and versions, and using the summaries Summary Official page About Auric Artisan about.md https://auricartisan.com/company/about/ Contact contact.md https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ FAQ page company faq.md https://auricartisan.com/company/faq/ Timeline timeline.md https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/ Accessibility statement accessibility statement.md https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/ Security page security page.md https://auricartisan.com/security/ Author page author.md https://auricartisan.com/company/author/chirag bansal/ Pricing page pricing page.md https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/ Summary Official page Legal index legal index.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/ Terms of Service terms of service.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/terms/ Privacy Policy privacy policy.md https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ Cookie Polic"},{"t":"How to read the policies","d":"Find a policy, read its effective date and version, navigate its sections, and use the plain-language summaries in these docs.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Find a policy","The parts of a policy page","Versions these summaries were written from","Things that apply to every policy","How to use the summaries","Related"],"x":" 1. Open https://auricartisan.com/legal/ Legal & Policies . 2. Each card names a document and describes it in one line. Select one to open it. The same index links to the Platform FAQ. Company pages — About, Timeline, Pricing, Accessibility, FAQ and Contact — are in the Company menu in the site header. Part What it tells you Auric Artisan · Legal and the title Which document you are reading Effective The date the document took effect Last updated The date of the latest change Version The document's version number Reading time An estimate ← All Policies Back to the index Key Points The document in a few bullets On this page Links to each numbered section Numbered sections Select a heading to expand or collapse it Plain language: , Current status: , Important: notes Short explanations inside a section Related Policies Links to connected documents Written on the date at the top of this page. If a policy's Last updated date is newer than the one below, read the official page for the changes. Document Effective Last updated Version Terms of Service 27 April 2026 12 August 2026 2.4 Privacy Policy 27 April 2026 27 July 2026 2.3 Cookie Policy 27 April 2026 23 May 2026 1.2 Acceptable Use Po"},{"t":"About Auric Artisan","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's About page — what the platform provides, its colour science, vision models, web analysis, theme generation, principles and independence.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/about.html","h":["At a glance","What the page covers, section by section","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/about/ last updated 27 July 2026 . The official page is authoritative; this is a summary to help you find your way. A platform for colour tools, colour science resources, articles and structured learning material. Web analysis across security, performance, responsive design, palette extraction and related checks. Theme generation for colour systems, interfaces and web design. CIE colour science: XYZ, Lab, LCH, Oklab, sRGB, Display P3, colour difference formulas, chromatic adaptation, gamut mapping and metamerism. More than 70 vision simulation models, based on Viénot 1999, Brettel 1997 and Machado 2009. An Ishihara style plate generator for learning and demonstration only — not a medical device. Every tool free on every tier; optional paid plan passes are one time purchases through Razorpay. Independent, and not affiliated with any government or institution. 1. About Auric Artisan — The platform is built and written by Chirag Bansal, who also writes every Learn article and the documentation. The name joins \"Auric\" gold, warmth, luminance and \"Artisan\" careful craft . The page calls the current release \"a working foundation — function"},{"t":"Acceptable Use Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Acceptable Use Policy — what you may do, what is prohibited, the web-analysis rules, and how the policy is enforced.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/acceptable-use-policy.html","h":["Key points","What you may do (section 2)","What is prohibited (section 3)","Web analysis and security testing (section 4)","Vision simulations and Ishihara-style tools (section 5)","Communication, collaboration and content (sections 6–7)","Enforcement (section 8)","Reporting (section 9)","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/acceptable use policy/ — version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. Use Auric Artisan for colour science, learning, theme generation and creative exploration. Use web analysis only on sites you own or are authorised to test. Do not use security analysis for intrusion, scanning abuse, bypassing controls or harm. Vision simulations and Ishihara style plates are informational, not medical diagnostics. Respect intellectual property, privacy, security and the law. Explore colour science and compare models. Read and reference the articles for learning and creative work. Build palettes, themes and design material. Create and export themes for legitimate sites, apps and brands. Review sites for performance, responsiveness, accessibility signals, palettes, security posture and interface quality. Run analysis on sites you own, manage or have permission to evaluate. Use the simulations for non certified personal, academic, creative or technical research. Anything unlawful. Using analysis or reports to attack, exploit, disrupt or access systems without authorisation. Bypassing security con"},{"t":"Accessibility statement","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Accessibility Statement — its commitment, what it aims to support, its stated limits and how to report a barrier.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/accessibility-statement.html","h":["The commitment","What it aims to support","Stated limits","Standard it reviews against","Reporting a barrier","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/ last updated 23 May 2026 . The official page is authoritative; this is a summary. For practical help using the site with assistive technology or comfort settings, see Accessibility of the site ../../../help/accessibility.md . The goal, in the statement's words: \"Everyone should be able to use Auric Artisan effectively, regardless of ability, device, or interaction method.\" Accessibility is treated as part of design and development. Because the platform has complex visual, analytical and experimental tools, the statement says full accessibility across every feature \"may not always be achievable\", and improvements are made where technically feasible. Where possible, the platform aims to support: Semantic HTML — proper heading hierarchy and landmarks; Keyboard navigation — all core functionality from the keyboard; Readable text — contrast aware design, scalable layouts and legible type; Assistive technology — compatibility with modern browsers and screen readers; ARIA attributes — added meaning for dynamic content and widgets; Focus management — visible focus indicators and a logical tab order. It encourages you to adjust"},{"t":"Author page","d":"A summary of the author page for Chirag Bansal, founder and engineer of Auric Artisan, including how the articles are written and whom to contact.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/author.html","h":["Who writes Auric Artisan","What the work covers","How the articles are written","Contact","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/author/chirag bansal/. Chirag Bansal is the founder and engineer of Auric Artisan and, in the page's words, \"the author of everything published here\". He builds and maintains the platform end to end — the colour engine, the tools, the site and the writing — works in India, and publishes the browser extension and the VS Code extensions. Colour science — the engine for CIE XYZ, L\\ a\\ b\\ , LCH, Oklab, sRGB and Display P3, colour difference formulas CIE76, CIE94, CIEDE2000, CMC , chromatic adaptation, gamut mapping with selectable rendering intents, and metamerism. Colour vision — simulation models following Viénot, Brettel and Mollon 1999 , Brettel, Viénot and Mollon 1997 , and Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes 2009 . The Ishihara style generator is a teaching tool, not a medical device. Accessibility — the rule engine behind the Analyzer: WCAG 2.2 and APCA contrast, ARIA 1.2 validation, accessible name computation, screen reader transcript modelling, colour vision deficiency checks and VPAT style reporting. Tooling — the cross browser extension and the VS Code extensions. The articles and documentation are written by hand, not commission"},{"t":"FAQ page","d":"A plain-language summary of the 32 questions on Auric Artisan's FAQ page, section by section, with notes where other pages give newer detail.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/company-faq.html","h":["Quick answers (from the top of the page)","The ten sections","Answers worth knowing","Where other pages give newer or more specific detail","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/faq/ last updated 27 July 2026; 32 questions in ten sections . The official page is authoritative; this summary helps you find the answer you need. For questions about these docs themselves, see the general FAQ ../../../help/faq.md . Auric Artisan is a colour science platform: tools, simulations, web analysis and learning resources. More than 70 vision simulation models based on the Viénot, Brettel and Machado algorithms, for education and design, not clinical use. Web analysis covers WCAG contrast, security headers, performance signals and palette extraction. Theme generation exports CSS custom properties, design tokens, Tailwind configuration, SCSS and Figma compatible output. Many tools work without an account. You own the content and exports you create. Only data needed to operate is collected; personal information is never sold. Simulation outputs are software models, not certified for clinical, regulatory or safety critical use. Every tool is free on every tier; paid plans are one time purchases through Razorpay. Section What it answers 1. Platform and company What Auric Artisan is, who it is for, that it is free, that it is no"},{"t":"Contact page","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Contact page — the three inboxes, the seven topics, reply times and what happens after you send a message.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/contact.html","h":["What the page is","The three inboxes and seven topics","Reply times by topic","The form","What happens next","Deep links","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/. This summary explains how the page is organised; the step by step guide is Contact and support ../../../help/contact and support.md . A single form that routes your message to one of three inboxes, depending on the topic you pick. The page says every message \"is read and answered by a person — there is no ticket queue and no bot in front of it\", and that replies can be late at weekends or during a release. It links Check the FAQ first at the top. Inbox What it is for Topics hello@auricartisan.com \"Everything that is not a bug, an integration, or a security matter.\" Using a tool , Billing , Something else developer@auricartisan.com Bugs and the API — \"Send the request, the response, and what you expected instead.\" A bug , API or integration security@auricartisan.com Vulnerabilities and data requests, \"Handled under the disclosure process on the security page, ahead of everything else.\" Security , Privacy or data The address shown on the page is what you are told; the site decides the destination from the topic you choose. Topic Reply time shown Using a tool 2–3 days Billing 1–2 days A bug 2–4 days API or integration 2–4 days"},{"t":"Content and Intellectual Property Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of who owns what on Auric Artisan — your inputs and outputs, the limited licence you grant, the platform's own IP, open-source parts and exports.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/content-and-ip-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","In practice","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/content and intellectual property/ — version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. You own what you provide and the outputs generated from it. Auric Artisan receives only a limited licence to process your inputs and deliver results. Palettes, themes, reports, exports and visual assets you generate are generally yours to use, subject to third party rights. Account, export, portfolio and billing features do not transfer ownership of your content. 1. User content and inputs — Prompts, files, URLs, screenshots, palettes, colour values, notes, drafts and code snippets remain yours. You must have the right to submit and transform them. 2. Limited processing licence — By submitting content you grant a limited, non exclusive, royalty free licence, only as needed to process it, cache it where technically required, show results to you, and use aggregated or anonymised technical patterns to improve quality. Ownership does not transfer. 3. Generated outputs — Colour science outputs, theme tokens and CSS variables, web analysis reports, learning material you create, and simulation results are "},{"t":"Cookie Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Cookie Policy — cookie categories, the storage list, the preferences panel and how to change or withdraw consent.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/cookie-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","The storage list (section 9)","The preferences panel (section 8)","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ — Cookie Policy & Preferences , version 1.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. Limited cookies and browser storage keep the site working and remember preferences. Account cookies session and CSRF are essential when you are signed in. No cookies for cross site tracking, behavioural profiling or invasive advertising. Web analysis and theme generation use temporary processing data, not marketing cookies. Preferences such as theme and eye rest are stored per browser and device. You can manage non essential cookies on this page or in your browser. 1. Overview — \"We use limited browser storage to keep the site working, remember your settings, support interactive tools, and understand basic platform performance. We do not use cookies to follow you across the web.\" 2. Cookies and local storage — What each is; some data disappears when the session ends, some remains until it expires or you clear it. 3. Current status — Sign in uses essential first party cookies. Payment providers may set their own cookies inside their checkout. 4. How cookies are used — Three practical groups: esse"},{"t":"Data Retention and Deletion Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of how long Auric Artisan keeps different kinds of data, how deletion requests are handled, and what may be kept for legal reasons.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/data-retention-and-deletion.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","How this applies to your account","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/data retention and deletion policy/ — version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. Only data needed to operate, secure and improve the platform is kept. Account, session, billing and API data are kept only as needed. Tool inputs are processed only as needed; temporary processing data is deleted or anonymised when no longer required. Security logs and abuse prevention records may be kept for a limited period. You can request deletion of applicable personal data through the contact channels. 1. Retention principles — Minimal retention: purpose limitation, storage limitation, accountability, and practices that follow what is actually deployed. 2. Types of data kept Data How long Contact and support messages As needed to respond and keep records Tool inputs URLs, colours, images, palettes, settings Only where necessary Generated outputs reports, palettes, themes, exports, previews May be temporarily stored, cached or delivered Usage analytics aggregated or anonymised May be kept to improve the platform Security logs IP addresses, request metadata, abuse signals, errors For security, "},{"t":"Browser Extension Privacy Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of the privacy policy for the Auric Artisan browser extension — what it accesses, what it stores locally, its permissions and what it never does.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/extension-privacy-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/extension privacy/ — version 1.0, effective and last updated 27 July 2026. The official policy is authoritative. The website itself is covered by the separate Privacy Policy privacy policy.md . The extension only touches page content when you use a tool on that page. Settings, saved colours and history live in your browser's extension storage. No analytics, no telemetry, and no page data is transmitted anywhere. Nothing is sold, rented or shared — \"there is nothing to sell\". Three permissions are optional and requested only when you turn on the feature that needs them. 1. Scope — The colour, accessibility and developer toolkit for Chromium based browsers Chrome, Edge and Firefox. 2. What it accesses Page content, only when you act — the eyedropper, contrast and accessibility audits, vision filters, element inspector and palette extraction read the page at the moment you use them; nothing scans in the background. Settings and library — kept in the browser's local extension storage. Optional account sync — if you connect the extension to an Auric Artisan account in future, only what you choose to sync would be sent. No account is require"},{"t":"Legal index","d":"What is on Auric Artisan's Legal and Policies index page, with one line on each of the twelve policies.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/legal-index.html","h":["The documents"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/ — Legal & Policies : \"Every document, policy, and term governing the use of Auric Artisan — clear, current, and in one place.\" The index header shows \"All policies effective: April 27, 2026\", \"Last updated: May 23, 2026\" and \"Version: 2.2\". Several policies have been updated since then; each policy page shows its own date and version. See How to read the policies getting started.md versions these summaries were written from . Document Index description Summary Terms of Service Platform usage agreement, eligibility, user responsibilities and legal terms Terms of Service terms of service.md Privacy Policy How personal data is collected, used, stored and protected; data rights Privacy Policy privacy policy.md Cookie Policy Cookie categories, local storage and preference management Cookie Policy cookie policy.md Security Policy Security principles, encryption, authentication, infrastructure and incident response Security Policy security policy.md Acceptable Use Policy Permitted and prohibited activities, enforcement and usage guidelines Acceptable Use Policy acceptable use policy.md Subscription and Billing Plan availability, checkout sta"},{"t":"Licence Agreement","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's License Agreement — the licence to use the platform, its restrictions, your rights in outputs, open-source parts and termination.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/licence-agreement.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/licenses/ — License Agreement , version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official agreement is authoritative. Using the platform is a limited, non exclusive, non transferable licence. Outputs you create — palettes, themes, reports, exports and simulations — remain yours. Web analysis is only for sites and assets you own or are authorised to test. Ishihara style outputs do not replace medical grade plates. Account, API, export and paid features are licensed only for legitimate use. The platform's code, branding, design systems and models remain Auric Artisan's. 1. Platform licence — A limited, non exclusive, non transferable, revocable licence to access and use the platform. Ownership of the software, design, brand, models and documentation does not transfer. 2. Current access status — Features vary by rollout, region and readiness. Pricing pages alone are not a licence to bypass access controls. 3. Restrictions — You may not copy, redistribute or resell the platform; reverse engineer or extract models or source code; scrape or crawl it without permission; sublicense or rent access; remove notices or branding;"},{"t":"Pricing page","d":"How Auric Artisan's pricing page is organised and what each section says, with a pointer to the full plan-by-plan documentation.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/pricing-page.html","h":["The opening","Key points (as the page lists them)","The sections","Plan cards on other pages","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/. The pricing page and the checkout are authoritative for prices. The full, figure by figure documentation is Plans and pricing ../../account and billing/docs/plans and pricing.md ; this page explains how the pricing page is laid out. Headline: Pricing — \"Every tool is free, forever\". Four facts: free tools, all of them; renewal: none — one payment; guarantee: 7 day money back; term: 1 month or 12 months. ↓ Compare plans and Talk to us . Every tool is free on every tier — no tool is locked behind a paywall. Paid plans sell conveniences and scale: batch, API access, higher limits and a monthly token allowance. The REST API is metered in credits — 1,000,000 a month on Specialist, 10,000,000 on Industrial Pro; overage is opt in, prepaid and never invoiced after the fact. Start free with no credit card. Whole site accessibility crawls, up to 24 pages a run, unlock on Artisan; branded WCAG reports arrive with Specialist. A paid plan is a one time pass for the term you choose; it does not auto renew, and carries a 7 day money back window. An account is required before any payment. Section What it holds Choose your plan The Monthly "},{"t":"Privacy Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Privacy Policy — what data is collected, how it is used, who it is shared with, how long it is kept and your rights.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/privacy-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","How to use your rights in practice","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ — version 2.3, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 27 July 2026. The official policy is authoritative. This summary is for understanding only. Only the minimum data needed to operate and improve the platform is collected. Sign in, sessions and security features process authentication data where enabled. Payments go through Razorpay; raw card, UPI or bank details are not stored. Web analysis inputs can include URLs, page metadata, screenshots, extracted colours and scan results. Theme, eye rest and interface preferences may be stored locally in your browser. Personal data is not sold or used for behavioural advertising. 1. Scope — Covers all Auric Artisan tools, pages and features. Using the platform means agreeing to these practices. 2. Current platform status — Accounts, the dashboard, API keys and one time purchases are live; recurring subscriptions are not offered. Payment credentials go to Razorpay and never touch Auric Artisan's servers. 3. Data collected Usage data — first party analytics, only with consent: the event name, the page path never query strings , the referrer's origin, and a few coarse properties such as d"},{"t":"Refund Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Refund Policy — what is sold, the 7-day money-back window, how to ask, how refunds are paid, and why there is nothing to cancel.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/refund-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/refund/ — version 4.0, effective and last updated 16 August 2026. The official policy is authoritative. The step by step guide is Refunds ../../account and billing/docs/refunds.md . Sold through Razorpay checkout: one time plan passes and prepaid API credit packs. Token packs are defined but not on sale; advertising bookings are arranged by hand. Nothing renews automatically; a plan pass covers its term and stops. There is no subscription to cancel. Every tool is free on every tier. One time plan purchases have a 7 day money back window from the purchase date. Approved refunds go back to the original payment method within 5–7 business days. A refund ends the plan benefits, or removes the tokens or API credits the purchase granted. Tokens and API credits are separate, and each is refunded on its own terms. Unused prepaid API credits are refundable within the same 7 day window; spent credits are not. Advertising bookings are refundable in full before the campaign starts. 1. What is sold today — Plan passes one month or twelve months and prepaid API credit packs. Advertising bookings are paid through a link sent after an enquiry. All paym"},{"t":"Security page","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Security page — how requests are protected, encryption, authentication, payments, what it does not claim, and responsible disclosure.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/security-page.html","h":["The overview","Defence-in-depth architecture","Request security pipeline","Encryption and data protection","Authentication and access control","Infrastructure security","Payments","What we do not claim","Responsible disclosure","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/security/ — Security at Auric Artisan last updated 23 May 2026, version 2.1 . This is the trust page. It is separate from the legal Security Policy, summarised in Security Policy security policy.md . The official page is authoritative. The page describes a layered \"defence in depth\" design and headlines four figures: 256 bit AES encryption, a 9 step security pipeline, more than 20 security modules and a 3 tier defence model. Three tiers and a token layer work together: server side checks that run before any request is handled; abuse detection that escalates from throttling to a challenge to a block; a behavioural check that scores signals such as pointer movement, typing cadence and timing without interactive challenges; and signed tokens verified on the server. Every request passes nine steps in order, and is rejected at the first one that fails: rate limiting, CSRF protection, request validation, session integrity, token verification, bot scoring, abuse analysis, escalating countermeasures soft throttle, visual challenge, temporary block, permanent ban and security logging. TLS 1.3 in transit, with HSTS. Stored data encrypted at rest by Cl"},{"t":"Security Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's legal Security Policy — principles, data protection, web-analysis scope, your responsibilities, limits, vulnerability reporting and incidents.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/security-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Reporting a vulnerability in practice","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/security/ — Security Policy & Safe Use , version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. For the technical description of how the platform is protected, see the separate Security page security page.md . Account, session, billing, API and tool traffic are protected where those features are enabled. Web analysis must only be used on sites you own or are authorised to test. Security checks in web analysis are informational — not a certified audit or penetration test. Collection and retention of submitted URLs, reports and metadata is kept to a minimum. No system can guarantee perfect security. 1. Principles — Minimisation, least privilege, responsible tooling, and improving controls as infrastructure matures. 2. Current infrastructure status — Payments are valid only through official live checkout flows. 3. Data and transmission security — Encrypted transport; limited access to submitted inputs and reports; secure, HttpOnly session cookies and CSRF checks for signed in requests; origin checks, request size limits, security headers and rate limits on sign in routes; local storage for pr"},{"t":"Subscription and Billing Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Subscription and Billing Policy — what is on sale, why nothing renews, tax, API credits, overage, spend caps, ceilings, expiry and downgrades.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/subscription-and-billing-policy.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/subscription billing/ — version 2.4, effective and last updated 16 August 2026. The official policy is authoritative. The practical guides are in Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md . One time plan passes are sold through Razorpay checkout cards, UPI, netbanking . Token packs are defined but not on sale — tokens arrive with a plan. Recurring subscriptions are not offered: a purchase grants a fixed period, never auto renews, and leaves nothing to cancel; to stop early, ask for a refund. An account is required before any payment. No one is charged unless an official checkout clearly shows the final terms. Every tool is free on every tier; paid plans add conveniences and higher quotas. API usage is metered in credits against a published allowance — 1,000,000 on Specialist, 10,000,000 on Industrial Pro. API credits and tokens are separate balances. API overage is opt in, off by default and strictly prepaid: no API usage is ever invoiced after the fact. Industrial Pro subscriptions started before 12 August 2026 keep their unlimited API allowance. 1. Current billing status — Account registration and checkout for one time "},{"t":"Terms of Service","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Terms of Service, section by section, with the official page as the authority.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/terms-of-service.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","What this means for you","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/terms/ — version 2.4, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 12 August 2026. The official Terms are authoritative. This summary is for understanding only; it does not change or add to them. Auric Artisan provides colour tools, colour science resources, web analysis, theme generation and visual simulations, including more than 70 vision simulation models. Web analysis is for sites and assets you own or are authorised to test. Accounts are live. One time purchases go through Razorpay; recurring subscriptions are not offered. API access is metered in API credits against a published monthly allowance; overage is opt in, prepaid and never invoiced afterwards. API credits and tokens are separate balances, and neither pays for the other. Outputs are exploratory and informational — not certified professional, medical, legal, security or accessibility advice. The Ishihara style generator does not replace medical grade Ishihara plates. 1. Introduction and agreement — Using the platform means agreeing to the Terms and the policies they reference. The plain language note: use the tools responsibly, respect ownership and safety limits, and understan"},{"t":"Timeline","d":"A summary of Auric Artisan's company timeline page, from the first planning milestone in June 2025 to version 0.9.11 in August 2026.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/timeline.html","h":["The entries","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/company/timeline/ — \"How we got here\". The page says Auric Artisan \"started as a colour science engine and became a platform\", marks the turning points, and fills in everything between them. For every change in a release, the Changelog https://auricartisan.com/library/changelog/ carries the detail from version 0.9.0 onward. The page loads its entries as you read. If it cannot load them it says \"The timeline could not be loaded.\" — refresh to try again. Date Version Entry 30 June 2025 0.0.1 Auric Artisan System Planning and Knowledge Architecture 5 July 2025 0.1.0 Core Color Science Engine Initialization 18 July 2025 0.2.0 Foundational Tools Release 2 August 2025 0.3.0 Gradient and Palette Systems 18 August 2025 0.4.0 Advanced Tooling Expansion 6 September 2025 0.5.0 Specialized Color Processing Tools 10 October 2025 0.6.0 Perception and Vision Research Systems 12 November 2025 0.8.0 Rendering, HDR and Gamut Systems 31 December 2025 0.9.0 Auric Artisan Pre Release Stabilization Date Version Entry 1 January 2026 0.9.1 Q1 Development Cycle Begins 12 January 2026 0.9.2 Engine Optimization Update 5 February 2026 0.9.3 Vision Simulation Upgrade 20"},{"t":"Transparency and Ethics Policy","d":"A plain-language summary of Auric Artisan's Transparency and Ethics Policy — its philosophy, what it commits to document, accuracy limits, automation, advertising, pricing fairness and independence.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/docs/transparency-and-ethics.html","h":["Key points","Section by section","Where the commitments show up in practice","Related"],"x":" Official page: https://auricartisan.com/legal/transparency/ — Transparency & Ethics Policy , version 2.2, effective 27 April 2026, last updated 23 May 2026. The official policy is authoritative. Auric Artisan explains what its tools can and cannot do. Web analysis outputs are guidance, not certified security, accessibility or performance audits. Vision simulations and the Ishihara style generator are exploratory, not medical diagnostics. Pricing, account, checkout and paid features apply only where clearly enabled. The platform stays independent and documents limitations, changes and data practices. 1. Philosophy — \"Tools should respect intelligence\": help people understand what they are doing instead of hiding it behind vague output; avoid inflated claims; make limits visible. 2. Operational transparency — A commitment to document what data is collected and why; what the tools can and cannot do; when outputs are estimates, heuristics or models; how submitted material is processed; what is still in development; and changes to terms, pricing, access, payments or availability. 3. Accuracy and limitations — Results can depend on browser behaviour, rendering, source quality, network c"},{"t":"Company and legal: supporting pages","d":"Supporting pages for the company and legal summaries — a glossary of policy terms and a map of related documentation.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder supports the summaries in docs ../docs/README.md . The glossary explains the legal and policy words those documents use; the related page maps each policy to the product documentation where it applies in practice. Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md Legal, privacy, billing and security terms in plain language Related related.md Which product docs each policy affects, and the other help pages "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the legal, privacy, billing and security terms used in Auric Artisan's policies.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" These definitions explain terms as the policies use them. They are not legal definitions and do not change the policies. Acceptable use — The rules on what you may and may not do with the platform; set out in the Acceptable Use Policy. Anonymise — To remove the link between data and a person, so the data remains but no longer identifies anyone. Auric Artisan anonymises payment records on account erasure. APCA — The Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, a newer way to measure text contrast, used alongside WCAG ratios in the Analyzer. Authorised testing — Analysing a site, page or asset you own, manage or have explicit permission to test. The only kind of web analysis the policies allow. CCPA / CPRA — California's consumer privacy laws, named in the Privacy Policy among the laws it aims to follow where they apply. Chargeback — A payment reversed by your bank or card issuer. Consent cookie consent — Your choice, recorded in your browser, about which optional cookie categories may run. CSRF — Cross site request forgery: a trick that makes your browser send a request you did not intend. The site uses a CSRF cookie and checks to prevent it. Data minimisation — Collecting and keeping"},{"t":"Related","d":"Where each Auric Artisan policy applies in the product, with links to the practical documentation.","p":"Website › Company and legal","u":"website/company-and-legal/others/related.html","h":["Where each policy applies","Help"],"x":" Policy or page Practical documentation Terms of Service ../docs/terms of service.md Getting started ../../../getting started/README.md , Account and billing ../../account and billing/README.md Privacy Policy ../docs/privacy policy.md Privacy overview ../../../help/privacy.md , Export your data ../../account and billing/docs/export your data.md Cookie Policy ../docs/cookie policy.md Cookie consent and privacy ../../site features/cookie consent and privacy/README.md Acceptable Use Policy ../docs/acceptable use policy.md Analyzer ../../tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md — only analyse sites you may test Content and IP Policy ../docs/content and ip policy.md Library ../../library/README.md , Portfolio ../../portfolio/README.md Data Retention and Deletion Policy ../docs/data retention and deletion.md Delete your account ../../account and billing/docs/delete your account.md Extension Privacy Policy ../docs/extension privacy policy.md Browser extension ../../../browser extension/README.md Licence Agreement ../docs/licence agreement.md Getting started ../../../getting started/README.md Refund Policy ../docs/refund policy.md Refunds ../../account and billing/docs/refunds.md "},{"t":"VS Code extensions","d":"Every Auric Artisan extension for Visual Studio Code, what each one does, its Marketplace ID and minimum VS Code version, and where its documentation lives.","p":"VS Code extensions","u":"vscode-extensions/README.html","h":["Themes and file icons","Icons and emoji","Colour, accessibility and code health — Auric Artisan Studio","Workspace tools","Install in one line","Which extension do I need?","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan publishes seventeen free extensions for Visual Studio Code under the publisher auric artisan . They bring the same design system as the website into your editor: colour and accessibility linting, a theme with a live Theme Studio, icon and emoji libraries, file icon themes, a live server, a file workspace, a font hub and a formatter. None of them sends telemetry. Two of them are packs that install a set in one step: the Icon Pack installs Modern, Drawn, Playful and Emoji, and the Studio Full Pack installs Color, Accessibility and Code Health. Every member stays its own extension that you can disable on its own. New to installing extensions? Start with Install and set up install and setup/README.md . Extension Marketplace ID VS Code Documentation Auric Artisan Theme auric artisan.auric artisan theme 1.75+ auric artisan theme auric artisan theme/README.md Auric Artisan File Icons auric artisan.auric artisan file icon 1.85+ auric artisan file icons auric artisan file icons/README.md Extension Marketplace ID VS Code Documentation Auric Artisan Icon Pack auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack 1.85+ auric artisan icon pack auric artisan icon pack/README.md Auric Icons: Moder"},{"t":"Install and set up the Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","d":"How to install, update, disable, remove and configure any of the seventeen Auric Artisan extensions for Visual Studio Code.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find the extensions","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan publishes seventeen extensions for Visual Studio Code under the publisher name auric artisan . They cover colour themes, file icons, icon and emoji libraries, colour and accessibility tooling, code health, a live development server, a file workspace, a font hub and a code formatter. Every extension is free and installs on its own. Two of them are extension packs : a pack contains no features of its own and simply installs a group of other extensions in one step. This folder covers everything that is the same for all seventeen: finding and installing an extension, installing from the command line or from a VSIX file, using the packs, installing in editors built on VS Code Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium , updating, disabling and removing, where settings live, how Settings Sync treats them, switching the interface to Hindi where an extension supports it, and where to report a problem. The guides for what each extension does live in that extension's own folder. This folder only gets you to the point where the extension is installed and configured the way you want. Anyone installing an Auric Artisan extension for the first time. Teams that want to install the same set of exte"},{"t":"Install and setup guides","d":"Contents of the installation and setup guides for the Auric Artisan VS Code extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These guides apply to every Auric Artisan extension for VS Code. Start with the getting started guide if you have never installed an extension before. The reference lists all seventeen extension IDs and the minimum VS Code version each one needs. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Find an extension in the Extensions view, check it is the right one and install it install from command line.md install from command line.md Install, list and remove extensions with code install extension and related flags install from vsix.md install from vsix.md Download a VSIX file and install it with Extensions: Install from VSIX… extension packs.md extension packs.md The Icon Pack and the Studio Full Pack: what they install and how to trim them forks and other editors.md forks and other editors.md Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium and other editors based on VS Code update disable uninstall.md update disable uninstall.md Automatic updates, installing a specific version, disabling and removing settings and sync.md settings and sync.md User and workspace settings, project files, Settings Sync, workspace trust display language hindi.md display language hindi.md Switch Auric Artisan Live,"},{"t":"Install an extension from the Extensions view","d":"Find the right Auric Artisan extension in VS Code, install it, and confirm that it is working.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","Install","Check it worked","Install several at once","Next steps"],"x":" The Extensions view is the panel inside VS Code where you search the Visual Studio Marketplace and install, update and manage extensions. This is the simplest way to install any Auric Artisan extension, and it needs a network connection to the Marketplace. Check your VS Code version. Open Help › About on macOS, Code › About Visual Studio Code . Each extension states the lowest version it runs on. The lowest version across the family is 1.74; Auric Artisan Live and Auric Artisan File System need 1.95. The reference reference.md lists every extension. Open a folder if the extension works on a project. Auric Artisan Live, File System and Formatter act on the folder you have open. The icon, theme and library extensions work without one. 1. Open the Extensions view: select the Extensions icon in the Activity Bar, or press Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. In the search box, type the extension ID with the @id: prefix. For example: text @id:auric artisan.auric artisan live The @id: prefix returns exactly one extension. You can also type a name such as Auric Artisan and browse the results. 3. Remove any other filter from the search box, such as @installed or @disabled . A leftover filter hides extens"},{"t":"Use an extension in Hindi","d":"Switch Auric Artisan Live, Auric Artisan Theme and Auric Artisan Emoji to Hindi, and understand which labels follow VS Code's own display language.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/display-language-hindi.html","h":["The interface-language setting","Switch Auric Artisan Live to Hindi","Switch Auric Artisan Theme to Hindi","Switch Auric Artisan Emoji to Hindi","Command titles and view names in Hindi","Extensions without Hindi"],"x":" Three Auric Artisan extensions include Hindi in the extension itself, with no separate download and no translation service: Auric Artisan Live , Auric Artisan Theme and Auric Artisan Emoji . The other fourteen extensions use English. Two separate things decide the language you see: The extension's interface language. This controls the extension's own panels, such as the Auric Live control panel, Theme Studio or Emoji Studio. Each of the three extensions has its own switch and setting. VS Code's display language. This controls native VS Code labels: Command Palette titles, sidebar view names, the Settings editor and VS Code's own notifications. Change it with the VS Code command Configure Display Language . Each of the three extensions has a setting with the same three values. Extension Setting Values Default What it changes Auric Artisan Live auricLive.interfaceLanguage auto , en , hi auto The Auric Live control panel, quick settings, Phone QR guidance, preview toolbar and common messages Auric Artisan Theme auricTheme.interfaceLanguage auto , en , hi auto Theme Studio and the Theme sidebar Auric Artisan Emoji auricEmoji.interfaceLanguage auto , en , hi auto Emoji Studio auto foll"},{"t":"The two extension packs","d":"What the Icon Pack and the Studio Full Pack install, how to install them, and how to keep only the parts you want.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/extension-packs.html","h":["Icon Pack","Studio Full Pack","Install a pack","Keep only some members","Packs and VSIX files"],"x":" An extension pack is an extension that contains no features of its own. It lists other extensions, and installing it installs all of them. Auric Artisan publishes two. Pack Extension ID Installs Minimum VS Code Auric Artisan Icon Pack auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack Auric Icons: Modern, Auric Icons: Playful, Auric Artisan Emoji, Auric Icons: Drawn 1.85 Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack auric artisan.auric artisan Auric Color, Auric Accessibility, Auric Code Health 1.74 Note the Full Pack's ID: it is the bare auric artisan.auric artisan , not auric artisan.auric artisan studio . The Icon Pack installs the four creative libraries together: Auric Icons: Modern — auric artisan.auric artisan modern icon Auric Icons: Drawn — auric artisan.auric icons drawn Auric Icons: Playful — auric artisan.auric icons playful Auric Artisan Emoji — auric artisan.auric artisan emoji The pack adds nothing of its own. Each library keeps its own commands and settings. When more than one icon collection is installed, they merge into one Icon Studio instead of adding separate sidebars. The Full Pack installs the three focused Studio extensions: Auric Color — auric artisan.auric color Auric Accessibilit"},{"t":"Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium and other editors","d":"Install the Auric Artisan VS Code extensions in editors built on VS Code that use a different extension gallery.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/forks-and-other-editors.html","h":["Install in a fork","Keeping extensions up to date in a fork","What to expect","Support"],"x":" Several editors are built from the VS Code source code. People call them forks . Cursor, Windsurf and VSCodium are common examples. They run most VS Code extensions, but many of them search a different extension gallery, usually Open VSX, instead of the Visual Studio Marketplace. The Auric Artisan extensions are published only on the Visual Studio Marketplace. They are not on Open VSX, so a search inside one of these editors may find nothing. The extensions still work in forks that keep VS Code's extension, colour theme and icon theme interfaces; you install them from a VSIX file. 1. Find the VS Code version your editor is based on. Open the editor's About dialog. Most forks show a VS Code version there. Compare it with the extension's minimum in the reference reference.md . 2. Download the VSIX of the extension you want from the Marketplace, as described in Install from a VSIX file install from vsix.md . If you want a pack, download each member instead; see The two extension packs extension packs.md . 3. Install it in the editor: Command Palette › Extensions: Install from VSIX… , or the Extensions view's … menu › Install from VSIX… , or the editor's own command line launcher, if "},{"t":"Get support","d":"Where to send a bug or question about an Auric Artisan VS Code extension, and how to gather the details that make it quick to solve.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/get-support.html","h":["Where to ask","What to include","Logs and built-in summaries","Check before you send"],"x":" Contact Auric Artisan: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ — the support address listed on every extension's Marketplace page. Frequently asked questions: https://auricartisan.com/company/faq/ — linked from the Marketplace pages as the place for questions. Collect these before you write. Each item saves a round of questions. 1. The extension and its version. Open the Extensions view, select the extension and read the version on its page, or run code list extensions show versions in a terminal. 2. Your editor and its version. In VS Code, Help › About has a Copy button. If you use Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium or another fork, say so. 3. Your operating system , and whether you are working locally, over Remote SSH, in WSL, in a container or in a virtual workspace. 4. What you did, what you expected and what happened. A short numbered list of steps is best. Say which command, button or setting you used. 5. The file language for example TypeScript or PHP if the problem involves a file. 6. The log or built in summary described below for your extension. Before sending, remove private paths, secrets, tokens, customer data and the contents of private files. Reduce the example to the sma"},{"t":"Install from the command line","d":"Use the VS Code command-line launcher to install, list, update and remove Auric Artisan extensions, including all seventeen at once.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/install-from-command-line.html","h":["Make sure code is available","Install one extension","Install the two packs","Install all seventeen","Other useful flags","Profiles"],"x":" VS Code ships a command line launcher called code . It can install and remove extensions without opening the Extensions view, which is useful for setting up a new machine, scripting a team's setup, or installing all seventeen Auric Artisan extensions in one go. It downloads from the Visual Studio Marketplace, so it needs a network connection. Windows and Linux. The installer normally adds code to your PATH . Open a new terminal and run code version . macOS. In VS Code, open the Command Palette Cmd + Shift + P and run Shell Command: Install 'code' command in PATH , then open a new terminal. VS Code Insiders uses code insiders instead of code . If code version prints a version number, you are ready. 1. Open a terminal. 2. Run code install extension followed by the extension ID: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan formatter 3. Wait for the message that the extension was successfully installed. 4. If VS Code is already open, the extension appears under Installed in the Extensions view. Reload the window Developer: Reload Window if it does not show at once. text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack code install extension auric artisan.auric a"},{"t":"Install from a VSIX file","d":"Download an Auric Artisan extension as a VSIX package and install it in VS Code or an editor that cannot reach the Visual Studio Marketplace.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/install-from-vsix.html","h":["When to use this route","Step 1: download the VSIX","Step 2: install the file","Step 3: confirm","Things to know"],"x":" A VSIX file is the package format for VS Code extensions: a single file ending in .vsix that contains everything the extension needs. Installing from a VSIX is the route to use when your editor cannot reach the Visual Studio Marketplace, for example Cursor, Windsurf or VSCodium, or a machine with restricted network access. Your editor is based on VS Code but searches a different gallery see Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium and other editors forks and other editors.md . The Auric Artisan extensions are published only on the Visual Studio Marketplace; they are not on Open VSX. You need to install on a computer without direct Marketplace access. You want to keep a copy of a specific version. A VSIX installed this way does not update itself from the Marketplace in an editor that cannot reach it. You repeat these steps for each new version. Every published version of every Auric Artisan extension can be downloaded from the Marketplace at an address of this form: text https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/ apis/public/gallery/publishers/auric artisan/vsextensions/<extension name /<version /vspackage <extension name is the part of the ID after auric artisan. , for example auric artisan live . <"},{"t":"Settings, sync and workspace trust","d":"Where Auric Artisan extension settings live, how to share them with a team, what Settings Sync carries between machines, and what each extension does in an untrusted folder.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/settings-and-sync.html","h":["User settings and workspace settings","Project configuration files","Sharing a setup with a team","Settings Sync","Workspace trust","Remote and virtual workspaces"],"x":" Every Auric Artisan extension is configured through normal VS Code settings, and three of them also read a project file you can commit to a repository. This page explains where each kind of setting lives and how they combine. VS Code keeps settings at several levels. A value at a more specific level wins. Level Where it is stored Applies to Default Inside the extension Everyone, until changed User Your personal settings.json Every window you open, in the current profile Workspace .vscode/settings.json in the open folder, or the .code workspace file Only that folder or workspace Folder .vscode/settings.json in one folder of a multi root workspace Only that folder To edit them: 1. Open File › Preferences › Settings Ctrl + , . 2. Choose the User or Workspace tab at the top. 3. Search for the extension's settings prefix, for example auricLive , or type @ext:auric artisan.auric artisan live to show only that extension's settings. 4. To edit the JSON directly, run Preferences: Open User Settings JSON or Preferences: Open Workspace Settings JSON . Each setting declares a scope , which limits the levels where it can be set: application — user settings only. It applies to every window. Exa"},{"t":"Update, disable and uninstall","d":"Keep Auric Artisan extensions up to date, install a specific version, switch an extension off, or remove it.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/update-disable-uninstall.html","h":["Updates","Disable","Uninstall"],"x":" These controls are part of VS Code itself and work the same way for every Auric Artisan extension. VS Code checks the Marketplace for new versions and, by default, updates installed extensions automatically. See pending updates. In the Extensions view, an extension with an update available shows an Update button. The view's … menu has Check for Extension Updates . Control automatic updates. The VS Code setting extensions.autoUpdate decides whether updates install on their own. You can also switch auto update on or off for one extension: right click it in the Extensions view and choose Auto Update the exact wording depends on your VS Code version . Read what changed. The Changelog tab on an extension's page shows its release notes. Each extension's folder in these docs has a user facing release notes page. Use this to stay on a version you know, or to go back after an update. 1. In the Extensions view, right click the extension or use the gear on its page . 2. Choose Install Specific Version… . 3. Pick the version from the list. 4. Reload the window if asked. From a terminal: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan live@0.2.0 After installing an older version, turn "},{"t":"Reference: extension IDs and requirements","d":"Every Auric Artisan VS Code extension with its exact ID, minimum VS Code version, published version and Marketplace address, plus the install commands and flags.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/reference.html","h":["All seventeen extensions","What each one is","Pack membership","Addresses","Command-line flags","VS Code commands used in these guides","Settings that control installation"],"x":" Every extension is published by auric artisan on the Visual Studio Marketplace and is free. \"Minimum VS Code\" is the lowest VS Code version the published package accepts. \"Version\" is the latest published version when this page was written 24 September 2026 . Extension Extension ID Minimum VS Code Version Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack auric artisan.auric artisan 1.74 0.1.0 Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast auric artisan.auric color 1.74 0.1.0 Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter auric artisan.auric a11y 1.74 0.1.0 Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk auric artisan.auric codehealth 1.74 0.1.0 Auric Artisan Theme auric artisan.auric artisan theme 1.75 0.2.0 Auric Artisan File Icons auric artisan.auric artisan file icon 1.85 0.1.1 Auric Artisan Icon Pack auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack 1.85 0.1.0 Auric Icons: Modern auric artisan.auric artisan modern icon 1.85 0.12.1 Auric Icons: Drawn auric artisan.auric icons drawn 1.85 0.12.1 Auric Icons: Playful auric artisan.auric icons playful 1.85 0.12.1 Auric Artisan Emoji auric artisan.auric artisan emoji 1.85 0.2.0 Auric Artisan Icon Studio auric artisan.auric artisan icon studio 1.85 0.1.0 Auric Artisan Icon Hub auri"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fix common problems when finding, installing, updating, configuring or removing an Auric Artisan VS Code extension.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Finding and installing","Packs","After installing","Settings"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom, the likely cause and what to do. Cause: a filter such as @installed , @disabled or @recommended is still in the search box, or the ID is misspelt. Fix: clear the search box and type @id: followed by the exact ID from the reference reference.md . Watch the IDs that are easy to get wrong: the Full Pack is auric artisan.auric artisan , Icon Hub is auric artisan.auric artisan icon lib , File Icons is auric artisan.auric artisan file icon . Cause: the editor searches Open VSX, and the Auric Artisan extensions are only on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Fix: install from a VSIX file. See Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium and other editors forks and other editors.md . Cause: your editor is older than the extension's minimum version. Live and File System need 1.95; Font Hub, the icon libraries, File Icons, Emoji, Icon Studio, Icon Hub and the Icon Pack need 1.85; Theme needs 1.75; Color, Accessibility, Code Health, the Full Pack and Formatter need 1.74. Fix: update VS Code Help › Check for Updates on Windows and Linux, Code › Check for Updates on macOS . In a fork, update the fork. Cause: the launcher is not on your PATH , or the terminal was opened before VS Code wa"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about installing, updating and configuring the Auric Artisan VS Code extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I have to install all seventeen extensions?","Are the extensions free?","Which VS Code version do I need?","Do they work in Cursor, Windsurf or VSCodium?","How do I install the same set on every machine?","Do the extensions update themselves?","How do I go back to an earlier version?","Can I share my settings with my team?","Can I use the extensions in Hindi?","Do the extensions send data anywhere?","What happens to my files if I uninstall?","Where do I report a bug?"],"x":" No. Each extension works on its own. Two packs install a set in one step: the Icon Pack Modern, Drawn, Playful and Emoji and the Studio Full Pack Color, Accessibility and Code Health . Yes. Every Auric Artisan extension is listed as free on the Marketplace, and none needs an Auric Artisan account. Each has its own licence; read it on the extension's Marketplace page before redistributing anything. It depends on the extension, from 1.74 up to 1.95. The reference reference.md lists each one. If you keep VS Code up to date, all seventeen work. Yes, in forks that keep VS Code's extension, colour theme and icon theme interfaces. Those editors usually search Open VSX, where the Auric extensions are not published, so you install from a VSIX file. See Cursor, Windsurf, VSCodium and other editors forks and other editors.md . Turn on VS Code Settings Sync, or run the code install extension lines from Install from the command line install from command line.md on each machine. For a project, list the IDs in .vscode/extensions.json so VS Code recommends them to everyone. In VS Code, yes, unless you turn automatic updates off. In an editor that cannot reach the Marketplace, you install each new"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for installing and setting up the Auric Artisan VS Code extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the installation guides: the terms they use, the keys and commands involved, what the extensions need from your editor, what uses the network, and where to go next for each extension. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the installation and setup guides shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keys and VS Code commands for managing extensions limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Editor versions, forks, remote and virtual workspaces, and other boundaries privacy.md privacy.md Which extensions use the network and what stays on your machine related.md related.md Links to each extension's own documentation and to Auric Artisan pages "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"The VS Code keys and commands you use to install, configure and manage the Auric Artisan extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keys","Commands","Extension shortcuts at a glance"],"x":" These are VS Code's own default keys on Windows and Linux. On macOS, use Cmd in place of Ctrl . Each extension's own shortcuts are listed in that extension's folder. Keys What they do Ctrl + Shift + X Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + P Open the Command Palette Ctrl + , Open the Settings editor Command Use it to Extensions: Install from VSIX… Install from a downloaded .vsix file Extensions: Check for Extension Updates Check for new versions now Developer: Reload Window Reload after installing, updating or changing a language Configure Display Language Change VS Code's own display language Workspaces: Manage Workspace Trust Trust or restrict the open folder Preferences: Open User Settings JSON Edit user settings directly Preferences: Open Workspace Settings JSON Edit workspace settings directly Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts Find and change shortcuts, and spot conflicts These are the default shortcuts the four workspace tool extensions declare. The full lists are in each extension's folder. Extension Keys Windows and Linux Command Auric Artisan Live Ctrl + Alt + L Auric Live: Go Live Auric Artisan Live Ctrl + Alt + K Auric Live: Open Preview Beside Auric Artisan File Sy"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the installation and setup guides.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Activity Bar — the vertical strip of icons at the side of the VS Code window. Some extensions add their own icon there. Application scope — a setting that can only be set in user settings and applies to every window. Command Palette — the searchable list of every command, opened with Ctrl + Shift + P . Extension ID — the unique name of an extension, in the form publisher.name , for example auric artisan.auric artisan live . Extension pack — an extension with no features of its own that installs a list of other extensions. Extensions view — the VS Code panel for searching, installing and managing extensions, opened with Ctrl + Shift + X . Fork — an editor built from the VS Code source code, such as Cursor, Windsurf or VSCodium. Launcher — the code command or a fork's equivalent that opens VS Code and manages extensions from a terminal. Marketplace — the Visual Studio Marketplace, the gallery where the Auric Artisan extensions are published. Open VSX — a separate, open extension gallery used by many forks. The Auric Artisan extensions are not published there. Profile — a named VS Code setup with its own extensions and settings. Project file — a configuration file kept in the reposit"},{"t":"Compatibility and limits","d":"What the Auric Artisan extensions need from your editor and environment, and the boundaries to know before you install.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Editor versions","Editors other than VS Code","Where extensions run","Remote and virtual workspaces","Workspace trust","Languages","Settings Sync","Versions in these pages"],"x":" The extensions need VS Code 1.74 or newer; some need 1.85 or 1.95. The reference ../docs/reference.md gives each minimum. A newer VS Code is always fine. The minimum is a floor, not a range. The extensions are published only on the Visual Studio Marketplace. They are not on Open VSX. They work in forks that preserve VS Code's extension, colour theme and icon theme interfaces. Each fork is not separately certified. In a fork that cannot reach the Marketplace, updates and pack members must be installed by hand from VSIX files. The extensions are for desktop VS Code and compatible editors. They are not browser extensions. VS Code can run an extension on your computer the \"UI\" side or next to the files the \"workspace\" side, for example on a remote server over SSH or in a container . Font Hub, Icon Hub, Icon Studio, File Icons and Emoji can run on either side. Live, File System and Formatter run next to the workspace files. Auric Artisan Live needs a real file system and a local port. It does not support virtual workspaces. Auric Artisan File System supports virtual workspaces with limits: no revealing in the operating system's file manager, no content hashing for duplicate detection a"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"A summary of which Auric Artisan extensions use the network, what they send, and where their data is stored.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/privacy.html","h":["Installing","Once installed","Where data is kept"],"x":" Installing, updating and searching for extensions happens between VS Code and the Visual Studio Marketplace. That is VS Code's own traffic, covered by Microsoft's terms, and it is the same for every extension. The Auric Artisan VS Code page states that none of the extensions contains telemetry. Most work entirely on your machine. Three use the network as part of their job: Runs a development server on your machine. With the default host 0.0.0.0 , other devices on your local network can reach it, subject to your firewall. Proxy routes you configure forward requests to the targets you name. The phone QR code is generated locally; no address goes to a QR service. Refreshes its catalogue, fetches preview fonts and downloads self hosting files from fonts.auricartisan.com . Switch this off with auricFontLib.network.enabled . Search queries, source code, favourites and usage history are not uploaded. The CDN still receives ordinary request information, such as your IP address. Checks icons.auricartisan.com for catalogue updates, and can be switched off in its settings. Your code, searches and favourites are not sent. Everything else ships inside the extension. Opening a website link from"},{"t":"Related extensions and pages","d":"Where to find the documentation for each of the seventeen Auric Artisan extensions, and related Auric Artisan pages.","p":"VS Code extensions › Install and setup","u":"vscode-extensions/install-and-setup/others/related.html","h":["Documentation for each extension","Auric Artisan pages"],"x":" Extension Documentation Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack, Auric Color, Auric Accessibility, Auric Code Health Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md Auric Artisan Theme Auric Artisan Theme ../../auric artisan theme/README.md Auric Artisan File Icons Auric Artisan File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Auric Artisan Icon Pack Auric Artisan Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Auric Icons: Modern Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Auric Icons: Drawn Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Auric Icons: Playful Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Auric Artisan Emoji Auric Artisan Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Auric Artisan Icon Studio Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md Auric Artisan Icon Hub Auric Artisan Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Auric Artisan Live Auric Artisan Live ../../auric artisan live/README.md Auric Artisan File System Auric Artisan File System ../../auric artisan file system/README.md Auric Artisan Font Hub Auric Artisan Font Hub ../../auric artisan font hub/README.md Auric Artisan Formatter Auric Artisan Format"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Studio","d":"What Auric Artisan Studio is, which of its four extensions to install, and how to get your first result in a few minutes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Studio is a family of Visual Studio Code extensions that check and improve the colour, accessibility and code hygiene of your project while you write it. It is published as four Marketplace extensions: three focused extensions that each do one job, and a Full Pack that installs all three at once. Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast reads every colour literal in your code, shows its values and contrast in a hover, lets you edit it with a picker, flags text that is too faint to read, and generates accessible palettes and shade scales. Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter checks your markup and CSS against 70+ static rules mapped to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2, grades the whole project, and lets you inspect any element's name, role and colours on hover. Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk looks in every file, in more than 40 languages, for hardcoded secrets, security footguns, risky APIs, debug leftovers, task markers, merge markers and oversized code, and writes machine readable records for continuous integration CI . Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack installs the three extensions above in one step. Each extension works on"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Studio docs","d":"The shared guides and reference pages that apply to every Auric Artisan Studio extension.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the guides that apply to the Studio as a whole: the screens every extension shares, how installed extensions combine into one Workstation, scanning, scores, reports and the CI gate. Features that belong to one extension are documented in that extension's folder: Auric Color ../color/README.md , Auric Accessibility ../accessibility/README.md and Auric Code Health ../code health/README.md . Start with Getting started getting started.md . If you are deciding what to install, read Choose what to install choosing an install.md first. File What it covers Getting started getting started.md Install, run your first scan, and a tour of the Activity Bar views, status bar, hovers and the Studio. Choose what to install choosing an install.md The four extensions compared, install shapes, and which extension owns which feature. The Workstation workstation.md How co installed extensions elect one host, hide duplicate views and share one Studio. The Overview view overview view.md The sidebar home: workspace card, This file card, suggestions, swatches and navigation, in each layout. The Command Center command center.md The Ctrl + Alt + . list and the six deterministic suggestion r"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Install the Studio, run your first project scan, and learn where every view, hover and status-bar item lives.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","Install","Your first scan","A tour of the screens","Your first fix","Where to go next"],"x":" This guide installs Auric Artisan Studio, runs a first scan and tours every place the Studio shows information. It assumes the Full Pack, which installs Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health together. If you install only one extension, the same screens appear with only that extension's parts; the differences are listed in Choose what to install choosing an install.md . You need Visual Studio Code 1.74 or newer. Open a folder or a multi root workspace. Several features the scan cache, reports, the remediation plan and the knowledge database write to a .auric artisan folder inside your workspace, so they need a folder to be open. No account, sign in, API key or network connection is needed. Everything runs on your machine. 1. Open the Extensions view with Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for auric artisan.auric artisan the Full Pack and select Install . VS Code installs the pack and its three members: Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. 3. Alternatively, run this in a terminal: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan The extensions start automatically once VS Code has finished loading. There is nothing to configure before the first us"},{"t":"Appearance","d":"Change the Studio's accent colour and understand how the Studio follows your VS Code light, dark and high-contrast themes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/appearance.html","h":["How the Studio follows your theme","Change the accent colour","The presets","Where the accent is stored","Readability of the accent","Branding colours","Related"],"x":" The Studio's own screens the Overview, the Studio tab and the colour pickers share one visual style that follows your VS Code theme. You can change one thing about it: the accent colour used for primary buttons, selected tabs and highlights. Your VS Code theme What the Studio looks like Dark Warm near black surfaces, light text, gold primary actions Light Paper coloured surfaces, dark text, gold primary actions High contrast dark or light VS Code's own high contrast colours and borders; the Studio does not repaint them Headings and scores use the Fraunces typeface and other text uses Manrope. Both are bundled with the extensions as small Latin subsets, so nothing is downloaded. What VS Code draws itself stays native and follows your theme: hovers, the Command Center list, the status bar, the Problems panel and the Project Issues tree. The gold Apply fix button in hovers always uses Auric gold. The accent colour recolours the Studio, the pickers, buttons, tabs and highlights, in the same way as the accent setting on https://auricartisan.com. 1. Open the Studio and select Settings at the foot of the rail. 2. In the Appearance card, select one of the 13 swatches, or the + swatch to p"},{"t":"Choose what to install","d":"Compare the four Studio extensions, see what each install shape gives you, and learn which extension owns which feature when several are installed.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/choosing-an-install.html","h":["The four extensions at a glance","What each extension does when installed alone","Who owns which feature","Install commands","Changing your mind later","Related"],"x":" Auric Artisan Studio is four Marketplace extensions. Three of them contain code and do one job each; the fourth is an extension pack that installs the other three. You can install any combination. This page explains what each shape gives you. Auric Color Auric Accessibility Auric Code Health Full Pack Marketplace ID auric artisan.auric color auric artisan.auric a11y auric artisan.auric codehealth auric artisan.auric artisan Main job Colour picking, palettes, contrast WCAG linting and project audits Secrets, security and hygiene checks Installs the other three Activity Bar views Overview, Color Picker Overview, Project Issues, Color Picker when colour is installed Overview None of its own Studio spaces on its own Color, Check Contrast , Brand, Settings Home, Check Findings, Contrast, Preview , Settings Health, Settings All spaces Keyboard shortcuts Command Center, Pick / edit color Command Center, Inspect Command Center Those of its members Settings 16 under auricColor. 24 under auricA11y. 28 under auricCodeHealth. None of its own Colour hovers, swatches and pickers in more than 40 languages. Contrast diagnostics underlines, quick fixes and Fix All Contrast Issues in File in styles"},{"t":"The CI gate","d":"Run the bundled auric-artisan command-line scanner, freeze a baseline, fail pull requests only on new issues, and upload SARIF to code scanning.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/ci-gate.html","h":["Get the scanner","Usage","What it scans","Console output","Adopt it on an existing codebase","GitHub Actions","Pre-commit hook","Same engine, same findings","Related"],"x":" The Studio extensions include a command line scanner, auric artisan , that runs the same colour, accessibility and code health engine as the editor, without VS Code and without any network access. Use it to fail a pull request when it introduces new problems, and to send findings to your code scanning dashboard as SARIF. CI continuous integration is the automated build and test run on every pull request. A baseline is a saved record of the findings a project already has, so a gate can fail only on findings that are new. The scanner is the file bin/auric artisan.js inside each installed Studio extension Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health . It is not published as a separate npm package. It needs Node.js; the GitHub Actions example below uses Node 20. VS Code installs extensions in the extensions folder of your user profile's .vscode folder, in a folder named after the extension and its version, for example: text ~/.vscode/extensions/auric artisan.auric codehealth 0.1.0/bin/auric artisan.js On Windows this is %USERPROFILE%\\.vscode\\extensions\\auric artisan.auric codehealth 0.1.0\\bin\\auric artisan.js . Run it with Node: text node ~/.vscode/extensions/auric artisan.a"},{"t":"The Command Center","d":"Open the Command Center with one shortcut, understand each of its sections, and learn the six deterministic rules behind its suggestions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/command-center.html","h":["Open it","Sections","The suggestion rules","Related"],"x":" The Command Center is a searchable list of everything the installed Studio extensions can do right now: suggested next steps, actions, recent colours, the worst findings and the files the Studio has written. It is a native VS Code quick pick, so it looks and behaves like the Command Palette. Press Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . on macOS . The shortcut works anywhere in VS Code. Or run Auric Artisan: Workstation: Command Center from the Command Palette Ctrl + Shift + P . The list is titled Auric Artisan — Command Center . Type to filter; the filter matches titles and their descriptions. Press Enter to run the highlighted item, or Escape to close. When several Studio extensions are installed, the shortcut opens the host's Command Center, which covers every installed capability. See The Workstation workstation.md . Sections appear in this order, and only when they have something in them. The same deterministic suggestions the Overview shows, up to three. Each shows its title and, as its description, the reason it fired. See The suggestion rules the suggestion rules . Only actions for installed capabilities are listed. Action Description shown Needs Scan project WCAG + contrast + CVD us"},{"t":"The Contrast Studio","d":"Tune one text and background pair, choose a passing colour that keeps the hue, see where its token is used, and write the fix back to your code.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/contrast-studio.html","h":["Linked and unlinked pairs","The header","The pair","Passing colours that keep the hue","Where the token is used","Apply the fix","Safety checks on write-back","Related"],"x":" The Contrast Studio is the Studio's Check › Contrast tool. It shows one text colour on one background, grades the pair against WCAG, lists the nearest passing colours that keep the same hue, and, when the pair came from your code, writes the fix back to the file or to the design token the colour comes from. It is available with Auric Accessibility or Auric Color. Contrast ratio is WCAG 2.x's measure of how far apart two colours are in brightness, from 1:1 identical to 21:1 black on white . WCAG asks for at least 4.5:1 for normal text level AA , 3:1 for large text and user interface parts, and 7:1 for level AAA. A pair is linked when you open it from a place in your code. The Studio remembers the file and position, shows where the pair lives, and can write a fix back. A pair is unlinked when you type colours in yourself or open the tool from a colour selection; you can still tune it and copy the result. Ways to open a linked pair: Open in Contrast Studio in a contrast hover. The quick fix Open in Auric Artisan Studio or Open in the Contrast Studio for values that cannot be rewritten in one click . Open Issue in Contrast Studio , the inline action on a contrast or colour vision row "},{"t":"Exports and health records","d":"Generate the project health report, write health.json, SARIF and trend history, and export Markdown summaries from the Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/exports-and-records.html","h":["The project health report","The health record","Studio Markdown exports","Related"],"x":" The Studio can turn a scan into files you can read, print, share or feed to other tools. All of them are generated on your machine and written to your workspace; nothing is uploaded. Output Made by Format Written to Project health report Generate Project Health Report Color, A11y & Code Health Markdown, JSON, HTML .auric artisan/project health. Health record Write Health Record health.json + SARIF , or automatically after each scan JSON .auric artisan/health.json SARIF export Same as the health record SARIF 2.1.0 JSON .auric artisan/health.sarif Trend history Same as the health record JSON .auric artisan/health history.json Accessibility summary Studio › Home › Report without Auric Code Health Markdown Where you choose WCAG summary Studio › Check › Findings › Export WCAG Markdown Where you choose Remediation plan Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan Markdown, JSON .auric artisan/ai remediation plan. Palette, shade and brand token exports Studio › Color and Brand tools CSS, JSON, Tailwind config Where you choose The two commands that make the project health report and the health record come with Auric Code Health. The health record files are also written automatically after every "},{"t":"The Icon Studio bridge","d":"Open the combined Auric icon library from any Studio extension, and understand which icon extension it opens.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/icon-studio-bridge.html","h":["Open the Icon Studio","What you need","Which extension opens","Related"],"x":" Every Studio extension has a shortcut to the Icon Studio , the combined icon library provided by Auric Artisan's icon extensions. The Studio itself contains no icons. It finds a compatible icon extension you have installed and opens that extension's library, which brings the Modern, Drawn and Playful collections together in one place. Auric Artisan: Open Unified Icon Studio in the Command Palette. Icon Studio in the Overview's navigation. Icons at the foot of the Studio's rail. Open unified Icon Studio in the Command Center. Its description tells you how many icon collections are installed and through which extension, or says install an Auric Icons provider to enable the combined library . At least one Auric icon extension that provides the library, for example: Auric Icons Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Auric Icons Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Auric Icons Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md See also the Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md documentation for the library itself. If none is installed, the command shows No compatible Auric Icons provider is installed. Icon extensions describe themselves to the Studio in the"},{"t":"The Overview view","d":"Every card, row and button in the Overview sidebar view, in its accessibility, colour and code-health layouts.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/overview-view.html","h":["The accessibility dashboard","The colour workbench","The code-health report","Keyboard and screen readers"],"x":" The Overview is the first view in the Studio's Activity Bar container. It is a compact home that shows how the workspace is doing, what is wrong in the file you are editing, and what to do next. Its layout depends on which extension hosts it: Layout Used when the host is What it centres on Accessibility dashboard Auric Accessibility alone or in a Workstation The workspace score and one row per installed capability Colour workbench Auric Color alone, or hosting Code Health The file you are editing, swatches and colour tools Code health report Auric Code Health alone The code health score and its seven categories Every layout opens with the Auric Studio heading a link to https://auricartisan.com and an Open the Studio button at the top right, and ends with a footer that shows Ctrl Alt . Command Center ⌘ ⌥ . on macOS . The Overview follows one gold action per view : the most useful action is drawn in gold, everything else in the theme's plain button style. When the open file has contrast pairs that can be fixed automatically, Fix N in this file is gold; otherwise the workspace card's main button is. Workspace heading with your workspace's name, and how long ago it was scanned, for ex"},{"t":"The remediation plan","d":"Generate the agent-ready remediation plan, understand every part of it, and use it with a coding agent you already have.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/remediation-plan.html","h":["Generate the plan","What the Markdown plan contains","The prompt for your agent","The JSON plan","Related"],"x":" Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan turns your last scan into a structured backlog of fixes: exact contrast repairs with computed colours, WCAG tasks, security and secret tasks, repeated patterns worth fixing once, a draft design token system, a validation checklist and a prompt you can hand to a coding agent. It is 100% deterministic and local . The plan is computed from your scan by fixed rules. No AI model is called, nothing is sent over the network, and the same scan always produces the same plan. The only part intended for AI is the prompt text in the plan, a fixed template written for an external coding agent that you choose to use for example Claude Code, Copilot or Cursor . The command is provided by Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. 1. Open a workspace folder. 2. Start the command in any of these ways: Auric Artisan: Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan in the Command Palette; Fix plan in the Overview's navigation; Fix plan for an agent in the Studio's Home, Findings or Health space; the … menu of the Project Issues view; Generate AI remediation plan in the Command Center; Draft tokens on the suggestion N color values repeat 4+ times . 3. The Studio uses a fre"},{"t":"Rulebook and knowledge database","d":"Search the local rulebook and knowledge database, build knowledge.json and rulebook.md for your workspace, and add validated team guidance.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/rulebook-and-knowledge.html","h":["What is in it","Search the database","Build the workspace knowledge database","Add team guidance with knowledge-overrides.json","Related"],"x":" Every Studio extension ships a local, versioned knowledge database : a searchable collection of the rules the Studio checks, the standards they come from, manual test procedures, policies, articles, glossary terms and rulebooks. It works offline and is filtered to the capabilities you installed. Kind What it is Accessibility Color Code Health Automated rule One entry per rule the engine runs, with severity, confidence and remediation 72 WCAG rules none 68 signatures Requirement Every WCAG 2.2 success criterion 86 none none Manual check A step by step manual test procedure 8 none none Rule category The seven code health categories none none 7 Policy A governance policy 3 brand 3 brand 4 code health Article A short practical guide 3 accessibility, 1 brand 1 brand 2 code health Rulebook A structured rulebook accessibility and brand brand code health Glossary Term definitions yes yes yes Official source Links to the standards the entries cite 14 shared sources same same The counts are for version 0.1.0. With all three extensions installed, the database holds 283 entries. Accessibility engineering rulebook Accessible brand governance rulebook Code health balanced baseline Confirm text "},{"t":"Scanning","d":"How project scans, live re-grading and background scans work, what is read, how the cache and .auricignore behave, and what the .auric-artisan folder contains.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/scanning.html","h":["Live diagnostics","Project scans","The scan cache","Live re-grade","Automatic background scans",".auricignore","The .auric-artisan folder","What static scanning can and cannot see"],"x":" The Studio checks your code in three ways. Knowing which is which explains when numbers change and when files are written. Kind What it covers When it runs Writes files? Live diagnostics The files open in editors As you type, about 300 ms after you stop No Live re grade The whole project score, from files held in memory As you type, after scan.liveDelayMs 700 ms by default No Project scan Every matching file in the workspace When you ask, or automatically if you turn on auto scan Yes: the scan cache, and health records if enabled Underlines, hovers and Problems entries for open files update as you type. They are always on and do not depend on any scan setting. What is checked depends on the installed extensions and their switches: contrast.enabled , a11y.enabled , codeHealth.enabled and codeHealth.diagnostics . Files larger than 1 MB are not analysed in the editor. A project scan reads the workspace, grades it and saves the result. How Uses a fresh cache? Scan project on the Overview, or Auric Artisan: Scan Project for Accessibility Use Cache Yes Rescan on the Overview or Studio, Force rescan in Studio Settings, or Auric Artisan: Force Rescan Project and Refresh Cache No, always r"},{"t":"Scores and grades","d":"How the overall, contrast, accessibility and code-health scores and their letter grades are calculated, with a worked example.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/scores-and-grades.html","h":["The letter grade","The overall score","The contrast sub-score","The accessibility (WCAG) sub-score","The code-health score","A worked example","Colours used for scores","Priority in hovers","Related"],"x":" Every score in the Studio is a number from 0 to 100, where 100 means nothing was found. The formulas are fixed, so two projects with the same score are comparable on what was scanned. Scores are a way to prioritise work and track progress. They are not an accessibility certification: static checks cover only part of WCAG, and manual testing is still needed. Grade Score A+ 95 or more A 90 to 94 B 80 to 89 C 70 to 79 D 55 to 69 F below 55 The same scale is used for the overall score, the code health score and the brand audit. The overall score is the one shown in the status bar, the Overview ring and the Studio's Home. When the project has both resolvable contrast pairs and markup or CSS files, the overall score is the average of the contrast and accessibility sub scores, rounded. When only one of them applies, the overall score is that one. When neither applies, there is no score and the grade shows — . Code health is scored separately and does not change the overall score. Every contrast pair the scanner resolved earns credit, measured against its own target 3:1 for large text and 4.5:1 otherwise, or 4.5:1 and 7:1 at the AAA threshold : The pair… Credit meets AAA for its text size"},{"t":"Accessibility of the Studio","d":"Use the Studio's own screens with a keyboard, a screen reader, zoom, reduced motion and high-contrast themes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/studio-accessibility.html","h":["Keyboard","Focus","Screen readers","Colour and contrast","High contrast and forced colours","Motion and zoom","Related"],"x":" An accessibility tool should be accessible itself. The Studio's own screens the Overview, the Studio tab and the colour pickers are built to meet WCAG 2.2 level AA. This page describes how to use them without a mouse, with a screen reader, and with high contrast, zoom and reduced motion settings. If you meet a barrier, it is a bug: report it through https://auricartisan.com. Every control can be reached and operated from the keyboard. Where Keys What they do Anywhere in a Studio screen Tab , Shift + Tab Move between controls Studio rail Arrow keys, Home , End Move between spaces; the space opens as you move A space's tab row Color, Check Arrow keys, Home , End Move between tools Findings and Health tools / Jump to the search box and select its text Findings and Health tools Escape Close an open picker, menu or tooltip; if none is open, clear the search Swatches, finding rows, file rows and other tiles Enter , Space Activate, as a click would Dropdown menus Down or Up on the button, then arrow keys, Home , End ; Escape Open the menu, move through options; close and return to the button Accent swatches Settings › Appearance Arrow keys, Home , End Move and select; on the custom swatc"},{"t":"The Studio","d":"Open the Studio tab, move between its spaces, and use the Home and Settings spaces.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/studio.html","h":["Open the Studio","The rail","The space header","The Home space","The Settings space","Keyboard use","Related"],"x":" The Studio is an editor tab that holds the Studio's larger tools: the workspace score and its details, the full list of findings, the Contrast Studio, colour generators, the brand audit, code health and settings. It is laid out as a rail of spaces on the left and the selected space's content on the right. Any of these opens it: Studio in the Overview, or the arrow button at the top right of the Overview. The status bar score item. Auric Artisan: Open Color Studio , Auric Artisan: Open Accessibility Studio or Auric Artisan: Open Code Health Studio from the Command Palette. An Open Studio: … entry in the Command Center. Links in hovers and quick fixes, such as Open in Contrast Studio , Tune the pair or Open in Preview . These open the Studio on the matching tool. Generate Accessible Palette or Check Contrast of Selection , which open the Palette or Contrast tool on the selected colour. The tab title shows which Studio you have: Auric Artisan — Color Studio , Auric Artisan — Accessibility Studio , Auric Artisan — Code Health Studio , or Auric Artisan — Workstation Studio when the host covers more than one installed extension. Only one Studio tab exists at a time; opening it again bri"},{"t":"Suppression and branding","d":"Silence a false positive with auric-disable comments, or classify a deliberate brand colour with auric-brand comments, by hand or with quick fixes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/suppression-and-branding.html","h":["Suppression directives","Suppress with a quick fix or hover","Branding directives","Suppression or branding?","Related"],"x":" Two families of comment directives let you tell the Studio about decisions you have made: Suppression auric disable … removes a WCAG or code health finding from the results and the score. Use it for false positives or rules you have consciously decided not to follow in one place. Branding auric brand … re classifies a colour finding as intentional brand identity. The finding stays visible in its own Branding group but leaves the score. Use it for deliberate brand colours, such as a logo lock up or a decorative accent. A directive is a special comment the Studio reads, written in the comment syntax of the file's language. Directive Silences auric disable line Findings on the same line auric disable next line Findings on the following line auric disable file Findings anywhere in the file Each directive can be followed by a scope : one or more tokens separated by commas or spaces, optionally after a colon. Without a scope, a directive silences every WCAG and code health finding it covers. Token Example Silences A rule ID auric disable line img alt That rule only A success criterion auric disable line 1.1.1 Every rule mapped to that criterion a11y auric disable file a11y All WCAG find"},{"t":"The Workstation","d":"How co-installed Studio extensions elect one host, hide duplicate views and present one Command Center and one Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/workstation.html","h":["How the host is chosen","What the host shows","What the other extensions do","Changes apply without a reload","One shared data folder","Things to know"],"x":" A Workstation is what you get when two or three Studio extensions are installed together. Instead of three sidebars, three dashboards and three copies of every finding, the extensions agree on one host that presents a single sidebar, one Command Center and one Studio covering every installed capability. A capability here means one extension's area: colour, accessibility or code health. The host is the first installed extension in this fixed order: 1. Auric Accessibility 2. Auric Color 3. Auric Code Health Installed Host Sidebar title All three the Full Pack Auric Accessibility Auric Accessibility Accessibility and Color Auric Accessibility Auric Accessibility Accessibility and Code Health Auric Accessibility Auric Accessibility Color and Code Health Auric Color Auric Color One extension That extension Its own name Every extension works out the same answer from the list of installed extensions, so there is nothing to configure. One sidebar. The host's Activity Bar container keeps its views. When Auric Color is installed and Auric Accessibility hosts, the host's sidebar also shows the docked Color Picker view. One Overview. The host's Overview shows a row for every installed capabil"},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, view, menu entry, setting, theme colour and workspace file contributed by the four Studio extensions, in one place.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/reference.html","h":["Extensions","Keybindings","Commands","Views","Menus","Settings","Theme colours","Status-bar items","Diagnostics","Workspace files","Command-line scanner"],"x":" This page lists everything the Studio extensions add to VS Code, across all four extensions. Each extension's own reference page describes its commands and settings in more detail: Auric Color reference ../color/docs/reference.md Auric Accessibility reference ../accessibility/docs/reference.md Auric Code Health reference ../code health/docs/reference.md Full Pack reference ../full pack/docs/reference.md The facts on this page are for version 0.1.0. Display name ID Settings prefix Categories Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast auric artisan.auric color auricColor. Visualization, Programming Languages, Other Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter auric artisan.auric a11y auricA11y. Linters, Programming Languages, Other Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk auric artisan.auric codehealth auricCodeHealth. Linters, Other Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack auric artisan.auric artisan none Extension Packs, Linters, Visualization, Other All need VS Code 1.74 or newer. The three code extensions start when VS Code finishes loading. Keys Windows, Linux Keys macOS Command Extensions Active when Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center All three The extension is not supp"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for problems that affect the Studio as a whole, from missing views to scans that skip files.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Views and screens","Scores and scans","Files and folders","Settings","Suggestions and the Contrast Studio","Still stuck?"],"x":" This page covers problems shared by all Studio extensions. Problems specific to one extension are in its own troubleshooting page: Auric Color ../color/docs/troubleshooting.md , Auric Accessibility ../accessibility/docs/troubleshooting.md , Auric Code Health ../code health/docs/troubleshooting.md and the Full Pack ../full pack/docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: This is intended. Installed together, the extensions form one Workstation. The host Auric Accessibility, else Auric Color, else Auric Code Health keeps its views; the others hide theirs. What to do: Use the host's sidebar. Its Overview, Command Center and Studio include every installed extension. See The Workstation workstation.md . Why: It is collapsed by default, and in a Workstation hosted by Auric Accessibility it appears only when Auric Color is installed. What to do: Expand Color Picker at the bottom of the sidebar, or run Auric Artisan: Pick / edit color . Why: Each installed extension contributes its own copy of shared commands such as Workstation: Command Center and Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database . What to do: Either works. For the Command Center, use Ctrl + Alt + . , which always opens the host's version covering "},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Studio as a whole.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" Yes. There is no account, API key or paid tier; every feature is included. The extensions are licensed under the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence 2.0: free to use for any purpose, personal or commercial, but not to redistribute, republish or resell. No. All analysis runs on your machine, the extensions make no network requests and collect no telemetry. The only links that leave VS Code are ones you choose to open, such as auricartisan.com or a W3C documentation page. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . No. Each works on its own. Install the Full Pack if you want colour, accessibility and code health together; otherwise pick the one you need. See Choose what to install choosing an install.md . The extensions combine into one Workstation, so you get one Overview, one Command Center and one Studio instead of three copies. See The Workstation workstation.md . No. It is generated by fixed rules from your scan, on your machine, with no model call. It contains a prompt you can give to a coding agent of your own, if you want to. See The remediation plan remediation plan.md . No. They come from six fixed rules, each checking one fact from your scan or open file. See The suggestion rules comma"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter","d":"What Auric Accessibility does, who it is for, how to install it, and a quick start from first scan to first fix.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Accessibility finds accessibility problems in your markup and CSS while you write it. It checks HTML, JSX and TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, common template languages and every CSS dialect against 70+ static rules mapped to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines WCAG 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2: missing alternative text, unlabelled fields, empty buttons and links, invalid ARIA, blocked zoom, invisible focus, keyboard traps, small targets, accessible authentication and more. ARIA checks use the WAI ARIA 1.2 role matrix and the HTML autofill grammar, so role and attribute errors are judged against the specification rather than a word list. WCAG is the W3C's standard for accessible web content. Each requirement is a success criterion with a level: A, AA or AAA. ARIA attributes such as role and aria label describe elements to assistive technology such as screen readers. Beyond the editor, Auric Accessibility scans the whole project, grades it from 0 to 100, lists every finding in a searchable tree, and shows a before and after preview of contrast fixes. Inspect shows any element's accessible name, role, colours and contrast when you hover it. A local knowledge database adds all 86 WC"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility docs","d":"The guides and reference pages for Auric Accessibility.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages cover Auric Accessibility's own features. Start with Getting started getting started.md . Features shared with the other Studio extensions the Overview, the Command Center, the Studio, the Contrast Studio, scanning, scores, suppression, exports and the CI gate are in the Studio docs ../../docs/README.md . File What it covers Getting started getting started.md Install, first diagnostics, first scan and a tour. Editor linting editor linting.md Supported languages, diagnostics, issue hovers, Apply fix and quick fixes. Inspect inspect.md The Inspect card for elements and CSS rules. Project scans project scans.md Scanning the project, the score, the status bar and what a scan covers. The Project Issues view project issues view.md The tree of findings: grouping, search, row actions and tooltips. The Check space: Findings and Preview check space.md The Studio's full findings list and the before and after preview. Rules rules.md Every rule, grouped by WCAG success criterion, with severity and what it catches. Audit profiles and contrast audit profiles and contrast.md WCAG 2.0, 2.1, 2.2 and 3.0 draft profiles; WCAG 2.x ratios and APCA. Manual evidence manual evidence.md The eig"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Accessibility","d":"Install Auric Accessibility, read your first WCAG finding, inspect an element, scan the project and find everything it adds to VS Code.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","Your first finding","Inspect an element","Scan the project","Where Auric Accessibility appears","With the other Studio extensions","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for auric artisan.auric a11y and select Install . Or run code install extension auric artisan.auric a11y . It starts when VS Code finishes loading. You need VS Code 1.74 or newer. Nothing needs configuring: the default audit profile is WCAG 2.2 and the default contrast target is 4.5:1. 1. Open an HTML file, or a JSX, TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro or PHP component. 2. Problems are underlined with a violet wavy line and listed in the Problems panel Ctrl + Shift + M with the source auric artisan . For example, an <img without alt shows: text Image has no alt attribute. — WCAG 1.1.1 Non text Content Level A, WCAG 2.0 . Add alt=\"description\" or alt=\"\" for purely decorative images . 3. Hover the underline. The card shows the criterion, a severity pill such as CRITICAL , the level and WCAG version, a priority such as Priority 94/100 · fix now , the file and line, the problem, the fix, and a before and after when a safe rewrite exists. 4. Select Apply fix to apply the rewrite, or press Ctrl + . for Ignore this WCAG 1.1.1 finding here and Ignore all accessibility findings in this file . See Editor linting editor linting.md . 1. Put the cur"},{"t":"Audit profiles and contrast standards","d":"Choose which WCAG version the audit targets, and choose between WCAG 2.x contrast ratios and APCA.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/audit-profiles-and-contrast.html","h":["Audit profiles","Contrast standards","Related"],"x":" WCAG has grown in versions: 2.1 and 2.2 each added success criteria to 2.0. An audit profile tells Auric Accessibility which version you are targeting, so it only reports criteria that apply. Profile Studio label Criteria checked 2.0 WCAG 2.0 Only criteria introduced in WCAG 2.0 2.1 WCAG 2.1 2.0 plus 2.1 criteria, such as reflow, text spacing, label in name and character key shortcuts 2.2 default WCAG 2.2 default Everything from 2.0 to 2.2, such as target size and accessible authentication 3.0 draft WCAG 3.0 draft +APCA All 2.x rules, plus APCA contrast on top of the WCAG 2.x ratio checks Criteria that depend on the profile: Introduced in Criteria with rules WCAG 2.1 1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose, 1.4.10 Reflow, 1.4.12 Text Spacing, 2.1.4 Character Key Shortcuts, 2.3.3 Animation from Interactions, 2.5.3 Label in Name WCAG 2.2 2.5.8 Target Size Minimum , 3.3.8 Accessible Authentication Minimum All other rules belong to WCAG 2.0 criteria and run in every profile. Studio › Settings › Accessibility audit › Audit profile , then Save settings ; or set auricA11y.a11y.profile in your settings. Editor diagnostics update immediately. Rescan the project afterwards: a cache made under another "},{"t":"The Check space: Findings and Preview","d":"Filter every finding in the Studio's Findings tool, and preview failing contrast next to its accessible repair in the Preview tool.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/check-space.html","h":["Findings","Preview","Related"],"x":" The Studio's Check space holds three tools. Findings and Preview come with Auric Accessibility; Contrast is the Contrast Studio ../../docs/contrast studio.md . Switch between them with the tab row under the space header. Findings lists every WCAG finding, failing contrast pair and colour vision risk from the last scan. Its tab shows the total count. Before a scan it says No scan yet and offers Scan project . Button What it does Export WCAG Saves wcag report.md , a Markdown summary by criterion with every finding. See Exports and health records ../../docs/exports and records.md studio markdown exports . Fix plan for an agent gold Generates the remediation plan ../../docs/remediation plan.md A section titled WCAG accessibility with the number of issues and files. It shows: badges for the accessibility sub score a11y 97 , counts by level A 3 · AA 1 · AAA 0 and counts by WCAG version; a badge for every success criterion found, such as 1.1.1 ×4 ; select one to show only that criterion, and again to clear it; impact filters: All , Critical , Serious , Moderate and Minor , each with its count; a search box, Filter by text, file, SC… , that matches the message, criterion title and number,"},{"t":"Editor linting","d":"Where Auric Accessibility checks your code as you type, how to read its diagnostics and hovers, and which fixes it can apply for you.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/editor-linting.html","h":["Supported languages","Diagnostics","The issue hover","Apply fix","Quick fixes","The status bar","Settings that affect linting","Related"],"x":" Auric Accessibility checks every open file it supports about 300 ms after you stop typing, and shows problems as underlines, hovers and entries in the Problems panel. No scan is needed for this. Rules VS Code languages Markup rules HTML, JavaScript React JSX , TypeScript React TSX , Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, Handlebars Markup rules, template dialects Twig, Liquid, Jinja, ERB, Razor, Blade, EJS, Nunjucks, Mustache, Edge when VS Code recognises the file type CSS rules CSS, SCSS, Sass, Less, PostCSS, Stylus Contrast checks CSS dialects, HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, Handlebars, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX, TSX, Markdown Plain JavaScript and TypeScript files .js , .ts get contrast checks for CSS in JS but not the markup rules; JSX and TSX files get both. Files larger than 1 MB are not checked. The markup rules understand framework syntax: JSX attribute names such as htmlFor and tabIndex , bound values such as :attr , attr.x and attr={…} , and template output such as {{ }} , <%= % and @expr . Values supplied at runtime are treated as unknown rather than wrong. Components such as <Button are not judged as the native <button . See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accura"},{"t":"Inspect","d":"Use Inspect to see any element's or CSS rule's accessible name, role, colours, contrast, colour-vision impact and WCAG issues, with a before-and-after preview.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/inspect.html","h":["Open the Inspect card","What it inspects","The card","Settings","Limits","Related"],"x":" Inspect shows, in a hover card, everything the file tells Auric Accessibility about one element or CSS rule: its accessible name and role, the colours that apply, the contrast verdict with APCA and a colour vision check, a rendered before and after preview, and the WCAG issues found there. An element's accessible name is what a screen reader announces for it, such as a button's text or an image's alt text. Its role is what kind of thing it is, such as a button, link or heading. Hover an element or a CSS rule when you are not over a colour value or an Auric finding . Keyboard: put the cursor inside the element or rule and press Ctrl + Alt + A Cmd + Alt + A on macOS , or run Auric Artisan: Inspect Accessibility of Element . It is also on the editor's right click menu. Inspect works in HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, Handlebars, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX, TSX and every CSS dialect CSS, SCSS, Sass, Less, PostCSS, Stylus . If the command cannot inspect, it says why: Message Meaning open a file and place the cursor on an element or CSS rule to inspect. No editor is active. Inspect works in HTML, JSX/TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, JS/TS, and every CSS dialect. The file's langua"},{"t":"Manual evidence","d":"The eight manual test procedures in Auric Accessibility's knowledge database, what each asks you to do, and how to record evidence for what automation cannot decide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/manual-evidence.html","h":["Open a manual check","The eight procedures","Record your evidence","Related"],"x":" Static checks can find a missing alt attribute, but not whether the alt text is accurate; they can find a click handler without a key handler, but not whether a whole task works from the keyboard. Auric Accessibility's knowledge database includes eight manual checks : step by step procedures for the parts of WCAG a person has to test. Each one says what to do, what counts as a pass or a fail, and what evidence to record. 1. Run Auric Artisan: Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database or Rulebook on the Overview or the Studio rail . 2. Manual checks are listed near the top, after the rulebooks, marked Manual check . Type part of a title, or a criterion such as 2.4.3 , to find one. 3. Select it. It opens as a Markdown document with its Procedure , Pass , Fail , Evidence to record and Official sources . The Accessibility engineering rulebook brings the rules and procedures together. Build Workspace Knowledge Database writes all of them to .auric artisan/rulebook.md and knowledge.json for your team. See Rulebook and knowledge database ../../docs/rulebook and knowledge.md . WCAG 2.1.1 and 2.1.2. Static analysis can find suspicious handlers, but only interaction testing proves complete keyboar"},{"t":"The Project Issues view","d":"Browse, group, search and act on every finding from the last scan in the Project Issues tree view.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/project-issues-view.html","h":["Before a scan","The title bar","The summary row","Group the tree","Rows","Search","Related"],"x":" Project Issues is a tree view in the Auric Accessibility sidebar. It lists every finding from the last scan or the live re grade , so you can work through a project without opening files one by one. The view shows two rows: Run a project scan WCAG, contrast, CVD and Open Auric Artisan Studio . Select either. Button Command Search Search Accessibility Issues : filter the tree Tree Group Accessibility Issues Type / File / Severity Play Scan Project for Accessibility Use Cache Studio Open Accessibility Studio Collapse All Collapses every group … menu Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan The Activity Bar icon shows a badge with the total number of issues WCAG, contrast, colour vision risk and code health , and the view's description reads, for example, WCAG 2.2 · score 82 . The first row reads Project accessibility: 82/100 B with the number of files scanned and a small score ring. Select it to open the Studio's Home. Hover it for a table of the score, audit profile, files scanned, WCAG issues, contrast failures, colour vision risks, branding when any , counts by level A, AA, AAA and by WCAG version, and links to Open full scan report , Group by… and Search issues . Run Group Accessib"},{"t":"Project scans","d":"Scan the whole project with Auric Accessibility, read the result, and keep the score up to date.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/project-scans.html","h":["Run a scan","Read the result","What the scan grades","Keep it current","After a scan"],"x":" A project scan reads every supported file in the workspace, grades it and saves the result, so you can see the whole project's state rather than just the open file. How What happens Scan project on the Overview Scans, reusing a fresh cache. After the first scan the button reads Rescan and forces a fresh read. Auric Artisan: Scan Project for Accessibility Use Cache Scans, reusing a fresh cache. Also the play button in the Project Issues title bar, and Scan project in the Command Center. Auric Artisan: Force Rescan Project and Refresh Cache Reads every file again and rewrites the cache. Also Rescan project in the Command Center, and Rescan in the Studio. Auric Artisan: Clear Workspace Scan Cache Deletes the cache; the score resets until the next scan. The message reads Auric Artisan: cleared .auric artisan scan cache. A notification, Auric Artisan: scanning project... , shows progress and can be cancelled. When the scan finishes, a message reports it: text Accessibility 82/100 B — 12 contrast + 30 WCAG issue s across 214 files scanned . cached instead of scanned means the fresh cache was reused. The buttons are Open Studio opens Home , Show Issues focuses the Project Issues view and"},{"t":"Rules","d":"Every WCAG rule Auric Accessibility checks, grouped by success criterion, with its impact, what it catches and how to fix it.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/rules.html","h":["How to read this page","Contrast criteria","Perceivable","Operable","Understandable","Robust","Rules that offer Apply fix","What the rules cannot judge","Related"],"x":" Auric Accessibility runs 70+ static rules 72 in the current package mapped to 29 WCAG success criteria, on top of the contrast checks. This page lists every rule by success criterion, in the order of WCAG's four principles: perceivable, operable, understandable and robust. Rule ID is what the editor, the Project Issues view, health.json and SARIF show, and what you can put in a suppression comment, for example auric disable next line img alt . Impact is how much the problem affects users: critical , serious , moderate or minor . It sets the Problems severity critical and serious are warnings, moderate is information, minor is a hint and the weight in the score. hint marks a best practice rule: a pattern worth fixing that does not by itself fail the criterion. Best practice findings are shown as hints Best practice related to WCAG … , have low confidence, and weigh half in the score. Checks says whether the rule reads markup HTML, JSX, TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML and template dialects or CSS every CSS dialect . Confidence and automation are given where a rule reports them. Other rules are high confidence and fully automated. Assisted means a person should confirm the finding."},{"t":"Auric Accessibility reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, menu entry and theme colour Auric Accessibility contributes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/reference.html","h":["Keybindings","Commands","Views","Menus","Settings","Theme colours","Studio spaces","Diagnostics codes","Files it writes","Related"],"x":" Facts for Auric Accessibility 0.1.0 auric artisan.auric a11y . It needs VS Code 1.74 or newer and starts when VS Code finishes loading. Categories: Linters, Programming Languages, Other. Keys Windows, Linux Keys macOS Command Active when Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Auric Accessibility is not suppressed it is always the host when installed Ctrl + Alt + A Cmd + Alt + A Inspect Accessibility of Element The editor has focus All titles appear in the Command Palette after Auric Artisan: , except the two marked row action. Title Command ID What it does Open Accessibility Studio auricA11y.openStudio Opens the Studio on Home Workstation: Command Center auricA11y.commandCenter Opens the Command Center list Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database auricA11y.openKnowledgeBase Searches rules, WCAG criteria, manual checks, policies and articles Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown auricA11y.writeKnowledgeDatabase Writes knowledge.json , rulebook.md and an overrides template Open Unified Icon Studio auricA11y.openIconStudio Opens the combined Auric icon library Scan Project for Accessibility Use Cache auricA11y.scanProject Scans the project, reusing a fresh c"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for Auric Accessibility's diagnostics, Inspect, scans and Project Issues view.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Diagnostics","Inspect","Scans and the Project Issues view","Related"],"x":" For problems shared by all Studio extensions scans, the data folder, settings , see the Studio troubleshooting page ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: One of these applies: the file's language is not one the rules check; plain .js and .ts files get contrast checks only, not markup rules; VS Code does not recognise the file type for example Svelte or Astro without their language extension , so the language is plain text; auricA11y.a11y.enabled is off; the file is larger than 1 MB; a suppression directive such as auric disable file covers it. What to do: Check the language in the status bar's language picker, install the language's extension if needed, and check the setting and any auric disable comments. See Editor linting editor linting.md supported languages . Why: The profile excludes its criterion for example target size needs the 2.2 profile , the value is supplied at runtime and is treated as unknown, the tag is a component rather than a native element, or the markup is generated by JavaScript. What to do: Check your profile in Audit profiles and contrast audit profiles and contrast.md , and see What the rules cannot judge rules.md what the rules cannot judge . Why: Static "},{"t":"Auric Accessibility FAQ","d":"Short answers about Auric Accessibility.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" 70+: the current package runs 72 static rules across 29 WCAG success criteria, plus the contrast checks. The Marketplace description gives the figure as 70 rules across 28 criteria. See Rules rules.md . No. Static checks cover only part of WCAG, and many criteria need a person to test with a keyboard, a screen reader, zoom and real content. Use the manual checks manual evidence.md for the rest. The score is for prioritising and tracking progress, not a certification. WCAG 2.2 by default. You can choose 2.0, 2.1 or the 3.0 draft which adds APCA . See Audit profiles and contrast audit profiles and contrast.md . Yes. It reads JSX and TSX, Vue, Svelte and Astro files, understands framework attribute syntax and bound values, and does not judge components such as <Button as native elements. It cannot see markup produced by JavaScript at runtime. Plain .js and .ts files get contrast checks for CSS in JS, not the markup rules; put JSX in .jsx or .tsx files to get both. Inspect works in all four. Six rules accesskey , autofocus , heading skip , positive tabindex , tiny font , text spacing important and unreferenced duplicate IDs flag patterns worth fixing that do not by themselves fail WCA"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility: other resources","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits and accuracy, related pages, release notes and privacy for Auric Accessibility.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for Auric Accessibility. Each points to the fuller Studio page where one exists. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Accessibility terms used in these docs. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and Command Palette titles. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the rules can and cannot judge, and how they were checked. Related related.md Related extensions, tools and standards. Release notes release notes.md Auric Accessibility's history from the changelog. Privacy privacy.md What it stores and writes. Back to the Auric Accessibility overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Auric Accessibility shortcuts","d":"Auric Accessibility's keyboard shortcuts, Command Palette titles and Studio keys.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard shortcuts","Command Palette titles","In the Studio"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + A Cmd + Alt + A Inspect Accessibility of Element editor focused Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Ctrl + . Cmd + . VS Code's quick fixes, including Ignore this WCAG … finding here Ctrl + Shift + M Cmd + Shift + M VS Code's Problems panel Type Auric Artisan in the Command Palette: Auric Artisan: Open Accessibility Studio Auric Artisan: Workstation: Command Center Auric Artisan: Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database Auric Artisan: Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown Auric Artisan: Open Unified Icon Studio Auric Artisan: Scan Project for Accessibility Use Cache Auric Artisan: Force Rescan Project and Refresh Cache Auric Artisan: Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan Auric Artisan: Clear Workspace Scan Cache Auric Artisan: Search Accessibility Issues Auric Artisan: Group Accessibility Issues Type / File / Severity Auric Artisan: Clear Accessibility Issue Search Auric Artisan: Check Contrast of Selection Auric Artisan: Inspect Accessibility of Element Auric Artisan: Mark Line as Intentional Branding Toggle Open WCAG Documentation and Open Issue in Contrast Studio are row buttons in the Project Issues view, "},{"t":"Auric Accessibility glossary","d":"Accessibility terms used in the Auric Accessibility documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Accessibility tree. The structure the browser gives assistive technology: each element's role, name, state and relationships. Accessible name. What assistive technology announces for an element, from its text, aria label , aria labelledby , alt , title or a <label . ACT aligned. Structured like the W3C's Accessibility Conformance Testing rules format, without claiming ACT conformance. APCA and Lc. The contrast model proposed for the WCAG 3 draft, and its lightness contrast value. Experimental in the Studio. ARIA. Attributes such as role , aria label and aria expanded that describe elements to assistive technology. Checked against WAI ARIA 1.2. Assisted. A finding a person should confirm; it weighs less in the score. Audit profile. The WCAG version targeted: 2.0, 2.1, 2.2 or 3.0 draft. Autofill token. A value of the autocomplete attribute, such as email or current password , from the HTML autofill vocabulary. Best practice hint. A rule that flags a pattern worth fixing that does not by itself fail WCAG. Component. A capitalised, dotted or namespaced tag in JSX, Vue, Svelte or Astro, such as <Button , which is not judged as a native element. Confidence. How sure a rule is that its f"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Accessibility's rules can judge, how their accuracy was measured, and what needs a person.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it does well","Measured accuracy","What it cannot judge","What the score is","Limits"],"x":" Reads markup with one shared tag reader that understands quoted values and JSX braces, so arrow functions and template expressions never cut a tag short, and matches attribute names whole. Tells components <Input , <Form.Label , <mat form field apart from native elements, and treats a file without <html or <body as a component or partial rather than a whole page. Ignores comments, script and style contents, PHP blocks and strings that only look like markup, while keeping reported lines and columns exact. Treats values supplied at runtime {{id}} , ${id} , :attr , attr.x , attr={…} as unknown, not wrong. Checks ARIA against the WAI ARIA 1.2 role matrix, HTML AAM implicit roles and the HTML autofill grammar. During development, the rules were checked against axe core on rendered HTML. On a regression suite of 264 cases, false positives fell from 132 to 0 and false negatives from 21 to 0. Of 83 rendered cases, 80 agree with axe; the three that differ are contested or best practice cases. Anything decided at runtime: markup generated by JavaScript, class driven semantics, component state, computed styles and the full CSS cascade. Relationships across files, such as a label defined in a"},{"t":"Auric Accessibility privacy","d":"What Auric Accessibility stores and writes, and when it uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/privacy.html","h":["What it writes","When the network is used"],"x":" Auric Accessibility analyses your code on your machine. It sends no code, results or telemetry anywhere and needs no account. Where What .auric artisan/ in your workspace The scan cache, a settings copy, the health record, SARIF and history after scans, the remediation plan, and the knowledge files you build Your settings The accent colour user settings and values you save in Studio › Settings workspace settings VS Code's storage for the extension The Project Issues grouping, dismissed suggestions, collapsed Studio sections, and small colour icons for tree rows Files you choose The WCAG and accessibility Markdown exports Only when you open a link yourself: WCAG docs and Open WCAG Documentation open the W3C's Understanding pages in your browser, and Auric Artisan marks open auricartisan.com. See the Studio privacy page ../../others/privacy.md for details. "},{"t":"Auric Accessibility release notes","d":"Auric Accessibility's version history, taken from the Studio changelog.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/release-notes.html","h":["Unreleased","0.1.0 — Initial Studio release"],"x":" Auric Accessibility shares one version number and one changelog with the other Studio extensions. This page lists the entries that concern accessibility. The complete history is in the Studio release notes ../../others/release notes.md . Listed under Unreleased in the changelog, as upcoming entries for the next numbered release detector 1.2.0 : The rules were checked against axe core on rendered HTML: on a 264 case regression suite, false positives fell from 132 to 0 and false negatives from 21 to 0; 80 of 83 rendered cases agree with axe. One tag reader for every rule: a JSX = or a Vue v if=\"n 0\" no longer cuts a tag short; attributes are whole names; bound values are respected. Components such as <Input , <Button and <Form are no longer judged as native elements. Correct markup no longer fails: required owned roles on <ul role=\"list\" , radio groups and table rows; required context in component files; aria selected on option ; lang on <style lang=\"scss\" ; image alt with aria label or spreads; Razor, Material and shadcn labels; unnamed forms; duplicate IDs inside <template . Accessible names now come from labelled svg and img children, template output and v text ; aria hidden text"},{"t":"Related to Auric Accessibility","d":"Extensions, Studio pages, website tools and standards related to Auric Accessibility.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Accessibility","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/accessibility/others/related.html","h":["Other Studio extensions","Shared Studio pages","Website tools","Standards"],"x":" Auric Color ../../color/README.md : colour hovers, pickers, palettes and contrast tools. Auric Code Health ../../code health/README.md : secrets, security and hygiene checks, health records and reports. The Full Pack ../../full pack/README.md : installs all three. Scanning ../../docs/scanning.md and Scores and grades ../../docs/scores and grades.md The remediation plan ../../docs/remediation plan.md Rulebook and knowledge database ../../docs/rulebook and knowledge.md The CI gate ../../docs/ci gate.md Analyzer ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Contrast Checker ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Accessibility Checklist ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/accessibility checklist/README.md Accessibility Compliance ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/accessibility compliance/README.md Vision Simulation ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md The browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md , for rendered pages. WCAG 2.2: https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/ Understanding WCAG 2.2: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/ WAI ARIA "},{"t":"Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk","d":"What Auric Code Health does, who it is for, how to install it, and a quick start from first finding to CI record.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Code Health is a language agnostic hygiene scanner for every file in your repository. It finds hardcoded secrets and credentials in URLs, security footguns such as disabled TLS verification, weak hashing, unsafe deserialization, command and SQL injection patterns and XSS sinks, risky APIs such as eval , forgotten debug statements, task markers such as TODO and FIXME , unresolved merge conflict markers, and oversized lines and files. It works in more than 40 languages. It reads source text with argument aware analysis: it can tell a constant from a dynamic value, so eval 'use strict' is downgraded while eval userInput is reported with high confidence. Every finding has a stable signature ID, a confidence level and a fix, and any secret it finds is redacted before it reaches the editor, the Studio, reports or files. Findings appear as you type, in a Code Health Studio with filters, and in health.json and SARIF 2.1.0 records for continuous integration CI , with a bundled command line scanner for pull request gates. Auric Code Health is one of the four Auric Artisan Studio extensions. It works on its own and joins the others in one Workstation. Everything runs on your machine. D"},{"t":"Auric Code Health docs","d":"The guides and reference pages for Auric Code Health.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages cover Auric Code Health's own features. Start with Getting started getting started.md . Features shared with the other Studio extensions the Overview, the Command Center, scanning, scores, suppression, exports, the remediation plan and the CI gate are in the Studio docs ../../docs/README.md . File What it covers Getting started getting started.md Install, first finding, first report and a tour. Categories and signatures categories and signatures.md The seven categories and every signature: what it detects, in which languages, and its confidence. Secrets and redaction secrets and redaction.md Secret detection, placeholder filtering, custom patterns, confidence and redaction. The Code Health Studio code health studio.md The Health space: score, categories, filters and findings. Health records health records.md health.json , SARIF and history for CI, fingerprints and baselines. Reference reference.md All 10 commands, the keybinding, all 28 settings and the views. Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. FAQ faq.md Short answers. Back to the Auric Code Health overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Code Health","d":"Install Auric Code Health, read your first finding, grade the repository and write your first CI record.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","Your first finding","Grade the repository","Explore the findings","Write the CI records","Where Auric Code Health appears","With the other Studio extensions","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for auric artisan.auric codehealth and select Install . Or run code install extension auric artisan.auric codehealth . It starts when VS Code finishes loading. You need VS Code 1.74 or newer. All seven categories are on by default. 1. Open any source file, in any of the 40+ supported languages. 2. Findings are underlined and listed in the Problems panel with the source auric artisan and a code such as code health:debug . For example: text Leftover debug statement console. . — Remove before committing, or route through a real logger. 3. Hover the underline. The card shows the signature's title for example Console debug output , a severity pill, the category for example Debug leftovers , the confidence, a priority, the location, requirement tags such as CWE 798 or OWASP A05:2025 where they apply, the line of code, the fix, and actions: Go to code , Rule details , Ignore here and Copy reference . The footer shows the signature ID and detector version, such as ch debug console v1.2.0 . 4. Press Ctrl + . for Ignore this debug finding here inserts auric disable next line debug above or Ignore all debug findings in this file . Secr"},{"t":"Categories and signatures","d":"The seven code-health categories and every signature Auric Code Health detects, with the languages it checks and its confidence.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/categories-and-signatures.html","h":["The seven categories","How the checks read code","Possible secrets","Security risks","Risky APIs","Debug leftovers","Task markers","Merge markers","Oversized","Search the rulebook","Related"],"x":" Auric Code Health groups its checks into seven categories . Within each, a signature is one specific detector with a stable ID, such as ch secret github token . The ID stays the same when the wording of a message improves, so records, baselines and suppression comments keep working. Every finding also records the detector version 1.2.0 in the current package . Category ID Problems severity Hover severity Score weight Setting Possible secrets secret Warning Critical 14 codeHealth.secret Security risks security Warning Serious 12 codeHealth.security Merge markers conflict Error Critical 10 codeHealth.conflict Risky APIs risk Warning Serious 4 codeHealth.risk Debug leftovers debug Information Minor 2 codeHealth.debug Task markers todo Hint Minor 0.25 codeHealth.todo Oversized size Hint Minor 0.5 codeHealth.size Each setting is auricCodeHealth.codeHealth.<category and is on by default. auricCodeHealth.codeHealth.enabled turns all of them off at once. A small per language reader marks comments and strings. Task markers must be inside comments; debug, risk and security signatures ignore commented out or quoted code. Secrets are found everywhere, including comments, because a key in a co"},{"t":"The Code Health Studio","d":"Use the Studio's Health space and the Overview to see the code-health score, filter findings by category and confidence, and act on them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/code-health-studio.html","h":["Open it","Before the first scan","After a scan","The Overview","Settings space","Related"],"x":" The Studio's Health space is Auric Code Health's full view of the repository: its score and grade, the seven categories, and every finding with filters. When Auric Code Health is installed alone, the Studio opens on it; in a Workstation, it is the Health space of the host's Studio. Auric Artisan: Open Code Health Studio , or Studio on the Overview, or the status bar item. Open Studio: Code Health in the Command Center. The tab is titled Auric Artisan — Code Health Studio or Workstation Studio in a Workstation . The space header reads Repository intelligence with the summary Find secrets, security footguns, debug leftovers, risky APIs, task debt, and oversized code. , and a chip showing how long ago the workspace was scanned. A Code Health Studio card explains what will be checked and offers Scan Code Health a fresh scan and Open data folder . Button What it does health.json + SARIF Writes the health record. See Health records health records.md . Report Generates the project health report Markdown, JSON and HTML . Rescan gold Scans the workspace again and refreshes the cache. Data folder : shows .auric artisan in your file manager. Fix plan for an agent : generates the remediation "},{"t":"Health records","d":"Write health.json, SARIF 2.1.0 and a trend history for CI, understand how code-health findings are recorded and fingerprinted, and gate on new issues with a baseline.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/health-records.html","h":["The three files","When they are written","Settings","How code-health findings are recorded","Fingerprints and baselines","Git information","Related"],"x":" Auric Code Health writes the project's findings to machine readable files, so CI systems, dashboards and code scanning tools can use them. The records cover every source the Studio scans: accessibility, contrast, colour vision, branding and code health. File Format Purpose health.json JSON A versioned record of scores, a summary and every issue, each with a stable fingerprint health.sarif SARIF 2.1.0 The same issues for GitHub code scanning and other SARIF tools health history.json JSON One entry per recorded scan, for tracking scores over time They are written to .auric artisan/ in your workspace. The full formats are described in Exports and health records ../../docs/exports and records.md the health record . Auric Artisan: Write Health Record health.json + SARIF , SARIF or health.json + SARIF on the Overview, the button of the same name in the Health space, and Write health.json + SARIF in the Home space's CI gate card. The record opens when it is written, and a message offers Open SARIF and Open Data Folder . Automatically after every project scan, when health.writeOnScan is on the default . Never during live re grades while you type. Setting Default Effect auricCodeHealth.hea"},{"t":"Secrets and redaction","d":"How Auric Code Health finds hardcoded secrets, avoids placeholders, scores confidence, supports your own patterns, and makes sure a secret is never stored.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/secrets-and-redaction.html","h":["What it finds","What it deliberately ignores","Confidence","Add your own patterns","Redaction","What to do about a secret","Limits","Related"],"x":" A hardcoded secret is a credential, such as an API key, token, password or private key, written directly into source code or configuration. Anyone who can read the repository can use it. Auric Code Health looks for secrets in every supported file, including comments, and treats them as its most serious category. Provider credentials with a recognisable shape: AWS access and temporary keys, GitHub and GitLab tokens, Slack tokens and webhooks, Discord webhooks, Google API keys and OAuth client secrets, Stripe secret and restricted keys, OpenAI and Anthropic API keys, npm, SendGrid and DigitalOcean tokens. Private keys : PEM blocks such as BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY followed by key data. JSON Web Tokens . Credentials in URLs postgres://user:password@host and connection strings Password=…; , AccountKey=… . Authorization headers with a literal Bearer or Basic token. Credential assignments : a key named like a credential DB PASSWORD , apiKey , client secret given a literal value, in code, JSON, YAML, INI, .env , properties, TOML, shell and XML. Your own patterns from codeHealth.customSecretPatterns . The full list with IDs is in Categories and signatures categories and signatures.md possible"},{"t":"Auric Code Health reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting and view Auric Code Health contributes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/reference.html","h":["Keybindings","Commands","Views","Settings","Diagnostics codes","Quick fixes","Studio spaces","Files it writes","Command-line scanner","Related"],"x":" Facts for Auric Code Health 0.1.0 auric artisan.auric codehealth . It needs VS Code 1.74 or newer and starts when VS Code finishes loading. Categories: Linters, Other. Keys Windows, Linux Keys macOS Command Active when Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Auric Code Health is not suppressed by a Workstation host All titles appear in the Command Palette after Auric Artisan: . Title Command ID What it does Open Code Health Studio auricCodeHealth.openStudio Opens the Studio on Health, or the Workstation host's Studio Workstation: Command Center auricCodeHealth.commandCenter Opens the Command Center list Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database auricCodeHealth.openKnowledgeBase Searches signatures, categories, policies, articles and sources Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown auricCodeHealth.writeKnowledgeDatabase Writes knowledge.json , rulebook.md and an overrides template Open Unified Icon Studio auricCodeHealth.openIconStudio Opens the combined Auric icon library Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan auricCodeHealth.generateAiPlan Writes the local remediation plan Generate Project Health Report Color, A11y & Code Health auricCodeHealth.projectHealthRep"},{"t":"Auric Code Health troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for Auric Code Health's findings, secrets, Studio and records.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Findings in the editor","Secrets","Studio, reports and records","Related"],"x":" For problems shared by all Studio extensions scans, the data folder, settings , see the Studio troubleshooting page ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: One of these applies: codeHealth.enabled or codeHealth.diagnostics is off; the category is turned off for example codeHealth.todo ; VS Code does not recognise the file's language, or the file is larger than 1 MB; a suppression comment covers the line or file. What to do: Check the settings under auricCodeHealth.codeHealth , and look for auric disable comments. Why: In languages the Studio can lex, task markers count only inside comments, so a TODO inside a string or identifier is ignored on purpose. Lower case markers need @todo , todo: or fixme: . Why: Debug signatures are limited to the languages where they are debug hooks: console.log in web languages, breakpoint in Python, a DEBUG prefixed fmt.Print in Go, and so on. Normal output such as print or fmt.Println is never reported. Why: Its argument is a constant, so the risk is lower; the message ends constant argument — lower risk . A dynamic argument is reported with high confidence. Why: The assigned value is a constant string or passes through a sanitiser function, which is s"},{"t":"Auric Code Health FAQ","d":"Short answers about Auric Code Health.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" More than 40: JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust, Java, C , C and C++, Kotlin, Swift, Ruby, PHP, shell, SQL, YAML, TOML, JSON, Markdown, HTML, CSS and many more. Some signatures apply only where they make sense; see Categories and signatures categories and signatures.md . No. It is a fast, high signal heuristic linter for the files in your workspace. It does not scan Git history, verify credentials or trace data flow. Use dedicated tools where compliance requires them. No. Every secret is replaced by redacted secret; N characters everywhere it could appear. See Secrets and redaction secrets and redaction.md . Each finding costs points by category secrets 14, security 12, merge markers 10, risky APIs 4, debug 2, oversized 0.5, task markers 0.25 , scaled by confidence and divided by the number of files. See Scores and grades ../../docs/scores and grades.md the code health score . No. They are separate. The overall score in the status bar and Overview combines contrast and accessibility only. Yes: set auricCodeHealth.codeHealth.todo to false . Every category has its own switch. Yes: Ignore here in the hover, the Ignore this … finding here quick fix, or an auric disable next lin"},{"t":"Auric Code Health: other resources","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits and accuracy, related pages, release notes and privacy for Auric Code Health.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for Auric Code Health. Each points to the fuller Studio page where one exists. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Code health terms used in these docs. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts and Command Palette titles. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the checks can and cannot find, and how accuracy was measured. Related related.md Related extensions, pages and standards. Release notes release notes.md Auric Code Health's history from the changelog. Privacy privacy.md What it stores and writes, and how secrets are protected. Back to the Auric Code Health overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Auric Code Health shortcuts","d":"Auric Code Health's keyboard shortcuts and Command Palette titles.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard shortcuts","Command Palette titles","In the Studio's Health space"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Ctrl + . Cmd + . VS Code's quick fixes, including Ignore this … finding here Type Auric Artisan in the Command Palette: Auric Artisan: Open Code Health Studio Auric Artisan: Workstation: Command Center Auric Artisan: Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database Auric Artisan: Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown Auric Artisan: Open Unified Icon Studio Auric Artisan: Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan Auric Artisan: Generate Project Health Report Color, A11y & Code Health Auric Artisan: Write Health Record health.json + SARIF Auric Artisan: Clear Workspace Scan Cache Auric Artisan: Open Workspace Data Folder Keys What it does / Focus the findings search box Escape Close pop ups, then clear the search Enter , Space Open the selected finding's file at its line For every Studio key, see the Studio shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md . "},{"t":"Auric Code Health glossary","d":"Code-health terms used in the Auric Code Health documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Argument aware. A check that reads a call's argument or an assigned value to tell a constant lower risk from a dynamic value higher risk . Baseline. A saved health record of existing findings, so a CI gate fails only on new ones. Category. One of the seven groups of checks: possible secrets, security risks, merge markers, risky APIs, debug leftovers, task markers and oversized. Confidence. How sure a signature is that a finding is real: high, medium or low contextual for argument aware risky API signatures . Reported separately from severity. Credential assignment. A key named like a credential, such as DB PASSWORD , given a literal value. CWE 798. The Common Weakness Enumeration entry for hard coded credentials, which every secret signature maps to. Deserialization. Turning stored data back into objects. Unsafe deserialization of untrusted data can run attacker code. Detector version. The version of the checking engine that produced a finding 1.2.0 in the current package . Entropy. How unpredictable a value's characters are. Random looking values are more likely to be real secrets. Fingerprint. An 8 character ID that identifies a finding across runs. Health record. health.json : "},{"t":"Auric Code Health limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Code Health's checks can and cannot find, and how their accuracy was measured.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What it is","Measured accuracy","What it does not do","Behaviour to know"],"x":" A high signal heuristic linter that reads the text of the files in your workspace. It favours precision: it reports the common, high confidence cases and tells a constant from a dynamic value. On a labelled set of examples used in development, including a held out set, precision is 1.00 in every category no false positives , and recall is 1.00 in every category except secrets, where 96% of the planted secrets were found. It does not build a syntax tree or trace data flow between functions, so it cannot tell whether a dynamic value is actually user controlled. It does not scan Git history, so a secret removed from the current files but still in history is not found. It does not check whether a credential is live. It is not a full static application security testing tool or a dedicated secret scanner. Secrets are found everywhere, including comments; other categories ignore comments and, where it matters, strings. Signatures run only in the languages where they apply; see Categories and signatures ../docs/categories and signatures.md . A file reports at most 300 findings. Lines over 240 characters are reported, except lines that start with a URL. Files over 800 lines are reported by"},{"t":"Auric Code Health privacy","d":"What Auric Code Health stores and writes, how it protects secrets, and when it uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/privacy.html","h":["Secrets are never stored","What it writes","When the network is used"],"x":" Auric Code Health analyses your code on your machine. It sends no code, findings or telemetry anywhere and needs no account. The bundled command line scanner makes no network requests either. When it finds a secret, only a note with its length redacted secret; 40 characters is kept. The secret itself never reaches the editor hover, the Problems panel, the Studio, the scan cache, health.json , SARIF, the history, the project health report or the remediation plan. See Secrets and redaction ../docs/secrets and redaction.md . Where What .auric artisan/ in your workspace The scan cache, a settings copy, health.json , health.sarif , health history.json , the project health report, the remediation plan and the knowledge files Your settings The accent colour user settings and values you save in Studio › Settings workspace settings VS Code's storage for the extension Dismissed suggestions and collapsed Studio sections The health record includes your current Git branch and commit, read from the .git folder. Review records before sharing them outside your team: they contain file paths and messages, never secret values. Only when you open a link yourself, such as auricartisan.com or an offici"},{"t":"Auric Code Health release notes","d":"Auric Code Health's version history, taken from the Studio changelog.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/release-notes.html","h":["Unreleased","0.1.0 — Initial Studio release"],"x":" Auric Code Health shares one version number and one changelog with the other Studio extensions. This page lists the entries that concern code health. The complete history is in the Studio release notes ../../others/release notes.md . Listed under Unreleased in the changelog, as upcoming entries for the next numbered release detector 1.2.0 : Accuracy measured on a labelled set, including a held out set: precision 1.00 in every category; recall 1.00 except secrets, 0.96 up from 0.53 . Secret detection now covers JSON, PHP, typed and Go assignments, prefixed names such as MYSQL PASSWORD , unquoted .env , YAML and INI values, OpenAI sk proj keys, Google keys ending in , and Azure and ADO.NET connection strings. False positives removed: placeholders such as CHANGE ME , {{API KEY}} , $VAR and SOPS ENC … ; translation labels, autocomplete tokens and key file paths; redis.eval and model.eval ; tagged SQL templates; phone masks read as XXX markers; Markdown underlines read as merge markers. One credential is one finding. Secret bytes no longer leak through task marker messages or security evidence into SARIF or health.json . Calls whose arguments cannot be read are reported at medium confi"},{"t":"Related to Auric Code Health","d":"Extensions, Studio pages and standards related to Auric Code Health.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Code Health","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/code-health/others/related.html","h":["Other Studio extensions","Shared Studio pages","Standards and sources"],"x":" Auric Accessibility ../../accessibility/README.md : WCAG linting, project scans and the Project Issues view. Auric Color ../../color/README.md : colour tools and contrast checks. The Full Pack ../../full pack/README.md : installs all three. Exports and health records ../../docs/exports and records.md The CI gate ../../docs/ci gate.md The remediation plan ../../docs/remediation plan.md Suppression and branding ../../docs/suppression and branding.md Rulebook and knowledge database ../../docs/rulebook and knowledge.md The official sources the code health entries in the knowledge database cite, and the SARIF specification: OWASP Top 10:2025: https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/0x00 2025 Introduction/ OWASP Application Security Verification Standard: https://owasp.org/www project application security verification standard/ OWASP Cheat Sheet Series: https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/ CWE 798, Use of Hard coded Credentials: https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/798.html NIST Secure Software Development Framework: https://csrc.nist.gov/Projects/ssdf SARIF 2.1.0: https://docs.oasis open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/sarif v2.1.0.html "},{"t":"Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast","d":"What Auric Color does, who it is for, how to install it, and a quick start from hover to fix.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Color turns every colour literal in your code into something you can read, understand and fix in place. Hover a colour such as 1d4ed8 , rgb 29 78 216 or oklch 0.49 0.22 264 to see its RGB, HSL, OKLCH and Display P3 values, its nearest CSS colour name, its contrast on white and black, and how it looks to people with colour vision deficiency. The hover is also a picker: select a tile to change the colour, keeping the token's own syntax. It also watches your stylesheets, markup and components for text that is too faint to read. Failing text and background pairs are underlined as you type, with a one click fix to the nearest passing colour of the same hue, and a Contrast Studio for tuning a pair and writing the fix back to the design token it comes from. The Studio adds generators for accessible palettes, OKLCH shade scales, colour vision previews and a brand audit on real text. Auric Color is one of the four Auric Artisan Studio extensions. It works on its own, and joins the others in one Workstation when they are installed together. Everything runs on your machine. Front end developers who edit colours in CSS, Sass, CSS in JS, Tailwind configs or component files. Designers and"},{"t":"Auric Color docs","d":"The guides and reference pages for Auric Color.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages cover Auric Color's own features. Start with Getting started getting started.md . Features Auric Color shares with the other Studio extensions the Overview, the Command Center, the Studio, the Contrast Studio, suppression and branding are in the Studio docs ../../docs/README.md . File What it covers Getting started getting started.md Install, first hover and pick, and a tour of what Auric Color adds. Hover and swatches hover and swatches.md Every part of the colour hover, the swatches, and the languages and formats supported. The colour pickers color picker.md The inline hover picker, the full picker panel and the docked Color Picker view. Picker modes picker modes.md Auric picker or VS Code's native picker, and exactly which VS Code settings each changes. Contrast diagnostics contrast diagnostics.md How pairs are found, WCAG and APCA modes, hovers, quick fixes and Fix All. Palettes and shades palettes and shades.md The Palette and Shades tools and their CSS, JSON and Tailwind exports. Colour vision colour vision.md The Vision tool, colour vision risk and confusable hues. The brand audit brand audit.md The Brand tool, token exports and the brand governance rulebook. Re"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Color","d":"Install Auric Color, read and edit your first colour, fix your first contrast problem, and find every place Auric Color shows up.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","Read a colour","Change a colour","Fix a contrast problem","Where Auric Color appears","With the other Studio extensions","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for auric artisan.auric color and select Install . Or run code install extension auric artisan.auric color . Auric Color starts when VS Code finishes loading. You need VS Code 1.74 or newer. Important: In its default mode, Auric Color replaces VS Code's own colour decorators the small squares VS Code draws before colours in CSS with its own swatches and picker. To do this it sets editor.colorDecorators to false in your user settings as soon as it starts, and sets it back to false if it is turned on again while this mode is active. To keep VS Code's own picker instead, run Auric Artisan: Restore native color picker use VS Code's . See Picker modes picker modes.md . 1. Open a file that contains a colour, such as a CSS file with color: 1d4ed8; . 2. A small swatch appears before the colour value, and the value gets a faint tinted outline. 3. Hover the value. The hover shows the colour's hex value, its nearest CSS name, its RGB, HSL, OKLCH and Display P3 values, its contrast on white and on black, and how it looks with protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. See Hover and swatches hover and swatches.md for every part of the hove"},{"t":"The brand audit","d":"Audit a brand's colour roles against real headings, body text, links and buttons, fix failing roles, export accessible tokens, and use the brand governance rulebook.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/brand-audit.html","h":["Open it","The header","Brand colours","Real-text preview","Role checklist","Fix failing roles","Load from scan","The brand score","Export","Brand governance in the knowledge database","Branding in your code","Related"],"x":" The Studio's Brand space checks a set of brand colours the way a reader meets them: as headings, body copy, captions, links, buttons and borders on your backgrounds. You can do it by hand, with no project, or start from the colours your last scan found. Select Brand on the Studio rail, or Open Studio: Brand in the Command Center. Select Brand in a colour hover's Open in Studio row. That colour becomes the Primary role. Select Audit as a brand on the Studio's Home project palette , Audit as brand → in the Palette tool, or Audit a brand by hand → on Home before a scan. The header card is titled Brand accessibility audit real text · WCAG + APCA + CVD and shows: a score ring with the brand score and grade; roles pass , for example 6/8 ; text pass , for example 5/6 ; and CVD risk , the number of checks that fail under colour vision simulation; Auto fix N roles when any check fails, or ✓ All roles pass ; Load from scan and Reset . Eight roles, each with a colour field: Role Meaning Starting value Background Page background FFFFFF Surface Cards, panels, raised areas F4F6F8 Body text Primary reading text 1A1A1A Secondary text Captions, hints, metadata 5B6470 Primary Brand or action colour"},{"t":"The colour pickers","d":"Use Auric Color's three pickers (inline in the hover, the full panel beside the editor, and the docked sidebar view) to edit colours in your code.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/color-picker.html","h":["The inline hover picker","Open the picker panel","The docked Color Picker view","Picker controls","When changes are written","Pickers inside the Studio","Related"],"x":" Auric Color gives you three ways to edit a colour in your code. All three write the change straight into the file, in the colour's own format, as an edit you can undo. Picker Where Best for Inline hover picker Inside the colour hover Quick changes without leaving the code Picker panel A tab beside the editor Precise editing, contrast checks, generating sets, rewriting every match Color Picker view Docked in the sidebar Keeping a picker open while you move between colours Point at a colour or click it and use the Spectrum , Hue , Alpha , Shades , Fix , Brand and Recent rows at the top of the hover. Each tile applies its colour and the hover reopens on the new value. Type exact… takes a typed value. See Hover and swatches hover and swatches.md picker rows . Put the cursor on a colour or select one and press Ctrl + Alt + C Cmd + Alt + C on macOS , or run Auric Artisan: Pick / edit color . It is also on the editor's right click menu. Select Spectrum picker in a colour hover. Click a colour literal when auricColor.colorPicker.clickAction is fullEditor , or when the colour hover is turned off. Select Open the color picker on the Overview, or Open full in the docked view. Select a colour"},{"t":"Colour vision","d":"Preview colours and your project palette under colour-vision deficiencies, and understand colour-vision risk and confusable hues.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/colour-vision.html","h":["The simulations","The Vision tool","Colour vision elsewhere","Related"],"x":" Colour vision deficiency CVD , often called colour blindness, makes some colours hard to tell apart. Colours that look clearly different to you can look alike to someone with a CVD. Auric Color shows you how your colours look and warns when a design relies on hue alone. Type What it means Protanopia No red cones about 1% of men Protanomaly Weak red Deuteranopia No green cones about 1% of men Deuteranomaly Weak green; the most common form, about 5% Tritanopia No blue cones; rare Tritanomaly Weak blue Achromatopsia Total colour blindness Achromatomaly Partial colour blindness Simulations use the Brettel 1997 method in linear light, which keeps white white and does not brighten reds. They are previews for design decisions, not a diagnosis or a medical measurement. Open the Studio's Color › Vision , select Vision in a colour hover's Open in Studio row or on the Overview, or choose Open Studio: Vision in the Command Center. Color vision simulation: enter a colour to see it as a swatch next to all eight simulations. Hover a swatch for its simulated hex; select it to copy. Project palette under color blindness after a project scan : your 16 most used colours in four rows, for typical vis"},{"t":"Contrast diagnostics","d":"How Auric Color finds low-contrast text as you type, what its messages mean, and how to fix one pair or a whole file.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/contrast-diagnostics.html","h":["Where contrast is checked","Contrast standards","What the diagnostics say","The contrast hover","Quick fixes","Fix every pair in a file","Refresh","Settings","Related"],"x":" Auric Color checks the text and background colours in your stylesheets, markup and components as you type, and underlines text that does not meet your contrast target. When Auric Accessibility is installed too, it publishes these contrast diagnostics instead, with the same behaviour and its own auricA11y.contrast. settings. Only one extension ever publishes them, so you never see a pair twice. CSS, SCSS, Sass, Less, PostCSS, Stylus, HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, Handlebars, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX, TSX and Markdown files, up to 1 MB each. The checker pairs a text colour with its background from: CSS rules and <style blocks; inline style=\"…\" attributes; JSX style objects: style={{…}} , sx={{…}} , css={{…}} ; styled components, Emotion and Linaria tagged templates styled.x … , css … , createGlobalStyle ; Vue, Angular and Svelte style bindings :style=\"{…}\" , ngStyle =\"{…}\" , style:color . It follows CSS custom properties color: var ink over background: var surface , including fallbacks and chains, and grades dark themes separately. See Limits and accuracy ../others/limits and accuracy.md for exactly how pairs are resolved and what cannot be seen. auricColor.contrast.standar"},{"t":"Hover and swatches","d":"Every part of Auric Color's colour hover and inline swatches, which colour formats are detected, and which languages are supported.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/hover-and-swatches.html","h":["Supported languages","Detected colour formats","Swatches","The colour hover","Turn the hover off","Recent colours","Related"],"x":" Auric Color finds colour literals in your code, draws a swatch before each one, and shows a detailed hover when you point at one. The hover, swatches and pickers work in these VS Code languages. Some of them need a language extension installed so VS Code recognises the file type. Group Languages Stylesheets CSS, SCSS, Sass, Less, PostCSS, Stylus Web and markup HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, XML, Markdown JavaScript family JavaScript, TypeScript, JavaScript React JSX , TypeScript React TSX , CoffeeScript Data and config JSON, JSON with Comments, JSON5, HJSON, YAML, TOML, INI, Properties Templates Handlebars, Pug, Jade, EJS, Twig, Razor, Blade Systems and apps C, C++, C , Objective C, Objective C++, Go, Rust, Java, Kotlin, Swift, Dart, Scala, Groovy, F , Visual Basic Scripting Python, Ruby, Lua, R, Julia, Perl, Shell script, PowerShell Functional and others Haskell, Elixir, Erlang, Clojure, Solidity, GraphQL, SQL, Dockerfile, Makefile Format Examples Hex, 3, 4, 6 or 8 digits abc , abcd , 1d4ed8 , 1d4ed880 rgb and rgba rgb 29 78 216 , rgba 29, 78, 216, 0.5 hsl and hsla hsl 221 76% 48% hwb hwb 221 11% 15% lab and lch lab 35 21 71 , lch 35 74 287 oklab and oklch oklch 0.49 0.22 264 col"},{"t":"Palettes and shades","d":"Generate harmony palettes that meet a contrast target and perceptually even OKLCH shade scales, preview them, and export them as CSS, JSON or Tailwind.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/palettes-and-shades.html","h":["The Palette tool","The Shades tool","Related"],"x":" The Studio's Color space has two generators: Palette , for sets of related colours that all meet a contrast target, and Shades , for a tonal scale of one colour. Both are in Auric Color. Select a colour in the editor and run Auric Artisan: Generate Accessible Palette also on the right click menu when text is selected . The selection becomes the seed; if it is not a colour, the seed is 2563EB . Select Palette in a colour hover's Open in Studio row, or on the Overview. Open the Studio and choose Color › Palette , or Open Studio: Palette in the Command Center. Control Values What it does Seed Any colour The starting colour Background Any colour default white The surface every swatch must read on Harmony Complementary, Split complement, Analogous, Triadic, Tetradic, Square, Double split, Monochromatic How the other colours relate to the seed on the colour wheel Min contrast 3:1 · UI / large, 4.5:1 · AA body, 7:1 · AAA body The ratio every swatch must reach on the background Preview as Typical vision, Protanopia · no red, Deuteranopia · no green, Tritanopia · no blue, Achromatopsia · no color Shows the swatches as seen with that colour vision deficiency Each colour field has a swatch b"},{"t":"Picker modes","d":"Choose between the Auric picker and VS Code's native colour picker, and learn exactly which VS Code settings each mode changes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/picker-modes.html","h":["The three set-ups","What Auric mode changes in your settings","Switch mode","Click behaviour in Auric mode","Related"],"x":" VS Code has its own colour picker: in CSS and in other languages when an extension provides colours it draws small colour decorators before colour values and opens a draggable picker when you hover or click them. VS Code offers no way for an extension to replace that picker, so two pickers would stack on top of each other. Auric Color solves this with a picker mode . Set up How to get it Swatches Clicking a colour Hover Auric picker default colorPicker.mode = auric , colorPicker.nativeHoverPicker = false Auric's swatches Auric's inline picker in the hover or per colorPicker.clickAction Full Auric hover with Spectrum, Hue and Alpha rows Auric with VS Code's sliders colorPicker.mode = auric , colorPicker.nativeHoverPicker = true VS Code's decorators The hover, per colorPicker.clickAction VS Code's draggable picker above Auric's readouts no Spectrum, Hue or Alpha rows VS Code native picker colorPicker.mode = decorators VS Code's decorators VS Code's picker Auric's readouts with only Shades and Brand rows In the last two set ups Auric Color supplies the colours it detects to VS Code's picker in non CSS languages too, so VS Code's picker also works in JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, Vue,"},{"t":"Auric Color reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, menu entry and theme colour Auric Color contributes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/reference.html","h":["Keybindings","Commands","Views","Editor right-click menu","Settings","Theme colours","Studio spaces","Diagnostics","Export files","Related"],"x":" Facts for Auric Color 0.1.0 auric artisan.auric color . It needs VS Code 1.74 or newer and starts when VS Code finishes loading. Categories: Visualization, Programming Languages, Other. Keys Windows, Linux Keys macOS Command Active when Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Auric Color is not suppressed by a Workstation host Ctrl + Alt + C Cmd + Alt + C Pick / edit color The editor has focus All titles appear in the Command Palette after Auric Artisan: . Title Command ID What it does Open Color Studio auricColor.openStudio Opens the Studio on Color › Palette, or the Workstation host's Studio Workstation: Command Center auricColor.commandCenter Opens the Command Center list Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database auricColor.openKnowledgeBase Searches the brand rulebook, policies, articles, glossary and sources Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown auricColor.writeKnowledgeDatabase Writes knowledge.json , rulebook.md and an overrides template Open Unified Icon Studio auricColor.openIconStudio Opens the combined Auric icon library Generate Accessible Palette auricColor.generatePalette Opens the Palette tool seeded with the selected colour or 2563EB Check Co"},{"t":"Auric Color troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for Auric Color's hovers, swatches, pickers and contrast diagnostics.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Pickers and decorators","Contrast diagnostics","Studio tools"],"x":" For problems shared by all Studio extensions, see the Studio troubleshooting page ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: In its default Auric mode, Auric Color turns off editor.colorDecorators in your user settings so two pickers do not stack. What to do: If you prefer VS Code's picker, run Auric Artisan: Restore native color picker use VS Code's . See Picker modes picker modes.md . Why: While Auric mode is active, Auric Color re applies its choice whenever the setting drifts, including after Settings Sync or another extension changes it. What to do: Change the mode instead of the setting: run Choose Color Picker Mode and pick VS Code native picker , or Restore native color picker use VS Code's . Why: Uninstalling does not reset the setting Auric Color changed. What to do: Set \"editor.colorDecorators\": true in your user settings and in any workspace settings Auric Color overrode . Why: Another extension provides its own colour decorators or picker, or colorPicker.nativeHoverPicker is on while you expect Auric's own picker. What to do: Turn off the other extension's colour feature, or run Disable native color picker use Auric Artisan . Why: One of these applies: the mode is VS Code n"},{"t":"Auric Color FAQ","d":"Short answers about Auric Color.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" More than 40: CSS and its dialects, HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro, PHP, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSX, TSX, JSON, YAML, TOML, Markdown, Python, Go, Rust, Java, C , C and C++, Swift, Kotlin, Dart, Ruby and many more. See Supported languages hover and swatches.md supported languages . Contrast checks run in stylesheets, markup, JavaScript, TypeScript and Markdown. Auric Color's default mode replaces them with its own swatches and picker, and turns editor.colorDecorators off. Run Restore native color picker use VS Code's to go back. See Picker modes picker modes.md . Yes. Hover tiles and Type exact… write in the token's own syntax, using the fewest decimals that keep exactly the same colour. The picker panel writes the format tab you choose. Within one file, tick Apply to all N matches in file in the picker. For a colour that comes from a CSS custom property, use Apply to token in the contrast hover or the Contrast Studio, which changes the definition so every use follows. The colour with the same hue and chroma whose lightness has been moved just far enough to reach the contrast target. It is the smallest visible change that passes. No. APCA is the contrast model proposed in the WCAG 3 wor"},{"t":"Auric Color: other resources","d":"Glossary, shortcuts, limits and accuracy, related pages, release notes and privacy for Auric Color.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for Auric Color. Each is short and points to the fuller Studio page where one exists. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Colour terms used in the Auric Color docs. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Auric Color's keyboard shortcuts and Command Palette titles. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the colour engine and contrast checks can and cannot tell you. Related related.md Related extensions, tools and pages. Release notes release notes.md Auric Color's history from the changelog. Privacy privacy.md What Auric Color stores and changes. Back to the Auric Color overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Auric Color shortcuts","d":"Auric Color's keyboard shortcuts, Command Palette titles and picker keys.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard shortcuts","Command Palette titles","Picker keys"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + C Cmd + Alt + C Pick / edit color editor focused Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center Ctrl + . Cmd + . VS Code's quick fixes, including Fix contrast Type Auric Artisan in the Command Palette Ctrl + Shift + P : Auric Artisan: Open Color Studio Auric Artisan: Workstation: Command Center Auric Artisan: Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database Auric Artisan: Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown Auric Artisan: Open Unified Icon Studio Auric Artisan: Generate Accessible Palette Auric Artisan: Check Contrast of Selection Auric Artisan: Fix All Contrast Issues in File Auric Artisan: Pick / edit color Auric Artisan: Choose Color Picker Mode Auric Artisan: Disable native color picker use Auric Artisan Auric Artisan: Restore native color picker use VS Code's Auric Artisan: Refresh Contrast Diagnostics Auric Artisan: Change Accent Color Theme the Studio Auric Artisan: Mark Line as Intentional Branding Toggle Keys What they do Arrow keys on the hue or opacity bar Change the value by 1 Shift for 10 Page Up , Page Down Change the value by 10 Home , End Jump to the minimum or maximum Left , Right on the spectrum Change satur"},{"t":"Auric Color glossary","d":"Colour and contrast terms used in the Auric Color documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Alpha. How opaque a colour is, from 0 transparent to 1 solid . Written as the last two digits of 8 digit hex or the last value of rgb and hsl . APCA and Lc. The Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm from the WCAG 3 working draft. It reports lightness contrast as Lc; Auric Color's default target is Lc 60. Experimental. Chroma. How colourful a colour is, as opposed to grey. The C in OKLCH. Colour decorators. VS Code's own small colour squares and picker for colour values. Colour literal. A colour written directly in code, such as 1d4ed8 or oklch 0.49 0.22 264 . Colour vision deficiency CVD . Reduced ability to tell some colours apart. Simulated types: protanopia, protanomaly, deuteranopia, deuteranomaly, tritanopia, tritanomaly, achromatopsia and achromatomaly. Colour vision risk. A pair that meets its contrast target for typical vision but not under a simulated deficiency. Confusable hues. Two project colours that look distinct normally but alike under a simulated deficiency. Contrast ratio. WCAG 2.x's brightness difference between two colours, 1:1 to 21:1. Targets: 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text and UI, 7:1 for AAA. Custom property. A CSS variable such as brand ink ,"},{"t":"Auric Color limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Color's colour engine and contrast checks measure, how accurate they are, and what they cannot see.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What is accurate","What it cannot see","What it is not","Size limits"],"x":" Colour conversions read every CSS Color 4 and 5 syntax and write back to exactly the same colour in the token's own format. Contrast ratios use the WCAG 2.x formula; verdicts use the exact ratio, and a ratio just under a target is never shown rounded up to it. APCA uses APCA W3 0.0.98G and matches that algorithm's published test values. Colour difference CIEDE2000 matches all 34 published Sharma test pairs. Colour vision simulation uses the Brettel 1997 method in linear light. Translucent colours are blended the way browsers blend them 8 bit alpha . Contrast scanning agrees with Chromium's rendering in 62 of 68 cases on the audit set used in development; the other six are deliberately skipped. Colours set by JavaScript at runtime, or by classes defined in another file. Which rule wins between two different selectors, inherited or computed values, pseudo elements and component states. Text over images or gradients, gradient clipped text and currentColor backgrounds. The rendered font size, so verdicts name the WCAG check rather than a size. Tailwind utility classes, integer colour literals such as 0xFF00FF , and colours built from variables in other languages. Colour vision simulat"},{"t":"Auric Color privacy","d":"What Auric Color stores, which settings it changes, and when it uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/privacy.html","h":["What it changes or stores","When the network is used"],"x":" Auric Color works entirely on your machine. It sends no code, colours or telemetry anywhere and needs no account. Where What Your user settings auricColor.appearance.accent ; the picker mode settings when you switch mode; and VS Code's editor.colorDecorators , which it turns off in Auric mode see Picker modes ../docs/picker modes.md Workspace settings Values you save in Studio › Settings VS Code's storage for the extension Your recent colours up to 12 , dismissed suggestions, whether you answered the picker question, and which Studio sections you collapsed Files you choose Palette, shade and brand exports, through a save dialog .auric artisan/ Only when you build the knowledge database, or when Auric Color is the host and scans run in the background Only when you open a link yourself, such as auricartisan.com from the Studio. The eyedropper reads the screen locally. See the Studio privacy page ../../others/privacy.md for the full picture. "},{"t":"Auric Color release notes","d":"Auric Color's version history, taken from the Studio changelog.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/release-notes.html","h":["Unreleased","0.1.0 — Initial Studio release"],"x":" Auric Color shares one version number and one changelog with the other Studio extensions. This page lists the entries that concern colour. The complete history is in the Studio release notes ../../others/release notes.md . Listed under Unreleased in the changelog, as upcoming entries for the next numbered release: Every CSS Color 4 and 5 syntax is parsed, including oklch , lab , lch , hwb , color , color mix , relative colour, none and transparent , with CSS gamut mapping for wide gamut colours. Invalid hex such as 12345g is rejected. CIEDE2000 colour difference matches all 34 Sharma test pairs; colour naming uses it. Colour vision simulation uses the Brettel 1997 method in linear light. The suggested fix is the nearest passing colour 888 on white becomes 767676 , 4.54:1 . Ratios just under a threshold never display as the threshold; translucent colours blend with 8 bit alpha. Writing colours back round trips every CSS format exactly. The contrast scanner was rebuilt on a CSS rule tree: large text at 3:1, blended translucency and opacity , dark themes graded as themselves, color mix , relative colours and light dark graded, disabled controls and Markdown code samples exempt. The Q"},{"t":"Related to Auric Color","d":"Extensions, Studio pages and website tools related to Auric Color.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Auric Color","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/color/others/related.html","h":["Other Studio extensions","Shared Studio pages","Website tools","Elsewhere"],"x":" Auric Accessibility ../../accessibility/README.md : WCAG linting, Inspect and project scans; takes over contrast diagnostics when installed. Auric Code Health ../../code health/README.md : secrets, security and hygiene checks. The Full Pack ../../full pack/README.md : installs all three. The Contrast Studio ../../docs/contrast studio.md Suppression and branding ../../docs/suppression and branding.md Appearance ../../docs/appearance.md The Command Center ../../docs/command center.md Contrast Checker ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Vision Simulation ../../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Basic Colour Tools ../../../../website/tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Design Engine ../../../../website/tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md Tonal Steps ../../../../website/tools/colorimetry and rendering/tonal steps/README.md The browser extension ../../../../browser extension/README.md , for colours on rendered web pages. The Studio's related page ../../others/related.md , with standards and more tools. "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack","d":"What the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack installs, who it is for, and how to get started with it.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack is a VS Code extension pack: an extension that contains no code of its own and exists only to install other extensions. Installing it installs the three Auric Artisan Studio extensions in one step: Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. Each of the three stays a real, separate extension. You can update, disable or uninstall any of them from the Extensions view without affecting the others. When they are installed together, they cooperate as one Workstation: one sidebar, one Command Center and one Studio covering colour, accessibility and code health. Like the rest of the Studio, everything runs locally, with no account, no telemetry and no paid tier. The pack does not install icon themes or icon libraries. Anyone who wants the complete Studio without choosing extensions one by one. Teams that want everyone on the same set of tools; one pack ID to recommend in a workspace. Marketplace ID: auric artisan.auric artisan Marketplace page: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan Install from a terminal: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan Version 0.1.0; requires VS Code 1.74 "},{"t":"Full Pack docs","d":"The guides and reference pages for the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages cover the pack itself: installing it, managing its three members and the facts in its manifest. For the features of the extensions it installs, see the Studio docs ../../docs/README.md . File What it covers Getting started getting started.md Install the pack, see what it installs and what appears afterwards. Manage the pack's members managing members.md Enable, disable, update and uninstall members, and what the Workstation does when you do. Reference reference.md The pack's ID, members, version, requirements and categories. Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Problems with installing or removing the pack. FAQ faq.md Short answers. Back to the Full Pack overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Getting started with the Full Pack","d":"Install the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack, check what it installed, and find the Workstation it creates.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","What gets installed","What you see afterwards","Recommend the pack to your team","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Open the Extensions view with Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for auric artisan.auric artisan , or Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack . 3. Select Install . Or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan You need VS Code 1.74 or newer. Extension ID What it adds Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast auric artisan.auric color Colour hovers, swatches and pickers in 40+ languages, contrast diagnostics, palettes, shades, colour vision and the brand audit Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter auric artisan.auric a11y 70+ WCAG rules, Inspect, project scans, the Project Issues view and the remediation plan Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk auric artisan.auric codehealth Secrets, security, risky APIs, debug leftovers, task markers, merge markers and size checks; health records, SARIF and reports The pack itself adds no commands, views or settings. To check what was installed, open the Extensions view and look under Installed , or open the pack's page in the Extensions view: VS Code lists the extensions it includes. The three extensions start once VS Code has finished loading, and form one Workstation hosted by Auric Accessibility: Activity Bar: one Auric icon, Aur"},{"t":"Manage the pack's members","d":"Enable, disable, update and uninstall the extensions the Full Pack installs, and see what the Workstation does in each case.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/managing-members.html","h":["Disable a member","Uninstall a member","Update members","What the Workstation does when members change","Uninstall the pack","Related"],"x":" The Full Pack is a convenience bundle, not a single product. Its three members are ordinary extensions, so VS Code's usual controls work on each one separately. 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Find the member, for example Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk . 3. Select the gear icon, then Disable for all workspaces or Disable Workspace for this workspace only . 4. If VS Code asks you to restart extensions or reload the window, do so. The other members keep working. To turn it back on, choose Enable or Enable Workspace in the same menu. 1. In the Extensions view, select the gear icon on the member. 2. Select Uninstall . The pack and the other members stay installed. To get the member back, install it again by its ID, or reinstall the pack. Members update like any other extension, automatically if you have auto update on, or from the Extensions view. All Studio extensions share one version number, so keeping them on the same version avoids surprises in the shared .auric artisan folder. The Workstation re elects its host as soon as the set of installed or enabled members changes, without a reload. Views appear or hide, an open Studio tab rebuilds with the new "},{"t":"Full Pack reference","d":"The Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack's ID, members, version, requirements and Marketplace metadata.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/reference.html","h":["Members","What the pack contributes","Marketplace description","Commands"],"x":" Property Value Display name Auric Artisan Studio — Full Pack Extension ID auric artisan.auric artisan Publisher auric artisan Auric Artisan Version 0.1.0 VS Code required 1.74 or newer Categories Extension Packs, Linters, Visualization, Other Keywords color, accessibility, a11y, wcag, contrast, code health, extension pack Licence Auric Artisan Free Use Licence 2.0 Website https://auricartisan.com Marketplace https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan Order Extension ID 1 Auric Color — Picker, Palettes & Contrast auric artisan.auric color 2 Auric Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 Linter auric artisan.auric a11y 3 Auric Code Health — Secrets, TODOs & Risk auric artisan.auric codehealth Nothing beyond its members: no commands, keybindings, views, settings or files. Every command, shortcut and setting you get comes from a member. See the Studio reference ../../docs/reference.md . \"The complete Auric Artisan Studio in one install: colour picking and palettes, 70 rule WCAG 2.2 accessibility linting, local rulebooks and team knowledge, and language agnostic code health scanning. Installs the three focused Studio extensions, which you can enable or disable inde"},{"t":"Full Pack troubleshooting","d":"Problems with installing, updating or removing the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack, and what to do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" For problems with the Studio's features, see the Studio troubleshooting page ../../docs/troubleshooting.md . Why: The three members form one Workstation hosted by Auric Accessibility; the other two hide their own views. What to do: Nothing is wrong. Use the Auric Accessibility sidebar; it includes colour and code health. See The Workstation ../../docs/workstation.md . Why: The member failed to install for example, a network interruption while VS Code downloaded it , or it was uninstalled or disabled later. What to do: Open the Extensions view, search for the member's ID auric artisan.auric color , auric artisan.auric a11y or auric artisan.auric codehealth , and install or enable it. Why: Your VS Code is older than 1.74, or VS Code cannot reach the Marketplace. What to do: Update VS Code, check your connection or proxy, and try again. Offline, install each member's package file with Extensions: Install from VSIX… instead. What to do: Disable or uninstall the members you do not need; the others keep working. See Manage the pack's members managing members.md . Or uninstall the pack and install only the extension you want. Why: One member updated before the others. What to do: Update "},{"t":"Full Pack FAQ","d":"Short answers about the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" None in what you get. The pack installs the same three extensions in one step and gives you one ID to recommend or install. No. It has no commands, views, settings or code. No. It installs only Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. The Open Unified Icon Studio command works when you install an Auric icon extension separately. See The Icon Studio bridge ../../docs/icon studio bridge.md . Yes. In the Extensions view, choose Disable Workspace on that member. See Manage the pack's members managing members.md . They coordinate so that each piece of work is done once: one extension draws colour swatches, one publishes each kind of diagnostic, and one runs live re grading and background scans. Heavy parts load only when first used. Yes, like every Studio extension. No account, API key or paid tier. Only to download and update from the Marketplace. The extensions run entirely offline. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . "},{"t":"Full Pack: other resources","d":"Glossary, related pages, release notes and privacy for the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the pack. The pack has no shortcuts or settings of its own, so there is no shortcuts page; see the Studio shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md for its members'. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Terms used when talking about the pack. Related related.md The member extensions and shared Studio pages. Release notes release notes.md The pack's version history. Privacy privacy.md What the pack and its members do with your data. Back to the Full Pack overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Full Pack glossary","d":"Terms used in the Full Pack documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Extension pack. A VS Code extension that installs a list of other extensions and adds nothing of its own. Member. One of the extensions an extension pack installs. The Full Pack's members are Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. Workstation. Two or three Studio extensions installed together and presented as one product, with one sidebar, one Command Center and one Studio. Host. The member that presents the shared Workstation: Auric Accessibility when installed, otherwise Auric Color, otherwise Auric Code Health. Suppressed extension. A member that is not the host; it hides its own views but keeps doing the work it owns. Capability. One member's area of work: colour, accessibility or code health. Disable Workspace . A VS Code option that turns an extension off for the current workspace only. For every other term, see the Studio glossary ../../others/glossary.md . "},{"t":"Full Pack privacy","d":"What the Full Pack and its members do with your code and data.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The pack contains no code, so it does nothing with your data by itself. VS Code downloads it and its members from the Visual Studio Marketplace. Its three members analyse your code entirely on your machine: no network requests, no telemetry, no account. They write their results to a .auric artisan folder in your workspace and keep a few preferences in VS Code's settings and storage. For the details, see the Studio privacy page ../../others/privacy.md . "},{"t":"Full Pack release notes","d":"The version history of the Auric Artisan Studio Full Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 — Initial Studio release","Unreleased"],"x":" The pack shares one version number with its members. The full history of what changed in the members is in the Studio release notes ../../others/release notes.md . The first public release of the Full Pack. Installs only the three Studio extensions: Auric Color, Auric Accessibility and Auric Code Health. Icon themes and icon libraries are not part of the pack. Each member stays independently installable, updatable and removable. The changelog lists no changes to the pack itself under Unreleased . The upcoming changes to its members are listed in the Studio release notes ../../others/release notes.md unreleased . "},{"t":"Related to the Full Pack","d":"The member extensions and Studio pages related to the Full Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio › Full Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/full-pack/others/related.html","h":["The members","Studio pages","Elsewhere"],"x":" Auric Color ../../color/README.md : colour picking, palettes and contrast. Auric Accessibility ../../accessibility/README.md : WCAG linting and project audits. Auric Code Health ../../code health/README.md : secrets, security and hygiene checks. Studio overview ../../README.md Choose what to install ../../docs/choosing an install.md The Workstation ../../docs/workstation.md Getting started with the Studio ../../docs/getting started.md Related tools and articles ../../others/related.md Installing and setting up Auric Artisan's VS Code extensions ../../../install and setup/README.md Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md , which the pack does not install but its members can open. "},{"t":"Other resources","d":"The glossary, shortcuts, limits, related tools, release notes and privacy information for Auric Artisan Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the supporting pages for the whole Studio: what the terms mean, every shortcut, what the checks can and cannot tell you, where else to look, what changed between versions, and what happens to your data. Each extension's folder has its own shorter versions of these pages that point back here. File What it covers Glossary glossary.md Every term used in the Studio docs, from APCA to Workstation. Shortcuts shortcuts.md Keyboard shortcuts, Command Palette titles and in Studio keys. Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What each check measures, how precisely, and what it is not. Related related.md Related extensions, website tools and Learn articles. Release notes release notes.md The version history, from the changelog shipped with the extensions. Privacy privacy.md What stays on your machine, what is written to disk, and what uses the network. Back to the Studio overview ../README.md . "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut, Command Palette title and in-Studio key for Auric Artisan Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keyboard shortcuts","Command Palette titles","Keys inside the Studio","Change a shortcut"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command Extension Ctrl + Alt + . Cmd + Alt + . Workstation: Command Center All three code extensions Ctrl + Alt + C Cmd + Alt + C Pick / edit color editor focused Auric Color Ctrl + Alt + A Cmd + Alt + A Inspect Accessibility of Element editor focused Auric Accessibility These VS Code shortcuts are useful with the Studio: Keys What it does Ctrl + . Show quick fixes for the underline at the cursor Ctrl + Shift + P Open the Command Palette; type Auric Artisan to list every Studio command Ctrl + Shift + M Open the Problems panel Ctrl + Z Undo a fix, including a whole Fix All Contrast Issues in File Every Studio command starts with Auric Artisan: . Title Extension Workstation: Command Center All three Open Color Studio Auric Color Open Accessibility Studio Auric Accessibility Open Code Health Studio Auric Code Health Open Rulebook & Knowledge Database All three Build Workspace Knowledge Database JSON + Markdown All three Open Unified Icon Studio All three Pick / edit color Auric Color Generate Accessible Palette Auric Color Check Contrast of Selection Auric Color, Auric Accessibility Fix All Contrast Issues in File Auric Color Choose Color Picker Mode Auric Col"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of every term used in the Auric Artisan Studio documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Accessible name. The text assistive technology announces for an element, such as a button's label or an image's alt text. It can come from visible text, aria label , aria labelledby , alt , title or a <label . ACT Accessibility Conformance Testing . A W3C format for writing accessibility test rules consistently. The Studio's knowledge entries are ACT aligned : they follow the format's structure but make no claim of ACT conformance. Activity Bar. The vertical bar of icons at the far left of VS Code. The Studio adds an Auric icon there. Alt text. The text alternative for an image, given with the alt attribute. APCA Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm . A contrast model proposed for the WCAG 3 working draft. It reports lightness contrast as Lc , roughly 0 to 106 in either polarity, and takes into account which colour is the text. The Studio offers it as an experimental option; an APCA result is not a WCAG 3 conformance claim. ARIA Accessible Rich Internet Applications . W3C attributes such as role and aria label that describe elements to assistive technology. The Studio checks them against WAI ARIA 1.2. Assisted automation . A finding the engine detects but a person should confi"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Studio's colour, contrast, accessibility and code-health checks measure, how they were checked for accuracy, and what they cannot tell you.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the scores are and are not","Colour science","Contrast checks","Accessibility (WCAG) checks","Code-health checks","Size and scale limits","Related"],"x":" The Studio is a static analyser: it reads your source text and does not run your code or render your pages. That makes it fast, private and repeatable, and it also sets clear limits. This page explains both. Scores are a prioritisation and progress measure , not a certification. A score of 100 means the static checks found nothing, not that the product is accessible or secure. Automated testing covers only part of WCAG. Many success criteria need a person: alt text quality, focus order in practice, screen reader announcements, media alternatives, error recovery and more. The knowledge database's manual checks ../accessibility/docs/manual evidence.md cover these. Excluded, skipped and unscanned files neither help nor hurt a score. The colour engine is shared by hovers, pickers, the Studio, scans and the command line scanner, so every surface gives the same numbers. Parsing. Hex 3, 4, 6 and 8 digits , rgb , hsl and hwb with angle units and none , lab and lch with CSS's D50 white point , oklab , oklch , color in srgb , srgb linear , display p3 , a98 rgb , prophoto rgb , rec2020 and xyz , color mix , relative colour syntax, the 148 CSS named colours and transparent . Invalid values su"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Studio does with your code and data, what it writes to disk, and when anything uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/privacy.html","h":["What never leaves your machine","When the network is used","The remediation plan and \"AI\"","What is written to your disk","Secrets","Sharing reports","Related"],"x":" Auric Artisan Studio analyses your code entirely on your machine. Your source code, colours, scan results, findings and reports. Telemetry: the extensions collect none. There is no account, sign in, API key or licence server. The extensions contain no network code. Their build is checked so that any code that could make a network request fails the build. The command line scanner makes no network requests either. Only when you choose to open a link: auricartisan.com , from the Auric Artisan marks and links in the Overview, the Studio and hovers. The Studio's screens will only open links to that one site. W3C documentation , from WCAG docs and Open WCAG Documentation links on findings, and links inside knowledge database entries to official sources. These open in your browser. Installing or updating the extensions from the Marketplace is handled by VS Code. Generate Agent Ready Remediation Plan calls no AI model and sends nothing anywhere. It writes a plan, including a prompt template, to your workspace. If you choose to give that prompt to a coding agent, that agent's own privacy terms apply. Where What When .auric artisan/ in your workspace Scan cache, settings copy, health record"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"The version history of Auric Artisan Studio, taken from the changelog that ships with the extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/release-notes.html","h":["Unreleased","0.1.0 — Initial Studio release"],"x":" All four Studio extensions share one version number. These notes are taken from the changelog bundled with the extensions the Changelog tab of each Marketplace listing , rewritten for readers of these docs. The changelog lists the following changes under Unreleased , which means they are not yet recorded against a version number; they are the upcoming entries for the next numbered release. The rest of these docs describe the extensions as they behave in the package currently offered on the Marketplace. Every engine was measured against an external reference, and each defect found was fixed with a permanent regression test: colour science against published reference values, contrast against Chromium's rendering, the WCAG rules against axe core, and code health against a labelled set of examples. Colour: Every CSS Color 4 and 5 syntax is parsed: oklch , lab , lch , hwb , color with Display P3, Rec. 2020 and other spaces, color mix , relative colour, none , angle units and transparent . Wide gamut colours use CSS gamut mapping. Invalid hex values such as 12345g are rejected. CIEDE2000 colour difference was added and matches all 34 Sharma test pairs; colour naming now uses it. Colour "},{"t":"Related","d":"Other Auric Artisan extensions, website tools, articles and standards that work alongside Auric Artisan Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-studio/others/related.html","h":["Inside this documentation","Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","The browser extension","Tools on auricartisan.com","Standards the Studio refers to"],"x":" Auric Color ../color/README.md , Auric Accessibility ../accessibility/README.md , Auric Code Health ../code health/README.md and the Full Pack ../full pack/README.md . Installing and setting up Auric Artisan's VS Code extensions ../../install and setup/README.md . Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md : the combined icon library that Open Unified Icon Studio opens. Icon collections that provide it: Auric Icons Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md , Auric Icons Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md and Auric Icons Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md . Auric Artisan Theme ../../auric artisan theme/README.md . The Auric Artisan browser extension ../../../browser extension/README.md brings colour and accessibility tools to web pages in your browser, where you can check what is actually rendered rather than the source. Tool Use it to Contrast Checker ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Check a colour pair in the browser Analyzer ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Analyse a web page Accessibility Checklist ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/accessibility check"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Theme","d":"What the Auric Artisan Theme extension for VS Code is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Theme is a colour theme collection for Visual Studio Code. It ships 54 ready made themes in six surface families Obsidian, Midnight, Parchment, Porcelain, Dusk and Forest plus two high contrast builds, one dark and one light. Every theme is keyed to a single accent colour, so the whole workbench can be re coloured in one step. The extension also adds a live editor for the theme, called Theme Studio . Theme Studio has six tabs Looks , Dials , Colours , Audit , Share and Preview . It gives you 11 complete looks, 37 theme dials and 107 individually editable colour slots. Every change applies to your editor straight away, and a contrast guard keeps text readable while you experiment. A compact Auric Theme view in the Activity Bar gives you quick access to variants, accents, looks and the contrast status without opening the full Studio. Theme Studio and the sidebar can be shown in English or Hindi, independently of VS Code's own display language. Developers who want a warm, carefully balanced theme that works in dark, light and high contrast settings. Designers and front end developers who want to tune an editor theme precisely, down to a single colour slot. Accessibility"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Theme guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Theme guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for the Auric Artisan Theme extension. Start with Getting started if you are new, then use the task guides for each workflow. The reference lists every command, setting, keybinding, dial, colour slot and option. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, switch to an Auric theme, tour Theme Studio and make a first change. choose a theme.md choose a theme.md The six families, 54 variants, high contrast builds and every way to switch. looks and dials.md looks and dials.md The 11 looks and the 37 dials, with search, filters and resets. edit colours.md edit colours.md Override any of the 107 colour slots with the custom colour picker. check contrast.md check contrast.md Read the Audit tab and contrast report; tune the contrast guard. compare and preview.md compare and preview.md Compare shipped and current palettes; copy colours as CSS. save share and export.md save share and export.md Presets, customisation JSON, clipboard and standalone theme files. theme sidebar.md theme sidebar.md Every part of the Auric Theme view in the Activity Bar. interface language.md interface language.md Switch Theme Studi"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan Theme","d":"Install the theme, switch to an Auric variant, tour Theme Studio and make your first live customisation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install the extension","2. Switch to an Auric theme","3. Open Theme Studio","4. Tour the Studio","5. Make a first change","6. Check it is still readable","7. Save your work","Result","Next steps"],"x":" This guide takes you from installation to a first saved customisation in a few minutes. You need Visual Studio Code 1.75 or later. The extension works in untrusted and virtual workspaces. Customisations only apply while one of the Auric Artisan themes is active. If another theme is active, the customisation commands ask you to pick an Auric theme first. 1. Open the Extensions view with Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for Auric Artisan Theme publisher auric artisan . 3. Select Install . You can also run this in a terminal: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan theme After installation, VS Code may show the Make it yours walkthrough on its Welcome page. It has four steps: Pick a variant , Change the gold , Open the Studio and Keep it readable . Each step has a button that runs the matching command. 1. Open the Command Palette with Ctrl + Shift + P . 2. Run Auric Theme: Switch Variant… . 3. The list shows all 54 themes. Each entry shows whether it is dark or light and the hex value of its canvas the editor background . The theme you are using is marked current . 4. Select a theme. VS Code switches immediately. You can also use VS Code's own Preferences: Color Theme pic"},{"t":"Check contrast","d":"Read the Audit tab and the plain-text contrast report, and control the contrast guard that keeps your theme readable.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/check-contrast.html","h":["Key terms","What is audited","Use the Audit tab","Use the sidebar","Open the plain-text contrast report","The contrast guard","Result"],"x":" Every colour the theme produces is checked against the surface it actually sits on. You can read the results in three places: the Audit tab in Theme Studio, the Contrast section of the sidebar, and a plain text contrast report. Contrast ratio WCAG : a number from 1:1 to 21:1 comparing the luminance of text and background. WCAG 2 AA asks for 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for large text and control boundaries; AAA asks for 7:1. APCA Lc: a perceptual contrast measure from the draft WCAG 3 work. Unlike the ratio, it accounts for polarity dark on light versus light on dark . Roughly, Lc 60 suits body text, Lc 45 large text, and Lc 30 is the floor for anything you must read. A negative value means light text on a dark background. Minimum: the threshold a particular pair is held to. Decorative washes are held to less than text. The audit checks 81 pairs per theme: editor text, all 26 syntax roles, the 14 text bearing ANSI terminal colours, source control decorations, and the text and borders of dropdowns, inputs, checkboxes, radios, buttons, badges, menus and quick picks. Form control borders are held to 3:1 against the fill they enclose WCAG 1.4.11 . 1. Open Theme Studio and select Audit "},{"t":"Choose a theme","d":"The six surface families, 54 variants and two high-contrast builds, and every way to switch between them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/choose-a-theme.html","h":["The families","Ways to switch","What happens to your customisations","Result"],"x":" Auric Artisan Theme ships 54 built in variants. A variant is one complete theme: a surface family the neutral backgrounds and text combined with an accent colour. Family Surface Polarity Variants Obsidian Warm charcoal Dark 10 Midnight Near black Dark 10 Parchment Warm cream Light 10 Porcelain Cool white Light 10 Dusk Violet tinted dark Dark 6 Forest Green tinted dark Dark 6 High contrast Gold, dark and light One dark, one light 2 Family Accents Obsidian, Midnight, Parchment, Porcelain Gold, Sapphire, Rose, Amethyst, Patina, Emerald, Ember, Crimson, Iris, Graphite Dusk Gold, Sapphire, Rose, Amethyst, Iris, Graphite Forest Gold, Patina, Emerald, Ember, Rose, Graphite High contrast Obsidian Gold High Contrast is dark; Porcelain Gold High Contrast is light Every theme appears in VS Code as Auric Artisan — Family Accent , for example Auric Artisan — Parchment Emerald . The two high contrast builds are Auric Artisan — Obsidian Gold High Contrast and Auric Artisan — Porcelain Gold High Contrast . See the reference reference.md all 54 themes for every theme and its ID. Tip: The variant's accent is only its starting point. You can re key any variant onto any of 17 accents, or a custom col"},{"t":"Compare and preview","d":"Use the Preview tab to compare the shipped palette with your current colours and copy the palette as CSS custom properties.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/compare-and-preview.html","h":["Compare palettes","Copy the palette as CSS","Result"],"x":" The Preview tab shows the shipped palette of the active variant next to your current palette, so you can see exactly what your changes did. 1. Open Theme Studio and select Preview or press 6 . 2. Open the Comparison view dropdown and choose: Side by side — both palettes the default . As shipped — only the variant's original palette. Your palette — only your current colours. 3. Each specimen shows a title bar, a short syntax colour sample a comment, keyword, variable, properties, a string, a number, a constant and a function call and six palette chips: bg.base , fg.default , accent.base , syntax.string , syntax.keyword and syntax.fn , each with its hex value. 4. Below the specimens, a line reads \"{count} colour slots differ from the shipped variant. Theme edits apply live.\" The specimen is an illustration drawn from the theme engine's colours. It is not a full VS Code editor, and it is not a \"try before you apply\" mode: every edit you make on other tabs is already live in your editor. 1. On the Preview tab, select Copy palette as CSS . 2. The full resolved palette is copied to the clipboard as CSS custom properties inside a :root block. Each slot becomes a property named auric foll"},{"t":"Edit individual colours","d":"Override any of the 107 colour slots on the Colours tab using the custom colour picker, and revert them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/edit-colours.html","h":["Open the Colours tab","Find a slot","Override a slot","Revert an override","Things to know","Result"],"x":" The theme is built from 107 colour slots . A slot is one named colour, such as Canvas bg.base or Keyword syntax.keyword , that many parts of the workbench or syntax highlighting draw from. On the Colours tab you can override any slot. An override wins over whatever the dials produced. 1. Open Theme Studio Ctrl + Alt + ; . 2. Select the Colours tab, press 3 , or select Explore colours → in the introduction. Slots are grouped into 12 collapsible cards: Group Contents Surfaces The planes the workbench is built from, deepest to nearest 8 slots . Text Foreground ramp, from body copy to disabled 6 . Lines Every border, divider and focus ring 7 . Accent The accent fills, emphasis and washes derived from it 7 . States Hover, active, selected and drop feedback 5 . Selection Editor selection, find, word and range highlights 10 . Semantics Error, warning, info and success, quiet and loud 8 . Semantic washes Tinted backdrops behind semantic messages 4 . Terminal The 16 ANSI colours 16 . Source control File decoration colours in source control views 9 . Syntax Token colours shared by semantic and TextMate highlighting 26 . Effects The shadow colour 1 . Select a group heading to expand or colla"},{"t":"Interface language (English and हिन्दी)","d":"Switch Theme Studio and the Theme sidebar between English and Hindi, and understand what follows VS Code's own display language.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/interface-language.html","h":["Choose a language","What changes and what does not","Result"],"x":" Theme Studio and the Theme sidebar can be shown in English or Hindi. You do not need a VS Code language pack for this. Use any of these: In Theme Studio's top bar, select Auto , English or हिन्दी . In the sidebar's language bar, select Auto , EN or हिं . Run Auric Theme: Choose Interface Language… and pick Auto VS Code , English or Hindi . The current choice is marked current . Set auricTheme.interfaceLanguage in Settings to auto , en or hi . Value Behaviour auto default Follows the VS Code display language. Hindi locales use Hindi; every other locale uses English. en Always English in Theme Studio and the sidebar. hi Always Hindi in Theme Studio and the sidebar. The choice is saved in your user settings and shared by both panels. The switch rebuilds the labels immediately. Your current tab, filters, expanded groups, scroll position and any text you had typed in the Share tab are kept. Part of VS Code Language used Theme Studio and the Theme sidebar Your auricTheme.interfaceLanguage choice. Theme names in the pickers and status bar VS Code's display language. With Hindi as the display language, all 54 names appear in Hindi, for example \"ऑरिक आर्टिजन — ऑब्सिडियन गोल्ड\". Command Pal"},{"t":"Looks and dials","d":"Start from one of 11 looks, then tune the 37 theme dials on the Dials tab, with search, filters and resets.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/looks-and-dials.html","h":["Apply a look","Tune dials on the Dials tab","What each group controls","Quick commands for common dials","Edit dials as settings","Result"],"x":" The theme is generated from a small number of decisions called dials. A dial is one setting, such as the accent colour or how strongly panes separate. Change a dial and every colour that depends on it is recomputed, with the contrast guard applied on top. A look is a named combination of dial values that you can apply in one click. Both are available in Theme Studio. Dials are also ordinary VS Code settings under auricTheme. , so you can change them in the Settings editor or in settings.json . 1. Open Theme Studio Ctrl + Alt + ; . 2. Select the Looks tab or press 1 . 3. Under The set , select a look. Look What it does Signature The theme exactly as shipped. Applying it clears every dial back to its default. Gallery Everything turned up: layered surfaces, gold edges, visible controls. Built for demos and projectors. Atelier Warm, soft and unhurried. Expressive italics, quiet chrome, pastel tokens. Foundry Monochrome tokens, flat chrome, no ornament. Lightness does all the work. Bullion One hue, top to bottom. Nocturne Deeper canvas, dimmer chrome, quieter comments. For working late. Vitrine Maximum colour separation: vivid tokens, rainbow brackets and guides. Clarity Accessibility "},{"t":"Save, share and export","d":"Keep your customisation as named presets, move it between machines as JSON, and export a standalone VS Code colour theme file.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/save-share-and-export.html","h":["Presets","Customisation JSON","Export a standalone theme file","Result"],"x":" Your customisation is small: the dials you changed plus any colour slot overrides. The extension gives you three ways to keep and move it. Method Where it lives Best for Preset Inside the extension, on this machine Switching between several set ups quickly. Customisation JSON Clipboard or any text file Moving a set up to another machine or sharing it. Theme file A .json colour theme file Using the result without this extension, or packaging it as your own theme. Important: Edits apply live and there is no general undo history. Save a preset or export JSON before large experiments. 1. Open Theme Studio and select Share or press 5 . 2. In the Presets card, type a name in Name this preset… up to 64 characters . 3. Select Save or press Enter . If you leave the name empty, the Studio shows \"Give the preset a name first.\" Saving again with the same name updates that preset. Names that differ only by Hindi characters or punctuation are kept as separate presets. You can also run Auric Theme: Save Current as Preset… from the Command Palette or the sidebar's … menu. It asks you to name the preset. In the Saved list, select Load beside a preset. Each entry shows the date and time it was save"},{"t":"The Theme sidebar","d":"Every part of the Auric Theme view in the Activity Bar, from the variant galleries to the contrast status and title-bar actions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/theme-sidebar.html","h":["Open the sidebar","Sections, top to bottom","Title-bar actions","Result"],"x":" The extension adds an Auric Theme icon to the Activity Bar. It opens a compact view called Theme that covers the most common tasks without opening Theme Studio. Select the Auric Theme icon in the Activity Bar. If you do not see it, right click the Activity Bar and make sure Auric Theme is ticked. Section What it does Header Shows the active theme name and a summary such as \"3 dials changed · 1 slot override\", or Shipped defaults . Language Auto , EN and हिं buttons switch the language of the sidebar and Theme Studio. Active theme card Shows the current theme with an Open Theme Studio button. Metrics Built in variants and Your changes . Variant A searchable dropdown of all variants, and Browse all swatches for the family galleries. Accent Swatches for the named accents, plus Custom with a colour picker for any hex colour. Look A dropdown of the 11 looks. Contrast The worst pair, a Pass or Fail chip and its ratio. Select it to open the Audit tab. Actions Reset and Export , and a link to auricartisan.com. Expand Browse all swatches to see one collapsible group per family: Obsidian, Midnight, Parchment, Porcelain, Dusk, Forest and High contrast. Each group shows its variant count and "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Theme reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, theme, look, accent, palette, colour slot and Theme Studio control in Auric Artisan Theme 0.2.0.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Looks","Accents","Syntax palettes","Terminal palettes","All 54 themes","Colour slots","Theme Studio controls by tab","Other surfaces","Messages you may see","Files and formats"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.2.0 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. All commands appear in the Command Palette under the category Auric Theme . Command ID What it does Open Theme Studio auricTheme.openStudio Opens or reveals the Auric Theme Studio editor tab. Switch Variant… auricTheme.selectTheme Quick Pick of all 54 themes with polarity and canvas colour; sets VS Code's colour theme. Cycle Variant auricTheme.cycleVariant Switches to the next of the 54 variants. Choose Accent Colour… auricTheme.pickAccent Quick Pick of the 17 named accents; sets auricTheme.accent.preset . Choose Look… auricTheme.pickLook Quick Pick of the 11 looks; applies the look. Choose Syntax Palette… auricTheme.pickPalette Quick Pick of the 9 syntax palettes; sets auricTheme.syntax.palette . Choose Interface Language… auricTheme.chooseInterfaceLanguage Auto VS Code , English or Hindi for the Studio and sidebar. Toggle Italics auricTheme.toggleItalics Switches auricTheme.syntax.italics between off and standard . Surprise Me auricTheme.randomize Clears your dials and applies a random curated accent, palette, warmth, separation, bracket and tab style. Reset Everything auricTheme.resetAll After"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Artisan Theme and Theme Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Start again from the shipped theme","Still stuck"],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do Dials and colour changes have no effect. A non Auric colour theme is active. Customisations are scoped to the Auric theme names. Run Auric Theme: Switch Variant… and pick an Auric theme. A message says \"customisations apply to the Auric Artisan themes. Pick one first.\" Same as above. Select Choose theme in the message. The status bar item is missing. It only shows while an Auric theme is active. Switch to an Auric theme. My colour override is not exactly the colour I typed. The contrast guard adjusted it to meet your minimum contrast. Lower Minimum contrast or turn off Enforce contrast in the Accessibility dials. Check the Audit tab afterwards. Overrides disappeared after switching theme. Colour overrides are stored per variant. Switch back to the variant where you made them, or save a preset and load it on the new variant. A warning keeps saying colour pairs no longer meet the minimum. Audit on apply reports failures after each change. Fix the failing pairs see the Audit tab , or turn off Audit on apply . \"Auric Theme: could not save auricTheme.…\" VS Code could not write your user settings, often because settings.json has a syntax error or is rea"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Theme and Theme Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the theme free?","How many themes are there?","Do I need Theme Studio to use the themes?","Does Theme Studio have a preview mode?","Is there undo?","Where are my changes stored?","Will my customisation sync to other machines?","Why did my accent colour get darker on a light theme?","Does the theme affect other colour themes?","What does \"Surprise Me\" change?","Can I use my customised theme without the extension?","Can the interface be in Hindi?","Does it work in remote, untrusted or virtual workspaces?"],"x":" Yes. The extension is free to install and use. 54: ten accents each for Obsidian, Midnight, Parchment and Porcelain, six each for Dusk and Forest, and two high contrast builds. See Choose a theme choose a theme.md . No. The themes work like any other VS Code colour theme. Theme Studio is optional. No. Every edit applies live. The Preview tab only compares palettes. Save a preset or export JSON before large experiments. There is no undo history. Use the per dial and per slot reset buttons, Reset all , or load a saved preset. Dials are VS Code user settings under auricTheme. . Colour overrides and presets are stored by the extension on this machine. The extension also writes theme scoped entries into VS Code's colour customisation settings so the changes show. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Dials are ordinary settings, so they follow VS Code Settings Sync if you use it. Presets and colour overrides are local; move them with customisation JSON see Save, share and export save share and export.md . On light themes the accent is darkened until it clears your minimum contrast. The brand gold, for example, is too light to read as text on the cream Parchment canvas. No. Customisations "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Theme: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Theme: glossary, shortcuts, limits, related products, release notes and privacy.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for the Auric Artisan Theme extension. They explain terms, list shortcuts, describe what the contrast checks can and cannot tell you, and record the release history and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the theme and Theme Studio. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings, Studio keys and every command. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the contrast audit measures and what the extension does not do. related.md related.md Other Auric Artisan extensions and website tools that pair with the theme. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history of each version. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored, where, and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Every keybinding, Theme Studio key and Command Palette command in Auric Artisan Theme.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Global keybindings","Keys inside Theme Studio","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Open Theme Studio Ctrl + Alt + ; Cmd + Alt + ; Cycle Variant Ctrl + Alt + ' Cmd + Alt + ' To change them, open Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts and search for \"Auric Theme\". Key Action 1 Looks tab 2 Dials tab 3 Colours tab 4 Audit tab 5 Share tab 6 Preview tab / Colours tab, focus the filter Escape Close a dropdown or picker; clear the colour filter Arrow keys, Home , End Move between tabs, dropdown options, swatches; adjust sliders Shift + arrow keys Larger slider and picker steps Page Up , Page Down Larger slider steps Double click a slider Reset it Enter in the preset name box Save the preset Open the Command Palette Ctrl + Shift + P and type \"Auric Theme\". Command Notes Auric Theme: Open Theme Studio Also on the status bar item and the sidebar. Auric Theme: Switch Variant… All 54 themes. Auric Theme: Cycle Variant Next variant. Auric Theme: Choose Accent Colour… 17 named accents. Auric Theme: Choose Look… 11 looks. Auric Theme: Choose Syntax Palette… 9 palettes. Auric Theme: Choose Interface Language… Auto, English or Hindi. Auric Theme: Toggle Italics Off or standard. Auric Theme: Surprise Me Random curated combination. Auric Theme: Reset Ev"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Artisan Theme and Theme Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Accent The single colour the whole theme is keyed to. Washes, borders, selections, the focus ring and the cursor are derived from it. Alpha Transparency. Alpha slots accept an opacity value, written as the last two digits of rrggbbaa . APCA Lc A perceptual contrast value from the draft WCAG 3 work. It accounts for polarity; a negative value means light text on a dark background. Audit The contrast check of 81 foreground and background pairs in the active theme. Canvas The editor background, slot bg.base . Chrome The workbench bars and frames around the editor: status bar, activity bar, title bar, side bar and tabs. Colour slot One named colour the theme is built from, such as syntax.keyword . There are 107. Contrast guard The step that nudges colours along OKLCH lightness until they meet your minimum contrast. Controlled by Enforce contrast . Contrast ratio The WCAG measure of luminance difference, from 1:1 to 21:1. Customisation JSON The portable document holding your changed dials and colour overrides. Dial One theme setting, such as Syntax palette or Depth . There are 37, all under auricTheme. . Family A set of variants sharing the same neutral surfaces, such as Ob"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the contrast audit measures, how precise it is, and what Auric Artisan Theme does not do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the contrast audit measures","What the audit does not tell you","How the contrast guard changes colours","What the extension does not do"],"x":" The audit covers 81 defined foreground and background pairs per theme: editor text, 26 syntax roles, 14 text bearing ANSI colours, source control decorations, and text and borders of common controls. Ratios use the WCAG 2 relative luminance formula on sRGB colours. Transparent colours are composited onto the surface they sit on before measuring. APCA Lc values are shown for guidance. APCA is part of draft WCAG 3 work and is not yet a conformance requirement. Each pair has its own minimum. Text is held to your Minimum contrast setting; control borders are held to 3:1; decorative washes are held to less than text. It does not check every colour VS Code can draw, or colours added by other extensions. It does not check your font, font size, font weight or display. It does not replace testing with real users. Contrast checks are guidance, not a guarantee that every possible customisation meets accessibility requirements. A pair marked Missing could not be measured because a colour it depends on is missing. The guard moves a colour along its OKLCH lightness until the pair clears the minimum, keeping hue and chroma. Very saturated or unusual colours may shift visibly. The guard applies t"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Theme stores, where it stores it and what, if anything, uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/privacy.html","h":["What is stored and where","What uses the network","Clipboard and files","Security"],"x":" Auric Artisan Theme works entirely inside VS Code. It has no account, no telemetry and no runtime package dependencies, and it does not contact a server. Data Where it is stored Dial values and interface language Your VS Code user settings, under auricTheme. . Theme scoped colour customisations Your VS Code user settings, in the colour, token and semantic token customisation blocks for the Auric theme names. Unrelated blocks are left alone. An untouched set up writes nothing. Colour slot overrides per variant and presets The extension's local storage in VS Code on this machine. Studio view state tab, scroll, open groups, searches The panel's own saved state in VS Code. Recent colours in the picker Memory only, for the current panel session. \"Local\" does not mean read only: customising the theme writes to your user settings. Nothing, automatically. The links to auricartisan.com in the Studio and sidebar open your browser only when you select them. The clipboard is read only when you run Apply Customisation from Clipboard , and written only when you copy. Files are written only when you run Export as Theme File… and choose a location. The Studio and sidebar load only files packaged "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan Theme, from 0.1.0 to 0.2.0.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.2.0 — 8 September 2026","0.1.1 — 10 August 2026","0.1.0 — 23 July 2026"],"x":" The current Marketplace version. 54 built in variants, up from 24. All existing theme IDs still work. Two new dark families, Dusk and Forest , with six accents each. Ten accent variants each for Obsidian, Midnight, Parchment and Porcelain. Compact collapsible family galleries in the sidebar, with small accent tiles, counts and keyboard navigation; the sidebar remembers which families are open. A searchable variant dropdown. The Preview tab: side by side palette comparison and Copy palette as CSS . Dial search and a Modified only filter. A direct custom accent picker in the sidebar. Numeric RGB and opacity channels in the colour picker, and up to eight recent colours per session. Theme Studio and the sidebar share a new workspace layout: introduction, active theme card, live counts and numbered tabs. Matching Hindi theme names in VS Code's pickers and in both panels. Devanagari friendly fonts and line height. Dropdowns no longer jump to the top or scroll the page behind them while you scroll; background updates keep the list position. Presets with distinct Hindi or punctuation only names no longer overwrite each other. Presets already overwritten in earlier versions cannot be recov"},{"t":"Related extensions and tools","d":"Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions, website tools and guides that work well with Auric Artisan Theme.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Theme","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-theme/others/related.html","h":["Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","Website tools","Learn more"],"x":" Extension How it relates Auric Artisan File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md File and folder icons for the Explorer, in Facet, Playful and Modern styles. Pairs with the theme for a complete look. Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md Search and insert icons and emoji into code. Auric Artisan Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio with the same English and Hindi interface switch. Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md Colour, accessibility and code health tools for your project files. Auric Artisan Live ../../auric artisan live/README.md Live server and preview; Theme Studio's layout follows the same workspace design. For installing and managing any of these, see Install and set up ../../install and setup/README.md . Tool Why it is useful with the theme Contrast Checker ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Check a single colour pair in detail, including WCAG and APCA values. Design Engine ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md Build a design system palette in OKLCH that you can mirror in your editor. Colour Science Lab ../../../website/tools/"},{"t":"Auric Artisan File Icons","d":"What the Auric Artisan File Icons extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan File Icons gives the VS Code Explorer a consistent set of file and folder icons in three styles: Facet , Playful and Modern . Each style is a separate VS Code file icon theme, so you choose one for your Explorer and can switch at any time. Together they contain 1,464 SVG assets. The extension adds File Icon Studio , available as a sidebar and as an editor tab. In its Library you search the artwork of all three styles and insert an icon into your code as inline SVG, JSX, an HTML image or a CSS background. In Appearance you recolour files and folders, adjust saturation, brightness and opacity, hide the Explorer arrows and choose a framework pack for Modern. In Workspace you manage smart detection, profiles, code hovers and settings imports. Smart detection adds a small badge, a category colour and an explanation to recognised folders and files, for example a React project folder or a generated file. You can also assign any icon to a specific file or folder from the Explorer's right click menu, and insert icons into code by hovering over tokens such as :icon file typescript: . Developers who want a distinctive, consistent Explorer and control over its colours. Teams who"},{"t":"Auric Artisan File Icons guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan File Icons guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Artisan File Icons. Start with Getting started, then use the guide for the job you want to do. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, open File Icon Studio, tour the screen and activate a style. choose a style.md choose a style.md Facet, Playful and Modern compared, and every way to switch. customise the explorer.md customise the explorer.md Colours, saturation, brightness, opacity, arrows and the Modern framework pack. assign icons.md assign icons.md Give a file, folder or pattern its own icon, and clear it. smart detection.md smart detection.md Badges, colours and explanations; built in rules; custom rules; workspace scans. profiles.md profiles.md Built in and saved profiles, export and import. insert icons into code.md insert icons into code.md Library cards, the inspector, the native picker and code hovers. modern and legacy.md modern and legacy.md Using File Icons with Auric Icons: Modern and moving from the old Playful extension. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, menu, colour and format. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md fa"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan File Icons","d":"Install File Icons, open File Icon Studio, tour its three tabs and activate a style in the Explorer.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Open File Icon Studio","3. Tour the Studio","4. Activate a style","5. Try a colour","Result"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later. No other icon extension is needed. No account is needed. The extension does not contact a server and never runs code from your workspace. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Artisan File Icons and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan file icon For an official downloaded .vsix file, run Extensions: Install from VSIX… and choose the file. Sidebar: select Auric File Icons in the Activity Bar. The view is called File Icon Studio . Editor tab: run Auric Artisan File Icons: Open File Icon Studio , or select the ↗ button Open in editor tab in the sidebar. Both have the same tools; the sidebar is compact. Area Contents Header \"Auric Artisan / File Icon Studio\", an auricartisan.com ↗ link, ↗ sidebar only and ⚙ All extension settings . Tabs Library , Appearance , Workspace . Target line \"Insert target · {file}\" when a writable editor is open, otherwise \"No editor target · open a writable file before inserting. Copy is always available.\" \"Your files, with character.\" A search box, the Artwork style , Show and Code format pickers, an Open folder artwork check box, the Use … in Explo"},{"t":"Assign icons to files and folders","d":"Give a file, folder, extension or pattern its own icon from the Explorer or in settings, and clear it again.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/assign-icons.html","h":["From the Explorer","In settings","Turn a detected project type into an icon","Result"],"x":" An association tells the icon theme which icon to show for a name. You can create associations from the Explorer or write them in settings. The Explorer actions appear when one of the Auric Artisan File Icons themes is active. 1. Right click a file or folder in the Explorer. 2. Open Auric File Icons and select Set File or Folder Icon . 3. Choose the scope: Resource Scope options A file, for example app.config.ts Exact filename , All \\ .config.ts files , Only parent/\\ .config.ts , Only parent/app.config.ts A file with no extension Exact filename , Only parent/name A folder All folders named \"…\" , Only \"parent/folder\" A workspace root folder No choice: it is set as a workspace root association. 4. Choose an icon from the list titled Set icon for … . Search by name or ID. The list shows icons for the Modern style when Modern is active, otherwise Facet's icons. 5. VS Code confirms, for example \"TypeScript assigned to All \\ .config.ts files.\" Select Reload when asked. Associations made this way are saved in the workspace settings, so they apply to this project only. 1. Right click the same file or folder. 2. Open Auric File Icons › Clear Custom File or Folder Icon . 3. Choose the same "},{"t":"Choose a style","d":"Compare the Facet, Playful and Modern Explorer styles and switch between them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/choose-a-style.html","h":["Switch style","What carries across styles","Live filename previews","Result"],"x":" File Icons contains three complete Explorer styles. Each is a separate VS Code file icon theme, and only one can be active at a time. Style Theme name in VS Code Artwork What you get Facet Auric Artisan File Icons: Facet 500 SVGs Faceted artwork: 200 file designs and 150 closed and open folder pairs. Playful Auric Artisan File Icons: Playful 500 SVGs A distinct playful palette and artwork covering the same file and folder catalog as Facet. Modern Auric Artisan File Icons: Modern 464 SVGs 219 file designs, 114 closed and open folder pairs, light alternatives and state overlays. The totals include open folder states, framework artwork and alternatives; they are not counts of unique file types. Facet and Playful share the same mappings: 270 file extensions, 453 exact filenames, 84 language IDs and 357 folder aliases. Modern uses its own mappings and supports four framework packs Angular, NestJS, React, Vue . 1. Open the Library tab. 2. Choose a style in Artwork style . This only previews the artwork. 3. Select Use Facet in Explorer , Use Playful in Explorer or Use Modern in Explorer . Command Result Auric Artisan File Icons: Activate Facet Icon Theme Facet becomes the file icon theme"},{"t":"Customise the Explorer","d":"Set file and folder colours, saturation, brightness, opacity, Explorer arrows and the Modern framework pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/customise-the-explorer.html","h":["Use the Appearance tab","Use the Configure menu","Modern framework pack","Toggle arrows quickly","Restore defaults","Settings files","Result"],"x":" Appearance settings recolour the Explorer artwork while keeping each icon's faceted light and dark structure. They apply to Facet, Playful and Modern together. They do not change the artwork you insert into code. 1. Open File Icon Studio and select Appearance . 2. Set any of these: Control What it does Range File color Recolours every file icon. Use the swatch, type a hex value, or Reset to default . default , rgb or rrggbb Folder color Recolours every folder pair. default , rgb or rrggbb Saturation Colour intensity. 0 is greyscale. 0 to 2, steps of 0.05 Brightness Overall lightness. 0.5 to 1.5, steps of 0.05 Opacity Transparency. 0.2 to 1, steps of 0.05 Hide Explorer arrows Hides the expand and collapse chevrons. On or off 3. Select Apply appearance . 4. If the artwork changed, VS Code shows \"Auric file icons updated. Reload the window to apply every icon change.\" Select Reload . If nothing needed rebuilding, it says \"No theme reload is needed.\" Restore defaults… runs Restore Icon Defaults see below . Run Auric Artisan File Icons: Open File Icon Studio Settings . A menu titled Configure Auric Artisan File Icons lists: Item What it does File color Choose from presets or a custom h"},{"t":"Insert icons into code","d":"Insert or copy File Icons artwork as inline SVG, JSX, an HTML image or a CSS background from the Studio, a native picker or a code hover.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/insert-icons-into-code.html","h":["Output formats","From the Library tab","From the Command Palette or editor menu","From a code hover","Result"],"x":" File Icon Studio lets you reuse the shipped file and folder artwork in your own code. Format Setting value Output Inline SVG svg A self contained <svg element, 24 × 24 by default. JSX jsx The SVG with JSX compatible attribute names. HTML image img A 24 × 24 <img with the SVG embedded as a data URI. CSS background css A background image declaration with the SVG embedded as a data URI. auricFileIcons.insertFormat sets the default format svg for the native picker and the Studio. Note: Code output always uses the shipped artwork of the chosen style. Your Explorer colour, saturation, brightness and opacity settings do not change exported code. Add meaningful alternative text when an icon conveys information. 1. Open a writable text file and place the cursor. The Studio's target line shows \"Insert target · {file}\". 2. In File Icon Studio, open Library . 3. Set Artwork style Facet , Playful or Modern and Show Files & folders , Files or Folders . 4. Type in Search icons placeholder \"TypeScript, React, src…\", up to 150 characters . Press / to jump to the search box. 5. Choose a Code format : Inline SVG , JSX , HTML image or CSS background . 6. Tick Open folder artwork to show folders in th"},{"t":"Modern and older Playful settings","d":"Use File Icons alongside Auric Icons: Modern, import Modern's file settings, and move from the old standalone Playful file icon extension.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/modern-and-legacy.html","h":["Using File Icons with Auric Icons: Modern","Moving from the standalone Playful extension","Not the same Playful","Result"],"x":" File Icons brings together Explorer styles that used to live in separate extensions. This page explains how to move your settings and avoid duplicates. File Icons includes Modern's Explorer artwork 464 assets and keeps its theme ID, auric artisan modern icon . The Auric Icons: Modern extension also has a general purpose 720 icon library, which File Icons does not include. Keep Auric Icons: Modern installed if you use its icon library. The Modern version currently on the Marketplace 0.12.1 still includes its own Auric Icons: Modern file icon theme under the same theme ID. With both installed, the File Icon Theme picker can show two Modern entries, and the two extensions use different settings auricIcons. for Modern, auricFileIcons. for File Icons . The File Icons documentation states that an updated Modern release no longer registers a file theme. Until you have that release, choose one extension to manage Modern's Explorer icons and use its settings. 1. Open File Icon Studio › Workspace › Import existing file settings . 2. Select Import Modern file settings , or run Auric Artisan File Icons: Import Modern File Icon Settings… . 3. Confirm the import. Only missing file theme setting"},{"t":"Profiles","d":"Apply a built-in icon profile, save your own, and move profiles between machines as JSON.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/profiles.html","h":["Apply a profile","Save your current set-up","Delete a saved profile","Export and import","Result"],"x":" A profile is a named, portable set of appearance settings, associations and smart detection settings. 1. Run Auric Artisan File Icons: Apply Icon Profile , or Apply profile… on the Workspace tab. 2. Choose a profile. Built in profiles are marked Built in ; your saved profiles follow. 3. Select Reload when asked. Built in profile Description Key values Classic Facet Balanced original colours and full smart decorations. Default colours, 1 / 1 / 1, badge and colour Vivid Studio Brighter, richer colour for large project explorers. Saturation 1.35, brightness 1.08 Focused Explorer Blue folders, softer files, hidden arrows and badge only smart matches. Files 718096 , folders 4AA3DF , opacity 0.88 Graphite Mono Near monochrome files and folders with semantic smart colours. 7B8796 , saturation 0.18, colour only High Visibility Maximum opacity, extra brightness and propagated badges. Folders E0A82E , saturation 1.2, brightness 1.18 Minimal Muted monochrome artwork with tooltip only smart explanations. 8993A1 , saturation 0, opacity 0.72, arrows hidden Built in profiles keep your custom associations and smart rules. Applying a saved or imported profile replaces them with the profile's own. "},{"t":"Smart detection","d":"Content-aware badges, colours and explanations in the Explorer, the built-in rules, custom rules and workspace scans.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/smart-detection.html","h":["Turn it on or off","Choose how matches appear","Explain, refresh and apply","Built-in folder rules","Built-in file rules","Category colours","Custom rules","Scan the workspace for folder icons","Bounds and exclusions","Result"],"x":" Smart detection looks at a folder's direct contents, its package dependencies, or the start of a small text file, and adds an Explorer decoration : a badge of up to two characters, a category colour and a hover explanation. For example, a folder containing Cargo.toml gets the badge RS and the explanation \"Rust project\". Decorations sit on top of the base icon; they do not replace its SVG. They run only while one of the Auric Artisan File Icons themes is active. On the Workspace tab, tick or clear Enable smart detection . Run Auric Artisan File Icons: Toggle Smart Icon Detection . VS Code confirms \"Smart icon detection enabled\" or \"disabled\". Set auricFileIcons.smart.enabled . Folder detection and file detection can be switched separately with auricFileIcons.smart.folders and auricFileIcons.smart.files . Run Auric Artisan File Icons: Configure Smart Icon Detection or Configure on the Workspace tab . The menu offers: Item Effect Enable / Disable smart detection Toggles detection for this workspace. Badge and color Badge plus category colour default . Badge only Badge without colour. Color only Category colour without a badge. Tooltip only Only the hover explanation. Refresh smart ma"},{"t":"Auric Artisan File Icons reference","d":"Every command, setting, menu, view, theme, colour and Studio control in Auric Artisan File Icons 0.1.1.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/reference.html","h":["File icon themes","Commands","Menus","Views","Settings","Theme colours","File Icon Studio controls","Artwork and mappings","Diagnostics report","Limits"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.1.1 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Theme name Theme ID Artwork Auric Artisan File Icons: Facet auric artisan file icons facet 500 SVGs Auric Artisan File Icons: Playful auric artisan file icons playful 500 SVGs Auric Artisan File Icons: Modern auric artisan modern icon 464 SVGs Category in the Command Palette: Auric Artisan File Icons . Command ID What it does Activate Facet Icon Theme auricFileIcons.activate Sets Facet as the file icon theme. Activate Playful Icon Theme auricFileIcons.activatePlayful Sets Playful as the file icon theme. Activate Modern Icon Theme auricFileIcons.activateModern Sets Modern as the file icon theme. Open File Icon Studio auricFileIcons.openStudio Opens the Studio editor tab beside the editor. Open File Icon Studio Settings auricFileIcons.configure The Configure Auric Artisan File Icons menu. Choose Folder Color auricFileIcons.pickFolderColor Folder colour presets or a custom hex. Toggle Explorer Arrows auricFileIcons.toggleExplorerArrows Shows or hides the Explorer chevrons. Insert Icon into Code… auricFileIcons.quickInsert Picker of icons in the active style; inserts in insertFormat . Set File or Fol"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Diagnostics"],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The Explorer still uses another icon set. Browsing a style in the Studio only previews it. Select Use … in Explorer , or choose the theme in Preferences: File Icon Theme . Colours or associations have not changed. VS Code caches icon themes until a reload. Accept the reload prompt, or run Developer: Reload Window . Still no change after reloading. Workspace or folder settings override user settings. Check .vscode/settings.json for auricFileIcons. values. Duplicate Auric themes or actions. The old standalone Playful extension is still installed, or Auric Icons: Modern also provides a Modern theme. Disable the old Playful extension. See Modern and older Playful settings modern and legacy.md . The Auric File Icons Explorer submenu has only Open File Icon Studio . The other actions need an Auric file icon theme to be active. Activate Facet, Playful or Modern. No Insert action, or \"No editor target\". No writable text editor is open. Open and click into a writable file first; Copy works without one. A token hover does not appear. The token is incomplete, hovers are off, or VS Code's editor hovers are disabled. Use a complete token copied from the inspec"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need another icon extension?","Can I use two styles at once?","Why do changes need a reload?","Does smart detection change the icon itself?","Does it run my project's code?","Can I use the icons in my own projects?","Is the Playful style the same as Auric Icons: Playful?","How is this different from Icon Studio?"],"x":" No. All three styles and their artwork are included. No. VS Code allows one file icon theme at a time. Switch whenever you like. VS Code caches icon themes. The extension rebuilds the theme when you change appearance or associations; a reload shows the new icons. No. It adds a badge, colour and explanation on top. Use Apply Detected Folder Icon or Scan Workspace for Folder Icons to make a detected icon permanent. No. Smart detection reads a bounded number of names and the start of small text files. It never executes anything. You can insert them into code from the Studio. The artwork is covered by the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence, which restricts redistribution, resale, republishing and extracting bundled artwork. Review it before reusing artwork outside the extension. No. They are different artwork. See Modern and older Playful settings modern and legacy.md not the same playful . File Icons changes your Explorer and offers its own file type artwork for code. Auric Artisan Icon Studio is a general icon and emoji browser and does not change the Explorer. See the comparison ../others/related.md . "},{"t":"Auric Artisan File Icons: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for Auric Artisan File Icons: terms, commands, limits, a comparison with the other Auric icon extensions, the release history and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in File Icons. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Commands, menus and in Studio keys. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the themes, smart detection and code output can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Icon Studio, Icon Hub, the Auric collections, Emoji and Icon Pack. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is read, stored and never sent. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Commands, context menus and in-Studio keys in Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keys inside File Icon Studio","Commands","Context menus"],"x":" File Icons has no default keybindings. Open Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts , search for \"Auric Artisan File Icons\" and assign keys to the commands you use most, such as Insert Icon into Code… or Open File Icon Studio . Key Action / Focus the icon search Arrow Up / Arrow Down Move through picker options Home / End First or last option Escape Close an open picker or the inspector Type \"Auric Artisan File Icons\" in the Command Palette. Group Commands Themes Activate Facet Icon Theme; Activate Playful Icon Theme; Activate Modern Icon Theme Studio Open File Icon Studio; Open File Icon Studio Settings; Insert Icon into Code… Appearance Choose Folder Color; Toggle Explorer Arrows; Restore Icon Defaults Associations Set File or Folder Icon; Clear Custom File or Folder Icon Smart detection Configure Smart Icon Detection; Refresh Smart Icon Matches; Explain Smart Icon Match; Toggle Smart Icon Detection; Apply Detected Folder Icon; Scan Workspace for Folder Icons Profiles Apply Icon Profile; Save Current Icon Profile; Delete Saved Icon Profile; Export Icon Profile to Clipboard; Import Icon Profile from Clipboard Other Show Icon Theme Diagnostics; Import Legacy Playful Settings…; Import"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Association A rule mapping an extension, filename, folder name or pattern to an icon ID. Badge Up to two characters shown beside a resource in the Explorer by smart detection. Decoration A badge, colour or tooltip VS Code adds to an Explorer item. Direct parent The folder immediately containing a file or folder; parent/name patterns only match this. Exclusion A folder name or pattern that smart detection never inspects. Facet The faceted Explorer style with 500 SVGs. File icon theme The set of icons VS Code shows beside files and folders. One is active at a time. Folder pair The closed and open versions of one folder icon. Framework pack Extra Modern associations for Angular, NestJS, React or Vue. Hover token Text such as :icon file typescript: that a code hover can replace with artwork. Icon ID The name of a shipped icon, such as test or database , used as an association value. Inspector The dialog showing a card's exact code output. Modern The Explorer style with 464 SVGs, shared with Auric Icons: Modern's theme ID. Playful The Explorer style with 500 SVGs and its own palette. Not the Auric Icons: Playful library. Profile A named, portable set of appearance, associa"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the File Icons themes, smart detection and code output can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Themes","Smart detection","Code output","Licence"],"x":" Only one file icon theme can be active in VS Code. Appearance and association changes need a window reload. Parent patterns match the direct parent only, not a recursive path. The asset totals include open folder states, framework artwork and alternatives; they are not counts of unique file types. Detection is a heuristic based on names, dependencies and the start of small files. It can miss projects or match unexpectedly; use Explain Smart Icon Match to see why. By default it considers up to 250 direct entries per folder and text files up to 64 KiB, cached for 15 seconds. The workspace scan checks up to 80 first level folders. Decorations supplement the icon; they do not replace the artwork dynamically. VS Code limits badges to two characters. Availability in remote and virtual workspaces depends on the file system provider. Output uses shipped artwork; Explorer appearance settings are not applied to it. Insertion adds no surrounding quotes and does not save the file. Check the insertion context and add meaningful alternative text where needed. Free to install and use under the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence. It is not an open source or unrestricted asset licence: redistribution,"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan File Icons reads, stores and writes, and confirmation that it has no telemetry.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/privacy.html","h":["What is stored","Diagnostics"],"x":" No account or telemetry. The extension does not automatically contact a server, run shell commands or execute workspace code. Website links open only when you select them. Bounded inspection. Smart detection reads up to 250 direct folder entries and text files up to 64 KiB by default, caches results for 15 seconds, and skips excluded, binary, oversized and unavailable files. Remote aware access. Inspection goes through VS Code's file system interface, which covers local, remote and virtual resources. What can be read or written depends on the provider. Explicit edits. Code is inserted only after your action, and hover actions check that the document has not changed. Data Where Appearance settings Your VS Code settings under auricFileIcons. user level when set from the Studio . Associations from the Explorer, smart style choices and scan results The workspace settings. Saved profiles VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Rebuilt theme files after customisation Inside the extension's own folder; the shipped artwork is not modified. Show Icon Theme Diagnostics writes counts and settings to a local output channel. It omits filenames and file contents and sends nothing anywhere."},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.1 — 22 September 2026","0.1.0 — 19 September 2026","Earlier Facet releases"],"x":" The current Marketplace version. Modern added as a third Explorer style, keeping its theme ID, its 464 SVG assets, light alternatives and four framework packs. 219 Modern file designs and 114 folder pairs in the Studio, sidebar, search, code inspector and hover insertion. Shared appearance controls now cover Modern, including three digit hex colours. A confirmed, scope preserving import of Modern's file settings that does not change its general library. A new README with a quick start, style comparison, screenshots, insertion guides, migration steps and troubleshooting. The Explorer activation button now shows Modern when Modern artwork is selected. The unified File Icon Studio, starting a new version series. The separate Playful project joined this extension, keeping the Facet and Playful theme IDs and all 500 Playful SVGs. Shared appearance settings, associations, smart decorations and profile tools across styles. A confirmed, non overwriting import of old Playful settings and exported Playful profiles. Matching editor tab and sidebar workspaces with Library , Appearance and Workspace sections, file and folder filters, open folder previews and progressive loading. Card actions, "},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How File Icons compares with Icon Studio, Icon Hub, the Auric icon collections, Emoji and the Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File Icons","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-icons/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","Which should I install?","How the Auric collections merge","Other related products"],"x":" Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network File Icons ../README.md Explorer file and folder icons in three styles, plus File Icon Studio. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes: Auric Icons: Modern 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Seven open source sets with colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Modern, Playful, Drawn and Emoji together. Through Modern None of its own Needs"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Icon Pack","d":"What the Auric Artisan Icon Pack is, what it installs, how to get it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Icon Pack is a standard VS Code extension pack : a single Marketplace entry that installs four Auric Artisan extensions together. It has no interface, commands or settings of its own. Installing the pack adds Auric Icons: Modern , Auric Icons: Playful , Auric Artisan Emoji and Auric Icons: Drawn . Once installed, Modern, Drawn and Playful share one icon library view, and Emoji keeps its own Emoji Studio. Each member keeps its own version, settings, licence and update cycle, and you can manage, disable or remove each one separately in the Extensions view. The pack does not include Auric Artisan Icon Studio the all in one catalog or Auric Artisan File Icons Explorer file and folder themes . Anyone who wants the four Auric creative libraries in one step. Teams who want to recommend one install to colleagues. Item Value Marketplace listing https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack Extension ID auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack Current version 0.1.0 Requires Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later, and access to the extension marketplace Price Free text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack 1. Open the Ex"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Icon Pack guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Icon Pack guides folder.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" The Icon Pack only installs other extensions, so its guides are short. For how to use each library, follow the links to the included extensions. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install the pack, check the four members and open them. reference.md reference.md The included extensions, requirements and what the pack does and does not contain. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Members that did not install, alternative marketplaces and local builds. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with the Icon Pack","d":"Install the Icon Pack, confirm its four member extensions and start using them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install the pack","2. Check the members","3. Start using them","Result"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later. You need access to the extension marketplace. The pack downloads its members from it. 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X . 2. Search for Auric Artisan Icon Pack and select Install . Or run code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan icon pack in a terminal, or use Extensions: Install from VSIX… with an official pack download. 1. Select the pack in the Extensions view. 2. Open its Extension Pack section. It lists: Auric Icons: Modern auric artisan.auric artisan modern icon Auric Icons: Playful auric artisan.auric icons playful Auric Artisan Emoji auric artisan.auric artisan emoji Auric Icons: Drawn auric artisan.auric icons drawn 3. Each should show as installed. To Do this Browse Modern, Drawn and Playful icons Select the Auric icon library in the Activity Bar: one merged library with a Library filter. Insert an icon from the keyboard Press Ctrl + Alt + I in a text editor. Insert an emoji Press Ctrl + Alt + J , or open Auric Emoji in the Activity Bar. Change your Explorer icons Run Preferences: File Icon Theme and choose Auric Icons: Modern . How the three icon libraries share one view is explained in The merged Icon Stud"},{"t":"Icon Pack reference","d":"The extensions included in Auric Artisan Icon Pack 0.1.0, its requirements and what it does and does not contain.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/docs/reference.html","h":["Included extensions","What the pack itself contains","Requirements","Not included","Licence"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.1.0 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Extension ID What it adds Auric Icons: Modern auric artisan.auric artisan modern icon 720 Modern and Sharp library icons, plus the Modern Explorer file icon theme. Auric Icons: Playful auric artisan.auric icons playful 1,225 emoji style icons in Color, Outline, Filled and Small. Auric Artisan Emoji auric artisan.auric artisan emoji Emoji Studio: 1,914 emoji, skin tones, shortcodes and editor insertion. Auric Icons: Drawn auric artisan.auric icons drawn 480 hand drawn icons in Color, Mono, Outline and Duotone. The pack uses the current publishing IDs. It does not install the retired auric artisan icons or auric artisan svg icons extensions. Item Present Commands None Settings None Views or keybindings None Background service or installer None Telemetry or workspace edits None Embedded copies of member extensions No; members are downloaded from the marketplace Requirement Value VS Code 1.85 or later Network Marketplace access to download members Category Extension Packs Extension Why you might want it Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md The separate all in one catalo"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"What to do when a pack member did not install, or when using alternative marketplaces or local builds.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do An included extension did not install. A network problem, an organisation policy, or an older VS Code version blocked it. Open the pack's Extension Pack section, find the missing member and check its installation error. Verify marketplace access and that VS Code is 1.85 or later. I installed the pack VSIX offline and the members are missing. A pack VSIX is not an offline bundle; it only lists the members. Connect to the marketplace, or install each member's own VSIX. I use an alternative marketplace and members are missing. Each member must be published there under the same ID. Check whether each member is available in your marketplace. Installing the pack does not move extensions between registries. I installed local development builds and the pack reinstalls members. VS Code identifies extensions by publisher and name, not folder name. Confirm your builds use the exact IDs listed in the reference reference.md . I only see one icon library view, not three. Modern, Drawn and Playful merge into one library when co installed. This is expected. Use the Library filter to pick a collection. An icon library view disappeared after installing Icon Studio."},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/docs/faq.html","h":["Is the pack another icon browser?","Does it work offline?","Does it include Icon Studio or File Icons?","Do the members update with the pack?","Can I uninstall one member?","Why are Modern, Drawn and Playful shown as one library?"],"x":" No. It only tells VS Code which four extensions to install. It adds no commands, views or settings. The members work offline once installed. Installing the pack needs marketplace access. No. Install them separately if you need them. See the reference reference.md not included . Each member updates on its own schedule through the marketplace. Yes. Manage each member individually in the Extensions view. They are designed to merge into one library when installed together. See The merged Icon Studio ../../auric icons modern/docs/merged icon studio.md . "},{"t":"Icon Pack: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for the Auric Artisan Icon Pack. The pack has no commands or keyboard shortcuts, so there is no shortcuts page; see each member extension for its shortcuts. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used on these pages. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the pack is and is not. related.md related.md Comparison of all Auric icon extensions. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What the pack does with your data. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Terms used in the Auric Artisan Icon Pack documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Extension pack A VS Code extension whose only job is to install a list of other extensions. Member One of the extensions an extension pack installs. Extension ID The unique publisher and name identifier of an extension, such as auric artisan.auric icons drawn . Marketplace The online registry VS Code installs extensions from. VSIX A packaged extension file that can be installed with Extensions: Install from VSIX… . Merged library The single icon library view shown when Modern, Drawn and Playful are installed together. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Auric Artisan Icon Pack is and what it does not do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" The pack is metadata only. It does not embed its members' VSIX files, duplicate their artwork or run an installer. A pack VSIX is not an offline bundle; installing needs marketplace access. If a member is unavailable in your marketplace or blocked by policy, the pack cannot install it. The exact interface you get depends on the member versions VS Code installs. Icon Studio and File Icons are not included. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Auric Artisan Icon Pack does with your data.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" The pack itself runs no code. It adds no telemetry, background service or workspace edits, and stores nothing. VS Code contacts the extension marketplace to download the four members, as it does for any extension. Each member has its own privacy behaviour: Auric Icons: Modern — Privacy ../../auric icons modern/others/privacy.md Auric Icons: Playful — Privacy ../../auric icons playful/others/privacy.md Auric Artisan Emoji — Privacy ../../auric artisan emoji/others/privacy.md Auric Icons: Drawn — Privacy ../../auric icons drawn/others/privacy.md "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 — 22 September 2026"],"x":" The first Auric Artisan Icon Pack, and the current Marketplace version. Groups Auric Icons: Modern, Auric Icons: Playful, Auric Artisan Emoji and Auric Icons: Drawn into one standard VS Code extension pack. Uses the active Playful and Drawn extension IDs instead of retired ones. Adds a gold Auric bundle icon, installation guidance and marketplace troubleshooting. Contains metadata only: no runtime code, background service or custom downloader. "},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How the Icon Pack's members compare with Icon Studio, Icon Hub and File Icons.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Pack","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-pack/others/related.html","h":["How the pack's icon libraries merge"],"x":" Extension In the pack Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Yes Modern icon library plus the Modern file icon theme. Yes 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Yes Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Yes Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Artisan Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Yes Emoji Studio. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md No One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md No Seven open source sets with colour controls, sprite and ZIP export, CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md No Explorer file and folder icons in three styles. Yes 1,464 SVG assets None With Modern, Drawn and Playful installed together, one of them hosts a single library with a Library filter and collection badges; the others hide their views. If you later install Icon Studio, it hosts al"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Modern","d":"What the Auric Icons: Modern extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Icons: Modern is two things in one VS Code extension. First, it is an original library of 720 modern SVG icons in two families, Simple Modern and Sharp Modern , each available in Color , Mono , Outline and Duotone variants. You search the library in an Icon Library view and insert icons into your code in a format that suits the file. Second, it is a file and folder icon theme for the VS Code Explorer, also called Auric Icons: Modern . The theme has 408 icons with a distinct file silhouette, true open and closed folder pairs, semantic colours, four framework packs Angular, NestJS, React and Redux, Vue and Pinia and custom associations. You can re tint folders, adjust saturation and opacity, and hide the Explorer arrows. Modern can be installed alone or alongside its sibling extensions Auric Icons: Drawn and Auric Icons: Playful . When they are installed together they show one shared library, labelled Icon Studio , with a Library filter and a badge on each card showing where it comes from. Developers who want a crisp, consistent Explorer icon theme that works at the 16 pixel Explorer size. Front end developers and designers who insert SVG icons into components, pages, styleshe"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Modern guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Icons: Modern guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Icons: Modern. The extension has two parts, the Explorer file icon theme and the Icon Library, and each has its own guide. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, turn on the file icon theme, open the Icon Library and insert a first icon. file icon theme.md file icon theme.md Folder colour, framework packs, saturation, opacity, arrows, associations and workspace detection. icon library.md icon library.md Search, filters, variants, preview surfaces, the smart guide and recommendations. insert copy and save.md insert copy and save.md Insert and smart insert, nine copy formats, save, open source and hover previews. merged icon studio.md merged icon studio.md How Modern, Drawn, Playful and Icon Studio share one library. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, keybinding, icon ID and control. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Icons: Modern","d":"Install Auric Icons: Modern, turn on its file icon theme, open the Icon Library and insert your first icon.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Turn on the file icon theme","3. Personalise the theme","4. Open the Icon Library","5. Insert your first icon","Result","Next steps"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later, or an editor that keeps VS Code's extension and icon theme features. Everything works offline. The extension has no telemetry and makes no network requests. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Icons: Modern and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan modern icon 1. Open the Command Palette Ctrl + Shift + P . 2. Run Preferences: File Icon Theme . 3. Choose Auric Icons: Modern . Or run Auric Icons: Modern: Activate Icon Theme . The Explorer now shows Modern file and folder icons. Folders use the Auric gold by default, and open folders have their own open artwork. Note: If you also have Auric Artisan File Icons installed, it offers a Modern style under the same theme ID. See Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . 1. Run Auric Icons: Modern: Configure… . 2. Choose Folder colour and pick a colour, for example Teal . 3. VS Code shows \"Auric Icons: Modern updated — … Reload to apply?\". Select Reload Window . See Use the file icon theme file icon theme.md for every option. 1. Select Auric Icons: Modern in the Activity Bar. The Icon Library view opens. 2. Or run Auric Icons: Modern: O"},{"t":"Use the file icon theme","d":"Activate the Modern Explorer icon theme and set folder colour, framework packs, saturation, opacity, arrows, custom associations and workspace detection.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/file-icon-theme.html","h":["Activate the theme","How changes are applied","The Configure menu","Folder colour","Framework packs","Saturation, opacity and arrows","Custom associations","Auric Artisan workspace icons","Restore defaults","Result"],"x":" A file icon theme decides which icon VS Code shows beside each file and folder in the Explorer, tabs and other lists. The Modern theme has 408 icons designed for the 16 pixel Explorer size. It maps 265 file extensions, 462 exact filenames and 265 folder names, with separate open and closed artwork for folders and light theme alternatives for monochrome marks. Run Preferences: File Icon Theme and choose Auric Icons: Modern , or Run Auric Icons: Modern: Activate Icon Theme . VS Code reads an icon theme once and caches it. When you change a Modern setting, the extension rebuilds its theme files. If the theme is active, you see \"Auric Icons: Modern updated — {summary}. Reload to apply?\". Select Reload Window to see the change, or Later to keep working. The original artwork is never modified, so any change can be undone by restoring defaults. A default install writes nothing and asks for no reload. Settings changed while VS Code was closed, or synced from another machine, are applied at start up. Run Auric Icons: Modern: Configure… . The menu shows the current value of each item. Item What it does Folder colour Opens the folder colour list below . Icon pack Opens the framework pack lis"},{"t":"Browse the Icon Library","d":"Search the 720-icon Modern library, filter by category, style and library, switch variants and preview surfaces, and use the smart guide and recommendations.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/icon-library.html","h":["Open the library","The screen","Search","Variants and Auto","Preview surface","The views","Recommendations","Cards","Density and batch size","Result"],"x":" The Icon Library holds 720 original icons: 420 Simple Modern and 300 Sharp Modern , across 33 categories such as Coding and development, Data and databases, Cybersecurity, Accessibility and Space and Astronomy. Every icon comes in four variants: Color , Mono , Outline and Duotone . Sidebar: select Auric Icons: Modern in the Activity Bar to open the Icon Library view. Editor tab: run Auric Icons: Modern: Open Icon Library , select the ↗ button Open full explorer in the view, or select the open preview icon in the view's title bar. The tab is called Icon Studio — Library . Area What it does Header \"Icon Studio\", Icon Library , a count line such as \"720 icons · 72 loaded\", and the ↗ button. Smart guide Up to four tip cards, such as \"TypeScript detected\" or \"Like icons you reuse\". Dismiss a tip with its × button. Turn the guide off with auricIcons.library.showGuide . Search Placeholder \"Search 720 icons — try “empty state” or “auth”\". Library Only shown when several collections are merged. All libraries or one collection. Category All categories or one category. Style All styles , Modern or Sharp . Variant Auto , Color , Mono , Outline , Duotone . Preview surface Auto , Light , Dark ."},{"t":"Insert, copy and save icons","d":"Insert Modern icons with language-aware output, copy them in nine formats, save SVG files, open the source and preview icon IDs on hover.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/insert-copy-and-save.html","h":["Insert from the Icon Library","Smart insert","Copy in a chosen format","Save an SVG file","Open the SVG source","Other Command Palette actions","Hover previews","Result"],"x":" 1. Open a file in a text editor and place one or more cursors, or select text to replace. 2. In the Icon Library, select Insert on a card. 3. The icon is inserted at every cursor. Multi line output keeps the indentation of the cursor's line. If no text editor is open, you see \"Open a text editor before inserting an SVG.\" When you work in the full editor tab library, the icon goes into the first visible file editor. With auricIcons.library.smartInsert on the default , Insert adapts to the language of the file: Editing in Output JavaScript, TypeScript, React JSX and TSX, MDX JSX element HTML, PHP, Handlebars, Vue, Svelte, Astro HTML markup Markdown Markdown image CSS, SCSS, Less CSS background JSON, JSONC, YAML, Python Data URI XML, SVG and any other language Raw SVG With the setting off, Insert always inserts raw SVG. The Smart Insert Icon command always adapts, whatever the setting. 1. In a text editor, press Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I on macOS , or run Auric Icons: Modern: Smart Insert Icon matches active language . 2. A list opens. With no search text, it starts with Recommended for this file , then All icons . Each row shows the category and tags and the collection when sever"},{"t":"The merged Icon Studio","d":"How Auric Icons: Modern, Drawn and Playful merge into one Icon Studio library when co-installed, and how Auric Artisan Icon Studio takes over hosting.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/merged-icon-studio.html","h":["What you see with two or three collections installed","Likes, recents and recommendations","Hover previews","When Auric Artisan Icon Studio is installed","Which extension is the host?","Result"],"x":" Auric Icons: Modern, Auric Icons: Drawn and Auric Icons: Playful are three extensions built on the same library. Each works on its own. When you install more than one, they cooperate so you get one library instead of duplicate sidebars. 1. One extension automatically becomes the host . The choice is made the same way every time, so it does not change from one start up to the next unless you install, update or remove a collection. 2. The host shows one Icon Library view headed \"Icon Studio\" that contains every installed collection. 3. A Library filter appears, with All libraries and one entry per collection, each with its icon count. 4. Every card shows a badge naming its collection, for example Drawn , with the tooltip \"From the Drawn library\". 5. The Variant buttons offer every variant any installed collection provides: Color, Mono, Outline and Duotone from Modern and Drawn, plus Filled and Small from Playful. If a collection does not have the selected variant, its cards fall back to Color. 6. The other extensions hide their Activity Bar view, their Command Palette entries and their Ctrl + Alt + I and Ctrl + Alt + R shortcuts. If you run one of their commands for example from a k"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Modern reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, icon ID, pack, category and library control in Auric Icons: Modern 0.12.1.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","File icon theme contents","Icon IDs for associations","Icon Library contents","Library controls","Limits","Messages you may see"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.12.1 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Icons: Modern . Command ID What it does Configure… auricIcons.configure Menu for folder colour, icon pack, arrows, saturation, opacity, detection and restore. Select Icon Pack auricIcons.selectIconPack Choose None, Angular, NestJS, React / Redux or Vue / Pinia. Select Folder Colour auricIcons.selectFolderColor Choose a preset or custom hex folder colour. Toggle Explorer Arrows auricIcons.toggleExplorerArrows Show or hide the Explorer chevrons. Detect Auric Artisan Workspace auricIcons.detectWorkspace Report whether the workspace has .auric artisan/ or .auricignore . Restore Default Settings auricIcons.restoreDefaults Clear all Modern theme settings. Activate Icon Theme auricIcons.activate Set Auric Icons: Modern as the file icon theme. Command ID What it does Open Icon Library auricIcons.library.openExplorer Opens the Icon Studio — Library editor tab. Search Icons auricIcons.library.searchIcons Choose an icon, then an action. Insert SVG at Cursor auricIcons.library.insertSvg Choose an icon and insert it. Smart Insert Icon matches active language auricIcons."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with the Modern file icon theme and Icon Library.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["File icon theme","Icon Library","Still stuck"],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do A setting change does not show in the Explorer. VS Code caches icon themes until the window reloads. Select Reload Window in the prompt, or run Developer: Reload Window . No reload prompt appears. The prompt only appears when Modern is the active file icon theme. Activate the theme first with Activate Icon Theme . \"could not apply customisation — … The default icons remain active.\" A value could not be applied, for example an invalid colour. Check the value in Settings; folder colour must be default or a three or six digit hex colour. A custom association shows a blank icon. The value is not one of the theme's icon IDs. Use an ID from the reference reference.md icon ids for associations . A workspace setting does not seem to apply. The extension's own commands write user level settings; a workspace value may override them. Check the workspace settings.json for auricIcons. values. The file icon theme picker lists two Modern entries. Auric Artisan File Icons also contributes a Modern style Auric Artisan File Icons: Modern with the same theme ID. Choose one extension to manage Modern and use its settings. See the note below. The workspace detection o"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Icons: Modern.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/docs/faq.html","h":["Is it free?","Do I have to use both the theme and the library?","Why does changing a setting need a reload?","Does folder colour change file icons too?","Can I use two framework packs at once?","What is the difference between Modern and Sharp?","How is this different from Auric Artisan File Icons?","Does Modern need the internet?","Where did the hand-drawn icons go?"],"x":" Yes. It is free to install and use for any purpose, personal or commercial. Redistribution, republishing and resale are not permitted. No. The file icon theme and the Icon Library are independent. Use either or both. VS Code reads icon themes once and caches them. The extension rebuilds the theme files when you change a setting, and a window reload shows the result. No. It re tints folders only. File icons keep the semantic colours that identify them. Use saturation and opacity to tone down all icons. No. One pack is active at a time. They are the two style families in the 720 icon library: 420 Simple Modern icons and 300 Sharp Modern icons. Filter by Style to see one family. File Icons offers three Explorer styles Facet, Playful and Modern with its own studio, smart decorations and profiles. This extension offers the Modern Explorer theme plus the 720 icon library. See the comparison ../others/related.md . No. It has no network access and no telemetry at runtime. Since version 0.4.0 the hand drawn Warm Drawn icons live in Auric Icons: Drawn . Install it alongside Modern to browse both in one library. "},{"t":"Auric Icons: Modern: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Icons: Modern.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for Auric Icons: Modern: the terms it uses, its shortcuts, what it can and cannot do, how it compares with the other Auric icon extensions, its release history and its privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the theme and library. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings and every command. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the theme and library can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons and the other collections. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, in-view keys and every command in Auric Icons: Modern.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys in the Icon Library","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Smart Insert Icon Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I Insert from Recent Ctrl + Alt + R Cmd + Alt + R Both need a focused text editor, and are only active while Modern hosts the library they step aside when Auric Artisan Icon Studio or a sibling collection hosts . Key Action / Focus search Escape Clear search; close a dropdown Arrow Up / Arrow Down Move between dropdown options Type \"Auric Icons: Modern\" in the Command Palette. Command Area Configure… Theme Select Icon Pack Theme Select Folder Colour Theme Toggle Explorer Arrows Theme Detect Auric Artisan Workspace Theme Restore Default Settings Theme Activate Icon Theme Theme Open Icon Library Library Search Icons Library Insert SVG at Cursor Library Smart Insert Icon matches active language Library Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag Library Insert from Likes Library Insert from Recent Library Toggle Like for an Icon Library Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations Library Copy SVG Library Save SVG As… Library Open SVG Source Library Older keybindings that use auricArtisanIcons. command IDs still work as aliases for the Library commands. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Icons: Modern.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Association A rule that maps a file extension, filename or folder name to an icon. Auto variant A variant choice that follows the language of the file you are editing. Catalog path The relative location of an icon file inside the bundled catalog. Data URI Text that embeds a file directly, starting data:image/svg+xml, . Duotone A variant drawn in two tones. Explorer arrows The chevrons beside folders in the Explorer that expand and collapse them. File icon theme The set of icons VS Code shows beside files and folders. Only one is active at a time. Framework pack Extra file icons for one framework's file types, such as Angular components or Vue composables. Host The one extension that shows the shared library when several Auric collections are installed. Icon ID The unique name of an icon. Library IDs end in a four digit number, such as analytics bar chart 0042 ; theme IDs are short names such as typescript . Icon Studio The heading of the shared library view, and also the name of the separate Auric Artisan Icon Studio extension. Mono A single colour variant. Preview surface The light, dark or automatic backdrop behind library cards. Semantic colour A colour that identi"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Modern file icon theme and Icon Library can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["File icon theme","Icon Library","Licence"],"x":" Icon themes match file and folder names without path context. A name such as settings.json cannot be given a special icon for one folder only, which is why .auric artisan/settings.json has no dedicated icon. Association keys are either .ext or an exact name. Wildcards in the middle of a name and folder paths are not supported. Changes need a window reload to appear. Workspace detection checks only the top of local workspace folders; remote and virtual folders are skipped. Only one framework pack can be active. Colour is never the only cue: each icon also has a distinct shape, so icons stay distinguishable at low saturation. The library is fixed to the installed version: 720 icons. New icons come with updates. Smart insert picks a format by language only, not by the exact cursor position. Check quotes and surrounding code. Recommendations are local rankings from the file you are editing and your likes and use, not an AI service. Hover previews recognise only Modern library IDs a hyphenated name ending in four digits . There are no size, colour or stroke controls for output; icons are inserted as drawn. Icon Studio and Icon Hub offer output controls. Free to use for any purpose. Red"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Icons: Modern stores, where, and confirmation that it makes no network requests.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/privacy.html","h":["What is stored","What the extension reads","What the extension writes"],"x":" Auric Icons: Modern runs entirely inside VS Code. It has no telemetry, no account and no network access at runtime. Data Where Theme and library settings Your VS Code settings under auricIcons. . A rebuilt copy of the theme when you customise it Inside the extension's own installation folder. The original artwork is never changed. Likes up to 500 , recent icons up to 60 , learned preferences and dismissed guide tips VS Code's extension storage on this machine. \"Don't ask again\" for workspace detection VS Code's storage for that workspace. Library search, filters, variant and preview surface The view's saved state in VS Code. To offer the theme in Auric Artisan workspaces, it checks whether .auric artisan or .auricignore exists at the top of each local workspace folder. It does not read their contents or walk your folders. For recommendations and smart insert, it reads the language, file name and up to about 60 lines around the cursor in the active editor. This stays in memory. Inserting changes your editor content. Copying writes to the clipboard. Saving writes a file only where you choose in a save dialog. Its own commands update your user settings. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Icons: Modern, from its first release to 0.12.1.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.12.1","0.12.0","0.11.0","0.4.0","0.3.0","0.2.0","0.1.0"],"x":" The current Marketplace version. Now covered by the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence 2.0 instead of MIT. The extension stays free to install and use for any purpose, personal or commercial. Redistribution, republishing to any marketplace, resale and derivative releases are no longer permitted. Marketplace README images now display correctly on the Marketplace page and in VS Code's extension view. Future Auric icon collections can join the shared library without every extension being updated. The library view, palette entries and shared shortcuts are disabled while another icon collection or Auric Artisan Icon Studio hosts the library. New Marketplace artwork. The shared library gained keyboard and pointer enlargement and a remembered Auto , Light or Dark preview surface. Verified the file theme alone and in every co install combination. Display name changed to Auric Icons: Modern . Extension ID, command IDs, settings and theme ID are unchanged. The library now carries the 720 modern icons Simple Modern and Sharp Modern . The 480 hand drawn icons moved to Auric Icons: Drawn . Co install cooperation: with Drawn or Playful installed, one library appears, with a Library filter and sourc"},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Auric Icons: Modern compares with Drawn, Playful, Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons, Emoji and the Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Modern","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-modern/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","How the three collections merge","Modern in File Icons","Retired extensions","Other related pages"],"x":" Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Auric Icons: Modern ../README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes: Auric Icons: Modern 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Seven open source sets with colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Explorer file and folder icons in three styles, plus File Icon Studio. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Modern, Playful, Drawn and Emoji together. Through Modern None of its own"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Drawn","d":"What the Auric Icons: Drawn extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Icons: Drawn is a library of 480 original hand drawn SVG icons for VS Code, in a style called Warm Drawn : organic geometry with friendly imperfections. Every icon comes in Color , Mono , Outline and Duotone variants, across 30 categories from Coding and development to Music and Audio. You browse the icons in an Icon Library view, search them by concept, description, tag or synonym, and insert them into your code in a format that suits the file: a JSX element in React, markup in HTML, a CSS background in stylesheets, an image in Markdown. You can also copy icons in nine formats, save SVG files and preview icon IDs by hovering over them in code. Drawn is a library only. It deliberately does not include a file icon theme for the Explorer, because its 64 pixel illustration style does not suit 16 pixel Explorer icons. Install Auric Icons: Modern alongside it for the family's Explorer theme; the two libraries then merge into one view. Front end developers and designers who want warm, illustrative icons for interfaces, documentation and empty states. Anyone who already uses Auric Icons: Modern or Playful and wants a third artwork style in the same library. Item Value Marketplace l"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Drawn guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Icons: Drawn guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Icons: Drawn, a library only extension of 480 hand drawn icons. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, open the Icon Library and insert a first icon. icon library.md icon library.md Search, filters, variants, preview surfaces, the smart guide and recommendations. insert copy and save.md insert copy and save.md Insert and smart insert, nine copy formats, save, open source and hover previews. merged icon studio.md merged icon studio.md How Drawn shares one library with Modern, Playful and Icon Studio. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, keybinding, category and control. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Icons: Drawn","d":"Install Auric Icons: Drawn, open the Icon Library and insert your first hand-drawn icon.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Open the Icon Library","3. Look around","4. Insert your first icon","5. Like the icons you reuse","Result","Next steps"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later, or an editor that keeps VS Code's extension features. Everything works offline. There is no telemetry and no network access. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Icons: Drawn and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric icons drawn Select Auric Icons: Drawn in the Activity Bar to open the Icon Library view, or Run Auric Icons: Drawn: Open Icon Library to open the larger Icon Studio — Library editor tab. If Auric Artisan Icon Studio or Auric Icons: Modern is also installed, the Drawn view may be hidden because the other extension shows a merged library that already contains Drawn. See Use Drawn with Modern and Playful merged icon studio.md . The view shows a header with the icon count, up to four smart guide tips, a Search box, Category and Style filters, Variant buttons Auto , Color , Mono , Outline , Duotone , Preview surface buttons Auto , Light , Dark , the All , ✦ For you , ♥ Likes and ↺ Recent chips, a ✦ Recommended for this file rail and the icon grid. 1. Open a file and place the cursor. 2. Type calendar in Search . 3. Select Insert on a card. With smart insert on the default "},{"t":"Browse the Icon Library","d":"Search the 480 Warm Drawn icons, filter by category, switch variants and preview surfaces, and use the smart guide and recommendations.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/icon-library.html","h":["Open the library","The screen","Search","Variants and Auto","Preview surface","The views","Recommendations","Cards","Density and batch size","Result"],"x":" The Drawn library holds 480 hand drawn icons in 30 categories. Each icon is available in Color , Mono , Outline and Duotone . Sidebar: select Auric Icons: Drawn in the Activity Bar. Editor tab: run Auric Icons: Drawn: Open Icon Library , select the ↗ button Open full explorer , or the open preview icon in the view's title bar. The tab is called Icon Studio — Library . Area What it does Header \"Icon Studio\", Icon Library , a count line such as \"480 icons · 72 loaded\", and ↗ . Smart guide Up to four dismissible tips, such as \"Markdown detected\" or \"Like icons you reuse\". Turn off with auricIconsDrawn.library.showGuide . Search Placeholder \"Search 480 icons — try “empty state” or “auth”\". Library Only shown when several collections are merged. Category All categories or one of 30. Style All styles or Drawn plus other collections' styles when merged . Variant Auto , Color , Mono , Outline , Duotone . Preview surface Auto , Light , Dark . Chips All , ✦ For you , ♥ Likes count , ↺ Recent count . Recommended rail ✦ Recommended for this file , with Refresh . Grid Cards that load as you scroll. Search by concept, description, tag or synonym; results are ranked as you type and personalised "},{"t":"Insert, copy and save icons","d":"Insert Drawn icons with language-aware output, copy them in nine formats, save SVG files, open the source and preview icon IDs on hover.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/insert-copy-and-save.html","h":["Insert from the library","Smart insert","Copy in a chosen format","Save and open the source","Other commands","Hover previews","Result"],"x":" 1. Open a file and place one or more cursors, or select text to replace. 2. Select Insert on a card. 3. The icon is inserted at every cursor; multi line output keeps the cursor line's indentation. Without an open text editor you see \"Open a text editor before inserting an SVG.\" With auricIconsDrawn.library.smartInsert on the default , Insert adapts to the file: Editing in Output JavaScript, TypeScript, React JSX and TSX, MDX JSX element HTML, PHP, Handlebars, Vue, Svelte, Astro HTML markup the SVG Markdown Markdown image CSS, SCSS, Less CSS background JSON, JSONC, YAML, Python Data URI XML, SVG and any other language Raw SVG With the setting off, Insert uses raw SVG. Smart Insert Icon always adapts. From the keyboard: press Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I on macOS in a text editor, search, and choose an icon. With no search text the list starts with Recommended for this file . Run Auric Icons: Drawn: Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag , choose an icon and a format: Format What you get Raw SVG The SVG markup. JSX element The SVG with JSX attribute names. React component export function IconName props { return <svg {...props} … ; } Markdown image ! Icon name data:ima"},{"t":"Use Drawn with Modern and Playful","d":"How Drawn merges with Auric Icons: Modern and Playful into one library, and how Auric Artisan Icon Studio takes over hosting.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/merged-icon-studio.html","h":["What happens when they are co-installed","Likes and recents","Hover previews","With Auric Artisan Icon Studio","A file icon theme for Drawn","Result"],"x":" Drawn works by itself. When Auric Icons: Modern or Auric Icons: Playful is also installed, the extensions show one library instead of duplicate sidebars. 1. One extension becomes the host automatically. With the current versions, that is Modern when it is installed; with only Drawn and Playful, Drawn hosts. 2. The host's Icon Library view headed \"Icon Studio\" contains every installed collection. 3. A Library filter appears, and each card shows a badge naming its collection. 4. The Variant buttons offer every collection's variants. If a collection lacks the selected variant for example Drawn has no Filled or Small , its cards fall back to Color. 5. The other extensions hide their views, Command Palette entries and shortcuts, and forward their commands to the host. This updates on its own when you install or remove a collection. No reload is needed. Likes and recent icons are stored by the extension that owns each icon. The merged view shows them together. If you uninstall Drawn, its icons and their history leave the merged view; the other collections keep theirs. Drawn previews only Drawn icon IDs, so hovering always shows one preview. Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan "},{"t":"Auric Icons: Drawn reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, category and library control in Auric Icons: Drawn 0.12.1.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","Library contents","Library controls","Limits"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.12.1 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Icons: Drawn . Command ID What it does Open Icon Library auricIconsDrawn.library.openExplorer Opens the Icon Studio — Library editor tab. Search Icons auricIconsDrawn.library.searchIcons Choose an icon, then an action. Insert SVG at Cursor auricIconsDrawn.library.insertSvg Choose an icon and insert it. Smart Insert Icon matches active language auricIconsDrawn.library.smartInsert Choose an icon and insert with language aware output. Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag auricIconsDrawn.library.copyAs Choose an icon and one of nine formats. Insert from Likes auricIconsDrawn.library.showFavorites Choose a liked icon and insert. Insert from Recent auricIconsDrawn.library.showRecents Choose a recent icon and insert. Toggle Like for an Icon auricIconsDrawn.library.toggleFavorite Like or unlike an icon. Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations auricIconsDrawn.library.resetPersonalization Confirm, then reset personalisation. Copy SVG auricIconsDrawn.library.copySvg Choose an icon and copy raw SVG. Save SVG As… auricIconsDrawn.library.saveSvg"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The Auric Icons: Drawn view is missing from the Activity Bar. Auric Artisan Icon Studio or Auric Icons: Modern hosts the shared library, which already includes Drawn. Use the host's library and filter by Library › Drawn , or set auricIconStudio.hostFamilyLibraries to false if Icon Studio is the host. Drawn commands are missing from the Command Palette. Same reason: they hide while another extension hosts. Use the host's commands; keybindings still work. Ctrl + Alt + I does nothing. The editor is not focused, another extension hosts, or the keys are bound elsewhere. Focus a text editor and check Keyboard Shortcuts . \"Open a text editor before inserting an SVG.\" No text editor is available. Open a file, click into it and insert again. I cannot find Drawn icons in the Explorer file icon picker. Drawn has no file icon theme. Install Auric Icons: Modern or Auric Artisan File Icons for Explorer icons. A card looks like Color after choosing Filled or Small. Filled and Small are Playful variants; Drawn falls back to Color. Choose Color, Mono, Outline or Duotone for Drawn icons. The format inserted is not what I expected. Smart insert chose a format for th"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/docs/faq.html","h":["Why is there no file icon theme?","Do I need Modern or Playful too?","Is Drawn included in Icon Studio?","Is it free?","Does it work offline?","Can I change icon size or colour on insert?","Where are my likes kept?"],"x":" Drawn's icons are 64 pixel illustrations. They do not have the paired 16 pixel folder shapes and file associations a good Explorer theme needs. Install Auric Icons: Modern for the family's Explorer theme. No. Drawn works alone. Installing them together gives you one merged library. Yes. Auric Artisan Icon Studio bundles the Drawn collection, so you do not need this extension to use Drawn artwork there. Yes, free to use for any purpose. Redistribution and resale are not permitted. Yes. There is no network access or telemetry. Not in this extension; icons are inserted as drawn. Auric Artisan Icon Studio has size and colour output settings. In VS Code's storage for this extension on your machine. They stay with Drawn even when another extension hosts the merged library. "},{"t":"Auric Icons: Drawn: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for Auric Icons: Drawn: terms, shortcuts, limits, a comparison with the other Auric icon extensions, the release history and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the library. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings and every command. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the library can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Modern, Playful, Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons, Emoji and Icon Pack. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, in-view keys and every command in Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys in the Icon Library","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Smart Insert Icon Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I Insert from Recent Ctrl + Alt + R Cmd + Alt + R Both need a focused text editor and are active only while Drawn hosts the library. Key Action / Focus search Escape Clear search; close a dropdown Arrow Up / Arrow Down Move between dropdown options Type \"Auric Icons: Drawn\" in the Command Palette: Open Icon Library , Search Icons , Insert SVG at Cursor , Smart Insert Icon matches active language , Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag , Insert from Likes , Insert from Recent , Toggle Like for an Icon , Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations , Copy SVG , Save SVG As… , Open SVG Source . See the reference ../docs/reference.md commands for IDs and details. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Auto variant A variant choice that follows the language of the file you are editing. Catalog path The relative location of an icon file inside the bundled catalog. Data URI Text that embeds a file directly, starting data:image/svg+xml, . Duotone A variant drawn in two tones. Host The one extension that shows the shared library when several Auric collections are installed. Icon ID The unique name of an icon, such as files blank document drawn 0001 . Icon Studio The heading of the shared library view, and also the name of the separate Auric Artisan Icon Studio extension. Mono A single colour variant. Preview surface The light, dark or automatic backdrop behind library cards. Smart guide Tip cards at the top of the library that react to your file and usage. Smart insert Choosing the output format from the language of the file you are editing. Variant One rendering of an icon: Color, Mono, Outline or Duotone. Warm Drawn The hand drawn style of this collection: organic geometry with friendly imperfections. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Icons: Drawn can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" The library contains 480 icons at the installed version; new icons come with updates. There is no Explorer file icon theme. Icons are inserted as drawn: there are no size, colour or stroke controls for output. Smart insert picks a format from the file's language, not the exact cursor position. Check quotes and surrounding code. Recommendations are local rankings from the file you are editing and your likes and use, not an AI service. Hover previews recognise only Drawn icon IDs a hyphenated name ending in four digits . Personalisation built up in the retired \"Auric Artisan Drawing Icon\" preview extension does not transfer; each extension keeps its own storage. Licence: free to use for any purpose; redistribution, republishing, resale and derivative releases are not permitted. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Icons: Drawn stores, where, and confirmation that it makes no network requests.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Auric Icons: Drawn runs entirely inside VS Code. It has no telemetry, no account and no network access at runtime. Data Where Settings Your VS Code settings under auricIconsDrawn.library. . Likes up to 500 , recent icons up to 60 , learned preferences, dismissed tips VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Search, filters, variant and preview surface The view's saved state in VS Code. For recommendations and smart insert, the extension reads the language, file name and up to about 60 lines around the cursor of the active editor. This stays in memory and is never stored or sent. Inserting changes your editor content, copying writes to the clipboard, and saving writes a file only where you choose in a save dialog. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Icons: Drawn.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.12.1","0.12.0","0.11.0","0.1.0"],"x":" The current Marketplace version. Now covered by the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence 2.0 instead of MIT. It stays free to install and use for any purpose; redistribution, republishing to any marketplace, resale and derivative releases are no longer permitted. Marketplace README images now display correctly. Future Auric icon collections can join the shared library without every extension being updated. The library view, palette entries and shared shortcuts are disabled while another icon collection or Auric Artisan Icon Studio hosts the library. New Marketplace artwork. The shared library gained keyboard and pointer enlargement and a remembered Auto , Light or Dark preview surface. Verified alone and co installed in VS Code. Initial release: 480 hand drawn icons in four variants and 50 categories, with the Icon Library, smart search with synonyms and personalisation, smart insert Ctrl + Alt + I , nine copy formats, hover previews, likes and recents Ctrl + Alt + R and per file recommendations. Cooperates with Auric Icons: Modern and Playful: one merged library with collections badged and filterable, each shown in its own variants, and personalisation kept per extension. Succeeds the "},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Auric Icons: Drawn compares with Modern, Playful, Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons, Emoji and the Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Drawn","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-drawn/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","How the three collections merge","Other related pages"],"x":" Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Auric Icons: Drawn ../README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes: Auric Icons: Modern 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Seven open source sets with colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Explorer file and folder icons in three styles, plus File Icon Studio. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Modern, Playful, Drawn and Emoji together. Through Modern None of its ow"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Playful","d":"What the Auric Icons: Playful extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Icons: Playful is a library of 1,225 emoji style SVG icons for VS Code: warm, expressive artwork in 24 categories, from Reactions and Status to Dashboard and Form Elements. Every icon comes in four variants: Color , Outline , Filled and Small . The Small variant is a redrawing with simplified detail for use at 16 to 24 pixels, not a scaled down copy. You browse the icons in an Icon Library view, search by name, concept, description or synonym, and insert them into your code in a format that suits the file. You can also copy icons in nine formats, save SVG files and preview icon IDs by hovering over them in code. Playful is a library only; it has no Explorer file icon theme. This collection is different from the Playful Explorer style in Auric Artisan File Icons, which is a separate set of 500 file and folder icons. Designers and front end developers building friendly, expressive interfaces, dashboards and admin panels. Anyone who wants emoji like artwork as real SVG they can style and ship. Users of Auric Icons: Modern or Drawn who want a third style in the same library. Item Value Marketplace listing https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric ic"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Playful guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Icons: Playful guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Icons: Playful, a library only extension of 1,225 emoji style icons. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, open the Icon Library and insert a first icon. icon library.md icon library.md Search, filters, the four variants, preview surfaces, the smart guide and recommendations. insert copy and save.md insert copy and save.md Insert and smart insert, nine copy formats, save, open source and hover previews. merged icon studio.md merged icon studio.md How Playful shares one library with Modern, Drawn and Icon Studio. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, keybinding, category and control. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Icons: Playful","d":"Install Auric Icons: Playful, open the Icon Library and insert your first emoji-style icon.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Open the Icon Library","3. Look around","4. Insert your first icon","Result","Next steps"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later, or an editor that keeps VS Code's extension features. Everything works offline. There is no telemetry and no network access. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Icons: Playful and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric icons playful Select Auric Icons: Playful in the Activity Bar to open the Icon Library view, or Run Auric Icons: Playful: Open Icon Library to open the larger Icon Studio — Library editor tab. If Auric Artisan Icon Studio, Auric Icons: Modern or Auric Icons: Drawn is also installed, the Playful view may be hidden because another extension shows a merged library that already contains Playful. See Use Playful with Modern and Drawn merged icon studio.md . The view shows the icon count, up to four smart guide tips, Search , Category and Style filters, the Variant buttons Auto , Color , Outline , Filled , Small , Preview surface Auto , Light , Dark , the All , ✦ For you , ♥ Likes and ↺ Recent chips, a ✦ Recommended for this file rail and the grid. 1. Open a file and place the cursor. 2. Choose Category › Reactions , or search for a word such as celebrate . 3. Select Smal"},{"t":"Browse the Icon Library","d":"Search the 1,225 Playful icons, filter by category, switch between Color, Outline, Filled and Small, and use previews, the smart guide and recommendations.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/icon-library.html","h":["Open the library","The screen","Search","Variants and Auto","Preview surface","The views","Recommendations","Cards","Density and batch size","Result"],"x":" The Playful library holds 1,225 icons in 24 categories. Each icon has four dedicated variants: Variant Use Color Full colour artwork. Outline Line drawing. Filled Solid shapes. Small A simplified redrawing for 16 to 24 pixels. There is no Mono or Duotone variant in this collection. Sidebar: select Auric Icons: Playful in the Activity Bar. Editor tab: run Auric Icons: Playful: Open Icon Library , select ↗ Open full explorer , or the open preview icon in the view's title bar. The tab is called Icon Studio — Library . Area What it does Header \"Icon Studio\", Icon Library , a count line such as \"1,225 icons · 72 loaded\", and ↗ . Smart guide Up to four dismissible tips. Turn off with auricIconsPlayful.library.showGuide . Search Placeholder \"Search 1,225 icons — try “empty state” or “auth”\". Library Only shown when several collections are merged. Category All categories or one of 24. Style All styles or Playful . Variant Auto , Color , Outline , Filled , Small . Preview surface Auto , Light , Dark . Chips All , ✦ For you , ♥ Likes count , ↺ Recent count . Recommended rail ✦ Recommended for this file , with Refresh . Grid Cards that load as you scroll. Search by name, concept, description"},{"t":"Insert, copy and save icons","d":"Insert Playful icons with language-aware output, copy them in nine formats, save SVG files, open the source and preview icon IDs on hover.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/insert-copy-and-save.html","h":["Insert from the library","Smart insert","Copy in a chosen format","Save and open the source","Other commands","Hover previews","Result"],"x":" 1. Open a file and place one or more cursors, or select text to replace. 2. Select Insert on a card. 3. The icon is inserted at every cursor; multi line output keeps the cursor line's indentation. Without an open text editor you see \"Open a text editor before inserting an SVG.\" With auricIconsPlayful.library.smartInsert on the default , Insert adapts to the file: Editing in Output JavaScript, TypeScript, React JSX and TSX, MDX JSX element HTML, PHP, Handlebars, Vue, Svelte, Astro HTML markup the SVG Markdown Markdown image CSS, SCSS, Less CSS background JSON, JSONC, YAML, Python Data URI XML, SVG and any other language Raw SVG With the setting off, Insert uses raw SVG. Smart Insert Icon always adapts. From the keyboard: press Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I on macOS in a text editor, search and choose. Run Auric Icons: Playful: Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag , choose an icon and a format: Format What you get Raw SVG The SVG markup. JSX element The SVG with JSX attribute names. React component export function IconName props { return <svg {...props} … ; } Markdown image ! Icon name data:image/svg+xml,… CSS background background image: url \"data:image/svg+xml,…\" ;"},{"t":"Use Playful with Modern and Drawn","d":"How Playful merges with Auric Icons: Modern and Drawn into one library, and how Auric Artisan Icon Studio takes over hosting.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/merged-icon-studio.html","h":["What happens when they are co-installed","Likes and recents","Hover previews","With Auric Artisan Icon Studio","Result"],"x":" Playful works by itself or beside Auric Icons: Modern and Auric Icons: Drawn . Installed together, they show one library. 1. One extension becomes the host automatically. With the current versions, Modern hosts when it is installed; otherwise Drawn hosts. Playful hosts only when it is the only collection installed. 2. The host's Icon Library view headed \"Icon Studio\" contains every installed collection. 3. A Library filter appears, and each card shows a badge naming its collection. 4. The Variant switcher offers every collection's variants. Playful's Filled and Small join Color, Mono, Outline and Duotone. Where a collection lacks the selected variant, its cards fall back to Color. 5. The other extensions hide their views, Command Palette entries and shortcuts, and forward their commands to the host. This updates by itself when you install or remove a collection. They stay with the extension that owns each icon. Liking a Playful icon in the merged view stores it with Playful. If you uninstall Playful, its icons and history leave the merged view. Playful previews only Playful icon IDs, so you never see two hovers. Auric Artisan Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md a"},{"t":"Auric Icons: Playful reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, category and library control in Auric Icons: Playful 0.12.1.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","Library contents","Library controls","Limits"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.12.1 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Icons: Playful . Command ID What it does Open Icon Library auricIconsPlayful.library.openExplorer Opens the Icon Studio — Library editor tab. Search Icons auricIconsPlayful.library.searchIcons Choose an icon, then an action. Insert SVG at Cursor auricIconsPlayful.library.insertSvg Choose an icon and insert it. Smart Insert Icon matches active language auricIconsPlayful.library.smartInsert Choose an icon and insert with language aware output. Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag auricIconsPlayful.library.copyAs Choose an icon and one of nine formats. Insert from Likes auricIconsPlayful.library.showFavorites Choose a liked icon and insert. Insert from Recent auricIconsPlayful.library.showRecents Choose a recent icon and insert. Toggle Like for an Icon auricIconsPlayful.library.toggleFavorite Like or unlike an icon. Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations auricIconsPlayful.library.resetPersonalization Confirm, then reset personalisation. Copy SVG auricIconsPlayful.library.copySvg Choose an icon and copy raw SVG. Save SVG As… auricIcon"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The Auric Icons: Playful view is missing. Auric Artisan Icon Studio, Modern or Drawn hosts the shared library, which already includes Playful. Use the host's library and filter by Library › Playful , or set auricIconStudio.hostFamilyLibraries to false if Icon Studio is the host. Playful commands are missing from the Command Palette. Same reason. Use the host's commands; keybindings still work. Ctrl + Alt + I does nothing. The editor is not focused, another extension hosts, or the keys are bound elsewhere. Focus a text editor and check Keyboard Shortcuts . \"Open a text editor before inserting an SVG.\" No text editor is available. Open a file, click into it, insert again. I chose Mono or Duotone and Playful cards look like Color. Playful has no Mono or Duotone; it falls back to Color in a merged library. Use Color, Outline, Filled or Small. Auto shows Color in a CSS file. Playful has no Mono variant, which Auto would use for stylesheets and data files. Choose a variant explicitly if you prefer Outline or Filled. I expected Playful Explorer file icons. Those belong to Auric Artisan File Icons the Playful Explorer style , a different set of artwork. I"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/docs/faq.html","h":["Are these emoji?","What is the Small variant for?","Is this the same as the Playful style in File Icons?","Why is there no file icon theme?","Do I need Modern or Drawn too?","Is it free and offline?","Can I change icon size or colour on insert?"],"x":" No. They are emoji style SVG icons: real vector artwork you can insert, style and ship, not Unicode emoji characters. For Unicode emoji, see Auric Artisan Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md . Small is a separate, simplified drawing for 16 to 24 pixels. Details that would blur at small sizes are removed. No. File Icons' Playful style is a set of 500 Explorer file and folder icons. This extension is a 1,225 icon library for your code and has no Explorer theme. Playful's earlier gallery theme did not meet the 16 pixel silhouette, folder pair and mapping standards of Auric Icons: Modern, which is the family theme. Install Modern alongside Playful for the Explorer theme. No. Playful works alone. Installing them together gives you one merged library. Yes. Free to use for any purpose redistribution and resale are not permitted , with no network access or telemetry. Not in this extension. Auric Artisan Icon Studio has size and colour output settings and includes the Playful collection. "},{"t":"Auric Icons: Playful: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for Auric Icons: Playful: terms, shortcuts, limits, a comparison with the other Auric icon extensions, the release history and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the library. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings and every command. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the library can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Modern, Drawn, Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons, Emoji and Icon Pack. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, in-view keys and every command in Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys in the Icon Library","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Smart Insert Icon Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I Insert from Recent Ctrl + Alt + R Cmd + Alt + R Both need a focused text editor and are active only while Playful hosts the library. Key Action / Focus search Escape Clear search; close a dropdown Arrow Up / Arrow Down Move between dropdown options Type \"Auric Icons: Playful\" in the Command Palette: Open Icon Library , Search Icons , Insert SVG at Cursor , Smart Insert Icon matches active language , Copy Icon As… JSX, CSS, Markdown, Data URI, Image tag , Insert from Likes , Insert from Recent , Toggle Like for an Icon , Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations , Copy SVG , Save SVG As… , Open SVG Source . See the reference ../docs/reference.md commands for IDs and details. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Auto variant A variant choice that follows the language of the file you are editing. Catalog path The relative location of an icon file inside the bundled catalog. Data URI Text that embeds a file directly, starting data:image/svg+xml, . Emoji style icon Expressive SVG artwork in the spirit of emoji. Not a Unicode emoji character. Filled A variant drawn with solid shapes. Host The one extension that shows the shared library when several Auric collections are installed. Icon ID The unique name of an icon, such as abstract balance 0001 . Icon Studio The heading of the shared library view, and also the name of the separate Auric Artisan Icon Studio extension. Outline A variant drawn in lines. Preview surface The light, dark or automatic backdrop behind library cards. Small A simplified redrawing for 16 to 24 pixels. Smart guide Tip cards at the top of the library that react to your file and usage. Smart insert Choosing the output format from the language of the file you are editing. Variant One rendering of an icon: Color, Outline, Filled or Small. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Icons: Playful can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" The library contains 1,225 validated icons at the installed version; new icons come with updates. There is no Mono or Duotone variant, and no Explorer file icon theme. Icons are inserted as drawn: there are no size, colour or stroke controls for output. Smart insert picks a format from the file's language, not the exact cursor position. Check quotes and surrounding code. Recommendations are local rankings from the file you are editing and your likes and use, not an AI service. Hover previews recognise only Playful icon IDs a hyphenated name ending in four digits . Some copy formats from the retired \"Auric Artisan Icons\" gallery Vue single file component, web component, CSS class and sprite are not offered, because they depend on runtime files an extension cannot ship. Licence: free to use for any purpose; redistribution, republishing, resale and derivative releases are not permitted. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Icons: Playful stores, where, and confirmation that it makes no network requests.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Auric Icons: Playful runs entirely inside VS Code. It has no telemetry, no account and no network access at runtime. Data Where Settings Your VS Code settings under auricIconsPlayful.library. . Likes up to 500 , recent icons up to 60 , learned preferences, dismissed tips VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Search, filters, variant and preview surface The view's saved state in VS Code. For recommendations and smart insert, the extension reads the language, file name and up to about 60 lines around the cursor of the active editor. This stays in memory and is never stored or sent. Inserting changes your editor content, copying writes to the clipboard, and saving writes a file only where you choose in a save dialog. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Icons: Playful.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.12.1","0.12.0","0.11.0","0.1.0"],"x":" The current Marketplace version. Now covered by the Auric Artisan Free Use Licence 2.0 instead of MIT. It stays free to install and use for any purpose; redistribution, republishing to any marketplace, resale and derivative releases are no longer permitted. Marketplace README images now display correctly. Future Auric icon collections can join the shared library without every extension being updated. The library view, palette entries and shared shortcuts are disabled while another icon collection or Auric Artisan Icon Studio hosts the library. The catalog grew from 1,220 to all 1,225 icons after five pieces of artwork were repaired. New Marketplace artwork. The shared library gained keyboard and pointer enlargement and a remembered Auto , Light or Dark preview surface. Initial release: 1,220 icons in four variants Color, Outline, Filled, Small and 24 categories, with the Icon Library, smart search, smart insert Ctrl + Alt + I , nine copy formats, hover previews, likes and recents Ctrl + Alt + R and per file recommendations. Cooperates with Auric Icons: Modern and Drawn in one merged library. Succeeds the retired, never published \"Auric Artisan Icons\" gallery extension. Its file ic"},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Auric Icons: Playful compares with Modern, Drawn, Icon Studio, Icon Hub, File Icons, Emoji and the Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Icons: Playful","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-icons-playful/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","Two different \"Playful\"s","How the three collections merge","Other related pages"],"x":" Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Auric Icons: Playful ../README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes: Auric Icons: Modern 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Seven open source sets with colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Explorer file and folder icons in three styles, plus File Icon Studio. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio for Unicode emoji. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Modern, Playful, Drawn and Emoji together. Through Moder"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Emoji","d":"What the Auric Artisan Emoji extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Emoji is a local emoji workspace for Visual Studio Code. It lets you search 1,914 emoji and put them straight into your code: from a searchable Quick Pick, from Emoji Studio in the sidebar or an editor tab, from shortcode suggestions as you type, or from a hover over a shortcode such as :rocket: . Emoji Studio has four views Library , For you , Favorites and Recent , nine categories, six skin tone choices, quick filters and grid or list layouts. An inspector shows each emoji's shortcode, code points, emoji version, keywords and related emoji, and previews its text in six output formats: the emoji itself, a shortcode, Unicode code points, HTML entities, a JavaScript escape or a CSS escape. You can also collect several emoji into a sequence and insert them together. The Studio can be shown in English or Hindi, and Hindi search words such as दिल or धन्यवाद find emoji. Everything is bundled and stays on your machine. Developers writing commit messages, documentation, UI strings, tests or chat bots that use emoji. Front end developers who need the right escape for HTML, JavaScript or CSS. Hindi speaking users who want a Hindi Emoji Studio. Item Value Marketplace listing h"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Emoji guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Emoji guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Artisan Emoji. Start with Getting started, then use the guide for how you prefer to work: from the editor, or from Emoji Studio. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, insert a first emoji, open Emoji Studio and tour it. insert from the editor.md insert from the editor.md Quick Insert, shortcode completions, code hovers, replacing shortcodes, recent and favorite pickers. emoji studio.md emoji studio.md Search, views, categories, filters, layouts, cards, suggestions and Workspace overview. inspector tones and formats.md inspector tones and formats.md The inspector, skin tones and the six output formats. sequences.md sequences.md Collect several emoji and insert or copy them together. interface language.md interface language.md English and Hindi in the Studio. reference.md reference.md Every command, keybinding, setting, key, category and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan Emoji","d":"Install Auric Artisan Emoji, insert a first emoji, open Emoji Studio and tour its screen.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Insert your first emoji","3. Open Emoji Studio","4. Tour the Studio","5. Insert from the Studio","Result","Next steps"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later. The extension works offline and in untrusted and virtual workspaces. It never runs workspace code. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Artisan Emoji and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan emoji For a local .vsix , use Extensions › … › Install from VSIX… . 1. Open a text file and place the cursor. 2. Press Ctrl + Alt + J Cmd + Alt + J on macOS , or right click and choose Quick Insert Emoji . 3. Type rocket and press Enter . The rocket emoji is inserted. Sidebar: select Auric Emoji in the Activity Bar view name Emoji Studio . Editor tab: press Ctrl + Alt + E Cmd + Alt + E , run Auric Artisan Emoji: Open Emoji Studio , or select the Emoji item in the status bar. The editor tab opens beside your code. The sidebar is compact, with visible card actions. Area Contents Brand bar \"Auric Artisan / Emoji Studio\", the website link, Language Auto , EN , हिं and Offline · private . Brand bar buttons Customize Emoji Studio gear and, in the sidebar, Open Emoji Studio in an editor tab . Tabs 01 Library , 02 For you , 03 Favorites , 04 Recent , with counts. Workspace overview Collapsed "},{"t":"Use Emoji Studio","d":"Search, browse and insert with Emoji Studio: views, categories, skin tones, quick filters, layouts, cards, suggestions and the Workspace overview.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/emoji-studio.html","h":["Search","Views","Filters","Layout","Cards","Keyboard in the grid","Suggested for you","Workspace overview","Studio settings","Result"],"x":" Type in Search placeholder \"Search 1,914 emoji — name, mood, :shortcode: or U+1F680\" . Press / or Ctrl + K Cmd + K to focus it. You can search by: name or keyword, such as developer or thanks ; an exact emoji; a shortcode, such as :rocket: ; a code point, such as U+1F680 ; common Hindi words, such as दिल , रॉकेट or धन्यवाद . Tab Shows 01 Library Every emoji matching the search and filters. 02 For you Favorites first, then the emoji you use most, then curated picks. 03 Favorites Emoji you starred. Press F or the heart on a card. 04 Recent Everything you inserted or copied, most recent first. In the narrow sidebar, Favorites and Recent buttons at the bottom switch views, and Back to library returns. Filter Options Category All or one of nine: Smileys & Emotion, People & Body, Animals & Nature, Food & Drink, Travel & Places, Activities, Objects, Symbols, Flags. More / Fewer expands the chip list. Skin tone Yellow standard or Light , Medium light , Medium , Medium dark , Dark . A note shows how many emoji it applies to. Quick filter full Studio All , Curated , Skin tone tone capable emoji only , Newest . Density full Studio Compact , Comfortable , Showcase . Clear filters resets searc"},{"t":"Insert from the editor","d":"Insert emoji without opening the Studio, using Quick Insert, shortcode completions, code hovers, shortcode replacement and the recent and favorite pickers.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/insert-from-the-editor.html","h":["Quick Insert","Shortcode completions","Hover over a shortcode","Replace several shortcodes","Recent, favorite and last emoji","Spacing","Result"],"x":" 1. Place the cursor or several cursors in a text file. 2. Press Ctrl + Alt + J Cmd + Alt + J , run Auric Artisan Emoji: Quick Insert Emoji , or right click › Quick Insert Emoji . 3. Search names, shortcodes, categories or Unicode, and choose an emoji. Quick Insert uses your preferred skin tone and spacing. Type : followed by part of a name. Suggestions appear: text :spa → sparkles :sparkles: :rock → rocket :rocket: :thinking → thinking face :thinking face: Accept a suggestion to insert the emoji. Turn completions off with auricEmoji.completions.enabled . 1. Write a complete shortcode with both colons, such as :rocket: or :waving hand: . 2. Hover over it. The hover shows a preview. 3. Choose Insert emoji , JavaScript or HTML . js // Before: hover over :rocket: inside the string const launch = \":rocket:\"; // After choosing Insert emoji const launch = \" the rocket emoji character \"; Only the hovered shortcode is replaced, in one undo step. Quotes, other cursors and surrounding code are untouched, and no whitespace is added. The emoji uses the skin tone shown in the preview. If the document changes before you click, hover again for a fresh action. An action cannot be reused after it h"},{"t":"Inspector, skin tones and output formats","d":"Inspect an emoji, preview and set skin tones, and choose among the six output formats.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/inspector-tones-and-formats.html","h":["Open the inspector","Skin tones","The six output formats","Result"],"x":" Select a card's … button, or focus an emoji and press I . In the narrow sidebar it opens as a sheet. Press I or Escape , or select Close inspector , to close it. The inspector shows: Part Contents Stage A large preview. Name and shortcode With Copy shortcode . Pills Emoji version for example \"Emoji 13.0\" , Skin tone if tone capable, Favorite if starred. Skin tone Previews of each tone. Copy as The six formats with their exact output. Keywords Search keywords. Actions Insert , Copy , Favorite / Remove favorite . Also try Related emoji. Choose between Yellow the standard appearance and five tones: Light , Medium light , Medium , Medium dark and Dark . 330 catalog entries support tone changes. Set the default with the Skin tone filter, or auricEmoji.preferredSkinTone none , medium , light , mediumLight , mediumDark , dark . In the inspector, select a tone to preview it \"Previewing {tone}. Your default is {default}.\" , then Make {tone} my default . Emoji that do not change with tone say \"This emoji does not change with skin tone.\" Your tone applies to card previews, insertion, Quick Insert, completions and shortcode replacement. Favorites and recents store the emoji, not the tone, so "},{"t":"Interface language (English and हिन्दी)","d":"Show Emoji Studio in English or Hindi and search with Hindi words.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/interface-language.html","h":["Choose a language","What changes","Hindi search","Result"],"x":" In Emoji Studio's brand bar, use the Language switch: Auto , EN or हिं . Run Auric Artisan Emoji: Choose Interface Language… also in the sidebar's title bar … menu . Set auricEmoji.interfaceLanguage to auto , en or hi . Value Behaviour auto default Follows VS Code's display language: Hindi locales use Hindi; others use English. en Always English in Emoji Studio. hi Always Hindi in Emoji Studio. Changing the language keeps your search, filters and sequence. Part Language Emoji Studio controls, categories, tones, formats and announcements Your auricEmoji.interfaceLanguage choice. Command Palette titles, Settings descriptions and notifications VS Code's display language Hindi versions are included . Emoji names, shortcodes and code points Their catalog spelling, always. Common Hindi words find emoji whatever the interface language, for example दिल heart , रॉकेट rocket and धन्यवाद thanks . Emoji Studio appears in your chosen language, and Hindi words help you find emoji. "},{"t":"Compose a sequence","d":"Collect up to 50 emoji in Emoji Studio and insert or copy them together.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/sequences.html","h":["Build a sequence","Edit it","Use it","Result"],"x":" A sequence is a short list of emoji you collect and then insert or copy in one go, for example rocket, sparkles and party popper. Use any of these: Focus an emoji and press Space . Shift click an emoji's preview. In the full Studio, turn on Compose . The switch shows \"Composing · {count}\", and selecting emoji adds them. The Sequence tray appears with the count and the emoji. Cards show \"In the sequence {n}×\". A sequence holds up to 50 emoji, repeats included; beyond that you see \"A sequence holds up to 50 emoji.\" Backspace outside text boxes removes the last emoji. Select an emoji in the tray to remove it. Escape clears the sequence after closing any open panel , or select Clear . Button Result Insert sequence Inserts the emoji characters at your cursors. \"Inserted {n} emoji: …\" Copy sequence Copies in your copy format. \"Copied {n} emoji: …\" When copying, shortcodes, Unicode labels and CSS escapes are separated by spaces; emoji, HTML entities and JavaScript escapes are joined directly. If no editor is active, Insert sequence copies instead. The sequence is restored if the Studio reloads, and changing the interface language keeps it. Your collected emoji are in your file or on your"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Emoji reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, key, view, category, format and message in Auric Artisan Emoji 0.2.0.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","Studio controls","Catalog","Messages you may see"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.2.0 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Artisan Emoji . Command ID What it does Open Emoji Studio auricEmoji.openStudio Opens the full Studio in an editor tab. Quick Insert Emoji auricEmoji.quickPick Searchable Quick Pick; inserts the chosen emoji. Insert Recent Emoji auricEmoji.insertRecent Quick Pick of recent emoji. Insert Favorite Emoji auricEmoji.insertFavorite Quick Pick of favorites. Copy Last Emoji Again auricEmoji.copyLast Copies the last emoji used. Replace Emoji Shortcodes in Selection auricEmoji.replaceShortcodes Replaces known :shortcodes: in the selection or current line. Clear Emoji History auricEmoji.clearHistory Clears recents and last emoji recall; keeps favorites. Focus Emoji Search auricEmoji.focusSearch Focuses the Studio search box. Choose Interface Language… auricEmoji.chooseInterfaceLanguage Auto, English or Hindi for the Studio. Keys Windows and Linux Keys macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + E Cmd + Alt + E Open Emoji Studio Ctrl + Alt + J Cmd + Alt + J Quick Insert Emoji Both work anywhere in VS Code. Key Action / or Ctrl + K Cmd + K Focus search Arrow keys on a preview Move throu"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do No hover action on a shortcode. The shortcode is incomplete or not in the catalog, or hovers are off. Use a complete shortcode with both colons, such as :rocket: . Check VS Code's editor hover setting and auricEmoji.hover.enabled . A hover no longer inserts. The document changed, or the action was already used. Keep the editor visible and writable, then hover again. The Studio copied instead of inserting. No writable editor was available, or your click action is Copy. Open a writable editor and place the cursor, then return to the Studio. Check Workspace overview for the target, and auricEmoji.clickAction . No suggestions after typing : . Completions are off, or VS Code's suggestions are disabled for this language. Turn on auricEmoji.completions.enabled . Emoji look different or appear as boxes. Emoji are drawn by your system's emoji font; older fonts lack newer emoji. Update your operating system's emoji font, or choose an older emoji. Extra spaces appear around inserted emoji. insertSpacing is auto or space . Set auricEmoji.insertSpacing to none . A JavaScript escape breaks my JSON. \\u{…} code point escapes are JavaScript syntax, not JSON. Use t"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/docs/faq.html","h":["Does it need the internet?","Why do emoji look different on another computer?","Does clearing history remove favorites?","Can I change the default skin tone?","What is the difference between Insert and the click action?","Is this the same as the emoji in Icon Studio?","Are Auric Icons: Playful icons emoji?"],"x":" No. The catalog and Studio are bundled. There is no telemetry and no account. Emoji are drawn by each system's emoji font. The characters are the same; the artwork differs. No. Clear Emoji History removes recent emoji and last emoji recall only. Yes: the Skin tone filter, Make {tone} my default in the inspector, or auricEmoji.preferredSkinTone . The card's Insert button always inserts. Selecting the emoji itself or pressing Enter runs your click action, which can be Insert, Copy, or Insert and copy. Icon Studio also includes 1,914 emoji for browsing alongside icons. This extension adds the full emoji workflow: sequences, completions, shortcode replacement, code hovers, six copy formats and a Hindi interface. No. Playful is a library of emoji style SVG artwork, not Unicode emoji characters. "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Emoji: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for Auric Artisan Emoji: terms, shortcuts, limits, a comparison with other Auric extensions, the release history and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in Emoji Studio. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings, Studio keys and commands. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the extension can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Icon Studio, the Auric icon collections and other extensions. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, Emoji Studio keys and every command in Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys in Emoji Studio","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Open Emoji Studio Ctrl + Alt + E Cmd + Alt + E Quick Insert Emoji Ctrl + Alt + J Cmd + Alt + J Key Action / or Ctrl + K Cmd + K Focus search Arrow keys Move between cards Enter Click action Shift + Enter Copy Space Add to sequence Backspace Remove last sequence item F Toggle favorite I Toggle inspector Escape Close panel, then clear sequence ? Keyboard map Type \"Auric Artisan Emoji\" in the Command Palette: Open Emoji Studio , Quick Insert Emoji , Insert Recent Emoji , Insert Favorite Emoji , Copy Last Emoji Again , Replace Emoji Shortcodes in Selection , Clear Emoji History , Focus Emoji Search , Choose Interface Language… . With VS Code's display language set to Hindi, these titles appear in Hindi. "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Click action What happens when you select an emoji or press Enter on it: insert, copy, or both. Code point The Unicode number of a character, written like U+1F680 . Copy format The text form used when copying: emoji, shortcode, Unicode, HTML, JavaScript or CSS. CSS escape A backslash form such as \\1F680 , valid inside CSS strings. Curated A hand picked selection of commonly useful emoji. HTML entity A form such as & x1F680; that HTML turns into the character. Inspector The panel showing an emoji's details and every output format. JavaScript escape A form such as \\u{1F680} , valid inside JavaScript and TypeScript strings. Sequence A list of up to 50 emoji collected to insert or copy together. Shortcode A text name between colons, such as :rocket: . Skin tone A modifier changing the skin colour of emoji that support it. Yellow The standard, unmodified appearance of tone capable emoji. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Artisan Emoji can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":[],"x":" The catalog has 1,914 entries in nine categories at the installed version; new emoji arrive with updates. Glyph appearance depends on your operating system's emoji fonts. Newer emoji may not display with older fonts. 330 entries support skin tones; others ignore the tone setting. Output formats are text representations, not complete code snippets. JavaScript code point escapes are not JSON escapes. Hover actions are single use and expire when the document changes; a failed hover edit does not fall back to the clipboard. Shortcode replacement leaves unknown tokens unchanged. Hindi search terms help you find emoji; names, shortcodes and code points stay in their catalog spelling. Editing remote or virtual files depends on the file system provider. Recent emoji are limited by auricEmoji.maxRecents 8 to 200, default 48 . A sequence holds up to 50 emoji. "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Emoji stores, where, and confirmation that it makes no network requests.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/privacy.html","h":["What is stored","Hover actions","Security"],"x":" The emoji catalog and Studio are bundled. The extension has no telemetry, no account requirement and no runtime package dependencies. It does not run workspace code or fetch remote content for its interface. Website links open in your browser only when you select them. Data Where Favorites, recents and last emoji VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Preferences Your VS Code settings under auricEmoji. . Studio interface state and sequences The Studio's saved state in VS Code. Document contents are not stored as history. When you hover over a shortcode, the extension briefly keeps that shortcode and its document position in memory so it can check your explicit edit. Hover links allow only the extension's insertion command, with single use tickets and document version checks. Nothing is written to disk or sent anywhere. The Studio uses a restrictive content security policy and builds its interface without executing imported content. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan Emoji.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.2.0 — 18 September 2026","0.1.0 — 8 August 2026","Earlier recorded versions"],"x":" The current Marketplace version: a connected workspace from search to code. Compact brand bar, sticky tabs and consistent cards in the Studio and sidebar. Search and the library first; a collapsible Workspace overview holds active file details, quick tools and statistics. Library , For you , Favorites and Recent views, category chips, tone swatches, quick filters, grid and list layouts and density controls. A compact sidebar with visible card actions; hover and focus actions in the full Studio. Native scrolling, visible focus, light, dark and high contrast support, and reduced motion. Hover over a complete shortcode such as :rocket: to insert the emoji, a JavaScript escape or an HTML entity, in one undo step. New setting auricEmoji.hover.enabled . Workspace overview shows the insertion target, cursor details and preferences, with last emoji insertion, shortcode replacement and history tools. A rebuilt inspector with a large preview, tone variants, a default tone control, keywords and related emoji. JavaScript and CSS escapes added, making six formats; the ledger previews exact output and can set the default copy format. Sequences: add with Space , Shift click or Compose mode; inse"},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Auric Artisan Emoji compares with Icon Studio, the Auric icon collections and other Auric extensions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Emoji","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-emoji/others/related.html","h":["Other related products"],"x":" Extension Main job Emoji Network Auric Artisan Emoji ../README.md The full emoji workflow: Studio, sequences, completions, hovers, shortcode replacement, six formats, Hindi interface. 1,914 None Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for Auric icons, emoji and seven open source sets. Emoji copy as character, shortcode, code points or HTML entities. 1,914 None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md 1,225 emoji style SVG icons artwork, not Unicode emoji . None None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Emoji with Modern, Playful and Drawn. Through Emoji Marketplace to install Emoji keeps its own view and commands even when Icon Studio hosts the Auric icon collections. For the full comparison of all Auric icon extensions, see Icon Studio: Related extensions and comparison ../../auric artisan icon studio/others/related.md . Auric Artisan Theme ../../auric artisan theme/README.md — shares the same Auto, English and Hindi interface switch. Install and set up ../../install and setup/README.md "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Icon Studio","d":"What Auric Artisan Icon Studio is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Icon Studio is one offline workspace in VS Code for finding icons and emoji and putting them into your code. It bundles every Auric Artisan icon collection Modern, Drawn and Playful , 1,914 emoji and seven open source icon sets: Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. In total it searches 17,234 catalog entries in 11 collections. You can browse in a compact sidebar or open a larger editor tab Studio. Search understands names, tags and synonyms for example, delete finds trash icons , and Hindi search aliases. Smart insert chooses an output format from the file you are editing: a JSX element in React, a string constant in JavaScript, markup in HTML, a CSS background in stylesheets, a Markdown image in Markdown, and a data URI in JSON, YAML or Python. You can also copy an icon in an explicit format or save SVG artwork to a file. Icon Studio does not change your Explorer file and folder icons; that is the job of Auric Artisan File Icons ../auric artisan file icons/README.md . It also includes all the Auric artwork itself, so you do not need to install the individual Auric collection extensions. Front end and full stack developers who insert icon"},{"t":"Icon Studio guides","d":"Contents of the Icon Studio guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Artisan Icon Studio. Start with Getting started, then use the task guides. The reference lists every command, setting, keybinding, collection, format and control. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, open the sidebar or editor tab, tour the screen and insert a first icon. search and browse.md search and browse.md Search, the four views, filters, styles, skin tones and infinite scrolling. insert copy and save.md insert copy and save.md Smart insert, explicit formats, saving SVG files and hover previews. commands and keybindings.md commands and keybindings.md Quick Pick workflows, shortcuts and inserting a fixed icon from a keybinding. auric collections.md auric collections.md How Icon Studio works alongside Auric Icons: Modern, Drawn and Playful. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, keybinding, collection, style and output format. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Icon Studio","d":"Install Icon Studio, open it in the sidebar or an editor tab, tour the screen and insert your first icon.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Open Icon Studio","3. Tour the screen","4. Insert your first icon","5. Keep useful icons close","Result","Next steps"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later. Icon Studio works offline and in untrusted and virtual workspaces. Files are only written when you save an icon through a save dialog. All collections are bundled. You do not need the individual Auric collection extensions. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Artisan Icon Studio and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan icon studio Sidebar: select Icon Studio in the Activity Bar. The view is compact and starts with the filters collapsed, leaving room for artwork. Editor tab: run Auric Icon Studio: Open Icon Studio , or select the ↗ button Open Icon Studio in an editor tab in the sidebar header. The tab opens beside your editor with the filters expanded. Opening the editor tab again brings the existing tab forward and focuses the search box. Area What it contains Header The Auric Artisan mark, \"Icon Studio / Creative workspace\", an Offline library badge and, in the sidebar, the ↗ button. View chips Library , For you , Likes and Recent . Likes and Recent show a count. Introduction \"Small details. Distinct character.\" Search Search your library with a / hint. The placeholder"},{"t":"Work with the Auric collection extensions","d":"How Icon Studio, Auric Icons: Modern, Drawn and Playful share one library interface, and how to keep their separate views if you prefer.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/auric-collections.html","h":["Default: Icon Studio hosts the collections","Keep the separate collection views","When the collections are installed without Icon Studio","Likes and recent icons","Other Auric icon extensions","Result"],"x":" The Auric artwork is also published as three separate extensions: Auric Icons: Modern , Auric Icons: Drawn and Auric Icons: Playful . Each has its own Icon Library view. Icon Studio already contains all three collections, so it is designed to avoid showing the same icons twice. With auricIconStudio.hostFamilyLibraries set to true the default : The separate Icon Library views of Modern, Drawn and Playful are hidden, together with their Command Palette entries and their Ctrl + Alt + I and Ctrl + Alt + R shortcuts. Icon Studio's own view, commands and shortcuts are active. Modern's Explorer file icon theme is not affected. It keeps working. Hovering over an Auric icon ID is still answered by the collection extension that owns it, so you see one preview, not two. 1. Open Settings and search for auricIconStudio.hostFamilyLibraries . 2. Turn it off false . The collection extensions show their own Icon Library views, commands and shortcuts again. Icon Studio's view and commands stay available, but its Ctrl + Alt + I and Ctrl + Alt + R shortcuts step aside so the shortcuts are not claimed twice. If none of the collection extensions are installed, Icon Studio's shortcuts stay active either"},{"t":"Commands and keybindings","d":"Use Icon Studio from the Command Palette and keyboard, including Quick Pick insertion and a fixed icon bound to a key.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/commands-and-keybindings.html","h":["Search everything and choose an action","Smart insert with one shortcut","Insert from Recent or Likes","Other commands","Insert a specific icon from a keybinding","Result"],"x":" You can use Icon Studio without opening its panel. Open the Command Palette Ctrl + Shift + P and type \"Auric Icon Studio\". 1. Run Auric Icon Studio: Search All Icons… also the search icon in the sidebar title bar . 2. A Quick Pick opens. With an empty search and recommendations on, it starts with Recommended for this file , then All icons . Each row shows the icon, its collection, category and tags. 3. Type to search. Up to 200 results are listed. 4. Choose an icon, then choose an action: Smart Insert matches this file Insert Copy Copy As… Save as SVG… SVG artwork only Toggle Like 1. Place the cursor in a text editor. 2. Press Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I on macOS , or run Auric Icon Studio: Smart Insert Icon matches active language . It is also on the editor's right click menu. 3. Choose an icon. It is inserted in the format that suits the file. Press Ctrl + Alt + R Cmd + Alt + R on macOS or run Insert from Recent . Run Insert from Likes also the heart icon in the sidebar title bar . Both run the action set in auricIconStudio.clickAction : insert default , copy , or insert and copy . If the list is empty, you see \"Icon Studio: no recent icons yet.\" or a prompt to like an icon fir"},{"t":"Insert, copy and save","d":"Insert icons with smart, language-aware output, copy them in an explicit format, save SVG files and preview Auric icon IDs on hover.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/insert-copy-and-save.html","h":["Insert into your file","Copy in an explicit format","Control the output","Save an SVG file","Hover previews in code","Result"],"x":" Every card has three main actions and three quick format buttons. Button What it does Insert or select the artwork Inserts into the editor. With smart insert on, the format follows the file's language. Copy Copies the plain format: SVG markup for SVG artwork, an HTML span for Material, the character for emoji. As… Opens a list of every format for that icon; the plain format is marked default . Quick buttons SVG artwork: JSX , URI data URI , CSS . Material: JSX , CSS , HTML . Emoji: Code shortcode , U+ code points , HTML entities . After each action, a status message confirms what happened, for example \"Rocket copied as data uri.\" 1. Open a writable file and place one or more cursors, or select text to replace. 2. In Icon Studio, select Insert on a card. 3. The output is inserted at every cursor. Selected text is replaced. If the output has several lines, each continuation line gets the same indentation as the cursor's line. Icon Studio inserts into the active editor or, if you clicked into the Studio, the last text editor you used. If no editor is available, the output is copied instead. Smart insert is on by default auricIconStudio.smartInsert . It picks the format from the edito"},{"t":"Search and browse","d":"Search 17,234 entries, switch between Library, For you, Likes and Recent, and refine by collection, category, style and skin tone.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/search-and-browse.html","h":["Search","The four views","Refine the results","Collections and styles","Scrolling","Card size","Result"],"x":" 1. Select Search your library , or press / anywhere in Icon Studio. 2. Type a name, tag or concept. The results update as you type. 3. Press Escape in the search box to clear it. Search is synonym aware and ranks results. For example, delete finds trash icons. Hindi search aliases are supported for many entries. The search also takes account of the icons you like and use. The chips at the top switch what the grid shows. View Shows Empty message Library Every entry that matches your search and filters. \"No icons found. Try another word, or choose All collections.\" For you Up to 96 icons ranked for the file you are editing and your likes and use. Hidden when recommendations are turned off. \"No recommendations yet. Open a file, or like and use a few icons to teach Icon Studio your style.\" Likes Icons you liked with the heart button. \"No liked icons yet. Press the heart on any card to keep it here.\" Recent Icons you inserted, copied or saved, newest first up to 60 . \"No recent icons yet. Icons you insert, copy or save appear here.\" Search and filters apply inside every view. Expand Refine library subtitle \"Collection, category & style\" . Control Options Collection All collections , or"},{"t":"Icon Studio reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, collection, style, output format, view and control in Auric Artisan Icon Studio 0.1.0.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","Studio controls","Collections","Output formats","Smart insert by language","Limits","Messages you may see"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.1.0 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Icon Studio . Command ID What it does Open Icon Studio auricIconStudio.openStudio Opens the editor tab Studio beside the active editor, or reveals it and focuses search. Search All Icons… auricIconStudio.searchIcons Quick Pick over the whole catalog, then an action list. Smart Insert Icon matches active language auricIconStudio.smartInsert Quick Pick, then insert with smart output. Copy Icon As… auricIconStudio.copyAs Quick Pick, then a format list; copies. Save Icon as SVG… auricIconStudio.saveSvg Quick Pick of SVG icons; saves through a dialog. Insert from Likes auricIconStudio.insertFavorite Quick Pick of liked icons; runs the click action. Insert from Recent auricIconStudio.insertRecent Quick Pick of recent icons; runs the click action. Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations auricIconStudio.clearPersonalization Asks for confirmation, then resets personalisation. Insert Icon by ID auricIconStudio.insertIcon Inserts a given icon; for keybindings and macros. Hidden from the Command Palette. Keys Windows and Linux Keys macOS Command When Ctrl + Alt"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Artisan Icon Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Reset personalisation","Still stuck"],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do No search results. A collection or category filter is narrowing the search, or you are in Likes or Recent. Select Reset filters , switch to Library , and try a simpler word or synonym. A style or skin tone option is missing. Styles differ by collection; the Style control only appears when one collection with several styles is chosen. Only some emoji support skin tones. Choose a single collection to see its styles. For you chip is missing. Recommendations are turned off. Turn on auricIconStudio.recommendations.enabled . For you is empty. There is no editor context and no likes or usage yet. Open a file, and like or use a few icons. Insert copied the icon instead. No editor was available to insert into. Open and focus a writable text editor, then insert again. \"VS Code could not apply the edit.\" The editor is read only or rejected the change. Use Copy , or open a writable file. A Material icon shows as a word in my app. Material output needs the Material font; the Studio's preview font is not installed in your project. Load the matching Material Icons font and styles in your application. I cannot save a Material icon or emoji as SVG. They are font g"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Icon Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/docs/faq.html","h":["Do I need Auric Icons: Modern, Drawn or Playful as well?","Does Icon Studio change my Explorer file icons?","Does it need an internet connection?","Is it the same as Icon Hub?","Can I change the size or colour of inserted icons?","Can I search in Hindi?","Why do Material icons not export as SVG?","Can I use the artwork in my own projects?","Where are my likes stored?"],"x":" No. Icon Studio bundles all three collections. Install the separate extensions only if you want their own interfaces, or Modern's Explorer file icon theme. No. It is an artwork browser and insertion tool. For Explorer file and folder icons, use Auric Artisan File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md . No. The catalog, artwork and Material preview fonts are bundled. Icon Studio makes no network requests. No. Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md covers the seven open source sets only, adds colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export and CDN insertion, and can check the website for catalog updates. Icon Studio adds the Auric artwork and emoji and works entirely offline. See the comparison ../others/related.md . Yes, through settings: auricIconStudio.size , auricIconStudio.color and auricIconStudio.strokeWidth . See Insert, copy and save insert copy and save.md control the output . Many entries have Hindi search aliases. The interface itself is in English. Material icons in this catalog are glyphs in a font, not SVG files. Icon Studio offers HTML, JSX, React, JavaScript, CSS and ligature name output instead. Auric artwork is covered by the Auric Artisan Free"},{"t":"Icon Studio: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Icon Studio: glossary, shortcuts, limits, comparison, release notes and privacy.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds supporting pages for Auric Artisan Icon Studio. It includes the comparison of all Auric icon extensions, the terms used, the keyboard shortcuts, what the tool can and cannot do, its release history and its privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in Icon Studio. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings, in Studio keys and every command. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What smart insert and search can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison of Icon Studio, Icon Hub, the collections, File Icons, Emoji and Icon Pack. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, keys inside the Studio and every Command Palette command in Auric Artisan Icon Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys inside Icon Studio","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Smart Insert Icon Ctrl + Alt + I Cmd + Alt + I Insert from Recent Ctrl + Alt + R Cmd + Alt + R Both need editor focus. They are active when Icon Studio hosts the Auric collections the default or when no collection extension is installed. The Auric collection extensions use the same keys, so only one extension claims them at a time. Key Action / Focus search Escape Clear search, or close an open dropdown Arrow Up / Arrow Down Open a dropdown; move between its options Home / End First or last option Enter Choose the focused option or button Tab Move on and close open dropdowns Command Default key Auric Icon Studio: Open Icon Studio None Auric Icon Studio: Search All Icons… None Auric Icon Studio: Smart Insert Icon matches active language Ctrl + Alt + I Auric Icon Studio: Copy Icon As… None Auric Icon Studio: Save Icon as SVG… None Auric Icon Studio: Insert from Likes None Auric Icon Studio: Insert from Recent Ctrl + Alt + R Auric Icon Studio: Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations None auricIconStudio.insertIcon Insert Icon by ID is available for keybindings and macros only. See Commands and keybindings ../docs/commands and keybindings.md ins"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Artisan Icon Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Catalog entry One icon or emoji in the bundled catalog. Its styles or tones are not counted separately. Collection A set of icons from one source, such as Auric Drawn or Tabler. Icon Studio has 11. currentColor A CSS keyword meaning \"use the surrounding text colour\", so an icon follows light and dark themes. Data URI A way to embed a file's content directly in text, starting data:image/svg+xml, . Font backed icon An icon drawn from a font glyph Material , not an SVG file. It needs the font loaded to display. For you A view of icons ranked for the file you are editing and your likes and use. Host collections The one extension that shows the shared library when several Auric collection extensions, or Icon Studio, are installed. Icon ID The unique catalog name of an icon, such as tabler rocket or files blank document drawn 0001 . JSX The HTML like syntax used in React components. Ligature name The word that a Material icon font turns into a glyph, such as home . Likes Icons you marked with the heart. Quick Pick VS Code's searchable pop up list at the top of the window. Recent Icons you inserted, copied or saved, newest first. Shortcode A text name for an emoji between co"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Icon Studio's search, recommendations and smart insert can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Catalog","Search and recommendations","Smart insert","Hover previews","Licences"],"x":" The catalog is fixed at the version you installed: 17,234 entries in 11 collections. New icons arrive with extension updates. Counts are catalog entries, not the number of style or tone variants. Emoji are drawn by your operating system's emoji font, so their look varies and very new emoji may not display on older systems. Material icons are font glyphs and cannot be exported as SVG. Search matches names, concepts, tags and synonyms, and uses Hindi aliases where available. It is not a full translation of the catalog. For you and Quick Pick recommendations are ranked locally from the text around your cursor about 60 lines either side , the file type, and your likes and use. They are suggestions, not an AI service. Smart insert picks a format by language. It does not look at the exact cursor position, so it cannot tell whether you are inside a string, a tag or a comment. It does not add imports, fonts or build configuration to your project. Inserted SVG includes an accessible name based on the icon name when the artwork has none. Decide whether each icon is decorative or meaningful and adjust the label. Only Auric icon IDs a hyphenated name ending in a four digit number are previewe"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Icon Studio stores, where, and confirmation that it makes no network requests.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/privacy.html","h":["What is stored","What Icon Studio reads","What Icon Studio writes","Clear your data"],"x":" Icon Studio is offline by design. The catalog, SVG artwork and Material preview fonts ship with the extension. It makes no network requests, has no account and collects no telemetry. Data Where Likes up to 500 , recent icons up to 60 and learned preferences for tags and categories VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Search text, filters and current view The panel's saved state in VS Code. Settings Your VS Code settings under auricIconStudio. . To rank recommendations and choose smart insert formats, it reads the language, file name and up to about 60 lines around the cursor of the file you are editing. This stays in memory and is not stored or sent anywhere. Inserting changes the editor content at your cursors or selections. Copying writes to your clipboard. Saving an SVG writes a file only through a save dialog you confirm. Review what you insert or export, especially with multiple cursors or a selection. Run Auric Icon Studio: Clear Likes, Recents and Learned Recommendations and confirm with Clear . "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan Icon Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0"],"x":" The first unified Icon Studio, and the current Marketplace version: Auric artwork, third party icon collections and emoji in one offline workspace. Search 17,234 bundled entries across 11 collections: Auric Modern, Drawn and Playful, Emoji, Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. Work in a compact sidebar or a full editor tab Studio, with a sticky header, Library , For you , Likes and Recent chips, and a collapsible Refine library section with Reset filters . Filter by collection, category, style and supported emoji skin tone. Search by synonyms, including Hindi aliases, with progressive loading as you scroll. Keep likes and recent items, with locally ranked For you recommendations. Language aware output for JSX, JavaScript, markup, CSS, Markdown and data URIs. Insert at multiple cursors, keeping continuation line indentation. Explicit copy formats and saving SVG artwork through a file dialog. Emoji as characters, shortcodes, Unicode code points or HTML entities. Font backed Material glyphs through markup and CSS; no SVG output for them. Hover previews for Auric icon IDs, deferring to an installed owning collection extension. Smart Insert with Ctrl + Alt "},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Icon Studio compares with Icon Hub, the Auric icon collections, File Icons, Emoji and the Icon Pack, and which to install for each job.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Studio","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-studio/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","Which should I install?","How the three collections merge","Name clashes to be aware of","Other related products"],"x":" Auric Artisan publishes several icon extensions for VS Code. They overlap on purpose, so this page explains which one does what. Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Icon Studio ../README.md One offline studio to search and insert every Auric collection, emoji and seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md Seven open source sets with size, colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional catalog metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes: Auric Icons: Modern 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Explorer file and folder icons, plus a File Icon Studio to insert that artwork. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoj"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Icon Hub","d":"What the Auric Artisan Icon Hub extension is, who it is for, how to install it and where to find each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Icon Hub is an icon workspace for Visual Studio Code, connected to the Auric icon tool at https://icons.auricartisan.com. It searches 12,895 icons 32,802 indexed style variants across seven open source collections: Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. All artwork and preview fonts are bundled, so browsing, previewing and exporting work offline. You can refine results by set, style, category and licence, shape the output with size, colour and stroke controls including a full custom colour picker with contrast tools , and insert code that suits your file. In HTML and web framework files, Insert uses the Auric icon CDN and connects a small loader file for you. You can also copy or save an icon in SVG, JSX, React component, HTML, data URI, CSS or CDN form, and export a selection of icons as an SVG sprite or a ZIP with licence notices. Icon Hub can check the website for updated catalog metadata in the background. This is optional, limited to five public JSON files, and never sends your code, searches or usage. Front end developers who use popular open source icon sets and want them tuned and inserted from the editor. Designers who want to reco"},{"t":"Icon Hub guides","d":"Contents of the Icon Hub guides folder, with one line on each guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the task guides and the complete reference for Auric Artisan Icon Hub. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, open the Hub, tour the screen and insert a first icon. browse and refine.md browse and refine.md Search, views, refinements, sorting, cards and the Smart Finder. shape the output.md shape the output.md Size, colour, stroke and the custom colour picker. insert copy and save.md insert copy and save.md Insert by language, the inspector, formats, Quick Search and saving. cdn insertion.md cdn insertion.md How Insert connects the Auric icon CDN, and what your site needs. collect and export.md collect and export.md Select icons and export an SVG sprite or a ZIP. catalog updates.md catalog updates.md Automatic and manual metadata checks, and turning them off. reference.md reference.md Every command, setting, keybinding, collection, format and message. troubleshooting.md troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes. faq.md faq.md Short answers to common questions. "},{"t":"Getting started with Icon Hub","d":"Install Icon Hub, open it in the sidebar or a full panel, tour the screen and insert your first icon.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you begin","1. Install","2. Open the Hub","3. Tour the screen","4. Insert your first icon","Result"],"x":" You need Visual Studio Code 1.85 or later. Browsing, copying and self contained SVG insertion work in untrusted workspaces. Connecting the CDN on Insert needs a trusted workspace. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for Auric Artisan Icon Hub and select Install , or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan icon lib You can also install an official VSIX with Extensions: Install from VSIX… . Sidebar: select Auric Icon Hub in the Activity Bar view name Icon Hub . Refinement controls start collapsed to leave room for artwork. Full panel: run Auric Icon Hub: Open Icon Hub , select the Hub's expand button Open Icon Hub in an editor tab , or select the Icons item in the status bar. Area Contents Header \"Auric Artisan / ICON HUB / CREATIVE WORKSPACE\", Refresh check for metadata updates , Website ↗ and the expand button. Views Library , Favorites , Recent , Selected . Introduction \"Find your symbol. Make it your own.\" and a catalog status badge such as \"Bundled catalog · offline ready\". Search Search your library Ctrl / Cmd K , placeholder \"Try arrow, rocket or navigation…\". Refine library Collection, style, category, licence and sort. Shape the output Si"},{"t":"Browse and refine","d":"Search Icon Hub, switch between Library, Favorites, Recent and Selected, refine by set, style, category and licence, and use the Smart Finder.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/browse-and-refine.html","h":["Search","Views","Refine library","Collections","Cards","Smart Finder","Density and batch size","Result"],"x":" Type in Search your library . Press Ctrl + K Cmd + K anywhere in the Hub to jump there. Every word you type must appear in the icon's name, ID, category, search terms or set. View Shows Library Every icon in the catalog. Favorites Only icons you starred. Recent Icons you used lately up to auricIconLib.maxRecents , default 40 . Selected Only the current selection. Expand Refine library \"Collection, style, category and license\" . Control Options Collection All sets , Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather, Material Style All styles , or a style such as Regular, Bold, Fill, Outline, Filled, Line, 24/outline, Round, Two tone Category All categories or one category License All licenses , MIT, ISC, Remix v1.0, Apache 2.0 Sort Relevance , Name , Set Reset filters clears the search and refinements. It keeps your selection and the current view. The first time you open the Hub, the collection and style start from auricIconLib.defaultSet and auricIconLib.defaultStyle . Collection Icons Styles Default style Licence Phosphor 1,512 Thin, Light, Regular, Bold, Fill, Duotone Regular MIT Tabler 5,093 Outline, Filled Outline MIT Lucide 1,714 Regular Regular ISC Remix 1,689 Line, Fill L"},{"t":"Catalog metadata updates","d":"How Icon Hub checks icons.auricartisan.com for updated catalog metadata, how to refresh manually, and how to turn checks off.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/catalog-updates.html","h":["What is checked","Automatic checks","Check now","Return to the bundled catalog","Turn checks off","Result"],"x":" Icon Hub ships with a complete catalog. It can also check https://icons.auricartisan.com for compatible updates to the catalog's metadata search terms, counts and similar data . Only five public JSON files under /data/ : meta.json , sets.json , stats.json , index.json and material.json . Requests are time limited 15 seconds , size limited, send no credentials and reject redirects. Downloaded metadata must match the bundled icon IDs, sets, styles and font mappings before it replaces the cache. Updates can improve search metadata. They never download new artwork or add icon sets; new artwork arrives with extension updates. With auricIconLib.remoteRefresh.onStartup on the default , Icon Hub checks when it activates, at most once per auricIconLib.remoteRefresh.intervalHours 24 hours by default, 1 to 168 . Failed attempts also wait for the interval. There is no continuous timer. Background failures never show pop ups. The Hub's badge shows the state: Badge Meaning Bundled catalog · offline ready Using the catalog shipped with the extension. Checking metadata… A check is running. Metadata up to date Compatible metadata was downloaded. Offline · using local catalog The check failed; the "},{"t":"Connect the icon CDN","d":"How Icon Hub's Insert connects your HTML and web-framework files to the Auric icon CDN, what file it creates, and what your site needs.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/cdn-insertion.html","h":["What happens on your first Insert","At runtime","Requirements and limits","Messages","Result"],"x":" In HTML and supported web framework files, Insert places an icon placeholder that is drawn at runtime by the Auric icon CDN script, https://icons.auricartisan.com/icon cdn.js . This works for all seven collections, including Material, whose glyphs load their matching font from the CDN. A CDN content delivery network is a web service that serves files, here icon data and fonts, to your pages. 1. Icon Hub checks the target file. It must be saved, local or in a VS Code remote workspace, and the workspace must be trusted. 2. It creates a small file called icons.auricartisan.com.js next to your source file and saves it. This bridge contains loader logic only: no fonts, no embedded font data and no icon catalog. 3. It connects the bridge to your file: File type Connection added HTML <script src=\"./icons.auricartisan.com.js\" defer data auric icons=\"cdn\" </script after <head JavaScript, TypeScript, React JSX and TSX import \"./icons.auricartisan.com.js\"; at the top, after any directives such as \"use client\" Vue, Svelte An import inside the component's <script block a block is added if there is none Astro A browser side <script with the import at the end of the file not a server only frontm"},{"t":"Collect and export","d":"Build a selection of icons in Icon Hub and export it as an SVG sprite or a ZIP with licence notices.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/collect-and-export.html","h":["Build a selection","Export","Limits","Result"],"x":" 1. Select the check button Add to the selection on each icon you want. 2. The selection tray at the bottom shows \"{n} selected\". 3. Switch to the Selected view to see only your selection. Selections are kept when you search, refine or reset filters, and when catalog metadata updates arrive. Button Result Copy sprite Copies the selected SVG icons as one SVG symbol sprite sheet. Export ZIP Saves a ZIP of the selected artwork with licence notices. Clear Empties the selection. Favorites are not changed. One SVG file per selected SVG icon, named after its set and name. MATERIAL ICONS.txt , if you selected Material icons: they are font backed, so they are listed by name and style instead of being exported as SVG. README.txt explaining that each icon remains under its upstream licence. THIRD PARTY LICENSES.md and a licence file for each selected set. Each export handles up to 200 icons. Output uses your current Shape the output size, colour and stroke. Each collection keeps its own licence MIT, ISC, Remix v1.0 or Apache 2.0 . Follow the attribution requirements when you use exported artwork. You have one sprite or ZIP containing exactly the icons you need, with their licences. "},{"t":"Insert, copy and save","d":"How Icon Hub's Insert adapts to your file, the inspector and its formats, Quick Search and the Command Palette, and saving icons to files.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/insert-copy-and-save.html","h":["Insert","The inspector","Formats","Save","From the Command Palette","Result"],"x":" Select Insert on a card, or in the inspector. Icon Hub inserts at every selection in the active editor or, if you clicked into the Hub, the last text editor you used. Editing in Insert produces HTML, Vue, Svelte, Astro A CDN icon placeholder element, and the CDN loader is connected. React JSX or TSX The CDN placeholder as JSX or a React component if you chose one in the inspector , and the loader is connected. JavaScript, TypeScript A named, quoted markup constant, and the loader is connected. CSS, SCSS, Less A self contained CSS declaration. SVG, XML and other languages Self contained SVG markup. See Connect the icon CDN cdn insertion.md for what the loader is and what it needs. Material icons can only be inserted into HTML or web framework files: \"Insert Material icons into HTML or a web framework file to connect your CDN. Use Copy for other formats.\" Read only editors are refused: \"The selected editor is read only. Use Copy instead.\" A rejected edit is reported, not recorded as a success. With no editor, the output is copied and VS Code says \"No writable editor selected; icon copied to the clipboard.\" Select a card's preview to open the inspector. It shows a large preview, the "},{"t":"Shape the output","d":"Set icon size, colour and stroke width in Icon Hub, and use the custom colour picker with contrast tools.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/shape-the-output.html","h":["The colour picker","Result"],"x":" Expand Shape the output \"Size, color and stroke\" . The controls apply to the previews and to everything you insert, copy, save or export. Control Effect Range Size Width and height of the output, in pixels. 8 to 512 Color The icon colour. Until you choose one, artwork uses currentColor and follows the editor's text colour. Any colour Stroke Stroke width for artwork drawn with strokes. 0.5 to 4 Stroke only affects stroke based artwork. It does not turn filled glyphs into outline icons. These controls are for the current session. To change the starting values permanently, set auricIconLib.size default 24 , auricIconLib.color default currentColor , or a six digit hex colour and auricIconLib.strokeWidth default 2 . Select the Color swatch to open the Auric colour picker. It includes: a colour spectrum; colour space inputs; named colours; recent choices; shade ramps; harmonies; WCAG and APCA contrast checks against a background you choose, with tools to adjust towards AA or AAA; an eyedropper, where the host supports it. The swatch tooltip reads \"Icon colour {hex} — contrast, ramps and harmonies included\". Previews and output use your size, colour and stroke, so what you insert matches"},{"t":"Icon Hub reference","d":"Every command, keybinding, setting, view, collection, format and message in Auric Artisan Icon Hub 0.1.0.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keybindings","Settings","Views and menus","Hub controls","Collections","Insertion by language","Limits","Messages you may see"],"x":" This reference describes version 0.1.0 as published on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Category in the Command Palette: Auric Icon Hub . Command ID What it does Open Icon Hub auricIconLib.openStudio Opens the full Hub panel. Quick Search Icons auricIconLib.quickSearch Search box, then a Quick Pick of matches; runs your click action. Smart Insert Icon auricIconLib.smartInsert Same flow as Quick Search; insertion follows the editor language. Copy Icon As… auricIconLib.copyAs Pick an icon and a format; copies. Save Icon As… auricIconLib.saveIcon Pick an icon; saves in your copy format. Show Favorite Icons auricIconLib.showFavorites Quick Search limited to favorites. Show Recent Icons auricIconLib.showRecents Quick Search limited to recent icons. Refresh Icon Catalog auricIconLib.refreshCatalog Checks for compatible metadata now. Clear Downloaded Icon Catalog auricIconLib.clearCache Returns to the bundled metadata. Open Auric Icon Tool auricIconLib.openWebsite Opens https://icons.auricartisan.com in your browser. Clear Icon Favorites and Recents auricIconLib.clearPersonalization Clears favorites and recents immediately, without a confirmation. Export Selected Icons auricIconLib.exportS"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common problems with Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":[],"x":" Symptom Why it happens What to do The catalog gained no new icons after Refresh . Refresh updates compatible metadata only. Install an extension update for new artwork. The badge says Offline · using local catalog . The metadata check could not reach or validate the website. Local browsing still works. Check your connection or try Refresh later; automatic retries wait for the interval. Material names such as 4k plus appear as text on my page. The Material font is not loaded, often from an older insertion that used a local font. Reinsert the icon with the current version so it uses a CDN placeholder, save the source, and reload the page with network access. Old spans are not rewritten automatically. CDN icons appear blank on my site. The page has no network access, your content security policy blocks the CDN, the bridge file is not served, or the CDN does not yet allow cross origin access to its catalog and fonts. Check network access, CSP and that the bridge is deployed. For self contained artwork, use Copy as SVG or Export ZIP . Insert says the workspace must be trusted. Creating the CDN bridge needs a trusted workspace. Trust the workspace, or use Copy . Insert says to save the "},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/docs/faq.html","h":["Why is the extension ID \"icon-lib\" when it is called Icon Hub?","Does Icon Hub work offline?","Does it upload my code or searches?","Why does Insert create a file in my project?","How do I get self-contained SVG instead?","Does it include Auric artwork or emoji?","Can I use exported icons commercially?"],"x":" The extension keeps its original ID, auric artisan.auric artisan icon lib , so existing auricIconLib. settings, favorites and recent items carry over. Its display name is Auric Artisan Icon Hub . Yes, for browsing, searching, previewing, copying, saving and exporting. The optional metadata checks and pages that use the CDN need a network connection. No. Metadata checks request five public JSON files and include no source code, search terms, favorites or usage. In HTML and web framework files, Insert connects the Auric icon CDN through a small loader file, icons.auricartisan.com.js . It is only created on an explicit Insert. Copy and Save never create files. See Connect the icon CDN cdn insertion.md . Use Copy or Save with the SVG format, export a ZIP, or insert into a CSS, SVG or other non web file. No. Icon Hub covers the seven open source collections. Auric Artisan Icon Studio adds the Auric Modern, Drawn and Playful artwork and emoji. Each collection keeps its own licence: MIT Phosphor, Tabler, Heroicons, Feather , ISC Lucide , Remix v1.0 Remix and Apache 2.0 Material . The ZIP export includes the licence notices. "},{"t":"Icon Hub: other information","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" Supporting pages for Auric Artisan Icon Hub: terms, shortcuts, limits, a comparison with the other Auric icon extensions, the release history and its network and privacy behaviour. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in Icon Hub. shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Keybindings, in Hub keys and commands. limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What Icon Hub can and cannot do. related.md related.md Comparison with Icon Studio, the Auric collections, File Icons, Emoji and Icon Pack. release notes.md release notes.md User facing history. privacy.md privacy.md What is stored and exactly what uses the network. "},{"t":"Shortcuts and commands","d":"Keybindings, keys inside the Hub and every command in Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Keybindings","Keys inside the Hub","Commands"],"x":" Action Windows and Linux macOS Quick Search Icons Ctrl + Alt + Shift + I Cmd + Alt + Shift + I Key Action Ctrl + K / Cmd + K Focus search Arrow keys Move between cards or dropdown options Enter Open the inspector for the focused card F Star the focused card Home / End First or last dropdown option Escape Close a dropdown or the inspector Type \"Auric Icon Hub\" in the Command Palette: Open Icon Hub , Quick Search Icons , Smart Insert Icon , Copy Icon As… , Save Icon As… , Show Favorite Icons , Show Recent Icons , Refresh Icon Catalog , Clear Downloaded Icon Catalog , Open Auric Icon Tool , Clear Icon Favorites and Recents . The editor right click menu has Smart Insert Icon and Copy Icon As… . "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the terms used in Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Term Meaning Bridge The small icons.auricartisan.com.js loader file Icon Hub creates next to your source on the first CDN Insert. Catalog metadata The data describing icons names, terms, counts , separate from the artwork itself. CDN A content delivery network: a web service that serves icon data and fonts to your pages. CDN placeholder An element such as <span data icon=\"set:name\" … that the CDN script turns into an icon. Content security policy A website rule listing which sources may load scripts, fonts and data. currentColor A CSS keyword meaning \"use the surrounding text colour\". Data URI Text that embeds a file directly, starting data: . Font backed icon An icon drawn from a font glyph Material , not an SVG file. Indexed variant One style of one icon. Icon Hub indexes 32,802. Selection Icons you ticked for export. Up to 200 per export. Smart Finder A local panel of recent icons and a rotating sample of the catalog. SVG sprite One SVG file containing several icons as reusable symbols. "},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Artisan Icon Hub can and cannot do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Catalog","Output","CDN insertion","Search","Licences"],"x":" 12,895 icons and 32,802 indexed variants in seven collections, bundled with the extension. Metadata updates never add artwork or sets; new artwork arrives with extension updates. The combined Remix sprite is excluded because it is not a standalone icon. Material is font backed and never exported as SVG. Stroke controls only affect stroke based artwork. The eyedropper in the colour picker depends on the host. Contrast checks in the colour picker are guidance for choosing a colour against one background. Exports are capped at 200 icons each. CDN pages need network access and a content security policy that allows the CDN. The bridge is created only for saved files in trusted workspaces; untitled files, untrusted workspaces and unsupported file types are refused. JavaScript imports need module aware tooling; server rendered frameworks need the bridge in a client entry. At release, the published README noted that cross origin access to the CDN's catalog files and fonts had not yet been enabled, so pages on other origins could show blank icons until it is. Previously generated local font stylesheets are not deleted automatically, and old local font spans are not rewritten. Search matche"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Icon Hub stores, exactly what uses the network, and what is never sent.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/privacy.html","h":["What uses the network","What is stored","What is written to your project","Security"],"x":" No account, telemetry or search upload is required. Feature What is contacted When Metadata checks Five public JSON files under https://icons.auricartisan.com/data/ On activation at most once per interval and when you select Refresh . Can be turned off. Open Auric Icon Tool and Website ↗ https://icons.auricartisan.com in your browser Only when you select them. Pages using CDN output The CDN script, catalog and fonts When a visitor loads your page, not from VS Code. Metadata requests send no credentials and include none of your source code, search terms, favorites or usage history. Like any web request, they reveal ordinary connection information such as your IP address to the host. To stop all catalog network checks, set auricIconLib.remoteRefresh.enabled to false . Data Where Favorites and recent icons VS Code's extension storage on this machine. Downloaded metadata The extension's private storage folder; cleared by Clear Downloaded Icon Catalog . Search, filters, selection and colour history The Hub's saved view state. Settings Your VS Code settings under auricIconLib. . Only the CDN bridge file, and only on an explicit Insert into a supported file in a trusted workspace. Copy, "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"User-facing history of Auric Artisan Icon Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 — 23 September 2026"],"x":" The first release of Auric Artisan Icon Hub , and the current Marketplace version. 12,895 icons and 32,802 indexed variants across Phosphor, Tabler, Lucide, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. A full editor panel and a compact Activity Bar sidebar, with sticky navigation and responsive cards. Search and refine by collection, style, category and licence, with sorting and a one click filter reset. Favorites, recent icons and a working selection. Collapsible filter and appearance sections, compact by default in the sidebar. Custom dropdowns for filters and the inspector's format chooser, with full keyboard support. The Auric colour picker: spectrum, colour space inputs, eyedropper where supported, named colours, recent choices, shade ramps, harmonies, and WCAG and APCA contrast checks with AA and AAA adjustment. currentColor kept until you pick a colour. Keyboard and hover tooltips, announced actions, focus kept on cards during updates, and support for narrow layouts, light themes, high contrast and reduced motion. CDN insertion for HTML and supported frameworks across all seven collections, including Material fonts, through a small reusable bridge created only on explicit Insert"},{"t":"Related extensions and comparison","d":"How Icon Hub compares with Icon Studio, the Auric icon collections, File Icons, Emoji and the Icon Pack.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Icon Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-icon-hub/others/related.html","h":["At a glance","Icon Hub or Icon Studio?","Other related products"],"x":" Extension Main job Explorer file icon theme Artwork Network Icon Hub ../README.md Seven open source sets with colour and stroke controls, sprite and ZIP export, and CDN insertion. No 12,895 icons Optional metadata checks; CDN output loads from the web Icon Studio ../../auric artisan icon studio/README.md One offline studio for every Auric collection, emoji and the same seven open source sets. No 17,234 entries in 11 collections None Auric Icons: Modern ../../auric icons modern/README.md Modern icon library plus the Modern file and folder icon theme. Yes 720 library icons; 408 theme icons None Auric Icons: Drawn ../../auric icons drawn/README.md Warm Drawn icon library. No 480 icons None Auric Icons: Playful ../../auric icons playful/README.md Emoji style icon library. No 1,225 icons None File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md Explorer file and folder icons in three styles, plus File Icon Studio. Yes: Facet, Playful and Modern 1,464 SVG assets None Emoji ../../auric artisan emoji/README.md Emoji Studio. No 1,914 emoji None Icon Pack ../../auric artisan icon pack/README.md Installs Modern, Playful, Drawn and Emoji together. Through Modern None of its own Needs the Marke"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Live","d":"What Auric Artisan Live does, who it is for, how to install it and where to find every guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Live full name Auric Artisan Live — Live Server & Preview is a local development server inside VS Code. Run Go Live and it serves your project folder over a real HTTP server on your own machine, opens it in your browser or in a preview beside your code, and updates connected pages when you save. It works for plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript, and it can also run or connect to a backend: PHP, Python, Ruby, Go, Java, Node.js and more. Around the server it gives you the tools you normally need a second terminal or a browser extension for: HTTPS with a generated certificate, an API proxy so your page and your backend share one origin, mock endpoints and a JSON file REST database for APIs that do not exist yet, a request inspector with curl and fetch copies and HAR export, slow network simulation, a phone QR code for testing on a real device, and an in page developer dashboard Alt + Shift + D showing page health, network, storage and server state. Everything runs locally. The extension has no runtime npm dependencies and no telemetry. It is a development server, not production hosting. Front end developers who want live reload and a quick preview while editing HTML, CSS and "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Live guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Live task guides and reference.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" Start with the getting started guide for a tour of every surface. Each task guide covers one workflow from start to result. The reference lists all 54 commands, the seven keyboard shortcuts and all 103 settings. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, the screen tour status bar, sidebar views, control panel, preview, dashboard and a first live reload session serve and live reload.md serve and live reload.md Go Live, choose the folder and port, reload triggers, hot swap, reload storm protection, exclusions preview and devices.md preview and devices.md The preview beside the editor, device presets, rotation, network address and phone QR code run targets and backends.md run targets and backends.md Detected runtimes and framework dev servers, custom commands, URL only backends, readiness php and cgi.md php and cgi.md Run .php pages through php cgi or the PHP built in server api proxy and mocks.md api proxy and mocks.md Proxy rules, mock routes with placeholders, the JSON REST database inspect requests.md inspect requests.md The Requests view and panel section: filter, sort, details, replay, curl/fetch, HAR browser dashboard.md browser dashboard.md The in pag"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan Live","d":"Install Auric Artisan Live, learn where each control lives, and run a first live-reload session.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","The screen tour","Your first live-reload session"],"x":" This guide installs the extension, tours every surface it adds to VS Code, and ends with a page that updates when you save. 1. Check that VS Code is version 1.95 or newer Help › About . 2. In the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for @id:auric artisan.auric artisan live and select Install . Or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan live 3. Open the folder that contains your website with File › Open Folder… . Auric Live serves folders; with no folder open, its view shows an Open Folder button instead. Backend runtimes PHP, Python, Node.js and so on are not included. Install the ones your project needs separately. On the right of the status bar: Go Live broadcast icon when nothing is running. Select it to start a server. The port number radio tower icon while a server runs, with +1 , +2 and so on when several workspace folders are live. Hover for a summary: run target, served root, live reload and connected pages, proxy rules and upstream state, mock routes, network profile and request count. Select it to open the Auric Live menu. A spinning icon with a warning background when the server is up but a proxied backend is not answering yet. Hide the item wi"},{"t":"Proxy an API, mock endpoints and a REST database","d":"Forward API paths to a backend, answer endpoints that do not exist yet, and serve a full REST API from a JSON file with Auric Live.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/api-proxy-and-mocks.html","h":["Proxy an API path to a backend","Mock endpoints","A full REST API from a JSON file"],"x":" Auric Live can answer a request in several ways. For each request it tries, in order: a mock route , the REST database , a proxy rule , then static files or a CGI handler . So you can forward a whole API to a real backend and still override one endpoint with a mock. A proxy forwards requests for a path to another server and passes the answer back. With /api proxied to your backend, the page and its API share one origin: no CORS workaround, no hard coded backend address in your front end code, and cookies behave as they will in production. 1. Run Auric Live: Add API Proxy Route… , or select the arrows button in the Routes and Mocks view title bar. 2. Proxy route 1 of 2 : enter the path prefix to forward, for example /api . It must start with / . 3. Proxy route 2 of 2 : enter where it should go, for example http://localhost:3000 . It must start with http:// or https:// . 4. Auric Live says Auric Live now forwards /api to http://localhost:3000. This lasts for the session. Choose Save to config file to keep it in auric.live.json . Rules added this way forward WebSockets and rewrite the Host header to the target. The short form maps a prefix to a target: json { \"proxy\": { \"/api\": \"http"},{"t":"Use the in-page browser dashboard","d":"Open the Auric Live developer dashboard over a served page to see page health, network delivery, server state, storage, environment, requests and console messages.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/browser-dashboard.html","h":["Open and close it","The header","The seven tabs","Console capture","The Auric cursor","Scrolling and keyboard","Performance of the dashboard itself"],"x":" Auric Live can place a developer dashboard over any page it serves. It shows how the page is doing and what the server is doing, without opening browser developer tools, and it works on a phone too. In a served page, press Alt + Shift + D . Change the keys with auricLive.dashboard.shortcut modifier names joined with + , for example Ctrl+Shift+. . Close it with the × button, or press Escape an open drop down closes first . The dashboard is on by default auricLive.dashboard.enabled . It is added to the page along with the live reload script. If a framework's own dev server handles reloading, Auric Live still adds the dashboard on its own auricLive.dashboard.independent . The dashboard's styles and menus are kept separate from your page in a Shadow DOM , so it does not restyle your site and your site does not restyle it. It makes no requests for external fonts or branding. Control What it does auricartisan.com ↗ Open the Auric Artisan website in a new tab Shortcut badge Shows the key combination that opens the dashboard Use site cursor / Use Auric cursor Switch between the Auric pointer and the page's own cursor Pause metrics / Resume metrics Stop or restart sampling ↻ Refresh dashbo"},{"t":"Serve over HTTPS","d":"Serve your site over HTTPS with a generated or imported certificate, and make browsers and phones trust it.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/https-and-certificates.html","h":["Turn HTTPS on with a generated certificate","Use your own certificate","Trust on a phone","Limits"],"x":" Browsers only allow some features in a secure context : service workers, navigator.clipboard , the camera, microphone and geolocation. On localhost plain HTTP counts as secure, but on any other address, such as your computer's network address on a phone, it does not. Serving over HTTPS makes those features testable on a phone. Two things are separate: Encryption. Auric Live encrypts the connection as soon as HTTPS is on. Trust. Whether the browser accepts the certificate without a warning depends on whether that device trusts it. Auric Live does not install trust on your computer or phone. 1. Run Auric Live: Toggle HTTPS , or use Toggle HTTPS in the Auric Live menu. 2. Confirm Enable HTTPS . The message explains that the server will use a self signed certificate and that the browser will warn once. 3. The server restarts on https:// . Addresses you copy and the phone QR code now use https:// . 4. The first time you open the site, the browser warns that the certificate is not trusted. Accept it for this address to continue. To make it permanent, set auricLive.https.enabled to true in settings or \"https\": { \"enabled\": true } in auric.live.json . The generated certificate is self sig"},{"t":"Inspect requests","d":"See every request the Auric Live server handles, find slow or failing ones, and copy, replay or export them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/inspect-requests.html","h":["The Requests view","The control panel's Requests section","Copy as curl or fetch","Replay a request","Export HAR","Privacy and limits","Output channel logging"],"x":" The request inspector records each request the Auric Live server handles: method, path, status, which handler answered, time taken, size, and by default headers and bodies. Credentials are masked before anything is stored. You can inspect requests in three places: the Requests view in the Auric Live sidebar; the 02 / Requests section of the control panel Auric Live: Open Control Panel or Auric Live: Open Request Inspector ; the Requests tab of the in page browser dashboard. Each row reads METHOD /path with status · handler · time beside it, for example GET /api/users — 200 · proxy · 34ms . Select a row to open Show Request Detail . Right click a row for: Replay Request Copy Request as curl Copy Request as fetch The title bar has Clear Request Log and Export Requests as HAR . The section searches the latest 200 captured requests. Control Options Search Type part of a path, method, status or handler. Ctrl + F Cmd + F on macOS focuses it Status All statuses , 2xx , 3xx , 4xx , 5xx Method All methods , GET , POST , PUT , PATCH , DELETE , HEAD , OPTIONS Handler All handlers , static , proxy , mock , rest , cgi , listing , redirect , error , client , live reload Sort Newest first , Slow"},{"t":"Simulate a slow network","d":"Slow down every client of the Auric Live server, including a phone, to test how your site behaves on slow connections.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/network-simulation.html","h":["Choose a profile","A custom profile","What is shaped","What it is not"],"x":" Network shaping makes the server answer as if the connection were slower: it adds latency a delay before each response and limits bandwidth how fast bytes flow . Because it happens in the server, it applies to every client, including a phone on your network where browser developer tools are not available. 1. Run Auric Live: Simulate Network Profile… , choose Simulate a network profile in the Auric Live menu, or use Network shaping in the control panel's Overview . 2. Pick a profile. The current one is ticked. Profile Latency Download Upload off none unlimited unlimited slow 3g 400 ms 400 kbps 400 kbps 3g 150 ms 1600 kbps 750 kbps 4g 40 ms 9000 kbps 3000 kbps cable 8 ms 30000 kbps 10000 kbps custom your value your value your value Rates are in kilobits per second. The choice lasts for the session. To keep it, set auricLive.throttle.profile in settings or throttle.profile in auric.live.json . Set the profile to custom and choose the numbers: Setting Default Range Meaning auricLive.throttle.latencyMs 0 0–60000 Delay added before each response auricLive.throttle.downloadKbps 0 0 or more Download ceiling; 0 means unlimited auricLive.throttle.uploadKbps 0 0–1000000 Upload ceiling; 0 mea"},{"t":"Run PHP sites","d":"Run .php pages in Auric Live through php-cgi or the PHP built-in server, and run other CGI scripts.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/php-and-cgi.html","h":["Run PHP through CGI","Run the PHP built-in server or a framework","In an untrusted workspace"],"x":" A plain static server sends a .php file to the browser as a download. Auric Live can run it instead, in one of two ways. Way How it works Best for PHP through CGI Auric Live runs each .php request through php cgi and serves the result itself Classic PHP sites made of .php pages, with live reload and the dashboard PHP built in server, Laravel or Symfony Auric Live starts PHP's own server or php artisan serve , or symfony server:start and forwards to it Front controller applications and frameworks CGI Common Gateway Interface is a standard way for a web server to run a program for each request and send back what it prints. With php cgi , $ GET , $ POST , headers, cookies, sessions and header calls all work. Both ways need PHP installed on your computer, and both need a trusted workspace. 1. Install PHP so that php cgi is on your PATH , or note its full path. 2. Open the folder and run Auric Live: Go Live . The first time, Auric Live notices the PHP files and offers Enable PHP . Choose it. Or choose PHP through CGI in Auric Live: Select Run Target… , or set auricLive.cgi.enabled to true . 3. Open a .php page. It runs, and its output is served. When you choose Enable PHP , the index l"},{"t":"Preview, devices and phone testing","d":"Preview your served site beside the editor at device sizes, and open it on a real phone with a locally generated QR code.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/preview-and-devices.html","h":["The preview beside the editor","Test on a real phone"],"x":" The preview is a browser frame inside VS Code, opened next to your code. It shows the served site and follows live reload exactly as a browser does. Auric Live: Open Preview Beside — Ctrl + Alt + K Cmd + Alt + K on macOS . Preview in the notification that appears when the server starts. Preview beside in the control panel's Overview . Set auricLive.open to preview to open it every time the server starts. If no server is running, opening the preview starts one first. There is one preview tab; opening it again moves it to the new address. Control What it does Reload Reload this frame Address box Type an address and press Enter , or select Go Device size Choose a size from the list below Rotate Swap width and height Reload all pages Reload every connected browser, not only this frame Open in browser Open the current address in your default browser Size readout The frame's width × height, and the scale when it is shrunk to fit Auric Artisan ↗ Open auricartisan.com in your browser Device Width × height CSS pixels Responsive Fills the panel iPhone SE 375 × 667 iPhone 15 393 × 852 Pixel 8 412 × 915 iPad 820 × 1180 Laptop 1280 × 800 Desktop 1600 × 900 When a size is larger than the panel,"},{"t":"Project configuration","d":"Keep an Auric Live setup with your repository in auric.live.json, control exclusions with .auricignore-live, and understand how settings, project files and session changes combine.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/project-configuration.html","h":["Where settings come from","The project file: auric.live.json","Workspace trust and the project file","Exclusions: .auricignore-live","Session records: .auric-live/","Multi-root workspaces"],"x":" Auric Live combines four layers. A later layer wins: 1. Built in defaults. 2. VS Code settings — user, workspace and folder settings with the auricLive. prefix. 3. The project file — auric.live.json in the workspace folder. 4. Session overrides — changes you make with commands, the Auric Live menu or the control panel. They last until you close or reload the VS Code window. So a repository can carry its own proxy, mock and CGI setup, and you can still try something for a moment without editing a file. 1. Run Auric Live: Create Project Config File , or select Create a config file in the Servers view when nothing is running. 2. Auric Live writes a starter auric.live.json in the workspace folder and opens it. The starter file: json { // Auric Artisan Live — project configuration. // Every key is optional and overrides the matching auricLive. setting. \"port\": 5500, \"spa\": { \"enabled\": false, \"fallback\": \"/index.html\" }, \"cleanUrls\": false, // Send /api to a backend you already run, so the front end talks to the // real thing without a CORS shim. \"proxy\": { \"path\": \"/api\", \"target\": \"http://localhost:3000\", \"changeOrigin\": true, \"ws\": true } , // Or answer /api yourself while that back"},{"t":"Run a backend or framework dev server","d":"Let Auric Live run your project's backend or framework dev server (PHP, Python, Ruby, Go, Java, Node.js and more), or connect to one already running, and serve it through one address.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/run-targets-and-backends.html","h":["Choose a run target","What is detected","The first-run suggestion","Framework dev server commands","Add your own command","Find a running backend","Waiting for a backend","Check prerequisites"],"x":" A run target is what actually serves your site. By default it is Static files : Auric Live serves the folder itself. For a project with a backend or a framework dev server, you can choose a different run target. Auric Live then starts that process, waits for it to be ready, and forwards requests to it, so you still use one address with the dashboard, request inspector, network simulation and phone QR code. Auric Live does not install runtimes or packages. PHP, Python, Ruby, Go, Java, Node.js and the rest must already be installed and on your PATH , and the project's dependencies must already be installed. Running a command needs a trusted workspace. In Restricted Mode only static files are served. 1. Run Auric Live: Select Run Target… Ctrl + Alt + J , select the Run target row in the Servers view, or use the control panel's 03 / Runtime section. 2. The list, titled Run target — folder name , shows in this order: your saved commands from auricLive.runProfiles ; the detected framework dev server, if any; detected language runtimes; Static files , which is always available. Each entry shows its command and why it was detected, for example manage.py is present . The current target has"},{"t":"Serve a folder with live reload","d":"Start the Auric Live server, choose what it serves and where, and control how and when connected pages update.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/serve-and-live-reload.html","h":["Start the server","Choose what is served","Choose the address","Control how pages update","Responses and caching","Changes while running","Stop"],"x":" Live reload means the pages you have open in a browser update by themselves when you change a file. Auric Live adds a small script to every HTML page it serves; the script listens to the server and refreshes the page, or swaps just the changed stylesheet or image, when you save. Use whichever is closest: Auric Live: Go Live — Ctrl + Alt + L Cmd + Alt + L on macOS , the Go Live status bar item, the Go Live button in the Servers view, or the editor's Run menu › Auric Live . Serve This Folder — right click a folder in the Explorer. That folder becomes the served root for this session. Open with Auric Live — right click an HTML, XHTML, PHP or Markdown file. The server starts if needed and opens that file's address. A file outside the served root cannot be opened this way. With several workspace folders, Go Live asks Which folder should Auric Live serve? . Each workspace folder gets its own server and port. Auric Live: Select Active Server chooses which one the panel and commands act on; Auric Live: Stop All Servers Ctrl + Alt + Shift + L stops every one. When the server starts: 1. What opens depends on auricLive.open : default opens your default browser, preview opens the preview besi"},{"t":"Reference: commands, keys and settings","d":"Every Auric Artisan Live command, keyboard shortcut, menu entry, view and setting, with types, defaults and ranges.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Keyboard shortcuts","Where commands appear","Views","Settings","Files Auric Live reads and writes"],"x":" This page lists everything Auric Artisan Live 0.2.1 contributes to VS Code: 54 commands, 7 keyboard shortcuts, 3 sidebar views and 103 settings. Command titles appear in the Command Palette with the Auric Live: prefix. Command ID Keys What it does Auric Live: Select Active Server auricLive.selectServer — Choose which workspace folder's server the panel and commands act on Auric Live: Toggle Browser Console Capture auricLive.toggleConsole — Turn browser console capture on or off for this session Auric Live: Use HTTPS Certificate and Key auricLive.configureCertificate — Import and validate a PEM certificate and matching private key, then turn HTTPS on Auric Live: Diagnose Project and Runtime auricLive.diagnose — Open a local report on configuration, run targets and prerequisites, with credentials redacted Auric Live: Go Live auricLive.goLive Ctrl + Alt + L macOS Cmd + Alt + L Start serving the workspace folder, or reopen a server that is already running Auric Live: Stop Server auricLive.stop — Stop the active server Auric Live: Stop All Servers auricLive.stopAll Ctrl + Alt + Shift + L macOS Cmd + Alt + Shift + L Stop every Auric Live server Auric Live: Restart Server auricLive.resta"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common Auric Artisan Live problems, from pages that do not update to phones that cannot connect.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Starting","Live reload","Backends and proxies","PHP","Phones and other devices","Requests","Preview and dashboard"],"x":" For anything not listed, run Auric Live: Diagnose Project and Runtime and Auric Live: Show Log , then see Get support ../../install and setup/docs/get support.md . Why: no folder is open. Auric Live serves folders, not single files. Fix: open the folder with File › Open Folder… , then go live. Why: usually the port is taken and auricLive.portStrategy is fail , or the address cannot be bound. Fix: choose Change Port in the message, set the port to 0 for a free one, or set the strategy back to increment . Show Log has the exact reason. Why: auricLive.showStatusBar is off, or no folder is open. Fix: turn the setting on, or use Auric Live: Go Live from the Command Palette. Why: Start , Stop and Restart Framework Dev Server only appear in trusted workspaces. Fix: run Workspaces: Manage Workspace Trust and trust the folder. Why: live reload is off, the trigger does not match how you work, the file is excluded, or the page was opened before the server started. Fix: 1. Check the Servers view: Live reload should show a number of connected pages, not off . 2. If files are written by a build tool rather than saved in VS Code, set auricLive.liveReload.reloadOnSave to change . 3. Check auricLi"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Live.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/docs/faq.html","h":["Is Auric Live a production web server?","Does it need Node.js or other software?","What is the default address?","Can other people on my network see my site?","Why does the page not reload for files my build tool writes?","Can I use it with Vite, Next.js, Angular or another framework?","Can I run PHP?","Can I serve several projects at once?","Does it work in an untrusted folder?","Does it work over Remote SSH, in containers or in virtual workspaces?","Does HTTPS remove the browser warning?","Is my request data sent anywhere?","Can I use it in Hindi?","How is it different from other live servers?"],"x":" No. It is a development server for your own machine. Do not use it to host a public site. Serving static files needs nothing extra. Running a backend needs that backend's runtime PHP, Python, Node.js and so on and the project's dependencies, installed by you. The extension itself has no runtime npm dependencies. http://localhost:5500 , or the next free port. Change it with auricLive.port . In a trusted workspace the default host 0.0.0.0 lets devices on your local network reach the server, subject to your firewall. Set auricLive.host to 127.0.0.1 to keep it on your machine, or turn on auricLive.auth.enabled to require a password. The default trigger reacts only to saves in VS Code, so generated and synchronised files cannot keep refreshing the page. Set auricLive.liveReload.reloadOnSave to change for build tools. Yes. Choose the framework's dev server as the run target. Auric Live starts it, forwards to it and keeps the framework's own hot reload in charge, while still adding its dashboard. Yes, through php cgi or the PHP built in server, with PHP installed. See Run PHP sites php and cgi.md . Yes. Each folder of a multi root workspace gets its own server and port. Use Select Active"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Live.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the Auric Artisan Live guides: terms, shortcuts, built in limits and safeguards, privacy, related products and the version history. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Auric Live documentation shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every keyboard shortcut limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md Built in limits, safeguards and what the measurements mean privacy.md privacy.md What stays on your machine and what uses the network related.md related.md Related extensions, tools and pages release notes.md release notes.md What changed in each version "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut Auric Artisan Live provides in VS Code, the control panel, the preview and the in-page dashboard.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/shortcuts.html","h":["VS Code","Control panel","Preview","In a served page"],"x":" These work whenever a folder is open. Change them in Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts by searching for auricLive . Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + L Cmd + Alt + L Auric Live: Go Live Ctrl + Alt + Shift + L Cmd + Alt + Shift + L Auric Live: Stop All Servers Ctrl + Alt + K Cmd + Alt + K Auric Live: Open Preview Beside Ctrl + Alt + Shift + K Cmd + Alt + Shift + K Auric Live: Open Live Menu Ctrl + Alt + J Cmd + Alt + J Auric Live: Select Run Target… Ctrl + Alt + U Cmd + Alt + U Auric Live: Reload Connected Pages Ctrl + Alt + Shift + I Cmd + Alt + Shift + I Auric Live: Open Control Panel The other 47 commands have no default shortcut. Assign one in the Keyboard Shortcuts editor if you use them often. Keys What they do Ctrl + F Cmd + F Focus the search box in the Requests section Escape Close request details and return focus, or close an open menu Arrow keys, type ahead, Enter Move through and choose from drop down menus Keys What they do Enter in the address box Load the typed address Keys What they do Alt + Shift + D Open the developer dashboard change with auricLive.dashboard.shortcut Escape Close an open dashboard menu, then the dashboard Left and right arrows, Home"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Auric Artisan Live documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Backend — the part of a site that runs on a server: an API, a PHP application, a framework dev server. CGI Common Gateway Interface — a standard way for a web server to run a program for each request and send back what it prints. Auric Live uses it to run PHP through php cgi . CORS cross origin resource sharing — the browser rules that decide whether a page from one address may call another. A proxy avoids CORS problems by putting the page and its API on one address. Cross origin isolation — a pair of response headers that unlock features such as SharedArrayBuffer , at the cost of blocking cross origin resources that do not opt in. Dev server — a framework's own development server, such as the one npm run dev starts for Vite or Next.js. Developer dashboard — the panel Auric Live places over a served page, opened with Alt + Shift + D . Handler — the part of Auric Live that answered a request: static , proxy , mock , rest , cgi , listing , redirect , error , client or live reload . HAR HTTP Archive — a standard JSON file format for a list of requests and responses. Hot swap — replacing a changed stylesheet or image in a page without reloading it. Live reload — updating open pages au"},{"t":"Limits and safeguards","d":"The built-in limits of Auric Artisan Live, why they exist, which ones you can change, and how to read its measurements.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Built-in limits","Deliberate boundaries","Network simulation accuracy","Reading the measurements","Redaction"],"x":" Auric Live keeps memory bounded and protects your data by design. Most limits can be changed; the safeguards around privacy and workspace trust are deliberate. Limit Default Change it with Requests kept by the inspector 500 auricLive.inspector.maxEntries 20–10000 Requests shown in the control panel Newest 200 — Body captured per request or response 256 KiB auricLive.inspector.maxBodyBytes 0–8388608 Incoming request body 8 MiB; larger bodies get 413; 0 rejects all non empty bodies auricLive.maxRequestBodyBytes Time to receive a request body 30 seconds; stalled bodies get 408; 0 disables it auricLive.requestBodyTimeoutMs Console capture Off; when on, 200 entries, 2,000 characters per message, 20 messages per second auricLive.console. Session records On; 200 request summaries, 12 sessions, about 5 MiB per session auricLive.records. Reloads before storm protection 3 in 10 seconds auricLive.liveReload.stormLimit , auricLive.liveReload.stormWindowMs Dev server restarts 5 auricLive.devServer.maxRestarts 0–50 Wait for a starting backend 25 seconds auricLive.upstream.waitTimeoutMs Proxy request timeout 30 seconds per rule timeoutMs in a proxy rule CGI script run time 30 seconds cgi.timeout"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Live keeps on your machine, what can reach the network, and how captured data is protected.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays on your machine","What can reach the network","How captured data is protected"],"x":" No telemetry. Auric Live sends no usage data anywhere. The server runs locally. Your files are served from your computer. Requests are recorded locally in the inspector, in memory, and optionally as local session records under .auric live/ . The phone QR code is generated locally. No address goes to a QR service. The translation into Hindi is bundled. No translation service receives your data. The dashboard makes no external requests for fonts or branding. Other devices on your network. With the default host 0.0.0.0 in a trusted workspace, devices on your local network can open the served site, subject to your firewall. Set auricLive.host to 127.0.0.1 to prevent this, or require a login with auricLive.auth.enabled . Proxy targets. Requests for proxied paths go to the targets you configure. Run targets. Commands you run as run targets do whatever they are written to do. Links you choose. Links to auricartisan.com in the panel, preview and dashboard open in your browser. Data Protection Credential headers Authorization , Cookie , Set Cookie and similar Always masked before storage Sensitive query parameters and JSON or form fields Redacted by default auricLive.inspector.redactSensit"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"What changed in each published version of Auric Artisan Live.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.2.1 — English and Hindi (11 September 2026)","0.2.0 — A more connected development workspace (8 September 2026)","0.1.0 — First release (31 July 2026)"],"x":" Dates are when each version appeared on the Visual Studio Marketplace. Hindi is built into the same extension; there is nothing extra to install and no translation service. Choose Auto , English or हिन्दी in the Auric Live panel header. The choice is saved in auricLive.interfaceLanguage . Auto follows VS Code's display language, including regional Hindi locales. The control panel, quick settings, request controls, inline Phone QR guidance and common messages are translated. All 54 command titles and the three sidebar view names have Hindi versions that follow VS Code's display language. New preview tabs use the selected language; reopen an existing preview to update it. Switching language keeps the current section and request filters, and does not restart the server. Technical messages without a translation stay in English. Served websites, request data, commands and the browser dashboard are not translated. HAR exports now record the installed extension version. Development workspace. The control panel's Overview, Requests, Runtime, Routing and Settings sections bring server controls, backend setup and diagnostics into one tab. Inline phone QR. Show a locally generated QR code in"},{"t":"Related","d":"Other Auric Artisan extensions and pages that work well alongside Auric Artisan Live.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Live","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-live/others/related.html","h":["Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","Setup","Auric Artisan pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan Formatter ../../auric artisan formatter/README.md — format the HTML, CSS and JavaScript you are previewing, with a diff preview first. Auric Artisan File System ../../auric artisan file system/README.md — create project structures, batch rename files and find related files in the Explorer. Auric Artisan Font Hub ../../auric artisan font hub/README.md — add web fonts to the pages you are serving. Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md — colour, accessibility and code health checks for the same project. Install and set up the Auric Artisan extensions ../../install and setup/README.md Use an extension in Hindi ../../install and setup/docs/display language hindi.md Settings, sync and workspace trust ../../install and setup/docs/settings and sync.md VS Code extensions: https://auricartisan.com/vscode/ Marketplace listing: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan live Contact and support: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ "},{"t":"Auric Artisan File System","d":"What Auric Artisan File System does, who it is for, how to install it and where to find every guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan File System adds a file workspace to the VS Code Explorer. It keeps VS Code's own Explorer, with its New File, New Folder, Rename and drag and drop, and adds the file work the Explorer does not do: creating whole project structures in one line, templates and framework presets, batch renaming with a preview, finding a file's test, style or story, tags, groups and profiles, a graphical Properties view, duplicate review, and a workspace trash you can restore from. Its commands appear in the Auric Files section of the Explorer, in an editor sized workspace panel, in an Auric Files submenu on Explorer and editor context menus, and in the Command Palette under Auric Files . There are 81 commands in seven groups: Create , Inspect & navigate , Edit & batch , Organise , Find & filter , History & recovery and Workspace . Operations are guarded: paths are checked, protected files cannot be renamed, moved or deleted, collisions are planned before anything changes, bulk operations ask first, and every Auric operation is recorded so you can undo it. Everything runs locally; no account is needed. Developers who create the same file patterns again and again: a component with its tes"},{"t":"Auric Artisan File System guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan File System task guides and reference.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" Start with the getting started guide for a tour of every surface. The task guides follow the extension's own groups. The reference lists all 81 commands, the 69 keyboard shortcut declarations and all 48 settings. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, the workspace panel and sidebar, menus, Quick Actions, a first task create files and structures.md create files and structures.md New file and folder, sibling and child files, batch creation with braces and ranges templates and generators.md templates and generators.md Templates, their file format and language, framework presets, custom generators rename move and copy.md rename move and copy.md Rename, batch rename modes, move, copy, duplicate, convert extension, previews and conflicts related files.md related files.md Navigate to tests, styles, stories, components and docs; generate missing companions; custom rules properties compare export.md properties compare export.md The Properties view, compact hovers, compare, merge, path copying and selection export organise tags groups profiles.md organise tags groups profiles.md Tags, groups, virtual folders, favourites, pins, highlights, exclusions, focus mode,"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan File System","d":"Install Auric Artisan File System, learn where its controls live, and complete a first task.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","The screen tour","A first task: create a component with its companions","Keyboard shortcuts at a glance","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Check that VS Code is version 1.95 or newer Help › About . 2. In the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for @id:auric artisan.auric artisan file system and select Install . Or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan file system 3. Open a workspace folder. File operations need a trusted workspace; in Restricted Mode you can browse, search, filter and navigate, but not create, rename, move, duplicate or delete. In the Explorer, below your file tree, expand Auric Files . It is a compact companion to the native Explorer, not a second file tree. It shows the same tools as the full workspace panel in a narrow layout. Its title bar has an Open File Workspace button for the larger panel. Run Auric Files: Open File Workspace , select Open workspace ↗ in the sidebar, or use the button in the Explorer title bar. The panel opens as an editor tab called Auric Files . From top to bottom: Area What it shows Header The Auric Artisan mark and a link to auricartisan.com Active workspace The workspace name, whether it is trusted and whether the index is ready, with Open Explorer → and Open workspace ↗ Summary Indexed files , Folders , Saved tags and Operations Auric op"},{"t":"Create files and structures","d":"Create single files and folders, sibling and child files, and whole nested structures in one line with braces and ranges.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/create-files-and-structures.html","h":["New file or folder","Sibling and child files","Batch creation","What happens to existing files"],"x":" All creation commands are in the Create group of the workspace panel, the Auric Files › Create submenu and the Command Palette. They need a trusted workspace. Command Use it to New File… Create one file or a folder, with a trailing / New Folder… Create one folder, including nested paths New Sibling File Create a file next to the selected file New Child File Create a file inside the selected folder Batch Create Files… Create many files from comma separated paths Batch Create Folders… Create many folders from comma separated paths Batch Structure… Type a mixed structure of files and folders New File from Template… Create from a template. See Templates and generators templates and generators.md New from Framework Preset… Create from a preset or custom generator. See Templates and generators templates and generators.md Create Related Files… Create a file's test, style, story and other companions. See Related files related files.md For creation directly in the root of a single folder workspace, use the native Explorer's New File and New Folder ; the panel's target actions need a file or subfolder as their target. 1. Run Auric Files: New File… Ctrl + N with the Explorer focused or New F"},{"t":"History, undo and the workspace trash","d":"Undo and redo Auric file operations, review the history, delete safely into the workspace trash, restore items and control the safety settings.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/history-and-workspace-trash.html","h":["Undo and redo","Delete into the workspace trash","Browse and restore","Empty the trash","Safety settings"],"x":" These commands are in the History & recovery group of the workspace panel and the Auric Files › Safety and History submenu. Every operation Auric Files performs create, rename, move, copy, duplicate, delete, convert is recorded as one step, however many files it touched. Command What it does Deck shortcut Undo Last File Operation Reverse the most recent Auric operation Ctrl + Alt + Z Redo File Operation Redo the last undone operation Ctrl + Alt + Y macOS Cmd + Alt + Shift + Z Show Operation History List recent operations; choose one to undo back to it Ctrl + Alt + A , then H When it works you see Undid operation . or Redid operation . If an undo cannot be completed, both the undo and redo lists stay as they were rather than pretending. The history keeps the last auricFiles.safety.historyLimit operations default 200, range 10–2000 . It is saved in VS Code's storage for the workspace, so it survives a restart. It records Auric operations only. Edits you make in the editor, VS Code's own Explorer actions rename with F2 , drag and drop and changes made by other tools are not in it, and it does not keep old copies of file contents. Keep using version control and backups. With no histor"},{"t":"Tags, groups and profiles","d":"Organise files without moving them, with tags, groups, virtual folders, favourites, pins, highlights, Explorer exclusions, focus mode and workspace profiles.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/organise-tags-groups-profiles.html","h":["Where the organisation is stored","Tags","Groups","Virtual folders","Favourites, pins, highlights and exclusions","Focus mode","Workspace profiles","Remove organisation"],"x":" Auric Files lets you organise files by meaning rather than by folder. None of these tools moves or changes a file: they store labels about files. The labels follow a file when you rename or move it with Auric Files. The commands are in the Organise group of the workspace panel and the Auric Files › Organize submenu. Tags, groups, virtual folders, flags, saved filters and profiles are kept in VS Code's storage for this workspace, on your machine. They are not written into your project, are not committed with it, and are not copied by Settings Sync. The one exception is Toggle Native Explorer Exclusion , which writes to the workspace's files.exclude setting. A tag is a named, coloured label you can put on any number of files. 1. Run Auric Files: Manage Tags… . 2. Choose New tag… . 3. Type the Tag name . 4. Choose a colour : gold, amber, orange, red, pink, purple, blue, teal, green or gray. In Manage Tags… you can also choose an existing tag to Rename or Delete it. 1. Select files in the Explorer. 2. Run Tag Files… Ctrl + Alt + A , then G with the deck , or choose Edit tags… in Properties. 3. Tick the tags to apply and untick any to remove. With no tags yet, the list says No tags yet"},{"t":"Properties, compare and export","d":"Inspect a file's properties, compare and merge files, copy paths, and export a JSON manifest of a selection.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/properties-compare-export.html","h":["Properties","Compact hovers in the Explorer","Compare two files","Merge files","Copy paths and reveal","Export a selection"],"x":" These commands are in the Inspect & navigate group of the workspace panel and the Auric Files › Navigate and Paths submenu. Properties shows the facts about a file or folder in one place: what the file system reports, plus what Auric Files knows about it. It reads metadata only, never the file's contents. Right click a file or folder in the Explorer and choose File Properties the first entry in the menu . Press Alt + Enter with the Explorer focused. Run Auric Files: File Properties . If VS Code does not pass a selected file some keyboard routes do not , a resource picker opens. In the workspace panel or the Auric Files sidebar, choose 02 Properties . Properties opens inside the existing workspace panel or sidebar rather than a new tab. General Row Meaning Name The file or folder name Full path The complete path or URI for remote and virtual files Type The extension in capitals for example TSX , Folder or Symbolic link Size The reported size; folders show Folder this is not a recursive disk usage total Created Creation time, where the file system records one; otherwise Unavailable Modified Last modification time Organisation Row Meaning Tags Tags assigned to the item, or None Group"},{"t":"Related files","d":"Jump between a file and its test, style, story, component and documentation, create missing companions, and teach Auric Files your own conventions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/related-files.html","h":["Go to a companion","See the whole group","Create missing companions","Relationship kinds","Settings","Add your own rules","Index"],"x":" Most source files come with companions : a component has a test, a stylesheet and a story; a module has documentation and type declarations. Auric Files knows the usual conventions for each framework preset, so it can open a file's companion in one step, show which ones are missing and create them. With a file open in the editor: Command Opens Deck shortcut Auric Files: Go to Related File… A list of every companion that exists Ctrl + Alt + R Auric Files: Open Matching Test The file's test Ctrl + Alt + A , then Q Auric Files: Open Matching Style The file's stylesheet Ctrl + Alt + A , then S Auric Files: Open Matching Story The file's story Ctrl + Alt + A , then W Auric Files: Open Matching Component The component a test, style or story belongs to Ctrl + Alt + A , then I Auric Files: Open Matching Documentation The file's documentation Ctrl + Alt + A , then Shift + D The shortcuts need auricFiles.keyboard.enableDefaultShortcuts . The same commands are in Auric Files › Navigate and Paths on a file's context menu, and in the Inspect & navigate group of the panel. Navigation works in both directions: from Button.tsx to Button.test.tsx , and from the test back to the component. Show Rel"},{"t":"Rename, move and copy","d":"Rename, move, copy and duplicate files one at a time or in batches, convert extensions, and review every change before it happens.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/rename-move-and-copy.html","h":["Before anything changes","Rename one file","Batch rename","Move or copy","Duplicate","Convert extensions","Undo"],"x":" These commands are in the Edit & batch group of the workspace panel and the Auric Files › Edit and Batch submenu. They need a trusted workspace. VS Code's own Rename F2 and drag and drop in the Explorer keep working as usual; the Auric versions add collision planning, protection, confirmations and undo. Command Use it to Rename… Rename the selected item Rename Current File Rename the file open in the editor Move… / Move Current File Move items, or the current file, to another folder Copy To… Copy items to another folder Duplicate / Duplicate Current File Make a copy beside the original Batch Rename… Rename many files by a rule, with a preview Batch Move… Move many items to one folder Convert Extension… Change the extension of many files Rename… , Move… , Copy To… and Duplicate act on the selection and run from the panel, the context menus or the shortcut deck; they are not listed in the Command Palette. The \"Current File\" versions act on the editor's file. Every operation is planned first: Protected paths. Anything matching auricFiles.safety.protectedPaths cannot be renamed, moved or deleted. By default that covers .git , node modules , .env files, .pem and .key files, and the npm"},{"t":"Search, filters and duplicates","d":"Search the workspace index, build and save filters, sort and group files, and review duplicate and empty files.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/search-filter-and-duplicates.html","h":["The workspace index","Search","Filters","Sorting","Grouping","Collapse and expand","Duplicate files","Empty files and folders"],"x":" These commands are in the Find & filter group of the workspace panel. They work on the workspace index : a list of the workspace's files and folders that Auric Files builds the first time you need it and keeps up to date. Searching and filtering work in untrusted workspaces too. It is built on demand, the first time a command needs it. The panel shows Index builds when needed until then, and Workspace index ready after. Folders in auricFiles.explorer.excludePatterns by default node modules , .git , dist , out , .next , pycache , target and vendor and anything your .gitignore excludes auricFiles.explorer.respectGitignore are never indexed, searched, compared or batch processed. One scan holds at most auricFiles.explorer.maxNodes entries default 20,000 . A larger workspace is marked as truncated, and counts say so. After the first scan, changes are followed automatically auricFiles.performance.watchWorkspace . Run Auric Files: Refresh to rebuild it by hand. 1. Run Auric Files: Search Files… , or Quick Open in Auric Files… Ctrl + Alt + O with the deck , which focuses the Explorer first. 2. Type part of a name or path. The title shows the default search mode. 3. Choose a file to open "},{"t":"Templates and generators","d":"Create files from templates, use the ten framework presets, and write your own templates and generators with variables, filters and conditions.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/templates-and-generators.html","h":["Create from a template","Create from a framework preset","Write your own templates","Generator profiles"],"x":" A template is a file pattern: a file name and a body with placeholders that are filled in when you create a file. A framework preset is a ready made set of templates and file relationships for one ecosystem. A generator is a template that can also create companion files in the same step. 1. Run Auric Files: New File from Template… Create group, or Ctrl + Alt + A , then T with the shortcut deck . 2. Choose a template. The list includes the active preset's built in templates, your generators and any templates in your template folders. 3. Choose the destination folder. 4. Answer the template's questions, such as the name. 5. The file and any companions the template defines is created, and the first file opens with the cursor where the template placed it. 1. Run Auric Files: New from Framework Preset… Ctrl + Alt + A , then P with the deck . 2. Choose a framework preset or custom generator. 3. Choose what to create from that preset's templates. 4. Choose the destination folder and answer its questions. Preset What it covers React Components, hooks, contexts, tests, styles and stories Vue Single file components, composables, Pinia stores and specs Angular Standalone components with thei"},{"t":"Reference: commands, keys and settings","d":"Every Auric Artisan File System command grouped as the product groups them, every keyboard shortcut, menu and setting, with types, defaults and ranges.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Where commands appear","Views and panels","Explorer badges","Settings","Files and settings Auric Files writes"],"x":" This page covers Auric Artisan File System 0.1.0: 81 commands, 69 keyboard shortcut declarations, one Explorer view and 48 settings. Commands appear in the Command Palette with the Auric Files: prefix. Commands are grouped as the workspace panel groups them. The Keys column gives Windows and Linux keys. Explorer keys work whenever the Explorer has focus. deck keys need auricFiles.keyboard.enableDefaultShortcuts . On macOS, Cmd replaces Ctrl in every shortcut, except Redo File Operation , which is Cmd + Alt + Shift + Z . \"Then\" means press the first combination, release, then press the second. Commands marked \"not in the Command Palette\" act on a selection and run from the panel, context menus or shortcuts. Files, folders and complete structures. Command ID Keys What it does Auric Files: New File… auricFiles.newFile Ctrl + N Explorer ; Ctrl + Alt + A , then Ctrl + N deck Create a file: choose the folder, type a name a trailing / makes a folder , optionally pick a template Auric Files: New Folder… auricFiles.newFolder Ctrl + Shift + N Explorer ; Ctrl + Alt + A , then Ctrl + Shift + N deck Create a folder, including nested paths Auric Files: New File from Template… auricFiles.newFrom"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common Auric Artisan File System problems.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Actions do nothing or are refused","Shortcuts","Creation","Related files, search and Properties","Duplicates, trash and history","Icon tools"],"x":" For anything not listed, set auricFiles.logLevel to debug , repeat the action, run Auric Files: Show Log , and see Get support ../../install and setup/docs/get support.md . Why: the workspace is not trusted. In Restricted Mode, browsing, search, filtering and related file navigation work, but nothing that changes files. Fix: run Workspaces: Manage Workspace Trust and trust the folder. Why: the action needs a file or folder as its target, and none is selected, or the selected item is outside the workspace. Fix: select an item in the Explorer or open a file, or use Choose… in the panel. Why: the panel's target actions need a file or subfolder; the workspace root itself is not a valid target for them. Fix: use VS Code's own New File or New Folder for the root, or choose a subfolder. Why: you are inspecting a file that is not in any open workspace folder. Fix: Properties still work. Open the file's folder as a workspace to use file actions on it. Why: it touches a path in auricFiles.safety.protectedPaths for example .env , lockfiles or node modules . Fix: do it with VS Code's own Explorer if you really mean it, or remove the pattern from the setting. Why: some keyboard routes do not t"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan File System.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/docs/faq.html","h":["Does it replace the VS Code Explorer?","Does it change my files when I tag or group them?","Is anything uploaded?","Can I undo a batch rename?","Where do deleted files go?","Should I commit .auric/?","Do tags follow a file when I rename it?","Does Export Selected Items zip my files?","Why is folder size shown as \"Folder\"?","Does it work over Remote SSH, in WSL or in virtual workspaces?","Why do most shortcuts not work?","Is the interface available in Hindi?","Do I need the Auric icon themes?"],"x":" No. VS Code's Explorer stays as it is. Auric Files adds a companion section, a workspace panel, menus and commands around it. No. Tags, groups, virtual folders, favourites, pins, highlights, filters and profiles are stored in VS Code's storage for the workspace. Only file operations create, rename, move, copy, duplicate, convert, delete change files, and Toggle Native Explorer Exclusion changes the files.exclude setting. No. Everything runs locally and no account is needed. Links to the Auric Artisan website and support open in your browser only when you choose them. Yes. Undo Last File Operation reverses the whole batch in one step. To .auric/trash in your workspace, unless you use Delete Permanently or turn off the workspace trash. Restore them with Restore from Trash… within the retention period 14 days by default . The trash lives in .auric/trash , and templates you share can live in .auric/templates . You may want to commit shared templates and keep the trash out of version control by adding .auric/trash/ to .gitignore . Yes, when you rename or move it with Auric Files. Changes made outside Auric Files may leave organisation data pointing at the old path. No. It writes a JSON"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan File System.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the Auric Artisan File System guides: terms, shortcuts, limits, privacy, related products and the version history. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the File System documentation shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every keyboard shortcut, including the optional deck limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What Properties can and cannot report, index and batch limits privacy.md privacy.md What stays local and what uses the network related.md related.md Related extensions and pages release notes.md release notes.md What changed in each version "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut Auric Artisan File System declares, the six that are always on and the optional deck.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Always on (Explorer focused)","Deck: direct shortcuts","Deck: chords","In the workspace panel","Native VS Code keys that still apply"],"x":" Auric Files declares 69 shortcuts. Six are always on while the Explorer has focus. The other 63 form the optional deck , which is off by default so the extension does not claim Ctrl + Alt combinations across VS Code. Turn the deck on with: json { \"auricFiles.keyboard.enableDefaultShortcuts\": true } Deck shortcuts work when a folder is open; a few such as Rename Current File need an editor to be open. Every command is also available from menus and the Command Palette, and you can assign or change any shortcut in Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts by searching for auricFiles . Some commands have both a direct shortcut and a chord. A chord is two key presses in a row: the first combination, then a second key. Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + N Cmd + N New File… Ctrl + Shift + N Cmd + Shift + N New Folder… Alt + Enter Alt + Enter File Properties Ctrl + Shift + M Cmd + Shift + M Toggle File Metadata Alt + S Alt + S Sort Ctrl + Alt + B Cmd + Alt + B Batch Structure… Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + Shift + D Cmd + Alt + Shift + D Compare Selected Files Ctrl + Alt + E Cmd + Alt + E Focus VS Code Explorer Ctrl + Alt + O Cmd + Alt + O Quick Open in Auric Files… Ctrl + A"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Auric Artisan File System documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Barrel — an index file that re exports other modules, such as index.ts . Batch operation — one action applied to many files at once, such as a batch rename. Brace expansion — writing {a,b} or {1..3} in a path to produce several paths. Companion file — a file that belongs with another: its test, stylesheet, story, documentation or types. Conflict — a planned change whose target already exists. Deck — the optional set of about 60 keyboard shortcuts turned on by auricFiles.keyboard.enableDefaultShortcuts . Filter — a set of conditions text, kind, tag, extension, path, size, date, flags, Git state that narrows the indexed file list. Focus mode — limiting Auric's indexed file lists to chosen paths. Framework preset — a ready made set of templates and relationships for one ecosystem, such as React or Go. Front matter — the settings block between two lines at the top of a template file. Generator — a template defined in settings that can create companion files in the same step. Group — a named set of files and folders from anywhere in the workspace. The panel calls creating one \"Create Workspace from Selection\". Guarded operation — a file operation that is planned, checked against protec"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Artisan File System reports and how precisely, its built-in limits, and what it deliberately does not do.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What Properties can report","Built-in limits","Deliberate boundaries","Keeping your work safe"],"x":" Properties shows what the file system reports through VS Code, and labels anything it cannot know. Detail Accuracy Name, path, type Exact Size As reported. Folders show Folder ; a recursive disk usage total is not calculated Created Only where the file system records a creation time; otherwise Unavailable Modified As reported Owner / creator Not available through VS Code; never guessed Permissions Only the read only flag. Its absence does not prove you can write the file. Full access control lists are not available Git status From the last index, and labelled so; refresh the index to update it Related files Found through the index; before it is built, shown as not indexed Version Counts Auric operations only Limit Default Setting Entries per index scan 20,000 500–200,000 auricFiles.explorer.maxNodes Matches per search 2,000 50–50,000 auricFiles.search.maxResults Paths from one brace expression 1,000 — Paths in one batch creation 2,000 — Operations kept for undo 200 10–2,000 auricFiles.safety.historyLimit Workspace trash size 256 MiB auricFiles.safety.trashMaxBytes Workspace trash retention 14 days 1–365 auricFiles.safety.trashRetentionDays Folders read at once while indexing 8 1–6"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan File System keeps on your machine and what, if anything, uses the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/privacy.html","h":["Everything runs locally","Where data is kept","Logging","Network"],"x":" File operations, the index, search, filters, duplicate review and Properties all run on your machine or next to the workspace, in a remote setup . No Auric Artisan account is needed. Properties reads file system metadata only, never file contents. Duplicate review reads contents only to compare files by hash when the content strategy is used, and only for files that share a size. Data Where Tags, groups, virtual folders, flags, saved filters, profiles, operation history VS Code's storage for this workspace, on your machine. Not written into the project and not copied by Settings Sync Workspace trash .auric/trash/ inside the workspace folder Native Explorer exclusions The workspace's files.exclude setting Explorer sort order The workspace's explorer.sortOrder setting Selection manifests Wherever you save them The Auric Artisan File System output channel logs paths relative to the workspace and never writes file contents. auricFiles.logLevel controls how much is written default warn . The extension's own features do not use the network. The workspace panel loads its scripts and styles from the extension itself. Opening the auricartisan.com link, support links or Marketplace images u"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"What changed in each published version of Auric Artisan File System.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 (11 September 2026)"],"x":" The first Marketplace release. An editor sized Auric Files workspace and a matching compact Auric Files section in the Explorer. File tools in seven searchable groups Create , Inspect & navigate , Edit & batch , Organise , Find & filter , History & recovery , Workspace , with keyboard operable sections that close their siblings, and Collapse all . Workspace summaries, the selected resource and a resource picker. VS Code's own Explorer and the Quick Actions… list are kept. Compact Explorer hovers replace long metadata tooltips. A Properties view with General , Organisation and Access & history cards, path copying, tag editing and group actions. Index dependent information and cached Git state are labelled; unavailable owner and permission details are never made up. One Auric Files submenu on Explorer and editor context menus, with File Properties kept directly in the Explorer menu. Multi selection in the Explorer is kept when opening the workspace. A selection outside the workspace can no longer fall back to a different file for file actions. Icon tools for the optional Facet and Playful icon themes. Native Explorer creation, rename, sorting, multi selection and file badges. Struct"},{"t":"Related","d":"Other Auric Artisan extensions and pages that work alongside Auric Artisan File System.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan File System","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-file-system/others/related.html","h":["Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","Setup","Auric Artisan pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan File Icons ../../auric artisan file icons/README.md — the Facet and Playful icon themes that the Icon tools section works with. Auric Artisan Formatter ../../auric artisan formatter/README.md — format the files you create, with a diff preview first. Auric Artisan Live ../../auric artisan live/README.md — serve and preview the project you are organising. Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md — colour, accessibility and code health checks. Install and set up the Auric Artisan extensions ../../install and setup/README.md Settings, sync and workspace trust ../../install and setup/docs/settings and sync.md VS Code extensions: https://auricartisan.com/vscode/ Marketplace listing: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan file system Contact and support: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Font Hub","d":"What Auric Artisan Font Hub does, who it is for, how to install it and where to find every guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Font Hub is a typography workspace inside VS Code. It holds the Auric Artisan font library: 2,023 font families, 547 of them variable, with metadata bundled in the extension so you can browse offline. Search and filter the library, open a family's specimen, glyphs, OpenType features and licence, compare families side by side, and get recommendations for a design intent, an industry or a colour palette. When you have chosen, Font Hub adds the font to your code from the Auric font CDN, fonts.auricartisan.com . Add to code adds a stylesheet link and a reusable class such as .auric font inter to an HTML, CSS or JavaScript file without touching your existing styles. Preview shows the change first in VS Code's own diff view, with Apply and Cancel . For other file types it copies an embed for you to place, and it offers every common format: HTML link, CSS @import , font family , @font face , Tailwind configuration, SCSS variables and design tokens. For self hosting, it exports a ZIP kit with the font files, CSS, a demo page and the required licence notices, where the licence allows it. Browsing works offline. Previews and downloads fetch from the Auric font CDN and are cach"},{"t":"Auric Artisan Font Hub guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Font Hub task guides and reference.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" Start with the getting started guide for a tour of the sidebar and the studio. The reference lists all 16 commands, the two keyboard shortcuts and all 13 settings. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, the sidebar and studio, the screen tour, a first font added to a page find and compare fonts.md find and compare fonts.md Search, filters, scopes, sorting, collections, Find your font, favourites, selection, comparison font details.md font details.md The twelve detail tabs: specimen, waterfall, suitability, pairings, features, glyphs, licence and more add fonts to code.md add fonts to code.md Add to code, Preview with Apply and Cancel, embed formats, multi family insertion, Quick Pick cdn and browser delivery.md cdn and browser delivery.md The CDN health check, CORS, content types and Content Security Policy self hosting kit.md self hosting kit.md Download a ZIP kit with fonts, CSS, demo and licences offline cache and network.md offline cache and network.md Offline catalogue, previews cache, refresh schedule, switching the network off moving from font library.md moving from font library.md Replacing the earlier Font Library extension reference.md referen"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan Font Hub","d":"Install Auric Artisan Font Hub, learn the sidebar and studio layout, and add a first font to a page.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","Two ways to open it","The screen tour","A first task: add a font to an HTML page","Keyboard","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Check that VS Code is version 1.85 or newer Help › About . 2. In the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for @id:auric artisan.auric artisan font hub and select Install . Or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan font hub 3. If the older Font Library extension is installed, disable or uninstall it first. See Moving from Font Library moving from font library.md . Font Hub works in untrusted and virtual workspaces. It only writes files when you choose an explicit save or insert. Sidebar. Select Auric Font Hub in the Activity Bar. The Font Hub view is a compact version of the studio. Studio. Run Auric Artisan Font Hub: Open Font Hub Ctrl + Alt + F , select Open studio ↗ in the sidebar, or select the Fonts item in the status bar. The studio opens as an editor tab with more room. Both share the same layout, controls, favourites and selection. The sidebar's title bar has Open Font Hub , Focus Font Search and Refresh Font Catalog from Auric CDN . Opening Font Hub creates no files in your project. From top to bottom: Area What it contains Header The Auric Artisan mark; auricartisan.com ↗ ; Open studio ↗ in the sidebar ; ↻ refresh the catalogue; ↗ open the we"},{"t":"Add a font to your code","d":"Add fonts from the Auric font CDN to HTML, CSS and JavaScript files with a reviewable diff, insert explicit embed formats, and add several families at once.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/add-fonts-to-code.html","h":["Automatic insertion","Preview before applying","Explicit formats","Copy an embed","Several families at once","From the editor's context menu","Using the font in your CSS"],"x":" Font Hub adds fonts from the Auric font CDN. Every embed points to a stylesheet at: text https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/<family id .css For example, Inter is https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/inter.css . Font Hub never substitutes another font service. Add to code on a font card and Auric Artisan Font Hub: Add Font to Code use Automatic mode by default. Automatic mode adds two things: the CDN stylesheet, and a reusable class named .auric font <family id that applies the font. It never replaces selected text, never changes your existing rules and never applies the font to the whole page. You decide where to use the class. What it adds depends on the active file: Active file What Automatic mode does HTML with a <head Adds <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"…\" and a small <style rule for the class just before </head CSS, SCSS, Less, PostCSS Adds @import url '…' ; before your normal rules after any @charset , @use or @forward and appends the class rule JavaScript, TypeScript Appends a small guarded block that adds the stylesheet and class to the page when it runs in a browser, and does nothing on the server JSX, TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro, data files and other languages Copies an HTML emb"},{"t":"Check CDN and browser delivery","d":"Run Font Hub's CDN health check and fix fonts that preview in VS Code but do not load on your website.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/cdn-and-browser-delivery.html","h":["Run the check","When fonts do not load on your site"],"x":" A font that previews in Font Hub can still fail on your website. Previews are fetched by VS Code itself, while your page's fonts are fetched by the browser, which applies extra security rules. The main one is CORS cross origin resource sharing : a browser only uses a font from another address if that server says the page is allowed to. 1. Run Auric Artisan Font Hub: Check Font CDN and Browser CORS , or select Check CDN health or CDN diagnostics , or Run a live check in Font Hub. 2. Font Hub sends small HEAD requests to the CDN for three things: Catalog — the catalogue file; Stylesheet — a family's stylesheet; Font file — that family's preview font. 3. Each request is made as if from the test address http://localhost:5500 . 4. The report shows, for each item, whether it is available, whether its content type is right, and, for the font file, whether CORS allows the test address. The overall result is Browser delivery ready only if every item is available with the right content type and the font file allows cross origin use. Otherwise it says Needs attention , with CORS missing for test origin when that is the problem. Check again reruns it. The check is a sample: one catalogue file"},{"t":"Find and compare fonts","d":"Search and filter the Auric font library, get recommendations for a design intent, and keep favourites, recents and a selection to compare.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/find-and-compare-fonts.html","h":["Search","Category and sort","Advanced filters","Preview text, size and density","Scopes","Find your font","Collections and recommendations","Favourites, recents and selection","The selection tray","Compare families","Quick Picks","System fonts","Scores are guidance"],"x":" Type in Search placeholder Family, designer, script, feature… . It matches family names, designers, scripts, OpenType features and licence information. Press / or Ctrl + K anywhere in Font Hub to jump to it, and Escape to clear it. Results appear as cards and load in batches of auricFontLib.pageSize 48 by default ; Show more loads the next batch. If nothing matches, No matching families offers Reset filters . Category — All categories or one of the library's categories: sans serif, serif, display, handwriting and monospace. Sort — order the results: Sort Order Alphabetical By family name Accessibility score Highest accessibility score first Readability score Highest readability score first UI score Highest UI and product score first Developer score Highest developer and code score first Editorial score Highest editorial score first Most weights Families with the most weights first Most glyphs Families with the most characters first Newest Most recently added first Variable first Variable families first Select More filters to show chips you can combine: Filter Chips Properties Variable , Italic , Monospace , 4+ weights Weights 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800, 900 OpenType Th"},{"t":"Font details","d":"Inspect a font family in Font Hub's twelve detail tabs, from the live specimen and waterfall to glyphs, features, styles and licence.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/font-details.html","h":["Specimen","Waterfall","Suitability","Pairings","Features","Develop","Glyphs","Charset","Styles","About","License","Use & Embed","Open on the web"],"x":" Select a family's name on its card to open the details panel. The header shows the family name and a short summary, with Favorite , Select and a close button × , or Escape . Twelve tabs sit below it. Previews are drawn with the real font, fetched from the Auric font CDN through VS Code and cached. If a preview cannot be loaded, the card and panel say Preview unavailable with the reason, and the rest of the details still work from the bundled catalogue. An editable sample: click it and type your own text. Size slider, 18 to 120 pixels 48 by default . Variable axes — for variable families, a slider for each axis such as weight or width , from its minimum to its maximum, starting at the default. OpenType controls — tick up to twelve of the family's features such as ligatures or small capitals to see them applied live. Copy family — copy the CSS font family value. Insert embed — add the font to the active file see Add a font to your code add fonts to code.md . The same text at eleven sizes, from 11 to 88 pixels, so you can see where the design stops working small or large. Variable families with a weight axis also get a Weight ramp . A Paragraph proof shows a paragraph at 13, 16 and 1"},{"t":"Moving from Font Library","d":"Replace the earlier Auric Artisan Font Library extension with Font Hub without duplicate commands, and know what carries over.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/moving-from-font-library.html","h":["Switch over","What carries over"],"x":" Font Hub 0.1.0 is the renamed and redesigned successor of an earlier extension called Font Library . Font Hub has a new extension ID, auric artisan.auric artisan font hub , so VS Code treats them as two different extensions. 1. Open the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X and find Font Library . 2. Select Disable or Uninstall . 3. Install Font Hub: search for @id:auric artisan.auric artisan font hub and select Install . 4. Reload the window if VS Code asks. If both are enabled at the same time, you see duplicate commands and views. Item Carries over? Settings auricFontLib. Yes. Font Hub uses the same setting names Command IDs auricFontLib. Yes, so your custom keyboard shortcuts keep working Favourites, recents and selection No. They were stored with the old extension Cached previews and font files No. Font Hub builds its own cache After switching, the Activity Bar shows Auric Font Hub and the Command Palette lists commands under Auric Artisan Font Hub . "},{"t":"Offline use, cache and network","d":"What Font Hub can do offline, how it refreshes and caches catalogue data and fonts, and how to switch its network use off.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/offline-cache-and-network.html","h":["What works offline","What uses the network","Switch the network off","Catalogue refresh","Cache","System fonts"],"x":" The extension includes a snapshot of the catalogue: every family's details and the licence notices. Without a network connection you can: search, filter, sort and browse every family; open details, including styles, charset, about and licence information; use favourites, recents, selection and the recommender; copy and insert embeds the page that uses them still needs the CDN when it loads . Font previews and self hosting downloads need the font files. Previews you have already seen stay available from the cache where possible; others need the network. Only one address is ever contacted: https://fonts.auricartisan.com . Font Hub validates every address before requesting it, and the Font Hub panels themselves cannot make network requests; all fetching goes through VS Code. Activity When Catalogue refresh On the schedule in auricFontLib.catalogRefresh , or when you run Refresh Font Catalog from Auric CDN Font previews When a card or detail panel needs a font that is not cached Licence text When you select Load full license text or build a kit Self hosting downloads When you download a kit CDN check When you run Check Font CDN and Browser CORS Search queries, your source code, favour"},{"t":"Export a self-hosting kit","d":"Download fonts from Font Hub as a ZIP kit with CSS, a demo page and licence notices, for hosting on your own server.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/self-hosting-kit.html","h":["Download a kit","What the kit contains","Licence checks","Limits"],"x":" Self hosting means serving font files from your own website instead of the CDN. Font Hub can package families into a ZIP kit ready to copy into a project. Use any of these: Download kit in a family's Styles or Use & Embed tab; Download in the Selected tray, for every selected family; Download self hosting kit in Quick Pick Font ; Auric Artisan Font Hub: Download Self hosting Font Kit , which lets you tick families in a list Choose font families . Then: 1. Font Hub checks each family's licence see below . 2. Choose where to save the ZIP. The default name is <family font kit.zip for one family or auric font selection kit.zip for several. 3. A progress notification, Preparing Auric font kit , shows each family as its files are fetched. 4. Saved self hosting kit for N families. Saving is always an explicit action; nothing is written into your project unless you save it there. Path Contents fonts/<family / The font files for every style css/<family id .css @font face rules pointing at those files, with font display: swap and variable weight ranges kept licenses/<family .txt The family's licence text, when there is one README <family .md Notes for each family index.html A demo page show"},{"t":"Reference: commands, keys and settings","d":"Every Auric Artisan Font Hub command, keyboard shortcut, menu entry, panel control and setting, with types, defaults and ranges.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Where commands appear","Panel controls","Keys inside Font Hub","Settings","Files Font Hub writes"],"x":" This page covers Auric Artisan Font Hub 0.1.0: 16 commands, 2 keyboard shortcuts, one Activity Bar view and 13 settings. Command and setting IDs use the auricFontLib prefix, kept from the extension's earlier name. Fifteen commands appear under Auric Artisan Font Hub: in the Command Palette; Show Logs appears under Auric Font Hub: . Command ID Keys What it does Open Font Hub auricFontLib.openStudio Ctrl + Alt + F Open the full studio in an editor tab Quick Pick Font auricFontLib.quickPick Ctrl + Alt + T Choose a family, then an action Add Font to Code auricFontLib.insertEmbed — Choose a family and add it to the active file in the default format Copy Font Embed As… auricFontLib.copyEmbed — Choose a family and a format, and copy the snippet Pick from Favorite Fonts auricFontLib.showFavorites — Quick Pick limited to favourites Pick from Recent Fonts auricFontLib.showRecents — Quick Pick limited to recent fonts Compare Selected Fonts auricFontLib.compareSelected — Compare up to four selected families Download Self hosting Font Kit auricFontLib.downloadKit — Export a ZIP kit for chosen families Refresh Font Catalog from Auric CDN auricFontLib.refreshCatalog — Refresh catalogue data now "},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common Auric Artisan Font Hub problems.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Fonts are not visible on your website","An embed is present but the text has not changed","Nothing changed after inserting","\"No HTML head found.\"","\"The document changed. Preview the font insertion again before applying.\"","\"Smart insertion supports documents up to 2 MiB.\"","\"This is a local system font.\"","Previews are missing or say \"Preview unavailable\"","The catalogue refresh was rejected","\"Self-hosting kit blocked.\"","\"Choose at most N families for one kit.\" or the 250 MB limit","\"Select at least two font families to compare.\"","Duplicate commands or views","\"Enable network access in Font Hub settings to run CDN checks.\"","A preview became stale"],"x":" For anything not listed, run Auric Font Hub: Show Logs and see Get support ../../install and setup/docs/get support.md . Include your extension version, the file language and the error message with anything private removed. Why: the stylesheet is not loaded, the font file is blocked often by CORS or a Content Security Policy , or the class is not applied. Fix: run Check Font CDN and Browser CORS , then check the browser's Network tab for both the stylesheet and the font file. A successful stylesheet response alone is not enough. See Check CDN and browser delivery cdn and browser delivery.md . Why: the setup only defines the .auric font <id class. Fix: add the class to your markup, or use the family's font family value in your own selector. Why: the setup was already in the file … is already configured in this document. , or the file type needs manual placement and the embed was copied to the clipboard instead. Fix: read the notification, then paste the embed where it belongs if it was copied. Why: the HTML file has no <head element, for example a partial or a component template. Fix: paste the copied embed into your page's head or your framework's layout. Why: the file was edited "},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Font Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/docs/faq.html","h":["How many fonts are there?","Does it work offline?","Does it use Google Fonts?","Will it change my existing CSS?","Why did it copy an embed instead of inserting?","Does it create files in my project?","Can I use the fonts commercially?","Are the scores reliable?","Is anything I do uploaded?","Why do settings start with auricFontLib?","Is the interface available in Hindi?"],"x":" 2,023 library families, 547 of them variable. With auricFontLib.includeSystemFonts on, metadata for common system fonts is added. Browsing, searching, details and licences work offline from the bundled snapshot. Font previews and downloads need the network unless they are already cached. No. Embeds point to https://fonts.auricartisan.com . Font Hub does not substitute another font service. No. Automatic insertion only adds a stylesheet and a new class. It does not replace selected text, edit your rules or apply the font to the whole page. You can preview every change first, and one undo removes it. For JSX, TSX, Vue, Svelte, Astro, data files and other languages, the right place for a font depends on your framework, so Font Hub copies the embed for you to place. It also copies when no editor is open. Opening Font Hub creates nothing. Files are only written when you insert into the active document, save a snippet, or save a kit. It depends on each font's licence. Check the License tab. The extension's own licence does not grant rights to any font. They are catalogue estimates from measured traits, useful for shortlisting. Always test with your real text, languages, sizes and colour"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Font Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the Font Hub guides: terms, shortcuts, what the scores and checks mean, privacy, related products and the version history. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Typography and delivery terms used in the Font Hub documentation shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every keyboard shortcut limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What scores, checks and insertion can and cannot guarantee; size limits privacy.md privacy.md What stays local and what uses the network related.md related.md Related extensions, tools and pages release notes.md release notes.md What changed in each version "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"The keyboard shortcuts Auric Artisan Font Hub provides in VS Code and inside its panels.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/shortcuts.html","h":["VS Code","Inside the sidebar and studio"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command Ctrl + Alt + F Cmd + Alt + F Auric Artisan Font Hub: Open Font Hub Ctrl + Alt + T Cmd + Alt + T Auric Artisan Font Hub: Quick Pick Font Other commands have no default shortcut. Assign one in Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts by searching for auricFontLib . Keys What they do / when not typing in a field Focus and select the search box Ctrl + K Cmd + K on macOS Focus and select the search box Escape Close the comparison, details panel or tray; otherwise clear the search Arrow keys on a font card Move to the next or previous card, or the card above or below Tab , Shift + Tab Move through controls; focus stays inside an open details panel, tray or comparison Arrow keys, type ahead, Enter in drop downs Choose a category, sort order, intent or industry "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the typography and delivery terms used in the Font Hub documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" @font face — a CSS rule that tells the browser where to download a font file and which weight and style it provides. Automatic insertion — Font Hub's default way of adding a font: a CDN stylesheet plus a reusable class, placed according to the file type. CDN content delivery network — a server that delivers files such as fonts to websites. Font Hub uses fonts.auricartisan.com . Charset / character coverage — which characters, grouped into Unicode ranges, a font can display. CORS cross origin resource sharing — the rule that lets a browser use a font from a different address only if that server allows it. Content Security Policy — a website setting that limits where styles, fonts and scripts may load from. Design intent — what the type has to do, such as UI and product text or editorial reading, used to rank recommendations. Design tokens — named values, such as a font family and its fallbacks, shared across a design system. Fallback stack — the list of fonts the browser tries if the chosen one is not available. Family — a set of related fonts sharing one design, in several weights and styles. Glyph — the drawn shape of a character in a font. OpenType feature — an optional font beh"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Font Hub's scores, recommendations, checks and insertion can and cannot guarantee, and its size limits.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Scores and recommendations","Previews","Automatic insertion","CDN check","Self-hosting kits","Catalogue"],"x":" Suitability and accessibility scores are catalogue estimates built from measured traits of the fonts, such as x height and how distinct similar characters are. They are guidance for shortlisting, not guarantees. Categories are assigned automatically and can occasionally be wrong for unusual designs. Recommendations blend the chosen intent, industry, palette and your local use. They are a starting point. Always check your real text, languages, sizes and colour contrast in the finished product. Previews use the real font files, fetched through VS Code and cached. A family may show Preview unavailable when offline or when a file cannot be fetched. Variable axis sliders and OpenType toggles only show what the preview font file supports. System font previews depend on the font being installed on your computer. Supports HTML files with a <head , CSS, SCSS, Less, PostCSS, JavaScript and TypeScript. Other languages get a copied embed. Works on files up to 2 MiB. It is deliberately conservative, not a complete HTML, CSS or JavaScript parser. It skips <head tags inside comments, scripts and styles, and it will not add a setup twice. Explicit formats insert at the cursor; they do not merge i"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Font Hub keeps on your machine and what it sends over the network.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/privacy.html","h":["What stays on your machine","What uses the network","Your website","Links"],"x":" Search queries, your source code, favourites, recents, selection and usage history. Recommendations that use \"local use\" are calculated on your computer. The cache of previews, font files and refreshed metadata, in VS Code's extension storage. No account, no analytics integration and no telemetry. Font Hub contacts one address, https://fonts.auricartisan.com , and only for: refreshing the catalogue on the auricFontLib.catalogRefresh schedule, or when you ask ; fetching fonts for previews that are not cached; loading full licence texts; downloading self hosting kits; the CDN check you run. Requests go through VS Code, not through the Font Hub panels, and every address is validated first. The CDN receives the ordinary information any web request carries, such as your IP address. Switch all of this off with auricFontLib.network.enabled set to false . Embeds that Font Hub adds make your visitors' browsers load fonts from fonts.auricartisan.com . If you would rather your site made no requests to it, use a self hosting kit instead. Explore Fonts on AuricArtisan.com and the auricartisan.com ↗ links open your browser. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"What changed in each published version of Auric Artisan Font Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 (24 September 2026)"],"x":" The first release under the name Auric Artisan Font Hub , with the new extension ID auric artisan.auric artisan font hub . Renamed from Font Library to Auric Artisan Font Hub , with matching typography icons in the Marketplace and the Activity Bar. A redesigned studio and compact sidebar with editorial typography, gold accents, sticky navigation and responsive cards. Add to code and Preview buttons directly on font cards. Editor context menu actions grouped under Auric Fonts . Custom drop downs, the shared colour picker, keyboard navigation, collapsible filters and native scrolling kept. Automatic, non duplicating CDN setup for HTML, CSS family files and JavaScript and TypeScript. Reusable font classes that do not change existing styles or replace selected text. A native diff preview with Apply and Cancel , stale document checks, and undoable, unsaved edits. A clipboard fallback for framework and other file types. Safe insertion of several families at once. Live CDN diagnostics for availability, content types and browser font CORS. Variable weight ranges kept in generated @font face snippets. 2,023 library families, 547 variable, with bundled metadata. Search, filters, specimens, "},{"t":"Related","d":"Other Auric Artisan extensions, tools and pages that work alongside Font Hub.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Font Hub","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-font-hub/others/related.html","h":["On the Auric Artisan website","Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","Setup","Support"],"x":" The same font library in a browser: https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/ — see also Font Library ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/font library/README.md . The font CDN service: Font CDN ../../../services/font cdn/README.md . Auric Artisan Icon Hub ../../auric artisan icon hub/README.md — the icon counterpart: search open source icons and insert SVG. Auric Artisan Live ../../auric artisan live/README.md — serve the page and check the font in a real browser. Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md — colour and contrast checks for the text you set. Install and set up the Auric Artisan extensions ../../install and setup/README.md Marketplace listing: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan font hub Contact and support: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Formatter","d":"What Auric Artisan Formatter does, who it is for, how to install it and where to find every guide.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan Formatter formats your code in VS Code. It rebuilds JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, CSS, HTML, Markdown, YAML and more from a real parse, and tidies the indentation and spacing of hundreds of other languages with a conservative structural engine. Every result passes a safety gate before it reaches your file: the output is re read and compared with the input, and if the formatter cannot prove the change keeps your code's meaning, it keeps your original text. It is built for adopting a formatter without surprises. Preview Formatting as a Diff shows the result beside your source before anything changes. A workspace scan formats every file in memory when the window opens and tells you how many would change, without writing anything. Formatter Studio lets you try the 391 options against your own code, find the few that matter for a file, and copy only the ones you changed into a configuration file. The same engine runs from a command line for CI checks. It reads existing Prettier configuration and .editorconfig , offers 13 presets including one byte compatible with Prettier 3 , and has no runtime dependencies. Developers who want consistent formatting with a preview before "},{"t":"Auric Artisan Formatter guides","d":"Contents of the Auric Artisan Formatter task guides and references.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" Start with the getting started guide. The reference lists the 21 commands, 3 keyboard shortcuts and 11 editor settings; the options reference lists all 391 formatting options. File What it covers getting started.md getting started.md Install, make it the default formatter, the screen tour, the setup walkthrough format and format on save.md format and format on save.md Format a document or selection, format on save, only modified lines, format on type, language lists preview diff.md preview diff.md The native read only preview with Apply, Discard, Refresh and Compare formatter studio.md formatter studio.md Studio and the Explorer sidebar: scope, options rail, Find what matters, diff, explain, custom rules workspace scan.md workspace scan.md The in memory scan, the Workspace tab, formatting selected or all files, CI mode in Problems configuration.md configuration.md Configuration files, precedence, overrides, .editorconfig , Prettier import, directives, ignore files presets.md presets.md The 13 presets and what each changes safety gate and tiers.md safety gate and tiers.md The five safety checks, native and universal tiers, Explain Formatting Decisions supported languages.md support"},{"t":"Getting started with Auric Artisan Formatter","d":"Install Auric Artisan Formatter, make it your formatter, learn where its controls are, and preview a first format.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Install","Make it your formatter","The setup walkthrough","The screen tour","A first format with a preview","Next steps"],"x":" 1. Check that VS Code is version 1.74 or newer Help › About . 2. In the Extensions view Ctrl + Shift + X , search for @id:auric artisan.auric artisan formatter and select Install . Or run: text code install extension auric artisan.auric artisan formatter The extension starts when VS Code opens and offers formatting for every language it supports. VS Code uses one formatter per language. If you have several installed, it asks which to use every time. Tell it to use Auric: Run Auric Formatter: Toggle Format on Save . It sets editor.defaultFormatter to auric artisan.auric artisan formatter and turns on editor.formatOnSave , in the workspace settings when a folder is open otherwise in user settings . Run it again to turn format on save off. Or add the settings yourself: json { \"editor.defaultFormatter\": \"auric artisan.auric artisan formatter\", \"editor.formatOnSave\": true } To use it only for some languages, scope the settings: json { \" typescript \": { \"editor.defaultFormatter\": \"auric artisan.auric artisan formatter\", \"editor.formatOnSave\": true } } VS Code's Welcome page Help › Welcome includes Set up Auric Artisan Formatter , five steps with buttons: 1. Choose a preset — Switch pres"},{"t":"Command line and CI","d":"Run the same Auric formatting engine from a terminal with auric-format, check formatting in CI, and use its flags and exit codes.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/command-line.html","h":["Where it is","Common tasks","Flags","Exit codes","Use it in CI"],"x":" auric format runs the same engine, options, configuration files and safety gate as the extension, from a terminal. Use it to check formatting in continuous integration CI or to format many files in a script. The command line ships inside the installed extension as the script bin/auric format.js . It needs Node.js 16 or newer. It is not published as a separate npm package at the time of writing. VS Code installs extensions in a folder named after the extension and version, for example: text ~/.vscode/extensions/auric artisan.auric artisan formatter 0.1.0/bin/auric format.js On Windows, ~ is your user folder %USERPROFILE% . Run it with Node: text node ~/.vscode/extensions/auric artisan.auric artisan formatter 0.1.0/bin/auric format.js check . The examples below write auric format for short. To use the bare name, create a shell alias or a small wrapper script that runs the command above. A CI machine needs the extension's files available in the same way; the engine itself has no runtime dependencies beyond Node.js. text auric format write src rewrite files in place auric format check . exit 1 if anything is unformatted auric format preset prettier w . start from a preset cat a.css au"},{"t":"Configuration","d":"Configure Auric Artisan Formatter with presets, configuration files, per-language and per-file overrides, .editorconfig, Prettier settings, inline directives and ignore files.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/configuration.html","h":["Where options come from","Configuration files","Create a configuration file","Choose a preset","Coming from Prettier",".editorconfig","VS Code settings","Inline directives","Ignore files","Plugins","Clear the cache"],"x":" The formatter has 391 options see the options reference options reference.md . You rarely need more than a handful: start from a preset and set only what you disagree with. From lowest to highest precedence: 1. A preset — \"preset\": \"prettier\" and twelve others. See Presets presets.md . 2. A configuration file — see the list below. 3. .editorconfig — for the options it can express. 4. VS Code settings under auricFormatter. , a command line flag, or an inline directive in the file itself. Inside a configuration file, languages by language id and overrides by file pattern beat the file's top level values. Auric Formatter: Explain Formatting Decisions for This File shows which layer set each option for the current file. The formatter looks for the first of these files, searching from the file's folder upward. Within a folder, this order is the precedence: File Format .auricformatrc JSON or YAML, detected automatically .auricformatrc.json JSON .auricformatrc.yaml , .auricformatrc.yml YAML .auricformatrc.js , .auricformatrc.cjs JavaScript CommonJS .auricformat.config.js , .auricformat.config.cjs JavaScript CommonJS auric.format.json JSON package.json Under an auricFormatter or auric for"},{"t":"Format files and format on save","d":"Format a document or selection, format on save (including only changed lines), format as you type, and choose which languages Auric formats.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/format-and-format-on-save.html","h":["Format a document","Format a selection","Format on save","Format as you type","Choose languages","Format many files","Files that are skipped"],"x":" Run Auric Formatter: Format Document . It uses Auric for this format even if another formatter is your default. Or use VS Code's own Format Document Shift + Alt + F on Windows once Auric is your default formatter. The status bar reports the result: the tier used, whether the file was already formatted, whether the safety gate kept your original text, or whether the file was skipped. 1. Select the code. 2. Run Auric Formatter: Format Selection , or right click and choose Format Selection . With nothing selected: Select some code first. A selection may grow to a complete syntax unit for example a whole statement or block so the result stays valid. 1. Run Auric Formatter: Toggle Format on Save . The message says Auric Formatter is now your default formatter and runs on save. 2. Save a file. It is formatted first. Running the command again turns format on save off Format on save is off. . Reformatting a whole file on its first save in a large codebase makes one huge diff and clutters git blame . Set: json { \"auricFormatter.formatOnSaveMode\": \"modifications\" } Format on save then formats only the lines changed since the last commit, using Git. The default, file , formats the whole file"},{"t":"Formatter Studio","d":"Use Formatter Studio and the Explorer sidebar to try options on your own code, see the diff and the reasons, and export a configuration.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/formatter-studio.html","h":["Open it","The layout","The Studio tab","Apply the result to your file","Save your configuration","The Studio command palette","Limits"],"x":" Formatter Studio the setup walkthrough calls it the Playground puts your code on one side, the formatted result on the other, and every option that applies in between. Change an option and the result updates as you type. Nothing you do in Studio touches your file until you explicitly apply it. Auric Formatter: Open Formatter Studio — Ctrl + Alt + Shift + P Cmd + Alt + Shift + P on macOS . Opens as an editor tab with the active editor's content loaded. The Auric Formatter section in the Explorer — a compact version of the same tools, with Open full Studio . Show Files That Need Formatting Ctrl + Alt + Shift + U opens Studio on its Workspace tab. The panel follows your VS Code theme light, dark and high contrast , respects reduced motion, and remembers its state when you reload. Control What it does Brand line The number of options and languages, and the version auricartisan.com ↗ Open the Auric Artisan website Lang The language to format the input as; searchable, grouped into Native printers and Universal engine Preset The preset to start from; searchable, each with a description Commands The Studio command palette also Ctrl + K Layout button Show or hide the options rail Control W"},{"t":"Options reference","d":"All 391 Auric Artisan Formatter formatting options in 17 categories, with type, default, allowed values and effect.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/options-reference.html","h":["How to use this page","Global","Common","JavaScript","TypeScript","CSS","HTML","Markdown","YAML","JSON","GraphQL","Universal","Alignment","Sorting","Comments","Blank Lines","Safety","Experimental"],"x":" Auric Artisan Formatter has 391 formatting options in 17 categories. This page lists every one. The eleven settings that control how the extension works in VS Code preset, format on save, the workspace scan and so on are in the reference reference.md . Each option can be set in four places. The same name works in all of them: Where How it is written VS Code settings \"auricFormatter.printWidth\": 100 A configuration file such as .auricformatrc \"printWidth\": 100 no prefix The command line print width 100 the name in kebab case; booleans also take a no form An inline directive in a file // @auric printWidth=100 The defaults shown are the extension's own defaults. A preset changes many of them; \"preset\": \"prettier\" , for example, switches every Auric only enhancement off. Anything you set yourself wins over the preset. See Configuration configuration.md and Presets presets.md . Options that only apply to some languages only affect files in those languages. Formatter Studio's Affects this file filter shows which options change the file you are looking at. Options marked \"Experimental\" are still settling; Formatter Studio hides them unless you tick Experimental . 21 options. Setting Type"},{"t":"Presets","d":"The 13 Auric Artisan Formatter presets, what each is for and which options each sets.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/presets.html","h":["Set a preset","The 13 presets","Which preset","What each preset sets"],"x":" A preset is a named starting point: a coherent set of option values. Choose the one closest to how your team already writes code, then override the few things you disagree with. Anything you set yourself wins over the preset; options you do not mention keep the preset's value. The default preset is auric . Auric Formatter: Switch Formatting Preset — pick from the list; it saves auricFormatter.preset and re runs the workspace scan. In a configuration file: \"preset\": \"prettier\" . This wins over the VS Code setting. In VS Code settings: \"auricFormatter.preset\": \"prettier\" . For one file: a leading comment with @auric preset compact . On the command line: preset prettier . In Formatter Studio: the Preset drop down, to compare presets on your own file before choosing. json { \"preset\": \"prettier\", \"printWidth\": 100 } This gives Prettier's exact behaviour at 100 columns instead of 80. Preset Builds on Options it sets Description auric — 50 The Auric house style: Prettier's layout plus the Auric enhancements. prettier — 281 Byte compatible with Prettier 3 at its own defaults, with every Auric only enhancement switched off. standard prettier 14 StandardJS: no semicolons, single quotes, and"},{"t":"Preview formatting as a diff","d":"See the formatted result beside your source in a read-only editor, compare the changes, and apply or discard them.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/preview-diff.html","h":["Open a preview","Act on the preview","Stale previews","Limits"],"x":" The native preview shows what formatting would do before your file changes. It opens a read only copy of the formatted result in a normal VS Code editor beside your source; no Studio panel opens. 1. Focus the source file in the editor. 2. Use any of these: Auric Formatter: Preview Formatting as a Diff Ctrl + Alt + Shift + F ; Cmd + Alt + Shift + F on macOS ; the Preview Formatting as a Diff button in the editor title bar; right click with nothing selected and choose Preview Formatting as a Diff ; Preview beside editor in Formatter Studio. 3. A read only tab named Preview — file name opens beside the source, with the same language highlighting. With text selected, only the selection is formatted in the preview it may grow to a complete syntax unit . If formatting fails or the safety gate refuses the change, no preview opens and a warning says why, for example Auric Formatter: the safety gate refused this change . The preview shows CodeLens links at the top and buttons in the editor title bar: Control What it does Apply formatting Replace the source with the preview, after confirming Apply formatting to file ? The source stays unsaved. You can undo this edit. Compare changes Open VS"},{"t":"The safety gate and formatting tiers","d":"How Auric Artisan Formatter checks every result before it reaches your file, what the native and universal tiers can change, and how to see why a file was formatted as it was.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/safety-gate-and-tiers.html","h":["The five checks","When a check fails","The tiers","See why a file was formatted as it was"],"x":" A formatter rewrites your source. That is only acceptable if it can show it did not change what the source means. Auric Artisan Formatter checks every file before you see the result. Check What it proves Option Token stream The output re reads to the same significant tokens as the input: no dropped argument, swallowed operator or mangled string safetyTokenCheck and safetyTokenCheckComments to include comments Comments Every comment in the input appears in the output safetyCommentPreservation String literals Every string and template keeps the same content safetyStringLiterals Reparse The output parses again with the same parser safetyReparse Idempotency Formatting the output again gives identical bytes safetyIdempotency off by default; safetyIdempotencyPasses sets the extra passes safetyNumericLiterals also requires every number to keep its value when its spelling changes. The gate knows which changes your options allow. With singleQuote on, it expects quotes to change; with cssTrailingSemicolon on, it knows the last ; before } is optional in CSS. A change your options do not allow is treated as corruption and reverted. Your original text is kept — not partly applied, not a best e"},{"t":"Supported languages","d":"Every language Auric Artisan Formatter formats, grouped by how much it can change.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/supported-languages.html","h":["Native tier","Universal tier: reindent and spacing (104)","Universal tier: spacing only (60)","Universal tier: whitespace only (60)"],"x":" The formatter recognises 253 languages by file extension, exact file name, shebang line and VS Code language id. What it does with each depends on its tier; see The safety gate and formatting tiers safety gate and tiers.md . Tier Languages What changes Native 33 registry entries; 31 verified native modes Anything layout related: the file is rebuilt from a real parse Universal: reindent and spacing 104 Indentation and spacing Universal: spacing only 60 Spacing between tokens; indentation untouched Universal: whitespace only 60 Trailing whitespace, blank lines, line endings, final newline The two native entries that are not yet verified are JavaScript React jsx and TypeScript React tsx : a file containing JSX elements falls back to the universal tier in version 0.1.0. To see the list yourself, run auric format list languages see Command line and CI command line.md . Formatter Studio's Lang drop down groups languages into Native printers and Universal engine . The \"Formatter id\" is the name used in the formatter's languages configuration. Language Formatter id File extensions or names JavaScript javascript .js .cjs .mjs .es .es6 .pac and more JavaScript React jsx .jsx TypeScript type"},{"t":"Scan the workspace","d":"See how many files would change before formatting a repository, review them in the Workspace tab, format them explicitly, or check without writing.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/workspace-scan.html","h":["What the scan does","Where the results appear","Run a scan on demand","The Workspace tab","Taking the change","Check without writing (CI mode)","Scan settings"],"x":" Adopting a formatter on an existing codebase is mostly a question of trust. Format on save quietly rewrites the first file you open; formatting the whole workspace rewrites thousands at once. The workspace scan is a third option: it formats every supported file in memory , tells you what would change, and writes nothing. A few seconds after the window opens auricFormatter.scanOnStartup , on by default , the formatter: reads every supported file in the workspace and formats it in memory; records whether each file would change, and how many lines it would gain and lose; notes files that fail to parse, are skipped, or trip the safety gate. Nothing is written to disk; your working tree and git status stay as they were. The scan also follows your work: saved and unsaved edits, external changes and created or deleted files update the results, and new files trigger a short, delayed rescan. Changing the preset or saving a configuration file re runs the scan, because they change what \"already formatted\" means. The status bar shows N unformatted with a warning background. The tooltip says N of M files would change if formatted. Nothing has been written — click to review them. When everythin"},{"t":"Reference: commands, keys and settings","d":"Every Auric Artisan Formatter command, keyboard shortcut, menu entry, status bar state, file and editor setting.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/reference.html","h":["Commands","Where commands appear","Status bar","Editor settings","Files","Workspace trust and virtual workspaces","Setup walkthrough"],"x":" This page covers Auric Artisan Formatter 0.1.0: 21 commands, 3 keyboard shortcuts, one Explorer view, a setup walkthrough, 11 editor settings and 391 formatting options listed in the options reference options reference.md . Commands appear in the Command Palette with the Auric Formatter: prefix. Command ID Keys What it does Format Document auricFormatter.formatDocument — Format the active file with Auric Format Selection auricFormatter.formatSelection — Format the selected code shown only with a selection Format Every File in the Workspace auricFormatter.formatWorkspace — Write every file the scan found would change asks first Format Every File That Needs It auricFormatter.formatAll — The same, from the scan results asks first Scan the Workspace Without Writing auricFormatter.scanWorkspace — Format every file in memory and report; offers Review them or Format them all Show Files That Need Formatting auricFormatter.showPending Ctrl + Alt + Shift + U Open Formatter Studio on the Workspace tab Check Formatting Without Writing CI Mode auricFormatter.checkWorkspace — Scan and list unformatted files in the Problems panel Open Formatter Studio auricFormatter.openPlayground Ctrl + Alt + S"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for common Auric Artisan Formatter problems.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Nothing happens when I save","VS Code asks which formatter to use on every save","The status bar shows a shield: \"your original text was kept\"","The file was skipped","JSX or TSX is only indented, not reformatted","A language is only lightly formatted","My configuration file is ignored","Output matches Prettier, not the Auric style","\"Select some code first.\"","Preview problems","Formatter Studio problems","Workspace scan problems","\"No Prettier configuration found in this workspace.\"","The command line is not found"],"x":" For anything not listed, run Auric Formatter: Report a Formatting Problem , add what happened and a small sample file, and see Get support ../../install and setup/docs/get support.md . Show the Formatter Log has the details of each run; set auricFormatter.logLevel to debug for more. Why: Auric is not the default formatter, format on save is off, or the language is excluded. Fix: run Toggle Format on Save , or check editor.defaultFormatter and editor.formatOnSave including language specific blocks such as \" typescript \" . Check auricFormatter.enabledLanguages and auricFormatter.disabledLanguages . Why: several formatters are installed and no default is set. Fix: run Toggle Format on Save , which sets editor.defaultFormatter , or set it yourself per language. Why: a safety check failed, so the formatter refused to change the file. Fix: open the log to see which check failed and where. Often the file has a construct the parser does not handle yet; the file is safe as it is. Report it with Report a Formatting Problem if you think the change should have been allowed. Why: it is larger than auricFormatter.maxFileSizeKb , looks minified, is in .auricformatignore or .prettierignore , has "},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan Formatter.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/docs/faq.html","h":["Will it rewrite my repository when I install it?","Can it produce exactly the same output as Prettier?","How do I keep git blame useful?","Could it break my code?","Which languages does it support?","Does it format JSX?","Where do I put my settings?","How do I find the option I want?","Can I use it in CI?","Does it send my code anywhere?","Is the interface available in Hindi?"],"x":" No. The startup scan only formats in memory and reports a count. Files are written only when you format them: on save if you turn it on , with a Format command, with Apply , or with Format selected or Format all files . The prettier preset is byte compatible with Prettier 3 at its own defaults, with every Auric only enhancement off. A project with only a Prettier configuration gets that preset automatically. Set auricFormatter.formatOnSaveMode to modifications so format on save only touches lines you changed, or use the minimal diff preset. When you do format everything, use the Workspace tab to take a folder at a time. Every result passes the safety gate: tokens, comments, strings and a reparse are checked before anything is written, and on failure your original text is kept. The universal engine can only change whitespace. Keep using version control as usual. 253 languages: 31 native modes plus 220 on the universal tier. See Supported languages supported languages.md . In version 0.1.0, files containing JSX elements are indented and spaced by the universal tier but not pretty printed. In a .auricformatrc at the project root, so everyone gets the same result. VS Code settings wor"},{"t":"Supporting material","d":"Contents of the supporting pages for Auric Artisan Formatter.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages support the Formatter guides: terms, shortcuts, limits and guarantees, privacy, related products and the version history. File What it covers glossary.md glossary.md Terms used in the Formatter documentation shortcuts.md shortcuts.md Every keyboard shortcut limits and accuracy.md limits and accuracy.md What the safety gate guarantees, known gaps and size limits privacy.md privacy.md What stays local related.md related.md Related extensions and pages release notes.md release notes.md What changed in each version "},{"t":"Shortcuts","d":"The keyboard shortcuts Auric Artisan Formatter provides in VS Code and inside Formatter Studio.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/shortcuts.html","h":["VS Code","Formatter Studio"],"x":" Windows and Linux macOS Command When Ctrl + Alt + Shift + F Cmd + Alt + Shift + F Preview Formatting as a Diff An editor has focus Ctrl + Alt + Shift + P Cmd + Alt + Shift + P Open Formatter Studio Any time Ctrl + Alt + Shift + U Cmd + Alt + Shift + U Show Files That Need Formatting Any time There is deliberately no shortcut for formatting every file. VS Code's own Format Document Shift + Alt + F on Windows and Format Selection use Auric once it is the default formatter. Assign shortcuts to other commands in Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts by searching for auricFormatter . Keys What they do Ctrl + K Open the Studio command palette Left and right arrows on the tabs Switch between 01 Studio and 02 Workspace Arrow keys, type ahead, Enter in drop downs Choose a language, preset, category or view Escape Close the command palette or an open drop down "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the terms used in the Auric Artisan Formatter documentation.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" CI continuous integration — automated checks that run on every change, where auric format check can fail a build if files are unformatted. CodeLens — clickable links VS Code shows above code; the preview uses them for Apply, Compare, Discard and Refresh. Configuration file — a file such as .auricformatrc that holds formatting options for a project. Default formatter — the formatter VS Code uses for a language, set with editor.defaultFormatter . Directive — a comment in a file that talks to the formatter, such as auric format ignore or @auric printWidth=120 . Format on save — formatting a file automatically each time you save it. Formatter Studio — the panel for trying options on your own code called the Playground in the walkthrough . Idempotent — formatting the output again changes nothing. Native tier — languages with a real parser and printer, rebuilt from their syntax tree. Option — one formatting choice, such as printWidth or singleQuote . There are 391. Parser — the part that reads source code into a structure the formatter can print. Passthrough — the lightest treatment, for unrecognised files: only whitespace at line ends, blank lines, line endings and the final newline. P"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What Auric Artisan Formatter's safety gate guarantees, its known gaps in version 0.1.0, and its size and time limits.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["What the safety gate guarantees","Known gaps in version 0.1.0","Limits","Deterministic output","What it is not"],"x":" With the default settings, a result is written only if the output re reads to the same significant tokens, keeps every comment and every string's content, and parses again. If any check fails, the original text is kept. The idempotency check formatting twice gives the same bytes is off by default because it doubles the work; the verified preset turns it on. The gate protects meaning, not taste: a result can pass every check and still not be the layout you want. Use Formatter Studio to tune it. JSX and TSX files containing JSX elements are formatted by the universal tier indentation and spacing only , not pretty printed. Universal tier languages only change whitespace. Some only change spacing or trailing whitespace. See Supported languages ../docs/supported languages.md . Format Every File in the Workspace on a folder's context menu formats every pending file in the workspace, not only that folder. The command line ships inside the extension and is not a separate npm package. Limit Default Setting Largest file formatted 4096 KB 0 removes the limit auricFormatter.maxFileSizeKb Parse time before a parse is abandoned 5000 ms 0 waits indefinitely auricFormatter.parseTimeoutMs Files in"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What Auric Artisan Formatter does with your code and settings.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/privacy.html","h":[],"x":" Everything runs locally. Formatting, the workspace scan, Formatter Studio and the command line run on your machine or next to the files in a remote setup . The engine has no runtime dependencies and makes no network requests. No telemetry and no account. The workspace scan only reads. It formats in memory; nothing is written until you choose a Format action. Configuration stays in your project files and VS Code settings. Report a Formatting Problem only opens a local document for you to review; nothing is sent until you choose to share it. It contains the formatter version, VS Code version, language, tier and the explanation for the active file, not the file itself. In an untrusted workspace , JavaScript configuration files and formatter plugins are not run. Links to auricartisan.com open your browser only when you select them. "},{"t":"Release notes","d":"What changed in each published version of Auric Artisan Formatter.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/release-notes.html","h":["0.1.0 (23 September 2026)"],"x":" Formatting output is treated as part of the extension's public behaviour: a change that makes an already formatted file format differently is at least a minor version and is listed under \"Formatting changes\", so a team can decide when to take the diff. The first Marketplace release. A native read only formatting preview beside the source, with Apply , Discard , Refresh and Compare Changes in the editor title and CodeLens. Format document, selection and every pending file; format on save, optionally only changed lines; format as you type. A status bar item reporting the tier and any safety reversion. Explain Formatting Decisions , Import Settings From Prettier , Generate a Configuration File , Switch Formatting Preset and Report a Formatting Problem . A setup walkthrough on the Welcome page. Formatter Studio and a matching Explorer sidebar, with searchable drop downs, a filterable option rail category, changed only, affects this file and experimental filters , Find what matters , and live Result , Diff and Explain views. Full document and Editor selection scopes, a preview toggle, and explicit Yes, apply and No, discard . Apply is bound to the original document and refuses stale, d"},{"t":"Related","d":"Other Auric Artisan extensions and pages that work alongside the Formatter.","p":"VS Code extensions › Auric Artisan Formatter","u":"vscode-extensions/auric-artisan-formatter/others/related.html","h":["Other Auric Artisan VS Code extensions","Setup","Auric Artisan pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan Studio ../../auric artisan studio/README.md — Code Health, Accessibility and Color checks that complement formatting. Auric Artisan Live ../../auric artisan live/README.md — serve and preview the pages you format. Auric Artisan File System ../../auric artisan file system/README.md — create and rename the files you format. Auric Artisan Theme ../../auric artisan theme/README.md — the editor theme the Formatter Studio panel follows. Install and set up the Auric Artisan extensions ../../install and setup/README.md Settings, sync and workspace trust ../../install and setup/docs/settings and sync.md VS Code extensions: https://auricartisan.com/vscode/ Marketplace listing: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=auric artisan.auric artisan formatter Contact and support: https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/ "},{"t":"Auric Artisan browser extension","d":"What the Auric Artisan browser extension is, who it is for, where to get it and how to start using it.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" Auric Artisan for the browser puts colour, accessibility and front end tools on every page you open. You pick a colour from the screen, check a colour pair against WCAG and APCA contrast, audit a whole page for accessibility problems, inspect any element, read a site's design tokens, and see the page as people with different kinds of vision see it. It is one extension, published as Auric Artisan , and every tool ships in the same install: there is no paid edition and no second download. The extension runs entirely on your device. It has no account, no sign in, no analytics and makes no network requests of its own. Everything you pick, audit or save stays in your browser's extension storage. The only traffic it causes is a page you choose to open, such as a link to auricartisan.com or a web search you start from the right click menu. The tools live in a workspace you open from the toolbar icon or dock beside the page in the browser's side panel the sidebar in Firefox . The workspace has a Home screen and four spaces, Colour , Check , Code and Saved , and a search field that finds any tool, setting or auricartisan.com page. Two optional features work on websites themselves, and both"},{"t":"Browser extension documentation","d":"The contents of the browser extension's how-to documentation, from installing to every tool and setting.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/README.html","h":["Files","Folders"],"x":" This folder explains how to install the Auric Artisan browser extension and use every part of it: the popup and side panel, each tool in the Colour, Check, Code and Saved spaces, the features that work on websites, and every setting. Start with Getting started getting started.md if you are new, or go straight to the tool you need. Page What it covers Getting started getting started.md Open the extension, take the tour, and do a first task in each space Hindi interface hindi interface.md Switch the interface to हिन्दी, and what does and does not change Permissions permissions.md Every permission the extension asks for, when, and why Reference reference.md Every control, option, output and limit in one place Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Symptoms, causes and fixes FAQ faq.md Short answers to common questions install/ install/README.md : Installing on Chrome and other Chromium browsers, Edge, Opera, Firefox and Safari; loading from a ZIP; updating and removing surfaces/ surfaces/README.md : The popup, Home, search, the side panel, what the extension draws on a page, and the element inspector colour/ colour/README.md : Picker, Page palette, Image, Gradient, Mix, Harmony, Scale an"},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Open the extension, learn the layout of the workspace, take the tour and complete a first task in each space.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/getting-started.html","h":["Before you start","Open the extension","Take the tour","The layout","A first task in each space","Next steps"],"x":" This page takes you from a fresh install to your first result in each part of the extension. If the extension is not installed yet, follow Install install/README.md first. Pin the icon. Browsers hide new extensions behind a puzzle piece or extensions menu. Pin Auric Artisan so its icon stays on the toolbar. Use an ordinary web page. Browsers do not let extensions run on their own pages, such as settings pages, the new tab page, chrome:// and about: addresses, or the extension stores. Page tools also cannot reach file:// pages unless you allow file access for the extension in the browser. Open any normal http or https site to try the page tools. Nothing on websites changes until you ask. The website pickers and the custom right click menu are off after install. You turn them on in Settings when you want them. You have three ways to open the same workspace: Where How Best for The popup Click the toolbar icon, or press Alt + Shift + A Quick checks; it closes when you click elsewhere The side panel Chromium or sidebar Firefox Choose Open the side panel in the header, or open it from the browser's own side panel or sidebar menu Longer sessions; it stays open while you browse Its own wi"},{"t":"Hindi interface","d":"Switch the extension's interface to Hindi (हिन्दी), what is translated, what stays as it is and why, and how the browser's own texts follow its language.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/hindi-interface.html","h":["Switch the language","What changes","What stays as it is","The browser's own texts","Related pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan speaks English and हिन्दी Hindi . The whole interface switches together, including what it draws on websites and every accessibility finding. 1. Open Settings › Appearance . 2. Under Language , choose हिन्दी . Each option is written in its own language, so you can always find your way back. You can also search for \"language\", \"hindi\" or \"भाषा\". Switching to Hindi applies at once. Open tabs follow without a reload. Switching back to English reloads the popup. Once Hindi is chosen, the popup opens in Hindi straight away; it never shows English first. the popup, the side panel and the separate window; Settings, search results, toasts and the tour; the website pickers, including the calendar's month and day names; the custom right click menu; the element inspector's cards and bar; every accessibility finding, including messages built from live values, such as \"8 failing\"; the entries in the browser's own right click menu. Search works in both languages: a Hindi interface finds tools by their Hindi or English names. Some text is deliberately never translated, because translating it would misreport what the page or the standard says: values read from the page, such as disp"},{"t":"Permissions","d":"Every permission Auric Artisan asks for, when the browser asks, why each is needed, and how to review or revoke them.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/permissions.html","h":["The short version","Asked for at install","Asked for only when you turn on the custom right-click menu","Where the page script does not run","Review or revoke permissions","Related pages"],"x":" When you install Auric Artisan, the browser warns that it can \"read and change your data on all websites\". This page explains exactly what the extension declares, when each permission is asked for, and what it is used for. The tools work on whatever page you use them on, so the extension needs access to all sites. A small script loads on each page and waits. Until you start a tool, it only reads your settings and listens for your commands. It does not read your content or change the page. Everything that changes a page, the website pickers and the custom right click menu, is off until you turn it on. Three extra permissions are asked for only if you turn on the custom right click menu. Nothing is sent anywhere. See Privacy ../others/privacy.md . Permission What the browser calls it Why it is needed Host access to all sites Read and change your data on all websites The page tools work on any page you choose; the optional pickers and menu must be ready before you use a page activeTab — Access to the tab you are on when you use the popup, a shortcut or a menu item scripting — Starts the page script in tabs opened before install, and runs the eyedropper in the page when needed storage"},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every control, option, output, setting, shortcut and limit of the Auric Artisan browser extension in one place.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/reference.html","h":["Product facts","Header and navigation (The popup)","Home (Home)","Tools","Picker","Page palette and Image","Gradient, Mix, Harmony, Scale, Convert","Contrast","Vision","Audit and Findings","Inspector and Inspect","Tokens and Snippets","Settings","Keyboard shortcuts","Limits","Files the extension writes"],"x":" This page lists every part of the extension in tables, for quick lookup. Each section links to the page that explains it in full. It describes version 1.0.2. Fact Value Name Auric Artisan Version described 1.0.2 Extension format Manifest V3 Browsers Chrome, Edge, Opera, Brave, Vivaldi and other Chromium browsers; Firefox 115 and later Interface languages English, हिन्दी Hindi Price Free Account None Network requests None of its own; only pages you choose to open Tools 18 Accessibility rules 80 in the engine; 78 run by the audit WCAG 2.2 A and AA Vision simulations 12 8 colour vision, 4 low vision Colour formats in the Picker 12 Control What it does Auric Artisan wordmark Opens auricartisan.com Search field Finds tools, settings and web pages / or Ctrl + K Open the side panel Docks the workspace; hidden in the side panel Open in its own window A 620 × 700 resizable window; hidden at Compact size Switch between light and dark Flips the theme Settings Opens Settings Spaces Home, Colour, Check, Code, Saved Site chip The site the page tools act on, or No page Take the tour ? Replays the tour Tool chips The tools of the current space Block Contents Colour of the day Swatch, date, HEX, O"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Symptoms, causes and fixes for the Auric Artisan browser extension — page tools, the eyedropper, pickers, the right-click menu, shortcuts, audits and data.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Page tools","Eyedropper and colours","Website pickers","Right-click menu","Shortcuts","Inspector","Audit","Data and appearance","Related pages"],"x":" Find your symptom, read why it happens, and try the fix. If nothing here helps, reload the page, then reload the extension from your browser's extensions page. Symptom Why What to do The site chip says No page , or a page tool does nothing Browsers do not let extensions run on their own pages settings, new tab, chrome:// , about: or on the web stores Open an ordinary web page Page tools do nothing on a local file Extensions cannot reach file:// pages by default In a Chromium browser: extensions page › Auric Artisan › Details › Allow access to file URLs A tool worked on other tabs but not on one opened before you installed The page was loaded before the extension existed Reload the tab. The extension also tries to start itself there when you use a tool. \"Could not scan this page\" or \"No active tab\" The page is protected, still loading, or no normal tab is active Wait for the page to load, click into it, and try again Nothing is found inside an embedded frame The extension runs in the top page only Open the frame's own address in a tab You limited the extension's site access Page tools work only on sites you allowed Allow the site from the extension's toolbar menu or details page Sy"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Auric Artisan browser extension.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/docs/faq.html","h":["Getting it","Privacy and permissions","Using it"],"x":" The Chrome Web Store for Chrome, Edge, Opera, Brave, Vivaldi and Arc, and Firefox Add ons for Firefox. Links are on https://auricartisan.com/extension and in Install install/README.md . Yes. Every tool ships in the one install. There is no paid edition and no account. No. There is no sign in anywhere in the extension, and it does not talk to auricartisan.com or anything else. Nothing: they are identical copies of the same Chromium package, named for their stores. Any of them works in any Chromium browser. The Firefox package is a separate build. It is not published for Safari. On a Mac you can convert the Chromium package with Apple's tools yourself, without a side panel. See Safari install/safari.md . From Firefox Add ons, yes. A copy loaded with Load Temporary Add on is removed when Firefox quits, because Firefox keeps only signed add ons. The tools work on whatever page you are looking at, and the extension cannot know in advance which pages those will be. A small script loads on each page and waits until you start a tool; everything that changes a page is off until you turn it on. See Permissions permissions.md . No. There are no analytics, accounts or remote calls. Everything"},{"t":"Check tools","d":"The tools in the Check space — Contrast, Vision, Audit and Findings — and the rules the audit applies.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/README.html","h":["Files in this folder","Key ideas"],"x":" The Check space holds the accessibility tools. Contrast checks any colour pair and fixes it. Vision shows the live page through twelve simulations. Audit checks the current page against WCAG 2.2, and Findings gathers everything wrong into one list. Page What it covers Contrast contrast.md Check a pair in WCAG and APCA, read the verdict, and find the nearest passing colour Vision vision.md Colour vision and low vision simulations on the live page, side by side, and capture Audit audit.md Run an audit, read the contrast results, outline problems on the page, and export Audit rules audit rules.md The 80 rules of the accessibility engine, by category, with their WCAG criteria Findings all findings.md The pooled list of problems, by severity, with actions for each WCAG contrast ratio compares the relative luminance of two colours, from 1:1 no contrast to 21:1 black on white . WCAG 2.2 asks for 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for large text at level AA, and 7:1 and 4.5:1 at AAA. APCA Lc Accessible Perceptual Contrast Algorithm, lightness contrast is the contrast method in the WCAG 3 drafts. It gives a signed score, where a higher absolute value reads more easily, and its guidance depends on"},{"t":"Findings","d":"One list of everything the tools found — accessibility, contrast and inspection problems — ordered by severity, with actions for each.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/all-findings.html","h":["Read the list","Actions","Keeping findings","Related pages"],"x":" Findings All Findings pools the problems the extension found in this session into one list, most serious first. It fills from three sources: Source Label What it adds The accessibility audit a11y Every rule failure and warning from the last audit The contrast scan color Every failing or borderline piece of text from the last audit The element inspector inspect The inspected element's text contrast, when it fails Until you run an audit, the list reads \"No findings yet. Run a page audit to fill this in.\" Three counts sit at the top: Failing , Warnings and Total . The Findings chip in the Check space shows the number of open failures and warnings. Findings are ordered with failures before warnings, then by impact: critical, serious, moderate and minor. Each finding shows: its source label; its title, such as \"Form field has no label\" or \"Contrast 3.12:1\"; a message naming the element and the problem, such as \"Sign up\" needs 4.5:1 ; the element's CSS selector; action buttons. Button Appears on What it does Show on page All Outlines the page's contrast problems for 15 seconds for an inspected element, highlights that element Copy selector All Copies the element's CSS selector Inspect A"},{"t":"Audit rules","d":"Every rule in the extension's accessibility engine, grouped by category, with its impact, WCAG 2.2 success criteria and whether the audit runs it.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/audit-rules.html","h":["Impact","How the score is calculated","Rules","Related pages"],"x":" The accessibility engine behind Audit and Findings has 80 rules in eight categories, mapped to 32 WCAG 2.2 success criteria . The audit runs at level AA, so it applies the 78 rules that test levels A and AA. The two AAA rules, enhanced text contrast 1.4.6 and reduced motion 2.3.3 , are part of the engine but are not run by the audit. The engine uses the WCAG 2.2 success criteria, the ARIA 1.2 role and attribute definitions and the HTML accessibility mappings bundled in the extension, so questions such as \"is this attribute allowed on this role\" are answered from the specifications rather than guessed. Accessible names are computed with the standard accessible name algorithm, following aria labelledby , labels, title and content. Each finding has an impact, the same scale most accessibility tools use: Impact Meaning critical Blocks some people from using the content at all serious A significant barrier; fix soon moderate Makes the content harder to use minor A nuisance or a best practice gap A finding is either a failure or a warning . A warning means a person must decide, for example contrast over an image. The score, from 0 to 100, counts distinct failing rules , not each failing"},{"t":"Audit","d":"Audit the current page against WCAG 2.2 A and AA, read the contrast results, outline problems on the page, and export the results.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/audit.html","h":["Run an audit","Read the contrast results","Outline problems on the page","The accessibility audit","Export","Limits","Other ways to audit","Related pages"],"x":" Audit the Page audit checks the current tab's colours and accessibility against WCAG 2.2. One run does two things: a contrast scan of the page's text, shown in the Audit tool itself; an accessibility audit by an 80 rule engine, run at level AA, so the 78 rules that test levels A and AA apply. Its findings go to Findings all findings.md . Everything runs in your browser. Nothing is sent anywhere, and results are kept only while the popup or side panel is open. 1. Open the page you want to check and wait for it to finish loading. 2. Open Check › Audit and choose Run the audit . Home › Audit opens it and starts at once. 3. The button reads Auditing… while it works. Large pages take longer; the page stays responsive. When it finishes, the button reads Run audit , so you can run it again after you change the page. Four counts sit at the top: Tested : Pieces of text the scan measured Failing : Text below its WCAG AA threshold: 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text Borderline : Text that passes, but by less than 1.5 for example 5.2:1 against 4.5:1 Review : Text over a background image, gradient or text shadow, where the true contrast cannot be measured exactly; check these by eye Below, each flag"},{"t":"Contrast","d":"Check a text and background colour pair against WCAG 2.2 and APCA, read the verdict and size guidance, and fix the pair to the nearest passing colour.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/contrast.html","h":["Open it","Set the pair","Read the results","Fix the pair","Other buttons","Related pages"],"x":" Contrast the Contrast checker tells you whether a text colour is readable on a background, in WCAG 2.2 and APCA, and finds the nearest colour that passes if it is not. Check › Contrast ; Alt + Shift + C ; Check as text or Check as background in the Picker; clicking a finding in Audit, or Check contrast in Findings; Contrast in a colour's detail card Page palette, Image, Scale ; Use text colour or Use background in Code › Inspect. 1. Set Text with its swatch or by typing a HEX value. 2. Set Background the same way. The pair starts as near black on gold. A Recent strip loads one of your latest colours as the text colour. A live preview shows the pair as large \"Aa\", a sentence, 14 px body text, and a button, a link and a chip. A banner shows the strongest WCAG level the pair clears and what that means: Verdict Ratio Meaning shown AAA 7:1 or more Excellent, fine for body text at any size AA 4.5:1 or more Passes for normal body text and everything larger AA Large 3:1 or more Large text and UI elements only Fail Below 3:1 Decorative use only, not for text The banner also shows the ratio and, when APCA is on, the APCA Lc score. The ratio WCAG ratio and six checks, each marked pass or fai"},{"t":"Vision","d":"See the live page through eight colour-vision deficiency and four low-vision simulations, compare side by side, and capture the result.","p":"Browser extension › Check","u":"browser-extension/docs/check/vision.html","h":["Simulations","Use it","Compare side by side","Capture","Other ways to start a simulation","Limits","Related pages"],"x":" Vision the Vision simulator filters the live page so you can see it the way people with different vision do. It helps you spot information carried by colour alone, low contrast areas and layouts that depend on peripheral vision. Group Simulation What it shows Colour blindness Protanopia No red sensitive cones Deuteranopia No green sensitive cones, the most common form Tritanopia No blue sensitive cones, rare Achromatopsia No colour vision Weaker forms Protanomaly Weak red sensitivity Deuteranomaly Weak green sensitivity Tritanomaly Weak blue sensitivity Achromatomaly Weak colour vision overall Low vision Cataracts Blur with a yellowed, washed out look Low vision Strong blur with reduced brightness Glaucoma Tunnel vision: the edges of the view darken AMD Age related macular degeneration: loss in the centre of the view 1. Open the page, then Check › Vision . 2. Choose a simulation. The page is filtered at once. 3. Drag Strength 0 to 100%, 100% by default to weaken or strengthen the effect. Strength applies to the eight colour vision simulations; the four low vision ones have a fixed strength. 4. Choose another simulation to switch, or Clear to remove the filter. The filter stays on "},{"t":"Code tools","d":"The tools in the Code space — Inspect, Tokens and Snippets — and every code format the extension can export.","p":"Browser extension › Code","u":"browser-extension/docs/code/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" The Code space is for developers. Inspect reads one element in depth and lets you try CSS on it live. Tokens reads a site's design tokens. Snippets keeps the code you want to reuse. Every colour tool also exports code; the formats are collected in one reference. Page What it covers Inspect inspect.md The element snapshot: Overview, Styles, A11y, DOM and Live CSS Tokens tokens.md CSS variables, fonts and type scale from any page, and their exports Snippets snippets.md The on device code vault: saving, searching, copying and exporting Code export formats code export.md Every format each tool can copy or download, with examples "},{"t":"Code export formats","d":"Every format the extension can copy or download, which tool produces it, and what the output looks like.","p":"Browser extension › Code","u":"browser-extension/docs/code/code-export.html","h":["One colour","A palette","A scale","A gradient","A page's tokens","An element","Checks and audits","Saved data","Related pages"],"x":" This page collects every format the extension exports, so you can find the tool that gives you the code you need. Unless a row says \"downloaded\", the output is copied to the clipboard. From the Picker's Code pane. Values below are for Auric gold, d3af37 . Format Output CSS brand: d3af37; CSS · wide gamut brand: oklch … ; Tailwind v4 @theme { color brand: oklch … ; } SwiftUI Color red: 0.827, green: 0.686, blue: 0.216 Jetpack Compose Color 0xFFD3AF37 Android XML <color name=\"brand\" FFD3AF37</color Transparent colours carry their opacity: SwiftUI adds opacity: , and Compose and Android put the alpha first. The Picker's value field copies the colour as a CSS value in any of its twelve formats. History and Library chips copy in the format set in Settings › Tools › Copy colours as : HEX, RGB, HSL or OKLCH. From Page palette and anything sent to it: Image, Harmony . Format Output HEX One RRGGBB per line CSS :root { color 1: …; color 2: …; } oklch The same :root block with oklch values JSON \" …\", \" …\" ASE An Adobe Swatch Exchange file, downloaded Tailwind module.exports = { theme: { extend: { colors: { \"color 1\": \" …\" } } } }; @theme @theme { color 1: …; } SCSS $color 1: …; Tokens W3C de"},{"t":"Inspect","d":"Select an element on the page and read its full snapshot in the popup — box model, styles, matched rules, accessibility, DOM, locators — and try CSS on it live.","p":"Browser extension › Code","u":"browser-extension/docs/code/inspect.html","h":["Select an element","The header","The five views","Findings from inspection","Related pages"],"x":" Code › Inspect Inspect Element is the in depth view of one element. You select the element on the page with the element inspector ../surfaces/inspector.md , and the extension shows its full snapshot, including every computed style and the rules that set them, and a Live CSS editor that changes the element on the page reversibly. 1. Open Code › Inspect . The panel explains: \"Pick an element on the page to read its rules, box model and accessibility, then try CSS on it live.\" 2. Choose Select element . The status reads \"Selection mode active · click an element on the page\". 3. Hover the page and click the element you want. 4. In the side panel or the separate window, the snapshot appears as soon as you click. In the popup, clicking the page closes the popup; open it again and Code › Inspect shows the element. The side panel is the most comfortable place to inspect, because it stays open while you click around the page. Until you select one, the panel says No element selected and lists the inspector's keys: P pin, C copy CSS, S selector and J JSON. Stop ends inspecting and undoes any Live CSS previews. Swatches for the text colour and background colour. The element's name and its siz"},{"t":"Snippets","d":"Keep reusable code in the extension's on-device vault — save from tools or paste your own, search, filter by site, copy and export.","p":"Browser extension › Code","u":"browser-extension/docs/code/snippets.html","h":["Save a snippet","Find a snippet","Use snippets","Limits","Related pages"],"x":" Snippets is a vault for code you want to keep: CSS, gradients, scales, tokens and your own notes. It is stored on this device only, in the browser's extension storage. From a tool: Tool Button Saves Gradient Save snippet The gradient declaration Scale Save The scale's CSS Tokens Save snippet The CSS variables Inspect › Live CSS Save snippet The CSS in the editor Or your own: 1. Open Code › Snippets and choose + New . 2. Paste or type the code when asked. 3. Give it a title, or leave it blank for \"Note\". Each snippet records its type, a title, the page and site it was saved from, and when. Search snippets… matches titles, types, code and site names. This site shows only snippets saved from the site in the current tab. Each card shows its type CSS, Gradient, Shades, Tokens, Palette, Contrast or Note , its title, how long ago it was saved and the site. Long code is shown shortened. Button What it does Copy on a card Copies that snippet's code Delete on a card Deletes that snippet at once Copy all Copies every snippet, each headed by a comment with its title, type and site Export file Downloads every snippet as a .txt file auric snippets and the date Clear all Deletes every snippet, a"},{"t":"Tokens","d":"Read a web page's design tokens — CSS custom properties, font families and type scale — and export them as CSS, W3C tokens, a Tailwind @theme block or JSON.","p":"Browser extension › Code","u":"browser-extension/docs/code/tokens.html","h":["Read the tokens","What it finds","Copy one token","Export","Related pages"],"x":" Tokens Design Tokens reads the design decisions a site has written down as CSS: its custom properties CSS variables , the font families it uses and its type scale. Use it to learn a design system, to start a theme from an existing site, or to check that a site uses its tokens consistently. 1. Open the page, then Code › Tokens . 2. Choose Read the tokens . A summary line appears, such as \"86 CSS variables · 3 font families · 9 sizes\". If the page defines no variables, a message says \"No CSS variables found on this page\". Some pages cannot be read, such as browser pages; the tool then says \"Could not scan this page\". After a scan, the button is labelled Scan design tokens ; choose it to read the page again. Section What it lists Limit CSS variables Every custom property the page's readable stylesheets define, with its value. Colour values get a swatch. 240 Fonts The font families used by elements with text, most used first, each shown in its own font with a use count 8 Type scale The font sizes used by elements with text, smallest first 16 Fonts and sizes are counted across up to 4 000 elements. Stylesheets from another site that the browser does not let the page read are skipped. O"},{"t":"Colour tools","d":"The tools in the Colour space — Picker, Page palette, Image, Gradient, Mix, and the Harmony, Scale and Convert tools behind the Picker.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" The Colour space holds everything for picking, reading and building colours. Its chips are Picker, Page palette, Image, Gradient and Mix. Three deeper tools, Harmony, Scale and Convert, open from links inside the Picker and from search , and each has a Picker back button. Most tools show a Recent strip of your latest colours; choose a swatch to load it into that tool. Page What it covers Picker picker.md Sample from the screen, read twelve formats, and use Specs, Harmony, Scale, Contrast, Vision and Code Page palette page palette.md Read every colour a page uses, view and sort it, and export it Image image.md Build a palette from an image or a capture of the visible tab Gradient gradient.md Build linear, radial and conic CSS gradients Mix mix.md Mix two colours in five colour spaces, or blend them Harmony harmony.md Nine harmony schemes on a colour wheel you can drag Scale scale.md Tailwind and Material scales, tints, shades and tones, with exports Convert convert.md Ten formats at once, each editable "},{"t":"Convert","d":"Type a colour in any of ten formats and read it in all the others at once, with random, invert and complement helpers.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/convert.html","h":["Fields","Helpers","Related pages"],"x":" Convert the Colour converter, \"every format at once\" shows one colour in ten formats. Type into any field and the others follow. Open it from the Picker's Specs pane Open the converter → or search for \"Convert\". Field Example input HEX d3af37 RGB rgb 211,175,55 HSL hsl 43,65%,52% HSV hsv 43,74%,83% CMYK cmyk 0,17,74,17 LAB lab 72 5 60 LCH lch 72 60 85 OKLCH oklch 76% 0.13 85 HWB hwb 43 22% 17% Name goldenrod Commas or spaces both work as separators. A swatch shows the current colour. Button What it does Random A random colour Invert The colour's inverse Complement The colour opposite on the hue wheel Picker at the top returns to the Picker. Note: CMYK here is a simple conversion from RGB, not a colour managed print profile. Use it as a starting point for print, not a proof. Picker picker.md , which reads twelve formats including OKLAB, XYZ and Display P3 Glossary ../../others/glossary.md "},{"t":"Gradient","d":"Build a linear, radial or conic CSS gradient from two or more stops, choose the interpolation space, and copy or save the CSS.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/gradient.html","h":["Build a gradient","Interpolation spaces","The CSS","Buttons","Related pages"],"x":" Gradient builds a CSS background gradient and writes the declaration for you. 1. Open Colour › Gradient . It starts with two stops: gold at 0% and near black at 100%. 2. For each stop, set its colour and its position with the slider or the number field 0 to 100% . 3. Choose + Stop to add a stop between the last two. Choose a stop's ✕ button to remove it; a gradient keeps at least two stops. 4. Choose the type: Linear , Radial or Conic . 5. Set the angle in degrees 0 to 360 . It sets the direction of a linear gradient and the starting angle of a conic one. 6. Choose the interpolation space: sRGB , OKLCH or HSL . The preview and a colour track update as you change anything, and the CSS appears below them. sRGB uses your stops as they are; the browser blends between them. Blends between very different hues can look grey in the middle. OKLCH and HSL write out 13 evenly spaced stops calculated in that space, so the middle of the gradient stays vivid. Note: The OKLCH option currently mixes in OKLab, the rectangular form of the same colour space. Results are close to OKLCH but hue paths between distant hues can differ. The output is a background: declaration, for example: css background:"},{"t":"Harmony","d":"Build a colour harmony from a base colour in nine schemes on a wheel you can drag, then copy, send or save it.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/harmony.html","h":["Use it","Schemes","Buttons","Related pages"],"x":" Harmony the Harmony builder finds colours that go with a base colour, using the standard colour wheel schemes. Open it from the Picker's Harmony pane Open the full harmony builder → or search for \"Harmony\". 1. Set the base colour with its swatch or type a HEX value. 2. Choose a scheme Triadic is the default . 3. Drag on the wheel to change the base colour's hue and saturation; its lightness stays the same. The wheel marks each colour in the harmony and draws lines between them. A strip below shows the colours. Scheme What it gives Complementary The base and the colour opposite it Split complement The base and the two neighbours of its opposite Analogous The base and its neighbours on the wheel Triadic Three colours evenly spaced around the wheel Tetradic Four colours forming a rectangle on the wheel Square Four colours evenly spaced Monochromatic Variations of the base hue Double split Split complements on both sides Compound A mix of analogous and complementary colours Button What it does Copy Copies the colours as a comma separated HEX list Send Loads the colours into Page palette, where every export is available Save Saves them to Saved › Library as a palette labelled with the "},{"t":"Image","d":"Build a palette from an image you drop, paste or choose, or from a capture of the visible tab, entirely on your device.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/image.html","h":["Get a palette from an image","Look at one colour","Use the palette","Related pages"],"x":" Image builds a palette from a picture. The image is read on your device and never uploaded. 1. Open Colour › Image . 2. Choose how many colours to read: 6 colours , 8 colours the default , 12 colours or 16 colours . 3. Give it an image, in any of these ways: drop an image file on the drop area; paste an image from the clipboard; click the drop area or focus it and press Enter to browse for a file; choose Capture the visible tab to use a screenshot of what the current tab shows. The drop area accepts PNG, JPG, WebP and GIF. A file that is not an image is refused with \"Not an image file\". Some tabs cannot be captured, such as browser pages; the tool then says \"Can't capture this tab\". The image appears with a line such as \"8 colors from your image\", and the colours below it. To keep extraction fast, the image is scaled down before its colours are counted, and similar colours are merged. Choose a colour to open its detail card, with its name, values and the buttons Pick , Contrast , Shades and Harmony , as in Page palette page palette.md . Button What it does Open in Page palette Loads the colours into Page palette, where every export is available Copy HEX Copies the colours as a HEX"},{"t":"Mix","d":"Mix two colours at any percentage in sRGB, linear RGB, LAB, OKLAB or HSL, or blend them with a blend mode, and copy the result.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/mix.html","h":["Use it","Choosing a space","Related pages"],"x":" Mix combines two colours, either by mixing them in a colour space or by blending one over the other. 1. Open Colour › Mix . 2. Set colour A and colour B with their swatches or by typing a HEX value. They start as gold and blue. 3. Drag the Mix slider 0 to 100%, 50% by default to set how much of B goes into the result. 4. Choose the colour space to mix in: sRGB , Linear RGB , LAB the default , OKLAB or HSL . 5. Choose a blend mode: Normal plain mixing, the default , Multiply , Screen , Overlay , Darken or Lighten . An 11 step strip shows the path from A to B, and the result swatch shows the current mix. 6. Choose the result swatch to copy the mixed colour. Space Good for sRGB Matching how most software and older CSS mix colours Linear RGB Physically based light mixing; midpoints look brighter LAB Perceptual mixing with even lightness steps OKLAB Perceptual mixing that keeps hues cleaner than LAB HSL Travelling around the hue wheel between two hues Gradient gradient.md Glossary ../../others/glossary.md "},{"t":"Page palette","d":"Read every colour a web page uses, switch between views and sorting modes, inspect a colour, and copy or export the palette.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/page-palette.html","h":["Read a page's colours","What it reads","View and sort","Look at one colour","Copy and export","Related pages"],"x":" Page palette reads the colours a web page actually uses, from its computed styles and its CSS variables, and turns them into a palette you can copy, export or save. It is also the way to sample page colours in Firefox, which has no screen eyedropper. 1. Open the page, then open Colour › Page palette . Home › Palette , or Alt + Shift + E , opens it and starts reading straight away. 2. Choose Read the page's colours . A line above the palette summarises the scan, for example \"18 distinct · 42 unique · 1830 elements · 6 CSS vars\": how many distinct colours remain after merging near duplicates, how many unique values were found, how many elements were read, and how many colours came from CSS variables. Up to 6 000 elements on the page. Twelve colour properties of each: text colour, background colour, the four border colours, outline colour, SVG fill and stroke, box shadow, caret colour and text decoration colour. CSS custom properties variables in the page's stylesheets whose value is a hex or rgb colour. These count three times, so brand and theme colours rise to the top. Nearly invisible colours under 5% opacity are skipped, and near duplicate colours are merged. Up to 48 colours ar"},{"t":"Picker","d":"Sample a colour from the screen or set one by hand, read it in twelve formats, and use the Picker's Specs, Harmony, Scale, Contrast, Vision and Code panes.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/picker.html","h":["The colour core","Actions","The detail panes","Tips","Related pages"],"x":" The Picker is the same colour picker auricartisan.com uses, with extra panes for accessibility and code. Open it from Colour › Picker , from Home › Pick a colour , from the colour of the day, or by choosing any colour swatch in Recent, History, Page palette, Image, Scale or Harmony. Spectrum Saturation and brightness : Drag to set saturation and brightness Hue slider: Drag to set the hue Opacity slider: Sets transparency. The opacity is carried into every value you copy. Value field and Colour format menu: Shows the colour in one of twelve formats. Every field is editable. The format menu searches as you type type \"ok\" for OKLAB and OKLCH . Copy button Copy the CSS value : Copies the ready to paste CSS value in the current format The twelve formats are HEX , RGB , HSL , HSV , HWB , CMYK , LAB , LCH , OKLAB , OKLCH , XYZ and P3 Display P3 . The Picker starts in the format chosen in Settings › Tools › Copy colours as HEX, RGB, HSL or OKLCH . Pick from page : Starts the screen eyedropper. Click any pixel on the screen; press Esc to cancel. The colour loads into the Picker and joins your history. Save to library the bookmark : Adds the colour to Saved › Library, or says it is already "},{"t":"Scale","d":"Generate Tailwind and Material colour scales, tints, shades and tones from one colour, inspect each step, and export the scale.","p":"Browser extension › Colour","u":"browser-extension/docs/colour/scale.html","h":["Build a scale","Look at one step","Export","Related pages"],"x":" Scale the Scale generator turns one colour into a full set of steps you can use as a design system's colour scale. Open it from the Picker's Scale pane Open the scale generator → or search for \"Scale\". 1. Set the base colour with its swatch or type a HEX value. 2. Choose the scale type: Type Steps Built in Tailwind 50–950 the default 11 steps, labelled 50 to 950 OKLCH, fitted to the sRGB gamut Material 50–900 10 steps, labelled 50 to 900 OKLCH, fitted to the sRGB gamut Tints 11 steps toward white HSL Shades 11 steps toward black HSL Tones 11 steps of saturation at the same lightness HSL A chip beside the name shows OKLCH · perceptual or HSL . The Tailwind and Material scales use even steps of perceived lightness with the hue held constant, so neighbouring steps look evenly spaced. 3. Type a Scale name up to 32 characters; brand by default . Every export uses it. Each step shows its label in black or white, whichever is more readable on it. The step nearest your base colour is marked, and its tooltip says \"your color\". Choose a step for its detail card: HEX, RGB, HSL and oklch values with copy buttons, and: Make base : rebuild the scale around this step; Pick , Contrast and Harmony"},{"t":"Install the extension","d":"Which browsers the extension supports and how to install it on each one, from a store or from a ZIP package.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/README.html","h":["Supported browsers","What the browser asks when you install","Files in this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan extension is one product with two store listings: the Chrome Web Store, which serves every Chromium based browser, and Firefox Add ons. Installing from a store is one click, survives restarts and updates itself. The product page, https://auricartisan.com/extension, also offers the packages as ZIP files, for anyone who prefers to load the extension from a folder they can read first. Browser Support Install from Google Chrome Full, with the side panel Chrome Web Store chrome and chromium.md Brave, Vivaldi Full, with the side panel Chrome Web Store chrome and chromium.md Arc Installs from the Chrome listing Chrome Web Store chrome and chromium.md Microsoft Edge Full, with the side panel Chrome Web Store or the Edge ZIP edge.md Opera Full, with the side panel Chrome Web Store or the Opera ZIP opera.md Firefox 115 and later Full, with the sidebar. The screen eyedropper is not available. Firefox Add ons firefox.md Safari on macOS Not published. You can convert the Chromium package yourself. There is no side panel. Convert with Xcode safari.md The extension is built on Manifest V3, the current extension format in Chromium browsers and Firefox. The Chrome, Edge and Opera"},{"t":"Install on Chrome and Chromium browsers","d":"Install Auric Artisan from the Chrome Web Store in Chrome, Brave, Vivaldi or Arc, pin it and open it.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/chrome-and-chromium.html","h":["Install from the Chrome Web Store","Open the side panel","Keyboard shortcuts","Allow the extension on local files","If something goes wrong"],"x":" Chrome, Brave, Vivaldi and Arc all install Auric Artisan from the same Chrome Web Store listing. None of them needs a separate store, and updates arrive automatically. 1. Open the listing: https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/auric artisan/bpmkaljljnlmbjfbmkbbbgiinlbpcocp 2. Choose Add to Chrome . Other Chromium browsers show the same button, sometimes with their own name. 3. Read the permission prompt and confirm. It says the extension can read and change your data on all websites; see Permissions ../permissions.md for what that means in practice. 4. The browser adds the extension and opens auricartisan.com once in a new tab. 5. Open the browser's extensions menu the puzzle piece icon in Chrome and pin Auric Artisan to the toolbar. 6. Open any normal web page and click the icon, or press Alt + Shift + A . You should see the popup with Home selected and the first run tour on top. Chromium browsers can dock the workspace beside the page, where it stays open while you browse. 1. Open the popup. 2. Choose Open the side panel in the header. The popup closes and the workspace opens in the browser's side panel. You can also open it from the browser's own side panel menu, where Auric"},{"t":"Install on Microsoft Edge","d":"Install Auric Artisan in Microsoft Edge from the Chrome Web Store listing, or load the Edge package from a ZIP.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/edge.html","h":["Install from the Chrome Web Store","Install from the Edge ZIP instead","Side panel and shortcuts","Related pages"],"x":" Edge is a Chromium browser, so it installs the Chrome Web Store listing directly and gets every feature, including the side panel. The product page also offers an Edge named ZIP, which is an identical copy of the Chromium package. 1. In Edge, open https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/auric artisan/bpmkaljljnlmbjfbmkbbbgiinlbpcocp 2. If Edge asks whether to allow extensions from other stores, allow it. Edge asks this once, the first time you install from the Chrome Web Store. 3. Choose the store's add button, then confirm the permission prompt. 4. Open the extensions menu on Edge's toolbar and show Auric Artisan on the toolbar. 5. Open a normal web page and click the icon, or press Alt + Shift + A . You should see the popup with Home selected and the first run tour on top. 1. Download the Edge package from https://auricartisan.com/extension. Its name starts with auric suite edge . 2. Unzip it into a folder you will keep. Edge loads the extension from that folder every time it starts. 3. Open edge://extensions . 4. Turn on Developer mode . 5. Choose Load unpacked and select the unzipped folder, the one with manifest.json at its top level. A copy loaded this way does not update i"},{"t":"Install on Firefox","d":"Install Auric Artisan from Firefox Add-ons, open the sidebar, and understand what differs in Firefox.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/firefox.html","h":["Install from Firefox Add-ons","Open the sidebar","What differs in Firefox","Keyboard shortcuts","Temporary install from a ZIP"],"x":" Firefox has its own package of Auric Artisan, published on Firefox Add ons AMO . It needs Firefox 115 or later. Because Mozilla signs it, it installs permanently like any other add on and updates itself. 1. Open https://addons.mozilla.org/en US/firefox/addon/auric artisan/ 2. Choose Add to Firefox . 3. Read the permission prompt and choose Add . 4. Firefox confirms the add on is installed and opens auricartisan.com once in a new tab. 5. Pin the extension to the toolbar from Firefox's extensions menu if it is not already shown. 6. Open a normal web page and click the icon, or press Alt + Shift + A . In Firefox the docked workspace is a sidebar, titled Auric Artisan workspace . Choose Open the side panel in the popup's header, or open it from Firefox's own sidebar menu, where Auric Artisan appears with the other sidebars. See Side panel ../surfaces/side panel.md . Screen eyedropper Pick from page , Pick a colour : Not available: Firefox does not offer the eyedropper interface extensions use. The Picker shows a hint instead. Use Page palette , which reads every colour the page uses. Side panel : A sidebar instead, with the same workspace Pick colour in the right click menu : Shows a "},{"t":"Load from a ZIP","d":"Load an unpacked copy of Auric Artisan from the ZIP packages on the product page, in a Chromium browser or in Firefox.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/load-from-a-zip.html","h":["The packages","Chromium browsers","Firefox","After loading"],"x":" The store listings are the easiest way to install and keep the extension current. The product page, https://auricartisan.com/extension, also offers the same packages as ZIP files. An unpacked extension is a folder of plain files you can read before you trust it. Browsers do not let a website open their internal extension pages, so you copy those addresses into the address bar yourself. Package File name starts with Use it in Chromium auric suite chrome Chrome, Brave, Vivaldi, Arc and any Chromium browser Edge auric suite edge Edge identical to the Chromium package Opera auric suite opera Opera identical to the Chromium package Firefox auric suite firefox Firefox 115 and later The Chrome, Edge and Opera files are byte for byte the same package, named for their stores. Take any one of them for any Chromium browser. The Firefox package is a different build. 1. Download and unzip. Unzip the package into a folder you will keep. The browser loads the extension from that folder every time it starts, so do not leave it in a Downloads folder you clear out. 2. Open the extensions page. Paste chrome://extensions into the address bar in Edge, edge://extensions ; in Opera, opera://extensions ."},{"t":"Install on Opera","d":"Install Auric Artisan in Opera from the Chrome Web Store listing, or load the Opera package from a ZIP.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/opera.html","h":["Install from the Chrome Web Store","Install from the Opera ZIP instead","Side panel and shortcuts","Related pages"],"x":" Opera is a Chromium browser. It can install Auric Artisan from the Chrome Web Store listing, and the product page also offers an Opera named ZIP that is an identical copy of the Chromium package. 1. In Opera, open https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/auric artisan/bpmkaljljnlmbjfbmkbbbgiinlbpcocp 2. If Opera asks you to add its helper for Chrome Web Store extensions, follow its prompt, then return to the listing. 3. Choose the store's add button and confirm the permission prompt. 4. Pin Auric Artisan from Opera's extensions menu. 5. Open a normal web page and click the icon, or press Alt + Shift + A . 1. Download the Opera package from https://auricartisan.com/extension. Its name starts with auric suite opera . 2. Unzip it into a folder you will keep. 3. Open opera://extensions . 4. Turn on Developer mode . 5. Choose Load unpacked and select the unzipped folder, the one with manifest.json at its top level. A copy loaded this way does not update itself. See Update and remove update and remove.md . Open the side panel in the popup's header docks the workspace in Opera's side panel. The default shortcuts are the same as in Chrome: Alt + Shift + A , C , E and V . Change them in Op"},{"t":"Safari","d":"Auric Artisan is not published for Safari; how to convert the Chromium package yourself on macOS, and what to expect.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/safari.html","h":["What you need","Convert and run it","What to expect"],"x":" Auric Artisan is not published for Safari, and there is no Safari listing. Safari takes web extensions through an Xcode project rather than a ZIP, so you can build a copy yourself on a Mac from the Chromium package. This route is for people comfortable with Apple's developer tools. A Mac with Xcode installed. The Chromium package from https://auricartisan.com/extension its name starts with auric suite chrome . 1. Unzip the Chromium package. 2. Open Terminal and run Apple's converter against the unzipped folder. Replace the folder name with the one you unzipped: bash xcrun safari web extension converter ./auric suite chrome 1.0.2 3. The converter creates an Xcode project. Open it, then build and run it. 4. In Safari, enable the extension in Safari's extension settings. The product page has a Copy command button that copies the converter command for the package version it offers. There is no side panel. Safari has no equivalent of the Chromium side panel or the Firefox sidebar, so the workspace is available only as the popup. The build is yours. Auric Artisan does not build, test or support a Safari version. Features that rely on Chromium or Firefox interfaces may not work. Updates "},{"t":"Update and remove","d":"How Auric Artisan updates, how to update a copy loaded from a ZIP, how to keep your data across a reinstall, and how to uninstall.","p":"Browser extension › Install","u":"browser-extension/docs/install/update-and-remove.html","h":["Updating","Keep your data across a reinstall","Remove the extension","Turn off parts instead of removing"],"x":" How you installed How it updates Chrome Web Store Chrome, Brave, Vivaldi, Arc, Edge, Opera Automatically. The store reviews each version before it ships. Firefox Add ons Automatically, signed by Mozilla ZIP, loaded unpacked in a Chromium browser Manually: see below ZIP, temporary add on in Firefox Load the newer package after each restart Safari conversion Convert and build the newer package 1. Download the newer package from https://auricartisan.com/extension. 2. Replace the contents of the folder you loaded with the newly unzipped files. Keep the same folder location. 3. Open the browser's extensions page chrome://extensions , edge://extensions or opera://extensions . 4. Choose the reload button on the Auric Artisan card. 5. Reload any tabs that were open before the update, so the page tools use the new version. To check your version, look at the Auric Artisan card on the extensions page. Your settings, colour history, library and snippets live in the browser's extension storage. Removing the extension deletes them. Before you remove it, or before moving to another browser or computer: 1. Open Settings › Data . 2. Choose Download a backup . A file named auric artisan backup foll"},{"t":"On websites","d":"The optional features that work on websites themselves — Auric pickers for form controls, the compact colour picker, the custom right-click menu — and the entries in the browser's own menu.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" Two optional features change how websites behave, and both are off until you turn them on: Auric pickers on websites give a page's colour, select, date, time, number, range, file and other form controls Auric versions. The site still receives every value exactly as before. The custom right click menu replaces the browser's menu with one built around what you clicked, while stepping aside for sites that have their own. A third, smaller feature is on by default: a few Auric Artisan entries in the browser's own right click menu. Neither optional feature runs on auricartisan.com, which has its own pickers and menu. Page What it covers Website pickers website pickers.md Turning the pickers on, each control type, search in long lists, theme, and where pickers stay native Colour picker on pages colour picker on pages.md The compact 296 px colour picker that replaces a page's colour inputs Right click menu right click menu.md Scenes, the header, the quick bar, filtering, submenus, pinning, the gear, keys, and stepping aside Browser menu items browser menu items.md The Auric Artisan entries in the browser's own right click menu For site owners for site owners.md How a site can keep its con"},{"t":"Browser menu items","d":"The Auric Artisan entries added to the browser's own right-click menu and toolbar-icon menu, what each does, and how to turn them off.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/browser-menu-items.html","h":["The entries","Turn them off","Related pages"],"x":" Separately from the optional custom menu, the extension adds a few entries to the browser's own right click menu, on pages and on the extension's toolbar icon. They are on by default. Entry What it does Inspect element Starts the element inspector on the page Extract page palette Opens the extension at Page palette and reads the page's colours Audit contrast on page Outlines the page's contrast problems, then opens the extension at Audit and runs it Simulate · Protanopia Filters the page for protanopia Simulate · Deuteranopia Filters the page for deuteranopia Simulate · Tritanopia Filters the page for tritanopia Simulate · Achromatopsia Filters the page for achromatopsia Clear vision filter Removes the vision filter The entries are translated when the interface is set to Hindi. If the extension's popup cannot open by itself, open it within 30 seconds and it goes straight to the tool you chose. After 30 seconds the request is dropped, so an old action never runs later on another page. Turn off Settings › Right click › Items in the browser's menu \"Add Auric Artisan entries to the browser's own right click menu too.\" . The entries disappear at once. Right click menu right click menu."},{"t":"Colour picker on pages","d":"The compact Auric colour picker that replaces a website's colour inputs — its layout, formats, the five panes, opacity and theme.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/colour-picker-on-pages.html","h":["Layout","The five panes","Behaviour","Theme","Related pages"],"x":" With the website pickers on and the Colour type switched on, every colour input on a page opens the Auric colour picker, the same picker auricartisan.com uses, in a compact 296 px popover. The page keeps a small swatch in place of its colour input; everything else lives in an isolated panel that the site's styles cannot affect. From top to bottom: 1. The spectrum and the Hue slider, plus an Opacity slider when the page's input asks for one. 2. The value field, with a Colour format menu. The menu lists the twelve formats HEX, RGB, HSL, HSV, HWB, CMYK, LAB, LCH, OKLAB, OKLCH, XYZ and P3 and searches as you type: type \"ok\" for OKLAB and OKLCH. 3. Five toggles: Shades , Harmony , Contrast , Vision and Page or Recent . At most one pane is open at a time. Shades : An 11 step OKLCH scale from 50 to 950 around the colour Harmony : Partner colours, rotated in HSL or OKLCH Contrast : How readable the colour is as text on white, black or the page's own background, with the closest passing colour when it fails AA Vision : The colour as people with the four main colour vision deficiencies see it Page / Recent : Colours the page uses, or colours you picked recently in the extension The pane you"},{"t":"For site owners","d":"How a website can keep its form controls native and keep the browser's right-click menu for visitors who use the Auric Artisan extension.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/for-site-owners.html","h":["Keep form controls native","Keep the browser's right-click menu","What the extension never does on your site","Related pages"],"x":" Visitors who use Auric Artisan can turn on its website pickers and its right click menu. Both are designed to leave designed sites alone, but you can also opt out explicitly with a few attributes. None of these affect visitors who do not have the extension. Where What to add Works On the control itself data aa picker skip Always On an ancestor of the control data aa picker skip While the visitor keeps Leave designed controls alone on the default On the control or an ancestor data native control , data aa native or data no enhance While Leave designed controls alone is on On a colour input data cp skip Always. Colour inputs follow their own rule; the attributes above do not apply to them. Example: html <select data aa picker skip <option Keep the browser's list</option </select <input type=\"color\" data cp skip Controls you have restyled for example with appearance: none or hidden behind your own widget are already left alone while Leave designed controls alone is on. Hidden, disabled and read only colour inputs are never replaced. For the whole page, add either attribute to the <html element: html <html data aa no ext menu html <html data native context menu or add a meta tag: html"},{"t":"Right-click menu","d":"The extension's optional right-click menu for websites — turning it on, scenes and their actions, the header, quick bar, filter, submenus, pinning, the gear, keys, and stepping aside.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/right-click-menu.html","h":["Turn it on","Anatomy","Scenes","The groups","The quick bar","Filter","The gear","Keys","Actions that need a permission","When the browser's menu appears instead","Messages you may see","Related pages"],"x":" The custom right click menu replaces the browser's menu on websites with one built around what you clicked. It puts that thing's own actions first, spelled out, and folds everything else into a few rows that open submenus, so the menu fits on one screen. It adds actions browsers bury or lack: QR codes, screenshots, read aloud, searching a selection on six engines, copying as Markdown, reopening a closed tab, and the extension's own tools. It is off by default. 1. Open Settings › Right click . 2. Turn on Custom right click menu . 3. The browser asks for three optional permissions: reading the clipboard for Paste , downloads for Save as and sessions for Reopen closed tab . Accept to finish. If you decline, the switch turns itself off again and the message says \"Permission declined — custom menu stays off\". You can grant a single permission later from Settings › Right click › Permissions . Shift + right click always opens the browser's own menu, even with the custom menu on. From top to bottom: 1. The header names what you right clicked, with the detail that matters. 2. The quick bar : one click buttons you choose. 3. The filter field \"Type to filter N actions\" . It has focus when th"},{"t":"Website pickers","d":"Give a website's form controls Auric pickers — colour, select, multi-select, suggestions, dates, times, number, range, file, checkbox and radio — and control where they apply.","p":"Browser extension › On websites","u":"browser-extension/docs/on-websites/website-pickers.html","h":["Turn them on","Controls","Search in long lists","Theme","Where pickers stay native","Related pages"],"x":" With the website pickers on, a page's own form controls open Auric panels instead of the browser's. The page's native control stays in place for form submission, and the site's code receives every value through the same input and change events it always does, so forms built with frameworks keep working. 1. Open Settings › Pickers . 2. Turn on Auric pickers on websites \"Colour, date, select and ten more open Auric panels instead of the browser's own.\" . 3. Reload any page that was already open. Each type has its own chip under Picker types , all on by default. The heading shows how many are on, for example \"13 of 13 on\". Chip Enhances What you get Colour Colour inputs The compact colour picker; see Colour picker on pages colour picker on pages.md Select Drop down lists A dropdown. Lists with more than 7 options open with a search field. Multi select Lists that allow several choices A dropdown with checkboxes, chips for what is chosen, an \"N/M chosen\" count, Select all and Clear Suggestions Text fields with a suggestion list A searchable suggestion list Date Date fields A calendar in your interface language Date & time Date and time fields Calendar and time panels Month Month fields"},{"t":"Saved","d":"The Saved space — your colour library and palettes, your colour history, and links to the full-size tools on auricartisan.com.","p":"Browser extension › Saved","u":"browser-extension/docs/saved/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" The Saved space keeps what you want to come back to. Library holds colours and palettes you saved on purpose, History holds the colours you picked recently, and On the web links to the full size tools on auricartisan.com. Everything is stored in your browser only. Page What it covers Library library.md Saved colours up to 500 and palettes the newest 30 : using, removing and exporting them History history.md Your last 50 colours, copying and reusing them, and turning history off On the web on the web.md The fourteen auricartisan.com tools and libraries the extension links to "},{"t":"History","d":"The extension's colour history — your last 50 colours, how to copy or reopen them, clear them, or turn history off.","p":"Browser extension › Saved","u":"browser-extension/docs/saved/history.html","h":["What goes into history","Use it","Clear it","Turn history off","Related pages"],"x":" History keeps the last 50 colours you picked or chose in the Picker, newest first, so a colour is never lost to a stray click. colours you pick with the screen eyedropper; colours you finish choosing in the Picker; colours you open in the Picker from elsewhere, such as Recent, Page palette or the colour of the day. The same colour is kept once, whatever its letter case. The newest 50 are kept. Open Saved › History \"Your last 50 colours.\" . Click a colour to copy it in the format set in Settings › Tools › Copy colours as . Double click a colour to open it in the Picker. Your most recent colours also appear on Home under Recent , and in the Recent strip of the Picker, Contrast, Harmony, Scale, Gradient and Mix. Clear empties the history at once. It does not ask first. Settings › Data › Clear history & library clears history and the library together, after you confirm. Turn off Settings › Tools › Keep a colour history . New colours are then not recorded. Colours already in history stay until you clear them. Library library.md Picker ../colour/picker.md Tools settings ../settings/tools.md "},{"t":"Library","d":"Save colours and palettes to the extension's library, reuse them, remove them and export them as JSON.","p":"Browser extension › Saved","u":"browser-extension/docs/saved/library.html","h":["Add to the library","Use the library","Export","Limits","Clear it","Related pages"],"x":" The Library keeps the colours and palettes you choose to save. It is stored in your browser's extension storage and is not synced between devices. From Button Adds Picker Save to library the bookmark The current colour. If it is already there, the extension says so. Page palette Save The whole palette Image Save palette The image's colours Harmony Save The harmony, labelled with its scheme The toolbar icon's badge shows how many colours are in the library. Open Saved › Library . It has two sections. Click a colour to copy it in the format set in Settings › Tools › Copy colours as . Right click a colour, or focus it and press Delete or Backspace , to remove it. \"Nothing saved yet.\" appears while the section is empty. Click a palette to open it in Page palette, where every export is available. Choose its ✕ to delete it. \"No saved palettes.\" appears while the section is empty. Export copies the whole library as JSON, with a colors list and a palettes list: json { \"colors\": \" d3af37\" , \"palettes\": { \"id\": 1790000000000, \"colors\": \" d3af37\", \" 1a73e8\" , \"label\": \"triadic\" } } To keep the library with your settings, history and snippets in one file, use Settings › Data › Download a back"},{"t":"On the web","d":"The links from the extension to the full-size tools and libraries on auricartisan.com.","p":"Browser extension › Saved","u":"browser-extension/docs/saved/on-the-web.html","h":["Links","Other links to auricartisan.com","Related pages"],"x":" On the web \"Open on the Web\" lists the full size tools on auricartisan.com, each opening in a new tab. Open it by searching for \"web\" or \"On the web\"; it belongs to the Saved space. Link Opens Analyzer The URL analyzer, https://auricartisan.com/tool/analyzer/ Palettes The palette library Harmony The harmony library Gradients The gradient library Shades The shades library Colour library The colour library Vision lab The vision simulation tool Ishihara plates The Ishihara plate generator Science lab The Color Science Lab Colour atlas The colour atlas generator Personalise The personalisation generator Accessibility The accessibility library Learn The Learn articles Workspace The library workspace The Auric Artisan wordmark in the header opens the home page. Home › On auricartisan.com : Collections, Accessibility Library, Learning Library and Documentation. Search results under On the web : Full Search, Collections, URL Analyzer, Tools, Color Science Lab, Accessibility Library, Documentation, API Reference and Learning Library. Page palette › Open opens the palette on auricartisan.com with its colours in the address. Each link is an ordinary page visit that you start. The extension s"},{"t":"Settings","d":"How to open the extension's Settings view, how it saves, and what each of its six sections holds.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/README.html","h":["Open and close it","Sections","Defaults at a glance"],"x":" Settings is a two pane view inside the popup, side panel or separate window: the section names on the left and the controls on the right. Choose Settings the sliders button in the header, or search for a setting by name and choose it: Settings opens at that section with the control focused. A plain open always starts at Appearance . Move between sections with the arrow keys, Home and End . \"Saved as you change them\": every change is stored the moment you make it, and open tabs pick up changes without a reload. Press Esc or choose Back to the tools to close Settings. Section What it holds Page Appearance Theme, accent colour, popup size, language Appearance appearance.md Pickers The website pickers: master switch, designed controls, 13 types, Never on list Pickers pickers.md Right click The custom menu, stepping aside, browser menu items, quick bar, layout, row height, sites, permissions Right click right click.md Tools Copy format, colour names, APCA, history, sound, deep audit, automatic outlines Tools tools.md Data Storage use, backup and restore, copy and paste settings, clearing and resetting Data data.md Shortcuts The keyboard map, changing shortcuts in the browser, replaying"},{"t":"Appearance settings","d":"Choose the extension's theme, accent colour, popup size and interface language.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/appearance.html","h":["Theme","Accent","Popup size","Language","Related pages"],"x":" Settings › Appearance controls how the extension looks, in the popup and side panel and in everything it draws on websites. System : Follows your operating system's light or dark mode, and changes when it does. On websites, the pickers and panels match the page they are on. Light : Always light Dark the default : Always dark The Switch between light and dark button in the header flips between Light and Dark. The accent colour tints buttons, focus rings, the website pickers, the right click menu and the inspector, and sets the starting colour of several tools. Text on the accent turns black or white, whichever reads better. Twelve presets: Preset Colour Auric gold the default d3af37 Champagne d6b56d Bronze b99355 Copper c57a32 Rose bd707b Pink e45183 Ruby a3002d Jade 48ae8b Sapphire 3768b3 Amethyst 9666ce Platinum b8bdc6 Graphite 9aa0ac For any other colour, use Custom : pick with the swatch, which previews while you drag and saves when you let go, or type a six digit hex value. The heading shows the preset's name, or \"Custom\" and the hex value. Choice Size Compact 460 × 520 Standard the default 560 × 600 Large 760 × 600 At Compact, the header hides its tagline and the Open in its "},{"t":"Data settings","d":"See how much the extension stores, back up and restore everything, move settings through the clipboard, and clear or reset data.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/data.html","h":["Stored in this browser","Backup","Settings only","Start over","Related pages"],"x":" Settings › Data shows what the extension keeps in your browser and lets you back it up, move it or clear it. Everything stays on your device. A storage meter: \"N used of M P% \". The bar turns to a warning colour at 80% of the browser's allowance for extension storage. Counts of History , Colors , Palettes and Snippets . Refresh storage usage the circular arrow recounts. \"Settings, history, library and snippets in one file. Nothing leaves your device.\" Button What it does Download a backup Saves auric artisan backup YYYY MM DD.json Restore from a file Opens a file chooser for a backup .json , then restores it json { \"app\": \"Auric Artisan\", \"kind\": \"aa backup\", \"schema\": 1, \"exportedAt\": \"2026 09 23T10:00:00.000Z\", \"settings\": { \"themeMode\": \"dark\", \"accentColor\": \" d3af37\" }, \"history\": \" D3AF37\", \" 1A73E8\" , \"libColors\": \" D3AF37\" , \"libPalettes\": { \"id\": 1790000000000, \"colors\": \" D3AF37\", \" 1A73E8\" , \"label\": \"triadic\" } , \"snippets\": { \"type\": \"css\", \"title\": \"…\", \"code\": \"…\", \"url\": \"…\", \"host\": \"…\" } } Snippets carry the address of the page they were saved from, so a backup contains those addresses. Keep it private if that matters. Everything in the file replaces what is stor"},{"t":"Pickers settings","d":"Turn the website pickers on or off, choose which control types they enhance, respect designed controls, and list sites where they never run.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/pickers.html","h":["Switches","Picker types","Never on","Related pages"],"x":" Settings › Pickers controls the Auric pickers that replace a website's form controls. What the pickers do is described in Website pickers ../on websites/website pickers.md . Switch Default What it does Auric pickers on websites Off The master switch: Auric panels replace the browser's own. Nothing below applies while it is off. Leave designed controls alone On Controls the site restyled, or replaced with its own widget, keep their own look Thirteen chips, all on by default. The heading counts them \"13 of 13 on\" . Untick a chip to keep that type native everywhere. Colour , Select , Multi select , Suggestions , Date , Date & time , Month , Week , Time , Number , Range , File , Checkbox & radio one chip for both . \"A file picker still opens the browser's own dialog — only the button is ours.\" Sites where every picker stays native. 1. Type a site into Add a site, e.g. example.com . You can paste a full address; only the site name is kept, without www. . 2. Choose Add . A message confirms \"Pickers stay native on example.com\". 3. Remove a site with its ✕ button. Subdomains are included: adding example.com also covers shop.example.com . The list holds up to 100 sites. auricartisan.com is"},{"t":"Right-click settings","d":"Turn the custom right-click menu on or off, let sites keep their own menus, control the browser menu entries, and set the quick bar, layout, row height, excluded sites and permissions.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/right-click.html","h":["Switches","Quick bar","Menu layout","Row height","Never on","Permissions","The menu's own gear","Related pages"],"x":" Settings › Right click controls both the extension's custom right click menu and its entries in the browser's own menu. How the menu works is in Right click menu ../on websites/right click menu.md . Switch Default What it does Custom right click menu Off Replaces the browser's menu on websites. Asks for three optional permissions; if you decline, it stays off. Step aside for a site's own menu On A page's own right click menu Figma, Google Docs wins. Off: the extension's menu takes every right click. Items in the browser's menu On Adds entries to the browser's own menu; see Browser menu items ../on websites/browser menu items.md The actions pinned across the top of the menu, with a count such as \"5 / 6\". \"One click actions across the top of the menu. Pin more with the star on any row.\" Remove one with its ✕ Unpin . Reset restores the defaults: Back, Forward, Reload, Copy page URL and Copy screenshot. When the bar is empty it reads \"Empty: pin actions with the star\". Choice Effect Focused the default What you clicked, then one row per group Everything Every group opened in one list Standard the default or Compact . Sites where the browser's own menu always stays. Add and remove site"},{"t":"Tools settings","d":"Set how colours are copied and named, whether APCA is shown, history and sound, and how deep the page audit goes.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/tools.html","h":["Related pages"],"x":" Settings › Tools changes how the tools behave. Control Choices Default What it does Copy colours as HEX, RGB, HSL, OKLCH HEX The format used when you click a colour in History or Library, and the Picker's starting format Colour names CSS names, XKCD, Off CSS names The nearest colour name shown in colour details. Off hides names. XKCD currently gives the same names as CSS names. Show APCA beside WCAG On or off On Shows the APCA Lc score, tiers and readable sizes in Contrast Keep a colour history On or off On \"The last 50 colours you picked or copied.\" Off stops recording new colours. Sound on pick On or off Off \"A short tick when the eyedropper lands.\" Also plays on copy. Deep page audit On or off On Contrast scan limits: 3 500 elements and 160 issues on; 1 800 and 80 off. Slower on large pages. Outline issues after an audit On or off Off \"Marks failing elements on the page as soon as the audit finishes.\" Audit ../check/audit.md Contrast ../check/contrast.md History ../saved/history.md "},{"t":"Shortcuts settings","d":"The keyboard map in Settings, how to change the browser-level shortcuts, and how to replay the tour.","p":"Browser extension › Settings","u":"browser-extension/docs/settings/shortcuts.html","h":["The keyboard map","Buttons"],"x":" Settings › Shortcuts lists the keys the extension answers to and links to where you change them. Action Keys Open Auric Artisan Alt + Shift + A Open the contrast checker Alt + Shift + C Read the page palette Alt + Shift + E Toggle vision simulation Alt + Shift + V Search in the popup / or Ctrl + K Inspector: pin · CSS · selector · JSON P , C , S , J Close a picker, panel or menu Esc The first four are browser level shortcuts and work from any page. Inspect an element on the page and Run a full accessibility audit are also available but have no key until you assign one. Change them in the browser : Opens your browser's extension shortcuts page: chrome://extensions/shortcuts in Chromium browsers, about:addons in Firefox then the gear menu › Manage Extension Shortcuts Replay the tour : Closes Settings and starts the five step tour The complete list, including the inspector's and the right click menu's keys, is in Keyboard shortcuts ../../others/shortcuts.md . "},{"t":"Surfaces","d":"The places the extension appears — the popup, Home, search, the side panel, the page itself and the element inspector.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" The extension shows one workspace in several places. The popup opens from the toolbar icon. The side panel the sidebar in Firefox holds the same workspace beside the page and stays open while you browse. A separate window holds it too. On the page itself, the extension draws only what you ask for: the element inspector, vision filters, audit outlines, and, if you turn them on, website pickers and a right click menu. Page What it covers The popup popup.md The header, the spaces bar, the site chip, tool chips, sizes, the separate window and the keys that move around Home home.md Colour of the day, the four on this page actions, Recent, Continue, Pinned and the auricartisan.com links Search search.md Finding tools, settings and auricartisan.com pages by name Side panel side panel.md Docking the workspace beside the page in Chromium browsers and Firefox On the page on the page.md Everything the extension draws on a website, and how to remove it Element inspector inspector.md The hover card, the pinned card, its seven sections and its keys Note: A redesign of these surfaces is built but not yet released: the side panel gains a rail of spaces and a \"This tab\" card, the popup becomes a q"},{"t":"Home","d":"What Home shows — colour of the day, one-click actions for the current page, recent colours, Continue, pinned tools and links to auricartisan.com.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/home.html","h":["Colour of the day","On this page","Recent","Continue","Pinned","On auricartisan.com","Related pages"],"x":" Home is the first screen in the popup, the side panel and the separate window. It starts work on the current page in one click and brings back what you were doing. A card at the top shows one colour, the same for everyone on a given date, with its date, HEX value, OKLCH value and nearest colour name. Choose the swatch or Open in picker to open it in the Picker. Choose the copy button to copy its HEX value. Four actions that do the work, not just open a tool. Each acts on the tab named in the site chip. Action Subtitle What happens Pick a colour Any pixel on screen Opens the Picker and starts the screen eyedropper Inspect Styles, box, contrast Opens Code › Inspect and starts selecting an element on the page Audit Contrast and WCAG Opens Check › Audit and runs the audit Palette Every colour used Opens Colour › Page palette and reads the page's colours In Firefox, Pick a colour opens the Picker, which explains that the screen eyedropper is not available. See Picker ../colour/picker.md . Up to twelve of the colours you picked or copied most recently, newest first. Choose one to open it in the Picker. History opens the full list of 50. Until you pick a colour, this reads \"Colours you p"},{"t":"Element inspector","d":"Inspect any element on a page — the hover card, the pinned card with contrast first, its seven sections, copying, and every key.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/inspector.html","h":["Start it","The hover card","The pinned card","Keys","When it closes","After inspecting","Related pages"],"x":" The element inspector reads any element on a web page and shows what matters to a designer, developer or accessibility tester, with contrast first. It works in two states: a light hover card that follows the pointer, and a pinned card with everything. The same element is then available in depth in Code › Inspect see Inspect ../code/inspect.md . Any of these starts the inspector on the current tab: Home › Inspect ; Code › Inspect › Select element ; the custom right click menu › Inspect element see Right click menu ../on websites/right click menu.md ; Inspect element in the browser's own right click menu; the Inspect an element on the page shortcut, once you assign a key in the browser it has none by default . A bar appears at the bottom of the page. It says Inspecting or Pinned , names the element, lists the main keys and has a Stop button. Move the pointer over the page. A highlight box outlines the element under it, and a small card follows the pointer with: the element's name tag, id and classes and its size in pixels; its display , role and landmark; contrast : a small \"Aa\" sample in the element's own colours, the ratio, and AA and AAA marks a tick or a cross ; a warning when a"},{"t":"On the page","d":"Everything the extension can draw on a website, when it appears, how it is isolated from the site, and how to remove it.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/on-the-page.html","h":["What can appear on a page","The audit outlines","Kept apart from the site","Where nothing appears","Related pages"],"x":" Most of the extension lives in the popup and side panel. A few features appear on the website itself. This page lists each one, when it appears, and how to make it go away. What Appears when Goes away when Element inspector : a highlight box, a card and a bar at the bottom You start Inspect Home, Code › Inspect, the right click menu or a shortcut You press Esc twice if a card is pinned , choose Stop , or go to another page Vision filter : the page recoloured or blurred, with a small status strip You choose a simulation in Check › Vision, the browser's right click menu, or press Alt + Shift + V You choose Clear , Clear vision filter , press Alt + Shift + V again, or reload Side by side comparison : half the page filtered You choose Side by side in Check › Vision, or Side by side in the right click menu You clear the filter Audit outlines : a red or amber outline and a label on each flagged piece of text Outline on page , Outline issues after an audit , or Audit contrast on page in the browser's menu After 15 seconds, or when you run the outlines again Live CSS preview : your CSS applied to one element You choose Apply to page in Code › Inspect › Live CSS You choose Reset or Stop We"},{"t":"The popup","d":"A tour of the popup — header, search, spaces, the site chip, tool chips, sizes, the separate window and keyboard movement.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/popup.html","h":["Header","Spaces bar","Tool chips","Sizes","Moving around with the keyboard","Toasts","The toolbar badge","Related pages"],"x":" The popup is the workspace that opens from the toolbar icon or with Alt + Shift + A . It closes when you click outside it. Everything in it is also available in the side panel side panel.md and in a separate window. Auric Artisan wordmark with the line \"Colour intelligence studio\" : Opens auricartisan.com in a new tab Search field Search tools, colours, settings : Finds any tool, setting or auricartisan.com page. Press / or Ctrl + K to focus it. See Search search.md . Open the side panel : Docks the workspace in the browser's side panel or sidebar, then closes the popup. Hidden when you are already in the side panel. Open in its own window : Opens the workspace in a separate, resizable 620 × 700 window and closes the popup. Hidden at the Compact popup size. Switch between light and dark : Flips the theme. Settings › Appearance adds a third choice, System. Settings : Opens the two pane Settings view. See Settings ../settings/README.md . Below the header: Home , Colour , Check , Code and Saved . Each is a tab; use the arrow keys, Home and End to move between them when one has focus. The site chip names the site the page tools will act on, for example fieldnote.app . It reads No page"},{"t":"Search","d":"Find any tool, setting, action or auricartisan.com page by name from the search field, and how results are ordered.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/search.html","h":["Use it","How results are ordered","What you can find","Related pages"],"x":" The search field in the header finds every tool, many settings, a few actions and pages on auricartisan.com. It is the quickest way to reach a tool whose space you do not remember. 1. Press / or Ctrl + K , or click the field. 2. Type. Every word you type must match; words can match the name, the description or hidden keywords for example \"right click\", \"backup\" or \"colour blind\" . 3. Use Up and Down to move through the results, or hover them. 4. Press Enter , or click a result, to run it. 5. Press Esc to clear the search. A Hindi interface can be searched in Hindi or English. The Language setting can also be found with \"भाषा\". Results are grouped under headings: Group What it holds Best match A result whose title is exactly what you typed, so typing \"Settings\" and pressing Enter opens Settings Tools The extension's tools; each result shows its space on the right Settings Individual settings; choosing one opens Settings at that section and focuses the control Actions Settings and Open in a Window On the web Pages on auricartisan.com, opened in a new tab Within a group, titles that start with your text come first. If nothing matches, the list says so. Colour Picker, Inspect Element,"},{"t":"Side panel","d":"Dock the Auric Artisan workspace beside the page in the Chromium side panel or the Firefox sidebar, and what changes there.","p":"Browser extension › Surfaces","u":"browser-extension/docs/surfaces/side-panel.html","h":["Open it","What is different in the panel","Open in a separate window instead","Close it","Related pages"],"x":" The side panel Chromium browsers or sidebar Firefox holds the same workspace as the popup, docked beside the page. Unlike the popup, it stays open while you click on the page, switch tabs and browse, so it suits longer sessions such as auditing several pages or inspecting a layout. In the popup, choose Open the side panel in the header. The popup closes and the panel opens in the current window. Or use the browser's own side panel or sidebar menu and choose Auric Artisan. In Firefox the sidebar is titled Auric Artisan workspace . Safari has no side panel. If Open the side panel does nothing, open the panel from the browser's own menu instead; some browsers only allow it from their own controls. The panel is the same page as the popup, laid out for a tall, narrow column: It fills the panel. There is no fixed size; widen the panel to give tools more room. The header wraps. The search field takes its own full width row, and the Open the side panel button is hidden. The Picker is one column. The colour field, sliders, value field and actions come first, followed by its sections one below another, including On this page the page's own colours and Recent . In the popup, the Picker is sp"},{"t":"Workflows","d":"End-to-end tasks that combine several of the extension's tools, step by step.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" Each page here walks through a real task from start to finish, using several tools together. They assume the extension is installed and you are on an ordinary web page. Page Task Audit a page and fix contrast audit a page and fix contrast.md Find a page's accessibility and contrast problems, fix the colours, and export a record Check and fix a brand colour check and fix a brand colour.md Test a brand colour as text and background, and find accessible variants that keep its hue Extract a site's design system extract a sites design system.md Read a site's colours, variables, fonts and type scale and export them as tokens Build a colour scale for Tailwind build a colour scale for tailwind.md Turn one colour into a named Tailwind v4 scale and keep it as a snippet Review a page for colour blindness review a page for colour blindness.md Check that a page does not rely on colour alone Inspect and debug an element inspect and debug an element.md Find why an element looks the way it does, try a fix live, and copy it Back up and move your data back up and move your data.md Keep your settings, colours and snippets safe, or move them to another browser "},{"t":"Audit a page and fix contrast","d":"Run the audit on a page, see its contrast problems on the page, fix a failing colour pair, review the other findings and export a record.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/audit-a-page-and-fix-contrast.html","h":["1. Run the audit","2. See where the problems are","3. Fix a failing pair","4. Review the other findings","5. Keep a record","6. Check again"],"x":" This workflow finds a page's accessibility problems, fixes its contrast failures and leaves you with a record to share. You need: the page open in a normal tab. The side panel is the most comfortable place to work, because it stays open while you look at the page. 1. Open the page and wait for it to finish loading. 2. Open the extension and choose Open the side panel . 3. On Home, choose Audit . The audit runs at once. You see four counts: Tested , Failing , Borderline and Review , and a row for each flagged piece of text. 1. Choose Outline on page . 2. Look at the page. Failing text has a red outline, borderline text an amber one, and each has a label such as 3.12:1 needs 4.5:1 . 3. The outlines disappear after 15 seconds; choose Outline on page again to redraw them. 1. In the list, choose the row you want to fix. Contrast opens with that text colour and background. 2. Check the verdict. For body text you need AA 4.5:1 at least. 3. Leave the fix target on AA 4.5:1 , or choose AAA 7:1 or an APCA target. 4. Choose Fix text . The text colour moves to the nearest lightness that passes, keeping its hue and saturation, and a message names the new colour. 5. If you would rather change t"},{"t":"Back up and move your data","d":"Back up your settings, colour history, library and snippets to a file, restore them, and move them to another browser or computer.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/back-up-and-move-your-data.html","h":["Back up","Restore on another browser or computer","Move only your settings","Before you uninstall","Related pages"],"x":" The extension keeps everything in your browser and does not sync it anywhere. To keep your work safe, or to move it to another browser or computer, use a backup file. 1. Open Settings › Data . 2. Check the counts: History , Colors , Palettes and Snippets . 3. Choose Download a backup . A file named auric artisan backup followed by today's date is saved to your downloads. 4. Keep the file somewhere safe. It contains your snippets and the addresses of the pages they came from. 1. Install the extension there; see Install ../install/README.md . 2. Copy the backup file to that computer. 3. Open Settings › Data › Restore from a file and choose the file. 4. The message \"Backup restored\" confirms it. Your theme, accent and other settings apply at once, and History, Library and Snippets fill in. Restoring replaces what is stored now with what is in the file. Back up the new browser first if it already has data you want. 1. On the first browser, choose Settings › Data › Copy settings . 2. Send the copied text to the other browser, for example through a note. 3. On the other browser, choose Paste settings and paste it. This moves your theme, accent, switches and site lists, but not your colo"},{"t":"Build a colour scale for Tailwind","d":"Turn one colour into a named, perceptually even Tailwind v4 scale from 50 to 950, check it, and keep it as a snippet.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/build-a-colour-scale-for-tailwind.html","h":["1. Choose the base colour","2. Open the scale generator","3. Set up the scale","4. Check the steps","5. Export","Related pages"],"x":" This workflow turns one colour into a full scale for a Tailwind v4 theme. Open the Picker and set your colour: pick it from a page, type it, or choose it from History or Library. 1. In the Picker, open the Scale pane to preview an 11 step OKLCH scale. 2. Choose Open the scale generator → . Scale opens with your colour as the base. 1. Keep the type on Tailwind 50–950 . The chip reads OKLCH · perceptual : the steps are even in perceived lightness and the hue stays constant. 2. Type the Scale name you want in your classes, such as brand or accent . 3. Find the marked step: it is the one nearest your base colour. 1. Choose a step to see its values. 2. Choose Contrast in its card and check it against white or your dark background. Typically lighter steps suit backgrounds and darker steps suit text on white; confirm with the checker rather than assuming. 3. If your brand colour should sit on a specific step, choose that step and Make base to rebuild the scale around it. 1. Choose @theme to copy a Tailwind v4 @theme block, or Tailwind for a Tailwind colour object. 2. Paste it into your CSS or config. 3. Choose Tokens instead if you keep colours as W3C design tokens. 4. Choose Save to kee"},{"t":"Check and fix a brand colour","d":"Test a brand colour as text and as a background in WCAG and APCA, see it through colour-vision simulations, and find accessible variants that keep its hue.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/check-and-fix-a-brand-colour.html","h":["1. Get the colour","2. Read its specs","3. Test it as text","4. Test it as a background","5. Check colour vision","6. Build accessible variants","Related pages"],"x":" Brand colours are often too light for text on white, or too dark for white text on top. This workflow tells you where a brand colour works and gives you accessible variants that still look like the brand. Do one of these: On the brand's site, choose Pick a colour on Home and click the colour Chromium browsers . Choose Colour › Page palette , Read the page's colours , and choose the colour. Type its value into the Picker's value field. 1. In the Picker, open the Specs pane. Note its contrast on white and on black and its WCAG levels. 2. Open the Contrast pane. Switch between White , Black and Page backgrounds. If it fails AA, the closest passing colour is offered. 1. Choose Check as text . Contrast opens with the brand colour as text. 2. Set Background to the background you use, for example ffffff . 3. Read the verdict and the APCA readable sizes. A colour may pass for large headings AA Large but not for body text. 4. Choose Fix text with the target you need. Note the new colour. 1. Go back to the Picker and choose Check as background . 2. Set Text to the text colour you plan to use on it, often white or near black. 3. Read the verdict. Choose Swap to test the reverse. 4. Choose Fi"},{"t":"Extract a site's design system","d":"Read a website's colours, CSS variables, fonts and type scale, and export them as W3C design tokens, Tailwind or CSS.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/extract-a-sites-design-system.html","h":["1. Read its tokens","2. Export the tokens","3. Read the colours actually used","4. Export the palette","5. Check a few components","Related pages"],"x":" Use this workflow to study how a site is built, to start a theme from an existing product, or to audit whether a site uses its tokens consistently. Respect the site's rights: reading its CSS for study is one thing, copying its brand is another. 1. Open the site and go to a representative page. 2. Open Code › Tokens and choose Read the tokens . 3. Read the summary: how many CSS variables, font families and sizes it found. 4. Scan CSS variables . Colour variables have swatches. Click one to copy var name , or Shift click to copy its value. 5. Look at Fonts most used first and Type scale smallest first . Choose the format your project uses: W3C tokens for design token tools. Colours, dimensions and other values are grouped. Tailwind @theme for a Tailwind v4 project. CSS vars for a plain :root block. JSON for everything, including fonts and sizes. Each copies to the clipboard. Choose Save snippet to keep the CSS variables in Snippets. Variables show what a site declares; computed colours show what it uses. 1. Open Colour › Page palette and choose Read the page's colours . 2. Switch the mode to Dominant k means to see eight representative colours, or Sort by hue to see families. 3. Com"},{"t":"Inspect and debug an element","d":"Find why an element looks the way it does, check its accessibility, try a CSS fix live on the page, and copy the result.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/inspect-and-debug-an-element.html","h":["1. Find the element","2. Read what applies","3. Try a fix live","4. Keep the fix","Related pages"],"x":" This workflow is for the question \"why does this look like that, and what would fix it?\", without opening the browser's developer tools. 1. Open the extension's side panel and go to Code › Inspect . 2. Choose Select element . 3. Hover the page. The hover card shows the element's name, size, contrast, font and colours as you move. 4. Use the arrow keys to move to the parent, child or siblings if the pointer lands on the wrong element. 5. Click to pin it. The side panel shows its full snapshot. 1. In Overview , read the box model, layout, colours, typography and effects. 2. In Styles , type a property into Filter properties or values… , for example margin , and read Matched rules to see which rule sets it and which rules it overrides. 3. In A11y , check its role, accessible name and contrast. 4. In DOM , read its attributes and markup, and copy a locator for your tests: CSS , JavaScript or Playwright . On the page, the pinned card shows the same element with contrast first. If the text fails AA, the card suggests the nearest text colour that passes AA . 1. Open Live CSS . It starts with the element's current CSS. 2. Change a declaration, for example the colour to the suggested passi"},{"t":"Review a page for colour blindness","d":"Check that a page does not rely on colour alone, using the vision simulations, side-by-side comparison and the contrast checker.","p":"Browser extension › Workflows","u":"browser-extension/docs/workflows/review-a-page-for-colour-blindness.html","h":["1. Look through the common types","2. Compare side by side","3. Try the milder forms and low vision","4. Record what you see","5. Check the numbers","6. Clear the filter","Related pages"],"x":" WCAG asks that colour is never the only way information is shown. This workflow helps you find places where it is: error states shown only in red, charts told apart only by hue, links distinguished only by colour. 1. Open the page, then Check › Vision . 2. Choose Deuteranopia , the most common type. Look at status colours, charts, badges, links and form errors. 3. Repeat with Protanopia , Tritanopia and Achromatopsia . 4. Ask of each coloured element: can I still tell what it means? Alt + Shift + V toggles deuteranopia at any time, which is handy while you scroll. 1. Choose Side by side . The left half stays as it is and the right half is filtered. 2. Compare the two halves at the same place on the page. 3. Choose ✕ to close it. 1. Choose the Weaker forms protanomaly, deuteranomaly, tritanomaly, achromatomaly . Use Strength to see how the effect grows. 2. Choose Low vision , Cataracts , Glaucoma and AMD to check that important content is not only at the edges or only in fine detail. Choose Capture to download a PNG of the filtered tab for a report or a ticket. 1. For a colour pair you are unsure of, open Contrast and set the two colours. 2. Read the Colour vision check : the ratio"},{"t":"Other material","d":"Background material for the browser extension — glossary, shortcuts, limits and accuracy, related tools, release notes and privacy.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" This folder holds the reference material that sits around the how to pages: the terms the extension uses, every keyboard shortcut, what its measurements can and cannot tell you, where to go next, what changed in each version, and what happens to your data. Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md Colour, contrast, accessibility and browser terms used in these pages Keyboard shortcuts shortcuts.md Every key: browser shortcuts, the popup, the inspector and the right click menu Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What each check measures, how precisely, and what it is not Related tools related.md Website tools, VS Code extensions and Learn material that pair with the extension Release notes release notes.md What changed in each version, and what is coming next Privacy privacy.md What stays in your browser, what uses the network, and how to delete it "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","d":"Every keyboard shortcut in the Auric Artisan browser extension — browser-level shortcuts, the popup, the element inspector and the right-click menu.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/shortcuts.html","h":["Browser-level shortcuts","In the popup and side panel","Element inspector (on the page)","Custom right-click menu (on the page)","Screen eyedropper"],"x":" These work from any page. Change them on the browser's shortcuts page: chrome://extensions/shortcuts in Chromium browsers, or about:addons › gear › Manage Extension Shortcuts in Firefox. Settings › Shortcuts › Change them in the browser opens it. Keys Action Name on the shortcuts page Alt + Shift + A Open the extension on the active tab Open Auric Artisan Alt + Shift + C Open the contrast checker Open contrast checker Alt + Shift + E Open Page palette and read the page's colours Extract page palette Alt + Shift + V Turn the deuteranopia simulation on or off Toggle deuteranopia simulation Unassigned Start the element inspector Inspect an element on the page Unassigned Open Audit and run it Run a full accessibility audit No macOS specific keys are documented; use your browser's shortcuts page to check or change them. Keys Action / Focus search when not typing in a field Ctrl + K Focus search from anywhere; closes Settings Up / Down Move through search results Enter Run the selected search result Esc Close an open colour picker, then Settings, then clear the search, then return to Home Left / Right , Home / End Move between spaces, or between Settings sections Up and Down also work t"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the colour, contrast, accessibility and browser terms used in the browser extension documentation.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/glossary.html","h":["Colour","Contrast and accessibility","Browser and code"],"x":" Accent colour. The colour the extension uses for its buttons, focus rings and highlights. You choose it in Settings › Appearance. ASE. Adobe Swatch Exchange, a palette file format many design applications can import. Chroma. How colourful a colour is, from grey no chroma to fully saturated. Chroma room in the Picker is how much more chroma a colour can take before it leaves a gamut. CMYK. Cyan, magenta, yellow and black, the inks of print. The extension converts to CMYK with a simple formula, not a print profile. Colour space. A system for describing colours with numbers, such as sRGB, LAB or OKLCH. Mixing or blending in different spaces gives different in between colours. Display P3 P3 . A wider gamut than sRGB, used by many modern screens. Colours outside sRGB can be written in CSS with color display p3 … or oklch . ΔE delta E . A number for how different two colours look. Under about 2, most people cannot see the difference. Gamut. The range of colours a screen or colour space can show. Harmony. A set of colours chosen by their positions on the colour wheel, such as complementary opposite or triadic evenly spaced three . HEX. A colour written as RRGGBB in hexadecimal, for examp"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What each of the extension's checks measures, how precisely, where it can be wrong, and what it is not a substitute for.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Contrast","The accessibility audit","Vision simulations","Colour values","Gradients","Tokens","What the extension is not","Related pages"],"x":" The extension's tools are practical checks for everyday design and development. This page explains what they measure and where their answers need your judgement. WCAG ratios follow the WCAG 2.x formula for relative luminance and are exact for the colours given. Large text is 24 px or more, or 18.66 px or more when bold, as WCAG defines it. APCA uses a simplified version of the APCA calculation, accurate enough for design feedback but not a certified result. APCA is still a draft method for WCAG 3; its thresholds may change. The background behind text is found by walking up through the element's parents to the first mostly solid background, combining translucent layers on the way. It cannot see backgrounds drawn by images, gradients, canvas or other elements positioned behind the text. Such text is flagged for review or marked as an estimate \"≈\" rather than passed or failed. Text coloured with some modern colour functions that browsers report in forms the check does not read is skipped. It is not reported as passing; it is simply absent from the results. The contrast report copied from Contrast labels its thresholds \"WCAG 2.1\"; the numbers are the same in WCAG 2.2. The audit runs 7"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Auric Artisan browser extension keeps, where, for how long, what uses the network, and how to delete it.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/privacy.html","h":["Promises","What is kept, and where","What uses the network","Backups","Delete your data","Safety measures","Related pages"],"x":" The extension collects nothing and sends nothing. There are no accounts, no analytics and no network requests of its own. Everything it keeps stays in your browser. The only traffic it causes is a page you choose to open. The full policy is at https://auricartisan.com/legal/extension privacy/. 1. No network requests. No analytics, tracking, crash reporting, remote settings or remote code. 2. No accounts. Nothing to sign in to, and no identifiers. 3. Nothing leaves your device unless you click. Links, web searches and translations open only when you choose them. 4. Nothing is written to websites' storage. On a page, the extension does not read or write the site's cookies, local storage or databases. 5. Page changing features are opt in. The website pickers and the custom right click menu stay off until you turn them on. The Firefox package declares to Mozilla, in its manifest, that it collects no data. Everything below lives in your browser profile. None of it is synced or sent. Data Contains page content? Kept until Settings No You reset them or uninstall Colour history 50 Colours only You clear it Library colours 500 and palettes Colours only You delete them Snippets 200 Yes: the"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"What changed in each version of the Auric Artisan browser extension, and what is built for the next release.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/release-notes.html","h":["Upcoming (built, not yet released)","1.0.2 — 2026-09-23","1.0.1 — 2026-07-31","1.0.0 — 2026-07-22","0.9.52","0.9.51","0.2.1","0.2.0","0.1.0"],"x":" The user facing history of the Auric Artisan browser extension, newest first. Store listings update after each store's review, so your browser may show an earlier version for a while; check your version on the browser's extensions page. A redesign called \"one studio, four surfaces\" lays out the same spaces Home, Colour, Check, Code, Saved for where you are: docked beside the page, drawn over it, and in a quick popup. The spaces become a rail down the left edge, with the theme, Settings and the tour at its foot, so the whole width goes to the tool. Each space names itself and the tab its tools act on. Home leads with This tab : the site the panel is linked to, whether the page tools reach it, and Pick , Inspect , Audit and Vision in one click. After an audit it says when it ran and what failed, with Show on page . Home lists the page's own colours; a click opens one in the Picker. The panel follows the tab: switching tabs refreshes Home. Pick a colour , Contrast with its shortcut , Inspect and Audit this page ; the last contrast pair; recent colours; Page palette , Vision and Search ; and Open the side panel , shown only where the browser has one. A score from the rule engine, what"},{"t":"Related tools","d":"Website tools, VS Code extensions and other Auric Artisan products that pair with the browser extension.","p":"Browser extension","u":"browser-extension/others/related.html","h":["Website tools","Libraries and learning","VS Code","Services","Policies"],"x":" The browser extension brings the most frequent checks to any page. The full size tools on auricartisan.com go deeper, and the VS Code extensions bring the same checks to your code. Tool Use it when Docs Analyzer You want a full report on any URL, not just the tab you have open Analyzer ../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Contrast Checker You need more contrast detail than the popup offers Contrast Checker ../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Vision Simulation You want to simulate vision on images and designs, with more controls Vision Simulation ../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Accessibility Checklist You need the manual checks an automated audit cannot make Accessibility Checklist ../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/accessibility checklist/README.md Ishihara Plate Generator You want colour vision test plates Ishihara plates ../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/ishihara plate generator/README.md Basic Colour Tools You want the colour tools in a larger workspace Basic Colour Tools ../../website/tools/colour workspace/basic colour tools/README.md Colour Science Lab"},{"t":"Services","d":"The Auric Artisan services you can use from your own sites and code — the Font CDN, the Icon CDN and the public REST API.","p":"Services","u":"services/README.html","h":["Folders"],"x":" Besides the website, the browser extension and the editor extensions, Auric Artisan offers services you use from your own projects: two content delivery networks that serve fonts and icons to your web pages, and a REST API that exposes its colour science and accessibility checks to your code. Folder What it covers font cdn/ font cdn/README.md fonts.auricartisan.com: the font families it serves, embedding them, the loader, self hosting and licences icon cdn/ icon cdn/README.md icons.auricartisan.com: the icon collections, the loader, embedding icons, and licences public api/ public api/README.md api.auricartisan.com: keys, authentication, plans and credits, every endpoint, errors and limits "},{"t":"Font CDN","d":"What the Auric Artisan Font CDN at fonts.auricartisan.com serves, who it is for, and how to put a font on your page in a few steps.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan Font CDN, at https://fonts.auricartisan.com, serves open licence font families to your web pages. Each family has its own stylesheet of @font face rules that you link like a Google Fonts stylesheet, and a small loader script can load families declaratively or from JavaScript. The font files themselves are served from the same host, so a page that uses the CDN makes no request to any third party. The catalogue holds 2,213 families and 4,883 font files, of which 550 families are variable fonts. Most are under the SIL Open Font License; others use Apache 2.0, public domain dedications, MIT or other open licences, and every family's own licence text is available. A small part of the catalogue is tagged Installed : system fonts that are listed for reference but not served, because their licences do not allow redistribution. You browse the catalogue, preview families in your own words, and copy embed code in the Font Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/. That page is documented with the website tools; these pages cover the CDN itself: what it serves, how to embed a family, the loader, self hosting and licences. Web designers and developers who want open licen"},{"t":"Font CDN documentation","d":"The contents of the Font CDN documentation, from a first embed to the loader API and self-hosting.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to use fonts from fonts.auricartisan.com on your own pages: linking a family's stylesheet, the loader script and its JavaScript API, and downloading a kit to host the files yourself. Page What it covers Getting started getting started.md How the CDN is organised, and a first family on a page Embed a family embed a family.md Link, @import , @font face and usage snippets; weights, italics and variable fonts Use the loader use the loader.md The font cdn.js script tag and the AuricFonts JavaScript API Self host a family self host a family.md Download kits: what they contain and how to install them Find a family find a family.md Finding a family and its id, on the Font Library page or from JavaScript Reference reference.md Every URL pattern, loader attribute, method, snippet and file Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Fonts that do not appear, wrong weights, licences and more FAQ faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"How the Font CDN is organised — family ids, stylesheets and font files — and how to put a first family on a page.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/getting-started.html","h":["How the CDN is organised","Family ids","Your first family","What a family stylesheet contains","Next steps"],"x":" Everything is served from https://fonts.auricartisan.com: Path What it is /css/<family id .css One stylesheet per family, with an @font face rule for each style /font/… The font files the stylesheets point to /font cdn.js The loader script /data/index.json The catalogue: one short record per family /data/detail/<group .json Full metadata for the families in a group A F , G L , M R , S Z /LICENSE.md The licence reference for the collection You do not need to know the file paths inside /font/ : the family stylesheet refers to them for you. Every family has an id , used in its stylesheet URL. The id is the family name in lower case, with apostrophes and quotation marks removed and every run of other characters replaced by a hyphen: Family Id Stylesheet Alegreya alegreya https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/alegreya.css Roboto Slab roboto slab https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/roboto slab.css Open Sans open sans https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/open sans.css The Font Library's Use & Embed tab always shows the exact URL for a family. 1. Add the family's stylesheet to the <head of your page: html <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/alegreya.css\" 2. Use the f"},{"t":"Embed a family","d":"Every way to embed a Font CDN family — link tag, CSS @import, @font-face rules and usage CSS — plus weights, italics, variable axes and several families at once.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/embed-a-family.html","h":["Link (recommended)","Import","Script and JS","@font-face","Usage","Weights and italics","Variable fonts","Several families at once","Related pages"],"x":" The Font Library's Use & Embed tab gives each family six ready snippets: Link , Import , Script , JS , @font face and Usage . Choose one, then Copy . The tab also shows the family's weights as chips under Selected weights , and a note naming the licence. This page explains each snippet. Add the stylesheet to your page's <head : html <! Self hosted stylesheet Google Fonts style <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/alegreya.css\" Put it before your own stylesheets so your CSS can use the family straight away. From inside a CSS file: css / In your CSS file / @import url 'https://fonts.auricartisan.com/css/alegreya.css' ; An @import must come before other rules in the file. A link tag is usually faster, because the browser finds it sooner. The loader script adds the stylesheet for you: html <! Auto load with the CDN script <script src=\"https://fonts.auricartisan.com/font cdn.js\" data families=\"Alegreya\" </script js // Programmatic load AuricFonts.load 'Alegreya' .then = { document.body.style.fontFamily = \"'Alegreya', serif\"; } ; See Use the loader use the loader.md . The @font face snippet gives the rules themselves, pointing at the font files on the CDN, for"},{"t":"Find a family","d":"Find a family and its id for the Font CDN, on the Font Library page or from JavaScript, and read what the catalogue records about it.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/find-a-family.html","h":["On the Font Library page","From JavaScript","Categories","Related pages"],"x":" The Font Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/ is the catalogue's front end. It renders every family in itself, lets you set your own words in it, and gives the embed code and kit for the ones you keep. Its main controls are: Search fonts \"Family, designer or foundry\" ; sorting by Alphabetical, Accessibility score, UI score, Readability score, Most weights, Most glyphs, Variable first, or Surprise me; category tabs and filters; Recommend , a recommender for a brief; Collections , curated sets; Selected , the families you have gathered for a combined embed or kit. Each family opens with tabs including Specimen , Suitability , Pairings , Glyphs , Features , Styles , About , License , Charset , Develop and Use & Embed . The page itself is documented with the website tools; see Related ../others/related.md . The loader can search the catalogue: js const hits = await AuricFonts.search 'mono' ; // name, designer or category const all = await AuricFonts.list ; Each record in the catalogue includes, among other fields, the family's id , name , group , category , weights , whether it is variable and its axes , whether it has italics, whether it is monospace, its license key, desig"},{"t":"Self-host a family","d":"Download a font kit from the Font Library, understand what it contains, and serve the family from your own site.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/self-host-a-family.html","h":["Download a kit","What a kit contains","Install it on your site","Point the loader at your copy","Families that cannot be downloaded","Keep the licence","Related pages"],"x":" Instead of loading fonts from fonts.auricartisan.com, you can download a family and serve it from your own site. The Font Library builds a ready to use kit in your browser. For one family: 1. Open the family in the Font Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/. 2. Choose Download kit \"Download N bundled font files with CSS and license notes\" . The same button is in the Styles tab under Download self hosting kit . 3. Your browser saves <Family font kit.zip . For several families: 1. Add them to your selection. They collect in the Your kit tray. 2. Choose Download in the tray it reads Download selected N . The file is named auric font selection kit.zip or after the family when there is one . The Font Library shows \"Preparing download kit...\" while it gathers the files, then \"Downloaded\" and the file name. For each family, a folder with: File What it is fonts/… Every font file the CDN serves for the family css/<family id .css @font face rules pointing at ../fonts/ , and a font <family id variable with a fallback demo.html A page that shows the family, using the stylesheet README.txt The family, category, designer, licence, file list and three steps to use it LICENSE.txt The fam"},{"t":"Use the loader","d":"Load Font CDN families with the font-cdn.js script tag or its AuricFonts JavaScript API, and configure where it loads from.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/use-the-loader.html","h":["Declarative: one script tag","Programmatic: AuricFonts","Family specs","Where it loads from","Related pages"],"x":" font cdn.js is a small script with no dependencies. It adds family stylesheets to your page, waits until fonts are ready, registers single font faces, and lets you search the catalogue. It creates a global object, AuricFonts also available as AuricFontLoader . html <script src=\"https://fonts.auricartisan.com/font cdn.js\" data families=\"Alegreya Roboto Slab Open Sans:wght@400;700\" </script Attribute What it does data families The families to load, separated by a vertical bar; each can carry a weight list see Family specs family specs data fonts Another name for data families data display The font display value for faces added with AuricFonts.face . Default swap . data base Load stylesheets and data from another address; see Where it loads from where it loads from For each family, the loader adds a <link rel=\"stylesheet\" for its CDN stylesheet to the page's <head , once. Include the script without data families , then call the API: html <script src=\"https://fonts.auricartisan.com/font cdn.js\" </script <script AuricFonts.load 'Alegreya' .then = { document.body.style.fontFamily = \"'Alegreya', serif\"; } ; </script js await AuricFonts.load 'Alegreya' ; // one family await AuricFonts.loa"},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every URL pattern, file, loader attribute, method and snippet of the Auric Artisan Font CDN.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/reference.html","h":["Catalogue","URL patterns","Stylesheet rules","Loader: script attributes","Loader: AuricFonts API","Font Library snippets","Downloads","Licence permissions shown per family","Related pages"],"x":" Fact Value Host https://fonts.auricartisan.com Families catalogued 2,213 Font files 4,883 Variable families 550 Families with italics 401 Served from the library 2,023 families Listed as Installed not served 190 families Categories Sans serif 780, serif 1,172, display 81, handwriting 97, monospace 83 Groups A F , G L , M R , S Z Catalogue built 2 June 2026 These figures come from the catalogue's own statistics, served at /data/stats.json and /data/meta.json . Pattern What it serves /css/<family id .css The family's stylesheet: a header comment and one @font face rule per file /font/<group /<FOLDER /<file Font files, referenced by the stylesheets /font cdn.js The loader script /data/index.json One record per family /data/detail/<group .json Full metadata for the families in a group /data/stats.json , /data/meta.json Catalogue statistics and build information /LICENSE.md The collection's licence reference The family id is the name in lower case, with quotation marks and apostrophes removed and other characters replaced by hyphens Roboto Slab becomes roboto slab . Property Value font family The family name font style normal or italic font weight One weight, or a range for variable fo"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Why a Font CDN family might not appear or look right, and what to do.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Related pages"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do The text stays in the fallback font The stylesheet URL is wrong, so it returns a \"not found\" page Open the stylesheet URL: it should start with a comment naming the family. Copy it from Use & Embed . The text stays in the fallback font, and the URL is right The CSS names the family differently Use the exact name in the stylesheet's font family , in quotes, for example 'Roboto Slab' The fallback shows briefly, then the font Normal: stylesheets use font display: swap Preload or use AuricFonts.load and wait for it before showing text that must not change Bold looks smeared or too heavy The family has no bold file, so the browser synthesises one Pick a weight the family has; the Styles tab lists them A weight has no effect on a static family Only the weights the family has can be shown Choose another weight or a variable family Italic looks slanted rather than true italic The family has no italic style Check the Styles tab, or choose a family with italics data families loads nothing A family name is misspelt, or the names are not separated by a vertical bar Use the exact family names; check the browser's network panel for a failed /css/ request AuricFonts is und"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Auric Artisan Font CDN.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" The CDN's stylesheets, files and loader are served publicly, and the Font Library page needs no sign in to copy embed code or download kits. Each font keeps its own licence terms; see Licences ../others/licences.md . No. It works the same way, with a stylesheet per family, but everything is served from fonts.auricartisan.com, including fonts that came from other open sources, and every family comes with its licence text and a downloadable self hosting kit. Most families are under open licences that allow commercial use, such as the SIL Open Font License. Check each family's License tab: it shows the licence and a permissions summary. The stylesheet always declares the whole family. Browsers generally download a font file only when the page uses that style. To ship exactly the files you want, self host and remove the rules you do not need. Yes: download the kit and serve it from your own site. See Self host a family self host a family.md . The family is a system font listed for reference. Its licence does not allow redistribution, so the CDN does not serve it and it cannot be downloaded. Yes. 550 families are variable; their stylesheets declare a weight range, and width where the f"},{"t":"Other material","d":"Background material for the Font CDN — glossary, licences, limits and accuracy, related tools and privacy.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the reference material around the Font CDN guides. The CDN has no keyboard shortcuts of its own and no public changelog; its catalogue build date is given in the Reference ../docs/reference.md . Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md Type and web font terms Licences licences.md The licences in the collection, what they allow, and how to comply Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the catalogue's categories, scores and licence data can and cannot tell you Related related.md The Font Library page, the VS Code Font Hub and other services Privacy privacy.md What a page using the CDN requests, and what the loader does "},{"t":"Licences","d":"The licences that cover the fonts on the Font CDN, what they allow, where to find each family's licence, and how to comply.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/licences.html","h":["The licences in the collection","Where to find a family's licence","The permissions summary","Complying","Related pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan does not claim ownership of any font on the CDN. Each typeface remains the property of its authors and is redistributed under its original licence. The collection's licence reference, at https://fonts.auricartisan.com/LICENSE.md, lists the licences and reproduces their texts. The reference describes the served collection as follows: Licence Commercial use Redistribute Modify Main condition SIL Open Font License 1.1 the default Yes Yes Yes Keep the licence; never sell the font alone; rename modified versions that use a Reserved Font Name Apache License 2.0 Yes Yes Yes Keep the licence and notices; state significant changes CC0 1.0 / public domain Yes Yes Yes None Bitstream Vera Fonts License Yes Yes Yes A modified version must be renamed without \"Bitstream\" or \"Vera\" The catalogue's own statistics also count a few families under MIT and one under a custom licence, and some with no licence text found. The Font Library marks those Unspecified or Custom . The License tab in the Font Library shows the licence name, a License URL where known, the original licence file, the copyright, a permissions summary and the Full license text. The stylesheet's header comment names the"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the type and web-font terms used in the Font CDN documentation.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" Axis. One dimension a variable font can vary along, such as weight wght , width wdth , slant slnt or optical size opsz . CDN content delivery network . A service that serves files, here fonts and stylesheets, to web pages. Fallback. A font the browser uses when the one you asked for is not available yet or lacks a character. Family. A set of related fonts sharing a name, such as Alegreya in regular, italic and several weights. Family id. The lower case, hyphenated form of a family name used in its stylesheet URL, such as roboto slab . @font face . The CSS rule that tells the browser where to find a font file and which family, weight and style it provides. font display: swap . A setting that shows text in a fallback font straight away and swaps to the web font when it arrives. Font stack. A font family list with fallbacks in order of preference. Glyph. A single drawn character shape in a font. Installed. A family listed in the catalogue but not served, because it is a system font whose licence does not allow redistribution. Kit. A ZIP file from the Font Library with a family's font files, stylesheet, demo page, notes and licence, for self hosting. Loader. The font cdn.js script tha"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Font CDN's catalogue data — categories, scores, licences, script coverage — can and cannot tell you, and the CDN's practical limits.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Catalogue data","Serving","The loader","Related pages"],"x":" Metadata comes from the font files themselves: names, designers, versions, weights, axes, character coverage, OpenType features and embedding flags are read from each font's internal tables. If a font's own data is wrong or missing, the catalogue is too. Categories are computed, not curated. Serif or sans is worked out from the outlines of letters such as I, H and L when a font does not declare it. A few families, such as rounded sans serifs, can land in the wrong category. Scores accessibility, UI, readability, developer and editorial are calculated from measurable features such as x height and how distinct confusable characters like I, l and 1 are. They are a starting point for choosing, not a verdict, and a few display fonts score higher than they should. Licences are detected from the licence files bundled with each family and from the font's name data. A family with no licence text found is marked Unspecified ; check it yourself. Script coverage lists the Unicode blocks a font has characters in. Having characters in a block does not guarantee complete or correct support for a language. Stylesheets declare the whole family; there is no per weight or per character subsetting in"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What a page that uses the Font CDN requests from it, and what the loader script does and does not do.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/privacy.html","h":["What your visitors' browsers request","What the loader does not do","Self-hosting","The Font Library page"],"x":" A page that uses the CDN makes requests to https://fonts.auricartisan.com and nowhere else for its fonts: You use Your visitors' browsers request A link tag or @import The family stylesheet, then the font files the page actually uses The loader with data families or load The loader script, the family stylesheets, then the font files list , search or get Also the catalogue data files As with any file host, the CDN receives the ordinary information that comes with each request. The loader served at https://fonts.auricartisan.com/font cdn.js: sets no cookies; writes nothing to the browser's storage; makes no requests other than the stylesheets and data files described above. If you prefer your visitors' browsers never to contact the CDN, download a kit and serve the files from your own site. See Self host a family ../docs/self host a family.md . Previews on the Font Library page are drawn in your browser from the CDN's files, and download kits are assembled in your browser. For the auricartisan.com website as a whole, see the site's privacy policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/. "},{"t":"Related","d":"The Font Library page, the VS Code Font Hub, the Icon CDN and other related Auric Artisan products.","p":"Services › Font CDN","u":"services/font-cdn/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Product Why Docs Font Library website Browse, preview, compare and pair families; copy embed code; download kits Font Library ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/font library/README.md Auric Artisan Font Hub VS Code Work with fonts from inside VS Code Font Hub ../../../vscode extensions/auric artisan font hub/README.md Icon CDN Icons served the same way, from icons.auricartisan.com Icon CDN ../../icon cdn/README.md Design Engine website Build a design system with fonts and colours Design Engine ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/design engine/README.md Public API Colour and accessibility checks for your code Public API ../../public api/README.md Links: Font Library: https://auricartisan.com/tool/font/ Licence reference: https://fonts.auricartisan.com/LICENSE.md "},{"t":"Icon CDN","d":"What the Auric Artisan Icon CDN at icons.auricartisan.com serves, who it is for, and how to put an icon on your page in a few steps.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan Icon CDN, at https://icons.auricartisan.com, serves 12,896 icons from seven open source sets, in 32,803 variants: Lucide, Phosphor, Tabler, Remix, Heroicons, Feather and Material. A small loader script turns placeholders such as <i data icon=\"lucide:house\" into inline SVG you can colour and size with CSS, and a JavaScript API returns any icon's markup or searches the catalogue. The SVG files are also served directly, for use in <img tags or your own build. Every set keeps its own open source licence MIT, ISC, Apache 2.0 or the Remix Icon License , all of which allow commercial use. The icons are drawn with currentColor , so they take the colour of the surrounding text unless you set one. You browse, recolour and resize icons, copy their code, and export selections as a ZIP or an SVG sprite in the Icon Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/. That page is documented with the website tools; these pages cover the CDN itself: the collections, the loader, embedding and licences. Web developers who want icons in plain HTML without a build step or an npm package. Designers and prototypers who want to try icons from several sets under one name scheme. React develo"},{"t":"Icon CDN documentation","d":"The contents of the Icon CDN documentation, from a first icon to the loader API, styling and self-hosting.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/README.html","h":[],"x":" These pages explain how to use icons from icons.auricartisan.com on your own pages: the icon sets and their styles, the loader and its JavaScript API, other ways to embed an icon, styling, and exporting icons to host yourself. Page What it covers Getting started getting started.md How the CDN is organised, icon names, and a first icon Collections collections.md The seven sets: styles, counts, grids and licences Embed an icon embed an icon.md Loader placeholders, inline SVG, JSX, data URI images, direct files and webfonts Use the loader use the loader.md The icon cdn.js script and the AuricIcons API Style, size and colour style size and colour.md Choosing a style, sizing, colouring and stroke width Export and self host export and self host.md ZIP and sprite exports, single SVG downloads, hosting the loader yourself Reference reference.md Every URL pattern, attribute, method and option Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Icons that do not appear or look wrong FAQ faq.md Short answers "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"How the Icon CDN is organised, how icons are named, and how to put a first icon on a page.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/getting-started.html","h":["How the CDN is organised","Icon names","Your first icon","Next steps"],"x":" Everything is served from https://icons.auricartisan.com: Path What it is /icon cdn.js The loader script /icon/<set /… The original SVG files, and the Material and Remix webfonts /data/sets.json The seven sets: styles, licence, grid and counts /data/index.json One record per icon, used for names and search /data/bodies/<set .<style .json The icon markup for one set and style, loaded by the loader as needed /data/material.json The code points for the Material webfont /LICENSE.md The licence reference for every set An icon is named by its set and its name, joined by a colon: lucide:house , tabler:home , phosphor:heart . The loader also accepts: Form Example Meaning set:name tabler:home This icon from this set set name tabler home The same name home The first set with this name: Lucide, Phosphor, Tabler, Remix, Heroicons, Feather, then Material Names are the set's own icon names in lower case with hyphens. Different sets name things differently: Lucide calls it house , Tabler calls it home . The Icon Library shows every icon's name and gives you the exact tag with Copy CDN tag . 1. Add the loader once, anywhere in the page: html <script src=\"https://icons.auricartisan.com/icon cdn.js"},{"t":"Collections","d":"The seven icon sets on the Icon CDN — their styles, icon counts, grids, whether they are stroke-based, and their licences.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/collections.html","h":["Grids and strokes","Material is a webfont","Remix categories","Categories in the Icon Library","Upstream sources","Related pages"],"x":" The CDN serves seven sets: 12,896 icons in 32,803 variants. An icon is one symbol, such as \"heart\"; a variant is one style of it, such as Phosphor's heart in bold or fill. Set Icons Variants Styles Default style Licence Lucide 1,714 1,714 regular regular ISC Phosphor 1,512 9,072 thin , light , regular , bold , fill , duotone regular MIT Tabler 5,093 6,146 outline , filled outline MIT Remix 1,690 3,229 line , fill line Remix Icon License v1.0 Heroicons 324 1,288 24/outline , 24/solid , 20/solid , 16/solid 24/outline MIT Feather 287 287 regular regular MIT Material 2,276 11,067 outlined , round , sharp , regular , twotone outlined Apache 2.0 Set Grid viewBox Drawn with Lucide 24 × 24 Strokes Phosphor 256 × 256 Fills Tabler 24 × 24 Strokes Remix 24 × 24 Fills Heroicons 24, 20 or 16, by style Strokes outline and fills solid Feather 24 × 24 Strokes Material Webfont Glyphs of a font Stroke width data stroke changes only icons drawn with strokes: Lucide, Tabler, Feather and Heroicons' outline style. Material icons are not SVG: the CDN serves them as five webfonts Regular, Outlined, Round, Sharp and Two Tone with their code points. The loader renders a Material icon as a character in the "},{"t":"Embed an icon","d":"Every way to put an Icon CDN icon on a page — loader placeholders, inline SVG, a React component, a data-URI image, direct SVG files and the Material and Remix webfonts.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/embed-an-icon.html","h":["CDN tag (the loader)","Inline SVG","JSX / React","Image with a data URI","Direct SVG files","Webfonts","Accessibility","Related pages"],"x":" The Icon Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/ gives every icon ready made code. Open an icon, set its style, size and colour, then choose a copy button or copy a block from the code panel. This page explains each option. Copy CDN tag gives a placeholder and the loader script: html <i data icon=\"phosphor:heart\" data style=\"fill\" </i <script src=\"https://icons.auricartisan.com/icon cdn.js\" </script data style appears only when you chose a style other than the set's default. Include the script once per page, and use as many placeholders as you like. The loader replaces each placeholder's contents with inline SVG when the page loads; see Use the loader use the loader.md . Best for: plain HTML pages, prototypes, content managed in a CMS. Copy SVG gives the icon's SVG markup, with your chosen colour and stroke applied. Paste it straight into your HTML. Nothing needs to load from the CDN afterwards. html <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke width=\"2\" stroke linecap=\"round\" stroke linejoin=\"round\" <polyline points=\"22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12\"/ </svg Give it a size with width and height attributes or CSS. Best for: a handful of icons you want in "},{"t":"Export and self-host","d":"Export icons from the Icon Library as a ZIP of SVG files or an SVG sprite, download single icons, and host icons or the loader yourself.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/export-and-self-host.html","h":["Collect icons in your kit","Download a ZIP","Copy an SVG sprite","Download one icon","Link files directly","Host the loader yourself","Keep the licences","Related pages"],"x":" You do not have to load icons from icons.auricartisan.com at run time. The Icon Library can export them for your own project. 1. In the Icon Library at https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/, open an icon and choose ＋ Select . 2. Selected icons collect in the Your kit tray, with a count. The tray notes that it is \"Kept in this browser\". 3. Choose Hide to put the tray away, and Clear to empty it. Choose Download ZIP in the tray. The file auric icons.zip contains: one SVG per icon, in a folder per set, named <name <style .svg ; a README.txt noting the number of icons and that each uses currentColor ; for Material icons, a text file per icon with its webfont character code instead of an SVG. Choose Copy sprite in the tray. The Icon Library copies one hidden <svg containing a <symbol for each selected icon, with the icon's id as its id : html <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"display:none\" <symbol id=\"lucide house\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" …</symbol </svg <! use: <svg <use href=\" ID\"/ </svg Paste it once near the top of your page, then use any icon with: html <svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" <use href=\" lucide house\"/ </svg A sprite needs no script and no further requests, and icons i"},{"t":"Style, size and colour","d":"Choose an icon's style, give it a size, colour it and change its stroke width, with the loader, CSS or the Icon Library.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/style-size-and-colour.html","h":["Style","Size","Colour","Stroke width","Related pages"],"x":" Many icons come in several styles: Phosphor's thin , light , regular , bold , fill and duotone ; Tabler's outline and filled ; Remix's line and fill ; Heroicons' 24/outline , 24/solid , 20/solid and 16/solid ; Material's outlined , round , sharp , regular and twotone . See Collections collections.md . With the loader, set data style=\"fill\" or pass { style: 'fill' } to svg . If you ask for a style the icon does not have, the loader uses the set's default style, or else the icon's first style. In the Icon Library, the Style buttons in an icon's panel switch between its styles, and the copied code follows. Served icons have no width or height of their own, only a viewBox , so always size them. With the loader: html <i data icon=\"lucide:house\" data size=\"24\" </i <! 24 px <i data icon=\"lucide:house\" data size=\"1.25em\" </i <! scales with text With CSS, for every icon at once: css data icon svg { width: 1em; height: 1em; vertical align: 0.125em; } Sizing in em makes icons follow the surrounding font size. Material icons are font glyphs and follow data size or the font size. Icons are drawn on a grid: 24 units for most sets, 256 for Phosphor, and 20 or 16 for some Heroicons styles. In the"},{"t":"Use the loader","d":"Render Icon CDN icons with the icon-cdn.js placeholders and the AuricIcons JavaScript API, including icons added after the page loads.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/use-the-loader.html","h":["Placeholders","Icons added later","Get an icon's markup","Find icons","How names are resolved","Where it loads from","Related pages"],"x":" icon cdn.js is a small script with no dependencies. It fills data icon placeholders with inline SVG, returns any icon's markup to your code, and searches the catalogue. It creates a global object, AuricIcons also available as AuricIconLoader . html <script src=\"https://icons.auricartisan.com/icon cdn.js\" </script <i data icon=\"lucide:house\" </i <i data icon=\"phosphor:heart\" data style=\"fill\" data size=\"32\" data color=\" e11\" data stroke=\"1.5\" </i Attribute What it does Example data icon The icon to show required : set:name , set name or name tabler:home data style One of the set's styles; otherwise the set's default fill , outline , 24/solid data size Width and height. A number is treated as pixels; a value with a unit is used as written. 24 , 1.5em data color The icon's colour; otherwise the text colour e11 , rebeccapurple data stroke Stroke width, for stroke drawn icons 1.5 When the page has finished loading or at once, if it already has , the loader replaces the contents of every element with data icon and marks it with a data icon done attribute. An element marked done is not processed again. If the icon cannot be found, the element is left as it was. Any element works, not onl"},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every URL pattern, set, style, loader attribute, method and export of the Auric Artisan Icon CDN.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/reference.html","h":["Catalogue","URL patterns","Sets and styles","Placeholder attributes","Script configuration","AuricIcons API","Icon Library outputs","Icon Library controls","Related pages"],"x":" Fact Value Host https://icons.auricartisan.com Sets 7 Icons 12,896 Variants 32,803 Catalogue built 3 June 2026 Icons by licence MIT 7,216; ISC 1,714; Remix v1.0 1,690; Apache 2.0 2,276 Pattern What it serves /icon cdn.js The loader /icon/<set /… SVG files, and the Material and Remix webfonts /icon/remix/fonts/remixicon.css Remix Icon's own webfont stylesheet /data/sets.json Set metadata: label, licence, styles, default style, grid, counts, home, credit /data/index.json One record per icon: id, name, set, styles, category, search terms /data/bodies/<set .<style .json SVG markup for one set and style a / in a style becomes /data/material.json Material code points by style /data/stats.json , /data/meta.json Catalogue statistics and build information /LICENSE.md The licence reference Set Styles default first Grid Stroke width applies lucide regular 24 Yes phosphor regular , thin , light , bold , fill , duotone 256 No tabler outline , filled 24 Yes remix line , fill 24 No heroicons 24/outline , 24/solid , 20/solid , 16/solid 24, 20, 16 Outline only feather regular 24 Yes material outlined , round , sharp , regular , twotone Webfont No Name resolution order when no set is given: Lucide,"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Why an Icon CDN icon might not appear, appear huge, show the wrong icon or ignore its colour, and what to do.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Related pages"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do Icons are huge, or fill their container Served SVGs have no width or height Set data size , or add CSS such as data icon svg { width: 1em; height: 1em; } A placeholder stays empty The name matches no icon Copy the name from the Icon Library; check the spelling and the set The wrong set's icon appears The set you named has no icon by that name, so another set's is used Use the set's own name, for example lucide:house rather than lucide:home Icons added after page load stay empty The loader fills placeholders once, when the page loads Call AuricIcons.inject after adding them An icon does not update when I change data icon Filled placeholders are marked data icon done Remove that attribute and the contents , then call inject again The colour does not change An <img or linked SVG file cannot inherit text colour Use the loader, inline SVG or a sprite; or pick the colour before copying data stroke has no effect The set is drawn with fills Choose a lighter or heavier style instead, for example Phosphor light or bold A style is ignored The icon does not have that style Check the icon's Style buttons; the loader falls back to the default A Material icon looks like a "},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Auric Artisan Icon CDN.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" No. The loader, data and files are served publicly, and the Icon Library needs no sign in. Yes. All seven sets use licences that allow commercial use, redistribution and modification: MIT, ISC, Apache 2.0 and the Remix Icon License. Keep the licence notices as each licence asks. See Licences ../others/licences.md . Their original authors: Lucide Contributors, Phosphor Icons, Paweł Kuna Tabler , Remix Design, Tailwind Labs Heroicons , Cole Bemis Feather and Google Material . Auric Artisan does not claim ownership of any icon. One loader and one naming scheme cover all seven sets, with no build step. If you use a single set heavily in a built app, that set's own package may suit you better. The loader fills placeholders in the page. With a framework that renders after page load, call AuricIcons.inject after rendering, or use Copy JSX for React components, or a sprite. Do nothing: icons use currentColor . Avoid data color and linked image files, which fix the colour. Yes: export a ZIP or a sprite from the Icon Library, or host the loader and its data yourself. See Export and self host export and self host.md . Served SVGs have no size of their own. Set data size or a CSS width and he"},{"t":"Other material","d":"Background material for the Icon CDN — glossary, licences, limits and accuracy, related tools and privacy.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/README.html","h":[],"x":" This folder holds the reference material around the Icon CDN guides. The CDN has no keyboard shortcuts of its own and no public changelog; its catalogue build date is given in the Reference ../docs/reference.md . Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md Icon and SVG terms Licences licences.md Each set's licence, what it allows, and how to comply Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the catalogue's names, categories and counts can and cannot tell you Related related.md The Icon Library page, VS Code icon extensions and other services Privacy privacy.md What a page using the CDN requests, and what the loader does "},{"t":"Licences","d":"The licence of each icon set on the Icon CDN, what it allows, and how to comply when you use or ship the icons.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/licences.html","h":["Licences by set","What each licence asks","Brand icons","Complying","Related pages"],"x":" Every icon on the CDN is free for commercial use, redistribution, embedding and modification, under the conditions of its set's own open source licence. Auric Artisan does not claim ownership of any icon: each set remains the property of its authors and is redistributed under its original licence. The licence reference at https://icons.auricartisan.com/LICENSE.md gives the details and the full licence texts. Set Licence Copyright Phosphor MIT Phosphor Icons Feather MIT Cole Bemis Heroicons MIT Tailwind Labs, Inc. Tabler MIT Paweł Kuna Lucide ISC Lucide Icons and Contributors Material Apache License 2.0 Google LLC Remix Remix Icon License v1.0 Remix Design Licence Commercial use Redistribute Modify Main condition MIT Yes Yes Yes Keep the copyright and licence notice ISC Yes Yes Yes Keep the copyright and licence notice Apache 2.0 Yes Yes Yes Keep the licence and notices; state significant changes to the files Remix Icon License v1.0 Yes Yes Yes A permissive, Apache 2.0 style licence; see its text Lucide is a community fork of Feather; the original Feather icons it derives from remain under MIT. Some sets include logos of brands and companies. Those logos remain trademarks of their "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the icon and SVG terms used in the Icon CDN documentation.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/glossary.html","h":[],"x":" currentColor . A CSS keyword meaning \"the current text colour\". Icons drawn with it take the colour of the text around them. Data URI. A way to put a small file, here an SVG, directly into an address, so an <img needs no separate download. Default style. The style the loader uses when you do not choose one, such as regular for Phosphor. Fill drawn icon. An icon made of filled shapes. Its weight comes from its style, not from a stroke width. Grid viewBox . The coordinate square an icon is drawn in, such as 24 × 24. It sets the icon's proportions, not its size on screen. Icon. One symbol, such as \"heart\". Variant: one style of it, such as a bold or filled heart. Inline SVG. SVG markup placed directly in the HTML, so CSS can colour and size it. JSX. The HTML like syntax React components are written in. Loader. The icon cdn.js script that fills data icon placeholders and offers the AuricIcons API. Placeholder. An element with a data icon attribute that the loader fills with an icon. Sprite. One hidden SVG containing many icons as <symbol elements, each shown elsewhere with <use href=\" id\" . Stroke drawn icon. An icon made of lines, whose thickness can be changed with a stroke width. S"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Icon CDN's names, categories, search and counts can and cannot tell you, and its practical limits.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Names and search","Categories","Counts","Markup","The loader","Related pages"],"x":" Names are the sets' own. The same idea can have different names in different sets house in Lucide, home in Tabler , and the same name can mean slightly different drawings. A name without a set, or a name the named set lacks, resolves to the first set that has it. Name the set, and copy names from the Icon Library, to be sure what you get. Search matches names, ids and each icon's search terms. It does not understand synonyms beyond those terms. Categories come from the sets that provide them. Almost half the icons 6,113 have no category, so browsing by category shows only part of the catalogue. The catalogue counts 12,896 icons and 32,803 variants. An icon counts once however many styles it has. The licence reference counts SVG files in the upstream folders 21,736 differently from the catalogue, which merges variants into icons. Served SVGs are normalised: their own width and height are removed, the viewBox is kept, and colours use currentColor . Size them yourself. Stroke width applies only to stroke drawn icons. Material icons depend on their webfont loading; until it does, they may show as plain characters. It fills placeholders once, when the page loads; call inject for later "},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What a page that uses the Icon CDN requests from it, and what the loader script does and does not do.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/privacy.html","h":["What your visitors' browsers request","What the loader does not do","Avoiding the CDN at run time","The Icon Library page"],"x":" You use Your visitors' browsers request from icons.auricartisan.com The loader with placeholders The loader, the index, the set list, one markup file per set and style, and Material data and fonts if used Linked SVG files Each file Inline SVG, JSX, data URIs or a sprite you pasted Nothing As with any file host, the CDN receives the ordinary information that comes with each request. The loader served at https://icons.auricartisan.com/icon cdn.js: sets no cookies; writes nothing to the browser's storage; makes no requests other than the data and font files described above. If you prefer your visitors' browsers never to contact the CDN, paste inline SVG or a sprite, or export a ZIP and serve the files yourself. See Export and self host ../docs/export and self host.md . Recolouring, resizing and exports on the Icon Library page happen in your browser, and your selection is \"Kept in this browser\". For the auricartisan.com website as a whole, see the site's privacy policy at https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/. "},{"t":"Related","d":"The Icon Library page, VS Code icon extensions, the Font CDN and other related Auric Artisan products.","p":"Services › Icon CDN","u":"services/icon-cdn/others/related.html","h":[],"x":" Product Why Docs Icon Library website Browse, recolour, resize and copy icons; export ZIPs and sprites Icon Library ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/icon library/README.md Auric Artisan Icon Hub VS Code Work with icons from inside VS Code Icon Hub ../../../vscode extensions/auric artisan icon hub/README.md Font CDN Fonts served the same way, from fonts.auricartisan.com Font CDN ../../font cdn/README.md Public API Colour and accessibility checks for your code Public API ../../public api/README.md Links: Icon Library: https://auricartisan.com/tool/icon/ Licence reference: https://icons.auricartisan.com/LICENSE.md "},{"t":"Auric Artisan REST API","d":"What the Auric Artisan REST API is, who it is for, where to find it, and how to make a first call.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/README.html","h":["Who it is for","Where to find it","Quick start","What you can do","In this folder"],"x":" The Auric Artisan REST API exposes the platform's colour science toolkit as JSON over HTTPS: colour conversions across 63 colour spaces, palettes, harmonies, gradients, shade scales and design tokens, WCAG and APCA accessibility checks, colour vision deficiency simulation, Ishihara plates, a URL analyzer, and large browsable collections of colours, palettes, harmonies, gradients, shade scales and accessible colour pairs. Every endpoint lives under /v1 . You authenticate with an API key you create in your Auric Artisan account dashboard. Usage is metered in credits : one credit for a standard request, more for heavier work such as rendering images. API access is included from the Specialist plan upward, with a monthly credit allowance, a per minute rate limit and optional prepaid overage. Discovery endpoints, such as the index, the catalogue and the OpenAPI document, are open to everyone so you can evaluate the API before buying. The API is documented on the site at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/, with a separate guide to the analyzer endpoints at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/analyzer/. The API also serves its own interactive reference and"},{"t":"Public API documentation","d":"The contents of the public API documentation, from creating a key to every endpoint, error and limit.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/README.html","h":["Files","Folders"],"x":" This folder explains how to get access to the Auric Artisan REST API, authenticate, understand what calls cost, and use each group of endpoints. The Reference reference.md lists every endpoint in one table. Page What it covers Getting started getting started.md Get a key, make a first call, read the response and its headers Authentication authentication.md API keys, the OAuth bearer token, key safety and revocation Plans, credits and quotas plans credits and quotas.md Plans, rate limits, credits per endpoint, overage, spend caps and ceilings, usage headers Request examples examples.md Ready to run requests for common tasks Errors errors.md The error format, every error code and what to do about it SDKs and tooling sdks and tooling.md Official clients and integrations Reference reference.md Every endpoint with its method, authentication, credits and purpose Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Common problems and fixes FAQ faq.md Short answers Folder What it covers endpoints/ endpoints/README.md One page per group of endpoints, with parameters, responses and examples "},{"t":"Getting started","d":"Get an API key from your dashboard, make a first request, and read the response and its usage headers.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/getting-started.html","h":["1. Check your plan","2. Create a key","3. Make a first request","4. Read the headers","5. Check your usage","6. Explore","Next steps"],"x":" This page takes you from no key to a working request. The API is a paid feature, included from the Specialist plan upward: Plan API access Apprentice free Not included Artisan Not included Specialist Included Industrial Pro Included A key created on a plan without API access authenticates, but metered endpoints refuse it with 402 PLAN UPGRADE REQUIRED , and the response names the upgrade path. In the dashboard, key creation says \"Available from the Specialist plan\" until you upgrade. You can still explore without a key. These discovery endpoints are open to everyone: GET /v1 , GET /v1/catalog , GET /v1/openapi.yaml , GET /v1/docs , GET /v1/tiers and GET /v1/health . 1. Sign in and open your dashboard at https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/. The API documentation calls this Dashboard › API Keys . 2. Under Your API Keys , choose Create your first key or Create key if you already have one . 3. Type a name in Key name e.g. \"CI pipeline\" and choose Create . 4. Copy the key and store it somewhere safe, such as a password manager or your deployment's secret store. \"This is the only time the full key is shown.\" Keys start with aa . You can hold up to 10 active keys, and Revoke any of "},{"t":"Authentication","d":"How to authenticate with the Auric Artisan API — API keys, the CLI's OAuth bearer token, keeping keys safe, and revoking them.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/authentication.html","h":["Methods","Keys are secret","Several keys","Revoke a key","Plan and access","Related pages"],"x":" Every metered endpoint requires a credential. Requests without a valid one receive 401 Unauthorized . Endpoints marked \"None\" in the Reference reference.md are public and unmetered. Method How to send it Best for API key recommended The x api key: aa … header, or the ?key=aa … query parameter Servers, scripts and CI; create keys in the dashboard OAuth bearer Authorization: Bearer <token , from the CLI's device flow The auric command line tool and interactive tools Prefer the header. A key in a query string can end up in server logs and browser history. bash curl https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/usage/me H \"x api key: aa YOUR KEY\" The full key is displayed once , when you create it. It is stored only as a SHA 256 hash, so nobody, including Auric Artisan, can recover it later. If you lose it, create a new one. Keep keys out of source code and front end code. Load them from environment variables or a secret store, as the examples do with $AURIC API KEY . Each successful request updates the key's \"last used\" time, which you can check in the dashboard to spot a key in use where it should not be. You can hold up to 10 active keys, for example one per service or environment. Rate limits, "},{"t":"Errors","d":"The Auric Artisan API's error format, every error code with its HTTP status, what each means, and how to respond.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/errors.html","h":["Error codes","429 or 402: which is which","Handling errors well","Related pages"],"x":" Errors are JSON with a stable code and a human readable message . Most include a request id ; quote it when you contact support about a specific call. json { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID INPUT\", \"message\": \"seed: not a number\" }, \"request id\": \"daebcbed 508b 4d4d 91ef 87ee99d32f03\" } Status Code Meaning and what to do 400 INVALID INPUT A parameter is missing or malformed; the message names the field 400 INVALID JSON The body is not valid JSON 401 UNAUTHORIZED or UNAUTHENTICATED No key, or a missing, invalid or revoked key 402 PLAN UPGRADE REQUIRED A valid key on a plan without API access; included from Specialist upward 402 INSUFFICIENT CREDITS Overage is on but the prepaid balance will not cover the call. Top up. 402 SPEND CAP REACHED Your monthly overage spend cap was reached. Raise it in the dashboard. 402 CREDIT DEBIT FAILED The balance could not be debited, so the request was not served and nothing was charged. Retry. 403 FORBIDDEN A valid key without rights for this route 404 NOT FOUND Unknown endpoint or resource id. GET /v1 lists every endpoint. 405 METHOD NOT ALLOWED Right path, wrong method; the Allow header lists what is accepted 413 PAYLOAD TOO LARGE The body is over th"},{"t":"Request examples","d":"Ready-to-run requests for common tasks with the Auric Artisan API.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/examples.html","h":["Convert a colour to OKLCH","Check contrast","Fix a failing pair","Generate a palette","Simulate colour-vision deficiency","Build a token system and export it","Audit a page's metadata","Check your usage","From JavaScript","Related pages"],"x":" Replace aa YOUR KEY with your key, or set AURIC API KEY in your shell and use $AURIC API KEY . bash curl X POST https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/color/convert \\ H \"x api key: aa YOUR KEY\" \\ H \"Content Type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"color\": \" d3af37\", \"to\": \"oklch\"}' bash curl X POST https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/color/contrast \\ H \"x api key: aa YOUR KEY\" H \"Content Type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\": \" 1a1712\", \"bg\": \" d3af37\"}' For WCAG 2.2 and APCA together: bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/accessibility/check\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\":\" 767676\",\"bg\":\" ffffff\"}' bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/accessibility/recommend\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\":\" c9a227\",\"bg\":\" ffffff\",\"target\":\"foreground\",\"minRatio\":4.5}' bash curl X POST https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/palette/generate \\ H \"x api key: aa YOUR KEY\" H \"Content Type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"method\": \"analogous\", \"count\": 5, \"hue\": 45}' bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/vision/simulate\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"color\":\" "},{"t":"Plans, credits and quotas","d":"What each plan includes, how credits are charged per endpoint, rate limits, overage, spend caps, the hard ceiling, and the headers that report usage.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/plans-credits-and-quotas.html","h":["What each plan includes","Credits","When you run out","Reading the meter","The dashboard","Beyond the largest plan","Related pages"],"x":" Limits follow your account plan. The rate limit, monthly credits and credit balance are pooled per account, not per key. Plan API tier Requests per minute Credits per month Hard ceiling Max keys Apprentice free Free — Not included — — Artisan Paid — Not included — — Specialist Pro 300 1,000,000 10,000,000 10 Industrial Pro Enterprise 3,000 10,000,000 100,000,000 10 GET /v1/tiers returns the machine readable version of this table, so a client can read its own terms instead of hard coding them. Note: Industrial Pro was sold as \"Unlimited\" before 12 August 2026. Subscriptions created before that date keep that promise: they are metered at 1,000,000,000 credits a month, a hundred times the new figure, and their hard ceiling scales with that allowance. The 10,000,000 figure applies to subscriptions started on or after 12 August 2026. The monthly quota is counted in credits , not calls. One credit is one standard request; endpoints that do more work cost more, so simple colour maths does not subsidise image rendering. Every response states its cost in the x credits cost header. 1 credit : Standard work: /v1/color/convert , /v1/color/contrast , /v1/science/convert , /v1/accessibility/che"},{"t":"SDKs and tooling","d":"The official clients and integrations for the Auric Artisan API — JavaScript, Python, the CLI, an MCP server, a Postman collection and GraphQL.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/sdks-and-tooling.html","h":["The CLI and OAuth","Generating your own client","Retries","Related pages"],"x":" The API documentation lists these official clients and integrations. All of them use the same /v1 endpoints. Client Package or location Notes JavaScript @auric artisan/api Node 18 and later, browsers and Workers. Typed methods for every endpoint. Python auric artisan Python 3.8 and later, standard library only, no dependencies CLI @auric artisan/cli For example auric contrast ' 222' ' fff' in your terminal MCP server Listed on the API page Gives Claude, Cursor or any MCP host direct access to the colour tools Postman Listed on the API page A ready made collection covering the whole API GraphQL POST /v1/graphql A single endpoint alternative, with a playground at GET /v1/graphql Note: The documentation names these packages; check your package registry for their availability and current versions before depending on them. The auric CLI signs in with a device flow and sends an OAuth bearer token Authorization: Bearer <token instead of an API key. See Authentication authentication.md . GET /v1/openapi.yaml returns the OpenAPI 3.1 document, which most API tools can import or use to generate a client. GET /v1/catalog returns the same information as JSON, with parameters and examples. The "},{"t":"Reference","d":"Every customer endpoint of the Auric Artisan REST API with its method, authentication, credit cost and purpose, plus the headers, input formats, plans and limits.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/reference.html","h":["Essentials","Colour input","Endpoints","Response headers","Plans","Limits stated in the documentation","Related pages"],"x":" Item Value Base URL https://api.auricartisan.com Version prefix /v1 Format JSON over HTTPS Authentication x api key header or ?key= query , or Authorization: Bearer from the CLI Key prefix aa Keys per account Up to 10 active Revocation Takes effect within a minute Specification GET /v1/openapi.yaml OpenAPI 3.1 ; GET /v1/catalog JSON Interactive reference GET /v1/docs Unless a field says otherwise, a colour can be sent as rrggbb , rgb , rgb r,g,b , an array r,g,b or an object {r,g,b} . Image fields take Base64 or a data URL. Auth \"None\" means public and unmetered; \"Key\" needs an API key or bearer token. Credits are per call; see Plans, credits and quotas plans credits and quotas.md . The documentation gives some costs as ranges 2–4, 10–12 ; the exact cost of every call is returned in x credits cost . Endpoints the documentation does not weight separately bill as standard work, 1 credit. Method Path Auth Credits Summary GET /v1 None — Index of every endpoint, with the current version GET /v1/health None — Liveness probe; always cheap, never touches storage GET /v1/ready None — Readiness probe: whether each backing store is bound GET /v1/methods/:tool Key 1 The algorithms a given too"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Common problems with the Auric Artisan API — keys, plans, limits, credits, inputs, collections and the analyzer — and how to fix them.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/troubleshooting.html","h":["Keys and access","Limits and credits","Requests","Collections","Analyzer","Getting help","Related pages"],"x":" Symptom Why What to do 401 on every call No key, a mistyped key, or a revoked key Send the key in x api key ; check it starts with aa ; create a new one if it was revoked or lost 401 right after revoking a key Revocation takes effect within a minute Use another key 402 PLAN UPGRADE REQUIRED Your plan does not include the API Upgrade to Specialist or Industrial Pro I cannot create a key in the dashboard Key creation is available from the Specialist plan Upgrade, or use the public discovery endpoints meanwhile I lost a key The full key is shown once and stored only as a hash Create a new key and revoke the old one 403 FORBIDDEN The key has no rights for this route Check the path; use an endpoint listed in the Reference reference.md Symptom Why What to do 429 RATE LIMITED Too many requests this minute Wait for Retry After ; spread calls out 429 IP RATE LIMITED Too many requests from one address Slow down, whatever key you use 429 QUOTA EXCEEDED Included credits used up, overage off Turn on prepaid overage and add credits, or wait for the reset in details.resets at 402 INSUFFICIENT CREDITS Overage on, prepaid balance empty Add credits in the dashboard 402 SPEND CAP REACHED Your monthl"},{"t":"FAQ","d":"Short answers to common questions about the Auric Artisan REST API.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/faq.html","h":[],"x":" Specialist and Industrial Pro. Apprentice free and Artisan do not include it. Yes, partly. The discovery endpoints are open without a key: GET /v1 , GET /v1/catalog , GET /v1/openapi.yaml , GET /v1/docs , GET /v1/tiers , GET /v1/health and GET /v1/webhooks/events . Up to 10 active keys. They share one allowance, because limits are pooled per account. The unit the monthly quota is counted in. A standard request costs 1 credit; heavier work costs more, up to 25 for an async job. Each response says what it cost in x credits cost . Calls return 429 QUOTA EXCEEDED until the monthly reset, and nothing is charged, unless you turned on prepaid overage. No. Overage is off by default, spends only credits bought in advance, stops at a spend cap you set, and stops unconditionally at ten times your included allowance. Nothing is invoiced after the fact. Purchased credits do not expire at period end. Full terms are in the Subscription & Billing Policy. It uses the same engines where it can, but some things differ. The analyzer endpoints read a page's source and refuse checks that need a browser, such as contrast; the website's Analyzer runs pages in your browser. API credits and the website's t"},{"t":"Endpoints","d":"The groups of endpoints in the Auric Artisan REST API, with a page for each group.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/README.html","h":["Conventions","Pages"],"x":" Everything lives under /v1 on https://api.auricartisan.com. Each page below covers one group of endpoints: what each does, its parameters, what it returns and an example. The Reference ../reference.md lists them all in one table. Colours in request bodies can be written as rrggbb , rgb , rgb r,g,b , an array r,g,b or an object {r,g,b} , unless a field says otherwise. Tool endpoints take JSON through POST , with content type: application/json . Collection endpoints take query parameters through GET and page with offset and next offset , or with cursor and next cursor for the scanned collections. Path parameters are written :name , for example /v1/science/spaces/:key . Examples use $AURIC API KEY for your key. Auth \"None\" means the endpoint is public and unmetered. Everything else needs a key; see Authentication ../authentication.md . Page Endpoints Discovery discovery.md Index, health, readiness, methods, formats, tiers, status, metrics, catalogue, docs, OpenAPI Colour and colour science colour and science.md Convert, contrast, the 63 space registry, dossier, Delta E, colour temperature, illuminants, metrics Palettes, harmonies, gradients and shades palettes harmonies gradients sha"},{"t":"Accessibility","d":"Check colour pairs against WCAG 2.2 and APCA, get accessible alternatives, audit images and palettes, map accessible foregrounds on a background, and browse the contrast corpus.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/accessibility.html","h":["POST /v1/accessibility/check","POST /v1/accessibility/recommend","POST /v1/accessibility/from-image","POST /v1/accessibility/map","POST /v1/accessibility/picks","POST /v1/accessibility/audit","The contrast corpus","Related pages"],"x":" Check a foreground and background pair against WCAG 2.2 and APCA. 1 credit. Field Type Required Description fg colour Yes Text colour. foreground is accepted too. bg colour Yes The surface behind the text. background is accepted too. standard string No WCAG 2.1 , WCAG 2.2 , WCAG 3.0 , Auric SD Flexible , Auric SD Strict , or all the default bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/accessibility/check\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\":\" 767676\",\"bg\":\" ffffff\"}' Suggest the nearest accessible alternative to a failing pair. It keeps the hue and moves the lightness, so the fix still looks like the brand. target chooses which colour may move; set the level with minRatio . Field Type Required Description fg colour Yes Text colour foreground also accepted bg colour Yes Surface colour background also accepted target string No Which side to move: foreground default or background minRatio number No Contrast ratio to reach. Default 4.5. bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/accessibility/recommend\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\":\" c9a227\",\"bg\":\" ffffff\",\"target\":\"foreground\",\""},{"t":"Analyzer","d":"Audit web pages from their markup through the API — stages and scope, what page source can and cannot answer, why there is no overall score, rendering reports, errors, recipes and costs.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/analyzer.html","h":["When to use the API, and when to use the tool","Quick start","Stages and scope","What page source can and cannot answer","Why there is no overall score","GET /v1/analyzer/stages","POST /v1/analyzer/inspect","POST /v1/analyzer/render","Errors","Recipes","What is not here yet","Credits","Related pages"],"x":" Three endpoints put the URL Analyzer behind a REST call: ask what it can check, run the checks you want against one page, and turn the result into a document. The full guide is at https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/analyzer/. Method Path Credits Purpose GET /v1/analyzer/stages 1 What the analyzer can check, and how much of it markup alone can answer POST /v1/analyzer/inspect 12 Audit one page from its markup. No browser, no rendering. POST /v1/analyzer/render 10 Turn a report into an HTML or PDF document The analyzer on the website and this API differ in one way that decides which you want: the API reads a page's source ; the tool runs the page in a real browser. The tool This API Runs the page Yes, in your browser No: it reads the source Contrast, accessibility engine, deep DOM Yes Refused, with a reason SEO, metadata, security headers, sitemap, responsive signals Yes Yes Good for One page, looked at closely Many pages, on a schedule Paid with Tool tokens API credits Use the API to watch many pages for what a crawler can see: a title that went missing after a deploy, a canonical pointing at staging, a weakened Content Security Policy, an image that returns 404. Us"},{"t":"Collections","d":"Browse the colour atlas, find the nearest catalogued colour, and filter the palette, harmony, gradient and shade-scale collections.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/collections.html","h":["Colour atlas","Palette library (five million palettes)","Harmony library (8,192 harmonies)","Gradient library (8,192 gradients)","Shade library (8,192 scales)","Related pages"],"x":" The API exposes large, measured collections you can filter and cite. Two kinds exist: Finite catalogues of 8,192 records the colour atlas and the harmony, gradient and shade libraries . A filtered browse reports matched , a real total, and pages with offset and next offset . Scanned collections too large to count in one request five million palettes, and the five million pair accessibility corpus described in Accessibility accessibility.md . A filtered browse scans a budget of records and reports scanned , hit rate , next cursor , exhausted and truncated . Important: In a scanned collection, truncated: true means the scan budget ran out before the page filled, not that nothing matches. Follow next cursor , or raise max scan , before concluding a filter is empty. exhausted: true means the collection really ended. Records in the libraries are derived from a published seed and their index rather than stored, so an id such as pal 1z or har 5k is citable: anyone can recompute the same record. Browse the 8,192 colour atlas under a filter. Hue ranges wrap, so hue from=340&hue to=20 gives the reds. Parameter Description hue from , hue to Hue range, 0–360; wraps past 360 min lightness , ma"},{"t":"Colour and colour science","d":"Convert colours, check a contrast ratio, and use the 63-space colour registry, dossiers, Delta E, colour temperature, illuminants and difference metrics.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/colour-and-science.html","h":["POST /v1/color/convert","POST /v1/color/contrast","GET /v1/science/spaces","GET /v1/science/spaces/:key","POST /v1/science/convert","POST /v1/science/dossier","POST /v1/science/delta-e","POST /v1/science/temperature","GET /v1/science/illuminants","GET /v1/science/metrics","Related pages"],"x":" Convert one colour between the common spaces. 1 credit. For the full 63 space registry with white point control, use /v1/science/convert . Field Type Required Description color colour Yes rrggbb , rgb , rgb r,g,b , r,g,b or {r,g,b} to string No One target space. Omit it to get every common space at once. bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/color/convert\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"color\":\" c9a227\",\"to\":\"lab\"}' The WCAG contrast ratio between two colours, with pass or fail at each level. 1 credit. Field Type Required Description fg colour Yes Foreground colour bg colour Yes Background colour deltaE number No Difference formula: 76, 94 or 2000 the default Returns ratio number , aa , aaa and aa large booleans . bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/color/contrast\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"fg\":\" 767676\",\"bg\":\" ffffff\"}' For WCAG 2.2 and APCA together, use /v1/accessibility/check accessibility.md . Every colour space the platform knows, with provenance: sixty three spaces across RGB working spaces, CIE spaces, perceptual and appearance models, HDR containers, pr"},{"t":"Discovery endpoints","d":"The public endpoints that describe the API itself — index, health, readiness, methods, formats, tiers, status, metrics, catalogue and documentation.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/discovery.html","h":["GET /v1","GET /v1/health","GET /v1/ready","GET /v1/methods/:tool","GET /v1/formats","GET /v1/tiers","GET /v1/catalog","GET /v1/docs and GET /v1/openapi.yaml","GET /v1/status and GET /v1/metrics","Related pages"],"x":" These endpoints describe the API. All but one are public and unmetered, so you can evaluate the API before buying. Method Path Auth Purpose GET /v1 None Index of every endpoint, with the current version GET /v1/health None Liveness probe; always cheap, never touches storage GET /v1/ready None Readiness probe: whether each backing store is bound GET /v1/methods/:tool Key The algorithms a given tool supports GET /v1/formats None Every export format, across every exportable resource GET /v1/tiers None Rate limit and monthly quota for each tier GET /v1/metrics None Process level counters in Prometheus format GET /v1/status None Human readable status page GET /v1/catalog None Every endpoint with its parameters and examples, as JSON GET /v1/docs None Interactive reference Redoc GET /v1/openapi.yaml None The OpenAPI 3.1 document Returns version string and endpoints string array . bash curl \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1\" Returns ok boolean and time ISO 8601 . bash curl \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/health\" Returns ready boolean and checks object . Use it in a deployment gate: /v1/health says the service is up, while /v1/ready says it can actually serve. bash curl \"https://api.aurica"},{"t":"Palettes, harmonies, gradients and shades","d":"Generate, score, classify, analyse, export and render palettes, harmonies, gradients and shade scales.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/palettes-harmonies-gradients-shades.html","h":["Palettes","Harmonies","Gradients","Shades","Related pages"],"x":" These endpoints build colour sets and measure the ones you already have. Valid method values come from GET /v1/methods/:tool , and valid export format values from GET /v1/formats . Generate a palette from a seed colour. 2–4 credits. Field Type Required Description method string No See /v1/methods/palette . Default triadic . hue number No Base hue, 0–360. Random when omitted. saturation number No 0–1. Default 0.7. lightness number No 0–1. Default 0.55. count integer No How many colours, 1–64. Default 5. seed integer No For a repeatable palette bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/palette/generate\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"method\":\"triadic\",\"hue\":45,\"saturation\":0.7,\"lightness\":0.55,\"count\":5}' Score a palette for harmony, contrast and accessibility. Field Type Required Description palette object Yes { colors: { rgb: r,g,b }, ... } , the shape /v1/palette/generate returns bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/palette/evaluate\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"palette\":{\"colors\": {\"rgb\": 201,162,39 },{\"rgb\": 29,42,62 },{\"rgb\": 255,252,247 } }}' Render a palette into "},{"t":"Design tokens and personalisation","d":"Generate a contrast-checked design-token system from one colour, export it for ten platforms, and run the brief-driven palette search and design-system generator.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/tokens-and-personalisation.html","h":["Design tokens","Personalisation","Related pages"],"x":" Turn one seed colour into a complete, contrast checked token system. 2–4 credits. Ramps are stepped in OKLCH so every hue is perceptually even, chroma follows a gamut aware envelope so the light and dark ends stay distinct, and foreground roles are measured: color on primary is whichever of white or ink actually clears 4.5:1. Field Type Required Description seed colour Yes The seed colour name string No System name used in file headers harmony string No analogous default , complementary , triadic or mono include string array No Any of color , space , radius , type . Default all. dark boolean No Include dark mode roles. Default true . Returns meta , contrast , out of gamut and tokens . bash curl X POST \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/tokens/generate\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" \\ H \"content type: application/json\" \\ d '{\"seed\":\" c9a227\",\"name\":\"Auric\",\"harmony\":\"analogous\"}' Render a token deck for a platform. There are ten targets, from CSS custom properties to Jetpack Compose. Field Type Required Description tokens array Yes Objects of { name, value, group? } : the tokens array from generate, or your own format string Yes See /v1/tokens/formats name string No System name for"},{"t":"Usage, jobs, webhooks and GraphQL","d":"Read your usage history and live feed, run long work as asynchronous jobs, subscribe to webhooks, and query the API through GraphQL.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/usage-jobs-webhooks-graphql.html","h":["Usage","Async jobs","Webhooks","GraphQL","Related pages"],"x":" Per day, per endpoint usage history. Parameter In Description since query Earliest day to include, YYYY MM DD . Defaults to seven days back. bash curl \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/usage\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" Your tier, limits and month to date consumption. bash curl \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/usage/me\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" json {\"tier\":\"pro\",\"plan\":\"specialist\",\"auth type\":\"api key\", \"limits\":{\"rate per minute\":300,\"monthly quota\":1000000}, \"this month\":{\"slot\":\"2026 08\",\"used\":412}} used counts credits, not calls. The last 100 individual calls, with rolling latency and error statistics. It answers \"what is happening right now\", where /v1/usage answers \"how much have I used\". Pass the returned cursor back as since to poll for new calls only. Parameter In Description limit query 1–100. Default 50. since query Sequence number from a previous cursor Returns cursor , stats and events . The same live feed, pushed over Server Sent Events SSE . It emits hello on connect with current stats, usage for each request, and heartbeat every 15 seconds. Connections are capped at 10 minutes; a browser EventSource reconnects on its own. 5 credits, charged once when t"},{"t":"Vision and Ishihara","d":"Simulate colour-vision deficiencies for a colour, a palette or an image, find pairs that become indistinguishable, and generate Ishihara plates.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/docs/endpoints/vision-and-ishihara.html","h":["GET /v1/vision/models","GET /v1/vision/conditions","GET /v1/vision/conditions/:slug","GET /v1/vision/matrices","POST /v1/vision/simulate","POST /v1/vision/palette","POST /v1/vision/audit","POST /v1/vision/simulate-image","POST /v1/ishihara/plate","POST /v1/ishihara/png","Related pages"],"x":" The vision endpoints distinguish two kinds of identifier: Models are simulation engines, such as brettel deutan . List them with GET /v1/vision/models . Conditions are documented vision conditions, such as deuteranopia or glaucoma . List them with GET /v1/vision/conditions . /v1/vision/simulate takes a model. The palette and audit endpoints take conditions. The colour vision deficiency models available. Every documented vision condition, and what can simulate it. One condition, with its severity, prevalence and a worked example. :slug is a condition slug such as deuteranopia or glaucoma . An unknown slug returns UNKNOWN CONDITION . bash curl \"https://api.auricartisan.com/v1/vision/conditions/deuteranopia\" \\ H \"x api key: $AURIC API KEY\" The colour vision deficiency matrices, for applying the transform yourself. How one colour appears under a vision deficiency. 1 credit. Field Type Required Description color colour Yes The colour model string Yes A model id such as brettel deutan ; see /v1/vision/models severity number No 0–1, for anomalous trichromacy A condition slug such as deuteranopia is refused here; the error names the model it maps to. To work with conditions, use POST /v1/"},{"t":"Other material","d":"Background material for the public API — glossary, limits and accuracy, related products, release notes and privacy.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/README.html","h":["Files in this folder"],"x":" This folder holds the reference material around the API guides: the terms they use, what the results can and cannot tell you, related products, the documentation's history, and what the API keeps about your use. Page What it covers Glossary glossary.md API, colour science and accessibility terms Limits and accuracy limits and accuracy.md What the results measure, how precisely, and what they are not Related related.md Website tools, the dashboard, and other Auric Artisan products Release notes release notes.md Dated changes stated in the API documentation Privacy privacy.md Keys, usage records, what analyzer requests fetch "},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Definitions of the API, colour-science and accessibility terms used in the public API documentation.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/glossary.html","h":["API terms","Colour science","Accessibility"],"x":" API key. A secret string, starting aa , that identifies your account on each request. Created in the dashboard and shown once. Async job. Work that takes too long for one request. You queue it, receive an id, then poll it or follow it over SSE. Credit. The unit your monthly quota is counted in. A standard call costs 1; heavier calls cost more. Cursor. A position in a scanned collection. Pass next cursor back as cursor to continue. Discovery endpoint. A public, unmetered endpoint that describes the API, such as /v1/catalog . GraphQL. A query language that lets one request ask several questions at once, through /v1/graphql . Hard ceiling. The absolute monthly limit, ten times the included allowance, that stops runaway usage. OpenAPI. A standard, machine readable description of an HTTP API, served at /v1/openapi.yaml . Overage. Usage beyond the included credits, paid from a prepaid credit balance, and only if you turn it on. Quota. Your included credits for the month. Rate limit. How many requests you may make per minute. Scope and stage. In the analyzer, a stage is one group of checks; scope is the list of stages you ask for. Server Sent Events SSE . A way for a server to push a str"},{"t":"Limits and accuracy","d":"What the Auric Artisan API's results measure, how precisely, and where they need judgement.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/limits-and-accuracy.html","h":["Colour science","Accessibility","Vision simulation","Collections","Analyzer","Operational limits","Related pages"],"x":" Delta E: CIEDE2000 is the headline figure and is verified against the Sharma reference set, the standard test data for that formula. Colour temperature is only meaningful near the Planckian locus. The response reports Duv and a meaningful flag; beyond about ±0.05 Duv, a temperature does not describe the colour. Nearest colour in the atlas uses CIE76 distance in Lab, and the response names the metric. Contrast checks work on the colours you send. They cannot know what is actually behind text on a real page; for that, measure the rendered page, for example with the website's Analyzer or the browser extension. APCA is a draft method for WCAG 3; its thresholds may change. /v1/accessibility/map returns null lightness for hues that can never reach the target on a background. That is a real answer, not a failure. /v1/accessibility/audit and /v1/accessibility/picks refuse to return colours that do not meet the target. Simulations model how colours may appear with a deficiency; they are not a diagnosis, and individual vision varies. /v1/vision/palette and /v1/vision/audit simulate colour conditions; spatial conditions are listed under refused . Library and corpus records are derived from a"},{"t":"Privacy","d":"What the Auric Artisan API keeps about your keys and usage, and what analyzer requests fetch, as its documentation describes.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/privacy.html","h":["Keys","Usage records","What you send","Analyzer requests","Webhooks","Related pages"],"x":" This page covers what the API's documentation says about data. The site's privacy policy, https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/, covers your account as a whole. The full key is shown once, when you create it, and stored only as a SHA 256 hash. Nobody can recover it later. Each successful request updates the key's \"last used\" time, visible in your dashboard. The API keeps a record of your use so it can meter and report it: per day, per endpoint history, available through GET /v1/usage ; the last 100 individual calls with latency and errors, through GET /v1/usage/live and the stream; your month to date credits, through GET /v1/usage/me . Error responses carry a request id so a specific call can be traced when you ask for support. The API processes the colours, palettes, images, reports and other values you send in order to answer the request. Do not send personal data you do not need to. POST /v1/analyzer/inspect fetches the public URL you name and reads its source. Private and reserved addresses are refused. POST /v1/analyzer/render fetches nothing: it renders the report you send. Webhook deliveries go only to the HTTPS URLs you register, and are signed so you can verify they cam"},{"t":"Release notes","d":"The dated changes to the public API that its documentation states.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/release-notes.html","h":["3 September 2026 — Analyzer API guide","12 August 2026 — Credits, overage and new Industrial Pro allowance","8 July 2026 — REST API reference","Upcoming"],"x":" The API has no separate public changelog. These are the dated facts its documentation states. The current version is always reported by GET /v1 . A guide to the three analyzer endpoints was published: GET /v1/analyzer/stages , POST /v1/analyzer/inspect and POST /v1/analyzer/render . The analyzer endpoints read page source only, refuse checks that need a browser, and return no overall score. Costs: 1, 12 and 10 credits. The REST API reference was updated. The monthly quota is counted in credits, with heavier endpoints costing more than one credit. Prepaid, opt in pay as you go overage, a monthly spend cap and a hard ceiling of ten times the included allowance. Industrial Pro's allowance became 10,000,000 credits a month for subscriptions started on or after this date. Earlier Industrial Pro subscriptions, sold as \"Unlimited\", keep 1,000,000,000 credits a month. The REST API reference was published, with API keys created in the account dashboard. The analyzer guide lists two things \"not here yet\": a rendered scan contrast, the accessibility engine and deep DOM comparison through the API and a whole site crawl as a job. "},{"t":"Related","d":"The dashboard, website tools and other Auric Artisan products that relate to the public API.","p":"Services › Public API","u":"services/public-api/others/related.html","h":["Your account","Documentation on the site","Website tools that share the API's engines","Other products"],"x":" Dashboard: create and revoke keys, watch usage and cost, buy credits and set spend controls at https://auricartisan.com/auth/dashboard/. See the Account and billing ../../../website/account and billing/README.md docs. Plans: compare plans at https://auricartisan.com/company/pricing/. Billing policy: https://auricartisan.com/legal/subscription billing/. REST API reference: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/ Analyzer API guide: https://auricartisan.com/library/documentation/api/analyzer/ Tool Docs Analyzer Analyzer ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/analyzer/README.md Contrast Checker Contrast Checker ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/contrast checker/README.md Vision Simulation Vision Simulation ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/vision simulation/README.md Ishihara Plate Generator Ishihara plates ../../../website/tools/accessibility and vision/ishihara plate generator/README.md Personalisation Generator Personalisation Generator ../../../website/tools/colour workspace/personalisation generator/README.md Colour libraries Colour libraries ../../../website/library/colour libraries/README.md Browser extension ../../../browser ex"},{"t":"Design tool plugins","d":"Which Auric Artisan plugins for design tools and launchers exist, what they are planned to do, and why none can be installed yet.","p":"Design tool plugins","u":"design-tool-plugins/README.html","h":["What exists","Planned capabilities in brief","When they are released","Related pages"],"x":" Auric Artisan is building small plugins that bring its colour and accessibility checks into design tools and launchers: Figma, Penpot, Sketch, Raycast and Alfred. None of them is published yet. There is no listing in the Figma Community, the Penpot plugin catalogue, the Raycast Store or elsewhere, and no download on auricartisan.com. This page will become full documentation for each plugin when it can be installed. In the meantime, the same checks are available today in the browser extension ../browser extension/README.md , in the VS Code extensions see the VS Code extensions section of these docs , and in the tools on https://auricartisan.com. Plugin Host Planned purpose Status Auric Artisan for Figma Figma Audit layers for WCAG and APCA contrast, generate palettes, fix failing pairs, preview colour vision Not published Auric Artisan for Penpot Penpot The same audit, palette, fix and vision workflow for Penpot files Not published Auric Artisan for Sketch Sketch on macOS Menu commands to audit a selection, auto fix failing pairs, generate a palette and preview colour vision Not published Auric Artisan for Raycast Raycast on macOS A Check Contrast command for any two colours, with "},{"t":"Help","d":"General help for Auric Artisan — frequently asked questions, a glossary, troubleshooting, accessibility, privacy, and how to get support.","p":"Help","u":"help/README.html","h":["Other places to look"],"x":" This folder answers questions that apply across Auric Artisan rather than to one tool: what things mean, why something is not working, how the site works with assistive technology, what happens to your data, and how to reach a person. Tool specific help lives in each tool's own troubleshooting page under Website tools ../website/tools/README.md . Page What it covers FAQ faq.md Common questions about the platform, the tools, accounts, payments, privacy and the other products Glossary glossary.md General, accessibility and colour science terms used across the product Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md Browser support, cookies and consent, sign in, payments, offline use, and clearing data Accessibility of the site accessibility.md Keyboard use, screen readers, comfort settings, and reporting barriers Privacy overview privacy.md What is stored locally, what is sent, analytics consent, third parties and your rights Contact and support contact and support.md Which inbox to write to, reply times, and how to write a message that gets a fast answer New to Auric Artisan: Getting started ../getting started/README.md . Account, plans and billing: Account and billing ../website/account and bil"},{"t":"Accessibility of the site","d":"How to use the Auric Artisan website with a keyboard, a screen reader or comfort settings, what the site aims to support, its known limits, and how to report a barrier.","p":"Help","u":"help/accessibility.html","h":["What the site aims to support","Using the keyboard","Comfort and reading settings","Screen readers","Known limits","Reporting a barrier"],"x":" This page is about using the Auric Artisan website itself with a disability or with assistive technology. For checking the accessibility of your own designs, see the accessibility tools under Website tools ../website/tools/README.md . The official statement is https://auricartisan.com/company/accessibility/, summarised in Accessibility statement ../website/company and legal/docs/accessibility statement.md . The Accessibility Statement names these aims: semantic HTML with headings and landmarks; keyboard access to all core functionality; readable, contrast aware and scalable text; compatibility with modern screen readers; ARIA semantics for dynamic widgets; and visible focus with a logical tab order. It says important areas are reviewed against WCAG 2.1 Level AA where practical. Keys What it does Tab / Shift + Tab Move between controls Enter / Space Activate a button or link Esc Close dialogs, panels and menus Ctrl + K Open search ? Open the guide when not typing Ctrl + , Open or close Settings Alt + R Reading mode on or off Alt + T Switch theme light, dark, system Alt + + / Alt + − / Alt + 0 Larger, smaller, or reset text size Alt + M Reduced motion on or off Tab lists — for examp"},{"t":"Contact and support","d":"How to reach Auric Artisan — choosing the right topic and inbox, reply times, attaching screenshots, what to include, and what happens after you send.","p":"Help","u":"help/contact-and-support.html","h":["Before you write","Choose the right topic","Send a message","Attach screenshots","Write a message that gets a fast answer","Security reports","Other addresses on the site","Open the form on a topic","Related"],"x":" Every message is read and answered by a person — the contact page says there is \"no ticket queue and no bot in front of it\". The contact form is at https://auricartisan.com/company/contact/. Many questions are answered in the FAQ faq.md , the FAQ page https://auricartisan.com/company/faq/ on the site, or Troubleshooting troubleshooting.md . Inside the site, press ? for the Guide or Ctrl + K to search. Each topic on the contact page shows links that might answer your question faster. The topic decides which inbox receives your message and how quickly you can expect a reply. Topic Goes to Use it for Reference field asks for Reply time Using a tool hello@auricartisan.com How to do something Link to the tool or page 2–3 days Billing hello@auricartisan.com Payments, refunds, receipts, discounts Order or invoice ID starts with order 1–2 days Something else hello@auricartisan.com Anything not listed Anything that helps place it Up to a week A bug developer@auricartisan.com Something broken, including accessibility barriers URL where it happened 2–4 days API or integration developer@auricartisan.com The REST API, keys, SDKs Endpoint, or a request ID 2–4 days Security security@auricartisan"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","d":"Fixes for general Auric Artisan problems — browser support, pages that look out of date, cookies and consent, sign-in, payments, offline use, language and theme, and clearing site data.","p":"Help","u":"help/troubleshooting.html","h":["Browser support","A page looks out of date or broken","Cookies and consent","Sign-in problems","Payments","Offline and the installed app","Language and theme","Clear site data and start fresh","Still stuck"],"x":" Each entry gives the symptom, the likely cause and what to do. Problems specific to one tool are covered in that tool's own troubleshooting page; account and payment problems in detail are in Account and billing troubleshooting ../website/account and billing/docs/troubleshooting.md . The website is built for current, modern browsers. The download page says the same package runs on Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, iOS and iPadOS, and that offline caching works \"anywhere with a service worker and a secure origin\". Symptom Why What to do A tool does not start, or a panel stays blank An old browser version, or a browser feature the tool needs such as canvas or WebGL graphics is turned off Update your browser; try another current browser Copy buttons do nothing The browser blocked clipboard access Allow clipboard access for auricartisan.com, or select and copy the text yourself The eyedropper in Settings is missing Not every browser offers a screen eyedropper Use the colour picker beside it A download or export window does not open A pop up blocker stopped it Allow pop ups for auricartisan.com The site behaves oddly in one browser only An extension ad blocker, script blocker i"},{"t":"Frequently asked questions","d":"Short answers to common questions about Auric Artisan — the platform, the tools, accounts, payments, privacy, languages, offline use and the other products.","p":"Help","u":"help/faq.html","h":["The platform","The tools","Accounts and payments","Privacy","Language, theme and offline","Other products","Getting help"],"x":" A colour science and accessibility platform: tools, libraries and learning material on the website, plus a browser extension, VS Code extensions and a REST API. See What Auric Artisan is ../getting started/what is auric artisan.md . One independent developer, Chirag Bansal, in India. The Security page notes the platform is operated by one person. See Author page ../website/company and legal/docs/author.md . Every tool is free on every plan, with no login needed to start. Paid plans add conveniences such as ad free browsing, watermark free exports, a monthly token allowance and higher limits. See The free tools model ../getting started/free tools model.md . The free plan's card on the pricing page says \"Sponsored slots ads support the free tools\". Paid plans include ad free browsing. The Subscription and Billing Policy says ads shown to free users are limited and consent gated, and that private data is not used for advertising profiles. No. It is an independent private platform. References to CIE, W3C or ISO standards are informational and do not imply affiliation. For design, accessibility evaluation, palette work and web work, the outputs follow published standards. They are guid"},{"t":"Glossary","d":"Plain-language definitions of the general, accessibility and colour-science terms used across Auric Artisan's tools and documentation.","p":"Help","u":"help/glossary.html","h":["General and site terms","Accessibility terms","Colour vision","Colour science","Colour harmony","Perception research"],"x":" Terms used across the website, the extensions and these docs. Tool specific terms are defined again in each tool's own glossary. Account and billing terms are in Account and billing glossary ../website/account and billing/others/glossary.md ; legal terms are in Company and legal glossary ../website/company and legal/others/glossary.md . Accent colour — The highlight colour the site uses for buttons and marks. Auric gold by default; you can change it in Settings . API — Application programming interface: a way for your own code to use Auric Artisan's functions over the internet. The REST API is metered in API credits. Cache — Copies of pages and files your browser keeps so they load faster or work offline. Collection — A named group of saved items in your library. Design tokens — Named values colours, sizes, spacing exported in a format a build system reads, such as JSON, so a design system can be shared between design and code. CSS custom properties — Variables in CSS, written like color primary , that design tokens are often exported as. Export — Saving a result out of a tool as a file PNG, SVG, PDF, JSON, CSS and so on or as copied text. Kit — A floating panel that opens over an"},{"t":"Privacy overview","d":"What Auric Artisan stores in your browser, what it sends to its servers and third parties, how analytics consent works, what each product collects, and how to use your privacy rights.","p":"Help","u":"help/privacy.html","h":["Stored in your browser","Sent to Auric Artisan's servers","Analytics and consent","Third parties","What each product collects","No sale, no tracking across sites","Your rights, in practice","Related"],"x":" This page brings together what the policies and the product say about your data. The authoritative documents are the Privacy Policy https://auricartisan.com/legal/privacy/ , the Cookie Policy https://auricartisan.com/legal/cookies/ , the Data Retention and Deletion Policy and, for the browser extension, the Extension Privacy Policy. Plain language summaries of each are in Company and legal ../website/company and legal/README.md . What Notes My Library palettes, gradients, collections, exports Stays on this device; not uploaded unless you publish or export it Tool state and drafts, including the Portfolio Builder draft Stays on this device Settings: theme, language, accent colour, text size, comfort options, eye rest The Privacy Policy says many preferences are not sent to the servers Your cookie choice Kept for up to a year The offline cache, if you prepared one The site's pages and data, for offline use Your sign in session and CSRF cookies Only when you sign in; up to 30 days or until sign out Anything in your browser is lost if you clear site data, and does not follow you to other devices. See Clear site data and start fresh troubleshooting.md clear site data and start fresh . "}];
